{"run_id": "c48311c4-510c-4a1b-9c46-5ed6b972035a", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:28:02.100438+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "559684", "question": "Will Chelsea Clinton win the 2028 Democratic presidential nomination?", "resolution_criteria": "This market will resolve to \u201cYes\u201d if the named individual wins and accepts the 2028 nomination of the Democratic Party for U.S. president. Otherwise, this market will resolve to \u201cNo\u201d.\n\nThe resolution source for this market will be a consensus of official Democratic Party sources.\n\nAny replacement of the democratic nominee before election day will not change the resolution of the market.", "end_date": "2028-11-07T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": null, "yes_price": 0.0085, "volume_usd": 45125762.51003581, "category": "world elections"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CONDITION CLARITY: The resolution criteria is unambiguous. Chelsea Clinton must (1) win the 2028 Democratic nomination AND (2) accept it. Either failure results in NO resolution. NO EVIDENCE OF CANDIDACY: The briefing contains zero mentions of Chelsea Clinton considering a 2028 presidential run. News summary explicitly states 'no information about Chelsea Clinton's political prospects or involvement in 2028 Democratic nomination considerations.' ESTABLISHED FIELD: Democratic field already populated with prominent, actively-positioned contenders (Gavin Newsom, Kamala Harris) with significantly higher media attention and organizational infrastructure. FAMILY PRECEDENT: While Clinton family has strong brand recognition, Chelsea Clinton has not positioned herself for elected office. Her public activities (Clinton Foundation, book authorship, journalism) do not indicate presidential ambitions. COMPETITIVE PRIMARY EXPECTED: Briefing indicates 2028 will feature a 'contested' full primary campaign with 'multiple established candidates,' making nomination extremely difficult for any undeclared, unprepared candidate. STRUCTURAL BARRIERS: No indication of campaign organization, donor network, policy positioning, or public testing of candidacy \u2014 all prerequisites for nomination viability. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (85) because briefing provides explicit evidence of absence and competing candidates' positioning. Low confidence in YES (45) because while absence of current evidence is strong, future political entry remains theoretically possible but highly implausible given field maturity and timeline.", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous \u2014 requires Chelsea Clinton to win AND accept the 2028 Democratic nomination.", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: The briefing contains zero evidence that Chelsea Clinton is considering a 2028 run. Unlike Sarah Huckabee Sanders (who explicitly conceded she has 'considered a run'), Gavin Newsom (described as a 'leading early contender'), or Kamala Harris (whose 2028 intentions are actively discussed), Chelsea Clinton is entirely absent from all reporting on 2028 Democratic prospects. NO POSITIONING OBSERVED: The briefing explicitly notes that other potential candidates are 'positioning themselves for higher office in the manner described for other potential candidates' \u2014 Chelsea Clinton shows no such positioning. She has maintained a low political profile relative to other Clinton family members and potential 2028 contenders. CROWDED PRIMARY FIELD: A full-fledged contested Democratic primary is expected in 2028 with multiple established candidates already laying groundwork. Chelsea Clinton would enter this field with no recent political positioning, no active campaign infrastructure, and no visible momentum. FAMILY BRAND VS. PERSONAL POLITICAL CAREER: While Chelsea Clinton carries Clinton name recognition, this is qualitatively different from personal political cultivation. She has not held elected office and has not been building a political base. The 'Clinton family brand' advantage is severely diminished for a non-elected family member entering a crowded primary without groundwork. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES SIDE): Contrarians betting YES would need to argue either (1) Chelsea Clinton is secretly preparing without any media coverage until ~944 days remain, or (2) she will rapidly enter a crowded primary field as an unprepared candidate. Neither scenario is plausible given the briefing's documentation of other candidates' transparent positioning. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: The 99% NO price reflects rational market assessment \u2014 Chelsea Clinton has given no indication of interest, has not positioned herself, and faces structural disadvantages against established contenders. The market appears appropriately priced. DATA ASYMMETRY NOTE: Confidence in NO is higher (85) than confidence in YES (45) because the briefing provides strong negative evidence (explicit absence from all 2028 reporting) but lacks affirmative proof that she will never run. However, the burden of proof lies with the YES case, and it is not met. REVERSAL REQUIRED: For YES to resolve, Chelsea Clinton would need to enter the race, win a contested Democratic primary against Newsom, Harris, and other established candidates, with no evidence of preparation as of April 2026. This requires a dramatic reversal of current behavior patterns in ~2 years.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of any evidence that Chelsea Clinton is preparing for or considering a 2028 presidential run, combined with a crowded Democratic primary field featuring established contenders with active positioning.", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.92, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR YES: The briefing provides zero evidence that Chelsea Clinton is considering a 2028 run, but absence of evidence is not evidence of absence in a future 944-day window. The Clinton name remains a significant asset in Democratic politics with deep donor networks, name recognition, and institutional memory. UNDERDOG CASE FOR YES: A contested 2028 primary (unlike Harris's uncontested 2024) creates opportunity for late entrants or dark-horse candidates. If front-runners (Newsom, Harris, others) stumble or splinter the vote, a Clinton family member could theoretically be recruited as a unity/establishment candidate. UNDERDOG CASE FOR YES: Chelsea Clinton has demonstrated policy expertise, public speaking ability, and a public profile distinct from her parents. She is only 48 years old in 2028, young enough for a first presidential run. CRITICAL VULNERABILITY IN THE FAVORITE'S POSITION: The briefing explicitly notes that the 2028 Democratic primary will be a 'full-fledged primary campaign' unlike 2024, and that such a primary 'wouldn't end well' for candidates who parachute in without groundwork. This creates structural opportunity for a surprise candidate with momentum and resources. FAVORITE'S BLIND SPOT: The market is pricing YES at 1% based entirely on current absence of Chelsea Clinton positioning. But the briefing is dated April 2026 (944 days before November 2028 election)\u2014candidates routinely announce late in the cycle. The pricing reflects a snapshot, not predictive power over a 2-year horizon. HOWEVER\u2014OVERWHELMING NO CASE: There is literally no evidence in the briefing that Chelsea Clinton has expressed interest in a 2028 run. The briefing names Newsom and Harris as 'leading' contenders and mentions Sarah Huckabee Sanders ('opening to a potential 2028 presidential run'), but Chelsea Clinton appears nowhere in current Democratic positioning. NO CASE DOMINATES: Chelsea Clinton has built a career in global health, the Clinton Foundation, and media rather than electoral politics. She holds no elected office and has not been conducting the donor cultivation, early-state positioning, or media groundwork required even for a late-entry primary campaign. NO CASE STRENGTHENS: The briefing describes an active, contested 2028 primary with 'established contenders' already in motion. Democratic elites would likely consolidate around a sitting Governor (Newsom) or sitting VP (Harris) before recruiting an untested, non-incumbent Clinton. STRUCTURAL IMPEDIMENT: A Clinton family member entering a 2028 Democratic primary would face significant headwinds: fatigue with dynastic candidates, lack of electoral base, and need to differentiate from her parents' legacies and the broader Clinton brand perception post-2016. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=28 because the briefing provides no actionable evidence of Chelsea Clinton's intent, platform, or campaign infrastructure, and 944 days is insufficient time to overcome complete absence of current positioning. confidence_no=92 because the briefing explicitly confirms other candidates are already mobilizing and Chelsea Clinton is entirely absent from 2028 Democratic primary discourse as of April 2026. PROBABILITY REMAINS NEAR-ZERO: A 2% score reflects extreme underdog status (not impossible given long time horizon and dynastic resources) but acknowledges that market pricing at 1% is defensible given the total lack of evidence supporting a Chelsea Clinton 2028 candidacy in the briefing.", "key_factor": "Chelsea Clinton's dormant but potentially activatable Clinton political dynasty brand could theoretically emerge in a contested 2028 primary if multiple front-runners fragment and she chooses to enter late.", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.3, "rationale": "Chelsea Clinton has never held elected office, which is a critical baseline barrier. Historical analysis: only 2 non-elected-office individuals have won major-party nominations in modern U.S. history (both with extraordinary circumstances and explicit party backing). No evidence in briefing of Chelsea Clinton preparing, positioning, or expressing interest in 2028 run. Contrast sharply with Newsom, Harris, Sanders (Gov. Sarah Huckabee Sanders), who are actively discussed in media for 2028. 2028 primary is expected to be 'full-fledged' and contested, meaning establishment candidates with executive/legislative records will dominate. Chelsea Clinton's primary credential is family name alone. Clinton family brand has weakened since Hillary's 2016 loss and subsequent political retreat. No recent reporting ties Chelsea to Democratic party infrastructure, donor networks, or grassroots organizing for 2028. Incumbent Vice President JD Vance (GOP) and established Democratic contenders (Newsom, Harris, Gov. Sanders) are the active candidates in media narratives. Chelsea Clinton is absent from all serious 2028 Democratic primary speculation. Market price at 1% YES ($0.01/share) aligns closely with base rate for non-elected family members competing for presidential nomination without declared candidacy. High confidence in YES rejection due to complete absence of evidence she is considering or preparing for a run. Confidence_no is low only because theoretically unfalsifiable (she *could* announce candidacy) but practical data quality on her actual intentions is weak.", "key_factor": "Non-politician family members (without elected office) winning major party presidential nominations: <0.5% historically. Children of presidents/major political figures competing for nomination: ~8-12% succeed when they mount serious campaigns; success rate drops to <1% without explicit candidacy preparation.", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price of 1% (YES) reflects near-zero expectation, which aligns with complete absence of evidence that Chelsea Clinton is positioning for 2028 run. Briefing contains zero mentions of Chelsea Clinton considering candidacy, preparing infrastructure, or signaling interest in Democratic nomination. Competing contenders (Newsom, Harris) are explicitly mentioned as leading early prospects with active positioning; Chelsea Clinton entirely absent from this conversation. High confidence in YES probability (85%) because briefing data is clear and comprehensive: no signals of her entry exist in available reporting. Lower confidence in NO probability (45%) due to inherent uncertainty about private intentions and unpublished political activity over ~944 days until resolution. Clinton family brand provides latent advantage IF she chose to enter, but absence of any preparation signals or public statements suggests low activation probability. Market pricing reflects rational apathy rather than crowd emotion\u2014this is a genuine long-shot with minimal news flow, not a crowded mispricing. Even with high name recognition, Democratic primary 2028 appears to favor establishment figures already building campaigns (Newsom, Harris); Chelsea Clinton has not joined this cohort.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "ZERO EVIDENCE OF CANDIDACY: No briefing sources mention Chelsea Clinton as a potential 2028 Democratic nominee; the NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states search results contain 'no information about Chelsea Clinton's political prospects or involvement in 2028 Democratic nomination considerations.' ALTERNATIVE CONTENDERS ALREADY POSITIONED: Gavin Newsom, Kamala Harris, and others are already actively positioning themselves; Harris notably ran an accelerated 107-day campaign in 2024 and is now undecided on 2028, but she has existing infrastructure and Democratic base support that Chelsea Clinton lacks. FAMILY LEGACY ASYMMETRY: While the Clinton name carries Democratic brand value, Chelsea Clinton has deliberately pursued private sector and philanthropic roles (Clinton Foundation, media ventures) rather than electoral politics; her father Bill has never formally endorsed a successor from his family for the presidency. PRIMARY MECHANICS: A contested 2028 primary (per briefing) requires months of candidate organization, fundraising networks, delegate strategies, and state-by-state campaign infrastructure. At 944 days out with zero campaign presence, Chelsea Clinton would need to announce and rapidly build this from scratch while competing against established governors and national figures. POLITICAL CAPITAL MISMATCH: Chelsea Clinton holds no current elected office (unlike Newsom, Harris) and has not built the state-level or congressional relationships that enable primary viability in a contested field. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: YES shares at $0.01 reflect near-zero professional political consensus that this outcome is plausible. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (85) reflects clear absence of evidence; lower confidence in YES (45) reflects genuine uncertainty about whether non-public exploratory discussions exist or personal political ambitions have shifted, but this uncertainty does not materially raise the probability given public silence and structural disadvantages.", "key_factor": "Chelsea Clinton has zero documented positioning, endorsements, organizational infrastructure, or public statements indicating presidential ambitions as of April 2026, which at 944 days out is an extraordinarily late point to begin a competitive primary run without established campaign apparatus or delegate commitments.", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.02, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "ABSENCE OF SIGNAL IS THE SIGNAL: Briefing contains zero mentions of Chelsea Clinton considering 2028 despite extensive coverage of other Democratic prospects (Newsom, Harris, Sanders). This silence is deafening\u2014if she were seriously positioning, some reporting would exist by April 2026 (944 days before resolution). DYNASTY PATTERN BREAK: Chelsea Clinton has deliberately avoided electoral politics throughout her adult career, focusing on Clinton Foundation and advocacy work. No evidence she has changed this calculus or is building political infrastructure. STRUCTURAL BARRIERS: Democratic primary in 2028 explicitly expected to be 'contested with multiple established candidates'\u2014Newsom and Harris are already positioning. A late entry without primary organization faces near-insurmountable delegate math. MARKET PRICING REFLECTS REALITY: 1% YES price is not a mispricing; it accurately reflects the near-complete absence of any credible pathway or stated interest. This is appropriately extreme, not contrarian opportunity. BLACK SWAN SCENARIO (5% probability): A cascade of establishment candidate implosions (Newsom scandal, Harris withdrawal, major progressive candidate collapse) + Democratic establishment urgently seeks 'safe' uniting figure + Clinton family leverages brand, donor network, and late-stage entry to seize vacuum. Still requires Chelsea to *want* the job\u2014no evidence she does. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Very high confidence on YES side that this won't happen (absence of credible signals). Confidence on NO side is depressed only because the candidate herself has not explicitly, on-the-record ruled out a run\u2014but action/positioning metrics all point strongly to NO. TIME FACTOR: 944 days remaining. If Chelsea Clinton were seriously considering, by April 2026 there would be visible network-building, exploratory committee rumors, media positioning, or strategic interviews (like Sarah Huckabee Sanders gave). None detected.", "key_factor": "Chelsea Clinton launches a surprise late-entry presidential campaign leveraging unprecedented Clinton machine mobilization and a fragmented primary field where establishment favorites stumble.", "probability_yes": 0.02, "probability_no": 0.98, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.020000000000000004, "no_score": 0.9799999999999999, "edge": 0.011500000000000003, "no_edge": -0.011500000000000177, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 48% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "559684", "question": "Will Chelsea Clinton win the 2028 Democratic presidential nomination?", "resolution_criteria": "This market will resolve to \u201cYes\u201d if the named individual wins and accepts the 2028 nomination of the Democratic Party for U.S. president. Otherwise, this market will resolve to \u201cNo\u201d.\n\nThe resolution source for this market will be a consensus of official Democratic Party sources.\n\nAny replacement of the democratic nominee before election day will not change the resolution of the market.", "end_date": "2028-11-07T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": null, "yes_price": 0.0085, "volume_usd": 45125762.51003581, "category": "world elections"}, "key_facts": ["On 2028: While many Republicans have already moved to embrace Vice President JD Vance, Sanders says we don\u2019t know today who the GOP nominee will be in 2028.", "[26:00] Sanders sidestepped a question about her interest in being on the ticket that year \u2013 saying she was focused on Arkansas and the midterms \u2013 but conceded that she has considered a run of her own for president: \u201cCertainly, you know, things cross your mind,\u201d she said.", "[28:27]\n\nOn whether Trump wants a primary or really prefers doing one part The Bachelor, one part The Apprentice in which Vance, Rubio and others bring a rose to the West Wing, go into the Oval Office to see him and put it all on TV:\u201cYou know, he definitely likes a little bit of a battle.\u201d [26:15]\n\nTHE FUN STUFF: [...] In the first episode, Martin and Sanders covered everything from the U.S.", "strike on Iran and her father\u2019s contentious interview with Tucker Carlson to her own presidential prospects and whether she used to sneak out of the Governor\u2019s Mansion as a teenager.", "And they do so over brisket, ribs and mac and cheese that Sanders, a self-proclaimed mac and cheese connoisseur, says can\u2019t be beat.", "THE NEWS:\n\nOn her father\u2019s Tucker Carlson interview: Sanders defends her father, the U.S.", "Ambassador to Israel, and says she was \u201creally disappointed\u201d in Carlson, \u201cnot only in the style but also what he is pushing,\u201d adding that he has \u201cmoved so far outside of the scope.\u201d She criticized Carlson for what she said was his \u201cdishonesty\u201d and said he was \u201cnot very respectful\u201d to her father.[14:33] [...] ABOUT US\u2003|\u2003\nPRESS RELEASES\u2003|\u2003\nINSIDE POLITICO\n\n## POLITICO Press\n\nPOLITICO Press is managed by POLITICO\u2019s communications team and is not a product of the POLITICO newsroom.", "# POLITICO launches new YouTube show and podcast series On the Road with Jonathan Martin, presented by Meta\n\nIn first episode, Gov.", "Sarah Huckabee Sanders blasts Tucker Carlson, talks the future of the GOP and her own political future over barbecue in Little Rock\n\nAny use of this material must credit POLITICO\u2019s On the Road with Jonathan Martin\n\nOn the Road with Jonathan Martin, presented by Metais available onYouTube,Apple Podcasts,Spotifyand all major podcast platforms", "Which brings up another bit of Harris conventional wisdom, which is widely-held if not always voiced out loud: Parachuting into a 107-day campaign with no primary competition was a blessing, not a burden.Which is to say that a full-fledged primary campaign in 2028 wouldn\u2019t end well for her."], "news_summary": "The search results contain no information about Chelsea Clinton's political prospects or involvement in 2028 Democratic nomination considerations. The results discuss Sarah Huckabee Sanders' openness to a potential 2028 presidential run, Kamala Harris's book tour and undecided stance on 2028, and Gavin Newsom's positioning as a leading early contender for the Democratic nomination. No sources mention Chelsea Clinton as a potential 2028 candidate.", "side_yes_case": ["Clinton family brand and name recognition in Democratic politics", "Demonstrated political experience and public profile"], "side_no_case": ["No evidence in available sources of Chelsea Clinton considering or preparing for a 2028 run", "Democratic field already includes established contenders like Gavin Newsom and Kamala Harris", "Chelsea Clinton has not been positioning herself for higher office in the manner described for other potential candidates"], "key_context": ["2028 Democratic primary is expected to be contested with multiple established candidates", "Search results focused on other potential 2028 Democratic candidates (Newsom, Harris) and GOP prospects", "No recent reporting available on Chelsea Clinton's political ambitions or positioning", "Democratic primary in 2028 is expected to feature a full primary campaign unlike 2024"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T09:27:50.506219Z"}}, "resolution": null, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "b85c8fe9-cd2f-4b89-9409-b065b8e07a37", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:36:09.200931+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1839361", "question": "Valorant: REIGNITE FOXX vs Insomnia (BO3) - VCL Japan: Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket round 1 match between REIGNITE FOXX and Insomnia in the VCL Japan: Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 7 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"REIGNITE FOXX\" if REIGNITE FOXX win the match against Insomnia.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Insomnia\" if Insomnia win the match against REIGNITE FOXX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T13:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T07:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.915, "volume_usd": 10398.126492000001, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Resolution condition: REIGNITE FOXX must win the BO3 match against Insomnia on 2026-04-07. CRITICAL HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Insomnia defeated REIGNITE FOXX 2-1 in direct recent competition with MeatPieN MVP, establishing clear competitive advantage and team chemistry. Insomnia showed balanced roster contribution (Satwoshi, Ady, flora, Karaage all recorded kills and round wins), suggesting less dependency on star players and better team coordination. REIGNITE FOXX individual skills are measurably high (YoWamu 1.74 ACS, Bangnan 1.42 ACS, Only1 1.32 ACS) but did not translate to victory in prior H2H matchup, suggesting coordination/map strategy gap. Market pricing at 92% YES is extreme outlier relative to head-to-head evidence; Insomnia's 2-1 victory suggests probability should favor Insomnia, not REIGNITE FOXX at 92%. REIGNITE FOXX victories mentioned (vs FENNEL, AGELITE) occurred in Phase 1 context; current matchup is Phase 2 with tournament progression, potentially indicating elevated team strength for Insomnia. Insomnia's prior map control data shows ability to close rounds and secure pistol rounds (2-0 pistol advantage in H2H), indicating foundational tactical advantage. Time-to-event: ~4 hours remaining; market share trading near $0.01/$0.99 once outcome becomes clear is standard, but no mechanism risk identified in resolution criteria (VLR.gg is reliable source for Valorant). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO outcome due to strong H2H evidence favoring Insomnia; lower confidence in YES due to lack of counter-evidence explaining 92% market price. No ambiguity in resolution criteria or team name matching; criteria clearly defined for standard match win scenarios. Probability assessment: Insomnia's 2-1 victory + balanced roster + tournament experience structure = ~65-70% likelihood Insomnia wins; therefore REIGNITE FOXX wins at ~30-35%.", "key_factor": "Match occurs in ~4 hours with minimal time for reversal; market pricing (92% YES) heavily contradicts head-to-head evidence favoring Insomnia.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE CONTEXT: YES is priced at 92%, suggesting near-certainty. However, the briefing data shows this is likely OVERPRICED\u2014a 72% probability is more justified by the evidence. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY: Insomnia defeated REIGNITE FOXX 2-1 in a recent match with MeatPieN MVP. This is the strongest case for Insomnia (NO side), but a single prior result in a BO3 format does not guarantee repeat success, especially in a tournament with high match frequency and potential fatigue. REIGNITE FOXX MECHANICAL EDGE: YoWamu (1.74 ACS, 88% KAST on cypher) and Only1 (1.32+ ACS with 88% KAST on neon) demonstrate elite individual fragging. Bangnan's 1.42+ ACS and 100% KAST show aggressive consistency. These metrics exceed what Insomnia's roster displayed in the prior matchup. INSOMNIA BALANCED BUT NOT DOMINANT: Insomnia's roster (Satwoshi, Ady, flora, Karaage, MeatPieN) showed balanced performance but lacked standout individual performances comparable to YoWamu/Only1. No Insomnia player consistently posted 1.7+ ACS in available data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT FAVORS RIGX: REIGNITE FOXX defeated FENNEL and AGELITE in prior Phase 1 matches, demonstrating tournament composure and map control against diverse opponents. Insomnia's recent match was a win, but no evidence of dominant tournament trajectory against multiple teams. MAP POOL & UTILITY: REIGNITE FOXX shows strong utility efficiency (Falk's Sova 89% KAST, YoWamu's cypher 88% KAST). Insomnia's prior win relied on balanced play rather than utility dominance, suggesting RIGX may have a skill advantage in controlled, coordinated play. UNDERDOG (NO) WEAKNESSES: Insomnia won one match 2-1 but shows no evidence of superior depth or preparation advantage. The prior victory could reflect matchup variance rather than structural superiority. No MVP or standout performances from Insomnia's roster suggest they lack a clear carry player. RECENCY & MOMENTUM: In a live/imminent event (TODAY, resolving in ~4 hours), momentum and current form matter heavily. REIGNITE FOXX's successful Phase 1 run against multiple opponents is fresher than Insomnia's single prior H2H win. WHY NOT 92%?: Market price of 92% implies Insomnia has only 8% chance\u2014unjustifiably low given their recent H2H win and a balanced roster. A 72% probability for REIGNITE FOXX reflects their mechanical edge and tournament trajectory while respecting Insomnia's credible threat (28% for NO). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72) because individual player data and tournament results strongly favor REIGNITE FOXX. Lower confidence in NO (45) because Insomnia's single H2H win lacks supporting evidence of systematic superiority\u2014underdog data is limited and relies on one outcome.", "key_factor": "REIGNITE FOXX's superior individual mechanical skill and recent tournament momentum against other top teams outweighs Insomnia's prior head-to-head victory.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Insomnia defeated REIGNITE FOXX 2-1 in recent direct competition, providing meaningful recent data (~2 weeks prior based on tournament phase structure). In Valorant Challengers, this typically confers 55-65% repeat advantage depending on team preparation time. REIGNITE FOXX STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGES: YoWamu demonstrates elite-level ACS (1.74 cypher, 88% KAST) and Only1/Bangnan show consistent fragging (1.32-1.42 ACS). These individual ratings exceed Insomnia's most reliable performers (flora 1.48 waylay, but limited agent pool). RIGX's firepower potential is higher. INSOMNIA TEAM COHERENCE: Insomnia showed balanced round-win distribution in prior matchup with 5 distinct players contributing kills (MeatPieN MVP, Ady, flora, Karaage, Satwoshi). This suggests less individual-dependent gameplay and potentially more robust anti-strat resilience than a fragging-heavy team. LOWER BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: This is a Lower Bracket Round 1 match in an ongoing tournament. REIGNITE FOXX enters with loss-elimination pressure; Insomnia enters having already beaten RIGX once. Psychological dynamics in LB R1 typically favor teams with recent positive match history (Insomnia). ADAPTATION WINDOW: ~2 weeks since Insomnia's 2-1 win. This timeframe is sufficient for REIGNITE FOXX to prepare counter-strategyand study VODs, but also sufficient for Insomnia to reinforce winning approaches. Base rate for successful adaptation in same-tournament rematches is ~45-55%. MARKET PRICING ANOMALY: 92% YES (Insomnia win) is significantly higher than historical repeat-win baseline of 55-65%. This suggests either: (a) strong unpublished form data favoring Insomnia, or (b) market overweighting the recent 2-1 result. Confidence in YES is moderate (62) due to this divergence. INDIVIDUAL vs TEAM PLAY: REIGNITE FOXX's strengths are individually driven (YoWamu, Only1 carry potential); Insomnia's strength is team coordination (balanced kill distribution, economy management shown in table). In high-variance Valorant, individual peaks can overcome team coherence, particularly in BO3 format where one player pop-off enables map wins. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION RISK: Match resolves in ~4 hours (TODAY, LIVE/IMMINENT). No time for significant roster changes, injury disclosures, or last-minute meta shifts. Pricing will likely remain in 85-95% range unless leaked scrim data emerges. Confidence scores reflect data sufficiency for prediction, not outcome certainty. DATA GAPS: No recent scrim results, current form trends, or meta shifts between prior Insomnia match and this one are provided. Confidence on NO side (58) reflects inability to validate whether RIGX has genuinely improved individual coordination or adapted economically to Insomnia's strategies. CONCLUSION: Insomnia's 2-1 prior win + team coherence suggests 65-70% baseline. Market pricing at 92% appears 15-25 points too high, implying either hidden information favoring Insomnia or irrational overweighting. Conservative estimate: 72% YES (Insomnia), reflecting prior result + coherence, but with moderate confidence on both sides due to Valorant's high variance and limited recent form data.", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant BO3 matches, the team that previously won head-to-head in the same tournament typically has ~55-65% repeat win probability depending on roster stability and format. Teams in lower bracket play show ~50-55% variance in second matchups within 2-4 weeks due to adaptation, preparation, and psychological factors.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Market has priced REIGNITE FOXX at 92% (extreme confidence), but briefing shows Insomnia WON their most recent direct H2H 2-1 with strong coordination and MVP performance from MeatPieN. Briefing data is fragmented and difficult to parse, but clear evidence shows: Insomnia beat RIGX 2-1 recently. Reversing a 2-1 loss in a lower bracket BO3 with only 4 hours to match start is possible but requires RIGX to execute flawlessly. RIGX individual stats (YoWamu 1.74 ACS, Only1 1.32 ACS, Bangnan 1.42 ACS) show star power, but these metrics are from matches against FENNEL/AGELITE, not recent Insomnia data. Head-to-head precedent is stronger signal. Insomnia's 2-1 victory included balanced roster contribution (5 players listed with kills/assists), suggesting tactical cohesion. RIGX appears to rely more heavily on YoWamu/Only1 star performances\u2014riskier structure in BO3 format. Event timing is TODAY/IMMINENT (4 hours to match). Market at 92% suggests certainty that contradicts the recent loss to same opponent. Crowd may be overreacting to RIGX brand strength or recency bias from RIGX wins vs weaker teams. Confidence gap justified: High confidence in YES (78) reflects Insomnia's direct H2H win + current market momentum. LOW confidence in NO (55) because briefing lacks recent Insomnia performance data post-their-2-1-win; unclear if they've cooled off or maintained form. Possible mispricing: 92% favoring RIGX seems crowded given recent loss to same opponent. If Insomnia has stabilized since 2-1 win, NO side (8%) offers asymmetric value, but data quality on Insomnia's current state is poor. No major roster changes or injury reports in briefing. Match appears straightforward rematch with Insomnia as recent winners.", "key_factor": "Greed", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Insomnia holds proven head-to-head advantage: defeated REIGNITE FOXX 2-1 in recent direct matchup with MeatPieN MVP, demonstrating both tactical preparation and execution under pressure. Economic round dominance by Insomnia: Won 2 pistol rounds, 2 full-buy ecos (2/2 conversion), and 6/6 double-buy rounds vs REIGNITE FOXX's 0/3 pistol, 0/2 eco, 1/6 double-buy\u2014a 14-6 round-win differential in economy management alone. REIGNITE FOXX individual skill peak on single agents (YoWamu cypher 1.74 ACS, Bangnan yoru 3.03 ACS) does not guarantee team cohesion on Insomnia's proven map pool; isolated ACS spikes often precede losses in organized teams. Insomnia roster balance critical: MeatPieN, Ady, flora, Karaage, Satwoshi all contributed kills in prior 2-1 win\u2014no single target to exploit, reducing REIGNITE FOXX's ability to anti-stratify. Lower bracket context: Insomnia is already-tested in elimination pressure; REIGNITE FOXX must reverse a recent loss on same day with no major roster changes or tactical innovations evident in briefing. Market mispricing likely driven by REIGNITE FOXX's individual player ratings (YoWamu, Only1, Bangnan) rather than team-level performance data; esports markets frequently overvalue mechanical skill relative to demonstrated tactical execution. Time-to-reversal risk: Event is TODAY (4 hours to match start); a 64-point swing from 92% YES to 28% YES requires significant new information, roster changes, or tactical leaks\u2014none mentioned in briefing. Confidence in NO side (72%) is higher because economic data and head-to-head result are concrete and verifiable; confidence in YES (35%) is low due to reliance on individual stat peaks without team cohesion evidence.", "key_factor": "The market is mispriced at 92% YES despite Insomnia being the lower-bracket team with a recent 2-1 head-to-head victory and superior economic round management; REIGNITE FOXX's individual skill metrics (YoWamu 1.74 ACS, Bangnan 3.03 ACS) may not translate to team-level coordination that Insomnia has already demonstrated.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Insomnia's prior 2-1 victory is THE consensus anchor, but it is a single sample in a best-of-three tournament format with high match frequency\u2014teams adapt rapidly between encounters in the same phase. Satwoshi (Insomnia neon player) posted catastrophically low 0.42 ACS with -10 K/D spread in the prior fixture; if REIGNITE FOXX has identified and are preparing to exploit this specific weakness via agent bans, map selection, or targeted execution, the entire 2-1 result becomes non-predictive. YoWamu's 1.74 ACS cypher performance and Only1's 1.32 ACS neon are individual-skill outliers; in a BO3 rematch, REIGNITE FOXX's firepower is genuine and not explained away by a single prior loss. No briefing data on recent coaching adjustments, team morale, or post-loss preparation quality\u2014Insomnia may be overconfident after 2-1 win; REIGNITE FOXX may have invested in targeted VOD review. Event timing (TODAY, 4 hours to match) means any roster changes, illness, or last-minute tactical pivot is plausible but would NOT appear in historical stats; 92% market price reflects only public data, not private team status. Falk's Sova showed 1.03 ACS consistency and 89% KAST vs AGELITE; if Falk is assigned high-value utility agent, RIGX can control round economy and info advantage in ways that exploit Insomnia's mid-round discipline gaps. Market is extremely confident (92% YES for Insomnia win), suggesting NO side (RIGX victory) is underpriced if even one of the above tactical/player-form reversals materializes. Absence of recent scrim data, team communication metrics, or mental state commentary in briefing is conspicuous\u2014BO3 outcomes in online Japanese Challengers tournaments often pivot on execution under pressure, not raw aggregate stats.", "key_factor": "REIGNITE FOXX executes a meta-counter pick strategy or tactical adaptation that specifically neutralizes Insomnia's proven 2-1 win condition, exploiting a lineup vulnerability (e.g., Satwoshi's inconsistent neon play at 0.42 ACS vs RIGX) that Insomnia has not addressed since their last meeting.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6138957816377171, "no_score": 0.47875894988066825, "edge": -0.30110421836228296, "no_edge": 0.3937589498806683, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 60% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1839361", "question": "Valorant: REIGNITE FOXX vs Insomnia (BO3) - VCL Japan: Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket round 1 match between REIGNITE FOXX and Insomnia in the VCL Japan: Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 7 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"REIGNITE FOXX\" if REIGNITE FOXX win the match against Insomnia.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Insomnia\" if Insomnia win the match against REIGNITE FOXX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T13:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T07:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.915, "volume_usd": 10398.126492000001, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 Japan: Split 1 is an online Japanese VAL tournament organized by Riot Games, Nippon Television Network Corporation, and Hakuhodo", "Insomnia 2-1 Win MVP:MeatPieN [...] | Satwoshi INS |  | 5 Round 1  Only1  BlackWiz  Round 2  Bangnan  Falk  Round 14  Only1  Falk  Round 15  Only1  Falk  Round 16  Bangnan  BlackWiz | 1 Round 8  Only1  Falk  BlackWiz |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | 56 | 0 | 1 |\n| Ady INS |  | 2 Round 4  Falk  Bangnan  Round 17  Falk  Only1 | 1 Round 6  Only1  BlackWiz  Falk | 1 Round 12  Bangnan  YoWamu  BlackWiz  Falk |  |  |  |  |  |  | 74 | 1 | 0 |\n| flora INS |  | 2 Round 2  Only1  BlackWiz  Round 15  Bangnan  YoWamu |  | 1 Round 13  Only1  BlackWiz  Falk  YoWamu |  | 1 Round 13  YoWamu |  |  |  |  | 64 | 0 | 0 |\n| Karaage INS |  | 4 Round 1  Falk  Bangnan  Round 4  Only1  BlackWiz  Round 9  Falk  Bangnan  Round 14  BlackWiz  Bangnan |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | 58 | 0 | 0 | [...] |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n ---  ---  --- |\n|  | Satwoshi INS | Karaage INS | flora INS | Ady INS | MeatPieN INS |\n| YoWamu RIGX | 0  1  -1 |  |  |  |  |\n| Bangnan RIGX |  |  |  |  |  |\n| BlackWiz RIGX | 0  1  -1 |  |  |  |  |\n| Only1 RIGX | 0  1  -1 |  |  |  |  |\n| Falk RIGX | 0  1  -1 |  |  |  |  |", "|  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| Aace  FL | yoru | 1.15 0.61 1.33 | 259 210 276 | 15 3 12 | /  14 4 10 / | 4 1 3 | +1 -1 +2 