 higher team rating (1.10 vs 1.08) over past 3 months", "ESC higher kills per round (0.75 vs 0.65) indicating more aggressive play", "ESC recent CCT Series 19 experience with multiple map wins (Inferno vs STATE documented)", "ESC shows consistent map pool performance across multiple tournaments"], "side_no_case": ["STATE lower deaths per round (0.68 vs 0.76) suggesting better defensive positioning", "STATE marginally higher KAST percentage (73.2% vs 74.0%) indicates more consistent participation", "ESC recent loss to Nemesis 0-2 in CCT Series 19 shows vulnerability", "ESC inconsistent results in Roman Imperium Cup (losses to Acend, G2)"], "key_context": ["Match format: Best of 3 (BO3) - requires winning 2 maps", "Tournament stage: CCT Season 3 Europe Series 20 Playoffs (Group A opening match)", "Event timing: April 7, 2026 with limited head-to-head historical data provided", "Both teams showing statistically similar performance metrics within 1-3% variance", "Online tournament format with international European competition"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T09:42:04.678562Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T13:11:06.582245+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "9083c2f6-e121-479e-87d5-5994a7e53a41", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:43:04.060968+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1899626", "question": "Counter-Strike: Rune Eaters vs eLITenergy (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Elimination match between Rune Eaters and eLITenergy in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rune Eaters\" if Rune Eaters win the match against eLITenergy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"eLITenergy\" if eLITenergy win the match against Rune Eaters.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T14:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T08:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.625, "volume_usd": 21327.274475000017, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Rune Eaters must WIN the match (not forfeit/disqualification scenarios which resolve 50-50). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no head-to-head history, no current 2026 team rosters, no recent win/loss records for either team, and no competitive ranking data. Market is pricing on limited information. eLITenergy FORFEIT HISTORY: Documented forfeit of prior Group A match due to scheduling conflict in SAME tournament creates legitimate concern about match completion. This is NOT predictive of in-game outcome but raises 50-50 resolution risk. Rune Eaters RECENT FORM: Lost close matches to BRUTE (17-19, 11-13) showing marginal competitive level but also showing PARTICIPATION in current event \u2014 slight positive signal on commitment. MARKET PRICING (62% YES / 38% NO): Suggests market is pricing in eLITenergy forfeit/no-show risk as primary driver of YES, NOT Rune Eaters' superior in-game capability. This is consistent with briefing's emphasis on eLITenergy's prior forfeits. BIFURCATED RISK: YES probability inflated by forfeit/cancellation risk (which resolves 50-50 per criteria, not to Rune Eaters). True in-game win probability for Rune Eaters likely lower than 62%. Raw match outcome (ignoring forfeit risk) estimated ~45-48% YES. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence eLITenergy has forfeit risk (documented history) justifies higher confidence_yes. Low confidence in either team's actual in-game ability (no comparative data) requires LOW confidence scores on both sides. EVENT TIMING (4 hours to match): LIVE/IMMINENT event with no new data expected before kickoff. Cannot verify eLITenergy participation status pre-match. Once match begins/completes, shares will trade to extremes (~$0.01/$0.99) regardless of official HLTV publication delay. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: 58% reflects (a) ~5-8 point premium for eLITenergy forfeit/cancellation risk, (b) slight discount for Rune Eaters' marginal recent form, (c) genuine uncertainty on in-game matchup quality. This is above market midpoint but below market price, reflecting confidence that prior forfeit data is already partially priced.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data on both teams' current 2026 form and eLITenergy's reliability risk creates material uncertainty; match timing (4 hours away) leaves no time for roster/participation verification before resolution.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES): eLITenergy has a concrete track record of scheduling conflict forfeits in Group A of this same tournament \u2014 they forfeited their Group A opening match previously, establishing a pattern of commitment/availability issues in this specific competition. FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES): Rune Eaters shows active tournament engagement with recent NODWIN Clutch Series 7 participation and no reported scheduling conflicts, suggesting higher availability and event prioritization. FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES): The 62% market price reflects confidence in the reliability differential \u2014 when one team has a documented forfeit history and the other does not in the same tournament, the market is correctly pricing in execution risk for the underdog. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (NO): eLITenergy's prior forfeit in Group A (same tournament, same stage) is not a one-off anomaly but evidence of systemic scheduling management issues \u2014 this is a predictive signal for THIS match, not ancient history. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (NO): Even if eLITenergy shows 'established roster infrastructure,' infrastructure only matters if the team shows up; documentation of prior non-appearance is the strongest possible negative signal in online qualifier environments. BALANCED ASSESSMENT: Rune Eaters' recent losses (17-19, 11-13 margins) do suggest marginal competitive level, which would normally pressure YES probability downward if this were purely skill-based. BALANCED ASSESSMENT: However, in a play-in stage regional qualifier, reliability/commitment often trumps marginal skill differences \u2014 a team that shows up and plays typically beats a team that forfeits, regardless of raw capability. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution. eLITenergy cannot retroactively change their scheduling conflict history. If they no-show again, Rune Eaters wins automatically. If they appear, a BO3 between marginal teams is uncertain but at least contested. DATA GAP ACKNOWLEDGED: Limited direct competitive data on eLITenergy's 2026 form, but their forfeit in THIS tournament is more informative than a skill assessment gap. Confidence in NO side is constrained by inability to verify eLITenergy's current readiness. MARKET PRICING JUSTIFICATION: The 62% YES price appropriately weights execution risk (high confidence in YES) over pure skill uncertainty (moderate confidence in NO). This appears fairly priced, not overpriced.", "key_factor": "eLITenergy's documented history of forfeiting Group A matches due to scheduling conflicts in this exact tournament series creates structural reliability risk that outweighs raw competitive uncertainty.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Forfeit Risk Cuts Both Ways: YES narrative leans heavily on eLITenergy's prior Group A forfeit as evidence of unreliability. However, that forfeit was explicitly due to 'scheduling conflict with another event'\u2014a one-time logistical problem, not structural weakness. The briefing shows this was a known event management issue, not indicative of competitive collapse. Market may be overweighting a scheduling anomaly as proof of team instability. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Rune Eaters' Losses Are Marginal, Not Disasters: The 'recent close losses' (17-19 Anubis, 11-13 Ancient) are presented as weakness but actually reveal skill parity. Losses by 2-2 rounds per map against BRUTE in a closed qualifier suggest Rune Eaters is firmly competitive at this tier\u2014not outmatched. These are not blowouts; they are tight, winnable scenarios. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Incomplete eLITenergy Dossier: The briefing admits 'Limited direct competitive data available on eLITenergy's current form in 2026.' YES is priced at 62% on the assumption eLITenergy is 'an established Russian team with roster infrastructure,' but this is unsupported inference, not data. Established rosters can underperform; infrastructure means nothing without current form. The market is pricing in reputation, not evidence. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 No Head-to-Head Data Favors Upset Thesis: The briefing explicitly states 'No head-to-head history found between these specific teams.' This eliminates any reason to assume Rune Eaters is structurally weaker. In a 62-38 split with zero historical precedent, the market is making a directional assumption without anchor data. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Play-In Stage Volatility: Briefing notes this is 'lower-tier competitive level' in play-in stage. Lower-tier matches are inherently more volatile; upsets are statistically more common when skill gaps are smaller and mental/logistical factors dominate. 62% on YES in a play-in BO3 with no prior matchup data is overconfident. TIMING RISK \u2014 Event is TODAY, ~4 hours to match start: With resolution imminent and no late-breaking forfeit/disqualification reports in the briefing, the logical remaining risk is in-match performance variance. Rune Eaters' competitive pedigree (close losses, recent NODWIN experience) combined with eLITenergy's unexplained current-form gap creates genuine uncertainty that 62-38 does not fully capture. DUAL-PERSPECTIVE: YES side assumes eLITenergy's prior forfeit is structural; NO side recognizes it was logistical. YES side assumes eLITenergy's 'establishment' matters; NO side notes absence of 2026 form data. YES side assumes Rune Eaters' losses prove weakness; NO side recognizes they were marginal and recent (proving engagement). Market is pricing on incomplete information asymmetry. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 48 (weak) because the briefing provides only reputational and one scheduling incident as evidence for YES; confidence_no = 62 (stronger) because Rune Eaters' recent form, close losses, and no historical disadvantage create a plausible upset foundation. However, both remain moderate due to data sparsity on eLITenergy's 2026 state.", "key_factor": "eLITenergy's documented history of scheduling conflicts and forfeit behavior in this exact tournament creates material risk that YES-side reliability narrative is overstated, while Rune Eaters' close competitive losses (17-19, 11-13) suggest skill parity rather than weakness.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "HISTORICAL BASE RATE: Online qualifier matches in regional Counter-Strike tournaments show 65-70% completion rate. Teams with prior forfeits in the same tournament have elevated forfeit risk (~2-3x baseline), but eLITenergy's single prior forfeit in this series is one data point. RELIABILITY SIGNAL (FAVORS YES ~+10-15%): eLITenergy's documented Group A opening match forfeit due to scheduling conflict is a concrete negative signal. Rune Eaters shows no reported scheduling conflicts. This is the strongest directional evidence in the briefing. COMPETITIVE FORM (FAVORS NO ~-5-10%): Rune Eaters' recent NODWIN match vs BRUTE ended in narrow losses (17-19, 11-13), indicating marginal competitive level. eLITenergy positioned as 'established Russian team with roster infrastructure,' though no current 2026 form data provided. MATCH TIMING & FORFEIT RISK: Match is TODAY at ~4 hours from briefing timestamp (2026-04-07 09:42 UTC, scheduled 14:10 UTC). Immediate timeline reduces likelihood of catastrophic scheduling conflicts emerging post-briefing but does NOT eliminate forfeit risk entirely. DATA GAPS LIMITING CONFIDENCE: No direct head-to-head history. No eLITenergy current-season roster/form data. No recent Rune Eaters win/loss record beyond two close losses. 'Established' descriptor for eLITenergy is vague and unsourced. Both teams play-in tier suggests lower stability overall. MARKET PRICING COHERENCE: YES = 62% reflects confidence that Rune Eaters wins on merit OR eLITenergy forfeits. Base-rate reasoning suggests 55-60% for eLITenergy forfeit risk + Rune Eaters competitive viability. Market price at 62% is slightly above base-rate estimate, implying minor overweight on Rune Eaters. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 42 (moderate) because forfeit history is real but single-instance; Rune Eaters' recent form is weak but participation confirmed. confidence_no = 38 (lower) because eLITenergy's 2026 competitive capability is entirely unquantified; no counter-evidence to establish they are favorites on merit.", "key_factor": "Counter-Strike team reliability in online qualifiers: ~65-70% show rate; prior forfeits are moderate predictors of future forfeits (~2-3x base rate); team with recent competitive experience vs. team with forfeit history favors experienced team by ~8-12 percentage points", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Current market price (62% YES) reflects moderate confidence in Rune Eaters, but this is built on SOFT SIGNALS rather than hard competitive data. eLITenergy's prior forfeit in same tournament (Group A opening match) is the strongest YES anchor \u2014 demonstrates organizational dysfunction or scheduling chaos, not competitive weakness. However, prior forfeit does NOT guarantee future forfeit; teams often correct logistics after one incident. Market may be overweighting single data point. Rune Eaters' recent form is marginal: lost 17-19 and 11-13 to BRUTE in same qualifier. These are tight, competitive losses, NOT dominant performances. Confidence in Rune Eaters beating eLITenergy is LOWER than the 62% price suggests. NO side (eLITenergy) has near-zero descriptive data in briefing. No recent match results, no roster info, no form indicators. This is a DATA GAP masquerading as weakness. Market shows RATIONAL APATHY: crowd has bid YES to 62% on a reliability narrative (eLITenergy forfeited before), not on direct competitive comparison. The briefing provides almost no evidence that Rune Eaters would beat eLITenergy in an actual match. EVENT TIMING = TODAY (~4 hours to match). Very little time for new information to shift market. Price is likely to remain sticky unless teams officially forfeit or withdraw. eLITenergy being 'established Russian team with roster infrastructure' is mentioned in NO case but appears nowhere in KEY FACTS or NEWS. This suggests analyst speculation, not briefing signal. Adjustment: Reduce confidence in YES from crowd sentiment (62%) to realistic competitive uncertainty. Rune Eaters marginal form + unknown eLITenergy form + eLITenergy org risk = closer to 55-58% YES than 62%. Confidence_no is LOW (45) because briefing provides zero competitive data on eLITenergy; we cannot confidently argue NO should be higher without roster, recent results, or head-to-head context.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "eLITenergy's forfeit history is tournament-specific: they withdrew from a Group A opening match due to scheduling conflict in the SAME NODWIN Clutch Series, signaling institutional commitment/infrastructure issues rather than one-off incident. Rune Eaters demonstrated competitive engagement by completing matches (BO3 vs BRUTE), albeit with narrow margins (17-19, 11-13), whereas eLITenergy's pattern suggests organizational fragility in qualifier-tier events. Play-in stage context: both teams are in lower bracket of regional qualifier, which typically attracts teams with inconsistent resources. Organizational reliability becomes a larger predictor than raw skill at this tier. No direct head-to-head data and limited 2026 form data for either team constrains confidence in skill-based prediction; forfeit pattern becomes primary differentiator. Timing risk (EVENT TIMING: TODAY, 4-hour resolution): if eLITenergy has scheduling conflicts as documented, risk of walkover/forfeit resolution (which resolves 50-50 per rules) is material but non-negligible. Market price (62% YES) reflects forfeit-risk discount already; additional discount justified only if direct evidence of active roster preparation exists for eLITenergy, which briefing lacks. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH on YES (forfeit pattern is concrete), LOWER on NO (Russian roster reputation alone insufficient without current form data in 2026).", "key_factor": "eLITenergy's documented forfeit pattern in this exact tournament series is a material reliability risk factor that outweighs roster pedigree in a same-day play-in match with 4-hour resolution window.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL RULES AMBIGUITY: The briefing states eLITenergy 'forfeited Group A opening match due to scheduling conflict' earlier in the same tournament. If eLITenergy forfeits THIS match (Group A decider), the market resolves 50-50 per resolution criteria ('forfeit before start = 50-50'), NOT to Rune Eaters. This flips the entire YES case from a competitive win to a probability reset. RECURRENT FORFEIT PATTERN: eLITenergy has already demonstrated organizational unreliability within NODWIN Clutch Series itself. A team that forfeited once in the same tournament series is statistically more likely to forfeit again than a team with clean participation. MARKET MISPRICING VECTOR: The 62% YES price assumes Rune Eaters will WIN competitively. But if eLITenergy forfeits (even with non-trivial probability ~10-15%), the actual YES probability collapses to ~(0.85 \u00d7 0.50) + (0.15 \u00d7 0.50) = 50%, making 62% a structural overweight. TIMING PRESSURE & ONLINE FORMAT: Match is 4 hours away, online only. eLITenergy's prior forfeit suggests logistical/organizational fragility. No evidence in briefing that eLITenergy has resolved scheduling conflicts since their earlier forfeit. RUNE EATERS COMPETITIVE FLOOR: Recent 17-19 and 11-13 losses to BRUTE suggest marginal T2 skill level. If eLITenergy shows up, they may be favored or even on Rune Eaters' level\u2014but the briefing provides zero direct competitive data on eLITenergy's 2026 form, creating asymmetric information. Without eLITenergy roster/form data, confidence in a pure competitive YES is weak. ABSENCE OF SIGNAL: Briefing is silent on eLITenergy's current roster, recent results, or participation confirmation for this specific match. This silence, combined with their prior forfeit, is a red flag for infrastructure stability. GENUINE UNCERTAINTY ON BOTH SIDES: Without head-to-head history and with eLITenergy form unknown, a 48% score reflects: (i) Rune Eaters' slight organizational reliability edge, (ii) offset by unknown competitive capability of eLITenergy, (iii) and elevated forfeit/resolution-reset risk. Confidence is suppressed on both sides due to data gaps.", "key_factor": "eLITenergy forfeits or withdraws due to scheduling conflict (recurrent pattern), triggering 50-50 resolution per market rules rather than a competitive victory for Rune Eaters.", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5595061728395062, "no_score": 0.4535227272727273, "edge": -0.06549382716049379, "no_edge": 0.0785227272727273, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56% for YES (need \u226560%); YES-side confidence too low: 52% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1899626", "question": "Counter-Strike: Rune Eaters vs eLITenergy (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Elimination match between Rune Eaters and eLITenergy in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rune Eaters\" if Rune Eaters win the match against eLITenergy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"eLITenergy\" if eLITenergy win the match against Rune Eaters.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T14:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T08:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.625, "volume_usd": 21327.274475000017, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Best of 3 (Online) * Group A decider match ** megoshort forfeit the match.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Group A opening match ** eLITenergy forfeit the match due to a scheduling conflict with another event.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Group B opening match ** Viggo substitutes KralleJ.", "NODWIN Clutch Series 7 Closed Qualifier.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Group B opening match.", "Complete overview of the CCT 2026 Contenders Europe Series 4 - Upper Bracket Semi-final #1.", "Its his LAST gwme for ence, and he is showing EVERYONE what hes capable of.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Swiss round 4 (teams with a 1-2 record).", "Complete overview of the Rune Eaters vs.", "BRUTE matchup at NODWIN Clutch Series 7 Closed Qualifier!"], "news_summary": "Rune Eaters and eLITenergy are scheduled to face off in a Best of 3 match in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A. eLITenergy has a history of scheduling conflicts, having forfeited a previous Group A opening match due to competing commitments. Rune Eaters has recent competitive experience in similar tournaments, including a close loss to BRUTE (17-19 on Anubis, 11-13 on Ancient) in the NODWIN Clutch Series 7 Closed Qualifier. Both teams are competing in the play-in stage of a regional qualifier.", "side_yes_case": ["eLITenergy has demonstrated reliability issues with prior forfeit due to scheduling conflict in same tournament", "Rune Eaters has recent match experience in NODWIN events showing competitive engagement", "Rune Eaters appears more committed to the event with no reported scheduling conflicts"], "side_no_case": ["eLITenergy is an established Russian team with roster infrastructure to compete", "Rune Eaters' recent performances show close losses (17-19, 11-13 margins) suggesting marginal competitive level", "Limited direct competitive data available on eLITenergy's current form in 2026"], "key_context": ["Match is Best of 3 format in play-in stage, suggesting lower-tier competitive level", "eLITenergy previously forfeited Group A match in same tournament series due to scheduling conflict", "NODWIN Clutch Series appears to be regional European/Eastern European qualifier", "Rune Eaters based in Kazakhstan, eLITenergy based in Russia - both regional competitors", "No head-to-head history found between these specific teams in search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T09:42:51.768713Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T14:10:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T13:25:04.082871+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "f8ce748c-9ac7-4f19-be8b-c4bb2c61ee08", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:44:12.294014+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1895692", "question": "Dota 2: Ilbirs eSports vs BALU (BO3) - European Pro League Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 match between Ilbirs eSports and BALU in the European Pro League Group A, initially scheduled for April 7 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ilbirs eSports\" if Ilbirs eSports win the match against BALU.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BALU\" if BALU win the match against Ilbirs eSports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.68, "volume_usd": 7454.281406999999, "category": "dota-2"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CASE FOR YES (Ilbirs eSports): Ilbirs showed clean 2:0 victory vs alohasquad (Feb 22, 2026); has documented EPL Season 2 experience; demonstrated map-winning capability in recent matches CASE AGAINST YES (Supporting BALU): Ilbirs suffered 0:2 shutout vs NAVI Junior (Feb 24, 2026, most recent match); lost 1:2 to Rune Eaters (Feb 20, 2026); shows inconsistency and potential roster vulnerability; unclear tournament standing or seeding CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 BALU: Briefing contains NO information about BALU's roster, recent tournament results, win/loss record, or competitive tier classification CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 HEAD-TO-HEAD: No prior match history between Ilbirs and BALU provided; cannot assess tactical familiarity, meta alignment, or historical matchup dynamics CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 CONTEXT: No information on EPL Group A standings, playoff implications, team motivation, or recent roster changes for either team Market price of 68% YES reflects strong confidence in Ilbirs, but this confidence cannot be supported by the briefing data alone \u2014 appears driven by market participants' external knowledge rather than documented evidence Ilbirs' recent form is MIXED at best (1:2, 0:2, 2:0 in last 3 documented matches) with no clear upward trajectory preceding this match With BALU being a complete unknown from the briefing perspective, assigning high probability to either outcome is speculative Probability set to 58 (slight lean toward YES per market consensus) reflects Ilbirs' documented participation and some positive recent results, but this is heavily discounted by lack of opponent data Confidence scores deliberately LOW on both sides (42/35) because briefing lacks sufficient data to confidently evaluate either team's true competitive strength, form trajectory, or tactical matchup", "key_factor": "Critically insufficient data on BALU's roster, recent performance, and competitive level makes reliable probability assessment impossible; market prices suggest confidence in Ilbirs that cannot be justified from briefing data.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES): Ilbirs eSports secured a clean 2:0 victory over alohasquad on Feb 22, 2026, proving capacity to win decisive BO3s in the same EPL Championship Season 2 environment they face today. FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES): Ilbirs has active EPL Group A participation and tournament infrastructure familiarity, suggesting operational competence and roster stability despite mixed recent results. FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES): BALU's near-complete absence from the briefing's tournament records and recent results creates an information asymmetry favoring the known quantity\u2014Ilbirs has documented wins against tier-comparable opponents. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO): BALU lacks any identifiable recent tournament results, head-to-head record, or roster information in provided data, making it difficult to construct a credible path to victory for the underdog. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO): Ilbirs's losses (0:2 to NAVI Junior Feb 24; 1:2 to Rune Eaters Feb 20) were against higher-tier or directly stronger opposition\u2014not evidence they collapse against mid-tier teams like BALU appears to be. CONTEXT RISK: Ilbirs showed inconsistency in close matches (1:2 loss pattern), but BO3 format only requires 2 map wins; their 2:0 win demonstrates they can execute when focused. TIMING RISK: Event resolves TODAY in ~5 hours with $7,454 volume\u2014modest liquidity typical of Tier 3 European Dota, but 68% YES price reflects genuine market consensus around Ilbirs' relative strength. DATA LIMITATION: No explicit head-to-head record or BALU roster data exists in briefing; confidence_no kept at 35 due to inability to validate NO side's actual competitive tier or recent form.", "key_factor": "Ilbirs eSports' demonstrated map-winning capability and EPL experience against an opponent with minimal competitive visibility in recent tournament records.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "ILBIRS STRENGTHS: Demonstrated ability to win cleanly (2:0 vs alohasquad Feb 22, 2026); EPL experience and tournament familiarity; market consensus at 68% suggests modest confidence in Ilbirs superiority. ILBIRS WEAKNESSES: Recent 0:2 loss to NAVI Junior (Feb 24) and 1:2 loss to Rune Eaters (Feb 20) show inconsistent form; mixed record in EPL Championship S2 suggests mid-tier competitive level; only ~5 days of roster/meta shifts between Feb 24 and April 7 results provided. BALU INFORMATION GAP: Briefing contains NO documented match results, roster information, or recent tournament placement for BALU; cannot assess team strength, meta comfort, or head-to-head record; this is the primary source of uncertainty. BASELINE REASONING: In lower-tier regional Dota (Tier 3 EPL), teams with visible recent tournament activity tend to outperform teams with minimal public record by ~60-65% win rate, but this assumes the lesser-known team is genuinely weaker\u2014not confirmed here. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: 68% YES / 32% NO pricing suggests significant confidence gap favoring Ilbirs; however, this could reflect greater market familiarity with Ilbirs rather than true skill differential. CRITICAL LIMITATION: Absence of any BALU data prevents asymmetric confidence scoring; confidence_no set to 35 (low) because NO side cannot be meaningfully evaluated; confidence_yes set to 45 (below-moderate) because Ilbirs form is mixed despite tournament visibility. ADJUSTMENT FOR TIMING: Event is TODAY (5 hours to match); high likelihood match will be played as scheduled; no evidence of forfeiture, roster issues, or cancellation risk; resolution should be binary and deterministic. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Anchor to market-derived consensus (68%) but discount slightly due to low confidence in NO-side evaluation and Ilbirs' inconsistent recent form; settle at 62 to reflect modest confidence in Ilbirs edge while acknowledging information asymmetry.", "key_factor": "In BO3 Dota 2 matches between teams of disparate competitive tier and visibility, the team with more recent tournament experience and documented wins typically wins 60-70% of the time; however, asymmetric information on opponent strength introduces significant uncertainty.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market price at 68% YES reflects modest confidence in Ilbirs, but briefing data is sparse and asymmetric. Ilbirs shows MIXED form in Feb 2026: 2:0 win vs alohasquad, but 0:2 loss to NAVI Junior (Feb 24) and 1:2 loss to Rune Eaters (Feb 20) \u2014 inconsistent performance in EPL Season 2. BALU: virtually NO competitive data in briefing. Absence of recent tournament records suggests either low profile, new roster, or weak competitive presence \u2014 creates uncertainty on both sides. 68% price implies ~32% for BALU, but we cannot properly evaluate BALU's actual strength. This is a data asymmetry that should reduce confidence in the YES side. Ilbirs recent loss to NAVI Junior (0:2) on Feb 24 is very recent (only ~6 days before this match) \u2014 shows they can be dominated by competent opponents. BO3 format means one bad series can resolve the market; Ilbirs' volatility (2:0 win followed by 0:2 loss) suggests they are inconsistent. No head-to-head history provided. Without direct matchup data, relying on general form is weak basis for 68% confidence. Market appears RATIONALLY priced given data quality: modest 68% reflects genuine uncertainty, not crowd exuberance. The 6% vig suggests balanced order flow. Confidence_yes at 58: we have some Ilbirs data showing they CAN win (alohasquad), but recent 0:2 loss undermines certainty, and BALU remains opaque. Confidence_no at 42: very low data quality on BALU side makes it hard to assess if they are competitive. Market may be underweighting them purely due to information absence. Adjust probability down slightly from 68% to 62% to reflect Ilbirs' inconsistency and lack of BALU comparative data, but market vibe is rational, not mispriced.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FORM VOLATILITY: Ilbirs demonstrated extreme swing outcomes in EPL Championship S2 (Feb 20-24, 2026): 1:2 loss \u2192 2:0 win \u2192 0:2 loss within 4 days. This pattern suggests either map pool vulnerabilities, drafting inconsistency, or psychological fragility under pressure\u2014not the profile of a dominant 68% favorite. SAMPLE SIZE ASYMMETRY: Only 3 recent Ilbirs matches available (Feb 2026); zero credible BALU data in briefing. The market price reflects trading activity ($7,454 USD volume) but the briefing provides no BALU roster, recent record, or head-to-head history. This creates information asymmetry favoring the market consensus but weakening confidence in YES. TIER 3 CONTEXT: EPL is explicitly Tier 3 European circuit. At this level, roster turnover, stand-in players, and practice-week meta shifts create higher volatility than Tier 1/2. Ilbirs' recent losses (especially 0:2 to NAVI Junior, a likely stronger organization) indicate they are not the dominant force the 68% implies. BO3 SENSITIVITY: A BO3 requires 2 map wins. Ilbirs' 1:2 loss to Rune Eaters shows they can lose tight series. Against an opponent with unknown strength, this magnifies downside risk. TIMING RISK: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. No pre-match analysis, roster confirmations, or late-breaking roster changes are available in briefing. For LIVE/IMMINENT events, reversals are rarer, but initial setup suggests pricing reflects trader confidence rather than expert modeling. NO-SIDE DATA GAP: Complete absence of BALU competitive record, recent results, or roster from briefing is the largest analytical constraint. Confidence in the NO side is artificially capped at 42 because BALU could range from a brand-new stack to a competent regional contender. MARKET IMPLIED: Current 68% YES / 32% NO pricing suggests Ilbirs has 2.1:1 odds, typical for a slight-to-moderate favorite in a Tier 3 BO3. This aligns with their 2:0 capability but conflicts with their volatility pattern. VERDICT: Ilbirs more likely to win, but not by the 2:1 margin the market prices. Set probability at 62 (reflecting modest edge) with asymmetric confidence (58 YES, 42 NO) due to missing BALU intelligence.", "key_factor": "Ilbirs eSports shows volatile form (2:0 wins, 0:2 losses, 1:2 close defeats within 4 days in late February) typical of mid-tier Tier 3 rosters with inconsistent meta adaptation; BALU's near-complete absence from the provided competitive record creates asymmetric information favoring market-implied underdog status.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides zero information about BALU's roster, recent results, head-to-head history, or competitive standing. This asymmetry is the primary vulnerability in market pricing. ILBIRS FORM COLLAPSE SIGNAL: Ilbirs lost 0:2 to NAVI Junior (Feb 24) just 2 days after beating alohasquad 2:0 (Feb 22). This 4-game swing in 48 hours suggests either severe inconsistency, tactical predictability, or internal disruption not captured by aggregate stats. META/PATCH SILENT: The briefing contains no mention of recent Dota 2 patch notes, hero pool shifts, or map pool changes between late February and early April 2026. In a 6-week gap, competitive Dota landscapes can invert; BALU may have adapted to a patch that exploits Ilbirs' signature heroes (Phantom Lancer, Terrorblade, Morphling featured heavily in player profiles). UNDERDOG ABSENCE: When a team has virtually no documented competitive presence in recent results (BALU), it often signals either: (a) they are genuinely weak, OR (b) they are not a regular EPL team and their true strength is unknown. A 32% NO price assumes (a); (b) creates 100% impact if true. ROSTER INSTABILITY CLUE: Yuragi (former OG/NAVI) has a fragmented history (inactive periods 2024-02-20 to 2024-03-08, 2024-10-24 to 2025-03-22). If Ilbirs is still rebuilding post-Yuragi integration or has benched/swapped players, this is not reflected in the briefing. BO3 HIGH-VARIANCE FORMAT: A single bad game 1 read or coach timeout miscalculation in a BO3 can cascade. Against an unknown opponent with unpredictable bans/picks, Ilbirs' recent 1:2 and 0:2 losses suggest vulnerability to game-state adaptation. MARKET MISPRICING DIRECTION: 68% YES prices in Ilbirs assumes dominance on thin data. The lack of any BALU competitive footprint should reduce confidence in that price, not increase it. A contrarian read: BALU's absence from the briefing is the canary. RESOLUTION SOURCE DELAY RISK: Match resolves TODAY (5 hours); if result isn't posted to DotaBuff within 2 hours of conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting applies. Tier 3 tournaments sometimes have admin delays; this introduces minor tail-end uncertainty but doesn't flip the core matchup. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: With ~5 hours to match start, any material roster/injury news would need to break in the next few hours to shift markets meaningfully. Current prices reflect pre-game information only; late-breaking lineup changes could trigger sharp reversals at $0.01/$0.99.", "key_factor": "BALU executes a pre-planned meta counter-strategy or brings in a stand-in player who exploits Ilbirs' recent map pool vulnerabilities that the briefing entirely omits.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.602840909090909, "no_score": 0.40499999999999997, "edge": -0.07715909090909101, "no_edge": 0.08500000000000002, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 52% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1895692", "question": "Dota 2: Ilbirs eSports vs BALU (BO3) - European Pro League Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 match between Ilbirs eSports and BALU in the European Pro League Group A, initially scheduled for April 7 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ilbirs eSports\" if Ilbirs eSports win the match against BALU.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BALU\" if BALU win the match against Ilbirs eSports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.68, "volume_usd": 7454.281406999999, "category": "dota-2"}, "key_facts": ["Logo\n\n###### General\n\n###### Specific\n\n# Yuragi\n\nUkraine\nEurope\nPhantom Lancer\nTerrorblade\nMorphling\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| 2020-04-09 \u2014 2021-01-02 | NOVA \"NOVA (CIS team)\") |\n| 2021-01-02 \u2014 2021-01-17 | Team Unique |\n| 2021-01-17 \u2014 2021-07-19 | Unique(Inactive) |\n| 2021-07-19 \u2014 2021-11-21 | Team Unique |\n| 2021-11-21 \u2014 2024-02-20 | OG |\n| 2024-02-20 \u2014 2024-03-08 | OG(Inactive) |\n| 2024-03-08 \u2014 2024-10-24 | Natus Vincere |\n| 2024-10-24 \u2014 2025-03-22 | NAVI(Inactive) |\n| 2025-03-22 \u2014 2025-07-01 | Natus Vincere |\n\n|  |  |  |\n --- \n| Ilbirs\") Ilbirs eSports | 0:2  (Bo3) | NAVI JuniorNAVI Junior NAVI Jr.", "|\n| February 24, 2026 - 11:00 CET  EP