elative to peers, and mid lane is meta-critical in LCK. Briefing data is entirely silent on Cracker's recent form trajectory, health status, or confidence level. We have no game logs, no recent streak data, no commentary on his performance trend\u2014only aggregate stats that mask volatile match-to-match variance. KRX's 3-2 head-to-head victory in Feb playoffs (most recent direct evidence) is the strongest signal favoring NO, yet the briefing contains zero analysis of what specifically enabled that win. Was it mid-lane counter-pick abuse? Lack of detail suggests an exploitable pattern. HLE's losses to Nongshim (0-3) and T1 Academy (0-2) in earlier rounds indicate vulnerability to academy rosters with strong mid laners. If Cracker was the weak link in those losses, this matchup may repeat that weakness against KRX. The briefing shows Cracker's champion pool as highly inconsistent: Taliyah 37.5% WR (8 games), Orianna 25% WR (4 games), Akali 100% WR (2 games), Ryze 100% WR (2 games). This volatility on high-frequency picks (Taliyah) suggests he may be vulnerable to counter-picking or meta shifts. HLE's +42 GDM is modest; it does NOT suggest dominant macro play. Against a KRX team that played HLE to a 3-2 series and has T1 Academy at 71% WR above it, macro advantage is marginal at best. Event timing is TODAY (7 hours to match). Any personnel change, last-minute health issue, or coaching decision to bench Cracker cannot be reversed. Market has no real-time update mechanism before match starts. The 40% YES price may overweight HLE's playoff win vs DK and Pyeonsik's strong stats, while underweighting the recent KRX 3-2 head-to-head result and Cracker's position-specific fragility.", "key_factor": "Mid-laner Cracker experiences a catastrophic performance collapse or is substituted due to unreported illness/emergency, forcing HLE to rely on a weaker replacement mid during a meta-critical patch phase where Taliyah/Orianna matchups are pivotal.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.37516778523489935, "no_score": 0.6244541484716157, "edge": -0.029832214765100673, "no_edge": 0.02945414847161576, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 66% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1855375", "question": "LoL: Hanwha Life Esports Challengers vs Kiwoom DRX Challengers (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Hanwha Life Esports Challengers and Kiwoom DRX Challengers in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 7 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Hanwha Life Esports Challengers\" if Hanwha Life Esports Challengers win the match against Kiwoom DRX Challengers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Kiwoom DRX Challengers\" if Kiwoom DRX Challengers win the match against Hanwha Life Esports Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match 