 and Season Finals tournaments", "Fearless Draft format was used, affecting champion availability and team composition strategy", "Average game duration of 33:54 suggests mid-game excellence and decisive play matter more than scaling", "TP vs GSMC head-to-head shows competitive series with victories split between teams across tournament finals"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T14:27:05.214727Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T17:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T18:37:13.736462+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "correct_buy", "summary": "Correct BUY NO \u2014 5/5 agents called NO; highest conviction: The Bull (78%)", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.15, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.78, "key_factor": "Team Phantasma's demonstrated ability to execute clean, decisive Game 2 victories against GSMC in tournament finals with strong support playmaking and vision control."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "In competitive LoL best-of-series, the underdog priced at 12% (~+700 implied odds) historically wins individual games at rates of 15-25% depending on skill gap magnitude and meta volatility. Game 2 outcomes in BO5s show slight patterns favoring teams that won Game 1, but individual game variance remains high (~25-30% upset rates even for heavy favorites)."}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Team Phantasma demonstrated superior Game 2 execution in both documented BO5 finals (Summer Super Cup 30:11 stomp, Season Finals consistent wins), while GSMC's support player (REAVER) consistently shows critical weaknesses in positioning/survivability (KDA 2.0-4.8, 11-14 deaths) that compound in high-pressure Game 2 scenarios where teams execute early game advantages."}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "GSMC's support player REAVER suffers a disconnect or unexpected substitution mid-series, forcing a rookie or underperforming stand-in into a critical Game 2 where vision control and late-game positioning determine the outcome."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.28, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.62, "key_factor": "Fear"}], "agents_against_winner": [], "median_prob": 0.18, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "00ba8cbe-039c-4adf-902e-da3cff2c4ecb", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T14:32:34.868436+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1816645", "question": "LoL: French Flair vs BIG (BO3) - EMEA Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between French Flair and BIG in the EMEA Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"French Flair\" if French Flair win the match against BIG.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BIG\" if BIG win the match against French Flair.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 26598.605883999997, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CONDITION: French Flair wins the BO3 match against BIG in EMEA Masters 2026 Winter Lower Bracket Quarterfinals on April 7, 2026. BIG STRENGTHS: Demonstrated recent form with 2-0 over G2 NORD and 2-1 over Eintracht Spandau; clear execution in BO3 format; competitive momentum entering playoffs. FRENCH FLAIR UNKNOWN: No search results detail recent form, roster composition, win/loss record, or trajectory into playoffs; cannot assess offensive/defensive capabilities or meta alignment. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 55% vs NO at 45% suggests modest BIG favoritism, but this may reflect information asymmetry (BIG is documented; French Flair is not) rather than true competitive gap. INFERENCE CONSTRAINT: BIG's documented success is real but limited to 2 matches; French Flair's absence from results could indicate either weaker standing or simply less media coverage/documentation. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams eliminated from upper bracket; both remain viable contenders; French Flair qualified through lower bracket just as BIG did, implying comparable minimum skill level. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Clear, unambiguous criteria; gol.gg is reliable LoL source; forfeit/walkover rules are explicit; name matching guidance is thorough. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: BIG's recent 2-0 dominance over G2 NORD (a credible opponent) provides edge, but lack of data on French Flair prevents high confidence in either direction; splitting difference slightly toward BIG's documented form gives ~62% for French Flair (38% for BIG). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72) driven by BIG's clear recent form; LOW confidence in NO (35) because French Flair's strength is entirely unstudied in available briefing. TIME PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY timing); no reversal opportunity; outcome will be deterministic once match concludes.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on French Flair's recent form, roster strength, and head-to-head dynamics creates asymmetric information favoring BIG in analysis but leaves NO side under-evaluated.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BIG MOMENTUM: BIG has won back-to-back playoff matches with a clean 2-0 sweep of G2 NORD immediately preceding this fixture\u2014this is the strongest available evidence of current form and playoff calibration. BO3 CONSISTENCY: BIG's 2-1 victory over Eintracht Spandau further demonstrates comfort in extended series, suggesting they are battle-tested and can adapt within a BO3. EXECUTION EVIDENCE: The briefing explicitly notes BIG showed 'clear game wins and strategic execution in recent matches'\u2014this is tangible competitive data, not speculation. FRENCH FLAIR OPACITY: The briefing explicitly states 'French Flair's recent performance and trajectory leading into this match is not detailed in available search results.' This is a critical data gap that favors the known quantity (BIG). NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: The absence of historical matchup records means we cannot identify French Flair's specific strategic strengths or weaknesses against BIG's playstyle. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams are in the lower bracket, so neither has secured top seeding, but BIG's demonstrable recent wins indicate they are the survivor-type team advancing through this stage. MARKET PRICING UNDERVALUES BIG: At 55% YES (BIG 45%), the market is pricing this as near