timeout dispute, or last-minute tactical leak surfaces in final hours, shares could swing 15-20 points before lock. Absence of head-to-head history (0-0 standing) means no established M80 counter-strategy or NRG adaptation data\u2014first matchups in Swiss are inherently volatile. Academy team label (NRG Academy) often masks individual player talent and coaching innovation; academy rosters sometimes beat expectations due to lower scouting burden and experimental tactics.", "key_factor": "NRG Academy executes a previously unseen tactical pivot or roster adjustment (mid-tournament substitution or coaching adjustment) that exploits M80's predictable map veto patterns, similar to how academy teams occasionally outprepare main rosters in high-pressure Swiss rounds.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5495833333333333, "no_score": 0.4556435643564357, "edge": -0.0004166666666667318, "no_edge": 0.00564356435643576, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 55% for YES (need \u226557%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828332", "question": "Valorant: M80 vs NRG Academy (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 4 match between M80 and NRG Academy in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"M80\" if M80 win the match against NRG Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"NRG Academy\" if NRG Academy win the match against M80.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 20480.148275000003, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["Swiss Stage: March 23<sup>rd</sup> - April 22<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "16-team Swiss System format; All matches are Bo3; Teams that reach 4 wins advance to Playoffs; Teams that reach", "Find detailed results about the VALORANT match between Evil Geniuses Academy and Division One in VCL NA: Stage 2 that took place on April 6, 2026 - 16:00", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in North America.", "1666 1642 1619 1596 1572 1549 1526 1503 Matches Played Rating.", "Challengers 2026: North America ACE Stage 1.", "Nightblood Gaming roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats,