confidence scores. SWISS FORMAT CONTEXT: In Swiss-system esports, teams at 2-1 are stakes-matched (both need wins to reach 4 and advance). No team has clinched or been eliminated, so motivation is equal. This removes strategic variance. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is TODAY (~9 hours to resolution). No cancellation/forfeit signals in briefing. Treat as binary match outcome.", "key_factor": "In esports BO3 matches between evenly-matched teams (identical records, no prior head-to-head), the higher-ranked or statistically superior team wins ~65-72% of the time; minor seeding/ranking advantages translate to 5-10 percentage point win-rate improvements.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.76, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market price (74% YES) reflects genuine competitive asymmetry: FlyQuest's +9 round differential vs Alliance Guardians' +2 suggests superior map control and consistency. FlyQuest's recent 2-0 stomp over Division One demonstrates momentum; Alliance Guardians' closest win was 2-1 over Nightblood Gaming, showing tighter margins. Standings ranking (FlyQuest 4th, Alliance Guardians 5th) corroborates the probabilistic edge but is marginal\u2014not an overwhelming gap. No crowd exuberance detected: 74% YES is cautious, not extreme (would be 85%+ if market were panicking into FlyQuest). This suggests measured confidence. Counter-signal: Alliance Guardians' identical 2-1 record and ability to secure 2-0 victories (vs ROTSE) demonstrates they are competitive; zero head-to-head history prevents certainty. Round count paradox (AG played 87 rounds vs FLY's 65) could indicate AG plays longer, closer matches\u2014resilience\u2014but also suggests inconsistent domination (round differential +2 vs +9 contradicts this). Market is slightly underpricing FlyQuest edge: round differential (+9 vs +2) is a substantial predictor in BO3 format; 74% may be conservative by 2-4 points. Confidence_no at 62 reflects legitimate uncertainty: no head-to-head data, Alliance Guardians' proven ability to win decisively, and Swiss format variance justify 26% baseline for upset. Event timing (TODAY, ~9 hours to match start) limits narrative shift potential; price should be stable unless injury/roster news surfaces (none reported). Market is Rational: price reflects data quality (strong YES fundamentals, credible NO counter-arguments) without sentiment distortion.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Both teams are 2-1 with equal playoff advancement pressure, but FlyQuest's recent 2-0 victory over Division One (currently 1-3 record) is a hollow indicator\u2014they faced a clearly weaker opponent, inflating their round differential. Alliance Guardians' 2-1 record includes wins against Nightblood Gaming (2-1, a mid-tier team) and Rise of the Scarlet Empire (2-0 domination), demonstrating resilience against more credible competition; their 87-85 round count (higher absolute rounds) may indicate longer series against stronger opponents. Round differential as a standalone metric is unreliable in Swiss systems: FlyQuest's +9 comes from 3 matches of varying opponent caliber; Alliance Guardians' +2 despite 3 wins suggests tighter competition, which often indicates stronger relative performance. Valorant agent meta, map pool comfort, and team communication shifts week-to-week; both teams are academy/lower-tier VCL franchises with likely roster volatility and limited strategic reputation data in public standings. No head-to-head history eliminates heuristic advantage; market price of 74% YES reflects a modest 3:1 confidence gap, reasonable given FlyQuest's marginal statistical edge but insufficient to justify higher confidence. Event timing (TODAY, ~9 hours to match) means no new roster news, patches, or scrimmage results will emerge; betting market at 74% suggests modest but not overwhelming FlyQuest favoritism\u2014professional bettors typically avoid extreme positions on Swiss-format upsets with identical records. Swiss system incentivizes risk-taking: both teams need wins; neither has a significant seeding cushion yet (4 wins needed for playoffs, 5+ teams already 2-1+), suggesting relatively balanced stakes and motivation.", "key_factor": "Round differential is a weak predictive signal in Valorant because it reflects aggregate map outcomes across different opponent skill levels; FlyQuest's +9 differential against weaker teams (Division One 0-3) carries less weight than Alliance Guardians' consistency against stronger competition (NRG Academy, Rise of Scarlet Empire).", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "ROUND DIFFERENTIAL PARADOX: FlyQuest's +9 differential is inflated by a 2-0 stomp of Division One (a 1-3 team), while Alliance Guardians' +2 comes from beating competitive opponents (NRG Academy 2-1, Rise 2-0, Nightblood 2-1). FlyQuest may not sustain dominance against equal-tier opponents. MATCH VOLUME SIGNAL: Alliance Guardians have played 87 total rounds across 3 matches vs FlyQuest's 65 rounds. This suggests AG's matches go to map 3 more often\u2014a hidden strength in close, competitive play. FlyQuest's 2-0 win over Division One inflates their differential without proving they win tight series. PLAYER SUBSTITUTION/ROSTER STABILITY UNKNOWN: The briefing contains zero mention of roster changes, illness, or player status for either team. In a LIVE/IMMINENT match (9 hours away), a last-minute sub or injury to FlyQuest's key player could be undetected by market participants relying on older standings data. PSYCHOLOGICAL ADVANTAGE: Both teams are 2-1. Alliance Guardians' recent wins (including a 2-1 clutch over Nightblood) may instill momentum in close games, while FlyQuest's 2-0 win over a weak team may create overconfidence going into a peer-level match. ABSENCE OF MAP POOL DATA: The briefing provides zero information on map bans, recent map performance trends, or champion preferences. Alliance Guardians could have a hidden strategic edge against FlyQuest's typical picks that isn't visible in aggregate round counts. MARKET OVERWEIGHT: 74% YES pricing assumes FlyQuest's ranking (4th) and round differential are decisive. Both metrics are marginal vs the actual head-to-head unknowns. Market efficiency gap exists. SWISS FORMAT PRESSURE: At 2-1, a loss drops a team closer to playoff elimination. Alliance Guardians may be playing with more desperation and focus, while FlyQuest (also at 2-1) may approach the match with less urgency if they assume they are favored.", "key_factor": "Alliance Guardians' resilience in close map play (87 rounds played vs FlyQuest's 65) masks a tactical adaptation or player substitution specifically designed to exploit FlyQuest's map pool weaknesses in a high-pressure must-win scenario.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.7072566371681417, "no_score": 0.29162790697674423, "edge": -0.027743362831858298, "no_edge": 0.02662790697674422, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "CONFIRMED", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.36054421768707484, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828342", "question": "Valorant: FlyQuest vs Alliance Guardians (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 4 match between FlyQuest and Alliance Guardians in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FlyQuest\" if FlyQuest win the match against Alliance Guardians.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance Guardians\" if Alliance Guardians win the match against FlyQuest.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T05:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T23:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.735, "volume_usd": 5512.513047000001, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["Swiss Stage: March 23<sup>rd</sup> - April 22<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "16-team Swi