 0.46, "probability_no": 0.54, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains ZERO match results, win-loss records, or recent form data for either NiP or IG\u2014only tournament structure and scheduling. This is asymmetric uncertainty, not evidence of IG dominance. MARKET PRICING ANOMALY: YES @ 46% (NiP underdog in a domestic LPL match) despite NiP being a credible international org. This suggests either contrarian positioning or that IG has recent documented dominance not reflected in the briefing. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL: Briefing explicitly states 'Limited direct performance data is available'\u2014yet the NO side (IG) is still priced at 53%. This pricing assumes IG superiority without evidence, suggesting misprice opportunity on YES side. BLACK SWAN: NiP may have discovered a scrim-tested meta adaptation or roster chemistry edge (e.g., new jungler synergy, AP bot lane pocket pick) that doesn't show in public scrims but is live-tested in Week 2. IG, as a legacy LPL fixture, may be predictable to aggressive international scouts. WEEK 2 TIMING: Early season group stage\u2014teams are still calibrating. NiP, as a non-Chinese org, may have structural preparation advantages (bootcamp discipline, anti-meta scouting) that raw win-loss records don't capture. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=35 (weak hand on evidence) and confidence_no=42 (slightly stronger, but still weak) reflect that BOTH sides lack data. NO side is NOT strongly supported\u2014just assumed. LIVE EVENT RISK: Resolves in ~5 hours. If match has started or is about to start, shares will rapidly trade to extreme (0.01 or 0.99) as outcome becomes clear. Current pricing at 46/53 suggests pre-match uncertainty, not settled confidence. CONTRARIAN POSITION: Council likely anchors on 'IG in LPL = domestic strong' without questioning whether NiP's international discipline or recent roster moves create a live upset vector.", "key_factor": "NiP's recent scrim performance or meta specialization (AP-heavy comps, lane-swap tactics) exploits IG's known weaknesses in a format where the briefing provides zero direct performance data on either team.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.4616129032258065, "no_score": 0.5390178571428571, "edge": -0.003387096774193521, "no_edge": 0.004017857142857184, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 32% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828734", "question": "LoL: Ninjas in Pyjamas vs Invictus Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 8 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ninjas in Pyjamas\" if Ninjas in Pyjamas win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Ninjas in Pyjamas.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.465, "volume_usd": 158772.21760599996, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "The 2026 Esports World Cup is an upcoming multi-game esports tournament held in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, hosted by the Esports World Cup Foundation (EWCF) and ESL", "LPL Split 2 2026 - Regular Season - Week 1-4.", "LPL Split 2 Week 2 continues on April 8 with Invictus Gaming vs Ninjas in Pyjamas and Team WE vs Top Esports.", "Track what Kalshi's markets predict for \"LPL 2026: Invictus Gaming vs.", "Ninjas in Pyjamas Map 2\", or trade it yourself.", "Ninjas in Pyjamas Map 1\", or trade it yourself.", "Ninjas in Pyjamas League of Legends match originally scheduled for Apr 8, 2026 at 5:00 AM EDT, then the market resolves to Yes.", "Don't miss the upcoming League of Legends match between Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming today, 8 April 2026."], "news_summary": "Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming are scheduled to face off in the LPL 2026 Split 2 regular season on April 8, 2026, as part of Group Ascend. This is an offline S-Tier tournament organized by TJ Sports running from April through June 2026 with 14 participating teams. The match was tracked on prediction markets including Kalshi with individual map winner markets available. Limited direct performance data is available in the search results to assess current form or head-to-head dynamics between these two teams.", "side_yes_case": ["Match officially scheduled and confirmed for April 8, 2026 with market verification via Sofascore", "Invictus Gaming competing in LPL's premier group stage format", "Prediction markets actively trading on map-level outcomes, indicating confidence in match execution"], "side_no_case": ["Ninjas in Pyjamas as potential underdog in Chinese domestic LPL competition", "No recent form or performance data provided in search results to establish competitive positioning", "Both teams lack documented recent match results or win/loss records in available information"], "key_context": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 regular season (April-June 2026) with 14 teams across multiple groups", "Group Ascend format with specific side selection rules noted for second meetings", "Match scheduled for early tournament stage (Week 2, April 8) with significant tournament runway remaining", "Individual map winner markets (Map 1, Map 2) actively traded on Kalshi platform", "Tournament determines qualification for Mid-Season Invitational international event"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-08T09:44:56.766984Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T15:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T20:14:04.778137+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "f1440edf-01fd-4f9e-b798-3f8847c98336", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T12:04:04.054621+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1828796", "question": "LoL: Top Esports vs Team WE (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Top Esports and Team WE in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 8 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against Team WE.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team WE\" if Team WE win the match against Top Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T18:20:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T12:20:00Z", "yes_price": 0.725, "volume_usd": 64901.174915000025, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "Resolution condition is clear: Top Esports must win the BO3 match against Team WE in LPL Split 2 2026 on April 8, 2026. Briefing data shows bookmaker odds of 1.40 (Top Esports) vs 2.90 (Team WE), implying ~67% win probability for Top Esports vs ~33% for Team WE. Market price (72% YES) slightly exceeds bookmaker implied probability (67%), suggesting modest overpricing of Top Esports by Polymarket participants. Top Esports noted as having stronger roster composition on paper and historically established LPL organization, supporting YES case. Counter-evidence: Top Esports displaying instability and poor form at split start; analysts note form concerns make them vulnerable to upset despite roster strength. Team WE underdog but competitive; analyst commentary suggests +1.5 maps is favorable value, indicating match not lopsided. Event timing is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution deadline (April 8, 7:00 AM ET = April 8, 12:00 UTC); match should have occurred or be imminent. DATA FRESHNESS: briefing dated April 8, 12:03 UTC, 5 hours before resolution deadline. Match status (played/pending/canceled) not explicitly confirmed in briefing. Probability score of 68 reflects: (a) bookmaker consensus favoring Top Esports at ~67%, (b) modest market premium suggesting 68% reasonable, (c) form instability introduces non-trivial upset risk, (d) BO3 format reduces variance but doesn't eliminate Team WE upset probability. Confidence split reflects asymmetry: confidence_yes=72 (clear bookmaker consensus, roster advantage supported) vs confidence_no=65 (form concerns and analyst skepticism about Top Esports immediate improvement documented, but Team WE competitive window remains uncertain absent recent head-to-head data). Resolution mechanism risk (gol.gg availability) is secondary; market will trade at extremes once outcome clear regardless of official source timing.", "key_factor": "Match timing and resolution source (gol.gg) availability within 2-hour window; no confirmation yet that match has occurred or will occur as scheduled today.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Top Esports hold a 67% implied win probability across external bookmakers with 1.40 odds, reflecting a clear consensus that their roster is stronger on paper. The market pricing of 72% on Polymarket is slightly HIGHER than bookmaker consensus, suggesting potential underpricing of the favorite. ROSTER ADVANTAGE: The briefing explicitly identifies Top Esports as possessing 'stronger roster composition compared to Team WE on paper' \u2014 this is a structural, pre-match advantage that does not require form recovery. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: Team WE's underdog status (2.90 odds, 28% market probability) reflects legitimate competitive gap. Despite analyst acknowledgment that Team WE can 'cause damage,' they remain clearly disadvantaged in head-to-head matchup quality. FORM VOLATILITY CUT BOTH WAYS: While Top Esports show 'instability and poor form at start of split,' this is WEEK 2 of a 4-week regular season. A single BO3 is a small sample; roster strength typically regresses toward mean in competitive play. Team WE cannot exploit volatility consistently in one match. ANALYST CONTRADICTION: Briefing notes Team WE +1.5 maps as a 'favorable betting proposition,' yet this same analyst predicts Top Esports won't improve 'immediately.' These statements are in tension \u2014 if Top Esports are unstable, the underdog has a real chance; but at 2.90 odds, Team WE are already priced to exploit that instability. Market has already discounted Top Esports' weakness. POLYMARKET PREMIUM: YES priced at 72% vs. 67% bookmaker consensus suggests smart money sees Top Esports favored above external markets, possibly reflecting confidence that roster gap will show up in a BO3 format. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS CONSISTENCY: Best-of-three reduces variance vs. single game. Top Esports' stronger roster has more opportunities to assert control; Team WE's 'capability to cause damage' is a one-off upset narrative, less likely to repeat across 3 maps. TIMING CONTEXT: Match is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution. No new form data will emerge; market is pricing on known information. The 72% price reflects mature consensus, not panic or mispricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72) because roster superiority and bookmaker consensus are concrete. Confidence in NO is lower (55) because Team WE's competitive viability is acknowledged but underspecified \u2014 no concrete evidence of recent map wins or tactical innovation against Top Esports specifically. RISK: Top Esports' 'unstable start' is the primary bull trap. If instability reflects deeper roster cohesion or meta misalignment issues, Team WE could exploit. However, instability at Week 2 has not historically prevented strong-roster teams from winning individual matches; it predicts playoffs struggles, not regular-season upsets.", "key_factor": "Top Esports' superior roster composition and 67% bookmaker consensus outweigh early-split instability in a single best-of-three match.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.71, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Team WE is correctly priced as underdog but the 28% probability undersells their upset potential given Top Esports' explicit form crisis. Analysts specifically flag Top Esports' 'unstable start' and 'unlikely to show improvement immediately,' which is damning for a team expected to win 72% of the time. FAVORITE'S FRAGILITY \u2014 Top Esports' 'stronger roster on paper' is a paper tiger if coordination and confidence are broken. Week 2 of split is still early enough that poor starts often cascade; Top Esports have not yet stabilized, making them vulnerable to a prepared underdog. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE \u2014 Best-of-three format favors the team with momentum and adaptability over raw strength. If Team WE takes Game 1, Top Esports' documented instability could lead to mental collapse in Game 2. BO3s are not linear; single-map momentum shifts are common. ANALYST CONSENSUS SIGNAL \u2014 Multiple mentions that analysts view 'Team WE +1.5 maps as favorable betting proposition' is a strong contra-indicator to the 72% YES price. Professional bettors don't label propositions 'favorable' on underdogs without cause; this suggests Team WE's actual strength exceeds market pricing. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE \u2014 The 1.40 odds for Top Esports reflect 'historical strength as established LPL organization,' not current form. This is precisely the narrative bias that creates upset opportunities: the market is anchored to past brand reputation rather than present-state data. DATA RECENCY \u2014 Briefing is dated 12:03 UTC on match day (resolves ~6 hours later). No updated form data, scrim results, or roster health news is provided, which means market pricing may not reflect last-minute developments that favor underdogs. MISSING COUNTERVAILING EVIDENCE \u2014 No briefing data supports Top Esports' readiness to overcome their form crisis. The case for YES relies entirely on roster quality and historical precedent, both of which are weak anchors when a team is explicitly 'unstable.' TEAM WE POSITIONING \u2014 Team WE are not a random upset pick; they are 'capable of causing damage' per briefing, meaning they have demonstrated competence. Combined with Top Esports' weakness, Team WE is not a lottery ticket but a calculated underdog. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION \u2014 YES confidence at 62 (moderate) reflects that Top Esports' roster quality and historical pedigree are real, but NO confidence at 71 (higher) reflects stronger evidence of Top Esports' current vulnerability and analyst consensus favoring Team WE value. The data asymmetry is real: form instability is more concrete than abstract roster strength.", "key_factor": "Top Esports' documented instability and poor form at split start creates a structural vulnerability that Team WE can exploit in a best-of-three format where momentum swings matter.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Market price (72% YES) moderately exceeds bookmaker consensus (67% implied win probability), suggesting minor overpricing of Top Esports but within reasonable variance. Top Esports roster strength is documented as superior on paper, establishing a fundamental edge that persists even during form dips. Top Esports instability at split start is a genuine concern but historically insufficient to flip a roster-favored team below 65% win likelihood in regular season Week 2 matches. Team WE underdog status (2.90 odds ~34%) aligns with historical upset frequency; analyst confidence in +1.5 map value reflects recognition of meaningful upset probability but not majority likelihood. BO3 format slightly favors roster-favored teams; stronger fundamentals can recover across multiple maps more reliably than in BO1. Event timing is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution; limited time for form reversal, making current roster differential the primary predictor. No evidence of team roster changes, key player injuries, or tournament format changes that would justify deviation from ~67-70% base rate for favored LPL teams. Confidence in YES is moderate-high (72) due to clear roster advantage and bookmaker consensus; confidence in NO is lower (55) due to limited concrete evidence of Top Esports collapse\u2014instability alone historically insufficient to downgrade favored teams below 65%.", "key_factor": "In LPL matches involving roster-favored teams with demonstrated form concerns, favorites win approximately 65-72% of the time despite instability; underdog upsets occur in ~28-35% of cases.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market price (72% YES) sits ABOVE bookmaker consensus (67% implied probability), suggesting slight overconfidence in Top Esports. Bookmaker odds (1.40 vs 2.90) show meaningful disagreement \u2014 professional betting markets see Top Esports as favored but not dominant. Key tension: Top Esports have stronger roster on paper BUT showing documented instability/poor form in split start \u2014 this creates legitimate upset risk. Analyst note of Team WE +1.5 maps as value proposition indicates professional assessment sees Top Esports underperforming roster potential. Polymarket pricing (72%) overweights roster strength and historical pedigree; underweights current form deterioration and early-split volatility. The 5-point spread between market price (72%) and bookmaker consensus (67%) is not extreme \u2014 suggests crowd is somewhat but not excessively bullish on favored side. NO side at 28% appears rationally priced for an underdog with demonstrated competitiveness, though briefing lacks specific Team WE recent performance data. Event timing (6 hours to resolution) means little time for narrative reversal \u2014 current odds reflect relatively settled expectations. Risk asymmetry: YES backed by roster composition + historical strength + bookmaker consensus; NO backed only by recent form concerns + lack of demonstrated Top Esports stabilization. Adjusting down slightly from 72% market price to 68% to reflect form instability and analyst value call on Team WE, but confidence in YES remains above 70% due to multi-factor support for favorite.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Top Esports holds 67% bookmaker consensus with 1.40 odds, well-aligned with the 72% market price\u2014indicates consensus, not mispricing. Critical instability flag: TE showing poor form at split start is a material weakness; LPL Week 2 form is predictive within a single split but volatile across roster changes, scrim outcomes, and patch meta. WE at 2.90 odds (+1.5 maps valuation per analysts) suggests professional assessment of competitive BO3 games; this is NOT a blowout prediction despite TE favoring. BO3 format amplifies variance: single-game upsets are less predictive in BO3 than BO1, but roster/coaching adjustments between games can exploit TE's documented instability. LPL S-tier tournament context: 14-team regular season means limited data on TE/WE matchup-specific prep; Week 2 is pre-meta stabilization, where coaching adaptability matters as much as raw talent. Bookmaker 67% > Market 72%: Market has drifted up 5%, possibly due to late money on TE narrative ('stronger roster on paper'); this slight overweighting of roster talent relative to current form is a minor YES overweight. No recent head-to-head data in briefing; cannot assess direct matchup history or draft affinities. Timing: Event is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution; sharp movement is unlikely unless late injury/roster news emerges (none reported). Confidence asymmetry: TE YES case is well-articulated (consensus, historical strength) but explicitly contradicted by form data; WE NO case is weaker in absolute strength but strong relative to betting odds, creating higher uncertainty about true probabilities.", "key_factor": "Top Esports' form volatility in Week 2 of a new split creates meaningful upset risk; the +1.5 map spread favoring WE suggests sharp bettors are pricing in competitive games rather than a dominant TE stomp, which should dampen confidence in the market's 72% YES price.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Top Esports' 'unstable start' is flagged but not explained\u2014absence of specific patch notes, scrim results, or roster change details suggests hidden volatility or personnel turbulence not yet public. Week 2 of LPL Split 2 is early enough for teams to still be experimenting with rosters and meta; a substitution mid-BO3 due to injury/illness is plausible and would dramatically shift map odds in Team WE's favor. Team WE +1.5 maps is explicitly called 'favorable' by analysts, indicating the true skill gap on individual maps may be closer than the 72% YES price reflects; if Top Esports' form is unstable, one roster disruption cascades. Market prices show 72% YES vs 28% NO, but betting odds cited are 1.40 vs 2.90\u2014this discrepancy suggests unconfident YES consensus; a minor personnel shock could trigger sharp reversal. The briefing is silent on recent scrim performance, coaching staff changes, player statements about motivation, and any illness/injury reports\u2014classic signal vacuum before upset. Top Esports as an 'established LPL organization' may be overweighted by casual market participants unfamiliar with current 2026 roster chemistry; Team WE is genuinely competitive in map-level skill. BO3 format means two maps must be won; if Top Esports loses map 1 due to underestimation or a sub-in, psychological momentum and meta familiarity heavily favor Team WE in maps 2\u20133. Time-to-reversal is short (~6 hours); only a personnel or tactical shock mid-series can flip this, making any such event a true black swan with outsized impact on resolution.", "key_factor": "Top Esports key player (likely mid or ADC) suffers unexpected illness, injury, or is benched mid-series due to internal conflict, forcing a substitute who has not practiced the current meta sufficiently.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6337142857142858, "no_score": 0.3789680589680589, "edge": -0.09128571428571419, "no_edge": 0.10396805896805889, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "CONFIRMED", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.37931034482758624, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828796", "question": "LoL: Top Esports vs Team WE (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Top Esports and Team WE in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 8 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against Team WE.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team WE\" if Team WE win the match against Top Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if htt