{"run_id": "795b11e2-ed28-43ec-a7e3-1a9433c3b4fb", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T23:51:20.252101+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1894574", "question": "Counter-Strike: F5 Esports vs regain (BO3) - ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket final match between F5 Esports and regain in the ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"F5 Esports\" if F5 Esports win the match against regain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against F5 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 6157.8451380000015, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: F5 Esports must win a Best-of-3 match against regain in the ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs Upper bracket final. EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled for April 7, 9:00 PM ET; briefing timestamp is April 7, 23:51 UTC (approximately 2 hours post-scheduled start). This is a LIVE/IMMINENT event, potentially already underway or completed. DATA QUALITY ASSESSMENT: Briefing document is almost entirely devoid of useful intelligence. Key facts section contains only fragmented comments about unrelated matches (Johnny Speeds vs QWENTRY, Mindfreak), generic ranking labels, and off-topic forum chatter. No F5 Esports or regain roster data, recent performance records, map pool strengths, or head-to-head history provided. CASE FOR F5 (YES): Market price of 38% suggests modest consensus backing. F5 qualified for playoffs (confirmed), indicating baseline competitiveness. No negative performance signals in available data. CASE FOR regain (NO): Equally qualified for playoffs. Market price of 62% reflects current market consensus. No performance data distinguishes regain negatively or positively vs F5. ANALYTICAL SYMMETRY: Without team form, recent results, roster changes, map preferences, or head-to-head records, this is a pure information vacuum. Both teams cleared the same qualification rounds to reach this stage. No substantive basis exists to favor either outcome. MARKET PRICE INTERPRETATION: Current 38/62 split suggests market participants either have private information or are anchoring on arbitrary factors. The briefing provides zero foundation to validate or challenge this pricing. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both set to 25 (LOW) because the briefing lacks sufficient data to confidently assess either side. A probability_score of 38 is assigned to mirror current market consensus, but this reflects market opinion, not data-driven analysis. High confidence would be unjustified given the complete absence of team performance intelligence. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Secondary concern. HLTV.org is reliable for Counter-Strike results. Walkover/forfeit/disqualification scenarios are possible but unpredictable without team context. CONCLUSION: This market cannot be meaningfully analyzed from the provided briefing. The 38% probability reflects market pricing, not analytical conviction.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no actionable team performance data, recent form, roster information, or head-to-head history to differentiate team strength \u2014 probability assignment is essentially arbitrary without substantive analytical foundation.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: regain is priced at 62%, reflecting modest market confidence. Both teams qualified for playoffs in ESL Challenger League Season 51 NA Cup 3, a legitimate mid-tier tournament, confirming baseline competitive parity. DATA SCARCITY IS THE DOMINANT FACTOR: The briefing explicitly states 'limited specific information about either team's recent performance or head-to-head matchups' and 'no recent form statistics or head-to-head record provided.' This asymmetric information vacuum makes confidence in either direction inherently weak. NO DISTINGUISHING PERFORMANCE METRICS: The briefing directly states 'No distinguishing performance data favors either team in results.' This is critical\u2014without map pool data, recent form, roster stability, or head-to-head history, the market's 62% NO pricing appears to reflect convention rather than evidence. UNDERDOG (YES) WEAKNESSES: F5 shows no negative sentiment in available data and qualified for playoffs, but this is symmetric to regain's position. The briefing notes 'Limited negative sentiment or criticism about F5' but offers NO positive evidence of form, recent wins, or map pool strength either. BOTH TEAMS IN IDENTICAL INFORMATIONAL POSITION: Both teams cleared earlier rounds; both appear in playoff bracket; neither has documented recent matches, roster changes, or performance trajectories. The briefing's 'KEY FACTS' section contains irrelevant noise (Johnny Speeds, QWENTRY, Mindfreak, Ivz\u2014none related to F5 vs regain) and fragmented HLTV ranking snippets with no actionable data. EVENT TIMING RISK: Resolves TODAY in ~7 hours. This is imminent, meaning late reverse odds swings are unlikely unless one team experiences catastrophic issues (roster no-show, forfeit). Market has stabilized at 62/38, suggesting this represents genuine uncertainty rather than volatile trading. WHY 62% FOR NO IS DEFENSIBLE: In true coin-flip scenarios, the market often prices slight favorites at 55-65% based on conventional wisdom, home region patterns, or historical tournament seeding. regain at 62% is modest\u2014not extreme. This modest favoritism is consistent with 'no clear data advantage' but slight nameplate or narrative edge. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_no = 65 reflects that market pricing (62%) is reasonable given data vacuum, but confidence_yes = 22 reflects that F5's 38% chance is severely under-evidenced. We cannot justify F5 as significantly weaker without comparative data. CONTRARIAN CONSIDERATION: If F5 has superior map pool, fresher roster, or recent upset form NOT captured in briefing, YES could be underpriced. However, briefing explicitly lacks this data, so this remains speculative. The Bull case for NO relies on market consensus in absence of counter-evidence, not on affirmative proof of regain superiority.", "key_factor": "Market consensus and regain's positioning as slight favorite in a data-scarce mid-tier NA CS matchup where no team demonstrates clear superiority.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides virtually NO actionable intel on either team \u2014 no recent form, no roster info, no head-to-head history, no map pool analysis, no individual player performance. Both teams qualified for playoffs, but that's the only commonality stated. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE IN NO: regain is priced at 62% (a 24-point favorite) despite the briefing offering ZERO evidence supporting this gap. Market is pricing conviction based on information absent from the briefing \u2014 a red flag for overestimation of the favorite's edge. MURPHY'S LAW ON THE FAVORITE: Heavy favorites in BO3 matches with minimal public data often suffer from inflated confidence. If regain is favored due to underground community consensus or betting syndicates rather than public form, that creates blind spots \u2014 upsets thrive in these conditions. UNDERDOG'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: F5 qualified to playoffs Upper Bracket (implied by 'Upper bracket final'). Reaching an Upper Bracket final suggests F5 has momentum and consistent performance. regain's path to UB final is equally valid, but neither briefing detail reveals why regain should be 24 points favored. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 is inherently less predictable than Bo1 \u2014 map selection, side preference, and tactical adaptation matter enormously. A 62% favorite in BO3 with no form data is fragile; F5 could steal maps or exploit regain's unproven map pool. TIMING AMPLIFIES UNCERTAINTY: Match resolves in ~7 hours (TODAY, LIVE/IMMINENT). Any news, roster issues, or technical problems affecting either team would crystallize now, but briefing is dated 2026-04-07 23:51 \u2014 very fresh but still shows zero intel. Market is trading on whisper networks, not public form. ABSENCE OF NEGATIVE SENTIMENT ON F5: Briefing notes 'Limited negative sentiment or criticism about F5' \u2014 this is significant. If F5 had clear weaknesses, community chatter would reflect them. The lack of damning evidence is a small but real asset. REGAIN'S LACK OF DIFFERENTIATION: regain has no distinctive strengths highlighted in briefing. It simply 'qualified' like F5. Why trust a 62% priced team with zero visible edge over one that scraped to UB final? CASUAL DATA NOISE IN BRIEFING: Several fragments reference irrelevant teams (Johnny Speeds, QWENTRY, Mindfreak, cutzmerets) \u2014 suggests the search results are contaminated. Real performance intel on F5 vs regain may exist but failed to surface. This *favors* the underdog, as mispricing is more likely when data is scarce. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT: Given extreme uncertainty and market confidence without visible justification, F5 at 38% is slightly underpriced. A fair coin-flip scenario would be 50-50; heavy NO pricing without evidence pushes F5 upward. However, confidence is LOW on both sides due to data poverty. CONFIDENCE REASONING: confidence_yes=28 because F5's path to UB final is real but unprovable from briefing; confidence_no=26 because regain's 24-point favorite status has zero public support in provided data. Both scores are low because the briefing is nearly empty of competitive intelligence.", "key_factor": "Extreme data scarcity creates asymmetric uncertainty favoring the underdog \u2014 market pricing at 38% may reflect overconfidence in regain despite zero substantive performance differentiation in briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.23, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Match resolves in ~7 hours (TODAY). This is LIVE/IMMINENT, leaving almost no time for reversal. Current market pricing of 38% YES / 62% NO is likely reflecting real-time information or informed betting, not equilibrium uncertainty. DATA ASYMMETRY SEVERE: Briefing provides zero actionable comparative data\u2014no recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength, map pool analysis, or recent match results for either team. Both teams qualified for playoffs, but qualification alone does not differentiate win probability in a BO3. BASELINE ASSUMPTION: In symmetric mid-tier esports BO3 playoff matches with no distinguishing information, base rate is ~50% for each team. However, the market is NOT priced at 50/50. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: Current prices (38% YES / 62% NO) deviate significantly from uninformed 50/50. This 24-point spread suggests either: (a) informed betting favoring regain, (b) perception that regain is the stronger team, or (c) recent pre-match intelligence not captured in the briefing. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION: Without access to team rosters, recent win rates, map veto advantages, or current form data, confidence in either direction is artificially low. The briefing explicitly states 'no recent form data' and 'no direct comparative analysis.' PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT RATIONALE: Assign probability_score = 38 (matching YES market price) as a baseline, reflecting that market participants have likely incorporated information unavailable in this briefing. Regain is priced as the marginal favorite. CONFIDENCE SCORES RATIONALE: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set to ~22\u201323 because the briefing lacks the granular data required to independently validate either team's strength. This is not a 'true coin flip' (50/50); the market has priced a lean toward regain. But we cannot reliably explain WHY from the briefing alone. NO HISTORICAL BASE RATE AVAILABLE: Specific historical rates for 'F5 Esports vs regain' or even 'mid-tier NA CS BO3 outcomes by seeding/qualification' are not available. This is a live match with limited pre-match public data. FORFEITURE/CANCELLATION RISK: Resolution criteria include 50-50 on cancellation, forfeit, or no winner within 7 days. With <7 hours to match start, cancellation risk is low but non-zero. This slightly reduces confidence in any prediction.", "key_factor": "In mid-tier esports BO3 playoffs with symmetric qualification, unmarked teams have ~50% win probability; market pricing at 38/62 suggests modest informational advantage toward regain or perception of regain strength", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects genuine uncertainty, NOT crowd exuberance or panic\u2014this is rational given total information vacuum. Briefing contains zero actionable data: no recent form, no head-to-head record, no roster info, no map pool analysis, no expert predictions. Both teams qualified for playoffs (binary fact), but qualification alone tells nothing about relative strength in BO3 format. Current price leans regain (62%), but this lean has no evidentiary basis in the briefing\u2014it is pure assumption or historical Polymarket price anchoring. The 24-point spread (38 vs 62) is UNJUSTIFIED by available data; should be closer to 50-50 if markets were reflecting information asymmetry honestly. Crowd appears RATIONALLY APATHETIC: low volume ($6.1k for TODAY event) suggests traders lack confidence in any signal and are avoiding the market. KEY RISK: Event timing is TODAY (~7 hours to resolution). Any reversal now requires major new information (team roster issues, DDoS, forfeiture)\u2014highly unlikely. For a LIVE/IMMINENT event with zero public form data, low confidence on BOTH sides is appropriate; neither side can justify >40% conviction. No evidence of crowd panic-selling or euphoria; market is simply betting blind. Current odds may reflect arbitrary previous price or default pessimism about F5. Probability_score set to 38 to match market price, but both confidence scores held LOW (28/26) because briefing provides NO independent reasoning to diverge from 50-50.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "DOMAIN CONTEXT: ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America represents Tier-2/3 competitive Counter-Strike, below franchised leagues (ESL Pro League, Blast Premier). At this level, teams experience frequent roster churn, limited sponsorship consistency, and variable preparation quality\u2014standard variance is HIGH. DATA VACUUM: Briefing contains NO team-specific performance metrics (recent Win-Loss records, map statistics, player fragging power, economic trading patterns, anti-eco conversions, or head-to-head results). This is not a minor gap\u2014it is catastrophic for predictive confidence in esports where form is volatile week-to-week. BRIEFING QUALITY: KEY FACTS section contains unrelated tournament snippets (Johnny Speeds vs QWENTRY, Mindfreak, Oceania Cup 3, LORGAR rankings) with NO substantive data on F5 Esports or regain. NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states 'limited specific information about either team's recent performance.' This is a red flag for market signal integrity. SYMMETRY OF QUALIFICATION: Both teams cleared playoff qualification thresholds, indicating near-parity in minimum skill floor. Playoff qualification alone does NOT differentiate tier-2 NA teams in predictive value. MARKET PRICE INTERPRETATION: 38% YES / 62% NO suggests market participants have information asymmetry favoring regain, OR regain has marginally stronger recent form/roster stability. However, with <$6.2K USD volume and zero supporting fundamentals in briefing, this pricing may reflect limited liquidity rather than sharp analysis. TIMING PRESSURE: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~7 hours. No time for roster confirmations, coaching staff verification, or pre-match scrimmage data to surface. Live matches can produce unexpected forfeits or technical issues in Tier-2 NA tournaments (see resolution criteria allowing 50-50 tie for cancellations/walkover). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 28 (low) because no evidence supports F5 specifically; confidence_no = 25 (lower) because equal absence of evidence for regain. The 38% market price is noted but NOT treated as ground truth given data poverty. Both confidence scores remain severely depressed due to missing fundamentals. INDUSTRY INSIDER KNOWLEDGE: In Challenger League, outcomes often hinge on: (1) which team had LAN practice in final 48h, (2) roster last-minute changes, (3) stand-in availability, (4) economic meta shifts in live patch. NONE of this appears in the briefing, making confident prediction impossible. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT WITH MARKET: probability_score = 38 matches market YES price, but this is NOT endorsement of market efficiency\u2014rather, it reflects capitulation to data insufficiency. With better fundamentals, this could legitimately be anywhere 25\u201375.", "key_factor": "Mid-tier NA Challenger League matches are inherently volatile due to roster instability, inconsistent practice schedules, and limited statistical history\u2014the 38% market price reflects genuine uncertainty rather than strong fundamentals favoring either side.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains almost no actionable intelligence on either team \u2014 no recent form, no head-to-head history, no roster composition, no map pool analysis. This is a BLIND MARKET masquerading as informed. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: The 38/62 split favors regain by 24 percentage points despite identical baseline information. This suggests market has access to external data (Discord, team announcements, recent scrim results, or community sentiment) NOT in the briefing. The council is trading on information asymmetry, not on analysis. BLACK SWAN \u2014 ROSTER AVAILABILITY: BO3 matches in online Challenger League are sensitive to last-minute player unavailability. With ~7 hours until start and no roster confirmation in briefing, a single stand-in substitution (illness, internet failure, family emergency) could neuter F5's map-reading or anti-strat execution. regain may have deeper bench depth or more stable roster continuity. ABSENCE OF RECENT FORM: The briefing explicitly states 'No recent form statistics or head-to-head record provided.' For a TODAY match, this is red flag #1. If F5 is on a losing streak or regain just upset a higher seed in quarters, the briefing would not capture it. The 62% NO price may already reflect regain's momentum. BO3 VOLATILITY: A best-of-3 requires 2 map wins. Map 1 outcome (random or skill-dependent) often sets psychological momentum. F5's meta understanding, anti-strat preparation, or map-specific utility economy could be weeks behind if they've been scrimming specific opponents. No data on this. COMPETITIVE TIER CONTEXT: ESL Challenger League Season 51 features high roster turnover, sponsorship-driven line-up changes, and academy teams rotating players. F5's roster may be mid-season rebuilding; regain may have been together for months. This structural difference is invisible in the briefing. CONFIDENCE FLOOR: Both confidence scores are LOW (28/27) because the briefing provides zero comparative evidence for EITHER side. The 38% YES price is market consensus, not analyst consensus. This is a pure sentiment/information-asymmetry market, not a skill-based prediction.", "key_factor": "A key F5 player is unavailable due to last-minute illness, internet outage, or personal emergency immediately before match start, forcing a roster substitution that destabilizes their BO3 strategy.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.41535911602209946, "no_score": 0.5433179723502305, "edge": 0.04035911602209946, "no_edge": -0.0816820276497695, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 31% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1894574", "question": "Counter-Strike: F5 Esports vs regain (BO3) - ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket final match between F5 Esports and regain in the ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"F5 Esports\" if F5 Esports win the match against regain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against F5 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 6157.8451380000015, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Complete overview of the Johnny Speeds vs.", "QWENTRY matchup at ESL Challenger League Season 51 Europe Cup 3!", "Ivz has 2 good maps to play and still bottom frag\u2026\u2026 these MF's suck.", "Please log in and sync your account with Steam to upvote.", "Mindfreak matchup at ESL Challenger League Season 51 Oceania Cup 3!", "Australia flamboyant (Map 1 - Overpass).", "Does cutzmerets own part of the org or something how tf he still here.", "LORGAR RANKINGS Season 1 Closed Qualifier.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Upper bracket quarter-final.", "World ranking HLTV regional ranking Regional rankings Global Valve ranking Valve ranking Global Valve Regional ranking Regional Valve ranking Global Valve"], "news_summary": "F5 Esports and regain are scheduled to compete in a Best-of-3 match at the ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup 3 Playoffs. The search results show limited specific information about either team's recent performance or head-to-head matchups. Both teams appear to be competing in North American Challenger League competition, which represents mid-tier competitive Counter-Strike. No recent form data, roster changes, or direct comparative analysis is available in the search results.", "side_yes_case": ["F5 appears in official ESL Challenger League playoff bracket as a competitor", "Limited negative sentiment or criticism about F5 in available data", "F5 qualified for playoffs, indicating they cleared earlier rounds"], "side_no_case": ["regain also qualified for and appears in official playoff bracket", "No distinguishing performance data favors either team in results", "No recent form statistics or head-to-head record provided"], "key_context": ["ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup 3 is a mid-tier competitive tournament", "Match format is Best-of-3 (BO3), requiring 2 map wins to advance", "Both teams are in playoff stage, indicating qualified status from earlier rounds", "Search results lack team roster information, recent map pool performance, or recent match results", "No direct head-to-head history or recent form trajectory data available"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T23:51:08.238598Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T07:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T07:12:56.889909+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "0decf9ee-a8df-4768-b825-04cb0767629c", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T23:54:30.996506+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1912093", "question": "Valorant: Murash vs Insomnia (BO3) - VCL Japan: Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Murash and Insomnia in the VCL Japan: Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 8 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Murash\" if Murash win the match against Insomnia.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Insomnia\" if Insomnia win the match against Murash.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T10:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T04:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.61, "volume_usd": 17.89, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "CONDITION TO RESOLVE YES: Murash must win the BO3 match against Insomnia on April 8, 2026, with the match completed and a decisive winner determined (not canceled, not forfeited pre-start, not delayed >7 days). MURASH FAVORED BY MARKET DATA: Betting odds 1.54 (Murash) vs 2.32 (Insomnia) imply ~65% implicit probability for Murash win; current market price 61% YES is slightly below betting consensus, suggesting modest undervaluation of Murash. RECENT FORM ADVANTAGE: Murash won 2-0 vs RIDDLE ORDER in quarterfinals (upper bracket); Insomnia lost 1-2 vs REJECT in upper semifinals; Murash demonstrates momentum while Insomnia is coming off a loss. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Murash defeated Insomnia 2-0 on Feb 4, 2026 (earlier phase of same tournament); this is strongest predictive signal but is ~2 months stale and does not account for roster/meta changes. COUNTERWEIGHT \u2014 INSOMNIA RESILIENCE: Insomnia's appearance in upper semifinals indicates they've beaten other lower-bracket teams; competitive odds at 2.32 suggest meaningful (~43%) win probability; lower-bracket teams can improve strategies between matches. COUNTERWEIGHT \u2014 MURASH VULNERABILITY: Briefing notes Murash previously lost 0-2 to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX, showing they are beatable by strong opponents; not an unbeatable team. BO3 FORMAT REDUCES VARIANCE: Best-of-3 format reduces upsets vs single-map play; favors more consistent/better team but still allows upsets ~35-45% of the time. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~10 hours). Very low risk of cancellation at this stage (tournament is live, both teams are present). Forfeiture/walkover risk is real but rare (~5-10% baseline). If match completes decisively, vlr.gg will almost certainly report within 2-hour window. DATA GAPS: No current roster information, no map pool analysis, no player stats from recent matches, no coaching changes, no meta shifts since Feb. This limits confidence on both sides but slightly favors relying on market consensus and recent form. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Murash is the probabilistic favorite based on betting market, recent form, and head-to-head history. However, Insomnia has sufficient competitive evidence to create meaningful uncertainty. Estimate: 62% Murash win (38% Insomnia win). Confidence in YES is moderate-to-high (72%) due to multiple converging indicators; confidence in NO is lower (58%) due to lack of recent evidence supporting Insomnia upset.", "key_factor": "Match scheduled for April 8 12:00 AM ET (~10 hours away); insufficient recent performance data on current team rosters and meta adaptation since Feb 4 head-to-head; forfeiture/walkover risk could trigger 50-50 resolution.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: Murash Gaming enters with tangible form advantage\u2014a clean 2-0 quarterfinals victory over RIDDLE ORDER immediately preceding this match, demonstrating current-state execution and team cohesion. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Murash defeated Insomnia 2-0 on Feb 4, 2026 in the same tournament structure, establishing a recent tactical blueprint and psychological edge in direct competition. BETTING MARKET CONSENSUS: Murash at 1.54 odds (61% implied) vs Insomnia at 2.32 (39% implied) reflects professional and sharp-money alignment toward Murash, a significant edge in a 10-team competitive field. INSOMNIA'S RECENT WEAKNESS: Insomnia lost 1-2 to REJECT in upper semifinals\u2014a three-map series loss indicating fatigue, tactical exploitation, or form regression rather than a close contest. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS CONSISTENCY: The best-of-three format reduces single-map upsets; Murash's demonstrated consistency (recent 2-0) should translate better in extended series than Insomnia's mixed results. ELIMINATION CONTEXT: This is Lower Round 2; loser exits playoff contention entirely. Murash's upward trajectory and recent victories suggest greater mental resilience and preparation depth for sudden-death stakes. UNDERDOG'S COUNTER-ARGUMENT LIMITATIONS: While Insomnia reached upper semifinals (implying earlier lower-bracket wins), that run ended in a 1-2 loss; no evidence of tactical innovation or player upgrades between Feb 4 loss and now suggests they remain vulnerable to Murash's established gameplan. VULNERABILITIES NOTED BUT CONTEXTUALIZED: Murash's prior 0-2 losses to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX are historical; more recent performance (2-0 RIDDLE ORDER) is more predictive of current form than losses from earlier phases. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Higher confidence in YES (72) than NO (58) because briefing provides clear momentum, head-to-head data, and betting alignment for Murash; Insomnia's case relies on speculation about updated strategies and recent-match uncertainty rather than concrete evidence.", "key_factor": "Murash Gaming's recent 2-0 momentum victory over RIDDLE ORDER combined with a decisive 2-0 head-to-head precedent against Insomnia in the same tournament.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.65, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Insomnia's trajectory: The briefing shows Insomnia reached upper semifinals (lost 1-2 to REJECT), proving they beat multiple lower-bracket opponents to advance. This is not a team in freefall; they've won recent matches and adapted their play. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Recency bias against Murash: Murash's 2-0 win over RIDDLE ORDER is recent, but RIDDLE ORDER appears weaker than other bracket contenders. The briefing lacks evidence that RIDDLE ORDER is a strong test case for measuring Murash's current form. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Murash's loss pattern: The briefing explicitly states Murash lost 0-2 to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX. This shows structural vulnerabilities, not isolated upsets. Murash can be shut down by teams with specific strategies. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 February win is stale: The 2-0 head-to-head from Feb 4, 2026 is over one month old. In competitive esports with frequent patches, meta shifts, and player bootcamps, a February result is weak predictive power for April. Insomnia has had 30+ days to prepare counter-strategies. MARKET MISPRICING \u2014 Betting odds lag team development: Murash at 1.54 (65%) implies dominant superiority, yet betting odds themselves show Insomnia at 2.32, indicating the market acknowledges meaningful uncertainty. The 61% YES price may reflect historical bias toward the February win rather than current form. FORMAT ADVANTAGE \u2014 Bo3 structure: While Bo3 reduces variance, it also allows teams to adapt mid-series. If Insomnia loses Map 1, they have two more chances to execute new strategies or exploit Murash weaknesses identified in real-time. ELIMINATION PRESSURE \u2014 Double-elimination stakes cut both ways: Yes, Insomnia faces elimination, but this can sharpen focus. Murash, as the higher-seeded favorite, faces pressure to justify favoritism. Upset psychology in esports is real\u2014underdogs often perform above expectation under elimination pressure. DATA GAP \u2014 Missing player performance metrics: The briefing provides team-level results but no individual player stats, agent pool strengths, or recent map pick rates. This asymmetric information favors the underdog case; hidden strengths in Insomnia's roster or role specialists may not be reflected in market pricing. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION \u2014 YES confidence at 65: Strong evidence for Murash (recent win, head-to-head, betting consensus) justifies moderate-to-high confidence in the favorite's case. However, the one-month staleness of the H2H and Murash's previous 0-2 losses prevent higher confidence. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION \u2014 NO confidence at 58: Insomnia's recent upper-bracket run and tournament progression provide credible evidence they can compete, but lack of recent direct head-to-head and a February loss to the same opponent create uncertainty. Confidence in underdog case is intentionally restrained, reflecting real competitive uncertainty. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION (42 for YES / 58 for NO): The market's 61% for Murash assumes the February 2-0 remains highly predictive. Adjusting for one month of meta evolution, Insomnia's upper-bracket semifinal run, and Murash's historical vulnerability to certain opponents, the true probability tilts toward underdog viability. 42% for YES reflects genuine upset risk; this is not a 35-65 mismatch but rather a competitive 42-58 Lower Round 2 duel.", "key_factor": "Insomnia's recent upper-bracket semifinal run demonstrates adaptive gameplay and tournament momentum that may have closed the skill gap since the February 2-0 loss to Murash.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market price (61% YES) aligns closely with betting odds (1.54 vs 2.32), suggesting efficient pricing by informed bettors with esports domain knowledge. Murash has demonstrated superior recent form: 2-0 victory over RIDDLE ORDER vs. Insomnia's 1-2 loss to REJECT in adjacent bracket positions. Head-to-head precedent: Murash defeated Insomnia 2-0 on Feb 4, 2026 (~2 months prior), suggesting structural team matchup advantage. Bo3 format reduces upset probability compared to single-map play; Murash's win streak provides momentum in longer series. Lower Round 2 elimination implications may benefit Murash psychologically if they treat it as do-or-die with less pressure than Insomnia's similar stakes. Counterweight: Insomnia's semi-finals appearance (beating multiple lower-bracket teams) indicates capability against similar tier opponents; not a clear skill gap. Insomnia's recent loss to REJECT (1-2) could reflect meta adaptation or tactical shifts, not fundamental decline; limited match history prevents certainty. Murash's prior 0-2 losses to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX show vulnerability to certain playstyles; Insomnia may target similar weaknesses. Base rate for favored teams in esports double-elimination lower brackets: ~62-65% win rate; Murash at 1.54 odds (39% implied NO) is slightly overpriced on market, but confidence in Murash advantage is moderate rather than high. Data gap: No recent map pool information, player roster changes, or coach strategy updates provided; restricts confidence ceiling to 72% on YES side. Event timing (TODAY, ~10 hours to resolution): limited time for new information; market prices unlikely to shift dramatically unless betting volume increases sharply.", "key_factor": "In competitive esports double-elimination lower bracket matches between teams with clear recent form differentials (win streak vs. recent loss), the favored team wins approximately 60-68% of the time in Bo3 formats.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market price (61% YES) aligns closely with betting odds favoring Murash (1.54 vs 2.32), suggesting rational pricing rather than crowd emotion. Murash momentum is real: 2-0 victory over RIDDLE ORDER + prior 2-0 head-to-head win over Insomnia (Feb 4) creates concrete evidence of superiority. Insomnia's 1-2 loss to REJECT in upper semifinals is concerning for a team needing to win now to stay alive in lower bracket. However, NO side has non-trivial support: Insomnia reached upper semifinals (beat other teams), Murash showed losses to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX (0-2), indicating vulnerability. Bo3 format adds stability; single-map variance is reduced, favoring the objectively stronger team on paper (Murash). Market lacks exuberance or panic\u201461% reflects genuine competitive uncertainty while acknowledging Murash's edge. Event is TODAY with ~10 hours to resolution; no time for major narrative shifts. Price reflects current information accurately. Confidence_yes higher (72) due to clear Murash data points; confidence_no lower (58) because Insomnia's recent form is murkier and upper semis appearance is not directly comparable. No obvious mispricing detected; market appears to be pricing in Murash's advantage proportionally to available evidence.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Murash Gaming holds clear recent momentum: 2-0 victory over RIDDLE ORDER in the immediately preceding round, indicating current tactical execution and team cohesion. Betting market pricing (1.54 vs 2.32) implies ~39% implied probability for Insomnia, closely matching the 39% NO price in this market\u2014suggesting efficient pricing with Murash favored but not prohibitively so. Historical head-to-head (Murash 2-0 Insomnia on Feb 4) is 2+ months old in esports terms; map pools, meta shifts, player form, and team roster adjustments can dramatically alter team strength over that span. Insomnia's path to upper semifinals indicates they defeated at least one lower-bracket opponent, demonstrating adaptive play; however, their subsequent 1-2 loss to REJECT (upper semifinal) suggests they hit a ceiling against top-tier competition. Lower Round 2 elimination context increases stakes for both teams, but Murash's winning trajectory (streak coming into this match) typically correlates with higher playoff qualification probability in esports. BO3 format reduces single-map variance; this favors the team with deeper map pool mastery and consistent execution\u2014Murash's current form suggests they hold this edge. Confidence_yes is higher (72) due to clear momentum, betting market alignment, and recent head-to-head precedent; confidence_no is moderate (55) because Insomnia's upper semis appearance proves they are capable of upset runs, and esports upsets via meta shifts or roster changes are not rare. Critical data gap: player-specific statistics, current roster composition, and confirmed map pool preferences are absent from briefing; if either team has undergone mid-season roster changes (common in Japanese esports), this analysis would need recalibration. Timeline is TODAY (~10 hours to match)\u2014reversal is unlikely given Murash's current form advantage; market price at 61% YES is reasonable and close to analytical estimate.", "key_factor": "In double-elimination lower bracket matches, momentum and recent map pool adjustments often outweigh historical head-to-head records; Murash's 2-0 win streak and superior betting odds (1.54 vs 2.32) indicate current form advantage, but Insomnia's upper semifinals run (beating teams to reach that stage) suggests adaptive capability that could narrow the gap.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "Murash favored by both market (61% YES) and betting odds (1.54), driven by recent 2-0 victory and prior Feb 4 head-to-head win \u2014 but recency bias may overweight a single match result. Insomnia's 1-2 loss to REJECT (upper semis) is