oit that directly counters Murash's core agent compositions, compounded by motivation asymmetry (Murash overconfident after 2-0 vs RIDDLE ORDER; Insomnia facing elimination desperation).", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6054325955734406, "no_score": 0.39779448621553887, "edge": -0.0045674044265593405, "no_edge": 0.007794486215538854, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "STRONG", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.639344262295082, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1912093", "question": "Valorant: Murash vs Insomnia (BO3) - VCL Japan: Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Murash and Insomnia in the VCL Japan: Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 8 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Murash\" if Murash win the match against Insomnia.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Insomnia\" if Insomnia win the match against Murash.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T10:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T04:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.61, "volume_usd": 17.89, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 Japan: Split 1 is an online Japanese VAL tournament organized by Riot Games, Nippon Television Network Corporation, and Hakuhodo", "Phase 1: March 19<sup>th</sup> - March 29<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "10 teams, Double-Elimination tournament; All matches are Bo3; Top 2 teams qualify to Playoffs and qualify to", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from REJECT vs.", "TBD - Upper Final match of Challengers 2026: Japan Split 1 Valorant event.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Murash Gaming vs.", "Insomnia - Lower Round 2 match of Challengers 2026: Japan Split 1 Valorant event.", "TBD - Lower Round 2 match of Challengers 2026: Japan Split 1 Valorant event.", "Find detailed results about the VALORANT match between Top gz and Dr Lyken \u0648\u0627\u0639\u0648\u0627\u0646\u0647 in Insomnia 26 - S1 that took place on March 20, 2026 - 21:00 EET.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from RIDDLE ORDER vs."], "news_summary": "Murash Gaming faces Insomnia in a Lower Round 2 match of VALORANT Challengers 2026: Japan Split 1, Phase 2, scheduled for April 7, 2026. Betting odds favor Murash Gaming at 1.54 versus Insomnia at 2.32. Murash Gaming comes off a 2-0 victory against RIDDLE ORDER, while Insomnia recently lost 1-2 to REJECT. Both teams are competing in the double-elimination lower bracket with playoff qualification implications.", "side_yes_case": ["Murash Gaming favored by betting market (1.54 odds vs 2.32 for Insomnia)", "Murash Gaming on winning streak with 2-0 victory over RIDDLE ORDER in upper quarterfinals", "Head-to-head advantage: Murash previously defeated Insomnia 2-0 in Split 1 (Feb 4, 2026)", "Insomnia showing inconsistency with recent 1-2 loss to REJECT in upper semifinals"], "side_no_case": ["Insomnia has played more recent matches and may have updated strategies", "Betting odds suggest competitive match with Insomnia at 2.32 indicating meaningful win probability", "Insomnia's upper semifinals appearance indicates they've beaten other lower-bracket teams", "Murash Gaming previously lost 0-2 to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX, showing vulnerability"], "key_context": ["Double-elimination Lower Round 2 match; loser is eliminated from playoffs contention", "Best of 3 (Bo3) format reduces variance compared to single maps", "Tournament structure: Phase 2 is continuation of VALORANT Challengers 2026: Japan Split 1", "Recent head-to-head: Murash 2-0 Insomnia on Feb 4, 2026 in earlier phase", "Match details pending player stats and map selection information"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T23:54:18.715998Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T10:10:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T10:46:10.514730+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "wrong_buy", "summary": "Wrong BUY YES \u2014 only 1/7 agents called NO (winner); loudest wrong voice: The Rules Lawyer (72%)", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bear", "prob": 0.42, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.58, "key_factor": "Insomnia's recent upper-bracket semifinal run demonstrates adaptive gameplay and tournament momentum that may have closed the skill gap since the February 2-0 loss to Murash."}], "agents_against_winner": [{"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "pro