environment; Group C advancement carries real playoff seeding implications. Underperformance under pressure is a classic qualifier upset vector. Market volume is moderate ($22.6k) but not high. This suggests limited sharp money and possible casual overweight on the higher-ranked/more-familiar name (Brute). Asymmetric information strongly favors the NO side here. Resolution criterion allows 50-50 ties on forfeit/disqualification. Qualifier-stage teams have higher admin/logistical failure rates. A mid-series technical dispute or unexpected walkover is low-probability but high-impact. No map pool or veto data provided. If Infurity has a specialist map Brute is weak on and forces it in veto, the series dynamic inverts. This is completely invisible in the briefing. Confidence in YES is LOW (35) because Brute's evidence is shallow and depends on old/unclear roster data. Confidence in NO is also relatively LOW (42) because Infurity is a complete unknown. This is a high-entropy market where the true probability could easily swing 20+ points on game-day roster confirmation or tactical preparation quality\u2014neither side deserves high confidence.", "key_factor": "INFURITY Gaming fields an unexpected roster substitution or tactical pivot (likely a ringer or fresh player) that exploits Brute's preparation gap, or Brute suffers a last-minute lineup disruption before the 4:00 AM ET start.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5218211920529802, "no_score": 0.5058781362007169, "edge": -0.07817880794701981, "no_edge": 0.10587813620071684, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 52% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1909431", "question": "Counter-Strike: Brute vs INFURITY Gaming (BO3) - United21 Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market 