T1's Week 1 loss to KT (0-2) suggests early-season adaptation struggles, but roster includes Faker (9.2 CS/min, 3.38 KDA), one of League's most accomplished mid laners. T1's 50% record is competitive parity in early LCK play, not disqualifying. HISTORICAL & EXPERIENCE EDGE: T1 has legendary franchise status and Faker's clutch performance history in high-stakes matches. However, this is speculative advantage not captured in current-season data. Gen.G's stronger current form (60% vs 50%) is empirically stronger signal. MISSING CRITICAL DATA: No direct T1 vs Gen.G head-to-head record provided. No champion select data, patch nuances, or player-specific matchup history (e.g., Faker vs Chovy tendencies). No Ban/Pick strategy implications. This creates 15-20 point confidence ceiling on either side. MARKET PRICING REALITY: Current market prices show YES (T1) at 36% ($0.35) and NO (Gen.G) at 64% ($0.65). This 28-point spread aligns with Gen.G's superior early metrics but underweights T1's experience and Faker's individual caliber. Spread suggests slight overestimation of Gen.G advantage. GAME 1 SINGLE-GAME VOLATILITY: LoL Game 1s can hinge on draft, early jungle proximity, bot lane matchups, and execution variance more than aggregate team strength. A 60/50 WR split does not dictate 64/36 Game 1 probability; single-game variance is higher. EARLY SEASON CONTEXT: Both teams are 4-5 weeks into season. Form may still be settling; sample sizes are modest. T1's Week 1 loss to KT (0-2) is concerning but single series, not season trend yet. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Criteria are clear\u2014first to win Game 1 wins market. gol.gg is primary source with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. No ambiguity in resolution criteria themselves. Mechanism risk is low (5-10 point discount). PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Combining Gen.G's superior current metrics (60% WR, elite individual stats) with T1's experience, Faker's caliber, early-season variance, and missing head-to-head data: P(Gen.G wins) \u2