0 teams competing", "Search results show historical/archived statistics rather than confirmed upcoming Game 1 fixture", "T1 and Gen.G both use diverse champion pools suggesting flexible preparation", "Early season LCK play may not fully reflect team capabilities as rosters settle", "No direct head-to-head record or specific Game 1 scheduling information provided"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-08T09:56:15.972030Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T16:10:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T20:14:10.104000+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "10867a6a-41de-4009-b446-52fb2cff32ab", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T11:47:20.202323+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1884269", "question": "Valorant: EDward Gaming vs Trace Esports (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between EDward Gaming and Trace Esports in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 8 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EDward Gaming\" if EDward Gaming win the match against Trace Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Trace Esports\" if Trace Esports win the match against EDward Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T17:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T11:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.825, "volume_usd": 47852.429999000036, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.64, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: EDward Gaming must win the BO3 match against Trace Esports. Resolution criteria are explicit and unambiguous\u2014standard competitive win resolves to YES. EDG FORM & MOMENTUM: EDG started VCT 2026 Stage 1 undefeated in week 1, indicating strong current momentum and preparation for this group stage. RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Most recent direct match (Jan 2025) shows EDG dominating 13-4 with all five roster members posting strong individual stats (CHICHOO 280 ACS, cb 260 ACS, etc.). This is the closest data point to current form. INDIVIDUAL PLAYER PERFORMANCE: EDG roster (CHICHOO, cb, Jieni7, nobody, Smoggy) demonstrated exceptional fragging in Shanghai Masters 2025 context with +/- differentials ranging +2 to +22. Trace Esports players (deLb, Kai, Xlele, FengF, Viva) show lower ACS and +/- metrics in available data. TRACE ESPORTS COUNTER-CASE: Trace did defeat EDG 13-10 in Aug 2024 (Upper Quarterfinals), proving they can compete. However, this is >7 months old relative to Jan 2025 dominance and current week 1 form. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-3 introduces adaptation and map selection strategy. While EDG favored, Trace retains ~20-25% realistic win probability through superior map prep, roster adjustments, or tactical reads. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 82% closely tracks this analysis, suggesting efficient market pricing reflecting EDG's demonstrable form advantage and Trace's viable but lower-probability pathway. TIMING & META: This is TODAY (6 hours to match). Recent form data (Shanghai Masters, week 1 VCT) is highly relevant. No roster changes or meta shifts flagged that would significantly alter competitive balance. RESOLUTION SOURCE CONFIDENCE: vlr.gg is standard esports resolution source; no ambiguity in team name matching (both teams clearly identifiable). No forfeit/disqualification risk evident from briefing. CALIBRATION: 78% reflects EDG's measurable form edge, recent dominant head-to-head, and strong week 1 momentum, offset by BO3 competitive format and Trace's proven capability to compete at professional level.", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; primary uncertainty is genuine competitive outcome on match day.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.79, "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "EDG MOMENTUM & CURRENT FORM: EDG went undefeated in week 1 of VCT China 2026 Stage 1, establishing themselves as a top group performer. This is the most recent and relevant data point\u2014events TODAY are heavily influenced by current momentum and confidence. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: EDG crushed Trace 13-4 in Upper Semifinals (Jan 2025), a comprehensive 9-map deficit. This was recent enough to reflect current meta understanding and not ancient history. The 13-4 scoreline indicates both map wins and strategic superiority. ROSTER PERFORMANCE ASYMMETRY: EDG's Shanghai Masters 2025 data shows all five players with exceptional stats: CHICHOO (280-305 ACS), cb (260-293 ACS), Jieni7 (220 ACS), nobody (210-239 ACS), Smoggy (191-249 ACS). In contrast, Trace Esports player stats from recent appearances show weaker individual performances (deLb 267 ACS, Kai 191 ACS, others lower), indicating a clear mechanical skill gap. TRACE'S COUNTERARGUMENT WEAKNESS: While Trace beat EDG 13-10 in Aug 2024, this is nearly 8 months old and predates the meta shifts that occurred through late