ic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "EDG's week-1 undefeated run in VCT China 2026 Stage 1 Group Omega is the strongest current-form signal; this is early-season group play where momentum compounds. Shanghai Masters 2025 stats show EDG roster cohesion at elite level: CHICHOO (ACS 305, +11), cb (ACS 293, +13), Smoggy (ACS 249, +5) indicate synchronized site execution and economy discipline. Jan 2025 13-4 demolition of Trace Esports was recent and comprehensive\u2014all EDG players posted positive K/D differentials, suggesting systematic map control rather than singular carry performance. BO3 format introduces non-trivial upset probability (~20-24%): Trace demonstrated competitive viability with 13-10 win over EDG in Aug 2024 UBQFs, implying map-pool awareness and anti-stratting capability. Trace roster (deLb, Kai, Xlele, FengF, Viva) has individual fragging potential shown in head-to-head data, but recent performance data is sparse; confidence in NO side is asymmetrically lower due to data freshness gap. Meta evolution between Jan 2025 and Apr 2026 agent selections (Trace using Viper/Neon/Omen core vs EDG's raze/reyna/chamber rotation) suggests both teams have adapted, but EDG's adaptation appears more recent and cohesive. Market price of 82% YES reflects appropriate baseline given EDG's current form and head-to-head dominance; no evidence of systematic mispricing given event timing (TODAY, ~6 hours to resolution). EDG's undefeated week-1 status carries slight psychological advantage in group-play context; Trace enters as underdog with limited recent international context vs current EDG roster. Resolution mechanics (VLR.gg official source, 2-hour fallback to credible reporting) are standard and carry no impact on in-game probability.", "key_factor": "EDG's week-1 undefeated streak in VCT 2026 Stage 1 combined with dominant recent map control statistics (multiple players with +10 to +22 K/D differentials) suggests superior current utility usage and positioning discipline, but BO3 format and Trace's proven Aug 2024 competitive win (13-10) against EDG indicate map-pool vulnerability that could enable a Trace upset on 1-2 maps.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "EDG's undefeated week-1 record is genuine and recent (April 2026), but briefing lacks specifics on opponents faced\u2014if they beat weak opponents, momentum may not translate to established teams. Trace Esports' most recent stat line (deLb 267 ACS, Kai 191, Xlele 143) is fragment-level individual performance data with no context on round context, economy management, or team cohesion\u2014superficial stats can mask tactical weaknesses or strengths. The 13-4 EDG victory in Jan 2025 is 3+ months old in-game time; meta patches, agent nerfs/buffs, and tactical evolution could have heavily favored Trace's playstyle since then (briefing silent on patch notes or meta shifts). BO3 format explicitly allows Trace to ban maps and adapt strategy\u2014EDG's week-1 success may be on a narrow 2-3 map pool that Trace can exploit if they've scouted recent EDG VODs. Briefing explicitly states 'Trace Esports team logo' with no recent 2026 match data for Trace, only historical 2024-2025 records\u2014this is a critical absence suggesting Trace's current roster form is unknown or they have recent changes not reflected in briefing. EDG's Shanghai Masters data (Feb 2026) shows exceptional individual ACS but those matches are not against Trace\u2014performance vs mid-tier opponents \u2260 performance vs prepared, determined playoff-quality teams. Roster continuity for Trace is unclear (Xlele, FengF, Kai, Viva, deLb listed but no 2026 confirmation)\u2014if any key player was benched, subbed, or transferred since Jan 2025, Trace's tactical identity may have shifted unpredictably. Market pricing at 82% YES suggests consensus overweighting recent EDG form and underweighting Trace's BO3 adaptation potential and unknown current state. EDG's TYLOO comparison in briefing (also undefeated week 1) provides no follow-up result\u2014if TYLOO later lost to a lower-seed team, it's evidence that week-1 perfection is fragile. No mention of head-to-head map pool matchups, bans, or player agent comfort on competitive picks (e.g., if Trace's Kai thrives on Neon and EDG's meta has shifted away from Neon-heavy postplants, TE may exploit this). Viva's +/- of -5 in recent stats + FengF's -7 suggest defensive positioning issues, but this could be a small-sample artifact or reflect that Trace was playing from behind\u2014BO3 reset eliminates momentum disadvantage.", "key_factor": "Trace Esports executes a coordinated meta shift or tactical innovation (lurk/support-heavy setup) that EDG's week-1 momentum-driven playstyle cannot adapt to across a BO3, similar to how early-season undefeated teams often collapse against teams that prepare specific map counters.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.772008368200837, "no_score": 0.22832402234636867, "edge": -0.052991631799163, "no_edge": 0.05332402234636863, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "CAUTIOUS", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.21212121212121218, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1884269", "question": "Valorant: EDward Gaming vs Trace Esports (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between EDward Gaming and Trace Esports in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 8 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EDward Gaming\" if EDward Gaming win the match against Trace Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Trace Esports\" if Trace Esports win the match against EDward Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T17:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T11:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.825, "volume_usd": 47852.429999000036, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["Nova Esports roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "(reposting because I sent this during CN matches this morning and I don't think anyone saw.", "I wanna see other people's thoughts on this.).", "Had a good streak, almost Diamond - and then the great downfall happened.", "In the first week of VCT China 2026 Stage 1, EDward Gaming and TYLOO went undefeated to start on top of their respective groups.", "VCT 2026: Americas Kickoff is an offline American VAL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This S-Tier tournament took place from Jan 15 to Feb 15 2026", "| 2024/7/18  Trace Esports  13/5  def  7/5  atk  6/0  Upper Final  Playoffs |  |\n| Corrode (9) |  |  |  |  | 6 |  |  | 60 |  | 60% |  | 34 | (3)  (4)  (1)  (1) |\n| 2026/2/07  Dragon Ranger Gaming  13/6  def  8/4  atk  5/2  Lower Round 5  Main Event |  |\n| 2026/2/06  TYLOO  13/7  atk  8/4  def  5/3  Lower Round 4  Main Event |  |\n| 2026/2/05  JDG Esports  13/5  atk  9/3  def  4/2  Lower Round 3  Main Event |  |\n| 2025/9/13  NRG  11/13  atk  6/6  def  5/7  Opening (C)  Group Stage |  |\n| 2025/8/22  Xi Lai Gaming  13/5  atk  9/3  def  4/2  Lower Round 3  Playoffs |  |\n| 2025/8/09  Dragon Ranger Gaming  10/13  def  5/7  atk  5/6  Upper Quarterfinals  Playoffs |  |\n| 2025/7/31  JDG Esports  13/5  def  8/4  atk  5/1  Week 4  Group Stage |  | [...] | 2025/1/25  Trace Esports  12/14  atk  7/5  def  5/7  OT  0/2  Grand Final  Main Event |  |\n| 2025/1/24  Bilibili Gaming  13/5  def  9/3  atk  4/2  Lower Final  Main Event |  |\n| 2025/1/22  Xi Lai Gaming  12/14  def  6/6  atk  6/6  OT  0/2  Lower Round 3  Main Event |  |\n| 2025/1/20  Trace Esports  4/13  atk  4/8  def  0/5  Upper Semifinals  Main Event |  |\n| 2024/8/25  Team Heretics  13/9  def  6/6  atk  7/3  Grand Final  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/8/23  LEVIAT\u00c1N  13/4  atk  8/4  def  5/0  Upper Final  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/8/17  Sentinels  13/9  atk  6/6  def  7/3  Upper Semifinals  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/8/11  Paper Rex  13/4  atk  9/3  def  4/1  Decider (D)  Group Stage |  |\n| 2024/8/04  FUT Esports  13/9  atk  8/4  def  5/5  Opening (D)  Group Stage |  | [...] | 2024/12/13  Trace Esports  14/12  atk  6/6  def  6/6  OT  2/0  Lower Round 1  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/12/11  Xi Lai Gaming  11/13  atk  6/6  def  5/7  Day 4  Group Stage |  |\n| 2024/12/09  JDG Esports  13/8  def  6/6  atk  7/2  Day 2  Group Stage |  |\n| 2024/11/22  DetonatioN FocusMe  9/13  def  7/5  atk  2/8  Round 1  Swiss Stage |  |\n| 2024/8/25  Team Heretics  13/4  atk  11/1  def  2/3  Grand Final  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/8/17  Sentinels  13/6  atk  10/2  def  3/4  Upper Semifinals  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/8/14  Trace Esports  13/10  def  10/2  atk  3/8  Upper Quarterfinals  Playoffs |  |\n| 2024/8/11  Paper Rex  13/8  atk  6/6  def  7/2  Decider (D)  Group Stage |  |\n| 2024/7/20  FunPlus Phoenix  13/9  atk  9/3  def  4/6  Grand Final  Playoffs |  |", "Trace Esports team logo\nEDward Gaming team logo\n\n|  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| deLb  TE | viper |  | 267 | 21 | /  17 / | 8 | +4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Kai  TE | neon |  | 191 | 16 | /  19 / | 5 | -3 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Xlele  TE | omen |  | 143 | 12 | /  18 / | 6 | -6 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| FengF  TE | waylay |  | 141 | 11 | /  18 / | 4 | -7 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Viva  TE | skye |  | 134 | 10 | /  15 / | 7 | -5 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nviper\nneon\nomen\nwaylay\nskye [...] |  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| CHICHOO  EDG | viper |  | 280 | 56 | /  34 / | 21 | +22 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| cb  EDG | raze neon |  | 260 | 48 | /  31 / | 14 | +17 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Jieni7  EDG | reyna chamber |  | 220 | 50 | /  36 / | 14 | +14 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| nobody  EDG | fade sova skye |  | 210 | 43 | /  33 / | 19 | +10 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Smoggy  EDG | omen |  | 191 | 39 | /  37 / | 33 | +2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nviper\nraze\nneon\nreyna\nchamber\nfade\nsova\nskye\nomen [...] viper\nkilljoy\nneon\nsova\nomen\n\n|  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| CHICHOO  EDG | viper |  | 305 | 16 | /  5 / | 9 | +11 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| cb  EDG | neon |  | 293 | 18 | /  5 / | 2 | +13 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Smoggy  EDG | omen |  | 249 | 13 | /  8 / | 14 | +5 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| nobody  EDG | sova |  | 239 | 13 | /  5 / | 8 | +8 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Jieni7  EDG | chamber |  | 185 | 11 | /  8 / | 1 | +3 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nviper\nneon\nomen\nsova\nchamber", "| R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| FengF  TE |  |  |  |  | /         / |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Kai  TE |  |  |  |  | /         / |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| LuoK1ng  TE |  |  |  |  | /         / |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Viva  TE |  |  |  |  | /         / |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| deLb  TE |  |  |  |  | /         / |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | [...] 2024/12/13 \n\nVCT 2024: Champions\n\nUBQF\n\n2 0\n\n2024/08/14 \n\nVCT 24: CN Stage 2\n\nUBF\n\n2 0\n\n2024/07/18 \n\nVCT 24: CN Stage 1\n\nW5\n\n2 0\n\n2024/05/05 \n\nVCT 24: CN Kickoff\n\nSF\n\n2 0\n\n2024/03/01 \n\nVCT CN EVO A2: Selection\n\nGF\n\n3 0\n\n2023/10/29 \n\nVCT CN EVO A2: Selection\n\nUF\n\n0 2\n\n2023/10/27 \n\nVCT CN EVO A1: Variation\n\nUBQF\n\n2 0\n\n2023/09/23\n\nPast Matches\n\n2 0\n\nvs."], "news_summary": "EDward Gaming and Trace Esports are set to face off in a BO3 match in VCT China 2026 Stage 1 Group Omega. EDG started VCT 2026 Stage 1 undefeated in the first week, demonstrating strong current form. Trace Esports has a mixed recent history against EDG, with one dominant loss (4-13) in January 2025 but also a competitive match in July 2024. The matchup features two established Chinese Valorant organizations competing in the early stages of the 2026 season.", "side_yes_case": ["EDG went undefeated in week 1 of VCT China 2026 Stage 1, showing current strong form", "EDG dominated Trace Esports 13-4 in Upper Semifinals (Jan 2025), with all players performing well", "EDG roster (CHICHOO, cb, Jieni7, nobody, Smoggy) showed exceptional individual performances in recent Shanghai Masters match with strong ACS and +/- stats", "EDG has historical map win advantage over Trace Esports based on recent matchup statistics"], "side_no_case": ["Trace Esports defeated EDG 13-10 in Upper Quarterfinals (Aug 2024), proving competitive capability", "Head-to-head record shows competitive matches; Trace Esports has tournament wins in same era", "Individual player performances from deLb, Kai, and Xlele in recent appearances show capable fragging potential", "BO3 format allows for adaptation and map selection strategy that could favor Trace Esports on specific maps"], "key_context": ["VCT China 2026 Stage 1 Group Omega is early season group play with significant tournament ahead", "EDG's undefeated week 1 start may represent peak confidence and momentum", "Recent Shanghai Masters 2025 data shows EDG's current roster form but limited Trace Esports context", "BO3 format means single matchup could go either way despite overall competitive imbalance", "Last direct EDG vs Trace matchup was Jan 2025 (4-13 loss for Trace); meta and roster conditions may have evolved since"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-08T11:47:06.333985Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T17:30:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T20:14:11.204217+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "4f4456a8-57c4-41c1-bb2e-8bfe125482db", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T14:29:37.896477+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1910336", "question": "Dota 2: Team Spirit vs Nigma Galaxy (BO3) - PREMIER SERIES Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between Team Spirit and Nigma Galaxy in the PREMIER SERIES Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Spirit\" if Team Spirit win the match against Nigma Galaxy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nigma Galaxy\" if Nigma Galaxy win the match against Team Spirit.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.175, "volume_usd": 110468.15896999992, "category": "dota-2"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Team Spirit wins the BO3 match; NO if Nigma Galaxy wins. Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (scheduled ~2.5 hours from briefing timestamp), so outcome is likely already determined or in progress. MARKET SIGNAL: Current prices (YES 18%, NO 82%) reflect strong confidence in Nigma Galaxy victory. High volume ($110K+) suggests informed positioning. CASE FOR NIGMA GALAXY (Supporting NO outcome): \u2014 Recent qualifying form: Defeated Natus Vincere 2-1 (ESL One Birmingham, 4 days ago); won FISSURE Universe Episode 8 2-0 twice (1 & 3 days ago). \u2014 Radiant performance: 44.83% win rate on stronger side shows consistency in macro play. \u2014 Hero pool: Hoodwink 69.23% WR (13 picks) demonstrates a signature strength; multiple playable heroes (Dragon Knight 40% WR, Jakiro despite 18% WR shows attempt at diversity). \u2014 Tournament context: Successfully navigating ESL One Birmingham Qualifiers at competitive level. CASE FOR TEAM SPIRIT (Supporting YES outcome): \u2014 Historical data reference: DreamLeague Season 27 (~1 month ago) shows Team Spirit beat Tundra Esports 2-1; Team Liquid lost to Spirit 1-2, suggesting Spirit competitive tier. \u2014 Nigma vulnerabilities: 43.14% global win rate and 40.91% Dire win rate indicate team struggles in certain rotations or patch matchups. \u2014 Hero ban patterns suggest Spirit may have strong counter-picks against Nigma's identified stars (Timbersaw heavily banned, suggesting meta weakness). \u2014 Limited recent direct matchup data for Team Spirit vs Nigma Galaxy creates uncertainty in Spirit's case. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: \u2014 No recent (within 7 days) direct Team Spirit vs Nigma Galaxy match data provided. \u2014 Team Spirit's current win rate, hero pool performance, and recent tournament placements NOT included in briefing. \u2014 Nigma Galaxy statistics span 51 matches over longer period; Team Spirit comparative data sparse. \u2014 Current patch and meta adaptation state unclear beyond ban/pick frequencies. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: \u2014 confidence_yes = 35: Brief supporting Spirit's competitive tier exists (DreamLeague Season 27 results), but lacks current form data. Nigma's clear recent momentum and statistical advantages create structural disadvantage for Spirit case. \u2014 confidence_no = 72: Nigma Galaxy's recent match wins (2-1, 2-0, 2-0 in last 6 days), consistent Radiant-side strength, and identified hero specializations (Hoodwink) provide clear supporting data. However, lack of direct recent matchup data and unknown Team Spirit roster/form prevents reaching 85+ confidence. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: \u2014 Market price (82% NO) closely reflects observable Nigma Galaxy form and Nigma's demonstrated recent competitive wins. \u2014 Team Spirit case relies on older reference data (1 month) and inferred weaknesses in Nigma's statistics; direct evidence of Spirit's current competitive state absent. \u2014 Set probability_score at 22 (reflecting ~20-25 range for YES given strong NO-side data and NO-side market consensus) rather than higher to account for structural uncertainty in Spirit's current form. \u2014 For LIVE/IMMINENT event, if outcome is becoming clear in real-time, shares will trade toward $0.01/$0.99 before official resolution; current pricing (18% YES) may already reflect partial match progression.", "key_factor": "Briefing data lacks direct Team Spirit vs Nigma Galaxy recent match history (only DreamLeague Season 27 reference ~1 month old); current roster compositions and patch-specific form unknown.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO \u2014 Nigma Galaxy): Recent ESL One Birmingham 2026 matches (4-6 days ago) show Nigma defeated both Natus Vincere 2-1 and Team Liquid 2-1 \u2014 both elite qualifier opponents. This recency is critical in volatile BO3 playoffs where meta adaptation and form matter enormously. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: Team Spirit lost 1-2 to Nigma in their most recent documented DreamLeague Season 27 matchup (~1 month ago). This is the clearest direct evidence available and directly contradicts the YES case. FORM TRAJECTORY: Nigma Galaxy's recent qualifier results (FISSURE Universe 2-0 victories, consistent wins vs top-8 competition) show upward momentum into playoffs. Team Spirit's recent data is less comprehensive in the briefing, suggesting weaker recent validation. STATISTICAL FLOOR: Nigma's 43.14% global win rate across 51 matches provides a larger sample than some competitors. While not dominant, their 44.83% Radiant win rate (better side performance) and recent 2-1 wins over legitimate opponents suggest current-patch strength. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES \u2014 Team Spirit): The briefing provides limited recent Team Spirit match data. The only clear recent result is their 1-2 loss to Nigma Galaxy. This absence of positive recent performance, combined with documented head-to-head loss, weakens Team Spirit's case significantly. META ADAPTABILITY: Both teams show hero pool dependencies (Nigma's Hoodwink 69.23% WR is their anchor; inconsistent Jakiro 18.18% WR shows volatility). However, Nigma's recent multiple 2-1 victories across different opponents suggest better meta read than Spirit, who lost their most recent direct matchup. BO3 FORMAT RISK: In best-of-three playoffs, momentum and recent form compound quickly. Nigma's documented 2-1 victories over strong opponents within the last week provide superior confidence than Spirit's underdocumented recent results. MARKET PRICING VALIDATION: The 82% NO / 18% YES split aligns with objective data: recent head-to-head loss by Spirit, recent qualifier dominance by Nigma, and minimal contradicting evidence in the briefing. Market appears correctly priced or even slightly conservative on NO. TIMING CONSTRAINT (LIVE/IMMINENT): With ~2.5 hours to match start, reversal would require major unforeseen news (roster changes, technical issues, forfeits). Current pricing reflects pre-match fundamentals accurately. No catalysts for Spirit comeback evident in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (78) reflects strong supporting evidence (recent head-to-head, qualifier wins, form trajectory). Moderate confidence in YES (35) reflects data gap \u2014 Team Spirit's recent performance is underspecified in briefing, leaving underdog case incomplete. This gap prevents full confidence in either direction but strongly favors the documented favorite.", "key_factor": "Nigma Galaxy's recent dominant form (2-1 victories over Natus Vincere and Team Liquid in ESL One Birmingham 2026 Qualifiers) combined with Team Spirit's documented weakness in their head-to-head matchup (1-2 DreamLeague Season 27 loss) establishes NO as the clear upper bracket favorite.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: 18% for Team Spirit reflects extreme confidence in Nigma despite insufficient direct head-to-head data. The briefing provides only fragmented Spirit-Nigma matchup history (1-2 loss in DreamLeague ~1 month ago), which is stale for a BO3 meta-dependent format. NIGMA'S STAT FRAGILITY: Global 43.14% win rate across 51 matches is middling, not dominant. Dire side vulnerability at 40.91% WR is material in BO3 where side selection and adaptation matter. Jakiro's 18.18% WR despite 11 picks signals hero-meta misalignment that opponents can exploit. HERO POOL DEPENDENCY EXPOSURE: Nigma's Hoodwink dominance (69.23% WR on 13 picks) is a tell\u2014extreme reliance on one hero invites strategic bans. With 12 bans in play, Spirit can neutralize Nigma's comfort pool faster than Nigma can adapt. Recent FISSURE victories (2-0) are against unknown/tier-2 opponents, not pressure-tested elite matchups. SPIRIT'S UNDERREPORTED STRENGTH: Despite the 1-2 DreamLeague loss, Spirit qualified and appears in PREMIER SERIES Playoffs\u2014implying upperbracket seeding or strong qualifier performance not fully detailed in briefing. BO3 playoff matches reward meta flexibility and preparation, areas where upset favorites often thrive. RECENCY & CONTEXT: Briefing data is 1-6 days old; meta-critical patch updates or roster adjustments post-qualifier are possible unknowns. Playoff matches are best-of format where one series win cascades; BO3 reduces variance relative to single-game upsets. NIGMA'S RECENT OPPONENTS: Victories over Natus Vincere (2-1), Pipsqueak+4 (2-1), and FISSURE tier opponents do not constitute proof against a hungry Spirit squad. Nigma has NOT faced Spirit recently; the market may be extrapolating from old data or assuming Nigma's qualifier performance transfers directly\u2014a common bias. SIDE SELECTION ASYMMETRY: Nigma's 44.83% Radiant vs 40.91% Dire gap (4% delta) is notable. In BO3, the side that controls game flow wins. Spirit, if priced as underdog, may have studied Nigma's Dire weakness and can exploit it if they win side selection or priority in early games. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes is set lower (35) because briefing lacks detailed Spirit form metrics, recent Spirit vs elite teams, or clear Spirit meta advantages. The case for Spirit rests on negativity (Nigma's weaknesses) rather than affirmative data. confidence_no is higher (72) due to Nigma's recent qualifier wins and stable metrics, but remains capped below 85 because the direct head-to-head is stale and BO3 format is inherently volatile. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING CAVEAT: With ~2.5 hours to match start, price volatility is extreme if new lineups, bans, or pre-game intel emerge. Early betting may not reflect final team form or meta reads. This compresses certainty on both sides. MURPHY'S LAW ON NIGMA: Market is pricing Nigma as a 'lock' (82% NO = Nigma wins). Overconfidence in qualifiers often leads to sloppy preparation, underestimating opponent adjustments, and suboptimal ban sequencing in BO3. Spirit, as the 18% underdog, likely enters with zero complacency.", "key_factor": "Team Spirit's recent competitive positioning in qualifier tournaments combined with Nigma Galaxy's inconsistent hero pool execution (Jakiro 18.18% WR) and vulnerability on Dire side (40.91% WR) suggests a BO3 upset is viable if Spirit prioritizes meta-dependent bans and side selection.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: 18% YES is extremely low, suggesting market consensus views Team Spirit as heavy underdog; this aligns with typical esports playoff underdog pricing (15-25% range). RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Team Spirit vs Nigma Galaxy shows Nigma winning 2-1 in ESL One Birmingham 2026 Qualifiers just 4 days ago; this is the most recent direct comparison and favors Nigma Galaxy. WIN RATE DIFFERENTIAL: Nigma Galaxy 43.14% global win rate is lower than comparative benchmarks shown (Team Liquid 50.75%), but recent form (2-0, 2-0, 2-1 victories in last 3 matches) suggests upward trajectory. SIDE-SPECIFIC PERFORMANCE: Nigma Galaxy 44.83% Radiant vs 40.91% Dire indicates typical meta weakness on Dire, but first-pick advantage in upper bracket may mitigate; Team Spirit pick order unknown from briefing. HERO POOL ANALYSIS: Nigma Galaxy shows Hoodwink 69.23% WR (13 games) suggesting pick-dependent strength, but also Dragon Knight 40% WR indicates vulnerability to bans; Team Spirit data incomplete in briefing (references show only losses to Spirit, not Spirit's raw stats). RECENCY BIAS CORRECTION: Last 1-6 days of qualifier matches show Nigma Galaxy 4-1 in recent series (2-0 Pipsqueak, 2-0 1000 Reasons, 2-1 Natus Vincere, 2-1 Pipsqueak again, 1-2 loss to Liquid); upward momentum observable. MISSING CRITICAL DATA: Team Spirit's global win rate, hero pool, recent form outside of the single 1-2 loss notation is NOT provided in briefing; this asymmetry in data quality reduces confidence in underdog case. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 format reduces variance vs BO1, but allows meta adaptation between games; ban patterns show Timbersaw (30 bans) and Huskar (12-20 bans) as primary removals, suggesting hero-dependent meta where prepared teams hold advantage. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Upper bracket quarterfinals in PREMIER SERIES suggest both teams are established; 18% for Team Spirit implies ~4.5:1 odds, consistent with historical underdog ratios in esports majors. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CRITICAL ISSUE: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~2.5 hours); market has already priced Nigma Galaxy heavily (82% NO); any reversal requiring Team Spirit victory is now probabilistically penalized by real-time trading; shares will trend toward $0.01/$0.99 once match outcome becomes clear. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Nigma Galaxy recent performance and direct head-to-head win are strongly documented (confidence_no = 72); Team Spirit data is sparse and narrative-dependent on single loss reference (confidence_yes = 35). BASE RATE ALIGNMENT: 18% YES price aligns with historical ~20% underdog win rates in esports playoffs; no statistical anomaly detected in market pricing.", "key_factor": "Dota 2 BO3 playoff matches: lower-seeded or underdog teams win ~20-25% of the time in upper bracket quarterfinals; market prices at 18% YES align with historical underdog performance in esports playoffs.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Market is pricing Team Spirit at 18% (heavily underdog), reflecting crowd fear/consensus toward Nigma Galaxy despite limited direct evidence in briefing. Briefing data shows Nigma Galaxy's recent form: 2-1 wins vs Natus Vincere (4 days ago), 2-0 vs 1000 reasons and Pipsqueak+4 (FISSURE Episode 8, 1-3 days ago)\u2014strong momentum into playoff match. Team Spirit's most recent direct matchup vs Nigma: 1-2 loss in DreamLeague Season 27 (~1 month ago)\u2014this is the strongest concrete data point favoring NO side, supporting current market bias. Nigma Galaxy's 43.14% global win rate across 51 matches is respectable but not dominant; however, 44.83% Radiant win rate (typically stronger side) shows competence on meta side. Team Spirit's case relies on inference (competitive positioning, Nigma's hero pool inconsistency like Jakiro 18.18% WR)\u2014but briefing contains no recent Team Spirit match results to validate competitive strength claim. Critical data gap: No recent Team Spirit results provided (last concrete match data is ~1 month old DreamLeague loss). Market may be pricing fear of a known quantity (Nigma's recent form) vs uncertainty of Spirit's current state. BO3 format in playoffs does favor adaptability, but recent meta ban patterns (Timbersaw 28-30 bans, Huskar 12-20) show both teams navigating same patch\u2014no asymmetric draft advantage visible. 18% YES price reflects rational pessimism about Spirit given Spirit's documented 1-2 loss and Nigma's recent 2-0, 2-1 streak. This is NOT an irrationally panic-driven mispricing on the NO side. Confidence in NO (72) is high due to recent Nigma form and direct head-to-head loss by Spirit. Confidence in YES (35) is low due to absence of recent Spirit match data and reliance on inference. Market is likely rational here: Nigma is favored because recent data supports it. Price of 18% for Spirit feels appropriately cautious given limited recent evidence of Spirit competitiveness.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Nigma Galaxy momentum: Recent 2-0 sweep against Pipsqueak+4 and 1000 reasons (FISSURE Episode 8, 1-3 days ago) demonstrates current form and confidence heading into playoffs Meta adaptation evidence: Nigma's hero versatility (Hoodwink 69.23% WR, Dragon Knight 40% WR, Jakiro 18.18% WR) shows willingness to pivot; the Jakiro low win rate suggests experimentation rather than over-reliance on single picks Side-specific strength: Nigma's 44.83% Radiant vs 40.91% Dire split mirrors meta trends favoring Radiant; in BO3 with side selection, this matters\u2014they win more from stronger starting position Team Spirit data scarcity: Only one recent qualifier match visible (DreamLeague Season 28, 14-15 days ago, 0-2 loss to Liquid/Virtus.pro). No recent ESL Birmingham 2026 Qualifier results provided, creating asymmetric information Head-to-head context: The 4-0-6 record cited refers to Team Liquid vs Nigma, not Spirit vs Nigma. Direct Spirit-Nigma matchups in briefing show one DreamLeague Season 27 result favoring Spirit (1-2), but outdated (~1 month ago) Hero ban meta insight: Timbersaw 28-30 bans, Dragon Knight 21 bans, Huskar 12-20 bans indicate contested meta. Nigma's recent wins suggest comfort playing into these bans; Spirit's lack of recent tournament data means no recent evidence of their meta adjustment Match duration stability: Both teams average 40-41 minute games, suggesting predictable macro gameplay where team coordination and recent practice yield advantage to team with fresher tournament experience Qualifier performance: Nigma's 2-1 win vs Team Liquid (ESL One Birmingham, 6 days ago) and 2-1 vs Pipsqueak+4 (5 days ago) in same qualifier show consistent playoff-adjacent performance LIVE/IMMINENT context: With ~2.5 hours to match start, minimal new information will emerge; current price of 18% reflects significant underdog positioning that requires Spirit to have prepared strategically superior draft/execution without recent public evidence Confidence asymmetry: Strong data supporting Nigma's recent form and meta positioning (confidence_no=72); limited Spirit data creates genuine uncertainty on their current state despite historical pedigree (confidence_yes=35)", "key_factor": "Nigma Galaxy's recent form (2-0 FISSURE victories 1-3 days ago, 2-1 ESL Birmingham qualifier wins) combined with 44.83% Radiant dominance and proven meta-adaptability across hero pools contrasts sharply with Team Spirit's 1-2 DreamLeague loss and sparse recent qualifier data, making the 18% YES price a significant undervaluation only if Spirit possesses undisclosed strategic preparation.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Nigma Galaxy is demonstrably stronger: 43% global win rate, but more critically they beat Natus Vincere 2-1 in ESL One Birmingham qualifiers 4 days ago and swept FISSURE Episode 8 2-0 just 1-3 days ago. Recent form decisively favors NO. Team Spirit's documented weakness: the briefing shows Spirit lost 1-2 to Nigma in DreamLeague Season 27 (~1 month ago), a direct head-to-head loss in a competitive context. No recent Spirit victories against Nigma are cited. Hero pool vulnerability in Nigma's favor: while Hoodwink shows 69% WR (69.23%), this indicates mastery and consistency, not fragility. Nigma's multiple strong picks (Dragon Knight 40%, Jakiro situational) show adaptability, not desperation. Market pricing (18% YES / 82% NO) reflects consensus correctly: an 82-point underdog (Spirit) requiring a BO3 upset against a team with superior recent form, better qualifiers trajectory, and direct head-to-head advantage is appropriately priced as a long shot. Black swan candidate\u2014meta counter-pick innovation: The briefing conspicuously lacks ANY patch notes or meta-shift analysis. If a very recent balance change (within 48 hours) heavily countered Hoodwink or Nigma's core heroes, and Spirit prepared specifically for that, Spirit could exploit Nigma's over-reliance on proven picks. However, this requires two conditions: (1) a patch happened after the briefing data cutoff, and (2) Spirit scouts and adapts faster than Nigma in Game 1. Absence of signal: no mention of Team Spirit's recent scrim results, roster changes, or coaching adjustments. If Spirit has a new pick/ban architect or stand-in player, that could swing BO3 volatility. But the briefing provides zero evidence for such a disruption. Timing pressure cuts both ways: with ~2.5 hours to match start, both teams are locked into preparation. Last-minute roster changes or technical substitutions are extremely unlikely per resolution criteria. Confidence asymmetry justified: High confidence in NO (72) because Nigma's recent form, direct head-to-head loss by Spirit, and consistent win rates across 51+ matches provide strong grounding. Low confidence in YES (35) because the briefing offers no Spirit-specific recent strength signals\u2014Spirit appears to have lost momentum in qualifiers relative to Nigma's 2-0s and 2-1 wins. BO3 format does increase variance compared to single games, but only if both teams are evenly matched. Spirit is not; Nigma holds a demonstrated edge.", "key_factor": "Team Spirit executes a hero-pool counter-meta pivot targeting Nigma's Hoodwink dependency (69% WR hero) with a recent patch shift or first-phase ban strategy that Nigma fails to adapt to in Games 2-3 of the BO3.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.2228571428571429, "no_score": 0.7776470588235295, "edge": 0.047857142857142904, "no_edge": -0.04735294117647049, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "CAUTIOUS", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.21212121212121218, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1910336", "question": "Dota 2: Team Spirit vs Nigma Galaxy (BO3) - PREMIER SERIES Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between Team Spirit and Nigma Galaxy in the PREMIER SERIES Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Spirit\" if Team Spirit win the match against Nigma Galaxy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nigma Galaxy\" if Nigma Galaxy win the match against Team Spirit.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable 