side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Vitality.Bee executes a first-blood-focused early game strategy that exploits Skillcamp's map control weaknesses in BO1 volatility, capitalizing on the 80% first blood spike observed in similar-tier competitors."}], "median_prob": 0.62, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "8c9a3f51-e682-4476-a44c-48329bcdfeee", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T17:43:23.243837+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1912880", "question": "Dota 2: Team Liquid vs L1ga Team (BO3) - PREMIER SERIES Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket quarterfinal 3 match between Team Liquid and L1ga Team in the PREMIER SERIES Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against L1ga Team.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"L1ga Team\" if L1ga Team win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.49, "volume_usd": 192501.8339399999, "category": "dota-2"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Resolution condition is straightforward: Team Liquid must win the BO3 match. Criteria text is unambiguous with no edge cases or loopholes detected. Team Liquid competes in Tier 1 tournaments (BLAST Slam VI, DreamLeague S28) vs L1ga's Tier 2 online focus \u2014 clear competitive tier gap favors Liquid. Liquid's recent Tier 1 performance: 2-0 vs Yandex (Feb 17), 3-1 and 3-0 playoff wins in BLAST Slam VI (Feb 13-15) demonstrate consistent BO3+ capability. L1ga shows solid Tier 2 form: 2-1 vs VP (Apr 5), 2-1 vs Pips+4 (Apr 6) \u2014 respectable but lower-tier competition. Data freshness concern: L1ga's most recent matches are Apr 5-6 (2 days before match); Liquid's most recent data is Feb 15-17 (~7 weeks old). Recent form trajectory unknown for Liquid. Liquid's Feb 2026 losses (0-2 vs Yandex on Jan 31; 0-1 vs Yandex on Feb 5) indicate vulnerabilities, but these are ~2 months stale and may not reflect current form. No direct head-to-head record exists; cannot calibrate matchup-specific factors. Tier gap and Liquid's Tier 1 tournament pedigree outweigh L1ga's recent win streak in lower-tier events. BO3 format typically favors better-prepared, higher-tier teams. Confidence in YES (72%) is stronger than confidence in NO (42%) due to: strong tier advantage, multiple recent Tier 1 BO3 wins, and systematic competitive gap. Confidence asymmetry reflects data poverty on NO side (L1ga's tier-appropriate but not exceptional 2-1 records). Mechanism risk is minimal: event is TODAY, resolves within 3 hours, and criteria reference credible source (Dotabuff) with consensus fallback. No ambiguity in team name matching or resolution condition.", "key_factor": "No direct head-to-head history between teams; tier classification and recent form currency create moderate predictive uncertainty, but resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: L1ga Team is currently priced as favorite at 51% despite operating in Tier 2, indicating market respects their recent momentum \u2014 they have won 4 consecutive matches (April 5-6) including 2-0 vs VP, demonstrating BO3 capability. UNDERDOG VULNERABILITIES: Team Liquid's tier advantage is overstated by February data; their recent record shows 0-2 and 0-1 losses to Yandex (Jan-Feb 2026) indicating form deterioration, and no match data exists for Liquid after February suggesting extended absence or poor recent performance. RECENCY BIAS FAVORS NO: L1ga's April 5-6 performances are extremely fresh (within 24-48 hours of this match), while Liquid's strongest wins (BLAST Slam VI in mid-February) are 7+ weeks old \u2014 momentum in esports is critical and heavily favors the team with recent victories. HEAD-TO-HEAD VACUUM: Zero direct history between these teams means market pricing at near-coin-flip (49-51) is appropriate; tier differences cannot overcome the recency and form gap when history is absent. BO3 EXECUTION RISK: While Liquid won BO3s in BLAST Slam VI, those were against lower-tier teams; L1ga has proven BO3 capability in same tournament format (PREMIER SERIES) with recent 2-1 wins, suggesting format familiarity. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (62%) due to clear recency advantage, concrete recent wins, and Liquid's documented recent losses; lower confidence in YES (45%) because Liquid's tier advantage is real but contradicted by stale form data and unexplained absence from recent competition. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Liquid's 2+ month information gap suggests either they played in untracked events or were inactive \u2014 either way, this absence undermines claims of tier superiority when facing a team demonstrating current form.", "key_factor": "L1ga Team's recent hot form with consecutive 2-0 and 2-1 victories in PREMIER SERIES matches (April 5-6) against established opponents, combined with Team Liquid's documented losses to Yandex in early 2026.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "UNDERDOG'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: L1ga shows immediate recent form (April 5-6, 2026) with consecutive 2-1 and 2-0 victories in the exact PREMIER SERIES tournament where this playoff match occurs. Team Liquid's most recent data is 2+ months old (February), creating a massive recency gap. FORM TRAJECTORY REVERSAL: Team Liquid lost 0-2 and 0-1 to Yandex in January-February 2026, suggesting downward trajectory heading into April. L1ga's recent wins (VP 2-1, Pips+4 2-0) show upward momentum and tournament-specific adaptation. TOURNAMENT-SPECIFIC ADVANTAGE: L1ga has been grinding PREMIER SERIES Tier 2 online matches continuously through April. They understand the meta, opponent pools, and format of THIS specific tournament. Liquid is parachuting in from a 2-month absence\u2014rustiness is underpriced. TIER ILLUSION: While Tier 1 vs Tier 2 typically favors Liquid, the briefing shows Liquid competing in ESL/BLAST/FISSURE events in early 2026, with mixed results (including 0-2 playoff exits). Tier alone doesn't guarantee form or readiness. BO3 CONSISTENCY CAVEAT: Liquid's BLAST Slam VI wins (3-1, 3-0, 3-2) are from February 13-15. These are 7+ weeks old. Recent BO3 performance in the PREMIER SERIES format is unknown for Liquid, while L1ga has demonstrated BO3 competence (2-1, 2-0 strings in April). DATA STALENESS UNDERMINES YES CASE: The briefing explicitly states Liquid data is from February 2026 while L1ga data is April 5-6. In esports, a 2-month gap is an eternity. Current patch, meta evolution, roster changes, and form are unknown for Liquid but evident for L1ga. MARKET OVERWEIGHTING TIER: The 51% NO price assumes Tier 1 tournament experience guarantees victory, but Liquid's recent record against Yandex (0-2, 0-1) contradicts dominance. L1ga's consistent 2-0/2-1 wins are more actionable recent evidence. NO DIRECT PRECEDENT: Zero head-to-head history means no comfort level for Liquid, no predictable matchups. This favors the team in form (L1ga) over the team with historical credentials but unclear current state (Liquid). PLAYOFF JITTERS: Liquid's last recorded playoff appearance was FISSURE Universe 4 (March 2025, note: 2025 not 2026), where they lost 1-2 to GG and 0-2 to PSV. L1ga just beat multiple teams in PREMIER SERIES qualifiers, showing comfort in high-stakes online matches. MURPHY'S LAW ON LIQUID: Overconfidence in tier status + 2-month absence + recent Yandex losses = fragile favorite. Market may be anchoring on name recognition rather than April 2026 form. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES because L1ga's recent April data is clear and positive. Lower confidence in NO because Liquid's 2-month data vacuum creates uncertainty\u2014they could be much worse or recovered. The underdog side has stronger evidence.", "key_factor": "L1ga Team's recency and momentum in PREMIER SERIES format (April 5-6 wins) versus Team Liquid's stale data (February 2026) and recent 0-2 losses to Yandex create form uncertainty that the market underprices.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "TIER CLASSIFICATION SIGNAL: Team Liquid competes in Tier 1 tournaments (BLAST Slam VI, DreamLeague S28, ESL One Raleigh) while L1ga operates primarily in Tier 2 online PREMIER SERIES events. Historical base rate favors higher-tier teams by ~65-70% in BO3 playoffs. LIQUID RECENT FORM: Demonstrated strong BO3+ capability with 3-1, 3-0, 3-2 victories in BLAST Slam VI playoffs (Feb 13-15, 2026). Defeated Yandex 2-0 in DreamLeague S28 (Feb 17, 2026). Consistent playoff performance against named opponents. L1GA RECENT FORM: Shows solid 2-0 and 2-1 results in PREMIER SERIES Tier 2 matches (April 5-6, 2026). Recent form is current (within 48 hours of match), while Liquid's most recent Tier 1 data is ~2 months old. Recency slightly favors L1ga narrative but does not override tier gap. LIQUID VULNERABILITIES: Losses to Yandex (0-2 in Jan 2026, 0-1 in Feb 2026) indicate recent struggles vs specific opponents. However, these occurred at Tier 1 level; performance vs Tier 2 opponent typically differs. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Absence of direct match history prevents calibration of team-specific dynamics. Increases baseline variance; tier-gap assumption becomes primary anchor. MATCH FORMAT CONSIDERATION: BO3 structure rewards consistency and meta mastery\u2014dimensions where Tier 1 experience typically provides edge. L1ga's consistent Tier 2 wins do not necessarily translate to Tier 1 BO3 capability. MARKET PRICING: YES at 49%, NO at 51%. Pricing reflects near-parity, slight lean to L1ga. This contradicts historical tier-based baseline (65%+ for Tier 1 over Tier 2). Suggests either: (a) market prices L1ga's recent form heavily, (b) perceives Liquid's Feb losses as structural, or (c) underweights tier classification. TIMING & CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Event is TODAY with ~3 hours to resolution. At this stage, live team news (absences, technical issues, morale) could shift odds sharply. However, briefing contains no such signals. Confidence in YES slightly exceeds confidence in NO because tier data is robust; confidence in NO is moderate because recent form recency and absence of historical L1ga Tier 1 performance are not fully offset by current pricing. BASE RATE CONCLUSION: Tier 1 vs Tier 2 BO3 favors Liquid ~68%. Market's slight NO tilt does not override structural tier advantage, though L1ga's current form and Liquid's recent losses warrant respect. Probability of 68 reflects tier baseline with modest downward adjustment for L1ga momentum and Liquid's Feb losses. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=72 because tier classification and BO3 capability gap are well-established in Dota 2 history. confidence_no=58 because L1ga's Tier 2-only track record and lack of Tier 1 playoff experience create data sparsity on their ceiling vs Liquid; recent wins are encouraging but not historically predictive at this tier jump.", "key_factor": "In Dota 2, Tier 1 teams defeat Tier 2 teams in playoff BO3 matchups approximately 65-75% of the time; however, tier classification alone explains only ~60% of outcome variance. Upset rates in online qualifiers/playoffs can reach 25-35% when seeding is tight.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market is near coin-flip (49-51) despite clear competitive tier gap\u2014Liquid plays Tier 1 tournaments, L1ga plays Tier 2 online events. This suggests market is pricing in uncertainty appropriately rather than overweighting pedigree. Liquid's recent Tier 1 performance (BLAST Slam VI playoffs: 3-1, 3-0, 2-0 wins; DreamLeague 2-0 vs Yandex) indicates elite BO3+ capability, supporting YES case. L1ga's form is FRESHER (April 5-6 matches vs Liquid's February data). Recent 2-1, 2-0 victories in PREMIER SERIES show current momentum and adaptation to format. Liquid's January-February losses to Yandex (0-2, 0-1) suggest recent vulnerability or meta shifts that may not have been corrected\u2014this is underweighted by market at 49%. No head-to-head history means market cannot rely on direct precedent; tier gap alone is insufficient predictor when formats differ (Tier 1 LAN vs Tier 2 online). TIMING CRITICAL: Match is TODAY, ~3 hours to resolution. Market is not panicking or showing late-hour reversal pressure; pricing suggests genuine uncertainty. Apathy risk: Market may be rationally ignoring form recency. L1ga's April matches are 2 months fresher than Liquid's best data; Liquid may be underperforming current rosters. Volume is substantial ($192k) but price hasn't moved to extremes\u2014suggests balanced order flow, no crowd exuberance on either side. Confidence_no is lower (45) because L1ga's Tier 2 status and lack of Tier 1 tournament evidence limits conviction in NO case, even with fresh form data. Confidence_yes is moderate (72) because tier gap is real but not decisive given format uncertainty and Liquid's recent losses.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "\u2022 TIER GAP IS DECISIVE: Team Liquid competes in Tier 1 tournaments (ESL One, BLAST Slam VI, DreamLeague S28) against top-tier EU/CIS teams; L1ga operates in Tier 2 online qualifiers\u2014this is not marginal; Tier 1 teams face 3-5x stronger opposition weekly, dramatically improving coaching, meta knowledge, and clutch execution \u2022 BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES SKILL DIFFERENTIAL: Best-of-three matches punish adaptability gaps; a Tier 1 team's deeper understanding of hero prioritization, itemization windows, and late-game position trading compounds across games\u2014L1ga cannot hide weak lanes or predictable playmaking for three consecutive games \u2022 LIQUID'S RECENT TIER 1 RESULTS: 3-0, 3-1, 3-2 victories in BLAST Slam VI Playoffs (Feb 13-15) and 2-0 vs Yandex (Feb 17) in DreamLeague; these are games vs credible opponents, not tier 2 padding\u2014demonstrates BO3+ execution under pressure \u2022 L1GA'S FORM IS MISLEADING: 2-0 and 2-1 wins (Apr 5-6) are vs tier 2 online opponents (VP stackers, Pips+4); victories against weaker competition inflate perceived form; qualifier/play-in victories do not translate predictively to playoff BO3s vs tier 1 competition \u2022 RECENCY CUTOFF CAVEAT: Liquid's most recent Tier 1 data is Feb 2026 (8 weeks prior); L1ga's data is Apr 5-6 (2-3 days prior); this 6-week gap is significant, but Liquid's Tier 1 pedigree and structural advantages outweigh L1ga's fresher qualifier wins\u2014meta evolution in Dota 2 favors teams with deeper resource pools and coaching \u2022 LOSSES TO YANDEX (0-2, 0-1 Jan-Feb) WARRANT CAUTION: Liquid lost to Yandex, suggesting Yandex has tactical reads; however, Yandex is also Tier 1 elite; losses to top-tier teams are not predictive of performance vs tier 2 opponents\u2014regression is unlikely \u2022 NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Complete absence of prior matchup history prevents tactical pattern recognition; this increases variance slightly but does not override the structural tier advantage\u2014blind matchups still favor the stronger team system \u2022 EUROPEAN ONLINE FORMAT: PREMIER SERIES Playoffs is European online circuit; both teams are presumably EU-based (CEST timing); no location/ping disadvantage for either side \u2022 UPSIDE SCENARIO FOR L1GA (30% confidence_no): If L1ga has recently upgraded roster or coaching, and Liquid's Feb form has degraded due to meta shifts or personnel changes, L1ga's recent tournament wins could signal emerging competence\u2014but this requires evidence not present in briefing \u2022 MISSING COUNTER-INTELLIGENCE: Confidence_no capped at 52 due to: (1) no scouting reports on L1ga's draft preparation, (2) no data on Liquid's April 2026 scrim performance or team stability, (3) unknown roster changes post-Feb, (4) potential meta shifts that could favor L1ga's archetype", "key_factor": "Tier classification in Dota 2 represents tournament prestige and opponent caliber; Liquid's Tier 1 tournament experience against elite teams (Yandex, Natus Vincere) provides significantly deeper metagame understanding and adaptation capacity than L1ga's Tier 2 online qualifier experience, which is the strongest structural predictor in BO3 formats where map preparation and team-level adaptability compound across three games.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Team Liquid operates in Tier 1 tournaments with recent wins vs Yandex (Feb 2026) and BLAST Slam VI playoff dominance, establishing clear competitive tier advantage over L1ga's Tier 2 online presence. L1ga Team's form is DRASTICALLY MORE CURRENT: 3 consecutive BO3 victories within 48 hours (April 5-6, 2026) vs Liquid's last available match in February 2026\u2014a 5-week staleness gap that obscures Liquid's true current state. Liquid's 0-2 and 0-1 losses to Yandex (Jan-Feb 2026) are the only recent HEAD-TO-HEAD data available; these vulnerabilities have never been publicly retested against anyone else, creating hidden weakness exposure. L1ga's April 6-8 online PREMIER SERIES run mirrors the exact tournament and timing of today's match\u2014they are literally warmed-up in the same format/servers/region, whereas Liquid's last PREMIER SERIES appearance is undocumented. NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: Zero past matches between these teams means meta-counter draft development by L1ga coaches against Liquid's known tendencies is entirely feasible and undetected. The briefing is conspicuously silent on: Liquid's recent practice results, lineup changes, or coach/support staff updates since February; L1ga's ceiling in a Tier 1 playoff bracket; patch-specific hero pool shifts favoring one team's playstyle. Market is priced 49-51 (virtual coin flip), reflecting genuine uncertainty\u2014the tier gap alone does not guarantee 70%+ Liquid odds when form recency and direct matchup data are this asymmetric. BLACK SWAN: L1ga fields a sub or makes a surprise lineup change, OR Liquid's roster/preparation is disrupted by a brief 48-hour illness/burnout from the 5-week gap between tournaments. If Liquid loses, it will not be due to incompetence but rather RECENCY BIAS in the briefing: we are relying on 5-week-old data while L1ga has 48-hour-fresh BO3 performance under identical conditions.", "key_factor": "L1ga Team exploits a recent meta shift or pocket strategy optimized against Liquid's standard draft patterns, leveraging their tight recent form (3 consecutive BO3 wins in April 2026) against Liquid's stale February-era tournament data.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6541818181818182, "no_score": 0.37303621169916434, "edge": 0.1641818181818182, "no_edge": -0.13696378830083566, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 65% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 71% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1912880", "question": "Dota 2: Team Liquid vs L1ga Team (BO3) - PREMIER SERIES Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket quarterfinal 3 match between Team Liquid and L1ga Team in the PREMIER SERIES Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against L1ga Team.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"L1ga Team\" if L1ga Team win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nI