alysis quality. The probability_score of 22 is a modest lean toward underdog YES, reflecting the market's extreme overconfidence as a vulnerability, not a strong conviction.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of reliable performance data creates information asymmetry where 84% NO confidence is unjustifiably extreme given the briefing provides zero team-specific analysis for either side.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.16, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero relevant information about Pcific Esports, GIANTX, their recent performance, roster status, head-to-head history, or VCT EMEA Group Omega standings. Search results returned unrelated college basketball and sports content (Tulsa/Auburn, Oklahoma/West Virginia) with no esports context. Market Price Signal: YES priced at 16% / NO at 84% suggests strong market consensus favoring GIANTX, but without underlying team data, cannot validate whether this reflects true competitive disparity or simply market assumption. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK: Event resolves TODAY in ~3 hours. Match is likely in-progress or imminent; reversal from current 16%\u219284% split would require major upset with minimal time for fundamental shift in available information. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Both sides lack evidentiary foundation. Market pricing exists (suggesting some participants have data), but briefing provides none. Cannot confidently assess either team's strength, recent form, or contextual tournament position. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three reduces upset likelihood vs. single-map elimination, but without team capability data, cannot quantify this effect. RESOLUTION PATH: Match resolves via VLR.gg within 2 hours post-conclusion; no ambiguity expected if match completes normally. BASE RATE PROXY: In professional esports, lower-seeded/underdog teams win Best-of-