 of Eternal Fire performance data and single-match sample size create substantial asymmetric information favoring the market price of 66% over deeper conviction.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "BBL's stat profile shows elite fraggers (Ros\u00e9 1.27 R, Loita 1.11 R) but critical vulnerability: support players generate minimal impact (Ros\u00e9 on Sova 0.96 R, Boo-equivalent role). Eternal Fire could weaponize slow defaults and post-plant control to suffocate BBL's aggressive playmaking. Briefing provides zero competitive intelligence on Eternal Fire's current form, roster, or recent results. This asymmetry strongly favors an underdog narrative\u2014market consensus at 66% YES suggests over-confidence in BBL based solely on their own positive stats, not head-to-head matchup analysis. BBL's KAST percentages (70\u201383%) indicate participation but mask round-win consistency: lovers rock swings 0.82\u20131.18 rating (36% variance), suggesting fragile clutch execution when fundamentals are tested. Eternal Fire may exploit late-round vulnerability. Single-map performance data (VIT vs GX economy stats) shows team-level inconsistency in 12\u201313 round segments; BBL's depth doesn't guarantee BO3 resilience if Eternal Fire targets map 2 or 3 with meta-read precision. Tournament timing (TODAY, ~6 hours to match) means no recent patch notes, roster changes, or scout updates visible in briefing. Last-minute stand-in, illness, or tactical preparation shift could flip a 66\u201334 market edge. Consensus view overlooks Eternal Fire's silence: either they are a true underdog with underreported strengths (roster synergy, IGL read, or anti-meta prep), or briefing data collection favored BBL coverage. Either scenario signals contrarian edge at NO. BBL's map-flip performance (Omen Loita 1.64 R vs 0.57 R) indic