team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.305, "volume_usd": 4.901959, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Resolution condition: InControl must win the BO3 match scheduled for April 8, 2026 at 9:00 PM ET (TODAY event, ~7 hours away). Market pricing (30% YES / 70% NO) suggests strong consensus favoring regain, aligned with available performance data. InControl advantage: Higher HLTV world ranking (#159) is the primary quantitative edge cited; suggests stronger peer-competitive standing. regain strengths: Recent ESL Challenger League run shows 4-0 record in tournament (beats FlyQuest RED 2-0, TSG 2-0, Zomblers 2-1, Akimbo 2-1); demonstrates momentum and consistency in exact tournament series. InControl's cited tournament record is mixed (0-2 loss at ESEA Season 56 finals on 2026-03-29; 2-3 loss at ESEA Season 55 on 2025-12-15), with no recent championship runs in comparable timeframe. regain roster stability: Consistent roster (dvrk, fuzenko, sasha, Zucar) with 7+ months tenure and strong individual ratings (fuzenko 1.18, Zucar 1.18, dvrk 1.04 Rating 3.0) indicates cohesion. Critical data gap: No direct head-to-head match history provided; no detailed InControl roster performance metrics or recent map statistics beyond one 13-7 Inferno win cited. Tournament context: Both teams in lower bracket final of same ESL Challenger League event; regain's path shows dominating record (2-0, 2-0, 2-1 victories) vs InControl's sparse recent data. World ranking (#159 for InControl) provides modest advantage but insufficient to overcome regain's demonstrated tournament momentum and consistency in THIS specific event. Confidence asymmetry: confidence_yes (35) reflects limited InControl performance data to justify the ranking advantage; confidence_no (42) reflects uncertainty about InControl's actual map-level capabilities and potential LAN-style day performance, but regain's tournament trajectory is clearer. Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (TODAY); no time for reversals; outcome will reflect actual team execution in next 7 hours. Criteria are clear and unambiguous regarding resolution; no ambiguity in team identification (InControl vs regain names are unambiguous).", "key_factor": "Insufficient comparative performance data between InControl and regain; world ranking differential (#159 vs unknown) is the only quantitative advantage, but regain has shown consistent recent tournament success in the same circuit.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "REGAIN'S MOMENTUM (favored side strength): regain has won 4 consecutive matches in the ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup #3 tournament (2-0 vs FlyQuest RED on 04/03, 2-0 vs TSG on 04/04, 2-1 vs Zomblers on 04/06, 0-2 loss on 04/08 then 2-1 vs Akimbo on 04/07 in parallel tournament), demonstrating sustained form in the specific event structure. This tournament-specific preparation and winning streak is a stronger predictor of BO3 playoff performance than static world rankings. INCONTROL'S WORLD RANKING ALONE IS INSUFFICIENT: InControl's #159 world ranking appears to reflect past accomplishments, but the briefing shows limited recent tournament results for InControl\u2014only scattered activity in 2025 with mostly losses (0-2, 0-2, 0-2 patterns in ESEA and CCT events). World ranking without recent results is a lagging indicator, especially in the fast-moving Challenger League circuit. REGAIN'S INTERNATIONAL DEPTH: regain's roster includes fuzenko (Ukraine, 7 months tenure, 1.18 rating in recent maps) and three solid US players (dvrk 1.04 rating, sasha 0.93 rating, Zucar 1.18 rating) with consistent 7-month team stability. This international experience in a developmental league suggests meta-game familiarity and cohesion that raw ranking does not capture. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT FAVORS REGAIN: This is a lower bracket final in an active tournament where regain has already proven it can execute. InControl's single recent map result cited (13-7 on Inferno vs F5) lacks context\u2014F5 is described as 'potentially beatable opposition' in the briefing's own analysis, and one map win is insufficient to counter four consecutive tournament wins by regain. DATA GAP ON INCONTROL: The briefing explicitly notes 'Limited comprehensive statistics available for regain compared to InControl' yet provides minimal substantive recent activity for InControl itself. The five-player roster (KmZ, C0C0, twigs, BAGEL, no1nx) has no recent tournament results, head-to-head records, or map statistics presented. This asymmetry actually favors regain because regain has demonstrated form; InControl's silence suggests either recent inactivity or poor results not highlighted. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams lost their upper bracket matches to reach this lower bracket final. regain's loss to BOSS (0-2 on 04/03 in PGL qualifier) is offset by four wins in the ESL event itself, showing resilience. InControl's path to this match is not detailed, creating uncertainty about how they arrived here relative to regain's documented climb. HEAD-TO-HEAD ABSENT: No direct comparative data exists between these teams. Market pricing NO at 70% reflects uncertainty weighted toward the team with clearer recent tournament success, which is regain. InControl's higher ranking is historical; regain's wins are current. CONFIDENCE IN NO IS MODERATELY HIGH (72): regain's four consecutive tournament wins in the exact event/format is the strongest available signal. However, confidence is not higher because world rankings do carry some predictive weight, InControl could have undisclosed preparation, and BO3 results depend on map pool matchups and in-match execution not visible in this briefing. CONFIDENCE IN YES IS LOW (35): InControl's case rests primarily on a world ranking with minimal supporting recent data and one map result against unranked opposition. The 30% price reflects fair skepticism; backing InControl requires belief that past ranking (likely 2024-2025 era) outweighs regain's documented April 2026 tournament momentum\u2014a risky assumption given the Challenger League's developmental volatility and rapid roster changes.", "key_factor": "regain's recent tournament momentum (4 consecutive wins in ESL Cup #3 leading into this lower bracket final) combined with InControl's lack of comparable recent success data creates a structural advantage for the NO side despite InControl's higher world ranking.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RANKING ADVANTAGE FOR YES: InControl's #159 world ranking provides a quantifiable edge. Higher-ranked teams in Challenger League typically win 55-65% of BO3 matches against lower-ranked or unranked opponents. REGAIN DATA DEFICIT: Briefing contains extensive regain match history (multiple 2:0 wins, 2:1 results in April 2026) but no explicit HLTV world ranking for regain. This asymmetry in available data creates uncertainty on both sides. RECENT FORM MIXED: InControl's 13-7 Inferno win vs F5 (2026-04-07) shows competence but against lower-tier opposition. regain's recent results (2:0 vs TSG, 2:0 vs FlyQuest RED on 2026-04-03-04) suggest solid recent form in tournament play. ROSTER STABILITY: InControl has maintained a 5-player roster (KmZ, C0C0, twigs, BAGEL, no1nx) with international depth (Lebanon, Canada). regain's roster (Zucar, dvrk, sasha, fuzenko) also shows international player (Ukraine), suggesting comparable structural stability. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 in C-Tier online events show higher upset rates (35-45%) than larger tournaments due to map pool variance, lag sensitivity, and lower stakes consistency. The 30% YES market price may undervalue the ranking advantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence supports InControl's ranking advantage (confidence_yes = 42), but insufficient regain ranking data limits ability to quantify the NO side (confidence_no = 38). Neither team has comprehensive head-to-head records in briefing. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CHECK: Event is TODAY (~7 hours to match). Market prices ($0.30 YES / $0.70 NO) show 70% backing regain. This suggests market may be pricing in regain's recent tournament success over InControl's ranking alone, or reflecting unknown regain strength not captured in briefing. BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: Challenger League BO3 upsets occur ~38-42% of the time. InControl's ranking advantage suggests ~60% win probability in isolation, but regain's recent win streak (4 consecutive 2:0 or 2:1 results in April) introduces uncertainty. Averaging to 38-40% for YES reflects narrowed edge due to form variance.", "key_factor": "In BO3 matchups between similarly-ranked Challenger League teams (C-Tier online events), the higher-ranked team wins approximately 55-65% of the time; however, upsets occur in 35-45% of cases due to map pool matchups, roster volatility, and day-to-day form variance in developmental circuits.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Market pricing InControl at 30% (underdog) despite higher world ranking (#159 vs unknown for regain) suggests crowd underweights ranking differential. Brief Case for YES relies heavily on world ranking advantage, but regain has demonstrated consistent recent tournament wins (multiple 2-0/2-1 results in April 2026). regain's recent match history shows active momentum: 2-0 vs FlyQuest RED (03/04), 2-1 vs Zomblers (06/04), 2-1 vs Akimbo (07/04) \u2014 strong form entering playoffs. InControl's most recent data point is a single map result (Inferno 13-7 vs F5 on 04/05), insufficient to establish current form; no full match results in briefing. Critical asymmetry: regain has comprehensive recent tournament results; InControl lacks comparable recent BO3 data in briefing. Market may be anchoring to static ranking rather than recent momentum. Both teams compete in C-Tier online circuit with high variance; world ranking alone is weak predictor in this volatile developmental tier. Low market volume ($5 USD) and tight odds (30/70) suggest minimal sharp action; crowd sentiment appears neutral-to-lazy rather than informed. Confidence in YES held back because regain's win streak and tournament participation are more densely documented than InControl's recent form. Confidence in NO held back because InControl's ranking advantage is legitimate, but insufficient recent data to quantify competitive gap. Event is TODAY (7 hours to resolution); no time for significant momentum reversals; market price likely reflects pre-match sentiment rather than in-play information.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "InControl holds HLTV world ranking #159 (objective, verifiable advantage), while regain's ranking is unavailable in briefing\u2014this asymmetry favors InControl analytically but does not guarantee playoff performance. Regain's recent match record shows 5 consecutive wins (2:1, 2:0, 2:0, 2:0 across multiple tournaments Apr 1-7), indicating strong current form and momentum entering this Lower Bracket Final; InControl's recent form less clearly documented. Both teams operate in C-Tier online Challenger League\u2014the developmental tier is known for high volatility, roster instability, and upset frequency; ranking gaps are less predictive than in established pro circuits. BO3 format introduces significant variance: single-map upsets are common, and map-veto advantage (unknown from briefing) can swing series; raw ranking alone does not determine BO3 outcomes. Regain roster includes fuzenko (Ukraine, Rating 1.18) and Zucar (Rating 1.18)\u2014both above-average performers by stats; InControl individual player stats unavailable for direct comparison. Event timing: match occurs TODAY with resolution ~7 hours away; no late-breaking roster changes, health issues, or technical failures are documented that would invalidate the matchup. InControl's recent Inferno result (13-7 vs F5) shows competitive play but does not establish superiority over regain\u2014opponent strength unclear. Briefing lacks: (1) regain's world ranking, (2) head-to-head history, (3) map-pool strengths for either team, (4) recent InControl playoff performance trajectory. This asymmetric data gap limits confidence in both directions. Market price (30% YES, 70% NO) suggests analytical consensus favors regain; this aligns with regain's recent win streak but may overweight recent form vs. structural ranking advantage. Lower Bracket Final context: regain entered with wins vs TSG, FlyQuest RED, Zomblers (Apr 3-6), suggesting regain earned this matchup; InControl's bracket path less documented.", "key_factor": "In Challenger League BO3 formats, map-veto dynamics and team-specific map pools matter more than raw ranking; InControl's #159 HLTV ranking is meaningful but incomplete without regain's ranking and recent head-to-head or mirror-match performance data.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "regain has logged a remarkable recent run: 2-0 vs FlyQuest RED (Apr 3), 2-0 vs TSG (Apr 4), 2-1 vs Zomblers (Apr 6), and 2-1 vs Akimbo (Apr 7), indicating a sharp upward trajectory into the playoffs. InControl's #159 world ranking is a historical data point with unknown recency; if it predates the last 2-4 weeks, it may not reflect roster changes, player form decay, or recent losses in this exact tournament structure. The briefing shows InControl as favorites (30% YES price = 70% NO price), yet provides minimal regain comparative data\u2014only roster names and partial stats. This information asymmetry is a classic market inefficiency favoring the underdog. regain's roster includes fuzenko (Ukraine, 1.18 Rating 3.0), Zucar (1.18 Rating 3.0), and dvrk (1.04 Rating 3.0) with 7 months stability\u2014competitive depth that contradicts a weak underdog narrative. Lower-bracket finals under high-intensity playoff pressure can favor momentum teams over seeded favorites, particularly in C-Tier ESL events where roster consistency is volatile. InControl's last visible ESL result is a 2-0 win vs F5 (Apr 5), but no subsequent playoff match data is provided; regain has visibly competed in parallel tournaments 2 days before this match, suggesting fresher gameplay rhythm. A BO3 format requires 2-map consistency; if InControl struggles on regain's comfort maps or if a key InControl player (KmZ, C0C0, twigs) underperforms, regain's balanced roster could exploit map-specific weaknesses. The market is pricing InControl at 30% (YES) based on ranking alone; regain's recent win streak and lack of visible weaknesses in the briefing suggest market overconfidence in the seeded favorite.", "key_factor": "regain's recent 7-game win streak (4-2 in ESL Cup #3 + dominant 2-1 performance in parallel Dust2.us series) combined with momentum-driven playoff performance could upset InControl's higher seed, especially if InControl's #159 ranking reflects older roster data and lacks recent LAN verification.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.3484251968503937, "no_score": 0.6714814814814816, "edge": 0.0434251968503937, "no_edge": -0.023518518518518494, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 54% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918242", "question": "Counter-Strike: InControl vs regain (BO3) - ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket final match between InControl and regain in the ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"InControl\" if InControl win the match against regain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against InControl.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlyin