ongshim RedForce NS | 4 | 3 | 1 | 75.00% | | 4 | DRXDRX KRX | 4 | 1 | 3 | 25.00% | | 5 | SOOPers DNS | 4 | 0 | 4 | 0.00% |  | Played With |  | Champion | \u2211 | W | L | WR | | 1 | Ryze Ryze | 7 | 5 | 2 | 71.43% | | 2 | Azir Azir | 7 | 3 | 4 | 42.86% | | 3 | Gwen Gwen | 6 | 4 | 2 | 66.67% | | 4 | Sivir Sivir | 5 | 3 | 2 | 60.00% | | 5 | K'Sante K'Sante | 4 | 3 | 1 | 75.00% |  | Played Against |  | Champion | \u2211 | W | L | WR | | 1 | Xin Zhao Xin Zhao | 9 | 5 | 4 | 55.56% | | 2 |", "LCK 2026 - Week 1-Week 1\n\nGEN\n\nBFX\n\nApr 8 - 19:00 KST\n\nLCK 2026 - Week 2-Week 2\n\nGEN\n\nT1\n\nApr 11 - 19:00 KST\n\nLCK 2026 - Week 2-Week 2\n\nGEN\n\nDK\n\nApr 16 - 17:00 KST\n\nLCK 2026 - Week 3-Week 3\n\nGEN\n\nBRO\n\n## Contents [...] Region:\n\nSouth Korea Korea\n\nCoach:\n\nSouth Korea Lyn South Korea Nova \"Nova (Park Chan-ho)\") South Korea Ryu\n\nManager:\n\nSouth Korea FIFAHUN\n\nApprox."], "news_summary": "DN SOOPers Challengers and BNK FearX Youth are both among the lowest-performing teams in LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, each with 29% win rates (2-5 records) and negative game differential metrics. Head-to-head history shows these teams have played multiple times across LCK Cup 2026, with results varying by match format and iteration. Both teams struggle with consistency and are competing at the challenger level in Korean esports.", "side_yes_case": ["DN SOOPers has slightly better game differential (-134 vs -192) suggesting marginally stronger macro execution", "DN SOOPers has won multiple head-to-head matchups in LCK Cup 2026 Week 3 (3-1 series win, individual game wins)", "DN SOOPers shows better game duration management (32:13 avg) compared to BNK FearX (29:12 avg)"], "side_no_case": ["BNK FearX won 3-2 in LCK Cup 2026 Playoffs Round 1 matchup against DN SOOPers, demonstrating playoff-level performance", "Both teams have identical 29% win rates with no clear statistical advantage for either side in current standings", "BNK FearX shows more competitive wins against stronger opponents (gen.G, T1, Brion) in recent LCK Cup matches"], "key_context": ["Head-to-head record shows mixed results: DN SOOPers won Week 3 series 3-1, BNK FearX won Playoffs R1 3-2, indicating context-dependent performance", "Both teams rank bottom-3 in LCK Challengers League with 29% win rates, making this a match between the league's weakest performers", "LCK Cup 2026 and Challengers League appear to be different tournament formats with different competitive dynamics", "Match is Best-of-3 format in Rounds 1-2 of Challengers League, suggesting early-stage competition", "Recent form trajectory shows both teams struggling consistently throughout the competition period"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T01:53:52.084271Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-09T11:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-09T10:30:54.513128+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "f32748df-5029-4a4b-b158-eeb139f8479d", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T01:55:31.632265+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1908377", "question": "Counter-Strike: MANA eSports vs FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between MANA eSports and FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C, initially scheduled for April 9 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MANA eSports\" if MANA eSports win the match against FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports\" if FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports win the match against MANA eSports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.79, "volume_usd": 144.86764599999998, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MANA's recent record shows mixed but competitive form: 3 wins (2-1, 2-0, 2-0, 2-1) in ECL and CCT Play-In Group C matches (March 25-30) demonstrate ability to win BO3s at B-tier level. Counter-evidence: MANA lost 0-2 to RUSTEC (March 28, CCT EU Play-In Play-In Stage) and 0-2 in NODWIN Clutch Series #6 Playoffs (March 31), showing vulnerability under qualifier pressure and playoff conditions. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports: No recent match history, roster details, or competitive context provided in briefing. Impossible to assess their current strength, recent form, or head-to-head tendencies. Market price of 79% YES suggests strong confidence in MANA, but this may reflect information asymmetry (MANA is searchable; Famalic\u00e3o is not) rather than proven superiority. MANA roster acquired KS- players (ammar, Caleyy, gejmzilla, BledarD, cerber) as of June 2026, but match history provided is from March-April 2026, before this acquisition. Roster composition for April 9 match is unclear from briefing. Event timing: Match is TODAY (~12 hours away). No cancellation, delay, or forfeit signals present in briefing. Match will likely occur as scheduled. Resolution criteria are clear: YES if MANA wins BO3, NO if Famalic\u00e3o wins BO3. No ambiguity in condition. HLTV will be primary source. MANA's recent 2-1, 2-0, 2-0 sequence (late March/early April) suggests current form favoring YES, but small sample size and absence of Famalic\u00e3o data create material uncertainty on NO side. No evidence of roster instability, withdrawal, or disqualification risk for either team as of briefing cutoff (April 9 01:54 UTC).", "key_factor": "Severe asymmetry in available competitive data: MANA has documented recent form, but FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports has virtually no searchable match history or roster information in briefing, making comparative strength assessment unreliable.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MANA secured 2-0 victories in CCT EU Play-In Group C on March 26-27, demonstrating group-stage competence in qualifier-level competition at the exact tournament type this match belongs to. MANA won a BO3 format match on March 25 (2-1 vs. unnamed opponent) in NODWIN Clutch Series #6 Round 5, directly proving capability in the same best-of-three format required today. Recent ECL Season 51 form shows three BO3 victories (2-1, 2-0, 2-1) across March 30\u2013April 4, indicating sustained competitive rhythm in online team play leading into this match. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports appears in briefing document as an opponent but has zero match history, roster details, or recent performance metrics provided\u2014this absence of data is a structural weakness for the underdog narrative. MANA's two recent losses (0-2 to RUSTEC on March 28, 0-2 in NODWIN Playoffs on March 31) occurred 8\u201310 days ago; the team has since recorded three BO3 wins in ECL, suggesting recovery or roster stabilization by April 9. The briefing explicitly states MANA acquired a new KS- roster (ammar, Caleyy, gejmzilla, BledarD, cerber) in June 2026\u2014timeline inconsistency suggests these matches (March\u2013April) may involve prior roster composition, but MANA still competed and won multiple series. 79% market pricing reflects substantial confidence in MANA; NO side priced at 21% suggests market participants lack confidence in FC Famalic\u00e3o's competitive standing relative to MANA. Underdog weakness: FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports' complete absence from competitive record in briefing (no matches, no roster, no tournament participation cited) implies either very low tier, inactive status, or minimal recent competitive history\u2014strong signal of unfavorable matchup. MANA's tournament diversity (ECL, CCT EU, NODWIN Clutch) shows active schedule and multi-format experience; by contrast, FC Famalic\u00e3o's presence only as opponent name suggests a lower-tier or lesser-known team without documented competitive profile. Market mispricing assessment: 76% probability for YES slightly below market price (79%), suggesting confidence in MANA is justified but market may be pricing in slight tail-risk around FC Famalic\u00e3o upset; confidence in YES estimate is moderately high (72%) due to documented MANA form, but confidence in NO estimate is low (38%) due to near-total absence of FC Famalic\u00e3o data\u2014asymmetric information favors the favorite.", "key_factor": "MANA's demonstrated BO3 win capability and group-stage dominance in CCT EU Play-In (2-0, 2-0 victories) versus FC Famalic\u00e3o's complete absence from recent competitive record.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE IN MANA: YES is priced at 79%, suggesting the market treats MANA as a heavy favorite despite clear evidence of instability. This pricing likely reflects selective memory of wins while ignoring recent qualifier-stage losses. MANA'S RECENT QUALIFIER COLLAPSE: MANA lost 0-2 to RUSTEC in CCT EU Play-In #20 Play-In Stage (March 28), just 12 days before this match. This is qualifier-level competition, same tier as NODWIN Play-In. A clean sweep loss suggests poor form or strategic vulnerability heading into today's match. PLAYOFF PRESSURE FAILURE: MANA lost 0-2 in NODWIN Clutch Series #6 Playoffs (March 31), indicating that when matches matter most (playoffs), they collapse. Today's match is also in a Play-In stage \u2014 early tournament pressure. Historical pattern suggests MANA underperforms in these contexts. INCONSISTENT MATCH-TO-MATCH FORM: MANA's record from late March shows: 2-0 win, then 1-2 loss, then 2-0 win, then 0-2 loss (RUSTEC), then 0-2 loss (Playoffs), then ECL wins. This volatility suggests the 0-0 scoreline outcome is unpredictable \u2014 not a 79% certainty for either team. NO COMPARATIVE DATA FOR FAMALIC\u00c3O: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited specific information is available about FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports' current roster and recent performance.' This asymmetric information gap inflates MANA's pricing. Famalic\u00e3o could be competitive; we simply don't have data to rule it out. RECENT MOMENTUM FAVORS FAMALIC\u00c3O BY DEFAULT: Since we cannot see Famalic\u00e3o's recent losses or weaknesses, the market is betting blind on MANA. If Famalic\u00e3o has been performing well in parallel tournaments (unmentioned in briefing), they could easily upset. The 21% NO price significantly undervalues unknown quality. ONLINE BO3 VOLATILITY: This is an online, B-tier regional qualifier match. Online CS2 matches are inherently volatile \u2014 single map upsets can cascade into series losses. MANA's 0-2 results show they can be completely shut down. ROSTER TIMING UNCERTAINTY: MANA's June 2026 KS- roster acquisition occurred AFTER the match date of April 9, 2026. This timeline inconsistency in the briefing raises questions about which roster actually plays today. If roster data is unreliable, so is team strength assessment. EARLY TOURNAMENT STAGE BIAS: MANA won early Group C matches (March 26-27) but then lost when facing Play-In stage pressure (March 28, 31). Play-In Group C is a gatekeeping round \u2014 MANA may already be demoralized or fatigued after qualifier losses. MURPHY'S LAW ON FAVORITES: 79% pricing assumes MANA will execute with near-certainty. But recent losses to RUSTEC and in Clutch #6 Playoffs prove they fail under pressure. What prevents another collapse today against an unknown opponent? UNDERDOG VALUE: Famalic\u00e3o at 21% implies a 4:1 underdog. For a BO3 online qualifier match with missing data on the underdog's strength, this is overconfident pricing. Even if Famalic\u00e3o is 40% to win, NO shares are mispriced. CAUTIOUS CONFIDENCE LEVELS: confidence_yes is 45 because MANA has shown they can win (ECL victories, early CCT wins) but recent form contradicts the market's certainty. confidence_no is 62 because lack of Famalic\u00e3o data prevents high confidence in NO, but the logical upside case is there.", "key_factor": "MANA's recent playoff collapse (0-2 loss to RUSTEC in CCT qualifier just days ago) reveals fragility under pressure that contradicts the market's overconfidence in their consistency.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MANA shows mixed but slightly positive recent form: 3 wins in ECL Season 51 (2-1, 2-0, 2-1) within 5 days, but also two decisive losses (0-2 to RUSTEC, 0-2 in NODWIN #6 Playoffs). Market price (79% YES) exceeds cautious base-rate estimate, suggesting modest overconfidence in MANA's superiority, but not dramatically so given available wins. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports data entirely absent from briefing \u2014 no roster, no recent match history, no tier classification. This is a critical asymmetry favoring the known quantity (MANA). MANA roster acquisition (KS- lineup, June 2026) post-dates all match records in briefing, creating uncertainty about actual competing lineup vs. historical performance. Online B-tier EU qualifiers show high variance; the 0-2 losses to RUSTEC and in NODWIN Playoffs indicate MANA is vulnerable to similarly-tiered or slightly superior opponents. BO3 format tilts toward favorites slightly more than BO1, and MANA's recent BO3 result was positive (2-1 on March 25), supporting confidence in format familiarity. Event timing is TODAY (12 hours to resolution); limited time for new information. Current market price reflects real-money positioning and likely incorporates some insider knowledge of team strength. Confidence in YES is moderate-high (68) due to positive recent win patterns and established org. Confidence in NO is low (42) because FC Famalic\u00e3o is an information black hole; cannot credibly assess their strength, only note that unknowns in esports often underperform markets' implied consensus. Probability estimate (72) reflects: base-rate slight MANA edge from wins + moderate market price credibility + FC Famalic\u00e3o opacity + caution against overweighting recent volatility in online qualifiers.", "key_factor": "In EU-regional qualifier-tier CS2 BO3 matches, teams with established rosters and recent online tournament wins (2-0, 2-1 patterns) historically win ~65-75% against lesser-known or unquantified opponents. However, volatility in online qualifiers and roster stability remain high-variance factors.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MANA shows mixed but competitive recent form: won 3 of last 5 matches (ECL 2-1, 2-0, 2-1 victories) but suffered two decisive 0-2 losses (RUSTEC, NODWIN Playoffs). The 79% YES price reflects a moderate favorite, not extreme overconfidence \u2014 realistic given MANA's regional experience in EU qualifiers. Critical asymmetry: MANA's recent match history is well-documented (wins vs unknowns, losses vs known opponents). FC Famalic\u00e3o has NO recent performance data in briefing \u2014 this creates rational uncertainty on the NO side. MANA's 0-2 loss to RUSTEC (March 28) and 0-2 loss in NODWIN Playoffs (March 31) suggest vulnerability, but these losses are 8-11 days old; team had time to adjust. Crowd is not exuberant: 79% YES is confident but grounded. No signals of irrational euphoria or panic in the briefing. Market may be slightly overweighting MANA's qualifier-level losses and underweighting their B-tier tournament victories, but only marginally. FC Famalic\u00e3o's complete absence from briefing data (no roster, no recent results, no head-to-head) justifies lower confidence in NO \u2014 market's caution is rational, not emotional. Volume ($145 USD) is low, suggesting limited market liquidity but not enough to invalidate pricing. MANA's June 2026 roster update (KS- acquisition with ammar, Caleyy, gejmzilla, BledarD, cerber) post-dates the recent matches shown; uncertain if this roster was in place for March/April matches referenced. Event timing: TODAY (~12 hours to resolution) \u2014 any reversal would require unexpected upset. 79% pricing appropriately reflects MANA as slight favorite with FC Famalic\u00e3o as realistic but underfavored challenger.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MANA recent record shows pattern typical of mid-tier EU teams: beats online B-tier opponents (ECL 2-1, 2-0, 2-1) but loses to Play-In stage competitors (0-2 RUSTEC, 0-2 NODWIN #6 Playoffs on March 31)\u2014this suggests MANA is competitive within their tier but struggles against higher seeding/organized teams. BO3 format favors consistency; MANA's volatility (winning 2-1 then losing 0-2 within days in early April) is concerning for a high confidence YES\u2014momentum is fragile at this tier. NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In is explicitly a play-in/qualifying stage, meaning both teams are fighting for advancement; seeding advantage, map veto, and preparation time are critical variables absent from briefing. MANA roster timeline shows June 2026 acquisition of KS- lineup (ammar, Caleyy, gejmzilla, BledarD, cerber)\u2014this is AFTER the April 9 match date. Data suggests MANA was competing with earlier roster in March-April. June roster change implies instability pre-that point. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports has zero match history, roster information, or performance metrics in briefing; cannot assess their actual competitive tier, recent form, or head-to-head tendencies. Market pricing at 79% YES implies strong community belief in MANA superiority, but this is not validated by comparative data. Qualifier-level BO3s (especially Play-In stage) are more dependent on meta knowledge, map preparation, and psychological resilience than skill gaps alone; limited vod availability or detailed match reports means MANA's form assessment relies on scorelines only, not underlying performance quality. Market price (79% YES) reflects market consensus but low volume ($145 USD) and TODAY event timing (resolves ~12 hours) means limited professional arbitrage; overconfidence on YES side is possible. Mispricing signal: If Famalic\u00e3o has better recent LAN/qualifier experience or tighter map prep than MANA (unknowable from briefing), 79% YES is inflated. Conversely, if MANA has dominant head-to-head history or recent internal scrim wins, 79% is underpriced. High confidence_yes (68) justified by MANA's documented recent wins and Play-In participation; low confidence_no (42) reflects severe data gap on Famalic\u00e3o\u2014cannot rule out competitive parity or upset potential without opponent information.", "key_factor": "MANA's mixed form (wins vs B-tier teams, losses vs Play-In stage opponents) and recent roster instability (June 2026 KS- acquisition post-dates most match data) suggest tier-level competition dynamics where qualifier seeding and map pool preparation matter as much as raw skill; Famalic\u00e3o's complete absence from briefing data creates asymmetric confidence.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MANA shows volatile form: 2-1, 2-0, 2-1 wins in ECL but consecutive 0-2 losses to RUSTEC and in NODWIN #6 Playoffs suggest fragility under pressure in higher-stakes matches. Famalic\u00e3o is a complete black box \u2014 no roster, recent results, or competitive history provided in briefing, making confidence in the NO side dangerously low despite 79% YES pricing. MANA's June 2026 roster overhaul (KS- lineup) is recent and potentially untested at this stage; integration issues or role conflicts could emerge in BO3 format. Online qualifier fatigue: MANA competing concurrently in ECL, CCT, and NODWIN tournaments may face scheduling stress or mental fatigue; Famalic\u00e3o's schedule unknown. Play-In format dynamics: MANA lost 0-2 in NODWIN #6 Playoffs, showing specific vulnerability to high-pressure/structured bracket play rather than group stages. Absence of Famalic\u00e3o intel is the core asymmetry \u2014 market likely pricing on MANA name recognition rather than relative strength assessment; a prepared underdog in an all-online qualifier context can exploit unprepared favorites. BO3 gives underdog two chances to steal a map via anti-meta picks or individual performances; single-elimination format favors prepared disruptors. MANA's 1-2 loss on March 25 in CCT Play-In Group C shows they do lose map 1s and can be dragged to game 3 \u2014 not invincible.", "key_factor": "FC Famalic\u00e3o executes a tactical innovation or map-pool exploit that MANA's recent online qualifier grind has not prepared them to counter, leveraging the complete absence of head-to-head intel and Famalic\u00e3o's anonymity in the briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6714855875831486, "no_score": 0.3763210702341137, "edge": -0.11851441241685146, "no_edge": 0.16632107023411374, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 64% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1908377", "question": "Counter-Strike: MANA eSports vs FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between MANA eSports and FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C, initially scheduled for April 9 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MANA eSports\" if MANA eSports win the match against FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports\" if FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports win the match against MANA eSports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rath