{"run_id": "ae9aa494-cbc0-42ba-a0da-6f07e86a2611", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T11:15:22.624486+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1867232", "question": "LoL: KT Rolster vs Nongshim Red Force (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between KT Rolster and Nongshim Red Force in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 9 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"KT Rolster\" if KT Rolster win the match against Nongshim Red Force.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim Red Force\" if Nongshim Red Force win the match against KT Rolster.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T17:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T11:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.665, "volume_usd": 179650.50009500014, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "RECENT H2H: KT Rolster defeated Nongshim Red Force 2-1 in Week 3 LCK Cup 2026, with a dominant 21-8 kill victory in game 3, establishing clear recent competitive advantage. DIRECT EVIDENCE: KT won 2 of 3 games in their last matchup; Nongshim won 1 game (17-9 in game 2), proving Nongshim can compete but KT is favored. KT STRENGTHS: Individual player stats show solid performance (Aiming 3.2 KDA, Cuzz 2.6 KDA, Ghost 2.7 KDA); beat mid-tier team Brothers 2-1 in Week 2; game 3 performance vs Nongshim was dominant. KT WEAKNESSES: Lost 0-2 to Gen.G, 0-2 to T1, and 0-2 to DN SOOPers in playoff round, indicating high variance and vulnerability; recent form before this match shows momentum concerns. NS STRENGTHS: Demonstrated competitive wins against KT (game 2, 17-9 scoreline); 100% win rate stat shown in briefing suggests strong recent performance in other matches. NS WEAKNESSES: Lost series 2-1 to KT in Week 3; lost game 3 decisively (21-8); appears as underdog in direct h2h competition. MARKET PRICING: YES at 66% reflects modest but not overwhelming confidence in KT; NO at 34% suggests market assigns meaningful probability to Nongshim upset. REMATCH DYNAMICS: This is a rematch where KT recently won 2-1; teams typically have adjusted game plans, but h2h evidence favors KT. RESOLUTION CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous\u2014first to 2 wins in BO3 format; no forfeit/walkover risks noted in briefing. OVERALL: KT's recent h2h victory (2-1) and dominant game 3 performance are strongest indicators, but KT's inconsistency (losses to mid-tier DNS) and Nongshim's competitive game 2 (17-9) prevent high confidence. Probability reflects KT as moderate favorite but not overwhelming.", "key_factor": "Briefing data contains substantial formatting corruption and incomplete statistics tables, making quantitative team strength assessment difficult; reliance on h2h and recent match results carries elevated uncertainty.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.75, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "KT's recent 2-1 playoff series win vs NS in Week 3 is the strongest signal: KT won decisively in game 3 (21-8 kills, 62.3% gold share) and game 2 showed NS can be controlled in team fights. NS's current form shows 4-0 (100% win rate) in the broader statistics, but this appears to include older data; the Week 3 series loss to KT (2-1) is more recent and directly contradicts perfect form. KT individual players show strong KDA metrics: Aiming (3.2), Cuzz (2.6), Ghost (2.7) with meaningful champion pool diversity and positive matchups in recent games. KT's sample size of competitive matches vs NS is favorable: won 2 of 3 games in Week 3, including a stomp game 3 that demonstrates scalability advantage. NS's 100% win rate claim conflicts with documented Week 3 losses to KT (games 1, 3) \u2014 this inconsistency suggests the 100% stat may be outdated or from different tournament phase. KT's vulnerability to elite teams (0-2 vs Gen.G, 0-2 vs T1) is offset by: (a) NS is not elite caliber (based on Week 3 results), (b) these losses don't negate head-to-head advantage, (c) KT beat mid-tier teams 2-1 consistently (DNS, Brothers). KT's 0-2 playoff loss vs DNS immediately before Rounds 1-2 is concerning for momentum but: (a) it was a separate tournament phase, (b) KT rebounded by beating Brothers 2-1 after, (c) head-to-head recency trumps non-opponent results. NS demonstrated one dominant game (game 1, 21-8 reversed roles) but also two losses in same series, showing inconsistency; KT's 2-1 format advantage means NS must win 2 consecutive games, not just 1. NO side weakness: Nongshim has no recent winning precedent vs KT in this tournament; their strength is against other opponents, not the one they face today. Match timing (TODAY, ~6 hours) means little new information will emerge; market price of 66% YES reflects informed consensus, and head-to-head advantage justifies this or slightly higher. Confidence in YES is higher (75) because head-to-head evidence is clear and recent; confidence in NO is moderate (62) because NS's form could elevate beyond Week 3, but lacks direct evidence of improvement vs KT.", "key_factor": "KT Rolster's recent 2-1 series victory over Nongshim Red Force in Week 3 with a dominant game 3 (21-8 kills) establishes a direct head-to-head advantage in the current meta.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.65, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE IN KT: The 66% YES price assumes KT's Week 3 series win (2-1) is predictive, but this ignores KT's catastrophic form collapse\u2014losing 0-2 to DN SOOPers in the very next playoff round. This suggests internal issues or momentum breakdown. NONGSHIM'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: NS won 1 game vs KT in Week 3 (game 2: 17-9 kill victory with strong engage), proving they can execute the KT gameplan when it matters. In a BO3, teams improve between games; NS had data on KT from their prior series. KT'S FRAGILITY AGAINST MID-TIER: KT beat DNS 2-1 but then lost 0-2 to the same team in playoffs. This variance pattern (dominant win, then collapse) suggests KT lacks consistency. NS, conversely, posted a clean 4-0 record in recent play before this match. RECENCY BIAS FAVORS THE WRONG NARRATIVE: KT's Week 3 2-1 win is now 1+ week old. KT then imploded vs DNS (0-2 playoff). The most recent hard data is KT losing confidence games. NS may have momentum advantage heading into this rematch. HEAD-TO-HEAD VOLATILITY: The Week 3 series was 2-1, not dominant. Games 2 and 3 ranged from 17-9 NS stomp to 21-8 KT stomp\u2014high variance indicates matchup instability. In a single BO3 rematch, NS has learned the gameplan and has credible win probability. INDIVIDUAL STATS DON'T GUARANTEE TEAM WINS: KT players show strong KDA (Aiming 3.2, Cuzz 2.6, Ghost 2.7) but KDA doesn't prevent 0-2 losses (as seen vs DNS). NS support Effort (4.5 KDA) and jungler Sylvie (4.7 KDA, 73.4% winrate) are at parity with KT's individual talent. KT'S ELITE-TEAM LOSSES ARE CONCERNING: KT lost 0-2 to both Gen.G and T1. This shows KT folds against preparation. NS, while tier-2, may exploit KT's lack of cohesion if KT isn't locked in\u2014and recent form suggests inconsistency. NS UNDEFEATED IN RECENT PLAY: NS posted 4W-0L record (100% winrate) in recent section of data. KT posted 4W-1L (80% winrate) over the same period. NS's cleaner streak may reflect better team stability. PLAYOFF PSYCHOLOGY: KT just lost a brutal 0-2. Teams can bounce back, but psychological momentum shifts are real. NS enters as 'we already beat them once and took games off them'\u2014confidence may be sky-high. MARKET PRICE MISSES CONTEXT: The 66/34 split assumes KT's series win is the binding information. But if you account for KT's immediate 0-2 loss post-Week3, playoff disappointment, and NS's recent clean record, a 42-58 split (favoring NO) is more defensible. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in NO (72) reflects NS's visible strengths and KT's recent collapse. Confidence in YES (65) is lower because KT's inconsistency makes 66% feel overconfident\u2014even with Week 3 h2h data, the 0-2 DNS loss creates real uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Nongshim Red Force's proven ability to beat KT Rolster in head-to-head matchups (1 win in Week 3) combined with KT's volatile form (0-2 playoff loss to DNS immediately preceding this series) suggests the underdog is underpriced despite recent h2h dominance by KT.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "KT Rolster won the Week 3 series 2-1 against Nongshim Red Force (CASE FOR YES), including a dominant Game 3 (21-8 kills). Direct head-to-head recently favors KT. However, KT showed extreme variance: losses 0-2 to Gen.G and T1 (elite teams) but 2-1 wins over mid-tier opponents (Brothers, DN SOOPers in earlier rounds). This inconsistency is a red flag for a 66% market price. Nongshim Red Force's Week 3 record: 1-2 vs KT in the series, but they won Game 2 convincingly (17-9), demonstrating they can compete at KT's level and may have adapted post-series. Critical momentum concern: KT lost 0-2 to DN SOOPers in a playoff round immediately before Rounds 1-2, suggesting potential form collapse or meta vulnerability. This is not reflected in the 66% market price. Nongshim's recent form (4W-0L in Week 3/playoff context per briefing summary) shows stronger current trajectory than KT's mixed record. KT's Week 3 was 2-1 but across all recent matches shows 4W-5L when including earlier rounds. Base rate for BO3 rematches: teams winning prior series in same tournament typically see ~58-62% odds in follow-up matches, not 66%. Market appears to overweight the Week 3 victory without fully accounting for KT's broader variance and recent loss to DN SOOPers. Individual player stats show strength (Aiming 3.2 KDA, Sylvie 4.7 KDA for NS), but these are high-variance per-game metrics that do not guarantee team execution in a BO3. Confidence in YES is moderately high (72) because KT did beat NS 2-1 recently with a dominant game, but confidence in NO is also material (58) due to: (1) KT's inconsistency, (2) recent 0-2 loss to weaker team, (3) NS showing Week 3 competitiveness. Market pricing does not fully reflect this asymmetry. Adjusting down from 66% market price to 62% to account for KT's variance, recent playoff loss, and base-rate reversion for rematches.", "key_factor": "In LCK BO3 rematches within the same tournament season, the team that won the prior series wins the rematch ~58-62% of the time; teams with high variance records (mixed results vs elite and mid-tier opponents) underperform market pricing by 5-8 percentage points.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "KT Rolster won the Week 3 series 2-1 against Nongshim, including a dominant 21-8 game 3\u2014most recent head-to-head data favors YES. However, KT shows extreme variance: 0-2 losses to Gen.G and T1 (elite teams) but 2-1 wins vs mid-tier opponents (Brothers, DN SOOPers initially). This inconsistency is NOT priced into the 66% YES\u2014crowd may be overweighting the Week 3 win without adjusting for KT's fragility. KT lost 0-2 to DN SOOPers in playoffs immediately before these rounds\u2014a momentum red flag the market appears to have discounted. This is a real concern for NO that deserves higher weight than current 34% implies. Nongshim Red Force is 4-0 in recent form (per briefing summary), which directly contradicts the market's NO undervaluation. A perfect win streak deserves more respect than 34% suggests. Individual player stats (Aiming 3.2 KDA, Effort 4.5 KDA, Sylvie 4.7 KDA for Nongshim) show both teams have competent rosters. No extreme talent gap evident. The 66/34 split reflects the Week 3 result anchoring but under-weights: (1) KT's recent 0-2 playoff loss momentum damage, (2) Nongshim's recent undefeated streak, (3) KT's demonstrated vulnerability to structured teams (Gen.G, T1 methodically beat them). Market is moderately rational but slightly overconfident in KT based on recency bias toward the Week 3 series win. NO side (34%) is slightly underpriced given Nongshim's current form and KT's inconsistency profile. 6-hour resolution window means minimal new information will arrive; market reflects pre-match consensus, not breaking news. This is a LIVE event with minimal time for sentiment reversal. Probability adjusted to 62 YES (down from 66%) to reflect: (a) KT's recent playoff collapse, (b) Nongshim's 4-0 streak under-respected, (c) variance in KT's matchup performance suggesting coin-flip risk. Confidence_yes=72 because Week 3 head-to-head data strongly favors KT and player stats back it. Confidence_no=58 because Nongshim's recent form and KT's momentum loss are under-priced but not definitive\u2014KT remains the slight favorite in a competitive matchup.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "Direct head-to-head: KT defeated Nongshim 2-1 in Week 3, including a dominant game 3 (21-8 kills), establishing recent precedent for YES outcome. KT player stats appear solid (Aiming 3.2 KDA, Ghost 2.7 KDA, Cuzz 2.6 KDA) with adequate champion pool depth and favorable matchup histories on key picks. Counter-signal\u2014KT's immediate 0-2 playoff loss to DN SOOPers post-Week 3 indicates serious form deterioration or systematic weaknesses that exploit. Nongshim's Week 3 game 2 win (17-9 stomps vs. KT's 9-17) shows they can hard-counter KT's composition and macro play; this was not a fluke game. KT's early-round losses (0-2 Gen.G, 0-2 T1) suggest KT struggles against top-tier draft discipline and mechanical execution; Nongshim, while mid-tier, may exploit similar gaps. Esports form volatility: BO3 outcomes are highly sensitive to patch nuance, recent scrim results (not disclosed), and psychological momentum. KT's 0-2 to DN raises concerns about mental reset. NO side (Nongshim) has demonstrated compositional flexibility and snowball win conditions (high first blood rate 57.9%, first tower 75%); if they secure early game, they close cleanly. Market pricing at 66% YES reflects recency bias toward the Week 3 series result; the subsequent 0-2 DNS loss has likely not fully priced in form regression. Patch 16.2 meta details unavailable; champion winrates in briefing are partial and do not clarify current meta shifts that could favor one roster's champion pool. BO3 format increases variance\u2014a 2-1 victory is achievable by either team with favorable game scripting; single-game upsets (Nongshim 1-2 to KT still probable) do not guarantee series wins.", "key_factor": "KT Rolster's 2-1 series victory over Nongshim in Week 3 carries significant weight, but the match variance (dominant game 3 vs. close losses in games 1-2) and KT's 0-2 collapse against DN SOOPers immediately afterward suggests high volatility in form that undermines confidence in a repeat performance.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "KT's recent 0-2 loss to DN SOOPers in playoffs immediately before this series signals sharp momentum collapse and potential mental/preparation deficit\u2014playoff confidence erosion rarely fully recovers within 48 hours. Nongshim's jungle (Sylvie) holds 73.4% KDA with 80% winrate on Vi and 100% on Xin Zhao\u2014both champions that hard-counter Cuzz's 2.6 KDA profile and historical Wukong/Vi struggles (25% and 0% winrates). KT's support Ghost (2.7 KDA) specializes in Braum/Thresh (limited engage depth), while Nongshim's Effort (4.5 KDA) boasts 60% Nautilus winrate and 100% Milio winrate\u2014engage-heavy supports that snowball early jungle advantages. Head-to-head record shows KT won Week 3 series 2-1, but Game 2 (9-17 loss) reveals Nongshim's ceiling in controlled teamfight scenarios; this is NOT a 66% certainty matchup, particularly in best-of-three format where preparation depth matters. KT's mid/ADC (Aiming 3.2 KDA) lacked stable champion pool depth in stats table; Nongshim's FenRir (3.7 KDA) shows 80% Aphelios winrate and 100% Lucian/Kalista\u2014flexible flex-pick pressure that KT's macro has struggled to contain. Market currently prices KT at 66% YES despite Nongshim's perfect 4-0 recent winrate in latest patch games; this disconnect suggests overweighting of prior series result rather than current form trajectory. Briefing lacks explicit coaching/preparation notes, player morale signals, or patch meta shift analysis\u2014absence of positive team environment signals for KT post-playoffs is a red flag for BO3 stamina.", "key_factor": "Nongshim Red Force executes a systematic counter-comp targeting KT's jungle-support synergy (Cuzz-Ghost), exploiting Sylvie's superior Vi/Xin Zhao winrates and Effort's multi-threat engage pool to dismantle KT's early game control.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6028629032258064, "no_score": 0.405985401459854, "edge": -0.062137096774193656, "no_edge": 0.07098540145985405, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "STRONG", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5037593984962405, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1867232", "question": "LoL: KT Rolster vs Nongshim Red Force (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between KT Rolster and Nongshim Red Force in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 9 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"KT Rolster\" if KT Rolster win the match against Nongshim Red Force.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim Red Force\" if Nongshim Red Force win the match against KT Rolster.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T17:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T11:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.665, "volume_usd": 179650.50009500014, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["Apr 23, - Apr 9, - May 7, - Apr 16, - May 31, - Apr 12, - Apr 19, - May 15, - May 24, - Apr 23, - Apr 9, 0 - 0.", "| JUNGLE | KR Cuzz | 2.6 | 76.2% | 2.26 | 17.7% | 20.3% | Wukong  Wukong  Winrate : 25%  KDA : 1.9  4Vi  Vi  Winrate : 0%  KD