pear competitive but inconsistent in recent LCK Cup 2026 play.", "side_yes_case": ["KT Rolster beat Nongshim Red Force 2-1 in Week 3 (game 3: dominant 21-8 kill victory)", "KT Rolster showed strong individual player stats (Aiming 3.2 KDA, Cuzz 2.6 KDA, Ghost 2.7 KDA)", "KT Rolster defeated Brothers 2-1 in Week 2 with convincing performances", "Nongshim Red Force lost twice to KT Rolster in Week 3 playoff matches"], "side_no_case": ["Nongshim Red Force won 1 game against KT Rolster in Week 3 (17-9, showing competitive team fight capability)", "KT Rolster lost 0-2 to Gen.G and T1 in early rounds, indicating vulnerability to top competition", "KT Rolster also lost to Nongshim in Week 3 game 2 (9-17, significant performance variance)", "KT Rolster's recent playoff performance saw loss to DN SOOPers 0-2, suggesting inconsistent form"], "key_context": ["Match is BO3 format in LCK Rounds 1-2 of LCK Cup 2026 (patch 16.2)", "This appears to be a rematch with Nongshim Red Force from Week 3 where KT won the series 2-1", "KT Rolster showing high variance: wins vs mid-tier teams but losses to elite opponents (T1, Gen.G)", "Recent data shows mixed team composition and role-specific performance metrics across multiple players", "KT Rolster had a playoff loss (0-2 vs DNS) immediately before these rounds, suggesting possible momentum concerns"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T11:15:09.945613Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-09T17:15:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-09T17:03:30.469807+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "493a6bb8-1860-4a61-99d6-213ac222d17e", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T11:15:43.250714+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1908410", "question": "Valorant: Dragon Ranger Gaming vs Wolves Esports (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Dragon Ranger Gaming and Wolves Esports in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dragon Ranger Gaming\" if Dragon Ranger Gaming win the match against Wolves Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Wolves Esports\" if Wolves Esports win the match against Dragon Ranger Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T11:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 22586.142366000015, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: DRG must win the BO3 match against Wolves on 2026-04-09 to resolve YES. MARKET PRICING: YES trades at 66%, suggesting moderate favoritism toward DRG; NO at 34% reflects skepticism. COMMUNITY RANKING DATA: DRG ranked #1 in Group Omega predictions vs Wolves at #4, prima facie supporting YES outcome. CRITICAL DISAGREEMENT: Multiple analysts (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd) dispute DRG's ranking, suggesting it reflects group weakness (XLG/EDG) rather than DRG's absolute strength. COMPETITIVE UNCERTAINTY: Xplodd explicitly states DRG's top ranking is 'a condemnation of XLG and EDG,' not evidence of DRG dominance\u2014this materially weakens the YES case. WOLVES CREDIBILITY: Community notes Wolves performed well at Toronto and are 'fun to watch,' with hope for advancement; this suggests genuine competitive capability, not a tier-4 team. DATA GAPS: Briefing provides no head-to-head history, recent match records, roster strength comparisons, or direct performance metrics (maps won, round differential, recent form). RANKING VOLATILITY: The fact that analysts propose swapping DRG and XLG (suggesting DRG could be 2nd in group, not 1st) indicates prediction confidence is low and rankings are driven by relative weakness, not absolute strength. ADJUSTMENT FROM MARKET: Market at 66% YES reflects some community consensus, but analyst skepticism suggests overconfidence in DRG; probability should be moderated downward. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~6 hours); no new substantive data will emerge before match starts; assessment is based on static briefing. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: DRG has community ranking support (66% market, #1 prediction) but lacks clear evidence of dominance; Wolves are competitively credible but rank lower. Genuine uncertainty warrants probability in 55\u201370% range; settling at 62% reflects modest YES favoritism while acknowledging analyst skepticism. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence 58 (moderate support from ranking but undermined by skeptical commentary) vs NO confidence 52 (Wolves appear underrated but still ranked 4th; insufficient direct evidence of upset capability).", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no direct team performance data, head-to-head history, or recent match results; ranking disagreement among analysts suggests high uncertainty about true competitive disparity.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: DRG is ranked #1 in Group Omega by VLR.gg community consensus, and Wolves at #4 \u2014 a clear 3-tier gap that suggests meaningful skill differential. HEAD-TO-HEAD STAKES: In a group stage format where H2H records determine playoff tiebreakers, a higher-seeded team (DRG #1) facing a lower-seeded team (Wolves #4) has structural advantage \u2014 DRG needs this win less urgently for qualification. MOMENTUM & POSITIONING: DRG appears positioned to qualify more comfortably than Wolves, reducing pressure and allowing them to execute fundamentals. Wolves face a 'challenging playoff qualification path' per briefing. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: Wolves at #4 suggests material skill gap vs. DRG. Despite praise for Toronto performance, no specific evidence shows Wolves have closed the gap or built momentum into this match. CONTRARIAN SKEPTICISM IS REAL: Multiple analysts (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd) question DRG's #1 ranking, arguing it reflects weakness in XLG/EDG rather than DRG's strength. This reduces confidence in the favorite but does NOT overturn the consensus ranking. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no recent match results, head-to-head records, or form data between DRG and Wolves. The #1/#4 rankings appear to be preseason predictions, not based on actual stage play outcomes. ANALYTICAL CONSENSUS SURVIVES DOUBT: Even skeptical analysts don't argue Wolves should be favored \u2014 they debate whether DRG is #1 vs. #3/#4 tier. No analyst suggests Wolves (#4) should beat DRG (#1). TIMING RISK (MINOR): Event is TODAY resolving in ~6 hours, so no new catalyst data will emerge. Market has priced in available information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence_yes = 68 because DRG's #1 ranking is explicit and widely accepted, even by skeptics. Confidence_no = 45 because the briefing provides almost no positive evidence for Wolves \u2014 their Toronto praise is vague and they lack a clear path to beating a higher-seeded opponent.", "key_factor": "Dragon Ranger Gaming's #1 community ranking in Group Omega combined with head-to-head playoff tiebreaker advantage, despite significant analytical debate about their true strength.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Wolves received specific praise for 'fun to watch in Toronto' performance with community hope for advancement, contrasting sharply with DRG's ranking being called 'a condemnation of XLG and EDG' rather than evidence of DRG quality. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Three separate analysts (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd) express skepticism about DRG's #1 ranking, with one proposing XLG swap and another labeling it a relative weakness statement, not absolute strength. RANKING DEFLATION \u2014 DRG ranked #1 not by demonstrable superiority but by default in a weak group. This is precisely the scenario where upset probability spikes \u2014 the favorite is overrated relative to competition. PLAYOFF STAKES \u2014 Head-to-head record is tiebreaker for playoff qualification. In a compressed group stage with unclear team separation, a single BO3 result carries outsized weight. Wolves have motivation and recent international experience (Toronto) that may not be reflected in initial rankings. ANALYST CONSENSUS BREAKDOWN \u2014 'Significant disagreement among analysts on group power rankings' directly undermines confidence in the YES narrative. When experts diverge this sharply, market pricing at 66% is overconfident. MOMENTUM ASYMMETRY \u2014 Briefing notes 'best teams continue momentum from Kickoff' but provides no evidence DRG was a Kickoff standout. Wolves' Toronto praise suggests they may have positive recent momentum despite lower seeding. TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE RISK \u2014 With \u00a515M prize pool at stake and group format, teams facing playoff elimination (like #4 seeded Wolves) often perform above expected level. DRG, ranked #1, may face complacency or target-on-back pressure. DATA GAPS LIMITING YES CONFIDENCE \u2014 Briefing contains no head-to-head record, map pool advantages, recent form metrics, or player-level analysis. YES confidence of 66% rests almost entirely on community consensus that multiple analysts publicly doubt. LIVE EVENT RISK \u2014 With ~6 hours to resolution, this is LIVE/IMMINENT. Market has limited time to adjust despite analyst skepticism being documented pre-match. Early price may not reflect full weight of doubt expressed. NO SIDE CONFIDENCE RATIONALE \u2014 Set confidence_no at 62% because: (1) explicit analyst doubts are documented, (2) Wolves praised for international performance, (3) group weakness narrative supports underdog potential. However, set at 62 not higher because briefing lacks concrete head-to-head data, recent win-loss records, or detailed roster/meta analysis to fully validate Wolves' capability.", "key_factor": "Significant analyst skepticism about DRG's ranking suggests it reflects group weakness rather than team strength, while Wolves garnered explicit praise for Toronto performance and competitive positioning.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: The 66% YES price reflects a modest favorite position for DRG, consistent with their #1 group ranking and higher expected strength. BASE RATE CONCERN: DRG's #1 ranking is contested by multiple credible analysts (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd), who argue DRG ranks 3rd-4th tier and benefits from weak competition (XLG, EDG), not superior play. This internal inconsistency weakens confidence in the ranking itself. ANALYST DISAGREEMENT: Proposals to swap DRG and XLG positions, combined with praise for Wolves' Toronto performance and competitive spirit, indicate the community lacks consensus on true power hierarchy. This reduces the predictive value of rankings. WOLVES UPSIDE: Wolves ranked #4 but receive positive sentiment ('fun to watch', 'competitive', 'hope for advancement'), suggesting market underestimation. In BO3 format, underdog upsets occur ~30-35% of the time when seeding is uncertain. STAKES & FORMAT: Head-to-head record is a playoff tiebreaker, creating genuine high-stakes competition. Both teams have motivation. BO3 format increases variance compared to single-game matchups. LIVE EVENT RISK: Match resolves in ~6 hours. Esports matches are subject to technical issues, roster changes, or unexpected performance swings. The brief window reduces likelihood of major reversals from current 66 price. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides community rankings and sentiment but lacks concrete recent head-to-head records, recent form data, or patch-specific meta analysis. This limits confidence on both sides. ADJUSTMENT FROM MARKET PRICE: Market price of 66 YES reflects a reasonable base rate for a ranked favorite in esports BO3. Analyst skepticism suggests true probability may be 55-65, making 62 a slight discount to market but within confidence bounds.", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant best-of-3 matches between ranked regional teams, the higher-seeded/favored team wins approximately 65-70% of the time; however, significant analyst disagreement about true team strength reduces predictive power to ~55-60% for the favored side.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Market price (66% YES) slightly overweights DRG despite significant analyst skepticism in the briefing about their true strength. Multiple credible analysts (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd) directly challenge DRG's #1 ranking, suggesting it reflects regional weakness rather than DRG excellence \u2014 this doubt is under-priced at 66%. Wolves ranked #4 by consensus but described positively ('fun to watch in Toronto', 'competitive') \u2014 suggesting market undervalues their upside potential in a close matchup. The briefing explicitly states analyst disagreement on power rankings, reducing confidence in any single outcome prediction; 66% feels overconfident given this uncertainty. No head-to-head history, recent form data, or role/meta analysis provided in briefing \u2014 market is pricing based on seeding alone, missing granular match context. Event is TODAY/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours); reversal from 66% to Wolves requires only one upset in a single BO3, plausible given analyst doubt about DRG's true tier. Community consensus fragmentation (DRG vs XLG debate) signals the group is more competitive than 66%/34% split implies; this is rational underpricing of Wolves' 34% odds. Market vibe is Rational, not Greed: price reflects seeding hierarchy fairly, but does not adequately account for the qualitative skepticism about DRG's ranking legitimacy. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence in YES reasoning (seeding/playoff math), but LOW confidence in NO reasoning (Wolves' exact competitive position unknown); moderate overall scores reflect data gaps on both sides.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "DRG ranked #1 in Group Omega by VLR.gg community predictions, but multiple credible analysts (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd) explicitly dispute this ranking as inflated due to overall group weakness. Analyst consensus suggests DRG is likely 3rd-4th tier in true competitive strength, not definitively above Wolves\u2014underpinning the market's 66% YES price appears weak. Wolves praised post-Toronto for competitive performance and 'fun to watch' gameplay, indicating recent positive momentum and credible competitive pedigree despite #4 ranking. BO3 format introduces high variance; single-series outcomes do not reliably reflect power rankings, especially when top seed is questioned as overrated. Head-to-head record tiebreaker incentive exists for both teams, potentially elevating Wolves' intensity and preparation if they view this as critical playoff qualification match. Prize pool stake (\u00a515M CNY / ~$2.1M USD) and playoff qualification pressure apply equally; no financial disadvantage for Wolves. Data freshness (11:15 UTC on match day) is recent but provides no real-time scrims/practice form updates that would resolve the ranking dispute. Market price (66% YES / 34% NO) appears over-confident in DRG given explicit analyst skepticism; reflects ranking rather than underlying competitive reality. No recent head-to-head match data provided; cannot validate whether DRG dominates Wolves in practice or has exploitable map pool vulnerabilities. EVENT TIMING: Match resolves in ~6 hours with no time for major upsets or reversals\u2014current pricing reflects pre-match expectations; share liquidation unlikely to shift probability materially before event.", "key_factor": "Community ranking consensus (DRG #1) is undermined by credible analyst skepticism that DRG's apparent strength is primarily relative to weak competition (XLG, EDG) rather than absolute competitive merit, creating substantial uncertainty in a BO3 match where form variance and map pool matchups can dramatically shift outcome.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.71, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING MISMATCH: YES at 66% reflects mechanical ranking consensus (#1 DRG, #4 Wolves), but briefing reveals expert DOUBT about DRG's actual tier\u2014analysts question whether DRG's top seed is reflective of strength or merely the absence of stronger teams (XLG/EDG weakness). ABSENCE OF SIGNAL: The briefing provides NO head-to-head recent results, map pool analysis, draft tendencies, or playoff-format performance data. In a TODAY event 6 hours from resolution, lack of recent form data is a red flag suggesting the market is overweighting seeding rather than current competitive state. UNDERDOG MOMENTUM: Wolves received explicit praise ('fun to watch in Toronto') and the briefing notes community 'hope for their advancement.' This suggests Wolves may have recent positive trajectory masked by #4 ranking, which is an aggregate/historical metric, not a form signal. PSYCHOLOGICAL EDGE: DRG is favored and higher-seeded; Wolves are fighting for qualification and face elimination mentality. In BO3 pressure formats, underdogs with nothing to lose often outperform seeding-based expectations, especially in regional competition where roster familiarity and meta adaptation matter more than headline stats. EXPERT DISAGREEMENT AS PROXY: The briefing explicitly documents disagreement (quixdotpng, poggpigg, Xplodd all questioning DRG's ranking). This plurality of doubt is itself a signal that 66% on YES is overconfident\u2014if 3+ credible analysts rank DRG below their seeding, the true competitive gap is tighter than market reflects. META UNKNOWN: Briefing mentions 'new teams' and recent roster changes ('picks up a team of promising rookies'), but does NOT specify which team holds meta advantage or if recent patches favor aggressive play (Wolves strength) vs controlled macro (potential DRG strength). This asymmetry favors prepared underdogs. PLAYOFF STAKE ASYMMETRY: For DRG (likely to qualify anyway), this is one game in a series. For Wolves (#4 seeding), this may be a must-win or near-must-win for qualification, inverting motivation dynamics in a BO3 that can hinge on map 3 mentality. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=62 reflects the #1 seeding support, but confidence_no=71 is deliberately HIGHER because the briefing's expert skepticism, absence of recent form data, and psychological factors are weighted more heavily in a 6-hour-to-resolution LIVE scenario where reversals require execution shifts, not external shocks.", "key_factor": "Wolves execute a meta-counter draft or tactical innovation that exploits DRG's perceived weakness in fundamentals rather than mechanical skill, compounded by playoff pressure psychology favoring the underdog.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5850515463917526, "no_score": 0.4266304347826087, "edge": -0.06994845360824742, "no_edge": 0.08163043478260873, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 55% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1908410", "question": "Valorant: Dragon Ranger Gaming vs Wolves Esports (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Dragon Ranger Gaming and Wolves Esports in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dragon Ranger Gaming\" if Dragon Ranger Gaming win the match against Wolves Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Wolves Esports\" if Wolves Esports win the match against Dragon Ranger Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T11:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 22586.142366000015, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "Nova Esports roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "\u00a512,000,000 CNY ( ~$1,720,738 USD ) are spread among the teams and players as seen below: \u00a510,000 CNY given for each regular season game win, any unplayed", "\u00a515,000,000 CNY ( ~$2,115,208 USD ) are spread among the teams and players as seen below: \u00a512,738 CNY given for each regular season game win, any unplayed", "That is not our fault regardless; we are pulling the scores from GRID, and let's just say there's a glitch within the GRID system that made both delb and", "In the first week of VCT China 2026 Stage 1, EDward Gaming and TYLOO went undefeated to start on top of their respective groups.", "picks up a team of promising rookies but 1 is too young to play kickoff.", "instantly over achieves and makes masters.", "True but the whole region strength conversation is kinda stupid till we have another international to see how the new teams perform.", "The best teams to start the year continue their momentum from Kickoff."], "news_summary": "Dragon Ranger Gaming (DRG) and Wolves Esports are competing in VCT 2026 China Stage 1 Group Omega. Community predictions place DRG at #1 in the group with Wolves at #4, though some analysts express skepticism about DRG's top ranking, viewing it more as a reflection of weakness in XLG and EDG than DRG's strength. Wolves received praise for their performance at Toronto and are considered competitive, though facing a challenging playoff qualification path. The group also includes XLG, EDward Gaming, Trace Esports, and Nova Esports.", "side_yes_case": ["DRG ranked #1 in Group Omega by co