{"run_id": "9f703fa7-51eb-4caa-9c18-e561803e5146", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T11:17:18.743614+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1922475", "question": "Overwatch: FURY vs Rankers (BO3) - OCS Pacific Stage 1 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Overwatch match between FURY and Rankers in the OCS Pacific Stage 1 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURY\" if FURY win the match against Rankers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rankers\" if Rankers win the match against FURY.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/overwatch/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/overwatch/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.575, "volume_usd": 8.884011000000001, "category": "overwatch"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Market resolves to FURY if FURY wins the BO3 match against Rankers on April 9 at 7:00 AM ET. CURRENT STANDINGS SUPPORT RANKERS: Rankers holds 1-1 record vs FURY's 0-2; Rankers' map differential is -2 vs FURY's -5; Rankers demonstrated ability to win at least one match. CASE FOR FURY: FURY may have higher intrinsic team quality despite poor results; early-stage group play performance is volatile; FURY could be motivated by 0-2 deficit; single BO3 outcome unpredictable between struggling teams. CASE FOR RANKERS: Superior recent record (1-1 vs 0-2) and better map differential (-2 vs -5) suggest better current form; Rankers has proven they can secure victories in this tournament; momentum typically favors winning team. DATA GAPS & UNCERTAINTY: Briefing standings table is corrupted/incomplete (duplicate entries, formatting errors); no direct head-to-head match history provided; no recent roster, player performance, or coaching changes mentioned; no odds from professional betting sources or esports analysts included. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Rankers' superior record in group stage provides moderate evidence for Rankers outcome. However, lack of direct comparison, corrupted data, and volatile early-season performance create substantial uncertainty. Confidence in Rankers case (confidence_no) is also low due to limited data quality for both sides. MARKET PRICING (57% YES for FURY) appears to overweight FURY despite worse record, suggesting market may be pricing in unmeasured factors (team quality, roster strength, recent scrim results, bracket implications) or may be mispriced. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Rankers' empirical performance edge (1-1 record, better map differential) gives them slight favorite status, but both teams are underperforming and a single BO3 between low-ranked teams is inherently uncertain. Slight lean toward Rankers (42 for FURY = 58 for Rankers) reflecting standings advantage, but low confidence across both directions due to poor data quality.", "key_factor": "No direct head-to-head data provided; briefing contains incomplete/corrupted standings table making team comparison unreliable; match occurs in ~6 hours with no recent team form or roster updates available.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RANKERS' RECORD ADVANTAGE: Rankers (1-1, 3-5 maps) has already secured a victory in group stage, while FURY (0-2, 1-6 maps) remains winless\u2014a critical confidence and momentum gap in best-of-three format. MAP DIFFERENTIAL STRONGLY FAVORS RANKERS: Rankers' -2 differential vs. FURY's -5 is a +3 map advantage, indicating Rankers consistently plays closer matches and wins tighter contests where clutch performance matters. MOMENTUM DISADVANTAGE FOR FURY: 0-2 starts in competitive Overwatch are psychologically damaging; FURY faces desperation play which can either fuel motivation or breed panic. Rankers has already proven they can execute under pressure. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA LIMITS CERTAINTY: The briefing provides no direct FURY vs. Rankers matchup history, preventing team comp or playstyle analysis. This uncertainty justifies moderate-not-extreme confidence rather than 70+. RANKERS' WIN DEMONSTRATES EXECUTION: One victory proves Rankers can coordinate and close out matches; FURY's complete loss of all maps suggests systemic issues (drafting