team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T03:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T21:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 22218.656251999986, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Akimbo Esports wins the BO3 match; NO if InControl wins. Clear binary condition with forfeiture/tie carve-outs. CRITICAL DATA QUALITY ISSUE: The briefing contains corrupted text ('regainregainregain', 'FarmVilleFarmVille', duplicate entries, incomplete statistics). This undermines confidence in any strength assessment for both teams. AKIMBO RECENT FORM (reconstructed from corrupted data): Loss to FarmVille 0-2 in CCT Series 4 (same tournament, 06/04); wins vs BOSS 2-1 and FarmVille 2-1 in Dust2.us Eagle Masters; loss 1-2 to regain in Eagle Masters 7 (07/04). Mixed-to-negative trajectory in relevant tournament. INCONTROL RECENT FORM (reconstructed from corrupted data): Wins vs Beneath Reality 2-0 (28/03), Zomblers 2-0 (12/03), Fisher College 2-1 (08/03); losses to Zomblers 0-2 (21/02), Marsborne 0-2 (18/02); 1-2 loss to Outfit 49 (16/02). Stronger recent trajectory but inconsistent. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams in CCT North America Series #4 Group A Elimination stage \u2014 same competitive tier, similar skill level expected at tier-2/3 NA scene. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct match history provided; cannot assess historical matchups or specific tactical advantages. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: Current market 38% YES / 62% NO suggests strong InControl favorability. This aligns with InControl's recent win streak vs Akimbo's mixed form and CCT tournament vulnerability. CASE FOR INCONTROL HIGHER PROBABILITY: Consecutive high-confidence wins (multiple 2-0s), recent ESEA Advanced placement success, Akimbo's recent 0-2 loss in same CCT tournament, InControl shows consistency across tournaments. CASE FOR AKIMBO NOT NEGLIGIBLE: Recent Dust2.us wins (2-1 results), tournament experience, BO3 format allows recovery, tier-2 NA scene is competitive and unpredictable. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Cannot assign high confidence to either side due to data corruption. InControl's recent form appears marginally stronger, but briefing quality is too degraded to justify confidence >55 on either prediction. Market price of 38% for Akimbo appears reasonable but unverifiable. MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): Resolution source HLTV.org is explicitly named; match is imminent (event timing TODAY, ~5 hours to resolution). Standard oracle risk is minimal for major CS tournament. 2-hour fallback to credible reporting is reasonable safeguard. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Current market of 38% YES reflects marginal InControl edge. Given data quality limitations and genuine competitive uncertainty in tier-2 CS, probability_score of 38 matches market pricing and represents: InControl as marginal favorite (62% chance) vs Akimbo as underdog (38% chance). This is defensible but not strongly confident.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is heavily corrupted/malformed with garbled match results and incomplete team statistics; actual team strength assessment is severely compromised.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO - InControl) STRENGTHS: InControl has demonstrable momentum with three consecutive wins (2-0 Beneath Reality 28/03, 2-0 Zomblers 12/03, 2-1 Fisher College 08/03) showing consistency across different opposition. AKIMBO'S CRITICAL WEAKNESS: Akimbo lost 0-2 to FarmVille on 06/04/2026 in CCT Season 3 North America Series #4 \u2014 the exact same tournament bracket occurring TODAY. This recent, same-tournament defeat is a direct negative indicator for a BO3 performance within 72 hours. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT ADVANTAGE: InControl's ESEA Advanced Season 56 finish at 1-2nd place (12/03-08/03) demonstrates higher-tier competitive success than Akimbo's comparable period performances, suggesting stronger tactical and mechanical depth. AKIMBO'S INCONSISTENCY: Akimbo's results show volatility: losses to regain (1-2, 1-2) alongside wins vs BOSS (2-1) and FarmVille (2-1). In a high-stakes BO3, this inconsistency favors the steadier InControl. UNDERDOG ARGUMENT (YES - AKIMBO): Akimbo has won twice against FarmVille in other tournaments (2-1 Dust2.us Eagle Masters 05/04) and BOSS (2-1), showing capability to beat mid-tier teams. No head-to-head history exists, so direct matchup dynamics are unknown. DATA QUALITY GAP: Briefing provides no individual player stats, map-specific performance data, or strategic tendencies for either team. InControl's coach (MAD) shows 47% winrate over 110 maps \u2014 mediocre. Neither team has standout roster information provided. TIMING PRESSURE ON REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~5 hours to match start). For Akimbo to overcome the market's NO pricing (62%), they would need a significant surprise. Their 0-2 loss 3 days ago in the same tournament makes this unlikely without major roster changes or external factors not mentioned in briefing. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: NO at 62% appears correctly calibrated given InControl's recent form advantage and Akimbo's same-tournament vulnerability. Market is not dramatically mispricin either side.", "key_factor": "InControl's superior recent form with consecutive 2-0 victories against established opponents (Beneath Reality, Zomblers) versus Akimbo's 0-2 loss to FarmVille in the same CCT tournament just 3 days prior.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "proba