tier opposition; performance trajectory unclear against stronger competition"], "key_context": ["Both teams competing in CCT North America Series #4 Group A - same tournament, suggesting similar competitive tier", "No direct head-to-head history provided in search results", "Match format is BO3, requiring teams to win 2 maps", "CCT Season 3 context shows both teams are active in North American competitive scene", "Recent matches from March-April 2026 suggest current form is relatively recent and relevant"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T22:15:35.030153Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T03:45:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-10T09:42:05.657804+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "18307568-f269-4193-874a-d85269114a0b", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T22:16:30.465739+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1860971", "question": "LoL: Apex Mission Impossible vs Supernova (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Apex Mission Impossible and Supernova in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Apex Mission Impossible\" if Apex Mission Impossible win the match against Supernova.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Supernova\" if Supernova win the match against Apex Mission Impossible.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.13, "volume_usd": 830.905666, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.13, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing document provides no statistics, match history, roster information, or performance metrics for either Apex Mission Impossible or Supernova in NACL 2026 Spring. ONLY IDENTIFYING FACT: Apex Mission Impossible is mentioned as a 6th place team, but no current standings are provided, Supernova's ranking is unknown, and relative competitive position cannot be assessed. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market price of 13% YES / 87% NO indicates strong market consensus favoring Supernova, but this reflects aggregated trader belief rather than publicly available performance data in the briefing. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION: The briefing explicitly states 'no details about Supernova, head-to-head records, recent form, or team composition' and 'no information on Supernova's recent match history or win-loss record'\u2014equivalent uncertainty exists for both teams. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: The resolution criteria are unambiguous; a decisive match result will resolve cleanly. No mechanical risk detected (team name ambiguity, forfeiture clauses, etc.). PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Without performance data, underlying win probability is genuinely unknown. The 13% market price likely reflects trader knowledge beyond this briefing, not information asymmetry favoring one side. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 25 and confidence_no = 25 reflect that the briefing provides NO reliable basis to estimate the outcome. The probability_score of 13 is set to match the current market price as the most informed available signal, but confidence is appropriately depressed due to complete absence of independent supporting evidence. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~6 hours to resolution). Match will be played or canceled; no significant reversal risk remains. Market will settle at $0.01/$0.99 immediately after outcome is clear.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no actionable data on either team's performance, roster, form, or head-to-head record\u2014market price of 13% YES appears to reflect strong consensus that Supernova is heavily favored, but this cannot be independently validated from the provided information.", "probability_yes": 0.13, "probability_no": 0.87, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.13, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 87% (favored), YES at 13% (underdog). As THE BULL for NO, I must advocate why Supernova wins\u2014but briefing provides almost NO actionable data on either team. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'search results provided contain information about VALORANT Challengers 2026 MENA and LCK Challengers League 2026, but do NOT contain specific information about the LoL match between Apex Mission Impossible and Supernova.' This is a massive red flag. WHAT WE KNOW ABOUT APEX: Only that Apex Mission Impossible is ranked 6th place in NACL 2026 Spring. No recent match history, win-loss record, roster composition, or form data provided. WHAT WE KNOW ABOUT SUPERNOVA: Essentially nothing. No ranking, record, roster, or recent performance data in briefing. Supernova is invisible in the provided materials. MARKET IMPLIES SUPERNOVA DOMINANCE: The 87% NO pricing suggests market participants have information suggesting Supernova is significantly stronger. This could reflect: (a) Supernova's superior recent form, (b) head-to-head historical advantage, (c) roster quality advantage, or (d) draft meta favorability. However, NONE of this is evidenced in the briefing. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS ANALYSIS: Apex's 6th place ranking in an A-Tier tournament suggests they are mid-table at best. If Supernova is ranked higher (likely, given 87% pricing), Apex faces an uphill battle. However, without Supernova's exact standing, this inference is speculative. TIMING RISK\u2014LIVE/IMMINENT: Match resolves TODAY in ~6 hours. By now, both teams' lineups, recent scrims, and patch familiarity are locked in. No major catalyst can shift the matchup fundamentally. The market price likely reflects informed betting closer to game time. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no = 28 (low) because briefing provides zero direct evidence about Supernova's strength, recent form, or roster. Even though market prices them at 87%, I cannot independently validate why. confidence_yes = 25 (low) for the same reason\u2014Apex's 6th place rank is the only concrete data, but insufficient to build a case. WHY NO IS FAVORED (BULL CASE): The 87% market price reflects sophisticated bettors who likely have access to: recent NACL match results, team rosters, scrim outcomes, and coaching trends. If Supernova is rated 6.7:1 favorite, they are almost certainly stronger on recent form, head-to-head record, or both. Apex at 6th place is likely in survival mode; Supernova is likely positioned for playoffs. REFUSAL TO INVENT: Briefing data is too thin to justify higher confidence in either direction. The market's 87% NO could be correct, but without supporting evidence in the briefing, I cannot confidently defend it beyond noting that market consensus favors Supernova and Apex's 6th place standing is weak. RESOLUTION: probability_score = 13 reflects the market's strong favor for NO (Supernova). This is the favored side I am advocating for, even though confidence is low because the briefing fails to supply the competitive data needed to independently verify that Supernova is truly 6.7x more likely to win.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 87% NO reflects strong consensus that Supernova is the heavy favorite, but briefing data is critically insufficient to validate either side's true competitive position.", "probability_yes": 0.13, "probability_no": 0.87, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero substantive information about either Apex Mission Impossible or Supernova's current form, rosters, recent match results, or head-to-head history in NACL 2026 Spring\u2014only a mention that Apex is ranked 6th. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: NO is priced at 87% despite complete informational parity; this extreme confidence suggests the market is anchoring to team name recognition, historical brand strength, or pure speculation rather than empirical matchup analysis. APEX'S HIDDEN POSITION: Apex Mission Impossible's 6th-place ranking is neutral-to-positive framing\u20146th in a competitive league suggests mid-tier competitive strength, not weakness. Market may be treating this as a 'lower seed = underdog' mistake. SUPERNOVA UNKNOWN FACTOR: Zero public information on Supernova's roster, recent performance, or standings position. If Supernova is a newly formed or lower-profile roster, the market's 87% confidence lacks empirical justification. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 matches are inherently less predictable than longer series; variance is higher, and upsets are more likely than the raw probability suggests. A single dominant game can swing momentum. TIMING IMPLICATION: Match resolves TODAY (~6 hours); live/imminent status means any late-breaking information (roster changes, player health, technical issues) cannot be priced in. This creates execution risk for the favored side. MURPHY'S LAW ON FAVORITE: If Supernova is the favored side by pure market consensus with no supporting data, overconfidence is baked in. Online tournament environments (NACL 2026 Spring is online) have higher forfeit, connection, or technical disruption risk\u2014disproportionately hurting heavily favored teams due to psychological overextension. ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE \u2260 EVIDENCE OF ABSENCE: The briefing explicitly states no head-to-head record, no recent scrim results, no comparative analysis. The 74-percentage-point gap (87% vs 13%) cannot be justified by silent information\u2014it indicates pure narrative or name bias. UNDERDOG CASE: Apex at 13% may be underpriced if it has coherent strategic preparation, recent hidden form, or favorable draft meta positioning that the sparse briefing simply does not capture. With zero countering data, the probability should be closer to 35-40%, not 13%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (28 and 26) because the briefing provides no empirical grounding for either side. Setting probability_score at 22 (slightly higher than raw 13%) reflects a skeptical view of the extreme favorite pricing, but uncertainty dominates.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of performance data on either team creates asymmetric pricing risk; the 13% YES price may reflect pure narrative positioning rather than empirical team strength comparison.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.13, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours) \u2014 very limited time for reversal; market price at 13% for YES reflects strong confidence in Supernova, likely based on pre-match data (roster strength, recent form, standings position) not visible in briefing. DATA GAP \u2014 CRITICAL: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either team: no head-to-head record, no recent match results for Apex or Supernova, no roster composition, no coaching staff, no scrim data, no patch/meta context. APEX MISSION IMPOSSIBLE: Only fact is 6th place ranking in NACL 2026 Spring (as of early April). No win-loss record, no recent form trajectory, no information on whether they are rising or falling. SUPERNOVA: No information whatsoever. Not even a ranking or mention in briefing data. MARKET PRICE INTERPRETATION: 13% for YES reflects strong market consensus favoring Supernova. This price suggests traders have access to information (team rosters, recent scrim results, meta advantage, player skill differential) not present in this briefing. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Cannot verify the YES case (Apex upset likelihood) due to absence of Apex recent form, roster strength, or head-to-head data. Similarly, cannot independently validate the NO case (Supernova superiority). Both confidence scores must be LOW. GENERIC ESPORTS BASE RATE: In esports BO3 matches, a team priced at 13% wins roughly 10-18% of the time, depending on bookmaker efficiency. Market is pricing Apex as a significant underdog. NO REVERSIBILITY EVIDENCE: Briefing provides no evidence of injury, roster change, meta shift, or other short-term factor that would justify overriding the market price in a match 6 hours away. RESOLUTION RISK: Match could be delayed >7 days (resolve 50-50), forfeited (resolve 50-50), or cancelled. Low probability but non-negligible given online format and potential technical issues. RECOMMENDATION: Defer to market price (13%) given lack of independent data. Probability_score of 13 reflects the market consensus without modification. Both confidence scores remain depressed because briefing data is insufficient to either validate or refute either side independently.", "key_factor": "North American Challengers League match outcomes: insufficient historical data on NACL-specific win rates; generic esports underdog upset rate ~15-25% when priced at 13%", "probability_yes": 0.13, "probability_no": 0.87, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "EXTREME DATA VACUUM: Briefing contains zero actionable intel on either team's current form, roster, or head-to-head dynamics. Search results are contaminated with VALORANT and LCK (Korean LoL) data\u2014completely irrelevant to NACL matchup. MARKET PRICING DETACHED FROM REALITY: 13% YES / 87% NO reflects strong consensus AGAINST Apex, but this conviction rests on nothing substantive. Crowd may be anchoring to stale seed/ranking info (Apex 6th place mention) without current NACL 2026 Spring data. BOTH SIDES EQUALLY OPAQUE: Cannot evaluate Supernova's standing, recent wins, or head-to-head record. Cannot validate whether Apex's 6th place ranking is current or outdated (tournament runs Mar 27\u2013Jun 5; match is Apr 9). Market may be pricing one team as 'expected to lose' purely by narrative, not evidence. IMMINENT EVENT + SHARE PRICE LOCK-IN: Match resolves in ~6 hours. Any reversal requiring significant new information (roster changes, team news, patch impact) is highly unlikely. Market will likely execute at current price regardless of true competitive balance. CONFIDENCE SYMMETRICALLY LOW: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are near floor (~22\u201325) because briefing provides zero comparative analysis. Market may be RIGHT (Supernova genuinely stronger), but not for reasons visible in provided data. This is rational apathy hiding behind false consensus. POSSIBLE PSYCHOLOGICAL PATTERN: If Apex is an underdog/academy team and Supernova is a higher-seeded squad, the 87% NO price could reflect lazy EV-negative betting on the 'favorite.' Alternatively, Supernova could be legitimately superior\u2014impossible to determine from briefing. RESOLUTION TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY with low USD volume ($831). Illiquidity + data blackout = potential for sharp moves if news breaks before 7pm ET match start, but window is very narrow.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.15, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable data on either team\u2014no rosters, no recent match results, no win-loss records within NACL 2026 Spring, no head-to-head history, no draft meta context, no patch notes. MARKET SIGNAL DOMINATES: Current market pricing (13% YES / 87% NO) is the only substantive signal available. In esports, such extreme pricing typically reflects either: (a) community consensus from betting/streaming platforms, (b) insider knowledge from coaching staff/analysts, or (c) public team announcements (roster moves, player illness, etc.) not captured in this briefing. APEX MISSION IMPOSSIBLE CONTEXT: Only data point is '6th place ranking' in NACL 2026 Spring. Without current standings, opponent strength, or recent form, this rank alone is insufficient to judge current trajectory\u20146th could indicate decline, plateau, or recovery phase. SUPERNOVA OPACITY: Zero briefing data on Supernova. No ranking, no roster, no recent results. Market's 87% confidence in Supernova must derive from sources external to this briefing. TIMING CRITICALITY: Match is TODAY (resolves ~6 hours from briefing timestamp). In esports, late-breaking information (roster confirmations, player availability, substitutions, server/technical issues) often emerges hours before match start and can materially shift odds. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY RISK: The extreme market skew (87% NO) with zero supporting detail in briefing suggests either the briefing is intentionally sparse (market expects traders to use external research) or the briefing curator lacks esports domain knowledge. Either way, confidence must be capped. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Match resolution path is unambiguous (first to 2 wins in BO3), but forfeit/cancellation clause exists\u2014given today's match timing, technical/network issues are non-trivial risks in online tournaments. DOMAIN SPECIALIST ASSESSMENT: As a 20+ year esports analyst, I recognize that a 13% YES price in a live LoL match with zero briefing data suggests market participants have access to team scrims, roster confirmations, or coaching insights not reflected here. Contra-betting against 87% consensus without supporting evidence is high-risk. However, lack of briefing data prevents high-confidence scoring either direction.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 13% YES / 87% NO suggests strong market confidence in Supernova despite complete absence of roster, form, or head-to-head data in the briefing\u2014a red flag indicating either sophisticated insider knowledge or severe information asymmetry favoring the NO side.", "probability_yes": 0.15, "probability_no": 0.85, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides almost zero actionable intel on either team\u2014no recent match results, rosters, coaching staff, scrim performance, or head-to-head history. The 13% YES / 87% NO market pricing suggests strong consensus favoring Supernova, but this consensus is built on absence of evidence, not evidence of absence. CONTRARIAN SIGNAL: The market's extreme confidence in Supernova (87%) despite zero competitive data points suggests either: (a) Supernova is objectively dominant by standings/seeding (likely), or (b) the market is overweighting limited reputational/brand signal. The briefing only mentions Apex at 6th place\u2014Supernova's ranking/record is completely absent. BLACK SWAN #1\u2014ROSTER VOLATILITY: Online NACL matches in early April often feature last-minute roster adjustments, player illness, or emergency subs due to schedule density. Apex, as a lower-seeded team, may deploy an unconventional jungler or support to counter Supernova's stereotyped early gameplan. If Supernova prepared for Apex's 'standard' roster and faces a stand-in or experimental pick, coordination gaps emerge rapidly in BO3 format. BLACK SWAN #2\u2014DRAFT META SHIFT: Patch notes released in the 48 hours before April 9 could favor off-meta champions that Apex has been practicing in scrims but Supernova (a presumed higher seed) has deprioritized. Lower seeds often innovate harder in draft due to lack of rep pressure; higher seeds lean on proven comfort picks. A single broken champion or item interaction could swing map 1. BLACK SWAN #3\u2014MENTAL/MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: Supernova's heavy market favorite status (87%) suggests they may be locked into must-win or playoff-seeding pressure; Apex, as underdog, plays with zero expectation and freer mental state. Psychological choking in online BO3 is real, especially against disciplined underdogs willing to go all-in on early aggression. DATA QUALITY ASSESSMENT: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are capped at ~25\u201328 because the briefing is essentially a blank slate for competitive intel. The 13% vs 87% market split is not based on provided match data, team stats, or form trends\u2014it reflects external market reputation not visible here. This makes contrarian upside plausible but not high-confidence. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY (~6 hours). No time for major roster changes or injuries to surface pre-match. However, this also means any pre-match scrims or draft prep advantages are baked in; Apex cannot improve their odds through additional practice. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE: $831 volume is modest for a NACL match, suggesting limited sophisticated betting activity. The 13/87 split may reflect casual consensus rather than sharp/informed positioning. This slightly increases black swan plausibility. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: 18% for Apex reflects the likelihood of one or more of the above disruptions (roster surprise, draft innovation, mental edge) overcoming what is almost certainly a raw skill/seeding gap favoring Supernova. The 69% gap (18 vs 87) is too large to ignore entirely on pure uncertainty, but Apex's 6th place finish suggests they are legitimately weaker. Final score balances severe data scarcity against realistic underdog mechanics.", "key_factor": "Apex Mission Impossible executes a surprise draft pivot or roster substitution (likely jungler/support swap) that exploits Supernova's predictable early game pathing, capitalizing on meta shifts not visible in aggregate standings.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.16102857142857144, "no_score": 0.8402116402116402, "edge": 0.031028571428571433, "no_edge": -0.02978835978835981, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 27% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1860971", "question": "LoL: Apex Mission Impossible vs Supernova (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Apex Mission Impossible and Supernova in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Apex Mission Impossible\" if Apex Mission Impossible win the match against Supernova.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Supernova\" if Supernova win the match against Apex Mission Impossible.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.13, "volume_usd": 830.905666, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["NACL 2026 Spring is an online North American LoL tournament organized by Riot Games and Liga ACE.", "This A-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 27 to Jun 05", "Click here for the complete statistics table.", "#, Country / Region, Representation, Players.", "Team RA'AD\n\n1:2(Bo3)\n\nOne More Esports\n\nJett\n\nTejo\n\nOmen\n\nKAY/O\n\nAstra\n\n22\n\nAbyss\n\nViper\n\nWaylay\n\nOmen\n\nSova\n\nTejo\n\n13\n\n103\n\nWaylay\n\nTejo\n\nViper\n\nSkye\n\nBrimstone\n\n13\n\n76\n\nBind\n\nViper\n\nWaylay\n\nBrimstone\n\nSkye\n\nNeon\n\n6\n\n51\n\nYoru\n\nTejo\n\nKilljoy\n\nKAY/O\n\nAstra\n\n11\n\n92\n\nPearl\n\nKilljoy\n\nWaylay\n\nAstra\n\nSova\n\nTejo\n\n13\n\n310\n\n| Map Veto |\n\n| TBD | BA