{"run_id": "690d5da7-c879-4051-a3d4-a7854421c901", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T22:18:21.289623+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1856523", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: LFO No Name vs Can You Be My Enemy (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: North Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket round 1 match between LFO No Name and Can You Be My Enemy in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: North Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 10 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LFO No Name\" if LFO No Name win the match against Can You Be My Enemy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Can You Be My Enemy\" if Can You Be My Enemy win the match against LFO No Name.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T10:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T04:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.84, "volume_usd": 0.0, "category": "rainbow-six-siege"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains only regional meta statistics (operator bans, map win rates) and roster turnover data, but NO head-to-head history, recent match results, or individual team win/loss records for either LFO No Name or Can You Be My Enemy. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES side trading at 84% suggests strong prior information or expert consensus not present in the briefing document. This creates asymmetry between briefing-only analysis (moderate YES lean) and market-implied probability. LFO NO NAME - Limited Evidence: No recent match results, roster stability data, or performance metrics provided. Cannot assess offensive/defensive strength or map comfort. CAN YOU BE MY ENEMY - Mixed Signals: Recent coaching hire (Hamamoto, 2026-03-06) suggests organizational investment, but only visible match in briefing shows 0:2 loss to DplusDplus (April 3, 2026 - 6 days ago). This recent loss is concerning for a lower bracket playoff match. RECENT PERFORMANCE CRITICAL: Can You Be My Enemy lost 0:2 to DplusDplus just 6 days before this playoff, mapping Lair and Clubhouse (both defender-heavy maps). No similar recent data for LFO No Name provided. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous - match must have a winner (BO3 format means 2 maps required). No tie or forfeit edge cases apparent given active tournament context. R