{"run_id": "b8a00ffb-34c1-43d9-bd58-d144f5b77da8", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T11:47:05.325748+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1930524", "question": "Counter-Strike: FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports vs UNiTY esports (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Elimination match between FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports and UNiTY esports in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports\" if FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports win the match against UNiTY esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNiTY esports\" if UNiTY esports win the match against FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.14, "volume_usd": 5114.197625000001, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNiTY esports has documented recent performance: 0-2 losses to Hashiras (9 Apr), ASTRAL (9 Apr), MANA (5 Apr), ENCE Academy (3 Apr), and other qualifier losses, suggesting weak current form. However, UNiTY also has recent wins: 2-0 vs Inner Circle Academy (6 Apr), 2-0 vs G2 Ares (4 Apr), 2-0 vs Qual4 (25 Mar), indicating competitive capability despite volatility. UNiTY maintains 980 Valve Global Ranking points (as of 9 Apr 2026), confirming they are an active mid-tier EU team with legitimate standing. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports has ZERO documented history in the briefing data\u2014no roster info, no recent match results, no VGR points, no tournament placements. This is a critical information asymmetry. The briefing explicitly notes 'FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports details are absent from search results', making strength assessment impossible. Market pricing at 14% YES / 86% NO suggests strong market consensus that UNiTY is the clear favorite, likely based on external data not provided in this briefing. Both are qualifier-level teams in NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C, not tier-1 competitors; outcome depends heavily on relative team strength. Absence of data on FC Famalic\u00e3o does not mean they are weak\u2014it may reflect a newer, smaller, or less documented team. Market pricing could reflect insider knowledge of roster quality. UNiTY's recent inconsistency (mixed 2-0 wins and 0-2 losses in successive matches) suggests vulnerability to an opponent of equal or higher caliber. BO3 format requires consistency; UNiTY's volatile recent form is a concern for YES backers if FC Famalic\u00e3o brings comparable or superior play. Market confidence at 86% for NO is substantial but not overwhelming (not 95%+); suggests meaningful but incomplete certainty about UNiTY's edge. Probability score reflects: (a) UNiTY's documented but mixed recent form as slight favorite, (b) complete lack of FC Famalic\u00e3o data preventing upside assessment, (c) market consensus favoring UNiTY substantially. Setting probability_score to 18 reflects: UNiTY is more likely to win based on documented activity vs. undocumented opponent, but significant data gap on FC Famalic\u00e3o prevents high confidence.", "key_factor": "FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports has zero documented competitive history in briefing data, making any comparative assessment speculative; resolution mechanism risk is minimal given HLTV reporting availability.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "NO (UNiTY loss) is priced at 86%, indicating strong market conviction that UNiTY will lose to FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports. UNiTY's recent match history is catastrophic: 0-2 vs Hashiras (9 Apr), 0-2 vs ASTRAL (9 Apr), 0-2 vs MANA (5 Apr), 0-2 vs ENCE Academy (3 Apr) \u2014 four consecutive clean sweeps in a 6-day window. This pattern of consecutive 0-2 losses across different tournaments (NODWIN Clutch, LORGAR Rankings, ESL Challenger League) suggests systemic team issues: roster cohesion failure, tactical breakdown, or potential morale/motivation collapse. UNiTY's sole recent win (2-0 vs Inner Circle Academy on 6 Apr and G2 Ares on 4 Apr) are against clearly weaker opponents; losses are against higher-tier regional teams (ASTRAL, ENCE Academy), indicating UNiTY struggles vs competitive opposition. The 980 Valve Global Ranking points cited for UNiTY are outdated/stale relative to the current form spiral \u2014 ranking points lag actual competitive level by weeks. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports complete absence from the briefing and search results is significant but NOT evidence of weakness \u2014 they may be intentionally lower-profile or the market may lack data. However, the absence of negative information is less damaging than UNiTY's documented collapse. In a BO3 format, consistency is critical. UNiTY's current inconsistency (mixing wins vs weak teams with 0-2 sweeps vs competitive teams) is a fatal liability across 3 maps. Match timing (today, ~5 hours to resolution) means no catalysts can reverse UNiTY's form collapse in time. Form reversals require days/weeks of practice; a single match cannot erase the pattern. The 86% NO price reflects market rationality: when one team has just suffered four consecutive 0-2 losses and the opponent is completely unknown, the unknown is the better bet \u2014 UNiTY's recent evidence is negative, FC's is neutral (absent). Contrarian case for YES is weak: relying on FC being 'surprisingly bad' requires inventing new information not in the briefing. The market is correctly penalizing UNiTY's documented form collapse. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_no is high (82) because UNiTY's recent losses are hard data and form-based predictions in esports are highly reliable short-term. Confidence_yes is low (28) because FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports data gap is genuine \u2014 we cannot rule out they are equally or more dysfunctional, making the YES case speculative.", "key_factor": "UNiTY's severe recent form collapse (four consecutive 0-2 losses in last 5 days across multiple tournaments) combined with lack of any public information on FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports demonstrates market confidence in the underdog's fundamental weakness.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNiTY's recent form is objectively poor: four consecutive 0-2 losses (vs Hashiras, ASTRAL, MANA, ENCE Academy) in the past 7 days, suggesting severe roster instability or tactical collapse heading into today's match. UNiTY has mixed BO3 results overall\u2014wins vs Inner Circle Academy, BASEMENT BOYS, Qual4, G2 Ares, but losses to bond1e (0-2) and repeated shutouts in qualifiers indicate they struggle against mid-tier competition in best-of series. FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports is completely absent from the briefing data\u2014no roster info, recent results, VGR ranking, or tournament history provided. This is a critical information gap favoring the underdog narrative. However, the absence of FC Famalic\u00e3o data does NOT automatically mean they are stronger. It could indicate they are a newer, lower-profile Portuguese team with minimal qualifier participation\u2014which would make them weaker, not stronger. UNiTY maintains 980 VGR points as of April 9 (yesterday), demonstrating established competitive pedigree and consistent participation in regional circuits, which is evidence of organizational stability despite recent losses. The briefing explicitly states both teams are 'mid-tier European squads competing in qualifier tournaments'\u2014this suggests comparable strength levels, not a vast gulf favoring UNiTY. BO3 format requires tactical depth and map pool strength across multiple matches. UNiTY's four consecutive 0-2 eliminations suggest they may lack map diversity or in-game adaptation\u2014a critical vulnerability FC Famalic\u00e3o could exploit. The market prices UNiTY at 86%, reflecting confidence in their qualifier experience and VGR ranking, but this may overweight historical data and underweight their recent form collapse (4 consecutive 0-2 losses in 7 days is severe). FC Famalic\u00e3o's anonymity in the data could reflect: (a) a rising team with limited tournament history (potential upset vector), (b) a weak academy or regional-only team (confirms UNiTY favoring), or (c) a team with recent roster changes not yet indexed by HLTV. Without concrete evidence of FC Famalic\u00e3o's strength, their competitive standing, or recent results, confidence in an upset must remain low. The briefing provides no factual basis to claim they are underrated. UNiTY's Valve Global Ranking and documented roster (K1-FiDa, NEOFRAG, MoriiSko, M1key, woozzzi) represent tangible competitive credentials that FC Famalic\u00e3o does not match in the briefing. The 14% price for YES reflects appropriate market skepticism about an unknown opponent facing an established regional team, even if that established team is in a form slump.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of FC Famalic\u00e3o performance data creates an information asymmetry that could conceal superior preparation or roster strength going into this qualifier match.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "UNiTY shows a catastrophic recent form trajectory: 0-2 vs Hashiras (04/09), 0-2 vs ASTRAL (04/09), 0-2 vs MANA (04/05), 0-2 vs ENCE Academy (04/03). Four consecutive playoff losses in 6 days signals either tactical collapse, roster instability, or morale crisis. Despite mixed record (some 2-0 wins vs Inner Circle Academy, BASEMENT BOYS, Qual4), the recent string of decisive losses in qualifier tournaments (ESL Challenger League, LORGAR Rankings) occurred immediately before this match, suggesting momentum is strongly negative. No credible data on FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports exists in briefing. Absence of information on a Portuguese/tier-2 EU team competing in Play-In qualifiers suggests it is likely lower-tier or emerging roster. Cannot assess relative strength. Market price of 14% YES reflects significant confidence in UNiTY despite poor form. This may incorporate: (a) UNiTY's Valve Global Ranking (980 points, mid-tier standing), (b) expectation of form reversal after losing streak, or (c) private knowledge of FC Famalic\u00e3o weakness. BO3 format amplifies consistency requirements. Teams on severe losing streaks rarely recover immediately; best-of-three magnifies map pool knowledge gaps. Base rate for underdog at 14% in qualifier BO3: Historical precedent suggests 15-25% win rates for teams priced this low, depending on recency of form data. UNiTY's 4-loss streak (last 6 days) pushes toward lower end of range. CRITICAL: Event is TODAY/IMMINENT (5 hours to match start, 2026-04-10 17:00 UTC). Market pricing likely already reflects near-final information. Sharp bettors have positioned; reversal unlikely without major roster news. Confidence_yes limited to 35: No FC Famalic\u00e3o data prevents validation of the UNiTY underdog thesis. If FC Famalic\u00e3o is a genuinely weaker team, 14% undervalues UNiTY. Confidence_no limited to 42: UNiTY's 4 consecutive 0-2 losses create genuine uncertainty about whether team can compete. Recent form alone would justify 10-12% probability; market at 14% suggests counterbalancing information not visible in briefing. Probability of 18: Splits difference between form-based pessimism (~10%) and market-implied probability (~14-18%) plus modest uncertainty buffer for missing FC Famalic\u00e3o data. Reflects moderate skepticism of UNiTY's ability to break losing streak in BO3 format.", "key_factor": "In qualifier-level BO3 matches between mid-tier European CS teams with asymmetric information, the underdog (14% market price) wins approximately 18-25% of the time; severe recent form collapse (4 consecutive 0-2 losses) depresses win probability further.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "\u2022 UNiTY's recent form is significantly negative: 0-2 losses to Hashiras (09/04), ASTRAL (09/04), MANA (05/04), ENCE Academy (03/04) within the last week \u2022 UNiTY shows inconsistent performance across multiple tournaments simultaneously, suggesting roster instability or poor preparation \u2022 Market price at 14% YES reflects the available data showing UNiTY's struggle; this is not irrational exuberance \u2022 FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports completely absent from HLTV records, tournament rosters, and recent match history\u2014zero competitive visibility in briefing \u2022 The asymmetry favors UNiTY by default: they are documented to exist and compete; FC Famalic\u00e3o is not referenced anywhere in provided data \u2022 Even a weak, struggling team (UNiTY at 980 Valve ranking) is a known entity vs. an unknown opponent with no verifiable competitive record \u2022 Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (5 hours to resolution); reversal would require FC Famalic\u00e3o to be a legitimate threat, which briefing provides zero evidence for \u2022 Low volume ($5.1k) on a qualifier-level match suggests limited market attention; NO side (86%) reflects rational pessimism about UNiTY's recent form rather than crowd panic \u2022 Market appears efficiently priced: UNiTY is favored despite poor recent results because they are the only team with documented existence and some ranking points \u2022 Confidence in YES is lowered due to complete absence of FC Famalic\u00e3o data\u2014cannot assess their actual strength; confidence in NO is high because UNiTY's documented recent losses are concrete", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNiTY demonstrated catastrophic recent form: 0-2 losses to Hashiras (09/04), ASTRAL (09/04), MANA (05/04), ENCE Academy (03/04)\u2014four consecutive whitewash defeats in a 6-day window indicates systemic collapse, not variance. In mid-tier qualifier CS:GO/CS2, BO3 format penalizes inconsistency; teams must maintain map pool viability. Four consecutive 0-2 results suggest roster coordination or tactical breakdown affecting multiple map performances. UNiTY's mixed record (wins vs Inner Circle Academy, G2 Ares, bond1e; losses vs established academy teams) indicates ceiling well below ASTRAL/Hashiras level\u2014FC Famalic\u00e3o positioning as underdog (14% YES price) suggests bookmakers assess it as at least peer-level or stronger. 980 Valve Global Ranking points for UNiTY is mid-tier EU qualifier baseline; no comparable data for FC Famalic\u00e3o in briefing, but market pricing (86% NO) implies FC Famalic\u00e3o ranked lower or unproven, yet market may be anchored to UNiTY's raw VGR rather than current form. Timing concern: Event TODAY (~5 hours to match start at 7 AM ET / ~11:46 UTC data freshness). UNiTY's last three documented matches all losses in past 48 hours\u2014zero recovery time or roster adjustment window before BO3 elimination. NO side confidence (72%) reflects: clear recent form data supporting UNiTY collapse, BO3 map pool vulnerability exposure, elimination-match pressure on struggling roster. YES side confidence (35%) reflects: complete absence of FC Famalic\u00e3o competitive data in briefing, preventing strength validation; market price (14%) may reflect genuine underdog status or bookmaker mispricing. Qualifier-level teams (NODWIN Play-In Group C) show high volatility; however, catastrophic loss streaks typically signal roster issues or tactical incoherence that persist across single-day tournaments rather than reverse sharply.", "key_factor": "UNiTY's recent form shows a devastating 0-2 loss streak across four consecutive qualifier tournaments (vs Hashiras, ASTRAL, MANA, ENCE Academy), suggesting structural team or morale issues that BO3 format will expose across map variety.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNiTY shows alarming form collapse: 5 consecutive 0-2 losses (Hashiras, ASTRAL, MANA, ENCE Academy) across multiple tournaments in 3-5 days suggests severe morale/coordination crisis, not just opponent skill gaps. Market prices at 14% YES / 86% NO imply heavy confidence in UNiTY, yet the briefing provides zero competitive data on FC Famalic\u00e3o\u2014this asymmetry creates risk that FC is underestimated. FC Famalic\u00e3o completely absent from HLTV records, news, rankings, or match history in briefing\u2014could indicate either a newly formed team (unpredictable) or a team with unconventional preparation that evades typical meta. UNiTY's 980 Valve Global Ranking points are middle-of-pack; wins over 'Inner Circle Academy' and 'G2 Ares' (academy teams) suggest inflated confidence against qualifier-level opponents. BO3 format amplifies variance: one team in free-fall (UNiTY) can lose map 1 catastrophically if mental state breaks; FC's unknown preparation could capitalize on this fragility. No head-to-head history between teams; UNiTY's recent opponents are mostly academy/regional squads\u2014FC's true skill level and style are completely opaque. Briefing silent on: FC roster, FC recent matches, FC map pool, coaching changes at either org, or internal roster issues that could shift match dynamics. Match is TODAY with ~5 hours to resolution; market confidence is locked in without real-time form updates; UNiTY's mental state could deteriorate further or stabilize, and briefing data cuts at 11:46 UTC with match at 17:00 UTC. Counter-argument (NO confidence remains high): UNiTY's VGR points and multiple tournament entries suggest institutional credibility; 86% market price reflects asymmetric information favoring NO. Absence of evidence on FC is not evidence of absence\u2014but lack of data on both teams' preparation, recent scrims, or personnel changes prevents high confidence in either direction.", "key_factor": "FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports fields an unexpected roster substitution or tactical innovation (e.g., a stand-in player or radical map pool strategy) that exploits UNiTY's recent mental/form collapse, or UNiTY suffers a critical player absence not yet reflected in public records.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.18484848484848485, "no_score": 0.8139240506329114, "edge": 0.04484848484848483, "no_edge": -0.04607594936708859, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "CAUTIOUS", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.16279069767441862, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1930524", "question": "Counter-Strike: FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports vs UNiTY esports (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Elimination match between FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports and UNiTY esports in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports\" if FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports win the match against UNiTY esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNiTY esports\" if UNiTY esports win the match against FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.14, "volume_usd": 5114.197625000001, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["The location of BLAST Open 2027 Season 1 will be Singapore, BLAST have announced.", "The small country hosted the \"sold-out\" World Final in 2024,", "HLTV.org\nHLTV.org\nHLTV.org\n\nHLTV.org\n\nAstralis\nJakob 'jabbi' Nygaard\n\n# Most damage / round\n\n# RANKING\n\nVitality\nVitality\nNatus Vincere\nFURIA\nFalcons\nPARIVISION\n\n# EVENTS\n\nPGL Bucharest 2026\nPGL Bucharest 2026\nIEM Rio 2026\nIEM Rio 2026\nBLAST Rivals 2026 Season 1\nPGL Astana 2026\nIEM Atlanta 2026\nIEM Atlanta 2026\n\n# FPL RANKING\n\nBryan 'Marro' Valles Valenzuela\nDanny 'Cxzi' Strzelczyk\nBelal 'AbbyDog' Embaby\nJohn 'arcade' Rogel\nMatthew 'Cryptic' Whitmore\n\n# GALLERIES\n\n# RECENT ACTIVITY\n\n# MINIGAME\n\n#