"], "side_no_case": ["UNiTY's recent qualifier record shows significant losses (0-2 vs Hashiras, 0-2 vs ASTRAL, 0-2 vs MANA, 0-2 vs ENCE Academy)", "Limited information on FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports prevents comparative strength assessment", "UNiTY's inconsistent performance across multiple tournaments suggests reliability concerns"], "key_context": ["NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group C is a qualifier-level tournament, indicating lower tier competition", "Match format is Best of 3 (BO3), requiring consistency across multiple maps", "UNiTY roster includes K1-FiDa, NEOFRAG, MoriiSko, M1key, woozzzi as of April 2026", "No head-to-head history or direct competitive data between these two teams in search results", "Both teams competing in European regional qualifier circuit rather than international events"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T11:46:26.774597Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T17:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-10T19:29:10.495636+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "fe7c6349-ef66-48b9-a1ba-9c91f755ad81", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T11:47:29.353817+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1928473", "question": "Counter-Strike: Entropy vs ImmuNe (BO1) - Parken Challenger Championship Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between Entropy and ImmuNe in the Parken Challenger Championship Group A, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Entropy\" if Entropy win the match against ImmuNe.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ImmuNe\" if ImmuNe win the match against Entropy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 2260.244854, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Entropy must win a BO1 match against ImmuNe in Parken Challenger Championship Group A on April 10, 7:00 AM ET. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no comparative strength data, recent form, head-to-head records, or roster information for either team. The tournament table shows Entropy Gaming with a 2-1 record in the group stage, but ImmuNe does not appear in the provided standings at all. ENTROPY VISIBILITY: Entropy Gaming appears in the standings (6th place, 2-1 record, +3 RD) indicating tournament participation and demonstrated competitive play. This is the only concrete performance data available. IMMUNE DATA ABSENCE: ImmuNe has zero representation in the briefing data\u2014no standings position, no match results, no performance indicators. This creates asymmetric information favoring NO side assessment. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: Current prices (YES 38% / NO 62%) align with Entropy's lower seeding position (6th of visible teams) relative to higher-ranked opponents. The pricing appears rational given limited data, not indicative of strong Entropy fundamentals. BO1 VOLATILITY: Best-of-1 format inherently reduces predictability and increases upset probability. This should anchor probability estimates toward 50%, not extreme values. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and straightforward\u2014match must be completed with a decisive winner. No ambiguity in team identification or resolution mechanism beyond standard online source delays. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes and confidence_no both set to 25 because (1) insufficient data on either team's strength prevents confident YES estimate, and (2) complete absence of ImmuNe performance data prevents confident NO estimate. The 38% probability_score reflects market consensus under information poverty, not strong analytical conviction. TIME CONSTRAINT: Event resolves in ~5 hours. Too imminent to significantly reassess without new performance data. Market pricing likely reflects all available public information at this stage.", "key_factor": "Severe data insufficiency: no performance metrics, head-to-head records, roster information, or recent form data available for either team; market pricing appears to reflect available information rather than underlying competitive reality.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO/ImmuNe @ 62%): The market has priced ImmuNe as the clear favorite despite zero performance data in the briefing. This pricing discrepancy suggests either: (1) ImmuNe has superior recent results not captured in search results, (2) roster/player strength favors ImmuNe, or (3) head-to-head history favors ImmuNe. In low-information environments, market consensus often reflects edge knowledge from esports analysts and bettors with deeper tournament data. UNDERDOG CASE (YES/Entropy @ 38%): Entropy Gaming demonstrated a 2-1 record in PROJECT V 2026 Split 2 Weekly #2, showing competitive form in recent weeks. However, this is the ONLY concrete performance data available for either team. Entropy's +3 round differential in the Parken standings (42-39 across 3 matches) places them 6th in the current group \u2014 a mid-table finish that does not suggest championship-level strength. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'No specific information about Entropy's or ImmuNe's recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength, or tournament performance is available.' This asymmetric information gap is the core driver of confidence reduction on BOTH sides. We are estimating market prices, not underlying truth. BO1 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-1 matches are inherently volatile and sample-size dependent. This format reduces the predictive power of form-based analysis and elevates randomness. However, this volatility affects BOTH teams equally \u2014 it does not swing the probability decisively in either direction. MARKET PRICING AS SIGNAL: A 62% NO price (vs. 38% YES) in a data-poor environment is noteworthy. Esports prediction markets on niche C-Tier tournaments are typically bet by informed community members with access to regional tournament data, scrim results, and roster knowledge. The market's 24-point spread suggests ImmuNe has demonstrable advantages that the briefing does not surface. OFFLINE TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Parken is a Danish offline event. ImmuNe's potential home-region advantage (if Danish-based or EU-based with lower travel friction) could explain market pricing. Entropy's travel logistics are unknown but represent a potential disadvantage in an unfamiliar venue. ENTROPY'S TOURNAMENT STANDING WEAKNESS: At 6th place in Group A with a +3 round differential, Entropy is not tracking as a top-4 team in this tournament. While tournament placement mid-tournament is not fully predictive, it suggests ImmuNe (if higher-placed) has accumulated more consistent wins. NO REVERSALS VISIBLE: The briefing contains no injury reports, roster changes, disqualifications, or other catalysts that would explain a sudden ImmuNe collapse. The underdog (Entropy) would need to execute flawlessly in a single map against a favorite with hidden form advantages \u2014 a low-probability scenario. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes is 28 (low) because Entropy's only visible edge (a 2-1 record elsewhere) is thin and does not counter the market's 62% ImmuNe price. confidence_no is 35 (also low) because the briefing provides no actual data on ImmuNe's strengths \u2014 we are trusting market consensus in a data-void. Neither side can be assessed with high confidence, but NO's market premium suggests structural information advantages. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: A 62 probability_score directly mirrors the market's NO price, reflecting the maxim that well-informed esports betting markets often price information correctly when data is sparse. The market premium for ImmuNe is treated as a credible signal absent contradicting evidence in the briefing.", "key_factor": "ImmuNe's market pricing to 62% reflects either superior recent form, roster strength, or head-to-head advantage not visible in the briefing data \u2014 a signal that institutional knowledge favors ImmuNe despite the information vacuum.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR ENTROPY (YES): Entropy demonstrated a 2-1 record in PROJECT V 2026 Split 2 Weekly #2, showing they can compete and win matches in organized tournaments. In a BO1 format, single-map variance is high \u2014 one strong map pick or preparation can swing the result. BO1 VOLATILITY: Best-of-1 matches are inherently unpredictable compared to longer series. The briefing offers NO head-to-head data, meaning historical matchups do not constrain the outcome. A single map eliminates comeback potential and maximizes the impact of preparation, anti-strat execution, and day-to-day form. DATA ASYMMETRY & MARKET MISPRICING: The briefing explicitly states ImmuNe has NO performance data or context in search results. The market may be pricing NO at 62% on name recognition, assumption of strength, or default bias rather than on concrete evidence. Entropy at least has a documented recent win-record. FAVORITE'S HIDDEN WEAKNESS: ImmuNe's lack of data could indicate they are a newer roster, lesser-known squad, or have not competed in tracked tournaments recently. The absence of evidence is not evidence of strength. A team with no public form data is harder to assess \u2014 they could be vulnerable if underprepared for an offline event. ENTROPY'S DEMONSTRATED FORM: Entropy went 2-1 in recent tournament play, including wins against tournament-level opposition. This is the only concrete performance signal in the briefing for either team. In the absence of counter-evidence for ImmuNe, Entropy's documented competitiveness is valuable. OFFLINE TOURNAMENT LOGISTICS: The match is offline in Denmark. If ImmuNe is based outside Denmark or Europe, travel fatigue, unfamiliar LAN environment, or preparation disruption could disadvantage them. No roster location data is provided, but this remains a possible edge for a locally-based or better-prepared Entropy. MARKET PRICING AS SIGNAL, NOT PROOF: YES at 38% reflects market consensus, but with only $2,260 in volume and no expert commentary in the briefing, this price may be thin and reactive rather than informationally efficient. The 62/38 split does not prove ImmuNe is stronger \u2014 it reflects uncertainty with a slight lean. CONFIDENCE CAPS DUE TO DATA SCARCITY: Confidence on both YES and NO sides is capped below 40 because the briefing provides insufficient concrete evidence for either team \u2014 no roster info, head-to-head records, recent form for ImmuNe, or tournament seeding context. The probability score of 42 reflects a slight lean toward Entropy based on documented recent wins, but this is a weak signal in a high-variance BO1. REALISTIC UPSET NARRATIVE: Entropy, having proven they can win recent matches, faces an ImmuNe team with zero documented performance context. In a single-map format, Entropy's preparation, map pool advantage, or in-game execution could prevail. The market may have overweighted ImmuNe's name or underweighted BO1 volatility. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 42 reflects YES slightly below the market underdog baseline (38%) because the briefing does not provide strong positive evidence for Entropy beyond a single recent tournament record, nor does it provide disqualifying evidence against ImmuNe. A BO1 with no head-to-head data and limited form visibility deserves near-parity pricing; Entropy's 2-1 record nudges it marginally above 40, but not confidently so.", "key_factor": "BO1 format inherently favors upset potential, and Entropy's recent 2-1 tournament record demonstrates competitive capability against tournament opposition.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head history, recent form differential, roster strength comparison, or player-level metrics available for either Entropy or ImmuNe. BO1 FORMAT INHERENT UNPREDICTABILITY: Best-of-1 matches in esports exhibit high variance due to single-map dependency, minimal adaptation opportunity, and map-veto luck. Historical BO1 outcomes deviate significantly from skill-based BO3 predictions. ENTROPY MARGINAL SIGNAL: Entropy Gaming shows 2-1 record (42-39 rounds, +3 RD) in Parken Group A pool play. This is a weak positive signal (slight positive round differential) but within noise margins for C-Tier competition. No external recent form data provided. IMMUNE NO DATA: ImmuNe absent from provided tournament standings and search results. Cannot assess relative skill, recent trajectory, or roster composition. Complete informational asymmetry. CURRENT MARKET PRICE (38% YES / 62% NO) implies ImmuNe favored by ~24 percentage points. This pricing may reflect:\n  (a) Public/betting community knowledge of ImmuNe's superior current form (not in briefing),\n  (b) Roster strength differences invisible to briefing data,\n  (c) Overweighting of ImmuNe based on historical brand/tournament seeding.\n  Without access to that information, cannot validate or refute the market's confidence in ImmuNe. BASE RATE FOR LOWER-TIER BO1: When team-specific data is unavailable and format is BO1, historical outcomes approximate 50-55% for any given competitive pairing. Market price of 62% NO suggests information asymmetry favoring ImmuNe knowledge. TIME URGENCY (5 hours to resolution): Match is imminent. Substantial roster changes, lineup surprises, or systematic reversals are unlikely at this stage. Market price reflects likely informed consensus. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are LOW (~26-28) because the briefing lacks the foundational data required to distinguish skill differentials. The 38/62 split appears to embed external information (likely from esports betting markets, team rankings, or roster data) not present in the document. Confidence asymmetry is minimal because we are equally blind to both teams' true strength. ASSESSMENT: Without roster, head-to-head, or recent form data, probability_score regresses toward 50. Market price of 38 YES / 62 NO suggests ImmuNe is preferred by available-but-unshown information. Modest adjustment to 45 (slightly favoring NO's market consensus) reflects low-confidence acceptance of market signal, balanced against BO1 volatility.", "key_factor": "In lower-tier CS2 BO1 matches (C-Tier, Valve Tier 2), outcomes are highly volatile. Historical base rate for favored teams in BO1 formats is ~55-60% win probability, but with minimal roster/form data, reversion to ~50% is warranted. BO1 inherent variance is ~\u00b115% around any predicted baseline.", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects extreme information asymmetry \u2014 briefing provides Entropy's recent record (2-1, +3 RD in tournament) but ZERO data on ImmuNe's performance, roster, or history. Entropy appears in tournament standings (6th place, 2-1 record) with measurable form; ImmuNe is completely absent from briefing \u2014 market may be pricing ImmuNe's unknown status as weakness rather than genuine competitive assessment. BO1 format inherently high-variance; with no head-to-head data, map pool compatibility unknown, and no roster information for either team, the 62% confidence in ImmuNe appears overconfident rather than data-driven. Rational apathy detected: market has settled on a price but lacks the information density to justify the 24-point spread. This is crowd consensus with low conviction, not a well-informed market. Entropy's tournament presence (measurable performance vs. ImmuNe's invisibility in briefing) could justify slight YES lean, but confidence in both sides must remain very low due to critical data gaps. No recent news, no roster changes, no player-level analysis \u2014 market is pricing largely on availability bias (Entropy visible in standings) rather than true competitive strength assessment. With ~5 hours to match start and no new information likely to emerge, current price reflects static sentiment rather than informed trading. Either team could easily reverse this with a BO1 upset. Confidence scores capped at 28/25: insufficient data on either side to support strong conviction. Both confidence levels remain depressed due to missing ImmuNe context and lack of H2H intelligence.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "Market currently prices YES (Entropy) at 38%, which is below even-money; this suggests modest sentiment favoring ImmuNe despite lack of ImmuNe performance data in briefing. Entropy Gaming appears in the provided group standings with a 2-1 record and +3 round differential (42-39), placing them 6th in a 8-team group\u2014mid-table performance, not dominant. No ImmuNe data exists in briefing; cannot assess roster quality, recent form, map pool, or head-to-head history; this asymmetry is critical in a BO1 where preparation and meta-read matter enormely. BO1 format in Counter-Strike is inherently volatile; single-map outcomes hinge on veto strategy, map comfort, and day-to-day form variation; round differential from group play (Entropy +3) is weak predictor for BO1. Offline Danish tournament context: Entropy may have logistical advantage if based in region; ImmuNe's location unknown, but travel burden could affect performance in BO1 (less time to adapt than BO3). Parken Challenger #4 is C-Tier (lowest professional tier); both teams are regional/semi-professional level; performance variance is higher and roster stability lower than tier-1 circuits. Group stage performance (2-1 record) places Entropy in knockout contention but not favorites; mid-table seed status does not indicate BO1 match advantage. Briefing explicitly notes 'limited relevant information' and 'no specific information about Entropy's or ImmuNe's recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength'; both sides of market are under-informed. Event timing is TODAY with ~5 hours to resolution; shares will likely trade toward $0.01 or $0.99 shortly before match if predictive power consolidates, but briefing data is too sparse to justify high confidence in either direction now. Confidence_yes=28 and confidence_no=26 reflect symmetric uncertainty: Entropy has marginal group-stage data (slight positive signal) but ImmuNe is a complete unknown (negative data quality, not necessarily a weak team). Probability_score=42 places Entropy as slight underdog in current market pricing; reasoning: Entropy's +3 RD is modest, BO1 favors unpredictability, and ImmuNe's absence from briefing prevents confident dismissal of their strength.", "key_factor": "BO1 format inherently inflates variance and reduces predictive power compared to BO3; Entropy's modest +3 round differential in group play suggests marginal edge but insufficient data on ImmuNe makes confidence asymmetrically weak on both sides.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "The briefing is conspicuously silent on ImmuNe's roster, recent form, and head-to-head history \u2014 a major data gap that prevents confident assessment of NO probability despite market pricing at 62%. Entropy appears in the tournament standings (2-1 record, +3 round differential), suggesting baseline competitive participation, but the table formatting is corrupted and provides no clarity on map pools, player lineups, or performance trajectory. BO1 format dramatically amplifies the variance of single-map outcomes; roster changes, tactical surprises, and map-specific expertise become disproportionately powerful \u2014 a factor often underpriced in low-information markets. This is a C-Tier Danish offline tournament with minimal mainstream coverage; roster churn, last-minute stand-ins, and logistical friction (travel, accommodation, practice time) are commonplace in regional Tier 2 CS2 and rarely reported in advance. The market prices Entropy at 38% despite it being the only team with ANY documented recent performance in the briefing (Glacial Guardians beat Entropy, but at least Entropy has a track record); ImmuNe has zero data points, yet the market assigns it 62% \u2014 possible sign of informed betting, but equally consistent with casual pricing on an underdog. Key absence: no information on whether either team has qualified for next rounds or is playing for pride/seeding; motivation asymmetry in Tier 2 tournaments can swing BO1 outcomes by 15\u201320 percentage points. Black swan scenario: ImmuNe's primary rifler or IGL is unavailable (visa delay, illness, family emergency common in regional tournaments), forcing a sub with inferior calibration to the team's usual antistrat pool \u2014 Entropy's 42 rounds in three matches suggest grindy, methodical gameplay that exploits such misalignment. Inverse risk: Entropy's 2-1 record masks a volatile form trajectory (e.g., beat weak opponents, lost to top seed); brief briefing data precludes trend analysis. Market volume ($2,260) is low for a live event in 5 hours, suggesting limited arbitrage activity and potential mispricing on either side.", "key_factor": "ImmuNe fields a substitute player or experiences a last-minute roster disruption that goes unreported until match start, offsetting Entropy's apparent competitive edge in the limited available data.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.44160000000000005, "no_score": 0.5512437810945274, "edge": 0.06660000000000005, "no_edge": -0.07375621890547257, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 55% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1928473", "question": "Counter-Strike: Entropy vs ImmuNe (BO1) - Parken Challenger Championship Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between Entropy and ImmuNe in the Parken Challenger Championship Group A, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Entropy\" if Entropy win the match against ImmuNe.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ImmuNe\" if ImmuNe win the match against Entropy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 2260.244854, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Parken Challenger Championship #4 is an offline Danish CS2 tournament organized by New Breed Agency and Esplay.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2", "| # | Team | Matches | Rounds | RD | Round 1 | Round 2 | Round 3 |\n ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| 1.", "| Sissi State Punks Sissi State Punks | 3-0 | 26-10 | +16 | To Be Determined | ALTERNATE aTTaX EVO Split | TwoFace Gaming Lotus |\n| 2.", "| TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer\") | 3-0 | 28-22 | +6 | To Be Determined | Reveal Multigaming Bind | Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Bind |\n| 3.", "| Glacial Guardians Glacial Guardians\") | 2-1 | 40-30 | +10 | Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Bind | Dortmund eSports Breeze | Exceptional GamingExceptional Gaming Haven |\n| 4.", "| Reveal Multigaming Reveal Multigaming | 2-1 | 35-29 | +6 | Ingenious EsportsIngenious Esports Lotus | TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer Bind | REH Gaming Haven | [...] | 4.", "| TeamOrangeGaming TeamOrangeGaming | 2-1 | 36-30 | +6 | Dortmund eSports Lotus | Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Split | ALTERNATE aTTaX EVO Lotus |\n| 6.", "| Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Entropy Gaming | 2-1 | 42-39 | +3 | Glacial Guardians Bind | TeamOrangeGaming Split | TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer Bind |\n| 7.", "| THE ONETHE ONE THE ONE\") | 2-1 | 37-35 | +2 | TwoFace Gaming Bind | Exceptional GamingExceptional Gaming Pearl | Ranglistenspieler Haven |\n| 8."], "news_summary": "The search results contain limited relevant information about the Counter-Strike: Entropy vs ImmuNe matchup at Parken Challenger Championship Group A. The results primarily reference Parken Challenger Championship #4 as a C-Tier offline Danish CS2 tournament, along with unrelated VALORANT and Dota 2 competition data. No specific information about Entropy's or ImmuNe's recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength, or tournament performance is available in the provided search results.", "side_yes_case": ["Entropy Gaming demonstrated competitive performance in recent tournaments (2-1 record in PROJECT V 2026 Split 2 Weekly #2)", "Limited information prevents confident assessment of either team's weakness"], "side_no_case": ["ImmuNe lacks any performance data or context in the search results", "No comparative strength indicators between the two teams available"], "key_context": ["Parken Challenger Championship #4 is a C-Tier Valve Tier 2 offline Danish CS2 tournament", "Match format is Best of 1 (BO1), which favors unpredictability and reduces sample consistency", "No recent head-to-head record or direct comparison data between Entropy and ImmuNe available", "Search results lack roster information, recent form, or player strength indicators for either team", "Tournament is offline in Denmark, potentially affecting team travel/preparation logistics"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T11:47:16.621994Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T17:10:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-11T14:27:43.689018+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "0ccbc74f-aa33-4850-868c-06ba8d5da2a7", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T11:54:09.157421+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1928479", "question": "Counter-Strike: \u00d8lgod Efterskole vs Team Eclipse (BO1) - Parken Challenger Championship Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between \u00d8lgod Efterskole and Team Eclipse in the Parken Challenger Championship Group B, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"\u00d8lgod Efterskole\" if \u00d8lgod Efterskole win the match against Team Eclipse.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Eclipse\" if Team Eclipse win the match against \u00d8lgod Efterskole.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.675, "volume_usd": 2138.6352159999997, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no head-to-head records, current roster compositions, recent match results, or comparative skill assessments for either \u00d8lgod Efterskole or Team Eclipse. \u00d8LGOD EFTERSKOLE EVIDENCE: Limited to departing player Nikodeon (July 2025) and fragmented historical results from lower-tier tournaments; no current roster data or recent performance metrics. TEAM ECLIPSE EVIDENCE: Virtually absent from briefing; no tournament results, player history, or competitive track record provided. MARKET PRICE ANOMALY: Current market pricing (68% YES / 32% NO) significantly favors \u00d8lgod Efterskole, but briefing provides no factual basis for this confidence differential. FORMAT RISK: Best-of-1 format (single map) introduces higher variance and reduces predictability compared to best-of-3; outcome less dependent on overall team strength. TIMING: Match occurs TODAY (~5 hours from data timestamp); no recent roster updates, injury reports, or pre-match analysis available in briefing. RESOLUTION CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous regarding win/loss determination; 50-50 resolution only applies to cancellation, ties, forfeits, or delays >7 days. INFERENCE CONSTRAINT: Cannot reasonably infer team strength from Nikodeon's departure alone or from \u00d8lgod's historical online tournament results; Team Eclipse's absence from briefing prevents any comparative assessment. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: Both confidence scores set to 25 (low) because briefing data is insufficient to distinguish YES from NO probability with any statistical validity. Market pricing suggests external information not captured in briefing.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data on either team's current roster, recent form, or head-to-head history prevents reliable probability estimation; market price (68% YES) appears to reflect information not present in the briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "YES CASE (FAVORED SIDE): \u00d8lgod Efterskole has documented professional history \u2014 Nikodeon played for the org in B/C-tier tournaments before joining MOUZ NXT, indicating the team has fielded competitive players and has tournament experience in organized structures like Parken. YES CASE: Market at 68% suggests consensus favors \u00d8lgod, likely based on organizational track record and presence in multiple tournaments (CCT, European Pro League, ESL Challenger League). The team's name appears in multiple tournament records from early 2026, signaling active participation. YES CASE: Team Eclipse has zero detectable competitive history in briefing \u2014 no tournament results, no player names, no tier classification. This asymmetry alone justifies modest YES bias; absence of evidence for Eclipse is weak evidence against them. NO CASE (UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES): \u00d8lgod's recent form is concerning \u2014 results show primarily 0-2 and 1-2 placings across B/C-tier online tournaments (Feb-Mar 2026). No wins documented in last 2 months before April 10. NO CASE: Nikodeon's July 2025 departure to MOUZ NXT suggests roster turnover and potential loss of a capable player. Current roster composition unknown; we cannot verify if replacement-level talent filled the gap. NO CASE: BO1 format introduces high variance \u2014 single-map eliminations reduce skill predictability. Even a favored team faces ~30-40% upset risk in BO1 against unknown opponents. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides zero information on Team Eclipse \u2014 no tournament history, no roster, no ranking tier. This is NOT evidence Eclipse is weak; it is evidence of insufficient data to evaluate them. Confidence_no is depressed due to this asymmetry, not because Eclipse is demonstrably strong. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Current rosters for BOTH teams are unknown as of briefing date (April 10, 2026 11:53 UTC). Match occurs in ~5 hours. Roster stability and player availability cannot be verified. MARKET CALIBRATION: 68% YES pricing appears reasonable given \u00d8lgod's prior competitive activity vs. Eclipse's complete invisibility in records. However, \u00d8lgod's recent 0-2 form pattern and roster turnover justify moderate compression from 68% toward 60-65%. REVERSAL RISK: For NO to win, Eclipse must overcome organizational obscurity and either \u00d8lgod must collapse significantly OR Eclipse must possess hidden depth. BO1 variance allows this, but \u00d8lgod's established tournament presence is a meaningful structural advantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes (58) because \u00d8lgod's documented history and Eclipse's absence creates a defensible case for YES. Low confidence_no (45) because Eclipse's competitive standing is entirely unknown \u2014 cannot credibly argue against a phantom opponent.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 68% reflects \u00d8lgod Efterskole's established competitive history and prior professional roster depth, but recent departures and inconsistent form warrant downward adjustment.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "ASYMMETRIC DATA PROBLEM: The briefing contains fragmented tournament history for \u00d8lgod Efterskole but ZERO concrete information about Team Eclipse's recent form, roster, or competitive standing. This asymmetry alone suggests YES pricing may reflect name recognition rather than evidence-based strength. \u00d8LGOD'S RECENT FORM IS WEAK: The available tournament data shows \u00d8lgod Efterskole's recent results (Feb-Mar 2026) are predominantly losses: 0-2 in CCT #16, 0-2 in CCT #15, 0-2 in ESL Challenger League, 1-2 in multiple events. This is not 'professional-caliber' form for a B/C-tier team entering a tournament favored at 68%. ROSTER DESTABILIZATION CONFIRMED: Nikodeon (a player from \u00d8lgod's history) departed to MOUZ NXT in July 2025. The briefing provides no current roster for \u00d8lgod Efterskole post-July 2025, indicating potential roster turnover or weakening at a critical juncture. BO1 FORMAT AMPLIFIES VARIANCE: A best-of-1 match (single map) has significantly higher upset potential than BO3. With minimal preparation differences, map-specific comfort and RNG elements matter more. The 68% YES price does not adequately discount this variance. TOURNAMENT TIER & CONTEXT: Parken Challenger is a C-tier online tournament (per briefing). Both teams are at or below professional-tier competition. The price gap (68% vs 32%) is large for a matchup where neither team has demonstrated consistent dominance in recent months. ECLIPSE'S ABSENCE = RISK, NOT PROOF: The briefing states 'Limited information on Team Eclipse's competitive history or performance' and 'No evidence of Team Eclipse's recent tournament results.' This is presented as a weakness, but the absence of evidence is NOT evidence of weakness. Team Eclipse could be: (a) an emerging roster with fresher form, (b) a team with different online/LAN profiles, or (c) a squad that has simply not been indexed in the available search results. Without HEAD-TO-HEAD records, the 68% YES pricing assumes \u00d8lgod's historical participation alone confers dominance. BETTING MARKET BIAS: At $2,139 USD volume, this is a low-liquidity market. The YES side at 68% may reflect casual bettors favoring a 'known' Danish team name (\u00d8lgod Efterskole) over an unfamiliar opponent (Team Eclipse), rather than substantive competitive analysis. UNDERDOG ARGUMENT: Team Eclipse's true competitive level is unknown. If Eclipse has: (1) a stable, motivated roster, (2) better map-pool discipline, or (3) stronger recent online form (unmeasured in briefing), they could exploit \u00d8lgod's visible inconsistency and post-Nikodeon roster questions. At 32% implied odds, Eclipse is undervalued if they have even marginally equal or superior preparation. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK: The event is TODAY (5 hours to match start). At this stage, almost no new information will emerge. The market is pricing on historical data and team reputation alone. For a BO1 match between two low-tier teams with asymmetric transparency, the 68-32 split likely overweights the 'known' team. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 35 because \u00d8lgod's recent tournament results are objectively poor (frequent 0-2 outcomes), but we lack Eclipse roster/form data to confirm they are better. confidence_no = 42 because Eclipse's complete absence from the briefing creates meaningful uncertainty \u2014 they could be strong, but we have no proof. Neither side can be assessed with high confidence; the briefing is too sparse to justify >60% confidence on either outcome.", "key_factor": "Team Eclipse's competitive record and roster composition remain entirely absent from the briefing, making the 68% YES pricing potentially overconfident in \u00d8lgod Efterskole without comparative data.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head records, current rosters, recent form comparisons, or ranking data provided for either team. TEAM ECLIPSE: Entirely absent from briefing search results \u2014 no tournament history, player information, or competitive tier classification available. This is a major asymmetry in available information. \u00d8LGOD EFTERSKOLE: Confirmed active C-tier competitor (Nikodeon played for them), but recent results show inconsistent performance (mostly 0-2, 1-2 placings in Feb-Mar 2026). Key player Nikodeon departed July 2025, suggesting potential roster degradation. BO1 VARIANCE: Best-of-1 format inherently has higher variance than BO3; upsets are more probable. This reduces confidence in any probabilistic prediction. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES at 68% implies confidence \u00d8lgod Efterskole is favored, but this price may reflect incomplete information on both sides rather than strong fundamental data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Parken Challenger Championship Season 4 Group B Lower Bracket Round 1 suggests both teams are seeded into lower bracket \u2014 neither has strong recent tournament performance implied by this placement. BASE RATE FOR UNKNOWN MATCHUPS: When head-to-head records, rosters, and recent form are absent for both competitors in a BO1, the true underlying probability is often closer to 50% than market prices suggest. Market may be anchored by asymmetric public information or registration seeding. ASSYMETRIC CONFIDENCE: High uncertainty on BOTH sides due to missing data. Confidence_yes=28 reflects inability to justify the 68% market price with provided evidence. Confidence_no=26 reflects inability to confidently argue against it given the Team Eclipse information void. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event is TODAY (~5 hours). No reversal opportunity; market will resolve imminently. This timing does not increase or decrease probability but does lock in uncertainty. CONCLUSION: Probability set near 52% (slight YES lean matching market) but with LOW confidence on both sides. This reflects the briefing's fundamental data insufficiency, not confidence in the 68% market price.", "key_factor": "In BO1 Counter-Strike matches between lower-tier teams with unknown head-to-head history, the market price typically reflects a slight favorite (+/- 5-15% from 50%) based on registration seeding or recent ranking data not available in this briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost no actionable intelligence on either team's current roster, recent form, or head-to-head history\u2014the two inputs most predictive of CS2 match outcomes. ROSTER INSTABILITY SIGNAL IGNORED: Nikodeon (\u00d8lgod's known player) departed July 2025; briefing suggests potential weakening, yet market prices YES at 68% with conviction. This disconnect suggests crowd may be overweighting historical brand recognition rather than current squad composition. TEAM ECLIPSE BLACKOUT: Zero competitive history, tournament results, or roster data in briefing for the NO side. Market is pricing Team Eclipse at only 32% despite complete information asymmetry\u2014suggests crowd confidence in YES is emotional rather than evidence-based. BO1 FORMAT HIGH VARIANCE: Single-map match outcome is inherently volatile and map-dependent; 68% confidence in either team is arguably overconfident given missing tactical/veto data and unknown map pools for both rosters. LOWER-TIER TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: C-tier online event in Group B (early bracket) with only $2,139 USD volume\u2014low liquidity and shallow participant pool. Price may reflect casual/small-sample betting rather than professional sharp consensus. APATHY PATTERN: Market has priced a 36-point spread (68 vs 32) on a match where the briefing provides near-zero comparative player strength data. This suggests crowd filled a vacuum with assumptions rather than reasoned analysis. NO RECENCY BIAS CORRECTION: Last confirmed \u00d8lgod roster data is from July 2025 (9 months old); no recent tournament results provided for either team in 2026. Market may be anchoring on outdated information. SYMMETRIC UNCERTAINTY: Both teams lack sufficient briefing data for confident differentiation. True probability likely closer to 50-55% than the current 68%, suggesting YES side is overpriced by crowd consensus rather than sharps. REVERSAL PRESSURE: With ~5 hours to resolution, any new roster roster news or format/bracket clarification would move market sharply; early crowd-driven pricing leaves room for correction if information surfaces.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "BO1 FORMAT VARIANCE: Single-map matches in CS2 carry ~50% inherent volatility due to map veto randomness, economic variance, and round-to-round momentum swings\u2014this structural uncertainty floor should cap confidence scores well below 70% on either side. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: No current roster information, head-to-head records, map pool compatibility, or recent 2026 performance data for either team exists in briefing. This is a data-void scenario, not a data-asymmetry scenario. NIKODEON DEPARTURE SIGNAL (WEAK): Loss of a proven B/C-tier player (Nikodeon to MOUZ NXT, July 2025) suggests \u00d8lgod Efterskole may have weakened, but this is ~9 months old and provides no information on current roster acquisition or performance trajectory. \u00d8LGOD EFTERSKOLE INCONSISTENCY: Historical results from early 2026 (Jan\u2013Mar) show pattern of 0-2 and 1-2 placings in lower-tier tournaments, indicating recent form weakness, but sample size is small and tournament tier context unclear. TEAM ECLIPSE OPACITY: Zero credible information on Team Eclipse's history, roster, tier level, or recent results. Cannot meaningfully assess relative strength. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 68% reflects belief in \u00d8lgod Efterskole despite data poverty, likely driven by name recognition or community perception rather than hard metrics. This inflated confidence is not justified by briefing. TIMING: Match resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY, IMMINENT). No time for roster verification, pre-match analysis, or team confirmations. Late-arriving roster changes or forfeits remain possible. RESOLUTION RULE RISK: Match scheduled as BO3 per KEY FACTS (Best of 3, LAN) but market description states BO1. Possible format mismatch or briefing error introduces low-probability but high-impact ambiguity.", "key_factor": "Best-of-1 format introduces extreme variance (~50% inherent volatility) that dominates outcome prediction; roster composition and recent form data are critically unavailable, making statistical confidence in either direction unreliable.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Zero head-to-head history, current rosters unknown, and no comparative recent form data for Team Eclipse \u2014 this is a coin-flip market masquerading as 68-32. ROSTER DECAY SIGNAL: Nikodeon's departure to MOUZ NXT in July 2025 is ~9 months old; \u00d8lgod's post-July performance is completely absent from briefing, suggesting either dormancy or untracked roster churn. ASYMMETRIC INFO ABSENCE: The briefing contains \u00d8lgod's old tournament results (Feb-Mar 2026) but ZERO recent results for Team Eclipse \u2014 absence of evidence for Eclipse does not equal evidence of weakness; could indicate they are new/reformed team with fresh signings. BO1 VOLATILITY: Single-map format in a C-tier challenger tournament introduces 15-20% upset probability floor; meta shifts, map vetoes, or anti-meta picks are impossible to detect without current team data. SILENT RECONSTRUCTION RISK: