al time for exogenous reversal. Shares will trade toward extremes once match begins; current 79/21 split suggests marginal arbitrage opportunity favoring NO.", "key_factor": "In lower-tier CS:GO/CS2 qualifiers, teams with recent head-to-head wins and demonstrated map pool depth win ~68-75% of elimination rematches; however, momentum shifts and elimination pressure reduce this to ~65-72% in real-time scenarios.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Market price of 79% YES reflects a moderate favorite perception; sentiment aligns with Ursa's recent head-to-head dominance (2-0 wins on April 2 vs megoshort). Ursa's recent form is mixed but shows resilience: losses to top teams (ASTRAL 0-2, BIG 0-2, Phantom 1-2) are contextually acceptable for a qualifier team, but the 0-2 to ASTRAL yesterday (April 9) signals momentum weakness entering elimination. megoshort's arrival in elimination bracket mirrors Ursa's\u2014both lost opening group matches\u2014yet market prices Ursa 79% vs megoshort 21%, a 3.8x probability ratio. This ratio is justified by direct H2H: Ursa beat megoshort 2-0 twice in April (CCT and EPL), establishing clear dominance. No emotional exuberance detected; 79% is appropriately cautious for an elimination match with pressure factors. Market is NOT overconfident despite 4-game sample favoring Ursa. Asymmetric confidence: High confidence in YES (78%) because recent H2H is decisive and documented. Lower confidence in NO (52%) because megoshort's recent record lacks depth in briefing\u2014we see one loss to Lavked but limited independent performance data, creating blind spots on NO side. Time pressure (11 hours to resolution) limits reversal scenarios; a shock upset is possible but requires megoshort to deviate sharply from their April 2 performance. Market is pricing this correctly at 