e_no_case": ["Ursa just suffered a 0-2 loss to ASTRAL in their opening match, showing vulnerability on April 9", "Ursa's recent form is inconsistent with losses to BIG (0-2), Phantom (1-2), and multiple ESL/CCT losses", "megoshort's elimination position suggests they are still in contention and may be underestimated", "This is an elimination match with high pressure; Ursa has lost elimination matches recently (0-2 to Nemiga on March 25)"], "key_context": ["This is a Group D elimination match in a closed qualifier, so the loser is eliminated from the tournament", "Both teams are already in the lower bracket after losses in their opening matches", "The match is Best of 3 format played online", "Ursa and megoshort have faced each other at least 4 times in March-April 2026 across multiple tournaments", "Scheduled for April 10, 2026 at 10:00 UTC"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T12:09:42.873981Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T23:00:00Z", "winning_side": null, "final_yes_price": 0.5, "checked_at": "2026-04-10T20:40:05.183918+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "dec549e0-cfbd-4fe3-817b-55ec026a602e", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T12:12:19.839927+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1908497", "question": "LoL: Bushido Wildcats vs Team Phoenix (BO3) - TCL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Bushido Wildcats and Team Phoenix in the TCL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 10 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bushido Wildcats\" if Bushido Wildcats win the match against Team Phoenix.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Phoenix\" if Team Phoenix win the match against Bushido Wildcats.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.885, "volume_usd": 3886.6994810000006, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Bushido Wildcats must win the BO3 match against Team Phoenix to resolve YES. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no head-to-head record, recent TCL Regular Season results for either team, or current win-loss standings. Cannot establish which team is favored based on direct evidence. BUSHIDO WILDCATS INDICATORS (WEAK POSITIVE): - Showed 2295 GPM in TCL 2026 Kickoff event, placing them 4th among listed teams (but 3rd/4th tier position) - Misa Esports led Kickoff with 2404 GPM; Bushido's 2295 suggests mid-tier macro play - Roster includes experienced co-owners (HolyPhoenix, Jahrein) with esports/streaming background, suggesting organizational stability - Recent roster additions (April 7 joins) suggest team was being finalized just before this match TEAM PHOENIX INDICATORS (INSUFFICIENT): - Appears in TCL 2026 Spring roster list but zero performance data, recent results, or metrics provided - No Kickoff statistics, no head-to-head record, no win-loss data mentioned - Complete absence of evidence prevents meaningful comparison MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES trading at 88% (~$0.89) suggests strong confidence in Bushido victory, but no corroborating data in briefing justifies this confidence level. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION: Briefing has slightly more structural information about Bushido (roster details, Kickoff performance, ownership) but almost nothing about Team Phoenix's current form or strength. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: gol.gg will be primary source with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. Team names are clear and unambiguous; no resolution risk from name matching. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: In absence of head-to-head data or recent season results, cannot confidently assign >75% to either team. Market pricing at 88% appears speculative. Slight lean to Bushido based on visible organizational experience and Kickoff participation data, but high uncertainty warrants moderate confidence on both sides. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: 45% confidence in YES reflects marginal evidence supporting Bushido (Kickoff stats, roster stability); 35% confidence in NO reflects near-complete data vacuum on Team Phoenix's actual competitive strength. Neither side has sufficient evidence for high confidence.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no head-to-head match history, recent regular season results, or current form data for either team; probability rests on incomplete information about both competitors' actual strength relative to each other.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTHS: Bushido Wildcats achieved 2295 GPM in TCL 2026 Kickoff, a respectable performance placing them in top-tier macro efficiency. This demonstrates solid mid-game resource management and structural play\u2014foundational for BO3 success. YES SIDE STRENGTHS: Roster includes HolyPhoenix and Jahrein as co-owners\u2014both established Turkish esports personalities with credibility and potentially meaningful organizational resources. This suggests stability and competent management, reducing organizational risk factors that plague emerging teams. YES SIDE STRENGTHS: Market pricing at 88% reflects strong consensus. While markets can misprice, 88% on a favored team in a TODAY/IMMINENT event suggests institutional confidence backed by data not fully visible in this briefing (team form, recent scrims, meta alignment, coaching quality). NO SIDE WEAKNESS: Briefing provides virtually no concrete performance data for Team Phoenix in TCL 2026 Spring. Absence of metrics, recent results, or roster-specific analysis creates an information asymmetry favoring the favored side\u2014Wildcats' data exists, Phoenix's does not. NO SIDE WEAKNESS: No head-to-head historical record provided. In a BO3, matchup history and meta familiarity matter. The lack of such data suggests Phoenix either lacks recent competitive matches or underperformed historically, otherwise data would likely surface. UNDERDOG RISK ASSESSMENT: To justify NO at only 12%, Team Phoenix would need significant structural advantages (superior recent form, favorable meta matchup, roster talent advantage) that are entirely absent from briefing. The data gap itself favors Wildcats by default. CAVEAT \u2014 DATA QUALITY: Briefing lacks recent W-L records, current standings, or recent match outcomes for both teams in TCL 2026 Spring. This creates genuine uncertainty. However, the asymmetry (Wildcats data present, Phoenix data absent) marginally favors Wildcats interpretation. TIMING FACTOR: Match is TODAY/IMMINENT (~11 hours to resolution). For YES to fail, Phoenix would need to execute a significant upset with no recent form indicators supporting their case. Reversals in imminent BO3s require clear evidence of underdog strength\u2014none provided. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=72 reflects reasonable backing from Kickoff metrics and roster stability, but tempered by limited Spring-specific data. confidence_no=38 reflects genuine uncertainty about Phoenix's capabilities\u2014the briefing provides almost no counter-case, making it difficult to justify high confidence in a 12% outcome.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 88% reflects strong consensus confidence in Bushido Wildcats, supported by their Kickoff event competitive performance and experienced roster with established esports figures.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (Team Phoenix): The briefing contains virtually no recent performance data, win-loss records, or match results for Team Phoenix in TCL 2026 Spring, despite extensive organizational info. This information vacuum is itself suspicious \u2014 a 12% underdog priced on NO side suggests market undervaluation of uncertainty. CRITICAL DATA GAP: While Bushido Wildcats' Kickoff performance is documented (2295 GPM, multiple match stats, player KDAs), Team Phoenix has no comparable metrics provided. In esports, form volatility is high; absence of data is NOT evidence of weakness. Bushido Wildcats' 2295 GPM ranks 4th in Kickoff event \u2014 solid but NOT dominant. Teams above them (Misa 2404, SU 2298) suggest competitive spread. This is mid-table performance, not championship-tier. Bushido Wildcats roster shows CRITICAL TURNOVER: Top laner Ersin, Jungle, Support, and Head Coach Thallnoss all joined 2026-04-07 \u2014 THREE DAYS BEFORE THIS MATCH. Mid Cengizhan joined 2025-01-19. This is a partially reconstituted roster with minimal practice time together. Co-owners HolyPhoenix and Jahrein bring brand recognition but no guarantee of competitive synergy. New org partnerships (\u0130stanbul Wildcats) in early 2026 suggest operational immaturity. Team Phoenix's longest Kickoff match (56:58 vs Dark Passage) suggests they can execute late-game macro \u2014 not a weakness indicator. High game duration correlates with competitive, close matches, not stomps. NO CONFIDENCE ON EITHER SIDE IS LOW (32-35): Briefing provides insufficient concrete data to evaluate Team Phoenix's current form, recent win rate, or specific player matchups. This is not evidence for Bushido Wildcats; it's an information desert. Market pricing YES at 88% appears driven by organizational brand recognition (HolyPhoenix, Jahrein) and Kickoff participation rather than recent TCL 2026 Spring performance. Hype does not predict BO3 outcomes. BO3 FORMAT VULNERABILITY: Bushido Wildcats' new roster has NOT been tested in a best-of-three series. Single Kickoff matches don't prove BO3 readiness. Team adaptation and draft flexibility under pressure are unknown. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Team Phoenix, if they have stabilized their roster or developed superior draft strategy since Kickoff, can exploit Bushido's integration issues in games 2-3. New teams often improve rapidly mid-season. VERDICT: 28% probability reflects that Bushido Wildcats are more likely to win (their name, org backing, and Kickoff data support this), BUT the 88% market price dramatically overstates confidence. A 76-point gap (88% to 12%) on a BO3 with a THREE-DAY-OLD roster and no recent head-to-head data is aggressive. Team Phoenix deserves 25-35% fair odds. Confidence in NO is not higher (32 vs 28 probability) because Bushido's organizational resources and Kickoff performance do provide edge; confidence in YES is only 35 because the new roster and lack of Team Phoenix data prevent conviction either direction.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of recent Team Phoenix performance data, head-to-head record, and form metrics in the briefing creates asymmetric information favoring the underdog.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no head-to-head history, recent win-loss records, or current season standings for either team. Cannot establish reliable base rate comparison. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: 88% YES (Bushido) represents strong confidence, but this pricing appears driven by market sentiment rather than documented performance differential. BUSHIDO WILDCATS CASE: Single Kickoff metric (2295 GPM) shows competence but is mid-tier\u2014Misa Esports led at 2404 GPM. Roster includes co-owners with esports background (HolyPhoenix, Jahrein) but roster stability is unclear (multiple join dates April 7, 2026, suggesting very recent composition). TEAM PHOENIX CASE: No performance metrics, roster details, or recent match data provided. Complete absence of data prevents reliable confidence in NO probability estimate. RECENCY CONCERN: Bushido Wildcats roster appears newly assembled (April 7, 2026 join dates for 3+ players). This late-season roster change could indicate either reinforcement or mid-season crisis\u2014briefing does not clarify. EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY (~11 hours until resolution). At this late stage, significant reversal would require unexpected forfeiture, disqualification, or technical failure\u2014all low-probability events. Market is likely to lock at current spread unless major external shock occurs. ESPORTS BO3 BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: In TCL, recent 88% prices on favorites typically mean that team has demonstrated clear recent superiority (multi-game sample). Without such data visible in briefing, confidence is substantially reduced. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: High confidence_yes (35) reflects that market has priced Bushido heavily and some organizational backing is evident; low confidence_no (28) reflects almost complete absence of Team Phoenix performance data\u2014cannot confidently defend either scenario. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT: Raw market price (88%) reduced to 62% due to lack of documented performance differential, uncertain roster stability, and insufficient comparative data. Assign meaningful probability to Team Phoenix upset given data vacuum.", "key_factor": "TCL regular season matches: no reliable historical base rate available; esports BO3 favorites (88% implied) typically reflect recent form and roster strength rather than structural advantage", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market priced at 88% YES reflects strong confidence in Bushido Wildcats, but briefing provides minimal direct evidence supporting such extreme certainty. Bushido Wildcats showed 2295 GPM in Kickoff \u2014 solid mid-tier performance, NOT elite (Misa led at 2404). This moderate metric does not justify 88% win probability. Team Phoenix's performance data entirely absent from briefing \u2014 creates dangerous information asymmetry. Market may be overweighting unknown vs. pricing in Team Phoenix's actual competitive strength. Bushido Wildcats roster shows very recent joins (April 7, 2026) for multiple players \u2014 potential coordination/synergy risk not reflected in 88% price. No head-to-head history, recent TCL Regular Season results, or current win-loss records provided. Market appears to be pricing on narrative (veteran co-owners, decent Kickoff stats) rather than hard season data. 88%/12% split is emotionally crowded \u2014 suggests greed-driven consensus rather than analytically balanced view. When briefing lacks comparative data, such extreme prices indicate crowd psychology overconfidence. Counter-signal: Team Phoenix listed in TCL roster but zero performance metrics provided \u2014 could indicate underdog value if Team Phoenix is competitive but under-scouted by market. Reasonable probability for YES should be 60\u201375% given Bushido's moderate Kickoff showing and recent team assembly. 88% reflects emotional overconfidence rather than edge-case evidence. LIVE/IMMINENT timing (11 hours) means reversal requires major upset with minimal time for market correction. Extreme confidence on either side is vulnerable.", "key_factor": "Greed", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "proba