ntle Mates' 'world-class Yoru player marteen' and double-duelist innovation hints at competitive pedigree despite limited data. ROSTER SIGNAL: Mention of Gentle Mates' Yoru specialist marteen and strategic double-duelist composition suggests recent roster stability and tactical sophistication\u2014positive signal absent for Karmine Corp in briefing. BETTING VOLUME & SPREAD: $93k USD volume with 76/24 split reflects moderate confidence, not extreme conviction. 4-point spread (YES + NO = 100%) suggests balanced orderbook without manipulation. REVERSE ENGINEERING MARKET MOVE: A +13pp surge 5 hours pre-match (when information density is highest) is more credible than early-week swings. Gentle Mates' move from ~60% EMA (7-day) to 76% current suggests positive late data, not just betting flow. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence set at 68 (moderately high due to recent momentum & late-game signal), NO confidence set at 35 (very low\u2014insufficient counter-data on Karmine Corp means we cannot justify >40% belief in their win; data parity would demand ~50 on both sides, but asymmetric data quality prevents it). LIVE EVENT RISK: With ~5 hours to match start, reversal to 50-50 requires forfeit/walkover (low probability in organized VCT). Shares will trade to ~$0.99/$0.01 once result is known but before official resolution\u2014market price is quasi-final. ALTERNATIVE HYPOTHESIS: If market is mispricing, it is on the Gentle Mates (YES) side\u2014overweighting late information. However, the synchronized 13pp move and timing suggest this is deliberate re-rating, not noise.", "key_factor": "Market price surge (+13pp in last 6 hours) suggests late information favoring Gentle Mates, likely from pre-match scrims or roster confirmation, but insufficient public data on either team's current stage performance prevents high-confidence assessment.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL DIVERGENCE: YES rose sharply +13pp on Apr 10 19:42 UTC (same day match, ~5 hours before resolution), but the briefing provides ZERO recent performance data, head-to-head history, or current standings for either team\u2014this suggests the market moved on information external to the briefing (team announcements, scrim results, lineup confirmations). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: briefing mentions Gentle Mates' 'double-Duelist approach' and marteen as 'world's best Yoru player,' suggesting confidence in their agent pool diversity; however, no win-loss record, map statistics, or recent form trajectory is provided\u2014this is a red flag for overvaluation based on roster hype rather than performance. KARMINE CORP OPACITY: Karmine Corp receives minimal mention; no roster names, recent results, or tactical tendencies are disclosed\u2014this creates asymmetric risk: if Karmine Corp has form, preparation, or roster advantages (e.g., recent signings, strong map pool), the 24% NO price may severely underweight their chances. TACTICAL META UNKNOWN: the briefing explicitly states 'limited specific information about Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp's current form'\u2014a recent patch, agent nerf (e.g., Yoru changes), or map pool rotation could render marteen's Yoru expertise less valuable than the market assumes. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT MISSING: each group has 6 teams, single round-robin, top 4 advance; the briefing does not reveal standings, playoff implications, or whether either team is already qualified or fighting for survival\u2014this affects motivation, risk-taking, and preparation intensity. VOLATILITY PATTERN: NO side shows 5.3pp/hr volatility (vs YES at 3.0pp/hr); the sharp -14pp swing on Apr 10 19:44 UTC suggests late uncertainty or negative news about Gentle Mates or positive news about Karmine Corp that the briefing does not capture. MODERATE PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: YES at 76% market price reflects strong but not dominant confidence; confidence scores capped at 45/38 because the briefing data is structurally insufficient to justify higher certainty on either side\u2014this is a live match with 5 hours to resolution and NO RECENT MATCH RESULTS for either team. BLACK SWAN VECTOR: Karmine Corp's underdog status (24% price) combined with zero performance disclosure creates a classic low-probability flip scenario\u2014if they are a team on form with a favorable map pool or tactical counter to double-Duelist comps, their true win probability could be 35\u201345%, not 24%.", "key_factor": "Karmine Corp's recent roster stability and tactical preparation (unknown from briefing) decisively outmatches Gentle Mates' double-duelist experimental setup, or a key Gentle Mates player (marteen or bipo) suffers unexpected underperformance due to map pool mismatch or meta shift.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6802873563218391, "no_score": 0.34607929515418506, "edge": -0.07471264367816088, "no_edge": 0.10107929515418507, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1856207", "question": "Valorant: Gentle Mates vs Karmine Corp (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Gentle Mates and Karmine Corp in the VCT EMEA Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 10 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against Karmine Corp.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Karmine Corp\" if Karmine Corp win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T00:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T18:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.755, "volume_usd": 93127.11153500006, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["37700793285201716671638873618148495356677277895795156963859864646833056709542", "87779714902843230246171432547899207995419399799244164744942468600671087644416"]}, "key_facts": ["VCT 2026: EMEA Stage 1 results, upcoming matches, and VODs.", "Group Stage: April 1<sup>st</sup> - May 1<sup>st</sup>, 2026.", "Each Group has 6 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers i