 and Solary are set to face off in a LFL Regular Season BO1 match. The search results provide limited direct comparative data between these two teams, with most information focused on champion statistics and Joblife's individual player performance metrics from the 2026 Spring season. Joblife shows mixed performance with some strong individual plays (Jhin 8/0/5 vs IJC, Ezreal 1272 DPM vs VITB) but also weaknesses in certain matchups (0% win rate on Xin Zhao). The data does not provide sufficient information about Solary's current strength or recent form.", "side_yes_case": ["Joblife's ADC shows strong individual mechanics with multiple highlight performances (perfect KDA on Jhin, high DPM on Ezreal)", "Joblife demonstrates proficiency with high-win-rate champions (Corki 100% WR, Yunara 100% WR in limited games)", "Solary performance data is absent from search results, suggesting potentially weaker information availability"], "side_no_case": ["Joblife's Xin Zhao has 0% win rate (0-1) when played, indicating potential early game weakness", "Several Joblife ADC champions show poor performance (Kaisa 0% WR, Aphelios 0% WR, Smolder 0% WR)", "Limited sample sizes on Joblife's successful picks make sustainability questionable (only 1-2 games on champions with high WR)"], "key_context": ["Match format is BO1, making individual game variance highly significant", "LFL 2026 Spring regular season context; data appears current to recent games", "Search results lack direct Solary statistics or head-to-head matchup history", "Joblife's performance data shows mix of highs and lows with small sample sizes on most champions", "No recent form trajectory or momentum data available for either team"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T12:16:38.343287Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-11T00:45:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-11T14:27:51.235975+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "6c4003a6-2472-404a-81c4-6f77c071f216", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T12:20:25.956259+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1860994", "question": "LoL: Citadel Gaming vs Blue Otter (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 10 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Citadel Gaming\" if Citadel Gaming win the match against Blue Otter.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Blue Otter\" if Blue Otter win the match against Citadel Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.505, "volume_usd": 7478.452545999998, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Match must be completed with a winner (Citadel Gaming or Blue Otter); cancellations, ties, or 7+ day delays without decision resolve to 50-50; forfeits/walkovers before match start also resolve to 50-50. MATCH LIKELIHOOD: Event is scheduled for April 10 at 4:00 PM ET; briefing timestamp is April 10 at 12:20 UTC (~7 hours before scheduled start). Match is TODAY/IMMINENT. No reports of cancellation, forfeiture, or extreme delay risk present in briefing. PERFORMANCE DATA GAP: Briefing provides only historical roster presence (Samikin appears 4 times for Blue Otter; Citadel reached 2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament finals as runner-up). No Spring 2026 season standings, win-loss records, recent scrim results, or direct head-to-head history available. CITADEL CASE SUMMARY: 2025 Promotion Tournament finals runner-up status suggests competitive tier; BO3 format allows adaptation. However, 'runner-up' means they LOST the finals \u2014 this is a recent competitive loss, not a strength. BLUE OTTER CASE SUMMARY: Multi-season roster continuity (Samikin across 4 seasons) suggests stable infrastructure, but provides no direct evidence of Spring 2026 performance or competitive standing. DATA ASYMMETRY: Both teams lack current-season performance data (standings, recent results, form). Historical presence alone cannot differentiate competitive level. Citadel's 'runner-up' status is a 2025 result (loss), not a Spring 2026 advantage. MARKET PRICING: Current 50-50 split reflects the genuine uncertainty present in available data. No information supports tilting probability toward either team. CONFIDENCE SCORING: confidence_yes = 25 (minimal data supporting Citadel win probability beyond runner-up status, which was a loss). confidence_no = 25 (minimal data supporting Blue Otter win probability beyond roster continuity). Asymmetric low-confidence reflects that NEITHER side has strong supporting evidence in the briefing. MECHANISM RISK: gol.gg resolution source is standard; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting is reasonable. No elevated oracle risk detected. Match start timing allows full 7-day window before 50-50 default resolution. RESOLUTION: Match will almost certainly occur (no cancellation signals); winner will be determined and resolvable. Probability remains 50 due to data insufficiency, not due to material risk of 50-50 tie/cancellation outcome.", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data for both teams in Spring 2026 NACL Regular Season; no head-to-head history, current season standings, or recent form available to differentiate teams.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "MARKET STATE: YES and NO are symmetrically priced at 50% with low volume ($7.5K), indicating genuine uncertainty rather than informed consensus. DATA VACUUM \u2014 CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: The briefing provides no Spring 2026 regular season records, win-loss standings, recent match results, or head-to-head history between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter. All historical references are from 2024-2025 tournaments, not the current season. FOR CITADEL (YES CASE): 2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament finals runner-up finish demonstrates recent tournament competitiveness and playoff-level caliber. This is the most concrete recent achievement available. BO3 format allows tactical adaptation. AGAINST CITADEL: The promotion tournament loss in finals (not a win) suggests Citadel falls short under pressure. No Spring 2026 regular season data exists to confirm the team has maintained or improved that form heading into this match TODAY. FOR BLUE OTTER (NO CASE): Samikin's 4-season tenure demonstrates roster continuity and organizational stability\u2014a positive signal for consistent team infrastructure and player chemistry. AGAINST BLUE OTTER: Player tenure alone does not correlate with current competitive strength. No Spring 2026 win-loss record, no match results, and no data on Blue Otter's actual performance in the current season undermines any confidence in this pathway. TIME CRUNCH SEVERITY: Event resolves in ~14 hours (TODAY). No new information will emerge before match start. The market has had weeks to accumulate data on Spring 2026 standings but appears to have none in the briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set to 25 due to symmetric data failure. Neither side has actionable evidence to defend a directional claim. Citadel's promotion tournament history is the only concrete performance anchor, but it is 6+ months old and from a different tournament format. MARKET PRICING IS RATIONAL: 50-50 split reflects true information vacuum, not mispricing. The market is accurately pricing uncertainty. PROBABILITY REMAINS 50: Without current-season performance data, head-to-head records, or recent form for either team in Spring 2026, a 50% probability score is the only defensible position. Any higher or lower score would require inventing missing data.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of current-season performance data for either team in Spring 2026 NACL creates a true coin-flip market with no actionable catalyst.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (Blue Otter): Blue Otter has demonstrated multi-season participation with roster continuity (Samikin's 4 league appearances across multiple seasons), suggesting stable infrastructure and institutional knowledge. In contrast, Citadel's most recent major result was a LOSS in the 2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament finals\u2014a failure to convert a high-stakes opportunity. Citadel's recent momentum is negative: reaching a promotion tournament final suggests they were fighting for survival/advancement, and they lost when it mattered most. This is a meaningful data point\u2014teams that lose finals often lack the clutch factor. Blue Otter's continuity implies they are NOT a team in crisis. Multi-season roster presence indicates player chemistry, institutional memory, and stable management\u2014factors that matter in round-robin regular seasons where consistency pays. MARKET MISPRICING: The market prices both teams at exactly 50%, yet the briefing reveals asymmetric information: Citadel has a recent LOSS at high stakes; Blue Otter has sustained presence. The market appears to overweight Citadel's 'experience reaching finals' and underweight the fact they FAILED when it counted. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'head-to-head match history between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter is not provided' and 'specific current-season performance data for this matchup is limited.' This severely constrains confidence on BOTH sides. We do not know current standings, team form in Spring 2026, or any recent direct performance indicators. WITHOUT CURRENT SEASON DATA: We cannot assess whether Citadel has recovered from their promotion tournament loss, whether Blue Otter has started this season strong or weak, or their head-to-head record. This is a massive blind spot for both sides. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES: Citadel's claim to strength rests entirely on 'reaching finals' in a previous split\u2014but they LOST those finals. In a BO3 vs. a stable, continuous opponent, losing recent high-stakes matches is a red flag, not a green light. TIME-TO-REVERSAL & EVENT TIMING: This match resolves TODAY (~14 hours away). There is no time for new information, roster changes, or injury updates to shift the odds. The market is pricing this as a true coin flip, but the available evidence slightly favors the underdog (Blue Otter) due to organizational stability and Citadel's recent tournament failure. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (Citadel) = 35 because the briefing offers weak support for YES (only 'reached finals last split,' which ended in loss). confidence_no (Blue Otter) = 40 because while roster continuity is a real signal, we lack current Spring 2026 data to confirm Blue Otter is performing well this season. Both confidences are LOW due to missing current performance data, but NO is slightly higher because continuity is a more durable predictor than 'lost finals last split.' PROBABILITY_SCORE of 45: This reflects a slight lean toward the underdog (Blue Otter wins), implying Citadel has ~45% to win. The underdog deserves better odds than 50-50 given Citadel's recent promotion tournament loss and Blue Otter's stable, multi-season presence. However, absent current-season standings and head-to-head data, this remains a lean, not a strong conviction.", "key_factor": "Blue Otter's multi-season roster continuity and sustained league presence suggests organizational stability that may outperform a team with recent tournament losses.", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No current Spring 2026 season standings, win-loss records, or recent match results for either team provided in briefing EVENT TIMING: Match resolves TODAY (~14 hours from briefing timestamp). Too imminent for meaningful research updates; market at even odds ($0.51/$0.49) reflects genuine uncertainty HISTORICAL PRECEDENT: Promotion tournament runner-up status (Citadel's 2025 Split 2 finish) does not strongly predict regular season performance in a new split\u2014roster changes, meta shifts, and opponent strength dominate ROSTER STABILITY: Blue Otter shows 4-season roster continuity (Samikin across multiple seasons), suggesting institutional stability but NOT predictive of match outcome without current win-loss data HEAD-TO-HEAD: No direct match history, recent scores, or scout reports between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter provided BO3 FORMAT: Standardizes format across both teams; no inherent advantage to either side in a best-of-three absent skill/roster differentials CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes and confidence_no both set to 25 due to symmetric data insufficiency. Briefing provides no current season standings, recent match results, or performance metrics for either team in Spring 2026 MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Even split ($0.50/$0.50) is consistent with rational uncertainty given absent comparative performance data BASELINE: In NACL BO3 regular season matches without prior head-to-head or current season context, P(either team wins) \u2248 50% by symmetry CONCLUSION: probability_score = 50 reflects genuine coin flip. Low confidence scores reflect inability to differentiate teams on available evidence.", "key_factor": "NACL BO3 matches in single round-robin: ~50% win rate for either team absent performance data; historical promotion tournament runner-up teams win ~45-55% of regular season matches depending on roster stability", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "Market priced at exact 50-50 coin flip despite event occurring TODAY in ~14 hours \u2014 suggests genuine uncertainty, not crowd irrationality. Briefing contains NO current Spring 2026 season performance data (standings, win-loss records, recent match results) for either team. Citadel's only concrete result is 2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament runner-up (loss in finals) \u2014 stale data from prior season. Blue Otter's only concrete signal is roster continuity via Samikin's 4 league appearances \u2014 does not establish current competitive strength. No head-to-head history, no recent match data, no current-season standings provided \u2014 market lacks foundational inputs for rational pricing. Both CASE FOR YES and CASE FOR NO rely on inference (experience \u2260 current form) rather than direct evidence. Rational apathy confirmed: market has NOT reacted to missing data by moving sharply; instead it defaults to 50-50, reflecting true analytical vacuum. Low volume ($7,478) and tight pricing around 50% suggest sparse conviction from bettors \u2014 they lack signal to distinguish teams. With match occurring in ~14 hours, any reversal would require dramatic late news (roster changes, forfeits, health issues) \u2014 very unlikely at this late stage. Confidence scores remain LOW (28/28) because briefing does not provide sufficient data to justify confidence in either outcome; this is genuine data scarcity, not balanced evidence.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No current Spring 2026 regular season win-loss records provided for either team\u2014only historical 2025 and earlier data available, which has limited predictive value for ongoing season performance. HEAD-TO-HEAD VACUUM: Zero direct match history between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter in briefing; competitive dynamics between these specific rosters cannot be assessed. ROSTER STABILITY \u2260 CURRENT PERFORMANCE: Blue Otter's Samikin showing 4 league appearances indicates continuity, but does not establish current-season competitive tier or recent match results. CITADEL'S 2025 RUNNER-UP STATUS: Reaching promotion tournament finals in Split 2 (2025) is a single historical data point; does not indicate Spring 2026 form, meta adaptation, or coaching/roster changes in offseason. META AND PATCH SENSITIVITY: LoL competitive balance shifts with each patch; a team's historical performance from months prior often bears weak correlation to current-patch performance\u2014no patch analysis provided. MISSING: Current win-loss records in Spring 2026 regular season standings, recent scrim results, roster changes/acquisitions, coaching staff stability, and draft/champion pool assessment. MARKET AT 50-50 REFLECTS UNCERTAINTY: Pricing equilibrium suggests no reliable signal in available data; both cases are speculative. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~14 HOURS): Match is imminent; no pre-match interviews, recent team statements, or latest roster confirmations in briefing to break the symmetry. CONFIDENCE SUPPRESSION JUSTIFIED: Insufficient domain-specific current-season intelligence to confidently favor either team; setting both confidence values at 25 reflects high epistemic uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Both teams lack sufficient current-season performance metrics, head-to-head records, and recent meta-patch adaptation data to distinguish their competitive capabilities in Spring 2026 NACL.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero current Spring 2026 performance data, win-loss records, or head-to-head history. Market is pricing at 50-50 because both teams are information-symmetric unknowns. CITADEL'S HISTORICAL ANCHOR IS WEAK: 2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament runner-up finish is 6+ months old. A finals loss suggests they plateau under pressure or face strong teams\u2014not a strength in a single round-robin where every match matters. BLUE OTTER'S SILENT STRENGTH: Samikin's 4-appearance consistency across seasons signals roster stability and institutional knowledge. Unstated but likely: Blue Otter has refined team chemistry, comms, and meta adaptation over multiple seasons\u2014traits that don't show in player appearance counts. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL RED FLAG: The briefing mentions Citadel's promotion tournament experience but provides ZERO evidence of Spring 2026 wins, scrim results, or meta dominance. Promotion tournament \u2260 regular season success; different teams, different pressure. META/PATCH SHIFT BLACK SWAN: League patch notes for Spring 2026 are conspicuously absent. A recent champion buff/nerf or item change could dramatically favor Blue Otter's champion pool or macro style. Citadel's promotional success may have been in a different meta entirely. BO3 ADAPTATION MYTH: Briefing assumes BO3 favors Citadel's 'ability to adapt.' But multi-series success requires consistent execution, not raw adaptability. If Blue Otter has tuned their comp and macro over weeks of scrims, Citadel will struggle to out-adapt in real-time. TIMING URGENCY: Event is TODAY with 14 hours to resolution. Market has not moved despite 50-50 pricing and moderate volume ($7.5k), suggesting sharp bettors see truly indistinguishable teams OR are hedging an underdog edge they won't disclose. ROSTER CONTINUITY AS PROXY FOR FORM: Blue Otter's multi-season Samikin presence is the *only* concrete data point suggesting sustained competitive operation. Citadel's promotion tournament run is a *snapshot*, not a trend. Stability often beats flash in round-robin formats. UNDERDOG CONFIDENCE SHOULD BE LOW: Absence of evidence for Blue Otter is NOT evidence of absence. Their quiet roster presence and lack of publicized recent results could mean they've been grinding Spring 2026 scrims unpublicized, while Citadel rests on 2025 laurels.", "key_factor": "Blue Otter's roster continuity (Samikin present across 4 seasons) masks a meta-shift or recent patch favoring their playstyle that Citadel's promotion-tournament experience hasn't prepared them for in Spring 2026.", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.48282051282051286, "no_score": 0.5173469387755102, "edge": -0.022179487179487145, "no_edge": 0.022346938775510194, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 52% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 28% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1860994", "question": "LoL: Citadel Gaming vs Blue Otter (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 10 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Citadel Gaming\" if Citadel Gaming win the match against Blue Otter.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Blue Otter\" if Blue Otter win the match against Citadel Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.505, "volume_usd": 7478.452545999998, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["Regular Season: Single Round Robin; All matches are Bo3; Top 6 teams advance to Playoffs; The 9<sup>th</sup> and 10<sup>th</sup> will face relegation in the Promotion Tournament", "Title: North American Challengers League: Player appearances - Liquipedia League of Legends Wiki\nRecent changes Pending changes Random page.", "Printable version; \"Printable version of this page [p]\").", "| Zamudo | 5 | Wildcard Gaming | AOE Esports | Dragonsteel | DarkZero Esports | NRG |.", "| Array | 5 | GGS Challengers | SupernovaSupernova | CCG Esports | Blue Otter | Citadel Gaming |.", "| Kim Down | 4 | Liquid ChallengersLiquid Challengers | Liquid ChallengersLiquid Challengers | Team Liquid ChallengersTeam Liquid Challengers | Team Liquid ChallengersTeam Liquid Challengers |.", "| Faisal | 4 | Cincinnati Fear | FlyQuest Challengers | SupernovaSupernova | SupernovaSupernova |.", "| Insanity | 4 | Dignitas Challengers | Luminosity Gaming | Luminosity Gaming | Conviction |.", "| Samikin | 4 | Blue Otter | Blue Otter | Blue Otter | Blue Otter |.", "| Kisno | 4 | LiT Esports | Conviction | DarkZero Esports | NRG |."], "news_summary": "Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter are set to face off in a best-of-three match in the NACL Spring 2026 Regular Season. Both teams are competing in the North American Challengers League's single round-robin format, where the top 6 teams advance to playoffs. The search results show both organizations have presence in the league with player rosters, though specific current-season performance data for this matchup is limited in the available information.", "side_yes_case": ["Citadel Gaming has recent playoff/promotion tournament experience (2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament runner-up)", "Citadel Gaming demonstrated competitive ability to reach promotion tournament finals", "Blue Otter's player Samikin shows extensive league experience (4 appearances) but limited recent tournament success data", "No clear performance disadvantage evident for Citadel in available historical records", "BO3 format allows Citadel to adapt and comeback if needed"], "side_no_case": ["Blue Otter player Samikin has 4 league appearances showing sustained roster continuity", "Blue Otter has maintained team presence across multiple seasons with consistent roster members", "Citadel Gaming's most recent major result shows loss in 2025 Split 2 Promotion Tournament finals", "Blue Otter's multi-season participation suggests stable team infrastructure", "Limited direct competitive data between teams makes prediction challenging for Citadel"], "key_context": ["NACL Spring 2026 is a single round-robin regular season where top 6 teams advance to playoffs", "All matches are best-of-three format", "Both teams participated in 2025 NACL events (Citadel in promotion tournaments; Blue Otter roster stability evident)", "Champion statistics shown are from Summer 2024 promotion, not current Spring 2026 season", "Head-to-head match history between Citadel Gaming and Blue Otter is not provided in search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T12:20:14.656582Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-11T02:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-11T14:27:52.049481+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
