 and in-match performance in a BO3 format. UNDERDOG CASE (NO - KR\u00dc): KR\u00dc's roster contains proven international talent (saadhak, mwzera, Less) with track records in high-level competitive Valorant, not an anonymous challenger team. UNDERDOG CASE (NO - KR\u00dc): Week 1 Group Stage matches historically breed upsets as Tier 1 teams shake off rust and adjust to tournament conditions; Sentinels may lack synergy if roster changes occurred due to visa issues. UNDERDOG CASE (NO - KR\u00dc): Market pricing (52% YES vs 48% NO) reflects only a modest 4pp margin \u2014 this is a near coin-flip that does NOT strongly support Sentinels dominance. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: Betting odds (1.56-1.72) imply 58-64% win probability for Sentinels, but this contradicts the lower Polymarket price (52%), suggesting professional sportsbooks may be overvaluing Sentinels or underpricing roster disruption risk. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: No detailed match statistics, map pools, or recent head-to-head data provided \u2014 Sentinels' 'established competitive pedigree' is asserted but not evidenced by recent form in the briefing. MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS UNDERDOG: Price has fallen 12.5pp over 7 days (55% \u2192 52% YES), indicating sophisticated traders are moving toward NO; sharp move of -6pp on Apr 10 08:00 UTC suggests material information (likely visa update) triggered selling of YES. PRICE MOVEMENT INTERPRETATION: 24-hour volatility of 2.6pp/hr in a match resolving in ~8 hours is elevated; this reflects genuine uncertainty, not confidence in Sentinels, and suggests market insiders consider the visa issue real and material. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Strong evidence exists for the visa issue (concrete mention) and KR\u00dc's player quality (named roster), but NO confirmation of match delay, roster substitution severity, or specific impact on Sentinels' preparation \u2014 set confidence_yes at 62 (solid but not overwhelming data supporting favorite), confidence_no at 58 (meaningful data for un