rg quality gap may persist. KR\u00dc's international roster (esp. saadhak) brings LAN experience and firepower, but playing on North American server/venue in Week 1 group stage typically favors local orgs with established bootcamp infrastructure. BO3 format and Group Omega stage (implies group-based advancement) suggests match is early elimination round; teams will be pre-prepared for opponent tendencies, reducing chaos factor. Match resolves in ~8 hours; no new roster/visa announcements expected to materially shift odds at this point unless official org statement drops.", "key_factor": "Visa-related roster instability in Week 1 group stage is a material force multiplier for underdog performance, but Sentinels' organizational tier-1 infrastructure and consistent betting consensus (58-64% implied) suggests the disruption is partially priced in by professional oddsmakers.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "VISA ISSUE RED FLAG: The briefing explicitly mentions 'potential visa issues affecting Sentinels' roster composition' \u2014 this is NOT a rumor, it's cited as NEWS SUMMARY material. In esports BO3s, a stand-in player or fractured roster coherence is catastrophic, especially Week 1 when synergy is already fragile. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: YES odds fell 12.5pp over 7 days and -5.5pp in 24 hours, with a sharp -6pp move on Apr 10 08:00 UTC (likely when visa complications became public or confirmed). The market is already pricing in player uncertainty, yet 52% YES still assumes Sentinels execute. One more roster confirmation = steeper drop. KR\u00dc'S PROVEN CORE: saadhak, mwzera, and Less are not randoms \u2014 they're established Brazilian/Latin American Tier 1 competitors with tournament pedigree. In a best-of-3 where Sentinels may be 4v5 or running a sub, KR\u00dc's cohesion advan