ost-match settlement. NO COLLEGIATE TRACK RECORD: Briefing shows only academy/pro teams in standings. Maryville's competitive history, seeding, or recent W-L absent. Impossible to weight odds without baseline competence data. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market priced YES at 60% despite zero supporting data; suggests irrational tilt toward underdog (narrative appeal) rather than rational analysis. If match is LIVE NOW, both confidence scores must drop sharply due to imminent resolution uncertainty. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE LOWER ON NO: Even though 'NRG org > collegiate team' is intuitive, lack of actual LoL roster/performance data means NO case is also speculative. Confidence_no capped at 35 to reflect uncertainty on both sides.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The standings table shows teams like YFP, SaD Esports, QoR, Evil Geniuses Academy, NRG Academy, Alliance Guardians, and Pigeons, but Maryville University and NRG Esports do not appear in the provided standings\u2014this is extremely unusual for a NACL regular season match and suggests the briefing may reference the wrong competition tier or contain incomplete data. NRG ORGANIZATIONAL FACTOR: NRG is a tier-1 esports org with infrastructure, but the briefing only mentions 'NRG Academy' in VALORANT/lower tiers, not a primary NRG LoL roster in NACL\u2014if the match is NRG Academy vs. Maryville, both teams would likely be academy/developmental level, not a professional main roster mismatch. MARYVILLE UNIVERSITY ABSENCE: Maryville University does not appear in the visible NACL standings table; collegiate/university teams rarely compete in professional NACL alongside academy rosters\u2014this suggests either misidentification of the league, a very recent expansion, or data corruption in the briefing. MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: YES (Maryville) is priced at 60%, implying market expects ~40% probability for NRG\u2014this is NOT a typical underdog premium for an amateur team vs. professional org, suggesting the market may have roster/competitive information not in the briefing. VOLATILITY ANALYSIS: Sharp 6-8pp moves on Apr 09-10 correlate with team roster announcements, injury news, or official schedule changes typical 24-48 hours before matches\u2014the briefing provides no such catalyst explanations, indicating missing context. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: The match is scheduled for April 10, 7:00 PM ET (event timing says TODAY, resolves ~9 hours from briefing timestamp Apr 10 19:49 UTC = 3:49 PM ET), meaning the match either occurs within hours or has already begun\u2014the briefing does NOT confirm whether it has started, been postponed, or been canceled. DATA FRESHNESS ISSUE: Briefing timestamp is 2026-04-10 19:49 UTC, but scheduled match time was April 10, 7:00 PM ET (~11:00 PM UTC), which is 3+ hours PAST the briefing timestamp\u2014this suggests either the match has already occurred (outcome unknown to analyst), is in progress, or was postponed. LEAGUE TIER MISMATCH: NACL is a professional/semi-professional league; Maryville University's presence in a NACL regular season would be unprecedented and contradicts standard esports competition structure\u2014either the league name is wrong (e.g., Collegiate LoL competition) or one team name is misidentified. INSUFFICIENT ROSTER DATA: No champion pool, player skill assessments, recent patch adaptation, or head-to-head records are provided for either team\u2014in a BO3 format (first to 2 wins), patch-specific meta knowledge and player mechanics are material factors. MARKET CONFIDENCE SYMMETRY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set LOW (28-32) because the briefing contains material inconsistencies that block reliable probability estimation in either direction; a coin-flip probability of 50 would be appropriate, but the YES price of 60% suggests market participants have external information. RECOMMENDATION: This market exhibits HIGH INFORMATION ASYMMETRY. The briefing data is internally contradictory and incomplete. Any confident probability estimate would require: (1) confirmation of actual team rosters competing, (2) verification of the correct league/competition, (3) real-time match status, and (4) recent head-to-head or form data absent from the briefing.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains a critical data inconsistency: it references a NACL standings table but does NOT list Maryville University or NRG Esports in the visible standings, suggesting either a data extraction error, wrong league tier, or that one/both teams are not primary NACL competitors\u2014this fundamentally undermines probability estimation.", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NACL standings table but neither Maryville University nor NRG Esports appears in the published roster \u2014 suggests both may be academy/lower-tier squads or the standings table is incomplete/outdated. CONTRARIAN SIGNAL: Market has risen +10pp over 7 days (YES strengthening) despite zero new competitive data in briefing \u2014 indicates off-chain information (scrims, roster announcements, or internal intel) driving sentiment rather than match history. SHARP MOVES PATTERN: Three major drops on YES (-6pp, -6pp, -5pp) in last 48 hours; highest volatility on YES side (2.4pp/hr vs 1.4pp/hr NO) suggests genuine uncertainty and late-stage news injection rather than settled expectation. NRG INFRASTRUCTURE PARADOX: NRG is established org but NO evidence of LoL roster strength in briefing \u2014 only NRG Academy mentioned in VALORANT context; main roster may be thin or newly formed, lacking game-ready depth. MARYVILLE COLLEGIATE ANGLE: University teams occasionally outperform academy squads due to fresh scrim prep and less-jaded mentality; if Maryville has scraped together a coherent 5-stack with recent bootcamp, they may exploit overconfidence. PATCH/META WINDOW: Briefing silent on current LoL patch; recent system updates (item rework, jungle changes) can favor certain comp styles; if Maryville prepped for specific meta and NRG is caught mid-adaptation, upset becomes plausible. STAKES ASYMMETRY: Maryville is fighting for relevance (potential relegation bracket team); NRG may be coasting mid-table with playoff spot secured \u2014 motivation gap in Bo3 where mental composure matters. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK: Event resolves in ~9 hours; market at 60% YES reflects genuine 50/50 scenario masked by organizational brand bias toward NRG; last 24hr -8pp drop on YES suggests smart money fleeing overconfidence. RESOLUTION AMBIGUITY: If match begins, forfeiture resolves to 50-50 (not the winner) \u2014 NRG logistics breakdown (transportation, admin error) becomes material risk factor not priced in. COUNCIL BLIND SPOT: Majority analysis likely anchors on 'NRG is professional org vs university team' heuristic without examining actual 2026 NACL roster strength, recent form, or whether NRG even fielded a committed LoL squad for this season.", "key_factor": "NRG roster availability crisis (illness, visa hold, or mid-match substitution of key player) forces academy-level lineup to field against Maryville's prepared roster.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.3743781094527363, "no_score": 0.6409311740890689, "edge": -0.23062189054726367, "no_edge": 0.24593117408906884, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 64% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 35% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1861017", "question": "LoL: Maryville University vs NRG Esports (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Maryville University and NRG Esports in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Maryville University\" if Maryville University win the match against NRG Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"NRG Esports\" if NRG Esports win the match against Maryville University.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to anoth