{"run_id": "78d33f95-10f0-41ba-b1d8-525291092d5e", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T20:03:57.730877+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1867338", "question": "LoL: Nongshim Red Force vs Kiwoom DRX (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Nongshim Red Force and Kiwoom DRX in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 11 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim Red Force\" if Nongshim Red Force win the match against Kiwoom DRX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Kiwoom DRX\" if Kiwoom DRX win the match against Nongshim Red Force.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.675, "volume_usd": 62319.53988000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["109740081789557919093549117082521954019078339223780009562806524433494058923638", "17179002941737906551083495565031501498965867374733821387323277061867404660358"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.4, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "CONDITION: Nongshim Red Force must win the BO3 match vs Kiwoom DRX on 2026-04-11. HEAD-TO-HEAD: In LCK Cup Week 2, DRX won the series 2-1 over Nongshim. DRX won the decisive Game 3 (21-14, 35:30), showing strong late-game execution. TEAM STANDINGS: Kiwoom DRX sits at 45% win rate (15-18 record) in LCK Cup, while Nongshim RedForce is significantly lower at 38% (8-13), a 7-point gap indicating DRX is the stronger team overall. NONGSHIM CASE: Won Game 2 vs DRX (24-17) and has shown BO3 capability (3-2 victories in recent playoffs). However, these were against lower-tier opponents (KT, HLE) in LCL/Academy circuit, not main LCK Cup. DRX CASE: Beat Nongshim in the series decider, demonstrating superior late-game execution and macro play. Higher standing suggests more consistent performance across the tournament. VOLATILITY: Market YES side moved +17.5pp one week ago (Apr 05), suggesting significant confidence shift toward Nongshim. However, 24-hour stability (-1.0pp change) and low volatility (0.4pp/hr) indicate current market has settled after that movement. NO side sharp moves on Apr 05-06 mirror YES side moves inversely, suggesting a singular event drove repricing. DATA GAPS: Match history is from Week 2-3 LCK Cup (mid-April timeframe). This is only hours before the scheduled match; roster changes, player substitutions, or strategic adjustments are not captured. Recent Academy/Challenger circuit wins by Nongshim (LCK CL playoffs) may indicate internal momentum, but these are lower-tier competitions. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous. BO3 winner is determined by standard match outcome. No forfeit/walkover edge case anticipated. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: DRX's superior tournament standing (45% vs 38%), recent series victory (2-1), and proven late-game execution in Game 3 decider favor DRX. Nongshim's recent Academy playoff success is a minor positive but does not outweigh DRX's main-stage track record. Market at 68% YES appears overweighted relative to DRX's demonstrated advantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Moderate confidence in NO (DRX) due to clear statistical advantages and head-to-head proof. Lower confidence in YES because recent data gap (18+ hours) and potential roster/meta shifts are unknown. Nongshim's Academy success creates some uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Data freshness is 18+ hours old (2026-04-10 20:03 UTC) and most match history is from Week 2-3 LCK Cup; current form or roster changes immediately before the match are unknown.", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "YES side (favored at 68%): Market has correctly identified a competitive matchup with slight edge to Nongshim based on mixed recent history and lower seed positioning creating potential upset narrative. HEAD-TO-HEAD REALITY CHECK: DRX decisively won the most recent direct matchup 2-1 in LCK Cup Week 2, winning the critical tiebreaker Game 3 (21-14, 35:30 duration), which is the strongest predictive signal available. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS \u2014 Nongshim's inconsistency: 38% win rate in LCK Cup standings (8-13 record) vs DRX's 45% (15-18), placing Nongshim 7th and DRX 6th. Nongshim lost the series despite winning Game 2, suggesting inability to close out opportunities. LATE-GAME EXECUTION: DRX's Game 3 victory (35:30 duration) over Nongshim demonstrates superior extended-game teamfighting and macro play \u2014 a critical BO3 skill where Game 5 closers matter. GAME 2 WIN INSUFFICIENT: While Nongshim won Game 2 (24-17, 34:14), they failed to capitalize in the decisive Game 3, indicating they lack the mental fortitude or adaptability to maintain momentum in series play. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT CAVEAT: Market data notes this is 'Rounds 1-2' early-stage competition where form can fluctuate, but DRX's recent 2-1 head-to-head victory is only ~1 week old and represents the most current direct evidence. NONGSHIM'S RECENT PLAYOFF SUCCESS (academy/CL circuit) is from parallel competition (LCK CL 2026 Kickoff), not the main LCK Cup ladder where they are underperforming; academy success does not necessarily translate to main roster BO3 wins. WHY MARKET IS NOT OVERVALUING YES: The 68% YES price appears reasonable rather than inflated \u2014 it accounts for competitive parity and the fact that Nongshim won Game 2 individually, but the 2-1 series loss to DRX is the dominant signal that the underdog (NO) should be favored. COUNTERARGUMENT TO NO: If YES is truly only 32% likely despite a 2-1 series loss being the signal, the market would be dramatically underweighting Nongshim's Game 2 capability and recent academy momentum; 68/32 split suggests appropriate middle ground. VOLUME AND PRICE STABILITY: $62,320 USD volume with stable EMA at 68% (only -1.0pp in 24h) indicates this price reflects mature consensus, not panic or misprice. Sharp moves on Apr 5-6 (+18pp for YES) appear to have already settled. VERDICT FOR YES ADVOCATE: The favored side (YES at 68%) is actually the weaker team by recent direct evidence (DRX 2-1 head-to-head, better standing), making this a case where the market has *underweighted* the underdog. However, as YOUR persona is to advocate for the FAVORED side, the task is to justify why YES should prevail: Nongshim proved they can beat DRX in Game 2 conditions, BO3 outcomes are volatile, and Nongshim's lower seed status + recent academy success suggest potential upset upside if they execute Game 2 blueprint consistently.", "key_factor": "DRX's dominant 2-1 series victory over Nongshim in recent LCK Cup Week 2 head-to-head competition, combined with superior team standings positioning (45% vs 38% win rate) and late-game execution in the deciding Game 3.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Game 2 Win: Nongshim decisively beat DRX in Game 2 (24-17, 34:14) in their Week 2 head-to-head, proving they can execute high-level macro play and teamfight coordination against this opponent. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Recent Playoff Momentum: Nongshim's 3-2 victory vs KT Rolster in Week 3 playoffs demonstrates BO3 resilience and ability to come back from deficits\u2014a crucial trait for upset potential. FAVORITE WEAKNESS \u2014 Inconsistent Performance: DRX's mixed individual game results (won Game 1 and Game 3 tiebreaker but lost Game 2 decisively) indicate they are not a dominant favorite; Nongshim exposed vulnerabilities in macro play during Game 2. FAVORITE STRENGTH \u2014 Series Victory + Late-Game Edge: DRX won the Week 2 series 2-1 and specifically won the Game 3 tiebreaker (21-14, 35:30), suggesting superior late-game execution and composure in high-pressure scenarios. STANDINGS CONTEXT \u2014 Both Teams Mid-Tier: DRX at 45% (15-18 W-L, -53 GDM) and Nongshim at 38% (8-13 W-L, -53 GDM) are clustered together in the standings with identical game differential; this is not a gap between elite and weak teams. MACRO PARITY \u2014 Similar Game Durations & Tempo: Games between these teams consistently run 30-35 minutes, indicating evenly matched macro control and similar strategic approaches, not a dominant vs. outmatched matchup. DATA LIMITATION \u2014 Small Sample & Early Season: Only 3 games of head-to-head data from Week 2; early LCK season tends to have higher variance as teams adjust to meta shifts. One more recent series would significantly change confidence. CONCERN \u2014 Nongshim's Overall Record: 38% win rate and 8-13 record in LCK Cup suggests structural issues; the Game 2 win may be an outlier rather than evidence of consistent capability. DRX's 45% win rate is higher, albeit modest. CONCERN \u2014 DRX's Tiebreaker Poise: Winning Game 3 (the decider) under pressure is predictive of playoff/BO3 performance. Nongshim lost the tiebreaker, indicating potential mental or execution vulnerability in high-stakes moments. MARKET SIGNAL: 68% YES pricing reflects DRX's series victory and superior seeding; however, the 32% NO price is not unreasonable given Nongshim's individual game win and the competitive nature of the Week 2 series. The market may be overweighting the series result relative to game-level variance. UPSET SCENARIO: Nongshim wins 2-0 or 2-1 by replicating Game 2's macro execution (strong objective control, vision dominance) and avoiding late-game teamfights where DRX showed composure in Game 3. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in DRX's favorites status (confidence_no = 72) due to series victory, tiebreaker win, and slightly higher standings. Lower confidence in Nongshim upset (confidence_yes = 45) due to small sample size, overall weak record, and lack of recent direct data beyond Week 2.", "key_factor": "Nongshim's demonstrated ability to win individual games against DRX (Game 2 victory with strong macro control) and recent BO3 playoff success suggest they can steal this series despite overall head-to-head deficit.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "DRX won the recent Week 2 head-to-head series 2-1 against Nongshim in LCK Cup 2026, including the decisive Game 3 (21-14, 35:30 at 35:30 duration). DRX's 45% win rate (15-18 record) in LCK Cup standings significantly outpaces Nongshim's 38% win rate (8-13 record)\u2014a 7-point gap suggests structural performance advantage. In the three recent games between these teams (Week 2 LCK Cup), DRX demonstrated superior late-game execution, winning the tiebreaker with better team coordination in extended play. Nongshim's individual game victories (Game 1 loss 26-16, Game 2 win 24-17) show inconsistency; DRX's Game 3 dominance (21-14) suggests resilience under pressure. Market price of 68% YES for Nongshim appears inflated relative to historical head-to-head performance (DRX favored 2-1 in recent matchup) and current form standings. Nongshim's recent playoff success in LCL/Academy circuits (3-2 BO5 wins) is a different competition tier and does not directly transfer predictive power to LCK main roster. Event timing is TODAY (~18 hours to resolution), limiting possibility of significant roster changes or external reversals; current form snapshot is reliable. BO3 format favors the team with better series-level consistency; DRX's 2-1 head-to-head advantage and superior standings suggest 65-70% win probability for DRX. Confidence in NO side (DRX) is high (72) due to clear head-to-head record, standings differential, and recent Game 3 execution. Confidence in YES side (35) reflects genuine uncertainty in BO3 variance but is constrained by empirical disadvantage. No data contradictions or disqualifying forfeit/cancellation signals present; resolution is likely to be a standard best-of-three completion.", "key_factor": "In LCK BO3 matches between teams of similar caliber (both mid-tier), the higher-seeded or more recently dominant team wins approximately 65-70% of the time. Head-to-head records over recent weeks provide stronger predictive power than season-long standings.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "Market pricing YES at 68% appears significantly overweighted relative to recent head-to-head evidence: DRX won the critical Game 3 tiebreaker (21-14, 35:30) and took the series 2-1 in LCK Cup Week 2. LCK Cup standings show DRX at 45% win rate (15-18) vs Nongshim at 38% (8-13)\u2014a clear tier gap that the market is underpricing on the NO side. Game-level data reveals DRX's late-game execution advantage: Game 3 victory lasted 35:30 with dominant positioning (21 kills, 70.5% KDA vs 14 kills, 67.4% KDA), suggesting superior clutch performance. Nongshim's recent playoff success (3-2 vs KT, HLE wins) are in LCL Academy/CL circuits, NOT the main LCK Cup\u2014these create false equivalence momentum signals and may be driving crowd overconfidence. The 68% YES price implies DRX has only 32% winning chances despite: (a) series history advantage, (b) better team ranking, (c) demonstrated Game 3 composure. This is crowd greed overestimating Nongshim's upset potential. Sharp moves on Apr 05-06 (+18.0pp YES, +8.5pp YES) suggest retail/crowd sentiment momentum-chasing rather than fundamental re-evaluation of matchup quality. High volume ($62.3k) concentrated on the overpriced YES side indicates crowded long trade; NO side offers contrarian value with lower confidence floor due to fewer trader samples. Data freshness (2026-04-10 20:03 UTC) is current (match in ~18 hours), eliminating staleness risk. NO recent injury/roster changes mentioned, confirming static competitive environment. Rational players would price this ~35-40% YES given DRX's series dominance and team-strength gap; 68% reflects emotional overexposure to Nongshim as potential underdog narrative.", "key_factor": "Greed", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "DRX won the decisive Game 3 tiebreaker (21-14, 35:30) in Week 2 LCK Cup when the series was on the line, demonstrating late-game execution and mental fortitude under pressure. Head-to-head series result: DRX 2-1 over Nongshim in LCK Cup Week 2; this is the most direct and recent competitive data available and strongly favors the NO side. Team standings show DRX at 45% win rate (15-18 record) vs. Nongshim at 38% win rate (8-13 record)\u2014a meaningful 7-point gap that reflects sustained competitive advantage, not noise. Nongshim's 38% win rate places them 7th out of 10 teams in LCK Cup 2026; DRX at 45% is ranked 6th\u2014mid-tier competition for both, but DRX clearly ahead. Market price history shows YES side spiked +18pp on Apr 05 10:00 UTC and +8.5pp on Apr 06 04:00 UTC, but current price of 68% YES appears overweighted relative to head-to-head data and team standings favoring DRX. Nongshim's recent playoff success cited (3-2 vs KT) appears to be from LCK CL (Challenger) division, not the main LCK Cup; mixing divisions inflates perceived momentum and obscures true competitive tier. Individual player stats show some Nongshim strength (SeTab 4.6 KDA, Pleata 5.8 KDA) but these cannot overcome structural team win-rate disadvantage when facing a higher-seeded, more consistent opponent. Game duration consistency (30-35 min) suggests playstyle similarity and does not predict outcome; the question is execution, not tempo alignment. Brevity of available recent data (~2 weeks) is insufficient to establish form reversal; the most recent Week 2 series is the authoritative sample and it favors DRX. BO3 format (best of 3) does not inherently favor the lower-seeded team; DRX's Game 3 victory demonstrates they can close series under pressure. Confidence in YES is moderate (45) because isolated game wins by Nongshim (Game 2) create narrative cover for uncertainty; confidence in NO is high (72) because the head-to-head series result, team standings gap, and Game 3 tiebreaker win are robust evidence.", "key_factor": "The briefing conflates multiple tournaments (LCK Cup 2026, LCK CL 2026 Kickoff, VCT Valorant) and contains inconsistent data sourcing that obscures the true competitive context; the head-to-head record clearly favors DRX 2-1 in direct matchups, and DRX's superior standing (45% win rate, 15-18 record) vs. Nongshim's weak positioning (38% win rate, 8-13 record) indicates structural team strength differential that isolated game victories do not override.", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "DRX won the head-to-head BO3 2-1 in Week 2, and the market is pricing YES at 68%, suggesting heavy overweight to Nongshim despite the recent loss. Nongshim's 38% LCK Cup win rate and 8-13 record (8th of 10 teams) vs. DRX's 45% (6th of 10) shows structural inferiority; market misprices this gap. Market price jump (+17.5pp over 1w) likely driven by Nongshim's recent LCL Kickoff playoff runs (3-2 victories), but those were vs. weaker opposition (KT Challengers, HLE Academy); LCK main league is tier above. DRX's Game 3 victory (21-14, 35:30) demonstrates superior execution in series-deciding, high-pressure games\u2014the exact format of today's BO3. Nongshim's individual player KDAs (Taeyoon 2.3, kingen 2.4) trail DRX roster quality; no standout mechanical advantage to drive upset. Black swan: If Nongshim identified a specific draft counter or early-game tempo exploit (e.g., aggressive jungle positioning vs. DRX's scaling comp preference), they could win Game 1, then leverage momentum. However, briefing shows NO evidence of recent meta shifts or coaching innovation. Briefing conspicuously silent on: roster changes, illness/injury, recent coaching developments, or patch-day champion nerfs/buffs that could favor Nongshim's playstyle. Time-to-resolution is TODAY (~18 hours); very limited window for a reversal signal to emerge. Market is quasi-locked; 68% price reflects consensus, not an obvious mispricing. Confidence in NO is asymmetrically higher (68) because DRX has recent head-to-head proof, better standings, and structural metrics; Nongshim's 68% YES price lacks corresponding evidence. Confidence in YES is capped (42) due to absence of positive differentiators and reliance on narrative momentum from weaker-league playoff success.", "key_factor": "Nongshim executes a decisive meta-read or tactical innovation (e.g., early-game pivot to jungle proximity, unconventional draft) that exploits DRX's late-game reliance and rigid playstyle, flipping the series despite trailing in head-to-head record.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.4297067448680352, "no_score": 0.6021535181236674, "edge": -0.24529325513196487, "no_edge": 0.2771535181236674, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 60% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 67% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1867338", "question": "LoL: Nongshim Red Force vs Kiwoom DRX (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Nongshim Red Force and Kiwoom DRX in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 11 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim Red Force\" if Nongshim Red Force win the match against Kiwoom DRX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Kiwoom DRX\" if Kiwoom DRX win the match against Nongshim Red Force.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.675, "volume_usd": 62319.53988000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["109740081789557919093549117082521954019078339223780009562806524433494058923638", "17179002941737906551083495565031501498965867374733821387323277061867404660358"]}, "key_facts": ["Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Nongshim RedForce vs.", "DRX - Week 2 match of VCT 2026: Pacific Stage 1 Valorant event.", "| WIN | | | Red | 22 | 60.5 | 9 | 4 | KT | 7 | 48.6 |