ime\nEDward Gaming\nEDward Gaming\nOh My God\nThunderTalk Gaming\nLGD Gaming\nUltra Prime\nLNG Esports\nEDward Gaming\nEDward Gaming\nOh My God\nThunderTalk Gaming\nLGD Gaming\nUltra Prime\nLNG Esports\nEDward Gaming\nEDward Gaming\nOh My God\nThunderTalk Gaming\nLGD Gaming\nUltra Prime\nLNG Esports\nEDward Gaming\nEDward Gaming\nOh My God\nThunderTalk Gaming\nLGD Gaming\nUltra Prime\nLNG Esports\nEDward Gaming"], "news_summary": "LPL 2026 Split 2 is an ongoing S-Tier offline tournament featuring 14 teams competing from April to June 2026. Team WE and Invictus Gaming are scheduled to face each other in a BO3 match within the Group Ascend bracket. Individual player statistics from Care (Team WE mid) and Creme (appears to be IG mid based on context) show both mid laners with strong overall records and champion pool depth, though with different aggression profiles.", "side_yes_case": ["Care (Team WE) maintains 62.5% win rate (5-3) with strong KDA of 4.3 and comfortable gold differential at 15 minutes (+346)", "Creme shows higher aggression metrics with 813.7 DPM (vs Care's 608.8) but lower vision control, suggesting potential vulnerability to early game pressure", "Team WE demonstrated success against NIP in recent matches with Care's standout Ahri performance (1/0/10)"], "side_no_case": ["Creme (IG) has higher win rate of 66.7% (4-2) with superior KDA of 6.0 and stronger kill participation at 63.4% vs Care's 54%", "Creme's Aurora pick achieved 1103 DPM with 100% win rate, indicating potential one-trick strength in high-impact champions", "Team WE shows inconsistent performance with 0-2 loss to IG already recorded on April 8, establishing recent head-to-head disadvantage"], "key_context": ["LPL Split 2 2026 tournament runs April 4 to June 2026 as offline S-Tier event with 14 teams", "Head-to-head record shows Team WE lost 0-2 to IG on April 8, prior to this scheduled Group Ascend match", "Both teams' mid laners show preference for similar champions (Ahri, Azir, Viktor), suggesting meta-driven matchup dynamics", "Match format is BO3, requiring series victory rather than single-game performance", "Early game farming patterns show both mids struggle with CS advantages at 15 minutes (0% ahead metric), indicating farm-neutral playstyles"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T20:10:38.136176Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "74676155633607408144480964921553786874268285102558560769489517893395445970525", "data_points": 41, "weighted_avg": 0.30733820524931355, "change_1w_pp": 4.0000000000000036, "change_24h_pp": -3.4999999999999973, "volatility_24h": 0.6546536707079769, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-06T10:00:59Z", "delta_pp": 8.500000000000002}]}, "no": {"token_id": "34474986880442753047059679489987729480478871692157718247585140735242575127582", "data_points": 44, "weighted_avg": 0.6940884143004145, "change_1w_pp": -4.0000000000000036, "change_24h_pp": 3.9999999999999925, "volatility_24h": 0.8451542547285174, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-05T00:00:24Z", "delta_pp": 5.000000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-06T09:00:13Z", "delta_pp": -11.5}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-10T20:10:38.486881Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-11T15:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-11T14:27:59.392240+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "fa111bdd-6fc8-466f-8810-f9ccd83ade3a", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T20:14:40.586420+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1867361", "question": "LoL: Dplus KIA vs Gen.G (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Dplus KIA and Gen.G in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 11 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dplus KIA\" if Dplus KIA win the match against Gen.G.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gen.G\" if Gen.G win the match against Dplus KIA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.115, "volume_usd": 15607.889385000019, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["68861406955641220050585388396808313213368556635215674511447552011405069727916", "112228909995558514432757102584861585268664013372031625044609994111601425832644"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.12, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market prices show YES at 12% (Dplus KIA) and NO at 88% (Gen.G), representing extreme confidence in Gen.G victory. Gen.G confirmed as 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2 standings, indicating strong early season performance. Dplus KIA's explicit standings ranking NOT provided in briefing, creating asymmetric information favoring the market consensus. Game 2 timeline data (vs HLE) shows Dplus KIA's Kanavi with repeated kills, objective control, and early plate dominance, but this is against HLE, not Gen.G\u2014insufficient for direct predictive value. Briefing explicitly states: 'Limited direct information about Dplus KIA vs Gen.G matchup' and 'Limited historical head-to-head data available'\u2014critical gap for a 12% YES probability. Sharp price moves on Apr 05 (-30.5pp YES, +33.0pp NO) suggest significant news event, but no corresponding event details provided in briefing. Market has traded for 1 week with clear directional bias; early mover consensus may reflect information not captured in search results. Bo3 format means either team can win 2-1; absolute certainty (88%) is mathematically unusual for competitive esports. Confidence in NO side is moderate (45) due to lack of Dplus KIA standings/recent form data; if Dplus KIA is top-4 team, 12% seems artificially low. Confidence in YES side is low (35) because Gen.G's strong record is confirmed, but without Dplus KIA's record comparison, cannot rule out market efficiency. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous for match outcome; no edge cases present. Event is TODAY (resolves in ~20 hours); reversal risk is minimal, market will settle on actual match result.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains corrupted/incomplete match data (game timeline shows mixed player names and unclear team attribution) and lacks sufficient recent head-to-head performance metrics or current team standings for Dplus KIA to justify the extreme market skew toward Gen.G.", "probability_yes": 0.12, "probability_no": 0.88, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.12, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Gen.G holds a 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2 standings, demonstrating concrete early-season success against LCK competition. This translates to a 5-2 game win rate, indicating consistent execution. MARKET STRUCTURE SIGNAL: Market has priced NO at 88% and YES at 12%, reflecting a decisive institutional consensus. The 7-day trend shows YES falling -38.5pp (from ~50% to 12%), indicating informed market participants moved sharply AGAINST Dplus KIA after April 5. This sharp move (-30.5pp on Apr 05 21:00 UTC) suggests material information favored Gen.G. MOMENTUM DIRECTIONALITY: Over the past 24 hours, NO has gained +3.0pp while YES has lost -2.5pp, showing continued market confidence in Gen.G despite the match being TODAY. This persistence near 88% despite proximity to resolution suggests not a late-session panic but sustained conviction. ASYMMETRIC DATA PROBLEM: Briefing provides detailed game 2 timeline for Dplus KIA vs HLE (Week 2), but NO direct recent performance data for Dplus KIA vs Gen.G specifically. The detailed Kanavi jungle activity (kills, objective control, plate captures 5:38-16:40) shows Dplus KIA CAN execute, but this is against HLE, not Gen.G. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES: Dplus KIA ranking in Rounds 1-2 standings is NOT provided in briefing data, creating information asymmetry. If Dplus KIA were competitive, their standing would likely be mentioned. Gen.G's explicit 2-1 standing suggests Dplus KIA finished below Gen.G in Rounds 1-2 seeding. BO3 FORMAT EFFECT: Series requires 2 wins. Gen.G's proven consistency (5-2 games = 71% game win rate) favors the higher-seeded team across multiple games. Dplus KIA would need to win 2 consecutive best-of-three games\u2014a higher burden than a single upset. CONTEXT: Both teams compete for MSI qualification in LCK Road to MSI, and Gen.G's Rounds 1-2 placement positions them favorably for playoff seeding. No indication in briefing that Dplus KIA has equivalent momentum or standings position. CONTRARIAN CHECK: The only apparent case for YES is the detailed Dplus KIA vs HLE game data showing Kanavi's early pressure and objective dominance. However, (a) this is one game against HLE, not Gen.G; (b) detailed data availability does not equal predictive power; (c) HLE's competitive level relative to Gen.G is not specified in briefing. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_no = 72 reflects strong market pricing (88%), confirmed Rounds 1-2 standings favoring Gen.G, and 7-day trend confirming NO. Confidence is not higher (e.g., 85+) because: (1) detailed Dplus KIA game execution shown; (2) BO3 introduces variance; (3) no explicit head-to-head matchup data. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION YES: confidence_yes = 28 reflects critical data gaps: no explicit Dplus KIA standings, no Gen.G recent form, no head-to-head history, and match is TODAY (~20 hours), limiting ability to validate if market repricing reflects late-breaking roster/form changes. Set below 35 due to information asymmetry strongly favoring NO side.", "key_factor": "Gen.G's proven 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2 combined with market consensus pricing NO at 88%, reflecting strong institutional confidence in Gen.G's established early-season dominance.", "probability_yes": 0.12, "probability_no": 0.88, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: YES fell 38.5pp over 7 days with a sharp -30.5pp drop on Apr 05, indicating sharp confidence collapse in DK. This aggressive repricing to 12% suggests either new information favoring Gen.G or coordinated conviction betting, both of which warrant skepticism. GEN.G STANDING: 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2 places Gen.G in competitive position, but this is early-season data\u2014not determinative of Bo3 matchup outcome. No evidence Gen.G has substantially stronger form than earlier records suggest. DPLUS KIA STRENGTH SIGNAL: The detailed game 2 vs HLE timeline shows Kanavi (jungler) with repeated early kills, objective control (Voidgrubs, plates across all lanes from 5:38-16:40), and sustained pressure. Early plate denial and multi-lane dominance indicate superior macro execution and win conditions. EARLY-GAME ADVANTAGE: Kanavi's kills at 2:50, 5:36, 5:55, 9:17, 9:46, 10:02, 11:40, 16:16, 16:34 (vs HLE) show pattern of explosive early game threat. In Bo3, winning early games creates psychological momentum and adaptation difficulty for opponents. BO3 FORMAT RISK FOR FAVORITE: Gen.G must win 2 of 3 games. Market prices Gen.G at 88%, implying ~94% win probability per game (assuming 0.94^2 \u2248 0.88 series win). This assumes consistency across 3 games\u2014Bo3 format favors teams with variance/adaptation capacity. DK's early-game aggression could steal Game 1, forcing Gen.G to adapt. DATA ASYMMETRY PROBLEM: Briefing provides detailed Dplus KIA game data (21 timestamped events vs HLE) but minimal concrete Gen.G match data. Cannot reliably assess Gen.G's current form, player performance, or matchup-specific vulnerabilities. This asymmetry inflates NO confidence artificially. GEN.G VULNERABILITY: No evidence provided of Gen.G's early-game defense, jungle response patterns, or recent losses/struggles. KT Rolster (with 3 Worlds 2022 winners) was only team to take a match win vs Gen.G in Spring, proving Gen.G is beatable by coordinated opponents. Dplus KIA's proactive jungle could replicate KT's success. UNDERDOG PRICING MISMATCH: 12% implies Gen.G wins >88% of the time in series\u2014extremely high confidence. Market may be anchored to Gen.G's general LCK prestige (2-1 record) without accounting for Dplus KIA's demonstrated mechanical edge in early-game execution and jungle priority. MISSING INTEL: No head-to-head history provided, recent roster changes for either team unknown, meta-shift impact unknown, and player form outside the HLE game unknown. These gaps favor the underdog (more unknown upside) than the favorite (more known downside). CONFIDENCE CAPS: YES confidence set to 28 (low) because concrete evidence for DK upset is limited to one partial game timeline vs HLE, not vs Gen.G. NO confidence set to 72 (moderate-high) because Gen.G's 2-1 record and market dominance suggest real strength, but data insufficiency and Bo3 format volatility prevent higher conviction.", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA's demonstrated early-game dominance and jungle control (Kanavi's multi-kill pressure, plate denials) suggests potential to exploit Gen.G in a Bo3 format despite market underpricing.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.14, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price of 12% reflects strong consensus that Gen.G is heavy favorite. Market has moved sharply downward (YES -38.5pp over 7 days, -2.5pp in 24h), indicating sustained confidence in Gen.G. STANDINGS DATA: Gen.G explicitly shown at 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2. Dplus KIA ranking not provided in briefing. This asymmetry favors the documented stronger seed. GAME-LEVEL DATA: One Dplus KIA vs HLE (not vs Gen.G) timeline provided showing early aggression by Kanavi (jungle). However, this is a different opponent and does not directly predict Gen.G matchup outcome. STRUCTURAL CONTEXT: LCK 2026 double round-robin format carries Rounds 1-2 records into subsequent rounds. Gen.G's documented 2-1 start is a meaningful advantage in BO3 context. HISTORICAL BASE RATE: BO3 series in professional LoL favor the higher-seeded team ~70% of the time when seeding differential is clear. Gen.G's explicit 2-1 record vs. Dplus KIA's absent record suggests Gen.G is higher seed. DATA GAPS: Briefing provides no direct head-to-head history, no Dplus KIA win-loss record for Rounds 1-2, no recent form comparison, and no player/roster injury information. One HLE game timeline does not establish Dplus KIA's capability vs. Gen.G. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=28 reflects uncertainty about Dplus KIA's actual strength (record not provided). confidence_no=35 reflects similar gap\u2014Gen.G's 2-1 record is known, but BO3 upsets occur and skill gap magnitude is unclear. Both confidences are low due to incomplete competitive data. TIMING NOTE: Event resolves in ~20 hours (TODAY). Market is already deeply settled at 12% YES. Major reversal would require unexpected roster issues or Gen.G collapse, which have <20 hours to materialize\u2014very low probability. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 12% market price is near base rate (28-30%) for true heavy underdog in BO3. Slight adjustment to 14% reflects minimal additional Dplus KIA evidence from HLE game, but this does not override the standings-based consensus.", "key_factor": "In LCK BO3 matches, the higher-seeded or stronger-record team wins approximately 65-72% of series. Gen.G's 2-1 match record (5-2 games) vs. Dplus KIA's unspecified standing suggests Gen.G is favored.", "probability_yes": 0.14, "probability_no": 0.86, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.14, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES crashed 38.5pp over 7 days with sharp -30.5pp drop on Apr 05, suggesting heavy selling or information flow favoring Gen.G. Current 12% YES reflects extreme crowding on NO side. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market has priced in Gen.G as heavy favorite (88% NO). This is crowded consensus territory where tail risk exists if Dplus delivers an upset. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing contains detailed Dplus KIA vs HLE match timeline (Game 2, Week 2) showing strong early game: Kanavi dominance, early plate controls (5:38+), objective control. Zero comparable Gen.G match detail provided. SIGNAL IGNORED: The match-level play data available (Dplus KIA) shows proactive early game execution and jungle pressure\u2014typically predictive of series momentum. Market appears to discount this in favor of standings position alone. STANDINGS CONTEXT: Gen.G 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2 is strong but insufficient to fully justify 88% YES pricing without head-to-head context or recent form comparisons. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINT: Briefing provides tactical detail for Dplus but zero comparable data on Gen.G's recent performance, playstyle, or matchup history. Cannot properly evaluate NO side strength. Confidence_no deliberately suppressed to 35. TIMING RISK: Match resolves in ~20 hours (TODAY). Sharp price moves on Apr 05 suggest prior information leakage or line movement on external odds. Current extreme pricing may reflect resolved uncertainty rather than mispricing. RATIONAL APATHY POSSIBLE: If Gen.G is genuinely dominant (3rd seed, better record), 88% is defensible. But lack of comparative match data in briefing means market may be pricing on reputation/seeding rather than current tactical form. VERDICT: YES is underpriced IF Dplus' strong early game execution vs HLE generalizes to this series. But crowding on NO and absence of Gen.G detail data suggest market has legitimate information advantage. Moderate value play on YES if you believe Dplus' tempo translates; otherwise NO is rationally priced.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.14, "probability_no": 0.86, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market fundamentals: Current 88% NO price significantly outweighs 12% YES, consistent with 38.5pp seven-day rise on NO side and -30.5pp sharp move Apr 05 suggesting informed money flowing toward Gen.G. Gen.G competitive positioning: Confirmed 2-1 match record (5-2 games) in Rounds 1-2 places them in upper standings; this is the only explicit win-loss data provided in briefing. Dplus KIA data asymmetry: Briefing contains detailed game 2 timeline vs HLE (Week 2) showing Kanavi jungle dominance with early kills (2:50, 5:36, 5:55) and objective control (Voidgrubs 9:46-10:02), but no win-loss record, current seeding, or head-to-head record vs Gen.G. BO3 format risk: Single game timeline does not confirm series trend; early game jungle pressure in one game vs HLE does not predict BO3 performance against Gen.G's likely different draft/macro strategy. Meta and roster unknowns: Briefing provides champion builds (Gnar, Kha, Annie, Corki, Nami, Ambessa, Nocturne, Syndra) from HLE matchup but no indication of Dplus KIA's current meta performance or whether these builds remain optimal for Gen.G series. Institutional seeding: Gen.G's 2-1 record implies higher playoff/bracket seeding probability; Dplus KIA's placement unknown, suggesting potential bracket disadvantage or unfavorable playoff matchup mechanics. Time-to-reversal constraint: Event resolves in ~20 hours; for Dplus KIA to overturn 88% NO pricing requires either significant underdog thesis (roster surprise, meta shift, coaching adjustment) that market has already priced in via sharp moves. Search result confidence gap: Case for NO relies on one team's tactical gameplay; Case for YES relies on record standing alone without recent form, head-to-head, or roster context. Market efficiency check: 12% YES price is substantially below historical LoL upsets (typical 15-25% for lower-seeded teams in BO3); this suggests either market confidence in Gen.G or Dplus KIA is substantially weakened post-Rounds 1-2.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 12% YES reflects Gen.G's superior Rounds 1-2 record (2-1, 5-2 games) and likely higher seeding, but the briefing lacks Dplus KIA's current record, recent head-to-head history, and roster/meta compatibility data critical to BO3 series prediction.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES priced at 12% with sharp 30.5pp drop on Apr 05, suggesting a major confidence swing away from DK. The 88% NO price reflects strong institutional conviction in Gen.G, but may be overweighting recent standings (2-1 record, 5-2 games) without capturing in-match volatility or roster flexibility dynamics. DATA ASYMMETRY PROBLEM: Briefing provides granular game timeline for DK vs HLE (showing Kanavi's jungle dominance and early plate pressure) but NO comparable detail on Gen.G's current form or matchup-specific vulnerabilities. This absence of counter-evidence should lower confidence in the NO side. KANAVI JUNGLE SIGNAL: The HLE game timeline shows Kanavi with extraordinary early-game presence (kills at 2:50, 5:36, 5:55; voidgrubs control starting 9:46; multiple subsequent plays). This is not a typical carry jungle\u2014this is a proactive, early-game tempo setter. If DK can replicate this pressure against Gen.G's bot lane or mid lane, the series shifts dramatically. GEN.G STRENGTH IS AGGREGATED: A 5-2 record across multiple games obscures which specific matchups Gen.G struggles in. The briefing notes KT Rolster took a 2-3 win against Gen.G despite being 5th seed\u2014evidence that even mid-tier teams can exploit Gen.G under the right conditions. BO3 VOLATILITY: This is a best-of-three, not a single game. DK only needs to win 2 games. If DK wins game 1 with their Kanavi-centric early game, game 2 becomes a must-win for Gen.G, raising mental/momentum stakes. Gen.G may panic-draft or deviate from optimal preparation. ROSTER/META X-FACTOR: The briefing conspicuously lacks information on whether DK or Gen.G have made recent roster changes, mid-season substitutions, or meta-read updates post-Rounds 1-2. LCK teams frequently rotate players for specific matchups. If DK has a substitution card (e.g., an alternate jungler or support for a specific meta) that Gen.G has not scouted, this flips the series. MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: Gen.G is ranked higher (Rounds 1-2 standings), meaning they may be satisfied with seeding and play conservatively. DK, unranked in briefing results, may be fighting for relevance and bring maximum aggression and preparation. MARKET UNDERPRICING OF UPSETS: The 12% YES price reflects consensus confidence in Gen.G, but in best-of-three formats, 12% is extremely low for a team with Kanavi-level jungle talent. Historical LoL data shows that any team with a dominant jungler has a hidden floor of ~20-25% in a single series due to map control and snowball potential. ABSENCE OF RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: The briefing provides zero direct evidence of DK vs Gen.G matchup history, recent trends, or head-to-head records. This information void should reduce confidence in the 88% NO assessment proportionally. INFERENCE: The market crash on Apr 05 (\u221230.5pp on YES) suggests either a major news event (Gen.G roster announcement, injury to DK player) or a shift in shareholder sentiment. The briefing does not document what triggered this move, which means the current 12% price may be overreacting to noise rather than fundamental strength.", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA executes a surprise mid-series roster substitution (likely Kanavi benched for a specific map or series rotation, or a meta-counter substitution) that disrupts Gen.G's preparation and exploits a tactical vulnerability in Gen.G's current composition flexibility.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.15133333333333335, "no_score": 0.8463270777479893, "edge": 0.03633333333333334, "no_edge": -0.03867292225201069, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 53% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1867361", "question": "LoL: Dplus KIA vs Gen.G (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Dplus KIA and Gen.G in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 11 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dplus KIA\" if Dplus KIA win the match against Gen.G.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gen.G\" if Gen.G win the match against Dplus KIA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve ba