{"run_id": "a0810ae4-5ee6-4360-80e0-5c0c26fca911", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T20:16:01.254790+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1893714", "question": "Valorant: Rex Regum Qeon vs VARREL (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Rex Regum Qeon and VARREL in the VCT Pacific Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rex Regum Qeon\" if Rex Regum Qeon win the match against VARREL.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"VARREL\" if VARREL win the match against Rex Regum Qeon.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 22361.567145000005, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["112799886753952412250465234117606310746979043660381635576119890240137633520837", "21548195383475596828420669722745195413923177256160634826752171961511081418478"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Rex Regum Qeon wins the BO3 match against VARREL on April 11, 2026. RRQ STRENGTH SIGNAL: Won 2-1 vs ZETA in Stage 1 Week 1 opener (April 5), demonstrating competitive Stage 1 capability. This is the most recent and relevant data point. RRQ CONSISTENCY CHECK: Kickoff performances show mixed results (2-0 vs PRX, 2-0 vs DFM, but 0-3 vs T1, 1-3 vs PRX). Suggests RRQ can beat mid-tier teams but struggles vs top tier. ZETA win is positive but not definitive. VARREL WEAKNESS SIGNAL: Lost 0-2 to T1 on April 3 (their Stage 1 opener). This is a clean sweep loss, suggesting early-stage struggles or lower competitive tier. VARREL KICKOFF RECORD: Losses to T1 (0-3), GEN (1-2), DRX (1-2), GE (0-2) in kickoff indicate consistent underperformance. No notable wins reported. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet.' This eliminates direct precedent analysis. MARKET CONSENSUS: YES at 66%, NO at 34% reflects moderate confidence in RRQ but substantial minority belief in VARREL upset (~1 in 3 chance). MARKET STABILITY: YES side stable at ~66% over 7 days; sharp intra-day moves on Apr 09 (\u00b16-10pp) suggest reactive trading but no new structural information apparent post-briefing date. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Data supports RRQ's victory more clearly (Stage 1 win vs VARREL's Stage 1 loss), so confidence_yes > confidence_no. However, BO3 volatility and lack of direct history limit certainty on both sides. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Match is TODAY (~20 hours out). Any reversal requiring major team changes is impossible. Market prices should reflect stable assessment. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are straightforward\u2014either RRQ or VARREL wins the BO3. No ambiguity in team names or match identification. Forfeit/walkover clauses would resolve 50-50, but unlikely. PROBABILITY DIRECTION CHECK: YES = RRQ wins. Briefing shows RRQ as favored (better Stage 1 record, recent wins). Probability of 66 for YES is appropriate. CONFIDENCE_YES RATIONALE: Stage 1 opener win, stronger recent form vs VARREL's 0-2 loss supports RRQ victory. Set at 72 (moderately high) due to limited sample size and no H2H. CONFIDENCE_NO RATIONALE: VARREL has shown weakness but BO3 format and lack of detailed player/meta analysis limits ability to definitively rule out upset. Set at 58 (moderate-low) reflecting data gaps on VARREL's true strength and potential improvements.", "key_factor": "No prior head-to-head data exists; small sample size from Stage 1 openers limits predictive confidence on both sides.", "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.33999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RRQ won their Stage 1 Week 1 opener 2-1 vs ZETA\u2014direct evidence of competitive performance at the current tournament level; VARREL lost 0-2 to T1, indicating early-stage struggles in Group Omega. RRQ's recent Kickoff form shows wins vs PRX (2-0) and DFM (2-0), suggesting baseline team strength and consistency; these are non-trivial opponents in a qualifying context. VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 is the only Stage 1 datapoint available; a shutout loss in Week 1 suggests either poor adaptation to Stage 1 meta, roster chemistry issues, or matchup weakness. No prior head-to-head history removes directional history bias; the match is evaluated purely on current form and recent performance. BO3 format is neutral\u2014does not structurally favor either team, but RRQ's demonstrated ability to win a map against ZETA suggests better round-by-round resilience. RRQ's Kickoff record shows vulnerability (0-3 loss to T1, 1-3 loss to PRX, 2-3 loss to NS), indicating inconsistency against elite teams; however, VARREL's 0-2 Stage 1 loss suggests even worse Stage 1 compatibility. Market pricing at 66% YES reflects this form gap and is likely accurate; the 7-day NO decline of -17pp and 24-hour NO decline of -2pp indicate erosion of confidence in VARREL over time. Sharp moves on Apr 09 (\u00b16\u201310pp swings) suggest late information or line adjustment; final stable pricing at 66% YES suggests consensus has settled toward RRQ as favorite. VARREL's potential rapid improvement is plausible but unsubstantiated by any in-tournament evidence; betting on an underdog's adjustment without data is speculative. RRQ's Stage 1 victory over ZETA is the strongest available signal of current competitive tier; it is more recent and tournament-relevant than Kickoff results.", "key_factor": "RRQ demonstrated Stage 1 competitive capability with a 2-1 victory over ZETA in their opener, while VARREL lost decisively 0-2 to T1, establishing a clear form gap entering this match.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RRQ FAVORED BUT INCONSISTENT: RRQ beat ZETA 2-1 (Stage 1 Week 1), but their Kickoff record shows critical weakness: losses to T1 0-3 and PRX 1-3. This suggests RRQ struggles against top-tier competition, not just warm-up variance. VARREL'S LOSS CONTEXT: VARREL lost 0-2 to T1 (April 3), but T1 is the reigning elite team in Pacific. A 0-2 against T1 is not dis