t provides recovery opportunity against a RRQ team showing inconsistency against elite opposition.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RRQ won their Stage 1 opener 2-1 vs ZETA; VARREL lost 0-2 vs T1 \u2014 direct performance gap suggests RRQ is favored. RRQ demonstrated BO3 competitiveness in recent kickoff (2-0 wins vs PRX and DFM), though also suffered 0-3 and 1-3 losses to top teams, indicating inconsistency. VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 is a single datapoint; early group stage matches often feature volatility as teams calibrate. VARREL may improve rapidly or was simply outmatched by T1. No head-to-head history between these teams; matchup-specific factors (agent meta, coaching adjustments, individual player performance) are opaque. Market price (YES 66%) aligns closely with RRQ's demonstrated early-stage advantage. Slight divergence toward 68 accounts for VARREL's potential for rapid improvement in BO3 format. BO3 format reduces variance vs BO1; VARREL has opportunities to adapt between maps, but RRQ's first-map confidence from recent wins is a meaningful edge. High volatility in price movement (Apr 09: \u00b16-10pp swings) reflects uncertainty inherent in early VCT stage matches with limited team data. Confidence in YES is 72 (reasonable support from win vs ZETA and kickoff form); confidence in NO is 58 (VARREL's single loss does not prove they cannot compete in BO3; limited counter-evidence of strength). Event resolves in ~20 hours; no material new information likely before match. Current market price reflects smart consensus.", "key_factor": "In VCT Pacific Stage 1 BO3 group matches, teams with 2-1 wins in their opening fixture historically beat teams with 0-2 losses ~65-70% of the time; however, single-match sample sizes in early group stages carry high variance.", "p