{"run_id": "6642d91e-5943-4750-9e63-0746dfdd3883", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T20:23:22.472368+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918605", "question": "Valorant: AKA HERO vs RIZON (BO3) - VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between AKA HERO and RIZON in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 11 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"AKA HERO\" if AKA HERO win the match against RIZON.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RIZON\" if RIZON win the match against AKA HERO.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.36, "volume_usd": 80.6, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["63317511318852451830924919082348661053132082195600798287967736683774674916899", "106563431367856612453003977144824540688204914057382661627679202866150580135561"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "AKA HERO is 0-2 (0-4 maps, -20 differential) vs RIZON 1-1 (3-3 maps, +5 differential) \u2014 substantial skill gap evidenced by standings and map performance. AKA HERO's 0-4 map record indicates systemic competitive deficiency, not just unlucky matchups; this suggests structural issues unlikely to reverse in one BO3. RIZON has demonstrated wins against comparable opponents (2-1 vs eSports Cologne) and sits 4 places higher in standings, reflecting consistent mid-tier competitive level. RIZON's inconsistent form (1-1) is a valid weakness, but their +5 map differential shows net strength; losses to CGN Esports (2nd place) and Cologne are reasonable for mid-tier play. Psychological 'nothing to lose' argument for AKA HERO is speculative; pressure relief rarely overcomes a 20-point map differential gap in competitive esports. BO3 format does favor upsets slightly (vs Bo1), but AKA HERO would need to win 2 maps against a team with +5 differential; probability remains low. Market price (36% YES) reflects sentiment slightly higher than fundamentals suggest; the briefing data supports a tighter probability around 25-30%. 24-hour move (+5pp for YES) and recent volatility suggest some late speculative action, but underlying match context heavily favors NO side. No evidence of roster changes, injuries, or meta shifts that would narrow the AKA HERO vs RIZON gap since standings were published (2026-04-10).", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; no ambiguity in team identification or resolution mechanism.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.85, "rationale": "NO (RIZON) is the favored side at 64% \u2014 the market has correctly identified the fundamental skill disparity based on objective standings data. AKA HERO is 0-2 (0-4 maps, -20 differential) versus RIZON's 1-1 (3-3 maps, +5 differential) \u2014 a 25-map swing gap that reflects consistent underperformance, not variance or bad luck. RIZON has already demonstrated wins against comparable/stronger opposition: beat eSports Cologne 2-1 (Cologne is also 0-2) and took maps off CGN Esports (the 2nd-place team), proving tournament-level competitive execution. The 'pressure relief' argument for YES is speculative and contradicts the data: last-place teams in group stages typically play *more* desperately and emotionally, not better. AKA HERO's systemic issues (0-4 record) suggest roster synergy, tactical, or individual skill problems \u2014 not mental blocks. RIZON's 1-1 record against a balanced field (wins vs Cologne, loss to stronger teams) positions them as a mid-tier threat. AKA HERO has lost to CGN (2nd place) 0-2 and likely faced other competitive teams \u2014 suggesting they are bottom-tier. The market's 64% NO price reflects appropriate confidence: RIZON is clearly the superior team by standings, map differential, and recent match outcomes. The market may even be *underpricing* NO slightly given AKA HERO's magnitude of failure. YES side arguments (RIZON's losses to stronger teams, 1-1 record as 'inconsistent') ignore that RIZON's 1-1 includes a win \u2014 they are not in freefall. AKA HERO's 0-2 is the actual crisis. BO3 format favors the higher-ranked team: RIZON needs to win 2/3 maps. Against a 0-4 team, they should be favored in most individual maps, making a 2-map series win likely. Event timing is THIS WEEK (~1.2 days): the match is imminent and no new data is likely to shift the standings-based assessment before resolution. Confidence asymmetry: high confidence in NO (85%) because standings, map differential, and head-to-head win records are objective and recent (April 4-10). Lower confidence in YES (72%) because YES requires a psychological/momentum narrative that lacks empirical support in the briefing, though theoretically possible in a single BO3.", "key_factor": "AKA HERO's catastrophic 0-4 map differential and last-place standing reveal a systemic competitive gap that psychological pressure relief cannot overcome in a single BO3.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "CASE FOR YES (AKA HERO upset): AKA HERO is last place (0-2, 0-4 maps, -20 diff) but this creates a paradoxical advantage\u2014no pressure, nothing to lose, team likely unified by adversity. RIZON's 1-1 record masks instability: they beat eSports Cologne 2-1 but also lost 1-2 to CGN Esports and 1-2 to eSports Cologne (same opponent), suggesting inconsistent anti-fragility. BO3 format amplifies variance: a single map win by AKA HERO in game 1 could shift momentum and psychological pressure onto RIZON, who are in precarious mid-table position with rising pressure to consolidate points. RIZON's +5 map differential is modest\u2014only 2 maps better than break-even across 6 maps played. This is not a dominant record; it reflects a team that is vulnerable to upset by a desperate, well-prepared opponent. CASE FOR NO (RIZON wins): The hard evidence overwhelmingly favors RIZON. AKA HERO's -20 map differential is severe and indicates systemic problems (fragging, coordination, economy management, or fundamental skill gaps) unlikely to vanish in one match. St