al, indicating inconsistent performance despite 2nd place", "Head-to-head history shows previous dominance by Galions but Esprit Sh\u014dnen may have adapted", "Tournament still in early stages; standings do not guarantee future results"], "key_context": ["BO3 format match in online Group Stage of B-Tier tournament organized by Riot Games", "Week 1 standings show early season records; multiple weeks of matches remaining", "Previous meeting: Galions defeated Esprit Sh\u014dnen 2-0 on April 5 (group stage match)", "Esprit Sh\u014dnen has 0 wins from 2 matches; Galions has 1 win from 2 matches", "Tournament includes 8 teams competing in round-robin group format"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T20:25:10.734072Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "55235071990517724638744998269483921621451210047748966481069077652658414880518", "data_points": 49, "weighted_avg": 0.23673328633053858, "change_1w_pp": 12.0, "change_24h_pp": 11.000000000000002, "volatility_24h": 3.695978410415355, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T07:00:43Z", "delta_pp": 5.499999999999999}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T08:00:43Z", "delta_pp": -6.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-10T01:00:52Z", "delta_pp": 13.0}]}, "no": {"token_id": "39930192902445018269231983611334713110803967934279035493670516586288420266224", "data_points": 40, "weighted_avg": 0.7666202715900484, "change_1w_pp": -12.0, "change_24h_pp": -10.999999999999998, "volatility_24h": 4.011347540529129, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T07:00:46Z", "delta_pp": -5.499999999999994}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T08:00:46Z", "delta_pp": 6.499999999999995}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-10T01:00:56Z", "delta_pp": -13.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-10T20:25:11.091642Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-12T00:15:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-12T07:52:34.551207+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "100b31e3-94eb-41c9-869f-af44730b60a8", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T20:31:15.685737+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1867407", "question": "LoL: HANJIN BRION vs KT Rolster (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between HANJIN BRION and KT Rolster in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 12 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HANJIN BRION\" if HANJIN BRION win the match against KT Rolster.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"KT Rolster\" if KT Rolster win the match against HANJIN BRION.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.175, "volume_usd": 21657.314426999998, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["112121405371280723903285439451690733542760078554089575720598370874470983855591", "21930783117824895695571222060626263868227113444650600011170438445918395516135"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: BRO must win the BO3 match against KT Rolster on April 12. RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: KT defeated BRO 2-1 in Week 2 LCK Cup 2026 (within same season). KT won games 2 and 3 decisively with superior macro play (92.7 GPM in game 2, 9 towers, 4 dragons). DIRECT EVIDENCE FAVORS KT: KT showed dominant execution in their series wins with strong team fighting. BRO's game 1 win (75.4 GPM, 14 kills) was not enough to overcome KT's adaptation in subsequent games. KT'S RECORD VS COMPARABLE OPPOSITION: KT beat DN SOOPers 2-1 (Week 1), showing ability to close series against mid-tier opponents. However, KT lost 0-2 to Gen.G and T1 (top teams), revealing inconsistency. BRO'S TOURNAMENT FORM: 32% win rate in LCK Cup 2026 (6-13 record), negative GDM (-145). Multiple 1-2 series losses: vs HLE, BNK FearX, DRX. Recent Week 3 losses to DRX (2-3 series loss) suggest performance plateau. KT'S RECENT REGRESSION: Week 3 performance poor (0-2 vs NS first, then 2-3 series loss vs NS). This is concerning for KT's form trajectory heading into rematch. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: BRO's 32% win rate vs KT's 35% win rate\u2014both weak overall, but KT slightly ahead. BRO shows tactical versatility (red-side wins vs DRX, HLE) but inconsistent execution (0-2 losses vs HLE, multiple forfeits in early weeks). MARKET PRICING: 82% for KT (NO) reflects strong confidence in KT's recent head-to-head dominance and superior series record. 18% for BRO (YES) reflects underdog status despite tactical competence. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Favors teams with consistent drafting and macro play. KT's Week 2 victory showed better adaptation across multiple games; BRO's inconsistency (winning game 1 but losing 2-3) is a structural weakness. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: No ambiguity in team identification or cancellation risk. gol.gg will have timely results. Forfeiture/walkover risk is minimal in professional LCK play. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES assessment because KT's Week 2 3-0 head-to-head clean performance is recent and robust. Lower confidence in NO because KT's Week 3 regression creates uncertainty about whether they maintain Week 2 level; BRO showed glimpses of competitive play in game 1 (Week 2) and against HLE (Week 2: 2-1 with dominant games). PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: KT's 2-1 Week 2 victory plus slightly better tournament record (35% vs 32%) plus macro edge justifies probability ~18-22 for BRO. Market at 18% is reasonable; slight edge to KT but not overwhelming given both teams' poor overall form.", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "KT IS THE FAVORITE AT 82%: Market pricing reflects KT's Week 2 dominance\u2014they won the series 2-1 with crushing performances in games 2 and 3, showcasing superior macro control and team fighting. HEAD-TO-HEAD EVIDENCE: In the recent Week 2 rematch, KT proved they can execute at a higher level than BRO across multiple games, particularly in gold management (92.7 GPM in game 2) and objective control (9 towers, 4 dragons in wins). BRO'S INCONSISTENCY ACROSS TOURNAMENT: BRO has lost 1-2 series to HLE, BNK FearX, and DRX\u2014this is a pattern of inability to close out opponents. Only 32% win rate in LCK Cup 2026 standings (6-13 record) is the second-worst in tournament. KT'S SERIES CLOSING ABILITY: KT beat DN SOOPers 2-1 in Week 1, demonstrating the ability to win series against mid-tier opponents. KT's 35% record (6-11) is slightly better than BRO's, though both teams struggle\u2014KT shows more frequent wins. BRO'S RED SIDE COMFORT DOESN'T OVERCOME MACRO DEFICIT: While BRO has won on red side historically (vs DRX, HLE), this is insufficient to overcome KT's proven superior team fighting and gold accumulation in recent head-to-head play. KT'S WEEK 3 DECLINE IS REAL BUT NOT DISQUALIFYING: KT lost 0-2 to NS and 2-3 to NS in Week 3, indicating form regression. However, this occurred AFTER their dominant Week 2 sweep of BRO, and regression is mutual\u2014BRO also lost to DRX 2-3 in same period. BRO'S WEEK 2 GAME 1 WIN LACKS REPLICABILITY: BRO's single victory in Week 2 (14 kills, 75.4 GPM) was not followed by series momentum\u2014they lost the next two games decisively. This shows BRO cannot sustain competitive intensity across a BO3. TOURNAMENT-LEVEL CONTEXT: Both teams are in lower half of standings (KT 9th, BRO 10th out of 10), but KT's recent head-to-head dominance (2-1 over BRO, 2-1 over DNS) outweighs BRO's marginal tournament gains. The rematch nature favors the team that already proved execution. CONTRARIAN CASE IS WEAK: The NO side (BRO wins) requires BRO to overcome a proven deficit from their Week 2 loss AND reverse recent form deterioration simultaneously. BRO's 1-2 series loss pattern makes closing out BO3s structurally harder. VOLATILITY AND VOLUME: YES side dropped 33pp over the week (-33.0pp), indicating market confidence in KT firming as new information emerged post-Week 2. Current 82/18 split reflects KT's concrete head-to-head evidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (78) reflects strong head-to-head data and KT's proven execution. confidence_no (62) reflects BRO's demonstrated ability to win individual games and red side comfort, but lacks macro-level superiority data to justify a comeback narrative.", "key_factor": "KT Rolster's decisive 2-1 victory over HANJIN BRION in Week 2 with dominant game 2 execution (92.7 GPM, 20 kills, 9 towers) establishes clear recent momentum and head-to-head superiority.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "KT FAVORED BUT SHOWING CRITICAL WEAKNESS: Market prices KT at 82%, but briefing reveals KT lost BOTH Week 3 series to Nongshim (0-2 then 2-3), indicating sharp recent form regression not fully reflected in pricing. BRO'S RED-SIDE STRENGTH UNDERVALUED: BRO won 3 red-side games including victories vs DRX and HLE in Week 2-3. Red-side meta advantage exists in BO3 format; BRO can secure at least 1 map. RECENT REMATCH CONTEXT: Week 2 KT victory (2-1) occurred 8+ days ago on patch 16.1. Meta shifts and roster confidence fluctuations favor unpredictability in quick rematches. KT'S ELITE TEAM VULNERABILITY: KT went 0-2 vs T1 and 0-2 vs Gen.G (top teams), yet beat BRO 2-1. This suggests KT's wins come against mid-tier opponents\u2014classification BRO fits. BRO GAME 1 EXECUTION: In Week 2 matchup, BRO took Game 1 decisively (14 kills, 75.4 GPM, 37:59). This proves BRO can execute vs KT with proper prep. KT GOLD CONTROL NOT DOMINANT IN TOURNAMENT: KT's gold advantage in Week 2 wins (92.7 GPM Game 2) was high but BRO forced 45+ minute game. Tournament data shows both teams struggle efficiency vs HLE (2399 GPM leader). PSYCHOLOGICAL MOMENTUM FACTOR: KT's 0-2 loss to Nongshim in Week 3 followed by 2-3 series loss in same week suggests tilt/confidence collapse. BRO, despite inconsistency, has no comparable downward spiral in recent data. SERIES LOSS FREQUENCY: Both teams have multiple 1-2/2-3 losses (BRO vs HLE, FearX, DRX; KT vs Nongshim twice), but KT's are MORE recent (Week 3), suggesting fresher damage to team morale. DRAFT FLEXIBILITY GAP UNCLEAR: No champion pool or draft data provided; BO3 advantage cannot be quantified. Absence of evidence = confidence penalty on KT's suspected advantage. MARKET OVERREACTION TO WEEK 2 RESULT: KT's Week 2 victory over BRO (2-1) drove YES down 33pp over 7 days. Market may have anchored too heavily on single result without weighing Week 3 collapse. UPSIDE SCENARIO: BRO wins 2-1 by securing Game 1 (strong recent record) + Game 3 (red-side advantage), while exploiting KT mental fragility and lack of confidence vs mid-tier teams post-Week 3. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on KT's Week 3 failures (confidence_no=72) but limited intel on BRO's internal form (no recent practice data, coaching adjustments). Confidence_yes held at 35 due to data gap on BRO's preparation.", "key_factor": "KT's catastrophic Week 3 collapse (0-2 vs NS, 2-3 vs NS again) suggests severe momentum loss and mental fragility that BRO can exploit with consistent red-side execution.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.65, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "KT defeated BRO 2-1 in Week 2 LCK Cup matchup (games 2-3 decisive wins with dominant control), establishing recent direct precedent favoring KT. However, KT's Week 3 form collapsed sharply: 0-2 series loss to Gen.G, then 2-3 loss to NS, then 1-2 loss to NS again\u2014three consecutive series losses indicate significant recent regression. BRO won game 1 vs KT in Week 2 with 14 kills and 75.4 GPM, proving capability to execute against KT on blue side. BRO's tournament win rate (32%, 6-13 record) and KT's rate (35%, 6-11 record) are nearly identical and both poor, suggesting structural team issues rather than clear skill gap. KT's head-to-head record vs top teams catastrophic (0-2 vs T1, 0-2 vs Gen.G), indicating vulnerability; BRO showed competitive wins vs HLE (2-1 in Week 2 with dominant game 2: 20 kills, 70.3 GPM). BRO's red-side win rate in tournament superior to blue; KT showed mixed side performance. BO3 format may favor BRO's ability to adapt across sides. Market price (18% YES / 82% NO) reflects KT recency bias from Week 2 win, but fails to weight KT's severe Week 3 collapse\u2014sharp 33pp decline in YES odds over 7 days suggests market correcting this. BRO's GDM (-145) vs KT's GDM (-97) shows KT slightly more efficient, but both teams significantly underperform elite tier (Gen.G +362). Time-to-event (1.8 days): imminent match with little time for team adjustments; recent form trends (KT down, BRO stable) likely to persist. Confidence asymmetry: strong data on KT's Week 3 collapse and BRO's competitive history vs mid-tier opponents; weaker data on underlying draft meta shifts or roster changes between Week 2 and Rounds 1-2. Base rate for team repeating BO3 win within 1-2 weeks typically 60-65%, but heavily discounted when winner enters with 3 consecutive series losses (KT's state). Historical precedent: teams on losing streaks rarely maintain betting favoritism despite recent head-to-head win; KT's -97 GDM and Week 3 trajectory suggest mean reversion risk.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches, teams winning recent head-to-head encounters (within 1-2 weeks) repeat victories ~60-65% of the time; however, this rate drops to ~45-50% when the winning team shows poor form vs top competitors and the losing team demonstrates selective strength.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "Market pricing at 18% YES reflects heavy recency bias toward KT's Week 2 series victory (2-1 over BRO), but this weighting ignores critical subsequent form collapse. KT's Week 3 performance is damning: 0-2 loss to Gen.G, then 2-3 loss to NS. This 1-4 record in 5 games post-Week-2 victory suggests genuine deterioration, not noise. BRO's recent trajectory is similarly poor but less clear-cut: losses to DRX (2-3 playoff, then competitive in Week 3) and NS (0-2) bookend some strong wins vs HLE (2-1 with 20+ kill victories). Head-to-head recency (Week 2) shows KT dominant in games 2-3 (92.7 GPM, 45:35 duration, 20-17 kill control), but BRO's game 1 win (75.4 GPM, 37:59 duration) shows the matchup is not one-sided. Current market reflects: (a) KT's Week 2 series win is still the dominant signal, (b) heavy discounting of Week 3 collapse as 'noise' or team fatigue, (c) low confidence in BRO's ability to capitalize despite improved Week 2 form vs HLE. Rational apathy detected: market has NOT repriced KT down to 35% despite a 1-4 Week 3 record. A 10-game sample (2 wins in Week 2, 1 win in Week 1, then 1-4 in Week 3) suggests KT's true win% is ~35-40%, not 82%. BRO's tournament record is 6W-13L (32%), worse than KT's 6W-11L (35%), but both teams are near-equivalent in strength and both deteriorating. The 64-point spread (18% vs 82%) is not justified by a ~3% difference in raw win rate. BO3 format favors adaptability and consistency. Neither team has shown recent consistency. BRO's draft flexibility (multiple red-side wins) may offer slight edge if series goes long. Market is crowded SHORT (NO at 82%), creating value on YES side if BRO can replicate Week 2 form vs HLE or steal a game 1 with red-side pick priority. Confidence in YES estimate is moderate (62): KT's Week 3 collapse is recent and substantial, supporting lower KT odds, but BRO is also deteriorating, making any reversal uncertain. Confidence in NO estimate is higher (75): market may be correctly identifying KT as marginally better despite recent losses, and a single BO3 is high-variance; even 35% true win-rate teams lose individual series. Time-to-reversal check: event is THIS WEEK (~1.8 days), so market is nearly locked in. Sharp moves on Apr 05 (-21.5pp for YES) and Apr 07 (-8.5pp for YES) indicate consensus formed early and hardened around Week 2 KT victory; limited new information will shift this before match.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.65, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "KT won Week 2 BO3 2-1 against BRO with superior gold conversion (92.7 GPM game 2), but this victory occurred 10+ days before this fixture on patch 16.1 standard competitive meta. CRITICAL CONCERN: KT's Week 3 performance (0-2 vs Gen.G, then 2-3 to NS) suggests significant form regression or coach/roster changes; BRO showed competitive wins vs HLE (2-1) in same week, indicating relative momentum trending toward BRO. BRO won game 1 in Week 2 matchup vs KT (14 kills, 75.4 GPM, red-side execution), demonstrating pick/champion comfort in early game; BRO's 3 red-side victories (DRX, HLE) show side-agnostic adaptability. KT's overall LCK Cup 2026 win rate (35%, 6-11 record) and GDM differential (-97) are among worst in tournament; BRO's 32% record (6-13) is marginally worse but with fewer total games played in Rounds 1-2 window. Macro efficiency metric: HLE leads GPM (2399/2324), BRO achieved 2296 GPM (top 3 in Rounds 1-2), suggesting BRO has better late-game gold management than KT's historical patterns. BO3 format favors draft flexibility and meta adaptation; meta shift between patch 16.1 (Week 2) and April 12 possible given 10-day gap\u2014no patch history provided, preventing certainty on draft priorities. Playin/Week 3 sample sizes show both teams' inconsistency, but KT's losses to lower-seeded opponents (NS beat KT 1-2 in Week 3 after KT 2-1 record vs DNS) raise concerns about mental tilt or systemic issues. BRO's series records show ability to win 2-1 formats (HLE Week 2), not just isolated games; KT's Week 3 regression (1-2 series loss to NS after strong start) indicates lack of resilience. Market price (18% YES, 82% NO) reflects heavy KT favoritism from Week 2 result, but 33pp drop in YES over 7 days and recent KT Week 3 collapse suggest sharp move was justified; current pricing may overshoot given BRO's week 2-3 competitive form. Tournament structure (LCK Cup Rounds 1-2 = April 12 = upper bracket or early playoff stage) means meta reads and recent scrim data critical; BRO's Week 3 competitive losses to DRX (2-3) still show team can contest full BO5 lengths against strong opposition.", "key_factor": "KT's Week 2 victory over BRO (2-1) came on patch 16.1 with decisive macro control, but KT's catastrophic Week 3 collapse (0-2 vs Gen.G, losses to NS) and BRO's recent ability to win series against HLE suggest momentum reversal and draft meta shift favoring BRO's teamfight composition by Rounds 1-2.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "KT's recent trajectory is sharply negative: Week 3 showed 0-2 loss to NS followed by 2-3 series loss to NS again, suggesting KT hit a form wall or psychological tilt rather than technical regression. BRO won game 1 of their Week 2 matchup on blue side with clean execution (75.4 GPM, 14 kills); they demonstrated they can compete with KT in isolated games when draft favors them. KT's win-rate against established top teams (T1, Gen.G) is 0-4 (0-2 and 0-2 losses), but BRO is NOT in that tier\u2014BRO is closer to mid-tier, where KT's meta vulnerability may be exposed. BRO's red-side win rate is notably superior to their blue-side consistency; three red-side wins (vs DRX, HLE) suggest they have a hidden draft/playstyle strength that could flip a BO3 if side selection favors them. KT's dominant Week 2 game 2 (92.7 GPM, 45:35 duration) was an anomalously long game where KT's scaling won; BRO can counter by forcing faster, tempo-based games where their early execution matters more. Tournament-wide gold efficiency data shows HLE leading at 2399/2324 GPM; KT and BRO are below that tier, suggesting neither team has solved the meta\u2014patch 16.1/16.2 transition may shuffle win conditions. No recent roster changes or injury updates are mentioned in briefing for either team; absence of such intel in THIS WEEK context is a data gap\u2014a key player absence would dramatically favor BRO. BRO's Week 3 loss to DRX came in a 2-3 series (not 0-3), indicating they remain competitive when playing from behind; KT's Week 3 collapse was more total (0-2 and 2-3), suggesting mental tilt is more likely for KT than BRO. Market has moved -33pp on YES side over 7 days, suggesting consensus is crystallizing around KT; contrarian edge exists if BRO's red-side draft flexibility and recent KT form decay are underweighted. BO3 format favors teams with adaptive drafting; BRO's mixed results suggest they may have developed patch-specific counters between Weeks 2-3 that could exploit KT's now-exposed mid-tier weakness.", "key_factor": "BRO executes a surprise meta shift or roster adjustment targeting KT's Week 3 form collapse, exploiting KT's vulnerability to mid-tier opponents and recent 0-2/2-3 series losses while leveraging superior red-side win rate.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.34355353075170847, "no_score": 0.6679166666666667, "edge": 0.16855353075170848, "no_edge": -0.15708333333333324, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 62% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1867407", "question": "LoL: HANJIN BRION vs KT Rolster (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between HANJIN BRION and KT Rolster in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 12 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HANJIN BRION\" if HANJIN BRION win the match against KT Rolster.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"KT Rolster\" if KT Rolster win the match against HANJIN BRION.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.175, "volume_usd": 21657.314426999998, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["112121405