{"run_id": "d3e13250-942b-4d17-8f82-c1ce5286ee84", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:51:09.574164+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1914542", "question": "Valorant: NAVI Junior vs Lost Puppies (BO3) - VCL NORTH//EAST Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between NAVI Junior and Lost Puppies in the VCL NORTH//EAST Group A, initially scheduled for April 11 at 9:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"NAVI Junior\" if NAVI Junior win the match against Lost Puppies.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Lost Puppies\" if Lost Puppies win the match against NAVI Junior.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.74, "volume_usd": 10214.680740000003, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["64043360539168422695666620916726602064664365968827937126941751089561463247543", "27720439956573878609949371163117225449161474555909131304521665297368634932926"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled for April 11 at 9:00 AM ET (13:00 UTC). Briefing timestamp is 14:50 UTC on April 11, meaning the match should have concluded ~1.5 hours ago or is currently in progress. This is a LIVE/IMMINENT resolution scenario. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side surged +36.0pp in the final 10 minutes (14:50 UTC move), rising from ~38% to 74%. This dramatic late move suggests real-time information flow \u2014 either a team took an early map lead, the match started strongly for NAVI Junior, or community consensus shifted based on early broadcast data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: NAVI Junior has documented tournament presence (team rating 1536-1584, Stage 1 playoff win vs Enisorail on 2026/03/21, consistent VCL participation). Lost Puppies has virtually no performance history in the briefing \u2014 no stats, no recent matches, no team profile. This asymmetry is significant. ORGANIZATIONAL FACTOR: NAVI Junior benefits from a major esports organization's infrastructure and experience. Junior teams of established orgs typically outperform unknown challengers in group stage Bo3s. MISSING DATA ON LOST PUPPIES: The briefing provides zero performance metrics for Lost Puppies (no match history, no team rating, no recent form). This is a substantial data gap that prevents confident evaluation of the NO side. MARKET BEHAVIOR: The 7-day weighted average shows YES at only 41% until the massive +36pp move 10 minutes before briefing timestamp. This suggests either: (a) the match started and NAVI Junior took an early advantage, or (b) breaking news/roster information emerged. Either way, the market repricing reflects recent information not fully captured in the briefing's static data. BO3 FORMAT & GROUP STAGE: Single match in group stage is high-variance, but NAVI's documented experience and organizational backing provide marginal edge over an unknown opponent. RESOLUTION RISK (SECONDARY): Criteria are clear \u2014 first team to win the match wins the market. No forfeit/walkover has been mentioned. VLR.gg resolution source is standard for Valorant. Minimal mechanism risk. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: The late market surge (74% YES) aligns with NAVI Junior's structural advantages and near-zero data on Lost Puppies. However, lack of real-time match data prevents ultra-high confidence. A 72% probability acknowledges NAVI's edge while respecting the missing information on Lost Puppies' actual strength. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 62 (good data on NAVI, organizational advantage, late market move supports YES) but tempered by uncertainty about whether the late move reflects actual match advantage or speculative betting. confidence_no = 48 (almost no data on Lost Puppies; cannot assess their true capability; this side is under-informed in the briefing).", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data on Lost Puppies prevents full confidence in either outcome; market may be reacting to real-time information (match may be live or just concluded at briefing time 14:50 UTC).", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.71, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM IS REAL: YES rose +44pp over 7 days and +34.5pp in 24 hours, culminating in a massive +36pp surge at 14:50 UTC (just 2+ hours before 19:00 UTC match start). This timing suggests late-arriving information (likely lineup confirmation, scrimmage results, or community consensus) that moved sophisticated bettors into YES. ORGANIZATIONAL ADVANTAGE: NAVI Junior is the junior/academy team of Natus Vincere, a tier-1 esports org with infrastructure, coaching, and financial resources. Lost Puppies has zero visible competitive history in the briefing\u2014no roster data, no match records, no rating tracking. This asymmetry strongly favors NAVI. TOURNAMENT PEDIGREE: NAVI Junior has documented VCL NORTH//EAST participation across Stage 1 and Stage 2, with a confirmed placement-round win vs. Enisorail (March 21, 2026) and current team rating tracking in the 1536\u20131584 range. This establishes continuity and competitive credibility. Lost Puppies is a blank slate. EXPERIENCE IN FORMAT: NAVI Junior has played multiple BO3 matches in this exact tournament format (single round-robin group stage). They've survived competitive filtering. Lost Puppies' experience level is entirely unknown, a massive red flag in a BO3 that requires tactical depth and mental resilience. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: Lost Puppies' complete absence from search results, match histories, and rating systems suggests either a newly formed roster, a team with minimal historical record, or a squad without recent tournament activity. Entering a BO3 against an experienced academy team with no track record is a severe structural disadvantage. CONFOUNDING: The briefing contains corrupted/partial player stats and mixed match data (references to sleepers, M80, NRG Academy, Maryville University alongside NAVI/Lost Puppies head-to-head). This noise prevents precise skill assessment, but the signal is clear: NAVI has institutional history; Lost Puppies does not. TIME-TO-REVERSAL IS MINIMAL: Match resolves in ~4 hours. The +36pp surge at 14:50 UTC (2+ hours pre-match) reflects final information settlement. For Lost Puppies to overturn this, they would need to be a genuinely strong roster keeping a low profile, an extremely unlikely hidden advantage with no evidence in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (72) is notably higher than confidence_no (45). YES side has clear supporting data: NAVI's org, tournament experience, team ratings, prior wins. NO side's confidence is LOW because Lost Puppies lack ANY counter-evidence\u2014we cannot validate their strength, so we cannot confidently rule out an upset. However, absence of evidence is weak counter to NAVI's presence of evidence. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: At 74% YES, the market is pricing in ~26% upset probability for Lost Puppies. Given zero visible competitive credentials and NAVI's established pedigree, this 26% may actually be slightly generous to the underdog, suggesting YES could be even stronger. The 71% estimate reflects slight caution on the missing Lost Puppies data, but leans decisively toward the favorite.", "key_factor": "NAVI Junior's established organizational backing and demonstrated VCL tournament experience versus Lost Puppies' absence from competitive records, combined with sharp YES-side momentum (+36pp in last 10 minutes reflecting pre-match information flow).", "probability_yes": 0.71, "probability_no": 0.29000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL ANOMALY: YES crashed from 59% weighted average (7-day EMA) to 74% current price, but the spike (+36pp in 10 minutes at 14:50 UTC on match day) is inconsistent with gradual confidence building. This suggests urgent, real-time information not visible in briefing data\u2014likely roster availability, technical forfeit risk, or NAVI Junior lineup issues. TIMING CRITICAL: Event is TODAY (~4 hours to resolution). A 36pp swing 10 minutes before match time indicates traders with live access to team/tournament information. NAVI Junior price surge despite data vacuum suggests reactive panic-buying based on missing context, not fundamental strength. NAVI JUNIOR FUNDAMENTALS WEAK: Only concrete evidence is a single 2-0 win vs Enisorail (March 21, 2026)\u2014one match in 3+ weeks ago. No recent Stage 2 match data provided. Being a junior academy team does NOT guarantee competitive edge; many academy squads underperform in group stages. LOST PUPPIES DATA GAP: Briefing explicitly notes 'limited specific information about Lost Puppies' recent performance or head-to-head record.' However, absence of data is not evidence of weakness. Lost Puppies' 26% price reflects market uncertainty, not proof of inferiority. Emerging/newer teams can upset established squads in single-elimination BO3s. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: Briefing shows one prior H2H result in VCL 26 NE Stage 1: NAVI Junior won 1-0 in a different format (LR5 losers bracket). This was ~2.5 weeks ago in Stage 1; teams may have shifted rosters, strategies, or preparation focus for Stage 2. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence (45%) reflects visible organizational backing for NAVI but thin recent form data. NO confidence (35%) is low because Lost Puppies' actual roster composition, recent scrim results, and current roster status are entirely absent from briefing\u2014cannot validate upset thesis with evidence, only identify data gaps. VOLATILE ORDERBOOK: 13.7pp/hr volatility + low USD volume ($10,215) indicates thin liquidity and high information asymmetry. Professional/insider traders may have moved shares in final hours; retail market likely overweighting NAVI's organizational pedigree without live form knowledge. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-three matches are high-variance. Group stage play (mid-tournament, not playoff-intensity matches) favors teams with deeper preparation and map diversity. Neither team's map pool or recent scrim performance is available, making NAVI's 74% price hard to justify without current roster/meta data. PROBABILITY REFLECTS UNDERDOG CASE: 