y be overconfident or NAVI Junior may have studied Lost Puppies extensively but the briefing's silence suggests public scouting data is minimal.", "key_factor": "Lost Puppies deploys an unexpected roster substitution or tactical meta-shift that exploits NAVI Junior's preparation assumptions, combined with NAVI Junior's Stage 2 form being weaker than their Stage 1 placement win suggests.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6679638009049773, "no_score": 0.3412847222222223, "edge": -0.07203619909502268, "no_edge": 0.08128472222222227, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 63% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1914542", "question": "Valorant: NAVI Junior vs Lost Puppies (BO3) - VCL NORTH//EAST Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between NAVI Junior and Lost Puppies in the VCL NORTH//EAST Group A, initially scheduled for April 11 at 9:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"NAVI Junior\" if NAVI Junior win the match against Lost Puppies.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Lost Puppies\" if Lost Puppies win the match against NAVI Junior.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the 