ogs' negative map differential suggests fundamental skill or coordination gaps"], "key_context": ["Tournament format: 8-team single round-robin groups; top 4 advance to playoffs; all matches are BO3", "XtremeDogs' current overall record appears to be 0-3 in the stage, though early match data shows 0-1 with maps 16-26", "Match scheduled for April 11, 2026 at 15:00 CEST during group stage window (April 4-14)", "No head-to-head history or recent form trajectory data available for either team beyond this tournament", "Limited competitive intelligence on Bitfix Gaming; unable to assess their roster strength or recent performance"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T14:52:15.336054Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "4701085353912870261128663265951670970153069016319403399872219157029516191086", "data_points": 41, "weighted_avg": 0.3306959556708168, "change_1w_pp": 30.999999999999993, "change_24h_pp": 39.49999999999999, "volatility_24h": 14.915087040596559, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T08:00:47Z", "delta_pp": -6.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T10:00:49Z", "delta_pp": 7.500000000000001}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:51:49Z", "delta_pp": 41.5}]}, "no": {"token_id": "12689172588157374949648130824305688013241103882152602813951386330860988001571", "data_points": 56, "weighted_avg": 0.6555593164724314, "change_1w_pp": -19.5, "change_24h_pp": -38.99999999999999, "volatility_24h": 9.591161796955811, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-11T13:00:50Z", "delta_pp": -29.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:00:50Z", "delta_pp": 7.000000000000001}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:51:45Z", "delta_pp": -19.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-11T14:52:15.653340Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-11T19:10:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-12T17:24:13.325891+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "7adb0255-42c8-42ab-994f-aeb03ee52b08", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:53:51.986502+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918592", "question": "Valorant: Dortmund eSports vs CGN Esports (BO3) - VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Dortmund eSports and CGN Esports in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 11 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dortmund eSports\" if Dortmund eSports win the match against CGN Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CGN Esports\" if CGN Esports win the match against Dortmund eSports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.275, "volume_usd": 6550.812734000005, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["15431384217846128096429066397576341526396196935771473746588596547486326263363", "39967104714177756292878436045879604010350698534755622614006872613856519098396"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Dortmund eSports wins the BO3 match against CGN Esports on April 11, 2026 at 11:00 AM ET. MARKET ALIGNMENT: YES = 28% current price; NO = 72%. Market strongly favors CGN Esports. CGN ESPORTS STRENGTH: 2-0 record with +21 map differential and 6 points in group stage indicates dominant early performance. Round stats (61 won vs 40 allowed) show offensive strength. DORTMUND ESPORTS DATA GAP: Recent matches listed (vs eSports Cologne Apr 7; vs TeamOrangeGaming Apr 8) but actual results/scores not provided in briefing. Standing and record described as 'not clearly detailed', preventing direct comparison. TEAM STRENGTH ASYMMETRY: CGN's quantified dominance (2-0, +21 map diff, 6p) vs Dortmund's opaque record creates information disadvantage for Dortmund side. In absence of contrary data, market's 72% NO weighting appears justified. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 does increase variance vs single-map format, creating upset potential. However, this is already factored into 28% YES odds and does not overcome the gap in demonstrated group stage performance. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: B-Tier German VCL event with competitive field (FOKUS, ALTERNATE aTTaX, Eintracht Frankfurt noted). No evidence that Dortmund is elevated above average in this tier. SHARP MOVES ON APRIL 9: Large downward moves on YES (-14.5pp, -9.5pp) and volatile swings on NO (+24.0pp) suggest new information or line movement based on anticipated match dynamics. Sharp moves favor NO direction. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES probability (72) because market price and CGN's documented strength align clearly. Lower confidence in NO (45) because Dortmund's actual performance metrics are absent from briefing\u2014cannot validate that they are truly weak, only that data is unavailable. RESOLUTION RISK: Criteria are clear (standard BO3 win); VLR.gg as primary source with fallback to consensus; forfeit/walkover = 50-50; cancellation/delay >7 days = 50-50. No material resolution ambiguity flagged.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no direct head-to-head history, individual player stats, or recent form data for Dortmund eSports; market price reflects strong NO conviction but lacks detailed comparative analysis to validate it.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTH: CGN Esports enters with a flawless 2-0 record, +21 map differential (+5.25 maps/game average), and 6 points in standings \u2014 metrics that indicate not just wins but decisive, dominant victories in a competitive B-Tier DACH tournament field. FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTH: Market pricing at 72% for CGN reflects rational consensus; the sharp 24-hour move of +7.0pp (with +24.0pp spike on Apr 09 10:00 UTC) suggests informed traders validated CGN's dominance with fresh information or match analysis. FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTH: CGN's offense rating of 61 rounds won vs 40 allowed shows sustained round control and efficiency \u2014 critical in Valorant where economy and map control compound across best-of-3 format. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES): Dortmund eSports' record and map count are notably absent from standings summaries despite briefing explicitly detailing CGN's metrics \u2014 this informational asymmetry strongly implies Dortmund is not tracking at CGN's level of performance. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES): Recent match experience vs eSports Cologne and TeamOrangeGaming (Apr 7-8) does not clarify Dortmund's win-loss record or competitive standing; the briefing frames these as context, not evidence of strength. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES): In Week 2 of group stage, teams with 0-2 or 1-1 records are fighting uphill momentum; if Dortmund is undefeated (matching CGN), briefing would highlight it alongside CGN's metrics \u2014 the omission is telling. MARKET MOMENTUM CONFIRMS FAVORITE: YES side fell -10.0pp over 7 days and -7.0pp in 24 hours (volatility 0.7pp/hr), indicating steady trader exit from Dortmund; NO side rose +10.0pp / +7.0pp with higher volatility (1.3pp/hr), showing conviction accumulation on CGN. BO3 FORMAT CONSIDERATION: While BO3 theoretically increases variance vs BO1, it also penalizes inconsistency and rewards map-pool mastery \u2014 CGN's consistent +21 differential across matches suggests they execute all three maps effectively, reducing the 'upset bounce-back' probability that favors lower-seeded teams. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: FOKUS, ALTERNATE aTTaX, and Eintracht Frankfurt are named as competitive top teams, yet CGN still sits at 2nd with perfect record \u2014 this indicates CGN is among the elite performers even in a stacked field, not merely stronger than a weak Dortmund. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) is warranted by clear statistical dominance and market consensus; confidence in YES remains moderate (35) because Dortmund's actual strength cannot be falsified from the briefing \u2014 they may be competitive, but briefing provides zero affirmative evidence of that. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event resolves TODAY in ~6 hours; any comeback by Dortmund would require overcoming a strong, consistent opponent with no statistical support for such an upset \u2014 extremely low probability of major unexpected coaching, roster changes, or external shocks in this timeframe. PRICE VALIDATION: At 28% for YES, the market is pricing in the possibility that Dortmund competes or has hidden strength; probability_score of 28 (not 15-20) reflects appropriate residual uncertainty, but market leans decisively toward CGN's documented superiority.", "key_factor": "CGN Esports' perfect 2-0 record with +21 map differential and 6 group stage points demonstrates consistent dominance that Dortmund eSports' sparse statistical profile cannot match.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH: The briefing provides NO concrete data on Dortmund's current record, map differential, or standing \u2014 this data gap is suspicious and may indicate the market has overweighted CGN's 2-0 record without proper context on Dortmund's actual strength level. UNDERDOG STRENGTH: Dortmund has demonstrated recent competitive activity (matches vs eSports Cologne and TeamOrangeGaming on Apr 7-8), suggesting active preparation and form, while CGN's last mentioned match is undated \u2014 currency of form is unknown for the favorite. UNDERDOG STRENGTH: BO3 format inherently reduces the predictive power of small sample records; a 2-0 team can lose 1-2 or 0-2 across three maps, making 72% pricing potentially overconfident for a group-stage match. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: CGN Esports' 2-0 record is based on only two matches (Week 1 of group stage) \u2014 statistically minimal data to justify 72% confidence in a BO3 matchup. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: The briefing states 'Dortmund eSports' current standing and record are not clearly detailed' \u2014 this absence of data cuts both ways: it may indicate weakness OR that market has underestimated available Dortmund information. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: Market price history shows sharp 24.0pp UPWARD spike on Apr 09 10:00 UTC for NO side, followed by +7.5pp move \u2014 this suggests volatile sentiment shift possibly driven by rumor or incomplete information rather than fundamental match data. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: YES side has fallen -10.0pp over 7 days with sharp -14.5pp drop on Apr 09, but briefing provides NO corresponding NEWS or REASONING that would justify such a dramatic confidence collapse in Dortmund. MARKET STRUCTURE: Only $6,551 USD volume indicates thin liquidity; large sharp moves are consistent with low-volume price discovery rather than confident information aggregation. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Dortmund takes a strong composition pick (Dortmund's agent pool/map pool advantage unknown but possible) and wins 2-0 or 1-2 in a BO3; the BO3 format gives 3 separate opportunities to demonstrate superiority, not a single snapshot. DATA CONSTRAINT: Briefing does NOT provide head-to-head history, recent form metrics (win rate, map win rate), agent pool comparisons, or coaching/roster changes for either team \u2014 confidence in underdog should remain moderate because Dortmund's true capability is genuinely unclear. FAIR PROBABILITY: Given CGN's 2-0 record vs. unknown Dortmund standing, 72% for NO is defensible, but the absence of Dortmund data + BO3 variance + thin market liquidity suggest 32% for YES (68% for NO) is more appropriately calibrated. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) because CGN's 2-0 record is a concrete fact; LOWER confidence in YES (35) because Dortmund's strength is genuinely obscured by data gaps and we cannot quantify their upset probability precisely.", "key_factor": "Dortmund eSports' recent match experience and BO3 format variance could exploit limited statistical visibility on CGN's true depth across multiple maps.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.26, "c