ing away from the 28% YES level.", "key_factor": "In competitive eSports BO3 matches, favorites (2-0 record teams) win ~65-70% of the time against less documented competitors; however, in regional Challengers-tier tournaments, upset rates are elevated to ~35-40% due to volatility and team variance.", "probability_yes": 0.26, "probability_no": 0.74, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CGN Esports' 2-0 record with +21 map differential is the only concrete performance data in briefing; market has priced this dominance heavily into NO side at 72%. Sharp 14.5pp drop on Apr 09 08:00 UTC suggests informed traders reacted to CGN's strength; price has stabilized downward, indicating consensus formed. Dortmund eSports' record is conspicuously absent from standings details \u2014 briefing explicitly notes 'current standing and record are not clearly detailed.' This data gap creates asymmetric uncertainty. BO3 format structurally favors underdog recovery (multiple map chances); market may be overweighting CGN's group stage dominance without accounting for volatility in BO3. Volatility spike on Apr 09 10:00 UTC (+24.0pp for NO) followed by stabilization suggests sharp move was based on CGN standings confirmation, not new information. Market is pricing CGN at 72% on limited sample (2 matches); in B-tier tournament with competitive field (FOKUS, ALTERNATE aTTaX, Eintracht Frankfurt mentioned), early-stage dominance often does not persist. Briefing provides NO case 3x more detailed than YES case; crowd psychology favors the 'known winner' story (CGN 2-0) over the 'mystery underdog' (Dortmund unstated record). Event timing is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution; minimal time for sentiment reversal. Current 72% NO price appears locked in by informed traders who saw CGN standings. Low volume ($6,551) and high volatility on NO side (1.3pp/hr vs 0.7pp for YES) suggest conviction is recent and possibly fragile \u2014 typical of fear-driven crowd repricing. Rational mispricing angle: Dortmund's true record/strength is unknown; if they are mid-tier rather than bottom-tier, BO3 odds shift materially. Market has no data to reject this hypothesis.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.26, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CGN Esports: 2-0 record, 4-1 map count (+3), 6 points in standings \u2014 objective evidence of consistent group stage dominance. Dortmund eSports: No standing position or win-loss record explicitly stated in briefing; recent matches mentioned (April 7 vs eSports Cologne, April 8 vs TeamOrangeGaming) but no results provided \u2014 suggests weaker group stage performance or record. Market pricing (28% YES / 72% NO) aligns with observable skill differential; recent 7-day decline of -10pp for YES reflects growing confidence in CGN through group stage matches. Sharp moves Apr 09 (\u221214.5pp YES, +24.0pp NO) suggest information cascade: likely CGN victory or strong recent performance data shifted trader expectations toward NO. BO3 format increases variance vs single-map play; lower-seeded teams win BO3s at ~25\u201335% rate in professional Valorant due to best-of format allowing map picks, playstyle adaptation, and player momentum swings. Dortmund's match history (vs eSports Cologne, vs TeamOrangeGaming) not tied to explicit results in briefing; absence from tournament standings is material negative signal. Low volume ($6,551 USD, 51 data points YES side) limits confidence in NO prediction; insufficient trader activity on underdog may mask structural information gaps about Dortmund's actual strength. VCL DACH is B-Tier regional qualifier tournament; teams are mid-tier German/EMEA organizations with high match variance; CGN's 2-0 start is strong but not predictive of 100% knockout performance. Resolution source (vlr.gg) is standard for Valorant esports; match occurs TODAY at 21:00 UTC (~6 hours from briefing timestamp), meaning minimal time for injury/roster changes or late-breaking news to shift outcomes.", "key_factor": "CGN Esports' 2-0 record with +21 map differential demonstrates quantifiable dominance in group stage, while Dortmund eSports' absence from clear standings suggests significantly weaker recent performance; however, BO3 variance and incomplete Dortmund statistics create material uncertainty on the NO side.", "probability_yes": 0.26, "probability_no": 0.74, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CGN's 2-0 record and +21 map differential are strong, but the briefing provides NO competitive analysis of Dortmund's actual strength\u2014only absence-of-data on their standings. Market has collapsed 10pp in 7 days toward NO, with sharp -14.5pp drop on Apr 09\u2014this suggests smart money detected a CGN edge or Dortmund weakness not reflected in early-week pricing. Briefing confirms Dortmund played eSports Cologne (Apr 7) and TeamOrangeGaming (Apr 8), but provides zero map scores, round counts, or win/loss outcomes\u2014competitive silence is conspicuous. BO3 format inherently favors underdog reversals in B-Tier tournaments; volatility on NO side (1.3pp/hr) suggests ongoing uncertainty, not settled conviction. Match is online/offline hybrid in DACH region\u2014latency, server stability, and home-crowd audio environment can create tactical advantages for locally-familiar teams; briefing provides zero commentary on this structural factor. Eintracht Frankfurt mentioned alongside CGN and others, implying tournament field is competitive and not dominated; no team has clearly run away with dominant stats. Resolution criteria allows 50-50 if match forfeited/withdrawn before start\u2014low-probability but high-impact personnel disruption (visa issue, illness, coach conflict) could flip market entirely in final hours. CGN's 61 rounds won vs 40 allowed is strong but comes from only 2 matches; small sample size means one off-series could mask deeper team instability or playstyle vulnerability. Dortmund's recent match activity (Apr 7\u20138) suggests active preparation and recent form data unavailable to briefing; if they won those matches, confidence in CGN's 2-0 leadership weakens significantly.", "key_factor": "Dortmund eSports fields a tactical meta-shift lineup or recent roster sub that exploits CGN's map pool weakness, or CGN suffers unexpected player illness/latency issues in an online/offline hybrid match environment.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.26393258426966293, "no_score": 0.7317426273458445, "edge": -0.011067415730337093, "no_edge": 0.006742627345844521, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 53% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918592", "question": "Valorant: Dortmund eSports vs CGN Esports (BO3) - VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Dortmund eSports and CGN Esports in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 11 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dortmund eSports\" if Dortmund eSports win the match against CGN Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CGN Esports\" if CGN Esports win the match against Dortmund eSports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.275, "volume_usd": 6550.812734000005, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["15431384217846128096429066397576341526396196935771473746588596547486326263363", "39967104714177756292878436045879604010350698534755622614006872613856519098396"]}, "key_facts": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 DACH: Evolution Stage 2 is an online/offline German VAL tournament organized by Riot Games and PROJECT V.", "Find detailed results about the VALORANT match between ESports Cologne and Dortmund eSports in VCL DACH: Stage 2 that took place on April 7, 2026 - 20:20", "Find detailed results about the VALORANT match between Dortmund eSports and TeamOrangeGaming in PV: Weekly #2 that took place on April 8, 2026 - 18:10 CEST.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from eSports Cologne vs.", "Dortmund eSports - Week 2 match of Challengers 2026: DACH Evolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "1594 1586 1578 1570 1562 1554 1546 1538 Matches Played Rating.", "Challengers 2026: DACH Evolution - VCL EMEA Qualifier.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Esprit Sh\u014dnen vs.", "WIP Esports - Week 3 match of Challengers 2026: France Revolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "Eintracht Frankfurt, 2-0, 4-2, 73-52, +21, 6p."], "news_summary": "Dortmund eSports and CGN Esports are set to face off in a Best-of-3 match during Week 2 of the VALORANT Challengers 2026 DACH: Evolution Stage 2 group stage. CGN Esports currently holds a strong position in standings with a 2-0 record and 4-1 map count, while Dortmund eSports' current standing and record are not clearly detailed in available results. This is part of the B-Tier German VALORANT tournament organized by Riot Games and PROJECT V.", "side_yes_case": ["CGN Esports has a perfect 2-0 record with strong +21 map differential in group stage", "CGN Esports ranks 2nd in tournament standings with 6 points, demonstrating consistent performance", "Dortmund eSports' record and map count not prominently featured in standings, suggesting weaker group stage performance", "CGN Esports' offense shown at 61 rounds won vs 40 allowed across matches"], "side_no_case": ["Dortmund eSports has recent match experience including games against eSports Cologne and TeamOrangeGaming", "Limited statistical data on Dortmund eSports' performance makes it difficult to assess their current strength", "BO3 format provides opportunity for lower-seeded team to stage comeback across multiple maps", "FOKUS and other top teams (ALTERNATE aTTaX, Eintracht Frankfurt) show competitive field is not dominated by single team"], "key_context": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 DACH: Evolution Stage 2 is B-Tier tournament with group stage format", "Match format i