{"run_id": "8fcb277b-9181-411d-9c7d-4d6e44f83874", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:56:29.093176+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1908444", "question": "Valorant: Caldya Esport vs F9 EICAR (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Caldya Esport and F9 EICAR in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Caldya Esport\" if Caldya Esport win the match against F9 EICAR.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"F9 EICAR\" if F9 EICAR win the match against Caldya Esport.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.405, "volume_usd": 759.946013, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["62708809541629550277753546367767711974766379632874023348309713038665344795687", "32058701447772830092019227062206431172968607341870120577984753713890503621926"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Caldya Esport wins the BO3 match against F9 EICAR on April 11, 2026. MARKET SIGNAL: Current prices show NO (F9) favored at 60% vs YES (Caldya) at 40%, and YES side has risen +12.5pp over 7 days, suggesting some recent sentiment shift toward Caldya. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: Caldya defeated F9 in Stage 1 (Jan 24: Caldya 1-2 F9 indicates Caldya won in BO3). This is the only direct match data available, favoring Caldya by 1 point. RECENT CALDYA FORM: Stage 2 Week 1 shows mixed results\u20142-1 win vs ES, 1-2 loss vs JL. This 1-1 record indicates inconsistency but capability to beat opponents. RECENT F9 FORM: Stage 2 Week 1 shows 2-1 win vs Joblife (Apr 5) and 1-2 loss vs Joblife (earlier date unclear\u2014likely typo or different opponent). Inconsistent data, but F9 has demonstrated wins in Stage 2. COMPETING SIGNALS: Caldya beat F9 in Stage 1 head-to-head, but both teams show mixed Stage 2 form. No clear evidence of roster changes or meta shifts that would invalidate Stage 1 result. STANDING CONTEXT: Briefing notes F9 appears '5th in group stage table' and 'higher in overall competitive standing,' suggesting slightly better positioning. However, exact records and playoff implications are unclear. DATA QUALITY GAPS: Briefing lacks detailed recent performance stats, map pool info, roster composition, or explicit tier rankings. Stage 1 result is 2.5+ months old; team meta and form may have shifted. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: 40% YES / 60% NO is consistent with moderate uncertainty. Recent +12.5pp rise in YES suggests informed trading, but low volume ($760) limits confidence in price efficiency. RESOLUTION RISK: Criteria are clear\u2014winner of the BO3 match determines outcome. Forfeits resolve to 50-50. No ambiguity detected in resolution mechanism. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Head-to-head advantage (Caldya +1) slightly favors YES, but recent mixed form and F9's higher standing create offsetting pressure. Event is TODAY with ~7 hours until match. Stage 1 result is meaningful but not definitive 2.5 months later. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES is slightly higher (58) because head-to-head data exists and Caldya demonstrated Stage 2 capability. Confidence in NO is lower (52) because F9's current form is murkier and tied to incomplete data. Both sides lack strong predictive signals.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is sparse on current team form, rosters, and meta shifts since Stage 1; Stage 1 head-to-head may not reflect current competitive dynamics.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: F9 EICAR is positioned 5th in VCL France Stage 2 group standings, indicating stronger overall competitive tier than Caldya. F9 secured a 2-1 victory vs Joblife in Stage 2 Week 1 (April 5), demonstrating active winning form in current season. F9's standing placement suggests consistent performance across multiple Stage 2 matches. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES: Caldya shows volatile, inconsistent Stage 2 form: 2-1 win (April 4) immediately followed by 1-2 loss (April 6). This back-to-back volatility in Week 1 suggests instability. Caldya's 1-2 loss rate matches their historical weakness (0-2 loss vs MDR in Stage 1). Recent losses outnumber recent wins in small sample. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONSIDERATION: Caldya defeated F9 1-2 in Stage 1 Week 3 (January 24, 2026\u20142.5 months ago). This is the briefing's only direct matchup data, but it is stale and pre-Stage 2 form evolution. Teams improve/decline between stages; January performance has low predictive power for April matches. NO advocates correctly discount this. FORM TRAJECTORY: F9's recent 2-1 win (April 5) is fresher than Caldya's last match (April 6, loss). F9 demonstrates positive momentum entering today; Caldya enters on a loss. 7-day market price action shows YES (Caldya) climbing +12.5pp and NO (F9) falling -12.5pp, but this likely reflects contrarian/momentum trading, not fundamental value. NO side's 60% price reflects appropriate skepticism of market overheating. MISSING DATA GAPS: Briefing does not provide current team rosters, recent scrim results, player availability, or detailed map pool analysis. F9's standing (5th) is stated but Caldya's standing is absent\u2014this asymmetry favors F9 narrative. No coach/strategic changes documented. Without this intel, confidence in either side must remain moderate. VOLATILITY & MARKET INEFFICIENCY: Sharp 9.5pp and 10.0pp moves on April 8 suggest retail/emotional trading rather than information-driven repricing. YES side's +12.5pp weekly rise from 26.5% to 39% appears overdone given Caldya's mixed/negative recent results. NO's -12.5pp decline reflects market overcorrection\u201460% is reasonable floor, possibly underpriced. RESOLUTION TIMING & RISK: Match resolves TODAY in ~7 hours. No time for new information. Low volume ($760) and wide bid-ask spread indicate illiquidity and potential mispricing on either side. This reduces confidence in market pricing but increases value of fundamental analysis. F9's group standing and recent 2-1 win are harder data points than Caldya's stale head-to-head. VERDICT FOR FAVORITE (NO): F9 EICAR's superior standing, fresher Stage 2 momentum (2-1 win), and Caldya's demonstrated inconsistency make F9 the safer favorite. Market price of 60% NO is defensible, though not heavily mispriced. Caldya's Stage 1 head-to-head win is an interesting contrarian point but is too old to override current standing/form divergence.", "key_factor": "F9 EICAR's superior current standing (5th in group stage) and recent Stage 2 competitiveness (2-1 win vs Joblife) outweigh Caldya's stale Stage 1 head-to-head advantage.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "CALDYA'S HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE: Caldya defeated F9 1-2 in January Stage 1 Week 3 matchup, establishing direct competitive edge. This is concrete evidence of Caldya's ability to take maps/rounds against F9, not speculation. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Caldya showed 2-1 victory in Stage 2 Week 1 (April 4), proving capability in current tournament format. F9's most recent Stage 2 result shows 0-2 loss to Nuxeria (April 6), suggesting vulnerability to competent opponents. FORM VOLATILITY FAVORS UNDERDOG: Both teams show inconsistency\u2014Caldya 2-1 then 1-2, F9 mixed results. In BO3 single matches, recent volatility means upset scenarios are plausible; Caldya could replicate their April 4 performance. MARKET PRICING TRAJECTORY SUPPORTS YES: YES side rose +12.5pp over 7 days (35\u219240%) with sharp +9.5pp move on Apr 8, suggesting informed traders are backing Caldya. This aggressive repricing away from 27.5% indicates potential mispricing on NO side. F9 STANDING CLAIM LACKS CONTEXT: Brief mentions F9 in 'top 5 standings' but provides no current group stage table, win-loss records, or seeding. This vague competitive positioning may be stale or contextually weak compared to concrete recent match results. NO SIDE'S VULNERABILITIES: F9's 0-2 loss to Nuxeria is concerning form heading into this match. Joblife win (2-1) is sole positive, but Joblife lost to F9 earlier (1-2 on Apr 5), creating conflicting signals about F9's true strength. TACTICAL UNCERTAINTY: No map-level data, player roster changes, or strategy information provided. Both teams' performances could reflect meta shifts or tactical adjustments between matches. Caldya's January win may reflect enduring strategic advantage. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT ACTIVE: Event resolves TODAY (~7 hours). For a BO3 match, substantial reversal in market odds would require significant pre-match news (roster issues, technical problems, or withdrawal). Low likelihood of major shift; current 40% YES represents genuine uncertainty. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in Caldya's proven capability (confidence_yes = 62) because head-to-head victory and recent 2-1 win are documented. Lower confidence in NO's durability (confidence_no = 48) because F9's actual competitive standing relative to Caldya remains ambiguous despite top-5 claim. UNDERDOG IS FAIRLY PRICED TO SLIGHTLY UNDERPRICED: YES at 40% reflects genuine competitive match, but Caldya's concrete advantages (head-to-head, recent 2-1 form) may justify marginally higher odds (~43-47% range). Current pricing reflects market skepticism that may overweight F9's standing claim relative to matchup-specific evidence.", "key_factor": "Caldya's proven head-to-head victory over F9 in Stage 1 combined with recent Stage 2 win (2-1) demonstrates capacity to beat this opponent despite current market underpricing.", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD ANCHOR: Caldya beat F9 1-2 in Stage 1 (Jan 24), but this was 2.5 months ago; form progression in online B-Tier tournaments typically invalidates single-match history across stage boundaries. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Caldya shows 1-1 record in Stage 2 Week 1 (2-1 win, 1-2 loss); F9 shows 1-1 record (2-1 win vs Joblife, 0-2 loss vs Nuxeria). Both teams exhibit identical volatility; neither has clear momentum. STANDINGS SIGNAL: F9 EICAR positioned 5th in group standings suggests higher overall competitive tier than Caldya, but briefing does not provide Caldya's standing rank. This introduces asymmetric information favoring NO side. QUALITY OF OPPOSITION: Caldya's 1-2 loss was to unnamed opponent (parsing error in briefing); cannot assess relative strength. F9's 0-2 loss to Nuxeria (who beat Caldya indirectly?) and 2-1 win vs Joblife provide mixed signals. MARKET PRICE MOTION: YES side rising +12.5pp over 7 days (from ~27% to 39%) suggests late smart money or insider confidence, but volume is low ($760 USD) and volatility is high (1.0pp/hr). Sharp moves on Apr 8-9 suggest news-driven trading, not fundamental repricing. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION RISK: Event resolves TODAY in ~7 hours. Market is illiquid and approaching closure. Final price (40% YES) may reflect liquidity takers rather than true consensus. At this juncture, reversals are costly and unlikely; if odds shift, it reflects new match intel (lineup changes, forfeits), not fundamental drift. BASE RATE CONSTRAINT: No reliable historical base rate for 'French B-Tier online Valorant team A vs B in stage 2 round-robin' exists in training data. Default VCL France match outcomes cluster near 50-55%, with slight home/seeding bias favoring higher-ranked teams. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES side has concrete data (prior H2H win, recent 2-1 proof of capability), but outdated. NO side benefits from standings signal (5th place) but lacks recent match context on Caldya's rank. Neither side has strong predictive signal. RESOLUTION RISK: 50-50 outcome possible if match is forfeited/canceled, but briefing provides no logistical warnings. Treat as play-as-scheduled. FINAL SYNTHESIS: Market price of 40% YES is slightly undervalued given Caldya's prior H2H w