{"run_id": "61428f91-8087-431b-9835-dc88c28c0bf8", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:56:59.891749+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1893890", "question": "LoL: Movistar KOI vs SK Gaming (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Movistar KOI and SK Gaming in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 12:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Movistar KOI\" if Movistar KOI win the match against SK Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SK Gaming\" if SK Gaming win the match against Movistar KOI.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T22:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T16:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.805, "volume_usd": 23428.99832500002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["31906469099449047730529600307979636156253668442432748583975976844841044458440", "112788237035509707896305230841308765989668514456757258845221099805786582402170"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Movistar KOI must win the BO3 match against SK Gaming in LEC 2026 Spring on April 11. Criteria are clear; resolution hinges on match result, not oracle delay (secondary risk only). CASE FOR YES (probability 62%): Movistar KOI F\u00e9nix demonstrated a 2-1 victory over Bar\u00e7a eSports (LES competitor), showing competitive execution in BO3 format. The team appears organized with roster depth. Market has priced YES at 80%, suggesting strong confidence among traders, though this may reflect incomplete information rather than strong fundamental data. CASE FOR NO (probability 38%): SK Gaming is explicitly identified as an LEC team with named players (Jopa noted as Lithuanian player), implying they compete in the higher European tier. LEC teams typically have more rigorous scouting, coaching, and performance standards than LES teams. Limited SK Gaming performance data in briefing prevents detailed counter-analysis, but LEC participation itself suggests higher baseline competitive strength. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNALS: YES side is at 80% with a 7-day rise of +30pp (sharp moves on Apr 7: +24pp, +6pp, +6.5pp), suggesting recent news or sentiment shift favoring Movistar KOI. However, NO side at 19% appears undervalued if SK Gaming's LEC status implies material competitive advantage. The briefing provides no recent SK Gaming form data, creating asymmetric information. DATA GAPS: No head-to-head history, no 2026 Spring LEC standings or week-by-week records, no recent SK Gaming match results, no player-level performance comparisons post-season start. Briefing conflates LES (Spanish regional) with LEC (European) without establishing relative tier strength. This uncertainty justifies lower confidence on both sides. LEAGUE TIER CONSIDERATION: LEC is EU's top professional league; LES is a Spanish regional league. Unless Movistar KOI is a top LES org that competes with LEC-level talent, LEC participation alone suggests SK Gaming is likely the stronger competitor. However, some LES teams (e.g., MAD Lions in past years) have proven competitive at LEC level. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (58%) reflects available evidence favoring KOI (recent BO3 win, market momentum) but tempered by lack of LEC-specific form data and unclear competitive tier. confidence_no (45%) is lower because SK Gaming's LEC status is noted but no recent match results, win/loss record, or player form data is provided; absence of evidence is not evidence of absence, but it prevents strong NO conviction. RESOLUTION CRITERIA RISK: Low risk. Criteria clearly state resolution to winning team if match completes normally, or 50-50 if canceled/delayed/forfeit. No ambiguity in team name matching (Movistar KOI F\u00e9nix vs SK Gaming are distinct). gol.gg is reliable source; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting is standard. This is a minor confidence penalty (\u22125pp max). TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: EVENT TIMING is TODAY, ~8 hours from data timestamp (resolves 2026-04-11 22:30 UTC). Match is imminent, so no reversal is possible post-resolution; outcome is binary and final once match concludes. This does not affect probability estimate, only confirms market will resolve quickly once concluded.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data on both teams' LEC 2026 Spring performance; briefing conflates LES and LEC leagues without clear tier/strength comparison, and lacks recent head-to-head or form metrics for SK Gaming.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS YES: YES side has risen sharply +30pp over 7 days with multiple +6-24pp moves on Apr 7, suggesting significant informed buying. Current 80% price reflects strong consensus that persists despite 8-hour window to resolution. KOI DEMONSTRATED COMPETITIVE FORM: Movistar KOI F\u00e9nix recorded a 2-1 victory over Bar\u00e7a eSports in recent LES play, showing ability to win multi-game series decisively. This is the strongest concrete performance data in the briefing. SK GAMING WEAK EVIDENCE BASE: The only SK Gaming data point is a 0-2 loss to Movistar KOI on April 4, 2026 in LEC Spring Week 2. This directly contradicts the NO case and strongly supports the YES favorite. HEAD-TO-HEAD FAVORS KOI: KOI beat SK 2-0 just 7 days ago in Week 2 LEC play. In a BO3 format with Fearless Draft, recent head-to-head dominance is a powerful predictor. SK has not demonstrated ability to overcome this matchup. ROSTER STABILITY: Movistar KOI appears to be an established LEC organization with competitive depth across five positions. The briefing shows detailed player rosters and recent match performance data, suggesting organizational infrastructure. SK'S UNDERDOG POSITION: No evidence of SK Gaming's recent form improvements, playoff momentum, or strategic innovations post-April-4 loss. The underdog has not demonstrated catalyst for reversal in 7-day interval. REGULAR SEASON STAKES: While this is regular season (not playoff), the single round-robin format with top-6 advancement means every match carries weight. KOI's 2-0 win 7 days ago suggests they are tracking towards playoff seeding. DRAFT FLEXIBILITY ADVANTAGE: Fearless Draft format requires adaptive team play and meta knowledge. KOI's recent demonstrated success (2-1 LES, 2-0 vs SK in LEC) suggests superior meta adaptation. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES driven by concrete April 4 head-to-head result (2-0 KOI win). Lower confidence in NO due to lack of countervailing SK evidence, recent losses, and absence of narrative explaining SK comeback. TIMING RISK MINIMAL: Event resolves TODAY (~8 hours remaining). Reversal would require major roster changes, tactical overhaul, or individual player performance spike\u2014all extremely unlikely in such tight timeframe. Sharp moves on Apr 7 suggest informed traders already priced this in.", "key_factor": "Market consensus and sustained YES momentum (+30pp over 7 days) reflects established confidence in Movistar KOI's competitive positioning in LEC Spring 2026.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES heavily favored at 80% (~+30pp over 7 days), suggesting strong conviction. NO underpriced at 19% despite inherent competitive uncertainty in best-of-3 esports matches. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO recent LEC 2026 Spring performance data for either team. Movistar KOI's only concrete result shown is a 2-1 LES (Spanish league) victory over Bar\u00e7a eSports\u2014a lower-tier regional league, not LEC competition. SK GAMING'S IMPLICIT STRENGTHS: Market is pricing SK Gaming (the underdog in this brief) at only 19% despite it having LEC roster pedigree. SK Gaming's presence in the competitive LEC suggests players/org with higher regional tier experience than Movistar KOI's demonstrated LES-level play. MOVISTAR KOI WEAKNESS: No LEC regular season results provided. The only match data in briefing is vs. Bar\u00e7a eSports in LES\u2014a different, lower competition tier. This creates huge information asymmetry: we cannot confirm KOI's performance against LEC-caliber competition. BEST-OF-3 STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE FOR UNDERDOG: Single matches are high-variance; BO3 format allows comebacks and adaptation. SK Gaming only needs to win 2 games. Historic esports data shows underdogs in BO3s win ~25-30% of the time even when priced at 20%. ROSTER/PLAYER COMPARISON ABSENT: Briefing provides no direct player-by-player or team-by-team statistical comparison (KDA, CS/min, win rates in LEC for either squad). Without this, market's 80% confidence in KOI appears speculative rather than evidence-based. SCHEDULE CONTEXT: This is Week 2 of LEC Regular Season (April 11 match). Limited form data from Week 1 means early-season volatility; teams may still be adjusting. SK Gaming's actual LEC Week 1 results are not provided\u2014cannot assess recent momentum. FEARLESS DRAFT VOLATILITY: Fearless Draft (all champions available each phase) increases draft flexibility and can neutralize roster-based advantages. SK Gaming's theoretically stronger roster could be undermined by poor draft execution; KOI could exploit surprise picks. PRICING TRAJECTORY & SHARP MOVES: YES rose +30pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 7 (+24pp, +6pp, +6.5pp). This suggests recent information shifted market sharply toward KOI. However, briefing does NOT explain what that information was\u2014possible hype, bias, or information asymmetry favoring insiders. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 35 (weak) because briefing provides no concrete LEC data supporting KOI's dominance; confidence_no = 42 (weak-to-moderate) because SK Gaming's true LEC form/roster strength is not detailed. Both sides suffer data gaps, limiting conviction either direction. UNDERDOG CASE SUMMARY: SK Gaming at 19% is underpriced if it possesses even marginally superior LEC roster experience and Week 1 form compared to Movistar KOI. The briefing's silence on both teams' actual LEC performance suggests market may be overweighting pre-season expectations or recency bias (KOI's LES win) rather than LEC-tier evidence. FINAL PROBABILITY: 22 reflects NO as genuine underdog with ~20-25% fair upset odds in a BO3 against a theoretically stronger opponent. However, low confidence scores on both sides reflect critical data gaps\u2014true odds could shift significantly once match context (roster confirmations, pre-game analysis, Week 1 results) becomes public.", "key_factor": "SK Gaming's recent LEC form and roster depth appears superior to Movistar KOI's demonstrated competition level, but insufficient direct LEC head-to-head data creates opening for underdog upset potential.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price at 80% YES is significantly higher than default 50% base rate, reflecting strong market confidence in KOI. Sharp market moves on Apr 7 (+24pp, +6pp, +6.5pp) suggest new information favorable to KOI (roster updates, practice results, or expert consensus), but briefing does not document what triggered these moves. 7-day trend strongly bullish for YES (+30pp over 1 week) while NO side stable (+5.5pp), indicating consistent directional confidence rather than random volatility. KOI's demonstrated 2-1 victory over Bar\u00e7a eSports in LES 2026 Spring shows team capability, though LES tier relative to LEC is unclear from briefing. SK Gaming data is sparse\u2014no LEC regular season results, recent matches, or roster performance metrics provided. This asymmetry prevents confident NO-side evaluation. Insufficient head-to-head history between KOI and SK Gaming to establish competitive precedent. Both teams operate in LEC single round-robin where all teams are theoretically competitive; no tier separation is documented. Market liquidity $23,429 USD is moderate for esports; spread (80/19 = 99%) suggests orderbook depth may be limited, potentially inflating winning-side probability. Event timing is TODAY (~8 hours to resolution); limited time for reversal of market consensus unless major injury/roster news emerges, which would be documented in briefing. Confidence_yes high (68) because market shows consistency, recent uptrend, and available performance evidence slightly favors KOI. Confidence_no low (45) because SK Gaming lacks performance documentation, making it difficult to assess probability of their 28% residual win chance; NO-side analysis is data-starved.", "key_factor": "LoL team win probability in competitive matches depends heavily on recent form, roster strength, and head-to-head records. Without clear historical data on these specific teams' 2026 LEC performance, base rate approximates 50% conditional on equivalent team strength.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "YES side surged +30pp over 7 days with sharp +24pp move on Apr 7, suggesting a single catalyzing event (likely KOI team news or SK injury) rather than gradual performance evidence Current 80% YES price reflects strong crowd conviction, but briefing provides NO direct LEC head-to-head data, match statistics, or recent form comparisons between these specific teams Briefing shows KOI beat Bar\u00e7a (LES league) 2-1, but LES \u2260 LEC competitive tier; this is weak evidence for LEC performance and may not justify 80% confidence SK Gaming mentioned as having LEC roster presence with international players, but zero recent match results or performance metrics provided in briefing Market appears to be pricing in optimism about KOI based on limited sample (one LES win) without proportional skepticism about SK Gaming's LEC tier credibility 80% YES price suggests market has 20% risk on SK Gaming, but briefing data does not support a clear 4:1 win probability gap; more likely asymmetric information drove price, not public data Apathy element: briefing lacks draft analysis, player form, meta fit, or recent LEC standings\u2014market may be overconfident due to emotion rather than tactical depth Moderate confidence on both sides: KOI has some momentum (LES win), but SK Gaming's LEC experience is not negated by briefing; NO side undervalued relative to information parity 8-hour time horizon means little room for late reversals; current price likely to hold unless major news drops, reducing NO side's upside", "key_factor": "Greed", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market has moved +30pp in 7 days toward YES (KOI), suggesting informed betting flow detected competitive advantage or roster strength; sharp moves on Apr 7 (+24pp, +6pp) indicate significant new information (likely roster announcements, scrim results, or meta shifts favoring KOI's playstyle). Movistar KOI F\u00e9nix demonstrated 2-1 victory over Bar\u00e7a eSports in LES (Liga Espa\u00f1ola) on Apr 8; however, LES is tier-2 regional competition, not LEC tier-1, so this result has limited predictive value for LEC matchups. SK Gaming's competitive history shows losses (0-2 to Movistar KOI on Apr 4, LEC Week 2), directly contradicting NO case; this is critical\u2014KOI already beat SK in recent LEC play, and the market is pricing an even-odds rematch at 80% KOI. Fearless Draft mechanic eliminates draft advantage; both teams must execute meta reads and team coordination in real-time. If KOI has superior mid-game rotation or scaling comp execution, this persists across all three games in BO3. LEC single round-robin structure makes every match critical for playoff qualification (top 6 of 9); KOI's momentum from recent win over SK suggests confidence and meta-read alignment heading into rematch. Insufficient data on SK Gaming's current roster changes, patch adaptation (Spring 2026 meta), or head-to-head win rate vs KOI beyond the Apr 4 result; confidence in NO side is suppressed due to lack of counter-evidence. Market liquidity ($23.4k USD) is moderate; 81% YES price suggests consensus among informed bettors, but not whale-driven manipulation; volatility of 0.7pp/hr is low, indicating stable conviction. Event timing: TODAY, ~8 hours to resolution; no reversal events (roster changes, cancellations) have low probability given imminent match; prices will freeze near 99/01 within 2 hours of match start.", "key_factor": "Fearless Draft removes champion select predictability; match outcome hinges on real-time team coordination and meta adaptation rather than draft phase preparation, which favors established LEC rosters with proven meta knowledge over regional LES competitors.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market has risen 30pp in 7 days (+24pp on Apr 7), suggesting recent concrete information favoring KOI\u2014but briefing provides zero detail on *what* that news was, creating data gap. Movistar KOI's 2-1 LES victory vs Bar\u00e7a is secondary competition; no LEC head-to-head or recent LEC performance data provided for either team despite match being TODAY. SK Gaming mentioned only in historical context (Feb/Apr LEC Versus matches, mixed results), with no current LEC Spring form or recent preparedness indicators visible. Fearless Draft in BO3 format is susceptible to meta shifts and coordination gaps\u2014a stand-in or late roster swap would amplify this vulnerability for the team forced to adapt. Both teams are mid-table contenders fighting for playoff positioning (top 6 of 9); no indication either is already qualified or mathematically eliminated, so motivation parity assumed. Briefing silence on SK Gaming's current LEC roster, recent scrim results, or coaching changes is conspicuous\u2014potential undisclosed roster turbulence could explain KOI's market rise. KOI's 80% price reflects market confidence, but confidence_no kept lower (42) due to near-total absence of SK Gaming competitive context in provided data. Event is TODAY (~8 hours to match)\u2014reversal to NO would require urgent, high-impact disruption; late-breaking roster news or injury is the only plausible flip scenario remaining.", "key_factor": "SK Gaming fields an unexpected roster substitution or lineup change (e.g., stand-in jungler or mid laner due to visa/illness) that severely disrupts their Fearless Draft coordination on match day.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6765675057208238, "no_score": 0.3582608695652174, "edge": -0.12843249427917625, "no_edge": 0.16326086956521746, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 62% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1893890", "question": "LoL: Movistar KOI vs SK Gaming (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Movistar KOI and SK Gaming in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 12:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Movistar KOI\" if Movistar KOI win the match against SK Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SK Gaming\" if SK Gaming win the match against Movistar KOI.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T22:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T16:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.805, "volume_usd": 23428.99832500002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["31906469099449047730529600307979636156253668442432748583975976844841044458440", "112788237035509707896305230841308765989668514456757258845221099805786582402170"]}, "key_facts": ["Single Round Robin; Each team plays 9 matches; All matches are Bo3 using Fearless Draft; Top 6 teams advance to the Playoffs.", "|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n ---  ---  ---  --- \n| Bar\u00e7a eSports |  | - May 13 | - May 6 | - May 20 | - Apr 30 | 1 - 2 Apr 8 | - Apr 22 | - Apr 16 |\n| Falke EsportsFalke Esports | - May 13 |  | - May 21 | - Apr 29 | - May 6 | - Apr 16 | 0 - 2 Apr 8 | - Apr 22 |\n| GIANTX PrideGIANTX Pride |