{"run_id": "9b2a6381-41de-430b-9d1c-159bd179b41b", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:57:42.661704+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1940442", "question": "Counter-Strike: ENCE vs  CSDIILIT (BO3) - Elisa Open Suomi Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper Bracket Final match between ENCE and  CSDIILIT in the Elisa Open Suomi Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 11 at 1:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ENCE\" if ENCE win the match against  CSDIILIT.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" CSDIILIT\" if  CSDIILIT win the match against ENCE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T23:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T17:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.63, "volume_usd": 2090.8235799999998, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["99170397579753499677052864328170814877041638740409125636100926621589432521324", "35657535018307751475861109911284490341511682968541660697491804420298079488054"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "ENCE holds significant ranking advantage (#120 globally vs CSDIILIT #152-165), indicating stronger tier and competitive pedigree. BO3 format structurally favors the stronger, more consistent team \u2014 upsets are harder to sustain across 3 maps than single-map formats. ENCE is established Finnish team with regional home-country advantage in Elisa Open Suomi (domestic tournament). Market price has risen sharply to 63% YES over past 24 hours (+12.5pp), suggesting informed betting has moved toward ENCE conviction. Limited recent form data means ranking differential is primary signal; no evidence of ENCE form collapse or CSDIILIT exceptional recent performance. Regional lower-tier tournament ($5,760 prize pool) has higher variance than Tier-1 events, but ranking gap is still substantial. No head-to-head history provided; cannot assess CSDIILIT exploit potential, but ranking suggests ENCE should win ~65-70% of such matchups in BO3. Event timing is TODAY (resolves in ~8 hours) \u2014 no reversal risk; match will be played and outcome will be clear, trading toward $0.01/$0.99 once result known. Resolution criteria are clear: straightforward match outcome, with 50-50 fallback only for cancellation/tie/forfeit/7-day delay (none anticipated). Confidence in YES is slightly higher than NO due to clear ranking advantage and BO3 structure; confidence in NO is lower due to lack of countervailing evidence (underdog narrative insufficient without recent form data).", "key_factor": "Team name 'CSDIILIT' may contain spelling discrepancy or abbreviation that could affect resolution if HLTV uses alternate naming; however, resolution criteria explicitly account for minor naming discrepancies.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "ENCE is the clear favorite with a 26-point ranking advantage globally (#120 vs #152-165), positioning them as the established tier-1 regional competitor in Finland. Market momentum strongly supports YES: +12.5pp over 24 hours with a sharp +8.0pp move on Apr 10 at 22:00 UTC, suggesting informed bettors and insiders have confidence in ENCE. NO side is collapsing: -4.5pp over 24 hours including a -5.5pp drop on Apr 11 at 08:00 UTC, indicating loss of confidence in the underdog even from contrarian positions. BO3 format historically favors stronger, more consistent teams over one-off upsets \u2014 ENCE's higher tier status and competitive experience give them multiple opportunities to win the series. ENCE holds regional home-country advantage as an established Finnish team with tournament pedigree, while CSDIILIT appears to be a lower-tier squad with less documented tournament history. Current 63% YES price appears fairly calibrated but potentially slightly underpriced given the ranking gap (26 points) and the directionality of recent betting flow. CSDIILIT's primary path to upset requires exceptional performance on a specific day, but lack of recent form data for either team means we cannot rule out ENCE underperforming or CSDIILIT overperforming. Confidence in YES is moderate-to-high (72) because ranking differential and market momentum are strong signals; confidence in NO is low (45) because underdog data is sparse and market flow is decisively against them. Event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours with online format, eliminating venue variables; resolution via HLTV.org is clear and unambiguous for a completed BO3 match.", "key_factor": "ENCE's significantly higher global ranking (#120 vs #152-165) combined with strong upward market momentum (+12.5pp in 24h) reflects informed betting on the stronger team in a BO3 format that rewards consistency.", "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.33999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.31, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: ENCE's #120 global ranking vs CSDIILIT's #152-165 represents a meaningful but not insurmountable gap; both are tier-2/3 regional squads in a low-tier Finnish tournament. MARKET MOMENTUM CONCERN: YES side surged +12.5pp in 24 hours with an +8pp spike on Apr 10 22:00 UTC. This dramatic 1-week reversal (from equilibrium to 63%) suggests potential overvaluation driven by ranking differential alone rather than concrete recent form data. CRITICAL DATA GAP ON ENCE: Briefing explicitly notes 'Limited recent performance data available in search results to assess current form' for ENCE. Market is pricing ENCE heavily on static ranking, not demonstrated recent results \u2014 a vulnerability. REGIONAL TOURNAMENT UNPREDICTABILITY: Elisa Open Suomi is a small-prize ($5,760), online-only, 4-team regional tournament\u2014exactly the environment where ranking-based predictions break down. 'Regional tournaments often have unpredictable outcomes' is supported by the briefing itself. CSDIILIT UPSET PROFILE: Although lower-ranked, CSDIILIT qualifies for an Upper Bracket Final in a 4-team playoff, proving they beat at least one opponent to reach this stage. They have demonstrated tournament competence despite ranking disadvantage. HEAD-TO-HEAD VOID: No historical matchup data provided. Without h2h context, ENCE's ranking advantage is theoretical; tactical matchups, map pool compatibility, and recent scrim form are entirely unknown. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 72 (strong data: ENCE ranking advantage, tier-level differential, BO3 format logic). confidence_no = 31 (weak data: CSDIILIT lacks documented recent form, no concrete upset evidence, only scenario-based reasoning about regional tournament volatility). The 41-point gap reflects significant unknowns about CSDIILIT's true capability. NO UNDERPRICING SIGNAL: Market at 37% NO reflects market belief in ranking-based prediction. However, the +12.5pp YES surge in 24 hours with no reported news catalyst suggests reactive overshooting rather than new fundamental information. CSDIILIT may be slightly underpriced in a low-information environment. TIME-TO-REVERSAL NOTE: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~8 hours). A CSDIILIT upset would require a single BO3 win on the day\u2014entirely plausible in a single-match event with no form reversion risk. This timing does NOT reduce the upset probability; regional BO3s are high-variance. VERDICT: ENCE is likely favorite, but pricing at 63% overweights ranking differential relative to uncertainty. Regional tournaments punish ranking-based predictions. Probability of NO = 28% reflects respect for ENCE's tier but acknowledges substantial uncertainty and modest underpricing of the underdog in a low-information playoff match.", "key_factor": "Regional tournaments with low prize pools ($5,760) and online-only formats often produce unpredictable outcomes where ranking differentials fail to predict actual match results.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "ENCE is ranked #120 globally vs CSDIILIT at #152-165: a 32-45 place differential suggests ~68-72% baseline win probability for ENCE in BO3 format. Market price of 63% YES is BELOW the historical base rate for this ranking gap in regional playoffs, suggesting potential value for YES side or market skepticism about ENCE's current form. BO3 format favors consistency and depth: higher-ranked teams have better map pools, more stable players, and superior preparation \u2014 historical advantage persists across BO3s. Event timing: LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~8 hours). Recent sharp move on NO side (-5.5pp at Apr 11 08:00 UTC) suggests late information or line adjustment, but insufficient time for major reversals. YES price has risen +12.5pp over 7 days and 24 hours; momentum and recent volatility favor ENCE bettors, consistent with pre-match confidence in the higher-ranked team. No head-to-head history or recent ENCE form data provided: this increases uncertainty about whether ENCE is currently underperforming or if market reflects genuine doubt about their preparation. Regional Finnish tournament context: small prize pool ($5,760) and online format reduce structural advantages; regional upsets occur ~20-25% of the time even with significant ranking gaps. Confidence_yes at 72: ranking differential is reliable, market price aligns reasonably with base rate, but lack of recent form data and live timing prevent higher confidence. Confidence_no at 45: NO side has minimal supporting evidence in briefing (no recent ENCE slump documented, CSDIILIT's strengths not detailed), creating asymmetric data quality favoring the YES case.", "key_factor": "In regional CS:GO/CS2 playoffs, the higher-ranked team (top 150 global) wins approximately 68-75% of BO3 matches against lower-ranked opponents (150+ global). Ranking differential of ~35-45 places typically correlates to 65-72% win probability for the favored team in best-of-three formats.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price at 63% YES aligns with fundamental ranking differential (ENCE #120 vs CSDIILIT #152-165), suggesting rational pricing rather than crowd panic or exuberance. Strong upward momentum on YES side (+12.5pp in 24h, sharp +8pp move on Apr 10 22:00 UTC) reflects confidence-building news or team updates, but magnitude of move is measured\u2014not panic-driven. NO side experienced -5.5pp sharp drop on Apr 11 08:00 UTC, consistent with underdog weakness as match approaches; this is expected reversion, not irrational selling. Volatility asymmetry (NO at 3.5pp/hr vs YES at 2.4pp/hr) indicates underdog uncertainty\u2014understandable given limited recent form data on both teams but especially CSDIILIT. Briefing admits 'limited recent performance data' for both teams, which should lower confidence on either side. YES confidence slightly higher because ranking differential is objective; NO confidence low because underdog potential is subjective without form data. BO3 format favors tier-1 consistency (ENCE advantage), and regional tournament context (small prize pool, online) reduces likelihood of major upsets vs established hierarchy. At 8 hours to resolution, price movement is stabilizing around 63%, suggesting market has digested available signals and reached equilibrium. No ignored signals detected. Current 63/37 split reflects appropriate risk-weighting: ENCE is favored but not overwhelmingly (not at 80%+), acknowledging underdog upset potential in regional play. Crowd sentiment appears 'Rational' rather than greedy\u2014YES side backing justified by rankings, NO side not abandoned despite underdog status. Market is neither overheated nor apathetic.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "ENCE #120 vs CSDIILIT #1