-guard in BO3 formats. The phrase 'limited recent performance data' in the briefing is a yellow flag for both teams\u2014when projections rely solely on historical ranking, not recent form, upset probability is higher than the market prices suggest. Confidence_no set to 45 (not 55+) because: briefing provides no CSDIILIT tactical profile, no recent wins/losses, no indication of roster depth or IGL quality\u2014we cannot credibly assess the underdog's true ceiling or preparation level.", "key_factor": "CSDIILIT executes a novel anti-meta tactical setup (likely economy management or map veto strategy) that neutralizes ENCE's established playstyle in a regional tournament where limited recent form data exists and online BO3 formats are volatile.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6062348178137653, "no_score": 0.3749382716049382, "edge": -0.02376518218623469, "no_edge": 0.004938271604938205, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5873015873015873, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1940442", "question": "Counter-Strike: ENCE vs  CSDIILIT (BO3) - Elisa Open Suomi Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper Bracket Final match between ENCE and  CSDIILIT in the Elisa Open Suomi Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 11 at 1:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ENCE\" if ENCE win the match against  CSDIILIT.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" CSDIILIT\" if  CSDIILIT win the match against ENCE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T23:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T17:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.63, "volume_usd": 2090.8235799999998, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["99170397579753499677052864328170814877041638740409125636100926621589432521324", "35657535018307751475861109911284490341511682968541660697491804420298079488054"]}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "World ranking HLTV regional ranking Regional rankings Global Valve ranking Valve ranking Global Valve Regional ranking Regional Valve ranking Global Valve", "If team dont win nothing, theyre not tier1?", "Bro, so CCT tournaments who won it, tier1 teams?", "Bro ur brain so small, now era vitality, they winning", "Whilst Jame is proud of the resilience his team is showing, he questions how high their current ceiling is.", "PARIVISION came into PGL Bucharest as the", "FaZe will be missing out on the IEM Cologne Major after falling at the final hurdle of their last-ditch qualification campaign, faltering to BIG 1-2 in the", "These dumb bots 3iqmax only EVER win a game if they are huge underdogs and expected to lose hard, when they are expected to win a map that enemy has 20%", "It was, but they got the name from an old Finnish 1.6 team."], "news_summary": "ENCE and CSDIILIT are competing in the Elisa Open Suomi (Finland) Playoffs, a regional Counter-Strike tournament with a $5,760 prize pool (April 10-12, 2026, online). ENCE is ranked #120 globally and represents the stronger tier, while CSDIILIT is ranked #152-165, making them the underdog. The match is a Best-of-3 playoff format in a 4-team regional tournament. Limited recent performance data is available in the search results to assess current form or head-to-head history.", "side_yes_case": ["ENCE significantly higher global ranking (#120 vs #152-165)", "ENCE competing at higher tier level in Finnish competitive scene", "Regional home-country advantage as established Finnish team", "CSDIILIT appears to be lower-tier squad with less tournament pedigree", "BO3 format favors stronger, more consistent team"], "side_no_case": ["CSDIILIT is regional underdog which can produce upset performances", "Limited recent form data available for ENCE in search results", "Regional tournaments often have unpredictable outcomes", "Small sample size makes projections unreliable", "ENCE recent performance trajectory not clearly documented"], "key_context": ["Best-of-3 playoff format in Elisa Open Suomi (regional Finnish tournament)", "Online tournament format (no venue factor)", "Small prize pool ($5,760 total) suggests lower stakes/tier", "No recent head-to-head match history provided in search results", "ENCE ranked #120