uirement is secondary; consensus sourcing available if delay exceeds 2 hours. FINAL ASSESSMENT: RED Canids favored due to superior team record, head-to-head win, BO3 pedigree, and macro metrics. paiN Gaming's explosive individual performances (Rabelo) and lower seeding create asymmetric downside surprise potential, justifying lower NO confidence. Probability 76 reflects ~24% chance paiN Gaming executes upset via Rabelo/Trigger carry or RED Canids BO3 choking.", "key_factor": "Resolution depends on gol.gg official publication within 2 hours post-match; insufficient data on paiN Gaming's BO3 performance consistency limits NO-side confidence assessment.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "RED Canids' recent BO series track record is decisive: 2-0 vs FURIA (Round 2), 3-1 vs FURIA (Round 4), and 3-1 vs ITZ\u2014demonstrating consistency in extended formats where paiN Gaming's BO performance is underdocumented. Direct head-to-head precedent favors RED: Week 2 CBLOL Cup 2026 victory with 31 kills, 66.9% gold share, and 29:05 game duration\u2014paiN Gaming held only 9 kills and 53% gold. RED Canids' macro advantage is quantifiable: 2299 GPM (fifth-best in Cup) indicates superior resource management and scaling\u2014critical in BO3 where economy compounds across games. RED Canids' roster depth in mechanical stats: Bull ranked in top 5 CSM (9.83), Rabelo produced 1 pentakill and top multikill count\u2014paiN's Rabelo's 15-kill outlier game masks inconsistency (lacks broader statistical dominance). paiN Gaming's tournament record is weak: 29% win rate (4-10) in CBLOL Cup 2026 standings, lowest among relevant competitors, suggesting systemic underperformance rather than isolated strong performances. RED Canids' consistency: 55% win rate (11-9) in Cup, steady performance across tournament phases (Weeks 1-3 multiple