ability winning 2-0 and 3-1 series, paiN Gaming's BO performance less documented in available data", "Match outcome may depend on which players assume primary carry roles (paiN's Rabelo vs RED's Bull/Duduhh)"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T14:59:22.628514Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "36246543237870711284838322264669580963375692245031309273478350130487267398140", "data_points": 44, "weighted_avg": 0.7689401510244939, "change_1w_pp": 10.999999999999998, "change_24h_pp": 0.5000000000000004, "volatility_24h": 1.4744853823816453, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "71810617806088006284875231988897083670797091703075867479431770972391055071533", "data_points": 76, "weighted_avg": 0.23769379888830153, "change_1w_pp": -11.000000000000002, "change_24h_pp": -0.5000000000000004, "volatility_24h": 1.4744853823816442, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-11T14:59:22.946641Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-12T00:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-11T23:00:12.099864+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "43e07d94-b7d6-4be2-8467-5d63650d9468", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:01:30.080492+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1902251", "question": "LoL: Shopify Rebellion vs Team Liquid (BO3) - LCS Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Shopify Rebellion and Team Liquid in the LCS Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shopify Rebellion\" if Shopify Rebellion win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against Shopify Rebellion.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.315, "volume_usd": 9231.825893000001, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["6995985558068240077510098377499512558435173645076011945527338827949545495396", "96191914550550802487459537717892801285521545772668856458638037711620026161604"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Shopify Rebellion wins the BO3 match against Team Liquid on April 11, 4:00 PM ET (scheduled ~11 hours from briefing timestamp). CURRENT MARKET PRICE: YES = 32%, NO = 68%. Current market implies 2:1 odds favoring Team Liquid. TEAM LIQUID STRENGTH INDICATORS: Comprehensive positive data\u2014100% win rate when ahead at 15min, +170 GPM differential, +523 gold lead at 15min, 100% first tower rate, +3.7 tower differential. Roster shows strong KDAs (Josedeodo 9.4, Quid 5.5, CoreJJ 5.0) with high kill participation across roles. TEAM LIQUID VULNERABILITY SIGNALS: Limited\u2014Yorick and Azir show 0% win rates, but these appear to be non-signature picks. Overall roster mastery on core champions (Rumble, Pantheon, Galio, Ryze, Seraphine) is extremely strong. SHOPIFY REBELLION DATA ASSESSMENT: Briefing contains ZERO actionable performance metrics for Shopify Rebellion\u2014no KDAs, no win rates, no gold stats, no head-to-head record, no roster confirmation. Brief mentions in draft context (DIG vs. SR games) show presence but no analytical depth. ASYMMETRIC DATA PROBLEM: We have exhaustive detail on Team Liquid's macro and micro performance but no corresponding baseline for Shopify Rebellion. This prevents genuine comparative probability estimation and inflates confidence uncertainty on the NO side. MARKET CONSENSUS SIGNAL: 32% YES / 68% NO suggests informed traders believe Team Liquid is 2x more likely to win. This may reflect industry knowledge of Shopify Rebellion's weaker standing or recent poor form, unavailable in this briefing. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous\u2014match must complete and produce a winner. Forfeit/disqualification/walkover scenarios resolve 50-50, but these are statistically rare in LCS regular season. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 35 (Team Liquid's strong metrics support NO outcome, but Shopify Rebellion unknown prevents high certainty in YES direction). confidence_no = 45 (Team Liquid's dominance suggests NO likely, but complete absence of Shopify Rebellion data creates genuine uncertainty about whether this matchup presents an upset scenario\u2014insufficient counter-evidence to reach 60+). PROBABILITY REASONING: Market price of 32% aligns with available evidence favoring Team Liquid. Absent any Shopify Rebellion performance signal suggesting competitiveness, probability_score = 32 reflects the current market consensus while acknowledging severe data asymmetry on the YES side.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no Shopify Rebellion performance data, roster information, or head-to-head matchup history, making probabilistic assessment heavily asymmetric and unreliable despite detailed Team Liquid statistics.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO = Team Liquid): Market correctly identifies Team Liquid as strong favorite at 68%. Team Liquid demonstrates elite macro execution with 100% win rate when ahead at 15 minutes\u2014this is the single most predictive metric in LoL, as early advantages convert to late-game wins in ~99% of cases at pro level. EARLY GAME DOMINANCE: Team Liquid's +523 gold differential at 15 minutes and +170 GPM sustained advantage indicate systematic, repeatable early game control. Combined with 100% first tower rate, they execute their win condition reliably. This is not variance\u2014it's consistent execution. ELITE INDIVIDUAL PLAY: Josedeodo (9.4 KDA, 74.2% kill participation) and Quid (5.5 KDA, 66.8% KP) are high-impact carries. CoreJJ (3.47 VSPM) shows elite roaming efficiency. These metrics suggest players capable of exploiting opponent mistakes immediately. CHAMPION MASTERY AS STABILITY: Multiple signature picks with 100% win rates (Rumble, Pantheon, Galio, Ryze, Seraphine, Rell) means Team Liquid likely plays predictable, high-confidence champions in each role. This reduces draft variability and ensures comfort on critical picks. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS - INFORMATION GAP: The briefing contains ZERO performance statistics for Shopify Rebellion. No KDA data, gold stats, win rate breakdowns, champion pools, or macro metrics. This absence is telling\u2014market data typically emphasizes the weaker team's limitations when available. The lack of data suggests Shopify Rebellion either underperforms or has not been closely tracked, neither of which favors an upset. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: Zero direct matchup history provided. In BO3 format, teams that understand each other's meta shifts and adaptations hold advantages. Team Liquid's consistent execution suggests they'll adjust across games better than an unknown opponent. MARKET PRICE MOMENTUM SUPPORTS FAVORITE: YES side has fallen from 36% (EMA) to 32% (current) over 7 days. Sharp -16pp move on Apr 08 01:00 UTC suggests informed traders accumulating NO shares. This money flow into the favorite typically reflects late-arriving information or sharper analysis. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES CONSISTENCY: Best-of-3 rewards the more fundamentally sound team. Team Liquid's systematic early game advantage (reproducible across multiple games) is more reliable than upset narratives in BO3 than in single-game formats. VULNERABILITY IS MINIMAL: Team Liquid shows losses only on Yorick and Azir (0% WR), but these are likely low-volume, situational picks. The absence of broad champion pool weaknesses across 5 roles suggests well-rounded team prep. SHOPIFY REBELLION UPSIDE CANNOT BE ASSESSED: Without comparative data, any argument for YES is speculative. The briefing includes extensive Dignitas vs. Shopify Rebellion data (showing mixed results), but that does not predict performance vs. Team Liquid. Dignitas \u2260 Team Liquid. TIMING & CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Event is TODAY (~11 hours to resolution). Any reversal requiring Team Liquid mental collapse or unexpected meta shift is extremely unlikely. Market has already priced in foreseeable chaos; additional catalyst generation is near-impossible at this timeframe. Confidence in NO is therefore high (~72). CONFIDENCE IN YES IS LOW: The complete absence of Shopify Rebellion data means any YES estimate is built on prior belief + uncertainty, not on comparable evidence. This justifies confidence_yes of only 35, reflecting genuine epistemic limitation rather than strong counter-narrative.", "key_factor": "Team Liquid's 100% win rate when ahead at 15 minutes combined with dominant early game macro (+523 gold at 15min, +170 GPM) creates a high-probability path to victory in BO3 format.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides exhaustive Team Liquid statistics (KDA, gold differential, win rates, champion pools, macro metrics) but ZERO concrete performance data for Shopify Rebellion\u2014no player stats, no recent results, no economy metrics, no champion proficiency. Team Liquid's 100% win rate when ahead at 15 min is impressive in isolation, but this aggregate statistic may reflect matchups against weaker LCS teams; without Shopify Rebellion's defensive metrics or scaling potential, we cannot assess whether TL can reliably achieve early leads against this opponent. Sharp market movement on Apr 08 (YES fell 16.0pp) suggests informed traders acquired new information, likely from pre-game scouting or team form assessment; this sharp decline from 35-36% to current 32% indicates consensus confidence in NO, but the absence of public briefing data for Shopify Rebellion means the market may be reacting to unpublished intelligence. Team Liquid shows CHAMPION VULNERABILITY: 0% win rate on Yorick and Azir, 33% on Anivia, Renekton, and Vayne. If Shopify Rebellion's draft is strong against TL's primary carries (Rumble, Galio, Ryze) or forces them into weak matchups, early game dominance becomes neutralized. Best-of-3 format favors the team with deeper draft pools and adaptation capacity; TL's reliance on signature picks (100% win rates on 2-3 champions per role) could be exposed if Shopify Rebellion targets bans strategically\u2014no draft flexibility data provided for either team. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~11 hours): Market is trading on asymmetric information. TL's published dominance is 1-2 weeks old; Shopify Rebellion's current form, roster health, and recent scrim results are unknown to public market participants. Late-game movement (Apr 08 -16.0pp) suggests insiders view Shopify Rebellion as undervalued. No head-to-head record, no direct matchup analysis, no information on whether Shopify Rebellion has historically competed well against TL or similar macro-focused teams. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in TL's statistical strengths (confidence_no: 48) is earned by strong public metrics. BUT confidence in Shopify Rebellion's weakness (confidence_yes: 32) is undermined by complete data absence\u2014we cannot confidently claim Shopify Rebellion is weak when we have no evidence of their actual performance level. Market price (32% YES / 68% NO) may reflect TL's reputation and public dominance rather than true win probability; Shopify Rebellion could be a mid-tier team with solid matchup advantages TL's aggregated stats don't capture. The briefing includes extensive irrelevant data (Age of Empires, CS:GO rosters, historical tournaments) suggesting incomplete or misfiled information\u2014this raises possibility that Shopify Rebellion performance data exists but was excluded, further undermining confidence in the NO side. Verdict: TL is favored for valid reasons (gold control, first tower, macro), but the underdog is GENUINELY UNDERPRICED due to complete information vacuum on Shopify Rebellion. A 32% price implies TL wins ~3 of 4 matchups; without performance data on the opponent, that confidence is not fully justified.", "key_factor": "Shopify Rebellion has zero performance data in the briefing, making Team Liquid's statistical dominance potentially inflated against an unknown opponent with unanalyzed matchup dynamics.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides extensive Team Liquid statistics but ZERO performance metrics for Shopify Rebellion\u2014no KDA, win rates, gold differential, or head-to-head record. Team Liquid demonstrates objectively strong macro indicators: +170 GPM, +523 gold@15min, 100% conversion when ahead at 15min, 100% first tower rate, +3.7 avg tower differential. However, these aggregate metrics reflect Team Liquid's overall season performance across multiple opponents\u2014not predictive of THIS specific matchup without Shopify Rebellion context. Current market price (32% YES for Shopify Rebellion) implies Team Liquid is heavily favored, consistent with their published strength metrics. Historical base rate for LCS matches: stronger-seeded or higher-performing teams win ~65-70% of regular season games, but BO3 format increases volatility vs. single games. NO INFORMATION on: (a) Shopify Rebellion's current win-loss record, (b) their roster composition vs. Team Liquid matchup dynamics, (c) head-to-head records, (d) recent form trends. Market price history shows SHARP REVERSAL Apr 08 (-16pp on YES side in 1 hour), suggesting either late-breaking news (match scheduled for Apr 11) or algorithmic rebalancing\u2014confidence in underlying data stability is LOW. EVENT TIMING: 'TODAY' with ~11 hours to resolution. Any major roster change, injury, or forfeit would drastically alter probability, but briefing provides no recent updates post-Apr 08 volatility. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: High confidence in Team Liquid's statistical dominance (confidence_yes=28 reflects strong pro-Liquid fundamentals), but very low confidence in robustness of NO prediction (confidence_no=35) due to complete absence of Shopify Rebellion comparative data. Market price of 32% YES suggests sophisticated bettors have information not visible in briefing\u2014respect the market, but acknowledge information asymmetry prevents high-confidence forecast either direction. Probability_score of 32 reflects: Team Liquid's strong form supports lower YES probability, market consensus aligns with that view, but lack of Shopify Rebellion data prevents conviction below 30 or above 35.", "key_factor": "LCS matchups are highly dependent on current season form and roster strength; without comparative performance data for the underdog, base rate suggests stronger-team favoring, but market mispricing risk is high due to information asymmetry.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market currently prices Team Liquid at 68% (NO side), but briefing provides ONLY Team Liquid performance data with no Shopify Rebellion comparative statistics. Team Liquid demonstrates elite-tier metrics: 100% win rate when ahead at 15min, +170 GPM gold differential, 100% first tower rate, exceptional KDA across all roles (Josedeodo 9.4, Quid 5.5, CoreJJ 5.0). Strong champion mastery on key picks: Rumble 100% WR, Pantheon 100% WR, Galio 100% WR, Ryze 100% WR\u2014indicates deep, refined champion pool. Team Liquid shows zero performance data for Shopify Rebellion; asymmetric briefing creates data vacuum on NO side, making fair evaluation of Shopify Rebellion's win probability impossible. Price history shows sharp volatility (Apr 08 \u00b116pp swings) typical of uncertainty-driven trading; lack of Shopify Rebellion data suggests market pricing based on narrative rather than comparative analysis. Current 32% YES price appears under-confident given Team Liquid's demonstrably strong macro fundamentals and role-by-role domination; market may be overweighting unknown opponent risk. Tournament context: LCS 2026 Spring is S-Tier offline competition; Team Liquid's metrics are from live competitive play, not inflated against weak opponents. Confidence_no set to 35 because briefing provides zero quantitative basis to evaluate Shopify Rebellion's chance\u2014cannot justify Team Liquid's heavy underdog price without opposing data. Confidence_yes set to 78 because Team Liquid's available metrics are comprehensive, recent, and consistently elite across all measured dimensions. Rational apathy detected: market may be treating this as 50-50 uncertainty due to incomplete briefing, but Team Liquid's documented strength should shift odds meaningfully higher.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Team Liquid demonstrates elite macro execution: +170 GPM sustained advantage, 100% first tower rate, and +3.7 average tower different