ably to BO3 victories, but the complete absence of Shopify Rebellion performance data severely limits confidence in the NO probability.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "ASYMMETRIC DATA GAP: Briefing provides exhaustive Team Liquid stats (KDA, gold%, champion pools, tower control, macro metrics) but ZERO offensive intelligence on Shopify Rebellion\u2014no KDA, no win rates, no champion preferences, no early-game tendencies. This absence is the contrarian's opening. TEAM LIQUID'S MACRO CEILING: 100% win rate when ahead at 15min is a conversion metric, not a guarantee of early-game dominance against a team that contests the 0-15 window aggressively. The +523 gold lead at 15min is an aggregate\u2014vulnerable to teams that threaten kills over cs-farming. CHAMPION POOL BRITTLENESS: Team Liquid shows 0% win rate on Yorick (1 game, 0.7 KDA) and 0% on Xin Zhao (1 game, 4.0 KDA). If Shopify Rebellion forces a draft with these champions or exploits a predictable blue/red-side pool bias (Karma/Orianna 100% blue, Varus 67%), Team Liquid loses draft flexibility. Briefing data hints at limited ad-hoc adaptation. JOSEDEODO DEPENDENCY: 74.2% KP (kill participation) on Pantheon (100% WR, 23.0 KDA) and Lee Sin (100% WR, 6.7 KDA) suggests Team Liquid's wins are jungler-centric. A support-heavy or counter-jungle meta that isolates Josedeodo from priority lanes could neutralize his statistical edge. Shopify Rebellion's jungle matchup is unknown. BO3 VOLATILITY: Match is BO3, not single-game. Team Liquid's aggregate stats mask potential game-1 vulnerabilities. If Shopify Rebellion takes game 1 with an unconventional win condition (split-push, poke comp, teamfight initiation) not in Team Liquid's recent meta, psychological pressure and draft constraints in games 2\u20133 could compound. OFFLINE TOURNAMENT INTANGIBLES: LCS 2026 Spring is offline. Crowd noise, stage jitter, or coaching miscommunication (absent from briefing) can disrupt a team's macro execution. Team Liquid's gold-farming playstyle is high-execution; offline format amplifies mechanical or decision-making variance. MARKET TRAJECTORY SIGNAL: YES odds fell 2.5pp over 7 days and -3.0pp in 24 hours. Sharp sell-off on Apr 08 (\u221216pp) suggests late-breaking roster, injury, or meta news favoring Liquid that briefing does NOT capture. Absence of this news in briefing = information asymmetry risk for YES bettors. EARLY-GAME AGGRESSION MISMATCH: Briefing shows Team Liquid's first-tower rate at 100% and tower differential at +3.7\u2014passive, scaling-friendly metrics. If Shopify Rebellion fields a composition that inverts the game into a brawl (high-damage team fight, early item power spikes), Team Liquid's late-game gold conversion becomes irrelevant. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in Team Liquid's dominance (72 on NO) is justified by overwhelming positive data; low confidence in Shopify Rebellion's upset (42 on YES) reflects data void, not weakness. Briefing's silence on Shopify Rebellion is a structural uncertainty that penalizes confidence on YES side.", "key_factor": "Shopify Rebellion's jungler or mid-laner executes a high-tempo gank-heavy meta adaptation that collapses Team Liquid's methodical macro play in game 1, forcing a disruptive reset before Team Liquid's gold-farming engine stabilizes.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.549390243902439, "no_score": 0.5154545454545455, "edge": 0.23439024390243896, "no_edge": -0.16954545454545455, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 55% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 47% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1902251", "question": "LoL: Shopify Rebelli