y noted but equally weak evidence for YES side. Market is processing sentiment (org legitimacy assumptions) not substance (missing stats). Low volume ($3,635) suggests thin liquidity and potential for whipsaw if any reliable form data emerges pre-match. Both confidence scores low (28/35): briefing is insufficient for robust evaluation of either side. Bookmaker likely possesses form/odds data not reflected here. Current 20% price may reflect sharp knowledge or may be panic mispricing\u2014cannot determine from briefing alone. Event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours with minimal time for reversal. If Be\u015fikta\u015f is underdog due to team stability rather than match form, 80% is overconfident. If SCARS is genuinely weaker, 20% may fairly reflect long-shot odds but lacks evidentiary support. Market sentiment = Fear-driven exodus from underdog. Price action velocity suggests emotional contagion, not information arrival. Rational skepticism warranted on both sides given data void.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: All performance statistics in the briefing are malformed (marked '/') \u2014 no actual ACS, K/D, KAST, ADR metrics exist. This eliminates objective mechanical skill assessment. MARKET REVERSAL SIGNAL: YES dropped 31pp over 7 days with sharp -9.5pp and -8.5pp moves on Apr 09. Sharp reversals this close to match time (8 hours) in esports betting typically indicate: (a) scrim results leaked, (b) roster changes announced, or (c) betting syndicates with insider access repositioning. ORG INFRASTRUCTURE ASYMMETRY: Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports is an established Turkish esports organization; TEAM SCARS affiliation/resources unknown. In Challengers-tier Turkish Valorant, org stability correlates with consistency, though does not guarantee outcome. NO HEAD-T