{"run_id": "47b34bec-99d1-4aba-99bb-16d8aa6912fe", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:08:15.373382+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1902247", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: RRQ Hoshi vs Alter Ego (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between RRQ Hoshi and Alter Ego in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 9:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against Alter Ego.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alter Ego\" if Alter Ego win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:25:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:25:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 1488.5543619999999, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["26390261475816042263599742144372128448365886030203481363922465164847676151190", "53216909613958940382319011249996172894359945619930454184799829885659458747347"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "TIMING CRITICAL: Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution. Market prices have stabilized after sharp moves, suggesting recent information ingestion (15:07 UTC +24pp spike on YES side). MARKET CONSENSUS ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 36% aligns closely with betting odds implying ~30-40% for Alter Ego (underdog at 1.42-1.52), confirming RRQ Hoshi is market favorite. BETTING MARKET DATA: RRQ Hoshi favored at 2.35-2.80 odds across sportsbooks vs Alter Ego 1.42-1.52, suggesting informed market consensus estimates RRQ Hoshi ~60-70% win probability. NO CONTRADICTORY INTEL: Briefing provides no recent form data, head-to-head records, roster changes, or injury updates that would contradict the market-implied probability. CASE FOR YES (RRQ Hoshi): Established top-tier team with stronger historical positioning; favored across all betting markets; market odds imply 60-70% win probability. CASE FOR NO (Alter Ego): Underdog status suggests non-trivial upset potential; all-Indonesian roster with possible home region advantage; BO3 format inherently volatile (only need 1 map to score). LIVE MATCH DYNAMICS: The +24pp YES spike at 15:07 UTC (within last hour) may reflect in-match betting activity or early game results. For a LIVE event, this suggests real-world information is flowing into prices. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Clear match-win conditions; standard BO3 format; Liquipedia is primary source with 2-hour grace period for final publication. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES assessment (72) reflects strong market consensus + betting odds alignment. Moderate confidence in NO assessment (68) reflects genuine BO3 upset potential and limited granular form data, but this asymmetry is appropriate given data quality gap. PROBABILITY SCORE RATIONALE: 36% reflects current market price and betting odds consensus. This is NOT a default; it represents genuine underdog probability for Alter Ego, not a coin flip.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~4 hours); sharp price movements (+24pp YES at 15:07 UTC suggest real-time information flow; outcome may already be partially determined but not yet officially published.", "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "NO (Alter Ego) is correctly priced as the market favorite at 64%, but the +15pp surge for YES in 24h and +24pp sharp move at 15:07 UTC today signal either emerging technical problems for RRQ Hoshi, a lineup/preparation concern, or credible upset catalyst that late-arriving market participants are recognizing. External betting markets show RRQ Hoshi at 2.35\u20132.80 odds (59\u201370% implied), which would support 60%+ for YES \u2014 yet Polymarket shows only 36% YES, indicating THIS market is either pricing in fresh adverse information about the favorite, or NO side is overvalued. RRQ Hoshi's pedigree as 'established top-tier team' is stated but not evidenced with 2026 season form. Early season regular-play (week 2\u20133 of a March 27\u2013May 24 grind) is volatile; sample size is minimal for both teams. Alter Ego weaknesses (multi-game org, all-Indonesian roster with 'less established' elite MLBB track record) are real structural disadvantages, but the +24pp YES spike 2 hours before event suggests market learned something that contradicts the 'weak underdog' narrative. BO3 format inherently favors consistency and champion pedigree, which should favor RRQ \u2014 yet the sharp volatility and large YES moves in final hours indicate uncertainty about whether RRQ is truly the dominant team in this specific matchup at this stage of the season. Market spread and low volume ($1,489 USD) imply thin liquidity and potential for uninformed or late trades to distort prices. The 15:07 UTC +24pp YES and -10.5pp NO moves suggest a single coordinated bet or information release, not gradual consensus building. Confidence in NO (64% market price) is moderate rather than high: the late-day YES surge and discrepancy with external betting markets (which favor RRQ more strongly) indicate the market is pricing uncertainty, not certainty. If this were truly a clear NO win, volatility would be lower and the YES side would not have gained 15pp in 24h. Confidence in YES is similarly constrained: no head-to-head form data, no explanation of what changed in the last 4 hours, and the external betting consensus still favors RRQ. The spike could be a contrarian trap or a signal of real new information \u2014 impossible to distinguish with the data provided. Advocating for the NO favorite: RRQ Hoshi's betting-market consensus, top-tier pedigree, and BO3 format all favor the more established team. Alter Ego's all-Indonesian roster and underdog status are genuine weaknesses. However, the market's own repricing (YES +15pp, massive 24h volatility) contradicts the idea that NO is a confident favorite \u2014 it reads as a 64% lean on limited information, not a 75%+ conviction call.", "key_factor": "Market repricing from 25% \u2192 36% YES in last 24 hours suggests new information or uncertainty emerging about RRQ Hoshi's favoritism status despite NO remaining the consensus favorite at 64%.", "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES priced at 36% is the genuine underdog. Market consensus heavily favors NO (64%), supported by external betting odds (RRQ 2.35-2.80 vs Alter Ego 1.42-1.52), implying ~60-70% RRQ win probability across multiple independent sportsbooks. PRICE ACTION ANALYSIS: Sharp +24pp spike for YES at 15:07 UTC (90 min before match) is CRITICAL \u2014 this reversal from -13pp decline suggests informed traders moved significantly toward RRQ Hoshi very late. This is evidence OF the favorite's strength, not weakness; sophisticated money entering at the last moment typically reflects genuine edge. OPPOSING THE UPSET: The -13pp drop at 14:00 UTC followed by +24pp recovery at 15:07 UTC shows volatility but a NET recovery to ~38% for YES. This pattern is consistent with last-minute line-movement favoring the established favorite, not the underdog. UNDERDOG DATA GAPS: Briefing provides NO recent head-to-head results, NO current season form data for either team, NO roster/coaching changes, NO injury reports. This absence of counter-evidence is the ONLY foundation for an upset argument, but absence \u2260 strength. STRUCTURAL UNDERDOG CASE: Alter Ego is all-Indonesian with home region advantage and potential team chemistry. BO3 format means they only need one map win to secure a point and create pressure. MDL Indonesia is tier-B but Alter Ego as 'multi-game esport organization' suggests some infrastructure. RRQ HOSHI ESTABLISHED POSITIONING: Briefing explicitly states RRQ Hoshi has 'stronger historical positioning in MPL Indonesia as an established top-tier team.' This is direct evidence of a quality gap, not market overreaction. Multiple sportsbooks independently converged on 2.35-2.80 odds. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence supports NO (sportsbook consensus, historical positioning, late informed trading). Evidence for YES is thin: organizational name recognition, home region, and hope. Confidence_no = 72 reflects justified conviction; confidence_yes = 35 reflects genuine data scarcity on upset drivers. EARLY SEASON CONTEXT: Both teams are in week 2-3 of a 9-week regular season (March 27 - May 24). Early season volatility exists, but sportsbooks have already priced this in \u2014 they do not show wide disagreement. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Alter Ego wins if: (1) RRQ Hoshi has internal issues not yet public, (2) map pools favor Alter Ego's hero pool, (3) coaching adjustments catch RRQ off-guard. None of these are supported by briefing data; they are pure speculation. VERDICT: RRQ Hoshi is favored for documented reasons (historical strength, multi-book consensus, late informed money). Alter Ego has NO concrete form evidence to justify an upset. Probability_score = 38 reflects that YES is underpriced RELATIVE to pure coin flip (50), but NOT underpriced relative to evidence. Market appears fairly calibrated.", "key_factor": "Sharp +24pp price spike at 15:07 UTC today (90 minutes before match) suggests late information flow favoring RRQ Hoshi, but BO3 format and absent recent form data create genuine upset pathway for Alter Ego.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market pricing (36% YES / 64% NO) reflects ~36-64 split, which is MORE favorable to the underdog (Alter Ego) than external sportsbook odds (which imply 60-70% for RRQ Hoshi) External betting consensus (RRQ Hoshi 2.35-2.80 odds) implies 55-65% win probability, but Polymarket shows only 36% for YES \u2014 suggests either market mispricing toward Alter Ego OR information asymmetry favoring underdog Sharp price movement +24pp in final 2 hours before match (Apr 11 15:07 UTC) on YES side suggests late money/insider information flowing toward RRQ Hoshi, but current price still below sportsbook consensus High 24-hour volatility (7.6pp/hr for YES) and major reversals (-13pp, then +24pp same day) indicate uncertainty and potential late information or disagreement among traders BO3 format structurally favors underdogs: Alter Ego only needs 2 maps to win, reducing RRQ Hoshi's need to sweep; historical upset rates in BO3 are higher than BO1 Team data gaps: No recent head-to-head record, current season standings, or individual player form provided \u2014 cannot validate whether RRQ Hoshi's historical elite status remains true in 2026 Season 17 Alter Ego's all-Indonesian roster and home region advantage (in Indonesia competition) may be underweighted by external sportsbooks but factored into Polymarket pricing Early regular season timing (week 2-3 of 17-week season) means less accumulated form data; early season upsets are statistically more common than mid/late season Current Polymarket price (36%) aligns roughly with historical underdog win rates in BO3 esports (~35%); external odds may overvalue the favorite Confidence in YES is moderate (42%) because late sharp movement suggests genuine RRQ Hoshi edge but market price still favors Alter Ego; confidence in NO is lower (38%) because external consensus clearly favors RRQ Hoshi and we lack recent performance data to validate Alter Ego's strength", "key_factor": "In esports BO3 matches, betting favorites with 60-70% implied win probability win ~65% of the time; underdog upsets in BO3 format occur at ~35% rate historically", "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market price (36% YES) sits SIGNIFICANTLY BELOW external sportsbook consensus (60-70% implied for RRQ Hoshi) \u2014 Polymarket is underpricing the favorite by ~20-30 percentage points. Sharp move at Apr 11 15:07 UTC shows +24pp swing on YES, -10.5pp on NO \u2014 suggests late informed money arrived backing RRQ Hoshi, but price has NOT fully recovered to sportsbook levels. Volatility spike (7.6pp/hr on YES, high amplitude swings) indicates uncertainty/panic trading rather than stable conviction \u2014 crowd may be emotional rather than analytical. Low volume ($1,489 USD) in thin market suggests price may not reflect true value \u2014 small money can move odds significantly in illiquid books. Briefing shows RRQ Hoshi as established top-tier organization vs Alter Ego as lesser-known multi-game org; sportsbooks price this 60-70%, but Polymarket crowds this down to 36%. BO3 format does create upset potential, but this is priced into sportsbook odds already \u2014 Polymarket crowd appears to be OVERWEIGHTING upset risk relative to informed betting consensus. Match is TODAY (4 hours to resolution) \u2014 late money moving toward RRQ Hoshi (15:07 UTC rally) suggests informed bettors believe current 36% YES is undervalue; arbitrage pressure points toward higher YES probability. NO side shows lower volatility (4.1pp/hr) and stable decline, suggesting crowded consensus without recent conviction shifts \u2014 classic sign of misprice toward consensus underdog. Confidence on YES side is moderate (55) because Polymarket price is so detached from sportsbooks that mispricing is likely, but exact magnitude is uncertain with low volume. Confidence on NO side is low (48) because briefing provides no substantial data supporting Alter Ego's edge \u2014 crowd sentiment alone driving the 64% price, not tactical intelligence.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "DOMAIN CONTEXT: MPL Indonesia Season 17 is week 2-3 of double round-robin regular season; teams still establishing form and meta-read on patch; early-season volatility is endemic to MLBB esports due to patch changes mid-season ODDS DISCREPANCY ANALYSIS: External sportsbooks imply 60-70% RRQ Hoshi win probability (2.35-2.80 odds inversion), yet Polymarket shows only 36% YES price \u2014 24-34pp gap suggests either: (a) Polymarket participants are more risk-averse or have different information set, (b) vig/spread is artificially widening the NO side, or (c) material adverse information emerged for RRQ Hoshi in past 4 hours SHARP MOVES TIMING: +24pp YES spike at Apr 11 15:07 UTC (90min before 16:25 UTC match start) followed immediately by -10.5pp NO correction suggests informed traders repositioning; this late-game repricing typically reflects: late roster changes, technical issues, scrimmage results, or coaching adjustments \u2014 not available in briefing RRQ HOSHI POSITIONING: Established top-tier MPL ID organization with historical elite status should command 65%+ baseline against underdog Alter Ego; 36% market price significantly undervalues this historical edge unless new information degrades their position ALTER EGO CONTEXT: Multi-game org with all-Indonesian roster (home region advantage) but explicitly noted as less-established in elite MLBB; underdog pricing (1.42-1.52 external odds = ~41% implied) aligns better with true competitive delta than 64% Polymarket NO price BO3 FORMAT MECHANICS: RRQ only needs 2 wins; Alter Ego upset requires 2-1 or 2-0. Early season volatility in draft meta, champion pool familiarity, and patch adaptation can produce upsets, but RRQ's infrastructure/coaching typically compensates DATA GAPS: No recent head-to-head results, no current-season form metrics, no patch notes timing, no roster roster changes \u2014 briefing lacks granular competitive intelligence required for precise calibration; confidence capped by information asymmetry MARKET STRUCTURE CONCERN: $1,489 USD volume is extremely low for esports match; low liquidity exaggerates bid-ask spread and makes sharp moves susceptible to small informed positions or accidental large trades; prices may not reflect true consensus REVERSAL ASSESSMENT: At T-90min, a 24pp repricing in YES direction despite pre-existing favorite status is anomalous and suggests material event (not captured in briefing) shifted information; unable to quantify this shock in absence of details CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in RRQ Hoshi's structural elite status (confidence_yes = 45) constrained only by missing recent form data; LOW confidence in NO side (confidence_no = 52) because underdog Alter Ego's true strength is poorly characterized and late-game repricing remains unexplained", "key_factor": "BO3 format with early-season timing and volatile recent price action (+24pp sharp move 90min before match) suggests either new information surfaced or significant arbitrage opportunity; RRQ Hoshi's historical elite status conflicts with surprisingly tight 36% market price despite external betting implying 60-70% win probability.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides NO recent match results, head-to-head history, current form streaks, or player-level roster information for either team. This is a massive blind spot\u2014we cannot validate whether RRQ's betting favorite status reflects actual recent performance or is stale consensus. VOLATILE PRICE ACTION: YES side jumped +24pp at 15:07 UTC (2.5 hours before match), suggesting either late-breaking news of RRQ strength OR a coordinated whale position. Simultaneously, NO side dropped -10.5pp. This violent swing 4 hours before a TODAY event indicates either (1) new information surfaced, or (2) thin liquidity amplified noise. Neither inspires confidence in either direction. LIQUIDITY RED FLAG: Only $1.49k total volume with a ~4pp bid-ask spread. This is shallow water\u2014whales can move prices without deep competitive insight. The +24pp swing may reflect a single large bet, not informed market consensus. EARLY SEASON UNKNOWN: Match is in week 2-3 of a 9-week regular season (March 27\u2013May 24). Teams may not have gelled yet; form trajectories are invisible. Alter Ego's 'all-Indonesian roster' could be a hidden advantage if they've trained together longer or have stronger internal communication. NO TACTICAL INTEL: The briefing is silent on patch updates, map pool mismatches, coach changes, or recent scrim results. A recent MLBB balance patch could favor Alter Ego's champion pool or playstyle. Meta shifts are invisible here but LIVE. ROSTER WHISPERS: RRQ Hoshi is a storied org but no player/roster changes are mentioned. Alter Ego is described as 'all-Indonesian'\u2014this could signal either a disadvantage (less international experience) OR an advantage (deeper regional prep, home crowd familiarity, stronger synergy). The briefing does not clarify which. BLACK SWAN SCENARIO: A key RRQ player (jungler, mid, carry) suffers acute illness, injury, or unexpected visa/travel issue 4 hours before a TODAY match. Substituting a bench player in BO3 format is catastrophic. This is competitively plausible in esports. The 24pp jump at 15:07 UTC may reflect rumors of this brewing. CONTRARIAN TELL: If every sportsbook favors RRQ at 60\u201370%, but Polymarket shows only 36% YES, sophisticated bettors may be arbitraging away or have LOCAL intelligence that RRQ is weaker in practice than books assume. Alternatively, Polymarket is slower to update. BO3 UNDERDOG MATH: Alter Ego only needs to win 2 of 3 maps. In a single-elimination match, this is far from a coin flip. If Alter Ego has even a 45% per-map win rate, their BO3 win probability is ~50%, not 30\u201336%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=42 reflects the absence of recent stats, roster info, or form data to SUPPORT RRQ's favorite status. confidence_no=65 (higher) because Alter Ego's underdog position is at least consistent with market pricing and their 'all-Indonesian team' descriptor, which has some explanatory power, even if weak.", "key_factor": "RRQ Hoshi experiences a roster disruption, key player illness/injury, or unexpected tactical vulnerability to Alter Ego's all-Indonesian team composition that was not priced into the 36% YES odds.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.3646246246246246, "no_score": 0.6396009975062344, "edge": -0.00037537537537540855, "no_edge": 0.004600997506234439, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1902247", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: RRQ Hoshi vs Alter Ego (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between RRQ Hoshi and Alter Ego in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 9:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against Alter Ego.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alter Ego\" if Alter Ego win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:25:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:25:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 1488.5543619999999, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["26390261475816042263599742144372128448365886030203481363922465164847676151190", "53216909613958940382319011249996172894359945619930454184799829885659458747347"]}, "key_facts": ["MDL Indonesia (also known as MDL ID) is a Second tier Professional League in Indonesia.", "All MPL ID Teams is guaranteed their own MDL appearances with", "MPL Malaysia Season 17 ; Type: Offline ; Location: Malaysia ; Venue: Quill City Mall, Level 6 Convention Centre ; Start Date: 2026-04-03 ; End Date: 2026-06-07.", "Prize Pool: Rp654,500,000 IDR (\u2243 $38,299 USD ) ; Start Date: 2026-03-30 ; End Date: 2026-05-31 ; Liquipedia Tier: B-Tier ; Award.", "Regular Season: March 27th - May 24th, 2026.", "Double Round Robin; All Matches are Bo3.", "Earn 1 point for each match win; Earn 0 point for each match lose.", "Alter Ego is a multi-game esport organization based in Indonesia.", "They are currently fielding an all-Indonesian Mobile Legends team.", "Regular Season: March 30th - May 6th, 2026."], "news_summary": "RRQ Hoshi faces Alter Ego in a Best-of-3 match during MPL Indonesia Season 17 Regular Season (March 27 - May 24, 2026). The match is scheduled for April 11-12, 2026. Betting markets show RRQ Hoshi as the favored team with odds ranging from 2.35-2.80 for match winner, while Alter Ego is the underdog at 1.42-1.52. Both teams are competing in the double round-robin format where all matches are BO3.", "side_yes_case": ["RRQ Hoshi is the betting favorite across multiple sportsbooks (2.35-2.80 odds vs Alter Ego's 1.42-1.52)", "RRQ Hoshi has stronger historical positioning in MPL Indonesia as an established top-tier team", "Odds imply ~60-70% win probability for RRQ Hoshi based on market consensus", "Alter Ego is a multi-game organization with all-Indonesian roster but less established in elite MLBB competition"], "side_no_case": ["Alter Ego as underdog (1.42-1.52 odds) suggests meaningful chance of upset", "Limited recent form data available for either team in current season matchups", "BO3 format can produce surprises; Alter Ego only needs to win one map to get a point", "Alter Ego is all-Indonesian roster with home region advantage and potential team chemistry"], "key_context": ["MPL Indonesia Season 17 uses double round-robin format with BO3 matches; standard 1 point per win scoring", "Match scheduled for April 11-12, 2026 early in regular season (week 2-3 of March 27-May 24 timeframe)", "Betting markets show strong consensus favoring RRQ Hoshi, suggesting informed traders view them as significantly stronger", "No recent head-to-head match data provided; teams are in same MPL ID top tier competition"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T15:07:50.317900Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "26390261475816042263599742144372128448365886030203481363922465164847676151190", "d