{"run_id": "45b98fa3-e16c-4042-ad00-6838ab42472a", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:14:52.728854+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1893865", "question": "LoL: G2 Esports vs Team Vitality (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between G2 Esports and Team Vitality in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 10:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win the match against Team Vitality.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Vitality\" if Team Vitality win the match against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:55:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:55:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 270829.1596630004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["75402608914449967250207624471898011372340723735500711563328146206037449546807", "64525848286537441921079050725487818343167363564531620604907539142839323486543"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: G2 Esports must win the BO3 match (2+ games of 3) against Team Vitality on April 11, 2026. CRITICAL TIMING: Event is TODAY with ~5 hours until resolution deadline. Market traded sharply at 15:13 UTC (-30pp on YES side), suggesting intra-match information flow. Current briefing timestamp is 15:14 UTC, placing us near or within the match window. G2 FORM EVIDENCE (HIGH CONFIDENCE): Recently won LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs championship, defeated KC 3-2 in finals and MKOI 3-0 in semifinals. Demonstrates strong current form with BO3 consistency and championship-caliber play. VITALITY FORM EVIDENCE (LOW CONFIDENCE): Only LEC Spring 2023 data available (6W-9L record, 6 wins in 9 games suggests ~67% win rate in that season). No 2026 Spring Regular Season standings, recent match history, or roster changes provided. Cannot assess current momentum or trajectory. HEAD-TO-HEAD: G2 defeated Vitality 1-0 in LEC Spring 2023 (single reference point, limited predictive value for BO3). MARKET SIGNAL: YES dropped from 72% EMA to 42% current (35.5pp weekly decline, 30pp decline at 15:13 UTC). This sharp reversal suggests market participants observed adverse information (in-game performance, draft disadvantage, or early map control loss). The magnitude and timing of the move indicate real-time game state knowledge beyond briefing data. ASYMMETRIC DATA: Briefing provides strong positive evidence for G2 (recent championship, BO3 success, head-to-head win) but limited negative evidence or current Vitality data. The sharp market reversal contradicts the one-sided brief, suggesting either: (a) Vitality performed better than expected in early games, or (b) G2 underperformed. Both scenarios reduce G2's win probability from raw form differential. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous. Match must be completed (not canceled or delayed 7+ days). Forfeits/walkovers resolve 50-50. Normal game result resolves to winner. Source: gol.gg within 2 hours or credible reporting. PROBABILITY REASONING: Baseline G2 favoritism (72% historical EMA) adjusted downward for sharp late market repricing (-30pp at 15:13 UTC). G2 championship form and head-to-head history support higher probability, but market reaction to live match data (unavailable in briefing) suggests competitive match with material uncertainty. Conservative estimate: 68% G2 win probability reflects strong underlying form tempered by real-time adversity signal. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES estimate (72) based on clear G2 form evidence and recent championship success. Low confidence in NO estimate (45) due to: (a) insufficient Vitality 2026 data, (b) inability to verify current match state, (c) no recent head-to-head or season performance data for Vitality, (d) limited counter-evidence beyond market repricing. Confidence gap reflects data quality asymmetry, not outcome certainty.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~5 hours); sharp price movement at 15:13 UTC suggests market participants possess real-time game information unavailable in briefing; inability to verify current match status creates moderate resolution risk.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "NO is favored at 58% and has gained +35.5pp over 7 days; YES collapsed -30pp in the last 6 hours alone\u2014this is extreme directional conviction, not noise. G2's recent Versus Playoffs title is real and demonstrates peak performance, BUT that was a different tournament phase; regular season play is often softer and more volatile. The briefing explicitly flags a critical data gap: 'Limited visibility into current 2026 Spring Regular Season standings and team form'\u2014we lack current season records, win-loss, patch adaptation, roster health, or recent scrim results. Market history shows YES was at 72% weighted EMA 7 days ago; the 35.5pp collapse is not gradual\u2014it's sharp reversal on Apr 11 (15:13 UTC: -30pp), suggesting new information reached traders hours before match time. Vitality's LEC Spring 2023 record (6-9) is stale; 2026 form could be much stronger or weaker\u2014we cannot assess trajectory without current season data. G2's head-to-head win over Vitality (Spring 2023, 1-0) is historical; matchups evolve with roster changes, meta shifts, and coaching adjustments over 3+ years. BO3 format is demanding: requires 2 map wins, not 1. Even strong teams drop series to mid-tier opponents in best-of formats when preparation or draft is off. Regular season matches carry lower stakes than playoffs; upsets are empirically more common in regular play than knockout stages\u2014this is a structural feature of esports competition. The sharp late-stage repricing (6 hours to match, -30pp for YES) suggests either: (a) injury/roster news, (b) scrim leaks favoring Vitality, or (c) professional sharp action sizing down G2 exposure. Any of these is credible. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH confidence in NO (52) because market structure + late vol + explicit briefing data gaps support the repricing. LOWER confidence in YES (35) because G2's recent accolades are real but don't negate missing current-season context or the late collapse. If G2 were truly as dominant in 2026 Spring as their Versus title suggests, the 42% YES price and the recent collapse would represent a major market misfire\u2014but the absence of current season records makes that claim unprovable. Probability of 38 (i.e., NO at 62%) reflects: G2's genuine recent form advantage offset by structural regular-season volatility, data gaps, and the market's late-stage reallocation away from YES.", "key_factor": "Massive 30pp sell-off of YES shares in the last 6 hours signals informed market repricing away from G2, likely reflecting team-specific intelligence unavailable in the briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: YES crashed -30pp in the last 6 hours (Apr 11 15:13 UTC), a massive reversal from 72% 7-day EMA. This sharp drop suggests late-arriving information favoring NO, but the timing (5 hours before match) is suspicious for actionable intel\u2014likely algorithmic or sentiment-driven rather than structural. DATA GAPS SEVERELY LIMIT CONFIDENCE ON BOTH SIDES: The briefing lacks 2026 Spring Regular Season standings, recent head-to-head results, current roster form, or Vitality's actual trajectory this year. Historical Spring 2023 data (3+ years old) has minimal predictive value. This is the core problem. G2 FORM CASE (favors YES, but limited scope): G2 won LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs\u2014a separate tournament. Playoff success \u2260 regular season form. The briefing conflates two different competitions. G2's championship run shows they *can* execute, but regular season is lower stakes and teams often experiment or rest. VITALITY RESILIENCE OVERLOOKED: Spring 2023 data shows Vitality went 6-3 despite losses\u2014that's a 67% win rate, not weak. The briefing dismisses this as 'mixed,' but it's actually solid mid-tier form. If Vitality has maintained or improved in 2026 Spring, the market may be overweighting G2's playoffs success. BO3 FORMAT INHERENTLY VOLATILE: BO3 requires 2/3 wins. Even if G2 is favored in individual games, the probability of winning a BO3 is nonlinear and sensitive to matchup dynamics, draft, and momentum shifts across games. Single-game dominance doesn't guarantee BO3 success. REGULAR SEASON VS PLAYOFF PSYCHOLOGY: Regular season games carry different intensity and preparation. Teams may prioritize specific matchups or test compositions. G2's Versus Playoffs dominance may not translate 1:1 to a regular season BO3 where Vitality has had time to prepare and may exploit specific weaknesses. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY, ~5 hours to resolution. The -30pp crash at 15:13 UTC (6 hours before match) occurred very late. No new substantive intel in briefing to explain this reversal. Could be pros, coaches, or team insiders with unpublished information, or market noise. Either way, high volatility near resolution suggests true odds may be closer to 50-50 than either extreme. VITALITY DATA FAMINE: The briefing has zero current-season performance data for Vitality in 2026 Spring. This is an underdog information gap. If Vitality's 2026 form is unknown, the market may have defaulted to 'G2 won playoffs, so G2 favored' without actual evidence. Vitality could be a top-4 team this season\u2014we don't know. AGAINST YES (tempers enthusiasm): G2's Versus Playoffs championship and BO3 success rate are real and impressive. The head-to-head historical win also supports YES. However, these data points are from different tournaments/years, creating a false narrative of dominance. VERDICT ON CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes = 35 (YES lacks 2026 season data to anchor the favorable narrative), confidence_no = 38 (NO also lacks Vitality's current form and recent H2H). Both sides have asymmetric information gaps. The -30pp crash suggests late-arriving information, but without transparency, we cannot trust it. Probability_score = 48 reflects genuine uncertainty, slight lean to NO due to market momentum, but insufficient data on both sides to be confident in either direction.", "key_factor": "Regular season volatility and BO3 unpredictability, combined with severe data freshness gaps that may mask Vitality's current 2026 form and recent matchup dynamics.", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "SHARP MARKET MOVE DETECTED: YES side collapsed -30pp in the 2-3 hours before match (~15:13 UTC on Apr 11), suggesting material information entered the market (likely team roster changes, practice scrim results, or on-site observations). This sharp reversal from 72% EMA to 42% current indicates sophisticated betting activity, not random noise. G2's playoff championship (LEC 2026 Versus) is real momentum but occurs in a DIFFERENT tournament phase than this regular season match. Playoff form does not deterministically predict regular season outcomes\u2014teams often rotate rosters, reduce preparation intensity, or face mental fatigue post-playoffs. Historical base rate for recent-form favorites in BO3 esports: ~60-70% win rate when they have demonstrated strength; however, the 30pp collapse in final hours suggests market participants (likely with access to team scrims, roster intel, or coaching staff signals) believe Vitality's actual strength is higher than G2's recent success implies. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing lacks 2026 Spring Regular Season standings, current roster composition, or recent head-to-head scrim data. The LEC Spring 2023 reference (6-9 record for Vitality) is 3 years stale in esports time. Current team compositions, meta alignment, and player transfers are unknown. Vitality's Spring 2023 record (6-9) was middling but not bottom-tier, suggesting organizational competence. The absence of negative news about Vitality in 2026 (no forfeits, no roster implosions reported) is weak evidence of baseline viability. BO3 format amplifies consistency requirements: a team needs to win 2 of 3 games, not just one dominant performance. G2's recent wins may reflect high peak performance in playoffs; regular season BO3s reward teams with deep champion pools and mid-game macro, not just peak mechanics. Market price at 42% YES (58% NO) after the collapse implies traders believe Vitality is now a slight favorite or near coin-flip. The 16pp spread between market (42%) and pre-collapse EMA (72%) is extraordinary and reflects either (a) genuine new information, (b) sharp betting recognizing a mispriced favorite, or (c) team-specific intelligence (e.g., G2 roster issue, Vitality practice dominance). TIMING SENSITIVITY: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). A reversal requiring G2 to overcome a 16pp swing in market sentiment with minimal time for new public information is low-probability unless the market move was a false spike (unlikely given volume and directionality). Conservative estimate: Apply 55-60% base rate for a recent-form favorite in regular season BO3, then discount 20-30pp for the sharp market reversal indicating sophisticated counter-thesis. This yields ~28-35% for YES (G2 Esports). Confidence asymmetry: confidence_yes=35 (data weak on G2's current form and Vitality's 2026 trajectory) and confidence_no=38 (similar weakness, plus uncertainty about whether market collapse reflects real intel or trading artifact). Both are below 50 due to missing roster, standings, and scrim data.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches between teams of disparate current form, the higher-form team wins ~65-75% of the time; however, regular season upset rates are 15-25% higher than playoff rates due to preparation variance and motivation differences.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MASSIVE RECENT REVERSAL: YES crashed 30pp in ~4 hours (Apr 11 15:13 UTC sharp move), suggesting urgent new information or insider knowledge entered the market just 5 hours before match start. CROWD PANIC SIGNAL: 24-hour YES decline of -33pp + 7-day decline of -35.5pp indicates sustained loss of confidence in G2, not noise. This is directional fear, not volatility. CURRENT PRICE (42% YES) sits FAR below 7-day EMA of 72% \u2014 suggests smart money fled YES side recently while crowd was still overweighting G2's playoff success. G2 RECENT FORM DATA IS STALE: Playoff wins cited are from 'LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs' (different tournament phase); no current Spring Regular Season standings or recent H2H data provided. VITALITY DATA ALSO SPARSE: Only LEC Spring 2023 (6-9 record) referenced; no 2026 Spring form visibility. Market may be pricing in unknown Vitality strength or G2 underperformance in regular season. BO3 FORMAT RISK: G2's recent playoff dominance (3-0, 3-2 wins) does NOT guarantee BO3 consistency in regular season. Upsets more common in lower-stakes matches. TIMING MISMATCH: Briefing cites G2's 'Versus Playoffs' championship but this is a regular season match \u2014 different intensity, preparation, and stakes. Market may be correctly de-rating playoff form. HIGH VOLATILITY (12-13pp/hr over 24h) + sharp -30pp move suggests information asymmetry or line-moving by informed bettors. Retail likely chased G2 highs; sharp money exited into that strength. NO SIDE (58%) now reflects rational skepticism: lack of current 2026 data on both teams, regular season context (lower intensity), and recent smart-money exodus from YES. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in NO (42) due to clear fear signal & volume migration; lower confidence in YES (35) due to stale playoff data & no current season context. Data gaps prevent high conviction either way.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market repricing is extreme and recent: YES dropped from 72% EMA (7-day) to 42% current in 24h, with -30pp single move at 15:13 UTC (3.5 hours before 19:55 match). This magnitude of reversal in a LIVE/IMMINENT event demands explanation beyond normal volatility. Playoff success does NOT predict regular season outcomes reliably: G2's LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs wins are in a different tournament phase with potentially different meta, patch, or seeding dynamics. Regular season BO3s have higher upset rates due to reduced preparation intensity and playoff-specific team cohesion effects fading. Critical data gap on current 2026 Spring standings: Briefing provides only LEC Spring 2023 head-to-head (G2 1-0 vs Vitality) and Vitality's 2023 record (6-9). NO current-season win-loss records, recent match results, or team roster/substitution status for either team in 2026 Spring are provided. This alone should constrain confidence on BOTH sides. Market microstructure signal: Heavy volume ($270k) with sharp repricing suggests informed traders (likely esports betting syndicates or team insiders with live scrimmage/scrim data) shifting conviction to Vitality. In LoL esports, 4-hour pre-match moves often reflect training facility intel not yet public. Vitality resilience narrative weakens without 2026 data: Citing 6-9 record from 2023 as 'mixed but resilient' ignores three years of roster turnover, coaching changes, and meta evolution. Current 2026 Vitality could be significantly stronger or weaker; briefing does not specify. BO3 consistency argument cuts both ways: YES case claims G2's recent 3-0/3-2 success proves BO3 reliability, but those were playoff matches where meta prep and mental clarity differ. NO case correctly notes BO3 requires win 2-of-3; single dominant team performances in playoffs don't guarantee 2-game consistency in regular season against an unfamiliar matchup state. Timing and resolution risk: Market resolves 19:55 UTC (5 hours from data timestamp). Any minute now, match will begin or team roster/scheduling changes will be announced. Once games start, share prices will rapidly collapse to $0.01/$0.99. The -30pp move at 15:13 UTC was likely in response to such news (team injury, substitute player, coach decision, or scrim results leaked). This suggests informed market is pricing Vitality as 58-72% favorite NOW, not G2. Esports-specific context: LoL professional meta shifts with patches; a team strong in playoffs (week N) can be disadvantaged 2-3 weeks later if champion pool or itemization changes. No patch/meta information in briefing. G2's Versus Playoffs wins may have exploited a meta no longer present on April 11. Confidence asymmetry justified: Confidence in NO is higher (42 vs 35) because the market repricing itself is the strongest signal available. When uninformed retail bettors (who backed G2 early) lose to professional esports bettors (who exited G2 after 15:13 UTC move), the margin and directionality of the move is credible. However, confidence on BOTH sides remains moderate because the REASON for the move (team news, meta, scrim results) is not specified in the briefing, only its existence is visible.", "key_factor": "The 30pp collapse in G2's price in the final 4 hours before match start (Apr 11 15:13 UTC) suggests either late-breaking team roster/health news, coaching decisions, or community intelligence about current-season form diverging sharply from playoff performance, which is atypical unless material information emerged.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "SHARP MARKET REVERSAL: YES crashed 30pp in a single 15:13 UTC move on Apr 11 (~4 hours before match), suggesting late-breaking information (roster change, player illness, scrim results, or internal team news) that briefing document does not capture. TEMPORAL DISCONNECT: G2's championship was in 'Versus Playoffs' (different tournament format), not regular season. Regular season BO3s notoriously feature higher upset rates than playoff BO5s where team depth matters more. BO3 VULNERABILITY: G2 may be unprepared for Vitality's specific meta-read or playstyle in regular season play. Versus Playoffs may have featured different champion pools, bans, or patch state than current match. VITALITY DATA SILENCE: Briefing provides only LEC Spring 2023 historical reference (3 years old for a fast-moving esport). 2026 Spring Vitality roster, coaching, form, and scrim momentum are completely opaque. PREPARATION ASYMMETRY: G2 likely focused internal resources on Versus Playoffs championship run; Vitality may have had lighter schedule and more time to prepare a specific BO3 gameplan against G2. MARKET STRUCTURE: Current 42% YES / 58% NO pricing reflects the late crash. High volatility (12-13pp/hr) indicates information asymmetry, not consensus. Early-week 72% YES EMA suggests arbitrageurs have since learned something the briefing lacks. BO3 RESET FACTOR: Even dominant teams drop individual games in BO3s due to adaptation, counter-pick success, or momentum swings. G2 must win 2-of-3; Vitality only needs 2 wins in a series where variance is higher than single-match play. UNDERDOG MOTIVATION: Vitality as 58% underdog in a regular season match (not a final) may have extreme motivation and less pressure, while G2 may treat this as preparation/rest after grueling playoff run.", "key_factor": "Vitality's roster or coaching staff has undergone a significant change since G2's Versus Playoffs victory that fundamentally alters their playstyle or meta-read, allowing them to exploit G2's preparation gap in a BO3 format where adaptation across three games becomes critical.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.4193617021276596, "no_score": 0.6169899665551839, "edge": 0.004361702127659628, "no_edge": 0.031989966555183935, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1893865", "question": "LoL: G2 Esports vs Team Vitality (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between G2 Esports and Team Vitality in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 10:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win the match against Team Vitality.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Vitality\" if Team Vitality win the match against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:55:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:55:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 270829.1596630004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["75402608914449967250207624471898011372340723735500711563328146206037449546807", "64525848286537441921079050725487818343167363564531620604907539142839323486543"]}, "key_facts": ["* [Page](/leagueoflegends/LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season \"View the content page [c]\").", "* [Talk](/leagueoflegends/index.php?title=Talk:LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Discussion about the content page [t]\").", "* [Edit](/leagueoflegends/index.php?title=LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season&action=edit \"This page is protected.", "* [History](/leagueoflegends/index.php?title=LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season&action=history \"Past revisions of this page [h]\").", "[What links here](/leagueoflegends/Special:WhatLinksHere/LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\").", "[Related changes](/leagueoflegends/Special:RecentChangesLinked/LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\").", "[Permanent link](/leagueoflegends/index.php?title=LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season&oldid=1004563 \"Permanent link to this revision of this page\").", "[Page information](/leagueoflegends/index.php?title=LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season&action=info \"More information about this page\").", "[What links here globally](/leagueoflegends/Special:GlobalWhatLinksHere/LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season).", "[[edit](/leagueoflegends/index.php?title=LEC/2026/Spring/Regular_Season&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Format\")]."], "news_summary": "This match involves G2 Esports and Team Vitality in the LEC Regular Season (BO3 format). Search results show G2 Esports recently won the LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs championship, defeating KC 3-2 in finals and MKOI 3-0 in semifinals, indicating strong current form. Historical data from LEC Spring 2023 shows Vitality with a mixed record, while G2 defeated Vitality 1-0 in that season. The regular season match represents standard league play with playoff implications.", "side_yes_case": ["G2 Esports recently won the LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs championship with dominant performances", "G2 has head-to-head victory over Vitality from LEC Spring 2023", "G2 demonstrated consistent BO3 success in recent playoffs (multiple 3-0 and 3-2 victories)", "G2's recent form trajectory is clearly upward with championship-level play"], "side_no_case": ["Vitality showed resilience in LEC Spring 2023 with 6 wins in 9 games despite some losses", "Regular season play differs from playoff intensity; upsets are more common", "Limited recent data on Vitality's 2026 form makes trajectory assessment difficult", "BO3 format requires consistency across multiple games, not just dominant single-game performances"], "key_context": ["BO3 (Best of 3) format requires winning 2 of 3 games", "G2 Esports recently won LEC 2026 Versus Playoffs (different tournament phase)", "Historical reference data is from LEC Spring 2023, not current 2026 season standings", "Limited visibility into current 2026 Spring Regular Season standings and team form", "Search results lack recent head-to-head or current season performance data for both teams"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T15:14:37.899841Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "75402608914449967250207624471898011372340723735500711563328146206037449546807", "data_points": 35, "weighted_avg": 0.717655705428951, "change_1w_pp": -35.5000000