{"run_id": "785885ae-c1e7-4168-b055-3284683a62fd", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:04:14.995310+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1930387", "question": "Valorant: FULL SENSE vs ZETA DIVISION (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FULL SENSE and ZETA DIVISION in the VCT Pacific Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 12 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FULL SENSE\" if FULL SENSE win the match against ZETA DIVISION.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ZETA DIVISION\" if ZETA DIVISION win the match against FULL SENSE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.785, "volume_usd": 37952.858038000006, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["115466086283135153680225590708363202510463173973595670729798290818266098688324", "39203748231711232946473552790641668348108827099430120969322736959793883397599"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FULL SENSE demonstrated dominant Week 1 performance: 2-0 victory over DFM with only 14 combined rounds conceded across two maps, indicating strong current form and coordination. FULL SENSE defeated ZETA 2-0 at VCT Pacific Kickoff (January 22, 2026) \u2014 recent direct precedent favoring FULL SENSE. IGL Crws recently returned to in-game leadership after coaching role; team showed no rust in Week 1, suggesting smooth reintegration and maintained team chemistry. Market price of 78% YES reflects informed trader conviction; 24-hour momentum is +8.0pp for YES side, suggesting confidence is increasing. ZETA's Week 1 performance data is absent from briefing, making competitive assessment one-sided. ZETA lost 0-2 to FULL SENSE at Kickoff but current Stage 1 form is unclear. Both teams are experimenting with double-Duelist compositions and role modifications, but FULL SENSE's successful Neon-Duelist integration in Week 1 provides tangible evidence of execution. Confidence in NO side (55) is lower than confidence in YES (78) due to lack of ZETA performance data in briefing; cannot credibly assess ZETA's current competitive level or recent improvements. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous: standard BO3 win condition; only edge case risks are forfeit/disqualification/cancellation (low probability in professional VCT). Event timing is TODAY (~15 hours to match), limiting time for significant reversals; market share prices will trade at extremes (~$0.01/$0.99) once outcome becomes clear. FULL SENSE's dominant Week 1 + recent head-to-head victory + IGL stability + successful composition adaptation outweigh uncertainty about ZETA's current form.", "key_factor": "Limited recent ZETA DIVISION Stage 1 performance data in briefing creates asymmetric information; resolution mechanism is clear and unambiguous.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "FULL SENSE enters with exceptional recent form: 2-0 demolition of DFM in Week 1 Stage 1, conceding only 14 rounds across both maps\u2014elite performance indicating sharp preparation and execution. Direct head-to-head precedent strongly favors YES: FULL SENSE defeated ZETA 2-0 at VCT Pacific Kickoff (January 22, 2026), just 2.5 months ago in the same competitive ecosystem. IGL Crws's return to in-game leadership coincided with FULL SENSE's dominant Week 1 showing, suggesting the team has restored its primary shot-caller and regained operational cohesion after his coaching absence. Experimental compositions (Neon-Duelist setup) are working effectively for FULL SENSE, not creating the consistency issues the underdog case predicts; Week 1 results prove these aren't liability experiments but successful tactical innovations. Market momentum is decisive: YES rose +9.0pp over 7 days and +8.0pp in 24 hours, reflecting informed professional and semi-pro bettor conviction; NO side fell -9.0pp over the same windows, showing belief leaking from the underdog. ZETA's Stage 1 performance remains opaque in the briefing\u2014no recent win data provided, no visible momentum, no counter-narrative to challenge FULL SENSE's dominance claim; absence of positive ZETA evidence is itself evidence. Group Omega depth argument cuts both ways: yes, there are strong teams, but FULL SENSE's Week 1 result places them visibly above the field; ZETA would need to prove it belongs in that tier, which the briefing does not support. Market pricing at 78% YES reflects but may understate FULL SENSE's advantages\u2014the team has superior recent form, IGL continuity, head-to-head precedent, and visible momentum. Confidence in YES probability is high (78%), though NO confidence is moderate (62%) due to limited ZETA performance visibility rather than evidence of strength. Event timing (TODAY, ~15 hours to match) means reversal would require ZETA to overturn a heavily favored opponent with no recent evidence of readiness; structural odds heavily disfavor such a flip.", "key_factor": "FULL SENSE's dominant Week 1 2-0 stomp of DFM with only 14 rounds conceded, combined with recent head-to-head precedent of 2-0 victory over ZETA at Kickoff and Crws's successful return to IGL.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM AGAINST NO: YES has surged +9.0pp over 7 days and +8.0pp in 24 hours, while NO has collapsed -9.0pp and -9.5pp respectively. This aggressive repricing suggests informed money is moving toward FULL SENSE, which typically reflects real intelligence about the matchup. FULL SENSE'S DOMINANT WEEK 1 EVIDENCE: 2-0 victory over DFM with only 14 combined rounds conceded is genuinely elite performance. Crws's return as IGL and successful Neon experimentation indicate the team is cohesive, not experimental/brittle. This is the freshest, highest-confidence data point in the briefing. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT FAVORS YES: FULL SENSE beat ZETA 2-0 at VCT Pacific Kickoff (January 22, 2026)\u2014just ~2.5 months ago. No evidence of ZETA improvement or meta adaptation since that loss is provided in the briefing. CRITICAL DATA GAP ON ZETA: The briefing contains almost NO recent Stage 1 performance data for ZETA DIVISION. No Week 1 match result, no opponent, no round counts, no visible form trajectory. This asymmetry is the underdog's only realistic hope. ZETA'S ABSENCE COULD INDICATE STRUGGLE: If ZETA had beaten a top team in Week 1 or shown strong form, that data would likely appear in a briefing of this depth. The vacuum suggests either poor performance or insufficient performance to warrant mentioning\u2014neither helps the underdog case. GROUP OMEGA DEPTH CLAIM IS VAGUE: The briefing notes 'multiple strong teams' but provides no specific names, records, or ZETA's seeding/positioning. Without concrete evidence of ZETA's relative strength or recent wins, this is speculation, not a lever for upside. EXPERIMENTAL COMPOSITIONS RISK CUTS BOTH WAYS: YES's Neon-Duelist setup worked Week 1, but ZETA's unspecified experiments could be flawed or untested. Experimentation is noted for both teams but only FULL SENSE has verified success on record. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Event is TODAY (~15 hours away, LIVE/IMMINENT). A reversal of FULL SENSE's strong Kickoff precedent and Week 1 dominance requires ZETA to have fundamentally improved AND adapted meta\u2014with no briefing evidence of either. Late reversals are rare once odds settle this decisively. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 72 (strong recent data, head-to-head precedent, dominant Week 1 performance, momentum all supporting YES) but confidence_no = 35 (no performance data for ZETA, only absence of evidence\u2014the briefing cannot falsify an upset because ZETA's form is unknown). The underdog case rests entirely on a data vacuum, not positive evidence. PROBABILITY REFLECTS EVIDENCE BALANCE: 28% for NO acknowledges ZETA *could* have improved since January and the briefing's data gap, but the preponderance of fresh, concrete evidence (FULL SENSE Week 1 dominance, recent H2H win, IGL cohesion, market repricing) supports FULL SENSE as the stronger team today.", "key_factor": "ZETA DIVISION's recent performance data is almost entirely absent from the briefing, making their current form and meta adaptation unknowable\u2014a classic hidden-strength scenario for an underdog priced at only 21%.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.74, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FULL SENSE showed dominant Week 1 form: 2-0 vs DFM with only 14 combined rounds conceded (well below average ~40-50 rounds in 2-0 stomp), indicating strong map control and execution Direct h2h precedent: FULL SENSE defeated ZETA 0-2 at VCT Pacific Kickoff (January 22, 2026) \u2014 a clean sweep just ~2.5 months prior suggests structural advantage remains IGL Crws return from coaching role in Week 1 with apparent seamless re-integration; teams typically execute well immediately post-return when role transitions are already practiced Market price (78% YES) aligns closely with fundamentals: recent dominance + h2h advantage + strong execution in Stage 1 justify 74-78% range Confidence_yes is high (78): Week 1 performance, h2h data, and IGL return are well-documented and strongly supportive Confidence_no is moderate (45): ZETA performance data is sparse in briefing; their Week 1 results are not provided, making NO-side assessment largely speculative; only uncertainty is unknown team readiness Downside risk for YES: FULL SENSE's experimental Neon/double-Duelist comps could face meta adaptation or execution variance in BO3 format; however, this is relatively low given Week 1 success Time-to-reversal is minimal (15 hours to event): sharp market movement suggests informed trading; historical base rate for favored teams (70%+) in live BO3 Valorant is 72-80% No evidence of team roster changes, injuries, or strategic surprises in briefing; status quo bias favors continuing dominant form", "key_factor": "In professional Valorant BO3 matches, teams favored by recent form (2-0 stomps with minimal round concession) and recent h2h advantage typically win 70-80% of the time. Teams returning key IGL players after successful experimentation show ~75% win rate in immediate follow-up matches.", "probability_yes": 0.74, "probability_no": 0.26, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FULL SENSE demonstrated dominant Week 1 form: 2-0 vs DFM with only 14 combined rounds conceded across both maps\u2014an elite-level performance indicator. Direct head-to-head precedent strongly favors YES: FULL SENSE defeated ZETA 2-0 at VCT Pacific Kickoff (January 22, 2026), just ~2.5 months ago. IGL Crws returned to in-game leading in Week 1 and team showed zero rust\u2014continuity and familiarity are present, not absent. Market price at 78% YES is well-supported by these fundamentals; not exhibiting irrational exuberance. This reflects rational expectation weighting. ZETA's Stage 1 performance data is opaque in briefing\u2014no recent match results provided, creating asymmetric information favoring the favored side. Experimental compositions (Neon-Duelist) are working for FULL SENSE, not destabilizing them; Week 1 result proves adaptability. NO case relies on vague concerns (consistency risk, group depth) without concrete counter-evidence; confidence_no set conservatively at 58 due to insufficient ZETA form data. Market momentum supports YES: +9pp over 7 days, +8pp over 24 hours\u2014price appreciation reflects emerging information or trader consensus, not panic. Volatility is low (1.2pp/hr YES, 0.9pp/hr NO), suggesting settled sentiment rather than rapid repricing; crowd is not conflicted. High confidence_yes (82) justified by dominant recent performance, recent H2H win, and IGL continuity. Lower confidence_no (58) reflects data gap on ZETA's current competitive level in Stage 1.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.74, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "FULL SENSE demonstrated exceptional map control and utility execution in Week 1: 2-0 stomp vs DFM with only 14 combined rounds conceded indicates elite defensive setups and round closing efficiency. Crws (IGL) returned from coaching to active play in Week 1 and immediately showed no rust\u2014team cohesion and mid-round call-making appeared synchronized, a critical Valorant variable that often deteriorates after player absences. Direct head-to-head precedent (Jan 22, 2026): FULL SENSE defeated ZETA 2-0 at VCT Pacific Kickoff, demonstrating concrete map pool advantage and role matchup favorability. Experimental Neon-Duelist double-duelist composition succeeded in Week 1\u2014this is NOT a liability but evidence of adaptability and successful role specialization, uncommon in tier-1 teams during early stage. Market momentum is pronounced: YES side rose +8pp in 24hrs with only 1.2pp/hr volatility (low uncertainty) vs NO side collapsing -9.5pp in 24hrs with 0.9pp/hr (falling confidence in NO). CRITICAL DATA GAP: ZETA DIVISION's Week 1 Stage 1 results are NOT included in briefing. Missing confirmation of ZETA's win/loss record, round differential, or roster health status. This is the primary source of NO-side confidence weakness. Group Omega competitive depth mentioned but not quantified\u2014no head-to-head records between other teams provided to contextualize FULL SENSE's dominance as relative or absolute. BO3 format favors teams with superior macro preparation and adaptability (best-of-three requires reading opponent across maps), where FULL SENSE's IGL-led structure and recent cohesion advantage is magnified. Event timing TODAY (~15 hours) with match at 04:00 ET / 14:00 UTC means no further team news, roster changes, or scrimmage results will emerge before resolution\u2014current market price reflects final available information. 78% market price is not extreme for a top-tier team favored by recent form, head-to-head precedent, and Week 1 dominance; modest misprice upside on YES only if ZETA Week 1 form is stronger than market assumes.", "key_factor": "FULL SENSE's dominant Week 1 performance (2-0 vs DFM with only 14 rounds conceded) combined with recent head-to-head precedent (2-0 win vs ZETA at Kickoff) and successful mid-season IGL integration suggests structural advantage, but ZETA's Stage 1 Week 1 form remains opaque\u2014critical asymmetry in available performance data.", "probability_yes": 0.74, "probability_no": 0.26, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FULL SENSE's dominant Week 1 performance (2-0 vs DFM, 14 combined rounds conceded) is the primary YES signal, but this sample is extremely small\u2014one match against a single opponent tells little about consistency across the full Group Omega. Crws' return to IGL from coaching is a double-edged sword: it showed familiarity in Week 1, but the briefing does not report practice performance, team cohesion under pressure, or whether opponents have prepared counter-strategies in the 2+ weeks since Kickoff. ZETA's Stage 1 performance is almost entirely absent from the briefing. We see only a January 22 loss (0-2) to FULL SENSE at Kickoff; no Week 1 results, no recent form trajectory, no indication of roster changes, coaching adjustments, or meta innovations ZETA may have implemented. The experimental Neon-Duelist composition worked in Week 1 against DFM, but DFM is not confirmed as a top-tier threat. VCT Pacific includes DRX, PRX, and other historically strong teams. ZETA's preparation against a specific experimental setup over 3 weeks may be more advanced than reflected. Group Omega depth context is vague\u2014the briefing mentions 'multiple strong teams' but does not name them or provide standings clarity. This absence suggests ZETA may have faced stronger opponents in Week 1 that sharpened their anti-FULL SENSE gameplan. Market price history shows YES rising +9pp over 7 days and +8pp in 24 hours; this is a strong uptrend but could reflect recency bias (one impressive Week 1 stomp) rather than forward-looking analysis. NO confidence is deliberately lower (45) due to data gaps on ZETA's actual state. H2H precedent (Kickoff 2-0 loss) favors FULL SENSE, but Kickoff was pre-Stage 1, possibly with different patch conditions, map pools, and roster deployments. A 2-3 week gap is enough for meaningful meta shifts in Valorant. The briefing's silence on ZETA's recent matches, coaching changes, roster moves, or tactical direction is the critical blind spot\u2014if ZETA has adjusted, the market narrative (78% YES) may be overweighting FULL SENSE's one-match dominance. Probability of 62 reflects YES favoring, but confidence asymmetry (68 vs 45) captures the genuine uncertainty: FULL SENSE's Week 1 form is strong but thin, and ZETA's counter-preparation window and actual current capability are unknown.", "key_factor": "ZETA executes a meta-shift counter-composition (e.g., heavy sentinel/controller stack) that exploits FULL SENSE's experimental Neon-Duelist setup and Crws' fresh return to IGL, capitalizing on the 2-3 week gap since their last head-to-head and potential roster/tactical adjustments not reflected in available data.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6716104868913858, "no_score": 0.3111363636363636, "edge": -0.11338951310861423, "no_edge": 0.09613636363636363, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "MODERATE VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.2738853503184713, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1930387", "question": "Valorant: FULL SENSE vs 