| 3 : 0 | SPE | View match details | [...] | Date | Tier | Type |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  ---  --- \n| April 4, 2026 - 20:10 KST | S-Tier | Offline | VCT Pacific: Stage 1 - Week 1 | VCT Pacific: Stage 1 - Week 1 |  | 2 : 0 | DFM | View match details |\n| February 8, 2026 - 17:00 KST | S-Tier | Offline | VCT Pacific Kickoff | VCT Pacific Kickoff |  | 0 : 2 | DRX | View match details |\n| February 6, 2026 - 17:00 KST | S-Tier | Offline | VCT Pacific Kickoff | VCT Pacific Kickoff |  | 1 : 2 | DFM | View match details |\n| January 31, 2026 - 17:00 KST | Undefined | Literal |  | VCT/2026/Pacific League/Kickoff |  | 0 : 2 | NS | View match details |\n| January 24, 2026 - 20:00 KST | S-Tier | Offline | VCT Pacific Kickoff | VCT Pacific Kickoff |  | 2 : 1 | DRX | View match details |", "The Group Omega standings after week one are:\n\n# Up next\n\nVCT Pacific Stage 1 will continue next week with the following matches:\n\nall bots\n\nSo true.", "nah except drx\n\nexcept GE\n\nNS Fluke\n\n10 minutes 2 comments vlr dead\n\nFlair\n\nMeow\n\nscore missing from rrq vs zeta\n\ntrash games only prx ns was good\n\nNRG fluke\n\nKC fluke\n\n:3 fluke\n\nPRX fluke, NS got hit by nerfs harder + Map pool got worse for NS & better for PRX\n\nWe as a collective need to abolish the word fluke\n\nno how else am I supposed to demean and diminish all non-TL wins\n\nyou being team liquid says a lot\n\nToronto and santiago both flukes\n\nT1 payed for that group I just know it.", "american and \u2018payed\u2019 \ud83e\udd40\n\naverage american [...] # Group Omega\n\nIn the most dominant match from the first week of play in Group Omega, FULL SENSE returned to the stage and downed DetonatioN FocusMe 2-0, allowing a combined 14 rounds across both maps.", "With in-game leader \nCrws \n returning to play after a short spell as head coach, the team seemed not to have missed a beat, cruising with a familiar voice in the middle seat."], "news_summary": "FULL SENSE and ZETA DIVISION are set to compete in a VCT Pacific Group Omega BO3 match. FULL SENSE demonstrated dominant form in Week 1 of Stage 1, defeating DetonatioN FocusMe 2-0 with only 14 combined rounds conceded, featuring returning IGL Crws and experimental Neon composition. Limited recent head-to-head data and ZETA's current performance level in Stage 1 are unclear from available results, though both teams are competing in the top-tier S-Tier VCT Pacific League.", "side_yes_case": ["FULL SENSE dominated Week 1 with 2-0 victory over DFM, conceding only 14 rounds total", "FULL SENSE IGL Crws returned to in-game leading and team displayed familiarity with new compositions", "FULL SENSE recent history includes VCT Pacific Kickoff win 2-0 over ZETA (January 22, 2026)", "Team appears well-prepared with successful Neon-Duelist experimentation working effectively"], "side_no_case": ["ZETA DIVISION recent head-to-head record shows loss to FULL SENSE 0-2 at Kickoff (January 22, 2026)", "Limited visible Stage 1 performance data for ZETA makes recent form assessment difficult", "FULL SENSE's experimental compositions with multiple new roles could create consistency issues", "Group Omega contains multiple strong teams with competitive depth potentially challenging both squads"], "key_context": ["VCT Pacific Stage 1 Group Omega - S-Tier official league match", "FULL SENSE just returned IGL Crws from coaching role in Week 1", "Recent precedent: FULL SENSE defeated ZETA 2-0 at VCT Pacific Kickoff (January 22, 2026)", "Both teams actively experimenting with double-Duelist and modified role compositions", "Match is part of ongoing group stage - full tournament format implications unclear"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T23:04:03.089054Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "115466086283135153680225590708363202510463173973595670729798290818266098688324", "data_points": 32, "weighted_avg": 0.7140104059829999, "change_1w_pp": 9.000000000000007, "change_24h_pp": 8.000000000000007, "volatility_24h": 1.1868010498925867, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "39203748231711232946473552790641668348108827099430120969322736959793883397599", "data_points": 44, "weighted_avg": 0.28869533149911236, "change_1w_pp": -9.0, "change_24h_pp": -9.5, "volatility_24h": 0.9322619368184987, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-11T23:04:03.273986Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-12T14:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-12T17:24:14.740275+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "e40ed7a7-57ea-4999-a8d5-8467cc785f05", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:08:56.282142+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1867384", "question": "LoL: BNK FEARX vs DN SOOPers (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between BNK FEARX and DN SOOPers in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 12 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FEARX\" if BNK FEARX win the match against DN SOOPers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers\" if DN SOOPers win the match against BNK FEARX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.635, "volume_usd": 23532.938835000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["10595427882555393944714994140736498423027193534271147505803345589969508929675", "104301444328712280468881725693849872696810797593153469424162796868334307449891"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if BNK FEARX wins the BO3 match; NO if DN SOOPers wins. Criteria are clear and unambiguous regarding win conditions. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides only generic LCK Rounds 1-2 champion statistics (Corki/Sion 100% WR, Anivia 66.67% WR) with no team-specific rosters, win-loss records, recent form, or head-to-head history for either team. MARKET PRICE AS SIGNAL: Current market prices show YES at 64% / NO at 36%, representing significant confidence in BNK FEARX. This 28-point spread reflects market consensus, likely based on information external to the briefing. PRICE MOMENTUM: YES side rose +13.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 05 (+16.5pp) and Apr 07 (+7.5pp), suggesting genuine information flow favoring FEARX rather than noise. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Strong upward momentum in YES pricing combined with complete absence of team-level data in briefing suggests market participants possess roster knowledge, recent match results, and head-to-head records not provided here. LIQUIDITY & VOLUME: $23.5k USD volume indicates this is an active, monitored market with multiple informed traders; unusual for significant mispricing given 15-hour time horizon. TIMING CONSIDERATION: EVENT TIMING is TODAY (~15 hours to resolution). At this stage, major roster changes, injuries, or scheduling issues would already be known. Reversal would require unexpected developments with minimal time. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Cannot independently verify either team's strength due to missing competitive data. Confidence in YES estimate is LOW (35) because reliance on market price signal alone. Confidence in NO estimate is also LOW (32) because no counter-evidence exists. Both sides equally data-starved. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Source is gol.gg with fallback to credible reporting within 2 hours. No ambiguity in team name matching (both names are standard abbreviations). Minimal oracle risk. FORFEIT/CANCELLATION RISK: Criteria establish 50-50 resolution for cancellations or walkouts. No briefing evidence of health issues, visa problems, or logistical concerns that would trigger this clause. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Market price of 64% for YES reflects aggregated information from informed traders. Without contradicting data, adopting market-implied probability is reasonable. Modest adjustment downward (64\u219264) reflects uncertainty, but no strong reason to deviate significantly from market consensus.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains only LCK meta statistics and no team-specific data (rosters, recent form, head-to-head records) for either BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers, making competitive analysis impossible.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES is priced at 64% (favorite) vs NO at 36% (underdog), with YES showing +13.5pp 7-day momentum (+16.5pp spike on Apr 05, +7.5pp on Apr 07). This rising trend and current favorite status suggest informed markets have positioned toward FEARX. MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: YES side gained 13.5pp over 7 days while NO side fell 13.5pp. Sharp move on Apr 05 (+16.5pp YES) suggests new information favored FEARX; Apr 07 volatility shows market confidence solidifying around the 64% level despite minor corrections. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES: NO side (DN SOOPers) has no specific performance data presented in briefing. Absence of positive information, combined with falling market odds, suggests SOOPers lacks notable recent wins or is perceived as weaker in current LCK meta. META ALIGNMENT UNKNOWN: Briefing shows Corki/Sion at 100% WR and Anivia/Gnar/Pantheon at 66.67% WR in LCK 2026 Rounds 1-2, but does not specify which team proficiency with these champions. FEARX's favorite status may reflect superior meta adaptation or draft skill. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO direct team rosters, win-loss records, recent form, or head-to-head history for BNK FEARX vs DN SOOPers. Cannot independently verify why FEARX is favored beyond market pricing itself. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 45 (market consensus visible but unvalidated by team data) and confidence_no = 35 (SOOPers underdog status unclear without counter-evidence). Market may be correct, but limited intel constrains conviction on either side. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Event resolves TODAY (15 hours to match start). Odds movement has stabilized; no further reversal catalysts evident in briefing. FEARX's 64% reflects pre-match settled market consensus rather than late-breaking news. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: BO3 format means FEARX must win 2 of 3 games. Market-implied 64% for series win is reasonable given typical competitive balance, but without team-specific data, this remains inference from price action rather than fundamental analysis. ADVOCATE POSITION: As the Bull for the favorite, FEARX's rising odds from ~50% to 64% over one week signals informed capital flow toward FEARX. Market participants with access to team intel, recent scrims, or meta meta-game appear to favor FEARX. The question is whether they are right. UNDERDOG CASE (why NOT to go higher on YES): SOOPers name recognition and lack of negative information could indicate a competitive lower-tier team capable of upset. BO3 format allows underdog to steal 1-2 games. Without roster/form data, cannot rule out 30-40% upside for SOOPers.", "key_factor": "Market consensus (64% YES) reflects accumulated betting information and professional analysis favoring BNK FEARX, though the briefing lacks direct team-specific data to independently validate this edge.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero team-specific performance metrics, roster compositions, or recent match histories for either BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers. All available data consists of generic LCK meta statistics (Corki/Sion 100% WR, Anivia 66.67% WR) unlinked to either team's proficiency. MARKET PRICING APPEARS OVERCONFIDENT: YES side has risen +13.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 05 (+16.5pp) and Apr 07 (+7.5pp), yet briefing provides NO justification for this upward drift. This suggests market momentum may be driving YES pricing rather than fundamental team strength. UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO: Without evidence of FEARX superiority (roster depth, recent wins, meta adaptability), the 64% YES price assumes FEARX dominance without supporting data. DN SOOPers' underdog status (36%) may reflect market narrative bias rather than actual competitive weakness. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS ADAPTABILITY: Best-of-3 series allow teams to adjust drafts and strategies between games. A team with superior meta reading or counter-pick preparation (unknown for both teams) could exploit weaknesses invisible in pre-match data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Rounds 1-2 of LCK spring season typically feature unpredictable results as teams are still calibrating meta interpretation and roster synergy. Early-season matches have higher upset potential than established tournament standings suggest. VOLUME & SPREAD SIGNAL UNCERTAINTY: $23,533 trading volume is modest; the YES/NO prices not summing to 100% (64%+36%=100%) indicates a tight orderbook spread, suggesting informed traders are also uncertain. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: Confidence_yes set to 28 (low) because briefing provides zero positive evidence for FEARX's actual strength \u2014 only market price inflation. Confidence_no set to 32 (low) because briefing equally lacks SOOPers' competitive advantages \u2014 both sides suffer severe evidence gaps. TIMING: Event resolves TODAY in ~15 hours. No new team data will emerge before match; this is a pure matchup evaluation in an information vacuum. Late-stage market movement (+1.0pp in 24hr) suggests diminishing new information flow. PROBABILITY REASONING: With no team-specific data favoring either side, base rate for underdog upset in BO3 LCK matches is ~35-45%. The 64/36 split is driven by narrative/momentum, not evidence. Adjusting down to 38% for YES reflects skepticism of the YES premium and recognition that SOOPers at 36% may be underpriced given information parity.", "key_factor": "Severe information asymmetry in briefing allows for underdog pricing inefficiency \u2014 neither team has documented form, roster strength, or head-to-head data, making 64% YES pricing potentially overconfident.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.22, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero team-specific information for BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers \u2014 no rosters, recent win-loss records, head-to-head history, or current form metrics Meta statistics provided (Corki/Sion 100% WR, Anivia 66.67% WR) are tournament-wide, not linked to either team's proficiency or draft tendencies Market price of 64% YES suggests material confidence in BNK FEARX, but briefing provides no justification for this deviation from 50-50 Price history shows 13.5pp rise over 7 days (+16.5pp spike Apr 05, +7.5pp A