itioning, yet briefing explicitly states search results 'lack direct competitive intelligence on either team's current form, roster composition, or head-to-head records' Market appears to be pricing on prior beliefs or external signals NOT present in this briefing \u2014 classic apathy to information quality With ~15 hours to resolution and NO new team-specific news in briefing, price has stabilized (24h change +1.0pp YES, +0.0pp NO) \u2014 suggests consensus has already locked in Sharp moves Apr 05-07 (+16.5pp, +7.5pp, -5.5pp on YES) indicate volatility driven by external reporting, not briefing-visible data Confidence asymmetry: Cannot justify YES at 64% without team comparisons (confidence_yes=35), but also cannot confidently argue for NO side without counter-evidence (confidence_no=28) RESOLUTION RISK: Match resolves TODAY; any tie/forfeit/cancellation triggers 50-50 resolution, yet no scheduling or team status information in briefing Market is pricing a default YES lean, but briefing reveals this is an information desert \u2014 suggests crowd has moved on from fact-checking into momentum trading", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No team rosters, player names, or individual player performance metrics provided for either BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers. NO DIRECT MATCHUP HISTORY: Briefing contains zero head-to-head records, recent form data (win/loss streaks), or historical performance between these two teams. META STATS UNLINKED: Champion pick/ban data (Corki/Sion 100% WR, Anivia 66.67% WR) reflects LCK-wide statistics, not which team excels at these champions or their draft strategy. ROSTER COMPOSITION UNKNOWN: Team synergy, primary win conditions, signature strategies, and player specializations completely absent from briefing. MARKET PRICE DRIVEN BY TRADER CONSENSUS, NOT FUNDAMENTALS: 64% YES price reflects aggregate trader belief, not analyzable team-specific evidence; 13.5pp rise over 7 days suggests information flow favoring FEARX, but source data not provided. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY (~15 hours); insufficient time for new data discovery; analyst must work with incomplete briefing. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Clear rules for match cancellation, forfeit, and tie scenarios reduce ambiguity risk, but do not resolve underlying team evaluation gap. NO INSTITUTIONAL KNOWLEDGE AVAILABLE: Briefing lacks esports intelligence typical of LCK analyst (team strength tiers, coaching quality, patch adaptation speed, tournament performance trends). CONFIDENCE SYMMETRIC FAILURE: Unable to justify YES OR NO side with confidence >28-30 due to complete absence of competitive intelligence on both teams.", "key_factor": "The briefing provides only generic LCK meta champion statistics (Corki/Sion 100% WR, Anivia 66.67% WR) without any team-specific pick/ban patterns, roster information, individual player mechanics, or head-to-head records\u2014making direct competitive prediction analytically impossible; market price of 64% YES reflects trader consensus rather than justified fundamentals.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero direct team performance data, roster composition, or head-to-head records for either BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers. Market confidence in YES (64%) rests entirely on external knowledge not present in the briefing. MARKET MOMENTUM MASKING UNCERTAINTY: YES side surged +13.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 05 (+16.5pp) and Apr 07 (+7.5pp, then -5.5pp). This volatility suggests information flow or speculative buying, not stable underlying conviction. The briefing provides no justification for this swing. META CHAMPIONS UNATTRIBUTED: Briefing identifies Corki/Sion (100% WR), Anivia (66.67% WR), Gnar/Pantheon (66.67% WR) as meta-dominant in LCK Rounds 1-2, but does NOT link these picks to either team's proficiency. If DN SOOPers has superior Sion/Corki execution or a hidden specialty (e.g. Anivia mid), they hold a concrete edge masked by aggregate stats. ROSTER OPACITY: Briefing mentions only player names (Woogiman, Misa, NL) with no role assignments, team affiliations clarified, or recent lineup changes noted. A mid-season sub or injury not yet public could dramatically shift the BO3 outcome\u2014SOOPers could have prepared a roster surprise. REVERSE INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Market has priced BNK FEARX heavily (64%) despite zero comparative data. This suggests consensus bettors are relying on brand recognition, historical pedigree, or external scouting reports entirely absent from the briefing. A contrarian edge exists if DN SOOPers has quietly improved or BNK FEARX is overrated on legacy. NO SIDE UNDER-PRICED: NO side (36%) lacks any stated weaknesses or disqualifying factors in the briefing. The absence of negative data on SOOPers is itself suspicious\u2014this could be a sleeping underdog with minimal public coverage but strong internal preparation. DRAFT FLEXIBILITY UNKNOWN: Briefing does not detail either team's champion pool depth, flex picks, or counter-pick strategies. In BO3 format, teams that can shift meta adaptation mid-series (e.g., SOOPers pivoting to Anivia/Gnar lanes BNK cannot contest) gain a massive edge. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY in ~15 hours. If a roster announcement, injury report, or scrim leak breaks in final hours favoring SOOPers, market cannot correct and shares will trade at distorted prices until resolution. CONFIDENCE SEVERELY DEPRESSED ON BOTH SIDES: absence of direct competitive intel means neither YES nor NO side can be defended with high conviction. Confidence scores capped at 35/32 reflect fundamental data insufficiency, not close competitive balance. MARKET PRICE INCONSISTENCY: YES at 64%, NO at 36% = 100% vig accounted for, but no underlying match statistics justify this 28-point gap. Either YES is overconfident on legacy bias, or briefing is deliberately withholding SOOPers' recent form data (possible if SOOPers has been hiding scrim results).", "key_factor": "DN SOOPers fields an unexpected roster substitution (likely mid or support) that exploits BNK FEARX's scouting gap, or a critical meta champion (Corki/Sion/Anivia) that BNK cannot draft/play at elite level despite recent market confidence.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5853508771929825, "no_score": 0.4243478260869566, "edge": -0.0496491228070175, "no_edge": 0.0593478260869566, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 33% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1867384", "question": "LoL: BNK FEARX vs DN SOOPers (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between BNK FEARX and DN SOOPers in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 12 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FEARX\" if BNK FEARX win the match against DN SOOPers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers\" if DN SOOPers win the match against BNK FEARX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.635, "volume_usd": 23532.938835000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["10595427882555393944714994140736498423027193534271147505803345589969508929675", "104301444328712280468881725693849872696810797593153469424162796868334307449891"]}, "key_facts": ["Active ; South Korea Woogiman, Park Jin-wook, 2025-02-17 ; South Korea Misa, Hong Sang-yeong, 2026-03-11 ; South Korea NL, Hwang Gyo-min, 2026-03-11 ; South Korea", "With 3 of the 5 Worlds 2022 winners, KT Rolster was the only team to take a match win against Gen.G in the Spring season, though they ended 5th after losing 2-3", "| 4 | [![Image 1392: Anivia](https://liquipedia.net/commons/images/thumb/8/81/Champion_icon_Anivia.png/25px-Champion_icon_Anivia.png)](https://liquipedia.net/leagueoflegends/Anivia \"Anivia\")[Anivia](https://liquipedia.net/leagueoflegends