f it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.575, "volume_usd": 24665.09965999999, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["104539274890305423427045495239693166855636441886163504918890471079891557644856", "3700601179190665942678343900146794725507866232780749697772668865313681117914"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Match must be played to completion and JD Gaming must win the BO3 series (first to 2 maps). Forfeit/walkout before start = 50-50 resolution per criteria. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains tournament structure info and scattered match results from other teams (All Gamers 2-1 TEC on March 31; EDG/XLG performance summaries) but provides almost NO direct evidence of JD Gaming's competitive level, roster quality, or recent form. LIMITED TEC DATA: TEC qualified for VCT China Stage 1 Group Alpha and lost 2-1 to All Gamers on March 31 (most recent concrete result). This shows TEC is group-stage competitive but potentially beatable by other Group Alpha opponents. JD GAMING DATA VOID: Briefing includes fragmented roster data (players like Lysoar, NoMan, Rarga listed under one team context; coaches paris/Fire3 under another) but no clear recent match results, win-loss record, or performance against comparable opponents. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market price at 57% YES (vs 43% NO) suggests market has access to information not in this briefing\u2014likely recent scrims, roster updates, or analyst commentary on comparative strength. This +7.5pp rise over 7 days indicates accumulating YES support. SYMMETRY OF UNCERTAINTY: Unable to confidently assess relative team strength. Brief shows both teams competed in same Stage 1 Group Alpha structure but provides no direct competitive comparison. In the absence of clear evidence favoring either side, market median (57% YES) serves as weak prior. TIMING: Event is TODAY (~16 hours until 2026-04-12 15:00 UTC). At this stage, match cancellation or forfeit risk is low unless major roster issues emerge immediately. Assume match will be completed. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Criteria are clear (BO3 winner resolves to winning team; forfeit before match = 50-50; incomplete match with one team forced to forfeit = winning team). VLR.gg is primary source with 2-hour publication window before alt sources used. No material ambiguity detected in resolution criteria. CONFIDENCE ADJUSTMENT: confidence_yes=28 reflects strong data gap on JD Gaming's actual competitive position. confidence_no=25 reflects equally weak data on TEC's current strength post-March-31-loss. Neither side has sufficient briefing support for high confidence. FINAL ESTIMATE: No solid ground to deviate from market price. Slight lean to 52 (vs 57) reflects modest skepticism that market-priced confidence is overweighted without seeing the supporting data, but uncertainty is genuinely high.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains fragmented roster/organizational data but critically lacks direct performance metrics, recent form, or head-to-head history for either JD Gaming or TEC Esports; market price (57% YES) likely reflects information not present in provided briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (YES) STRENGTHS: JD Gaming defeated TEC 2-1 on March 31, 2026 in VCT China Stage 1 Group Alpha \u2014 this is the most recent direct head-to-head evidence and shows JD Gaming can execute against TEC in the exact format and competition tier being wagered on. MARKET MOMENTUM ALIGNS WITH FAVORITE: YES trades at 57-58% with +7.5pp 7-day rise, reflecting informed market movement toward the favorite. The sharp moves on Apr 11 (+9.5pp, +10.0pp) suggest new information favoring JD Gaming entered the market closer to match time. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: TEC lost to All Gamers 2-1 just days before their prior matchup with JD Gaming, indicating inconsistent performance against group rivals. No evidence in briefing shows TEC has improved roster or form since the March 31 loss. INCOMPLETE DATA ON BOTH SIDES: The briefing contains fragmented tournament records but lacks detailed recent form data for either team post-March 31. JD Gaming's broader tournament trajectory is unclear from search results. This asymmetric data gap slightly reduces confidence in both directions. 24-HOUR VOLATILITY SIGNALS UNCERTAINTY: Both sides show high volatility (5.6pp/hr YES, 5.3pp/hr NO) with sharp reversals. The -5.5pp 24-hour drop for YES suggests some uncertainty crept in, though YES remains favored. This volatile micro-movement reflects genuine analytical difficulty but does not overturn the direct H2H evidence. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT FAVORS CONSISTENCY: Stage 1 Group Alpha is ongoing with teams playing rapid succession (all teams already 2 matches deep after Week 2 Day 1 per briefing). Teams showing form early (EDG, XLG in Omega) maintain it; JD Gaming's recent win positions them as the stronger momentum play. RESOLUTION RISK IS LOW: Match is TODAY (16 hours to event). Forfeit/cancellation probability is minimal for an official VCT stage match. Outcome depends almost entirely on in-game performance, not administrative outcomes. CASE FOR NO (UNDERDOG): TEC Esports qualified for VCT China Stage 1, indicating baseline competitive caliber. BO3 format allows teams to adapt mid-series; TEC could have prepared adjustments since March 31 loss. However, no evidence in briefing supports a TEC roster upgrade or tactical evolution. Absence of positive TEC form data post-loss is the underdog's critical weakness. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 52 (moderate \u2014 direct H2H evidence is strong but single data point in volatile meta; recent coaching change noted for JD Gaming on Feb 22 adds personnel context but outcome unclear). confidence_no = 48 (slightly lower \u2014 TEC's recent loss to JD Gaming directly undermines NO case; insufficient counter-narrative in briefing to justify higher NO confidence). MARKET PRICE REASONABLY REFLECTS FUNDAMENTALS: 57% for YES aligned with one recent head-to-head victory and stronger short-term momentum. Market is not egregiously mispricing; slight undervaluation of YES possible but not extreme given data scarcity.", "key_factor": "JD Gaming's recent 2-1 victory over TEC on March 31, 2026 in the same group stage competition demonstrates direct competitive advantage in the current meta.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTHS (TEC/NO side): TEC qualified for VCT China Stage 1 Group Alpha, a major tournament gate. The briefing shows All Gamers beat TEC 2-1 on March 31, 2026, indicating TEC is competitive at S-Tier level and can take maps off established opponents. TEC's presence in the same group as JD Gaming, TYLOO, BLG, FPX, and AG suggests roster parity. UNDERDOG VULNERABILITIES (TEC/NO side): The All Gamers 2-1 loss shows TEC lost to a group rival recently. The briefing notes 'strongest teams in the first week... come from Group Omega: EDG and XLG,' not Group Alpha, which may suggest Group Alpha lacks a clear dominant force\u2014but does not confirm TEC is weak. FAVORITE WEAKNESS (JD Gaming/YES side): The briefing contains almost NO concrete data on JD Gaming's recent form, roster strength, or head-to-head record vs. TEC. Fragmented tournament data in search results is insufficient to establish JD Gaming as superior. This is a critical data gap. FAVORITE STRENGTH (JD Gaming/YES side): JD Gaming is rated 57% by market, suggesting informed traders believe JD Gaming has form or matchup advantage. However, this belief is not substantiated by the briefing data provided\u2014market price alone cannot override missing evidence. HISTORICAL HEAD-TO-HEAD: Zero direct JD Gaming vs TEC match data in briefing. The market is pricing YES at 57% on speculation or external knowledge not contained in this briefing. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Stage 1 Group Stage is ongoing (April 6+ matches reported). Both teams are competing in the same group; this is not a qualitative matchup (established vs. upstart) but peer competitors. The briefing explicitly states both teams are in Group Alpha. MARKET VOLATILITY: YES side has sharp moves (+9.5pp, -7.5pp, +10.0pp) in last 24 hours; NO side similarly volatile (+10.0pp, +7.5pp, -7.0pp). High volatility on both sides suggests uncertainty, not confidence in favorite. RESOLUTION TIMING: Event is TODAY (~16 hours to resolution). Market is LIVE/IMMINENT. Sharp moves suggest new information or hedging activity, but briefing data is stale (last 4+ days). Any fresh intel (injury, roster change, recent scrim result) is not captured here. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides more evidence about TEC's competitive tier (beat Kickoff opponents, took map vs All Gamers) than about JD Gaming's recent strength. Confidence in YES should be lower than confidence in NO due to this gap. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: With symmetrical data gaps and TEC's demonstrated competitiveness in recent matches, this is genuinely close to a coin flip. Slight underdog adjustment: 42% for YES reflects NO's underpricing (43% market) given lack of concrete JD Gaming form evidence and TEC's peer-level qualification.", "key_factor": "TEC Esports' qualification and competitive parity with established Group Alpha rivals, combined with insufficient evidence of JD Gaming's recent form advantage.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains fragmented tournament results but provides NO direct JD Gaming vs TEC Esports head-to-head history, recent JD Gaming form, or roster strength metrics. This severely limits confidence in either direction. CASE FOR JD GAMING (YES): All Gamers defeated TEC 2-1 on March 31, suggesting TEC is beatable by group competitors; however, this single datapoint does not establish JD Gaming as favored\u2014it only shows TEC is not dominant. CASE FOR TEC ESPORTS (NO): TEC qualified for VCT China Stage 1 Group Alpha and competed in Kickoff tournament, confirming baseline competitive status. However, the briefing provides no recent form data, win-loss record, or roster changes specific to TEC post-March 31. JD GAMING FORM UNKNOWN: Search results mention JD Gaming (JDG) in tournament structure but provide no match results, scores, or recent performance. This asymmetric data gap prevents meaningful probability anchoring. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: Current YES=57% / NO=43% reflects slight JD Gaming favoritism. Market has been volatile (7.5pp weekly swing, sharp 10pp moves on Apr 11). High volatility with low data density suggests noise rather than signal. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three matches reduce variance vs. single-map formats, making upset wins less likely and favoring stronger competitors. However, without roster/form data for either team, this does not break the tie. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams compete in same group (Group Alpha); neither has demonstrated clear dominance. Week 1 results (Apr 1-2) show mixed outcomes; strongest teams (EDG, XLG) are in Group Omega, not Alpha. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event is TODAY (~16 hours until resolution). Sharp 24-hour swings (+9.5pp, -7.5pp) suggest informed traders may have match-specific intelligence (e.g., roster news, scrim results) not in briefing. This argues for lower confidence even if probability is near 50. BASE RATE: In Valorant group-stage BO3s between evenly-matched competitors with unknown recent form, outcomes cluster near 50%. The All Gamers vs TEC result (2-1) is single-sample noise; insufficient to shift prior away from 50%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes and confidence_no both set LOW (~28 and ~26) because the briefing lacks actionable data on either team's recent performance, roster health, or head-to-head history. A coin-flip outcome (54% YES) reflects true epistemic uncertainty, not predictive strength.", "key_factor": "VCT group-stage BO3 matches show no strong predictive signal for either team without recent head-to-head data; ~50% base rate for evenly-matched competitors in preliminary rounds.", "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.45999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market is pricing this as near coin-flip (57% YES vs 43% NO), reflecting deep uncertainty about both teams. Briefing contains NO direct head-to-head history, recent JD Gaming form data, or TEC Esports recent results \u2014 critical data gaps for confident prediction. Only concrete data point: All Gamers beat TEC 2-1 on March 31, 2026 \u2014 suggests TEC is beatable but not dominant; does not clarify JD Gaming's relative strength. Both teams qualified for VCT China Stage 1 Group Alpha, indicating baseline competitive parity; this supports near-50/50 odds. Market volatility is HIGH (\u00b15-10pp moves on Apr 11) but price remains anchored near 57%, suggesting traders lack conviction either direction \u2014 consistent with apathy rather than greed or fear. NO actionable signal in briefing to justify moving probability significantly away from 50; current 57/43 split reflects rational uncertainty. Confidence scores are both LOW (38/35) because br