{"run_id": "55dd363e-412e-4b22-a0e0-30ec83a9ea27", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:13:33.149578+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1902279", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: Geek Fam ID vs RRQ Hoshi (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between Geek Fam ID and RRQ Hoshi in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 12 at 6:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Geek Fam ID\" if Geek Fam ID win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against Geek Fam ID.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T16:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T10:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 609.2728900000001, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["54056471206744506658614158435257600613256473796685090521520416122504498619766", "90856610985240323459773643986594691946708251144067505487889926680933802977792"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Match must be played to completion with a decisive winner (not canceled, tied, forfeited, or delayed >7 days). The criteria are clear and unambiguous. MATCH TIMING: Scheduled for April 12 at 6:15 AM ET (~17 hours from briefing timestamp). Imminent event with low reversal risk given time remaining. DATA VACUUM: Briefing provides zero information on team standings, recent match results, roster strength, head-to-head history, meta/patch considerations, or any performance indicators for either Geek Fam ID or RRQ Hoshi. MARKET SIGNAL: YES (Geek Fam ID) trading at 58%, NO (RRQ Hoshi) at 42%. Market has price advantage to Geek Fam ID of +16pp. This 58/42 split is the only substantive signal available. PRICE VOLATILITY: Sharp swings Apr 11 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b110.0pp, \u00b17.5pp) suggest market uncertainty or late-breaking information not captured in briefing. 24-hour volatility 4.7-5.4pp/hr indicates ongoing information flow. 7-DAY TREND: YES +4.5pp (rising), NO -4.5pp (falling). Directional confidence toward Geek Fam ID over the week, but causes unclear from briefing. ASSIGNMENT RATIONALE: In absence of team performance data, defer to market consensus (58/42). This is not a confident assessment but a necessity given data gaps. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores are low (28/27) because briefing provides no factual basis to evaluate either team's likelihood of winning. Market price is being used as proxy for aggregated expert/informed betting, not internal analysis. MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): Resolution sources and criteria are well-specified. Liquipedia is reliable for esports results. Forfeiture/cancellation risk appears low for a scheduled MPL Indonesia regular season match. CONCLUSION: Probability 58 is market-driven, not analysis-driven. Confidence in both YES and NO are equally low due to complete absence of team performance intelligence.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no team performance data, head-to-head history, roster information, or recent form metrics\u2014outcome assessment relies entirely on market price, which may embed information not visible in the briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "YES side (Geek Fam ID) is the market favorite at 58%, priced 16pp higher than NO \u2014 suggesting some market participants hold a preference for Geek Fam ID to win. However, the briefing contains NO team performance data, recent match results, head-to-head history, roster information, or form metrics for either Geek Fam ID or RRQ Hoshi. The search results explicitly state: 'no team-specific data, recent performance metrics, or head-to-head information is available' \u2014 this is a critical data gap that prevents confident analysis of either side. Market volatility is HIGH (5.4pp/hr on NO side, 4.7pp/hr on YES side) with sharp reversals on Apr 11 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b110.0pp swings), suggesting uncertainty and potential information asymmetry among traders rather than settled conviction. The 7-day trend shows YES rising +4.5pp and NO falling -4.5pp, but without causal factors identified in the briefing, this directional move may reflect emotional trading or scattered insider knowledge rather than fundamental competitive assessment. Both teams compete in MPL Indonesia Season 17 (March 27\u2013May 24, 2026) under a Double Round Robin BO3 format; neither team's standing, win-loss record, or playoff positioning is disclosed. With ~17 hours until match resolution (TODAY event), there is insufficient time for reversal of the favored side's market position through major announced catalyst \u2014 any pivot would require breaking news (injury, forfeit, etc.) not present in the briefing. The 58% price for YES reflects a modest lean toward Geek Fam ID, consistent with market consensus, but this consensus is NOT anchored to disclosed facts about either team's strength, form, or recent performance. Confidence in YES (32%) is LOW because no affirmative evidence supports Geek Fam ID's superiority \u2014 the favorite status appears to be baked into the price without supporting data, making this a 'price-following' belief rather than an evidence-based judgment. Confidence in NO (28%) is EQUALLY LOW because there is no evidence favoring RRQ Hoshi either \u2014 the underdog position is equally unsupported, leaving true competitive assessment impossible. In the absence of performance data for BOTH sides, the 58/42 split appears to be a near coin-flip with a slight directional tilt; repeating the market price (58%) as the probability_score reflects epistemic humility rather than conviction. A true 50-50 would be unjustified given the market's clear 16pp lean toward YES; deferring to market price acknowledges the pricing signal while recognizing the weak confidence foundation.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 58% reflects modest consensus favoring Geek Fam ID, but this advantage lacks evidentiary support in available data.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"age