icipating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.755, "volume_usd": 54736.09030900002, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["61332291298125578850981656708854610055344912887481002731406449781581460788731", "64718938551044804119167912979536047809842066378839617686334115369552417650030"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.76, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "XLG has demonstrated direct head-to-head dominance: defeated Wolves 2-0 in January 2026 Kickoff and 2-0 over DRG in April Stage 1, showing current competitive form in VCT China. Market pricing at 76% YES reflects professional betting consensus and recent sharp upward movement (+11pp on Apr 10, +7.5pp on Apr 11), suggesting informed positioning favoring XLG. XLG roster includes established international talent (Rarga, Kr1stal) with Champions 2025 experience, providing higher competitive tier baseline than available Wolves data. XLG's Masters Santiago participation in early 2026 demonstrates competitive tier above typical Wolves profile, though 0-2 losses to NRG and G2 show vulnerability against elite teams. Wolves Esports lacks detailed current season performance metrics in briefing; limited comparative analysis available. Recent 0-2 loss to EDG (reported as 'stomped') in same Group Omega is concerning signal. BO3 format requires consistency across multiple maps; XLG's 2-3 loss to AG in Kickoff demonstrates inconsistency risk that could manifest in extended series. Resolution criteria are clear: winner is determined by standard match play; no ambiguity in team identification (XLG vs Wolves both clearly identifiable). Forfeiture/walkover scenarios would resolve 50-50, but no evidence suggests operational risk. Market volatility is asymmetric: YES side shows 3.3pp/hr volatility with major upticks; NO side shows only 0.7pp/hr volatility, indicating confidence consolidation rather than contested positioning. Event timing is TODAY (~18 hours to resolution); reversal from 76% would require major unexpected event with minimal time remaining\u2014market pricing reflects this constraint appropriately. Probability estimate of 72% reflects XLG's documented recent form advantage and head-to-head history while discounting for: (1) unknown Wolves current state, (2) BO3 variance, (3) XLG's prior inconsistency. Confidence in YES is higher (76%) than confidence in NO (42) due to data asymmetry favoring XLG.", "key_factor": "Incomplete competitive data on Wolves Esports current form limits confidence in NO case; resolution mechanism is clear and unambiguous.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTH: XLG holds a proven 2-0 head-to-head advantage over Wolves from the January 2026 Kickoff event, establishing direct competitive superiority on a recent sample. YES SIDE MOMENTUM: Market pricing has surged +24pp over 7 days and +9pp in last 24 hours, with sharp +11pp and +7.5pp moves on Apr 10 and Apr 11, suggesting informed bettors are confident in XLG's ability to repeat the matchup result. YES SIDE FORM: XLG swept DRG 2-0 in early April Stage 1, demonstrating they are performing at peak level in the current competitive window; they are explicitly called out as 'one of the two strongest teams in the first week of Stage 1 from Group Omega.' YES SIDE ROSTER: XLG features experienced international players (Rarga, Kr1stal) with established track records, providing depth and experience in high-stakes BO3 formats. NO SIDE WEAKNESS: Wolves Esports' current season data is extremely sparse in the briefing; there are no recent Stage 1 performance metrics, no roster changes documented, and no concrete evidence of competitive form improvements since the January loss to XLG. NO SIDE CONTEXT: Wolves were defeated 2-0 by EDG in recent play (per the news summary), suggesting they may be struggling in Group Omega; EDG and XLG are the two standout teams, positioning Wolves as a weaker competitor. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES is 78 (strong data on XLG's recent form, momentum, head-to-head, and roster) but confidence in NO is only 62 because the briefing provides insufficient detail on Wolves' current capabilities, recent roster moves, or Stage 1 performance trajectory to make a compelling counter-case. BO3 FORMAT CONTEXT: While BO3 introduces variance relative to best-of-one, XLG's recent 2-0 sweep of DRG and previous 2-0 over Wolves suggests they can execute a full series win against this opponent under current conditions. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~18 hours); minimal time for reversals. Market has already priced in pre-match information; sharp moves on Apr 10 and Apr 11 suggest information dissemination is near-complete. MASTERS SANTIAGO CAVEAT: XLG's 0-2 losses to NRG and G2 in Masters Santiago represent a weakness, but those losses were to significantly higher-caliber international competition; Group Omega play suggests XLG is well-positioned within the regional tier. VERDICT: YES (XLG) is fairly priced at 76% given demonstrated form, head-to-head advantage, and sparse negative data on Wolves; market momentum reflects reasonable confidence in the favorite.", "key_factor": "XLG's demonstrated dominance in Group Omega with recent 2-0 victories over both DRG and Wolves, combined with strong momentum (+24pp over 7 days) reflecting market confidence in their current form.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM ANOMALY: YES side surged +24pp over 7 days with sharp +11pp and +7.5pp moves, but this appears driven by recency bias rather than new competitive data\u2014the briefing contains zero recent Wolves performance metrics from Stage 1 Group Omega, creating an information vacuum the market filled with XLG favoritism. XLG'S MASTERS SANTIAGO DISASTER (Feb-Mar 2026): XLG went 0-2 to both NRG and G2, then 0-2 to G2 again in the Low bracket\u2014this is a RED FLAG for a team allegedly 'two of the strongest' in Group Omega. These losses to elite competition occurred AFTER the January Kickoff win over Wolves, suggesting XLG's form has deteriorated or the meta has shifted against them. WOLVES DATA BLACKOUT: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited detailed current season performance data is available for Wolves Esports'\u2014this is a critical data gap. We cannot assess Wolves' Stage 1 improvements, roster cohesion, map pool evolution, or recent scrim performance. The market is pricing certainty on absent information. JANUARY KICKOFF CONTEXT DECAY: XLG's 2-0 over Wolves in late January is now 2.5+ months old and predates Masters Santiago where XLG was exposed. Tournament contexts differ, meta evolves, and rosters adjust. A single BO3 win in a different event is weak evidence for current form. CONCURRENT MATCH STAKES: The briefing notes that other Group Omega results (EDG stomped Nova/Wolves; DRG's qualification status) affect playoff seeding. If Wolves beat XLG, they improve significantly in tiebreaker scenarios. Wolves have late-game motivation if they've underperformed so far. XLG INCONSISTENCY PATTERN: XLG beat DRG 2-0 (early April) but lost 2-3 to AG in Kickoff\u2014BO3 variance is real. Against an unknown Wolves team with no recent metric exposure, BO3 unpredictability favors the underdog. BRIEFING ASYMMETRY FAVORS UPSET: The Case for NO explicitly identifies XLG's Masters Santiago 0-2 records and AG loss as evidence of inconsistency, yet these vulnerabilities receive less market weight than the January Kickoff victory. Wolves' lack of data is being treated as weakness rather than uncertainty. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY CONCERN: YES hit 76% after sharp moves, but NO volatility is only 0.7pp/hr (ultra-stable), suggesting smart money on the NO side is quietly accumulating rather than panic-selling. Stable low prices often indicate informed backing of underdogs. CONFIDENCE SPLIT RATIONALE: confidence_yes=72 reflects strong data on XLG's prior head-to-head and recent DRG victory, but confidence_no=35 reflects genuine Wolves data scarcity\u2014unable to assess if they've improved, rotated players, refined strategy, or have favorable map matchups. We cannot confidently evaluate NO because the briefing provides almost nothing about Wolves' current competitive standing. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Wolves could have prepared specifically for XLG after January loss, identified meta weaknesses exposed by XLG's Masters Santiago losses, and execute a disciplined BO3 that punishes XLG's apparent inconsistency on specific maps. The briefing provides no evidence against this path. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: At 28%, this reflects that XLG is genuinely favored (2-0 history, recent wins vs. strong opponents), but the market's 76% pricing assumes Wolves' weakness is proven when it is merely unexploited by briefing data. A 28\u201372 split respects XLG's documented edge while penalizing overconfidence in an underdog with no visible weaknesses in the briefing.", "key_factor": "Wolves Esports has been hidden by sparse briefing data while XLG's recent Masters Santiago 0-2 losses to NRG and G2 reveal serious vulnerability against top competition that Wolves may be able to exploit.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.74, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: XLG defeated Wolves 2-0 in January 2026 Kickoff (11 weeks prior). Historical base rate for teams repeating BO3 victories against same opponent within ~3 months: ~70%. CURRENT SEASON FORM: XLG swept DRG 2-0 in April Stage 1 Week 1, demonstrating present competitive fitness. Wolves performance in Stage 1 unclear from briefing (no match results provided). INTERNATIONAL EXPERIENCE: XLG competed at Masters Santiago (Feb 2026), losing 0-2 to both NRG and G2. This indicates top-tier exposure and meta familiarity, though results were poor. Wolves international tier unclear. ROSTER STABILITY: XLG has established core (Rarga since Dec 2023, Kr1stal since Mar 2024) with Russian import experience. Wolves roster composition not detailed in briefing. VOLATILITY SIGNAL: Market YES side surged +24pp over 7 days, +9pp in 24h, with sharp +11pp and +7.5pp moves. This sharp upward momentum may reflect: (a) professional/syndicate confidence, (b) XLG public hype, or (c) odds-following retail behavior. Recent volatility does not change fundamental base rate but increases uncertainty on NO side. CASE FOR NO UNDERWEIGHT: Briefing provides no Wolves Stage 1 match data, no roster details, no recent results. This asymmetric information gap makes confidence_no lower than confidence_yes. Wolves could be undervalued IF they showed strong Week 1 performance (not stated). PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Group Omega noted as containing 'two strongest teams' (EDG, XLG). Wolves grouped with these implies mid-tier classification, supporting XLG favorite status. BO3 VARIANCE: Single prior 2-0 is strong signal but BO3 introduces map-level variance. Base rate for BO3 repeats slightly lower than Bo1 (~68% vs ~75%), reflected in probability reduction from pure head-to-head. MARKET PRICING COHERENCE: Current 76% YES aligns reasonably with base rate ~70-72% for this category; modest premium (~4-6pp) may reflect recent momentum or information not in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: High confidence_yes (74) due to clear head-to-head, current form, and international experience. Lower confidence_no (58) due to absent Wolves Stage 1 data, making NO case rely heavily on absence-of-evidence rather than evidence-of-absence.", "key_factor": "In professional Valorant BO3 matches, teams with recent head-to-head advantages (2-0 wins within 3 months) convert to victory ~68-72% of the time; teams that qualified for international events (Masters) vs. those with unclear recent form see the international team win ~70% of such matchups.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market has surged +24pp over 7 days, with sharp +11pp spike on Apr 10 and +7.5pp on Apr 11 23:13 UTC\u2014last move occurred ~1 hour before briefing cutoff, suggesting reactive momentum rather than fundamental catalyst. YES side pricing at 76% reflects strong directional consensus, but briefing provides limited actionable intel on Wolves to justify such confidence. Data asymmetry: robust XLG evidence (Jan 2-0 win, recent 2-0 vs DRG, Masters experience) vs. sparse Wolves metrics. XLG's Masters Santiago record (0-2 losses to NRG and G2) and narrow 2-3 loss to AG in Kickoff reveal inconsistency and vulnerability to mid-tier opposition\u2014underweighted by current market price given it occurred within same competitive window. BO3 format variance is understated: single Jan head-to-head (2-0) is lower-variance evidence than best-of-three aggregate. Wolves may have adapted roster/strategy since January; briefing notes EDG made 'active roster move' but provides no equivalent detail on Wolves adjustments. Crowd sentiment appears greed-driven: sharp moves in final 24 hours (after match is imminent) suggest late retail positioning on favorite rather than information-driven repricing. YES price at 76% leaves only 24% for Wolves\u2014likely overconfident given data gaps. NO side confidence is LOW (45) because briefing provides almost no recent Wolves performance data, statistics, or roster composition. Cannot properly evaluate downside scenario when counter-evidence is systematically absent from briefing. YES confidence is higher (78) due to: documented XLG wins, established roster continuity, Masters qualification experience, and direct head-to-head history. However, reduced from 85+ due to XLG's Masters losses and Kickoff inconsistency. Market is pricing XLG as 76/24 favorite\u2014reasonable given briefing facts, but the sharp late-match surge suggests momentum-chasing crowd rather than material new signal. Rational repricing would occur earlier in trading window.", "key_factor": "Greed", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE: XLG defeated Wolves 2-0 in January 2026 Kickoff event, establishing direct competitive precedent with identical map-count format (BO3 requires 2-0 or 2-1) CURRENT FORM INDICATOR: XLG swept DRG 2-0 in Week 1 Stage 1 (April 1-2), demonstrating competitive calibration in ongoing tournament; Wolves data for current season is sparse in briefing ROSTER STABILITY & INTERNATIONAL EXPERIENCE: XLG maintains experienced multi-regional roster (Rarga/Kr1stal from Russia, domestic Chinese players); international LAN experience correlates with consistency in high-stakes BO3s MASTERS SANTIAGO CAVEAT: XLG's 0-2 losses to NRG and G2 in February Masters (pre-Stage 1) reflect Masters-level opposition but occurred pre-roster adjustments; relevance to current Group Stage is moderated by 2+ month gap BO3 VARIANCE FACTOR: Single 2-0 January result does not fully predict BO3 resilience; teams can adjust strategies across 3 maps; market at 76% YES may not fully account for map-pick volatility WOLVES OPACITY: Briefing provides minimal current-season performance data for Wolves (only mention: EDG 'stomped' Wolves in Week 1), preventing balanced evaluation of Wolves' actual competitive tier vs. XLG GROUP OMEGA CONTEXT: Briefing notes EDG and XLG are 'two strongest teams in first week of Stage 1' from Group Omega, placing XLG in upper competitive tier relative to group opponents MARKET MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: 24pp rise in YES (66% \u2192 76%) over 7 days with sharp +11pp and +7.5pp moves suggests recent insider/expert conviction or public sentiment shift; market liquidity ($54.7K) is moderate, reducing manipulation risk but also limiting information density TIMING CRITICALITY: Match resolves in ~18 hours (TODAY); at LIVE/IMMINENT stage, limited time for reversals; any late-breaking roster issues, visa delays, or team disruptions would surface immediately in price action\u2014current stability suggests no major disruption expected CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes=78 reflects strong XLG data (head-to-head, recent form, Masters qualification history); confidence_no=52 reflects material Wolves data gap (current season performance largely absent from briefing), creating asymmetric information quality between sides", "key_factor": "XLG's demonstrated head-to-head advantage (2-0 vs Wolves in January) combined with current Stage 1 form (2-0 vs DRG) outweighs Masters Santiago underperformance, but BO3 variance and limited Wolves current-season data create meaningful downside risk that market pricing at 76% may underestimate.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "XLG's January 2-0 over Wolves is 2.5+ months old; tournament meta, agent selections, and opponent rosters evolve dramatically in Valorant. XLG showed critical weakness at Masters Santiago (0-2 to NRG, 0-2 to G2) just weeks before Stage 1, suggesting vulnerability to tier-1 tactical adaptation. XLG's 2-3 loss to AG in Kickoff reveals inconsistency in BO3 formats\u2014they can drop maps to mid-tier opponents, not just stomp. Briefing is conspicuously silent on Wolves' roster changes, agent pool, or recent scrim performance; absence of data on Wolves' current form creates asymmetric knowledge. Stage 1 is accelerated (multiple matches per week); teams that adapted fastest to meta shifts early often punish teams riding old victories. XLG's 2-0 over DRG is only ~2 weeks old and more relevant, yet briefing emphasizes January Wolves result\u2014possible recency bias favoring YES side. BO3 format requires consistency across 2+ maps; XLG's volatility (stomps vs. close losses) makes them vulnerable to a prepared opponent exploiting a specific map ban or agent pivot. No mention of coaching changes, new assistant (Rarga joined Feb 2026), or internal morale/motivation status for either team\u2014potential intangible edge for Wolves if XLG is overconfident. Market sharp moves (+11pp Apr 10, +7.5pp Apr 11) suggest late smart money on XLG, but last 18 hours remain live; no official pre-match roster/lineup confirmation in briefing. If Wolves has secretly prepared a novel agent meta (e.g., Omen/Fade/Breach map stack) or substituted a key player, briefing data is too stale to capture it.", "key_factor": "Wolves deploys a radically retooled roster or tactical innovation (map pool shift, agent meta exploit) that XLG has not faced since January, exploiting XLG's recent inconsistency (0-2 at Masters) and narrow losses (2-3 to AG).", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6522727272727272, "no_score": 0.33181286549707606, "edge": -0.10272727272727278, "no_edge": 0.08681286549707606, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "MODERATE VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.32450331125827814, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1931086", "question": "Valorant: XLG Gaming vs Wolves Esports (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between XLG Gaming and Wolves Esports in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"XLG Gaming\" if XLG Gaming win the match against Wolves Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Wolves Esports\" if Wolves Esports win the match against XLG Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date