s need for tactical pivots; FUT Academy may face VET disadvantage if they must deviate from anti-Galatasaray strategies. BO3 format amplifies early-game economy discipline and agent synergy\u2014domains where REBORN's 4 consecutive map wins suggest superior fundamental execution compared to FUT Academy's single-match validation. VCL T\u00fcrkiye Birlik Stage 2 is regional Tier-2/3 circuit; roster stability and scrim infrastructure favor established teams (REBORN appears more embedded in Turkish scene). FUT Academy designation suggests academy/developmental status, typically indicating less mature macro-play. Current market price (78% YES) reflects informed betting\u2014sharp money has flowed +18.5pp in final 3 hours (Apr 12 17:13), suggesting last-minute substantive information (roster confirmation, scrim results, or odds arbitrage awareness). Map veto symmetry (Omen, Neon, Sova, Viper) reduces tactical surprise; outcome determined by execution depth rather than meta innovation\u2014axis favoring REBORN's proven 4-map consistency. Confidence_no set to 45 due to: (i) FUT Academy's minimal competitive history in briefing, (ii) no head-to-head precedent, (iii) academy team status implies higher variance in peak performance. FUT Academy could upset via unexpected agent innovation or individual mechanical outperformance, but briefing provides no evidence for this scenario.", "key_factor": "REBORN's +26 map differential from 4 consecutive wins indicates sustained team synergy and agent pool mastery under tournament pressure, while FUT Academy's single 2-0 match provides insufficient sample size to assess consistency against elite opposition in a BO3 format.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "REBORN's 2-0 record with +26 map differential spans two different opponents (ghosts, Fire Flux), demonstrating adaptability; FUT Academy's perfect 2-0 comes only vs. Galatasaray\u2014limited tactical surface. FUT Academy's +17 differential is impressive per-map but compressed into a single series; REBORN's +26 is spread across 2 series, suggesting more consistent execution under varied pressure. Market sharp move at Apr 12 17:13 UTC (+18.5pp for YES) suggests late information arrival\u2014possible scouting intelligence, practice scrim results, or roster/preparation status updates not captured in public standings. 5-day preparation gap (Apr 7\u201312) creates risk that FUT Academy over-prepares for REBORN's known meta-aligned agents (Omen, Neon, Sova, Viper) but neglects unprepared counters or off-meta pivots REBORN might deploy. Group stage format incentivizes REBORN (already 2-0) to experiment with secondary compositions; FUT Academy (1-0, high pressure to avoid early loss) may be more rigid, playing into REBORN's adaptation strength. Briefing silent on head-to-head history, scrim results, coach quality, or player morale\u2014any of these could flip momentum; lack of countervailing evidence on FUT Academy's depth limits confidence in NO to 54. REBORN's undefeated trajectory and map win streak momentum (4-0) is a strong confidence signal; however, single-elimination BO3 format means FUT Academy only needs two maps, creating non-linear upset potential. FUT Academy's selective play interpretation (prepared for stronger opponents) is speculative; equally plausible they have limited roster depth or upcoming roster changes masked by low match count.", "key_factor": "FUT Academy's minimal match exposure (1 game vs. mid-tier Galatasaray) masks critical weaknesses in high-pressure map pools or agent flexibility that REBORN's 2-game sample and diverse opponent testing exposes in direct confrontation.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6672659176029963, "no_score": 0.3253412462908012, "edge": -0.11773408239700378, "no_edge": 0.11034124629080122, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "MODERATE VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.2738853503184713, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918504", "question": "Valorant:  REBORN vs FUT Academy (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between  REBORN and FUT Academy in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B, initially scheduled for April 12 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" REBORN\" if  REBORN win the match against FUT Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FUT Academy\" if FUT Academy win the match against  REBORN.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant 