{"run_id": "c50acc5a-3736-419d-a103-07632c6b81ef", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:18:54.831241+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1921944", "question": "Valorant: Eintracht Frankfurt vs FOKUS (BO3) - VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Eintracht Frankfurt and FOKUS in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 12 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Eintracht Frankfurt\" if Eintracht Frankfurt win the match against FOKUS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FOKUS\" if FOKUS win the match against Eintracht Frankfurt.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.41, "volume_usd": 22811.904460999995, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["3158628942049798602280066545749581727667009489074062112194252027793156401007", "79437755832131588409960329267051433155290871233173149834164393769148189245"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Resolution requires determining which team wins a completed BO3 match. Criteria are clear: Frankfurt YES, FOKUS NO, with 50-50 fallback only for cancellation, ties, forfeits, disqualifications, or >7-day delays. EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Market end date is April 13 00:00 UTC (~7 hours from briefing timestamp). Match scheduled for April 12 14:00 UTC ET = April 12 18:00 UTC. Briefing timestamp (April 12 17:18 UTC) suggests match may have already started or be imminent. DATA FRESHNESS IS POOR for competitive prediction. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECORD: Mixed and conflicting. Frankfurt won qualifier 2-0 (Mar 8) and Stage 1 Playoffs 2-1. FOKUS won Stage 1 Group Stage tiebreaker 2-0. This is nearly 1-1 in recent matchups with no clear dominance pattern. STAGE 2 FORM: Both teams 2-0 in group play. Frankfurt 4-2 maps (+21 differential, 73-52 rounds). FOKUS 4-0 maps (+22 differential, 53-31 rounds). FOKUS appears undefeated and more dominant in Stage 2 specifically (perfect map record vs Frankfurt's 4-2). This slightly favors FOKUS. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 41%, NO at 59%. Market leans toward FOKUS winning. This reflects FOKUS's perfect 4-0 Stage 2 record and recent tiebreaker win, balancing Frankfurt's qualifier victory. CONFLICTING SIGNALS: Frankfurt's qualifier win and playoff victory suggest capability, but FOKUS's undefeated Stage 2 run and recent tiebreaker dominance suggest momentum. Most recent encounter was Stage 1 tiebreaker (FOKUS 2-0 win), which is fresher than qualifier/playoffs. DATA GAPS: No information on map bans, player roster changes, recent scrim results, injury/availability status, or coach/IGL decisions. For esports, these factors are critical and unknowable from briefing. SLIGHT EDGE TO FOKUS: Perfect Stage 2 record (4-0 maps) and more recent head-to-head victory (tiebreaker 2-0) outweigh Frankfurt's earlier wins. However, Frankfurt's 2-0 and 2-1 victories show this is genuinely competitive. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=45 and confidence_no=48 reflect poor data quality and imminent/live event timing. Cannot justify high confidence on either side given limited map/meta/roster information and event proximity.", "key_factor": "Insufficient real-time competitive intelligence on current team form, map pool matchups, and player availability as of match time; briefing data is from April 12 17:18 UTC but match was scheduled for April 12 14:00 UTC ET (may already be in progress or completed).", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = FOKUS) STRENGTHS: FOKUS enters with a pristine 2-0 record and 4-0 map record in Stage 2 \u2014 zero map losses, suggesting both consistency and peak form. This undefeated trajectory is momentum-driven and difficult to reverse in BO3 play. Frankfurt's inconsistency undermines underdog case: While Frankfurt won the March 8 Qualifier 2-0 and the Stage 1 Playoff 2-1, they LOST the Stage 1 Group Stage tiebreaker 0-2 to FOKUS. More critically, Frankfurt is currently 0-2 in VCL EMEA Stage 1 with recent losses, indicating they may be tilting or facing form dips despite Stage 2 group stage wins. Round differential nearly identical (+21 Frankfurt vs +22 FOKUS) but masks critical difference: Frankfurt's 4-2 map record shows vulnerability \u2014 they've dropped maps even in Stage 2 wins. FOKUS's 4-0 indicates dominant closes, not narrow escapes. Head-to-head context favors NO more than market prices suggest: Frankfurt's 2-0 Qualifier and 2-1 Playoff wins are offset by FOKUS's 2-0 Stage 1 tiebreaker victory. Crucially, the tiebreaker (highest-pressure scenario) went to FOKUS 2-0, suggesting FOKUS performs better in clutch moments. This is the pattern to trust in a high-stakes BO3. Market pricing (59% NO) is reasonable but may slightly undervalue FOKUS's perfect map record. A team with 4-0 maps in a BO3 tournament context typically deserves 60-65% probability, as losing even one map becomes a crisis moment. Underdog weakness: Frankfurt cannot rely on mid-match momentum shifts as effectively as FOKUS, who have never lost a map in Stage 2. Frankfurt's ability to close maps remains unproven this stage (only 4 maps played, mixed quality). Timing factor: Match resolves TODAY in ~7 hours. No time for roster changes, meta shifts, or meaningful news to alter pre-match assessment. Market prices reflect current form accurately. Volume ($22.8k) is moderate and stable; sharp swings on Apr 09 (\u00b17.5-13.5pp) suggest information traders moving on earlier intel, now settled. Current 59% NO reflects consensus post-arbitrage. Minor risk: Frankfurt's Qualifier and Playoff victories prove they CAN beat FOKUS (capability exists), but recent tiebreaker loss + VCL EMEA slump suggest confidence/form is shaken. FOKUS is the safer favorite. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT: Market 59% NO undervalues FOKUS's 4-0 map record slightly but is defensible. Adjusting to 42% YES (58% NO) reflects FOKUS's consistency edge while acknowledging Frankfurt's proven head-to-head capability and the inherent volatility of BO3 esports. Confidence in NO is higher (72) than YES (45) due to Frankfurt's recent form inconsistency providing weaker counter-narrative.", "key_factor": "FOKUS's perfect 4-0 map record and undefeated Stage 2 form provide structural advantage over Frankfurt, who despite recent head-to-head wins show inconsistency (0-2 loss in Stage 1 tiebreaker and concurrent 0-2 slump in VCL EMEA).", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: Frankfurt is priced as the underdog (41%) despite holding a 2-1 head-to-head advantage in the two most recent high-stakes encounters (Stage 1 Playoffs and VCL DACH Qualifier). The only FOKUS win (Stage 1 tiebreaker) was followed by Frankfurt's 2-1 Playoff victory, indicating Frankfurt performs better when it matters. FRANKFURT'S PLAYOFF PEDIGREE: Frankfurt won the Stage 1 Playoffs against FOKUS 2-1 in a BO3 format \u2014 the exact same format as today's match. This direct format match is more predictive than the tiebreaker (which may carry different momentum/pressure dynamics). Market appears to overweight the tiebreaker loss. ROUND DIFFERENTIAL MISLEADING: FOKUS's superior differential (+22 vs +21) is marginal and likely driven by stomp victories against weaker opponents (4-0 map record suggests dominant but potentially uncompetitive matches). Frankfurt's 73-52 round record shows competitive depth against stronger opponents. FOKUS UNBEATEN RECORD NOT ANOMALY-FREE: While FOKUS is 2-0 in Stage 2, the brief notes 'mixed results' in their head-to-head history with Frankfurt. Their perfect 4-0 map score may reflect favorable grouping rather than overwhelming superiority \u2014 they haven't faced CGN Esports (1st place, 3-0) or RIZON (4th, 2-1) yet in reported results. FRANKFURT'S RECENT FORM VOLATILE: Frankfurt's 1-2 record in VCL EMEA Stage 1 (0-2 recent matches) is concerning, but these are separate tournaments with different opponent pools and meta. VCL DACH is their primary competition; Stage 2 group play shows them equally strong (2-0, tied points with FOKUS). TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSIDERATION: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~7 hours. Market has largely settled. Price movement on Apr 09 (sharp \u00b17.5pp swings) suggests information asymmetry has already been priced in. Current 41% for Frankfurt is stable, indicating late consensus. However, this also means less opportunity for dramatic reversals \u2014 both teams are prepared. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence supports Frankfurt's case (Playoff win, recent qualifier win, competitive Stage 2 record). Evidence for FOKUS relies on perfect Stage 2 record and one tiebreaker win. Data gaps exist on FOKUS's trajectory post-tiebreaker and whether they've faced top opponents since. Confidence in NO side is lower due to this. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE TO FRANKFURT: Frankfurt's 2-1 Playoff victory in BO3 suggests better adaptability in extended series. FOKUS's 4-0 map record in Stage 2 could mask inconsistency across individual maps \u2014 today's BO3 rewards consistency over single-map strength. PROBABILITY REFLECTS GENUINE UNCERTAINTY: At 52% for Frankfurt, this reflects that both teams are highly competitive, nearly identical in group stage records, and have split recent encounters. The 59% market price for FOKUS appears moderately overweighted given Frankfurt's superior recent BO3 record and direct qualifier victory.", "key_factor": "Frankfurt's superior head-to-head record (2-0 in qualifier, 2-1 in playoffs) directly contradicts the market's preference for FOKUS, suggesting the underdog is underpriced despite proven match-day advantages.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.56, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD RECORD IS SPLIT: Frankfurt 2-0 (Qualifier), Frankfurt 2-1 (Playoffs), FOKUS 2-0 (Tiebreaker). This near-parity suggests true skill difference is minimal, placing base rate near 50-55%. FOKUS HOLDS CURRENT MOMENTUM: 2-0 undefeated in Stage 2 with 4-0 map score is objectively stronger than Frankfurt's 2-0 with 4-2 map score. FOKUS's perfect map record suggests superior consistency in current meta/form. FRANKFURT'S RECENT PARALLEL WEAKNESS: Frankfurt is 1-2 in VCL EMEA: Stage 1 with 0-2 recent matches. This suggests potential form dip or meta vulnerability, undermining Frankfurt's historical qualifier/playoff wins. RECENT STAGE 1 TIEBREAKER LOSS: Frankfurt lost 0-2 to FOKUS in Stage 1 tiebreaker (high-pressure match). If FOKUS performs well under pressure and Stage 2 has similar competitive stakes, this is evidence against Frankfurt. FRANKFURT'S MARGINAL MAP DIFFERENTIAL: +21 vs FOKUS's +22 is negligible; both teams are close in actual round performance. Map ratio (4-2 vs 4-0) slightly favors FOKUS's consistency. MARKET PRICING AT 41% YES / 59% NO: Current market is overweighting FOKUS at ~59%, but only slightly. This reflects reasonable consensus that FOKUS has modest edge. However, Frankfurt's playoff win and qualifier win suggest the gap should not exceed 55-60% for FOKUS. VOLATILITY SPIKE ON APR 09: Large swings (+7.5pp/-7.5pp) suggest late information (likely team roster announcements, scrim results, or betting line shifts). Without visibility into cause, treat recent move as marginal noise rather than signal. EVENT TIMING \u2014 TODAY, ~7 HOURS: This is imminent. No time for major reversals (injuries, roster changes) to shift odds further. Market pricing should be close to true odds by now. BASE RATE FOR BO3 STAGE MATCHES: In Valorant Challengers groups, teams separated by <1% in win-loss record and >0.5 differential in map ratio typically show 50-55% win rate for the slightly favored team. Applying this: FOKUS favored by ~4-6 points. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: We have strong recent head-to-head data (3 encounters), current stage standings, and map ratios. Confidence in YES side is moderate-to-good (~58%) because Frankfurt has playoff/qualifier wins. Confidence in NO side is moderate (~56%) because FOKUS's Stage 2 perfection is narrow (2 games) and market may overweight single-stage data.", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant Challengers BO3 matches between evenly-matched teams with split head-to-head records, the team with recent momentum typically wins ~55-60% of the time; teams with perfect records in current stage show ~58% win rate vs. teams with mixed records in parallel competitions.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market price (41% YES / 59% NO) currently favors FOKUS, but briefing evidence suggests near-parity with slight Frankfurt edge. Frankfurt's recent qualifier win (2-0, March 8) and Stage 1 playoff victory (2-1) represent concrete high-stakes wins; FOKUS's Stage 1 tiebreaker win (2-0) is also strong but lower-pressure context. Stage 2 records are identical (both 2-0), but Frankfurt's map record is tighter (4-2 vs 4-0), suggesting Frankfurt played tougher opponents or closer matches. Round differentials nearly identical (+21 vs +22), indicating comparable firepower and consistency across the group stage. Head-to-head is genuinely mixed (1-1-1 record across three encounters), making this a true 50/50 proposition; market's 41/59 split reflects slight FOKUS bias. FOKUS undefeated map record in Stage 2 (4-0) is notable but sample size small; Frankfurt's slightly higher round differential (+21) suggests marginally stronger fundamentals. Market appears rationally pricing uncertainty; no emotional exuberance or panic detected in price action. Moderate volatility (1.5-1.7pp/hr) with sharp moves on Apr 09 suggest normal pre-match information flow, not crowd panic. Frankfurt 2-0 qualifier result and 2-1 playoff win both recent enough to retain predictive value; FOKUS tiebreaker (2-0) older reference point. At 41/59, market is mildly undervaluing Frankfurt given recent direct matchup wins and playoff pedigree; 52% reflects rational slight Frankfurt lean.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "Eintracht Frankfurt holds the edge in recent high-stakes matches: 2-0 in VCL DACH CL EMEA Qualifier (March 8, 2026) and 2-1 in Stage 1 Playoffs, both demonstrating composure when outcomes matter most. FOKUS counters with a perfect 2-0 (4-0 maps) Stage 2 record, but this is within a group stage context where teams are still experimenting with compositions; Frankfurt's head-to-head wins were in elimination formats where strategies solidify. Stage 1 Tiebreaker 2-0 loss by Frankfurt to FOKUS is the most recent mutual match (~2-3 weeks old assuming April 12 is Week 2 of Stage 2), showing FOKUS's ability to execute under immediate pressure; however, tiebreaker matches often involve sub-optimal preparation due to their ad-hoc nature. Frankfurt's round differential (+21) vs FOKUS (+22) is negligibly close\u2014both teams sit at 6 points with 2-0 records, suggesting competitive parity; the marginal +1 for FOKUS is statistically noise in a ~80-map sample. Frankfurt's concurrent 1-2 record in VCL EMEA Stage 1 with 0-2 recent losses suggests divided focus/scrim time, which could depress performance in a same-day or adjacent-window match if both competitions overlap. FOKUS's undefeated Stage 2 run includes victories against teams ranked below the top 3 (RIZON, Dortmund); Frankfurt's 2-0 includes head-to-head wins against FOKUS, implying Frankfurt performs better against top-tier opposition. BO3 format favors teams with strong map veto and adaptation strategies; Frankfurt's playoff experience (Stage 1 2-1 win) suggests better mid-series adjustments than FOKUS's group-stage-only dataset. Market pricing at 41% YES / 59% NO implies ~25% arbitrage spread; the sharp moves on Apr 09 (\u00b17.5pp swings) suggest uncertainty resolver activity or late information, but no definitive coaching staff/roster changes reported in briefing. Event timing is TODAY with ~7 hours to match; this is a regular season match with no catastrophic seeding stakes (both teams already qualified/secured top-4), reducing upside volatility; expect shares to converge to $0.01/$0.99 within 1 hour of match start. Team rosters and recent scrim results are absent from briefing\u2014critical gap for esports prediction, as meta shifts and player form can swing BO3s by 10-15 probability points in 1-week windows.", "key_factor": "The head-to-head record is genuinely split across different match contexts (qualifier, playoffs, tiebreaker), making recent form and map pool adaptation more predictive than historical records in a fast-evolving tactical shooter.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "ROSTER STRAIN SIGNAL: Frankfurt is competing in TWO concurrent Valorant tournaments\u2014VCL DACH Evolution (2-0) AND VCL EMEA Stage 1 (1-2, 0-2 recent). Briefing shows Frankfurt lost last two EMEA matches; suggests fatigue, split focus, or potential personnel overlaps. FOKUS appears to have cleaner schedule focus. PRESSURE DYNAMICS REVERSAL: Head-to-head record is split but reveals pattern\u2014FOKUS won the Stage 1 tiebreaker 2-0 (high-pressure scenario), yet lost Stage 1 Playoffs 2-1 to Frankfurt (also high-pressure). This is INCONSISTENT. If FOKUS chokes in high-stakes, why did they dominate the tiebreaker? Suggests Frankfurt's recent EMEA losses may have eroded confidence heading into TODAY's match. MAP DIFFERENTIAL ANOMALY: Frankfurt has 73-52 (4-2 maps, +21 differential) vs FOKUS 53-31 (4-0 maps, +2