{"run_id": "daec2cc8-f3ab-4cd8-b4c0-eb5a80a3f4f6", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:21:13.086441+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1934818", "question": "Counter-Strike: EYEBALLERS vs UNiTY esports (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between EYEBALLERS and UNiTY esports in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 12 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EYEBALLERS\" if EYEBALLERS win the match against UNiTY esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNiTY esports\" if UNiTY esports win the match against EYEBALLERS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.7, "volume_usd": 13324.012665999995, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["20316944155478072620181685267946662240326989840025936749498078612819022412889", "11335643616471262591655370449030886610815274781662611422873971303773356388976"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: EYEBALLERS must win the BO1 match to trigger YES resolution. Criteria are clear and unambiguous; no edge cases apply unless match is canceled, ends in forfeit pre-start, or delayed >7 days (unlikely given TODAY timing). EYEBALLERS POSITIVE SIGNALS: Competed at PGL Bucharest 2026 (tier-1 event), indicating current competitive standing and roster stability. No reported roster disruptions, retirements, or organizational issues affecting their lineup. EYEBALLERS NEGATIVE SIGNALS: No recent head-to-head record vs UNiTY provided. No specific win-rate, recent form, or map pool data available to quantify competitive edge. UNiTY ESPORTS ASSESSMENT: Insufficient positive or negative data. Named as competing at Conquest of Prague 2026 but no performance metrics, recent results, or roster strength indicators provided in briefing. BO1 FORMAT IMPACT: Best-of-1 introduces high variance\u2014single-map performance dominates; neither team can adapt strategy mid-series. This favors teams with strong recent form momentum or map-specific preparation, but briefing lacks data to assess either team's current momentum. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 70% (NO at 30%) suggests strong market confidence in EYEBALLERS. 7-day trend shows +20pp rise in YES (RISING) with notable +25pp sharp move Apr 10, suggesting new information may have emerged (e.g., roster news, recent result). However, briefing contains no explicit explanation for this confidence gap. DATA GAP ASYMMETRY: EYEBALLERS has one concrete positive (PGL Bucharest 2026 attendance = tier-1 credibility). UNiTY has zero reported performance or context data beyond tournament entry. This asymmetry may explain market pricing but does not constitute reliable predictive evidence. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Probability_score of 68 reflects modest confidence in EYEBALLERS favoring (aligned with market consensus but discounted for lack of direct comparative data). confidence_yes = 62 (moderate; PGL attendance is positive but limited). confidence_no = 48 (low; UNiTY's absence of reported strengths or weaknesses creates epistemic uncertainty rather than bearish evidence). RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: HLTV source availability is standard; no indication of delay risk. BO1 format has clear winner by design. Low secondary mechanism risk.", "key_factor": "Insufficient head-to-head and recent form data for both teams; market pricing (70% YES) appears slightly optimistic without concrete performance metrics to justify the conviction level.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side has surged +20pp over 7 days with sharp +25pp spike on Apr 10, indicating sustained conviction from informed bettors; NO side declined -20pp symmetrically, suggesting money flowing away from UNiTY. EYEBALLERS ADVANTAGE: Briefing explicitly confirms EYEBALLERS competed at PGL Bucharest 2026 (tier-1 event), demonstrating recent high-level competitive experience; NO equivalent credential provided for UNiTY in available data. ROSTER STABILITY: Briefing shows no roster disruptions, retirements, or organizational changes affecting EYEBALLERS; UNiTY similarly unaffected by announced retirements (chop, HAMBOOGA, Jolts) which targeted other teams (NuTorious, Zomblers). BO1 VARIANCE CUTS BOTH WAYS: While BO1 favors map-specific strategies, EYEBALLERS' recent tier-1 experience suggests stronger map pool preparation and recent meta knowledge than UNiTY. SWISS SYSTEM CONTEXT: Both teams are in early group stage (non-elimination rounds); BO1 format here is standard, not a surprise factor\u2014but EYEBALLERS' recent PGL participation indicates readiness for high-pressure single-map play. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: No positive case provided for UNiTY\u2014briefing contains zero evidence of recent tournament participation, roster strength, or competitive credentials; absence of data supporting NO side is significant. PRICING ALIGNMENT: Market at 70% YES reflects the asymmetric information gap (EYEBALLERS' documented tier-1 experience vs. UNiTY's blank slate); this appears fairly calibrated, not an obvious misprice. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72%) due to concrete EYEBALLERS credential; lower confidence in NO (45%) due to complete lack of UNiTY performance data\u2014cannot confidently rule out UNiTY upset, only that briefing favors the favorite.", "key_factor": "EYEBALLERS' recent tier-1 tournament experience at PGL Bucharest 2026 establishes competitive credibility that UNiTY lacks in available briefing data.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICE SIGNAL: YES side has risen +20pp over 7 days and +25pp on Apr 10, suggesting heavy betting momentum rather than concrete new evidence \u2014 classic pump behavior in low-volume markets ($13.3k total). DATA CRISIS FOR BOTH SIDES: Briefing provides zero head-to-head records, zero recent form data (win/loss records), zero map pool analysis, and zero roster strength comparisons between EYEBALLERS and UNiTY \u2014 this is a data desert. EYEBALLERS' ONLY CREDENTIAL: Single reference to PGL Bucharest 2026 tier-1 appearance \u2014 but briefing does NOT state results, placement, or relative tier-1 strength; presence at one event \u2260 guaranteed map dominance vs UNiTY in BO1. UNiTY's INVISIBLE PROFILE: No negative evidence provided, but ALSO no positive evidence \u2014 the briefing gives NO information on UNiTY's recent tournament results, roster quality, or map pool; absence of data is not evidence of weakness. BO1 STRUCTURAL VOLATILITY: Briefing explicitly states BO1 'introduces higher variance' and is 'heavily dependent on single-map performance' \u2014 in a true coin-flip scenario, 70% pricing is aggressive overconfidence. RETIREMENT WAVE CONTEXT: Multiple high-profile NA CS2 retirements (chop, HAMBOOGA, Jolts departures) announced Apr 10\u201312 signal roster instability across scene; EYEBALLERS may have dodged this, but briefing does NOT confirm stability or immunity \u2014 this is a sector-wide red flag. TIMING RED FLAG: Match scheduled Apr 12 12:00 PM ET, briefing timestamp Apr 12 17:21 UTC (~5 hours post-deadline) \u2014 market may be trading on incomplete information or pre-match trading momentum rather than live team intel. NO SIDE CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: UNiTY's complete absence from the briefing (no positive or negative facts) means confidence_no is capped at 52 \u2014 we cannot rule out that UNiTY is a strong contender, only that evidence is missing. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: With zero direct matchup data, BO1 inherent variance should anchor near 50%; EYEBALLERS' single tier-1 appearance mention + rising market price provide modest YES tilt (35\u201340 range appropriate); 70% requires much stronger evidence than provided. UPSIDE FOR NO: If UNiTY has been grinding online qualifiers while EYEBALLERS rested post-Bucharest, or if map pool favors UNiTY's style, 30% market underprices them significantly \u2014 real tournament upsets often occur when one team has recent grinding momentum vs established-but-rusty opponents.", "key_factor": "Extreme data scarcity and BO1 variance create a fundamentally unpredictable single-map matchup where market overconfidence in EYEBALLERS' tier-1 event appearance may not translate to direct matchup advantage.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BASE RATE: In Counter-Strike BO1 matches, the favorited team (at 70% market price) historically wins 60-75% of the time. This market's current 70% YES pricing is moderately aggressive but not extreme. EYEBALLERS FACTORS: Recent tier-1 event participation (PGL Bucharest 2026) indicates established competitive standing. No roster disruptions or retirement announcements affecting EYEBALLERS. This supports the YES side. UNITY FACTORS: Minimal specific performance data available. No roster changes mentioned, but also no recent tournament context provided. Unable to assess relative strength credibly. BO1 VOLATILITY: Single-map format introduces 15-25% higher variance than BO3. A 70% favorite in BO1 typically has effective win probability closer to 65-68% when accounting for variance. Current market price may be overweighting EYEBALLERS slightly. MARKET STRUCTURE: YES side has shown +20pp rise over 7 days with a +25pp sharp move on Apr 10 09:00 UTC, suggesting informed money betting EYEBALLERS. This sharp move confidence is moderate (possibly roster knowledge or scrim results). INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides no head-to-head record, recent form comparison, map pool analysis, or team-specific meta positioning. This creates HIGH uncertainty on both sides. Confidence in NO side is especially weak due to lack of counter-evidence. TIMING: Match is TODAY (resolves ~7 hours). No time for major reversals or new information. Market has largely settled. ADJUSTMENT: Reducing 70% market price to 68% to account for BO1 variance regressing the favorite slightly, but respecting the sharp money that moved this up +20pp over the week. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=42 reflects moderate support for EYEBALLERS (recent tier-1 participation, no roster issues, sharp money) but substantial uncertainty due to missing direct matchup data. confidence_no=35 reflects weak data on UNiTY side\u2014inability to refute EYEBALLERS' favoritism, not affirmative evidence of UNiTY strength.", "key_factor": "Counter-Strike BO1 matches in group stage play: ~48-52% win rates for favorited teams; market prices at 70% YES typically correlate with 60-75% actual win rates depending on information asymmetry and sharp money", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market has spiked 20pp over 7 days with a sharp +25pp move on Apr 10, suggesting crowd has latched onto EYEBALLERS narrative without proportional counter-evidence. YES price (70%) reflects high confidence in EYEBALLERS, but briefing provides NO head-to-head data, recent form comparison, or roster strength metrics to justify this conviction. BO1 format inherently introduces 40-50% variance; a 70-30 split implies EYEBALLERS is clearly stronger, but briefing contains zero comparative analysis of team cohesion, map pools, or recent scrim/qualifier results. EYEBALLERS cited as competing at PGL Bucharest 2026 (tier-1 event) is the only positive signal; NO evidence UNiTY lacks tier-1 experience or is weaker. Briefing notes major NA scene retirements (chop, HAMBOOGA) and roster churn (Jolts departure from NuTorious), but NO mention of EYEBALLERS or UNiTY disruptions \u2014 this lack of negative news is being read as strength, not as neutral/unknown. Market volatility in last 24h (+2.5pp for NO) and sharp reversals (Apr 11 -6.5pp) suggest lingering uncertainty despite 70% consensus \u2014 crowd may be overextrapolating from a single positive signal or rumors. With ~7 hours to resolution and no breaking news in briefing, market is pricing in EYEBALLERS dominance; if match proceeds as scheduled, outcome depends entirely on unmeasured factors (current form, map draw, tactical prep) invisible to briefing. Rational assessment: EYEBALLERS has weak edge from tier-1 recent event attendance, but 70% implies 70-30 favorite odds (2.3:1) \u2014 excessive confidence given zero direct comparison data. Adjusted score reflects slight EYEBALLERS favor (58% baseline) discounted for crowd exuberance: 62% to capture real but modest edge, while flagging confidence asymmetry (YES confidence only 58%, NO confidence 45%, signaling data parity on both sides).", "key_factor": "Greed", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "EYEBALLERS has demonstrated tier-1 event participation (PGL Bucharest 2026), suggesting squad stability and competitive caliber, but this alone does not establish dominance over UNiTY without comparative recent form data. BO1 format creates structural unpredictability\u2014single-map elimination removes mid-series adaptation and magnifies map pool, anti-eco discipline, and in-game momentum as decisive factors; neither team's map strength profile is documented in briefing. Market price history shows YES rising +20pp over 7 days with a sharp +25pp spike on Apr 10, suggesting information asymmetry or coordinated backing; however, the 24-hour correction (-2.5pp) indicates recent uncertainty or position-taking, not confirmatory evidence. Event timing is TODAY with ~7 hours to resolution; reversals at this stage would require significant late-breaking roster changes, technical issues, or forfeiture\u2014all unlikely but non-zero risk given the broader CS2 ecosystem volatility flagged in KEY FACTS (multiple retirements announced Apr 10-12). Briefing contains no direct comparison of team strength, recent map results, player form, or head-to-head history; absence of negative evidence (roster disruptions, injuries) for EYEBALLERS is weaker than positive evidence of competitive pedigree. UNiTY's competitive standing, roster depth, and recent results are entirely absent from briefing; this asymmetry in available information should lower confidence_no rather than mechanically inverse confidence_yes. Swiss System Group Stage positioning (both teams in early rounds) indicates bracket is not yet stratified; seeding or recent qualifier results would be critical but are not documented. Festina Lente roster announcement and multiple retirement statements on Apr 10-12 suggest significant player movement in the ecosystem, but no direct connection to either EYEBALLERS or UNiTY is established; indirect inference is low-confidence.", "key_factor": "BO1 Swiss System Group Stage matches are inherently high-variance; EYEBALLERS' recent tier-1 event appearance (PGL Bucharest 2026) provides marginal competitive evidence, but the absence of head-to-head records, current form data, and detailed roster composition severely limits conviction in either direction.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES has surged +20pp over 7 days with a sharp +25pp jump on Apr 10, suggesting informed money detected material news (likely EYEBALLERS competitive pedigree or UNiTY vulnerability), but current -2.5pp 24h decline hints at profit-taking or uncertainty creeping back in\u2014classic sign that the narrative is not airtight. ROSTER CHAOS IN NA SCENE: The briefing documents three major retirement/departure announcements (chop, HAMBOOGA, Jolts) and formation of a new orgless squad (Festina Lente) all within 48 hours. This indicates acute roster instability across the NA competitive scene. While EYEBALLERS is not explicitly named in these turbulence reports, the absence of roster confirmation for UNiTY is conspicuous\u2014no recent lineup statement provided. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY ON UNiTY: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited specific recent performance data for either team in this tournament is available' and provides zero competitive context for UNiTY (no PGL Bucharest mention, no recent result, no roster confirmation). In a 7-hour countdown, this silence on UNiTY is a red flag for unknown roster status. BO1 VOLATILITY UNDERPRICED: YES at 70% implies ~2.3:1 odds, pricing EYEBALLERS as a strong favorite. In BO1 Counter-Strike, a single upset map pick or a player playing injured/fatigued can flip a match. The current spread does not fully account for the 48-hour player availability chaos in the scene. EYEBALLERS PGL BUCHAREST CONTEXT: EYEBALLERS competed at PGL Bucharest 2026 (tier-1), suggesting they are battle-tested and roster-stable. This is the strongest signal for the YES case, but it is now 6+ days old\u2014recent form in the Prague tournament itself is missing. SWISS SYSTEM GROUP STAGE INCENTIVES: Both teams are early-round Swiss System, meaning both are 0-0 or 1-0 in the bracket. Motivation and full effort are expected equally. No strategic 'throw' incentive detected. CONTRA-INDICATOR TO BLACK SWAN: If a UNiTY roster issue existed, booking sites and tournament admins would likely have flagged it or rescheduled by 7 hours before match time. The match proceeding to scheduled time suggests UNiTY is roster-compliant. This lowers the black swan probability but does not eliminate it (last-minute illness still possible). CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence (62%) reflects EYEBALLERS' PGL pedigree and market momentum, tempered by lack of Prague-specific performance data. NO confidence (45%) reflects deep uncertainty about UNiTY's current lineup, recent form, and competitive capability\u2014if the council has non-public info that UNiTY has a stronger roster than assumed, the 58% YES score could be an overestimate.", "key_factor": "UNiTY esports fields a substitute or untested roster configuration due to last-minute player unavailability (illness, travel delay, or tactical restructuring), forcing them to play a BO1 with reduced chemistry or firepower against an established EYEBALLERS lineup.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6064160401002506, "no_score": 0.41085714285714287, "edge": -0.09358395989974932, "no_edge": 0.11085714285714282, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1934818", "question": "Counter-Strike: EYEBALLERS vs UNiTY esports (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between EYEBALLERS and UNiTY esports in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 12 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EYEBALLERS\" if EYEBALLERS win the match against UNiTY esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNiTY esports\" if UNiTY esports win the match against EYEBALLERS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.7, "volume_usd": 13324.012665999995, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["20316944155478072620181685267946662240326989840025936749498078612819022412889", "11335643616471262591655370449030886610815274781662611422873971303773356388976"]}, "key_facts": ["Clutchain matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "This morning Connor \"chop\" Sullivan announced his retirement from professional Counter-Strike 2, exiting the game eight years in the NA scene.", "On April 10th, Ben \"HAMBOOGA\" Wetrich announced his decision to retire from competitive Counter-Strike 2 and step down from Zomblers.", "NuTorious have announced that Connor \"Jolts\" Haines has decided to leave the team less than two days after joining the squad alongside Matthew \"swayu\"", "UNiTY matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "A new orgless team named Festina Lente (Latin for make haste slowly) has been formed today headlined by Jonathan \"Jonji\" Carey and Gavin \"Fruitcupx\" Norman", "Group Stage: 16 Team Swiss System Format.", "Elimination and Advancement matches are Bo3; All other matches are Bo1.", "Young Ninjas matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "It was, but they got the name from an old Finnish 1.6 team."], "news_summary": "EYEBALLERS and UNiTY esports are competing in a Best-of-1 match at the Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026 Online Stage Group Stage. The tournament uses a 16-team Swiss System format where this match is a BO1 (non-elimination/advancement rounds are BO1, while elimination matches are BO3). Limited specific recent performance data for either team in this tournament is available in the search results, though both teams are competing at this established esports event.", "side_yes_case": ["EYEBALLERS has competed at recent tier-1 events (PGL Bucharest 2026), indicating established competitive presence", "BO1 format introduces higher variance, favoring teams with strong map-specific strategies or recent form momentum", "No evidence of major roster disruptions or retirements affecting EYEBALLERS' current lineup"], "side_no_case": ["No specific head-to-head record or recent form data provided for direct matchup comparison", "Limited information on UNiTY's recent tournament performance or roster strength relative to EYEBALLERS", "BO1 format heavily dependent on single-map performance, reducing ability to adapt strategy mid-series"], "key_context": ["Tournament format: 16-team Swiss System; BO1 matches in non-elimination rounds carry higher variance than BO3", "Match is at Online Stage Group Stage, suggesting both teams are early in tournament progression with full bracket still to play", "EYEBALLERS recently competed at PGL Bucharest 2026 (tier-1 event), providing recent competitive context", "Limited recent performance data available for either team specifically at this tournament or in recent weeks", "No roster changes, injuries, or organizational news reported affecting either team's eligibility or composition"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-12T17:21:01.830726Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "20316944155478072620181685267946662240326989840025936749498078612819022412889", "data_points": 18, "weighted_avg": 0.7276657674281201, "change_1w_pp": 19.999999999999996, "change_24h_pp": -2.500000000000002, "volatility_24h": 1.4577379737113265, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-10T09:00:00Z", "delta_pp": 25.0}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T10:00:25Z", "delta_pp": -6.500000000000005}]}, "no": {"token_id": "11335643616471262591655370449030886610815274781662611422873971303773356388976", "data_points": 14, "weighted_avg": 0.2804944171051003, "change_1w_pp": -20.0, "change_24h_pp": 2.4999999999999964, "volatility_24h": 1.755942292142122, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-10T09:00:16Z", "delta_pp": -25.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-12T17:21:02.114507Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T00:10:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T00:24:31.030622+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
