nal fade or crowd panic about LOS. Data freshness (Apr 12 17:21 UTC) is recent; event resolves Apr 13 01:00 UTC (~8 hours away). Market is live/imminent, low time for reversal. Briefing contains no recent injury reports, roster changes, or meta shifts that would explain market skepticism of LOS favorite status. 42% YES odds imply LOUD is ~38% better than raw standings suggest \u2014 no evidence in briefing supports this valuation gap. Rational apathy hypothesis: market may be underreacting to LOS's objective strength (2-0, 2nd place) and overweighting generic BO3 underdog narrative.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "LOS demonstrably superior: 2-0 (1-1) record vs LOUD 1-1 (2-2), +4 map differential advantage, 2nd place seeding vs 4th place Recent competitive evidence: LOS defeated FURIA in CBLOL Cup 2026 playoffs (demonstrating tournament-level performance); LOUD struggling in early regular season days BO3 format dynamics: While BO3 increases upset probability vs BO1, LOS's map advantage means LOUD requires 2-1 comeback from deficit\u2014possible but structurally less likely LOUD structural weakness: 1-1 split record and tied-4th placement indicate inconsistency; 2-2 overall spread across events shows competitive ceiling below LOS Market pricing (42% YES / 58% NO) appears slight undervalue of LOS\u2014suggests market may be overcorrecting for BO3 adaptability narrative Market volatility spike (Apr 09: \u00b112pp swings, Apr 11: -5.5pp) indicates uncertainty typical of regional esports; sharp moves suggest news events (roster changes, recent matches) but briefing lacks specifics Data freshness concern: Briefing timestamp 2026-04-12 17:21 UTC with match ~8 hours away; standings may not reflect last-minute roster or meta shifts in CBLOL Resolution risk minimal: Official gol.gg source clear; tie/forfeit scenarios low probability in established regional format Confidence asymmetry justified: Strong YES confidence (72) backed by standings, recent wins, map differential; lower NO confidence (55) reflects lack of specific LOUD momentum data or meta counters to LOS composition", "key_factor": "LOS's 2-0 regular season record with +4 map differential and 2nd place standing represents a structural advantage in BO3 format, but LOUD's resilience across split formats and mid-table positioning (tied 4th) suggests sufficient mechanical parity that a 62-38 split correctly reflects LOS dominance while respecting BO3 upset potential.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL ANOMALY: YES (LOS) side fell 9pp over 7 days despite dominant stats (2-0, +3 differential, 2nd place). Sharp volatility on Apr 09 (+6.5pp then -12.0pp) suggests late-game information arrival that market has priced in but briefing does not capture. BRIEFING DATA GAPS: No player-level roster information, no recent scrim results, no coaching changes, no map bans/preferences for either team. BO3 format requires adaptation across multiple maps \u2014 LOS's 2-0 regular season record may reflect favorable map pools that LOUD has studied or countered. FORM VS AGGREGATE DISCONNECT: LOUD's 1-1 split (2-2 overall) could mask a 0-1 then 1-0 trajectory (improving) or 1-0 then 0-1 (declining). The briefing presents snapshots, not momentum. If LOUD is on an upswing while LOS faces complacency, odds shift sharply in BO3. PSYCHOLOGICAL EDGE: LOS is higher-seeded and favored (42% \u2192 58% NO); LOUD is the underdog. In BO3 elimination-format matches, underdogs who lose Game 1 often adjust for Game 2. If LOS takes Game 1 overconfidently, LOUD's 1-1 record suggests they don't fold \u2014 they regroup. META/PATCH SILENCE: No patch notes, meta shifts, or champion pool updates mentioned. A recent 12.x patch could favor LOUD's champions or mid-lane focus while punishing LOS's macro playstyle. RECENT FURIA WIN NOISE: LOS's CBLOL Cup victory over FURIA may be inflating confidence in a different tournament context (cup vs regular season, possibly different roster management philosophy). TIMING RISK: Match scheduled Apr 12 3:00 PM ET but data freshness is Apr 12 17:21 UTC (~1h before or after match). Market has 8 hours to resolve \u2014 if match is delayed or rescheduled due to technical issues, tiebreaker rules (50-50 if delayed >7 days) could apply, but more likely: final lineup announcements or last-minute roster swaps happen post-data-snapshot. VOLATILE MARKET BEHAVIOR: 24-hour volatility 0.9pp/hr on NO side, sharp moves on Apr 11 (-5.5pp) suggest leaked information or insider trades. If council consensus is LOS-bullish, contrarian positioning favors the 58% NO price as a value trap. BO3 STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE: LOUD's 1-1 record, while weaker aggregate, could reflect 2-1 and 1-2 results against different opponents. If one of those maps was a stomp, LOUD may have cleaner read on specific team strengths than LOS's distributed 2-0.", "key_factor": "LOUD's recent 1-1 split masks a hidden winning streak or meta-adaptation that punishes LOS's playstyle in BO3 format, combined with potential roster rotation or substitute player deployment that the briefing does not disclose.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5632929782082324, "no_score": 0.4355670103092784, "edge": 0.14829297820823245, "no_edge": -0.14943298969072155, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 56% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 59% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1892904", "question": "LoL: LOS vs LOUD (BO3) - CBLOL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between LOS and LOUD in the CBLOL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 12 at 3:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LOS\" if LOS win the match against LOUD.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LOUD\" if LOUD win the match against LOS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T01:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-