{"run_id": "ac9d8aad-0113-41b5-b7a9-bca92e037e9f", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:22:48.598712+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1700801", "question": "Valorant: Cloud9 vs Leviat\u00e1n Esports (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Cloud9 and Leviat\u00e1n Esports in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 12 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Cloud9\" if Cloud9 win the match against Leviat\u00e1n Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leviat\u00e1n Esports\" if Leviat\u00e1n Esports win the match against Cloud9.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.57, "volume_usd": 56754.110753999994, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["22857921000622385995940539269549464587304217497730044339578261329919998819734", "63767421704783462614534417404247857545846937996242126282531639248699219357929"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Cloud9 must win the match against Leviat\u00e1n in a completed best-of-three Valorant match. Resolution criteria are clear: if match is played and completed, the winner resolves YES/NO accordingly. Forfeit/disqualification before match start = 50-50. HISTORICAL EVIDENCE (2023-2025): Briefing explicitly states Cloud9 'consistently defeated Leviat\u00e1n in head-to-head matchups across multiple tournaments' with 'consistent pattern from 2023-2025 seasons.' This is the strongest data point supporting YES outcome. TEAM STRENGTH DIFFERENTIAL: Cloud9 'consistently rated higher in competitive rankings among North American teams' while Leviat\u00e1n 'struggled with consistency, showing mixed results.' Cloud9's 'stronger performance metrics and rating differential' support YES probability ~55-60%. LEVIAT\u00c1N COUNTER-CASE (WEAK): Leviat\u00e1n wins cited (G2, NRG, KR\u00dc) are from 2024-2025; however, these do not contradict Cloud9's historical dominance in head-to-head matchups specifically. Leviat\u00e1n's Esports World Cup 2025 performance is mentioned but not contextualized against Cloud9. BO3 format 'creates opportunity for upset potential' but this is true of all competitive matches\u2014not specific evidence of Leviat\u00e1n strength. 2026 SEASON FACTORS: 'Potentially updated rosters and meta shifts' introduce uncertainty. However, briefing provides NO specific roster changes, player moves, or 2026-specific performance data. Cannot weight roster changes without evidence. Historical trend from 3 prior seasons favors Cloud9 continuation. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Current YES = 57%, NO = 43%. Briefing shows YES side RISING (+3.0pp over 7 days), suggesting market confidence tracking toward Cloud9. This is roughly consistent with historical head-to-head advantage, suggesting market has priced in available information. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Event is TODAY (~10 hours from briefing timestamp 2026-04-12 17:22 UTC, scheduled for 2026-04-12 21:00 UTC per 'April 12 at 5:00PM ET'). Match timing is imminent. Small but non-zero risk of: (a) technical delay beyond 7 days (\u219250-50), (b) forfeit before start (\u219250-50), (c) incompleted match with mid-game forfeit (\u2192resolves to winner, not 50-50 per criteria). Last-minute roster changes unlikely but possible in esports. These risks warrant modestly lower confidence, not lower probability. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 72 (strong historical data, clear ranking differential, market alignment). confidence_no = 55 (Leviat\u00e1n's counter-wins exist but are not against Cloud9 specifically; 2026 roster unknowns cut both ways; BO3 upset probability is real but not extraordinary; insufficient data to confidently rule out Cloud9 dominance continuation). PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 58 reflects: ~3-year historical Cloud9 dominance (pointing toward 60-65%), slightly tempered by 2026 unknowns and BO3 variance (pointing toward 55-57%), and market consensus at 57%. No material new evidence shifts this substantially. YES probability ~58% is defensible; NO probability ~42% accounts for Leviat\u00e1n's past tournament wins and potential meta/roster changes. CRITERIA CLARITY: Resolution criteria are explicit and unambiguous for standard match completion. Forfeiture/disqualification clauses are clearly defined. Primary outcome condition (Cloud9 wins) vs. alternative conditions (Leviat\u00e1n wins, 50-50 scenarios) are mutually exclusive and well-specified.", "key_factor": "Match timing (scheduled ~10 hours from briefing) creates potential for last-minute roster changes, technical delays, or forfeiture scenarios that could trigger 50-50 resolution clause; insufficient current roster/meta data for 2026 season.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "YES CASE (Favored Side): Cloud9 is priced at 57% and momentum has risen +3pp over 7 days, indicating market confidence is increasing in their favor. Historical dominance: Briefing explicitly states Cloud9 has 'consistently defeated Leviat\u00e1n in head-to-head matchups across multiple tournaments' spanning 2023-2025, establishing a clear empirical pattern. Ranking advantage: Cloud9 is 'consistently rated higher in competitive rankings among North American teams,' suggesting structural team quality and skill differential. Performance metrics: Cloud9 demonstrates 'stronger performance metrics and rating differential in recent matches'\u2014quantifiable edge in firepower and efficiency. Leviat\u00e1n consistency problem: Briefing notes Leviat\u00e1n has 'struggled with consistency, showing mixed results against other top Americas teams,' undermining reliability even in favorable matchups. NO CASE (Underdog Weaknesses): While Leviat\u00e1n did beat G2, NRG, and KR\u00dc in 2024-2025, these wins do not overcome the sustained historical gap; sporadic upsets against mid-tier opponents \u2260 capability to beat a consistently ranked-higher opponent. EWC 2025 context: Leviat\u00e1n's positive Esports World Cup results are valuable but against an unknown opponent set and do not directly address Cloud9 matchup-specific advantage. BO3 format ceiling: Best-of-three does create upset variance, but this applies symmetrically\u2014if anything, it benefits the higher-rated team with more preparation and meta knowledge. 2026 roster reset: Both teams have 'potentially updated rosters and meta shifts,' but this cuts both ways; Cloud9's higher ranking suggests they adapted better to new conditions. Market mispricing check: YES at 57% appears justified or slightly underpriced given 3-year dominance + ranking advantage + recent metrics; NO at 43% likely overweights Leviat\u00e1n's sporadic wins without normalizing for historical pattern. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence on YES (72) because historical H2H data is concrete and multi-season; moderate-lower confidence on NO (58) because briefing lacks specific 2026 roster details, recent scrim results, or meta-specific analysis that could support an upset scenario.", "key_factor": "Cloud9's dominant 3-year head-to-head record against Leviat\u00e1n combined with superior competitive ranking and consistency across top-tier competition.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET BIAS TOWARD RECENCY & NARRATIVE: YES side has risen 3pp over 7 days despite NO data suggesting Cloud9 strengthened or Leviat\u00e1n weakened. The briefing offers only historical dominance (2023-2025) as justification\u2014past seasons may not reflect 2026 roster updates, meta shifts, or individual player form changes. LEVIAT\u00c1N'S CONCRETE WINS UNDERWEIGHTED: Briefing explicitly documents Leviat\u00e1n wins vs G2 Esports, NRG, and KR\u00dc Esports (2024-2025) plus Esports World Cup 2025 success. These are not flukes\u2014they prove Leviat\u00e1n can execute against elite competition, yet market prices them at only 43%. ROSTER & META UNCERTAINTY: Both teams entered 2026 season with 'potentially updated rosters' per briefing. Historical 2023-2025 dominance is rendered less predictive if Cloud9 lost key players or Leviat\u00e1n acquired talent. Briefing provides ZERO current roster details, creating information asymmetry that favors upset odds. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES UPSET LIKELIHOOD: Best-of-three requires Leviat\u00e1n to win only 2 of 3 maps. Even against a stronger opponent, variance in map pool matchups, draft execution, and momentum swings create realistic upset lanes. Briefing notes BO3 'creates opportunity for upset potential' but market has not repriced accordingly. CLOUD9'S EVIDENCE IS STALE: 'Consistent dominance across 2023-2025' and 'stronger performance metrics' are historical claims with no specific 2026 data provided. Without current LAN results, recent scrim performance, or 2026 season metrics, the YES case rests on inference rather than fresh evidence. LEVIAT\u00c1N'S CONSISTENCY ARGUMENT IS OVERSTATED: Briefing does mention 'mixed results' and 'inconsistency' against other top teams\u2014this is a weakness. However, 'inconsistency' does not equal 'always loses to Cloud9.' Inconsistency can manifest as upset wins, and Leviat\u00e1n's documented wins prove they are not helpless. TOURNAMENT RESET NARRATIVE: Briefing explicitly states 'fresh season offers reset conditions' and new VCT model changes. This reduces the predictive power of multi-year head-to-head records and creates room for Leviat\u00e1n to perform above historical baseline. TIMING & MARKET ILLIQUIDITY: $56,754 volume is moderate; market may lack depth to reflect Leviat\u00e1n's true capability. Oddsmakers often shade favored teams higher in low-liquidity esports markets due to recreational YES bias. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: YES confidence (72%) is high because Cloud9's historical dominance is documented and explicit. NO confidence (45%) is lower because current Leviat\u00e1n roster strength, 2026 form, and map-specific prep are not detailed in briefing\u2014genuine data gap for underdog analysis. However, documented wins vs tier-1 teams (G2, NRG) elevate NO confidence above 30. PROBABILITY REFLECTS BOTH SIDES: Cloud9 remains favorite (57% \u2192 62% implied if adjusted) due to strong historical record, but Leviat\u00e1n's 43% pricing undervalues recent demonstrated capability and meta uncertainty. Fair value likely 55-45 or 54-46 Cloud9, making current 57-43 slightly overpriced on YES. Setting probability_score to 38 reflects NO as genuine underdog with realistic upset path.", "key_factor": "Leviat\u00e1n's demonstrated wins against top-tier opponents (G2, NRG, KR\u00dc) in 2024-2025 and Esports World Cup 2025 performance prove capability to compete at Cloud9's level, yet market heavily discounts upset potential in BO3 format.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.63, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "- Historical head-to-head data strongly favors Cloud9: documented multiple wins across 2023-2025 tournaments vs. Leviat\u00e1n's inconsistent record against top opponents.\n- Cloud9 consistently ranked higher in competitive tiers during reference periods; stronger rating differential in recent matches cited.\n- Leviat\u00e1n's counterargument relies on selective wins (G2, NRG, KR\u00dc) and EWC 2025 performance, but briefing emphasizes their overall inconsistency vs. Cloud9's dominance.\n- BO3 format does introduce upset potential (typical 10-15% upset premium in esports), but briefing provides no evidence of roster changes, meta shifts, or recent form reversals that would materially challenge the historical trend.\n- Market price (YES 57%) is slightly below my assessment, reflecting some uncertainty about 2026 season reset and roster updates not detailed in briefing.\n- 2026 season is fresh, reducing confidence in historical extrapolation; briefing acknowledges 'potentially updated rosters' but provides no specific roster data.\n- Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~10 hours); very limited time for reversal or new information; market has stabilized at 57% YES with minimal 24-hour movement.\n- Confidence_yes higher (72) due to strong historical precedent; confidence_no lower (58) due to insufficient data on 2026 roster changes and meta evolution that could favor Leviat\u00e1n.\n- Modest 63% estimate reflects anchoring to historical Cloud9 dominance while acknowledging season-reset uncertainty and BO3 upset baseline.", "key_factor": "Cloud9 has won multiple consecutive head-to-head matchups against Leviat\u00e1n across 2023-2025 seasons; Cloud9 maintains higher competitive ranking positioning in Americas tier.", "probability_yes": 0.63, "probability_no": 0.37, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Cloud9's dominant historical H2H record (2023-2025) vs Leviat\u00e1n is the primary driver of YES pricing; briefing explicitly states 'consistent defeated Leviat\u00e1n in head-to-head matchups across multiple tournaments' YES side has been rising (+3.0pp over 7 days), suggesting market confidence building around Cloud9's structural advantage; 57% reflects modest but justified favorite status NO case relies on isolated 2024-2025 wins (G2, NRG, KR\u00dc) and Esports World Cup results\u2014meaningful but insufficient to overcome Cloud9's persistent dominance pattern BO3 format cited as NO's upset lever, but briefing provides no evidence that Leviat\u00e1n performs better in BO3 specifically vs BO1; generic upset potential shouldn't move market significantly Critical data gap: 2026 roster changes and meta shifts are mentioned as potential reset factors but no roster details or roster strength comparison provided; confidence_no capped at 55 due to this uncertainty Market price (57% YES) aligns rationally with briefing evidence; no sign of crowd panic or irrational exuberance\u2014trading appears grounded in historical pattern recognition Event resolves TODAY in ~10 hours with no recent performance data from 2026 season yet; market is pricing based on pre-season history + logical team strength tiers Volume ($56.7K) is moderate; no extreme concentration suggesting sharp money or panic; sentiment appears balanced between both sides' defensible positions Slight confidence asymmetry: briefing strongly documents Cloud9 dominance (high confidence_yes at 72), but roster/meta uncertainty limits ability to dismiss Leviat\u00e1n (confidence_no at 55 rather than 40)", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Historical record heavily favors Cloud9 across multiple seasons (2023-2025), establishing clear skill/team chemistry gap vs. Leviat\u00e1n. Cloud9 consistently ranked higher in competitive tiers and maintained stronger rating differential in recent matches pre-2026. Leviat\u00e1n has demonstrated inconsistency against top-tier opponents and selective win patterns (G2, NRG, KR\u00dc in 2024-2025), suggesting ceiling limitations. BO3 format mathematically increases upset potential vs. BO1; Leviat\u00e1n's proven ability to win maps against competitive teams suggests non-zero game-win probability per map. 2026 season represents roster/meta reset; briefing lacks current rosters, mechanical updates, or recent scrims\u2014critical data gaps that reduce confidence in historical extrapolation. Market price (57% YES) slightly overvalues Cloud9 relative to historical dominance; suggests modest misprice favoring YES, consistent with rising 7-day trend (+3pp). Leviat\u00e1n's Esports World Cup 2025 results mentioned but not detailed; insufficient context on whether those wins signal genuine 2026 improvement or anomalies. Event timing (TODAY, ~10 hours to resolution) means minimal time for reversal; current market price likely reflects pre-match analysis and is stable. Confidence_yes higher (72) due to clear historical pattern and competitive positioning; confidence_no lower (55) due to lack of 2026 roster/meta specifics for Leviat\u00e1n assessment. Probability set at 58 (slight upside from 57% market price) reflecting modest YES lean while acknowledging meaningful BO3 upset risk and season-reset uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Cloud9's historical dominance (2023-2025) provides strong baseline, but BO3 format and early-season roster/meta volatility in 2026 create meaningful upset probability that the briefing may underweight.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, 