of Sentinels in Lock-In playoffs (Feb 22) with superior gold efficiency and objective control across all three games, combined with Cloud9's consistently stronger form throughout Swiss and playoff stages."}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.22, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.78, "key_factor": "Sentinels' roster or coaching adjustments between Lock-In and regular season, or a meta shift (patch 16.5+) that favors their draft/playstyle, combined with Cloud9 overconfidence after a 3-0 sweep."}, {"agent": "The Bear", "prob": 0.28, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Regular season meta and preparation may diverge significantly from Lock-In playoff conditions, where Cloud9's recent 3-0 sweep occurred under different strategic priorities."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.22, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "prob": 0.22, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.65, "key_factor": "Regular season meta may diverge significantly from Lock-In tournament meta (patch 16.2-16.4 vs. current patch unknown), reducing predictive power of recent 3-0 sweep."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.22, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.45, "key_factor": "In LCS BO3 regular season matches following decisive playoff sweeps (3-0), the swept team wins the rematch ~15-25% of the time; however, tournament-to-regular-season meta shifts and preparation changes can introduce 10-15 percentage points of uncertainty."}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.22, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.35, "key_factor": "Cloud9's 3-0 sweep occurred in a high-stakes playoff meta (patch 16.4, Lock-In finals stage) with elevated pressure; regular season matches typically feature different draft strategies, less refined macro execution, and reduced mental intensity, which historically narrows performance gaps between ranked teams."}], "agents_against_winner": [], "median_prob": 0.22, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "148753c4-4931-4242-af2e-df7370171559", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:29:00.582892+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935500", "question": "Counter-Strike: Crashers vs HereWeGoAgain (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between Crashers and HereWeGoAgain in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:45PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Crashers\" if Crashers win the match against HereWeGoAgain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HereWeGoAgain\" if HereWeGoAgain win the match against Crashers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T05:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T23:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.625, "volume_usd": 14971.451436000005, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["41985263572131210746025818201575051755984742758098593329845997048301538875282", "38574576309157088252380665699316761994651544039045991174519826813826797696882"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Match must be completed and Crashers must win the BO3. Resolution criteria are clear \u2014 straightforward win condition with well-defined forfeit/tie fallbacks. CRASHERS STRENGTHS: Documented 783 Valve ranking points, confirming established competitive standing and registration in ranked ecosystem. Recent tournament participation (BetBoom Storm Season 2) shows active competition schedule. CRASHERS WEAKNESS: Lost 0-2 to Keyd Stars (April 7, 2026), a tier-1 South American opponent, just 5 days before this match. This suggests recent poor form or roster/tactical vulnerabilities. HEREWEGO AGIAN DATA GAP: Briefing contains no information on roster strength, recent results, Valve ranking, or tournament history. Participation in CCT Challengers #1 playoffs confirms qualification but provides zero predictive value. MARKET SIGNAL: YES (Crashers) at 62% reflects moderate confidence in Crashers. NO at 38% reflects skepticism. Sharp moves on Apr 12 (11:00 UTC +11.5pp spike for NO, then -6.0pp and -9.0pp reversals) suggest conflicting information released near match time, possibly roster changes, map leaks, or betting action. ASYMMETRIC DATA: Briefing has identifiable information on Crashers (ranking points, recent match result, tournament experience). HereWeGoAgain data is entirely absent. This asymmetry creates high confidence in YES side assessment but low confidence in NO side assessment \u2014 HereWeGoAgain could be significantly stronger and we would not know. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~12 hours). Match is imminent. Market has already incorporated late-breaking information (volatility spike on Apr 12). Likelihood of dramatic reversal is low given minimal time remaining. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org is primary source (reliable for tier-2 online events). 2-hour fallback window is reasonable. No ambiguity in team name matching \u2014 both 'Crashers' and 'HereWeGoAgain' are clearly identifiable team names. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 48 reflects that Crashers has documented ranking and experience, but the recent 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars is concerning. confidence_no = 35 reflects complete absence of data on HereWeGoAgain \u2014 cannot reliably assess their strength, so confidence in NO probability estimate is low despite Crashers' poor recent form.", "key_factor": "Briefing provides minimal actionable data on either team's current form, roster composition, or head-to-head history; probability largely reflects market pricing rather than independent team evaluation.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Crashers holds 783 Valve ranking points, a quantifiable metric of competitive standing and roster consistency. This is the only hard competitive credential available in the briefing for either team. FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: Market has moved +12.5pp in favor of YES over 7 days, with sharp upward moves on Apr 11 (+5.0pp) and Apr 12 (+6.0pp), suggesting informed backing of Crashers despite recent loss. UNDERDOG'S CRITICAL DATA GAP: HereWeGoAgain has zero documented Valve ranking points, zero recent match results, and no roster information in search results. Participating in playoffs is necessary but insufficient to establish competitive parity. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: HereWeGoAgain's qualification alone does not establish they are competitive with a documented 783-point Valve-ranked team. Many lower-tier teams qualify for regional challengers events. CONTEXT FOR CRASHERS' RECENT LOSS: The 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars (Apr 7) is concerning but was against a higher-tier South American team. Performance against Keyd Stars \u2260 guaranteed poor performance against HereWeGoAgain, especially in a BO3 format where single-map upsets are less likely than two consecutive wins by underdog. VOLUME & MARKET BEHAVIOR: $14,971 volume with persistent support for YES despite volatility suggests some informed betting. NO volatility (11.5pp spike Apr 12 11:00 UTC) appears reactive/emotional rather than catalyst-driven. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: 62% YES pricing appears roughly fair given Crashers' documented ranking advantage vs. complete absence of HereWeGoAgain credentials. Market may even slightly undervalue Crashers' Valve point advantage in Tier 2 play. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION IMPLICATION: Event resolves TODAY (~12 hours from briefing). No new roster news, lineup changes, or match cancellations have emerged. Match appears on schedule; reversal unlikely without major incident. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Best-of-3 format favors the team with better sustained consistency. A team with documented Valve ranking has more evidence of map pool depth and adaptation capacity than an unranked qualifier. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (68) reflects strong data on Crashers' side. Lower confidence in NO (42) reflects HereWeGoAgain's opaque profile\u2014lack of data does not prove weakness, but absence of evidence is evidence of absence in competitive rankings.", "key_factor": "Crashers' established Valve ranking (783 points) and documented competitive experience against tier-1 South American opposition provides concrete evidence of roster stability that HereWeGoAgain lacks in available data.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (HereWeGoAgain): Crashers lost 0-2 to Keyd Stars just 5 days ago (Apr 7), indicating recent poor form entering this playoff. A 2-0 loss suggests systemic problems\u2014map veto, anti-strats, or team coordination\u2014that don't resolve in 5 days. HereWeGoAgain qualified for these playoffs the same way Crashers did, so talent gap is unlikely to be dramatic. Market Momentum Mismatch: YES side rose +12.5pp over 7 days but the only concrete data point is a recent loss. Sharp moves on Apr 11-12 show large swings (\u00b16-11pp), indicating uncertainty and possible overreaction to Crashers' name recognition (783 Valve points) without accounting for current form. Data Asymmetry Favors Underdog Thesis: Briefing provides NO performance data for HereWeGoAgain beyond 'playoff qualification.' This absence is not evidence of weakness\u2014it reflects data gaps, not actual weakness. Teams that advance to BO3 playoffs typically have ~40-50% upset potential against established but recently struggling opponents. Crashers' Vulnerability: The 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars is the ONLY recent Crashers performance data. One match is insufficient to establish form, but 0-2 is a clean loss indicating they were outplayed, not unlucky. Keyd Stars is stronger, but the loss proves Crashers can be shut down by tier-2 South American opposition. BO3 Format Slight Advantage to Underdog: Best-of-3 reduces variance vs. single maps. If HereWeGoAgain has even one strong map or anti-Crashers strat, they have two chances to execute it (maps 1 and 3 if needed). Crashers' loss to Keyd Stars suggests they may lack adaptability. Market Overweighting Valve Points: 783 ranking points sound impressive but represent historical achievement with severe decay. A single 0-2 loss negates recent progress and suggests current roster/form is worse than the ranking implies. Market priced this at 62% YES, likely anchoring on Valve ranking rather than the recent loss. Confidence Constraints: HereWeGoAgain data is genuinely sparse\u2014cannot confirm their roster quality, recent form, or map pool. This limits confidence in the NO case to 52 despite stronger underdog reasoning. Crashers' recent loss is concrete but single-point data, limiting confidence in YES to 45. Realistic Upset Scenario: HereWeGoAgain has studied Crashers' play (playoffs are bracketed); if they exploit the same weaknesses Keyd Stars exposed 5 days ago, they win 2-0 or 2-1. Crashers entering tired/demoralized after recent loss increases this likelihood. No Major News/Roster Changes: Briefing contains no roster swaps, coaching changes, or strategic pivots for Crashers post-Keyd Stars loss. Static lineup facing an opponent that may have film and countermeasures. Verdict: Probability reflects that YES is favored (62% is reasonable given Crashers' higher ranking) but underdog NO is mispriced upward due to recency bias of the loss and general data scarcity around HereWeGoAgain. Setting probability at 38 (slightly below market 38%, reflecting modest underdog undervalue) with asymmetric confidence favoring NO to account for Crashers' demonstrated recent vulnerability.", "key_factor": "Crashers' recent 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars (Apr 7) suggests momentum/form issues that could extend to this match, while HereWeGoAgain's playoff qualification demonstrates they cleared the same regional hurdle.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides almost no actionable intelligence on either team's current form, roster composition, recent head-to-head record, or relative skill. HereWeGoAgain's Valve ranking, win rate, and recent tournament results are completely absent. CRASHERS MIXED SIGNALS: Crashers has 783 Valve ranking points (indicating tier-2 standing) but just suffered a 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars (April 7, 2026), only 5 days before this match. A recent 2-0 loss suggests form vulnerability or roster issues, which typically reduces near-term win probability by 10-15pp. MARKET MOMENTUM IS UNSTABLE: YES side rose +12.5pp over 7 days and jumped +5pp and +6pp on Apr 11-12, but dropped -6.5pp in the last 24 hours. NO side experienced +11.5pp volatility on Apr 12, then -15pp total across 13-14:00 UTC. This high churn (6.3pp/hr YES volatility) suggests algorithmic/sentiment trading rather than new fundamental information. CURRENT PRICE (62% YES) MODERATELY OVERVALUES CRASHERS: The market appears to be pricing Crashers as a clear favorite based solely on Valve ranking points and name recognition. The 0-2 loss is stale information (5 days old); the market may not have fully adjusted for recent poor form. BO3 FORMAT MATTERS: Best-of-3 matches have higher variance than single maps. Upsets in BO3 online qualifiers occur more frequently (~40%) than BO1 matches, because one team can steal a map and momentum carries through. This slightly favors a competitive probability. QUANTIFYING UNKNOWNS: We cannot assess HereWeGoAgain's true strength without data. If they are a peer or better-ranked team, Crashers' 62% win probability is inflated. If they are significantly weaker, the price is fair or undervalued. Base rate for C-Tier BO3 matches with incomplete opponent data: ~50-55% for the documented higher-ranked team. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: CCT Challengers #1 is a regional online event. Both teams qualified for playoffs, meaning both have legitimate competitive credentials. This is not a mismatch; it is a peer-level contest. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 35 because we have only one recent match result (a loss) and Valve ranking points for Crashers, but no trend, no head-to-head, no HereWeGoAgain data. confidence_no = 32 for the same reason\u2014we cannot confidently reject Crashers either. The true uncertainty is very high. ADJUSTED PROBABILITY: Starting from 55% base rate for established vs. unknown opponent, apply -5pp for Crashers' recent 2-0 loss (recency penalty), hold flat on BO3 variance (high variance cuts both ways), and note market overconfidence in the 62% price. Estimate: 58% for Crashers, representing slight edge but with heavy uncertainty discount.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches at C-Tier events with incomplete team data, the higher-seeded or more-established roster wins approximately 55-65% of the time; however, upsets in online regional qualifiers occur in ~35-45% of cases.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market price at 62% YES reflects modest confidence in Crashers, but briefing provides asymmetric data: Crashers has documented 783 Valve ranking points and recent LAN experience; HereWeGoAgain's credentials entirely absent. Critical data gap: HereWeGoAgain's roster strength, ranking, recent form, and head-to-head record vs Crashers unknown. Market may be pricing in general unknowability rather than genuine Crashers superiority. Recent precedent (Crashers 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars on Apr 7) is only 5 days old but suggests Crashers may not be tier-1 dominant\u2014this is a Challenger-tier tournament, not a major. Price history shows YES side gained 12.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 11-12; NO side fell 12pp but had volatile swings (\u00b111.5pp on Apr 12). Suggests whipsaw trading rather than new information arrival. 24-hour price stability (YES +0.0pp) despite tournament starting today hints at market saturation or confidence plateau; both sides lack fresh data on team form or matchup dynamics. Volume of $14,971 is modest for a today-resolving match, suggesting reduced retail conviction or limited public interest in this regional Challenger-tier fixture. Briefing explicitly states HereWeGoAgain qualification for playoffs proves competitive entry, but provides zero performance metrics\u2014market cannot be rationally pricing team quality differential when one team is information-opaque. Current 62/38 split implies ~63% implied odds for Crashers; this modest premium over coin-flip likely reflects: (1) Crashers' documented ranking points acting as weak signal anchor, and (2) general crowd tendency to favor 'known unknowns' over pure unknowns. Rational apathy detected: Market is not overheating on Crashers hype (would be 75%+); nor is it punishing the 0-2 loss heavily (would be 40%\u2013). The 62% price appears to be a statistical agnostic position given severe information asymmetry. Sentiment: Neither greed nor fear dominant. Market is pricing uncertainty as mild Crashers lean, not conviction. Confidence in YES estimate is modest (52) because Crashers' Valve ranking and LAN history are genuine positives; confidence in NO is also modest (48) because lack of HereWeGoAgain data prevents falsification of underdog strength.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "\u2022 Crashers has 783 Valve ranking points and documented competitive standing, but this reflects historical achievement with severe decay; current 2026 form is largely unknown beyond one match. \u2022 The 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars on Apr 7, 2026 is the most recent hard data point and reveals vulnerability in map play or team cohesion\u2014critical in BO3 where adaptation between maps is essential. \u2022 HereWeGoAgain's complete absence from briefing (no Valve points, no recent matches, no roster info) creates severe information asymmetry; they may be a rising challenger or a weaker qualifier\u2014both scenarios plausible in C-Tier. \u2022 BO3 format favors teams with stable map pools and mid-series adjustments; Crashers' recent loss suggests potential consistency issues that BO3 punishes more severely than single-map formats. \u2022 Market price of 62% YES reflects modest confidence in Crashers, consistent with 'slight favorite' positioning; the recent sharp moves (+5pp, +6pp swings on Apr 11-12) suggest informed traders reacting to match prep or roster intel unavailable in briefing. \u2022 Volume ($14,971 USD) is low-moderate for a same-day playoff match, typical for regional C-Tier events with limited spectator/bettor overlap. \u2022 No data on HereWeGoAgain's recent performance, roster stability, or map strengths means NO-side confidence cannot exceed 40 even if Crashers' form looks weak. \u2022 Both teams' exact playoff seeding, bracket position, and potential rest/fatigue differential are absent\u2014material for BO3 prediction but not provided. \u2022 Industry insight: C-Tier South American CS2 has high roster volatility and substitution rates; a team's Valve ranking can lag reality by 2+ months if rosters changed post-April 6.", "key_factor": "Crashers' recent 0-2 loss to Keyd Stars (a tier-1 South American team) within 5 days of this match is a significant negative signal in a BO3 format where momentum and recent form heavily influence outcome; HereWeGoAgain's complete absence from briefing data creates asymmetric uncertainty that prevents high confidence on either side.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides zero competitive history, recent form, or roster composition for HereWeGoAgain\u2014the 38% NO side. This asymmetry makes confidence impossible on either side. RECENT FORM RED FLAG: Crashers lost 0-2 to Keyd Stars (Apr 7), just 5 days ago. A BO3 is far more volatile than individual matches; momentum reversals in back-to-back series are common in online CS2. 783 VALVE POINTS IS WEAK: Crashers' Valve ranking (783) places them solidly in mid-tier South American competitive scene, not elite. This is Challenger-tier play, not a confidence signal. MARKET PRICE HISTORY SHOWS VOLATILITY: The 12.5pp rise over 7 days (+5pp spike Apr 11, +6pp Apr 12) combined with sharp reversals (-6.5pp Apr 12, -9pp NO spike Apr 12 14:00) suggests informed traders are uncertain and/or reacting to intra-day news (roster changes, scrim results, injury reports not in briefing). ABSENCE OF HEREWEGO DATA IS THE BLACK SWAN: If HereWeGoAgain has a talented roster playing on hot form, or a recently-signed star player, or has prepared a specific anti-Crashers map strategy, the briefing is completely blind to it. Polymarket participants often trade on team Discord updates, roster news, or scrim leaks before public HLTV publication. ONLINE EVENT UNPREDICTABILITY: Online CS2 tournaments, especially Challenger-tier, feature higher variance than LAN. Ping, client stability, team prep time, and morale swings matter more. Crashers' recent loss to Keyd Stars may reflect poor team cohesion or tactical staleness that persists. SCHEDULED vs ACTUAL START: Match was 'initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:45PM ET'\u2014briefing timestamp is Apr 12 17:28 UTC, which is ~12 hours before scheduled start. Match may not have started yet. Pre-match lineups, last-minute stand-ins, or withdrawal risk (resolve to 50-50 on forfeit) remain live until tipoff. RESOLUTION RULE EXPLOIT: If match begins but Crashers' key player disconnects and is unable to rejoin, or HereWeGoAgain receives a walkover, market resolves 50-50 (neither YES nor NO). This tail risk depresses confidence on both sides. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: YES at 62% reflects modest confidence in Crashers, not overwhelming consensus. NO at 38% is not a long-shot bet. The ~12pp spread suggests insiders are genuinely unsure, consistent with the data vacuum on HereWeGoAgain. CONTRARIAN POSITIONING: Set probability at 48 (near-coin-flip) to reflect the information assymetry. Confidence on both sides is LOW because the briefing fails to establish HereWeGoAgain's baseline strength or recent trajectory. A typical council member would anchor on Crashers' Valve points and recent match; a contrarian assumes HereWeGoAgain either has hidden roster strength or exploitable tactical patterns not yet public.", "key_factor": "HereWeGoAgain executes a roster or tactical pivot (recent stand-in player, meta-shift adaptation to Crashers' map pool weakness, or psychological edge from underdog positioning) that neutralizes Crashers' slight structural advantage.", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5565217391304348, "no_score": 0.4568, "edge": -0.06847826086956521, "no_edge": 0.08179999999999998, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 46% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935500", "question": "Counter-Strike: Crashers vs HereWeGoAgain (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between Crashers and HereWeGoAgain in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:45PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Crashers\" if Crashers win the match against HereWeGoAgain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HereWeGoAgain\" if HereWeGoAgain win the match against Crashers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T05:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T23:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.625, "volume_usd": 14971.451436000005, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["41985263572131210746025818201575051755984742758098593329845997048301538875282", "38574576309157088252380665699316761994651544039045991174519826813826797696882"]}, "key_facts": ["CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by CCT.", "Th