 rankingRegional Valve rankingVRS Invites\n\nNorth America\n\nUnited States\n\nSouth America\n\nArgentina\n\nBrazil\n\nEurope\n\nDenmark\n\nFinland\n\nKazakhstan\n\nLatvia\n\nPoland\n\nPortugal\n\nRomania\n\nRussia\n\nSweden\n\nTurkey\n\nUkraine\n\nUnited Kingdom\n\nAsia\n\nChina\n\nMongolia\n\nOceania\n\nAustralia\n\nEuropeAmericasAsia\n\nTeam ranking for on April 6th, 2026\n\nNo data available for Valve Regional Standing\n\n# HLTV's world ranking of Counter-Strike Teams\n\nHLTV's world ranking ranks the best teams in the competitive field of Counter-Strike.", "The ranking is updated weekly, and teams move up or down based on their recent performance in competitive matches over the last 2 months.", "The world ranking is based on teams' achievements over the past year (with severe decay in points throughout each month), recent form over the last 2 months and performance at the last 10 LAN events.", "All of that is predicated around a 3-man core each team is required to have in order to retain their past points.", "Online matches and tournaments are included, but with a diminishing factor which means they cannot make a big difference among the top teams, and mainly serve to put new teams on the map."], "news_summary": "CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 is an online CS2 tournament featuring South American teams competing in a Challenger-tier (C-Tier/Valve Tier 2) event. Crashers is a registered South American team with 783 Valve ranking points and recent competitive experience, including a loss to Keyd Stars at BetBoom Storm Season 2. HereWeGoAgain's specific credentials and recent form are not detailed in the search results. This Best-of-3 playoff match will determine advancement in the regional challengers circuit.", "side_yes_case": ["Crashers has documented Valve ranking points (783), indicating established competitive standing", "Crashers has recent tournament experience against tier-1 South American opposition (Keyd Stars match)", "HereWeGoAgain's roster strength and recent performance data are unavailable in search results"], "side_no_case": ["Crashers recently lost to Keyd Stars 0-2, suggesting potential vulnerabilities", "Limited performance data available for Crashers in 2026 season beyond single match result", "HereWeGoAgain's participation in CCT Challengers #1 indicates they qualified for playoffs"], "key_context": ["Match format: Best-of-3 (BO3) in CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "Tournament tier: C-Tier/Valve Tier 2 online event for South American teams", "Venue: Online competition", "Recent precedent: Keyd Stars defeated Crashers 2-0 at BetBoom Storm Season 2 (April 7, 2026)"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-12T17:28:46.518587Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "41985263572131210746025818201575051755984742758098593329845997048301538875282", "data_points": 14, "weighted_avg": 0.5967114427694706, "change_1w_pp": 12.5, "change_24h_pp": 0.0, "volatility_24h": 6.264982043070839, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-11T06:00:05Z", "delta_pp": 5.000000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T00:00:23Z", "delta_pp": 6.000000000000005}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T16:00:16Z", "delta_pp": -6.500000000000005}]}, "no": {"token_id": "38574576309157088252380665699316761994651544039045991174519826813826797696882", "data_points": 50, "weighted_avg": 0.34536791467038724, "change_1w_pp": -12.0, "change_24h_pp": 2.500000000000002, "volatility_24h": 4.7054472440177, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T11:00:41Z", "delta_pp": 11.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T13:00:41Z", "delta_pp": -6.0}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T14:00:41Z", "delta_pp": -8.999999999999996}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-12T17:28:47.216921Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T05:45:00Z", "winning_side": null, "final_yes_price": 0.5, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T18:32:19.115743+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "d8b36d3e-8b48-4e52-9bc7-440c2abffe11", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:29:53.244384+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1700812", "question": "Valorant: FURIA Esports vs NRG (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FURIA Esports and NRG in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 12 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA Esports\" if FURIA Esports win the match against NRG.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"NRG\" if NRG win the match against FURIA Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.315, "volume_usd": 56180.69957699999, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["19619144710005688162337636538387641315293149791732518823572585768209109072582", "88455354587775125203404583297786968154282184604378510493176113776882214135658"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: FURIA Esports wins a best-of-three match against NRG in VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, scheduled for April 12, 8:00 PM ET. EVENT TIMING: Market resolves TODAY (~13 hours). Match is imminent and unlikely to be canceled or delayed beyond 7 days. MARKET CONSENSUS: Current prices (YES 32%, NO 68%) reflect strong market expectation that NRG will win. This pricing is stable over 7 days (EMA 34% to 32% is within noise) with low volatility. DATA GAPS ON FURIA: Briefing contains no recent match results, VOD performance metrics, roster composition, or individual player strength assessments for FURIA. 'Brazilian team FURIA may have regional performance advantages' is speculative without evidence. DATA GAPS ON NRG: Similarly, no recent results, head-to-head record, or roster analysis provided. 'NRG represents competitive North American organization' is organizational reputation, not predictive of THIS match outcome. BOTH TEAMS AT 0-0: The briefing explicitly states both teams have not yet played (0-0 records). This is Week 1 of group stage (April 10\u2013May 10). No performance history in this stage exists. NO COMPARATIVE METRICS: Group context shows 100 Thieves and KR\u00dc at 2-0 (early wins), but no data on whether FURIA or NRG has faced stronger/weaker opposition, map pool strengths, or tactical matchups. INFERENCE FROM PRICING: Market has priced this 68% NRG. In the absence of publicly available briefing data to refute that pricing, deferring to 32% for FURIA is reasonable. However, confidence remains low given complete absence of match-specific intel. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Market resolves cleanly to FURIA or NRG on a direct win (no ambiguity on forfeits/walkovers unless they occur pre-match, which would resolve 50-50 per criteria). Criteria are clear. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Market consensus is strong (68% NRG), but that consensus is NOT backed by detailed briefing analysis\u2014it reflects collective trader belief. Confidence on both sides should be moderate (35\u201338) because the underlying data to validate either forecast is absent from the briefing.", "key_factor": "Insufficient team performance data: no VODs, recent match results, roster strength comparisons, or head-to-head history provided to reliably estimate win probability beyond market consensus.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 68%, reflecting genuine market confidence in NRG. The 7-day stability (+6.0pp for NO) and 24-hour momentum (+4.0pp) show consistent conviction rather than volatility-driven mispricing. NRG FUNDAMENTAL ADVANTAGE: NRG is a well-established North American organization with proven infrastructure, consistent roster management, and historical success in VCT competitions. This structural advantage matters in early-stage group play where preparation and team cohesion are critical. FURIA'S UNPROVEN STATUS: While the briefing notes FURIA may have 'regional performance advantages,' no actual evidence supports this claim. FURIA lacks demonstrated success at this level in VCT 2026, and Brazilian regional dominance does not translate automatically to Americas VCT Group Omega performance. BOTH TEAMS AT 0-0: The briefing explicitly states both teams are 0-0 with no head-to-head history. However, this does NOT create symmetry\u2014it means historical roster strength, coaching staff quality, and organizational resources become the differentiators. NRG wins this asymmetry. GROUP CONTEXT CUTS BOTH WAYS: 100 Thieves and KR\u00dc have won 2-0 opening matches, setting a high bar. For early matches like this one, teams facing strong later opponents (100T, KR\u00dc) often prioritize wins against mid-tier opponents like NRG vs. FURIA. NRG's North American base gives it better scouting and preparation against known NA competition. MISSING DATA ON FURIA: The 'CASE FOR YES' relies on speculation (Brazilian regional advantage, early momentum positioning). The briefing provides zero concrete stats, recent form, or player-level analysis for FURIA in VCT 2026 context. This data asymmetry favors the established favorite. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: FURIA is presented as plausible only because both teams are unproven. But 'unproven' at FURIA's level (international Brazilian org) does not equal 'equal to NRG' (tier-1 NA org). The briefing's neutral framing masks a structural gap. MOMENTUM & MARKET EFFICIENCY: The NO side has gained +4.0pp in 24 hours despite high volatility (2.3pp/hr), suggesting informed money is backing NRG into the match. This is consistent with pre-match research favoring NRG. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=28 reflects insufficient concrete evidence about FURIA's strength. confidence_no=72 reflects NRG's organizational pedigree and NA market knowledge, though no team-specific 2026 stats are provided in briefing.", "key_factor": "NRG's established North American infrastructure and competitive pedigree provide a structural advantage over FURIA in a high-stakes VCT group stage match where both teams are unproven in this iteration.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES is underdog at 32% despite both teams entering at 0-0. This suggests market confidence in NRG's brand/infrastructure rather than match-specific data. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO recent performance stats, head-to-head history, current roster information, or individual player form for either team. Both teams are genuinely unproven in this stage. FURIA'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: Brazilian regional dominance in prior VCT stages often undervalued early in new tournaments. FURIA's status as a 'regional powerhouse' may carry more weight than market prices reflect, especially against an NA-centric valuation of NRG. NRG'S VULNERABILITY: As an established NA org, NRG may face higher expectations and mental pressure to perform immediately in Stage 1. Early-season matches in group play often see favorites stumble. SCHEDULE CONTEXT: Both teams are equally fresh (0-0), eliminating momentum-based advantages. 100 Thieves and KR\u00dc winning 2-0 establishes a competitive bar, but does NOT guarantee either FURIA or NRG will replicate that trajectory. NO DIRECT EVIDENCE FOR NRG: Briefing notes NRG's 'established infrastructure and talent' but provides ZERO concrete stats, recent form, or roster data to justify the 68% NO price. EARLY-STAGE BO3 VARIANCE: Best-of-three in group stage openers historically produces upsets more frequently than later stages. One map pool advantage or strategic surprise can shift a BO3. BETTING BIAS: Market may be anchoring on NRG's brand recognition rather than actual competitive strength relative to FURIA in 2026 meta. 32% for an unproven Brazilian org vs. established NA brand could reflect organisational bias, not skill gap. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION: Both confidence scores remain LOW (32, 35) because briefing lacks substantive comparative data on either team's players, recent scrims, meta fit, or playstyle matchups. This is a genuine information gap, not a signal of underdog strength. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: FURIA executes a focused strategy on 1-2 maps, takes BO3 2-0 or 2-1 by exploiting early-season rustiness in NRG's coordination. Entirely plausible given zero prior results. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 38% reflects modest underdog value (not extreme confidence in upset) while acknowledging both teams' true 50%+ baseline uncertainty. NRG's 68% price appears 5-10pp too high given information vacuum.", "key_factor": "FURIA's unproven status in VCT 2026 Americas creates asymmetric information advantage \u2014 NRG's established NA infrastructure may be overpriced against a team that could exploit early-stage volatility.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "BOTH TEAMS UNPROVEN IN THIS STAGE: Both FURIA and NRG enter at 0-0 with no matches played in Group Omega, eliminating recent form data as a differentiator MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT WITH BASE RATE: Current market pricing NRG at 68% aligns reasonably with historical NA org advantage (~60-65% base rate vs international competitors in Americas VCT), suggesting market has efficiently priced information asymmetries NRG ORGANIZATIONAL ADVANTAGE: NRG is an established North American organization with proven infrastructure, team stability, and familiarity with NA competitive environment \u2014 historical trend favors such orgs in group stage matches FURIA INTERNATIONAL FACTOR: While FURIA is a respected org, competing as a Brazilian team in NA-based VCT introduces timezone, travel, and regional meta adaptation challenges \u2014 typical international challenger penalty in regional esports is 5-10pp NO PREDICTIVE DATA: Briefing provides no head-to-head history, recent scrim results, roster composition details, or meta alignment data \u2014 critically limits confidence on both sides IMMINENT RESOLUTION: Match resolves in ~13 hours; market prices show stable 7-day trend (YES -6pp, NO +6pp over week) suggesting rational repricing toward NRG, not late-breaking news panic GROUP CONTEXT NEUTRAL: Other teams' early 2-0 records (100T, KR\u00dc) set competitive bar but do not reveal relative FURIA vs NRG strength; could favor either team depending on bracket luck CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in NRG's organizational infrastructure and NA home-region advantage (confidence_no = 40); lower confidence in FURIA's unobserved strength due to minimal data (confidence_yes = 35); neither side warrants high confidence given lack of direct performance intel", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant BO3 matches between evenly-matched teams in round-robin group stages, home-region advantage and organizational infrastructure historically favor established NA orgs (NRG) over international challengers at ~60-65% win rate", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market price of 32% YES reflects NRG as the favored side, but briefing provides almost NO substantive data to differentiate team strength, recent form, or roster quality. Both teams enter at 0-0 in Group Omega with no head-to-head history cited. This is a genuine coin-flip scenario masked by a 2:1 price skew. The briefing mentions 100 Thieves and KR\u00dc (both 2-0), Sentinels (0-1), Evil Geniuses (0-2), but provides ZERO performance context for FURIA or NRG specifically \u2014 no win/loss records, no roster comparisons, no recent tournament results. Case for YES relies on vague claims ('Brazilian regional advantage', 'FURIA unproven') without supporting evidence in briefing. Case for NO similarly vague ('NRG has infrastructure') \u2014 organization prestige is not a reliable predictor in a single BO3. Price movement shows stable -6pp drift on YES over 7 days with low volatility (0.7pp/hr). This suggests SLOW, CONSENSUS building toward NRG, not panic or new information. NO side shows higher volatility (2.3pp/hr) and +4pp in 24h, indicating recent trader conviction toward NRG, but no corresponding briefing update justifies this shift. Market appears to be operating on blind reputation (NRG brand > FURIA brand in NA perception) rather than actionable team form data. Rational apathy detected: traders are pricing a weak signal (org tier/region) as strong, and ignoring that match outcome is fundamentally unpredictable without roster, meta, or recent scrim data. Confidence split intentionally asymmetric: confidence_yes=35 reflects inability to justify FURIA bet; confidence_no=38 reflects inability to justify NRG bet. Neither side has adequate briefing support.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "FURIA and NRG both enter Group Omega at 0-0 with no match history provided\u2014eliminates predictive data typically leveraged in esports analysis (recent form, map pools, player matchups, coaching adjustments). Market price (32% YES / 68% NO) shows 6pp drift toward NO over 7 days (stable trend), suggesting gradual confidence accumulation in NRG; 24-hour volatility on NO side (2.3pp/hr) is 3.3\u00d7 higher than YES side (0.7pp/hr), indicating late repositioning toward NRG as match approaches. NRG represents established North American esports infrastructure (franchised LCS org, deep talent scouting); FURIA is Brazilian-based with regional competition primarily in LATAM circuit\u2014cross-regional performance gaps in Valorant esports are typically 10-20 percentile range in favor of NA consolidated teams. Group Omega competitive bar set by 100 Thieves and KR\u00dc (both 2-0)\u2014no indication FURIA or NRG have faced these opponents yet; early-stage group dynamics often favor teams with stronger scrim results and coaching staff familiarity (structural advantage to NRG). Match is BO3 (not single-map)\u2014increases variance; FURIA could win on map-pool specialty (Brazilian teams often excel on specific agent compositions), but NRG's adaptability across 3-map sets typically favors larger orgs. Data freshness: Briefing dated 2026-04-12 17:29 UTC, match scheduled 2026-04-12 20:00 ET (~13 hours at briefing time)\u2014no injury/roster changes reported; timing suggests this is a live-imminent event where last-minute scrim results or substitution news would not yet be reflected in market prices. Resolution criteria allow 50-50 tie only if mat