{"run_id": "d226fde1-7ec4-4a90-bd3a-b4f6ba33bc37", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:33:34.678303+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1937816", "question": "Counter-Strike: Phantom vs HEROIC Academy (BO3) - European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 3 match between Phantom and HEROIC Academy in the European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Phantom\" if Phantom win the match against HEROIC Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HEROIC Academy\" if HEROIC Academy win the match against Phantom.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 940.0580140000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["100472309833546018925086609164995354234274303253178943377243513880028669379141", "81457557270274440206475170815962678892293107727538745812868573315084399736170"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Phantom wins the BO3 match; NO if HEROIC Academy wins. Standard match completion required. HEROIC ACADEMY STATISTICAL ADVANTAGE: 48.4% series win rate vs Phantom's 40% over 3-month sample; HEROIC Academy 38.7% 2-0 win rate vs Phantom's 20% indicates superior dominant-format performance. PHANTOM'S VULNERABILITY: 60% series loss rate with 34.3% 0-2 shutout losses suggests susceptibility to sweeps; elevated 5.8% overtime occurrence vs HEROIC Academy's 2.7% indicates tighter map control by opponent. HEROIC ACADEMY'S CONSISTENCY: Lower loss-rate magnitude (51.6% vs 60%) and higher 2-0 win percentage suggest more reliable series-level execution in BO3 format. SAMPLE SIZE QUALIFICATION: Phantom 35 matches (86 maps) vs HEROIC Academy 31 matches (73 maps) provides reasonable statistical basis; however, briefing notes 3-month window with no match-specific data for April 13. CRITICAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head history, no team form in last 48 hours, no recent lineup changes or roster news for either team provided in briefing. Market price movement (YES from 48% EMA to 60% current) suggests recent information flow not captured in historical data. SHARP MOVE ANALYSIS: Apr 12 01:00 UTC +23pp surge on NO side, followed by corrections, indicates trading on real-time intelligence (likely match previews, team announcements, or betting-desk analysis) absent from briefing. PROBABILISTIC INFERENCE FROM STATISTICS: HEROIC Academy's superior series win rate (48.4% vs 40%), 2-0 dominance (38.7% vs 20%), and lower shutdown loss rate (25.8% vs 34.3%) support NO outcome; however, magnitude of advantage is moderate, not decisive. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: Current 60% YES price contradicts historical statistics favoring HEROIC Academy; this suggests either (a) recent team news favoring Phantom not in briefing, (b) betting-desk mispricing, or (c) liquidity asymmetry. Confidence reduced accordingly. COMPETITIVE TIER CONTEXT: Both teams regional/academy level with no tier-1 international pedigree; match outcome more volatile than established-roster matchups. TIMING RISK (SECONDARY): Match scheduled ~13 hours from briefing timestamp. Event LIVE/IMMINENT status means low probability of cancellation/delay forfeit (criteria would resolve 50-50). Standard completion and winner determination highly likely. CONCLUSION: Statistical evidence favors HEROIC Academy (probability_score = 35 for Phantom/YES), but recent market repricing and data gaps reduce confidence in both directions. Assigned 62% confidence_yes (reasonable statistical signal) and 58% confidence_no (recent price movement suggests unmeasured favorable factors for Phantom).", "key_factor": "Briefing contains fragmented and unreliable performance data with significant gaps in direct matchup information; no recent form data immediately preceding this match", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "YES (HEROIC Academy) is favored at 60% market price, reflecting structural performance advantages in recent form. HEROIC Academy's 48.4% series win rate substantially outpaces Phantom's 40% over identical 3-month sample\u2014an 8.4pp gap is material in regional competition. Critical differentiator: HEROIC Academy converts 2-0 dominant wins at 38.7% vs Phantom's 20%\u2014in a BO3 playoff, cleanly dominating both maps is high-equity outcome. Phantom's weakness is stark: 34.3% 0-2 shutout losses suggests vulnerability to being swept, exactly the format risk in playoff BO3s. HEROIC Academy shows lower variance/overtime frequency (2.7% vs 5.8%), indicating more consistent, controlled map play\u2014advantage in knockout stage. Phantom's 25.7% 1-2 losses + 34.3% 0-2 losses = 60% total loss rate is substantial red flag; they are losing series more often than winning. 24-hour market volatility was extreme (+27pp for YES, -27pp for NO across 13 hours with sharp reversals Apr 11-12), suggesting information asymmetry or late whispers; sharp move on Apr 13 00:31 UTC (-9pp for NO, +9pp for YES) may reflect pre-match momentum toward favorite or roster clarity. NO (Phantom) case is weak: individual player ratings (KEi 1.35, Kylar 1.33) are cited but lack context vs HEROIC Academy opponents; raw capability does not offset match-result disadvantages. No head-to-head data provided; cannot assume Phantom has specific tactical edge or recent upset patterns vs HEROIC Academy specifically. Market pricing at 60/40 appears rational given HEROIC Academy's structural statistical edge; not overpriced. Confidence in YES is 72 because briefing contains concrete 3-month performance metrics favoring HEROIC Academy; confidence in NO is only 48 because Phantom's case relies on partial player ratings and general capability rather than performance data\u2014true strength/weaknesses of Phantom relative to HEROIC Academy remain opaque. Event timing is TODAY (~13 hours to resolution); no time for reversal-driving news (roster changes, injuries, standings drama); market is pricing live competitive matchup where stronger recent form (HEROIC Academy) is heavily favored.", "key_factor": "HEROIC Academy's sig