e baseline\u2014suggesting YES side is overpriced relative to recent 3-month performance data. 24-hour volatility (6.4pp/hr on NO, 5.2pp/hr on YES) and sharp moves (Apr 12 \u00b123pp, Apr 13 -9pp) indicate speculative positioning rather than new performance data\u2014likely noise before live resolution. No direct head-to-head history provided; teams compete at European regional/academy tier, reducing confound from reputation or meta familiarity. Event timing is TODAY (~13 hours to resolution); high volatility and price swings in final 36 hours typically reflect late betting noise and position squeezes, NOT fundamental team strength shifts. Confidence_yes set to 35 (not higher) because briefing provides only aggregate 3-month statistics\u2014no individual map pools, recent form trajectory, roster changes, or tactical adjustments documented. Confidence_no set to 45 (lower than confidence_yes) due to limited counter-evidence: HEROIC Academy's 25.8% loss rate proves teams CAN beat them, but no specific Phantom edge identified in briefing. Base rate for regional academy-tier best-of-threes: team with +8pp series win rate advantage and +17.9pp 2-0 rate advantage historically favored ~60-65%, but current market pricing (60% YES) inverts this logic entirely.", "key_factor": "In best-of-three Counter-Strike playoff matches, the team with superior recent series win rate (48.4% vs 40%) historically wins ~55-60% of the time; teams with 34%+ 0-2 loss rates show elevated vulnerability to sweeps.", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price (60% YES) aligns closely with underlying data: HEROIC Academy's 48.4% series win rate vs Phantom's 40% supports YES side, though margin is modest (~8pp). Sharp volatility spikes (\u00b118-23pp in 24h) suggest information asymmetry or late-breaking roster/tactical intel\u2014typical for regional playoff matches with limited spectator engagement. Phantom weakness is structural: 34.3% 0-2 shutout losses vs HEROIC Academy's 25.8% indicates vulnerability to dominant play, not random variance. HEROIC Academy's 38.7% 2-0 dominance rate nearly double Phantom's 20% is the strongest signal in briefing; market underweights this slightly. Crowd appears rationally priced, not exuberant: 60% YES reflects genuine edge without euphoria; NO side (40%) captures Phantom's non-trivial win paths. Data quality gap on NO side: no direct h2h, no player form trending, no tactical adjustments mentioned\u2014this justifies lower confidence_no despite reasonable case statements. Time-to-resolution (13h) limits reversal scenarios; late-breaking roster changes or strategic reveals could shift 5-7pp in either direction but insufficient time for major reversals. Sample sizes adequate (35 vs 31 matches) to trust relative win rates; statistical noise ~\u00b14pp suggests true edge exists for HEROIC Academy around 5-8pp. Market vibe: Rational\u2014price reflects fundamentals without panic or excessive sentiment amplification; spread tight (20pp between YES/NO) despite volatility.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing lacks direct head-to-head match history between these teams in EPL S6 \u2014 essential for playoff predictions where team-specific dynamics (map veto, playstyle matchup, meta familiarity) dominate regional play. STATISTICAL BASELINE: HEROIC Academy shows 48.4% series win rate (31 matches) vs Phantom 40% (35 matches) over 3-month window \u2014 HEROIC Academy favored by ~8pp in raw series outcomes, supporting YES at ~50-55% floor. VOLATILITY RED FLAG: YES side swung +27pp in 24 hours with sharp moves (Apr 1