across 15 games in S-tier tournament; JD Gaming showed 50% win rate (4-4) in 2025 Regional Finals\u20142026 trajectory favors Bilibili significantly. BO3 format does introduce variance compared to BO5 (reduced sample size, single upset more impactful), but Bilibili's 3-0 precedent demonstrates they can close series decisively against this specific opponent. JD Gaming data gap is critical weakness in NO-side confidence: only 2025 results visible (50% in Regionals), no 2026 EWC qualifier matches shown; suggests either lower bracket placement or fewer matches to date\u2014implies weaker current form. Concurrent LPL Split 2 competition (starts April 4) could create fatigue, but Bilibili's recent match density (2 EWC + FST matches in prior weeks) suggests they manage schedule better. Market pricing at 80% YES reflects informed consensus; 7-day EMA of 76% with +4.5pp rise indicates late money flowing toward BLG, typical of teams with strong pre-match intel. Resolution risk (forfeiture/disqualification) is negligible for both tier-1 LPL organizations; standard match completion expected.", "key_factor": "Bilibili's dominant 3-0 FST victory over JD Gaming in March 2026, combined with perfect 2-0 EWC qualifier record and superior individual player metrics (mid/ADC KDAs of 17.5), strongly favors YES despite BO3 variance; however, JD Gaming's roster continuity and late-season LPL performance data gaps create meaningful NO-side uncertainty.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Bilibili's 100% qualifier record (2-0) and dominant FST March sweep (3-0 vs JDG) are strong fundamentals, but FST was 3 weeks ago\u2014significant meta/roster window. CRITICAL ABSENCE: JD Gaming's recent qualifier performance is almost entirely missing from briefing; only one historical data point (50% in 2025 Regional Finals) and a single 3-0 loss in March. This asymmetry masks their current state. Jungle position shows a major personnel signal: briefing shows Jungle role held by IGY (2020-2022), Invictus Gaming (2022-2024), Bilibili (2024-2025), then JD Gaming (2025-12-09 to 2025-11-28), then BACK to Bilibili (2025-12-01 to Present). This suggests JDG's jungle roster may have rotated or stabilized only recently. BLG's current EWC sample size is tiny (2 games, both crushing wins). Outlier performance on 2-game sample with limited champion diversity (Jarvan/Pantheon jungle only) suggests possible adaptation vulnerability in BO3 series against a prepared opponent. Simultaneous LPL Split 2 launch (Apr 4) creates dual-tournament fatigue burden for both teams; Bilibili's recent matches are all EWC/FST isolated tournaments, not concurrent multi-league scheduling stress. BO3 format inherently higher variance than BO5; Bilibili's 3-0 stomp does not guarantee 2-0 in compressed series where one off-game or early-game adaptation can swing momentum. JD Gaming's champion pool in 2025 Regional Finals (Jarvan IV, Naafiri, Pantheon, etc.) overlaps heavily with meta\u2014suggests they are NOT out of meta or fundamentally weaker, merely less visible in recent qualifier rounds. Market price (80% YES) has risen +4.5pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24h with near-zero volatility on YES side but 1.8pp/hr volatility on NO. This suggests retail confidence in Bilibili, not sharp money signaling uncertainty. No injury, roster lockdown, or coaching change information provided for either team\u2014data silence on morale/internal factors favors underdog scenario if JDG has resolved recent issues. Briefing is visibly polluted with Valorant stats (EDward Gaming, VCT content), suggesting data aggregation error and reduced confidence in search quality. JD Gaming's LoL qualifier data likely exists but was not retrieved.", "key_factor": "JD Gaming's recent roster swap (Jungle returning mid-2025 to present) creates fresh m