 S28, 14 days ago) and 0-3 loss in DreamLeague Division 2 Tier 2 (Feb 12, 2026); this pattern suggests Nigma is mid-tier but functional. Lower-bracket playoff positioning implies both teams lost their initial matches; Nigma Galaxy's presence in multiple qualifier circuits indicates they are established enough to compete at tier-2/3 level, while ALIS VENTORUS' invisibility suggests they may have lost by attrition rather than competitive failure. Market pricing (9% YES / 91% NO) reflects the data asymmetry heavily favoring Nigma Galaxy; the +20pp spike and -20.5pp reversal in the last 24 hours suggests sharp-line movement on information or betting sentiment rather than fundamental analysis shift. Head-to-head record absent; no direct matchup data available to calibrate relative strength; this increases uncertainty on both sides. Dota 2 qualifier ecosystem: teams in visible circuits (Nigma) have higher skill floor than teams absent from records (ALIS VENTORUS); lower bracket is typically where weaker-qualified teams face elimination. Event timing (TODAY, resolves ~6 hours) means match outcome is imminent; any reversal requiring ALIS VENTORUS comeback would require significant in-game execution or Nigma collapse, less likely given established form differential.", "key_factor": "Nigma Galaxy's recent qualifier form (2-1 wins in ESL One Birmingham vs mid-tier teams, but 0-2 losses to tier-1 teams like Virtus.pro) suggests competitive but not elite-level play; ALIS VENTORUS' near-total absence from visible qualifier records indicates either a newly formed stack, academy/secondary roster, or significantly weaker competitive tier.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.16, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "Nigma Galaxy is heavily favored (91% market price) based on tier-1 qualifier visibility and recent 2-1 wins, but their recent f