{"run_id": "11446f17-f5f2-4011-b702-2b0e9abe5527", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T09:34:50.005919+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1951390", "question": "Counter-Strike: ex-RUBY vs Metizport (BO3) - European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 4 match between ex-RUBY and Metizport in the European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 6:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ex-RUBY\" if ex-RUBY win the match against Metizport.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Metizport\" if Metizport win the match against ex-RUBY.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T16:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T10:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 14513.920569, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["59888436946674685658257121425343158469686238699248410823726886936804366942160", "48118669031836969761838215445375183003166545802485727010769965030336827610104"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: ex-RUBY must win the match (BO3 format, 2 maps required) against Metizport in European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs Quarterfinal 4. CURRENT MARKET SIGNAL: YES = 58% / NO = 42% reflects modest ex-RUBY favoritism. YES side has risen +9.0pp in 24hrs with sharp +11.5pp move at 04:00 UTC today, suggesting informed traders may have new intelligence. HISTORICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides only CCT Season 3 context (earlier tournament). ex-RUBY showed 3-1 record with +21 round differential; Metizport lost 0-2 to QWENTRY. However, this is from a different tournament with unclear roster continuity to Series 6 Playoffs. ROSTER & FORM UNCERTAINTY: No current Series 6 rosters, recent form data (last 2-4 weeks), or head-to-head record for this specific playoff matchup provided. Playoff contexts often differ sharply from group stage performance. CASE FOR ex-RUBY (YES): Strong CCT Season 3 record (3-1), defeated TNC 2-0 and WOPA 2-1. Market momentum suggests recent positive intelligence or betting action consolidating on ex-RUBY side. CASE FOR METIZPORT (NO): Defeated Bebop 2-1 in CCT Season 3, showing ability to win competitive matches. CCT loss to QWENTRY 0-2 reflects vulnerability but does not eliminate them. Limited data cuts both ways. VOLATILITY & TIMING: High 24-hr volatility (9.9pp) and recent sharp moves suggest market participants may have access to team news, practice results, or betting syndicates with direct intel. The +11.5pp move at 04:00 UTC (2.5 hours before match start) is consistent with late-breaking information or lineup confirmation. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES (42) is LOW relative to probability (58) because the briefing provides insufficient current data to justify a 58% conviction \u2014 market price may reflect private intelligence rather than public facts. Confidence in NO (38) is similarly LOW because counter-evidence is equally sparse. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are clear and unambiguous. Match must be completed with a winner; forfeits/walkovers \u2192 50-50; cancellation beyond 7 days \u2192 50-50. HLTV.org is the resolution source. TECHNICAL RISK: Community commentary in briefing mentions 'radarhack' allegations and one user claiming ex-RUBY got +3.5 odds 'when they down' on map 1. This suggests the match may already be underway or maps in progress. If match is LIVE, shares should be trading at ~$0.01/$0.99 once outcome is mathematically certain; current 58/42 pricing suggests match is not yet decisively resolved. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Market price of 58% for ex-RUBY is PLAUSIBLE given available data, but confidence is LOW in both directions due to missing current roster, form, and head-to-head context. Probability follows market consensus rather than being strongly derived from briefing facts. Set probability at 58 to match market; lower confidence scores to reflect data gaps.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains only historical CCT Season 3 data from an earlier tournament; no current roster information, recent form data, or Series 6-specific context available to validate which team is favored.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CASE FOR YES (ex-RUBY): Market has moved +8.5pp in favor of ex-RUBY over 7 days and +9.0pp in 24 hours, driven by recent tournament form data showing ex-RUBY's 3-1 CCT record with +21 round differential\u2014a clear statistical edge that justifies the 58% price. FORM ADVANTAGE: ex-RUBY defeated TNC Esports 2-0 (clean sweep) and WOPA Esports 2-1 in recent play, demonstrating both map versatility and ability to close out close series\u2014critical skills in BO3 playoff format. METIZPORT'S WEAKNESS: Metizport lost to QWENTRY 0-2 in CCT Season 3, the most recent documented matchup, showing they are vulnerable to structured opponents and can be shut down entirely in best-of series. UNDERDOG FRAGILITY: While Metizport beat Bebop 2-1, this single win is insufficient counter-evidence against ex-RUBY's multiple recent victories and superior +21 round differential. One close win vs. a 3-1 record is not competitive. MOMENTUM DRIVER: The +11.5pp sharp move on Apr 13 04:00 UTC (just hours before match) suggests informed market participants (likely bettors with lineup/form data) are backing ex-RUBY, adding confidence to the favorite's position. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: This is an elimination match (quarterfinal)\u2014ex-RUBY's tournament-tested lineup with recent wins under pressure is more reliable than Metizport's inconsistent performances. DATA GAPS (limiting confidence on NO side): Search results lack current roster verification, head-to-head Series 6 Playoffs specifics, and Metizport's recent form outside CCT Season 3. NO confidence capped at 45 because underdog's true strength cannot be validated from briefing. UNVERIFIED CONCERNS: Community commentary mentions 'radarhack' allegations and other technical concerns, but these are unverified and unlikely to affect official resolution. Not factored into probability but noted as noise. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: YES side shows 9.9pp/hr volatility vs. NO's 6.1pp/hr, indicating ex-RUBY supporters are actively trading on new information, while Metizport backers are passive\u2014typical of a market recognizing a true favorite. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: 58% for YES reflects genuine form advantage (multiple recent wins, superior metrics) rather than overreaction. Market appears fairly priced or slightly undervaluing ex-RUBY given the one-sided recent evidence. RESOLUTION TIMELINE: Event resolves TODAY in ~7 hours with high confidence (BO3 playoffs are almost never rescheduled or forfeited at this stage), so outcome depends entirely on match performance, not external delays.", "key_factor": "ex-RUBY's recent tournament momentum (3-1 CCT record, decisive wins vs TNC 2-0 and WOPA 2-1) combined with strong +21 round differential contrasts sharply with Metizport's 0-2 loss to QWENTRY, positioning ex-RUBY as the more form-confident team in a high-stakes BO3 playoff.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET TREND FAVORS YES: YES has risen +9.0pp in 24 hours with a sharp +11.5pp move at 04:00 UTC today, suggesting informed money and/or tip-off activity backing ex-RUBY as the event approaches. This 7-hour proximity makes large reversals unlikely without major news. DATA QUALITY GAP (BOTH SIDES): Briefing is primarily CCT Season 3 data from an unspecified timeframe; no current roster information, recent form prior to playoffs, or direct head-to-head record for Series 6 Playoffs. This ambiguity limits confidence in any direction. EX-RUBY'S INCONSISTENCY IS REAL: ex-RUBY's 3-1 record masks a 1-2 LOSS to WOPA Esports in CCT Season 3\u2014in a playoff elimination context, this inconsistency is more damaging than a regular-season loss. They also allow competitive maps (TNC 2-0 win, WOPA 2-1 win shows close matchups). METIZPORT'S UNDERRATED CLUTCH FACTOR: Metizport defeated Bebop 2-1 (described as 'strong opponents'), demonstrating ability to win tight BO3s under pressure. The 0-2 loss to QWENTRY is a data point, but CCT Season 3 is insufficient to characterize overall form. PLAYOFF CONTEXT FAVORS UNDERDOGS: In elimination BO3 formats, the lower-seeded/underdog team often performs above regular-season metrics due to desperation, focus, and map veto leverage. Briefing does not specify seeding, but if Metizport is lower seed, BO3 structure benefits them. COMMUNITY COMMENTARY NOISE: Comments about 'radarhack' and 'free +3.5' lack verification and appear to be post-match speculation. Cannot be used as evidence for either team's quality. VOLUME AND SPREAD: $14.5K volume is moderate for a playoff match 7 hours away; YES/NO prices sum to ~100%, suggesting reasonable orderbook efficiency. The +9pp YES move is likely driven by credible intelligence (roster availability, map pool leaks, insider bets) rather than panic buying. INSUFFICIENT DATA ON METIZPORT RECENT FORM: The briefing provides only 2 concrete data points for Metizport (loss to QWENTRY 0-2, win vs Bebop 2-1). Without recent pre-playoff matches, scrim results, or roster confirmation, confidence in NO cannot exceed low-to-moderate levels despite plausible upset factors. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT: With ~7 hours to match start, YES's rising trend and high market allocation (58%) suggest information asymmetry has already priced in favorable factors for ex-RUBY. A collapse from 58\u219242 would require breaking news (roster disqualification, server issues, forfeit threat) with minimal time to react. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: ex-RUBY is slight favorite with evidence of strong tournament performance but inconsistency. Metizport is underdog but shows BO3 competitiveness. Market at 58/42 is defensible given data scarcity, but underdog has ~35-40% genuine shot if it exploits map veto or ex-RUBY's known vulnerabilities (WOPA performance suggests mid-tier teams can compete).", "key_factor": "Metizport demonstrated clutch capability against strong opponents (Bebop 2-1) while ex-RUBY showed inconsistency with a 1-2 loss to WOPA in the same tournament, suggesting the underdog's resilience in high-pressure BO3 formats is undervalued.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: This is a LIVE/IMMINENT event resolving in ~7 hours. The market has moved +9pp toward YES in 24 hours with sharp volatility (+11.5pp spike at 04:00 UTC today). This suggests either breaking news about team roster/form or pre-match odds information flowing into the market. With minimal time to reversal, current pricing likely reflects real information asymmetry. BASE RATE FOR PLAYOFF BO3S: In professional CS:GO/CS2 European playoffs, seeded/favored teams win ~65-68% of BO3 matches. The current 58% YES price is BELOW historical average for favorites, suggesting either ex-RUBY is unseeded/underdog OR market is pricing in genuine weakness. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: CCT Season 3 historical context (ex-RUBY 3-1, Metizport variable performance) is months old. NO ROSTER CONFIRMATION for Series 6. NO RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD. NO CURRENT FORM DATA. This creates massive uncertainty on both sides \u2014 confidence must be LOW for both. CASE FOR YES (ex-RUBY) WEAKNESSES: Single-game losses recorded (1-2 vs WOPA); CCT data does not confirm current Series 6 roster; no recent match results provided in briefing; technical/performance concerns mentioned in community comments but unverified. CASE FOR NO (Metizport) WEAKNESSES: 0-2 loss to QWENTRY in CCT Season 3 shows vulnerability; similarly dated data; no evidence of recent upswing; equally unverified current roster status. MARKET DIRECTION ANALYSIS: YES has 4 data points (sparse, EMA 56%) vs NO has 11 data points (more stable, EMA 46% but declining). The asymmetry in volatility (YES 9.9pp/hr vs NO 6.1pp/hr) and sharp morning spike sugge