less choking risk in a do-or-die scenario. COMMUNITY COMMENTARY NOISE: Briefing mentions 'radarhack' allegation and other community posts without verification. In esports, unverified competitive integrity concerns can trigger last-minute roster swaps, coach interventions, or psychological destabilization if amplified in team discord. EXTREME TIME CONSTRAINT: With ~7 hours to resolution and $14.5K volume, this is a LIVE/IMMINENT event. Any reversal (Metizport upset) requires rapid execution and no margin for error recovery. However, this same constraint means the market may not have yet priced in any late-breaking roster/tactical intelligence released in the last 3-4 hours.", "key_factor": "Metizport executes a tactical meta-shift or roster substitution (stand-in player, map pool surprise) that exploits ex-RUBY's apparent structural vulnerabilities in specific map picks under playoff pressure.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5638271604938272, "no_score": 0.45885304659498205, "edge": -0.02117283950617277, "no_edge": 0.043853046594982015, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 46% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1951390", "question": "Counter-Strike: ex-RUBY vs Metizport (BO3) - European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 4 match between ex-RUBY and Metizport in the European Pro League Series 6 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 6:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ex-RUBY\" if ex-RUBY win the match against Metizport.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Metizport\" if Metizport win the match against ex-RUBY.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a 