{"run_id": "11b8df1c-2343-4efa-ac66-61c0fdf6e2a9", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T09:59:30.391395+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1796825", "question": "LoL: Weibo Gaming vs Anyone's Legend (BO3) - Esports World Cup China Qualifier Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between Weibo Gaming and Anyone's Legend in the Esports World Cup China Qualifier Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 14 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Weibo Gaming\" if Weibo Gaming win the match against Anyone's Legend.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Anyone's Legend\" if Anyone's Legend win the match against Weibo Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.325, "volume_usd": 16938.249233000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["95931579888277082693485988608236902696815940682287577136887851970878030982154", "49006138632392715893699434322167195142968778301278654304998370277927192137523"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Weibo Gaming must win the BO3 match against Anyone's Legend in Upper Bracket Semifinal 2 of EWC China Qualifier Phase 2. CURRENT MARKET PRICING: YES at 32% reflects strong NO (Anyone's Legend) consensus. This is NOT a pricing error signal \u2014 the briefing explicitly states market pricing shows 'nearly identical odds (WBG 48%, AL 48%)', and YES side has declined 2.5pp in 24h, suggesting modest real-money conviction toward NO. TEAM PARITY \u2014 CASE FOR LOWER YES PROBABILITY: Both teams are LPL Split 1 co-leaders with identical credentials: (1) 2-0 quarterfinal victories on same dates; (2) equivalent seeding status; (3) equal direct EWC qualification pathway. The briefing explicitly flags 'performance parity' and notes that 'patch-driven aggressive metas could favor either team unpredictably,' introducing symmetric uncertainty. WEIBO GAMING FACTORS (supports YES): Won 2-0 vs iG (respectable opponent); demonstrated consistency as LPL Split 1 top seed; upper bracket positioning provides psychological/structural advantage (one loss = lower bracket, not elimination). ANYONE'S LEGEND FACTORS (supports NO): Matched WBG's 2-0 performance against TES (comparable or equal-tier opponent); held co-seed status pre-tournament; double-elimination format means upper bracket loss does not eliminate qualification chances, reducing stakes asymmetry. BRACKETING & META VOLATILITY: The briefing notes 'patch changes could affect outcomes' and that lower bracket matches begin April 13 (tomorrow), meaning a full week exists for meta evolution post-Phase 2. This introduces structural unpredictability that slightly favors the underdog (AL/NO side) in a coin-flip scenario. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL INTERPRETATION: YES at 32% vs. NO at 68% represents strong consensus favoring Anyone's Legend. Across seven days, YES has remained STABLE (\u00b10.0pp net change), indicating this is not a flash mispricing but a sustained real-money allocation. The 24-hour decline of 2.5pp (YES) further suggests late information or conviction accumulation favoring NO. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: HIGH confidence_yes (72%) because the briefing provides clear team performance data (2-0 victories, seeding parity, LPL credentials). MODERATE confidence_no (68%) because the briefing does not provide granular matchup data (head-to-head record, champion pool overlaps, recent scrim results, or player-level form updates that would justify a 32/68 split over 50/50 parity). The market's 32/68 pricing appears grounded in real information not fully disclosed in this briefing, so we defer partially to market consensus while flagging the data gap. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK (minimal): Match begins TODAY at 4:00AM ET (~7 hours); gol.gg publishing timeline is 2 hours post-conclusion, well before market END DATE (April 13, 17:00 UTC). No ambiguity in forfeit/walkover rules; criteria are clear. FINAL ASSESSMENT: The briefing presents two identically positioned top seeds with symmetric case statements. Market pricing (32/68) deviates from that symmetry, suggesting either: (1) real information advantage favoring AL not captured in this briefing, OR (2) recreational betting bias. Given IMMINENT timing (7 hours), new information is unlikely; market price should be treated as signal. Probability_score set to 32 (matching current YES price) reflects deference to market consensus while maintaining measured confidence reflecting underlying parity and data gaps.", "key_factor": "Match is TODAY/IMMINENT (7 hours to start) \u2014 market prices reflect minimal new information arrival; post-match oracle verification via gol.gg or credible consensus should be straightforward.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Anyone's Legend secured an identical 2-0 quarterfinal victory (vs TES) to Weib