lution). This suggests either new information entered the market (likely team roster/matchup details published closer to match time) that heavily favors Hanwha, or algorithmic/momentum traders responding to low liquidity ($21.5k volume). EVENT TIMING CRITICALITY: Market resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). Match is LIVE/IMMINENT. The sharp recent move suggests traders with real-time access to LCK CL information are pricing Hanwha significantly higher. However, no such information is visible in the briefing, creating resolution risk. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Criteria clearly specify official gol.gg as primary source, with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. No mechanism risk apparent, but lack of pre-match roster/form data in briefing suggests the match details may not be fully documented. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Cannot validate confidence_yes above 28 due to absence of Nongshim Esports Academy's recent record, roster, or head-to-head data. Cannot validate confidence_no above 32 due to absence of Hanwha Life Esports Challengers' recent record or team composition. Both sides suffer from severe information scarcity relative to the market price skew. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Market currently prices YES at 41%, NO at 59%. The briefing provides no substantive evidence to support either outcome. The recent sharp move toward NO (Hanwha) suggests informed traders have access to information not in this briefing. Conservative approach: match market slight NO lean (38 for YES = 62 for NO) while heavily discounting confidence on both sides due to data insufficiency.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains fragmented match data from unrelated LCK CL Split 2 games (T1 Academy vs Nongshim, Nongshim vs FEARX) but no direct head-to-head history, recent form data, or roster composition for either team in the April 13 matchup, making any probability estimate highly speculative.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "pro