": "LCK Challengers League academy teams show ~50% baseline win rates in round-robin formats; home/away advantage and recent form typically shift odds by 5-15pp in either direction", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "SHARP REVERSAL SIGNAL: YES dropped 34.5pp in 24 hours with a massive -36.5pp move at 10:01 UTC (4 hours before match). This is NOT gradual repricing\u2014it's panic or hard intel. TIMING RED FLAG: Event resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. A 36.5pp move this close to resolution suggests either new match-critical information (roster changes, cancellation risk, injury) or algorithmic liquidation. Briefing contains NO such news. ASYMMETRIC DATA VACUUM: Briefing provides Nongshim match records (vs T1 Academy, FEARX Youth) but zero Hanwha Life Esports Challengers match records. Market may be pricing in that Hanwha has weaker recent form, but briefing does NOT confirm this. CROWD PANIC vs REALITY: The 7-day EMA for YES was 66%; current is 41%. If Nongshim truly was favored a week ago, the sharp reversal suggests either: (a) new negative intel NOT in briefing, or (b) crowd capitulation on poor early-match trends or betting algorithm cascades. NO SIDE RISING STEADILY: +13pp over 7 days on NO (smoother +35pp in 24h), suggesting less panic and more deliberate repositioning. This contrasts with YES's whipsaw volatility. ACADEMY/CHALLENGER OPACITY: Both teams are secondary-league rosters. Scout data, player form, and recent wins/losses are sparse in briefing. Market is pricing blind or on signals external to this briefing (Discord, Korean esports forums, team announcements). RESOLUTION IMMINENT + UNCERTAINTY: With 5 hours to match start, NO volatility is lower (12.1pp/hr vs 26.5pp/hr). This suggests YES buyers panicking while NO holders are calm\u2014classic sign of crowded longs unwinding into re