nt lineup confirmations for TODAY's match vs Hanwha. This absence during a LIVE event is suspicious. ACADEMY LEAGUE VOLATILITY: LCK CL 2026 Split 2 is inaugural with all-ten-org rosters. Academy teams rotate personnel, promote/demote on short notice, and have weaker bench depth than main league. A surprise sub in a BO3 is far more likely here than in LCK main. HANWHA'S MAIN ROSTER STRENGTH MISMATCH: Briefing notes Hanwha main roster went 3-1 in Rounds 1-2, yet their Challengers team has NO visible match record in search results. This asymmetry suggests either (a) the Challengers roster is stronger than expected and under-scouted, or (b) recent lineup changes have occurred that briefing does not capture. TIMING & VOLATILITY PATTERN: Sharp +36pp move for NO at 10:00 UTC followed by match start in ~5 hours implies real-time intel or scheduled roster announcement. Academy league rosters are sometimes finalized or changed on match day. BO3 ADAPTATION PENALTY: A forced substitution in game 1 of a BO3 is catastrophic\u2014Nongshim would have no time to practice a new composition with the stand-in. Hanwha (if healthy) gains adaptation advantage. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing shows NO confidence-building match records for Hanwha Challengers specifically, yet market is now favoring them 59%. This suggests traders have external intel (roster confirmations, scrims, or known roster issues with Nongshim) not reflected in the document. CONTRARIAN POSITION: If every other analyst assumes Nongshim is favored due to documented recent matches, they miss that those matches may have featured a healthier/different roster than today. The market's late swing suggests a known availability problem has surfaced for Nongshim.", "key_factor": "Nongshim Esports Academy suffers a critical roster availability issue (key player illness, family emergency, or last-minute substitution) immediately before or during the BO3, forcing reliance on an untested stand-in mid or jungle.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "