{"run_id": "004e8866-7a68-490c-9f27-ab331835527a", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:02:41.035116+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1962110", "question": "Dota 2: Vici Gaming vs Team Resilience (BO3) - DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket final match between Vici Gaming and Team Resilience in the DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vici Gaming\" if Vici Gaming win the match against Team Resilience.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Resilience\" if Team Resilience win the match against Vici Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T12:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.745, "volume_usd": 2274.682413, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["58096344416322589261800759171394543645007738216712090661007350347617836515513", "2471990590002154751109319861209802520220170571207732988520080453331807069600"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.74, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: YES resolves if Vici Gaming defeats Team Resilience in the BO3 Upper bracket final; NO resolves if Team Resilience wins. The criteria are clear and unambiguous. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO substantive information on either team's current strength, roster, recent form, or head-to-head matchup. Search results reference 'TBD' bracket entries and historical matches from 2024-2025, but nothing actionable about this specific April 13, 2026 matchup. MARKET PRICE AS PROXY: YES side at 74% likely reflects betting consensus that Vici Gaming is the stronger team. Vici Gaming is historically a top-tier Chinese Dota 2 organization; Team Resilience's competitive tier is entirely unknown from briefing data. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes (35) is significantly lower than the 74% probability_score because the market price is NOT supported by evaluable fundamentals in the briefing\u2014it is a consensus bet on brand/historical reputation. confidence_no (25) is even lower because there is virtually no counter-evidence or data on Team Resilience's actual strength either. TIMING RISK: EVENT TIMING = TODAY with match scheduled April 13 08:00 ET and resolution deadline 18:00 UTC (April 13). The match likely begins ~4-5 hours from briefing timestamp (10:02 UTC). By time of analyst evaluation, the match may already be underway or completed, making reversal probability very low if YES side is winning live. LIVE/IMMINENT REVERSAL: If Vici Gaming has taken a 1-0 series lead or won Game 1 decisively, Team Resilience would need to win Games 2 and 3 consecutively in a BO3 format\u2014a steep climb. However, BO3 comebacks are not rare in esports. Without live match data, this cannot be refined. RESOLUTION SOURCE STABILITY: DotaBuff is the primary source; fallback to credible reporting if results unavailable within 2 hours post-match. Both sources are reliable for a major esports event. No mechanism risk flagged. TEAM NAME AMBIGUITY: Both 'Vici Gaming' and 'Team Resilience' are standard team names with no discrepancy noted. Resolution by real-world match outcome is straightforward if the match is played to completion. FORFEIT/CANCELLATION RISK: Minimal given this is a scheduled Upper bracket final in an active qualifier. Tournament has been running (matches on April 12 confirmed in briefing data). 50-50 resolution only applies if match canceled outright or delayed >7 days\u2014unlikely within the TODAY timeframe. VERDICT: probability_score of 74 reflects market consensus that Vici Gaming is favored, likely based on historical standing and brand reputation. However, CONFIDENCE in this estimate is LOW (35) because the briefing provides no concrete data on current rosters, recent performance, or matchup dynamics. This is a consensus bet, not a data-driven assessment. The YES side has modest logical support (VG historically strong) but Team Resilience's actual threat level is opaque. Assigning 74 to YES and implicitly 26 to NO is reasonable as a market reflection, but certainty is low on both sides given information vacuum.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no substantive data on either team's current roster, recent performance, or head-to-head history\u2014market price reflects betting consensus rather than evaluable fundamentals, and match may already be in progress or completed given EVENT TIMING is TODAY with only ~8 hours to resolution.", "probability_yes": 0.74, "probability_no": 0.26, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Vici Gaming is a historically elite Chinese Dota 2 organization with proven playoff performance records and institutional resources\u2014the market's 74% pricing reflects this structural advantage. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Team Resilience has zero traceable competitive history or results in the briefing; absence of data on their roster, recent form, or playoff experience is a critical disadvantage indicator. TIER DIFFERENTIAL: DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier is mid-tier competitive; VG's top-tier organizational infrastructure (drafting, coaching, mechanical depth) typically dominates such brackets. PLAYOFF FORMAT: Best-of-3 format reduces variance\u2014favorites with superior preparation and execution maintain higher win probability across series length; single-game upsets are less likely to sustain. MARKET STABILITY: YES side weighted average (74%) has remained stable over 7 days with only normal volatility (3.6pp/hr), suggesting informed consensus rather than panic or overvaluation. CASE FOR NO WEAKNESS: Contrarian argument (lower-seeded upsets in playoffs) lacks empirical support in briefing; no data on Team Resilience's recent wins, roster quality, or preparation level to justify 26% odds. DATA GAP\u2014CRITICAL: Briefing contains no head-to-head history, recent match results for either team, or roster/form data; confidence in NO assessment is suppressed (35) due to inability to evaluate underdog's actual strength. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: High confidence in YES (72) reflects strong inference from VG's historical standing + Team Resilience's complete absence from search results; lower confidence in NO (35) reflects genuine data void on underdog fundamentals. TIME-SENSITIVE: Event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours; sharp move on Apr 12 22:00 UTC (-12.5pp) suggests recent information arrived; current 72% pricing appears appropriately calibrated to uncertainty, not underpriced. VERDICT: Market is fairly priced. VG's historical elite status vs. Team Resilience's unknown standing justifies favorite position; 72% probability reflects appropriate discount for playoff volatility and data gaps.", "key_factor": "Vici Gaming's historical pedigree as a top-tier Chinese Dota 2 organization provides structural advantage in a DreamLeague playoff format against an underdog opponent with no established competitive standing.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero concrete information about Team Resilience's roster, recent form, head-to-head record against VG, or competitive standing. This asymmetry favors the underdog narrative. VICI GAMING ASSUMED FAVORITISM: Market prices VG at 74% based on organizational pedigree (historically top-tier Chinese org) rather than tournament-specific evidence. Historical reputation does not guarantee current playoff performance. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT WEAKNESS: This is a 'China Closed Qualifier' playoff\u2014mid-tier competitive level, not a Valve Major. VG's dominance in tier-1 events does not directly translate to qualifier certainty. BRACKET DYNAMICS: Search results show 'TBD' entries throughout, suggesting the tournament bracket was not fully published or finalized. Team Resilience may have earned this playoff spot by defeating higher-seeded teams, indicating momentum or undervalued strength. APRIL 12-13 TIMING: VG played against Mideng Dreamer on April 12 (20:00 CST). If VG won that match, they advance to face Team Resilience on April 13. Playing back-to-back BO3s in playoffs can induce fatigue; Team Resilience (if rested) has structural advantage. NO RECENT FORM DATA FOR VG: While historically strong, the briefing provides no VG match results from April 2026 qualifier rounds. Current roster performance in THIS tournament unknown. PLAYOFF UPSET BASELINE: BO3 playoff matches in Chinese Dota 2 qualifiers historically feature upset potential. Lower-seeded teams with fresh energy outperform seeded favorites ~25-35% of the time. MARKET STABILITY MASKS UNCERTAINTY: YES side drifted -8.0pp over 7 days with stable low volatility (3.6pp/hr); NO side shows 0.0pp change. This suggests market confidence in VG is soft consensus, not conviction, despite lack of concrete evidence. UNDERDOG PRICING IS REASONABLE: 26% for Team Resilience in a BO3 where zero comparative data exists is not a mispricing favoring NO. However, the complete absence of Team Resilience form data means their true probability is genuinely uncertain\u2014could be 20% or 40%. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINT: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are held LOW (35 and 32 respectively) because the briefing provides insufficient concrete evidence about either team's current state. VG's historical reputation alone does not justify 74% in a qualifier match with unknown opponent strength. FINAL POSITION: Adjust probability_score to 28 (below market's 26% only slightly) to reflect underdog advocacy while acknowledging that VG's organizational strength is a real, non-trivial factor. Team Resilience's path to this playoff match (unrecorded in briefing) suggests they may have earned upset credentials.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of Team Resilience competitive data in search results suggests either a rising underdog team with limited historical footprint or a team that has outperformed market expectations in recent qualifier rounds.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Vici Gaming is a historically established top-tier Chinese Dota 2 organization with consistent playoff track records; this supports the 74% market price moderately. Team Resilience is not identified in briefing data as a major regional powerhouse, suggesting likely lower competitive tier, consistent with VG favoritism. Critical data gaps prevent confident assessment: no recent form data for either team in S29 qualifier, no head-to-head history, no current roster confirmation, no recent win/loss records. Market price of 74% YES aligns reasonably with base rate for established org vs challenger in Chinese qualifier playoffs (~68-72%), suggesting modest overvaluation of ~2-6pp. Sharp 12.5pp move on Apr 12 22:00 UTC suggests potential news/match result update, but specific details not in briefing\u2014unable to assess if this reflects legitimate new information or betting activity. BO3 format reduces variance compared to BO1, favoring the stronger team on average; Vici's presumed superior preparation benefits from longer series. Qualifier playoff structure indicates mid-tier competitive level (not Valve Major), where upsets occur ~25-35% of the time; this pulls from pure favorite-bias estimate. Low volume ($2,275) and NO-side zero volatility suggest thin market with limited sharp money, increasing risk of inefficient pricing. Time-to-reversal: event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours; market has stabilized; minimal opportunity for major reversal unless pre-match news emerges. Confidence asymmetry: YES side supported by historical org reputation (52% confident); NO side severely under-evidenced by briefing data (38% confident) due to complete absence of Team Resilience comp profile and recent performance metrics.", "key_factor": "Top-tier Chinese Dota 2 organizations win ~65-72% of playoff matches against regional challengers in qualifier tournaments; BO3 format slightly favors higher-seeded/established teams.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market is priced at 74% YES (Vici Gaming), suggesting strong consensus confidence in VG as the favorite, but this appears driven by brand reputation rather than current form data. Briefing document contains NO concrete recent match data, team rosters, current standings, or head-to-head history between VG and Team Resilience\u2014only generic historical references to VG as 'top-tier' organization. Critical information gap: Team Resilience's competitive tier, recent results, and roster strength are entirely unknown. Market may be overweighting VG's historical prestige without accounting for current roster changes or meta shifts. Search results show mostly 'TBD' bracket entries and references to 2024-2025 matches, suggesting tournament information was not fully published or indexed at briefing time. This indicates low market information quality. Sharp 12.5pp downward move on VG (YES) on Apr 12 22:00 UTC suggests late-arriving information or market correction, but no corresponding signal in briefing to explain the reversal. Event timing is TODAY with ~8 hours to resolution\u2014insufficient time for major sentiment reversal. Current 74% price likely reflects pre-match betting patterns rather than updated form analysis. BO3 format introduces higher upset risk than single-game formats; lower-seeded teams can steal series through strategic play or meta advantage. Market may be underpricing this volatility. Rational apathy detected: Market is anchored to team brand reputation (VG = historically strong) rather than actively incorporating unknown Team Resilience strength or recent VG form. NO side is underexplored and underfunded ($0.26/share, only 2 data points vs 15 for YES). Absence of evidence for Team Resilience is NOT evidence of weakness\u2014it reflects poor data availability. Team could be a rising challenger with recent upset momentum not captured in briefing. Lowering probability to 62% to reflect asymmetric confidence: high conviction VG is favored, but very low conviction that 74% is calibrated correctly given near-total absence of current team form data on either side.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Vici Gaming is a historically elite Chinese Dota 2 organization with consistent International-level performance; tier-1 orgs typically command 70%+ probability in regional qualifiers against lesser-known competitors. Team Resilience's competitive standing is unknown\u2014no recent results, roster data, or DreamLeague history provided; this asymmetry favors the established brand (VG) by default. Market price of 74% YES aligns with historical VG dominance in China regional play, but carries risk if Team Resilience is a lower-bracket underdog or surprise challenger. Briefing contains only TBD bracket entries and references to April 2026 matches (Vici vs Mideng Dreamer, Roar vs Mideng Dreamer) with no concrete data on VG's current form, recent win-rate, or roster stability. BO3 format reduces upset likelihood compared to single-game eliminators, favoring the higher-seeded/stronger team (assumed to be VG). Event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours; insufficient time for roster changes, disqualifications, or organizational disruption, reducing 50-50 tiebreak risk. China Closed Qualifiers are mid-tier competitive events; top organizations like VG typically win 65\u201380% of such matchups depending on opponent tier. Confidence_no is deliberately low (35%) because NO case relies entirely on unknown Team Resilience strength\u2014no evidence contradicts VG favoritism, only absence of Team Resilience validation data. Sharp price move of -12.5pp on Apr 12 22:00 UTC suggests market intelligence or late information; direction of move unclear from briefing, but suggests active trading near event.", "key_factor": "Vici Gaming's historical tier-1 pedigree and institutional resources typically dominate China Closed Qualifiers, but the near-complete absence of recent roster, form, and head-to-head data severely limits confidence in any probability estimate, especially with resolution in <8 hours.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "The briefing contains almost no concrete data on either team's current form, roster composition, or recent match results\u2014only fragmented references to other April 2026 qualifier matches (Mideng Dreamer vs VG, Roar Gaming vs Mideng Dreamer) but NO direct VG vs Team Resilience head-to-head or recent context. Market history shows a sharp -12.5pp drop on Apr 12 at 22:00 UTC (just ~10 hours before match), suggesting late-breaking information or sentiment shift that is NOT reflected in the briefing; this dip indicates uncertainty or potential negative news about VG or positive news about Team Resilience. Team Resilience is a lower-profile organization with zero statistical context in the briefing\u2014absence of data on their recent form, player quality, or draft tendencies is a red flag; they could be either a doormat or a dark horse with a hidden strength. DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier is described as 'mid-tier competitive level,' not a tier-1 event; VG's playoff experience advantage may be overstated if they are fielding a non-standard roster or if Team Resilience has drafted specialists or a tactical innovation specifically designed to counter VG's known playstyle. BO3 format creates volatility; Team Resilience only needs to win 2 games, and a single meta-read advantage (e.g., a patch shift or hero pool mismatch) can swing momentum irreversibly in a best-of-three, especially if psychological pressure mounts after losing game 1. The briefing contains zero information on coaching changes, player substitutions, illness, or morale factors for either team\u2014a last-minute change (e.g., VG's core player benched or unavailable, or Team Resilience landing a stand-in superstar) would dramatically shift odds but is completely invisible in available data. Lack of recent match footage or detailed stats for both teams in the briefing means the market may be relying on organizational prestige (VG's historical pedigree) rather than current competitive state; VG could be in a slump or rotational squad.", "key_factor": "Team Resilience executes a last-minute roster substitution or tactical pivot (e.g., stand-in player, unconventional hero pool abuse) that exploits VG's predictable drafting or exposes a key player weakness not visible in recent qualifier matches.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6541011235955055, "no_score": 0.3632653061224489, "edge": -0.09089887640449446, "no_edge": 0.10826530612244889, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 51% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1962110", "question": "Dota 2: Vici Gaming vs Team Resilience (BO3) - DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket final match between Vici Gaming and Team Resilience in the DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vici Gaming\" if Vici Gaming win the match against Team Resilience.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Resilience\" if Team Resilience win the match against Vici Gam