{"run_id": "26e478bf-c126-4fa2-ac6d-81637478845d", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:05:40.395269+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1961349", "question": "Dota 2: Ivory vs Team Nemesis (BO3) - DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket final match between Ivory and Team Nemesis in the DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ivory\" if Ivory win the match against Team Nemesis.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Nemesis\" if Team Nemesis win the match against Ivory.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T12:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.305, "volume_usd": 743.588013, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["17849318444785003143523820667201947651127282081583700364979535480736658793830", "14086763538124304741722022802557813681757693679424402878797189760946851019848"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Ivory wins the BO3 Upper Bracket Final match vs Team Nemesis on April 13, 2026 at 8:00 AM ET. DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Ivory defeated Team Nemesis 2-1 in a recent BO3 on January 9, 2026\u2014this is the strongest direct evidence favoring Ivory. GROUP STAGE PLACEMENT: Team Nemesis finished 2nd (qualified to Closed Qualifier), while Ivory finished 4th (also qualified). This suggests Team Nemesis had stronger group stage performance. PLAYOFF PERFORMANCE DISPARITY: The brief shows Ivory lost 0-2 to Execration in playoffs, indicating potential struggles against elite teams. No equivalent playoff loss is documented for Team Nemesis in the brief. TEMPORAL GAP: The January 9 head-to-head is ~3 months old. Roster changes, meta shifts, and team development over that period are unknown. Current form cannot be assessed from briefing. MARKET SIGNAL: NO side (Team Nemesis) trades at 70%, suggesting informed traders believe Team Nemesis is favored despite Ivory's recent H2H win. This market repricing (NO +20.5pp in 7 days) suggests new information shifted odds materially toward Nemesis. VOLATILITY CONTEXT: The sharp move on Apr 12 (\u22129.5pp then +34.0pp on NO side) suggests recent news or roster/meta developments unfavorable to Ivory, but the brief does not document what changed. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence exists for Ivory's recent H2H win and direct competitive capability. However, evidence is stale and tournament context (playoff seeding, bracket position) is ambiguous. No counter-narrative is fully documented in brief (why Nemesis favored now when Ivory won recently?). CRITERIA CLARITY: Resolution criteria are clear\u2014first team to win the BO3 match resolves to their name. No ambiguity in team name matching (both are unambiguously identified in brief). DUAL-PERSPECTIVE: Ivory has recent direct H2H proof of superiority (2-1 win); Team Nemesis has superior group stage placement and apparent market consensus shift. Neither signal is overwhelming. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Market price (70% NO / 30% YES) reflects informed traders who likely have access to recent team form, roster status, and meta context not visible in this brief. Ivory's January H2H win provides 5\u201310pp floor of confidence, but the dramatic recent market move toward Nemesis (20.5pp in 7 days) suggests material new information has eroded Ivory's relative position. Setting probability_score at 32 (slightly above market YES of 30) to modestly credit the January H2H while respecting the market repricing.", "key_factor": "Briefing data contains match results from January 2026 (~3 months ago) but tournament bracket structure is unclear; verification of current rosters and recent form is impossible from provided sources.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET POSITIONING: NO is priced at 70%, reflecting market consensus that Team Nemesis is the stronger team. The 40pp confidence gap (70% vs 30%) is substantial and warrants examination of whether it is justified. SEEDING ADVANTAGE: Team Nemesis finished 2nd in group stage; Ivory finished 4th. In single-elimination playoffs, seeding typically correlates with team strength and recent form. A 2nd-place finish substantially outweighs a 4th-place finish as a predictor. HEAD-TO-HEAD TRAP: While Ivory won 2-1 vs Team Nemesis on January 9, 2026 (~3 months ago), this single match is insufficient to override group-stage data collected over the same qualifying period. The January result is a data point, not a reversal of the broader competitive hierarchy. PLAYOFF MOMENTUM: Ivory lost 0-2 to Execration in their playoff match (date unclear from briefing, but included in recent results). This 0-2 loss suggests Ivory struggles against elite opposition and has not translated their January win over Nemesis into sustained playoff success. TEAM NEMESIS CONSISTENCY: Team Nemesis reached the finals/upper bracket with a 2nd-place group finish, indicating more reliable performance across multiple matches rather than a single BO3 upset. EXECUTION IN CRITICAL ROUNDS: The briefing shows Team Nemesis qualified to the Closed Qualifier (indicating advancement from this qualifier stage), while Ivory's trajectory post-January is less clear. Team Nemesis appears more consistent in advancing. MARKET SHARP MOVES: The NO side experienced a +34.0pp move on Apr 12 23:00 UTC (within the last 12 hours), suggesting sharp/informed bettors are heavily backing Team Nemesis at this late stage. Combined with the prior -9.5pp move, this indicates volatility but net conviction toward NO. UNDERDOG CASE\u2014WEAK: The argument for Ivory rests primarily on a single January win and 4th-place group finish. Neither constitutes sufficient evidence to overcome a 2nd-place seeding in a knockout format where recent form matters more than three-month-old head-to-head results. ROSTER STABILITY NOTED: Briefing confirms roster data from January 2026 suggests stability, but Ivory's and Team Nemesis's current rosters are not explicitly compared. No evidence of roster instability or substitutions affecting either team. TIMING CRITICALITY: Event resolves TODAY (~8 hours from briefing timestamp). Very limited time for reversals; market prices and sharp money have effectively locked in. NO side's 70% pricing reflects strong consensus with little runway for sentiment shifts. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72%) reflects clear seeding hierarchy and group-stage data. Lower confidence in YES (35%) reflects reliance on a single dated head-to-head result and lack of recent playoff success evidence for Ivory.", "key_factor": "Team Nemesis's superior group-stage seeding (2nd vs 4th) combined with Ivory's recent 0-2 playoff loss to Execration indicates Team Nemesis has the edge in current form despite the January head-to-head result.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UNDERDOG'S STRONGEST ASSET: Ivory won the most recent direct encounter 2-1 vs Team Nemesis on January 9, 2026\u2014this is concrete, recent evidence of competitive superiority in a BO3 format against the exact opponent today. Head-to-head records often outweigh seeding in predicting rematches. SEEDING INVERSION SIGNAL: Ivory finished 4th while Team Nemesis finished 2nd in group stage, yet Ivory beat Nemesis 2-1 in their direct matchup. This inversion suggests either (a) Ivory's performance improved post-group-stage, (b) Nemesis had a seeding advantage but weaker direct matchup gameplay, or (c) meta/roster changes favored Ivory. The market may be over-weighting group stage placement without accounting for H2H superiority. TEAM NEMESIS CONTEXT GAP: The briefing provides limited recent performance data for Team Nemesis beyond their 2nd place group finish. No direct recent match results vs other playoff opponents are shown. The 70% pricing may reflect seeding optics rather than hard evidence of current form. IVORY'S PLAYOFF SHOWING: Ivory lost 0-2 to Execration in playoffs, confirming they faced the tournament favorite. However, this single loss does not invalidate their H2H win vs Nemesis\u2014different matchup dynamics apply. Execration beat both teams, establishing they are tier-1; Ivory and Nemesis are tier-2 contenders where H2H matters. MARKET VOLATILITY FAVORING YES: The YES side rose +4.0pp in 24 hours (29% \u2192 30%), while NO experienced wild swings (+20.5pp overall with +34.0pp spike then -9.5pp reversal on Apr 12). This volatility on the NO side suggests uncertainty and potential overpricing of the favorite; high volatility often indicates mispricing susceptibility. RECENCY & FORM DECAY: The group stage data is 3+ months old (January 9, 2026 matches referenced; current date April 13, 2026). In esports, roster changes, meta shifts, and player form can evolve significantly. Ivory's January H2H win is far more recent to today's match than group stage results from January. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence is 62 because Ivory's H2H victory is concrete and recent, directly supporting an upset case. NO confidence is lower at 48 because the briefing offers no specific recent performance snapshots for Team Nemesis post-group-stage, making it harder to defend their 70% pricing with hard evidence. RISK TO UPSET THESIS: Team Nemesis did finish 2nd (higher seed), and the broader tournament structure shows Execration \u226b Nemesis \u2248 Ivory. If the gap between 2nd and 4th seed is meaningful and stable, Nemesis should win. However, the briefing does not provide post-January match results for Nemesis to confirm their form held, creating asymmetric evidence favoring the upset. PLAYOFF BO3 FORMAT: This is a single BO3 match, not a series of games, increasing variance and making H2H precedent more predictive than seeding alone. Ivory's 2-1 win proves they can beat this opponent in exactly this format. MARKET MISPRICING HYPOTHESIS: At 30% YES, Ivory is priced as a 70-30 underdog despite having defeated Team Nemesis 2-1 in recent play. This appears to overweight seeding and underweight direct matchup evidence, suggesting YES is underpriced. A fair price given H2H might be 40-50% YES.", "key_factor": "Ivory's decisive 2-1 head-to-head victory over Team Nemesis on January 9, 2026 demonstrates a direct matchup advantage that contradicts their lower seeding and may reflect evolving form not fully captured by group stage results.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "SEEDING ADVANTAGE TO NEMESIS: Team Nemesis finished 2nd in group stage vs Ivory's 4th place. Historical data shows higher-seeded teams in single-elimination BO3s win approximately 65-70% of the time in regional qualifiers. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY FAVORS IVORY: Ivory defeated Team Nemesis 2-1 on January 9, 2026 (~3 months ago). This is the most recent direct matchup and typically carries significant weight (~20-25pp) in BO3 predictions, particularly when decisive (not razor-thin). CONFLICTING SIGNALS: Market currently prices YES at 30%, which underweights Ivory's recent head-to-head win. A team that beat their opponent 2-1 three months ago should trade higher than 30% in a direct rematch, all else equal. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT\u2014MIXED: Ivory lost 0-2 to Execration (1st seed), suggesting weakness vs top tier. However, Team Nemesis also finished 2nd, not 1st, implying similar tier. Execration's dominance does not clearly favor Nemesis over Ivory. ROSTER STABILITY ASSUMPTION: No roster changes explicitly documented between January and April 2026. Assuming stable rosters, the January 2-1 result is directly applicable. MARKET VOLATILITY & SHARP MOVES: NO side saw +34.0pp and -9.5pp moves on Apr 12, suggesting late information flow (possible team news, injury, or lineup issues). Without explicit briefing detail, this is flagged as unknown risk to both sides; confidence_no set lower due to opacity. BASE RATE LOGIC: Seeding advantage (~65-70% for 2nd seed) combined with head-to-head recency advantage (~20-25pp for recent winner) yields a pull toward 45-55% for Ivory. Market at 30% appears to overweight seeding and underweight recency. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT: Balancing seeding (favors Nemesis, ~65-70% base) against recent H2H win (favors Ivory, +20-25pp weight), estimated P(Ivory) \u2248 32-38%. Setting probability_score to 32 reflects slight Nemesis structural advantage but meaningful Ivory recency edge. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=62 reflects decent historical precedent for H2H recency in regional BO3s and clear Jan 2026 win. confidence_no=48 reflects uncertainty around late-stage market moves (sharp swings Apr 12) and lack of explicit negative information on Ivory in briefing.", "key_factor": "Southeast Asia Dota 2 qualifier BO3 matches: seeded/favored teams win ~65-70% of the time; head-to-head recency typically carries 15-25pp weight against seeding", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Market pricing at 30% YES aligns closely with concrete evidence: Team Nemesis finished 2nd in group stage vs Ivory's 4th place, a clear structural advantage. Head-to-head recency (Jan 9, 2026: Ivory won 2-1) is the strongest pro-YES signal in briefing, but it is ~3 months stale in esports terms\u2014roster changes, patch updates (7.40b), and meta shifts are material. Ivory's 0-2 loss to Execration in playoffs (shown in match history) signals vulnerability against top-tier opposition, contradicting the Jan 9 win narrative. Team Nemesis qualified directly from group stage (2nd seed) while Ivory finished 4th, indicating Team Nemesis had superior consistency across multiple matches, not just one BO3. Market has shown sharp volatility (Apr 12: -9.5pp then +34.0pp swing on NO side), suggesting late liquidity events (possible line updates from regional betting syndicates or insider confidence)\u2014this is rational repricing, not panic. NO side rose +20.5pp over 7 days while YES rose only +4.0pp, indicating gradual confidence shift toward Team Nemesis, not crowd exuberance\u2014steady repricing toward fundamentals. At 30% YES, market is NOT undervaluing Ivory's head-to-head win; it is correctly discounting it with proper weight to team seeding, recent tournament form, and time decay. Ivory has roster continuity (gohan, Ken, Rupido, Dric~, Grimz listed), as does Team Nemesis (23savage, Mac, Raven, Jhocam, Jaunuel), so team stability is not a confound. NO side confidence is moderate (55) due to: (1) reliance on group stage proxy when playoff form may differ, (2) limited recent match data between these teams post-January, (3) small market volume ($744 USD) means price may reflect local SEA bettor consensus rather than global sharp money. YES side confidence is higher (72) because the Jan 9, 2026 head-to-head result is hard evidence, even if stale; team identities are clear; and the 2-1 scoreline shows Ivory can compete with this opponent under known conditions. Market is pricing rationally: Team Nemesis slight favorite due to seeding + consistency, but Ivory retains meaningful 30% probability due to recent proven wins. This is not a mispricing driven by sentiment, but a fair odds split on limited but valid information.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY RISK: Ivory's 2-1 victory over Team Nemesis occurred on January 9, 2026. This market resolves April 13, 2026 \u2014 a 94-day gap in Dota 2 competitive play. The game received at least one major patch (7.40b referenced in briefing data), and roster compositions show player swaps (e.g., Ivory's position 1 changed from 'Karma\u4e36' to 'gohan' between January and later tournament appearances). This historical result has severely diminished predictive value. GROUP STAGE PLACEMENT DISPARITY: Team Nemesis finished 2nd in qualifying, Ivory finished 4th. This represents a two-seed advantage and suggests Team Nemesis demonstrated superior consistency over the full group stage round-robin (or equivalent format). In single-elimination playoffs, seeding reflects accumulated performance data. PLAYOFF PERFORMANCE SIGNAL: The briefing shows Ivory lost 0-2 to Execration (1st seed) in what appears to be an earlier playoff round. This suggests Ivory struggled against top-tier opposition when matched fairly. Team Nemesis's results against Execration are not shown in detail, but 2nd seed status implies more competitive standing. MARKET PRICE VOLATILITY & REVERSAL: NO side surged +20.5pp over 7 days with a massive +34.0pp spike on Apr 12 23:00 UTC, then corrected -9.5pp. This suggests late information (scrims, roster announcements, or insider knowledge) shifted sentiment sharply toward Team Nemesis. With ~8 hours to resolution, this move likely reflects genuine new evidence rather than noise. LOW VOLUME & SHARP REVERSALS: Only $744 USD traded; high volatility (10.5pp/hr on NO side) indicates thin liquidity and potential information asymmetry. Large late-stage reversals in low-volume markets often precede match-day news (roster confirmation, practice results, injury, or withdrawal rumors). META UNCERTAINTY: The 94-day gap between the January matchup and this April playoff likely coincides with multiple ranked season resets and meta shifts. Dota 2 hero viability and counter-picks shift dramatically with balance patches. Ivory's January win may reflect a meta no longer in play. CURRENT MARKET PRICE (70% NO) vs. HISTORICAL H2H: The market implies ~30% Ivory, yet Ivory beat Nemesis head-to-head recently. If the historical result alone were relevant, Ivory should trade higher. The divergence suggests the market has incorporated newer information (group stage seeding, recent form, rumors) that outweighs the January upset. CLOSED QUALIFIER CONTEXT: This is a qualifier to DreamLeague Season 28, meaning stakes and preparation intensity are high. Teams likely focused differently on group stage vs. playoff preparation. 4th place finishers often enter playoffs with less bye advantage and momentum, even if capable. ROSTER STABILITY CONCERN: Player name changes between tournament appearances suggest potential roster flux. If Ivory experienced mid-season roster changes after January (or before this April event), team synergy and mechanics may have degraded relative to Team Nemesis, which shows more stable rosters. CONFIDENCE SPLIT JUSTIFICATION: YES confidence (62) reflects the tangible January 2-1 result and reasonable belief that Ivory can still compete; NO confidence (58) is lower because Team Nemesis's recent form post-group-stage is not explicitly detailed in the briefing, and the late market reversal lacks clear public justification in the provided document. Confidence asymmetry reflects data gaps on both sides.", "key_factor": "The January 9 head-to-head victory by Ivory (2-1) is now 3+ months stale in a competitive environment where meta patches (7.40b shown), roster changes (player name differences visible between tournaments), and team chemistry evolution significantly alter matchup dynamics.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "ROSTER INSTABILITY (Ivory): The briefing shows two different Ivory rosters\u2014January 2026 featured Karma/Teehee, but the most recent squad lists gohan/Grimz. This is a core lineup shift that fundamentally changes team chemistry and playstyle, undermining the January 2-1 victory as predictive. STABLE OPPOSITION: Team Nemesis roster (23savage, Mac, Raven, Jhocam, Jaunuel) appears consistent across all documented matches, suggesting continuity in preparation and adaptation since January. GROUP STAGE SEEDING REVERSAL: Team Nemesis finished 2nd seed vs Ivory's 4th, a meaningful gap that reflects extended tournament performance, not a single BO3. The January win may have been a meta/draft anomaly rather than structural superiority. PLAYOFF TOURNAMENT FATIGUE: Ivory faced Execration (1st seed) in prior playoffs and lost 0-2, indicating struggles against top-tier competition when stakes are highest. No equivalent recent data shows Team Nemesis in playoff collapse scenarios. META/PATCH EVOLUTION: The briefing references Dota 7.40b with January match data; ~3 months of patches (Jan\u2192Apr) likely shifted hero viability. Ivory's January draft success may no longer apply if their core heroes were nerfed. SHARP MARKET MOVEMENT SIGNAL: NO side jumped +34pp on Apr 12 23:00 UTC, then dropped 9.5pp\u2014suggesting late information (roster change confirmation, injury, or scrimmage result) that retail traders reacted to. This volatility is a red flag for Ivory, not a contrarian buy signal. PSYCHOLOGICAL EDGE: Team Nemesis secured higher seeding in group stage despite January loss, suggesting either tactical adjustment or improved mental resilience. Teams that recover from losses often outperform regression to prior form. INSUFFICIENT RECENT DATA: No documented matches between Ivory and Team Nemesis post-January; the briefing is silent on their spring 2026 performance, match histories after Jan, or injury/substitution rationale. This silence on a 3-month gap is conspicuous. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) reflects Team Nemesis's structural advantage (seeding, roster stability). Confidence in YES is deliberately suppressed (35) due to unresolved roster changes and lack of recent data to validate the January precedent.", "key_