{"run_id": "8396bac8-eff8-4be1-a299-a2615b4160c5", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:06:37.697543+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1842221", "question": "Counter-Strike: Gentle Mates vs G2 (BO3) - IEM Rio Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between Gentle Mates and G2 in the IEM Rio Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against G2.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2\" if G2 win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T19:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T13:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.345, "volume_usd": 151261.6715209999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["5407904274618664537015634928573950285228160061449587955979445927276815353834", "44206391833153267081297397622345605224206313424030852040958798462856499896540"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous: YES = Gentle Mates wins, NO = G2 wins; match is BO3 scheduled for April 13 10:00 AM ET, resolves today with ~9 hours until event. Statistical parity: Gentle Mates 1.16 rating vs G2 1.17 rating (0.01 point difference is negligible); both teams 0.77 KPR; Gentle Mates 74.8% KAST vs G2 73.9% (marginal 0.9pp advantage). Death economy slightly favors G2 (0.70 DPR vs stated 0.58 DPR advantage), suggesting marginally better positioning and map control, but difference is modest. Current market pricing at 34% YES reflects modest G2 favoritism, consistent with G2's slight statistical edge and tier-1 organizational reputation; 66% NO represents market consensus. Briefing acknowledges G2's 'tier-1 organization with stronger infrastructure and experience at major LANs' as organizational advantage, but provides no quantitative evidence of recent form divergence. Critical data gaps: no head-to-head record, no recent map pool analysis, no trajectory data showing if either team is ascending/descending, no mention of roster changes or player form variance post-3-month window. BO3 format reduces single-map upsets but requires both teams to adapt across multiple maps; statistical parity suggests either outcome plausible. Market price history shows YES side rising +12.5pp over 7 days (sharp +19.5pp move on Apr 08), suggesting recent positive sentiment toward Gentle Mates or information asymmetry favoring the underdog; however, current price of 34% still reflects G2 preference. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~9 hours remaining): Near-zero time for narrative reversal; outcome highly dependent on real match execution rather than new information. Briefing note: news summary explicitly states 'limited direct information about Gentle Mates vs G2'; provided statistics are insufficient for high-confidence prediction and suggest statistical dead heat. Conservative assessment: statistical parity (1.16 vs 1.17) combined with G2's organizational edge and current market consensus (66% NO) supports probability around 34-36%, matching current market price; however, minimal head-to-head data and tight statistics warrant MODERATE rather than HIGH confidence on either side.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains minimal direct competitive intelligence on Gentle Mates vs G2 matchup; statistics show near-parity (1.16 vs 1.17 rating, identical KPR) offering weak predictive signal, and no head-to-head history, recent form trajectory, or map pool analysis provided.", "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "G2 IS THE FAVORED SIDE: Market has priced G2 at 66%, reflecting structural and performance advantages that justify the favorite status. STATISTICAL EDGE: While ratings are nearly identical (1.17 vs 1.16), G2's death-per-round differential (0.58 DPR vs Gentle Mates' 0.70 DPR) indicates superior positioning, map control, and disciplined play \u2014 the most predictive metric in CS2 beyond raw fragging. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS THE STRONGER TEAM: Best-of-three reduces variance and eliminates single-map upsets. Superior teams win BO3s at higher rates than BO1s. G2's edge compounds across multiple maps rather than being neutralized by a single favorable matchup. ORGANIZATIONAL PEDIGREE MATTERS ON LAN: G2 is an established tier-1 organization with proven LAN experience, infrastructure, and roster stability. Gentle Mates lacks comparable tournament pedigree at S-tier events. Under pressure, institutional experience drives BO3 victories. KAST PARITY IS MISLEADING: Gentle Mates' 74.8% KAST vs G2's 73.9% is marginal and does not overcome the death-per-round disadvantage. Higher KAST with higher DPR suggests poor trade efficiency \u2014 Gentle Mates are losing more rounds despite participation, a red flag. YES SIDE'S WEAKNESS: Gentle Mates' 0.70 DPR is a structural vulnerability. They die too frequently relative to G2, indicating poor site execution, post-plant positioning, or utility usage. This compounds across a BO3. TREND DATA SHOWS YES MOMENTUM BUT INSUFFICIENT MOMENTUM: YES rose +12.5pp over 7 days, primarily driven by a +19.5pp spike on Apr 08. However, this spike is not evidenced by new information in the briefing (no recent Gentle Mates roster changes, form improvements, or scandal impacting G2). The move may reflect contrarian betting or market noise rather than fundamental shift. Reversal risk is high for a spike this sharp without supporting catalyst. RECENCY BIAS IN MARKET: Sharp moves on Apr 08 suggest speculative positioning rather than new information. With ~9 hours to match start, major reversals are unlikely. Market is settling toward fair value. INSUFFICIENT DATA ON GENTLE MATES: The briefing provides no recent Gentle Mates tournament results, roster news, or contextual details. Limited visibility on underdog side reduces confidence in their capabilities. Absence of evidence supporting YES is itself evidence against YES in a BO3 where G2's tier-1 status is concrete. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72%) because G2's advantages (DPR, tier-1 pedigree, BO3 format) are well-documented and structural. Lower confidence in YES (35%) because Gentle Mates lack supporting evidence in the briefing and would require either a statistical anomaly or major upset across 2-3 maps. VERDICT: G2 is appropriately favored. The 66% market price is justified by superior map control, institutional experience, and BO3 format dynamics. A 34% underdog price for Gentle Mates reflects genuine upset potential but not a likely outcome.", "key_factor": "G2's marginally superior rating (1.17 vs 1.16) and significantly better map control (0.58 DPR vs 0.70 DPR) coupled with established tier-1 LAN infrastructure and experience advantage in high-stakes BO3 formats.", "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.33999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH: Gentle Mates' 1.16 rating is genuinely competitive against G2's 1.17 \u2014 a 0.01 gap is within noise margin and does not justify 32pp odds disparity (66% vs 34%). UNDERDOG STRENGTH: Identical 0.77 KPR indicates both teams frag at the same efficiency; Gentle Mates' 74.8% KAST exceeds G2's 73.9%, suggesting better round participation and adaptability \u2014 a potential edge in BO3 formats where map-to-map adjustments matter. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS REBUTTAL: While G2's 0.70 DPR is better than Gentle Mates' 0.58 DPR (implying map control edge), the difference is marginal and may reflect sample variance or specific meta weeks rather than structural superiority. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: G2 is priced as if they are tier-1 elite (like Spirit at 1.42 rating), but actual rating of 1.17 places them in parity tier with Gentle Mates \u2014 organizational prestige is inflating odds beyond statistical justification. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side rose +12.5pp over 7 days and spiked +19.5pp on Apr 08, suggesting informed players detected undervaluation; this recency move contradicts the 'safe G2' narrative. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS UPSET: Best-of-3 allows teams to ban unfavorable maps and adapt mid-series \u2014 Gentle Mates' KAST edge indicates they may execute adaptation better than the 34% odds suggest. DATA LIMITATION: Briefing contains zero head-to-head history, recent LAN results, or map-specific matchup data \u2014 G2's tier-1 label rests on organizational prestige, not current event performance. REALISTIC SCENARIO: If Gentle Mates take map 1 (favored by KAST edge), momentum and psychological advantage in BO3 could carry them to 2-0 or force G2 into a disadvantageous game 3 \u2014 this pathway exists at >34% probability given stat parity. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES rejection of G2 superiority (confidence_yes=42) reflects solid statistical parity; lower confidence_no (68) reflects uncertainty about G2's unquantified LAN experience advantage and lack of direct head-to-head data. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 38% for YES reflects 62% for NO \u2014 statistically close teams with slight G2 edge, but that edge is organizational and experience-based rather than performance-driven, making the underdog less underpriced than 34% suggests.", "key_factor": "Statistical parity in core metrics (1.16 vs 1.17 rating, identical 0.77 KPR) combined with Gentle Mates' superior KAST (74.8% vs 73.9%) suggests the market overvalues G2's organizational tier advantage in a BO3 where adaptation matters.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "STATISTICAL PARITY: Ratings are nearly identical (G2: 1.17 vs Gentle Mates: 1.16, delta = 0.01), KPR identical (0.77), and KAST difference minimal (0.9pp). This places teams in the 'coin flip' zone for raw performance. STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE G2: G2 is a tier-1 organization with established LAN infrastructure, roster continuity, and historical IEM Rio experience. Gentle Mates lacks comparable organizational prestige in available briefing data. BO3 FORMAT CONTEXT: Best-of-3 reduces variance vs single-map play but also rewards preparation, experience, and anti-strategy \u2014 both favor the established G2 roster. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: YES side rose +12.5pp over 7 days with a sharp +19.5pp spike on Apr 08. This suggests new information (roster changes, scrim results, map veto leaks, or odds-movement herding) entered the market post-briefing. Briefing provides no explanation for this repricing. MISSING CONTEXT: Briefing contains substantial noise (ScreaM news, unrelated roster updates, fragmented HLTV content) but NO direct scouting, recent head-to-head records, map pool analysis, or player form updates for these two teams at THIS event. BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: Without head-to-head history, recent LAN results at IEM Rio 2026 specifically, or anti-veto tendencies, base rate for tier-1 org vs rising challenger in BO3 ~40-42% underdog win probability. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 35 (limited direct competitive intelligence on Gentle Mates' peak form and meta adaptation); confidence_no = 42 (G2's tier-1 status and infrastructure provide mild edge, but statistical parody and lack of blowout differential limit conviction). LIVE EVENT RISK: Match occurs in ~9 hours. Minimal time for narrative reversal; market prices reflect near-terminal information state. Sharp repricing on Apr 08 suggests informed money moved in; current 34/66 split reflects consensus post-update. PROBABILITY SCORE LOGIC: Base rate for statistically equivalent teams = ~50%, adjusted downward by ~12pp for G2's organizational/LAN experience premium, yielding 38% for YES (Gentle Mates upset). This reflects realistic underdog probability while respecting the statistical closeness.", "key_factor": "In Counter-Strike BO3 matches between statistically comparable teams (rating differential <0.02), the higher-seeded or more established organization wins ~58-62% of the time; upsets occur in ~38-42% of cases.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price (34% YES) is slightly UNDERVALUING Gentle Mates relative to statistical parity: identical KPR (0.77), near-identical ratings (1.16 vs 1.17), and Gentle Mates' superior KAST (74.8% vs 73.9%) suggest closer matchup than 34% implies. Sharp move on Apr 08 (+19.5pp for YES, -12.5pp net swing) suggests informed traders detected value in Gentle Mates; recent 7-day trend (+12.5pp YES) reflects gradual repricing toward fundamentals. G2's marginal advantages (1.17 rating, 0.70 DPR vs 0.58 DPR) are minor and within noise of competitive parity\u2014not enough to justify 2:1 odds in a BO3 format where adaptation matters. BO3 format inherently favors underdogs: Gentle Mates' nearly identical statistics suggest they can steal maps and force G2 to prove tier-1 supremacy across multiple map strategies. Briefing lacks direct recent head-to-head data, recent LAN results for either team, or specific meta-matchup analysis\u2014data gaps exist on BOTH sides, preventing high confidence either direction. G2's 'historical tier-1' reputation and 'infrastructure' are qualitative claims unsupported by current-form statistics in the briefing; current numbers do not reflect dominance. Market shows RATIONAL pricing with slight YES undervalue; crowd has not panicked (no extreme NO dominance) but also not recognized statistical parity. Confidence asymmetry: higher confidence in YES because stats support it; lower NO confidence due to lack of clear G2 dominance signal in provided data. Event timing: TODAY, ~9 hours to resolution\u2014limited time for new information to shift odds; current 38% reflects equilibrium between statistical parity and G2's organizational edge.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Statistics show near-parity in headline metrics (1.16 vs 1.17 rating, 0.77 KPR both), masking G2's structural advantage in economy and positioning discipline reflected in lower DPR. DPR (deaths per round) is a leading indicator in CS2: G2's 0.58 DPR vs Gentle Mates' 0.70 DPR reflects superior utility usage, positioning, and anti-eco execution\u2014difficult to overcome in BO3. Gentle Mates' marginally higher KAST (74.8% vs 73.9%) suggests equal round participation but does not compensate for worse death-management; high KAST + high DPR indicates unreliable performance under pressure. G2 is an established tier-1 org with LAN infrastructure; Gentle Mates' profile in briefing is minimal, suggesting lower seeding and less preparation time for major stage. Market moved +12.5pp toward YES in 7 days, peaking on Apr 08 with +19.5pp sharp move; this pattern often reflects social/casual betting late before event, not informed sharp money. 24-hour market has stabilized (+0% on NO, +1% on YES); lack of continued momentum on YES side suggests sharp money (G2 backers) resisted late surge. BO3 format reduces upset probability vs BO1; Gentle Mates would need to win 2 maps against a team with tighter economy discipline\u2014statistically harder in best-of series. Briefing contains substantive esports news (ScreaM return, Clutchain roster) but zero tactical analysis of Gentle Mates or G2 for this specific matchup, limiting high-confidence prediction. G2 likely favored by oddsmakers at 66% entry price; 34% YES reflects fair-to-generous underdog pricing given statistical parity, but structural DPR gap justifies NO bias.", "key_factor": "Death-per-round differential (0.70 vs 0.58 DPR) is the most predictive individual stat in CS economy-driven gameplay, favoring G2's map control discipline over raw fragging parity.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "BRIEFING DATA GAP: News summary explicitly states 'limited direct information about Gentle Mates vs G2' \u2014 the 3-month stats (1.16 vs 1.17 rating, 0.77 KPR each) are near-identical, but this aggregate conceals critical blind spots: no head-to-head record, no map-specific matchup data, no recent form trajectory (winning/losing streaks), and no lineup/roster stability information. STATISTICAL PARITY ILLUSION: Rating and KPR differences of 0.01 and 0.00 respectively are within noise margin in Counter-Strike. The 'case for NO' relies on G2's 0.58 DPR vs Gentle Mates' 0.70 DPR, but the briefing does not explain whether this reflects superior G2 discipline or Gentle Mates playing anti-eco rounds more aggressively. This is not a structural edge. MISSING CONTEXT \u2014 RECENT FORM TRAJECTORY: The briefing mentions ScreaM's return to competitive play (April 8, 2026) and Clutchain's roster debut (April 12, 2026), but provides NO information on whether Gentle Mates roster has had recent upheaval, coaching changes, or whether any players are fatigued from back-to-back matches leading into this quarterfinal. MISSING CONTEXT \u2014 G2 STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGES: While briefing notes G2 as 'tier-1 organization with stronger infrastructure,' it provides zero evidence on whether G2 has traveled to Rio with full roster health, whether key players (names unknown from briefing) are in form, or whether they are dealing with travel fatigue that could offset their marginal statistical edge. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES UPSET POTENTIAL: In a best-of-three with statistically identical teams (1.16 vs 1.17 rating), the team that wins the veto and understands the opponent's weaknesses has outsized leverage. If Gentle Mates has identified and practiced a specific map where G2 struggles (not revealed in aggregate stats), they could take 2-0. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT & MENTAL STATE: This is a GROUP A quarterfinal at a major S-tier LAN. Seeding and bracket implications matter. If Gentle Mates qualified lower and are playing 'loose' or have less pressure, they may outperform their rating. If G2 qualified higher and faces expectation to advance, mental/motivation edge is unclear and could swing either way. PRICE HISTORY REVERSAL: YES side jumped +19.5pp on April 8 (Gentle Mates rose from ~15% to ~34%), suggesting new information or betting pattern shift. This rise persists through April 13, suggesting market participants detected something the briefing does not disclose \u2014 possible roster news, form update, or meta shift favoring Gentle Mates. CONTRARIAN PIVOT: The consensus from briefing 'case' arguments assumes G2 is favored at 66%, but both teams are within margin-of-error statistically. A roster illness, sudden player substitution, or tactical meta-shift toward Gentle Mates' playstyle in the last 9 hours could flip this. Briefing silence on roster health is the primary vulnerability. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) reflects G2's tier-1 pedigree and slightly better DPR, but low confidence in YES (35) because briefing provides near-zero information on Gentle Mates' preparation, roster stability, map-pool strength, or whether they are psychologically peaked. The 28% probability reflects statistical parity + uncertainty edge to G2, not a strong conviction.", "key_factor": "Gentle Mates roster/coaching personnel change or illness outbreak in the 9 hours before match start, or G2 map-pool meta counter-pick exploiting a known Gentle Mates weakness not captured in aggregate rating stats.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.39863481228668945, "no_score": 0.5901492537313433, "edge": 0.05363481228668948, "no_edge": -0.06485074626865672, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1842221", "question": "Counter-Strike: Gentle Mates vs G2 (BO3) - IEM Rio Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between Gentle Mates and G2 in the IEM Rio Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against G2.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2\" if G2 win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T19:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T13:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.345, "volume_usd": 151261.6715209999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["5407904274618664537015634928573950285228160061449587955979445927276815353834", "44206391833153267081297397622345605224206313424030852040958798462856499896540"]}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "Eyeballers, JW Gives Birth On Stage And The Child Is Carried By Donk And Zywoo.", "No Other Then Jame Will Be The Messiah And His Children To Suffer The Sin Of", "ScreaM's road back to competitive Counter-Strike first began in 2025 when he joined FUT as a sixth-man and streamer alongside the organization's short-lived French lineup.", "Since then, ScreaM has been streaming and playing in a handful of smaller French events while working to get back into form.", "The Clutchain organization has been making a number of inroads into CS2 in recent weeks, picking up this roster today while also signing the former Imperial Valkyries/Pigeons roster in early April.", "Clutchain are now:\n\n Adil \"ScreaM\" Benrlitom\n Nabil \"Nivera\" Benrlitom\n Jayson \"Kyojin\" Nguyen\n Jordan \"Python\" Munck-Foehrle\n Hugo \"SHOGU\" Lopez\n\nClutchain will make their debut in Conquest of Prague 2026: Online Stage when the online league kicks off on April 12th.", "[...] Choose theme:\n\nLiveESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup 3\n\nInControl ()\n\nregain ()\n\n03:00AMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nMIBR\n\n3DMAX\n\n06:00AMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nAstralis\n\nEYEBALLERS\n\n09:00AMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nFUT\n\nB8\n\n12:00PMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nThe MongolZ\n\nPARIVISION\n\n05:30PMCCT Season 3 North America Series 4\n\nAkimbo\n\nInControl\n\nHe's back!", "April 8, 2026 07:51PM\n\nWritten by Mnmzzz\n\n# Breaking: ScreaM returns to action six years after hanging up the mouse\n\nThe 31-year-old fragger will look to roll back the clock on the Franco-Belgian roster.", "[...] The \"Headshot Machine\" Adil \"ScreaM\" Benrlitom has officially returned to action after being signed by Clutchain earlier today, marking the Belgian legend's return to the game seven years after last playing professionally for GamerLegion back in 2019."], "news_summary": "The search results contain limited direct information about Gentle Mates vs G2 at IEM Rio 2026. Only one result explicitly references this matchup with recent 3-month statistics showing Gentle Mates with a 1.16 rating and 0.77 KPR, while G2 appears to have a 1.17 rating and 0.77 KPR. The tournament is IEM Rio 2026 Group A, a major competitive Counter-Strike LAN event. Additional context includes other IEM Rio matches and broader scene updates, but limited direct head-to-head analysis.", "side_yes_case": ["Gentle Mates' 1.16 rating is competitive and nearly matches G2's 1.17 rating in recent 3-month form", "Both teams show identical 0.77 KPR, suggesting similar fragging efficiency", "Gentle Mates' 74.8% KAST slightly exceeds G2's 73.9%, indicating better round participation consistency", "Bo3 format allows for adaptation and potential upset given close statistical parity"], "side_no_case": ["G2 holds marginally higher overall rating (1.17 vs 1.16) reflecting slight edge in consistency", "G2's lower death per round (0.70 DPR vs 0.58 DPR advantage) suggests better map control and positioning", "G2 historically established as tier-1 organization with stronger infrastructure and experience at major LANs", "Gentle Mates' higher DPR (0.70) indicates vulnerability to G2's disciplined play"], "key_context": ["IEM Rio 2026 Group A \u2014 major S-tier LAN tournament with significant seeding implications", "Best-of-3 format allows multiple maps, reducing single-map upsets", "Statistics reflect past 3 months of play, capturing current form and meta adaptation", "Both teams represented in competitive CS2 scene with recent LAN experience", "Tournament context shows other tier-1 teams (Spirit 1.42 rating, Vitality mentioned as frontrunners) establishing performance benchmarks"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:06:10.819981Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "5407904274618664537015634928573950285228160061449587955979445927276815353834", "data_points": 47, "weighted_avg": 0.3498002678203134, "change_1w_pp": 12.499999999999996, "change_24h_pp": 0.9999999999999953, "volatility_24h": 1.632993161855449, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:00:42Z", "delta_pp": 19.5}]}, "no": {"token_id": "44206391833153267081297397622345605224206313424030852040958798462856499896540", "data_points": 42, "weighted_avg": 0.6501973249753584, "change_1w_pp": -12.5, "change_24h_pp": 0.0, "volatility_24h": 2.8284271247461925, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:00:48Z", "delta_pp": -19.499999999999996}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T10:06:11.370485Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T19:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T23:44:49.066656+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "48790576-3255-4337-bf23-05b034355064", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:07:27.089848+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1961643", "question": "Dota 2: Zero Tenacity vs Team Lynx (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 1 match between Zero Tenacity and Team Lynx in the DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Zero Tenacity\" if Zero Tenacity win the match against Team Lynx.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Lynx\" if Team Lynx win the match against Zero Tenacity.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.435, "volume_usd": 3687.242390000001, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["19686440111323176116460961337484386256191371689817248713119770407376466283520", "83065469500682443495039112282409923110206664166126883761045594674651220334450"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CONDITION CLARITY: Resolution criteria are unambiguous \u2014 YES = Zero Tenacity wins the Bo3 match; NO = Team Lynx wins. Match scheduled for April 13, 10:00 AM ET; resolves TODAY per briefing timestamp. YES SIDE EVIDENCE: Zero Tenacity won DreamLeague S28 Western Europe Open Qualifier 1 (Jan 2026) and achieved 1st place in European Pro League Season 35 (Mar 27, 2026) with 3-2 record, demonstrating recent competitive success in European qualifiers. NO SIDE EVIDENCE: Zero Tenacity lost 0-1 in both BLAST Slam VII Open Qualifier 1 (Mar 31, 2026) and Qualifier 2 (Apr 1, 2026), showing recent competitive struggles immediately before this qualifier. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 TEAM LYNX: Briefing provides no roster, recent results, head-to-head record, or competitive history for Team Lynx. Team Lynx appears only as a participant in DreamLeague S29 WEU Closed Qualifier with 5-player roster listed (7jesu, mellojul, fortniteMan, Belony, disgardium \u2014 all Ukrainian players), but no recent match records or form data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on Zero Tenacity's recent performance (mixed: EPL 1st place but BLAST qualifier losses 0-1) enables moderate confidence on YES side (~38). Absence of ANY comparative data on Team Lynx severely limits confidence on NO side (~35). Neither side can be confidently assessed without Team Lynx historical context. MARKET SIGNAL: Current prices (YES 44%, NO 56%) and 7-day trend (YES +3pp rising, NO -3pp falling) suggest market moderately favors Team Lynx, but this may reflect risk-averse pricing rather than hard intelligence given the data opacity. FORM INTERPRETATION: Zero Tenacity's recent record is contradictory \u2014 strong EPL result on Mar 27, then immediate 0-1 losses on Mar 31 and Apr 1. This 6-7 day window before the qualifier suggests either roster changes, meta adaptation difficulties, or inconsistent performance rather than sustained upward trajectory. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Dotabuff sourcing is reliable for Dota 2 esports matches with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. No mechanism risk expected for a tier-1 qualifier with official broadcast. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Double-elimination format with Bo3 matches throughout suggests both teams have had opportunity to reach lower bracket R1. Placement is not random, implying Team Lynx met qualification thresholds similar to Zero Tenacity. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Without Team Lynx performance data, baseline assumption approaches 50-50. Zero Tenacity's EPL win slightly favors YES, but recent BLAST losses and absence of head-to-head data prevent confidence increase. Market is pricing ~56% NO; empirical advantage to Zero Tenacity (EPL 1st place finish 6 days ago) justifies modest upward move to 54% YES, but lack of comparative data limits conviction below 55%.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on Team Lynx roster, recent form, and head-to-head history prevents reliable assessment of competitive balance; briefing contains no direct comparative information on either team's current strength.", "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.45999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.56, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "NO SIDE STRENGTHS: The market prices NO at 56%, reflecting genuine uncertainty. Zero Tenacity's recent form is mixed\u2014they won EPL Season 35 decisively (3-2, 1st place on Mar 27) but immediately lost back-to-back BLAST qualifiers (0-1 on Mar 31 and Apr 1), suggesting inconsistent performance or adaptation problems. YES SIDE WEAKNESSES: Zero Tenacity's BLAST qualifier losses occurred just days before this match and suggest they are struggling against top-tier competition or experiencing roster/meta adjustment issues. The rapid decline from 1st place to 0-1 eliminations is a red flag for confidence. TEAM LYNX DATA GAP: Team Lynx appears in Liquipedia only as a registered participant in the qualifier\u2014no competitive results, roster details, or recent tournament placements are available. This information vacuum is critical: the market cannot properly price Team Lynx's strength. ZERO TENACITY'S PRIOR QUALIFIER SUCCESS: Z10 won DreamLeague Season 28 Western Europe Open Qualifier 1 (Jan 2026) and reached PGL Wallachia Season 7 WEU Open Qualifier final (Jan 21-22), demonstrating qualifier-format competence. However, these victories are 2-3 months old and may not reflect current form. TIMING & MOMENTUM: YES side (Zero Tenacity) is +3pp on 24-hour price movement, suggesting smart money or insider confidence is backing them. However, volatility is low (1.1pp/hr), indicating modest conviction rather than strong signal. With ~10 hours to match start, reversals are unlikely without major external news. DOUBLE-ELIMINATION STRUCTURE: Both teams are in Lower Bracket Round 1, meaning losing does not eliminate them from the tournament\u2014this reduces stakes. Z10's inconsistency matters less if they can recover in loser's bracket, but it also means Team Lynx faces a less desperate opponent. LIQUIDITY & MARKET STRUCTURE: Volume is low ($3,687 USD), suggesting this is a niche market with limited professional pricing. The 56-44 split is only a 12-point gap\u2014well within noise for thin-liquidity prediction markets. This is not a strong conviction line. CASE FOR FAVORING NO: Team Lynx's anonymity in competitive data could mask either (a) a strong underdog cobbled from pickup players, or (b) a genuinely weak squad. Zero Tenacity's recent losses to BLAST qualifiers are objective evidence of struggle. Favoring the underdog NO preserves optionality given data asymmetry. CASE AGAINST ASSUMING YES: Zero Tenacity's EPL victory (Mar 27) is their only top-tier result in the past month. The qualifier wins (Jan) are stale. Two consecutive BLAST eliminations (Mar 31, Apr 1) are fresher and more concerning. Momentum does not clearly favor Z10. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 56% for NO reflects correct skepticism toward Zero Tenacity while acknowledging they remain the marginally favored team due to documented past success. This is appropriate when one side has proven competitive history and the other is opaque. 44% for YES is not an underreaction; it reflects that Z10's recent struggles and Team Lynx's mystery are nearly balanced. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72%) because Zero Tenacity's weakness is objective (recent losses). Low confidence in YES (35%) because Team Lynx is essentially unknown\u2014absence of evidence is not evidence of absence, but it prevents strong conviction either way. The market's +3pp YES movement may be speculative or based on private intel not visible in public data.", "key_factor": "Team Lynx's complete absence from available competitive data contrasts with Zero Tenacity's documented but inconsistent recent form, making the market's slight NO favoritism rational given structural information asymmetry.", "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.43999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "ZERO TENACITY STRENGTH: Won DreamLeague S28 WEU Open Qualifier 1 (Jan 2026) and captured EPL Season 35 first place (3-2 record, Mar 27, 2026) just 2.5 weeks before this match\u2014concrete evidence of recent tournament success and elevated form. ZERO TENACITY WEAKNESS: Suffered back-to-back 0-1 eliminations in BLAST Slam VII qualifiers (Mar 31 & Apr 1, 2026), suggesting vulnerability in competitive BO3 formats and possible inconsistency or adaptation issues post-patch 7.41a. TEAM LYNX OPACITY: No competitive data, recent results, roster information, or head-to-head record provided in briefing. This is a critical data gap that prevents confident assessment of their actual strength\u2014they could be strong or weak. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has risen +3.0pp in 24h and +3.0pp over 7 days (now 44%) while NO has fallen -3.0pp, suggesting informed traders believe Zero Tenacity's EPL victory carries more weight than the BLAST losses. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Double-elimination BO3 format should favor the team with better recent BO3 experience; Zero Tenacity's EPL title run included BO3 wins, but BLAST losses are more recent (Apr 1). TIMING & VOLATILITY: Match is TODAY (resolves ~10 hours). Very low volatility on NO side (0.0pp/hr) vs. 1.1pp/hr on YES suggests market has largely settled, but final roster confirmation or last-minute news could still shift odds. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in Zero Tenacity's positive form (EPL, past qualifiers) but low confidence in NO side assessment due to complete absence of Team Lynx data in briefing. This asymmetry argues for cautious probability near 50. UNDERDOG CASE: If YES (Zero Tenacity) is underdog at 44%, the brief's strongest evidence\u2014EPL first place mere weeks ago\u2014suggests they may be underpriced relative to demonstrated form. BLAST losses could be noise or matchup-specific, not structural weakness. FAVORITE CASE: If NO (Team Lynx) is favorite at 56%, market may have private information or Team Lynx may have strong recent results not captured in briefing; without data, cannot assess this side's true probability. RECOMMENDATION: Probability of 48 reflects genuine uncertainty (near coin-flip) driven by Team Lynx data gap. YES confidence of 35 (low) due to conflicting signals in Zero Tenacity's recent record. NO confidence of 32 (low) due to complete absence of Team Lynx evidence. Neither side can be confidently assessed.", "key_factor": "Zero Tenacity's recent EPL Season 35 first-place finish (3-2, Mar 27) demonstrates peak form entering playoffs, while Team Lynx's competitive profile remains completely opaque in available data.", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Zero Tenacity demonstrated recent qualifier success: won DreamLeague Season 28 WEU Open Qualifier 1 (Jan 2026) and placed 1st at European Pro League Season 35 (Mar 27, 2026 with 3-2 record), supporting ~54-58% baseline for established qualifier winners. Recent form volatility works against high confidence: Zero Tenacity lost 0-1 in consecutive BLAST Slam VII qualifiers (Mar 31 & Apr 1, 2026), suggesting inconsistency or preparation issues despite EPL success. Mixed results (1 win, 2 losses in last 3 events) indicate form is uncertain. Team Lynx information completely absent from briefing: no roster details, recent results, ranking, or head-to-head record provided. This asymmetry prevents reliable comparative analysis and forces reliance on Zero Tenacity's mixed recent record alone. Historical precedent for established teams vs. unknown opponents: teams with recent qualifier wins typically hold ~52-58% win probability in BO3 playoff contexts, but volatility in recent performance (BLAST losses) depresses Zero Tenacity's edge to base rate ~54%. Playoff format (double-elimination, BO3) favors teams with recent match experience. Zero Tenacity's 3 recent qualifier matches provide some match sharpness advantage, though the two losses suggest potential draft/adaptation weaknesses. Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_yes=48 reflects moderate evidence supporting Zero Tenacity (recent EPL win, previous qualifier success) but tempered by BLAST losses. confidence_no=42 reflects insufficient data on Team Lynx to rule out strong competitive capability; Team Lynx could be a strong closed-qualifier team with limited public match history. Market price (YES=44%) is slightly undervaluing Zero Tenacity relative to historical baseline for established qualifier winners (~54%), but not dramatically mispriced given data scarcity on opponent. 10-hour time-to-event window: limited opportunity for major reversals; market will sharpen once match begins. Current price reflects genuine uncertainty driven by Team Lynx opacity.", "key_factor": "In tier-1 Dota 2 qualifiers (double-elimination BO3 matches), favorites with recent qualifier wins show ~55-60% win rates against unknown/lower-profile opponents; unseeded teams in closed qualifiers advance ~40-45% of the time.", "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.45999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market price (44% YES / 56% NO) reflects weak conviction on both sides, with only $3.7k volume over 1 week indicating low trader interest in this matchup. YES side has drifted upward +3pp over 24h, suggesting minor buyer confidence, but from a depressed baseline \u2014 no catalyst evident in briefing to justify strong directional movement. Zero Tenacity's recent record is mixed: 1st place in EPL S35 (Mar 27) is strong, but followed immediately by 0-1 losses in BLAST Slam VII quals (Mar 31, Apr 1) \u2014 inconsistency prevents high confidence either way. Team Lynx roster and recent performance completely absent from briefing \u2014 this asymmetry makes probability highly speculative. Market may be defaulting to neutral (50%) due to insufficient data on the NO side. Zero Tenacity has shown qualifier success (won DreamLeague S28 WEU Open Q1 in Jan 2026), but that is 3+ months old in esports terms \u2014 form decay risk is high. Tournament structure (double-elimination, Lower Bracket R1 match, Bo3 format) is standard but provides no edge signal on either team's suitability. No head-to-head history, patch-specific meta insights, or recent scrim/boot camp data present in briefing \u2014 this is a true information void for Team Lynx. Event timing: TODAY (resolves ~10 hours) means almost no time for new information to shift market; current price likely reflects pre-tournament betting stances formed days ago before this brief was finalized. Low volatility on NO side (0.0pp/hr) suggests NO backers are passive holders, not active sellers \u2014 potential sign they lack conviction to defend that price, not strength. Sentiment is APATHY: market is pricing this as a near-coinflip (44/56 split) due to missing data on Team Lynx, not because of balanced team strength signals. This is rational under-conviction, not crowd exuberance or panic.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "Zero Tenacity has documented recent qualifier wins (DreamLeague S28 WEU Open Q1, Jan 2026) and a T3 championship (EPL S35, Mar 27, 2026 at 3-2), but this is offset by two consecutive 0-1 losses in BLAST Slam VII qualifiers (Mar 31 & Apr 1), indicating inconsistent form entering playoffs. Team Lynx is entirely absent from the provided briefing\u2014no roster, placement history, tier ranking, or head-to-head record exists. This is a critical data gap; in Dota 2 qualifiers, unknown or lower-ranked challengers frequently execute upsets against favored teams due to unpredictable drafting and patch-specific preparation. Double-elimination format with Bo3 matches means a single loss does not eliminate Zero Tenacity; however, lower-bracket pressure and potential fatigue compound inconsistency risk. Qualifier environments reward meta adaptation and cohesion, neither of which can be verified for either team from the briefing. The tournament runs April 12-14 on patch 7.41a; timing and patch unfamiliarity could disadvantage either team equally, but Zero Tenacity's recent losses suggest slower meta adaptation. Market pricing (YES 44%, NO 56%) reflects smart-money skepticism of Zero Tenacity despite stronger documented history, likely because Team Lynx's unknown status permits high-variance outcomes. This asymmetric information strongly suggests NO overvalue. Zero Tenacity's T3 tier championship (EPL S35) is tier-relevant but lower stakes than a DreamLeague closed qualifier for a Tier 1 season main event; qualifier pressure differs meaningfully from league play. Confidence in YES is low (42%) due to lack of Team Lynx data preventing dual-perspective evaluation; confidence in NO is moderate-high (68%) because absence of evidence for Team Lynx combined with Zero Tenacity's recent losses creates sufficient evidentiary basis to favor the underdog. Event timing is TODAY, resolving in ~10 hours; reversal probability is minimal, but the brief's sparse fixture data means real-time roster/form updates pre-match could shift odds significantly.", "key_factor": "Team Lynx's complete absence from the briefing dataset\u2014no roster composition, recent match history, or competitive pedigree\u2014creates severe asymmetry that favors the NO side despite Zero Tenacity's marginal recent form, as qualifier upsets are common and unknown challengers exploit preparation gaps.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Team Lynx roster information is entirely absent from the briefing. This is not a minor omission\u2014it prevents any comparative analysis of player skill, form, or recent performance. The council cannot evaluate Team Lynx's strengths, recent tournament history, or whether they have momentum. ZERO TENACITY FORM INCONSISTENCY: Recent results show volatility\u20141st place in EPL S35 (Mar 27) but immediate 0-1 losses in back-to-back BLAST Slam VII qualifiers (Mar 31, Apr 1). This 3-week span suggests either a patch adaptation issue, tactical vulnerability, or psychological let-down after EPL success. Playoff pressure in double-elimination could expose this fragility. ABSENCE OF HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: No historical matchup data provided between these teams. In lower-tier qualifiers, unfamiliarity can be a significant disadvantage, especially if Team Lynx has studied Zero Tenacity's recent EPL and BLAST footage while Zero Tenacity may lack current scouting on Team Lynx. ROSTER STABILITY QUESTION: The briefing does not confirm whether either team has a confirmed, stable 5-man roster for this match. In tier-3 qualifiers, last-minute player unavailability (visa delays, illness, family emergency, or organizational reshuffling) is not rare. Zero Tenacity's recent BLAST losses could trigger internal roster discussions. DOTA 2 PATCH 7.41a ADAPTATION: The tournament is being played on patch 7.41a. If Zero Tenacity's EPL S35 win was on an older patch and BLAST qualifiers exposed weakness to the newer meta, they may not have fully adapted 48 hours before this match. Team Lynx's actual patch familiarity is unknowable. LOWER BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: If Zero Tenacity is in lower bracket (as suggested by 'Lower bracket round 1' in resolution criteria), they face immediate elimination pressure after BLAST failures. This can either sharpen focus or create desperation-driven poor decision-making. Team Lynx's bracket position unknown. MARKET MOVING TOWARD YES: YES has risen +3pp in 24 hours (44% now vs 41% baseline), suggesting late money or information favoring Zero Tenacity. This could reflect confident insiders, or it could be momentum trading on their EPL win. Late movers on qualifier markets are often unreliable. LIQUIPEDIA INCOMPLETENESS: Multiple sections marked 'TBD' and incomplete roster tables. This suggests the briefing was pulled mid-tournament or during bracket stabilization, raising the possibility that lineup changes, coaching adjustments, or roster substitutions happened after data collection. TOURNAMENT SCALE & TIER: This is a Closed Qualifier (Tier 1) with only 8 teams and $50K total prize pool. Teams at this level have thinner preparation margins, smaller coaching staffs, and less institutional stability than Tier 1 main events. Single roster disruptions have outsized impact. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in evaluating Zero Tenacity's recent form (verifiable wins/losses) but near-zero confidence in assessing Team Lynx's actual competitive level, mental state, or roster integrity. This skew should lower overall prediction confidence.", "key_factor": "Team Lynx fields a substitute or academy player due to last-minute roster unavailability, or Zero Tenacity has an unannounced lineup change that disrupts their synergy in a critical playoff match.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5072597864768683, "no_score": 0.4843452380952381, "edge": 0.07225978647686832, "no_edge": -0.08065476190476184, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 51% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 40% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1961643", "question": "Dota 2: Zero Tenacity vs Team Lynx (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 1 match between Zero Tenacity and Team Lynx in