 efficient given available data, but slightly undervalues EFP's demonstrated superiority. Sharp move on Apr 12 (+19.0pp) suggests informed money entered YES side, then partial retracement indicates some uncertainty, but overall trend favors YES. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams in same professional league (VCL T\u00fcrkiye Stage 2); BJK's previous loss to same opponent in same tournament structure provides direct comparative evidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (74%) reflects clear head-to-head data and EFP's dominant performance. Lower confidence in NO (45%) reflects genuine uncertainty about BJK's current form, unobserved preparations, and roster changes\u2014data gaps on the underdog side. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: vlr.gg has strong track record for timely publication of VCL T\u00fcrkiye results. Low mechanism risk, though 2-hour fallback window exists if unforeseen delays occur.", "key_factor": "Match timing (10:30 AM ET = 2:30 PM UTC, approximately 4 hours before market end) creates tight resolution window; vlr.gg publication delay beyond 2 hours could trigger fallback consensus mechanism.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "YES CASE: EFP already defeated BJK 2-0 in the group stage with sterben earning MVP, indicating clear skill/form advantage in the current tournament meta and against this specific opponent. YES CASE: The briefing describes EFP's 'dominant performance' and 'superior individual play' in the prior matchup, suggesting structural team cohesion issues at BJK rather than one-off performance variance. YES CASE: Market pricing YES at 56% (+6.5pp over 7 days) reflects accumulating confidence in EFP; sharp +19pp move on Apr 12 suggests informed traders recognized EFP's advantage before settling at current level. YES CASE: EFP roster displays consistency across multiple players (ip0TT, deminatiX, ef1sS show strong K/D and ACS metrics in available stats), reducing reliance on single carry performance. NO CASE: BJK has now seen EFP's full playbook from the first match and can prepare targeted anti-strats, map vetos, and player-specific counters for the rematch. NO CASE: BO3 format (vs. prior BO3) gives BJK two additional opportunities to win at least one map by adapting mid-series, unlike a single decisive map. NO CASE: Lack of recent performance data for BJK post-first-loss limits ability to assess whether they've made roster changes, improved coordination, or identified EFP weaknesses. NO WEAKNESS: Rematch context typically favors the team that has already won, especially by 2-0, because the victor's preparation is already validated; BJK must successfully invent new answers rather than simply execute better. NO WEAKNESS: No evidence in briefing that BJK has made adjustments, roster changes, or demonstrated improved form since the 2-0 loss; burden of proof is on the underdog to show material improvement. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES due to concrete head-to-head result with MVP designation and dominant descriptor; lower confidence in NO because briefing provides no counter-evidence of BJK's current form, preparation level, or roster status post-loss. MARKET ASSESSMENT: YES at 56% may actually undervalue EFP slightly; a 2-0 prior result in the same tournament vs. same opponent typically commands 60%+ probability in rematches unless evidence suggests material change in opponent quality.", "key_factor": "Eternal Fire Passion's convincing 2-0 head-to-head victory with sterben MVP performance demonstrates superior individual skill and map control against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in the same tournament structure.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Y