{"run_id": "b6f21d5b-05db-4748-9ad6-476d39438c8b", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:15:03.921245+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1960163", "question": "Valorant: WIP Esports vs Mandatory (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between WIP Esports and Mandatory in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"WIP Esports\" if WIP Esports win the match against Mandatory.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Mandatory\" if Mandatory win the match against WIP Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.225, "volume_usd": 3542.00038, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["79720653084492924093002587346392543562573583154000840152650396731915516959625", "85921010026849250616845778279286856674699903574117753032854252425357516361584"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "WIP Esports enters as clear favorites: undefeated 3-0 record with +30 round differential vs Mandatory's 2-1 with +20 differential. Map win rate advantage for WIP (6-2 vs 5-2) and higher seeding position (1st vs 2nd) suggests stronger aggregate performance across the stage. However, Mandatory's +20 round differential and 2-1 record demonstrate competitive strength and ability to win matches in this group. Close map differential (6-2 vs 5-2 = only 1 map difference) suggests matches are contested; not blowouts by WIP. BO3 format (first to 2 maps) introduces variance: Mandatory's competitive positioning means they have realistic paths to steal maps and win the series. Briefing provides no head-to-head record, recent trend data, player-level stats, or patch-specific meta context to distinguish these teams further. Market price (YES 22% / NO 78%) appears to overweight WIP's standing position and undervalue Mandatory's demonstrated competitive closeness. WIP's 3-0 record is strong but small sample (only 3 matches); Mandatory's 2-1 is limited data on both sides. Lack of VOD/streaming context or caster insights prevents assessment of draft favorability, tactical adaptability, or momentum. Probability estimate reflects WIP's statistical edge (undefeated, +30 diff) but acknowledges meaningful competitive parity and Mandatory's win capability. Confidence in YES is higher (72) due to clear statistical advantages; confidence in NO is lower (55) because briefing provides insufficient counter-evidence to fully justify market's 78% NO price. Event timing is TODAY (~12 hours): match is imminent, reducing likelihood of cancellation/delay scenarios that would resolve to 50-50.", "key_factor": "Briefing lacks detailed head-to-head history, recent form trends, and individual player/coaching performance data that would inform a more precise prediction.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO = Mandatory wins): Market has priced NO at 78%, reflecting Mandatory's competitive standing and the inherent uncertainty in best-of-3 esports formats. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES = WIP Esports wins): Despite WIP Esports' 3-0 record, the market discounts them at only 22%, suggesting either overvaluation of Mandatory's comeback potential or significant hidden information (roster changes, scrim results, opponent prep) not visible in the briefing. WIP ESPORTS DOMINANT FORM: 3-0 record with +30 round differential is substantially stronger than Mandatory's 2-1 with +20. This 10-round differential gap reflects consistent superior performance across all matches played. MAP WIN RATE ADVANTAGE: WIP Esports' 6-2 map count versus Mandatory's 5-2 shows WIP winning 75% of maps while Mandatory wins 71.4% \u2014 a narrow but consistent edge that favors the undefeated team in a BO3 format where map selection and momentum are critical. MANDATORY'S COMPETITIVE FLOOR: However, Mandatory's +20 round differential is respectable \u2014 not a weak team, suggesting this is not a mismatch. Mandatory has proven ability to beat group opponents, creating legitimate 20-25% upset scenario. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA GAP: Briefing explicitly notes 'limited head-to-head context available' \u2014 this is a critical missing data point. If Mandatory has previously beaten WIP Esports or has strong scrim evidence, market pricing of 78% NO may be justified despite WIP's superior record. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 esports matches contain inherent variance. Even 70-30 favored teams lose BO3s regularly due to map pool dynamics, vetoes, and single-match upsets. Market's 78% NO price reflects appropriate acknowledgment of this variance. PLAYOFF IMPLICATIONS: Both teams competing for standing position adds urgency and preparation intensity to both squads, potentially tightening the match outcome beyond raw statistics. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES side has risen 4 percentage points in 24 hours (from ~18% to 22%) while NO has fallen 6.5pp (from ~84% to 78%), suggesting recent information is shifting sentiment toward WIP Esports or uncertainty is increasing. This could indicate late breaking scrims, roster news, or anticipation of WIP's dominant form continuing. VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hour volatility of 1.2pp/hr for YES (higher) versus 1.0pp/hr for NO (lower) indicates YES side is attracting more recent trading activity, not necessarily conviction shift. CONVICTION ASSESSMENT: NO side at 78% remains strongly favored by market despite WIP Esports' perfect record \u2014 this suggests either: (1) market has legitimate uncertainty about WIP's sustainability, (2) Mandatory is underrated based on scrim/hidden data, or (3) esports markets price in volatility heavily. BULLISH CASE FOR NO (MANDATORY): If Mandatory wins, it would represent a disciplined upset of a 3-0 team with better round differential, suggesting they solved WIP's meta/playstyle or had superior preparation. The 78% pricing suggests this outcome is credible but less likely. DATA ASYMMETRY WARNING: Briefing provides excellent quantitative standing data but zero qualitative intel on team form, recent roster changes, coach adjustments, or scrim results. This asymmetry means confidence in NO should be tempered \u2014 we're missing half the story.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' perfect 3-0 record with +30 round differential versus Mandatory's 2-1 record and +20 differential demonstrates a clear momentum and form advantage in a head-to-head matchup with playoff implications.", "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: YES is priced at 22% but has risen +4.0pp in 24 hours while NO fell -6.5pp, suggesting recent market repricing toward YES \u2014 potential recognition of Mandatory's viability. WIP ESPORTS DOMINANCE (supports NO): 3-0 record, +30 round differential, and 6-2 map count show clear superiority. WIP leads standings with statistically dominant performance. MANDATORY'S HIDDEN STRENGTH (supports YES): +20 round differential places Mandatory within 10 round differential of WIP \u2014 this is a tight competitive gap. Mandatory's 2-1 record shows they can beat quality opponents in this group. MAP DIFFERENTIAL NARROW (supports YES): WIP's 6-2 map count vs Mandatory's 5-2 is only a 1-map gap. Close map records indicate individual matches are competitive and not lopsided. BO3 FORMAT VARIANCE (supports YES): Best-of-3 introduces inherent variance. Even a team with +10 round differential advantage faces ~25-35% upset probability in BO3 format due to map-pick strategy, mental momentum swings, and single-map variance. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA ABSENT (supports YES uncertainty): Briefing provides no direct WIP vs Mandatory matchup history. Without h2h context, we cannot rule out unfavorable matchups or hidden advantages for Mandatory. MANDATORY NOT INFERIOR (supports YES): Third-place standing does not mean Mandatory is significantly weaker \u2014 they are separated from WIP by only 1 map and 10 rounds. Group stage clustering often shows tight competitive bands. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Data strongly supports WIP's statistical dominance (confidence_no: 72), but lacks depth on Mandatory's form variability, recent momentum, player health, or map-specific matchup data (confidence_yes: 35). The briefing does not provide recent match VODs, individual player stats, or coaching adjustments. TIME-TO-EVENT: Match resolves TODAY in ~12 hours. No time for roster changes or major news shifts. Market has priced in available information. VERDICT: While WIP is likely favorite (probability_score: 28 for YES reflects ~72% NO confidence), the underdog case rests on competitive round differential, BO3 variance, and absence of direct h2h context. Mandatory is underpriced relative to their statistical proximity to WIP, but WIP's 3-0 record and leadership remain strong evidence.", "key_factor": "Mandatory's competitive +20 round differential and 2-1 record demonstrate they operate at nearly equivalent skill level to WIP, and BO3 format introduces variance that can favor the underdog in best-of series.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "WIP Esports holds clear statistical advantages: undefeated 3-0 record, +30 round differential (vs Mandatory's +20), and superior map win rate (6-2 vs 5-2). In BO3 Valorant group stage matches, the team with stronger record and round differential typically wins 65-75% of encounters; WIP's lead is material but not decisive. Mandatory's 2-1 record and +20 round differential indicate competitive capability\u2014this is not a mismatch, but rather a match between a strong leader and a solid challenger. BO3 format introduces volatility compared to single-map play; the 3-map requirement allows for map-pick strategy and comeback potential that moderates the favorite's typical win rate. Market price of 22% YES appears modestly underpriced relative to WIP's statistical dominance and undefeated record; rising YES share trend (+4.0pp over 24h) suggests modest repricing toward fundamentals. No head-to-head historical data available between these specific teams; relying on group-stage performance differential and base-rate expectations for undefeated vs. second-place teams. Event timing is TODAY (~12 hours to resolution); high confidence in YES is justified by clear performance metrics, but confidence_no is moderate (54%) due to limited granular team-matchup data and inherent BO3 variance. Confidence_yes (72%) reflects strong statistical support; confidence_no (54%) reflects data scarcity on Mandatory's specific tactical matchups and recent form trends against similar opponents.", "key_factor": "In competitive BO3 Valorant matches, the higher-seeded/better-performing team wins approximately 65-75% of the time; teams with perfect records (3-0) maintain that performance in subsequent matches at roughly 70% historical rate in group stages.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "WIP Esports holds a clear statistical edge: 3-0 record vs 2-1, +30 vs +20 round differential, 6-2 vs 5-2 map count\u2014these are material advantages that justify a favorite price. Market is pricing WIP at 22% YES, implying Mandatory is heavy favorite (78% NO). This is INVERTED relative to standings data, which shows WIP as the dominant team. The 4pp YES rise over 24h suggests market is slowly correcting toward recognizing WIP's form advantage, but correction is incomplete. Mandatory's +20 differential and 2-1 record ARE competitive\u2014this is not a bottom-tier team. BO3 format introduces variance; Mandatory has realistic upset potential (25-30% range). Crowd appears BEARISH on WIP despite superior metrics. This could reflect: (a) uncertainty about head-to-head history, (b) recent Mandatory momentum not captured in week 1 stats, (c) general contrarian sentiment favoring underdogs in esports. No recent news, VODs, or performance updates provided post-standings snapshot (dated 2026-04-13 10:14 UTC, ~12h before match). Market lacks fresh intel; pricing may reflect stale information. BO3 format and esports volatility support higher upset probability than raw standings suggest (Mandatory 25-30%), but WIP's +30 differential dominance should reflect in higher YES confidence than current 22% market price. Rational pricing should favor WIP in 55-70% range given the statistical gap. Current 22% suggests either: crowd sentiment undervaluing form differential, or hidden information about Mandatory's recent practice/roster adjustments not in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES estimate (72) because standings data is clear and recent. Low confidence in NO estimate (45) because briefing lacks detail on Mandatory's hidden form, head-to-head matchup history, or recent scrim results that might justify heavy underdog pricing.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "WIP Esports demonstrates dominant form: 3-0 record, 6-2 map count, +30 round differential indicates consistent anti-eco execution, map pool depth, and economy discipline across three consecutive victories. Mandatory ranks 2nd but shows measurable gap: 2-1 record with +20 round differential represents ~25% weaker round differential per map (20 vs 30), translating to approximately 2-3 fewer rounds won per 25-round map\u2014significant in close BO3 scenarios. Map differential (6-2 vs 5-2) reflects both teams' map pool strength; WIP's extra map win suggests either superior map selection adaptability or stronger secondary map performance, both critical in BO3 where teams ban strategically. Valorant BO3 format heavily favors form and momentum: teams with undefeated records carry psychological advantage and proven read on opponent tendencies; WIP has not yet faced game pressure of losing a map in this stage. Limited head-to-head historical data: briefing does not provide direct matchup records or map-specific performance data between these teams, reducing confidence in predicting Mandatory upset scenarios. Economic discipline differentiator in Valorant: +30 vs +20 round differential likely reflects superior buy round conversions and anti-eco execution\u2014core skills that become more pronounced in best-of formats where opponent economy resets occur. Mandatory's competitive standing (2-1, +20) suggests they are not an outlier team, but margin of performance delta indicates WIP's superiority is structural, not random variance. Event timing LIVE/IMMINENT (12 hours to resolution): this removes possibility of last-minute roster changes, emergencies, or tactical shifts; current standings reflect true team strength at match time. Market price (YES 22%, NO 78%) appears undervaluing WIP's dominant form; a +30 differential team with 3-0 record typically commands 60-70% probability in BO3, not 22%, suggesting market inefficiency favoring Mandatory believers or sharp money hedging. Valorant regional France competition (VCL) typically features 8-12 teams with known rosters and minimal roster churn; both teams' records are reliable indicators of relative strength.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' 3-0 undefeated record with +30 round differential represents sustained map control and economy management superiority across multiple matches, a structural advantage in BO3 format that compounds across best-of series, though Mandatory's +20 differential suggests they remain tactically competitive at the round level.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_n