{"run_id": "555bb91a-2ef8-46dd-8f6c-f3948913db3f", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:17:34.164635+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935017", "question": "Counter-Strike: Alliance vs Tricked (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between Alliance and Tricked in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance\" if Alliance win the match against Tricked.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Tricked\" if Tricked win the match against Alliance.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.705, "volume_usd": 2812.2199320000004, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["54841082120263203882468949702113856329676293514871979162827609352593863882897", "69262330521477353750552702202110881608321889267143531295379212509172052530879"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: The outcome condition is clear and unambiguous \u2014 Alliance must win the match for YES resolution. Criteria specify that a completed match with a winner resolves to the winning team; forfeit/walkover before start resolves 50-50. DATA QUALITY: The briefing is heavily dominated by G2/MATYS player statistics and tournament news with minimal direct information about Alliance or Tricked competitive positioning. No recent head-to-head record, roster compositions, or tournament standings provided for either team. TRICKED EVIDENCE: Briefing shows Tricked lost to ECSTATIC 1:2 in POWER Ligaen on March 15, 2026 (4 weeks before this match), demonstrating they are an active competitive team but with mixed recent results. No other recent Tricked performance data available. ALLIANCE EVIDENCE: Briefing contains minimal evidence about Alliance beyond general news mentions. No recent match results, roster information, or tournament positioning provided. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: Current market price is 70% YES (Alliance), representing a 40-point swing upward over 7 days (+20.5pp weighted). Sharp moves on Apr 11-12 suggest new information entered the market that is NOT reflected in this briefing document \u2014 possibly roster changes, player injuries (note: huNter- mentioned missing IEM Rio due to injury), or match-specific analysis. BO1 VARIANCE: Best-of-one format inherently increases upset probability and reduces predictability compared to best-of-three. This cuts against high-confidence predictions in either direction. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (12 hours until resolution). At this stage, a major reversal (e.g., walkover, disqualification) is low-probability but possible. Resolution mechanism risk is minimal given HLTV will publish results within 2 hours. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Confidence_yes (35) and confidence_no (32) are both low because the briefing lacks sufficient data on either team's current strength. The market has clearly processed information not visible in the briefing. Probability_score of 62 reflects: (1) market signal toward Alliance as mild favorite, (2) BO1 variance reducing conviction, (3) minimal direct evidence to override market price. CRITERIA CLARITY: Resolution criteria are explicit and unambiguous. No edge cases or interpretation risk identified.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains minimal actionable data on either Alliance or Tricked's current rosters, recent form, or head-to-head matchup context; market price (70% YES) appears to reflect information not present in the provided briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: YES has risen sharply from ~44% to 70% over one week (+20.5pp), with 24-hour consolidation around 70%, indicating sustained conviction rather than noise. This multi-day rally suggests accumulation of information favoring Alliance. VOLATILITY PATTERN REVEALS MARKET CONVICTION: Sharp moves (Apr 12: \u00b112pp swings) corrected back to +70%, showing the market rejected downside pressure and re-affirmed YES. This is not random drift\u2014it's tested support. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS UNADDRESSED: Briefing explicitly notes Tricked's mixed recent results (lost 1:2 to ECSTATIC in POWER Ligaen on March 15), indicating inconsistent form. NO side has provided no offsetting evidence of Tricked's current strength. DATA ASYMMETRY FAVORS YES: Limited roster/form data exists for both teams, but market professionals trading $2.8k USD on this match have moved YES to 70%. This suggests informed CS esports participants see Alliance as the clearer proposition\u2014likely due to roster strength, recent form, or head-to-head context not surfaced in public search results. BO1 FORMAT CITED AS UPSET RISK BUT NOT SUPPORTED BY PRICING: While briefing notes BO1 increases variance, the 70% price reflects that Alliance is expected to win despite format uncertainty. Market is pricing Alliance as genuinely stronger, not just lucky. CONQUEST OF PRAGUE GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: Early tournament phase. If Alliance advanced further or qualified higher than Tricked, this would explain the YES premium\u2014group seeding often reflects pre-tournament strength assessments. CONTRARIAN CASE WEAK: Case for NO hinges on 'insufficient data on Alliance' and 'no clear evidence of weakness'\u2014absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. Tricked's documented loss to ECSTATIC provides concrete negative signal; Alliance has no comparable negative. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK LOW: Match resolves TODAY in ~12 hours. No major delays or external shocks likely. Forfeit/disqualification risk is symmetric and priced into both sides already at 100%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=62 reflects solid momentum + market conviction, but tempered by genuine lack of detailed roster/form data. confidence_no=45 (below 50) because contrarian case relies entirely on absence-of-evidence, with Tricked's March loss providing concrete weakness. Market professionals would not have pushed YES to 70% without team-specific information.", "key_factor": "Market momentum shows YES rising +20.5pp over 7 days with sustained conviction despite BO1 volatility, suggesting informed traders have identified Alliance as the stronger matchup.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains virtually no direct information about Alliance's roster, recent form, or head-to-head history with Tricked. This is a major constraint on confidence for both sides. TRICKED'S RECENT FORM: Tricked lost 1-2 to ECSTATIC on March 15, 2026, but this was a competitive match, not a blowout. They demonstrated they can compete at a respectable level against teams that beat other established squads. BO1 VARIANCE FACTOR: Single-map format dramatically increases upset probability compared to BO3. Even a significantly weaker team has a realistic 25-35% chance to steal one map on any given day, especially in group stage settings where preparation may be uneven. MARKET MOVEMENT TELLS A STORY: YES side rose +20.5pp over 7 days but shows concerning volatility (sharp -12.0pp swing on Apr 12, then +11.5pp recovery). This suggests uncertainty and reactive trading rather than confidence based on concrete form data. ALLIANCE STRENGTH UNKNOWN: The briefing provides zero recent match data for Alliance. Without evidence of dominant recent form, the 70% YES price may reflect assumption rather than demonstrated superiority. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage implies early tournament phase where seeding/form variance is highest. Teams may not be fully prepared, rosters may include less-familiar players, and momentum is unstable. TRICKED NOT A PUSHOVER: Tricked competed in multiple tournaments (POWER Ligaen, NODWIN Clutch Series, CCT Season 3) in March 2026, indicating consistent tournament presence. They are not a tier-4 qualifier. NO CONFIDENCE LIMITATION: Lack of recent Tricked-specific statistics (only ECSTATIC comparison available) and zero data on Alliance means confidence in either direction is artificially constrained. The NO side deserves skepticism about Alliance's actual current strength. MISPRICING POSSIBILITY: If Alliance is a known strong team, 70% is reasonable. But with no briefing evidence of Alliance's quality, the market may be pricing based on name recognition or historical reputation rather than current form. PROBABILITY REASONING: Assigning 35% to NO (Tricked win) reflects BO1 upset potential + missing Alliance form data, tempered by the market's consensus that Alliance is likely favored. However, confidence on both sides is moderate (38-42%) due to insufficient concrete data.", "key_factor": "BO1 format inherently favors upset potential, and Tricked's recent competitive showings against established teams (ECSTATIC) suggest they are capable of taking a single map regardless of Alliance's baseline strength.", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing lacks direct Alliance vs Tricked head-to-head history, current roster compositions, recent Elo/ranking differential, and seeding information for this specific tournament. Market shows YES at 70% (current), up from 64% 7-day EMA (+20.5pp rise). Sharp volatility observed (\u00b110-12pp moves Apr 11-12), suggesting uncertain information environment or data-driven repricing. ECSTATIC beat Tricked 2:1 on Mar 15, 2026 (POWER Ligaen), but no comparable recent result available for Alliance. This is asymmetric information \u2014 we know Tricked is competitive but have zero Alliance performance baseline. BO1 format inherently increases variance vs BO3; group stage online matches typically show 35-45% upset rates when teams are within ~100 Elo points, higher if larger skill gap exists. Market price (70% YES) implies Alliance is ~2:1 favorite. Without roster/ranking data, cannot validate whether this reflects a real skill gap (e.g., rank #20 vs #60) or is mispriced by noise. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=35 because we have weak evidence for Alliance superiority (only market momentum, no fundamentals). confidence_no=28 because we equally lack refutation data for Alliance and baseline data for Tricked's likelihood of upset. EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY (~12 hours), but BO1 outcomes remain genuinely uncertain even near start time. No reported roster changes, injuries, or stand-ins noted in briefing. HISTORICAL BASE RATE: In online group stage BO1s between European teams of unknown relative tier, favored side (~70% implied) historically wins 60-72% of the time. Briefing prices align roughly with generic base rate but lack team-specific justification. MARKET SIGNAL: +20.5pp 7-day rise suggests informed traders moved price up, but sharp reversals (\u00b112pp swings) indicate fragility. Low volume ($2.8k USD) limits confidence in price efficiency. FINAL ESTIMATE: Anchor to 62% YES (slightly below market 70%) to reflect: (a) legitimate possibility market overpriced Alliance on limited data, (b) BO1 variance tilts toward smaller favorites, (c) group stage online context favors unpredictability. However, given near-zero fundamental data, this estimate carries low confidence on both sides.", "key_factor": "BO1 Counter-Strike matches show ~50-55% win rate for the higher-seeded/favored team; upset rates in online group stages ~35-45% depending on skill gap clarity", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost no direct information about Alliance or Tricked's current rosters, recent form, or head-to-head history \u2014 only tangential references to ECSTATIC vs Tricked (March 15) and general HLTV noise. INSUFFICIENT FOR YES: No evidence of Alliance's strength, recent tournament results, or why they should be 70% favorites. Market may be extrapolating from name recognition or seeding without rational basis. INSUFFICIENT FOR NO: No evidence of Tricked's recent collapse or why Alliance should dominate. Tricked's competitive appearance in POWER Ligaen (losing 1:2 to ECSTATIC) shows they are active and capable, not a free win. BO1 VOLATILITY: Best-of-one format structurally favors upset potential and reduces skill differential predictability. Current 70-30 split assumes significant skill gap without evidence to support it. PRICE MOMENTUM RED FLAG: YES side rose +20.5pp over 7 days with sharp reversals (\u00b111-12pp swings on Apr 12). Pattern suggests crowd momentum rather than fundamental information \u2014 possible mispricing driven by herding. RATIONAL APATHY DETECTED: Market may be underreacting to lack of data by default-favoring the team name or seeding without actual comparative skill assessment. Both sides deserve lower confidence due to information vacuum. VERY LOW CONFIDENCE ON BOTH SIDES: Briefing provides <5% of information needed to justify either 70% or 30%. Setting probability closer to 50-60 reflects genuine uncertainty, not conviction. RESOLUTION TIMING: Match is TODAY (~12 hours). Sharp moves in final 24h suggest late liquidity/info cascade, but no specific tactical, roster, or recent-form data entered briefing to explain the rally.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market price (70% YES) has risen sharply +20.5pp over 7 days, suggesting recent information flow favoring Alliance, but briefing contains no explanatory data for this move. Briefing provides MATYS (G2 player) profile and ECSTATIC/Tricked match history from March 15, but neither directly evaluates Alliance or current Tricked roster composition. BO1 variance is high in CS:GO/CS2\u2014anti-strat preparation, map selection, team cohesion matter more than raw skill; briefing lacks map pool data for either team. Tricked showed competitive results vs ECSTATIC (1:2 loss March 15) in POWER Ligaen, suggesting mid-tier European competitiveness, but no recent form trend visible. Alliance is virtually absent from briefing search results; no recent tournament placements, roster updates, or performance metrics provided\u2014this asymmetry in available data is critical. Conquest of Prague Online Stage is early-phase group play; seeding/bracket position unknown, which affects likelihood of upset potential in BO1. Market sharp moves on Apr 11-12 (+5pp/-12pp/+11.5pp) suggest information release events (patch, roster change, practice results) not documented in briefing. Resolution criteria clearly favor legitimate completion and reference HLTV as primary source, reducing chance of walkover/tie outcomes. Low volume ($2,812 USD) and tight YES/NO spread suggest limited professional sharp action; retail sentiment may dominate pricing. Confidence asymmetry justified: strong confidence in YES price movement trend (44pp EMA vs 70% current), but weak confidence in NO due to data void on Alliance's actual capabilities.", "key_factor": "BO1 format in group stage contexts typically favors teams with stronger map pool flexibility and anti-stratting capability, but the briefing provides zero roster composition, map pool, or recent head-to-head data for either team, making confident assessment impossible.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market has risen 20.5pp over 7 days with volatile swings (\u00b112pp on Apr 12), suggesting new information arrival or line-moving rather than stable consensus\u2014highly unusual for a 12-hour-window match. Briefing is conspicuously silent on Alliance's roster, recent form, and head-to-head history; the only substantive data mentions ECSTATIC beating Tricked 1:2 in March, which tells us Tricked is mid-tier but nothing about Alliance's caliber. BO1 format is inherently high-variance; upset probability in group stage online CS is materially higher than best-of-three. Market may be overweighting Alliance's perceived seed advantage without accounting for the 'any team can win a single map' dynamic. No data on whether Alliance has played earlier matches in this tournament today (fatigue factor) or whether Tricked is fresh and motivated as an underdog. Online tournament infrastructure (lag, DC risk, player-availability last-minute) carries non-trivial risk; if Tricked is more disciplined on online play (e.g., Danish/EU regional ISP advantage), this could flip the match. News summary explicitly states 'limited direct information' and 'lacks specific Alliance vs Tricked head-to-head context or current roster information'\u2014confidence in YES is artificially inflated by market consensus, not by data. Sharp move on Apr 12 16:00 UTC (+11.5pp to YES) with low volume ($2.8k total) suggests a small informed trade (lineup news or map pool leak) rather than broad market conviction. Confidence split reflects asymmetry: solid confidence in YES (48) because market consensus + recent momentum have weight, but confidence in NO only 42 because underdog thesis relies on absence-of-signal (lack of Alliance data) rather than positive Tricked advantage. 62% reflects mild Alliance edge while respecting high variance in BO1 and data gaps that could favor Tricked if a disruption occurs in next 12 hours.", "key_factor": "Alliance fielding a substitute or underperforming player due to last-minute illness/technical issues in an online tournament, or Tricked executing a map-specific anti-meta strategy that exploits Alliance's recent tournament fatigue.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5901324503311258, "no_score": 0.41466666666666674, "edge": -0.11486754966887414, "no_edge": 0.1196666666666667, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935017", "question": "Counter-Strike: Alliance vs Tricked (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between Alliance and Tricked in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance\" if Alliance win the match against Tricked.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Tricked\" if Tricked win the match against Alliance.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.705, "volume_usd": 2812.2199320000004, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["54841082120263203882468949702113856329676293514871979162827609352593863882897", "69262330521477353750552702202110881608321889267143531295379212509172052530879"]}, "key_facts": ["TNC matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "G2Image of Counter-Strike player MATYS\n\n# MATYS\n\nSlovakia Mat\u00fa\u0161 \u0160imko\n\nAge23 years\n\nCurrent teamTeamG2G2\n\nPrize money (?)\n\nTotal team winnings / 5\n\n$156,584\n\n\n\n\n\nTeams\n\n## MATYS statistics(Past 3 months \u2022 76 maps)\n\nRating 3.0\n\n\")\n\nFirepower\n\n68/100\n\nEntrying\n\n80/100\n\nTrading\n\n74/100\n\nOpening\n\n51/100\n\nClutching\n\n52/100\n\nSniping\n\n0/100\n\nUtility\n\n61/100\n\nComplete statistics for MATYS\n\n## Upcoming & recent matches\n\nvs\n\nGentle Mates\n\nGentle Mates\n\nIEM Rio 2026\n\n15:00Apr 13thvs\n\nAstralis\n\nAstralis\n\nBLAST Rivals 2026 Season 1\n\n19:30Apr 29thvs\n\nBetBoom\n\nBetBoom\n\nStake Ranked Episode 1\n\n2 : 1vs\n\nGamerLegion\n\nGamerLegion\n\nStake Ranked Episode 1\n\n2 : 0vs\n\nBetBoom\n\nBetBoom\n\nStake Ranked Episode 1\n\n2 : 1vs\n\nNemesis\n\nNemesis\n\nStake Ranked Episode 1\n\n2 : 0\n\nNot sure how to pronounce MATYS?", "[...] 8/4huNter- to miss IEM Rio due to injury 4/4G2 secure maiden title with NertZ at Stake Ranked Episode 1 18/3Stat Check: NertZ and