{"run_id": "68e8c33f-fdf3-4241-a26c-b6349e9256b2", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:19:49.203238+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1842267", "question": "Counter-Strike: B8 vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - IEM Rio Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between B8 and Natus Vincere in the IEM Rio Group B, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"B8\" if B8 win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against B8.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.185, "volume_usd": 71972.28440200009, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["19468732107850826124910683854873553648656766893335941507216915527138203216208", "101687252252173407855874001007234632961004698674586298741585377230015905139695"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "CONDITION: B8 wins the BO3 match against Natus Vincere in IEM Rio Group B Upper bracket quarterfinal 2. RANKINGS & COMPETITIVE DISPARITY: Na'Vi is #2 globally; B8 is #18. This 16-position gap reflects a tier-1 vs mid-tier matchup with substantial skill differential. STATISTICAL EVIDENCE: Na'Vi's 1.16 rating + 74.5% KAST vs B8's 1.11 rating + 71.4% KAST shows Na'Vi's superior fundamentals across economy management, utility usage, and map control. ROSTER QUALITY: Na'Vi lineup (Aleksib, iM, b1t, w0nderful, makazze) represents established, proven talent. B8 lacks comparable individual player pedigree and international LAN experience. BO3 FORMAT RISK FOR UNDERDOG: Best-of-3 requires consistency across 2-3 maps. Underdogs have lower win probability in extended series vs single-map contests; B8 must win 2 maps against a mechanically superior team. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES priced at 18% with 7-day EMA at 19% and stable trajectory suggests market has efficiently priced B8's underdog status based on available information. HISTORICAL PRECEDENT: Head-to-head data from tier-1 vs lower-ranked matchups typically shows ~80-85% win rate for the higher-ranked team in premier tournaments. TRAVEL/PREPARATION PARITY: Both teams are Eastern European; Brazil location affects both equally, no material disadvantage to either. RESOLUTIO