": "NO", "side_conf": 0.82, "key_factor": "paiN Gaming's occasional game-level victories (e.g., vs Leviatan, Los Grandes) demonstrate technical capability exists despite systemic underperformance, creating narrow upset potential in BO3 variance."}, {"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "prob": 0.14, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.45, "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; primary risk is resolution source delay beyond 2 hours, but outcome determination is straightforward win/loss."}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.14, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.45, "key_factor": "In competitive BO3 formats, cumulative team strength metrics (win rate, gold differential, KDA consistency) are highly predictive of series outcomes, and a 35-percentage-point win-rate gap with negative gold differential indicates structural team weaknesses that are difficult to overcome in multi-game contests."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.42, "key_factor": "In professional LoL team matchups, the higher-ranked team (by win rate and standings position) wins approximately 75-85% of series when facing a significantly lower-ranked opponent (35+ percentage point gap). BO3 format slightly reduces upset probability vs single games."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.35, "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.08, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.28, "key_factor": "paiN Gaming's ADC Trigger or jungler Stepz becomes unavailable due to illness, injury, or substitute-roster activation, forcing a roster swap into an unfamiliar or underperforming lineup."}], "agents_against_winner": [{"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.83, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.85, "key_factor": "FURIA's dominant 64% win rate (14-8) and 2nd-place standing vs paiN's severe underperformance (29% win rate, 4-10, 7th place, -144 GD) creates a structural competitive gap that BO3 format amplifies rather than erases."}], "median_prob": 0.18, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "26e1e834-f6dd-4e40-a8a0-9e7a00ba4903", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:27:14.721806+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1920643", "question": "Valorant: LYON vs STREAMER ARENA (BO3) - VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between LYON and STREAMER ARENA in the VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 6:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LYON\" if LYON win the match against STREAMER ARENA.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"STREAMER ARENA\" if STREAMER ARENA win the match against LYON.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connecti