{"run_id": "4e6404c4-1a5b-42a2-9e6a-131f07d3b5cd", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:28:04.453109+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1964116", "question": "Counter-Strike: VP.Future vs Z7 Esports (BO3) - Exort Series Contenders Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 4 match between VP.Future and Z7 Esports in the Exort Series Contenders Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"VP.Future\" if VP.Future win the match against Z7 Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Z7 Esports\" if Z7 Esports win the match against VP.Future.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T18:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T12:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 659.247104, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["6605382354722542231444129159197120678200134466016451178757968708512938184468", "20745674552212655943818569312368062920735686158465927803414929535900172817662"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "The briefing explicitly states: 'the search results contain no specific information about VP.Future or Z7 Esports, their roster compositions, recent performance records, head-to-head matchups, or any other details directly relevant to predicting the outcome of this particular match.' Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous: a standard match resolution to the winning team, with 50-50 fallback only for cancellation, tie, extended delay, or forfeit before start. Market price currently sits at 60% YES / 40% NO, suggesting traders believe VP.Future is slightly favored; however, this price reflects zero informational advantage in the briefing document. Event timing is TODAY (resolves in ~8 hours), meaning the match is imminent or live. A reversal from current market prices would require significant real-world evidence (team form, roster changes, odds movement) that is absent from the briefing. Recent price action shows +9.5pp movement toward YES in 24 hours, but this reflects trader sentiment, not predictive data about either team's actual strength. No HLTV rankings, recent match results, player-level analysis, or tournament context specific to these two teams is available to distinguish competitive capability. Both teams are confirmed participants in a 28-team C-Tier European online tournament (Exort Series #25), meeting minimum competitive standards, but parity of strength cannot be inferred. Swiss system format means both teams face opponents of similar Swiss-bracket records; this does not provide predictive power between two specific teams without knowing their current Swiss standing or head-to-head history. Absence of contradicting evidence for either team is not evidence of strength for either side\u2014it is absence of evidence.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no substantive information about VP.Future or Z7 Esports\u2014no roster data, recent form, head-to-head history, rankings, or any predictive indicators for either team.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: YES has risen 9.5pp in 24 hours with a sharp +6pp spike at 10:27 UTC today, while NO has fallen 11pp and exhibits 12pp/hr volatility\u20144x higher than YES's 2.8pp/hr. This asymmetric volatility and recent sharp moves suggest informed betting activity toward VP.Future, the only concrete directional signal available. MARKET STRUCTURE: YES at 60% represents genuine consensus, not a default. The 9.5pp rise in a single day on an imminent event (resolves in ~8 hours) indicates late information or recalibration, not noise. Professional bettors typically act close to resolution when more data emerges. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: NO side's extreme 12pp/hr volatility and -14pp drop at 10:27 UTC indicates panic or correction, not accumulation. If Z7 Esports had genuine backing, NO would show tighter volatility with sustained buying. Instead, the pattern suggests traders exiting NO positions. DATA VACUUM PROBLEM: The briefing contains zero team-specific information (rosters, recent form, head-to-head records, HLTV rankings for VP.Future or Z7 Esports). Neither team appears in available search results. This creates genuine uncertainty for both sides, but market prices incorporate information we cannot see\u2014late-day scrims, roster availability, or other real-time signals. C-TIER CONTEXT: Exort Series #25 is C-Tier, not elite. Both teams cleared inclusion thresholds but lack public statistical visibility. However, if one team has a documented recent upset or player issue (not in briefing), sharp bettors would move the market\u2014which aligns with the YES momentum pattern. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES is higher (45) than NO (35) because the price movement itself is evidence of directional belief, even without causal data. Confidence in NO is suppressed because we lack defensive evidence\u2014no explanation for why Z7 Esports should be favored despite being the underdog and seeing volatility exits. IMMINENT EVENT RISK: With ~8 hours to resolution, major reversals are unlikely. The 9.5pp move happened very recently, suggesting late information. If VP.Future had a roster issue or forfeit risk, NO would spike, not fall. The absence of negative reversal suggests VP.Future remains operationally viable. PROBABILITY NOT OVERCONFIDENT: 62% reflects the YES momentum but acknowledges the near-total absence of causal data. This is not a 75+ conviction score\u2014it is a modest edge derived from price movement and volatility asymmetry alone. Z7 Esports retains a meaningful 38% (implicit) chance given the data vacuum.", "key_factor": "YES side momentum (9.5pp 24-hour rise with sharp +6pp move at 10:27 UTC) suggests late-breaking information favoring VP.Future, but extreme NO volatility (12pp/hr) signals market uncertainty rather than confidence.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero concrete information about either team's roster, recent form, head-to-head record, map pool strength, or individual player performance \u2014 this is an extreme disadvantage for confidence in either direction. MARKET SIGNAL MISREAD: YES side has risen +9.5pp in 24h with only 11 data points (EMA 50%), while NO side shows -14pp sharp move at 10:27 UTC with only 3 data points. This asymmetry suggests emotional/momentum trading rather than information-driven repricing. NO SIDE VULNERABILITY: The sharp -14pp drop on NO coupled with 12.0pp/hr volatility (vs YES's 2.8pp/hr) indicates a flash-move or cascading exit by NO backers, not necessarily fundamental weakness. This creates an oversold opportunity for contrarian positioning. SYMMETRICAL BRIEFING STRUCTURE: The 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' sections are identical copy-paste ('No contradicting evidence', 'Swiss system format', 'European CS2 tournament') \u2014 this reveals that the briefing has ZERO differentiating data favoring either team. Market is pricing based on noise, not skill. UNDERDOG ANGLE \u2014 NO'S HIDDEN CASE: Without team-level data, the market cannot justify the 60-40 split. Z7 Esports may have: (a) strong recent online form not captured in HLTV rankings, (b) favorable map matchups against VP.Future, (c) roster continuity/synergy advantages, or (d) momentum from earlier wins in the Swiss bracket \u2014 all unobservable in this briefing. SWISS FORMAT NEUTRALITY: Both teams face similarly-ranked opponents; neither has structural advantage. If both teams are truly equal in quality (most likely given zero differentiating data), odds should approach 50-50, not 60-40. LOW VOLUME & RECENCY: Only $659 in volume, and the -14pp NO drop occurred just ~8 hours before resolution. This is insufficient time for market correction; the NO side may still be mispriced from panic selling. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT: Event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours. Sharp price moves this close to resolution often reflect psychological factors (herd selling) rather than late-breaking information, which can be reversed once actual play begins. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=25 because briefing provides zero positive evidence for VP.Future's edge; confidence_no=28 because briefing provides zero positive evidence for Z7's weakness, and recent volatility suggests overshooting. PROBABILITY SETTING: 38 reflects a modest underdog lean for NO, acknowledging that the 60% YES price is likely inflated by momentum trading on thin data. A true 50-50 scenario would justify ~42-45 for NO; 38 factors in a small chance that the initial 60% reflects genuine sharp-group information not visible in this briefing. However, without that information being documented, the burden of proof favors the underdog NO side at current pricing.", "key_factor": "Extreme data vacuum makes market pricing speculative; NO side's 40% odds may reflect genuine uncertainty rather than true weakness, and recent sharp -14pp volatility on NO suggests panic selling rather than fundamental deterioration.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.2, "confidence_no": 0.2, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable information about VP.Future or Z7 Esports \u2014 no rosters, rankings, recent results, head-to-head history, or individual player performance metrics. MARKET TIMING: Event resolves in ~8 hours (TODAY/IMMINENT). At this stage, market should be highly informed if either team had significant form advantage, yet current 60-40 split shows modest lean toward YES without explanatory data. PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: YES side rose +9.5pp over 7 days and +6pp in last sharp move (Apr 13 10:27 UTC). This could reflect late-breaking team news, roster confirmations, or odds correction \u2014 but briefing provides no source for this movement. SWISS SYSTEM CONTEXT: Both teams are competing in Round 4 of a 16-team Swiss format. This implies both survived early rounds, suggesting baseline competence, but does not distinguish between them. TOURNAMENT TIER: C-Tier online European tournament with limited coverage. HLTV data fragments in briefing are unrelated to these two teams. BASE RATE: Without team-specific data, historical precedent for unknown-vs-unknown BO3 in structured competition suggests ~50% for either outcome. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set to 20 because briefing provides symmetric lack of evidence for both teams. If strong data existed favoring one side, that side's confidence would be high while the other remained low \u2014 but here, absence of information is complete for both. MARKET PRICE DIVERGENCE: 60-40 split suggests market participants have information (recent form, roster health, streamer commentary, betting syndicate activity) not present in this briefing. Absent access to that information, probability_score must revert to 50. RESOLUTION RISK: Match scheduled 8 hours away; low risk of cancellation/forfeit under normal conditions, but briefing does not confirm match is confirmed live.", "key_factor": "In competitive CS:GO/CS2 BO3 matches between similarly-seeded teams in Swiss format tournaments, base rate approximates 50-50 absent roster/form data; however, confidence is severely constrained by absence of team-specific information.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.6, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on VP.Future or Z7 Esports \u2014 no rosters, recent form, head-to-head history, HLTV rankings, or player-level analysis. MARKET PRICE LACKS FOUNDATION: Current 60% YES price appears arbitrary rather than grounded in team-specific fundamentals; no news or signal in briefing justifies this asymmetry. SHARP MOVE SIGNAL (+6pp YES, -14pp NO at 10:27 UTC) suggests informed trading activity occurred, but briefing provides no catalyst or reasoning to validate this directional shift. RISING YES TREND CONTRADICTS DATA VACUUM: 7-day and 24-hour +9.5pp moves on YES side imply crowd confidence, yet briefing offers no comparative team strength, recent performance, or tournament context to support elevated VP.Future odds. NO SIDE VOLATILITY SPIKE (12.0pp/hr) indicates uncertainty or late-breaking information, but no explanatory news event is documented in briefing; possible late injury, roster change, or tactical intel not captured. SWISS FORMAT CONTEXT NEUTRAL: Both teams face similar-record opponents; this structures the bracket but does not differentiate competitive quality between VP.Future and Z7 Esports. C-TIER TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Lower-tier online event with 28 teams and 16 advancing; no prestige or sponsorship signal differentiates either team's skill tier. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market may be driven by betting volume bias, team name recognition (VP legacy vs Z7 obscurity), or late insider information not documented in briefing. RESOLUTION TIMING: Match is TODAY with ~8 hours to event start; sharp moves in final hours often reflect hard information (roster leaks, odds shift at betting syndicate level) rather than sentiment drift. CONFIDENCE SUPPRESSION: Without team performance data, rosters, or recent form, confidence on BOTH sides must remain low (~28 each); probability_score of 60 reflects current market price, not conviction. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION RISK: If the +6pp VP.Future spike reflects genuine pre-match intelligence (coach talk, scrim results, lineup confirmation), the market may be efficiently priced ahead of briefing documentation. NO BASIS FOR REVERSAL: Current briefing offers no counter-argument to challenge the 60% YES price; a rational analyst cannot justify 40% or lower without contradicting team strength data that simply does not exist in the document.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.6, "probability_no": 0.4, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides tournament structure (Exort Series #25, Swiss BO3, C-Tier) but zero competitive intelligence on VP.Future or Z7 Esports\u2014no roster compositions, regional strength, recent match records, or head-to-head history. MARKET SIGNAL MISMATCH: YES side rose +9.5pp in 24h with sharp +6.0pp move at 10:27 UTC; NO side collapsed -14.0pp with -14.0pp volatility spike same timestamp. This suggests informed traders (likely with HLTV lineups, recent scrims, or roster knowledge) have conviction the briefing document lacks. TIMING CRISIS: Match resolves in ~8 hours (TODAY label). By this point, both rosters are locked, recent form is fixed, and map veto is imminent or underway. A reversal from 60% YES to below 50% would require extraordinary new information (team emergency forfeiture, disqualification)\u2014highly unlikely at 8-hour mark. SWISS SYSTEM STRUCTURE: Round 4 match implies both teams have survived 3 prior rounds with similar win-loss records. This provides minimal differentiator; in Swiss at this stage, skill variance between teams is typically modest. ESPORTS DOMAIN INSIGHT: In CS2 competitive play, team strength is driven by: (1) individual player skill/ratings, (2) in-game leadership/IGL quality, (3) anti-eco and utility economy execution, (4) map pool overlap and bans. None of this data is present. MARKET LIQUIDITY & VIG: Only $659 USD volume on a LIVE event suggests low participation and potential mispricings on either side. The 60% YES price is not clearly justified by briefing content alone. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=35 and confidence_no=32 (both LOW) because the briefing is equally devoid of data supporting or refuting either team. Market movement suggests external information exists (high confidence those traders have data), but that data is hidden from this analysis. RESOLUTION RULES AUDIT: Cancellation, forfeiture, or 50-50 tie resolution clauses are present but unlikely given imminent start time and tournament context. Standard completion assumed. PROBABILITY NEAR PARITY: Absent team-specific intelligence, a coin-flip (50) is technically justified. The +9.5pp YES rise in 24h and market momentum push probability slightly toward 58, but this reflects trader conviction, not briefing evidence. Confidence is deliberately held low to reflect epistemic humility.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains zero actionable team-specific intelligence (roster strength, recent form, head-to-head records, map pool compatibility) despite the event being LIVE/IMMINENT in ~8 hours, making reliable prediction impossible; market movement (+9.5pp YES, -14.0pp NO volatility asymmetry) suggests informed traders have external data, but that data is not present in the briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero roster, form, or head-to-head data for either VP.Future or Z7 Esports. No HLTV rankings, recent results, or player names are provided for either team. MARKET SIGNAL DISCONNECT: YES has risen +9.5pp in 24 hours and NO has fallen -11.0pp with a +6.0pp sharp move at Apr 13 10:27 UTC. This suggests incoming information (likely a lineup announcement, team confirmation, or analyst consensus) favored VP.Future within the last 4 hours. TIMING VULNERABILITY: With ~8 hours to resolution, any reversal requires a rapid, high-impact disruption. Roster changes in online tournaments often happen last-minute, especially in lower-tier C-Tier events where squad depth and availability vary. ABSENCE OF SCOUTING DATA: The briefing is silent on VP.Future's and Z7 Esports' competitive tier within European CS2, their recent Swiss system performance, and their map pool compatibility. This silence is the black swan incubator. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (~28, ~26) because the briefing provides NO substantive evidence for either team. The 55% YES score reflects only the observed market recent drift, not underlying competitive reality. SWISS SYSTEM STRUCTURAL FACTOR: Both teams are 4 rounds deep in a 16-team bracket. Their current records determine opponent seeding, but the briefing does not state either team's round 3 result or current standing. An upset loss by VP.Future in round 3 (not reflected in briefing) would suggest lower skill, favoring Z7. LOW VOLATILITY ON YES VS HIGH ON NO: NO side volatility is 12.0pp/hr vs YES at 2.8pp/hr, suggesting NO-side traders have less conviction and more uncertainty. This absence of NO-side confidence could reflect underdog-status positioning rather than true weakness. ONLINE TOURNAMENT INFRASTRUCTURE RISK: Exort Series is online-only. Server crashes, payment disputes, or platform issues (though rare) are structural tail risks that could flip either team's ability to field a full roster or execute pre-match strategy. CONTRARIAN LENS: If the rest of the council assumes VP.Future is favored based on the +9.5pp recent drift, they are anchoring to market momentum in an information vacuum. The true competitive balance could be much closer\u2014or reversed\u2014if Z7 has higher current form (round 3/4 record unknown in briefing).", "key_factor": "VP.Future's roster or Z7 Esports' roster experiences an unexpected last-minute substitution, illness, or technical issue (player unable to connect, account lockout) that destabilizes preparation or in-game coordination in the final 8 hours before match start.", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5456310679611651, "no_score": 0.46134020618556704, "edge": -0.049368932038834856, "no_edge": 0.05