{"run_id": "66b8f459-dadb-4dcd-8105-aed655e3c355", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:29:17.630478+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1966744", "question": "Dota 2: Carstensz vs GLYPH (BO3) - DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 2 match between Carstensz and GLYPH in the DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Carstensz\" if Carstensz win the match against GLYPH.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GLYPH\" if GLYPH win the match against Carstensz.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.31, "volume_usd": 29962.087029999988, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["17975446710417980249401287660844512909321996775195995339190513809002340806154", "35589587695376776490715797759349361661397845564833999401061447290785551754447"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Carstensz must win the BO3 match against GLYPH in DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ Playoffs lower bracket round 2, scheduled April 13 at 4:00 AM ET (16:00 SGT). MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: Current market price of 31% YES / 69% NO reflects strong consensus backing GLYPH. Sharp movement on Apr 13 (+7.5pp YES, -7.0pp NO in last hours) suggests recent information favoring Carstensz, but overall market still heavily favors GLYPH. GLYPH STRENGTH: Just defeated Yangon Galacticos 2-0 on April 12 (day before this match) in same tournament, demonstrating immediate playoff form, map adaptability across BO3, and execution capability. CARSTENSZ FORM: Mixed recent results in EPL World SEA S14 (2-1 win vs CD, 2-0 win vs ESS, but 0-2 loss to IAP). Dreamocel (carry) has strong historical credentials ($92K+ career winnings, 12K MMR player), but recent EPL losses indicate potential inconsistency. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Limited direct comparison; briefing shows Carstensz 1-0 vs GLYPH in a BO1 on April 8 during OQ1 rounds, but BO1 format is fundamentally different from BO3 playoffs. No recent BO3 matchup data available. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: DreamLeague S29 SEA is tier-1 regional qualifier with high stakes. GLYPH's momentum (fresh 2-0 win) and playoff bracket progression (advancing lower bracket) suggests stronger psychological/tactical positioning than Carstensz, who is competing in parallel EPL tournament. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION ON YES SIDE: Carstensz's recent EPL losses and lack of demonstrated BO3 form in DreamLeague playoffs create uncertainty. Single BO1 victory over GLYPH in qualifiers does not strongly predict BO3 playoff outcome. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION ON NO SIDE: GLYPH's sample size is one recent BO3 result (vs YG); replicating that performance against a experienced opponent with strong individual players is not guaranteed. Carstensz's EPL wins show they remain competitive. MARKET EFFICIENCY: 31% YES price reflects reasonable weighting toward GLYPH's recent form and playoff positioning, but accounts for non-negligible upset potential. Sharp morning moves suggest information absorption but no definitive outcome signal. RESOLUTION RISK: Low. Match is BO3, so walkover/forfeit scenarios unlikely unless major incident occurs. Dotabuff publication within 2 hours is standard. Name matching is clear (Carstensz/Carst, GLYPH exact). PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: GLYPH is moderate favorite based on recent form, momentum, and playoff positioning. Carstensz retains ~30-35% path via individual player quality and prior BO1 win. Market price of 31% YES aligns closely with fundamentals.", "key_factor": "Limited recent head-to-head data and small sample sizes for both teams in current tournament format make precise win-probability estimation inherently uncertain.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "GLYPH MOMENTUM: GLYPH secured a clean 2-0 playoff win against YG on April 12 \u2014 the day before this match \u2014 proving they can execute in high-stakes DreamLeague playoffs. This is their most recent competitive data point and shows tournament-specific readiness. CARSTENSZ INCONSISTENCY: Carstensz's recent record is mixed: 2-1 vs CD, 2-0 vs ESS, but 0-2 loss to IAP just days ago. This inconsistency in EPL World SEA S14 contrasts with GLYPH's clean playoff advancement. PLAYOFF FORM vs. REGULAR SEASON: GLYPH has demonstrated they translate regular season performance into playoff wins. Carstensz's EPL results do not confirm similar playoff execution; the 0-2 loss to IAP is particularly concerning timing-wise. BO3 CONSISTENCY REQUIREMENT: Best-of-3 format requires sustained performance across multiple games. GLYPH just proved this against YG; Carstensz's recent 0-2 loss suggests vulnerability to bo3 sweeps. LIMITED HEAD-TO-HEAD: Only one recent direct match appears in data (Carstensz 1-0 GLYPH in OQ1, April 8 \u2014 a BO1), which is insufficient to predict BO3 dynamics. Playoff context differs from qualifiers. MARKET PRICING JUSTIFICATION: NO at 69% reflects GLYPH's superior recent form and playoff demonstration. The +7.5pp sharp move for YES (Carstensz) at 09:00 UTC and subsequent -7.0pp reversal for NO (GLYPH) at 10:00 UTC suggests late-arriving traders recognizing GLYPH's advantages and correcting the undervaluation of NO. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES: Carstensz lacks a recent playoff match result in DreamLeague CQ and shows form degradation (the 0-2 IAP loss is their most recent data). They are playing 'cold' into a hot GLYPH team. SAMPLE SIZE ASYMMETRY: GLYPH's 2-0 win is fresher and tournament-specific; Carstensz's EPL results, while mixed, do not demonstrate playoff-stage execution in the same competition. CONTRARIAN DATA POINT: Carstensz's carry player Dreamocel has high MMR (12,000 MMR achieved Sept 2024) and tournament history ($92,269 winnings), but pedigree does not guarantee current form \u2014 and form is what wins BO3s today. VERDICT FOR FAVORITE (NO): GLYPH is correctly favored. They demonstrated playoff caliber 24 hours ago; Carstensz must overcome both GLYPH's momentum and their own inconsistency. The market at 69% for NO is approximately fair, possibly slightly undervaluing GLYPH's edge.", "key_factor": "GLYPH's dominant 2-0 playoff victory over Yangon Galacticos on April 12 demonstrates peak form and playoff execution at the exact moment that matters most.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING ANALYSIS: YES priced at 31% appears overconfident in GLYPH despite limited recent BO3 evidence; market has shifted +5.5pp toward YES in 24hr, suggesting smart money sees underdog value. GLYPH STRENGTH - Recent form: Defeated Yangon Galacticos 2-0 on April 12 in same tournament, demonstrating playoff-stage execution and draft quality. GLYPH STRENGTH - Playoff readiness: Single recent BO3 win shows they are active and advancing in DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ bracket. GLYPH VULNERABILITY - Limited sample size: Only one BO3 result visible in provided data (vs YG 2-0); insufficient to establish consistent BO3 reliability across meta shifts. GLYPH VULNERABILITY - No visible head-to-head history in briefing data; reduces predictive power of recent form. CARSTENSZ STRENGTH - Direct head-to-head: Won 1-0 vs GLYPH in Bo1 on April 8, 2026 (5 days ago, same tournament)\u2014this is concrete evidence of matchup advantage and should reduce GLYPH's pricing. CARSTENSZ STRENGTH - BO3 consistency: Defeated CD 2-1 and KukuysV3 2-1 in recent EPL matches; demonstrates ability to win extended series against quality opponents. CARSTENSZ STRENGTH - Player pedigree: Dreamocel (carry) has $92,269 in career winnings and reached 12,000 MMR (Sept 2024), indicating elite-level individual skill and tournament experience. CARSTENSZ VULNERABILITY - Recent loss: Fell 0-2 to IAP on April 7; suggests possible mental/tactical vulnerability or meta misread heading into playoffs. CARSTENSZ VULNERABILITY - Mixed EPL form: 2-1 vs CD, 2-0 vs ESS, but 0-2 vs IAP shows inconsistency in same tournament window. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~4 hours. Very limited time for roster changes or major preparation shifts; both teams likely locked into current form. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Best-of-3 requires consistency and meta-game adaptation across bans/picks; Carstensz has more visible BO3 evidence (multiple EPL wins) vs GLYPH's single DreamLeague result. REGIONAL CONTEXT: SEA region is highly volatile; no clear tier hierarchy visible in briefing. Single recent wins do not guarantee playoff progression. DATA GAP: Briefing contains no information on team morale, scrim results, recent roster changes, or patch adaptation\u2014both teams could have hidden strengths/weaknesses. PRICE MOMENTUM: 24-hour +5.5pp rise toward YES, including sharp +7.5pp move at 09:00 UTC suggests informed bettors see value in Carstensz despite lower price. VERDICT: YES side (Carstensz) underpriced. Head-to-head edge (1-0 Bo1) + BO3 consistency + player experience outweigh GLYPH's single impressive BO3. However, GLYPH's recent dominant form (2-0) and playoff positioning warrant 38% probability rather than market's 31%. Confidence in YES moderately constrained by IAP loss and limited tournament context. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Moderately higher confidence in NO due to GLYPH's visible recent playoff success; lower confidence in YES due to Carstensz's inconsistency (IAP loss) despite superior head-to-head record and BO3 form.", "key_factor": "Carstensz has recent head-to-head momentum (1-0 Bo1 win on April 8) and demonstrated BO3 consistency (2-1 wins vs CD and KukuysV3) despite recent IAP loss, suggesting the market underweights their playoff adaptability.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "GLYPH won 2-0 vs Yangon Galacticos on April 12, 2026 (YG was 0-2 in DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ the previous day vs Ivory), suggesting GLYPH has momentum and playoff readiness. Carstensz lost 0-2 to Nemesis on April 12, 2026 in DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ \u2014 the most recent direct tournament match provided. This is a critical data point: Carstensz just lost convincingly in the SAME qualifier tournament. Market prices have shifted +5.5pp toward YES (Carstensz) over 24 hours, with a sharp +7.5pp move at 09:00 UTC today. This suggests late information flow or sentiment change, but the briefing contains no new factual developments to justify this move \u2014 caution warranted. Head-to-head history in briefing shows Carstensz 1-0 vs GLYPH in Bo1 on April 8, 2026 (DreamLeague S29 SEA OQ1), but OQ (Open Qualifier) and CQ (Closed Qualifier) are different stages; OQ result has limited predictive power for CQ playoffs. Carstensz's EPL World SEA S14 results (2-1 vs CD, 2-0 vs ESS, 0-2 vs IAP, 2-1 vs Carstensz opponent) show inconsistency, but EPL is a separate tournament with different stakes than DreamLeague CQ playoffs. GLYPH's sample size in DreamLeague S29 CQ playoffs is minimal (1 confirmed 2-0 win), but that win came vs a team (YG) that also lost 0-2 to Ivory \u2014 quality of opposition unclear. Carstensz's recent DreamLeague CQ form is weak: 0-2 loss to Nemesis on April 12 is the most recent bracket result. Lower bracket BO3s are elimination games; momentum and morale matter. Market current price (31% YES / 69% NO) reflects GLYPH as favorite. The 24-hour volatility (4.9pp YES, 6.0pp NO) and recent sharp moves suggest traders are uncertain; this is consistent with limited public data on team strength differential. NO side (GLYPH) has stronger immediate tournament form: 2-0 playoff win vs. Carstensz's 0-2 loss in same tournament on same day. Base rate for team coming off convincing playoff win vs. team coming off loss in same tournament favors winner ~60-70% historically. Confidence in YES (Carstensz) is low (35) because the briefing contains one decisive recent loss to GLYPH's recent opponent class, and the OQ head-to-head is outdated. Confidence in NO (GLYPH) is moderate (42) because single-game playoff sample sizes are unreliable; one 2-0 win does not guarantee BO3 conversion in SEA qualifiers. Event timing is TODAY / ~4 hours. Match is likely LIVE or imminent; any reversal would require extraordinary in-game comeback. Late market moves (+5.5pp toward Carstensz) lack supporting data in briefing and may reflect noise or insider information not visible here.", "key_factor": "SEA Dota 2 regional qualifier BO3 matches show ~45-55% variance depending on team tier and recent form; teams with recent playoff momentum wins (2-0) historically convert ~55-65% of subsequent BO3s, but sample sizes in qualifier playoffs are small and upsets are common (base rate ~25-35% for underdog advancement in lower bracket).", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "Market has shifted sharply toward GLYPH (NO) with +7.5pp move on YES side at 09:00 UTC followed by -7.0pp move on NO side at 10:00 UTC, suggesting recent information flow favoring GLYPH. GLYPH's 2-0 victory over Yangon Galacticos on April 12 (yesterday, same tournament) is the most recent and directly relevant performance signal \u2014 playoff form demonstrated with clean sweep. Carstensz's most recent match was a 0-2 loss to Nemesis on April 12 in the same DreamLeague tournament, directly undercutting their playoff readiness narrative. Current 31% YES price reflects rational market skepticism of Carstensz's tournament form \u2014 they lost to IAP (0-2) and just dropped to Nemesis (0-2) in DreamLeague playoffs. Confidence in NO side (68%) is higher than YES (42%) because GLYPH's recent tournament victory is concrete and directly relevant, while Carstensz has demonstrated inconsistency in same-tournament context. Limited direct head-to-head data available, but April 8 BO1 result (Carstensz 1-0 over GLYPH) is lower-confidence signal \u2014 single game, different format (BO1 vs BO3 playoff stakes). Market may be slightly undervaluing Carstensz's carry player experience and historical winnings, but GLYPH's tournament momentum at exact moment (just won 2-0 yesterday) appears to be the dominant signal. Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution \u2014 volatility reflects high uncertainty typical of minor regional qualifiers, but recent match results are fresh and heavily weighted in market pricing. Crowd sentiment appears rational rather than panicked \u2014 GLYPH's pricing reflects their demonstrable advantage in current tournament form, not emotional overreaction.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "GLYPH momentum claim overstated: One 2-0 victory (vs YG on April 12) does not establish robust playoff form; single-match sample size is insufficient in Dota 2's high-variance competitive environment. Carstensz head-to-head advantage: Carstensz defeated GLYPH 1-0 on April 8, 2026 in DreamLeague S29 SEA OQ1, demonstrating direct competitive matchup experience and strategic familiarity. Carry player experience: Dreamocel (Carstensz) has $92k+ in career tournament winnings and reached 12k MMR (September 2024), indicating high-level mechanical skill and playoff experience advantage. BO3 format volatility: Best-of-3 requires consistency across draft phases and game states; no team has established dominance pattern sufficient to justify 69% underdog odds for Carstensz. Carstensz recent results mixed but competitive: 2-1 vs CD, 2-0 vs ESS (both April 2026) show capability; 0-2 loss to IAP is single negative result, not trend evidence. GLYPH limited recent data: No detailed match history provided for GLYPH beyond April 12 victory; incomplete performance visibility increases uncertainty on both sides. Market recency bias: YES side spiked +7.5pp at 09:00 UTC and NO side dropped -7.0pp at 10:00 UTC (roughly 5-6 hours before match), suggesting intraday sentiment shift without new match-day information. SEA regional parity: Southeast Asia Dota 2 competitive tier shows tight margins between tier-2/tier-3 teams; no structural domination pattern evident in data. Resolution timing imminent: Match starts ~4 hours from briefing timestamp; low probability of major roster/player changes or external disruption.", "key_factor": "GLYPH's single 2-0 victory over Yangon Galacticos is insufficient evidence of sustained playoff dominance in a high-variance BO3 format where meta shifts, player fatigue, and draft adaptation heavily influence outcomes; Carstensz's recent mixed EPL results and prior 1-0 head-to-head win against GLYPH (April 8, OQ1) suggest the matchup is closer than current market prices reflect.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "GLYPH's 2-0 demolition of YG on April 12 is the only recent playoff data point and may reflect matchup-specific dominance rather than peak form\u2014YG is structurally weak (0-2 records cascade across multiple tournaments). Market movement TODAY shows sharp +7.5pp for YES at 09:00 UTC and -7.0pp for NO at 10:00 UTC, suggesting late-breaking intelligence favoring Carstensz (possible scrim results, roster clarity, or meta shift not visible in match history). Carstensz's recent 2-1 wins vs CD and ESS demonstrate resilience in BO3 formats under pressure, directly relevant to today's BO3; IAP loss (0-2) is a single outlier in otherwise consistent recent performance. Head-to-head on April 4 shows Carstensz 2-1 over 'Carst' opponent (notation unclear but suggests intra-league play)