{"run_id": "eda35713-67d0-48ec-814b-62eb1c6677e1", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T18:26:21.234392+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963170", "question": "Valorant: UCAM Esports Club vs FALKE ESPORTS (BO3) - VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between UCAM Esports Club and FALKE ESPORTS in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against FALKE ESPORTS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FALKE ESPORTS\" if FALKE ESPORTS win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:40:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:40:00Z", "yes_price": 0.245, "volume_usd": 50274.08927300001, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["57628374770664949582620450542097128678115926684611532310275931410712638839911", "51415966831688563381603021682311584735597072061676340228173182407511718202923"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: UCAM Esports Club wins the BO3 match (2 maps) vs FALKE ESPORTS. Resolution criteria are unambiguous \u2014 match must be played to completion; forfeits/walkovers resolve 50-50. MARKET SIGNAL: Current price is YES=24% (down sharply from 68% on Apr 13 01:00 UTC, -31.5pp in 24h). The -57pp drop at Apr 13 18:25 UTC suggests new information strongly favored FALKE, likely from live match performance or pre-match roster/form revelation. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution (2026-04-13 22:40 UTC). Match scheduled 2:00PM ET (April 13) = 6:00PM UTC, already begun or recently completed at data cutoff (18:25 UTC). Market price reflects near-real-time outcome signal. AVAILABLE DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing contains detailed agent selections and map vetoes from multiple past matches (Maps: Haven, Split, Pearl, Lotus, Bind, Fracture, Breeze; agents shown: Neon, Omen, Cypher, Viper, Sova, etc.) but NO win rates, recent head-to-head records, or current roster strength comparisons between UCAM and FALKE. CASE FOR UCAM (YES, ~22%): Search results mention 'UCAM demonstrated competitive performance in recent Challengers matches with strong individual statistics from players like Famsii and B1SK' and 'playoff format experience.' However, no quantified win rate, streak data, or direct comparison to FALKE provided. CASE FOR FALKE (NO, ~78%): Market sharp move (-57pp at 18:25 UTC, ~5.5h before scheduled match conclusion) indicates STRONG real-time signal favoring FALKE. This timing suggests either live match performance (FALKE leading after maps 1-2) or pre-match intelligence (roster advantage, opponent withdrawal threat, or form differential). NO counter-evidence in briefing supports UCAM. DATA QUALITY GAPS: (1) No recent head-to-head results. (2) No win-loss records for either team in Spring 2026. (3) No commentary on roster changes, player injuries, or team cohesion. (4) Map pool data shown is historical; unknown whether UCAM/FALKE's actual map strengths match historical meta. MARKET INTERPRETATION: 24% YES price reflects rational market belief that FALKE has ~78% win probability. Sharp -57pp move at 18:25 UTC (match likely live or just-completed) suggests strong directional signal, not speculative repositioning. This is the most reliable data point available. CONFIDENCE SPLIT REASONING: confidence_yes=28 (low): Minimal positive evidence for UCAM; no recent form, no head-to-head advantage, market pricing and sharp move both favor FALKE. confidence_no=32 (low): Lack of detailed FALKE roster/form data and no direct match metrics prevent high confidence; rely primarily on market signal and inferred match progress. CRITERIA AMBIGUITY: None flagged. Team names are unambiguous; BO3 format is standard; 50-50 provision only applies to cancellation/forfeiture (not applicable here based on market activity). RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Low. VLR.gg is established esports source; 2-hour fallback to 'credible reporting + video evidence' is reasonable for a Spanish regional match. No team name ambiguity. ~5% downward adjustment to confidence_no for potential oracle delay, but outcome resolution itself appears likely by deadline.", "key_factor": "Briefing data contains extensive agent/map veto details but no recent head-to-head records, win rates, or current form metrics for either team; resolution mechanism is clear but outcome assessment is severely data-constrained.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "NO SIDE MOMENTUM: The market has undergone a dramatic 57pp swing in favor of NO (FALKE) in the last 6 hours, rising from ~19% to 76%. This sharp, recent move typically reflects informed trader activity or updated information about team form, roster status, or matchup dynamics. TIMING & IMMINENCE: Event resolves in ~4 hours. A 57pp move this close to match start is unlikely to be noise\u2014it suggests traders with confidence in FALKE's ability to win are entering at good odds before execution. BRIEFING DATA ASYMMETRY: The briefing provides extensive historical match data and map veto patterns for UCAM across multiple tournaments, but contains NO recent performance metrics, roster updates, or head-to-head data for either team in their current state. This asymmetry is critical. UCAM CASE WEAKNESSES: While UCAM shows historical competitiveness and map flexibility, the briefing notes 'limited specific recent form data for UCAM in direct comparison to FALKE's current state.' No recent win/loss record, player performance, or playoff momentum is documented. FALKE CASE WEAKNESSES: Search results explicitly state 'Search results do not provide FALKE's recent match statistics or roster performance metrics.' We cannot independently justify FALKE's dominance from briefing data alone. MARKET PRICE AS SIGNAL: In a data-scarce environment with imminent resolution, the 76% NO price reflects the collective confidence of active traders. The magnitude and recency of the swing (6 hours before start) suggests this is weighted information, not speculation. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: This is a lower bracket quarterfinal\u2014both teams are already in elimination territory, suggesting survival motivation but also that one team may be experiencing poor form (typical for LB teams). NO CONTRADICTORY EVIDENCE: The briefing provides zero recent data points that would contradict the NO-side bet (e.g., UCAM's recent 2-0 streak, roster upgrades, or direct head-to-head advantage). Absence of supporting evidence for YES is itself evidence against YES. CONFIDENCE CAVEAT: Confidence in NO is only moderate (42) because the briefing lacks direct performance metrics to substantiate FALKE's favoritism. We are largely betting on market efficiency and trader information asymmetry, not on documented team strength. CONFIDENCE IN YES IS LOW (28): No recent statistics, no head-to-head advantage, no roster news, and significant adverse market movement all weigh against the YES underdog. However, BO3 upsets are possible and historical data shows UCAM can compete\u2014hence not lower.", "key_factor": "Sharp 57pp NO-side movement in the last 6 hours (18:25 UTC) suggests informed betting activity favoring FALKE, reflecting likely superior recent form or matchup advantage.", "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES was trading at 68% (EMA) just hours ago and crashed 57pp to 24% at 18:25 UTC \u2014 this is an extreme reversal with only ~4 hours to match start, suggesting either (1) definitive roster/player availability information emerged, (2) sharp money detected a critical vulnerability in UCAM, or (3) the market is correcting a mispriced underdog. UCAM STRENGTHS (EVIDENCE-BASED): Briefing explicitly documents UCAM competitive performance in recent Challengers matches with strong individual statistics from players like Famsii and B1SK; historical playoff format experience across multiple Stage tournaments; demonstrated map veto flexibility across Haven, Split, Pearl, Lotus, Bind, Fracture, Breeze in multiple iterations shows preparation and adaptability. UCAM VULNERABILITY: Limited recent head-to-head data against FALKE specifically and no direct performance comparison metrics provided in briefing; insufficient form trajectory data compared to opponent makes confidence assessment difficult. FALKE CONTEXT: Briefing provides almost NO concrete recent performance data, roster statistics, or form metrics for FALKE beyond confirming they exist in VCL Spain ecosystem; market heavily favors them (76%) despite apparent data scarcity, which is unusual and may reflect unpublished sharp information OR market overreaction to the crash. TIMING CRITICAL: Event resolves in ~4 hours; a 57pp move 4 hours before match is either (a) a last-minute tactical/roster revelation that definitively favors FALKE, or (b) a momentum-driven panic that overshot. Sharp money would have this information before the general market; general market panic comes later. The magnitude suggests (a) is more likely, but briefing contains zero evidence of what changed. BO3 COMEBACK POTENTIAL: Best-of-three format gives UCAM two chances to win maps; if maps are competitive, variance favors the series length format. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing has more UCAM-specific evidence (named players, playoff experience, map flexibility) than FALKE-specific evidence (none provided). This structural gap means confidence in the NO outcome must be lower despite the price, because the briefing provides no justification for 76% confidence in FALKE. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes set to 28 (low) because the 57pp crash suggests real information favored FALKE, and we lack data to defend UCAM against whatever triggered it. confidence_no set to 35 (also low) because the briefing provides essentially zero concrete data supporting FALKE's 76% price \u2014 the confidence gap reflects data absence, not balanced competitive analysis. VERDICT: UCAM at 24-32% is likely underpriced relative to the briefing's own evidence density, but the 57pp crash indicates late-arriving information we cannot see. Probability reflects slight underdog lean for UCAM with heavy uncertainty penalty for missing context.", "key_factor": "UCAM's demonstrated map veto flexibility and playoff experience combined with a massive 57-point market swing in the final hours suggesting late information asymmetry favoring FALKE, which may be overcorrecting.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL DOMINANCE: Market has shifted dramatically from 68% YES (weighted avg) to 24% YES in 24 hours, with a -57pp move at 18:25 UTC. This represents a sharp, late reversal likely driven by insider information, team form updates, or broadcast evidence of team preparation/roster status available 4 hours before match. RECENCY & TIMING: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (4 hours to resolution). Late-stage market moves at this proximity typically reflect real information (coach statements, player status, streamed warm-ups, betting syndicate repositioning) rather than noise. The 35.7pp/hr volatility on NO side and sharp move timing suggests market participants obtained actionable intelligence. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing contains extensive historical map veto/agent data from UCAM's matches but NO recent performance metrics for FALKE. Search results mention 'FALKE ESPORTS and HGE Esports match on April 12' but provide no outcome or stat comparison. Cannot independently evaluate FALKE's current form, roster momentum, or recent wins/losses. CASE FOR YES WEAKENED: UCAM player stats (Famsii, B1SK) reference historical Challengers performance, not recent Rising Phase 1 form. 'Established experience in playoff formats' is not predictive at this competitive tier where roster churn is high. Map veto flexibility shown in past tournaments does not guarantee current map pool performance. CASE FOR NO UNDERDEVELOPED: Briefing explicitly states 'limited specific recent form data for UCAM in direct comparison to FALKE's current state.' This gap applies equally to NO\u2014lack of FALKE data means I cannot confidently articulate why FALKE should win beyond market behavior. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE: YES price at 24\u00a2 is consistent with a heavy underdog facing a live match in 4 hours. At this stage, if UCAM had significant technical/roster advantage, shares would trade closer to 15\u00a2 or lower. The 24\u00a2 floor suggests some residual belief in UCAM, but the -57pp move indicates late information shifted consensus sharply toward FALKE. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Neither confidence score exceeds 30 because the briefing lacks actionable comparative data. confidence_yes=28 reflects that UCAM has some documented experience and player history, but lacks recent form proof against FALKE. confidence_no=26 reflects that FALKE's superiority is inferred entirely from market behavior rather than documented team strength\u2014a weaker evidentiary foundation. The market move is a signal, but not a substitute for team-level analysis. PROBABILITY SETTING: Anchoring to 22 reflects (a) market consensus at 76% NO, (b) the presumption that late moves encode real information, and (c) heavy discounting of UCAM's ability to overcome the late-game momentum shift. Slight deviation below market price (22 vs. 24) accounts for residual uncertainty about FALKE's actual roster/form, which remains opaque in the briefing.", "key_factor": "VCL Spain Rising Phase playoffs: ~45-55% win rates for teams in lower bracket quarterfinals; limited historical data on UCAM vs FALKE specific matchups", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market shows extreme reversal: YES fell 57pp in 4 hours (18:25 UTC), from ~81% to 24%, suggesting panic-driven capitulation rather than new match data. UCAM was 76% favorite 6 hours ago; current 24% price reflects emotional exodus, not fundamental shift in team quality. Briefing provides zero recent head-to-head or direct FALKE performance data\u2014market appears pricing in missing information via fear, not evidence. Both teams are Spanish Rising-level competitors with comparable historical tournament participation; briefing shows no clear skill gap justifying 4:1 underdog odds. Sharp move timing (18:25 UTC, ~4 hours before match) suggests late rumors, lineup changes, or betting syndicate repositioning rather than public news. High volatility (35.7pp/hr on NO side) indicates low conviction; market is guessing, not analyzing. Briefing contains extensive map veto/agent data but no recent form, win-loss records, or roster changes for either team\u2014confidence in both sides must be capped. UCAM's prior competitive history and playoff experience (mentioned in briefing) argue against 76% collapse to 24%; current price is overcorrected fear. Match resolves in ~4 hours with high uncertainty; traders likely fleeing position rather than discovering hard intel. Rational: YES side (UCAM) should be 40-50% given symmetry of data gaps; NO side overheated on crowd panic.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains extensive historical agent/map veto data from multiple prior matches but NO current roster confirmation, recent form metrics, or head-to-head records for either UCAM or FALKE in Phase 1 Playoffs specifically. PRICE ACTION SIGNAL: YES crashed from ~68% to 24% in the last 24 hours with a violent -57pp move at 18:25 UTC (4 hours before scheduled match). This degree of reversal suggests credible external information (roster change, player unavailability, upset prediction from trusted casters/analysts) entered the market after the briefing cutoff. INSUFFICIENT DIRECT COMPARISON: Briefing shows UCAM historical performance data (agents, map picks) but provides NO equivalent FALKE statistics, preventing balanced evaluation of relative team strength. Asymmetric data favors NO confidence being lower. SPANISH RISING TIER CONTEXT: VCL Spain Rising is mid-tier competitive Valorant (below franchised VCL proper). Teams at this level exhibit higher variance in performance and roster stability. BO3 format allows comebacks, reducing predictability. MARKET STRUCTURE OBSERVATION: Current prices (YES 24% vs NO 76%) imply strong market consensus shift toward FALKE in final hours. High volatility (35.7pp/hr on NO side) indicates uncertainty and active trading, not settled conviction. TIMING SENSITIVITY: Match resolves in ~4 hours (TODAY). For LIVE/IMMINENT events with this compressed timeline, large recent reversals reflect real-time information asymmetry rather than slow-moving fundamentals. The 18:25 UTC swing is material. BRIEFING LIMITATIONS: Data freshness note indicates 2026-04-13 18:25 UTC, yet briefing contains no explicit statement about FALKE recent form, roster, or why the market moved so decisively. This is a red flag for incomplete information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes is only slightly higher than confidence_no because (1) briefing data on UCAM is richer but outdated, (2) FALKE data is almost absent, and (3) the recent market move contradicts the historical UCAM data provided. Both sides suffer from incomplete information.", "key_factor": "Market experienced massive -57pp swing at 18:25 UTC (4 hours before match start), suggesting material news, roster changes, or expert prediction shift that is not captured in the provided briefing data.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES crashed from 68% EMA to 24% in 24 hours (-31.5pp), with a violent -57pp reversal at 18:25 UTC (4 hours before match). This is NOT gradual consensus drift \u2014 it signals either late-breaking intel or sharp money repositioning. A move this violent this close to match time suggests either roster news, practice scrim results, or coaching staff confidence shift. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides extensive agent/map veto tables from UCAM's recent matches but NO parallel FALKE performance metrics, recent form, or head-to-head history. The council is evaluating UCAM on granular map pick patterns while flying blind on FALKE's current state. This imbalance is itself a red flag. LOWER-BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: This is a lower-bracket quarterfinal \u2014 both teams have already lost once. UCAM in particular may carry urgency/desperation, while FALKE (if seeded higher) could have morale/preparation gaps. BO3 format amplifies volatility when one team is mentally sharper. PLAYOFF RECENCY: UCAM demonstrated playoff experience in Stage 1, but no data on FALKE's playoff pedigree or clutch performance. Rising/Challengers tournaments reward teams that peak under pressure; insufficient info on FALKE's historical tournament execution. MAP VETO SIGNAL SILENCE: Briefing shows UCAM's veto patterns across multiple iterations, suggesting consistency. But it does NOT show UCAM's recent win rates on their picked/banned maps vs. the current meta. If FALKE has studied UCAM's predictable veto tendencies and prepared specifically for them, this consistency becomes liability. AGENT META SHIFT: The detailed agent selections span multiple prior tournaments (Stage 1, earlier phases). If Valorant received a balance patch or agent nerf between those matches and today (April 13), UCAM's established playbooks could be gutted while FALKE pivoted faster. TIMING PRECISION: Match is 'TODAY' with ~4 hours to resolution. At this stage, final roster confirmations, substitution announcements, and injury/illness disclosures happen in final hours. A single player benched or a stand-in subbed in could flip coaching strategy entirely. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=35 (weak, due to missing FALKE comparator data and inability to validate UCAM's true recent form vs. current opponent); confidence_no=42 (only slightly higher, because briefing lacks FALKE's recent metrics, their playoff history, and current roster/coaching state). Both sides suffer severe information gaps; market price disparity (76% NO) may overweight the 24% YES collapse without enough countervailing detail.", "key_factor": "UCAM field a roster substitution or tactical pivot specifically tuned to exploit FALKE's recent meta shifts, or FALKE suffers a last-minute player availability/connectivity issue in a lower-bracket match where preparation margins are razor-thin.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.26451612903225813, "no_score": 0.7352226720647774, "edge": 0.019516129032258134, "no_edge": -0.019777327935222577, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 35% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963170", "question": "Valorant: UCAM Esports Club vs FALKE ESPORTS (BO3) - VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between UCAM Esports Club and FALKE ESPORTS in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against FALKE ESPORTS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FALKE ESPORTS\" if FALKE ESPORTS win the match against UCAM Esports Club.