en Esprit's recent form. Volume low ($306 USD) with high volatility (6pp/hr): Illiquid market vulnerable to panic cascades. Sharp moves on Apr 12 may reflect emotional exit rather than legitimate edge. Joblife head-to-head win is the only truly compelling differentiator in briefing data, but occurred 7 days ago in dynamic esports environment where form shifts rapidly. Market pricing suggests ~88% conviction in Joblife; brief on both teams shows closer competitive reality (~55-60% range more justified by stats alone). Fear-driven repricing detected: crowd has overestimated Joblife's advantage beyond what recent match record and statistical gap support.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT (PRIMARY SIGNAL): Joblife defeated Esprit Sh\u014dnen 2-1 on Apr 06, providing direct recent competitive evidence in the same tournament and format. In esports, recent H2H is highly predictive of near-term rematch outcomes, especially within 1 week. ROUND DIFFERENTIAL AS STRUCTURAL INDICATOR: Joblife's 0 RD vs Esprit Sh\u014dnen's -8 RD reflects consistent economy management and round-closing discipline\u2014core Valorant fundamentals. An 8-round deficit over ~27 maps played indicates systematic weaknesses in Sh\u014dnen's ability to convert close situations. STANDINGS PLACEMENT REFLECTS AGGREGATE PERFORMANCE: Joblife's 5th-place ranking over Sh\u014dnen's 6th is modest separation, but in an 8-team league mid-season, this reflects accumulated wins and map records (Joblife 4-5 maps vs Sh\u014dnen 3-5). Both are 1-2 in matches, but Joblife's map edge suggests slightly better individual map execution. SH\u014cNEN'S SOLE WIN (CALDYA) INSUFFICIENT COUNTER: While Sh\u014dnen's 2-1 victory vs Caldya Esport (Apr 04) demonstrates capability, Caldya is in 4th place with a 2-2 record\u2014notably Joblife beat Sh\u014dnen after Sh\u014dnen beat Caldya. This suggests Joblife's playstyle or meta adaptation is specifically well-suited to counter Sh\u014dnen, not a general skill disparity. MARKET PRICING (12% YES / 88% NO) REFLECTS INFORMED CONSENSUS: The sharp 22pp move on Apr 12 20:00 UTC aligns with likely information release (match schedules, team roster confirmations, or community betting consensus). The market has converged to heavily favor Joblife, consistent with H2H precedent and standings data. LOW SAMPLE SIZE AND VOLATILITY IN ESPORTS: Valorant team performance in early season is volatile; however, H2H data from the same tournament week is more stable than general standings at this stage. The 39.5pp rise in NO confidence over 7 days suggests market participants accessed H2H information or team scrim results. TIMING & MATCH IMMINENCE: Event resolves in ~7 hours (TODAY, Apr 14 01:00 UTC). No unexpected roster changes, illness, or forfeiture indicators are present in the briefing. Match is extremely likely to proceed as scheduled, making reversal scenarios minimal. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 72 because H2H precedent and round differential provide strong structural evidence favoring NO. confidence_no = 45 because esports upsets occur (meta shifts, individual player form, sub appearances) and the briefing lacks granular player-level stats, veto strategy, or recent scrim intel\u2014typical domain information not disclosed here.", "key_factor": "Head-to-head precedent (Joblife 2-1 over Esprit Sh\u014dnen on Apr 06) is the single strongest predictive signal in a low-sample competitive esports environment, combined with Joblife's superior round differential (+0 vs -8) indicating tighter map control fundamentals.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET CRASH SIGNAL: YES collapsed 20.5pp in 24h with sharp -22pp move on Apr 12 20:00 UTC. This suggests hard intel (roster news, scrim results, or official lineup announcement) hit the market. Briefing does NOT disclose what triggered the crash \u2014 a silent data gap. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT IGNORED: Joblife already beat Esprit Sh\u014dnen 2-1 on Apr 06. Market is treating this as dispositive, but BO3 rematches in esports often feature prep-counter-prep cycles. Esprit Sh\u014dnen may have studied that loss and designed a hard-counter draft/strat. ROUND DIFFERENTIAL MIRAGE: Joblife's +0 RD vs Esprit Sh\u014dnen's -8 RD is tight enough to suggest noise, not skill gap. Both teams are genuinely volatile (1-2 records, no playoff momentum). This is not a tier-1 vs tier-8 mismatch; it's a coin flip masquerading as a 12% underdog. PLAYOFF PRESSURE ASYMMETRY: Both teams at 1-2 with 'remainder of season' remaining. Esprit Sh\u014dnen may be hungrier or more cohesive under pressure if Joblife has internal complacency post-victory over Sh\u014dnen on Apr 06. Briefing is silent on morale/coaching. AGENT/MAP POOL BLINDNESS: Briefing provides NO agent stats, map bans, or individual player performance data. Valorant is heavily meta-dependent. A single agent nerf or map rotation could flip matchup odds. Esprit Sh\u014dnen could specialize in post-patch meta Joblife has not adapted to. SUBSTITUTE OR ILLNESS WILDCARD: Resolve timing is TODAY, ~7h out. A last-minute player unavailability or stand-in sub (injury, visa, illness) disclosed on match day would NOT be reflected in 1-week price history. This is structurally possible under esports logistics. TIMEZONE/SCHEDULING FATIGUE: BO3 resolves late evening EU time (0100 UTC Apr 14). Fatigue or map-side variance in later rounds favors the team with better mental discipline or subs bench depth \u2014 invisible in aggregate stats. CONTRARIAN EDGE: Market is 88% confident in Joblife on thin volume ($306 total) and one recent win. Overconfidence in a rematch scenario is common in esports prediction markets. 12% YES is plausible if you believe the meta or roster unknowns favor Esprit Sh\u014dnen. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=72 because Joblife's stats-based advantage is weak (h2h precedent, slight ranking edge) and easily overturned by hidden tactical/roster variables. confidence_no=45 because briefing offers NO scouting data, coaching intel, or recent form breakdown to validate Joblife's assumed dominance. The NO case rests on inference, not evidence.", "key_factor": "Esprit Sh\u014dnen executes a tactical meta shift (agent/economy pivots) that exploits a known weakness in Joblife's recent defensive setups, compounded by untracked player form variance or substitute roster positioning in a high-pressure must-win scenario.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.21233333333333332, "no_score": 0.7840399002493766, "edge": 0.09733333333333331, "no_edge": -0.10096009975062337, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1960168", "question": "Valorant: Esprit Sh\u014dnen vs Joblife (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Esprit Sh\u014dnen and Joblife in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 3:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Esprit Sh\u014dnen\" if Esprit Sh\u014dnen win the match against Joblife.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Joblife\" if Joblife win the match against Esprit Sh\u014dnen.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T01:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T19:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.115, "volume_usd": 306.441029, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["78136033396023401274443420961105344893153618875147338657678278738451263198440", "107020831265690436421054474723428982393725971822586544776931980804971401022198"]}, "key_facts": ["Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "R, ACS, K, D, A, +/\u2013, KAST, ADR, HS%, FK, FD, +/\u2013", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from WIP Esports vs.", "Caldya Esport - Week 4 match of Challengers 2026: France Revolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "Nuxeria Esport - Week 1 match of Challengers 2026: France Revolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "## Format\n\n## Results\n\n### Standings\n\n| Standings Week 1  Week 1 | | | | | | |\n ---  ---  --- \n| 1.", "| WIP EsportsWIP Esports WIP Esports | 3-0 | 6-2 | 99-69 | +30 |\n| 2.", "| F9 EICARF9 EICAR F9 EICAR | 3-1 | 6-4 | 113-100 | +13 |\n| 3.", "| Mandatory Mandatory | 2-1 | 5-2 | 75-55 | +20 |\n| 4.", "| Caldya EsportCaldya Esport Caldya Esport\") | 2-2 | 6-6 | 120-117 | +3 |\n| 5."], "news_summary": "Esprit Sh\u014dnen and Joblife are competing in the VALORANT Challengers 2026 France: Revolution Stage 2 regular season. Esprit Sh\u014dnen holds a 1-2 record with 3-5 map record and -8 round differential, placing 6th. Joblife has a 1-2 record with 4-5 map record and 0 round differential, placing 5th. Both teams are in the lower half of standings but remain competitive in a 8-team format where most teams have played multiple matches.", "side_yes_case": ["Joblife has superior round differential (0) compared to Esprit Sh\u014dnen (-8), indicating closer competitive matches", "Joblife is currently ranked 5th while Esprit Sh\u014dnen is 6th, suggesting slightly better overall performance", "Joblife has won 4 maps to Esprit Sh\u014dnen's 3 maps, demonstrating better map-level consistency"], "side_no_case": ["Esprit Sh\u014dnen defeated Caldya Esport 2-1 (Apr 04), showing ability to beat ranked opponents", "Both teams have identical 1-2 match records with limited separation in performance", "Esprit Sh\u014dnen has shown direct competitive performance against mid-tier teams similar to Joblife's level"], "key_context": ["BO3 format: Best-of-three match determines winner", "Both teams are 1-2 in standing with only 1 match win each through multiple weeks", "Tournament is mid-stage group play with 8 teams competing; top teams (WIP Esports 3-0, F9 EICAR 3-1) significantly ahead", "Head-to-head record shows Joblife defeated Esprit Sh\u014dnen 2-1 on Apr 06 in earlier matchup", "Both teams remain in playoff contention range with remainder of season to improve positioning"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T18:29:40.696543Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "78136033396023401274443420961105344893153618875147338657678278738451263198440", "data_points": 15, "weighted_avg": 0.12546724930797357, "change_1w_pp": -20.5, "change_24h_pp": -20.5, "volatility_24h": 6.036632676081432, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T20:00:53Z", "delta_pp": -22.0}]}, "no": {"token_id": "107020831265690436421054474723428982393725971822586544776931980804971401022198", "data_points": 25, "weighted_avg": 0.8629878747544849, "change_1w_pp": 39.5, "change_24h_pp": 39.5, "volatility_24h": 4.707239399775458, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T19:00:46Z", "delta_pp": 19.000000000000007}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T20:00:45Z", "delta_pp": 21.999999999999996}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T18:29:41.281936Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-14T01:30:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T23:45:12.737067+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
