fidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Contra is objectively stronger: 3rd vs 5th seed, 4-3 vs 3-4 record, +22 vs -49 map differential, and a clean 2-0 H2H victory on Feb 24 all point to YES winning ~70-75% of the time in a vacuum. However, the briefing is silent on critical competitive factors: no individual player performance metrics, no recent scrim results, no patch/meta shifts between Feb 24 and April 13 (nearly 7 weeks), no coaching adjustments or roster changes documented. LAZER's trajectory is hidden: the briefing shows only aggregate W-L records, not whether LAZER is on a winning or losing streak. If LAZER won 3 straight before the playoffs while Contra cooled off, this isn't visible in the summary. Playoff format introduces volatility: Contra may have benefited from a favorable regular season schedule; LAZER's 3-week preparation gap (last match Mar 11 vs LYON, loss 0-2) could indicate either rust OR a structured reset for a new tactical approach. Map pool and meta are unspecified: if ACE Masters features a different map rotation or a recent game patch favors aggressive/antistrat Valorant (LAZER's potential strength), Contra's Feb 24 dominance becomes less predictive. No mention of key personnel issues: the briefing lists coaches and IGLs but does not confirm all players are available. A last-minute absence or substitution for either team could swing the series, especially if LAZER brings in a fresher or more anti-Contra specialist. Market price rise from 53% (7-day EMA) to 76% (current) is steep and driven by sentiment, not new public data: the sharp moves on Apr 10, 11, and 13 suggest information asymmetry or speculation, not confirmed roster/meta news. Base case: Contra wins 72% because the evidence is strong on fundamentals (rank, H2H, map diff). Confidence in YES is moderate-high (78%) because the H2H and standings are objective. Confidence in NO is LOW (45%) because the briefing does not articulate a credible LAZER structural advantage\u2014only speculative tournament dynamics. The 28% NO tail risk (LAZER upset) hinges on hidden meta adaptation, undisclosed roster adjustments, or playoff mentality shifts that the data cannot measure. This is plausible but not yet visible in any briefing signal.", "key_factor": "LAZER executes a targeted meta counter-pick strategy or roster adjustment (potential substitute player) that exploits a specific tactical vulnerability in Contra's Stage 1 playstyle, combined with playoff-format adaptation that hasn't been tested in head-to-head play.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6749090909090909, "no_score": 0.31069148936170216, "edge": -0.09009090909090911, "no_edge": 0.07569148936170217, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "MODERATE VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.3071895424836601, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1920648", "question": "Valorant: Contra vs LAZER (BO3) - VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Contra and LAZER in the VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group B, initially scheduled for April 13 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Contra\" if Contra win the match against LAZER.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LAZER\" if LAZER win the match against Contra.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. 