o any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.78, "volume_usd": 964.7909569999998, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["23306015103473931602338448812772591509825972170721987422567158967206877614934", "93129942166968585106323796335641380981015903376326833767629289586852914163357"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides NO Dota 2-specific information about Team Lynx, MODUS, their recent performance, rosters, head-to-head records, or meta alignment. Search results returned only PUBG Mobile, Honor of Kings, and Age of Empires IV data\u2014completely irrelevant to this match. MARKET PRICE AS SOLE SIGNAL: Current market prices show YES (Team Lynx) at 78% and NO (MODUS) at 22%. With no independent competitive data available, this price represents the only market signal of relative team strength. PRICE TREND CONTEXT: YES side has risen 14.5pp over 7 days and 24 hours, with a sharp +9.0pp move on Apr 13 at 16:00 UTC (9.25 hours before match). This suggests real-money traders have updated their confidence in Team Lynx winning, but the briefing provides no explanation for this directional shift. EVENT TIMING CONSTRAINT: This is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~1.6 hours at 20:00 UTC). By this point, match outcome may already be partially revealed via livestreams, which could explain sharp price moves. Market prices will converge to ~$0.01/$0.99 once outcome is clear, even before official Dotabuff resolution. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes = 35 reflects moderate trust in the 78% market price signal, but WITHOUT team data, this is speculative inference from price action alone. confidence_n