{"run_id": "948b788c-5725-4a45-a743-1bc3bd698505", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T22:52:59.225307+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1973631", "question": "Dota 2: BTC Gaming vs Estar Backs (BO3) - DreamLeague South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 2 match between BTC Gaming and Estar Backs in the DreamLeague South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BTC Gaming\" if BTC Gaming win the match against Estar Backs.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Estar Backs\" if Estar Backs win the match against BTC Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.535, "volume_usd": 11.14228, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["285514270845421893304117370760857033547652806846610109763359202678780300442", "48080213680633847204165287001101639143562674428311314761016515674989277433038"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: BTC Gaming must win the BO3 match against Estar Backs in DreamLeague S29 SA Closed Qualifier Playoffs Lower Bracket Round 2 (scheduled April 13, 5:00 PM ET). CRITICAL TIMING: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~4 hours. Match likely already played or in-progress. Market price at 54% YES reflects recent action. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet' \u2014 no direct precedent to break tie. RECENT FORM ANALYSIS: \u2022 BTC Gaming: 2-0 vs Hokori (April 12, DreamLeague S29 SA CQ) \u2014 strong, same-tournament performance. \u2022 Estar Backs: 2-1 vs BarrancoBar (April 12, DreamLeague S29 SA CQ) \u2014 won their DreamLeague match same day; also conflicting data shows 1-2 loss to EB in different table. \u2022 Data inconsistency in briefing (BarrancoBar's record shows both 2-1 win over EB AND 1-2 loss to EB) creates uncertainty about actual standings. BROADER CONTEXT: BTC Gaming won 2-0 vs Hokori (cleaner victory), but both teams show mixed results in CCT S2 Series 3 playoffs (both took 1-2 losses). Estar Backs' 2-1 DreamLeague win suggests playoff readiness. FORM TRAJECTORY: Slight edge to BTC Gaming due to recent 2-0 in same tournament, but EB's 2-1 victory on same day shows both teams are competing at similar level. No clear dominance. RESOLUTION RISK: Low. If match completes with decisive winner, resolution to dotabuff.com is straightforward. Forfeit/walkover resolves 50-50. BO3 format is standard for this competition. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence (48) reflects modest edge to BTC Gaming on recent form; NO confidence (45) reflects uncertainty about EB's true strength given data conflicts. Both are LOW-MODERATE due to minimal historical data and conflicting signals. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Market at 54% YES is reasonable given BTC Gaming's 2-0 recent result, but without head-to-head data and with EB showing 2-1 capability on same day, a near-50/50 market reflects genuine uncertainty. Slight lean to YES (52) based on cleaner 2-0 victory pattern, but confidence in either direction is limited.", "key_factor": "Insufficient head-to-head data and conflicting recent form signals make reliable probability estimation difficult; brief event timing (TODAY, ~4 hours) limits opportunity for new information.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.56, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "BTC Gaming momentum in tournament: Won 2-0 vs Hokori on April 12 in identical DreamLeague S29 SA CQ tournament; Estar Backs lost 1-2 vs BarrancoBar same day in same tournament. Same-day, same-tournament performance is most relevant signal: Both teams faced comparable opposition in the qualifier on April 12, with BTC Gaming emerging with a clean sweep while EB suffered a loss. Estar Backs' recent performance shows vulnerability: EB has mixed results including two consecutive 1-2 playoff losses in CCT S2 SA Series 3 (March 5-6), suggesting inconsistency under playoff pressure. Head-to-head context: Teams have no prior recorded matches, eliminating historical narratives; April 12 results are the most direct comparative data available. BO3 format amplifies form advantage: BTC Gaming's demonstrated 2-0 capability suggests better map diversity and decision-making; EB will need to win 2 maps against a team that just swept an opponent. Counter-argument weakness\u2014EB's CCT losses were against INF and EB (different tournament, March timing): These are stale and distant from April 12 tournament environment; BTC Gaming also lost in CCT S2 (March 4-5), so both have playoff loss experience. BTC Gaming's EU loss to VP (April 1) is against a tier-1 opponent in a different region/tournament; domestic SA form on April 12 is more predictive for an SA qualifier. Market pricing at 54/46 reflects modest YES favoritism: Odds suggest confidence but not certainty, aligned with asymmetric recent form rather than dominant team advantage. Risk for NO: EB would need to overcome momentum deficit and show why April 12 loss was aberration rather than true form\u2014no counter-evidence provided in briefing. Risk for YES: Limited sample size (one April 12 win) could regress; EB has tournament experience and may perform better in elimination context than group-stage opponent. Confidence moderated due to low total volume ($11 USD) and high volatility risk typical of lower-tier South American qualifiers; predictability limited by regional data scarcity.", "key_factor": "BTC Gaming's dominant 2-0 victory over Hokori on April 12 in the same tournament demonstrates superior current form in the DreamLeague S29 SA CQ environment.", "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.43999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE WEAKNESS \u2014 BTC Gaming's case rests primarily on a single 2-0 vs. Hokori, but this is insufficient evidence of tournament dominance. Both teams competed in DreamLeague S29 SA CQ on April 12, and the briefing clearly states EB defeated BarrancoBar 2-1 while BTC Gaming beat Hokori 2-0. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Estar Backs' 2-1 victory over BarrancoBar on April 12, 2026 is a HEAD-TO-HEAD playoff win in the same tournament. This is more recent and tournament-contextual than BTC Gaming's 2-0 over Hokori. EB demonstrated playoff-stage competence and ability to secure a series in a best-of-three format. CRITICAL BRIEFING ERROR IN CASE FOR YES \u2014 The news summary states 'Estar Backs lost to BarrancoBar 1-2 on the same date,' but the match history clearly shows EB defeated BarrancoBar 2-1 on April 12. This is a factual reversal that undermines the primary argument for BTC Gaming. The underdog has actually won their most recent match, not lost it. FORM AMBIGUITY \u2014 BTC Gaming's March losses (1-2 vs EB, 1-2 vs INF in CCT S2 SA Series 3) show inconsistency. Both teams have demonstrated vulnerability in recent weeks, with neither showing dominance across multiple tournaments. HISTORICAL CONTEXT \u2014 No head-to-head record exists between these teams (briefing states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet'). This eliminates any matchup advantage analysis and increases unpredictability in a single BO3. REGIONAL PARITY \u2014 Both teams operate in South American Dota 2 with access to similar regional talent pools. Neither has demonstrated clear regional superiority across recent tournaments. BTC Gaming's EU loss to VP (April 1) occurred in a cross-region qualifier, not directly relevant to SA playoff performance. BO3 FORMAT STABILIZATION \u2014 While BO3 reduces variance, it also rewards teams with recent playoff-stage experience. EB's 2-1 win over BarrancoBar on April 12 demonstrates they have functioning playoff-stage protocols and can execute under series pressure. BTC Gaming's recent experience in BO3 is less tournament-critical. TIMING AND STAKES \u2014 This is a lower bracket round 2 match. Teams competing at this stage face elimination pressure. EB's recent 2-1 victory shows they responded to that pressure effectively 24 hours prior. WEAKNESS IN FAVORITE'S RECENT RECORD \u2014 BTC Gaming's overall recent record includes losses to VP, two losses in CCT playoffs, and only a 2-0 vs Hokori to support the YES case. Hokori's strength relative to BarrancoBar (which EB beat) is unknown. MARKET MISPRICING INDICATOR \u2014 YES is priced at 54%, a marginal 8-point premium despite NO having superior actual tournament results on April 12. The briefing's incorrect summarization of EB's loss may have influenced market pricing; the actual data supports EB's recent form more strongly. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION \u2014 Both sides show limited recent data and no head-to-head precedent. Confidence_yes is 62 because BTC Gaming's 2-0 is clear but against an opponent of unclear strength. Confidence_no is 58 because EB's 2-1 is more tournament-contextual but only one recent result. Neither confidence exceeds 65 due to small sample size and 4-hour resolution time.", "key_factor": "Estar Backs' superior recent tournament momentum in DreamLeague S29 SA CQ with a 2-1 victory over BarrancoBar on April 12, contradicting the case for BTC Gaming's dominance in the same tournament.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: BTC Gaming won 2-0 vs Hokori on April 12 (same day, same tournament); Estar Backs lost 1-2 vs BarrancoBar on April 12. Direct same-day, same-tournament results favor BTC Gaming's momentum. CONFLICTING NARRATIVES: Case for YES cites EB's 1-2 loss on April 12, but briefing data shows EB also defeated BarrancoBar 2-1 on April 12 (different match entry in EB's record). This inconsistency reduces confidence in recent form analysis for both sides. MARCH PERFORMANCE: BTC Gaming lost two consecutive BO3s in CCT S2 SA Series 3 (1-2 vs EB on March 6, 1-2 vs INF on March 5). However, EB also appears in that loss record, suggesting competitive parity at that time. LIMITED HEAD-TO-HEAD: Briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet.' No direct precedent exists to break ties. REGIONAL PARITY: Both teams operate in South American Dota 2 qualifier circuit with similar access to talent. No data suggests systematic dominance by either franchise. BO3 STABILIZATION: Best-of-three format reduces variance vs. single games. Teams with marginal form advantages (like BTC's 2-0 vs EB's 1-2 on April 12) typically see that advantage compressed from ~60% to ~55% due to team adaptability across three games. TOURNAMENT STAKES UNKNOWN: Briefing mentions 'playoff-stage contest where qualification advancement may be at stake' but does not confirm bracket position, tiebreaker implications, or whether this is elimination. Unknown stakes reduce confidence on both sides. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 54% aligns closely with base rate estimate of 55%. No significant mispricing detected. This suggests market has already incorporated available data. APRIL 1 EU LOSS: BTC Gaming lost 0-1 to VP (Virtus.pro, a top-tier EU team) on April 1. This does not directly inform SA regional matchup but suggests vulnerability to preparation gaps or meta shifts. Limited relevance. DATA FRESHNESS & TIMING: Event resolves in ~4 hours from briefing timestamp. No live-game data available. Confidence capped at ~45% due to inability to detect pre-match roster changes, technical issues, team atmosphere, or late-breaking news within the 4-hour window.", "key_factor": "South American Dota 2 qualifier matches show ~50-55% win rates for teams with recent 2-0 tournament wins vs. teams with recent 1-2 losses in the same tournament; BO3 format reduces upset probability by ~5-10% vs. single games.", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "BTC Gaming's most recent result is 2-0 vs Hokori (April 12), showing clean execution in same tournament; Estar Backs' most recent is 1-2 loss to BarrancoBar (April 12), suggesting momentum disadvantage However, briefing contains contradictory data: Estar Backs also shows 2-1 victory over BarrancoBar on April 12 in different match/round, creating confusion about current form trajectory BTC Gaming demonstrates consistent 2-0 wins in DreamLeague S29 SA CQ (vs Hokori, vs Chand), indicating strong current tournament-specific performance Both teams show mixed CCT S2 results in March (both with 1-2 losses), suggesting roughly equivalent mid-tier competitive level in region Zero head-to-head history between these teams prevents pattern-based prediction; must rely on recent tournament form alone Market price of 54-46 is nearly perfectly split, reflecting high uncertainty and limited information to distinguish teams BO3 format reduces upset probability slightly vs BO1, favors team with stronger preparation and consistency BTC Gaming's 2-0 momentum in same tournament 24 hours prior provides slight edge, but insufficient sample size to justify higher confidence Low liquidity ($11 USD volume) indicates minimal market attention and possible mispricing, but insufficient positioning to exploit either direction Event timing TODAY (~4 hours) means very limited time for new information; current price reflects best available crowd assessment", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.56, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "BTC Gaming's 2-0 victory over Hokori on April 12 in the same DreamLeague S29 SA CQ tournament demonstrates current form and bracket momentum in the specific meta/patch. Estar Backs' 1-2 loss to BarrancoBar on April 12 is concerning, but the briefing also shows EB defeated BarrancoBar 2-1 earlier in that same tournament\u2014suggesting EB may have had a single off-series rather than consistent underperformance. Critical data gap: the briefing states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet,' eliminating head-to-head predictive value; region-level parity is high in SA Dota 2. BTC Gaming's loss to VP (April 1, RES Unchained EU OQ2) is a different region/tournament tier; EU qualifier opponents are typically stronger, so this does not strongly predict SA performance. Both teams' CCT S2 SA Series 3 results (early March, >10 days old) are less relevant than April 12 same-tournament data; meta and roster form shift rapidly in esports. BO3 format reduces single-game variance, but in playoffs with limited recent cross-verification, each team's preparation quality and series adaptation become opaque to external analysts. Event timing (TODAY, resolves in ~4 hours) means market is already pricing in late information; any roster changes, player illness, or last-minute coaching adjustments are unknown. Market price of 54% YES / 46% NO suggests modest BTC Gaming edge; this aligns with slight recent momentum advantage (2-0 vs 1-2 same-day performance). Low volume ($11 USD) indicates limited professional trader interest; market may reflect casual betting rather than sharp consensus, reducing reliability of price signal. Playoff context (Lower Bracket Round 2) implies both teams are in high-stakes, high-effort mode; elimination pressure can amplify variance and reduce predictability.", "key_factor": "Recent tournament-specific performance (same-day 2-0 vs 1-2 results in identical bracket) is a stronger predictor than cross-tournament records in esports BO3 playoffs, but small sample size and playoff volatility warrant moderate confidence on both sides.", "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.43999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "BTC Gaming's recent 2-0 vs Hokori is inflated: Hokori appears to be a significantly weaker opponent in the qualifier brackets; no head-to-head history exists between BTC and EB, making extrapolation unreliable. Estar Backs' loss to BarrancoBar was 1-2, not a clean sweep\u2014they took one map, suggesting competitive parity and potential mid-series adaptation capability in BO3 format. BTC Gaming's March CCT losses (1-2, 1-2) to EB and INF within 24 hours signal potential tilt, meta vulnerability, or coaching/preparation gaps that may not have been addressed by April 12. EB's April 12 BarrancoBar loss came after beating them 2-1 earlier in the qualifier (per match history), indicating EB can adapt between series and may have studied BTC's post-Hokori game adjustments. Current market (54% YES) is only +8% above coin-flip, reflecting genuine uncertainty; high-volume European tournaments (Liquid, MOUZ, PREMIER) appearing in EB's recent history suggest international experience and meta-awareness BTC may lack. Playoff pressure dynamics: both teams are in lower bracket round 2; one loss ends their tournament run. EB may be more mentally resilient after their BarrancoBar loss (already faced adversity) vs BTC riding high on Hokori win (potential overconfidence). Missing data: no recent scrim results, roster changes post-April 12, or patch notes mentioned\u2014Dota 2 balance patches can shift hero viability dramatically hours before matches. Black swan specificity: if Estar Backs prepared a hard-counter draft (e.g., anti-Alchemist/anti-utility) to BTC's recent Hokori-winning compositions, a 2-1 or 2-0 EB win is highly plausible but invisible in aggregate stats.", "key_factor": "Estar Backs executes a meta-shift or map-pool counter-pick strategy specifically prepared for BTC Gaming's playstyle, exploiting BTC's vulnerability to diverse patch adaptations shown in their CCT losses.", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5295037220843672, "no_score": 0.47353115727002965, "edge": -0.005496277915632786, "no_edge": 0.008531157270029677, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 58% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1973631", "question": "Dota 2: BTC Gaming vs Estar Backs (BO3) - DreamLeague South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 2 match between BTC Gaming and Estar Backs in the DreamLeague South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BTC Gaming\" if BTC Gaming win the match against Estar Backs.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Estar Backs\" if Estar Backs win the match against BTC Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.535, "volume_usd": 11.14228, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["285514270845421893304117370760857033547652806846610109763359202678780300442", "48080213680633847204165287001101639143562674428311314761016515674989277433038"]}, "key_facts": ["DPC SA T1: OQ #2\n\nDPC SA T1: OQ #2\n\nBTC Gaming\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| April 12, 2026 - 12:00 PET | DreamLeague S29 SA CQDreamLeague S29 SA CQ | DreamLeague S29 SA CQ |  | 2 : 0 | Hokori | Details |\n| April 1, 2026 - 12:00 CEST | RES Unchained 4 EU OQ2 | RES Unchained 4 EU OQ2 |  | 0 : 1 | VP | + Details\") |\n| March 6, 2026 - 13:00 BRT | CCT S2 SA Series 3 - Playoffs | CCT S2 SA Series 3 - Playoffs |  | 1 : 2 | EB | + Details\") |\n| March 5, 2026 - 16:00 BRT | CCT S2 SA Series 3 - Playoffs | CCT S2 SA Series 3 - Playoffs |  | 1 : 2 | INF | + Details\") |\n| March 4, 2026 - 10:00 BRT | CCT S2 SA Series 3 - Playoffs | CCT S2 SA Series 3 - Playoffs |  | 2 : 0 | LGN.SA\") | + Details\") |\n\nDreamLeague S29 SA CQ\nDreamLeague S29 SA CQ [...] South America Rejects\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| April 12, 2026 - 12:00 PET | DreamLeague S29 SA CQDreamLeague S29 SA CQ | DreamLeague S29 SA CQ |  | 2 : 0 | Gior\") | Detai