r 2-1 in their DreamLeague S29 SA CQ opener (April 12, 2026)", "BTC Gaming's loss to VP in RES Unchained 4 EU OQ2 (April 1, 2026) suggests vulnerability against stronger opponents", "BTC Gaming lost twice in CCT S2 SA Series 3 playoffs with 1-2 results (March 5-6)", "Limited recent head-to-head data between these specific teams"], "key_context": ["This is a playoff-stage match in DreamLeague S29 SA Closed Qualifier (likely affects stakes and team preparation)", "Both teams compete in the South American region with access to similar talent pool and competitive level", "Recent matches (April 8-12, 2026) show both teams in active tournament play", "BO3 format reduces variance compared to single-game matches", "Sample size of recent results is limited, making form-based predictions less reliable"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T22:52:47.113826Z", "price_history": null}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-14T03:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-14T10:12:18.168535+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "9f8c4a56-4fa8-4d57-9303-93aa4af7c27f", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T22:55:06.498227+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918548", "question": "Valorant: Team Evictix vs Pigeons (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Team Evictix and Pigeons in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Evictix\" if Team Evictix win the match against Pigeons.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Pigeons\" if Pigeons win the match against Team Evictix.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T04:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T22:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.195, "volume_usd": 57720.285306000005, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["40223149503937835937389235065202349569414537356392758366922985651723270733750", "57461985672384547049497524731597479632196429194371213621696279429133875496292"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "TIMING CRITICAL: Event timing shows 'TODAY' with ~5 hours to resolution (2026-04-14 04:15 UTC). Briefing timestamp is 2026-04-13 22:53 UTC, indicating match is LIVE or recently concluded. Market show sharp -27.0pp drop on YES (Evictix) at 22:52 UTC on 2026-04-13, suggesting real-time information reached traders that Evictix is underperforming or losing. RECORD-BASED DISADVANTAGE: Evictix is 1-3 in Swiss Stage R5, meaning they have lost 3 of 4 matches. Pigeons' exact record is not explicitly stated, but context suggests they are competitive/better-positioned given the market odds (80% NO = 20% YES). INDIVIDUAL PERFORMANCE DATA: Head-to-head statistics show Evictix players with consistent negative K/D trends (shawz: -1 to -4 across opponents; Slammed: -1 to -2; Scottie: -5 on multiple maps). Pigeons' Andersin shows exceptional economy (111) and stable performance. Zamal shows high kill count (5 in recent round). These metrics suggest Pigeons roster depth and consistency. COUNTERARGUMENT (dre/tdawgg): Evictix has individual positives (dre showing positive differentials on some maps; tdawgg +2 vs Zamal). However, these are isolated wins within larger negative sample, not indicative of team-level dominance. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES price fell 32.5pp over 7 days and 25.0pp over 24 hours. The sharp -27.0pp drop at 22:52 UTC (match day, likely during or immediately after map play) indicates traders reacted to live game information with high confidence toward NO side. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous. Match must conclude with a winner by standard rules (no forfeits/walkovers/cancellations indicated). Resolution will use vlr.gg within 2 hours post-event or consensus reporting. No ambiguity in team identification. PROBABILISTIC INFERENCE: Market price (20% YES / 80% NO) reflects both historical record disadvantage and real-time game information from live play. While markets can misprice, a 27pp swing specifically at match time during R5 (where record-based pressures are high) suggests informed trader reaction to observed gameplay. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: High confidence in NO (62) because (1) pre-match record disadvantage is clear, (2) sharp real-time market move provides additional signal, and (3) individual player stats show Pigeons consistency. Lower confidence in YES (45) because briefing lacks explicit confirmation of current map state, live score, or remaining match length\u2014the outcome may technically be partially determined but not officially called. However, the -27pp move at 22:52 UTC on match day is strong directional evidence.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE as of briefing timestamp (22:53 UTC on scheduled match day); outcome may already be determined but not yet reflected in official sources, creating potential for market share trading at extremes (~$0.01/$0.99) before formal resolution.", "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO - Pigeons 80% price): Evictix enters at 1-3 in Swiss Stage R5, indicating sustained underperformance and likely psychological disadvantage heading into a must-win scenario. A 1-3 record in a competitive VCL environment suggests structural team issues, not variance. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES - Evictix 20% price): Evictix's individual player statistics reveal systemic underperformance. shawz shows -3 to -4 K/D differentials across multiple opponents; Slammed consistently negative (-1 to -2); Scottie severely negative (-5 in multiple matchups). This is not noise\u2014it reflects roster-wide skill gaps. PIGEONS' CONSISTENCY: Andersin (Pigeons) demonstrates elite economy management (111) and stable K/D performance across encounters. Zamal recorded 5 kills in a recent round with strong round economy (69). These metrics indicate higher individual ceiling and floor than Evictix counterparts. MARKET MOMENTUM CONFIRMS THESIS: YES (Evictix) has collapsed from 44% EMA to 20% current price (-25pp in 24h, including -27pp sharp move Apr 13 22:52 UTC). This sharp reversal suggests new information or professional/informed trader activity recognizing Evictix's vulnerability. NO momentum (+25pp 24h, +26pp sharp move) reflects growing confidence in Pigeons. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA LIMITATION: Briefing contains individual K/D matchup tables but no recent direct Evictix vs Pigeons series results. However, the directional consistency of Evictix negatives and Pigeons positives across diverse opponent sets (Andersin, Kouf, Zamal, cuz, Cohburg) suggests the gap is real, not matchup-dependent. SWISS CONTEXT & STAKES: In Swiss elimination format at R5, Evictix (1-3) is fighting for survival; Pigeons is likely better-positioned. Evictix's psychological pressure is heightened while their execution metrics lag. Teams with poor fundamentals (reflected in K/D) rarely execute clutch rounds under pressure. YES CASE WEAKNESS: The brief argues Evictix has 'competitive individual players like dre and tdawgg with strong map-specific performances.' However, dre is -1 overall (across 5 matchups) and tdawgg is mixed (+2 on one map, -3 on another). This is inconsistency, not dominance. tdawgg's volatility and Scottie's severe negatives (-5, -5) are red flags, not hidden strengths. VOLUME & CONFIDENCE: $57.7K USD traded volume indicates moderate liquidity; the sharp 27pp swing toward NO on Apr 13 late evening (just hours before match) likely reflects pro/serious money recognizing Evictix's poor form. Retail contrarian bets on YES at 20% are possible but unsupported by data. RESOLUTION TIMING: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. No reversal catalyst (roster changes, surprise form spike) is credible with this timeframe. Evictix's 1-3 record and negative K/D differentials are locked in; Pigeons' superior individual metrics are established. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no (82) reflects strong directional data on Pigeons' performance edge and Evictix's clear underperformance trajectory. confidence_yes (35) reflects absence of recent direct head-to-head results and possibility of map-specific upset (BO3 is volatile). However, the weight of systemic evidence favors NO decisively.", "key_factor": "Evictix's 1-3 Swiss record and systemic negative K/D differentials across their roster versus Pigeons' consistent individual performances (Andersin, Zamal) signal a clear skill and momentum advantage for the NO side.", "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.21999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "EVICTIX UNDERDOG CASE: YES is priced at 20% (severely undervalued) despite showing competitive individual player metrics across multiple matchups. dre maintains positive K/D consistency; tdawgg demonstrated +2 differential against Zamal; individual performances suggest roster capability to compete. PIGEONS' HIDDEN VULNERABILITIES: Scottie (Pigeons player) shows severe fragmentation with -5 K/D differentials against both Scottie EVX and Kouf, suggesting inconsistent individual performance. This roster-level inconsistency is a legitimate red flag for a team priced at