{"run_id": "14e45503-7aa2-4778-8bb4-1536ec6e6c03", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T22:57:25.817012+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918543", "question": "Valorant: Alliance Guardians vs QoR (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Alliance Guardians and QoR in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance Guardians\" if Alliance Guardians win the match against QoR.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"QoR\" if QoR win the match against Alliance Guardians.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T04:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T22:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.35, "volume_usd": 1385.366141, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["69600105900936699361990805146620912845395253640672513024105039671451895643462", "108127830738231344993585889482070686321749163626554540349403827581711754005817"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Alliance Guardians win the BO3 match; NO if QoR wins. Criteria are clear and unambiguous for a completed match. CRITICAL TIMING ISSUE: Scheduled match was April 13, 2026 at 19:00 EDT (~13:57 UTC). DATA FRESHNESS is 2026-04-13 22:57 UTC (approximately 9 hours after scheduled start). EVENT TIMING marked as 'TODAY' with end date 2026-04-14 04:30 UTC suggests market resolves in ~6 hours. Match has likely already been played. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES = 35%, NO = 65%. Current market pricing heavily favors QoR, with 7-day trend showing YES falling 18pp and NO rising 18.5pp. This represents strong market confidence in a QoR victory. DATA QUALITY: Briefing provides zero performance metrics, head-to-head records, recent form data, or player statistics for either team. Cannot independently verify which team is favored based on competitive strength. CASE FOR YES (Alliance Guardians): Match confirmed scheduled; both teams active in Stage 2. No substantive performance data supports this outcome. CASE FOR NO (QoR): Market pricing strongly favors QoR (65% vs 35%). QoR confirmed active in Stage 2 (April 6 match vs SRB noted). Market consensus is QoR are favorites, but briefing provides no explanation for this preference. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: vlr.gg is primary source