o evidence of their skill tier or tactical matchup. Current YES price of 35% is already discounting Guardians heavily; contrarian signal is that market may be *overcorrecting* on limited information \u2014 but 7-day downtrend + sharp Apr 11 move suggests informed money, not panic. Confidence in NO is only 42% because the driver (personnel? form?) is hidden. If Guardians' 18pp 7-day drop reflects a known roster concern (injury, suspension, internal drama), that is already priced in. Flip scenario: *no* such issue exists, market overestimated the problem, Guardians' fundamentals are stronger than QoR's. But absence of recent stats makes this speculative. Resolution criteria mention forfeiture/disqualification \u2192 50-50 tie; extremely low probability but non-zero black swan if either org has compliance or financial issues.", "key_factor": "Alliance Guardians fields a substitute or academy-level player mid-series due to last-minute illness/technical issue, severely disrupting team synergy and clutch execution in a BO3 that likely hinges on map 3.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.3869154228855721, "no_score": 0.5813740458015266, "edge": 0.03691542288557215, "no_edge": -0.0686259541984734, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 37% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918543", "question": "Valorant: Alliance Guardians vs QoR (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Alliance Guardians and QoR in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance Guardians\" if Alliance Guardians win the match against QoR.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"QoR\" if QoR win the match against Alliance Guardians.\n\nIf the match is ca