{"run_id": "76779289-68c7-433f-a04b-73c85dbe0d37", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T22:58:33.142721+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1971717", "question": "Dota 2: South America Rejects vs Heroic (BO3) - DreamLeague South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket final match between South America Rejects and Heroic in the DreamLeague South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"South America Rejects\" if South America Rejects win the match against Heroic.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Heroic\" if Heroic win the match against South America Rejects.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.335, "volume_usd": 2675.677428, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["114051326797465731198170493108631865368112574474353737006916277080432972949338", "25872299350375631672707303783875295734359631068336884083639082052341367912695"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "CONDITION: Per\u00fa Rejects must win the BO3 match against HEROIC in the DreamLeague S27 South America Closed Qualifier Playoffs Upper bracket final. SEEDING ADVANTAGE (YES): Per\u00fa Rejects finished 1st in the ESL One Birmingham 2026 SA qualifier while HEROIC finished 2nd, indicating superior performance in the most recent direct competition between these same regional teams. RECENT FORM UNCERTAINTY: The briefing contains severely fragmented match history with dates ranging from September 2025 to April 2026, creating temporal inconsistencies that obscure which matches represent current team form. Most detailed recent results shown are from September 2025 (3+ months old relative to April 2026 event date). NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct match history between Per\u00fa Rejects and HEROIC is provided in the briefing. Cannot assess team-specific dynamics, playstyle matchups, or historical tendencies in head-to-head competition. HEROIC COMPETITIVE TIER: HEROIC roster (Yuma, TaiLung, Wisper, Thiolicor, KJ) includes internationally-experienced players and finished 2nd in the same qualifier, confirming they are a credible opponent capable of BO3 upset. PLAYOFF VARIANCE: Qualifier placement does not guarantee playo