": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "SEEDING ADVANTAGE: Per\u00fa Rejects finished 1st in the ESL One Birmingham 2026 SA Qualifier; HEROIC finished 2nd in the same event. First-place finishers historically convert to playoff wins at ~65-70% rates in esports BO3s. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Per\u00fa Rejects show stronger recent BO3 record (2-1 vs Chimpanzini Bananini, Sept 24, 2025); HEROIC's recent match history in briefing is sparse, limiting confidence in NO-side trajectory assessment. MARKET PRICE DRIFT: YES has fallen 17.5pp over 24 hours (48% \u2192 34%), while NO has risen 16.5pp (53% \u2192 66%). This sharp reversal suggests new information (likely scrim results, roster changes, or meta shifts favoring Heroic). Sharp downward moves on YES 8 hours before match suggest informed trading. VOLATILITY SIGNAL: YES-side volatility (25.1pp/hr) is 2.1x higher than NO (11.7pp/hr), indicating uncertainty among YES backers; large -26.5pp move on Apr 13 22:57 UTC suggests conviction shift toward NO. DATA GAP ON HEROIC: Briefing provides limited recent head-to-head or performance context for HEROIC beyond qualifier placement. No recent BO3 results, scrim data, or player form metrics available for confidence on NO outcome. PLAYOFF VOLATILITY: Regional qualifiers show tighter skill distributions than international Tier 1 events; seeding advantage is real but not dominant. Upsets in 30-35% of cases when teams are regionally balanced. TIMING CRITICALITY: Match resolves in ~8 hours (TODAY, IMMINENT). Reversal requiring Heroic upset is non-trivial but possible within remaining prep window. Market pricing at 34% YES reflects realistic underdog odds. BASE RATE ANCHOR: First-seed vs second-seed BO3 in regional esports qualifiers: ~62% win rate for higher seed. Current market (34% YES) implies ~30% unexplained discount vs h