r issues, scrim results, or technical problems unknown to briefing but priced in by insiders. This uncertainty depresses YES confidence. Match resolves in ~8 hours with live/imminent timing: Sharp moves in final 2 hours typically signal real information rather than noise in esports betting. Market may have superior intel on team form/readiness not captured in Liquipedia qualifier data from Jan-Feb 2026. Rational case for Rejects at 34%: Seed advantage alone should command 55-65% in typical playoff; current underprice suggests market is pricing in legitimate HEROIC threat (experienced roster, playoff adaptation potential). Rejects deserve moderate favorite status but volatility collapse suggests crowded short position got liquidated. Resolution risk: Match 'initially scheduled for April 13 at 9:00PM ET' per resolution criteria\u2014briefing timestamp shows April 13 22:58 UTC. If match was scheduled ~04:00 UTC April 14, it may be LIVE or JUST STARTING now. No confirmation of completion in briefing. This timing opacity adds uncertainty to NO confidence.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Per\u00fa Rejects achieved 1st place in the same regional qualifier where HEROIC placed 2nd, indicating direct head-to-head superior performance in the most recent comparative assessment. Recent BO3 performance: Per\u00fa Rejects won 2-1 vs Chimpanzini Bananini (Sept 24, 2025); HEROIC's recent BO3 records show mixed results, including 0-2 losses in multiple Tier 1 events (Mar 2026, Feb 2026). Seeding advantage: Top-seed positioning typically correlates with better preparation, morale, and bracket positioning in playoff formats, though not deterministically. Timeline concern: The briefing references events from Sept 2025 (qualifier performance) to Jan 2026 (playoff placement), but the match is scheduled for Apr 13-14, 2026\u2014creating a ~3-month gap where team roster changes, meta shifts, or player form degradation could alter matchup dynamics. Roster stability unknown: No information provided on whether either team's roster remains unchanged since the ESL One Birmingham qualifier. Player substitutions or coaching changes could invert the seeding advantage. Historical playoff unpredictability: Esports playoffs frequently produce upsets when teams face elimination pressure; qualifier standings are not deterministic predictors of BO3 series outcomes. Market repricing analysis: YES fell from 48% (7-day EMA) to 34% (current); sharp -26.5pp move on Apr 13 22:57 UTC suggests new information (likely match-related intelligence, betting syndicate positioning, or team announcement) entered the market shortly before this analysis. Confidence asymmetry: Strong evidence supports Rejects' favoritism (qualifier placement, seeding), but limited data on HEROIC's preparation, recent form, or roster integrity constrains confidence in the NO side estimate. Volume ($2,676 total) indicates moderate retail/semi-professional participation; market may reflect casual assumption of seeding advantage without deep Dota 2 strategic knowledge. Resolution timing: ~8 hours remain; any reversal requiring material adverse events (roster disqualification, forfeiture) is extremely unlikely given proximity to start time.", "key_factor": "Per\u00fa Rejects' 1st-place finish in the ESL One Birmingham 2026 qualifier over HEROIC (2nd place) is the most reliable predictive signal available, but the 6-month gap since that event and playoff format volatility introduce meaningful uncertainty.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA RECENCY ISSUE: The briefing's KEY FACTS reference Sept 2025 qualifier data, but R