{"run_id": "f536a97f-07e9-46f3-94af-89f9b339f8a5", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T23:00:56.331088+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935096", "question": "LoL: DN SOOPers Challengers vs T1 Academy (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between DN SOOPers Challengers and T1 Academy in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 14 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers Challengers\" if DN SOOPers Challengers win the match against T1 Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1 Academy\" if T1 Academy win the match against DN SOOPers Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.275, "volume_usd": 1053.166019, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["2941264865700525185063164459077274977335336604124442538032550545174850333018", "103143877164293064762662002592811011176734814807910422185634632986825706254718"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: DN SOOPers Challengers must win the BO3 match vs T1 Academy on 2026-04-14 (per resolution criteria). This is a straightforward competitive outcome; no ambiguity in criteria text. T1 ACADEMY CASE (NO side, currently 72%): T1 organization has strong historical performance in academy competition (3-0 playoff win vs NS Challengers Feb 2026); established infrastructure, coaching standards, and player development. However, current 2026 form data is INCOMPLETE in briefing\u2014no recent match results, win-loss record, or roster composition provided. DN SOOPER CHALLENGERS CASE (YES side, currently 28%): Sparse mention in search results; no documented recent performance, roster info, or competitive history provided in briefing. This is a significant data gap. Cannot assess current form, player quality, or win probability based on available evidence. PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: Market moved sharply against YES on Apr 10-11 (YES dropped ~26pp, then recovered +5pp). Volatility suggests information release or market adjustment, but no corresponding briefing data explains the move. This indicates market may possess information not in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: T1 Academy has some documented historical success (Feb 2026 playoff 3-0), supporting higher confidence in NO evaluation. DN SOOPers has near-zero documented track record, creating high uncertainty on YES side. Confidence scores reflect this asymmetry: confidence_no (42) > confidence_yes (35). MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: YES price (28%) is substantially lower than NO (72%). This 44pp spread suggests market participants have information about relative team strength. The briefing provides only partial justification (T1 historical win, DN unknown), but market pricing may reflect additional intelligence (recent form, roster changes, expert analysis) not captured in briefing. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event is TODAY (resolves ~15 hours). No reversal or major development time remains. Current market price likely reflects near-final assessment by informed traders. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Source is gol.gg (standard for LCK esports); credible fallback to video evidence if delayed. No elevated mechanism risk; match will produce a clear winner (no forfeit/disqualification indicated). BEST ESTIMATE: Given T1 Academy's documented competitive history in this league, DN SOOPers' unknown status, and market consensus at 28% YES, probability_score = 28 reflects NO side favoring. Confidence is moderate on both sides due to incomplete briefing data on both teams' current 2026 form.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains minimal direct performance data on DN SOOPers Challengers (limited roster/form history), and T1 Academy's current 2026 form is incompletely documented; head-to-head history absent; market may be reflecting information asymmetry rather than predictive certainty.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = T1 Academy wins) STRENGTHS: Market has priced T1 Academy at 72% (strong consensus). This reflects T1's documented 3-0 playoff victory over NS Challengers in February 2026, showing T1 Academy can dominate at this level. T1 organizational infrastructure: T1's academy program benefits from parent organization's coaching, player development systems, and competitive resources. Academy teams under elite orgs typically outperform challengers. DN SOOPers Challengers opacity: The briefing shows almost no concrete performance data for DN SOOPers. Limited documentation in search results suggests either: (a) weaker team with minimal track record, or (b) new/underexposed team. Both scenarios favor the known quantity (T1 Academy). UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES = DN SOOPers wins): No documented recent wins, playoff appearances, or roster strength provided. Zero head-to-head history against T1 Academy. The case for YES rests entirely on T1 Academy potentially underperforming, not on DN SOOPers' proven strengths. Market price stability: NO side has risen +22.5pp over 7 days and remains stable in last 24h (+1.0pp). This sustained confidence suggests informed money moving toward T1 Academy, not panic or uncertainty. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 Both teams' 2026 current-season form is incomplete. The briefing contains a February 2026 T1 Academy win but no April 2026 recent matches for either team before this match. This asymmetry favors the team with historical credibility (T1). Academy-level dynamics: T1 Academy roster may feature substitute/younger players, but so does DN SOOPers (implied by lack of main roster presence). T1's depth of talent and coaching staff likely compensates. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 72% reflects T1 Academy as clear favorite but acknowledges meaningful underdog risk (28%). This aligns with academy-level volatility where development squads can surprise. However, the 72% NO price appears fairly set given available data. Confidence asymmetry note: confidence_no is 72 (high) because T1's February 2026 dominance and org strength provide concrete evidence. confidence_yes is only 45 because DN SOOPers' case relies on absence of data and speculation about potential upsets, not positive evidence of competitive strength.", "key_factor": "T1 Academy's demonstrated dominance in 2026 LCK Challengers League academy competition (3-0 sweep in February 2026) combined with organizational infrastructure advantages and DN SOOPers Challengers' minimal documented competitive history.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is deeply underpriced at 28% given the information vacuum. The briefing explicitly states 'DN SOOPers Challengers appears as a relatively unknown entity with minimal documented performance history' \u2014 this is a data gap, not evidence of weakness. FAVORITE'S WEAKNESS #1 \u2014 INCOMPLETE 2026 FORM: T1 Academy's case rests entirely on a February 2026 3-0 win vs NS Challengers. The briefing admits 'T1 Academy's recent match records in 2026 are not fully documented.' We have no data on T1 Academy's performance in the ~2.5 months between February and April 2026. In developmental esports, form changes rapidly. FAVORITE'S WEAKNESS #2 \u2014 ACADEMY TEAM VOLATILITY: The briefing notes 'Academy teams are inherently developmental rosters that may underperform against stronger challenger squads.' T1 Academy is NOT the main roster; player turnover, injury, or roster experimentation could explain underperformance in April 2026. UNDERDOG'S HIDDEN STRENGTH #1 \u2014 ABSENCE \u2260 WEAKNESS: DN SOOPers being 'unknown' in search results is NOT evidence they are weak. Challenger League teams outside T1's ecosystem receive minimal English-language coverage. DN SOOPers could be a well-coached regional contender with strong 2026 form that simply isn't indexed in the available sources. UNDERDOG'S HIDDEN STRENGTH #2 \u2014 APRIL TIMING: The match is TODAY (April 14, 2026). If DN SOOPers had performed poorly in Rounds 1-2 (which began before April 14), market odds might reflect recent upset losses or roster issues. The flat 28% price suggests no crisis, but also no recent credible data confirming T1 Academy's current dominance. PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES side dropped -22.5pp over 7 days and -4.5pp in 24 hours. This is consistent with a slow bleed of confidence in the underdog, not a sudden shock reveal. The April 10 -26.0pp move on YES occurred 4 days ago with no supporting evidence provided in the briefing \u2014 possibly market overreaction rather than informed repricing. RESOLUTION RISK: Match occurs in ~15 hours. No cancellation or forfeit mentioned. Assuming the match plays as scheduled, it is a true 3-game BO3 where variance is real. T1 Academy's favorite status is defensible but NOT overwhelming given the data gaps on both sides. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 28 reflects genuine data scarcity on DN SOOPers (cannot definitively say they're weak). confidence_no = 45 reflects uncertainty about T1 Academy's current 2026 form and the inherent volatility of academy competition. Neither side has strong evidential grounding. UPSIDE FOR YES: If DN SOOPers is a cohesive, well-resourced challenger team (plausible but unverified), a BO3 win at 28% implied odds is fair value or better. The market may be overweighting T1's brand name and February playoff result while ignoring 2.5 months of unobserved competitive drift. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: DN SOOPers wins 2-1 in a competitive BO3 where T1 Academy's developmental roster (possibly with rotational players) cannot sustain intensity across three games. This is consistent with challenger-level esports outcomes. FINAL PROBABILITY: 32% for YES reflects genuine uncertainty due to data gaps, underdog value in a 28% market, and real variance in BO3 format. This is NOT a coin flip (50%) because T1 Academy's February form and organizational strength provide meaningful advantage. But 28% appears too low given the informational desert around DN SOOPers and the absence of 2026 trend data for either team.", "key_factor": "DN SOOPers Challengers' complete absence from available documentation creates information asymmetry that may mask genuine competitive strength or recent roster changes not reflected in the market.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "BASE RATE: T1 Academy has documented 3-0 victory over NS Challengers (Feb 2026 Kickoff Playoffs), demonstrating strong performance in academy competition. T1 organization's track record suggests ~70-75% win rate for academy squads vs challenger teams historically. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market prices (28% YES / 72% NO) align with base rate expectation that T1 Academy is favored. The market has been stable around 28% for YES over the past week, suggesting consensus consensus reflects T1 dominance. DATA GAP - DN SOOPers: Briefing provides virtually no performance history, roster information, or recent form for DN SOOPers Challengers. This represents critical asymmetric information \u2014 we know T1 Academy's strength but cannot properly evaluate DN SOOPers' capability, limiting confidence on both sides. DATA GAP - T1 Academy 2026 Form: Only one 2026 match documented (Feb 25 3-0 sweep). No April 2026 recent form data available. Current condition and roster status unknown. STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE T1: Academy designation + T1 organization infrastructure + documented playoff capability suggests systematic edge. However, academy teams can underperform in group stage matches. IMMINENT EVENT (15 hours): Match resolves TODAY. Limited time for major reversal events. Market has stabilized, indicating information consensus. VOLATILITY PATTERN: Sharp -26pp move on Apr 10 (likely when match details confirmed or roster news emerged), then +5pp reversal on Apr 11. This suggests information cascade completed; current 28% likely reflects settled assessment. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in T1 Academy strength (historical data clear). Low confidence in DN SOOPers evaluation (data missing entirely). Cannot validate NO side's 72% with equivalent rigor. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Market price of 28% YES reflects T1 Academy as heavy favorite. This aligns with historical academy dominance, but lack of DN SOOPers data prevents high confidence. Probability score mirrors current market pricing given information constraints.", "key_factor": "T1 Academy historically dominates LCK Challengers League academy-level competition (3-0 sweep vs NS Challengers Feb 2026); academy teams win ~70-75% of matches vs challenger squads, but DN SOOPers identity and recent form are opaque.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market has priced DN SOOPers at only 28% (strong NO consensus), but briefing provides minimal hard data on DN SOOPers' actual strength \u2014 creates asymmetric information gap favoring underdog. T1 Academy's only documented 2026 performance is a 3-0 sweep vs NS Challengers (Feb 2026), but that's 2+ months old; no current form data contradicts the 72% YES price, but also doesn't strongly support it. Briefing explicitly notes 'sparse direct information' about DN SOOPers and 'incomplete' 2026 form data for T1 Academy \u2014 market appears to be pricing on brand reputation (T1 org strength) rather than recent match evidence. Low volume ($1,053) + stable 28% price over 7 days suggests crowd consensus built on T1 brand halo, not fundamentals; DN SOOPers' anonymity may be masking a competitive roster. No head-to-head history provided; no roster-level analysis of either team; no explanation for why DN SOOPers deserves only 28% despite being scheduled opponent in official league. Market showing rational apathy: accepting T1 Academy favorite status without scrutinizing whether a 72% price is justified by actual evidence vs. organizational prestige. Confidence asymmetry reflects data reality: reasonably confident in T1 Academy's competitive pedigree (high confidence_no), but very low confidence in assessing DN SOOPers (low confidence_yes) due to near-total information vacuum. Probability stays at market price (28% YES) because briefing offers no concrete signal to contradict it, but both confidence scores remain below 50 due to systematic data insufficiency on both sides.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "T1 ACADEMY FUNDAMENTALS: T1 org maintains systematic player development infrastructure; Academy teams historically seed top-tier challengers into main roster. Feb 2026 3-0 playoff sweep vs NS Challengers demonstrates acute competitive capability at this exact tier. DN SOOPER\u0421 OPACITY: Minimal documented match history, no roster depth data, no 2026 win-loss record in briefing. Unknown variables (roster stability, recent scrims, player injuries) create asymmetric information favoring T1's known strength profile. MARKET PRICE ASYMMETRY: 28% YES / 72% NO reflects heavy T1 Academy favoritism. 7-day YES trend (-22.5pp) suggests information flow toward T1 confidence; sharp move Apr 10 (-26pp on YES) likely represents pre-match T1 hype or DN SOOPers news. ACADEMY TIER VOLATILITY: LCK Challenger matches show higher variance than main LCK (younger rosters, less stable meta prep). Single match BO3 outcome is binomial; even heavy favorite (T1) carries ~25-30% upset risk in academy context. MISSING CRITICAL DATA: No 2026 DN SOOPers match results, no recent T1 Academy form beyond Feb playoff, no head-to-head history, no roster overlap/meta info. Briefing explicitly states 'sparse direct information' and 'incomplete' current form. RESOLUTION TIMING: Event is TODAY (~15h to match). Share prices will rapidly converge to $0.01/$0.99 once match begins/concludes. Current market reflects pre-match consensus but lacks real-time player status updates (illness, substitution) possible in next 15 hours. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence (35) reflects that T1 Academy is objectively stronger on available evidence but DN SOOPers remain unmodelable. NO confidence (42) reflects T1's clear historical edge but incomplete 2026 form data limits certainty to 'likely but not overwhelming.'", "key_factor": "T1 Academy's historical dominance in LCK Challengers (3-0 sweep vs NS.C in Feb 2026) is the strongest signal, but incomplete 2026 roster/form data and DN SOOPers' opacity create material uncertainty that market's 72% NO confidence may not fully capture.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has crashed -22.5pp over 7 days (now 28%), with sharp -26pp move Apr 10 and stabilization, suggesting informed money fled DN SOOPers on internal/roster news not visible in briefing. DATA VOID ON DN SOOPER: Briefing contains almost zero performance data, roster composition, or recent form for DN SOOPers\u2014this asymmetry of information cuts both ways: either DN SOOPers is genuinely inferior (justifying 28%), or their recent trajectory/roster changes are unknown to market. T1 ACADEMY ROTATION RISK: T1 historically rotates academy talent into main roster mid-season and benches academy players when they plateau; if best DN SOOPers academy players were called up or motivation is low in developmental league, this BO3 format punishes complacency. ACADEMY FORMAT VOLATILITY: BO3 in challengers league is not a single-game coin flip; a team that executes one clean win condition in Games 1\u20132 can force Game 3 where mental/momentum shifts are decisive\u201428% YES implies <1 in 3.5 chance, but BO3 upsets are structurally more plausible than single-game upsets. TEMPORAL PROXIMITY: Event is TODAY (15 hours to resolution); if roster changes, injuries, or coaching announcements dropped in last 12 hours in Korean esports channels not reflected in briefing, market has already priced some of this in (hence the -4.5pp 24h move). T1 ACADEMY PEDIGREE CUT BOTH WAYS: February 2026 3-0 vs NS Challengers is 6+ weeks old in esports; meta has shifted, rosters rotate, and a developmental team's baseline strength does not guarantee consistency across seasons. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes=35 (low) because briefing provides no DN SOOPers data to validate 28% floor; confidence_no=42 (low) because T1 Academy 2026 form is also sparse and academy teams are inherently volatile; both sides lack depth to justify high confidence.", "key_factor": "DN SOOPers deploys a substitute or academy-level roster with fresh meta preparation that exploits T1 Academy's predictable early-game pathing, while T1 Academy faces internal rotation or motivation gap due to main roster prioritization.", "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.3587096774193549, "no_score": 0.6196845425867508, "edge": 0.08370967741935487, "no_edge": -0.10531545741324921, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 45% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935096", "question": "LoL: DN SOOPers Challengers vs T1 Academy (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between DN SOOPers Challengers and T1 Academy in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 14 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers Challengers\" if DN SOOPers Challengers win the match against T1 Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1 Academy\" if T1 Academy win the match against DN SOOPers Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.275, "volume_usd": 1053.166019, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["29412648657005251850631644590772749773353366041244