{"run_id": "cee2134a-f241-48d8-8adc-fb3ed0062178", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T23:23:17.701511+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1796795", "question": "LoL: Invictus Gaming vs Top Esports (BO3) - Esports World Cup China Qualifier Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket round 1 match between Invictus Gaming and Top Esports in the Esports World Cup China Qualifier Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 13 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Top Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.445, "volume_usd": 108837.68008000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["94625042272564344801804488585225860650616778447812730853981941011385568297088", "10796956428283163965849019862698814920332676682593018452759200668782986252749"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Match must be completed with a winner declared (not canceled, not forfeit, not delayed >7 days). Criteria are clear and unambiguous. MATCH TIMING: Scheduled April 13, 4:00 AM ET; briefing timestamp April 13 23:22 UTC (~19 hours after scheduled start). Match should have occurred or be imminent. No cancellation reported in briefing. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO actionable competitive intelligence\u2014no current rosters, no recent match results, no head-to-head records, no meta analysis, no seeding/standings information for the qualifier. MARKET PRICE INSIGHT: Current market (YES 44%, NO 56%) reflects market consensus, but with $108k volume and high volatility (\u00b17pp in 24h), pricing appears driven by betting activity rather than information asymmetry resolution. 24-HOUR PRICE MOVEMENT: YES rose +7pp in last 24h while NO fell -6pp, suggesting late activity favoring Invictus Gaming, but without underlying data to justify directional conviction. ORGANIZATIONAL CONTEXT: Both teams are established Chinese LoL organizations. Invictus Gaming has wealthy backing (Wang SiCong); Top Esports has competitive pedigree. Neither factor dominates prediction without roster/form data. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): gol.gg is reliable source; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting + video evidence is robust. Mechanism risk is LOW (\u22645% impact on final resolution). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: Cannot justify high confidence in either direction given complete absence of competitive data. Market pricing (44/56) is reasonable in information void but represents consensus weight, not fundamental analysis. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Default to market consensus (44% YES) adjusted slightly for recency (24h uptick in YES buying suggests marginal momentum), but confidence scores remain depressed due to data vacuum on both sides.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data: no current rosters, recent form, head-to-head records, or meta information available to assess either team's likelihood of winning.", "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO = Top Esports at 55%): Top Esports is described as a 'major Chinese LoL organization with competitive pedigree,' positioning it as the more established franchise in LPL ecosystem. The briefing provides organizational legitimacy but lacks recent form data to quantify this advantage. UNDERDOG POSITIONING (YES = Invictus Gaming at 44%): While Invictus Gaming has significant financial backing from Wang SiCong and established organizational infrastructure (founded 2011), the briefing explicitly notes inability to assess current team strength without roster or recent performance data. Wealth alone does not guarantee competitive success in esports. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: The briefing explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head record, current rosters, or recent form data available' and 'Search results did not contain specific information about either team's current competitive standing or recent performance.' This is catastrophic for confident probability estimation in a competitive match. MARKET PRICING SIGNALS: NO side has risen +1.0pp over 7 days (RISING trend) and currently prices at 55%, suggesting marginal professional confidence in Top Esports. YES side fell -1.0pp over 7 days but surged +7.0pp in last 24 hours, indicating recent volatility and possible late money movement. The spread remains narrow (11pp), reflecting genuine uncertainty. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK (IMMINENT EVENT): Match resolves in ~18 hours. Given LIVE/IMMINENT timing, any probability above 50 requires strong conviction data. Current pricing is essentially a coin flip with minor Top Esports lean \u2014 this is appropriate given data vacuum. ORGANIZATIONAL FACTORS DO NOT RESOLVE MATCH: Invictus Gaming's billionaire backing (Wang SiCong) is organizational advantage, not match-specific advantage. Top Esports' 'competitive pedigree' is similarly vague without current roster strength, meta fit, or recent Win/Loss record. Neither statement reliably predicts BO3 outcome. CASE AGAINST STRONGER NO CONVICTION: If Top Esports were clearly superior, briefing would contain recent tournament results, head-to-head records, or roster power rankings. Absence of such data suggests market may be relying on brand name rather than performance analysis. CASE AGAINST STRONGER YES CONVICTION: Invictus Gaming's financial resources do not appear to have translated into documented recent success metrics in provided briefing. Without evidence of current form, roster upgrades, or meta advantage, underdog positioning at 44% appears justified. VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hour swings (+7pp YES, -6pp NO) in a match occurring TODAY suggest information asymmetry and late-breaking developments not captured in briefing document. This reinforces that confidence levels should remain conservative. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: At 55% NO, market is pricing a slight favorite with genuine uncertainty. This is appropriate. Setting probability_score at 55 (NO wins, thus YES = 45 probability) reflects: (1) marginal Top Esports organizational edge, (2) lack of contradictory evidence, (3) inability to justify higher conviction given data vacuum, (4) imminent resolution timeline preventing major reversals.", "key_factor": "Market equilibrium at 55/44 split reflects genuine uncertainty, with NO side's slight edge driven by Top Esports' established LPL pedigree, but insufficient competitive data prevents high conviction in either direction.", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'Search results provided limited direct information' and 'No specific match details, recent form data, head-to-head records, or qualifier standings were available.' This is a severe constraint on confidence for BOTH sides. YES SIDE (Invictus Gaming) STRENGTHS: Backed by Wang SiCong (Forbes-ranked wealthy individual), organizational stability since 2011, access to resources. These are structural advantages but do not directly predict match outcome without roster/form data. YES SIDE WEAKNESSES: Zero evidence of current roster quality, recent tournament placings, or head-to-head advantage vs Top Esports. Cannot build a compelling upset case without knowing Invictus Gaming's actual competitive standing. NO SIDE (Top Esports) STRENGTHS: Described as 'major Chinese LoL organization with competitive pedigree.' Market has priced this side at 55% (modest favorite), suggesting some confidence. However, briefing provides NO specific evidence of recent wins, roster strength, or qualifier performance. NO SIDE WEAKNESSES: Equally data-starved as YES side. 'Competitive pedigree' is vague and historical; current form is unknown. Market may be overweighting brand name without recent performance justification. MARKET SIGNAL INTERPRETATION: YES fell 1.0pp over 7 days (trending down) but rose +7.0pp in last 24 hours. This suggests late money moving toward Invictus Gaming. NO is the statistical favorite at 55%, but the tight spread (44% vs 55%) indicates genuine uncertainty in the market itself. UPSET OPPORTUNITY ANALYSIS: For YES to be genuinely underpriced, Invictus Gaming would need hidden advantages (meta fit, recent scrim wins, roster synergy, patch advantage) not captured in search results. Briefing provides zero evidence of these. Conversely, Top Esports' 55% pricing may reflect bookmaker caution rather than strong conviction. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (resolves ~18 hours). Market is LIVE/IMMINENT. Any sharp reversal toward YES would require unexpected team performance, roster surprises, or match cancellation \u2014 all