{"run_id": "3e8e30c9-0e6d-446b-a27b-0f48e714a6c2", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T23:30:26.633858+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1962523", "question": "Valorant: Trace Esports vs Dragon Ranger Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Trace Esports and Dragon Ranger Gaming in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 14 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Trace Esports\" if Trace Esports win the match against Dragon Ranger Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dragon Ranger Gaming\" if Dragon Ranger Gaming win the match against Trace Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.435, "volume_usd": 5458.498504000001, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["71521698410155028282731311947784719125172556460696888417345046038329019505078", "61916265896196448694520891755319390641142815546427906245941213581585132622801"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Trace Esports must win the BO3 match against Dragon Ranger Gaming on April 14 at 7:00 AM ET. Criteria are clear; no ambiguity in win condition. CURRENT MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: YES side at 44% / NO side at 56%. Market reflects mild Dragon Ranger Gaming favoritism. DATA QUALITY ASSESSMENT: Briefing provides VCT China 2026 tournament context but almost no substantive competitive data on either team \u2014 no recent match results, player rosters, head-to-head records, or performance metrics. CONDITIONAL REFERENCE RISK: Briefing mentions 'If TE wins 1 map against NOVA, DRG will qualify for Stage 1 Playoffs' \u2014 this is a DIFFERENT match (TE vs NOVA), not the TE vs DRG match being resolved. This creates potential confusion but does NOT directly inform TE vs DRG outcome. TEAM PROMINENCE OBSERVATION: Briefing notes 'minimal mention of Dragon Ranger Gaming' and 'limited negative information about Trace Esports' \u2014 weak signal. Absence of information is not predictive evidence. MARKET PRICE HISTORY: YES side down 6.5pp over 7 days (stable); NO side down 15.5pp (falling). Sharp moves on Apr 13 suggest recent information flow, but briefing does not explain the drivers of these moves. INFERENCE FROM STRUCTURAL CLUES: DRG's playoff qualification contingent on external TE vs NOVA result suggests DRG may be lower-seeded or weaker positioned, possibly indicating slight competitive disadvantage. However, this is indirect and speculative. PLAYOFF SEEDING FORMAT: Market is for a 'seeding match' in playoff positioning phase. Both teams likely have similar competitive tier; seeding matches often produce unpredictable outcomes. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Insufficient data to distinguish YES vs NO with confidence. Market price (44% YES / 56% NO) reflects mild Dragon Ranger Gaming lean, but no briefing evidence supports material confidence in either direction. NO REASON TO MOVE FROM MARKET PRICE: Without team performance data, recent form, or head-to-head context, analyst probability should remain close to market consensus. Setting probability at 44% aligns with YES market price and reflects genuine epistemic uncertainty. CONFIDENCE SCORES (BOTH LOW): confidence_yes = 28 (insufficient data to support YES case beyond market price); confidence_no = 26 (insufficient data to support NO case beyond market price). Asymmetry is minimal because briefing data gap is symmetric. EVENT TIMING CONSIDERATION: Match resolves in ~17 hours (TODAY). No reversal window for material new information. Confidence scores remain low due to data deficit, not time pressure.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains fragmented and incomplete data about both teams' competitive standing, recent form, and head-to-head history \u2014 insufficient evidence to calibrate probability materially away from market price.", "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE FAVORS NO: The 56-44 split reflects professional esports bettors' conviction in Dragon Ranger Gaming's superiority. This 12-point NO advantage is substantial and persistent across the 1-week window, with NO only experiencing recent downward volatility (-15.5pp 7-day, -8.1pp/hr volatility) that appears driven by short-term noise rather than fundamental reversal. NO SIDE'S CONVICTION DESPITE NARRATIVE INVERSION: The briefing frames Dragon Ranger as dependent on external outcomes (Trace Esports beating NOVA for DRG's playoff qualification), yet NO remains favored. This inversion suggests the market has identified that DRG's 'contingency' status actually reflects realistic odds\u2014DRG is positioned as an underdog in absolute terms but is the stronger direct competitor against Trace Esports. TRACE ESPORTS' LACK OF PROMINENCE: The briefing explicitly states 'minimal mention of Dragon Ranger Gaming in available results suggests lower prominence,' yet this applies equally (or more critically) to Trace Esports. The absence of specific positive performance data for TE combined with NO-side favoritism suggests TE is the weaker team despite being framed as having qualification scenarios. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION ADVANTAGE: The case for YES is purely structural ('qualification may hinge on this matchup') rather than evidence-based. The case for NO lacks specific stats but is backed by market consensus and pricing persistence. In esports betting, consensus among informed bettors (reflected in NO's 56% anchor) typically outweighs narrative speculation. VOLATILITY PATTERN REVEALS UNDERDOG BID: YES underwent sharp swings on Apr 13 (\u00b17-9pp moves), characteristic of small-size underdog positions being accumulated. NO's single -13.5pp move was corrected, suggesting stabilization. The wild YES volatility indicates retail/speculative interest in the underdog, not fundamental re-evaluation favoring Trace. STRUCTURAL QUALIFICATION LOGIC CUTS AGAINST TRACE: If DRG's qualification truly depends on TE beating NOVA, then TE beating DRG in *this* match would be a prerequisite. The fact that DRG is still favored despite this dependency chain suggests either: (a) DRG is substantially stronger, or (b) the TE-vs-NOVA result is already factored as unfavorable to TE. Either way, it supports NO. DATA GAPS DISPROPORTIONATELY HURT YES: The complete absence of head-to-head records, recent form, or individual performance metrics makes YES claims purely speculative. For the underdog (YES) to overcome a 12-point deficit, it needs affirmative evidence\u2014speculation alone is insufficient. Lack of evidence favors the market consensus (NO). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_no is set to 65 (respectable conviction based on market structure and betting consensus), while confidence_yes is 28 (severe data gap makes it impossible to confidently affirm the underdog without concrete TE performance data). This reflects the briefing's inability to support an YES verdict against the NO-favoring market.", "key_factor": "Dragon Ranger Gaming is the market favorite (56% NO pricing) despite being characterized as having weaker direct control over qualification, suggesting informed betting has identified structural or performance advantages for DRG that overshadow the narrative disadvantage.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has fallen 6.5pp over 24h (stable) while NO side has collapsed 15.5pp over 7 days with a sharp -13.5pp drop on Apr 13 08:00 UTC, suggesting informed money may have shifted toward YES or away from NO on recent information. UNDERDOG ADVANTAGE (YES): Briefing states DRG's playoff qualification depends on TE winning vs NOVA\u2014implying TE controls its own destiny in THIS match for direct qualification. This asymmetric motivation (TE fighting for direct entry vs DRG fighting for conditional entry) favors the team with clearer path forward. UNDERDOG ADVANTAGE (YES): No negative performance data exists for Trace Esports in the briefing; absence of unfavorable recent results is a data vacu