states 'Find the full overview of odds, lineups, and predictions here on HLTV.org!' but provides none of that data\u2014indicating search results failed to capture match-specific public information. SYMMETRICAL UNCERTAINTY: No information favors either team over the other; both teams are uncharacterized in the provided briefing. CONFIDENCE FLOORS: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set to 18 because the briefing lacks sufficient data to support confident estimation of either outcome, even probabilistically.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains no verifiable team statistics, recent form data, head-to-head records, player rosters, or map pool information\u2014all critical inputs for CS:GO match prediction\u2014making any probability estimate beyond a coin flip methodologically unsound.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero substantive intel on either team\u2014no recent form, head-to-head record, player ratings, map pool compatibility, or lineup confirmation. Both 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' sections explicitly state 'insufficient data' for both teams. MARKET TIMING RED FLAG: Event resolves TODAY in ~8 hours. Sharp 8pp swings in past 24 hours (\u00b18pp moves at 02:00 and 07:00 UTC) suggest last-minute information asymmetry\u2014insiders may know roster changes, injury status, or tactical pivot not yet public. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL CANARY: Search results mention MOUZ NXT vs GenOne and generic tournament chat, but zero tactical breakdown, caster insights, or team announcements about ex-RUBY or Phantom specifically. This silence 8 hours before match start is unusual for a $50k tournament. FORFEIT/ROSTER RISK: Resolution criteria explicitly allow 50-50 outcome if match is forfeited or a team withdraws before start. Lower-tier/lesser-known teams in group stage tournaments have higher no-show or last-minute withdrawal rates than consensus acknowledges. BO3 CASCADE MECHANIC: If Game 1 is won decisively by underdog due to meta surprise (new patch, pocket strat on a map both teams share), momentum and map veto control flip\u2014BO3 favors psychological inertia, not raw skill in group stage. CURRENT ODDS ODDITY: Market sits at 58% YES (ex-RUBY favored), but briefing provides *zero* justification for why ex-RUBY should be favored over Phantom. This could indicate either: (a) one team is objectively stronger but briefing failed to capture it, or (b) odds are being driven by early money flow on a genuine coin-flip match. CONTRARIAN THESIS: Set probability at 45 (near-parity) because insufficient data forces genuine uncertainty. Market's +8.5pp swing toward YES in 24 hours may reflect real edge OR algorithmic momentum in thin liquidity ($12k volume). Confidence scores deliberately LOW on both sides (28, 27) to reflect this severe information asymmetry. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are near floor (28, 27) because briefing provides no empirical foundation for high conviction on either side. Any analyst claiming >60% confidence on this match without team form data is overfitting to market price.", "key_factor": "A player no-show, last-minute roster substitution, or severe lag/server issue in Game 1 forces a tactical disadvantage that cascades through the BO3 format, flipping the favored team's edge.", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5108888888888888, "no_score": 0.49308571428571435, "edge": -0.07411111111111113, "no_edge": 0.07808571428571431, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 51% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 26% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1973306", "question": "Counter-Strike: ex-RUBY vs Phantom (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between ex-RUBY and Phantom in the NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 14 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ex-RUBY\" if ex-RUBY win the match against Phantom.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Phantom\" if Phantom win the match against ex-RUBY.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 12023.556888, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["22269259372876023939704680199045158754434220555981074563703342952115694571134", "36978961465467638409191058557598156805821558701879891967194866541394976275261"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["IDK, how did i get 3.9 odds at 1-1 score here?", "Nivera never was bad, solid tier 1 player, just missed opportunity after Vitality (avg 1.16 then).", "All the people in YT chat complaining about Furia yellow jerseys \"copying Vitality\"; 1; Yellow is on Brazil flag 2; Yellow is not on French flag 3;", "If team dont win nothing, theyre not tier1?", "Bro, so CCT tournaments who won it, tier1 teams?", "Bro ur brain so small, now era vitality, they winning", "ex-RUBY vs Phantom odds and prediction at NODWIN Clutch Series 7.", "Find the full overview of odds, lineups, and predictions here on HLTV.org!", "GenOne matchup at NODWIN Clutch Series 7!", "btw this is Lavked map and Arcred can take CT side but they want to play TT XDDD."], "news_summary": "The search results provide limited direct information about the ex-RUBY vs Phantom BO3 match at NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage. The available data focuses on other matches at NODWIN Clutch Series 7 (such as MOUZ NXT vs GenOne) and various other CS:GO tournament discussions. No specific match statistics, recent form data, or head-to-head records for ex-RUBY versus Phantom are present in the results.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data available to assess ex-RUBY's strengths", "No performance metrics or player ratings provided for ex-RUBY", "Match context and tournament structure unclear from search results"], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data available to assess Phantom's strengths", "No performance metrics or player ratings provided for Phantom", "No comparative analysis between the two teams in results"], "key_contex