ny participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 108060.88969800006, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["99640395644693224765850350535962024025663852720596880875212601881826365922600", "107267926467667206999119492887288461895560052269651681258239611638773766928711"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Resolution condition is clear: Solary wins the BO5 vs Misa Esports in EMEA Masters Playoffs lower bracket final, scheduled April 14 11:00 AM ET. Critical data gap: Briefing contains almost exclusively Valorant match data (Misa Esports Valorant team, Valorant player stats, Valorant match results vs Enterprise/MDR), not League of Legends. Single LoL reference found is Misa vs Los Heretics (draft/KDA tables), not Solary vs Misa matchup, and appears to be from different tournament stage. No information available on: Solary's roster, recent performance, draft strengths, individual player form, or head-to-head record vs Misa. No information available on: Misa LoL team's recent form (only Valorant performance documented), roster composition, meta preferences, or playoff track record. Market price asymmetry (NO 58% vs YES 42%) and 7-day downtrend in YES (-18pp) suggest informed traders have evaluated teams, but briefing provides zero League of Legends data to validate or refute that view. Cannot determine if price movement reflects genuine Solary weakness or just liquidity imbalance. Event timing is TODAY (~9 hours), but near-term reversal risk is moot when underlying competitive assessment is impossible. Default to 50 due to complete information symmetry on both sides\u2014neither side can be rationally favored without LoL-specific data. Confidence scores both set to 25 reflecting severe data insufficiency: briefing fails to support probability estimation for either competitor.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no League of Legends competitive data\u2014only Valorant match statistics and community discussion unrelated to the Solary vs Misa LoL matchup, making it impossible to assess team strength, recent form, head-to-head history, or meta-relevant factors.", "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO / Misa Esports at 58%): The NO side has captured sustained market momentum \u2014 rising 18 points over 7 days and 8.5 points in 24 hours \u2014 indicating confident backers. Sharp moves on Apr 10 (+11pp) suggest new information or late-arriving smart money. This is the consensus favorite and market liquidity ($108k) supports genuine price discovery. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES / Solary at 42%): Solary has experienced consistent erosion (-18pp over 7 days, -10pp in 24 hours), showing no recovery catalysts. The sharp reversals on Apr 09 (\u00b110pp, \u00b19pp) appear to be noise/volatility rather than structural support for the YES case. Lack of price stability indicates weak conviction among Solary backers. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains almost zero League of Legends competitive intelligence on either team. Search results are dominated by Valorant match data and community chat fragments. No head-to-head history, recent LoL form, player roster comparisons, or draft meta information is provided. This makes probability-setting extremely difficult. MISA ESPORTS SIGNAL: The only LoL reference in the briefing is Misa vs Los Heretics match data (showing Misa wins 38:16 and 28:48), which demonstrates recent tournament success. While this is not d