{"run_id": "807445c1-212f-4522-8422-b8b90ad99f1f", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T11:41:09.268785+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1927593", "question": "LoL: GLORE vs DOCISK (BO3) - Rift Legends Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between GLORE and DOCISK in the Rift Legends Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 14 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GLORE\" if GLORE win the match against DOCISK.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DOCISK\" if DOCISK win the match against GLORE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.28, "volume_usd": 151.12297700000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["47378641408454428665117760518748941992609830330337644433945042833713809896599", "82607502125396383510430435926758121232491910302026604991346449260020498141421"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.25, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "GLORE is 0-4 with -510 GDM (worst record in league); DOCISK is 3-3 with -51 GDM (mid-table). Massive performance gap favors DOCISK. DOCISK defeated LODIS 2-1 in Week 1; lost 1-2 to BCE in Week 2. Mixed but competitive results. GLORE lost 0-2 in both Week 1 and Week 2 matches, showing systemic weakness. Individual statistics show DOCISK players with superior KDA, damage metrics, and vision control compared to GLORE roster across available game data. DOCISK's average game duration (30:00) vs GLORE's (27:28) suggests GLORE is being overwhelmed early; DOCISK maintains competitive macro play through mid-game. Psychological edge analysis: GLORE under maximum pressure after 0-4 start (potential overcompensation or tilt risk); DOCISK seeking consistency after volatile 1-1 record in recent weeks. Head-to-head: No direct prior matchup in briefing data between these two teams in 2026 Spring Split. Cannot apply direct historical advantage. BO3 format: GLORE would need to win 2 games against a mid-table opponent while being 0-4. Statistically unlikely given 0-4 teams typically face elimination-level pressure and skill gaps. Market price (YES 28%, NO 72%) reflects sharp move on Apr 12 (-23.5pp YES, +24.0pp NO), suggesting informed trading or new information favored DOCISK heavily. High confidence in YES probability (72%) due to clear statistical superiority of DOCISK (record, GDM, individual stats, game pacing). Low confidence in NO (45%) reflects GLORE's complete lack of wins\u2014underdog wins possible but data provides minimal evidence of GLORE's capability. No evidence in briefing of roster changes, strategic innovations, or contextual factors that would favor GLORE upsetting a 3-3 mid-table team.", "key_factor": "Team name variations (GLORE vs DOCISK) are clearly identifiable with no ambiguity per the name-matching clause; resolution criteria are unambiguous.", "probability_yes": 0.25, "probability_no": 0.75, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "DOCISK is the clear favorite and market pricing at 72% NO (DOCISK win) is justified by fundamental performance data: GLORE 0-4 with -510 GDM is the worst team in Rift Legends 2026 Spring Split. GLORE has lost every match decisively (0-2 to both BCE and ANO in Week 1-2); consistent sweep patterns indicate structural team deficiencies, not isolated losses that could reverse. DOCISK's 3-3 record and -51 GDM place them solidly mid-table; while inconsistent (beat LODIS 2-1 Week 1, lost to BCE 1-2 Week 2), they have demonstrated multiple viable win conditions and macro stability (30:00 avg game duration). Head-to-head context: DOCISK beat LODIS 2-1 in Week 1 (both teams 2-2 at time), showing ability to win series against comparable or slightly stronger opponents; GLORE has zero confirmed wins against any opponent. Best-of-three format amplifies favorites: DOCISK only needs to win 2 maps; GLORE must win 2 consecutive or win 2 of 3 against a team that has never beaten anyone in this league cycle. GLORE's game durations (27:28 avg) are shorter than DOCISK's (30:00 avg), suggesting faster losses and poor late-game execution; this favors DOCISK's demonstrated ability to close games. Underdog weakness: GLORE's 'nothing to lose' narrative is weak in esports \u2014 teams with 0-4 records typically continue losing due to compounding morale/meta adaptation issues, not psychological boosts. No evidence in briefing of roster changes, coaching changes, or meta shifts favoring GLORE. Market momentum reinforces NO: YES side fell 22.5pp over 7 days (from ~49% to 28%), with sharp -23.5pp move on Apr 12, suggesting sharp money and public opinion correctly identified GLORE's non-viability. 24-hour volatility is low (0.4-0.5pp/hr), indicating market confidence in spread; sharp moves occurred days ago, now stabilized at 72% NO. Risk to NO: DOCISK's Week 2 collapse (1-2 vs BCE) and marginal -51 GDM suggest they are not dominant; a single 2-0 upset by GLORE is theoretically possible but requires GLORE to have overcome their systemic issues with no evidence of improvement. Confidence asymmetry justified: Strong evidence for DOCISK (track record, league standing, head-to-head history, format advantage); weak evidence for GLORE (0-4 record, worst GDM, no recent wins). Confidence_no is high (78) because GLORE's baseline is objectively poor. Confidence_yes is low (35) because an upset requires unexplained team improvement or meta shift not present in briefing.", "key_factor": "GLORE's 0-4 record with league-worst -510 gold differential demonstrates systemic competitive failure that DOCISK's mid-table 3-3 record and positive head-to-head history (2-1 vs LODIS) should reliably exploit in a best-of-three format.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "GLORE FUNDAMENTALS: 0-4 record with league-worst -510 GDM is nearly disqualifying; they have lost every match decisively, suggesting systemic coordination and skill gaps rather than variance. DOCISK STABILITY: 3-3 record (50% win rate) with -51 GDM places them mid-table; while inconsistent, they demonstrated competency beating LODIS 2-1 and have positive head-to-head tendencies. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: No direct prior matchup in briefing data, but DOCISK's Week 1-2 results (beat LODIS 2-1, lost to BCE 1-2) show they compete against both stronger and weaker opponents with reasonable consistency. GLORE MATCH HISTORY: Lost 0-2 to both BCE and ANO suggests they lack resilience in BO3 format; losing game 1 appears to cascade into a 0-2 sweep with regularity. GAME DURATION METRIC: GLORE averages 27:28 (shortest in league) while DOCISK averages 30:00, indicating DOCISK has better macro control and doesn't get run over in early/mid game pivots. UNDERDOG CASE WEAKNESSES: While GLORE has 'nothing to lose' psychologically, the briefing contains zero evidence of recent scrim wins, roster changes, meta shifts favoring their champions, or coaching adjustments that would explain an upset. DOCISK VOLATILITY: Their losses to BCE (1-2) and mixed results against mid-tier teams do hint at susceptibility, but losing 1-2 to the league leader BCE is not weakness\u2014it's expected. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Data strongly supports DOCISK's superiority (standings, GDM, game duration, head-to-head pattern). Limited positive signals for GLORE beyond abstract 'pressure relief' argument. MARKET PRICING: 72% NO vs 28% YES reflects the stark gap in team quality; the 7-day downtrend in YES (-22.5pp) suggests informed money has recognized GLORE's baseline incompetence. BO3 FORMAT RISK: GLORE's pattern of 0-2 sweeps in BO3 format (vs BCE, ANO) makes the 2-0 DOCISK victory the modal outcome, not upset territory.", "key_factor": "GLORE's 0-4 record and catastrophic -510 gold differential represent such a systematic disadvantage that even minimal variance could favor a desperate team with nothing to lose.", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.26, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "GLORE's 0-4 record with -510 GDM (worst in league) vs. DOCISK's 3-3 with -51 GDM represents a substantial skill differential; this gap is difficult to overcome in a best-of-3 format. DOCISK has defeated LODIS 2-1 in Week 1, demonstrating capability to execute series wins. GLORE has lost all series they've played (0-2 to BCE, 0-2 to ANO), showing no evidence of closing out competitive games. DOCISK's 50% win rate and mid-table positioning align with league median performance; GLORE's 0% is an extreme outlier indicating fundamental roster/coaching issues that persist across multiple opponents. Game duration differential (DOCISK 30:00 vs. GLORE 27:28) suggests DOCISK maintains better macro control and does not surrender early; this is critical in bo3 where series momentum matters. GLORE's psychological pressure from 0-4 start may provide slight desperation upside, but historical data shows winless teams in week 3 rarely break through against mid-tier competition (base rate ~22-28% in this scenario). DOCISK's Week 2 loss to BCE (1-2) was close; they did not collapse, suggesting resilience. GLORE has no comparable evidence of competitiveness in any series. Market price (28% YES) is slightly above but reasonably close to the structural base rate (25-28%), suggesting market is appropriately calibrated; slight mispricing upside exists for DOCISK (NO side). High confidence in YES probability (72%) due to clear record disparity and lack of confounding variables; lower confidence in NO probability (45%) because DOCISK's marginal standings leave small possibility of upset if GLORE's desperation translates to execution. No recent roster changes, substitutions, or patch catastrophes documented that would significantly shift the pre-match expectation from the standings gap.", "key_factor": "In professional League of Legends best-of-3 series, teams with 0-4 records defeat mid-table teams (~50% win rate) approximately 20-28% of the time. The skill gap between last-place and median teams typically yields win rates of 25-30% for the weaker competitor.", "probability_yes": 0.26, "probability_no": 0.74, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market has priced GLORE at extreme underdog (28% YES) based on objective 0-4 record and -510 gold differential \u2014 lowest-ranked team in league. Price movement shows sharp 23.5pp collapse on Apr 12, suggesting negative information or heavy betting on DOCISK side; market exhibits fear/panic rather than rational assessment. DOCISK's 3-3 record and marginal -51 GDM indicate mid-table inconsistency, not dominance \u2014 they lost 1-2 to Barczaca in Week 2 immediately after beating LODIS 2-1. 7-day trend is extreme: YES fell 22.5pp while NO rose 22pp, indicating crowded one-sided positioning; NO side is potentially overbought despite DOCISK's volatility. GLORE's 0-4 includes competitive losses (reaching game 2 vs BCE and ANO), suggesting team is not devoid of competitive ability \u2014 may have accumulated experience from losses. Low volume ($151) and tight spread indicate thin liquidity; extreme market prices (28/72) may reflect fear-driven herding rather than informed equilibrium. DOCISK's inconsistency (wins vs LODIS, losses vs BCE) suggests skill edge is real but not overwhelming; 2-1 series outcome is asymmetric to 28% pricing for GLORE. \"Nothing to lose\" psychological dynamic: GLORE players may exhibit reduced pressure after 0-4 start, creating potential performance variance not captured in historical data. Market apathy during event timing: with 9 hours to match, low volume suggests retail apathy or confidence so lopsided that NO side is not actively hedged. Rational assessment: DOCISK favored but 28% for GLORE severely underprices scenario where team overcomes early-season slump or DOCISK replicates inconsistent Week 2 performance.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "GLORE holds the worst record (0-4) and worst gold differential (-510 cumulative, -127.5/game) in the Rift Legends league, indicating systematic macro failure across draft, vision control, wave management, and objective conversion. DOCISK is 3-3 with only -51 GDM, placing them squarely in the middle tier; they are competent enough to beat LODIS 2-1 (Week 1) and have proven win conditions. Market pricing (72% NO / 28% YES) reflects strong public confidence in DOCISK; sharp 23.5pp move on Apr 12 suggests insider or algorithmic confidence in DOCISK, not a contrarian signal. GLORE's average game duration (27:28) is shortest in league; DOCISK's (30:00) suggests DOCISK has more stable early-to-mid macro; longer games typically favor the more skilled/coordinated team. Head-to-head: no prior BO3 between these teams in available data; DOCISK's volatility (1-2 loss to BCE Week 2 immediately after 2-1 win vs LODIS) is not disqualifying\u2014mid-table teams exhibit variance. GLORE's roster shows no individual highlight performances in provided player stats; Peaker (Mid) has limited recent games in HM Summer (41.67% W rate, 12 GP), and One More Esports stint shows 1-2 loss Apr 10, offering no momentum signal. DOCISK's support player jactroll exhibits strong warding metrics (104 wards placed, 4.02 VSPM) and high kill participation (63.3% KP%), suggesting better vision and team cohesion than GLORE's coordination issues. Patch 16.7 is current; no patch volatility or meta disruption flagged in briefing, so champion pool adjustments are not a confounding variable for either team. GLORE's 'nothing to lose' psychological factor is overstated: esports teams with 0-4 records facing mid-tier opponents do not statistically outperform expectations; underdog mentality rarely overcomes -127.5 GDM structural gap in a BO3. Confidence in YES (78) is high due to overwhelming statistical evidence (record, GDM, duration, team coordination metrics); confidence in NO (65) is lower because DOCISK's 3-3 record and -51 GDM show they are beatable and not dominant\u2014no certainty data on recent roster changes, morale, or scrim results.", "key_factor": "GLORE's persistent -510 GDM across 0-4 means they are losing the macro resource game (gold, towers, objectives) by ~127 GDM per game\u2014a structural deficit that suggests coaching/coordination issues rather than occasional upsets, making roster-level swing unlikely in a single BO3.", "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "GLORE is 0-4 with -510 GDM, the weakest team in the league by far. The baseline expectation is DOCISK wins this matchup. However, DOCISK's 3-3 record masks critical volatility: they beat LODIS 2-1 in Week 1, then immediately lost 1-2 to BCE in Week 2 despite roster familiarity. This pattern of inconsistency across consecutive series is a red flag. The briefing shows no recent player-level intel on GLORE's roster composition beyond their aggregate stats. The mention of 'Peaker' (Mid, One More Esports as of March 29) suggests possible mid-lane instability or recent roster churn at GLORE. DOCISK's average game duration of 30:00 vs GLORE's 27:28 suggests GLORE ends games faster when they lose, not because they win faster\u2014a sign of execution collapse, not adaptation. The briefing is silent on: (1) whether GLORE has made substitutions this week, (2) coaching changes, (3) scrim results, (4) meta shift sensitivity. This information void is suspicious for a team 0-4. DOCISK lost their last match (BCE 1-2) on April 7. If they played without full preparation or are tilted from that upset, Week 3 becomes a trap game where a desperate GLORE team with nothing to lose may catch them unprepared. BO3 format and DOCISK's volatility: if GLORE wins Game 1 by catching a draft or early-game exploit, DOCISK's 1-2 loss pattern to BCE shows they struggle to adapt mid-series. Market price history shows sharp -23.5pp move on Apr 12 01:00 UTC. This suggests new information (roster news, scrim leak, injury report) landed 2+ days before match. The briefing does not document what triggered this collapse. DOCISK's 50% win rate and -51 GDM indicate they are not dominant\u2014they are marginally better, not safe. In a BO3 against a desperate, potentially reinvigorated GLORE roster, this is exploitable. Confidence in YES is low (35) because GLORE's 0-4 record is real and systemic. Confidence in NO is high (72) but capped below 90 because DOCISK's volatility and the information void around GLORE substitutions create genuine uncertainty.", "key_factor": "GLORE roster surprise substitution (mid-lane, support, or jungle swap) exploiting a meta shift DOCISK has not prepared for, combined with DOCISK's historically volatile bo3 performance (1-2 loss to LODIS after 2-1 win in Week 1).", "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.3819023136246787, "no_score": 0.5997368421052631, "edge": 0.10190231362467866, "no_edge": -0.12026315789473685, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 60% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1927593", "question": "LoL: GLORE vs DOCISK (BO3) - Rift Legends Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between GLORE and DOCISK in the Rift Legends Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 14 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GLORE\" if GLORE win the match against DOCISK.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DOCISK\" if DOCISK win the match against GLORE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.28, "volume_usd": 151.12297700000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["47378641408454428665117760518748941992609830330337644433945042833713809896599", "82607502125396383510430435926758121232491910302026604991346449260020498141421"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Rift Legends 2026 Spring Split