o the opponent 0-2 in the preceding 9 days show win rates of 20-35% in rematches.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.25, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CRITICAL HEAD-TO-HEAD: ALTERNATE aTTaX defeated AKA HERO 2-0 on April 5 (9 days ago), establishing direct dominance. Market pricing at 30% YES reflects this baseline correctly. FORM DIVERGENCE: AKA HERO shows extreme volatility (2-1 win vs RIZON, then 0-2 losses to FOKUS and CGN). This inconsistency in a BO3 format favors the more stable opponent. DEFENSIVE BREAKDOWN: AKA HERO conceded 40+ kills from single opponents (Pa1ze vs FOKUS), exposing tactical vulnerabilities that ALTERNATE aTTaX exploited in their April 5 victory. RECENT MOMENTUM: Market fell -19.5pp over 7 days, with sharp -24.5pp drop on Apr 13 04:00 UTC. This suggests new intelligence (likely April 12 match updates confirming ALTERNATE aTTaX's continued competitive form) caused rational repricing downward for AKA HERO. NO COUNTER-SIGNAL: Briefing provides no evidence of AKA HERO recent coaching changes, roster alterations, or strategic innovation post-April 5 loss that would justify betting against ALTERNATE aTTaX's proven 2-0 dominance. MARKET EFFICIENCY: 30% YES price is NOT crowded or irrational\u2014it reflects documented underdog status with limited upside case. The -19.5pp 7-day decline shows market correctly incorporated new match data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72%) due to direct precedent + form data. Confidence in YES only 35% because the case for AKA HERO rests on isolated RIZON win and MVP highlight, not sustained evidence of improvement vs the team that beat them 2-0. TIMING NOTE: Match resolves in ~7 hours (TODAY). Current price reflects pre-match information; no major news catalyst in last 24h to justify reversal. Market stable near 30%.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.25, "probability_no": 0.75, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "Direct precedent is highly predictive: ALTERNATE aTTaX defeated AKA HERO 2-0 on April 5 (9 days ago), establishing skill/meta advantage in same tournament ecosystem; in Valorant, team compositions and agent pool strategies are relatively static across 2-week windows, so recent H2H results are strong indicators. AKA HERO defensive fragility pattern: Lost 0-2 to FOKUS with opponent recording 40+ kills indicates systemic vulnerability to disciplined duelist plays; lost 0-2 to CGN Esports on Apr 4; this suggests not random bad days but coaching/utility setup issues. Contextual win against RIZON (2-1) is insufficient counterweight: RIZON is lower-tier opponent; prayy MVP performance in one match does not indicate meta adaptation needed to counter ALTERNATE aTTaX's proven 2-0 formula. Market price (30% YES) reflects rational underweighting of AKA HERO given H2H precedent; 7-day declining trend (-19.5pp) suggests informed traders downgraded AKA HERO as match approached, not panic selling. ALTERNATE aTTaX stability: Multiple tournament appearances with mixed results, but the Apr 5 2-0 victory is the most recent direct evidence; no contradictory recent results showing AKA HERO adaptation or meta shift. BO3 format slightly favors consistency: Best-of-3 reduces variance vs. single map; AKA HERO's volatility (2-1 win then 0-2 loss) suggests lack of repeatable system; ALTERNATE aTTaX's prior 2-0 stomp indicates coaching consistency. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution): Sharp Apr 13 moves (-24.5pp YES, +8.0pp YES reversals) suggest last-minute information, possibly training scrims or roster changes; cannot verify but market volatility near resolution often reflects informed updates in esports. Confidence_no elevated (68%) due to: direct H2H precedent, pattern of AKA HERO defensive failures against similar opponent archetypes, market consensus shift. Confidence_yes limited (42%) because: single upset win vs RIZON insufficient, no roster/meta adaptation evidence, 9-day gap allows teams to evolve but briefing shows no such updates.", "key_factor": "Direct H2H precedent (ALTERNATE aTTaX 2-0 over AKA HERO on Apr 5) combined with AKA HERO's defensive vulnerabilities against aggressive duelists (exposed by Pa1ze/FOKUS) represents a structural mismatch rather than random variance.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "DIRECT H2H DOMINANCE: ALTERNATE aTTaX defeated AKA HERO 2-0 on April 5 (9 days ago in competition time). This is the single strongest predictor in a BO3 format \u2014 teams rarely reverse a clean sweep without roster changes or tactical innovations. FORM TRAJECTORY REVERSAL: Market has collapsed YES from 52% (7-day EMA ~33%, but sharp -24.5pp drop on Apr 13 04:00 UTC) suggesting new information (likely ALTERNATE aTTaX's recent wins or AKA HERO injury/roster news). Current 30% YES reflects consensus that AKA HERO is now underdog. INCONSISTENCY AS SIGNAL: AKA HERO's recent form is 2-1 W vs RIZON, then 0-2 L vs FOKUS, then 0-2 L vs CGN. This pattern suggests vulnerability to top-tier opponents but unpredictability \u2014 if aTTaX takes matchups lightly or if HERO has identified a tactical counter (rare but plausible in weekly tournament play), a 2-1 reverse is possible. MISSING ROSTER/PATCH DATA: Briefing explicitly does NOT provide AKA HERO or ALTERNATE aTTaX current roster, recent substitutions, or player status (illness, visa, scrim results). If HERO benched a struggling player or aTTaX rotated a key duelist, market pricing may not have incorporated this. Patch 12.05 referenced but no agent-pool or meta-shift detail provided. PLAYOFF-STYLE MOTIVATION: VCL DACH Evolution Stage 2 Group Stage Week 3 is mid-tournament. If AKA HERO is eliminated/clinched or aTTaX has already advanced, motivation gap could flip expectations. Briefing does not provide standings or qualification math. PARALLEL TOURNAMENT FATIGUE: Both teams are competing in weekly tournaments alongside main stage. aTTaX's 'multiple weekly tournaments' participation may indicate scrim volume/fatigue; HERO may be fresher or more focused. Unquantified factor. MVP PERFORMANCE SIGNAL: prayy earned MVP vs RIZON but HERO still lost 0-2 to FOKUS \u2014 suggests individual fragging does not translate to team cohesion. aTTaX's 2-0 win suggests structural advantage (utility, site takes, executes) that survive individual matchup swings. MARKET STRUCTURE: YES at 30\u00a2 reflects ~30% consensus. This is not a 'trap' price (too extreme); it reflects reasonable view of aTTaX dominance. However, 7-day -19.5pp collapse suggests sharp conviction shift, NOT gradual adjustment \u2014 implies binary news event (roster, injury, scrim leak) not yet public. VOLUME CONSTRAINT: Only $1,030 USD total volume is minimal. Market is illiquid; professional bettors may be absent. Sharper syndicates may have already moved line on proprietary intel (roster changes, injury reports) not in briefing. TIMING CRITICALITY: Event is TODAY, 7 hours to match. If AKA HERO has a sub or unannounced tactical pivot, it will NOT be visible in this briefing. Confidence in both YES and NO is artificially suppressed because we are blind to real-time roster/health intel.", "key_factor": "AKA HERO roster substitution or tactical pivot exploiting a map-pool vulnerability in ALTERNATE aTTaX that prior head-to-head (April 5 2-0 loss) did not expose due to meta shift or player illness masking recent form.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.27674922600619195, "no_score": 0.7245473684210527, "edge": -0.028250773993808043, "no_edge": 0.029547368421052655, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "MODERATE VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.43884892086330923, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1958184", "question": "Valorant: AKA HERO vs ALTERNATE aTTaX (BO3) - VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between AKA HERO and ALTERNATE aTTaX in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 14 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"AKA HERO\" if AKA HERO win the match against ALTERNATE aTTaX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALTERNATE aTTaX\" if ALTERNATE aTTaX win the match against AKA HERO.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.305, "volume_usd": 1030.039322, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["52834699171816472048835243060861976906164546850069886327140220490715943233372", "85809880954284484955358266694427543796867869828647315025969884640385225486159"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 DACH: Evolution Stage 2 is an online/offline German VAL tournament organized by Riot Games and PROJECT V.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Otakar Esports vs.", "Falke Esports - Lower Round 4 match of Challengers 2026: Spain Rising Stage 3 Valorant event.", "eSports Cologne roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "RIZON roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "Sanford \"Sanford\" Vinuya (born June 24, 2006) is a Filipino player who is currently playing as an EXP Laner for Team Liquid PH.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from eSports Cologne vs.", "CGN Esports - Week 3 match of Challengers 2026: DACH Evolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "Find detailed results about the VALORANT match between ESports Cologne and ALTERNATE aTTaX in VCL DACH: Stage 2 that took place on April 12, 2026 - 17:00", "Find detailed results about the VALORANT match between ALTERNATE aTTaX EVO and Dortmund eSports in PV: Weekly #3 that took place on April 12, 2026 - 19:30"], "news_summary": "AKA HERO and ALTERNATE aTTaX are set to compete in a Best-of-3 match in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage tournament during Week 3. AKA HERO recently suffered a 0-2 loss to FOKUS but previously defeated RIZON 2-1, showing inconsistent performance. ALTERNATE aTTaX has been competing in both the main stage and weekly tournaments, with recent activity against various opponents. Both teams are part of the German Valorant Challengers ecosystem competing for advancement in the evolution stage.", "side_yes_case": ["AKA HERO defeated RIZON 2-1 recently with strong individual performances, particularly from player prayy who earned MVP honors", "ALTERNATE aTTaX's recent match history shows mixed results with participation in multiple weekly tournaments suggesting potential inconsistency", "AKA HERO showed competitive individual skill in head-to-head metrics against quality opponents like RIZON"], "side_no_case": ["AKA HERO lost 0-2 to FOKUS in Week 2, with opponent Pa1ze recording 40+ kills indicating defensive vulnerabilities", "ALTERNATE aTTaX defeated AKA HERO 2-0 in a recent April 5 match, establishing direct head-to-head advantage", "AKA HERO has struggled against multiple top competitors including CGN Esports (0-2 loss on April 4)"], "key_context": ["Direct precedent: ALTERNATE aTTaX previously defeated AKA HERO 2-0 on April 5, 2026", "Tournament format: VCL DACH Evolution Stage 2 Group Stage Week 3 competition, B-Tier Riot Games organized event", "Recent form trajectory: AKA HERO shows volatility with both 2-1 wins and 0-2 losses in consecutive matches", "Both teams are competing in Valorant Challengers 2026 DACH ecosystem with ongoing weekly tournaments running parallel", "Match on Patch 12.05 per available tournament information"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-14T15:03:14.972432Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "52834699171816472048835243060861976906164546850069886327140220490715943233372", "data_points": 49, "weighted_avg": 0.3322985286726474, "change_1w_pp": -19.5, "change_24h_pp": 2.9999999999999973, "volatility_24h": 0.4576965872801594, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-13T04:00:35Z", "delta_pp": -24.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T06:00:37Z", "delta_pp": -7.999999999999999}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T07:00:36Z", "delta_