If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.445, "volume_usd": 4374.720492, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["75142970716180004557064700239471478626223991474509389149849747851607296471673", "98211819232740337168916401537859294120692335404938972588491314946404534939119"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Nightblood Gaming must win the BO3 match against SaD Esports on April 14, 2026 at 4:00 PM ET. NIGHTBLOOD GAMING (YES case): Entered Round 5 with 2-2 record, demonstrating tournament resilience and competitive parity in Swiss system. Team has proven they can compete in this stage. However, 2-2 record indicates marginal performance\u2014neither strong nor weak. SAD ESPORTS (NO case): Historical rating data (1604-1823 range) significantly exceeds Nightblood Gaming's range (1538-1639), suggesting higher individual skill ceiling. However, this historical data is stale and may not reflect current roster or 2026 form. Most recent match data from July 2025 predates the current tournament entirely. CRITICAL DATA GAP: SaD Esports' current tournament record, recent 2026 match results, and roster composition are not provided in briefing. Nightblood Gaming's individual player stats are present but SaD Esports' current 2026 stats are absent, creating severe asymmetry in available intelligence. SWISS SYSTEM CONTEXT: Both teams at Round 5 suggests similar competitive standing within tournament structure. A 2-2 team playing another Round 5 opponent implies SaD Esports likely has comparable record (not 4-0 or 0-4), reducing rating differential's predictive value. MARKET PRICING: Current market prices (YES 44%, NO 56%) reflect broader uncertainty. Recent volatility (\u00b16pp swings on Apr 10-11) suggests active disagreement among traders, not consensus conviction either direction. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (~9 hours to resolution). No recent news updates on team form, roster changes, or meta shifts. Market participants have had limited time to incorporate any late-breaking information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Nightblood Gaming data is relatively clear (2-2 record, player stats visible). SaD Esports data is incomplete (historical ratings only, no 2026 tournament record, no recent match data). This justifies lower confidence_no despite a probability favoring the NO side. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Low. Match will be played, VLR.gg coverage is standard for VCL, and no forfeit/walkover indicators present. Resolution should be binary and unambiguous. ASSESSMENT: Given stale SaD Esports data, Swiss-parity context, and Nightblood Gaming's demonstrated tournament competitiveness, market pricing slightly favors SaD Esports based on historical strength, but this edge is modest and uncertain. Probability reflects marginal NO advantage tempered by data insufficiency.", "key_factor": "Critical information gap: SaD Esports' current 2026 tournament record and recent form are unavailable; match occurs TODAY with insufficient data on either team's current roster strength or recent performance in this specific tournament.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "NO SIDE (FAVORED) STRENGTHS: Market has correctly identified SaD Esports as slight favorite at 55%. Historical rating data shows SaD consistently rated 70\u2013180 points higher than Nightblood across multiple tournament snapshots, suggesting deeper talent pool and better prepared roster. SaD's competitive pedigree is evident\u2014participation in Challengers 2025 ACE Stage 3 demonstrates sustained presence in high-level Valorant Challengers scene, indicating organizational stability and player development systems. Nightblood's 2\u20132 record entering Round 5 is a vulnerability marker. In Swiss format, 2\u20132 at Round 5 is materially worse than 3\u20131 or higher; this indicates they've struggled against similarly-seeded opponents and face genuine elimination pressure. YES SIDE (UNDERDOG) WEAKNESSES: Nightblood's tournament resilience narrative is overstated. A 2\u20132 record is not 'resilience'\u2014it's a below-median position that suggests they've won only 50% of their early matches and face an uphill climb to 4 wins. SaD Esports' most recent individual match data is from July 2025 (7+ months old pre-briefing), creating data staleness risk. However, the team-level historical ratings (spanning multiple tournament windows) likely reflect more recent updates and provide stronger signal than single old match stats. Market price history shows YES volatility: +8.0pp in 24h and sharp swings (Apr 10\u201311). These swings suggest retail trader noise rather than fundamental new information. NO side has more stability (\u20138.0pp in 24h but lower volatility), consistent with a consolidated favorite. Briefing provides detailed player-level stats tables but does NOT include head-to-head history, recent form comparison, or SaD's current 2026 season record. This asymmetry favors the historically-higher-rated team (SaD) as a tiebreaker. Swiss format equalizes seeding but does not equalize skill. Both teams at similar record does NOT mean equal strength; Nightblood may have had easier opposition or gotten lucky. SaD's superior historical ratings suggest they will perform better when matched against equivalent-strength peers. PROBABILITY REASONING: SaD's rating advantage (~100pt median gap) is material in esports (equivalent to ~0.5\u20131.0 skill tiers