{"run_id": "5b9e1fe5-d3cf-4d17-b861-cda5d9f92840", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T17:05:34.231095+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1971839", "question": "Counter-Strike: ALKA vs HereWeGoAgain (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket round 1 match between ALKA and HereWeGoAgain in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 14 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALKA\" if ALKA win the match against HereWeGoAgain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HereWeGoAgain\" if HereWeGoAgain win the match against ALKA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.58, "volume_usd": 21447.598153, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["59205767011672933343344858108512465013142002336281253143846183896927543484096", "64020296966349765376683435065254175962537617400947201023240894211888975584028"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: ALKA wins the BO3 match against HereWeGoAgain in CCT South America Challengers #1 Lower Bracket Round 1, scheduled April 14 5:00PM ET (resolves via HLTV or credible reporting within 2 hours). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing explicitly states 'no recent performance data, head-to-head records, or team roster information for either squad was found' and 'No publicly available HLTV rankings' are available. Both teams lack identifiable competitive profile. MARKET PRICE AS ONLY SIGNAL: YES price at 58% and NO at 42% represents the only substantive information available. This pricing suggests modest ALKA favoritism but without underlying justification documented in briefing. PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: NO side has risen +12.5pp over 7 days with +8.0pp sharp move on Apr 14 10:00 UTC, suggesting late-breaking information or sentiment shift favoring HereWeGoAgain. However, no explanation for this move is provided in briefing. SYMMETRIC KNOWLEDGE VACUUM: Since no performance, roster, or competitive intelligence exists for either team, neither side can be said to be favored based on merit. Current market prices appear to reflect sentiment or information not documented in this briefing. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: confidence_yes = 28 due to total absence of supporting data for ALKA's competitive position. confidence_no = 28 for identical reason\u2014HereWeGoAgain lacks any documented strength either. Anchoring to market price (58%) is a fallback given zero underlying analysis possible. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Criteria are clear and unambiguous. Match outcomes will be definitively resolvable via HLTV or credible video evidence. No ambiguity in team name matching (both team names are explicitly listed in criteria). EVENT TIMING NOTE: Event is TODAY with resolution in ~10 hours. Market is LIVE/IMMINENT. If either side gains decisive advantage pre-match, shares will trade toward $0.01/$0.99 before official HLTV publication. Current 58/42 split suggests genuine uncertainty or pending information. CONCLUSION: Probability_score = 58 reflects current market consensus in the complete absence of substantive competitive data. This is a low-confidence estimate anchored to price, not fundamental analysis. Both confidence scores are critically depressed due to total data vacuum.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no competitive data, head-to-head records, roster information, or recent performance metrics for either ALKA or HereWeGoAgain; probability estimate is anchored entirely to current market price with minimal underlying information to validate either side.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.56, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO team performance data, rosters, head-to-head records, HLTV rankings, or recent form for either ALKA or HereWeGoAgain. Both teams are operating in obscurity within a C-Tier regional tournament. MARKET STRUCTURE SIGNAL: YES (ALKA) is priced at 58% \u2014 a modest 16pp edge, suggesting modest confidence rather than strong conviction. The 42/58 split reflects high uncertainty. SHARP UNDERDOG MOMENTUM: NO side has risen +12.5pp over 7 days and +12.5pp in 24 hours with a +8.0pp single spike on Apr 14 at 10:00 UTC. This sustained rise in HereWeGoAgain's price suggests either: (a) new information favoring them entered the market, or (b) informed bettors are moving against the ALKA favorite. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: NO side shows 4.3pp/hr volatility; YES side shows 0.0pp/hr. This indicates HereWeGoAgain is actively traded with recent conviction shifts, while ALKA's price is stagnant \u2014 a red flag for a favorite in a live event 10 hours from resolution. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK: With ~10 hours to match start (TODAY timing), ALKA needs to hold this 58% level into match time. The recent 12.5pp drift toward HereWeGoAgain in the final 24 hours suggests late-arriving information or sharp action that the market has not yet fully repriced. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS CLAIM (FAILED): The briefing provides NO documented weaknesses for HereWeGoAgain. Market price alone (42%) does not explain why they should lose \u2014 absence of evidence is not evidence of absence in an information-starved market. FAVORITE STRENGTH CLAIM (FAILED): ALKA has no documented advantages either. The 58% price may simply reflect early market pricing or regional perception, not concrete competitive superiority. LIQUIDITY & CONFIDENCE: $21,448 volume in a 10-hour window for a regional BO3 is modest. The market is thinly traded, increasing the likelihood that recent sharp moves reflect small batches of informed action rather than consensus. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is scheduled for Apr 14 5:00 PM ET, resolves Apr 15 03:00 UTC. Timing is tight; any delays, technical issues, or forfeits trigger 50-50 resolution per rules. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: YES at 56% reflects: (1) slight market favorite status, (2) severe data deficiency on both sides, (3) recent momentum favoring NO, and (4) low confidence in any directional claim. This is near a coin flip with a weak favorite tilt \u2014 justified only by current market pricing, not fundamental edge.", "key_factor": "Market consensus currently favors ALKA at 58%, but this is undermined by severe data asymmetry and sharp recent volatility favoring the underdog.", "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.43999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states no HLTV rankings, head-to-head records, rosters, or recent performance metrics exist for either team. Both confidence scores are inherently capped at ~28-30 due to insufficient evidence for either side. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT IS THE ONLY SIGNAL: YES has FALLEN -2.0pp over 7 days (59% \u2192 57%) while NO has RISEN +12.5pp (26% \u2192 38.5%) with a sharp +8.0pp spike on Apr 14 10:00 UTC. In data-starved markets, sustained directional moves by active traders often reflect private information or expert consensus. UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO: The +12.5pp rise in NO pricing suggests informed participants (likely South American regional experts, coach networks, or scrims intelligence) detected HereWeGoAgain's edge. A +8.0pp single move 17 hours before match start is not noise \u2014 it indicates a catalyst (roster discovery, form spike, or matchup advantage insight). FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITY: YES at 58% is supported by zero positive data points in the briefing. No roster strength, recent wins, or form advantage is documented. The market may be anchoring on ALKA's name recognition alone without evidence of current competitive strength. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES UPSETS: Best-of-3 eliminates single-map flukes but also allows lesser teams to steal series if they exploit specific map bans or tactical preparation. In C-Tier tournaments with limited scouting, preparation variance is often underestimated. VOLUME AND SPREAD: $21k total volume is modest for a regional match. The 2pp bid-ask spread suggests moderate liquidity but not deep institutional confidence in either side. This environment favors contrarian trades by knowledgeable regional players. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: CCT South America Challengers #1 is a Swiss Group Stage playoff\u2014both teams have already survived qualification. HereWeGoAgain's presence here means they beat at least one opponent. The briefing provides no evidence ALKA is stronger or that HereWeGoAgain is a weak lower-bracket entry. NO RECENT FORM DATA CUTS BOTH WAYS: While the briefing lacks concrete evidence for HereWeGoAgain, it equally lacks any counter-evidence. The 42% NO pricing is not irrational; it reflects genuine uncertainty, not proven weakness. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Given the complete absence of performance data for both teams, a 50-50 coin flip is theoretically justified. However, the 12.5pp recent rise in NO and the +8.0pp Apr 14 spike suggest marginal edge to the underdog. Set probability_score at 42 (NO at 58% implied by YES at 42%) to reflect BOTH the market's historical YES preference AND the recent momentum shift toward NO. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 25 because YES has no supporting data and is declining. confidence_no = 28 because NO's rise is backed only by price action, not documented team strength. Neither side merits high confidence in a data-void market.", "key_factor": "HereWeGoAgain has captured 12.5pp of market share over 7 days with a sharp +8.0pp move on Apr 14, suggesting informed traders detected value or new information favoring the underdog in this data-sparse matchup.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No team performance metrics, HLTV rankings, head-to-head records, recent match results, or roster information available for either ALKA or HereWeGoAgain. MARKET SIGNAL PRESENT: YES side trading at 58% (modest premium over 50%) suggests informed bettors or local South American betting community may have embedded knowledge not captured in English-language sources. RECENT MOMENTUM REVERSAL: NO side has risen 12.5pp over 7 days with +8.0pp sharp move on Apr 14 10:00 UTC; suggests late-breaking information favoring HereWeGoAgain (possible roster news, practice results, or injury report). VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: NO side shows 4.3pp/hr volatility vs YES side 0.0pp/hr\u2014indicates active trading and information flow toward HereWeGoAgain side in final 24 hours. EVENT TIMING (IMMINENT): Match resolves in ~10 hours; major reversals now require significant breaking news (withdrawal, DQ, forfeit); probability of such events is low but non-zero per resolution criteria. BASE RATE FOR C-TIER REGIONAL CS2: No reliable historical win-rate data for South American C-Tier Valve Tier 2 tournaments; cannot anchor to global esports base rates without risking category error. SYMMETRIC IGNORANCE: Briefing provides no legitimate basis to favor either team fundamentally; market price 58/42 is a thin premium that likely reflects small informational edge among regional betting community. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINT: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set to 28 due to severe data asymmetry\u2014we lack any objective performance metrics for either squad, making calibrated confidence impossible. Market price used as tiebreaker only. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Setting score to 55 (slight YES bias) reflects the current market price of 58% discounted modestly for risk of late-stage momentum on NO side; this is NOT a conviction estimate but a market-informed placeholder given data vacuum.", "key_factor": "In symmetric information BO3 esports matches with no public ranking data, the market-implied odds (58% YES) typically reflect some informational advantage among bettors; absent that data, reversion to ~50% is expected.", "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.44999999999999996, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero substantive information about either team's strength, form, roster, or head-to-head record. Market is pricing based on sentiment, not evidence. STRIKING PRICE MOVEMENT: NO side surged +12.5pp in 24h (sharp +8.0pp spike on Apr 14 10:00 UTC) despite no new public information in briefing. This suggests informed traders or insiders have non-public knowledge favoring HereWeGoAgain. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY RED FLAG: YES (ALKA) started favored at ~61% a week ago; now declining to 58% while NO gains. Market is rotating away from ALKA without disclosed reason\u2014classic sign of informed repositioning. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: NO side shows 4.3pp/hr volatility vs YES's 0.0pp/hr. High volatility on underdog (NO) indicates late-arriving sharp money, not retail panic. This is rational contrarian betting, not emotion. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT IRRELEVANT: Briefing provides tournament structure (C-Tier, Valve T2, BO3) but zero competitive intelligence. Market cannot rationally distinguish ALKA from HereWeGoAgain quality. IMMINENT RESOLUTION (10h remaining): Insufficient time for major news to reverse the +8pp spike. Sharp money betting NO appears positioned and confident. Late reversal to YES would require ALKA breakthrough news (roster announcement, etc.)\u2014very unlikely given current silence. INFERENCE: The 42% NO price reflects informed market participants with superior information, not crowd panic. YES at 58% may be overpriced due to inertia from earlier week consensus. Current spread (58/42) appears to undervalue HereWeGoAgain. CONFIDENCE SUPPRESSION: Both confidence scores set low (28/26) because briefing offers zero empirical basis to evaluate either team. Unable to robustly defend either side. Probability_score (55) reflects near-coin-flip with slight lean toward market consensus, but this should not be trusted without 