resolution. SPECIALIST ASSESSMENT: Without HLTV data, recent demos, or internal tournament bracket seeding, probability is pure noise. Market at 58/42 reflects prior belief neutralized by information asymmetry; NO surge suggests counter-consensus positioning by better-informed participants.", "key_factor": "In C-Tier regional tournaments with minimal public data, market pricing reflects pure liquidity-driven speculation rather than informed analysis; the 12.5pp NO surge in 24h suggests late smart money repositioning, but without team roster, recent form, or head-to-head data, any directional conviction is unfounded.", "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA VACUUM: Zero performance data, rosters, head-to-head records, or recent form for either team. Both sides are flying blind\u2014confidence in either direction is artificially constrained. MARKET STRUCTURE REVERSAL SIGNAL: HereWeGoAgain side has surged +12.5pp in 7 days with +8.0pp spike on Apr 14 at 10:00 UTC, despite ALKA being priced as favorite. This aggressive accumulation on the underdog suggests informed traders may have private intelligence (roster changes, scrim results, tactical innovation) not in public briefing. ONLINE BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: No home-crowd advantage, no venue stability, no public scouting. Each map can flip on anti-stratting or player mentality. BO3 is a momentum format\u2014one map upset can psychologically cascade into series loss for the heavier favorite. ABSENCE OF CONSENSUS: Briefing explicitly notes 'limited specific information' for both teams. This is NOT evidence ALKA is stronger\u2014it is evidence the market is pricing on name recognition or seeding alone, not actual form. HereWeGoAgain's 7-day climb suggests contrarian positioning. LOWER-BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: If ALKA is a seeded/expected winner, they may carry elimination pressure. HereWeGoAgain has nothing to lose and may have prepared specifically to counter ALKA's assumed defaults or map pool. TIMING PRESSURE: Match resolves in ~10 hours; sharp move on Apr 14 10:00 UTC occurred ~7 hours before briefing snapshot, suggesting real-time information flow (scrim leaks, player roster confirmation, illness report) not yet public. SOUTH AMERICAN REGIONAL INSULARITY: Limited global transparency on regional CS2 meta\u2014tactical innovations or underdog roster moves may not propagate to prediction market analysts until match broadcast. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY APPLIED: YES confidence (28) reflects near-total lack of ALKA form data. NO confidence (32) reflects same void for HereWeGoAgain, but the +12.5pp surge and +8.0pp spike imply some informed crowd believes HereWeGoAgain's chances exceed headline 42%.", "key_factor": "HereWeGoAgain executes a meta-shift exploit or anti-ALKA tactical preparation that catches ALKA unprepared, compounded by potential player fatigue or connection instability in an online BO3 format where momentum swings are acute.", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.5201036269430052, "no_score": 0.4835897435897436, "edge": -0.0598963730569948, "no_edge": 0.06358974358974356, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 52% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 28% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1971839", "question": "Counter-Strike: ALKA vs HereWeGoAgain (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket round 1 match between ALKA and HereWeGoAgain in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 14 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALKA\" if ALKA win the match against HereWeGoAgain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HereWeGoAgain\" if HereWeGoAgain win the match against ALKA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.58, "volume_usd": 21447.598153, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["59205767011672933343344858108512465013142002336281253143846183896927543484096", "640202969663497653766834350652541759625376174009472010232408942118889755