{"run_id": "70b4a7af-e489-47a7-b52d-0dbce75b1941", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T17:10:18.808604+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918563", "question": "Valorant: Shopify Rebellion Black vs FlyQuest (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Shopify Rebellion Black and FlyQuest in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 14 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shopify Rebellion Black\" if Shopify Rebellion Black win the match against FlyQuest.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FlyQuest\" if FlyQuest win the match against Shopify Rebellion Black.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T05:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T23:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 16.798964, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["85994207680611032991075254705552281636382646728485781421613468328301849958303", "34118380265554984333371094727265677960255440397606050831682551035934843701868"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Shopify Rebellion Black must win the BO3 match scheduled for April 14, 7:00 PM ET. This is a straightforward match outcome condition with clear resolution criteria. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides conflicting information about FlyQuest's record (claims '2-0 start' but also notes '1-1 record (R3) as of April 7'). This undermines the reliability of the performance assessment. FLYQUEST EVALUATION: Available data shows FlyQuest defeated Division One and Alliance Guardians (described as 'sleepers'), with rating of 1746. However, the record contradiction and vague opponent descriptions limit confidence in this assessment. SHOPIFY REBELLION BLACK EVALUATION: The briefing explicitly states 'Shopify Rebellion Black's current standing and recent performance in Stage 2 are not detailed in the search results.' This is a critical gap. Only historical Stage 1 playoff success (2-0 vs sleepers) is mentioned, which may not reflect current Stage 2 form. ASYMMETRIC DATA QUALITY: Briefing provides marginally more information about FlyQuest than SRB, but both teams lack sufficient current match data for a reliable head-to-head assessment. The data freshness timestamp (April 14, 17:09 UTC) is very recent but still pre-match. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: Current odds show 60% YES (SRB) / 40% NO (FlyQuest). The market has risen +10pp over 7 days (April 9 sharp move of +9pp), suggesting market confidence in SRB. However, low volume ($17) indicates thin liquidity and potential noise. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three format reduces variance compared to single-game outcomes, but without reliable skill/form differentials, this does not strongly favor either team. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Criteria explicitly reference vlr.gg as primary source with fallback to credible reporting. Match is TODAY, so resolution should occur within 2-3 hours of completion. This risk is minimal. CONTRA-MARKET ASSESSMENT: The 60-40 market split is not strongly supported by the briefing data. Market confidence in SRB appears to reflect the recent +9pp move on April 9, but the briefing provides no new information explaining this move or validating the higher YES probability. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 28 (low \u2014 insufficient Stage 2 data for either team, contradictory record info, thin evidence base). confidence_no = 32 (low but slightly higher \u2014 FlyQuest has at least some documented recent matches, though record is unclear). Neither side has strong data support. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Given data asymmetry slightly favoring FlyQuest (despite contradictions) and market momentum toward SRB, probability_score of 38 reflects genuine uncertainty with slight lean toward FlyQuest as the outcome, below the market's 60% YES price. This suggests potential market mispricing on the YES side.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains contradictory FlyQuest record data (2-0 vs 1-1) and provides insufficient performance metrics for Shopify Rebellion Black, preventing reliable comparative analysis.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE ISSUE: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited performance data available for Shopify Rebellion Black in Stage 2 to assess current form.' The search results contain mostly template placeholders (roster, upcoming matches, recent results sections are blank for SRB). This is a MAJOR RED FLAG for confidence. FLYBURST'S DOCUMENTED STRENGTH: FlyQuest demonstrated 2-0 wins vs Division One and Alliance Guardians with a 1746 rating \u2014 concrete, verifiable data. These are not trivial opponents; they signal consistent performance and map control execution. YES SIDE MOMENTUM TRAP: The 60% YES price reflects a +10pp 7-day rise and a sharp +9pp move on Apr 09. However, this rising momentum may be driven by hype or incomplete information rather than fundamental team strength. The briefing provides NO narrative explaining WHY YES is rising \u2014 classic indicator of noise-driven pricing. ASYMMETRIC DATA QUALITY: The briefing's NEWS SUMMARY explicitly notes 'limiting direct comparative analysis' due to SRB data gaps. When one side (FlyQuest) has documented metrics and the other (SRB) is opaque, markets often overprice the favorite on hope. This creates value on NO. BO3 FORMAT EXPLOITS UPSET PATHS: BO3 matches allow lower-rated teams to steal wins through superior strategy, preparation, or map-specific execution. One strong Map 1 performance by SRB could swing the series. The 40% NO odds do not sufficiently price this execution-based volatility. SRB'S PRIOR CAPABILITY: SRB defeated 'sleepers' 2-0 in Stage 1 playoffs, proving they can execute at high levels. This evidence is buried in the brief but contradicts any narrative that SRB is weak or out of form. CONFIDENCE BREAKDOWN: confidence_yes = 28 (low) because SRB performance in Stage 2 is genuinely unknown; confidence_no = 35 (also low) because FlyQuest's 2-0 record is verifiable but we have no intel on SRB's counter-preparation, current roster health, or recent scrim data. Both sides lack sufficient evidence for high confidence. IMMINENT TIMING RISK: Match resolves TODAY (~12 hours). By the time this analysis publishes, pregame intel, team announcements, or last-minute roster changes may have already shifted the true probability. The current 60/40 split may already embed live-market corrections unavailable in this briefing (data freshness: Apr 14 17:09 UTC, match scheduled Apr 14 7:00 PM ET = ~12 hours away). PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market is pricing YES at 60%, suggesting confidence that FlyQuest's superior rating and 2-0 record will hold. However, the near-complete absence of SRB Stage 2 data means the market is implicitly assuming 'no news = weak team,' a dangerous assumption in esports where teams can rapidly improve or execute upset strategies. A true 50-50 coin flip on unknown SRB + known FlyQuest advantage suggests YES should trade at ~55%, not 60%. This makes YES slightly OVERPRICED. RECOMMENDATION: YES is the market favorite and has been rising, but is overpriced given data asymmetry. NO at 40% offers better value because FlyQuest's documented advantage (1746 rating, 2-0 record) is NOT sufficient to overcome the uncertainty around SRB's actual Stage 2 form and BO3 upset potential. Probability_score of 42 reflects skepticism of the 60% YES price while acknowledging FlyQuest's documented edge.", "key_factor": "Critical data asymmetry: FlyQuest's documented 1746 rating and 2-0 Stage 2 start versus almost no accessible performance data for Shopify Rebellion Black's current form, making the market's 60% YES pricing vulnerable to overconfidence despite favorable early trading momentum.", "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET TREND ANALYSIS: YES has risen +10pp over 7 days (driven by Apr 9 +9pp spike), but shows -2pp in last 24h. NO is falling but shows +2pp volatility in final 24h\u2014possible late-arriving counter-narrative or sharp-money activity not yet reflected in consensus price. FLYQUEST APPARENT STRENGTH\u2014BUT OVERSTATED: News cites FlyQuest's 2-0 early start (Division One, Alliance Guardians), but KEY CONTEXT reveals FlyQuest was 1-1 as of Apr 7. This is NOT dominant\u2014they've already lost a match in Stage 2. A 1-1 record does not justify 60% favorite pricing in BO3 format. SHOPIFY REBELLION BLACK\u2014DATA GAP IS THE UNDERDOG'S FRIEND: Briefing explicitly states 'Shopify Rebellion Black's current standing and recent performance in Stage 2 are not detailed.' This absence of negative data is NOT evidence they are weak. Stage 1 record shows 2-0 playoff victory over sleepers, proving capability to execute. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE FOR UNDERDOG: Best-of-3 series reduce variance vs Bo1. If SRB has ANY map-pool edge or recent roster adjustment not captured in stale rating snapshots, BO3 gives them multiple opportunities to exploit it. Market pricing 60-40 in BO3 implies small skill gap\u2014realistic for unknown matchup. RATING DISCREPANCY UNRELIABLE: FlyQuest's 1746 rating is cited, but no SRB rating provided. Ratings may be outdated (data freshness: Apr 14 17:09 UTC, match scheduled Apr 14 19:00 UTC\u2014only ~1.8 hours buffer). Esports ratings lag roster changes and meta shifts. FLYQUEST MOMENTUM NARRATIVE UNSUPPORTED: 2-0 record cited, but immediately contradicted by 1-1 record as of Apr 7. Which is current? If 1-1, narrative breaks. If 2-0 since Apr 7 (R4-R5), timeline is unclear\u2014briefing is internally inconsistent. SRB PLAYOFF PEDIGREE OVERLOOKED: Defeating sleepers 2-0 in Stage 1 playoffs demonstrates SRB has tournament-level execution. They are not a random low-tier team\u2014they qualified for playoffs, suggesting top-8 finish or better in Stage 1. VOLUME & PRICE ELASTICITY: Only $17 USD volume suggests thin market. Sharp move on Apr 9 (+9pp for YES) may have been low-volume spike, not fundamental consensus shift. Underpricing of NO side is