{"run_id": "5247fcf8-b302-44bb-84b8-5e25c1319bdd", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T17:42:09.536838+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1973375", "question": "Counter-Strike: 1WIN vs Bebop (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between 1WIN and Bebop in the NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 14 at 1:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"1WIN\" if 1WIN win the match against Bebop.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bebop\" if Bebop win the match against 1WIN.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T23:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T17:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.68, "volume_usd": 6386.4240279999985, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["106758091365684866398636293249632610205758548292616247935947447467184303513353", "108204244710860936323637650067080802766696247961955220372727933905287463666051"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if 1WIN wins the BO3 match; NO if Bebop wins. No forfeit/cancellation loopholes appear applicable given match is scheduled for today (April 14, 2026 at 19:00 UTC) with ~5 hours to event start. CURRENT MARKET SIGNAL: YES trading at 68% vs NO at 32%, reflecting strong confidence in 1WIN victory. However, this 32-point swing in 24 hours is extreme and suggests speculative repositioning rather than new substantive information. DATA ASYMMETRY ON 1WIN: Briefing provides NO direct competitive data on 1WIN's roster, recent form, tier-level standing, or head-to-head record against Bebop. This is the primary uncertainty driver. DATA ON BEBOP: Limited but present\u2014recent match history shows competitive play (16-12 Ancient, 14-16 Nuke, 16-14 Inferno), indicating mid-tier capability. Bebop can win close maps but results are mixed. CONTEXT CLUES: Both teams qualified for NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, suggesting roughly similar competitive levels. However, qualification to a regional qualifier does not strongly differentiate tier-1 vs tier-2 performance. CASE FOR 1WIN (YES): Market consensus suggests 1WIN is stronger. Sharp 19.5pp move on Apr 14 01:00 UTC followed by -5.0pp at 13:00 UTC then +7.5pp at 17:40 UTC suggests late-stage confidence in 1WIN, possibly from