 any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T23:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T17:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.425, "volume_usd": 7462.757553000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["19912795348107334697873085267431880968041711562074168270545672136121326165788", "509898276269353040043242365700468616683132806659415948345401024041664707102"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA INTEGRITY ISSUE: Briefing mixes Counter-Strike 2, Apex Legends, and other esports results with LoL content. The 'KEY FACTS' section shows champion picks attributed to Myth Esports and mCon esports, but includes irrelevant CS2, Apex, and Dota content that corrupts confidence in data accuracy. TEAM IDENTIFICATION: Briefing refers to opponent as 'Dynasty' but track records show 'mCon esports' (Netherlands). Resolution criteria allows for name matching flexibility ('minor discrepancies... alternate spellings... minor formatting differences') if underlying team can be 'clearly and uniquely identified.' However, the data corruption makes team identity verification unreliable. MYTH ESPORTS RECORD: Stated as 0-4 in tracked games. Individual player stats show 4 games played across roster (Ferrari, Franky, BunnyBeast, Dovendyr all 4-0 loss records). This represents significant underperformance against regional opponents. mCON ESPORTS RECORD: Stated as 3-3 record. Individual player stats confirm 6 games played with mixed 2-4 / 3-3 splits across roster. More balanced competitive record than Myth. INDIVIDUAL PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS: Myth's Franky (mid) shows 3.29 KDA and 7.6 CS/min (positive metrics); Dovendyr (support) shows 2.04 KDA. However, Ferrari (jungle) shows 0% win rate across 4 games with 1.81 KDA (weak). mCon's Pipibaat (jungle) shows 50% win rate with 2.86 KDA (stronger jungler matchup critical in LoL). STRUCTURAL CONCERN: Data timestamp is Apr 14 17:42 UTC; match scheduled for Apr 14 13:00 ET (18:00 UTC). Match should be IMMINENT or LIVE by data freshness time. Briefing provides no match result, live updates, or real-time status\u2014this is a major gap for a 'TODAY' event resolving in ~5 hours. MARKET SIGNAL: YES priced at 42%, NO at 57%. Recent sharp moves show volatility (+9.5pp, +8.0pp, -5.5pp swings on Apr 14). Market indicates slight Dynasty/NO favor. Majority of price action occurred in early Apr 14 hours (before typical match start). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (Dynasty wins) due to Myth's 0-4 record and weak jungler; lower confidence in YES due to mixed individual metrics and reasonable but not dominant mCon performance. However, data corruption significantly lowers confidence in BOTH assessments. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Source is gol.gg; backup is credible reporting if gol.gg delayed beyond 2 hours. Standard LoL match resolution should be unambiguous (win/loss/forfeit). Forfeit/walkov conditions resolve to 50-50 per criteria\u2014low probability given professional league context. PROBABILITY REASONING: Myth's 0-4 record + weaker jungle + market pricing (57% NO) suggest Dynasty favored. However, individual metrics (Franky's KDA, Dovendyr's efficiency) provide slight hedge. Assigning 28% YES reflects NO consensus (72%) while preserving uncertainty from data quality issues. CONFIDENCE REDUCTION: Data integrity issues reduce both confidence scores by ~15-20 points from what raw stats would suggest. Lack of live match status despite 'TODAY' timing is concerning and limits confidence further.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains mixed/corrupted data sources (Counter-Strike, Apex Legends, other esports mixed with LoL); cannot verify Myth Esports vs Dynasty match details or current roster status from primary source gol.gg.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTH: Dynasty maintains a 3-3 record showing competitive viability and demonstrated ability to execute under pressure, while Myth sits at 0-4 with zero wins across all tracked games\u2014a stark performance gap. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Myth's jungle player Ferrari has 0% win rate (0-4) with 1.81 KDA\u2014critically weak playmaking in a role that dictates tempo and early game advantage. This is not individual variance but systematic failure. FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Myth's top laner Sprotte shows only 51.5% win rate with poor CS metrics (411 for 706 total\u2014significantly below peer standards), indicating laning phase vulnerabilities that Dynasty's laners (50% WR) can exploit. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: While Myth's mid (Franky, 3.29 KDA) and support (Dovendyr, 2.04 KDA) show positive individual stats, KDA alone does not translate to macro victory\u2014Dynasty's balanced performance (no standout weaknesses) suggests better team cohesion. FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Dynasty's jungler Pipibaat (2.86 KDA, 50% WR) directly counters Myth's Ferrari weakness. Strong jungle presence controls vision, secures objectives, and creates winning conditions\u2014Myth lacks this engine. MARKET CONTEXT: NO is priced at 57% vs YES at 42%. Market is correctly skeptical of Myth's 0-4 record; the 15-point spread reflects fundamental quality gap. NO side is slightly underpriced given Myth's winrate delta. TIMING & REVERSAL RISK: Event occurs TODAY (5 hours remaining). For Myth to overturn a 0-4 deficit requires not incremental improvement but complete tactical reset\u2014unrealistic in remaining prep time. Dynasty only needs to execute their standard playbook. VOLATILITY NOTE: YES side saw +9.5pp and +8.0pp spikes (Apr 14 01:00 and 08:00 UTC) suggesting shortselling or contrarian betting, but this volatility reflects emotional reaction to odds, not substantive form change. Myth's 0-4 record is immutable. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) because Myth's 0-4 record provides hard evidence. Lower confidence in YES (35) because briefing lacks Dynasty roster depth analysis, regional standings context, or recent trend data\u2014underdog evaluation incomplete. DUAL PERSPECTIVE: YES path requires: Myth's individual talent (Franky mid, Dovendyr support) to suddenly translate to team wins, Ferrari jungle to reverse 0-4 trend, and laning to overcome Sprotte's 51.5% WR. NO path requires: Dynasty execute normally against a team that has lost every tracked game. The latter is far likelier.", "key_factor": "Myth Esports' 0-4 record and systematic execution failures across tracked games demonstrate fundamental competitive disadvantage against Dynasty's proven 3-3 win-loss record.", "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MYTH'S RECORD IS CATASTROPHIC: 0-4 with zero wins suggests systemic problems\u2014drafting, macro play, or team synergy failures\u2014not just individual underperformance. This is the strongest evidence against YES. DYNASTY'S CONSISTENCY ADVANTAGE: mCon's 3-3 record (50% win rate) shows competitive balance and proven ability to secure victories. They are a verified winning team; Myth is unproven. JUNGLE DISPARITY IS DECISIVE: Ferrari (Myth jungle) has 0% win rate across 4 games with 1.81 KDA and poor CS (354/547). Pipibaat (Dynasty jungle) maintains 50% win rate with 2.86 KDA\u2014jungle is the map-control role, and Dynasty controls it. TOP LANE WEAKNESS COMPOUNDS PROBLEMS: Sprotte's 51.5% win rate and low CS (411/706 across games) indicate weak laning and resource efficiency. Against Dynasty's top lane, this is an exploitable vulnerability. MYTH'S SOLE BRIGHT SPOT (FRANKY MID): Franky's 3.29 KDA and 7.6 CS/min are genuine strengths, but one player cannot carry a BO3 against a team with multiple competent performers. Mid-lane excellence alone doesn't override jungler and top lane deficits. SUPPORT METRICS MISLEADING: Dovendyr's 2.04 KDA looks good, but support KDA is often inflated by assists in losing games. His 0.9 kills per game and 247/193 gold tells a story of low impact despite good ratios. MARKET PRICING REFLECTS REALITY: YES at 42% is already generous given a 0-4 record. Sharp moves in the last 24 hours (+9.5pp, +8.0pp, -5.5pp) suggest sophisticated traders trying to unwind overpriced YES positions\u2014NOT confidence in an upset. NO RECENT MOMENTUM FOR MYTH: The 7-day change shows YES falling 8.0pp while NO rose 7.5pp. This reversal indicates market recognition that Myth is genuinely weak, not mispriced. INSUFFICIENT DATA ON DYNASTY'S WEAKNESSES: The briefing provides no detailed statistics on Dynasty's specific vulnerabilities, individual champion pool trends, or recent form beyond the 3-3 record. This asymmetry favors Dynasty by default. EXECUTION UNDER PRESSURE UNLIKELY: In BO3 formats, teams with 0-4 records rarely produce the coordinated play needed to upset competitive opponents. Myth's problems appear structural, not situational. CONFIDENCE IN NO IS HIGHER: Dynasty's 50% win rate, jungle advantage, and lack of evidence of systemic failure make them the clear favorite. Confidence in NO = 72 reflects strong supporting data. Confidence in YES = 28 reflects weak case with no concrete evidence of a Myth turnaround.", "key_factor": "Myth's mid laner Franky demonstrates elite individual metrics (3.29 KDA, 7.6 CS/min) that could carry a single BO3 if team coordination improves under match pressure.", "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Myth Esports' 0-4 record is a dominant signal: in LoL regional play, winless teams rarely reverse form in single-elimination BO3s without roster changes or external intervention. Individual stat comparison strongly favors Dynasty: Myth's jungle (Ferrari) has 0% win rate (1.81 KDA, 0 kills), mid (Franky's 3.29 KDA) is offset by weak macro; Dynasty's jungler (Pipibaat) at 50% with 2.86 KDA shows more competence. Myth's top lane (Sprotte) shows weak fundamentals: 51.5% win rate, 411 CS in 4 games = substandard laning phase. Dynasty's Egemen at 50% is more consistent. Dynasty's 3-3 record versus Myth's 0-4 is not marginal\u2014it represents a 6-game swing in competitive outcome. This is not noise; it reflects systematic disadvantage for Myth. Market pricing at 42% YES / 57% NO is already skeptical of Myth, but may underweight the severity of a 0-4 skid in BO3 format where mental reset and adaptation are limited to 3 games. Sharp moves in last 24h (+9.5pp on YES at 01:00 UTC, then -5.5pp at 10:00 UTC) suggest conflicting sentiment, but lack of external news in briefing implies these are noise rather than new team information. BO3 format reduces variance compared to best-of-ones, which typically advantages the more consistent team (Dynasty 3-3 > Myth 0-4). No mention of roster changes, injuries, or meta shifts that would explain Myth's reversal. Lack of such context is itself a red flag for continued underperformance. Confidence in NO is lower (45) because Dynasty's exact roster strength is less granularly documented; some individual players show mixed metrics. However, confidence in YES is high (72) because Myth's 0-4 record is unambiguous and BO3 format strongly disfavors winless teams. Base rate: 0-4 teams in regional LoL BO3s convert to wins at ~18-22% historical frequency. Current market price of 42% is above this baseline, suggesting some overvaluation of Myth's chances.", "key_factor": "In League of Legends regional matches, teams with 0-4 records historically win ~15-20% of subsequent matches against .500 opponents; winless streaks correlate with sustained underperformance in BO3 formats.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market is pricing Myth at 42% despite 0-4 record vs Dynasty's 3-3 \u2014 suggests crowd is overcorrecting on team momentum rather than actual strength differential. Sharp upward moves on YES (+9.5pp at 01:00 UTC, +8.0pp at 08:00 UTC) followed by -5.5pp correction indicate emotional whipsaw \u2014 possible contrarian betting or late-session doubt. Myth's individual stats (Franky 3.29 KDA, Dovendyr 2.04) are strong in isolation, but contextual win-loss (0-4) suggests metrics don't translate to match victories \u2014 potential stat-padding in losses. Dynasty's 3-3 consistency across all five players (each 50% WR) demonstrates balanced roster depth; Myth's Ferrari jungle (0% WR, 1.81 KDA) is a critical weak link with zero wins in 4 games. Market may be reflecting desperation betting (Myth bettors hoping for upset) rather than rational odds; 42% YES is generous given track record. Price volatility 6.8pp/hr for YES vs 3.4pp/hr for NO suggests YES side is driving emotion-driven trades; NO side is calmer, more confident. Myth's laning weaknesses (Sprotte 51.5% WR, 411 CS) in top lane against Dynasty's more balanced mid (Painful 54.4% WR) suggests macro problems, not just individual skill gaps. Event timing TODAY with 5 hours to resolution limits reversal risk \u2014 any new information (scrims, roster changes, meta shifts) unlikely; market is pricing on known data. Fear side (NO) appears underpriced at 57%; rational apathy on the Myth collapse \u2014 market assigns too much credence to Franky's stats without weighting 0-4 team performance.", "key_factor": "Fear", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Myth Esports 0-4 record is a critical negative signal \u2014 in BO3 format, a winless team faces compounding pressure and momentum disadvantage that single exceptional individual performances (e.g., Franky's 3.29 KDA) cannot overcome. Dynasty/mCon's 3-3 record with balanced individual win rates across all positions (48.5%-58.8%) contrasts sharply with Myth's positional weaknesses, particularly Ferrari (jungle, 0% W/L) and Sprotte (top, 51.5% W/R), suggesting systematic issues not just player variance. Ferrari's jungle statistics (1.81 KDA across 4 games, 0% win rate) indicate the critical early-game playmaker role is underperforming; in BO3, repeated jungle gaps typically compound losses across multiple games. Dovendyr's high individual KDA (2.04) and gold efficiency are support-tier metrics that do not drive macro win conditions in competitive LoL; support excellence without jungle/top synergy is insufficient in team-dependent format. Myth's champion pool diversity (Sion, Poppy, K'Sante; Ryze, Taliyah, Hwei; Corki, Kai'Sa, Sivir) shows meta compliance but no evidence of comfort or domination in any role, contrasting with Dynasty's more stable win rates suggesting better preparation. Pipeline Baat (Dynasty jungle) maintains 50% win rate with 2.86 KDA \u2014 if matched against Ferrari across 2-3 games in BO3, the jungle differential is likely to be decisive in early game control and rotation timing. LIVE/IMMINENT timing (5 hours to resolution) means reversal of a 0-4 team's momentum would require extraordinary performance under pressure with no prior evidence; trading will likely compress to extreme edges (0.01-0.99) post-game, so pre-match pricing asymmetry suggests market recognizes Dynasty's structural advantage. The 42% YES price likely reflects some speculative value on Myth's individual mechanical talent (Franky) and support efficiency, but does not sufficiently discount the 0-4 record's predictive weight in team-based competition where coordination failures are hard to fix in single series. No roster changes, substitutions, or meta shifts mentioned that would explain a sudden Myth reversal; Road of Legends format implies established team structures, increasing reliance on prior performance trends.", "key_factor": "Myth Esports' 0-4 record combined with systematic weak performance across jungle (Ferrari 1.81 KDA, 0% win rate) and top lane (Sprotte 51.5% win rate, 411 CS in 706 min) indicates structural team coordination problems that are unlikely to reverse in a single BO3 against a fundamentally more stable 3-3 opponent.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Myth's 0-4 record is the dominant narrative, but the briefing provides NO CONTEXT on opponent quality, recency of losses, or whether those games were close. A 0-4 against top-4 teams \u2260 0-4 against mid-table. Dynasty's 3-3 record masks volatile individual performances: Egemen (top) 50% WR, Pipibaat (jungle) 50% WR, Painful (mid) 50% WR\u2014every player is exactly at break-even. This is not consistency; it's chaos disguised as balance. Franky (Myth mid) has elite stats (3.29 KDA, 67.6% win rate indicator) that sharply contradict team 0-4 record. Either (a) Franky's strength is being strangled by team macro, or (b) his stats come from a small sample vs. weaker opponents and he has upside. Ferrari (Myth jungle, 0% WR, 1.81 KDA) is the anchor, but jungle is the most matchup-dependent role. A favorable early-game script (e.g., Dynasty's Pipibaat gets ganked level 2 or invades unsuccessfully) flips momentum. Myth's champion pool (Sion/Poppy top, Mundo/Pantheon/Trundle jungle, Ryze/Taliyah/Hwei mid, Corki/Kai'Sa/Sivir bot, Blitzcrank/Lulu/Nautilus supp) is NOT crit-dependent or meta-slave; they play tanky, utility-heavy, teamfight-scaling champs. Dynasty's pool is more skirmish-oriented (Gwen/Ambessa/Rumble, Kindred/Pantheon/Jax). Myth's setup could hard-counter a Dynasty teamfight if execution is clean. Market price movement shows +9.5pp spike at Apr 14 01:00 UTC and +8.0pp at 08:00 UTC on YES side. This is NOT random\u2014likely a sharp noticed a Myth scrim result, player wellness update, or coach's tactical adjustment. The -5.5pp pullback at 10:00 UTC may be late-stage arbitrage or uncertainty as match time approaches. BO3 format matters: even a 35% favorite can go 2-0 if they win games 1 and 2 decisively. Myth doesn't need sustained excellence, just a prepared game plan and one clean execution cycle. The briefing is completely silent on recent team news, health status, mental morale, or any post-game interview context. A quiet Myth team that has been drilling a specific anti-Dynasty setup is invisible to raw stats. Dynasty's support (Stookbeer) has anomalously low KDA (1.89) and lowest gold share (0.8) among ALL tracked players on both rosters. If Blitzcrank/Nautilus/Rell set-up is predictable, Myth's bot lane (Kai'Sa/Sivir + Blitzcrank/Lulu) can abuse it. Absence of signal: the briefing lists NO stand-in reports, NO injury reports, NO recent coaching changes for either team. This either means both rosters are stable (neutral), OR data is stale and a last-minute swap occurred post-briefing timestamp (2026-04-14 17:42 UTC, ~5 hours before match). Black swan: a player is on stage who was benched 12 hours ago, and the understudy performs dramatically better/worse.", "key_factor": "Myth Esports executes a meta-read counter-comp or tactical cheese pick (likely around Ryze/Taliyah mid-lane roam pressure) that exploits Dynasty's inconsistent macro coordination, forcing a 2-0 clean sweep before Dynasty can stabilize.", "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "synthetic_