n conviction; 7-day falling trend (-15pp from ~71% to 64%) indicates gradual market repricing toward GIANTX. Briefing lacks: head-to-head record, current Group Omega standings, BBL's recent form post-Kickoff, roster changes/stability for either team beyond vague coaching references. Community sentiment in briefing focuses on Fnatic vs Vitality analysis, not BBL vs GIANTX; no direct comparative intelligence reduces confidence in granular matchup assessment. Bo3 format reduces variance but briefing does not provide map pool strengths/weaknesses for either team\u2014this is a critical data gap that limits confidence on both sides. Event timing: TODAY (~7 hours to match). At this proximity, market price reflects real bettors' late-game information and conviction. 64% represents consensus view informed by most recent intel. Market is NOT displaying panic (NO not sub-25%) or irrational exuberance (YES not above 75%); this suggests rational repricing to a competitive matchup where BBL retains slight edge from Kickoff credentials but GIANTX is clearly competitive. Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_yes=72 (Kickoff win is concrete; recent form signals are strong) vs confidence_no=55 (GIANTX firepower is real but limited historical context in briefing; their pre-Kickoff performance is not detailed, only single recent win vs PACIFIC).", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "BBL Esports won VCT EMEA Kickoff (Jan-Feb 2026), most recent credible competitive signal; 10-week gap to Stage 1 (Apr 1) introduces meta/patch drift and adaptation risk in Valorant's fast-evolving environment. GIANTX showed concrete recent performance: 2-1 victory over PACIFIC with dual-Duelist carry potential (ara & westside >58 kills each); demonstrates firepower and map-specific strength in current