me team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 3723.5788930000017, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["46040212347203243327941874848141426227058290824617336247015958381935484227732", "64456015853245592578624623159879522241978033849605987024267574487791678176387"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "USE demonstrates strong recent form: 8+ consecutive wins in Prime League Winter Split 2026 regular season with consistent high-level play (72-75% CS efficiency, positive gold differentials). Market price at 66% YES aligns with underlying strength differential evident in available data, suggesting early consensus formation around USE favoritism. Critical asymmetry: USE's detailed match history available; Team Orange Gaming has NO available performance data, win/loss record, or recent competition results to assess relative strength. BO1 format inherently increases variance and upset probability compared to best-of-series formats\u2014single-game outcomes are less deterministic than aggregate series performance. Without Team Orange Gaming performance metrics, cannot fully justify a high confidence_no score; the absence of data does not confirm weakness, only indicates analytical blind spot. Match timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution) means minimal time remains for late information updates; current market price likely reflects information available to sophisticated traders. USE's 3rd place playoff finish and regular-season dominance suggest solid mid-to-upper tier positioning, but opponent context remains opaque. probability_score of 68 reflects USE's demonstrable recent form (pushing probability above 50%) while acknowledging BO1 variance and complete lack of comparative opponent data (preventing higher confidence). confidence_yes set at 72 due to strong USE data; confidence_no set at 35 due to absence of Team Orange Gaming information\u2014cannot confidently assess NO outcome when one side's data is entirely missing.", "key_factor": "Team Orange Gaming has zero available performance data, making it impossible to assess their relative strength or recent form; BO1 format introduces inherent match variance that can produce upsets.", "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.31999999999999995, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "USE MOMENTUM: USE has won every single match documented in the Winter Split 2026 regular season (8 consecutive victories visible), including wins against established opponents (EINS, KHK, EWI, AOMA, SGE, BIG), demonstrating sustained form and consistency. INDIVIDUAL QUALITY: Mid-laner SE Kanin shows strong individual metrics across victories\u2014high KDA, reliable champion pool, and dominant laning phases\u2014indicating elite-level play that carries team performance. OPERATIONAL EXCELLENCE: USE maintains 72-75% CS efficiency and strong gold generation across matches, suggesting disciplined macro play, resource conversion, and win condition execution. OPPONENT INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: No performance data, win-loss record, roster strength, or competitive context exists for Team Orange Gaming in the briefing. Market pricing at 66% YES reflects this information gap\u2014betting against USE requires assuming Team Orange Gaming is competitive despite zero evidence. TOURNAMENT POSITIONING: USE's Winter Split playoff appearance (3rd place matches) confirms mid-to-upper-tier competitive status in Prime League, whereas Team Orange Gaming's tier remains unknown. BO1 VARIANCE CUT BOTH WAYS: While BO1 format increases match variance, USE's documented consistency across 8 different matchups suggests they execute reliably even in single-game scenarios. Variance typically favors the better-prepared, more-skilled team in high-stakes single games. MARKET STABILITY: YES pricing has been stable at 66% (EMA) over 7 days with only minor 24-hour volatility (\u20131pp), suggesting informed market consensus rather than wild speculation. The +13pp 7-day move reflects accumulated confidence, not panic. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Team Orange Gaming's complete absence from briefing data\u2014no wins, no losses, no roster information\u2014indicates either a lower-division team, new roster, or significantly weaker recent performance than USE. If competitive, their stats would likely be available. CONSERVATIVE PROBABILITY: Keeping score at 66 (matching market price) rather than inflating to 75+ reflects genuine BO1 uncertainty and incomplete opponent profile. However, the direction and magnitude of YES confidence is justified by the evidence presented. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes at 72% reflects strong USE data, while confidence_no at 35% reflects minimal Team Orange Gaming information\u2014this asymmetry is appropriate when one side is data-rich and the other is data-poor.", "key_factor": "Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition's documented 8-game winning streak in Winter Split 2026 regular season against a Team Orange Gaming opponent with zero performance data in the briefing.", "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.33999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNDERDOG (NO) STRENGTHS: Team Orange Gaming is essentially a data blackhole\u2014zero search results for their S16 performance, head-to