single-game performance, especially if Team Orange Gaming plays a pocket strategy or unconventional draft. Team Orange Gaming has ZERO performance data in briefing\u2014this is not evidence of weakness but a critical information void. They could be a promoted team, academy squad, or genuinely underperforming, but we cannot rule out a strategic upset. Market price +13pp jump on Apr 12 suggests news event (roster announcement, scrim results, or injury), but that event is not documented in briefing\u2014potential late-breaking information the market has priced in but briefing lacks detail. Prime League 1st Division includes mixed tiers of competition; USE's 3rd-place finish in Winter Split playoffs suggests they are strong but NOT the league's clear #1\u2014Team Orange Gaming's true rank/seeding unknown. No head-to-head history provided; teams meeting for first time increases upset probability, as USE cannot exploit known weaknesses. Map veto/selection in BO1 can heavily favor one team's pool; if Team Orange Gaming has superior performance on USE's banned/unfavored maps, single-game format traps USE in disadvantageous pool. USE's CS efficiency (72-75%) is high but not elite-tier; suggests they win via macro/teamfighting advantage rather than laning dominance\u2014vulnerable to early jungle ganks or mid-game invades by scrappy, high-tempo opponents. Briefing explicitly notes 'No search results were found regarding Team Orange Gaming'\u2014absence of data is a red flag that either (a) Orange is a lower-tier/academy team with predictable loss, or (b) information gap exists and Orange is being underestimated by market. Match resolves TODAY in ~7 hours; any roster/health issue would emerge in final hours, but briefing cutoff (Apr 15 13:54 UTC) vs match time (21:00 UTC) leaves 7-hour window for unbreakable surprises.", "key_factor": "Team Orange Gaming fields a substitute or academy roster, or USE suffers a key player illness/technical issue hours before the match, neutralizing USE's preparation advantage.", "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.6404660564779749, "no_score": 0.4090863444013557, "edge": 0.04499999999999993, "no_edge": 0.355, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5267175572519084, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.13043478260869557, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.06521739130434778, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1958142", "question": "LoL: Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition vs Team Orange Gaming (BO1) - Prime League 1st Division Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition and Team Orange Gaming in the Prime League 1st Division Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 15 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition\" if Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition win the match against Team Orange Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Orange Gaming\" if Team Orange Gaming win the match against Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 3723.5788930000017, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["46040212347203243327941874848141426227058290824617336247015958381935484227732", "64456015853245592578624623159879522241978033849605987024267574487791678176387"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Title: Unicorns of Love Sexy Edition match list in S16 - Games of Legends\n| WIN | 3-2 | Blue | 21 | 60.5 | 9 | 1 | EINS | 13 | 51.1 | 2 | 3 | 27:45 | EINS vs USE (5) | 16.4 | 3RD.PLACE | Prime League 1st Div 2026 Winter Split |.", "| WIN | | | Blue | 15 | 69.2 | 8 | 3 | EINS | 7 | 61.3 | 7 | 2 | 34:04 | EINS vs USE (3) | 16.4 | 3RD.PLACE | Prime League 1st Div 2026 Winter Split |.", "| WIN | | | Blue | 18 | 71.7 | 11 | 4 | EINS | 4 | 57.1 | 2 | 1 | 32:03 | EINS vs USE (1) | 16.4 | 3RD.PLACE | Prime League 