a available for Team Orange Gaming prevents comparative analysis", "BO1 format increases variance and eliminates opportunity to adapt between games", "USE's recent matches may have been against weaker opponents (limited context on opponent strength)"], "key_context": ["Match format is BO1 (single game), increasing variance vs best-of-series formats", "Prime League 1st Division 2026 Winter Split regular season (currently ongoing)", "USE previously competed in playoffs (3rd place matches) indicating mid-tier tournament positioning", "Historical data shows USE competed in S14 (2024) with mixed results, showing competitive experience", "No head-to-head history or Team Orange Gaming statistics available in search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-15T13:54:01.080502Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "46040212347203243327941874848141426227058290824617336247015958381935484227732", "data_points": 55, "weighted_avg": 0.6576381495184886, "change_1w_pp": 13.0, "change_24h_pp": -1.0000000000000009, "volatility_24h": 0.5268524740492021, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:00:53Z", "delta_pp": 11.5}]}, "no": {"token_id": "64456015853245592578624623159879522241978033849605987024267574487791678176387", "data_points": 17, "weighted_avg": 0.33715311492655486, "change_1w_pp": -2.0000000000000018, "change_24h_pp": 0.9999999999999953, "volatility_24h": 0.2886751345948099, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-15T13:54:01.812824Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-15T22:09:31.886368+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "3bc09b48-75d1-4dd2-9e32-cbaece4c88d9", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T13:55:24.535201+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1986901", "question": "Counter-Strike: B8 vs Aurora Gaming (BO3) - IEM Rio Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket semifinal 1 match between B8 and Aurora Gaming in the IEM Rio Group B, initially scheduled for April 15 at 11:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"B8\" if B8 win the match against Aurora Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Aurora Gaming\" if Aurora Gaming win the match against B8.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T21:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T15:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.345, "volume_usd": 241182.28972800024, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["3513311378827576827060629206693226783456913540452337262759365386103858758809", "92166797435686345505386178944446872679211626532844872378024471735352749847357"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.34, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Match must complete with a winner; B8 wins = YES outcome. MARKET ALIGNMENT: Current market price of 34% YES / 66% NO reflects significant confidence in Aurora Gaming, despite B8's higher world ranking (17th). DATA QUALITY CRITICAL GAP: The 'KEY FACTS' section contains fan commentary and fragmented tournament observations that provide no actionable information about B8 vs Aurora relative strengths. References to 'JT's troops', Vitality's securing titles, and roster speculation (kyousuke, Magisk, Magisk) do not compare the two teams in this match. CASE FOR B8 (YES): World ranking of 17th, wins vs Passion UA and Legacy in same tournament. However, B8 lost to Natus Vincere, showing vulnerability to top-tier opponents. Ranking advantage is real but modest. CASE FOR AURORA (NO): Demonstrated comeback ability (10-12 to 16-13 turnaround mentioned), though framed as 'Aurora played bad' initially. Team characterized as having calm, serious, motivated roster. No ranking data provided; Turkish team origin noted but no global ranking comparison. DIRECT COMPARISON ABSENT: Briefing provides no head-to-head history, recent form trends in same tournament phase, or comparative map pool analysis between B8 and Aurora. MARKET PRICE AS SIGNAL: The 66% NO (Aurora) price and stable 1-week history suggests market participants have access to information beyond this briefing (likely HLTV live odds, recent scrim results, roster updates, or expert consensus). The 34/66 split is not extreme but reflects material confidence gap. TIMING: Event is TODAY with ~8 hours to resolution. No time for major reversals; outcome will depend on in-match performance. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Clear criteria. Match must complete with winner; draw, cancellation >7 days, or pre-match forfeit \u2192 50-50. Mid-match forfeit \u2192 winner's team resolves. HLTV is primary source; credible reporting backup within 2 hours. Low oracle risk. CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=32 and confidence_no=28 both LOW because briefing data does not provide robust statistical or form-based reasoning for either outcome. Market price (34%) is better calibrated than the sparse briefing warrants. Assigning probability_score=34 reflects market consensus while acknowledging low confidence in both directions \u2014 neither side's case is well-supported by the provided data.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is fragmentary and does not provide sufficient recent form, head-to-head history, or reliable player/roster information to confidently assess either team's likelihood of winning.", "probability_yes": 0.34, "probability_no": 0.6599999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO/Aurora) STRENGTHS: Aurora has proven capability to recover from 10-12 deficits to 16-13 victories, indicating mental resilience and mid-game adaptation. The briefing explicitly notes Aurora players as 'calm, serious, and motivated,' which are psychological factors that enable comebacks in high-pressure BO3 formats. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES/B8): B8's tournament record shows critical vulnerability\u2014they lost decisively to Natus Vincere, a top-tier opponent. While they beat Passion UA and Legacy (lower-bracket teams), these wins lack the quality evidence needed to project B8 as tournament contenders. Their 17th global ranking, while respectable, places them below Aurora's demonstrated tournament performance. COMEBACK EVIDENCE: The briefing contains specific evidence of Aurora's comeback ability ('How did Aurora come back from 10-12 to 16-13?'), which is directly relevant to BO3 dynamics where momentum and clutch rounds determine map outcomes. This is not attributed to opponent error but to Aurora's tactical execution. B8 INCONSISTENCY: B8's mixed performance (wins vs. lower opposition, losses vs. strong teams) suggests they lack the consistency needed in a BO3 elimination scenario. The briefing notes their positioning in the lower bracket, implying stakes are already high and pressure increases. ROSTER/MOTIVATION FACTOR: Aurora's pending roster changes and noted motivation contrast with no equivalent catalyst mentioned for B8, suggesting Aurora entered this match with fresh institutional energy. MARKET STABILITY: The 66% NO pricing has remained completely stable over 7 days with zero volatility, indicating professional/sharp money has settled on this line. The $241k volume confirms adequate liquidity and no obvious mispricings. LIMITED HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited direct head-to-head data' between these teams, meaning the market's 34/66 split likely reflects broader tournament context (B8's losses to Natus Vincere, Aurora's comeback narrative) rather than outdated or biased data. DATA QUALITY CAVEAT: The KEY FACTS section is fragmentary and incoherent, making detailed tactical analysis impossible. This argues for LOWER confidence on both sides\u2014the market price of 66 reflects informed betting, but our ability to independently validate it is limited. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 35 (Aurora's comeback ability and B8's Na'Vi loss are weak proxies for a specific BO3 outcome; tournament seeding is unclear) vs. confidence_no = 72 (the favored side's psychology + B8's established weakness to tier-1 opponents provide structural support, and market stability suggests consensus).", "key_factor": "Aurora Gaming's demonstrated ability to mount significant comebacks from double-digit deficits, combined with B8's documented losses to top-tier opponents, supports the market's 66% NO pricing.", "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.33999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH (YES/B8): B8 holds a 17th global ranking vs Aurora's lower tier status, and secured wins against Passion UA and Legacy in the tournament. UNDERDOG STRENGTH (YES/B8): B8's lower bracket positioning suggests stronger structural tournament performance so far. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY (NO/Aurora): Aurora explicitly criticized in briefing for 'inconsistent performance' and 'poor decision-making' in recent matches\u2014not just one loss but pattern of volatility. FAVORITE RESILIENCE (NO/Aurora): However, Aurora's comeback from 10-12 to 16-13 (likely a single map) demonstrates real clutch execution ability under pressure\u2014not flukey, but calculated play in close moments. FAVORITE MOMENTUM (NO/Aurora): Briefing notes Aurora players are 'calm, serious, and motivated' with roster changes pending; psychological state matters in BO3 elimination matches. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO direct head-to-head history between B8 and Aurora, severely limiting predictive confidence on either side. CRITICAL DATA GAP: No recent form data (last 2 weeks) for either team provided; both teams' current practice, map comfort, and player health unknown. B8 VULNERABILITY: B8 lost to Natus Vincere, indicating vulnerability to tier-1 opponents; unclear if Aurora is tier-1 or tier-2 relative to B8. MARKET STABILITY: Prices have held at 34/66 split for 7 days with zero volatility\u2014suggests either strong consensus or lack of new information; given data gaps, likely the latter. UPSET SCENARIO: If Aurora's 'inconsistency' stems from motivation/preparation issues rather than structural skill gaps, a motivated, roster-adjusted Aurora could exploit B8's mixed recent form. REALISM CHECK: 34% for the underdog is not extreme; market reflects genuine uncertainty given fragmentary briefing data; not a sharp mispricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong case for B8's ranking and wins, but weak data on current form and head-to-head dynamics limits confidence in either outcome.", "key_factor": "Aurora Gaming's demonstrated ability to mount comebacks from double-digit deficits (10-12 to 16-13) suggests clutch execution under pressure that B8 may lack.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.34, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "- B8 is ranked 17th globally with tournament wins vs. Passion UA and Legacy; Aurora is Turkish team with demonstrated comeback ability but inconsistent execution\n- Market price of 34% YES (66% NO) suggests Aurora is favored despite B8's higher ranking \u2014 indicates market perceives Aurora's momentum/comeback ability as compensating factor\n- Historical base rate: higher-ranked team in BO3 typically wins 55-65%; B8's 17th ranking would suggest ~55-60% baseline win probability, but current market price (34%) significantly undervalues this ranking advantage\n- Aurora's comeback victories (e.g., 10-12 to 16-13) show clutch execution but briefing notes this was partly due to opponent mistakes, not necessarily superior play\n- Critical data gaps: no recent head-to-head record, limited direct form comparison, fragmented coverage limits confidence in either direction\n- B8 loss to Natus Vincere suggests vulnerability, but NaVi is elite-tier team \u2014 not a meaningful negative signal\n- EVENT TIMING (LIVE/IMMINENT in ~8 hours): stable market pricing over 7 days with zero volatility suggests either strong consensus or information asymmetry; lack of movement as match approaches is atypical for competitive esports where new information (scrim results, roster confirmation, map veto trends) typically emerges\n- Confidence asymmetry justified: stronger data supporting B8's ranking advantage (YES case) than supporting Aurora's intangible momentum factors (NO case); market may be overweighting narrative of comebacks\n- Assign probability_score to current market consensus (34%) but with moderate confidence on both sides due to insufficient granular form data and limited head-to-head precedent", "key_factor": "In professional Counter-Strike BO3 matches between similarly-ranked teams at premier tournaments, the higher-ranked team wins approximately 55-65% of the time; comebacks from significant deficits occur in ~15-20% of matches.", "probability_yes": 0.34, "probability_no": 0.6599999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.34, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market is STABLE at 34/66 for 7 days with ZERO volatility \u2014 suggests crowd indifference, not conviction on either side. Moderate volume ($241k) for a TODAY match 8 hours from resolution indicates low engagement relative to tournament importance. CASE FOR YES (34% priced): B8 ranked 17th globally, beat Passion UA and Legacy, but lost to Natus Vincere (stronger opponent). Rankings support slight underdog undervaluation. CASE FOR NO (66% priced): Aurora showed comeback ability (10-12 to 16-13 example cited), roster stability, player motivation. But market may be OVERWEIGHTING comeback narrative without hard evidence of form advantage. KEY DATA GAP: Briefing lacks recent head-to-head results, current form trends, map-specific matchups, or detailed player/coach performance metrics. This explains flat price and low conviction. FRAGMENTED NEWS COVERAGE: Briefing contains tangential fan commentary (Furia delusion, Vitality dominance, Magisk/kyousuke debates) unrelated to B8 vs Aurora. Suggests limited quality intel reaching market participants. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market appears to have settled on NO (66%) based on Aurora's comeback reputation, but lacks fresh data to justify confidence. This is RATIONAL APATHY, not GREED or FEAR. MISPRICING SIGNAL: YES side (34%) may be slightly undervalued if B8's wins (Passion UA, Legacy) represent stronger tournament performance than Aurora's comebacks against presumably weaker opponents. However, insufficient direct evidence to confidently exploit. IMMINENT RESOLUTION: Match begins in ~8 hours. Current price reflects consensus doubt on B8, but consensus is shallow (zero volatility). Small information release could shift price quickly. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Weak confidence on both sides reflects genuine data scarcity. NO side (66%) benefits from Aurora's documented comebacks but lacks proof of current form. YES side (34%) has ranking support but demonstrated vulnerability to top teams.", "key_factor": "Apathy", "probability_yes": 0.34, "probability_no": 0.6599999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "B8's 17th global ranking provides baseline competitive credibility, but rankings are historical and don't capture tournament-specific meta or current roster form. Aurora's comeback victories indicate high-level composure under pressure and anti-eco/buy-round discipline\u2014core Counter-Strike fundamentals that predict BO3 resilience. B8's loss to Natus Vincere (a top-tier opponent) is expected; however, wins vs. Passion UA and Legacy do not establish dominance over mid-tier competition. KEY CONTEXT: Market pricing (34% YES / 66% NO) reflects bookmaker confidence in Aurora, consistent with Aurora's documented comeback ability and resilience narrative. BO3 format favors teams with strong anti-tilt psychology and map pool depth. Aurora's stoic roster composition ('calm, serious, motivated') aligns with BO3 sustainability. Limited head-to-head history and fragmented recent form data prevent high-confidence calibration on either side; KEY FACTS section contains unstructured commentary rather than concrete performance metrics. B8 positioning as 'lower bracket' competitor (implied) suggests potential motivation asymmetry\u2014but Aurora's tournament trajectory (comebacks) suggests they enter with momentum. Map pool (7 maps) favors teams with recent scrim depth and meta-read; briefing lacks veto history or map-specific strength data for either team. Time-to-resolution: ~8 hours (TODAY), market is stable (0.0pp volatility 24hr), volume moderate ($241k). Pricing reflects settled consensus, not late-breaking shifts. Technical gap: Briefing emphasizes Aurora's comeback narrative but lacks quantitative support (round-win %, economy efficiency, T-side win rate). This asymmetric data quality lowers confidence on both sides but slightly favors the NO case since market prices it at 66%.", "key_factor": "Aurora Gaming's documented ability to execute comebacks from double-digit deficits (10-12 \u2192 16-13) suggests superior round-economy management and mid-round adaptation capabilities, which are critical in BO3 formats where momentum shifts are decisive.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Market is stable at 34% YES for 7 days with zero volatility\u2014suggests either consensus-driven mispricing or genuine equilibrium; the flatness itself is suspicious for a same-day event. Briefing emphasizes Aurora's comeback pattern (10-12 to 16-13 turnaround explicitly mentioned) as evidence of poor play, but this is a BLACK SWAN misinterpretation: teams that consistently claw back from large deficits in BO3 lower brackets possess exceptional mental resilience and anti-eco fundamentals under pressure\u2014exactly what B8 may lack. B8's loss to Natus Vincere (a tier-1 team) is presented as 'vulnerability'; however, Aurora's comebacks were achieved *against* competition, not in scrims. B8's global rank #17 inflates confidence\u2014rankings are backward-looking and don't capture tournament-specific form or map pool exploitation. Aurora described as 'calm, serious, motivated' with roster changes pending\u2014pending changes could signal pre-match confidence/stability OR indicate last-minute personnel shifts that could disrupt B8's preparation if scouting reports are stale. Map pool analysis absent: if Aurora has superior Nuke/Overpass/Anubis read relative to B8's Dust2/Mirage strength, a BO3 veto sequence could heavily favor the underdog's comfort. Briefing provides pool but no team-specific performance breakdown. Lower bracket context is vague ('crucial positioning match')\u2014if this is sudden-death elimination for B8 but a survivor's bracket for Aurora, psychological pressure asymmetry is the hidden variable. Fragmented coverage explicitly noted in briefing limits recent form comparison; B8's wins vs. Passion UA and Legacy are tier-3 opponents, offering false confidence in a BO3 against a team known for pressure comebacks. B8 favored at 34% despite Aurora's proven late-round execution in THIS tournament; market may be anchored to pre-tournament seeding rather than live performance delta.", "key_factor": "Aurora Gaming's demonstrated ability to execute coordinated comebacks from double-digit deficits (10-12 to 16-13 pattern) reflects superior late-round discipline and anti-eco execution that could neutralize B8's early-game structural advantages in a high-pressure elimination match.", "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.6799999999999999, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}],