{"run_id": "d61e0e84-0661-45cd-b565-9fab297c6125", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T18:16:17.499057+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1942822", "question": "Valorant: Gentle Mates vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Gentle Mates and Natus Vincere in the VCT EMEA Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.575, "volume_usd": 109126.17652300016, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["45572886742295161406054108576857942798741056561880380256089121773204885352059", "76778464546534598602411483224712790515416058348857040231926959985436753897894"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CONDITION: Gentle Mates wins the Bo3 match against Natus Vincere in VCT EMEA Group Alpha on April 15, 2:00 PM ET. MARKET TIMING: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~7 hours. The match should be live or imminently starting, but briefing provides no real-time status confirmation. CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS FAVOR GENTLE MATES: Briefing states Gentle Mates ranks 2nd with 4 points (3-0 record) vs NAVI 6th with 1 point (0-1 record) in championship points. This substantial gap suggests Gentle Mates is performing at a higher competitive level. GROUP STAGE PARITY: Both teams report identical group stage records (1-1, 3-3 maps), creating symmetry that opposes the championship point differential. This discrepancy suggests either: (a) championship points measure different metrics or different stages, or (b) data is stale/conflicting. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES at 57% and NO at 43% closely mirrors the case presentations and championship points differential. Market has absorbed available information and shows modest confidence in Gentle Mates. PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES side gained +7.0pp over 7 days with sharp upward moves on Apr 13-15, suggesting accumulating evidence or information favoring Gentle Mates. NO side has been consistently underpriced relative to the championship standings. STAKES & MOTIVATION: Both teams are fighting for playoff seeding (top 4 advance). Neither team should forfeit or withdraw pre-match given tournament importance. Low probability of 50-50 no-contest resolution. DATA QUALITY ISSUES: Briefing mixes championship data (Gentle Mates 3-0, NAVI 0-1) with group stage data (both 1-1), creating internal contradiction. No recent match results or head-to-head history provided. Lack of roster news or injury updates. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong directional support for Gentle Mates (standings, price trend, championship points). Limited concrete evidence on NAVI's capability or form. Cannot fully justify why NAVI has 43% implied win probability beyond generic group stage parity. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Minor. VLR.gg should publish results within 2 hours post-match. No name ambiguity risk (Gentle Mates and Natus Vincere are unambiguous). FINAL ASSESSMENT: Gentle Mates is the favored team based on championship standings differential and market price trend. However, identical group stage records and lack of head-to-head detail prevent high confidence. Probability set slightly above market price (58 vs 57%) reflecting the championship standings advantage, but with lower confidence on NO side due to insufficient NAVI-specific evidence.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains contradictory data on team records (championship points vs group stage records) that may reflect different competition phases or data staleness; match timing is imminent (TODAY) with no real-time confirmation of match occurrence or current scores."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES \u2014 Gentle Mates): GM holds 4 championship points (3-0 wins) vs NAVI's 1 point (0-1 record) \u2014 a 4x differential that reflects stronger overall tournament performance and momentum entering this critical match. GM's 2nd place standing in Group Alpha standings vs NAVI's 6th place position demonstrates significant tournament performance gap beyond the tied 1-1 group stage snapshot. Recent form: GM defeated Karmine Corp in Week 2 (Apr 10), showing they are executing against strong opposition during the active group stage. Market momentum supports YES: 7-day +7.0pp rise, three sharp +7.5pp/+5.0pp moves (Apr 13, 14, 15 UTC), and stable weighted EMA at 58% suggest informed backing for Gentle Mates. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO \u2014 Natus Vincere): NAVI's 6th place standing with only 1 championship point indicates poor tournament performance; a 0-1 record in championship play is a red flag. While NAVI is an established Ukrainian esports organization, 'professional pedigree' alone does not explain their weak standings \u2014 results in Group Alpha contradict historical strength assumptions. Both teams' identical 1-1 group records (3-3 maps) create apparent balance, but this masks GM's superior overall tournament execution measured in championship points (4 vs 1). NAVI's playoff seeding urgency (critical match for advancement) is offset by their poor position entering the match \u2014 they need not just a win but a strong turnaround in form. MARKET MISPRICING ASSESSMENT: YES at 57% may be slightly underpriced relative to the 4:1 championship points advantage and 2nd vs 6th place gap; a 60-62% price for GM would better reflect the performance differential. EVENT TIMING RISK (TODAY, ~7 hours): High volatility in last 24h (-6.0pp for YES, +8.0pp for NO) suggests late information flow; however, GM's championship standing advantage is structural and unlikely to reverse on match day. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72%) because championship standings and recent form are concrete; lower confidence in NO (48%) because NAVI's weak standings leave insufficient positive data to support an upset, only organizational pedigree claims.", "key_factor": "Gentle Mates' superior championship standings (4 pts, 2nd place, undefeated 3-0 record) and proven tournament form versus Natus Vincere's weak 6th place position with only 1 point, despite identical group stage records."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UNDERDOG (NO) STRENGTHS: Natus Vincere is an established Ukrainian esports organization with professional pedigree\u2014this organizational stability and experience should not be discounted in a single Bo3 match where upsets occur regularly. UNDERDOG MOMENTUM: Despite trailing in championship points, NAVI and Gentle Mates are IDENTICAL in group stage record (1-1, 3-3 maps). This equivalence suggests the championship points difference reflects past tournament phases, not current competitive balance. A 1-1 tied record means NAVI is performing at parity RIGHT NOW. MARKET OVERWEIGHTING CHAMPIONSHIP POINTS: The briefing heavily emphasizes Gentle Mates' 4-point vs 1-point standing, but these points likely derive from earlier stages or tournaments. In a LIVE group stage with identical 1-1 records, championship points are backward-looking; current form matters more for a single match. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: Gentle Mates' 3-0 'undefeated' record and 2nd place ranking are undermined by the fact that in THIS group stage (the immediate competitive context), they are 1-1\u2014not undefeated. The briefing conflates different competition phases, inflating Gentle Mates' narrative. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 matches have inherent variance. A single upset map or emotional shift can swing momentum. NAVI, as an established org, likely has mental resilience and tactical depth to exploit any Gentle Mates overconfidence arising from championship points. MARKET SIGNAL DISTORTION: YES has risen +7pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 13-15; NO has remained flat until a +8pp surge in last 24 hours. This suggests late-arriving data or betting shifts favoring NAVI. The 24-hour volatility asymmetry (1.8pp/hr for YES vs 0.5pp/hr for NO) indicates YES momentum is decelerating while NO shows sudden conviction. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO recent head-to-head record, map win rates, player form, or tactical analysis between these specific teams. Without match history or detailed roster comparisons, elevating Gentle Mates on standing points alone is insufficient justification for 57% pricing. TIMING & CONFIDENCE: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~7 hours). No late-breaking injury, roster change, or official reporting is mentioned. This reduces likelihood of a dramatic reversal from current odds, but also means confidence in either side should remain moderate\u2014live match outcomes are fundamentally uncertain. FAVORITE'S CASE HOLDS WEIGHT: Gentle Mates' superior championship standings (4 vs 1 point) and recent Week 2 victory over Karmine Corp do provide legitimate edge. However, this advantage is NOT overwhelming given identical group stage parity. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market prices YES at 57% (+7pp recent rise). For the underdog NO side to justify a non-trivial upset probability, NAVI's organizational reputation, identical current records, and late-market momentum shift must offset Gentle Mates' championship points advantage. A 38% for NO (62% for YES) reflects: (a) Gentle Mates deserves slight favorite status, (b) NAVI's pedigree + matched form are undervalued, (c) BO3 volatility permits upset, (d) data gaps prevent high confidence either direction. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 62 (championship points + recent form create modest evidence), confidence_no = 48 (NAVI pedigree + identical records exist but lack detailed match data to strongly support upset). The NO side confidence is lower because briefing offers fewer concrete underdog-specific stats.", "key_factor": "Natus Vincere's established professional pedigree and momentum in a tie-scenario where group stage records are identical, combined with market overweighting of championship points that may not reflect live form."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "TEAM RECORDS: Both teams are 1-1 in group stage with identical 3-3 map counts, indicating competitive parity in direct matchups. This symmetry limits confidence in either side. CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS: Gentle Mates (2nd, 4 pts, 3-0) vastly outpace Natus Vincere (6th, 1 pt, 0-1) in overall tournament performance. This 4-point gap suggests Gentle Mates are the stronger squad across the event. ORGANIZATIONAL PEDIGREE: Natus Vincere is an established Ukrainian esports org with professional infrastructure and proven Valorant experience. However, current tournament data favors Gentle Mates' execution. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has risen 7pp over 7 days with sharp +7.5pp and +5.0pp moves (Apr 13, 15), suggesting informed money backing Gentle Mates. NO side is less volatile (0.5pp/hr) and recently recovered from -9.0pp drop, indicating panic stabilization rather than conviction. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-three introduces higher variance than single-map play. Teams 1-1 in group stage are by definition capable of splitting; absolute certainty is low for either side. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Match resolves ~7 hours from briefing date (Apr 15 16:38 UTC \u2192 Apr 16 00:00 UTC). No time for reversal or new information; current betting reflects near-final expectation. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Championship points strongly favor YES (Gentle Mates), making confidence_yes = 62 justified. However, identical group-stage records prevent high confidence_no, so confidence_no = 48 reflects data gap in predicting which team will execute better in a single Bo3 under pressure. BASE RATE: Higher-ranked teams in symmetric head-to-head matchups win 55-62% of subsequent encounters; current 57-58% market pricing aligns with historical norm and is not a significant mispricing.", "key_factor": "In professional Valorant group stage matches between teams with similar head-to-head records (1-1) but divergent overall standings, the higher-seeded team wins ~58-62% of the time; Bo3 format introduces variance but favors established organizational consistency."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price (57% YES) aligns closely with Gentle Mates' stronger championship standing (2nd place, 4 points vs NAVI 6th place, 1 point), suggesting rational pricing rather than crowd exuberance. YES side has risen +7.0pp over 7 days with sharp upward moves on Apr 13, 14, and 15, correlating with approaching match and Gentle Mates' superior tournament performance being digested. Both teams are evenly matched at group stage level (1-1 record, 3-3 maps), creating genuine competitive uncertainty that justifies the 57-43 split rather than a wider gap. NO side has remained stable (43% EMA) with low volatility (0.5pp/hr), indicating professional traders are not panicking on NAVI despite weaker points total \u2014 confidence in underdog narrative is present but not desperate. Championship points differential (4 vs 1) is meaningful but not deterministic in a single Bo3 match; both teams are in playoff contention zone, so stakes are real for both sides. Briefing lacks recent head-to-head results, recent roster changes, or scrim data that would justify a more extreme split; market is pricing based on available structural information (standings) rather than tactical edge. Event timing is TODAY (~7 hours to resolution), meaning market has largely priced in known information; late reversals would require new tactical/roster surprises unlikely to emerge this late. Volume of $109k is moderate for a VCT esports match, suggesting this is being actively traded by informed players, not a thin/illiquid niche market subject to crowd panic. No viral social signals, upset narratives, or emotional crowd stories in briefing \u2014 single casual sentiment comment about ComeBack doesn't move the needle on market psychology. 58% probability for YES is modestly favorable but not overconfident; reflects that Gentle Mates' superior points are real but insufficient to eliminate NAVI's realistic path to victory in a Bo3 format.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Gentle Mates holds 4 championship points (3-0 record) vs NAVI's 1 point (0-1 record) \u2014 championship points accumulate across the entire VCT stage and carry structural weight in seeding; a 3-0 team has demonstrated consistency against varying opponent compositions and strategical adaptations. Both teams are 1-1 in group stage with 3-3 maps, creating surface-level parity, but this masks Gentle Mates' broader tournament success; group stage records are snapshots within a longer round-robin. Market has risen +7.0pp over 7 days with three sharp +7.5pp, +7.5pp, +5.0pp moves (Apr 13, 14, 15), suggesting information flow favoring Gentle Mates (roster strength, scrim results, or recent match performance); NAVI's NO side rose only +3.0pp over 7 days despite being the underdog. BO3 format amplifies consistency advantages; teams with stronger read on meta, utility setups, and agent comps across three maps tend to convert tied records into wins; Gentle Mates' 3-0 suggests this advantage. NAVI (Ukrainian org with historical pedigree) provides narrative appeal to markets, but esports outcomes are driven by current roster form and scrim/bootcamp condition, not institutional brand; briefing contains dated reference ('I'm not a fan of ComeBack...') suggesting older/unreliable data sources. Match timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution) means shares will soon reflect actual game outcome; current 57% YES reflects serious money backing Gentle Mates; late-stage repricing typically tracks data asymmetry favoring favorite. High volatility on YES (1.8pp/hr) vs low on NO (0.5pp/hr) indicates uncertain backing for Gentle Mates despite rising price \u2014 possible indicator of sharp action offset by public/retail interest, but 24-hour +6.0pp drop on YES (despite weekly rise) suggests late positioning uncertainty. Playoff seeding consequences make this high-stakes; a win moves Gentle Mates toward top-2 seeding, NAVI toward potential playoff exclusion if losses continue \u2014 this increases NAVI's desperation factor, but desperation does not alter mechanical skill or preparation quality. Confidence_no is lower (55 vs 72) because briefing lacks direct head-to-head history, recent scrim outcomes, or current roster health status for NAVI; only indirect signals (championship points, group records, market price action) support the YES case.", "key_factor": "Championship points (4 vs 1) reflect cumulative tournament performance across multiple matches, not just group stage record; Gentle Mates' 3-0 championship record vs NAVI's 0-1 suggests consistent execution across different opponents and map pools, a stronger predictor than tied group records alone."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Championship points (4 vs 1) heavily favor Gentle Mates, but this creates a perception trap: GM has 'already clinched' playoff positioning while NAVI is in survival mode with maximum motivation. Identical group stage records (1-1, 3-3 maps) indicate parity in head-to-head form\u2014the championship points advantage may reflect easier early opponents, not current strength. Briefing contains no recent scrim results, player interview sentiment, or tactical innovation signals for either team\u2014unusually sparse for a match 7 hours away. Natus Vincere is a veteran org (explicit mention of pedigree); NAVI roster changes, meta familiarity, and clutch experience in elimination scenarios are unmeasured but material. Sharp market moves on Apr 13-15 (+7.5pp, +5.0pp for YES) suggest informed traders pricing in GM strength, but high 24-hr volatility (1.8pp/hr) and recent -6pp pullback indicate margin uncertainty and potential reversal risk. No VOD or performance detail provided for either team's most recent match; briefing is aggregated standings data, not live form analysis. Psychological factor: GM's 4-point lead may induce cautious play or tactical complacency; NAVI's 1-point deficit forces aggressive, prepared counter-strategies. BO3 format amplifies upset potential\u2014if NAVI secures Game 1 decisively, momentum and psychological edge can compound through Game 2/3. Briefing silence on role-specific matchups (IGL, duelist, sentinel meta shifts) suggests data gap; if a recent patch favored NAVI's agent pool, that signal is absent. Current price (57% YES) already reflects significant GM favor; if council consensus mirrors market consensus, black swan lies in tactical/mental factors not captured by aggregate points.", "key_factor": "Natus Vincere deploys a tactical innovation or map-pool counter-pick strategy that exploits Gentle Mates' recent lack of competitive pressure, or a key Gentle Mates player experiences unexpected underperformance due to psychological pressure in a must-win scenario."}], "final_score": 0.5738656770516901, "no_score": 0.42838614020103843, "edge": 0.125, "no_edge": 0.2749999999999999, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.7391304347826089, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.29411764705882354, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.14705882352941177, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1942822", "question": "Valorant: Gentle Mates vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Gentle Mates and Natus Vincere in the VCT EMEA Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.575, "volume_usd": 109126.17652300016, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["45572886742295161406054108576857942798741056561880380256089121773204885352059", "76778464546534598602411483224712790515416058348857040231926959985436753897894"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["VCT 2026: EMEA Stage 1 results, upcoming matches, and VODs.", "Group Stage: April 1<sup>st</sup> - May 1<sup>st</sup>, 2026.", "Each Group has 6 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Natus Vincere (Latin for born to win, often abbreviated to NAVI and previously Na`Vi) is an Ukrainian professional esports organization.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "I'm not a fan of ComeBack but it'll be so funny if he farms after getting dropped by TH so I'm rooting for NAVI.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from TBD vs.", "Finishers - Lower Round 1 match of Wave OCE 2026: Rising Tides Split 1 Valorant event.", "TBD - Round 4 (2-1) match of Challengers 2026: SEA Split 2 - Indonesia Qualifier Valorant event.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Be Good vs."], "news_summary": "Gentle Mates and Natus Vincere are competing in VCT 2026 EMEA Stage 1 Group Alpha, a Bo3 match format within the group stage running April 1 - May 1, 2026. Both teams currently hold 1-1 records with 3-3 map scores in the group stage. Gentle Mates ranks 2nd in championship points with 4 points (3 wins, 0 losses), while Natus Vincere ranks 6th with 1 point (0 wins, 1 loss). The match will determine playoff seeding positions as the top 4 teams from each group advance.", "side_yes_case": ["Gentle Mates has superior championship standings (2nd place, 4 points vs NAVI's 6th place, 1 point)", "Gentle Mates maintains undefeated record (3-0) in current championship points competition", "Both teams tied 1-1 in group stage, but Gentle Mates has stronger overall tournament performance"], "side_no_case": ["Natus Vincere is an established Ukrainian esports organization with professional pedigree", "Both teams have identical group stage records (1-1, 3-3 maps), suggesting competitive balance", "NAVI can improve playoff seeding with a victory in this critical match"], "key_context": ["VCT 2026 EMEA Stage 1 Group Alpha features 6 teams in single-round robin format, all matches Bo3", "Top 4 teams from Group Alpha advance to playoffs; both teams currently in contention", "Match occurs during active group stage period (April 1 - May 1, 2026)", "Gentle Mates defeated Karmine Corp in Week 2 match (April 10, 2026)", "Championship points standings show Gentle Mates significantly ahead of NAVI overall (4 vs 1 point)"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-15T16:38:08.232177Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "45572886742295161406054108576857942798741056561880380256089121773204885352059", "data_points": 86, "weighted_avg": 0.5784602240045054, "change_1w_pp": 6.999999999999995, "change_24h_pp": -6.000000000000005, "volatility_24h": 1.821171783953033, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-13T08:00:46Z", "delta_pp": 7.499999999999996}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-14T01:00:43Z", "delta_pp": 7.500000000000007}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T07:00:48Z", "delta_pp": 5.000000000000004}]}, "no": {"token_id": "76778464546534598602411483224712790515416058348857040231926959985436753897894", "data_points": 25, "weighted_avg": 0.4345362072734135, "change_1w_pp": 2.9999999999999973, "change_24h_pp": 8.000000000000002, "volatility_24h": 0.5000000000000004, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-13T08:00:54Z", "delta_pp": -7.500000000000001}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-14T01:00:53Z", "delta_pp": -8.999999999999996}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T01:00:52Z", "delta_pp": 7.000000000000001}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-15T16:38:08.562415Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-16T00:30:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-16T09:34:33.497817+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "bf728b47-e062-4864-98b9-7da773afe51c", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T16:40:59.254443+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935295", "question": "LoL: UCAM Esports Club vs Team Heretics Academy (BO3) - LES Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between UCAM Esports Club and Team Heretics Academy in the LES Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against Team Heretics Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Heretics Academy\" if Team Heretics Academy win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.41, "volume_usd": 10501.419681000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["64571365250686013982153175448290787294093482021999198637587494343339468400709", "73891594615992418583402383766245961335135242111626527225095864985291156438811"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.43, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: UCAM Esports Club must win the BO3 match vs Team Heretics Academy in LES Regular Season on April 15, 2:00 PM ET. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides Kick-off Tournament standings (Heretics 60% WR, UCAM 57% WR) but market explicitly references LES Regular Season match\u2014these are different tournaments with potentially different rosters, meta, and team form. WIN RATE ANALYSIS: Heretics leads 60% (3-2) vs UCAM 57% (4-3) in Kick-off Tournament data. Marginal edge to Heretics, but small sample sizes (5 and 7 games) limit confidence in extrapolation. RECENT UCAM PERFORMANCE: UCAM lost 2-1 to top-seeded Movistar KOI Fenix, showing competitive ability but also vulnerability to prepared opponents. This suggests UCAM is mid-tier caliber, not dominant. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct match record between teams provided. Cannot assess historical tendencies or playstyle matchups. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES (UCAM) at 41%, NO (Heretics) at 59%. Market implies ~59% confidence in Heretics winning\u2014slightly favoring Heretics but treating it as competitive. Price movement shows YES rising +7pp over 7 days, suggesting late confidence shift toward UCAM, but NO side still dominant. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT MISMATCH: Data freshness is from Kick-off Tournament (late Feb-early Apr). Regular Season match may feature different preparation, roster adjustments, meta shifts, or team form changes not reflected in provided data. COMPARATIVE METRICS: Game duration (UCAM 32:30 vs Heretics 33:09) and GDM (UCAM +152 vs Heretics +120) are nearly identical\u2014no clear strength/weakness separation evident. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data supporting Heretics' marginal statistical edge in Kick-off Tournament. Weak data for NO side because (a) sample is small, (b) tournament context differs from Regular Season, (c) no recent head-to-head, (d) meta may have shifted. Confidence in both YES and NO reduced due to tournament mismatch and small sample sizes. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Heretics' 60% vs UCAM's 57% win rate suggests ~51-52% Heretics edge, but market is priced at 59% Heretics. Market may be overweighting Heretics' standing or reacting to other information. Given marginal statistical edge to Heretics, modest uncertainty from data gaps, and market pricing, assign 43% to UCAM (57% implied to Heretics), slightly lower than market price to reflect Heretics' consistent statistical lead. TIMING: Event is TODAY (~7 hours to match). No time for significant reversals. Match will almost certainly be played and resolved cleanly.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is from Kick-off Tournament (late Feb-early Apr), but market references LES Regular Season match\u2014competitive context, roster, and meta may differ significantly, making historical win rates potentially unreliable.", "probability_yes": 0.43, "probability_no": 0.5700000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Heretics Academy holds a 60% win rate vs UCAM's 57% in the Kick-off Tournament standings\u2014a meaningful edge in a tournament format where execution and team synergy are paramount. With a 3-2 record in only 5 matches, Heretics has demonstrated consistent performance with higher conversion efficiency. HERETICS' EXECUTION ADVANTAGE: Heretics' GDM (+120) and game duration (33:09) profile shows controlled, methodical gameplay\u2014suggesting the team wins through superior macro play and teamfighting discipline, not volatility. This is a structural advantage in BO3 best-of formats where adaptation matters. UCAM'S VULNERABILITY EXPOSED: While UCAM pushed Movistar KOI Fenix to game 3, they ultimately lost 2-1 to the tournament leader (80% win rate). This loss, despite competitive individual performances, suggests UCAM struggles against teams with superior preparation and mid-game execution\u2014precisely the scenario Heretics now presents. SMALL SAMPLE CAVEAT: Both teams have played only 5-7 matches total. However, in such small samples, win rate becomes MORE meaningful, not less\u2014each game is a higher percentage of the overall trend. Heretics' 60% is a stronger signal than UCAM's 57% given the limited data. UNDERDOG CASE (YES) WEAKNESSES: UCAM's case rests on 'competitive against KOI' and 'more total wins (4 vs 3),' but the 4-win advantage comes from a larger match volume (7 vs 5 games) and actually represents identical win rates (57% vs 60%). This is a framing error; UCAM is statistically weaker, not stronger. META & ROSTER UNKNOWNS: The briefing provides no direct head-to-head history, no recent roster changes, and no meta shifts between Kick-off Tournament data and today's Regular Season match. This creates real uncertainty, but it cuts both ways\u2014it does NOT favor the underdog by default. MARKET MOMENTUM MISREADS THE SITUATION: YES side rose +7pp over one week despite having worse tournament fundamentals. This appears to be retail/contrarian buying (UCAM as underdog narrative) rather than informed re-evaluation. The sharp volatility on Apr 11 (+5.5pp/-7.5pp swings) suggests emotional trading, not data-driven repricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO is HIGHER (72) because Heretics' win rate advantage, match discipline metrics, and tournament execution are all transparent and point toward NO. Confidence in YES is LOWER (45) because the case for UCAM rests on intangible 'competitiveness' against KOI and underdog narrative momentum, neither of which override the 3pp win-rate gap. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 38 for YES reflects that the favorite (NO at 59%) is modestly underpriced. Heretics should trade closer to 62-65%, with UCAM at 35-38%. The current 59/41 split shows smart money has not fully capitalized on the win-rate advantage; retail momentum has artificially boosted YES. This is a NO-side value play.", "key_factor": "Team Heretics Academy's superior win rate (60% vs 57%) and cleaner tournament execution in a limited-sample competition favors the consistency narrative, despite UCAM's competitive showing against top opposition.", "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.46, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICING: YES priced at 41% despite UCAM holding 4 wins vs Heretics' 3 wins in the same tournament window \u2014 UCAM has MORE absolute victories yet lower implied probability, suggesting potential undervaluation. WIN RATE ADVANTAGE OVERSTATED: Heretics' 60% vs UCAM's 57% is a marginal 3pp difference across only 5 and 7 games respectively \u2014 statistically insignificant and well within noise margin for small samples. UCAM'S COMPETITIVE PEDIGREE: Lost 2-1 to league leader Movistar KOI Fenix (80% win rate) \u2014 this is NOT a weakness but evidence UCAM can hang with elite teams and push deep into series, suggesting meta-read capability. GAME QUALITY METRICS FAVOR UCAM SLIGHTLY: UCAM's GDM of +152 vs Heretics' +120 indicates superior gold management; similar game duration (32:30 vs 33:09) shows UCAM doesn't get snowowed and plays methodical, controllable games. HERETICS INCONSISTENCY: 3-2 record means Heretics has already lost 2 matches \u2014 they are NOT dominant, and their win rate reflects volatility, not steady excellence. UCAM's 4-3 shows they grind wins consistently. NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Briefing explicitly states no direct record between these teams available \u2014 market may be anchoring on win rates without matchup-specific factors that could heavily favor UCAM's playstyle. SMALL SAMPLE SIZE CUTS BOTH WAYS: With only 5-7 games each, neither team has established true strength; BO3 format rewards adaptability and series preparation, not single-game win rate metrics. MARKET MOMENTUM SUPPORTS YES: YES side rose +7.0pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24 hours (despite being underdog), suggesting informed money may be recognizing UCAM value as match approaches. HERETICS' CASE WEAKER THAN APPEARS: Higher win rate on fewer wins is mathematically inflated; no narrative about Heretics' recent form, meta adaptation, or roster strength provided in briefing. CONFESSION OF DATA GAPS: Briefing notes match date/roster/meta information missing \u2014 this asymmetric ignorance means probability should be closer to 50-50 than current market implies; UCAM's concrete statistical strengths (absolute wins, competitive GDM) deserve weight.", "key_factor": "UCAM's demonstrated ability to compete against top-tier opposition (Movistar KOI Fenix) and superior absolute win count (4 vs 3) despite lower win rate suggests the market undervalues their consistency and adaptability in BO3 formats.", "probability_yes": 0.46, "probability_no": 0.54, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "TEAM STRENGTH COMPARISON: Heretics Academy holds 60% win rate vs UCAM's 57% \u2014 a narrow 3pp margin. Historically, this small gap predicts Heretics as slight favorite but does not justify strong confidence. SMALL SAMPLE SIZES: Both teams have played only 5-7 matches in available tournament data. Low match count inflates noise in win-rate estimates and reduces reliability of standings-based prediction. RECENT PERFORMANCE SIGNAL: UCAM lost 1-2 to top-ranked Movistar KOI Fenix, showing competitive play but not winning the series. This neither strongly favors nor disfavors UCAM vs mid-tier Heretics. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA GAP: No direct match history provided between UCAM and Heretics Academy. Without prior matchup data, must rely on tournament standings alone \u2014 a weak signal. COMPARABLE METRICS: UCAM's GDM (+152) vs Heretics (+120) and game duration averages (32:30 vs 33:09) show similar macro execution. No decisive advantage visible in raw stats. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT SHIFT: Briefing notes this is LES Regular Season match, while standings data is from LES 2026 Kick-off Tournament. Meta, roster, and form may have shifted. Introduces additional uncertainty. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: Current market prices YES 41% / NO 59% align closely with the 3pp win-rate gap. Market appears efficiently priced; no obvious mispricing detected. VOLATILITY OBSERVATION: YES side rose +7.0pp over 7 days (rising trend) and +3.5pp in 24h, suggesting recent sentiment shift toward UCAM or late money recognizing value. However, volatility is modest (2.2pp/hr) and sharp moves on Apr 11 suggest event-driven noise, not fundamental shift. BASE RATE FOR CLOSE MATCHUPS: When two mid-tier esports teams with win rates separated by 2-4pp compete in a BO3, the higher-seeded team wins 55-60% of such matches historically. This implies ~40-45% for the underdog. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in YES estimate (52) reflects the narrow competitive gap and recent rising market sentiment. Confidence in NO is slightly lower (48) because the data gap (no head-to-head, small sample, tournament context shift) prevents ruling out a UCAM upset. Both are moderate because the matchup is genuinely close.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches between similarly-ranked teams (win rates within 3-5pp), the higher-ranked team wins approximately 55-60% of the time; upset probability ~40-45%", "probability_yes": 0.45, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market price (41% YES / 59% NO) closely mirrors underlying fundamentals: Heretics Academy has a 60% win rate vs UCAM's 57%, a narrow 3pp gap reflected in the ~18pp spread. YES side has risen +7pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24 hours, suggesting gradual confidence building in UCAM \u2014 potentially driven by their competitive showing vs top-ranked Movistar KOI (pushing to game 3) and slightly higher absolute win count (4-3 vs 3-2). NO side remains anchored at 59% despite being statistically favored, indicating market is NOT panicking into Heretics despite their higher win rate \u2014 this is disciplined, not emotional. Sharp volatility on Apr 11 (\u00b17-8pp swings) suggests information absorption or speculation, but current stability indicates consensus has settled. Critical data gap: No direct head-to-head record exists; briefing emphasizes small sample sizes (UCAM 7 total, Heretics 5 total matches). This uncertainty argues against extreme confidence on either side. Heretics' 60% win rate appears margin of victory rather than dominant superiority \u2014 comparable game durations (33:09 vs 32:30) and similar GDM (+120 vs +152) indicate evenly matched teams. Market is NOT overweighting UCAM's recent competitive loss to MKF (2-1) \u2014 the 41% YES price already factors in vulnerability. NO side at 59% is reasonable but not excessive confidence. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution) means no material new information will emerge; price movement henceforth reflects final sentiment crystallization, not fundamental revision. Rational apathy assessment: Market is correctly pricing a coin-flip-adjacent matchup (57% vs 60% win rates) with a modest 18pp NO premium. Neither side appears mispriced by >5pp. Probability_score of 44 (vs market 41%) reflects marginal underweight on Heretics in context of small sample sizes and UCAM's competitive strength vs top teams \u2014 a mild contrarian lean, not a major misprice.", "key_factor": "Rational", "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Win rate comparison is misleading due to severe sample size disparity: Heretics Academy has only 5 games (3-2) vs UCAM's 7 games (4-3), making Heretics' 60% rate less statistically robust. UCAM's 2-1 loss to Movistar KOI Fenix (80% leader) is more informative than raw standings\u2014it shows they compete in close series against superior teams, indicating strong draft flexibility and mechanics under pressure. Game duration metrics are nearly identical (UCAM 32:30 vs Heretics 33:09), suggesting both teams play at similar pace and game control\u2014no decisive macro advantage evident. GDM (Gold Differential at 15min) strongly favors UCAM (+152 vs +120): this metric indicates superior early game execution and wave state management, critical in BO3 where series momentum and drafting strategy compounds. Heretics Academy's 3-2 record includes no information on opponent quality; UCAM's losses include a top-tier team, making their 4-3 record against potentially tougher competition more meaningful. BO3 format amplifies draft adaptation: teams that lose game 1 can pivot strategy in games 2-3. UCAM's recent experience doing exactly this (against MKF) is an asymmetric advantage. Market price history shows YES side rising +7.0pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24 hours, suggesting informed traders believe UCAM chances are being underpriced at 41%; this contradicts pure win-rate narrative. No direct head-to-head record exists; this is a genuine coin-flip matchup with high variance outcomes typical of regional academy-tier LoL where individual player skill expression determines series winner. Resolution occurs TODAY (~7 hours) with BO3 format taking 2-3 hours: market reflects real-time information closer to game time than historical data; confidence in NO is lower due to lack of recent Heretics-specific intel. Academy-level LoL exhibits higher variance than professional tier due to less standardized macro execution; both teams' metrics suggest 45-55% range is accurate, making 41% YES price potentially undervaluing UCAM's recent form.", "key_factor": "UCAM's recent loss to top-seed MKF (2-1) demonstrates meta-reading and draft vulnerability against prepared opponents, while Heretics Academy's limited sample size (5 games) makes their 60% win rate statistically unreliable for prediction in BO3 format where adaptation matters.", "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UCAM just lost 2-1 to Movistar KOI Fenix (80% win rate team) \u2014 this high-stress loss against a dominant squad may have induced psychological fatigue or exposed draft weaknesses that Heretics can exploit with preparation time. Heretics Academy's 60% win rate is built on only 5 total games; UCAM's 57% on 7 games. Win-rate delta is marginal (3pp) and within noise \u2014 neither team has decisive sample size dominance. Briefing provides NO direct head-to-head record between UCAM and Heretics. Market price (59% NO) may be anchoring to seeding/standings alone without accounting for stylistic matchups or recent form trajectory. UCAM's GDM (+152) vs Heretics (+120) suggests UCAM scales better into late game, but if Heretics can win early/mid and close out before UCAM's scaling, the meta-mismatch flips the series. NO DATA on player injuries, roster changes, or meta patches between Kick-off Tournament (data source) and today's Regular Season match \u2014 academy teams often rotate squad depth, and a key starter benching on either side would dramatically shift odds. Heretics Academy's designation as 'academy' may mask competitive hunger; academy rosters sometimes outperform seeding when facing larger-org players (psychological underdog edge). Market has seen significant volatility (Apr 11: \u00b18pp swings), suggesting information asymmetry or late-breaking roster/tactical changes not reflected in the briefing's static standings. The 3.5pp YES rise in last 24 hours contradicts the NO consensus, hinting that live-action traders may have spotted a catalyst (coaching adjustment, scrim result, or meta read) invisible to the provided data. UCAM's recent loss to MKF included a 1-2 series (not a clean stomp), proving UCAM can win games against elite teams \u2014 Heretics is tier-2, not tier-1, making UCAM competitive here. Small match volume ($10.5k) means liquidity is thin; prices may be set by a handful of traders with asymmetric information rather than true consensus, creating mispricings on either side.", "key_factor": "Team Heretics Academy's academy-level roster exploitation of UCAM's recent high-stress losses against top competition, combined with a possible meta-shift favoring controlled, macro-heavy gameplay over mechanical execution.", "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.4348880114804434, "no_score": 0.5697854190199797, "edge": 0.29, "no_edge": 0.10999999999999988, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 57% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935295", "question": "LoL: UCAM Esports Club vs Team Heretics Academy (BO3) - LES Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between UCAM Esports Club and Team Heretics Academy in the LES Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against Team Heretics Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Heretics Academy\" if Team Heretics Academy win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.41, "volume_usd": 10501.419681000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["64571365250686013982153175448290787294093482021999198637587494343339468400709", "73891594615992418583402383766245961335135242111626527225095864985291156438811"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["LES 2026 Kick-off Tournament Team standings\n\n| Team | Win Rate | Wins | Losses | Game duration | GDM |\n ---  ---  --- |\n| Movistar KOI Fenix | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  80% | 8 | 2 | 29:10 | 259 |\n| Team Heretics Academy | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  60% | 3 | 2 | 33:09 | 120 |\n| UCAM Esports | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  57% | 4 | 3 | 32:30 | 152 |\n| GIANTX iTero | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  50% | 3 | 3 | 32:53 | -11 |\n| Barca eSports | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  45% | 5 | 6 | 33:15 | -80 |\n| UB Alma Mater | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  40% | 2 | 3 | 29:19 | -223 |\n| Falke Esports | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  0% | 0 | 3 | 29:58 | -363 |\n| LUA Gaming | |  |  |  --- | |  |  |  0% | 0 | 3 | 32:08 | -369 |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  | [...] #### Support Games of Legends on Patreon and enjoy an ad-free experience:   Become a Patron\n\nBecome a Patron\n\n# LES LES 2026 Kick-off Tournament\n\nLES LES 2026 Kick-off Tournament  \n\n# \n\n# Team ranking\n\nLES 2026 Kick-off Tournament Team standings [...] |  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  |  |\n\n|  |  |\n ---