ET \u2248 TODAY in briefing timeline) means outcome will be determined within hours. No ambiguity in resolution criteria if match completes normally. gol.gg is specified as primary source with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting\u2014both are standard and reliable. INABILITY TO ASSESS BOTH SIDES: No roster strength data, recent win-loss records, head-to-head history, or meta compatibility information for either Winthrop or Supernova in League of Legends. Cannot differentiate win probability between competitors. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Market price (36/64) and volatile history suggest SOME traders have information. Absence of that data in this briefing means confidence in both YES and NO estimates must remain very low (\u226425). FINAL PROBABILITY: Aligning probability_score to current market midpoint (36%) acknowledges market consensus signal in absence of independent data validation. This is a passive calibration to market price, not a confident forecast.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no actionable intelligence on either team's LoL roster, recent form, head-to-head record, or competitive standing in NAC; team identities cannot be verified against official sources.", "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 64% (favored) vs YES at 36% (underdog). As the Bull advocate for the favored side, I am arguing Supernova wins this BO3. MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: The 7-day trend shows NO rising +15pp (strongest directional signal in the briefing), while YES has fallen -15pp. This represents a consistent shift in belief toward Supernova over the past week. PRICE STABILITY: NO side shows higher recent volatility (1.4pp/hr vs 0.6pp/hr for YES) but the net 7-day movement is unidirectional upward, suggesting informed traders are moving toward Supernova despite daily noise. SHARP MOVES INTERPRETATION: Apr 13's -18pp move on YES (followed by +18pp on NO) and Apr 14's oscillations suggest event-driven repricing. The most recent net shift from Apr 13\u201314 left NO higher, indicating the correction favored Supernova. DATA GAPS ARE SYMMETRIC: The briefing contains NO specific roster, recent win-loss records, or head-to-head history for either team. This symmetry means the market price differential (64% vs 36%) cannot be explained by public information in the briefing alone. IMPLICATION OF SYMMETRIC DATA GAP: When data is absent for both sides equally, the market price becomes the primary signal. The 28pp spread strongly suggests professional bettors or early information moved the line toward Supernova. WINTHROP DATA CONTAMINATION: Available Winthrop data is from Marvel Rivals (Georgia Tech Gold vs Winthrop 3:2 at Alienware Clash 2026), not League of Legends. This confirms the briefing has no clean LoL form data for either team. TIMING PRESSURE: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~9 hours). With no new public information breaking in the briefing, the market had ~7 days to price in team quality. The consistent drift toward NO suggests embedded information or scout reports favored Supernova. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS FRAMING: Winthrop (YES) has experienced a 15pp erosion of support over 7 days with no counter-catalyst listed in the briefing. Absence of bullish news for an underdog reinforces the market move. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 28 and confidence_no = 32 both remain LOW because the briefing contains zero actionable team data (rosters, head-to-head, recent LoL results). Neither side can be evaluated on merit. However, NO's confidence is marginally higher because 7-day price momentum is an observable market signal that points to Supernova, even if the underlying reason is opaque. BULL CASE FOR NO: The market has voted with its feet over a full week. Professional liability suggests this 64% price reflects either superior team strength in Supernova, recent roster changes favoring them, or scout feedback. The consistency of the +15pp trend (despite volatility) is the strongest evidence in an information vacuum. WHY NOT HIGHER FOR NO: The 28pp spread is justified partly by data scarcity. A BO3 can flip on execution, map pool, and draft. Winthrop is not priced below 36%, meaning the market retains ~1-in-3 belief they can take the series. Without roster details, I cannot dismiss Winthrop entirely. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: The 64-36 split with symmetric missing data suggests the line is stable and internalized by traders. No sharp moves in the last 4 hours (24-hour change: YES +4pp, NO -4pp) indicate the market has settled post-information-cascade.", "key_factor": "Market consensus and 7-day momentum favor NO (Supernova), with NO side rising +15pp over the week despite high volatility and insufficient team-level data.", "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero concrete League of Legends match results, roster information, or head-to-head records for either Winthrop or Supernova in the NAC. All available esports data references Marvel Rivals or different tournaments entirely. MARKET PRICING WITHOUT FOUNDATION: YES side has fallen 15pp over 7 days and NO has risen 15pp, yet the briefing provides NO evidentiary basis for this directional shift. This suggests the market is pricing based on speculation, hearsay, or off-chain consensus rather than published performance data. VOLATILE TRADING PATTERN: Sharp moves of \u00b118pp (Apr 13) and \u00b111.5pp (Apr 14) indicate high uncertainty and low conviction among traders. With $490 total volume and 9 hours to resolution, this is a thin, speculative market. WINTHROP'S HIDDEN CASE: Winthrop appears in esports results (Georgia Tech Gold match), indicating active competitive participation in collegiate circuit. If Winthrop has been competing in B-Tier and C-Tier tournaments recently with measurable results, there may be unpublished performance trends favoring them that market hasn't factored in. SUPERNOVA'S OPACITY: Supernova receives no mentions in the briefing data whatsoever. The absence of any results, roster info, or tournament history makes it impossible to assess their recent form, team stability, or competitive trajectory. Betting 64% on an entirely data-dark opponent is speculative. UNDERDOG VALUATION CHECK: At 36%, Winthrop is moderately underpriced if both teams are equally mysterious. A true coin-flip market with no predictive data would price at ~50%. The 14pp discount suggests market has real (off-chain) conviction toward Supernova, but that conviction is not substantiated in this briefing. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Best-of-3 reduces variance compared to single-game formats. If Winthrop has any structural matchup advantage (draft, playstyle, regional meta), a 3-game series gives more opportunity to exploit it than a one-off match. RECENCY & MOMENTUM: 24-hour movement favored YES (+4pp) while 7-day trend favored NO (-15pp). This divergence suggests recent information may have supported Winthrop, but earlier information (stale or speculative) had favored Supernova. Weigh recent micro-signals carefully. RESOLUTION RISK MITIGATION: Match is TODAY (9 hours). Forfeit/cancellation resolves to 50-50, but no evidence in briefing suggests this risk is elevated. Assume match plays as scheduled. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (28 and 26 respectively) because the briefing contains insufficient data on either team. We cannot reliably assess Winthrop's actual competitive strength or Supernova's weaknesses. The probability_score of 38 reflects a modest lean toward YES (underdog) based on market repricing volatility and data scarcity favoring the discount side, but this is a genuine data-starved call. 