onfident scoring on EITHER side. MARKET SIGNAL MISMATCH: YES has risen +8pp in 24hrs with sharp volatility (+22.5pp spike at 16:00 UTC, then -18.5pp reversal). This wild swing suggests either late information asymmetry (insiders know roster/meta changes not public) or momentum trading divorced from fundamental data. The +8pp rise could reflect leaked scrims or pre-match intel favoring Nemiga, but no briefing data confirms this. PLAYOFF PRESSURE WILDCARD: This is Upper Bracket Semifinal 2 (high stakes, single-elimination format). Teams already eliminated or through to next round (Group Stage vs win-or-go-home) exhibit radically different risk profiles and morale. Briefing is silent on both teams' qualification status and psychological momentum heading into today. INNER CIRCLE UNDERVALUATION VECTOR: Market prices YES at 56%, implying Nemiga is the consensus favorite. However, the briefing offers zero evidence of Nemiga's superiority. In the absence of contradictory data, an underdog in a BO3 playoff context (where tactical surprise and single-series variance loom large) retains a 40-50% win probability that may be underpriced if Inner Circle has a stylistic or draft edge the market has not yet priced. META / PATCH TIMING: No briefing info on recent Dota 2 patch notes or hero pool shifts. A meta swing favoring Inner Circle's core heroes (released buffs, nerfs to Nemiga's signature picks) could be the 5% asymmetric factor that flips the series. ROSTER STABILITY UNKNOWN: Neither team's current 5-player lineup, recent subs, or injury/visa status is mentioned. A last-minute stand-in or returning star player could shift win equity by 15-20pp, yet briefing is silent. CONFIDENCE PENALTIES JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=22 and confidence_no=21 reflect genuinely insufficient data to anchor either estimate. A 48% probability_score (near coin-flip) is appropriate when the briefing contains zero competitive intelligence on either competitor. This is not a 'default' cop-out\u2014it is the honest Bayesian posterior given a total absence of signal on both sides. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Match resolves in ~4 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT). No time for late-breaking news to shift the market significantly before tip-off. Sharp moves already occurred (16:00-16:46 UTC swings), suggesting insiders may have acted; public briefing lag is evident.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle executes a previously-unscouted tactical innovation (hero pick meta shift, position rotation, or map control strategy) that directly counters Nemiga's known draft tendencies, forcing a 2-0 or 2-1 upset in a high-stakes playoff environment.", "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror"}], "final_score": 0.536237283241746, "no_score": 0.4637203168269907, "edge": 0.1399999999999999, "no_edge": 0.26, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 26% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1985640", "question": "Dota 2: Nemiga Gaming vs Inner Circle (BO3) - European Pro League Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between Nemiga Gaming and Inner Circle in the European Pro League Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nemiga Gaming\" if Nemiga Gaming win the match against Inner Circle.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle\" if Inner Circle win the match against Nemiga Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.56, "volume_usd": 34486.276690000006, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["64996157495265813222774959762626665123611205878653128190351280381445059889395", "40287916404177610505401499643604319057733974249176123247582254646103180392398"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Dotabuff is t