{"run_id": "7ffe70fd-9bef-4ed7-93e6-9f47bfea2398", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T23:01:32.622189+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1990762", "question": "Counter-Strike: METANOIA WOLVES vs Vexa (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket round 2 match between METANOIA WOLVES and Vexa in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"METANOIA WOLVES\" if METANOIA WOLVES win the match against Vexa.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vexa\" if Vexa win the match against METANOIA WOLVES.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.79, "volume_usd": 2615.748906, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["37505387659319480940189877629580262092508310114179279092935454679857332119422", "27408669440450370215510042554562386958144496340404671070643343012099073293125"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: The match must complete with a winner determined (not canceled, tied, forfeited, or delayed beyond 7 days). Current market prices (YES 79%, NO 21%) reflect strong confidence in a decisive outcome. VEXA STRENGTHS: Demonstrated qualifying form with consecutive wins (13-10 vs Faith, 13-5 vs ALKA Gaming on Apr 4). Beat GameHunters 2-0 in ESL Challenger League on 22/03. Competitive pedigree established in South American circuit. METANOIA WOLVES CONTEXT: Listed as tournament participant but briefing lacks specific recent match results or performance metrics. News summary mentions forfeiture concern in BetBoom Storm #2, suggesting potential reliability/availability questions. However, no evidence of inability to compete in this specific event. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT: Sharp volatility on Apr 15 (22:00 UTC: -29.5pp; 23:00 UTC: +40.5pp) suggests real-time information flow or match result leakage. Current 79% YES price implies market-informed confidence in METANOIA WOLVES. This steep move suggests informational advantage rather than arbitrary drift. BO3 FORMAT vs QUALIFIER BO1: Vexa's qualifier wins were in BO1 format; lower bracket round 2 is BO3, increasing consistency demands. Single-elimination playoffs punish any map veto or preparation weakness. This is a material uncertainty not fully captured by qualifier performance alone. LACK OF HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No documented match history between these teams. Briefing contains GameHunters roster data and Vexa qualifier results but no direct competitive comparisons. This asymmetry limits confidence in either direction. TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE: Double-elimination bracket; this is lower bracket round 2, not upper bracket. Both teams are established enough to reach this stage. Vexa's qualification confirms tournament participation; METANOIA WOLVES' registration confirms participation. TIME-TO-REVERSAL ANALYSIS: Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to match start (scheduled 5:00 PM ET Apr 15, ~2026-04-15 21:00 UTC, resolution 2026-04-16 03:00 UTC). At this proximity, the 79%/21% split reflects near-final information state. Large reversals would require extraordinary circumstances (team no-show, technical disaster) \u2014 very unlikely at this stage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 62 (moderate \u2014 Vexa's qualifier wins and market signal are positive, but BO3 format introduces uncertainty and lack of head-to-head data limits conviction). confidence_no = 45 (lower \u2014 METANOIA WOLVES lacks documented recent performance and forfeiture concern exists, but team is tournament-registered and market signals weakness, not impossibility). The market's 79% YES reflects informed pricing; confidence_yes at 62 reflects data gaps preventing higher certainty. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org is primary source with 2-hour publication window fallback. Given match completion is imminent and high-stakes nature, reporting risk is minimal. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 78% YES reflects (i) strong market signal, (ii) Vexa's qualifying performance, (iii) time-proximity reducing reversal risk, (iv) moderated by lack of METANOIA WOLVES recent data and BO3 format uncertainty. 22% NO reflects non-zero probability of upset or competitive match under BO3 conditions.", "key_factor": "Match timing and result reporting risk is minimal given EVENT TIMING = TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution; primary uncertainty is lack of detailed head-to-head data and limited recent match history for METANOIA WOLVES in the briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.75, "probability_yes": 0.75, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "VEXA'S QUALIFYING MOMENTUM: Vexa won both Round 1 BO1 matches decisively (13-10 vs Faith, 13-5 vs ALKA), securing main event qualification. These scorelines indicate clean map control and round-by-round advantage. BO1 vs BO3 CONSIDERATION: While BO3 is more demanding, Vexa's decisive wins (not close 13-10 sweats) suggest structural map advantage, not luck. BO3 extends this advantage if Vexa controls vetoes and plays consistent CS. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: YES moved +11.5pp in 24h with sharp +40.5pp spike (Apr 15 23:00 UTC), suggesting informed traders saw Vexa's qualifier performance or internal tournament intel. The 79% current price reflects consensus confidence in Vexa. METANOIA WOLVES OPACITY: No recent match results provided in briefing. Tournament participant status confirms registration, but lack of documented recent form in CCT Challengers #1 is concerning vs. Vexa's documented Round 1 dominance. FORFEITURE SIGNAL AGAINST METANOIA: The briefing notes METANOIA reportedly forfeited a BetBoom Storm #2 match, raising questions about roster stability, internet reliability, or commitment during the concurrent tournament window (April 11-19). SOUTH AMERICAN CS2 CIRCUIT CONTEXT: Both teams play in the same regional ecosystem. Vexa's 13-5 blowout vs ALKA (a regional competitor) and 13-10 vs Faith indicate Vexa can execute fundamentals at tournament tempo. UNDERDOG'S PATH: NO (Vexa loss) requires METANOIA to overcome a team that just beat two opponents decisively in playoff-style BO1s. Without evidence of METANOIA's recent form or head-to-head history, betting against the demonstrated qualifier winner is speculative. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence is 72 because Vexa's qualifier wins are tangible, recent, and in the same tournament. NO confidence is only 35 because METANOIA's case rests on absence of data (no documented recent losses) rather than positive evidence of strength. VOLATILITY NOTE: 24h volatility of 20.4pp (YES) and 29.0pp (NO) with -29.5pp/+40.5pp swings suggests retail uncertainty and possible information asymmetry. Informed traders may have seen METANOIA roster issues or internal odds shifting toward Vexa. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~4 hours to resolution). For 79% favorite to lose requires METANOIA to execute a high-level comeback with minimal time for narrative shift. Sharp reversals at this stage are rare absent match-fixing concerns (low probability). PRIZE POOL CONTEXT: $2,500 C-Tier tournament. Vexa's Round 1 wins put them on track for main event (1st-4th place) prize qualification. METANOIA's path is unclear without documented performance.", "key_factor": "Vexa's decisive Round 1 qualifier performances (13-10, 13-5) demonstrate superior firepower and map control in this tournament's South American competitive environment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "VEXA'S QUALIFYING STRENGTH IS REAL BUT LIMITED: Vexa won two BO1 qualifier matches decisively (13-10 vs Faith, 13-5 vs ALKA Gaming), demonstrating sharp form. However, these are single-map matches against open qualifier opponents\u2014a fundamentally different test than BO3 playoff play. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE UNCLEAR FOR VEXA: The briefing notes Vexa's qualifier wins were BO1; the playoff match is BO3. BO3 requires map pool consistency, tactical adaptation across multiple games, and stamina. Qualifier momentum does not guarantee BO3 success. No data shows Vexa's BO3 record or map-pool depth. METANOIA WOLVES' PARTICIPATION PROFILE: METANOIA WOLVES is registered as a CCT South America tournament participant with a listed roster. The briefing confirms their establishment in the competitive circuit, though recent match results are sparse. This suggests organizational stability, not fragility. FORFEITURE CLAIM LACKS CONTEXT: The briefing mentions METANOIA WOLVES 'reportedly forfeited a BetBoom Storm #2 match.' Without date, opponent, or circumstantial detail, this is weak evidence of systemic issues. A single forfeit in an unrelated tournament does not predict playoff performance. MARKET PRICING SUGGESTS OVERCONFIDENCE IN VEXA: YES is priced at 79%, heavily favoring Vexa despite the absence of BO3 data, head-to-head records, or playoff history. The sharp +40.5pp move in YES in the 24 hours before match time suggests late money on Vexa without fresh fundamental data\u2014potentially reactive trading rather than informed positioning. VOLATILITY SPIKE INDICATES UNCERTAINTY: The 24-hour volatility of 29pp on the NO side and sharp reversals (-41pp, then +40.5pp) suggest genuine uncertainty in the market. This contradicts the 79% consensus\u2014if Vexa's edge were as solid as the price implies, volatility should be lower and directional. TOURNAMENT TIER AND PRIZE POOL: This is a C-Tier, $2,500 prize pool online event. Both teams are competing at comparable levels; neither has a prestige advantage. Vexa's qualifier success is within a weak field (Faith, ALKA Gaming); METANOIA WOLVES' historical participation does not guarantee playoff underperformance. NO DIRECT MATCHUP DATA: Zero head-to-head records, map preferences, or roster overlap analysis is available. Without this, assigning 79% to Vexa is speculative. METANOIA WOLVES' true strength is not documented but also not refuted. UNDERDOG CASE SUMMARY: METANOIA WOLVES is priced as a 21% underdog despite being an established tournament participant. Vexa's qualifier wins, while impressive, are not playoff-tested. The BO3 format is a major escalation in difficulty from Vexa's BO1 path. The market may be extrapolating qualifier form too aggressively without accounting for format risk. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in the NO case (58) because Vexa's qualifier form is documented and the BO3 escalation risk is real. Lower confidence in the YES case (32) because METANOIA WOLVES' recent form is nearly absent from the briefing, making it harder to build a strong affirmative case. Leaving 4pp ignorance mass (28 + 68 = 96) reflects this asymmetry\u2014neither side has complete data.", "key_factor": "METANOIA WOLVES' established tournament participation history and BO3 resilience may overcome Vexa's qualifier-stage momentum, which has not yet been tested in the more demanding playoff format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "VEXA EVIDENCE (supports YES): Vexa demonstrated decisive Round 1 qualifier wins (13-10 vs Faith, 13-5 vs ALKA Gaming), showing map control and team cohesion in online play. VEXA EVIDENCE (supports YES): Qualifying wins in BO1 format against tournament participants indicate competitive baseline and preparation for main event. METANOIA WOLVES EVIDENCE (supports NO): Tournament briefing lists METANOIA WOLVES as registered participant with established roster, indicating legitimacy and prior competitive experience in CCT circuit. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Vexa's qualifier wins were BO1 (single map). BO3 requires strategic depth, map-pool versatility, and consistency across 2-3 maps\u2014performance does not always transfer. Historical BO3 upset rate in lower brackets is ~30-35%. DATA GAP - METANOIA WOLVES: Briefing provides almost no recent match history for METANOIA WOLVES. One mention of a forfeited BetBoom Storm #2 match raises availability concerns, but sample size is n=1 and context (date, round, importance) is unclear. DATA GAP - HEAD-TO-HEAD: No documented prior matches between these teams. Cannot anchor on historical H2H patterns. MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price of 79% is ~9pp above base-rate expectation (~70%) for a qualifier-winner vs. tournament participant in BO3 lower bracket. This modest premium suggests slight overconfidence in Vexa, but not extreme mispricing. VOLATILITY NOTE: 24-hour volatility of 20.4pp (YES) and 29.0pp (NO) reflects uncertainty typical of C-Tier matches with thin information sets. Sharp moves (\u00b129.5pp to \u00b141pp) suggest marginal new information or late bets, not definitive signal. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event resolves TODAY (~4 hours). No time for major reversals; market is pricing based on available roster/qualifier data. Likelihood of late forfeiture or disqualification is low (<5%), so 50-50 tie resolution risk is minimal. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Confidence in YES (38) reflects moderate conviction in Vexa's qualifier edge, but tempered by BO3 format switch and lack of Vexa playoff match data in this specific tournament. Confidence in NO (32) reflects genuine data sparsity on METANOIA WOLVES\u2014their recent record, form, and roster stability are not documented, creating meaningful ignorance mass (72 + 28 = 100, but either could shift \u00b115pp with additional context).", "key_factor": "In CS2 lower-bracket playoff BO3 matches at C-Tier tournaments, the team with stronger recent qualifier performance wins ~65-70% of the time; however, single-elimination volatility and map diversity in BO3 introduces significant uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market has risen 11.5pp in 24h to 79% YES, driven by Vexa's qualifying form (13-10 vs Faith, 13-5 vs ALKA). Sharp volatility spike (\u00b140pp on Apr 15 23:00 UTC) suggests emotional repricing rather than new hard data. Crowd enthusiasm appears overheated: Vexa won BO1 qualifier matches, but BO3 playoff format is structurally different and demands sustained play across 3 maps. METANOIA WOLVES identity and recent form are obscured in briefing\u2014no direct playoff match data provided, creating information asymmetry. Reported METANOIA forfeit in a different tournament (BetBoom Storm #2) is weak evidence of reliability issues; does not directly predict playoff performance. Vexa's qualifier wins were against lower-tier opponents (Faith, ALKA); no head-to-head record vs METANOIA documented. YES price at 79% implies ~4:1 odds; at 4-hour timeframe with minimal new catalyst, this is vulnerable to a NO reversal if METANOIA shows up prepared. Low volume ($2,616 USD) and high volatility suggest thin liquidity and crowd-driven emotional moves, not institutional conviction. Greed bias: market has likely overweighted Vexa's recent qualifying momentum and underweighted the structural difficulty of BO3 competition. NO side (21%) is compressed and neglected\u2014typical of a crowded one-sided trade. If METANOIA performs competitively or takes early maps, sharp reversal likely. Confidence asymmetry: strong YES signal (Vexa qualifiers), weak NO signal (METANOIA opacity). Leaving ~55pp ignorance mass reflects data gap on METANOIA's playoff readiness.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET TIMING RISK: Event resolves in ~4 hours (TODAY). The extreme 24h volatility (+40.5pp swing in YES, -41pp in NO within 1 hour on Apr 15 23:00 UTC) suggests late-breaking information (team roster confirmation, player availability, stream start data) rather than fundamental repricing. Sharp moves this close to event start typically correlate with concrete match-day intel (lineup confirmations, warm-up scrim results, or technical issues). BO1 VS BO3 FORMAT MISMATCH: Vexa's qualifier credentials (13-10 vs Faith, 13-5 vs ALKA) are BO1 performances. BO1 is high-variance, map-dependent; BO3 requires map veto strategy, mid-series adaptation, and roster consistency across 3+ maps. Briefing provides zero BO3 match history for either team in this tournament\u2014cannot assess their depth or map pool. ROSTER/AVAILABILITY AMBIGUITY: Briefing lists 'GameHunters' roster data (bsd, Lich, pedrinzy, etc.) but these players are NOT clearly linked to METANOIA WOLVES or Vexa by name in the document. The note about METANOIA WOLVES forfeiting a BetBoom match suggests potential roster churn or availability constraints, but timing and cause are unclear. NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Briefing explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head records between these teams are documented.' This eliminates the strongest predictor in esports matchups (team-specific meta, coach read, player psychology). Must rely on tournament bracket inference only. BRACKET POSITION UNKNOWN: Briefing does not specify whether this is a lower-bracket round 2 match (as market question implies) or upper-bracket placement. If METANOIA WOLVES is already in lower bracket, they may have lost to stronger opposition earlier\u2014a negative signal. If they're upper-bracket, the inverse applies. VEXA'S QUALIFIER TRAJECTORY POSITIVE BUT NOISY: Beating Faith and ALKA Gaming in BO1s shows competence in South American C-Tier circuit, but both opponents appear to be mid-tier teams (Faith placed 5-8, ALKA placed 5-8 in prize pool structure). No indication Vexa faced top-seed teams. MARKET PRICE ASYMMETRY: YES at 79% is a strong favorite. This reflects either (a) late information favoring METANOIA WOLVES, or (b) public perception skew. Low volume ($2,616 total) means small order imbalances can swing percentages sharply. Confidence in YES is moderate (42) because the data supporting it is thin. RESOLUTION CRITERIA FORFEIT RISK: Matches that end in forfeit/disqualification resolve 50-50. With ~4 hours to match start, technical issues, roster disputes, or no-shows remain possible in online South American events. This adds tail-risk symmetry not captured by the 79/21 split. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Confidence_yes (42) < confidence_no (35) because both sides are underdetermined. Briefing provides Vexa's BO1 qualifier results (concrete but format-mismatched) but zero playoff data for either team. The sharp late-market move suggests informed traders have real-time intel (stream start, roster roster confirmation) that the briefing cannot capture. This information advantage should reduce confidence in any historical analysis.", "key_factor": "Vexa's qualifier wins were BO1 (single-map, high variance), but this playoff match is BO3 (three-map, requires map pool consistency and tactical adaptation)\u2014a significant format escalation that nullifies much of the signal from their open-qualifier performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.31, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market has spiked 40.5pp in the last 2 hours (Apr 15 23:00 UTC), suggesting NEW INFORMATION not in briefing\u2014likely roster confirmation, scrim results, or official match start signal. This recency and volatility indicate institutional knowledge favoring YES, but extreme swings also signal uncertainty. Vexa's qualifier wins (13-10 Nuke, 13-5 Dust II) are map-specific BO1 performances, NOT validated across full BO3 rotation. Nuke and Dust II are narrow map pools; Vexa may lack Inferno/Overpass/Mirage/Ancient/Anubis consistency. METANOIA WOLVES identity is opaque in briefing\u2014no recent match record provided, but tournament listing confirms registered roster. Absence of data is NOT evidence of weakness; could indicate they've been seeded higher or operate outside public qualifier visibility. Forfeit on BetBoom Storm #2 (mentioned for WOLVES) is dated ~1 week ago; insufficient signal for current form. CCT Challengers is a distinct event; teams may have rotated or prioritized this event. BO3 format heavily favors preparation and map flexibility. Vexa's qualifier success relied on 2-3 standout map performances; if METANOIA has researched Vexa's tendencies, they can ban/counter-pick strategically. No head-to-head history means tactical matchup is entirely unknown. Vexa is unproven against upper-bracket caliber opponents; METANOIA's lack of documented losses could also indicate earlier-round exits OR careful scheduling. Tournament is LIVE/IMMINENT (4 hours to resolution). Sharp swing from 55% YES \u2192 79% YES in 2 hours suggests late-breaking lineup confirmation or scrim leak favoring METANOIA or disfavoring Vexa. Market is pricing in real-time information. Low volume ($2,616 total) means thin liquidity; price movements can be driven by a few large bets from insiders (team scouts, analysts with tournament access) rather than aggregate wisdom. Vexa's 13-5 rout of ALKA on Dust II was dominant, but ALKA is an academy-tier team. METANOIA WOLVES tournament seeding/bracket placement unknown\u2014could be significantly higher-caliber opponent. NO-side confidence is LOW (45%) because briefing provides almost NO defensive data on Vexa's macro game, anti-strat capabilities, or full-roster consistency. We're betting against Vexa based on sparse evidence, not strong counter-signal.", "key_factor": "METANOIA WOLVES fields a substitute or demonstrates tactical adaptation to Vexa's qualifying-phase meta (BO1 Nuke/Dust II wins), negating Vexa's form advantage in a BO3 requiring map pool flexibility."}], "final_score": 0.7085583140550945, "no_score": 0.33226204712359736, "edge": -0.08411764705882352, "no_edge": 0.4958