lication, or (b) cancellation/delay announced. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Criteria specify HLTV.org as primary source, with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. Given timing (~6 hours to resolution), official results should be published well before deadline. MARKET PRICE AS PROXY: In absence of team performance data, market prices (29% YES / 71% NO) reflect aggregate trader belief. The sharp recent reversal from ~50% YES to 29% YES within 24 hours is the only signal available and suggests strong evidence favoring Banger Gang or against Clutchain Female. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Briefing lacks data to evaluate Clutchain Female's strength (confidence_yes = 22) AND lacks data to evaluate Banger Gang's strength (confidence_no = 23). Confidence scores are both very low because substantive information on EITHER side is absent. Market price movement is used only as a weak signal, not as evidence. GENDER/TIER CONTEXT: Female-focused CS teams in lower-tier ESEA Advanced leagues typically have minimal media coverage, making pre-match assessment inherently difficult. This is structural, not a gap that can be filled. OUTCOME CONDITION CLARITY: Resolution criteria are unambiguous regarding what constitutes a win (match completion with winner determined). No edge-case risk identified in criteria text. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT: probability_score set to 29 (matching current market YES price) as best available estimate given complete data absence. probability_no_score set to 71 (matching market NO price). These reflect market consensus only, not independent analysis.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on team strength, recent form, or head-to-head history; market price movement (sharp -21.5pp drop for YES in last 6 hours) may reflect recent match outcome or insider information not captured in briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationa