 in a BO5. This suggests competitive capability, though the timing is 3+ months old. KT CHALLENGERS FORM: KT's 2-1 win over Nongshim in Jan 2026 and implied consistency in BO3s form a slight edge. However, no recent BO3 data for KT Challengers specifically is provided in the briefing. DATA FRESHNESS & AMBIGUITY: The briefing is timestamped April 15, 2026 17:45 UTC, yet contains match results from January\u2013April 2026 across different tournament phases (Kickoff, regular season, playoffs). It is unclear whether Rounds 1-2 is a new phase or a repeat/rematch structure. The fragmented nature reduces confidence in both directions. MARKET PRICING: YES = 63% (KT Nongshim win favored). This suggests market believes Nongshim will win. Probabilities are inverted: to bet on KT, one buys NO at 37%. Market has risen +13pp over 7 days, indicating growing confidence in a Nongshim victory, likely reflecting recent form or news not fully captured in the briefing. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Without clear recent team form data for the Academy squads and given only a 3-month-old H2H in KT's favor, plus market pricing favoring Nongshim and rising trends, a neutral-to-slight-NO lean is justified. KT's head-to-head edge is meaningful but not determinative. Assigning 38% to YES (Nongshim) implies 62% to NO (KT). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES is modest (45) because the H2H favors the opposite and recent data is sparse for Academy rosters. Confidence in NO is slightly higher (52) because the Jan 2026 H2H and main team form data support KT, though the Academy-level form uncertainty still limits high confidence. Neither side has overwhelming support.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains fragmented and temporally inconsistent data (references to January 2026 matches, April 2026 main LCK results, and unclear chronology), creating ambiguity about team form and the exact stage of the Rounds 1-2 matches; resolution mechanism itself is clear but underlying match context is murky."}, {"agent_n