ta shifts that could reverse the Jan 22 result. Confidence in NO is moderately high due to H2H, but uncertainty about Nongshim's current strength (unpriced improvements) lowers NO confidence below 70. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~17 hours). No new significant information can emerge to overturn the established H2H trend in such a short window. BULL CASE FOR YES (CONTRARIAN): If Nongshim has added roster talent or strategic depth since January, they could upset KT. The briefing provides no evidence of such changes, making this a speculative case.", "key_factor": "KT Rolster Challengers' recent 2-1 head-to-head victory over Nongshim (Jan 22, 2026) and consistent BO3 performance in the current LCK CL season establish them as the stronger team in direct matchups."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.5800000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing conflates two distinct entities \u2014 Nongshim Esports Academy (CL team) vs. Nongshim RedForce (main LCK team). Most recent performance data (April 2-11) refers to RedForce (0-2 vs KT, 0-2 vs DRX in S-Tier LCK 2026), NOT Academy. Academy's most recent CL match data is from Feb 2026 playoffs, ~2.5 months old. HEAD-TO-HEAD: KT Rolster Challengers defeated Nongshim Esports Academy 2-1 on Jan 22, 2026 (LCK CL Kickoff). This is the only direct comparison available. Typical BO3 advantage from recent H2H in academy circuits: ~60-65% for the prior winner, but confidence is moderate due to roster turnover risk in 2+ month gap. NONGSHIM ACADEMY STRENGTH: Defeated Dplus KIA 2-0 (Jan 16, 2026, Week 1) and advanced to Playoffs Round 1, beating HLE Challengers 2-3 (Feb 9). This shows capability, but timeline places all data pre-March. No April performance data for Academy team. KT ROLSTER CHALLENGERS STRENGTH: Won Jan 22 H2H 2-1; also defeated Gen.G Global Academy 1-2 (Jan 19), KRX/DRX 0-2 (Jan 16). Recent performance is absent; KT Challengers matches post-Jan are not in briefing. Cannot assess current roster strength. MARKET SIGNAL: YES at 63% implies confidence in Nongshim Academy. This contradicts the Jan 22 H2H loss. Sharp moves on Apr 11-13 (+12.5pp YES, then -7.5pp) suggest breaking news or uncertainty, but no news event is detailed in briefing\u2014only scheduled match. TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE: 'Rounds 1-2' language is ambiguous. Briefing shows regular season (WEEK1, WEEK2 in Jan) and playoffs (Feb). No clarity on whether April 16 match is a rematch in new round-robin or playoff context. Seasonal reset could alter team composition. BASE RATE CONSIDERATION: Academy/Challenger BO3 matches with 2+ month gap between H2H and rematch show ~48-52% volatility around the prior winner's rate. Prior winner (KT, 2-1) would anchor ~60%, but uncertainty around roster changes and match context depresses confidence sharply. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong historical H2H favors KT (Jan 22, 2-1), but no recent data on either team's current roster or form. Nongshim's playoff advancement (Feb) is outdated. KT's recent performance is entirely absent. This creates equal ignorance on both sides. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Market price of 63% YES reflects a ~2.3:1 odds spread favoring Nongshim Academy. This conflicts with the Jan 22 H2H victory for KT. Without intervening data (March-April performance, roster updates, meta shifts), I anchor to the H2H (KT favored ~60%) but apply significant regression toward 50% due to time gap and missing information. Result: ~42% YES (58% NO implied).", "key_factor": "LCK Challengers League BO3 matches show ~50-55% win rate for teams favored by recent head-to-head; however, academy/challenger circuit volatility is high (~\u00b115pp) due to roster fluidity and limited match history"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market currently prices YES (Nongshim) at 63%, but briefing shows KT won the direct H2H 2-1 on Jan 22, 2026 \u2014 this is a concrete data point favoring the NO side. YES side has rallied +13pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 11-12; this suggests crowd enthusiasm for Nongshim, possibly driven by recency bias or narrative hype rather than hard evidence. NO side (KT) has been systematically sold off (-13pp / 7d), creating potential value if the H2H precedent and KT's demonstrated BO3 consistency hold. Briefing contains fragmented team roster/performance data (Nongshim RedForce vs Nongshim Esports Academy naming confusion; mixed LCK vs LCK CL match results). This ambiguity limits confidence in both directions. Nongshim's playoff advancement is noted, but occurred in Feb 2026; current April matchup is a new stage in the season. Previous success does not guarantee current form. KT's recent LCK main team form (0-2 losses to Nongshim RedForce and DRX) could indicate the parent org/challenger org is under pressure; unclear if this bleeds into Challengers roster performance. Low volume ($292 USD) and tight spread (63/37) suggest thinly traded market with few informed traders; crowd may be overweighting Nongshim narrative. Time-to-reversal: Event is TODAY (~17h). Any new roster info, injury, or scrim results would have emerged by now. Market is close to resolution; large swings imply sentiment-driven repricing rather than fundamental news. Inverting the market: If NO (KT) wins, the 63/37 pricing creates significant profit for contrarian NO holders; if YES wins, the crowd gets a modest confirmation. Asymmetric payoff structure favors underdogs (KT) in thin markets. Probability_score set to 38 to reflect: (1) KT's documented H2H win, (2) crowd overweighting Nongshim, (3) low data quality on current roster form. Confidence_no > confidence_yes due to concrete H2H fact vs. softer narrative for YES.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.5, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA ISSUE: Briefing mixes Nongshim RedForce (main LCK roster, 0-2 losses to DRX/KT on Apr 11 & 9) with Nongshim Esports Academy (CL developmental team). These are distinct entities with different player pools, coaching, and competitive level. HEAD-TO-HEAD ANCHOR: KT Rolster Challengers defeated Nongshim Esports Academy 2-1 on Jan 22, 2026 (LCK CL Kickoff). This is the only direct H2H data for the academy-level teams. ~3 months have elapsed; roster/meta shifts are material in LoL. NONGSHIM ACADEMY RECORD (Jan-Feb 2026): Won 2-0 vs Dplus KIA (Week 1), won 2-0 vs BRION (Week 1), won 2-3 vs HLE in Playoffs R1 (Feb 9). Showed upward trajectory post-Kickoff, suggesting adaptation/improvement since Jan 22 loss to KT. KT CHALLENGERS RECORD (Jan-Feb 2026): Wins include 2-1 vs Gen.G GA (Jan 19), 2-0 vs DRX (Jan 16), 2-1 vs Nongshim (Jan 22). Consistent performer in Kickoff/early season. APRIL 2026 META: No team-specific performance data provided for April. Briefing is dated Apr 15 17:45 UTC but contains no April match results for either Nongshim Academy or KT Challengers. Unable to assess current form. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES (Nongshim) at 63% implies marginal market confidence. Sharp moves on Apr 11-12 (+12.5pp YES, -12.5pp NO) suggest sentiment shift ~4 days ago, but no corresponding match result in briefing. Possible external news or betting flow, not backed by resolved match data. VOLATILITY & VOLUME: Low volume ($292 USD), 1.0-1.1pp/hr volatility. Thin market suggests low liquidity and potential for mispricing; confidence in either direction must be modest. TIMING: Event is TODAY (resolves ~17 hours from data timestamp). No time for new information to materially change team compositions, though meta/draft prep is complete by this stage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes (45) lower than confidence_no (50) because YES case relies on single Jan H2H win by KT, with no April validation. NO case (KT wins) is supported by same H2H but lacks evidence of Nongshim's recent April form. Both sides suffer from missing current-season performance data. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: KT's Jan H2H victory + consistent Kickoff record marginally favors KT in a coin-flip scenario. Nongshim's playoff advancement suggests competitive tier, but Jan loss to KT is most recent direct evidence. Outputting 38 (YES) / 62 (NO) reflects slight KT edge with high uncertainty. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is BO3, not forfeit/cancel risk high. Market should resolve cleanly within 2 hours per resolution criteria.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains severe data contamination: it conflates LCK Challengers League (academy/developmental) with LCK main league and Nongshim RedForce (main roster), making reliable team strength assessment impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing conflates Nongshim Esports Academy (academy/CL team) with Nongshim RedForce (main LCK roster). Recent stats shown (RedForce's 0-2 vs DRX, 0-2 vs KT, 2-0 vs DNS) are from the main LCK lineup in April 2026, NOT the Academy squad playing in CL Rounds 1-2. This is a foundational misdirection. TEMPORAL MISMATCH: The only direct H2H cited (KT 2-1 NS) is from Jan 22, 2026 Kickoff. Rounds 1-2 occurs April 16, 2026 \u2014 a 3-month gap. Academy rosters are fluid; player promotions, substitutions, and meta shifts are routine in CL. SPARSE ACADEMY DATA: The briefing provides minimal recent match history for Nongshim Esports Academy specifically. The playoff advancement claim (Feb 9, NS 3-2 HLE) is the most recent firm CL result, but no April-specific form trajectory is visible for the Academy side. KT CONSISTENCY ILLUSION: KT's 2-1 Kickoff win is strong, but KT's recent main-roster form vs Nongshim RedForce (0-2 LCK on Apr 9) suggests KT may be slumping or facing meta misalignment. If KT's Academy mirrors the main roster's downturn, the Jan advantage evaporates. COACHING CONTINUITY UNKNOWN: Nagne (HLE Challengers head coach 2022-24) joined T1 Esports Academy in Nov 2025. No explicit coaching staff data for NS Academy in April 2026; if there was a coaching change or interim situation post-Kickoff, it could dramatically shift preparation quality and in-game execution. META/PATCH SHIFTS: LCK CL operates on the same patch as main LCK. If a significant patch landed between Jan and Apr (highly likely in a 3-month span), champion pool resets, itemization changes, and macro adjustments favor teams with deeper flexibility. Academy roster turbulence often reveals itself in inability to adapt to meta pivots. MARKET RISE MOMENTUM DRIVEN BY UNINFORMED FLOW: YES side has risen 13pp over 7 days with sharp +12.5pp spike on Apr 11. This timing (day before match) suggests late-arriving volume from casual bettors anchoring to the Jan H2H without accounting for roster/meta evolution. Professionals would have updated their model weeks ago. MORALE/MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: Nongshim Academy's playoff advancement (Feb 9) signals organizational investment and rising confidence. KT Academy, despite Jan Kickoff win, may lack narrative momentum if the main team is struggling (0-2 this week to DRX/NS RedForce). BO3 FORMAT FAVORS UNDERDOG ADAPTATION: Nongshim, if roster-adjusted, has 2+ games to exploit unprepared KT defaults. KT, relying on stale Jan game plans, risks losing early map control and having no pivot strategy mid-series. VOLUME TOO LOW TO SIGNAL CONFIDENCE: $292 USD volume is microscopic for a BO3 match. Market lacks professional price discovery; the 63/37 split reflects casual betting noise, not sharp consensus. Black swan probability materially underpriced.", "key_factor": "Nongshim Esports Academy roster or coaching adjustment (player substitution, mid-match lineup swap, or tactical overhaul by interim staff) implemented between the January kickoff and April Rounds 1-2, creating a fundamentally different team dynamic that KT has no recent film on."}], "final_score": 0.40102072550682144, "no_score": 0.6015061552053805, "edge": 0.06999999999999995, "no_edge": 0.32999999999999996, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 60% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 49% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935142", "question": "LoL: Nongshim Esports Academy vs KT Rolster Challengers (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Nongshim Esports Academy and KT Rolster Challengers in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 16 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim Esports Academy\" if Nongshim Esports Academy win the match against KT Rolster Challengers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"KT Rolster Challengers\" if KT Rolster Challengers win the match against Nongshim Esports Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's for