{"run_id": "5fb07f9c-e94b-43b6-8a71-6cbd550769ac", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T17:49:32.661096+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935165", "question": "LoL: Hanwha Life Esports Challengers vs Gen.G Global Academy (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Hanwha Life Esports Challengers and Gen.G Global Academy in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 16 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Hanwha Life Esports Challengers\" if Hanwha Life Esports Challengers win the match against Gen.G Global Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gen.G Global Academy\" if Gen.G Global Academy win the match against Hanwha Life Esports Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T11:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T05:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.725, "volume_usd": 2286.5267230000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["35613843576585728475052139353127855419846230621169769985708564247860143237220", "102431159405558195564259079811403386059994438254414626686020573469177054341003"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CONDITION: Hanwha Life Esports Challengers defeats Gen.G Global Academy in a BO3 match, scheduled April 16 at 1:00 AM ET (TODAY, ~17 hours away). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing conflates main LCK standings (Hanwha Life Esports 3-1, 2nd place) with Challengers League performance. No explicit Hanwha Life Esports Challengers roster record provided. Gen.G Global Academy record stated as 1-4 with -3 differential, but context unclear (CL vs main league). CASE FOR YES (probability 62): - Gen.G Global Academy explicitly shown as 1-4 in LCK CL with -3 differential (weaker record if accurate) - Academy/Challengers teams typically feature younger/less proven talent than main rosters - Hanwha institutional presence and 3-1 main roster form suggests competitive org infrastructure - Current market price 72% YES reflects trader confidence, though with high volatility (+22.5pp 7-day swing) CASE FOR NO (probability 38): - Gen.G organization historically strong; academy rosters can punch above weight with focused preparation - No explicit Hanwha Life Esports Challengers roster record in briefing \u2014 main team record may not transfer to CL - BO3 is single match; Rounds 1-2 standings do not guarantee head-to-head outcomes - Sharp price volatility (\u00b126pp swings Apr 11) suggests trader uncertainty and possible information asymmetry - Limited match-specific history between these two teams in briefing CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: - confidence_yes = 45: Hanwha appears to have better standing record, but conflation of main/CL rosters creates substantial epistemic gap. Academy performance is unpredictable. - confidence_no = 42: Gen.G Global Academy's true strength is underdetermined in briefing. No explicit head-to-head data or recent CL match details provided. - Both sides lack granular evidence (recent form, roster composition, direct matchups); probability leans YES only due to relative standing comparison, not strong signal. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Criteria are clear (first-to-2-wins BO3). Source (gol.gg) is standard esports database. No ambiguity in team identification. Forfeit/cancellation clauses are unambiguous. Low risk of procedural resolution failure. TIMING: Event is TODAY (~17 hours); market is essentially locked. Reversal would require unexpected cancellation or major team news, both low-probability at this stage.", "key_factor": "Critical data gap: briefing contains only main LCK standings for Hanwha Life Esports (3-1), not the Challengers roster; Gen.G Global Academy's actual CL record and head-to-head history are unclear, making team-strength assessment highly uncertain."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: YES at 72% reflects market consensus that Hanwha Life Esports Challengers outperformed Gen.G Global Academy during Rounds 1-2 (3-1 vs 1-4 record, +3 vs -3 game differential). FORM & STANDING ADVANTAGE: Hanwha finished 2nd place in LCK standings with positive game differential; Gen.G Academy finished with -3 differential, indicating sustained competitive weakness across multiple matches. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Gen.G Global Academy's 1-4 record (20% win rate) is a significant red flag. An academy roster struggling this badly in preliminary rounds faces uphill odds in a BO3 elimination-style format. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side gained +22.5pp over 7 days (now 70% EMA), suggesting informed traders are backing Hanwha as data accumulates. Sharp moves on Apr 11 show conviction swings but momentum remains bullish. MATCHUP CONTEXT: While academy teams can surprise, Gen.G's documented poor performance (1-4, -3) across Rounds 1-2 provides concrete evidence of underperformance, not just speculative underdog potential. STRUCTURE CONCERN: Briefing notes that Hanwha main roster data is more available than specific Challengers League matchup history, creating slight asymmetry in confidence\u2014but the win-loss record differential (3-1 vs 1-4) is unambiguous. UNDERDOG COUNTER-NARRATIVE: Gen.G's institutional resources and academy player depth could theoretically enable a upset, and academy vs challengers match-specific data is sparse. However, a 1-4 record is hard to overcome in a single BO3. RESOLUTION CLARITY: BO3 format means one match decides outcome; head-to-head is unpredictable, but Hanwha's trajectory and Gen.G's weakness across 5 prior matches favor the favorite. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence is 62 (decent) because Rounds 1-2 records provide concrete evidence. NO confidence is low (35) because Gen.G Academy's poor record leaves limited narrative for a comeback, and counterarguments rely on vague 'institutional advantage' rather than performance data.", "key_factor": "Hanwha Life Esports' superior Rounds 1-2 record (3-1, +3 differential) vs Gen.G Global Academy's weak 1-4 record (-3 differential) establishes a structural competitive advantage that favors the established team."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.34, "probability_yes": 0.34, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (Gen.G Global Academy): The briefing conflates Hanwha Life Esports' main roster performance (3-1, +3 differential) with Hanwha Challengers' likely different roster composition; this is a critical error. Hanwha Challengers is explicitly distinct from the main team, and no direct performance data for Hanwha Challengers is provided. Gen.G organization has demonstrated elite institutional resources (visible in main LCK standings at 2-2, competitive positioning). Academy rosters backed by top organizations often contain high-ceiling players preparing for promotion or recovering from injury\u2014not merely 'weaker' players by default. The briefing acknowledges Gen.G academy 'could be seeded stronger academy players' and notes academy teams 'can exceed expectations with focused preparation for specific matchups.' This is a realistic pathway for upset that contradicts the binary 'academy = weaker' framing. CRITICAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head match history between Hanwha Challengers and Gen.G Global Academy is provided. No recent form data for either Challengers team exists in the briefing. Market is pricing on assumption, not evidence. TIMING RISK: Match resolves TODAY (17 hours). Sharp volatility on Apr 11 (+/- 26-27pp in both directions) suggests fast money moving on new information (likely lineup announcements, patch changes, or scout reports). Current 72% YES pricing may reflect outdated or overcorrected consensus. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES: Hanwha Challengers' roster and recent form are completely unknown. If Hanwha is using younger/experimental players or second-string lineup, Gen.G's focused academy roster with strong org backing could have significant matchup advantages. BO3 format rewards consistency and preparation\u2014two areas where Gen.G org excels. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: 72% YES on a Challengers league match with no head-to-head data and asymmetric roster visibility is aggressive. NO side priced at 28% despite being backed by Gen.G's resources and institutional strength suggests possible overcorrection toward Hanwha's main roster narrative. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence supports Gen.G's organizational advantages and the absence of Hanwha Challengers performance data (confidence_no = 42). However, the briefing provides no concrete recent match results, player forms, or patch impact for either Challengers team (confidence_yes = 28 reflects underdog uncertainty, not evidence of weakness). PROBABILITY RATIONALE: probability_score = 34 reflects Gen.G's underdog pricing (28%) adjusted upward modestly for organizational strength and preparation advantages in a BO3, but heavily discounted by the lack of concrete Hanwha Challengers performance data. probability_no_score = 58 reflects reasonable confidence that Gen.G's institutional backing and academy roster depth could deliver an upset, but stops well short of 66% (100 - 34) because the favorite's specific form remains opaque.", "key_factor": "Gen.G's institutional strength and academy roster depth could exploit Hanwha Challengers' thinner roster in a best-of-three format where preparation and coaching matter."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "EVENT CATEGORY: LoL Challengers League BO3 match (low-tier/academy competition). Historical base rate for favored teams in academy-level BO3s is approximately 60-70% win probability. HANWHA CASE (YES): Hanwha Life Esports main roster finished 3-1 (6-3 games, +3 differential) in Rounds 1-2, suggesting stronger organizational depth and player quality. Academy/challenger teams typically inherit some institutional advantage from stronger parent orgs. GEN.G ACADEMY CASE (NO): Gen.G Global Academy finished 1-4 in LCK CL with -3 differential, significantly weaker record than Hanwha's main team. Gen.G org has resources, but academy roster performance in early rounds was poor. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing conflates Hanwha main team (3-1) with Hanwha Challengers roster \u2014 these are likely DIFFERENT rosters competing in different leagues. No direct performance data provided for Hanwha Challengers specifically. This severely undermines confidence in YES case. ADDITIONAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head match history between these specific rosters provided. No scouting reports, recent scrims, or player-level analysis available. Standings data is from Rounds 1-2 (early April); unclear if teams have shifted form or roster since then. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES at 72% appears inflated relative to available evidence. Sharp volatility on Apr 11 (+26.5pp, -27.5pp swings) suggests reaction to news (likely roster/injury updates) rather than fundamental information in briefing. Market may be overweighting main team performance. TIMING RISK: Match resolves in ~17 hours (TODAY). Very little time for new information to emerge. High market price (72%) combined with low confidence-justifying data suggests market is responding to external intel (team news, scrims, DM conversations) not visible in briefing. BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: Without clear evidence that Hanwha Challengers > Gen.G Academy on roster talent/form, default to ~55-60% for the team with stronger organizational backing (Hanwha main org \u2192 Hanwha Challengers likely gets better academy players). Market at 72% implies high confidence in a claim we cannot directly verify. CONFIDENCE CEILING: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no capped at ~45 because briefing lacks direct CL match data, specific roster comparisons, and recent form updates. Market price does not match evidence quality available. FINAL ESTIMATE: Hanwha Challengers favored (~62% base rate) due to stronger org and Rounds 1-2 context, but market overpricing (72%) relative to thin evidence justifies modest reduction. Assign 62 to YES to reflect slight organizational advantage while flagging low conviction due to data gaps.", "key_factor": "In LoL esports BO3s, the higher-seeded or better-ranked team wins ~65-70% of the time; academy/challenger teams upset established rosters ~20-30% of the time."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market currently prices YES at 72%, reflecting Hanwha Life Esports Challengers as favorite \u2014 this aligns with the available data showing Hanwha main roster's 3-1 record in Rounds 1-2 vs Gen.G Global Academy's 1-4 record. Critical caveat: The briefing conflates HANWHA MAIN ROSTER (3-1, +3 differential) with HANWHA CHALLENGERS, and similarly conflates LCK main league standings with LCK Challengers League rosters. These are distinct competitive tiers; Challengers roster \u2260 main roster. Data gap: No specific match history between Hanwha Life Esports Challengers and Gen.G Global Academy is provided. The 3-1/1-4 records are for main/academy in different leagues or contexts, not predictive of head-to-head Challengers League outcome. Gen.G's institutional strength (as evidenced by main roster 2-2 record, 5-4 games, +1 differential in LCK proper) suggests academy could exceed raw win-loss expectations if well-coached and prepared for this specific matchup. Academy teams vs academy teams are less predictable than main rosters; talent scattering and coaching focus vary. Single BO3 is high-variance; standings predict direction but not guarantee. Sharp moves on Apr 11 (+26.5pp swing YES, then -27.5pp swing, then +26.0pp) suggest market uncertainty and possible information releases; current 72% appears relatively settled after volatility. Market has risen +22.5pp over 7 days (from ~50% to 72%), indicating sustained confidence in Hanwha Challengers. This rise may reflect additional CL-specific data not captured in briefing summary. Resolution in ~17 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT): reversal to Gen.G would require a significant upset. Current 72% YES price leaves 28% for NO, which is plausible but implies strong Hanwha favorite. Sentiment appears Rational: market is not exuberant (not 85%+) nor panicked (not 55%-); 72% reflects moderate-to-strong confidence backed by available record differential, accounting for academy team volatility. Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_yes=62 (data supports Hanwha's better record) vs confidence_no=48 (academy upside and matchup-specific unknowns create fog on NO side). Ignorance mass of 97 (68+35-6 slack) reflects real data gaps on Challengers League specifics.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA AMBIGUITY: Briefing provides Hanwha Life Esports main roster record (3-1, +3 differential) but market asks about Hanwha Life Esports *Challengers* (a separate roster). These are different teams entirely in LCK ecosystem\u2014main roster players do not play in CL matches. GEN.G ACADEMY PERFORMANCE: Gen.G Global Academy finished 1-4 in LCK CL Rounds 1-2 with -3 game differential, indicating weakness within CL competitive tier. This is the most relevant data point for predicting this specific matchup. ROSTER COMPOSITION UNKNOWNS: No specific player names, coach quality, or recent scrimmage data provided for either Challengers/Academy roster. CL teams often field developmental players; institutional pedigree (Gen.G org) does not guarantee individual player caliber. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-three introduces higher variance than full season standings. A 1-4 team can win individual series, especially with meta preparation or favorable draft. Gen.G's -3 differential suggests systemic issues (game knowledge, macro play, coordination) less likely reversed by single-series prep. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES side rose +22.5pp over 7 days with sharp volatile swings (+26.5pp Apr 11, -27.5pp same day). Suggests algorithmic/noise trading rather than fundamental information arrival. Current 72% YES reflects mild underdog premium on Gen.G but not extreme confidence. HANWHA CHALLENGERS FORM: No specific CL record provided for Hanwha Challengers team. Briefing assumes main roster strength transfers down, which is unreliable\u2014academy teams can outperform challenger teams or vice versa depending on player allocation. GEN.G INSTITUTIONAL ADVANTAGE: Despite poor CL record, Gen.G organization has coaching infrastructure, scrim partners, and analytic depth. However, a 1-4 record suggests these advantages have not translated to CL wins; structural problems likely persist. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event resolves TODAY (~17 hours). No recent news, roster changes, or injury reports available. Market is pricing based on season standings + organizational reputation, not fresh match intel. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES side (Hanwha Challengers) supported by assumption that Hanwha main > Gen.G academy, but main roster data is not applicable. NO side (Gen.G) has explicit CL season data (1-4, -3) showing underperformance, but no explanation of why or whether it reflects true team strength vs. meta mismatch. RESOLUTION CRITERIA RISK: Forfeit, disqualification, or cancellation resolves 50-50. Low LCK Challengers viewership/infrastructure suggests elevated operational risk vs. main league, though still unlikely. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Gen.G Global Academy's 1-4 CL record is a genuine weakness indicator; Hanwha Challengers' inferred strength from main roster is methodologically flawed but directionally plausible. Probability slightly favors Hanwha, but confidence is moderated by data gaps on Hanwha CL roster quality and Gen.G's potential upside from focused BO3 preparation. Price of 72% YES is roughly justified but not heavily mispriced.", "key_factor": "The briefing conflates Hanwha Life Esports' main LCK roster (3-1, 2nd place) with their Challengers League team, which are separate squads with different player pools and competitive levels; Gen.G Global Academy's -3 differential in CL rounds suggests structural weakness, but academy rosters can still field competitive lineups against challenger squads."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA CONFUSION: Briefing conflates Hanwha Life Esports main roster (3-1, +3 differential in main LCK) with Hanwha Life Esports Challengers roster. These are DIFFERENT teams. The 3-1 record does NOT apply to the Challengers team playing today. Gen.G Global Academy finished 1-4 in LCK CL, but Hanwha Life Esports Challengers' actual CL record is NOT provided in the briefing. Win probability gap (72% YES) may rest on false equivalency between main roster strength and Challengers roster strength. Market price at 72% YES reflects confidence in Hanwha brand/main roster, not evidence of Hanwha Challengers competitive edge. Academy mismatch reasoning is inverted: if both are academy/challenger-tier, Gen.G's institutional resources could be the differential. Sharp 26.5pp YES swing on Apr 11 01:00 UTC, then -27.5pp reversal at 17:00 UTC, then +26.0pp recovery at 23:00 UTC suggests information asymmetry or coordinated repositioning. Recent volatility (\u00b127pp in 22 hours) indicates lack of consensus among informed bettors. Match is TODAY (17 hours to resolution); no recent head-to-head match data, no injury reports, no roster confirmations provided. Absence of challenger-specific performance metrics is the briefing's largest blind spot. BLACK SWAN: Hanwha Challengers could field a significantly weakened roster (academy call-ups, injury substitutions, or players rested from main roster conflicts) that Gen.G Academy has prepared for in scrims. Gen.G's academy coaching staff may have exploited meta shifts or map pool weaknesses invisible to main-roster-focused public analysis. BO3 format is high-variance for academy-level play; a single well-prepared game 1 can swing momentum. Limited sample size and recent roster fluidity in LCK mean single-match prediction is close to a coin flip when stripped of main-roster inference. Confidence_yes at 42 reflects over-reliance on main roster proxy data and absence of Challengers-specific performance history. Confidence_no at 38 reflects equal uncertainty about Gen.G Academy's actual strength and preparation level. Price at 72% YES suggests market is applying main roster dominance heuristic, not Challengers head-to-head analysis. Contrarian edge: downgrade YES probability due to missing Hanwha Challengers roster depth/injury data and upgrade Gen.G's institutional upside in academy format.", "key_factor": "Hanwha's Challengers roster experiences a sudden roster substitution, injury, or format-specific meta mismatch that Gen.G Global Academy's academy players exploit through superior scrim preparation and meta adaptation over the past 48 hours."}], "final_score": 0.626731327268235, "no_score": 0.3935924200306649, "edge": -0.025000000000000022, "no_edge": 0.42499999999999993, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 48% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935165", "question": "LoL: Hanwha Life Esports Challengers vs Gen.G Global Academy (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Hanwha Life Esports Challengers and Gen.G Global Academy in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 16 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Hanwha Life Esports Challengers\" if Hanwha Life Esports Challengers win the match against Gen.G Global Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gen.G Global Academy\" if Gen.G Global Academy win the match against Hanwha Life Esports Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T11:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T05:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.725, "volume_usd": 2286.5267230000004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["35613843576585728475052139353127855419846230621169769985708564247860143237220", "102431159405558195564259079811403386059994438254414626686020573469177054341003"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Apr 9, - May 7, - Apr 16, - May 31, 0 - 2.", "Apr 12, - Apr 19, - May 15, - May 24, - Apr 23, 0 - 1.", "LCK 2026 Season is an offline Korean LoL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 01 to Sep 13 2026 featuring 10", "Image 782: Corki\n\nImage 783: Nami\n\nMVP: Kanavi (100 pts)\n\n|  | Bans |  |\n --- \n| Image 784: Anivia Image 785: Varus Image 786: Nocturne Image 787: Nautilus Image 788: Nami | Game 1 | Image 789: Karma Image 790: Rumble Image 791: Pantheon Image 792: Yunara Image 793: Bard |\n| Image 794: Anivia Image 795: Varus Image 796: Pantheon Image 797: Lee Sin Image 798: Wukong | Game 2 | Image 799: Karma Image 800: Rumble Image 801: Ryze Image 802: Aurora Image 803: Galio |\n\nImage 804Image 805Image 806:  807:  808: \n\nView match details\n\nImage 809: T1T1\n\n0\n\n2\n\nImage 810: Gen.G EsportsGEN\n\nApril 8, 2026 - 19:02 KST\n\nImage 811: T1T1\n\n0:2(Bo3)\n\nImage 812: Gen.G EsportsGen.G\n\nImage 813: Jayce\n\nImage 814: Jarvan IV\n\nImage 815: Ryze\n\nImage 816: Kalista\n\nImage 817: Renata Glasc\n\n25:52\n\nImage 818: Sion [...] 3\u20131\n\n6\u20133\n\n+3\n\n3.", "Image 111: Gen.G EsportsGen.G Esports\n\n2\u20132\n\n5\u20134\n\n+1\n\n4.", "Image 112: Nongshim RedForceNongshim RedForce\n\n2\u20132\n\