{"run_id": "fef35376-94da-4a79-bdc7-2323e06c5e5e", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T18:25:28.961070+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1982224", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Team Secret vs Fnatic (BO3) - Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Team Secret and Fnatic in the Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 3:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Secret\" if Team Secret win the match against Fnatic.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fnatic\" if Fnatic win the match against Team Secret.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T23:55:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T17:55:00Z", "yes_price": 0.405, "volume_usd": 2537.144241, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["82207532521631738681025394622823840418945026993171740130124911684961792290869", "21650104269162174388082261085745475649802262513406392884545035522480857708486"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "TIMING: Match is scheduled for April 15, 2026 at 21:00 CEST (~5 hours from briefing timestamp 2026-04-15 18:25 UTC). Event is LIVE/IMMINENT with minimal time for significant reversals. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Team Secret wins the BO3 match in normal play. Clear binary outcome unless match is canceled, ends in forfeit/disqualification, or delayed >7 days (triggering 50-50 resolution). TEAM SECRET DATA: Group stage record 0-0-0-1 with 4-7 round differential (-3 net), placed 4th-5th in group with 0 points. This indicates poor group stage performance and elimination in early rounds. FNATIC DATA: Group stage performance NOT detailed in briefing. No ranking, record, or round differential provided. Only confirmation that Fnatic qualified for lower bracket. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION: Strong negative data on Team Secret (weak group finish); NO comparable data on Fnatic. Cannot assess relative competitive standing or head-to-head likelihood. MARKET SIGNAL: Current price YES=40% / NO=60% reflects NO-side favoritism. Sharp price moves on Apr 15 (+28pp for YES at 04:00 UTC, -26pp at 18:24 UTC) suggest recent information shifted sentiment toward Fnatic, but briefing does not explain the driver. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINTS: Lacking head-to-head data, recent form trajectory, roster info, or meta context, confidence on BOTH sides must be low. YES confidence=28 (weak data supporting Team Secret win); NO confidence=32 (marginally stronger from market signal and Fnatic's unknown-but-likely-superior group position, but still thin). PROBABILITY REASONING: Team Secret's -3 round differential and 0-point group finish suggest weakness. Fnatic's qualification without documented failure suggests equilibrium or strength. Market price (40/60) broadly aligns with limited data favoring Fnatic, but absence of Fnatic's group record prevents high conviction on either side. RESOLUTION RISK: Liquipedia publication within 2 hours is typical for live esports; low risk of oracle delay affecting outcome. Forfeit/disqualification risk is minimal in a scheduled playoff match. BO3 format allows decisive winner in normal play. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Probability_score=38 (Team Secret win) reflects slight-to-moderate underdog position based on weak group finish, constrained by heavy data gap on Fnatic. Probability_no_score=62 (Fnatic win) reflects marginal favoritism from market signal and implicit group-stage superiority, but both confidence scores remain depressed due to missing competitive context.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data on both teams' recent form, head-to-head record, and current roster strength; briefing provides only group stage records without map-level detail or meta context."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = Fnatic) ANALYSIS: Market has priced Fnatic (NO) at 60%, reflecting a modest but meaningful edge. This pricing persists despite severe data asymmetry \u2014 no group stage record provided for Fnatic, making direct comparison impossible. Team Secret's documented weakness is stark: 0-1 record, -3 round differential in group stage (4-7 rounds). This is below .500 performance in a competitive tournament, suggesting coordination, fragging, or strategic issues that may persist in playoffs. Fnatic's omission from the briefing statistics could indicate either: (a) stronger group performance not disclosed, or (b) data collection gap. Market price (60%) suggests traders have additional information or regional knowledge favoring Fnatic. Lower bracket context: both teams lost group stage, but degree of loss matters. Team Secret's explicit -3 differential is a quantifiable disadvantage signal; Fnatic's absence from the stats could indicate better relative performance. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES = Team Secret) WEAKNESSES: Team Secret's 4-7 round record across their group stage matches is the most concrete data point in the briefing and cuts against them. A -3 round differential in a balanced group typically indicates one or more significant losses. BO3 format amplifies weaknesses: if Team Secret has coordination or map-veto disadvantages, they must win 2-of-3 against a team that likely performed better in group stage. No positive momentum or form trajectory data exists for Team Secret. The briefing offers no recent wins, no map comfort indicators, no player roster strength assessment \u2014 all negatives relative to a team that 'qualified for playoffs.' If Fnatic had demonstrably worse group performance, the briefing would likely highlight it as a YES case; its absence suggests Team Secret's weakness is the more salient factor. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: confidence_yes set to 28: Team Secret's -3 round differential is a real negative, but without Fnatic's group stats, we cannot quantify the gap. The case FOR Team Secret is absence of contrary evidence, not presence of supporting evidence \u2014 very weak foundation. confidence_no set to 35: Market pricing at 60% is rational given data scarcity, but we lack the actual competitive metrics that would justify higher confidence. Fnatic's group performance is completely unknown; they could have faced weaker opponents or played poorly. Market confidence is not the same as analytical confidence. Probability_score of 38 reflects: Team Secret's documented weakness (-3 differential) makes them clear underdogs, but BO3 variance and unknown opponent strength leave meaningful uncertainty. Not a strong NO conviction, but a clear lean. Sum of probabilities (38 + 62 = 100) reflects genuine 50/50 baseline with a modest tilt toward NO based on available data asymmetry, not high-conviction analysis.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 60% for NO reflects rational uncertainty given both teams' weak group stage performance and complete absence of head-to-head or recent form data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL & VOLATILITY: YES side shows EMA of 70% over 7 days but currently trades at 40%\u2014a sharp 30pp swing. The 24-hour volatility of 22.1pp/hr and two massive reversals (+28pp then -26pp) on Apr 15 suggest uncertainty and possibly mispriced shares. NO side's EMA of 30% (7-day) declining to 60% (current) is less volatile\u2014indicates confidence but could reflect herding rather than fundamental data. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides ZERO information on Fnatic's group stage record, round differential, or competitive standing. We know Team Secret went 0-0-0-1 with -3 RD, but we cannot assess whether Fnatic's performance was materially stronger. This asymmetry is the core issue. TEAM SECRET'S CASE: 4-7 round differential (-3 net) is weak, but in a lower bracket BO3 format, a single upset run is plausible. Round differential in group play does not perfectly predict knockout match outcomes\u2014tactical adjustments, momentum, and map veto can shift dynamics. Team Secret's group stage struggle is NOT proof they cannot beat Fnatic in a single series. FNATIC'S CASE: Market prices Fnatic at 60% (NO), implying meaningful favorite status. However, without explicit comparative data (head-to-head record, Fnatic's group RD, recent tournament performance), this pricing rests on incomplete information. The briefing offers no evidence of Fnatic's strength relative to Team Secret. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams are in lower bracket\u2014both have already failed in group play. This is NOT a David vs. Goliath scenario; this is two weakened teams competing for survival. In such matchups, single-series volatility is higher than when seeding clearly separates competitors. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES VARIANCE: Best-of-three series increase upset probability relative to single-map formats. Team Secret needs to win 2 maps; map veto and tactical preparation can negate raw strength gaps. PRICE HISTORY RED FLAG: The +28pp spike at 04:00 UTC followed by -26pp reversal at 18:24 UTC on Apr 15 suggests sharp disagreement among traders. This is consistent with genuine uncertainty, not settled consensus on Fnatic dominance. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: Confidence_yes = 28 (low) because we lack concrete performance data for Team Secret relative to Fnatic and have no head-to-head history. Confidence_no = 32 (low, not high) because we also lack Fnatic's comparative strength data; the market's 60% pricing is based on incomplete information. Both sides are underfunded with evidence. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 42% for YES reflects that Fnatic's favorite status is reasonable given lower bracket context, but the absence of comparative data prevents conviction. Team Secret is not obviously outmatched; they are simply unknown. In a lower bracket BO3 with thin info on both sides, 40\u201345% for the underdog is defensible. TIMING & EXECUTION: Match is TODAY (5 hours away). No reversal scenario (e.g., roster changes, emergency forfeit) is credible at this point. The outcome hinges on live match play, not news. This limits upside for probability revision.", "key_factor": "Team Secret's presence in lower bracket is not disqualifying\u2014both teams lost in group stage and the briefing provides no comparative strength data to establish Fnatic's superiority."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET TIMING: Event is TODAY, resolves in ~5 hours. Sharp moves (+28pp YES, -26pp NO at 04:00 UTC; reversal at 18:24 UTC) suggest late-breaking information or insider trading; current 40% YES price reflects informed betting after these reversals. TEAM SECRET WEAKNESS: 0-1 record in group stage with 4-7 round differential (-3 net) places them clearly in lower bracket. This is objectively weaker than average group-stage performance, suggesting fundamental skill/coordination gaps. FNATIC UNKNOWN: Fnatic's group stage record is not provided in briefing. This is a critical data gap. If Fnatic also has poor record, both teams are equivalently weak (lowers confidence on both sides). If Fnatic finished stronger, YES probability should be lower. BASE RATE FOR LOWER BRACKET: In esports lower-bracket elimination, seeding/group-stage performance typically predicts 55-65% of match outcomes. Secret's poor showing (-3 differential) suggests ~35-40% win probability absent other data. VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hr volatility of 22.1pp/hr on YES side is 2x the NO side (11pp/hr), indicating low confidence/thin liquidity ($2.5k total volume). Extreme swings suggest speculative trades, not fundamental data shifts. RESOLUTION RISK: Match format (BO3) and potential forfeiture/delay clauses create 50-50 resolution scenarios. Low probability but non-zero given esports organizational instability. Reduces effective YES/NO discrimination. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Briefing contains zero direct competitive history between Secret and Fnatic. Must rely entirely on group-stage proxy signals. Secret's negative differential is stronger evidence than Fnatic's missing data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data arguing AGAINST YES (Secret's poor group record). Weak data on NO side (Fnatic unspecified). Thus confidence_no is LOW (32) despite betting weight favoring NO at market price (60%). ANCHOR TO BASE RATE: Historical lower-bracket performance differential of -3 maps in group stage correlates to ~35-45% match-win probability in elimination. Current 40% YES aligns with this; 60% NO price appears fairly efficient.", "key_factor": "Lower bracket esports matches: ~45-50% upset rate; established team performance variance in BO3 formats: \u00b115pp around seeding expectation"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market is pricing YES at 40%, NO at 60% \u2014 reflects modest confidence in Fnatic but lacks strong directional conviction. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Fnatic's group stage record, round differential, and current form are completely absent from briefing. Cannot evaluate NO side rigorously. Team Secret visible weakness: 0-0-0-1 record, 4-7 round differential (-3), places them 4th-5th in group. This is objective evidence of group stage struggles. Team Secret's poor round differential (-3) suggests either tactical issues or individual skill gaps \u2014 concerning for a lower bracket match where no margin for error exists in BO3. NO DATA on recent scrims, roster changes, player form, or head-to-head history between Secret and Fnatic \u2014 impossible to assess momentum or stylistic matchups. Market shows 22.1pp/hr volatility on YES side vs 11.0pp/hr on NO side \u2014 YES side experiencing 2x the whipsaw, suggesting uncertainty and poor conviction among traders. Sharp moves: +28pp on YES (Apr 15 04:00), then -26pp (Apr 15 18:24) suggest reactive trading without fundamental analysis, not signal-driven moves. Current price (40% YES) appears to slightly OVERVALUE Team Secret relative to their group stage evidence, but lack of Fnatic data prevents confident arbitrage call. Low volume ($2,537 USD) indicates thin liquidity and low trader confidence \u2014 not enough aggregated information to trust either side. RATIONAL APATHY DETECTED: Market is taking a weak midpoint stance (40/60) rather than strongly committing to either team based on available evidence. Given Team Secret's objective weakness visible in data and complete absence of offsetting strength signals, probability_score of 38 reflects this asymmetry. Fnatic remains opaque \u2014 NO side confidence set low (35) due to missing fundamental performance data, not because of evidence supporting Secret. Ignore sharp recent price swings; they appear noise-driven in thin market. Focus on Team Secret's verifiable -3 round differential as anchor.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Team Secret's documented group stage record (0-0-0-1, -3 RD) shows they lost their only match decisively; in R6S, negative round differential this large signals either poor defensive utility usage, weak map control principles, or coordination breakdowns\u2014not random variance. Fnatic's group stage performance data is absent from briefing; this creates asymmetric information\u2014NO side evidence is weaker, justifying lower confidence_no despite higher probability_no_score. Market prices show YES at 40% despite 7-day EMA favoring YES at 70%; sharp moves (\u00b128pp Apr 15 03:00-04:00 UTC) suggest late news or lineup/roster updates affecting Secret\u2014likely negative if market sold off to 40%. BO3 format (best 2 of 3) in elimination bracket does reduce single-match variance compared to BO1, but Team Secret's structural -3 RD gap persists across multiple maps in veto pool. Event timing is TODAY (resolution ~5 hours); match at 21:00 CEST Apr 15 is imminent; reversal requiring Team Secret to completely neutralize their evident round-win deficit is possible but requires exceptional in-game adaptation unlikely to resolve structural weaknesses. Liquipedia Tier A tournament with $45k prize pool; both teams are legitimate regional competitors, but qualifier status (lower bracket) is not evidence of parity\u2014group stage seeding is usually predictive of elimination bracket outcomes. No recent scrim results, player form updates, or roster changes provided in briefing; unable to assess whether Team Secret's weakness is persistent or tournament-day form variance. Fnatic's absence from performance table could indicate they placed higher in group (top 2-3) and entered upper bracket, making lower bracket opponent assignment asymmetric skill-wise. R6S map veto system (4 bans, 1 pick per team, 1 decider) means neither team can fully avoid unfavorable matchups; Secret's apparent structural weakness suggests they may struggle on multiple map types.", "key_factor": "Team Secret's significantly negative round differential (-3 in group, 4-7 rounds) in a tactical 5v5 game indicates potential structural weaknesses in anti-strat depth or map control execution that are difficult to overcome in elimination BO3 formats regardless of single-match variance."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.35, "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL ANOMALY: YES side rallied +28pp at 04:00 UTC (15 hours before match start), then collapsed -26pp at 18:24 UTC. This sharp reversal within same day, combined with low volume ($2,537), suggests either: (1) sharp traders with private intel exiting positions, (2) technical correction after over-leverage, or (3) late-breaking roster/lineup news not yet in briefing. FNATIC OPACITY: Briefing provides zero competitive data on Fnatic's group stage performance, round differential, or recent form. Market currently prices Fnatic 60% (NO), yet the confidence gap suggests traders are guessing. A team with hidden weaknesses or recent roster instability could underperform. TEAM SECRET STRUCTURAL WEAKNESS: 0-0-0-1 record and -3 round differential in group stage is genuinely poor. However, lower bracket opponents often have similar struggles. No evidence Team Secret is fundamentally worse than Fnatic\u2014only that Secret had a bad group stage. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-three in tactical team games (R6S) has higher variance than series stats suggest. Map veto, side selection, and tactical preparation matter enormously. Briefing notes map veto structure (TBD) but no strategic meta or anti-veto tendencies for either team. TIMING PRESSURE & PSYCHOLOGICAL EDGE: Lower bracket quarterfinal is 'win or go home.' If Fnatic is favored by market consensus (60%), they may face overconfidence or complacency. Conversely, Secret enters with maximum desperation\u2014a known psychological advantage in elimination rounds. SILENT ROSTER/COACHING VARIABLE: No mention of recent roster changes, injuries, substitutes, or coaching decisions for either team. In tactical esports, a single key player benched, illness, or last-minute sub can swing a BO3 by 15-20 percentage points. INFORMATION ADVANTAGE ASYMMETRY: Market EMA (70% YES over 7 days) vs current price (40% YES) represents a 30pp gap\u2014unusual for same-day event with high stakes. This suggests material new information entered market in last 24 hours (likely negative for Secret) that the briefing does not capture. CONFIDENCE SUPPRESSED: Both confidence scores set LOW (28/32) because briefing lacks head-to-head data, recent form trajectories for either team, tactical tendencies, and player-level performance metrics. High volatility and information asymmetry justify epistemic humility. BLACK SWAN DIRECTION: The 04:00 UTC rally suggests informed traders briefly saw Secret as stronger (~70% YES), then exited. This could indicate: (a) Secret roster announcement attracting sharps, (b) Fnatic lineup uncertainty, or (c) a meta shift favoring Secret's playstyle. If true, current 40% YES is an underweight. CONTRARIAN POSTURE: Consensus (market 60% Fnatic) rests on Secret's poor group stage record. But group stage \u2260 knockout performance. Secret may have pivoted tactics, identified meta gaps, or recovered from early-tournament coordination issues. Fnatic's silence in briefing is suspicious\u2014no data means no way to judge if they are truly better.", "key_factor": "Team Secret roster changes, tactical innovation on map veto, or Fnatic's participation legitimacy/technical issues not yet public\u2014combined with the 28pp YES rally at 04:00 UTC suggesting informed trading ahead of scheduled 21:00 CEST match."}], "final_score": 0.37963050195933196, "no_score": 0.620367624404532, "edge": 0.29499999999999993, "no_edge": 0.10499999999999998, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 33% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1982224", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Team Secret vs Fnatic (BO3) - Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket quarterfinal 