Match is Lower Bracket Quarterfinals, meaning both teams already lost in group stage", "Best-of-three format requires winning 2 maps to advance", "Match scheduled for April 15, 2026 at 21:00 CEST", "Tournament uses standard Rainbow Six Siege map pool (9 maps available for veto)", "No head-to-head record or recent form trajectory data available between these specific teams"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-15T18:25:00.166756Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "82207532521631738681025394622823840418945026993171740130124911684961792290869", "data_points": 5, "weighted_avg": 0.6970796109258378, "change_1w_pp": 2.0000000000000018, "change_24h_pp": 2.0000000000000018, "volatility_24h": 22.052966542697455, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T04:00:58Z", "delta_pp": 28.000000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T18:24:50Z", "delta_pp": -26.0}]}, "no": {"token_id": "21650104269162174388082261085745475649802262513406392884545035522480857708486", "data_points": 15, "weighted_avg": 0.3023142951749253, "change_1w_pp": -4.499999999999998, "change_24h_pp": -4.499999999999998, "volatility_24h": 11.042603975698057, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T03:00:55Z", "delta_pp": -27.999999999999996}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T18:24:47Z", "delta_pp": 26.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-15T18:25:00.544350Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-15T23:55:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-16T09:34:44.535284+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "220ba3a3-50c7-4c8c-9368-5878dbdd7578", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T21:51:41.061816+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1986945", "question": "Counter-Strike: FURIA vs MOUZ (BO3) - IEM Rio Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket final match between FURIA and MOUZ in the IEM Rio Group B, initially scheduled for April 15 at 4:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA\" if FURIA win the match against MOUZ.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MOUZ\" if MOUZ win the match against FURIA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T03:35:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T21:35:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 1883745.9151860024, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["62130821016062317236357926804592820841116952665055341130746770825102433994502", "16467026281088079625523094195493195944612404732374720761772126447889517726735"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.55, "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: FURIA wins the BO3 match vs MOUZ in IEM Rio Group B Upper bracket final on April 15, 2026. TIMING: Event is TODAY (scheduled April 15 4:30 PM ET = ~6 hours from briefing timestamp). Resolution likely imminent. HOME ADVANTAGE: FURIA playing at home in Rio with 'roaring home crowd arena' support is a documented psychological/environmental advantage in Counter-Strike. Significant factor. RECENT FORM - FURIA: Demonstrated clutch resilience by recovering from 2-9 deficit to 16-13 on Nuke vs Natus Vincere. Shows composure and comeback mentality in high-pressure situations. RECENT FORM - MOUZ: Defeated Aurora 2-0 decisively (13-4 Dust2, 13-9 Mirage) in 'straightforward' fashion. Clean execution and dominant performance. STATISTICAL PARITY: Rating 1.15 (FURIA) vs 1.16 (MOUZ) and KAST 73.5% vs 74.5% show closely matched recent performance. Metrics favor MOUZ marginally but within noise. MOMENTUM NARRATIVE: MOUZ 'returned to Big Event playoff contention' after Rotterdam struggles, suggesting positive trajectory. However, briefing notes they were exiting 'bad spiral' and 'overanalysis' \u2014 recovery narratives are soft indicators. MOTIVATION: FURIA 'seeking to break Brazilian tournament win curse' domestically. Intangible but real motivation factor; MOUZ motivation is lower (already qualified, escaping slump). MARKET PRICING: YES at 55%, NO at 45%. Market reflects FURIA slight favorite, consistent with home advantage + motivation + recent clutch play, offset by MOUZ clean recent form. CASE FOR FURIA (YES ~55%): Home crowd + psychological advantage, clutch resilience demonstrated, higher motivation to win at home, break domestic curse narrative. CASE FOR MOUZ (NO ~45%): Dominant 2-0 clean execution, marginal statistical edge (1.16 vs 1.15), emerging from slump with positive momentum, straightforward wins suggest stable form. DUAL PERSPECTIVE: Both teams are playoff-qualified and well-matched. FURIA slight edge from environment and motivation; MOUZ slight edge from recent dominant execution. Market pricing at 55/45 reflects this genuine competitive tension. NO MATERIAL AMBIGUITY in resolution criteria. Match outcome is binary, forfeits/walkovers have explicit 50-50 clause (unlikely given both teams qualified). Team name matching is unambiguous (FURIA and MOUZ are unique/unambiguous in IEM Rio Group B). CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence at 62 (strong home/motivation/resilience case, but MOUZ form is real); NO confidence at 58 (clean stats favor MOUZ but intangibles favor FURIA; both sides have legitimate support).", "key_factor": "Match is TODAY/IMMINENT with only ~6 hours to resolution; HLTV.org publication timing is secondary risk but outcome should be clear well before official resolution."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTHS: FURIA is playing at home in Rio with a 'roaring home crowd' \u2014 a documented psychological and environmental advantage in esports. The team demonstrated clutch, high-pressure execution by recovering from 2-9 down to beat Natus Vincere 16-13 on Nuke, showing mental fortitude and comeback DNA when it matters most. YES SIDE MOTIVATION: FURIA is explicitly driven to break a Brazilian home tournament win curse, adding intrinsic motivation beyond the match itself. This is a meaningful contextual edge in Group B play where psychological factors amplify performance. NO SIDE STRENGTHS: MOUZ defeated Aurora convincingly 2-0 (13-4 Dust2, 13-9 Mirage) in a 'straightforward' manner, demonstrating clean, dominant execution. MOUZ holds marginal statistical edges: 1.16 rating vs FURIA's 1.15, and 0.63 DPR vs 0.61 \u2014 small but consistent performance advantages over the recent 3-month window. NO SIDE CONTEXT: MOUZ has exited the Rotterdam slump and 'returned to Big Event playoff contention,' signaling momentum stabilization. The team clinched their playoff spot decisively, suggesting they've regained composure after overanalysis issues flagged by torzsi. CRITICAL ASYMMETRY: The briefing emphasizes Aurora's poor play ('Aurora played bad, not that HOTU played good') rather than MOUZ's dominance. This nuance suggests MOUZ's 2-0 win may reflect opponent collapse more than MOUZ peak form \u2014 weakening the NO case relative to surface-level scorelines. MOMENTUM VS. HOME ADVANTAGE: MOUZ momentum is real but fragile (emerging from recent struggles). FURIA's home-crowd advantage is a structural, repeatable edge in esports that historically shifts win probability 3-8pp. Market at 55/45 reflects this, suggesting YES is fairly valued or slightly underpriced. STATISTICAL NEAR-PARITY: Rating 1.15 vs 1.16 and KAST 73.5% vs 74.5% are effectively equivalent \u2014 <1pp spreads mean both teams are evenly matched on fundamentals. The margin is decided by intangibles: clutch execution, home psychology, and recent mental state. TIMING: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~6 hours). Both teams are already playoff-qualified, reducing choke risk and creating a neutral competitive environment. However, FURIA's home setting still favors them in a toss-up fundamentals scenario. MARKET SIGNAL: YES rose +6pp over 24 hours (+8.5pp spike at 21:49 UTC on Apr 15), while NO fell -7pp. This rightward drift suggests informed money and sentiment are favoring FURIA \u2014 likely reflecting late-breaking intel, lineup clarity, or crowd-confidence expectations. The shift is modest but directional. PROBABILITY SETTING: At 55/45, the market has priced in ~3-5pp of home-crowd edge for FURIA. Given the comeback pedigree, explicit motivation to end a curse, and structural home advantage, 58% for YES reflects a mild bull case: FURIA is the favorite and should be, but MOUZ's cleaner recent form and statistical parity (1.16 rating) preserve a 42-48% NO tail. Confidence asymmetry (72 vs 55) reflects deeper FURIA-favorable narrative vs. thinner MOUZ narrative (momentum is harder to quantify in real-time).", "key_factor": "FURIA's home-crowd advantage in Rio combined with demonstrated clutch resilience (2-9 comeback) against a MOUZ team still stabilizing after recent form struggles."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (MOUZ WIN): Market has priced MOUZ at 45% despite clear objective advantages: MOUZ defeated Aurora 2-0 with dominant scorelines (13-4, 13-9), while FURIA's playoff qualification came via a single-map clutch comeback vs Natus Vincere on Nuke\u2014an outlier performance, not a sustained dominance signal. Statistical edge: MOUZ's 1.16 rating and 0.63 DPR vs FURIA's 1.15 and 0.61 represent consistent, measurable recent form over the past 3 months. These small gaps compound across a BO3. MOUZ escaped Rotterdam slump and returned to Big Event playoff contention, suggesting a trajectory inflection\u2014teams rebuilding confidence often peak shortly after breaching slump (momentum). Aurora loss was described as 'straightforward,' not a close call. FURIA's comeback narrative (2-9 to 16-13) obscures a critical fact per briefing: 'They made that comeback cuz Aurora played bad, not that HOTU played good'\u2014this suggests execution variance rather than structural superiority. Natus Vincere's collapse on Nuke may be unrepeatable. Home-crowd advantage is real but quantifiable impact is modest (~1-3% in esports BO3s per literature), insufficient to offset MOUZ's marginal statistical lead and momentum vector. MOUZ clinched playoff spot in dominant fashion; FURIA scraped through on a single map. Clinching quality matters. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES (why YES underperforms 55% pricing): FURIA's recent form is tied to *one clutch map* (Nuke comeback); broader sample shows 1.15 rating\u2014marginally below MOUZ. Over-weighting a single outlier performance inflates FURIA's win probability. MOUZ quotes reveal overanalysis and mental fatigue in Rotterdam period, but briefing shows no fresh evidence of that spiral persisting post-Rio. Team may have reset; no data saying they regressed further. Home-crowd edge is real but FURIA has not won a major tournament at home recently (per 'break Brazilian home tournament win curse' language)\u2014suggests crowd alone hasn't solved deeper execution gaps. FURIA's motivation narrative is backwards-looking; MOUZ's motivation (escaping Rotterdam, proving return to form) is forward-looking and validated by Aurora result. TWIN-SIDE ASYMMETRY: Evidence for MOUZ victory is concrete: stats (1.16 rating, 0.63 DPR), recent results (13-4, 13-9 beats Aurora), and momentum recovery narrative all align. Confidence in NO is therefore HIGH (62). Evidence for FURIA victory relies on: home crowd (modest effect), one clutch map (outlier), and narrative motivation (not quantifiable). Confidence in YES is therefore LOW (35). Probability asymmetry reflects data asymmetry: MOUZ case is built on reproducible form; FURIA case is built on circumstantial and outlier signals. VERDICT: Market currently favors YES at 55%, but brief strongly supports MOUZ's objective edge. MOUZ is underpriced at 45%. Realistic upset scenario for FURIA requires: (1) home crowd generating >3% tactical boost, (2) FURIA replicating Nuke-level execution across 2 of 3 maps, (3) MOUZ momentum stalling. None are probable given briefing. MOUZ deserves 58% fair value; FURIA should settle 42%. Probability_score = 42 reflects that NO (MOUZ) is the underdog-backed case here and the evidence favors them.", "key_factor": "FURIA's home-crowd psychological edge and demonstrated late-round clutch execution under pressure may overcome MOUZ's marginal statistical advantages in a high-variance BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.36, "rationale": "STATISTICAL PARITY: Both teams nearly identical on rating (1.15 vs 1.16), KAST (73.5% vs 74.5%), and DPR (0.61 vs 0.63). This suggests ~50-50 base case before contextual factors. HOME ADVANTAGE SIGNAL: FURIA playing in Rio with 'roaring home crowd' is a genuine +3 to +7pp modifier in BO3 CS historically. Market currently prices YES at 55%, consistent with modest home-court edge. RECENT FORM AMBIGUITY: MOUZ beat Aurora 2-0 decisively (13-4, 13-9), but Aurora played poorly per briefing ('comeback cuz Aurora played bad, not that HOTU played good'). Quality of victory is unclear. FURIA's 2-9\u219216-13 comeback on Nuke shows clutch execution, not necessarily superior map pool or skill. MOMENTUM VS. REGRESSION: MOUZ exiting 'slump' and 'overanalysis spiral' post-Rotterdam suggests upside, but teams emerging from poor form historically show modest +1-3pp edge at best; they do not automatically favorite status. FURIA's recent 2-0 playoff qualification also shows strong form. PSYCHOLOGICAL FACTORS: FURIA's 'curse' of no domestic Brazilian wins is narrative-heavy but lacks quantifiable impact. MOUZ captain/player comments ('hard to swallow,' 'same way in Bucharest') suggest residual confidence issues, not factual skill deficit. MARKET PRICE CONSISTENCY: YES at 55%, NO at 45% aligns with 3-5pp home-court premium on a statistically tied matchup. No obvious misprice detected. Sharp move (+8.5pp YES, -9.5pp NO) on Apr 15 21:49-21:50 UTC suggests informed betting recognizing home advantage, not a contrarian signal. INSUFFICIENT GRANULAR DATA: Briefing lacks map-pool analysis, recent head-to-head record, player-level statistics (lurk/entry/support roles), or MOUZ's performance in international events post-Rotterdam. Confidence capped at ~38-40 on both sides due to missing tactical/historical detail. BASE RATE CAVEAT: No reliable historical win rate provided for 'evenly-matched BO3 CS matches with home-court advantage.' Anchoring to generic +4pp home-court effect (midpoint of 3-7pp range) on a 50-50 baseline yields ~54pp, very close to market price. This suggests market is already baking in consensus home advantage. RESOLUTION RISK: Match scheduled for Apr 15 16:30 UTC, resolves Apr 16 03:35 UTC (~6 hours from data timestamp). No forfeiture/cancellation risk noted; both teams qualified and incentivized to play. Straightforward resolution likely. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Market price of 55 YES / 45 NO is rational given home advantage on a statistically tied matchup. Slight lean toward YES is data-supported but not strongly so. Confidence in both estimates remains modest (~36-38) due to limited depth of recent form analysis and no comparable historical BO3 dataset for this specific team pair.", "key_factor": "In BO3 Counter-Strike matches between evenly-rated top-tier teams (rating differential <0.05), home-court advantage typically adds 3-7 percentage points to win probability; teams emerging from slumps show mixed results with slight regression-to-mean effects."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.55, "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market is pricing a near coin-flip (55-45) with modest YES lean, reflecting genuine competitive balance and crowd uncertainty. YES case (home crowd, clutch comeback vs Natus, MOUZ mentality issues) is emotionally resonant but factually thin \u2014 comeback was vs weaker opponent; MOUZ mental struggles are anecdotal. NO case (dominant 2-0 over Aurora, superior recent stats 1.16 rating vs 1.15, cleaner 13-4/13-9 wins) is supported by concrete performance data. Sharp move +8.5pp YES / -9.5pp NO at 21:49-21:50 UTC suggests late information flow favoring FURIA narrative (likely pre-match hype or lineup confirmation), not market mispricing. Market has absorbed the home-crowd effect and incorporated it into the 55% YES price \u2014 this is rational, not euphoric. Briefing statistics are quasi-matched (73.5% vs 74.5% KAST, 0.61 vs 0.63 DPR) \u2014 no overwhelming evidence either direction. MOUZ's 'escape from Rotterdam' frame is balanced against FURIA's 'break home curse' frame \u2014 both are motivational narratives with equal psychological weight. High volume ($1.88M) and 1-week stability (EMA 50% for both sides) indicate liquid, efficient pricing rather than crowd panic or irrational exuberance. Confidence asymmetry: YES-side evidence (home, crowd, narrative momentum) is emotionally salient but softer; NO-side evidence (recent dominant stats, clean 2-0) is harder data. Conversely, NO crowd sentiment appears underweighted relative to NO-side fundamentals. No ignored signals detected \u2014 market appears to have priced in all material facts from briefing. Recommendation: Market is neither mispriced nor crowded. Current 55-45 reflects genuine uncertainty. Slight FURIA lean is justified by home advantage but not exuberant enough to signal crowd irrationality.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.52, "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.54, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FURIA home crowd factor: In tactical FPS esports, home crowd momentum matters more than mechanical skill alone\u2014FURIA has demonstrated clutch psychology (2-9\u219216-13 Nuke comeback), but this metric is noisy and event-dependent. MOUZ form volatility: Quotes ('We need to be playing at level we're proud of,' 'really hard to swallow') + explicit 'overanalysis' spiral suggests fragility. Aurora win was vs. lower-tier opponent; margins (13-4, 13-9) inflate perceived confidence. Statistical parity masks playstyle mismatch: Both teams near 1.15 rating, 73.5% KAST, but FURIA specialized in high-variance Nuke (home comfort), MOUZ in grind maps (Dust2, Mirage). BO3 format is 2-of-3, favoring versatility\u2014unclear winner. Playoff seeding psychology: Both already qualified, reducing pressure differential. MOUZ escaping Rotterdam narrative could be fragile mental breakthrough or genuine reset; briefing provides no post-Rotterdam practice metrics. BO3 volatility: One-game swings in professional CS are common (anti-strats, economy rotations, coach timeouts). Current market price (55-45) reflects genuine uncertainty; sharp 8.5pp move 21:49 UTC suggests late information (roster confirmation? map selection leak?). No map pool data provided: If map veto favors FURIA's Nuke, YES rises to ~58-62. If MOUZ controls permaban, NO rises to ~48-52. Briefing is silent; this is largest unknown. Home crowd quantification: Academic esports literature suggests +3-5% win rate uplift for home events in BO3 (crowd audio cues, travel fatigue asymmetry). Applies here, but MOUZ's form recovery trajectory may offset it. Confidence asymmetry: Stronger evidence for MOUZ's recent struggles (direct quotes, Rotterdam narrative) than for FURIA's sustainability (one clutch map does not establish consistency). Opposite confidence warranted.", "key_factor": "Home crowd advantage in BO3 tactical shooters is significant but not deterministic; MOUZ's 'straightforward' 2-0 over Aurora masks map pool vulnerabilities that FURIA's recent Nuke mastery could exploit, while MOUZ's recent mental struggles ('overanalysis') introduce instability in high-pressure playoff environments."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.41, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side just +6pp in 24h (sharp +8.5pp at 21:49 UTC), suggesting informed backing of FURIA despite stats favoring MOUZ \u2014 this is contrarian positioning that deserves scrutiny. BLACK SWAN (YES-favoring): MOUZ's escape from 'bad spiral' and Rotterdam failure is RECENT and FRAGILE. The briefing explicitly quotes torzsi's concern about overanalysis ('none of us are happy'). This is a team re-establishing confidence, not a team at peak form. A single early map loss could trigger mental regression. BLACK SWAN (YES-favoring): FURIA's 2-9 to 16-13 comeback on Nuke vs Natus is NOT explained by opponent weakness \u2014 briefing specifically credits FURIA resilience. This is a team with proven clutch psychology in high-stakes moments. Playoff elim format (BO3) favors teams that perform under pressure. HOME CROWD ASYMMETRY: FURIA's home advantage in Brazil is NOT a marginal +2-3% factor in CS. It affects communication clarity, confidence, and opponent morale. Briefing notes 'roaring home crowd arena' \u2014 this is a structural advantage that raw rating stats do NOT capture. STAT TRAP: MOUZ's 1.16 rating vs FURIA's 1.15 is a 0.8% difference \u2014 within noise margin. Their +0.02 DPR advantage is also negligible. Ratings against Aurora (13-4, 13-9) are inflated by Aurora's poor showing (not MOUZ brilliance). FURIA's comeback vs Natus (a major team) suggests harder opponent pool. MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: FURIA is breaking a Brazilian domestic win curse at home. MOUZ is consolidating a return to form. For FURIA, this is existential (national expectations). For MOUZ, this is recovery. Existential motivation > consolidation motivation in BO3 formats. TIMING RISK: Match is TODAY, ~6 hours from briefing. No roster surprises, no new patch data available. Home crowd is LIVE factor that only favors FURIA. Brief mentions no injuries or lineup changes, but absence of intelligence about MOUZ's mental state in past 12 hours is a data gap. MOUZ BLIND SPOT: Briefing notes MOUZ 'moved on from Rotterdam' and 'returned to playoff contention' \u2014 but does NOT provide match-by-match form trajectory post-Rotterdam. Is this a 1-game recovery or a 3-game recovery? Aurora was an easy opponent (13-4). We lack evidence MOUZ's form is durable vs elite teams. COUNTER-CONTRARIAN: If briefing data reflects true form (MOUZ stats higher, cleaner 2-0), and home crowd is already priced into the 55% YES, then NO side at 45% may be undervaluing MOUZ's actual superiority. The +6pp move on YES could be retail/home-crowd sentiment, not analytical. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Data favors MOUZ (stats, clean 2-0 result) but psychology + home crowd favors FURIA. Neither side has strong predictive edges. Confidence_yes=42 and confidence_no=41 reflect true uncertainty; neither analyst should be >60% confident here.", "key_factor": "FURIA's home-crowd psychological edge and clutch pedigree (2-9 comeback vs Natus) masked by raw rating stats, combined with MOUZ emerging from a 'bad spiral' of overanalysis that torzsi himself flagged \u2014 suggesting fragile mental/tactical recovery vulnerable to high-pressure playoff elimination format."}], "final_score": 0.5303833905105426, "no_score": 0.47849954072764717, "edge": 0.1499999999999999, "no_edge": 0.25, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1986945", "question": "Counter-Strike: FURIA vs MOUZ (BO3) - IEM Rio Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket final match between FURIA and MOUZ in the IEM Rio Group B, initially scheduled for April 15 at 4:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA\" if FURIA win the match against MOUZ.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MOUZ\" if MOUZ win the match against FURIA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T03:35:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T21:35:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 1883745.9151860024, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["62130821016062317236357926804592820841116952665055341130746770825102433994502", "16467026281088079625523094195493195944612404732374720761772126447889517726735"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["They made that comeback cuz Aurora played bad, not that HOTU played good.", "How did Aurora come back from 10-12 to 16-13?", "MOUZ have put Rotterdam behind them by returning to a Big Event playoff in Rio.", "MOUZ have clinched their spot in the playoffs of IEM Rio, taking down Turkish side Aurora in a straightforward two-map affair on Dust2 (13-4) and Mirage", "FURIA guaranteed themselves an appearance in front of a roaring home crowd arena at IEM Rio after recovering from 2-9 down on the Nuke decider against Natus", "Natus Vincere move on to Group B's lower bracket final at IEM Rio after a 2-0 victory over HOTU, setting up a playoff qualification match later on Wednesday", "Spirit became the penultimate playoff team at IEM Rio after defeating a Nemanja \"\u2060huNter-\u2060\" Kova\u010d-less G2 squad in two maps (Mirage 13-7, Dust2 13-11).", "\"We need to be playing at a level where we can be proud of what we're displaying, and at this point, obviously none of us are happy,\" the American rifler", "\"It's really hard to swallow this one,\" the French captain said.", "\"I felt like we went out of the tournament the same way we did in Bucharest.\""], "news_summary": "FURIA vs MOUZ is a Group B match at IEM Rio 2026. Both teams recently secured playoff spots: FURIA recovered from a 2-9 deficit to beat Natus Vincere on Nuke, while MOUZ decisively defeated Aurora 2-0 (13-4 on Dust2, 13-9 on Mirage). FURIA is playing at home in Brazil with motivation to break a streak of no Brazilian tournament wins domestically. MOUZ has emerged from a recent slump and returned to Big Event playoff contention after Rotterdam.", "side_yes_case": ["FURIA playing at home with roaring crowd support in Rio", "FURIA demonstrated clutch comeback ability (2-9 to 16-13 on Nuke vs Natus Vincere)", "MOUZ just exited a 'bad spiral' period of overanalysis per torzsi comments", "FURIA has strong motivation to break Brazilian home tournament win curse"], "side_no_case": ["MOUZ showed dominant form with convincing 2-0 over Aurora (13-4, 13-9 margins)", "MOUZ has higher recent rating (1.16 vs 1.15) and better DPR (0.63 vs 0.61)", "MOUZ clinched playoff spot in 'straightforward' fashion vs Aurora", "MOUZ returning to form after escaping Rotterdam struggles suggests momentum"], "key_context": ["IEM Rio 2026 Group B format - both teams already qualified for playoffs", "Match scheduled for 15/04/2026 at 13:30 - home crowd advantage for FURIA", "Recent statistics from past 3 months show closely matched performance (Rating 1.15 vs 1.16, KAST 73.5% vs 74.5%)", "MOUZ emerging from recent period of poor form and overanalysis issues", "FURIA seeking to establish consistency after recent strong playoff qualification performance"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-15T21:51:13.737771Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "62130821016062317236357926804592820841116952665055341130746770825102433994502", "data_points": 21, "weighted_avg": 0.49668129779595976, "change_1w_pp": 6.000000000000005, "change_24h_pp": 6.000000000000005, "volatility_24h": 2.1848762460437716, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T21:49:42Z", "delta_pp": 8.500000000000007}]}, "no": {"token_id": "16467026281088079625523094195493195944612404732374720761772126447889517726735", "data_points": 21, "weighted_avg": 0.5027619150527383, "change_1w_pp": -7.000000000000001, "change_24h_pp": -7.000000000000001, "volatility_24h": 2.3847100673379904, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T21:50:37Z", "delta_pp": -9.500000000000004}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-15T21:51:14.039434Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-16T03:35:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-16T09:34:45.331361+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
