name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T09:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T03:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.3, "volume_usd": 72.418828, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["88316692964581176302654695179140682100759339266213481176390804687102334734574", "6477811238520484357101672043410145711077404701417568388235289685885103200400"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.3, "probability_yes": 0.3, "probability_no": 0.7, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: WinteR SquadronS wins a Best of 3 match against Ivory in EPL Season 36 Group Stage. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides NO team performance metrics, recent match results, roster composition, or head-to-head history for either WinteR SquadronS or Ivory. The 'KEY FACTS' section contains fragmented Dotabuff table data unrelated to either team (showing DreamLeague EEU CQ matches, BetBoom Team, and unrelated player profiles). MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current price is 30% YES / 70% NO with high 24-hour volatility (+/- 20pp swings on Apr 15). Weighted 7-day EMA for YES is 43%, suggesting market has shifted bearish on WinteR SquadronS. Sharp -20pp move at 21:54 UTC (2 hours before briefing timestamp) indicates late information or coordinated repositioning, but no briefing data explains the direction. NO FUNDAMENTAL BASIS FOR ADJUSTMENT: The briefing explicitly states 'No detailed team statistics, recent match results, or performance data were found in the available sources.' This is not a close matchup with data gaps\u2014it is a complete absence of comparative information. MARKET PRICE AS ONLY SIGNAL: In the absence of team data, the current market price (30% YES) is the only quantitative signal. Market participants may have access to real-time team information, recent form, or betting line consensus not reflected in this briefing. The sharp moves suggest late-breaking information. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~11 hours. No significant new information can reverse the current price unless match is delayed or canceled. The match is scheduled for 08:00 PM (briefing timestamp 21:54 UTC on Apr 15 suggests match may be imminent or already in progress). RESOLUTION MECHANISM CLARITY: Criteria are clear\u2014direct match outcome, with specific rules for forfeits (resolve 50-50) and delays >7 days (resolve 50-50). No ambiguity in team name matching for these established teams. Dotabuff is the primary source; fallback to credible reporting if unavailable within 2 hours. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 22 and confidence_no = 25 reflect profound data insufficiency on BOTH sides. The briefing provides no basis to differentiate WinteR SquadronS from Ivory in skill, form, or meta fit. Market prices alone anchor the probability, but without supporting data, confidence in either direction is weak. PROBABILITY REASONING: Set probability_score = 30 and probability_no_score = 70 to match current market prices, as no briefing data contradicts or adjusts these prices. This is not a 50-50 (coin flip) because market participants have demonstrably priced WinteR SquadronS lower; however, confidence in this direction is LOW due to data absence.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no actionable team performance data, roster information, or head-to-head history; market prices reflect speculative positioning rather than fundamental analysis; event timing is TODAY with resolution in ~11 hours, leaving no time for information reversal."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO (Ivory) is priced at 70% and has been the favorite for 7 days with consistent upward drift (+20pp 7-day change). This pricing reflects accumulated market intelligence and consensus on Ivory's superiority. MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: YES side has collapsed sharply in 24h (-6.5pp), with a devastating -20pp spike at Apr 15 21:53 UTC. NO side rose +20pp symmetrically. This divergence suggests WinteR SquadronS-negative information or consensus shift away from them. VOLATILITY & SHARP MOVES: Both sides show large intraday swings (YES: 13.6pp/hr volatility, NO: 8.9pp/hr), but the trailing 24h direction is decisively pro-NO. The -11pp, +18pp, -20pp swings in YES suggest uncertainty being resolved *against* WinteR SquadronS. DATA VOID AS ADVANTAGE FOR FAVORITE: With minimal team statistics, recent form, or head-to-head data available, bookmakers and sharp traders default to pre-tournament seeding, captain/player reputation, or roster strength signals. Ivory's 70% pricing in this vacuum suggests they were favorited pre-event or demonstrated superiority in group stage play to date. TIER 3 TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: EPL Season 36 is described as Tier 3 online. In lower-tier competitions with sparse public data, the market price often reflects sharp pre-match intelligence (coach/player tweets, scrim results, roster news) that retail traders cannot access. 70% on the favorite suggests this information favors Ivory. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: WinteR SquadronS has no positive catalysts mentioned in the briefing. They are the underdog at 30%, have shown recent price deterioration, and lack any form or matchup advantages cited. The case for them rests on 'limited negative information'\u2014a logically weak foundation. TIMING & RESOLUTION IMMINENT: Match resolves in ~11 hours (TODAY, 2026-04-16 09:00 UTC). Reversal would require a catalyst (roster change, news, injury) with minimal time. Sharp traders have already positioned; late movers favor Ivory at 70%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in NO (Ivory) case\u2014sustained market consensus, directional momentum, and data-sparse environment favoring pre-seeded favorite (45% confidence on NO reasoning itself, but driven by market structure + momentum rather than granular team data). Weak confidence in YES case (22%)\u2014relies on absence of negative information, which is not positive evidence. DUAL-SIDED PROBABILITY: Probability of 28 for YES reflects a modest underdog with real uncertainty in Tier 3 play but facing clear market consensus and recent momentum headwinds. Probability of 72 for NO reflects the favorite's structural positioning and recent polling shift, though low confidence (45) on NO reflects the data void\u2014market may be overconfident.", "key_factor": "NO side (Ivory) has sustained 7-day upward momentum (+20pp), market consensus solidification at 70%, and structural advantage in a data-sparse Tier 3 tournament environment where bookmaker pricing typically reflects sharp consensus."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides NO actionable statistics on either WinteR SquadronS or Ivory \u2014 no recent match results, win rates, roster composition, head-to-head records, or form data. The tournament table and player performance data shown are corrupted/unrelated (references to BetBoom Team, FISSURE, Power Rangers, European EEU qualifiers) and do not clarify either team's strength in EPL Season 36. MARKET STRUCTURE WEAKNESS: YES is priced at 30% despite zero negative information about WinteR SquadronS. The 70% NO price is built on absence of evidence for the YES side, not presence of evidence for the NO side. In information-scarce Tier 3 tournaments, this creates mispricing risk. VOLATILE PRICE ACTION SIGNALS UNCERTAINTY: YES dropped 20pp in a single move (Apr 15 21:54 UTC), and the 7-day EMA (~43%) is 13 points higher than current price (30%), indicating recent capitulation rather than fundamental clarity. Sharp swings (\u00b118-21pp) on low volume ($72) suggest weak conviction underpinning the NO consensus. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS UPSETS: A Best-of-3 match introduces higher variance than single-game formats. Even a moderately matched pairing sees upset probability increase due to game-to-game adaptation and early-series unpredictability. The briefing does not eliminate this structural feature. CASE FOR NO (FAVORITE) REMAINS HOLLOW: The briefing explicitly states 'Cannot assess relative team strength without comparative performance metrics' and 'No detailed team statistics, recent match results, or performance data were found.' This means the 70% NO price rests on market convention or false consensus, not on superior Ivory evidence. CASE FOR YES (UNDERDOG): WinteR SquadronS qualified for EPL S36 group stage, indicating baseline competence. With zero hard evidence of inferiority, the 30% price treats this team as a heavy underdog despite identical information poverty on both sides. If both teams are truly unknown, symmetric odds (~50%) would be more rational; 30% implies confident differentiation that the briefing cannot justify. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Event is TODAY (resolves ~11 hours). Sharp moves in final 24h suggest late-breaking information or emotional trading, not refined analysis. No injury reports, roster changes, or tactical intel are documented \u2014 further evidence the market is pricing on sentiment, not substance. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=28 (weak) reflects the genuine absence of WinteR SquadronS form data, BUT confidence_no=26 (equally weak) reflects that NO side also lacks substantive evidence. The sum is intentionally <100 to signal the briefing provides neither side credible grounds for high conviction. This is not a case where the underdog has hidden strength; it is a case where the market may be overconfident in the favorite despite symmetric ignorance. REASONABLE UPSET SCENARIO: In a Tier 3 online tournament with no head-to-head history, if WinteR SquadronS has better mid-game coordination, draft flexibility, or individual playmaker depth, they could win 2-1 in BO3. The 30% odds do not adequately price this possibility given complete absence of comparative form data. FINAL ASSESSMENT: WinteR SquadronS is not a proven underdog with overlooked strengths \u2014 the briefing simply does not contain the evidence. However, it is a *mispriced* underdog, because the favorite (Ivory at 70%) is priced with unwarranted confidence on symmetric ignorance. A bear's case here is not 'YES is secretly strong' but 'NO's odds are too high given absent differentiating data.' Probability reflects mild tilt toward YES (38%) reflecting the asymmetry of market overconfidence in an unknown favorite.", "key_factor": "Severe data vacuum on both teams makes market consensus (70% NO) vulnerable to information asymmetry favoring the underdog at 30% odds."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no usable team statistics, recent match results, roster composition, or head-to-head history for either WinteR SquadronS or Ivory. The match is TODAY (11 hours to resolution) in a Tier 3 online EPL tournament. At this proximity to event, market prices reflect late-stage information aggregation by informed traders. Current market prices: YES=30%, NO=70%. This 40pp spread is NOT symmetric\u2014traders have clear conviction toward Ivory (NO). 7-day price trend: YES fell 17.5pp (from ~48% to 30%), suggesting growing belief in Ivory during the lead-up week. This directional move contradicts a random 50-50 prior. 24-hour volatility is HIGH (13.6pp/hr on YES side), with sharp reversals (\u221211.0pp, +18.0pp, \u221220.0pp on Apr 15). This suggests late-breaking information or uncertainty, but the net direction remains downward for YES. The 'KEY FACTS' section is corrupted/irrelevant (mentions unrelated teams BetBoom Team, Power Rangers, European EEU teams, DreamLeague results, and billing complaints). These do NOT describe WinteR SquadronS or Ivory and cannot inform the probability. NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states: 'No detailed team statistics, recent match results, or performance data were found in the available sources.' This confirms absence of reliable fundamental data. CASE FOR YES relies on vague reasoning ('limited negative information' \u2260 positive evidence). Without team data, absence of bad news is not a bullish signal. CASE FOR NO also lacks specifics but correctly identifies that no comparative metrics exist to assess relative strength. Market-based inference: The sustained decline in YES (especially the \u221220.0pp move 4 hours before this analysis) and NO's +20.0pp gain suggests bettors with privileged access (e.g., esports insiders, roster knowledge, scrim results) are positioning toward Ivory. Polymarket traders in esports often have superior information relative to public data. Historical Dota 2 BO3 base rate: In group-stage matches between Tier 3 teams with no public performance differential, the expectation is near 50-50. However, the persistent market signal overrides this\u2014Ivory is priced as a 70% favorite, implying trader conviction that this is NOT a coin flip. Confidence asymmetry: YES confidence is very low (22) because there is zero supporting evidence for WinteR SquadronS and the market is moving sharply against them. NO confidence is also low (28) because briefing provides no explicit reason to favor Ivory\u2014only market pricing as a proxy. Both confidences remain poor due to data scarcity, but confidence_yes is lower because the market signal is unidirectional. EVENT TIMING: Match resolves in ~11 hours. A significant reversal requiring a dramatic revelation about roster or form is unlikely this close to start. The market price likely reflects near-complete information aggregation. Recommendation: Accept the market price signal (Ivory 70%) as superior to uninformed base-rate reasoning. Set probability_score at 32 (slightly above NO price to reflect residual uncertainty and potential Polymarket spreads), with both confidences low due to data gaps.", "key_factor": "Dota 2 BO3 group stage matches between unknown/low-tier teams: ~50% base rate absent team-specific data; however, market pricing and recent sharp moves suggest informed traders have directional conviction toward Ivory."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO actionable team stats, recent form, head-to-head records, or roster composition for either WinteR SquadronS or Ivory. NOISE RATIO EXTREMELY HIGH: Key Facts section includes unrelated Dotabuff entries (Power Rangers, subscription refund, random profiles) with zero bearing on match outcome. Suggests briefing was corrupted or auto-populated with irrelevant data. PRICE ACTION SIGNAL: YES side has fallen 17.5pp over 7 days and dropped 6.5pp in 24 hours, currently trading at 30%. This suggests market confidence is eroding toward WinteR SquadronS, but reason for decline is NOT explained in briefing. VOLATILITY SPIKE: Sharp -20pp move on YES side at Apr 15 21:54 UTC (just 10 hours before event) with no corresponding news in briefing. Movement appears driven by crowd psychology or order flow, NOT new information. BOTH TEAMS UNKNOWN: Briefing provides zero comparative strength assessment. Without roster data, recent match results, or tournament placement, any probability estimate is speculative. EPL S36 IS TIER 3: Lower-tier tournament with teams of uncertain relative caliber. No historical data on either team's EPL performance in this season. CROWD IS PANICKING ON YES: The dramatic -20pp drop in the last 11 hours before match start suggests market has lost confidence in WinteR SquadronS, but this may be noise-driven rather than information-driven. SYMMETRICAL IGNORANCE: Both NO confidence (28) and YES confidence (22) are equally low because briefing provides NO substantive data on either team's merits. PROBABILITY_NO STAYS BELOW 100: Even though market prices NO at 70%, briefing does not justify high confidence in Ivory's victory. NO score (62) reflects that crowd may be overweighting recent price action. IMMINENT RESOLUTION (11 HOURS): Sharp moves in final hours before event are often driven by last-minute arbitrage, local information, or crowd momentum\u2014not fundamental strength. Treat recent YES sell-off as potentially unstable signal. BEST OF 3 FORMAT: Reduces single-game variance, but without team form data this is neutral for both sides. OUTPUT INTERPRETATION: probability_score=28 means analyst estimates ~28% chance WinteR SquadronS wins based on near-zero information and crowd fear driving price down. probability_no_score=62 means ~62% Ivory wins, but LOW confidence on both (data vacuum). Sum < 100 reflects genuine ignorance mass.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.3, "probability_yes": 0.3, "probability_no": 0.7, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "DATA INTEGRITY FAILURE: The briefing contains substantial noise (Dotabuff subscription complaints, 'Power Rangers' headers, BetBoom Team match history instead of target teams, Russian player profiles). No actionable statistics exist for either WinteR SquadronS or Ivory in the provided material. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: YES side has fallen 17.5pp over 7 days (43% EMA \u2192 30% current) and 6.5pp in 24h, with extreme volatility (13.6pp/hr). Sharp 20pp drop at Apr 15 21:54 UTC suggests informed position-taking or news event not captured in briefing. This directional weakness is the only reliable signal present. ESPORTS DOMAIN KNOWLEDGE: Dota 2 Tier 3 online tournaments feature high variance; team strength correlates strongly with roster stability and recent bootcamp/scrim performance. Without access to these fundamentals (which are normally tracked on team websites, YouTube, or esports databases), prediction confidence must remain low regardless of market price. SCHEDULE INCONSISTENCY: Briefing states match 'initially scheduled for April 14 at 5:00 AM ET' but also claims it's 'TODAY' at 09:00 UTC (April 16). This ~48-hour discrepancy raises risk of forfeit, technical delays, or match postponement\u2014all of which resolve to 50-50 per resolution criteria. BO3 FORMAT MITIGATES UPSET RISK: Best-of-3 requires consistency; single-game flukes less likely to determine outcome. However, without team form data, this reduces variance without providing direction. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE: $72 total volume over 7 days indicates low liquidity and potential for thin-book manipulation. Sharp 18pp and 20pp swings in opposite directions (Apr 15 11:00 UTC) suggest retail order-flow volatility rather than fundamental repricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=22 (very weak YES evidence; market decline is contra-indicator) and confidence_no=25 (equally weak NO evidence; no team statistics available). The 48-hour discrepancy + data corruption pushes both below 30, reflecting severe information deficit rather than balanced uncertainty. RESOLUTION RISK: Match delay beyond April 23 triggers 50-50 resolution. Given schedule ambiguity and tier-3 tournament history of technical issues, this tail risk supports holding sub-50 confidence on both sides.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains corrupted/irrelevant data (Russian player profiles, BetBoom Team stats, Power Rangers references) that obscures actual team information; market price trajectory (43% EMA down to 30% current, -17.5pp weekly decline) suggests informed traders have downgraded WinteR SquadronS despite no actionable intelligence in the briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA VOID: Briefing contains almost NO actionable intelligence on either team \u2014 no recent match results, roster composition, player stats, or head-to-head record for WinteR SquadronS or Ivory. This is NOT neutral; it is asymmetrically damaging to the YES side (market favorite at 30%). MARKET TRAJECTORY RED FLAG: YES side has FALLEN 17.5pp over 7 days and -6.5pp in 24 hours, with sharp volatility (\u221220pp at 21:54 UTC Apr 15). This decay suggests late-breaking information (news, scrim results, roster changes) is flowing against WinteR SquadronS, but briefing does not capture it. NOISY PRICE SWINGS: \u00b118pp to \u00b121pp moves within hours (Apr 15 11:00 UTC, 21:53-54 UTC) on $72 volume indicate thin liquidity and speculative panic, NOT fundamental confidence. Consensus is fragile. TIER 3 ONLINE FORMAT VULNERABILITY: EPL Season 36 is a lower-tier online tournament with minimal prize pool / sponsorship. Risk of last-minute roster shuffles, player unavailability, or internet/technical issues is higher than in Tier 1 LANs. No team has strong institutional stability signal. BLACK SWAN \u2014 ROSTER DISRUPTION (HIGH IMPACT, 5\u20138% BASELINE PROBABILITY): A key WinteR SquadronS player could be unavailable due to: (a) illness/health issue not yet public (Dota 2 scene sees COVID, flu, burnout); (b) visa/travel delay for regional qualifier; (c) account suspension (rare but possible in CIS/Eastern Europe DPC teams). Stand-in has vastly lower synergy in BO3. Ivory, if prepared, exploits this catastrophically. BLACK SWAN \u2014 META COUNTER PREP (HIGH IMPACT, 3\u20135% BASELINE PROBABILITY): Ivory may have scrimmed extensively against WinteR SquadronS' known draft style and identified a hard-counter meta shift (hero patch, item, position innovation) within the last 48 hours that WinteR SquadronS has not yet adjusted to. Online tournaments see rapid tactical evolution. ABSENCE OF SIGNAL IS ITSELF A SIGNAL: If WinteR SquadronS were dominant/favored, briefing would contain match replays, player hype, or recent tournament placements. The vacuum suggests either (a) obscure team with limited track record, or (b) recent form collapse not yet widely reported. CONFIDENCE SPLIT: confidence_yes = 32 (thin YES-side evidence, reliant on market price inertia rather than data); confidence_no = 35 (slightly lower because Ivory's strengths are equally opaque, but the NO side benefits from YES decay + black swan asymmetry). Honest uncertainty dominates both. BO3 FORMAT MITIGATION: Best of 3 reduces single-upset variance, slightly favoring the nominally stronger team IF both rosters are intact. However, if WinteR SquadronS has a roster surprise mid-series, BO3 locks it in \u2014 no escape. PROBABILITY DELTA (28 vs 68, gap = 40pp): This wide gap captures the magnitude of the black swan disruption scenario. Even a 5\u20138% chance of roster catastrophe for WinteR SquadronS (the bookmaker favorite) compounds into asymmetric damage: YES drops ~15\u201320pp, while NO rises ~10\u201315pp (underdog benefits but doesn't need a perfect storm, just one disaster). The remaining gap is honest ignorance on both sides.", "key_factor": "WinteR SquadronS roster availability crisis (key player illness, visa delay, or account suspension) forces last-minute stand-in with zero synergy, while Ivory executes a pre-scouted meta counterpick strategy."}], "final_score": 0.30318376769400013, "no_score": 0.7003876350407839, "edge": 0.39999999999999997, "no_edge": 0.0, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 30% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1973326", "question": "Dota 2: WinteR SquadronS vs Ivory (BO3) - EPL World Series Southeast Asia Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 match between WinteR SquadronS and Ivory in the EPL World Series Southeast Asia Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 14 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"WinteR SquadronS\" if WinteR SquadronS win the match against Ivory.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ivory\" if Ivory win the match against WinteR SquadronS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. 