{"run_id": "1e9b6780-6802-44f6-b07f-90d03ef14726", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T22:51:29.393719+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1979627", "question": "Valorant: AB3 Esports vs Contra (BO3) - VCL Latin America North: ACE Masters Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Winners match between AB3 Esports and Contra in the VCL Latin America North: ACE Masters Group B, initially scheduled for April 15 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"AB3 Esports\" if AB3 Esports win the match against Contra.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Contra\" if Contra win the match against AB3 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.2, "volume_usd": 156.48276199999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["86236354617724269998360643515995220447730496141483206325311055298528599168122", "21724679339362905221006313714116326466514800872787175869469718040597950062447"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES price has collapsed from 68% to 20% in last 24 hours (-31pp sharp move at Apr 15 10:00 UTC), suggesting new information favoring Contra has emerged. STANDINGS DATA: Contra ranks 2nd with 80 circuit points; AB3 Esports ranks 7th with 0 points \u2014 significant competitive gap favoring Contra. BETTING CONSENSUS: Pre-match odds of 1.25 for Contra indicate professional consensus on Contra superiority (~55-60% implied probability in standard odds framework). DATA QUALITY GAP: Briefing contains fragmented player statistics (paganus, dedmos, Peloncito stats) without clear team attribution or recency; unable to assess recent form or player performance trends reliably. MAP POOL ANALYSIS: Map bans show AB3 banning Breeze, Pearl; Contra banning Split, Haven. Remaining map is Corrode (likely Lotus/Ascent variant). No data on team map pool strengths, making ban strategy assessment unreliable. BO3 FORMAT: While BO3 creates comeback opportunities, this does not offset the structural competitive gap indicated by standings and odds. TIMING RISK: Match scheduled Apr 15 9:00PM ET (~8 hours from briefing timestamp of Apr 15 22:50 UTC). Market may be pricing in partial or full knowledge of match outcome if it has already started or concluded. CONTRA PROBABILITY: Standings (80 pts, rank 2) + odds consensus (1.25) + market movement (sharp +31pp drop in NO) supports ~70-80% true probability for Contra win. AB3 PROBABILITY: Zero circuit points and lower ranking suggest <30% win probability, but BO3 format and incomplete form data prevent ruling out upset entirely. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in Contra's advantage (confidence_no=62) based on standings and odds; lower confidence in AB3 assessment (confidence_yes=35) due to missing form data and potential match-in-progress reporting lag.", "key_factor": "Incomplete match data in briefing prevents comprehensive form analysis; match timing (TODAY, ~8 hours until resolution) means outcome may already be partially or fully determined but not yet reported to market."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = Contra) CASE: Contra ranks 2nd in circuit standings with 80 points vs. AB3's 0 points\u2014a decisive structural advantage indicating Stage 1 consistency and tournament-proven execution. Market pricing reflects this gap accurately: NO side at 80% aligns with Contra's dominant circuit position and professional betting consensus (1.25 odds favoring Contra). AB3's 0-point standing is not explained in the briefing as recent roster adjustment or early-stage variance; without such context, it signals fundamental competitive weakness relative to Contra. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES = AB3): AB3 has failed to accumulate any circuit points in Stage 1 while Contra secured 2nd place\u2014this is a 16x competitive gap, not margin-of-error noise. BO3 format argument for AB3 is weak: yes, BO3 allows comebacks, but this applies equally to any match. It does not explain how a 7th-place team beats a 2nd-place team when form data shows Contra ahead. Map selection/ban data (AB3 bans Breeze/Pearl; Contra bans Split/Haven) is incomplete in briefing\u2014we cannot extract strategic advantage from partial bans without knowing resulting map pool or team map-specific win rates. MOMENTUM & PRICE ACTION: YES side collapsed 31pp in 24 hours (from ~51% to 20%), mirroring a sharp move on Apr 15 10:00 UTC. This suggests real information flow favoring Contra, not algorithmic noise. NO side rose 31pp symmetrically, indicating market confidence in Contra is INCREASING as match approaches\u2014consistent with a clearly dominant favorite. RISK TO FAVORABLE CASE: Brief explicitly notes 'incomplete match data; full player statistics and recent form details are unavailable.' We cannot access individual player form, recent scrim results, or day-of roster news that could flip outcomes. However, absence of disruptive news (injury, substitution, technical issue) in briefing suggests status quo holds: Contra favored, AB3 underdog. CRITICAL TIMING: Event resolves TODAY (~8 hours from briefing timestamp). No time for major catalysts to reverse a 60-point circuit gap. Market has already priced in available information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) because circuit standings and betting consensus are objective, stable data. Lower confidence in YES (35) because we lack granular player/form data to justify why 0-point AB3 would upset 80-point Contra.", "key_factor": "Contra's commanding 80-point circuit lead and 2nd-place ranking in Stage 1 demonstrates sustained competitive dominance that AB3 Esports (0 points, 7th place) has not yet matched."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has collapsed 31pp in 24 hours (from ~51% to 20%), suggesting either late information arrival favoring Contra or sharp money fleeing AB3. This sharp move on Apr 15 10:00 UTC is suspicious timing given match is TODAY \u2014 suggests possible leaked scrim results or roster/injury news not captured in briefing. CONTRA'S FOUNDATION: Contra legitimately strong \u2014 ranked 2nd with 80 circuit points vs AB3's 0 points. This is not marginal; it reflects Stage 1 performance across multiple matches, not a single outlier. Professional betting odds (1.25 for Contra) align with market pricing (80%), showing consensus. AB3'S DATA VOID: Briefing provides zero recent match results, player statistics, or form data for AB3. The '0 points' could mean: (a) new roster shuffling/synergy issues, or (b) genuinely underdeveloped team. Without concrete evidence of competitive capability, claiming 'recent adjustments' is speculation. Confidence on YES side cannot exceed 32 due to this data gap. MAP VETO ASYMMETRY: AB3 bans Breeze + Pearl; Contra bans Split + Haven. This creates two 'leftover' maps (likely Bind, Abyss, Ascent/Haven-alternate). Data shows AB3 PICKED Bind and contested Abyss, but no win/loss record on these maps is provided. Veto strategy alone does not override 80-point ranking gap. BO3 COMEBACK POTENTIAL: BO3 format does allow 0-1 comebacks, but this is a general structural advantage, not specific to AB3. Contra, being the stronger team on average, benefits equally from BO3's reset mechanics if they drop map 1. TIMING & SHARP MONEY: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~8 hours. The -31pp collapse happened Apr 15 10:00 UTC. If sharps or insiders dumped YES, they likely have concrete information (scrim results, player substitution, illness) not in public briefing. Trust the price move. PLAYER STAT SNIPPET AMBIGUITY: Briefing includes fragmented player stats (paganus, dedmos, Peloncito with odd K/D ratios and win rates like 81%, 75%) but does NOT clearly attribute these to AB3 or Contra, and labels are incomplete. Cannot extract actionable intel. CONTRA'S CONSISTENCY ARGUMENT: 80 points across Stage 1 means Contra won multiple best-of matches against diverse opponents. AB3's 0 points suggests they either faced higher-seeded teams early (bad draw) or struggled across the board. Latter is more likely in round-robin format. UPSET REALISM: For AB3 to win, they must take 2 of 3 maps against a team that has proven consistent across Stage 1. Plausible scenarios: (1) AB3 exploits one map pool heavily (e.g., Bind pick), wins 2-0 or 2-1. (2) Contra underestimates and loses early maps. (3) Roster disruption on Contra's side (not mentioned). Without evidence for any, base case is Contra's dominance holds. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 32 because data on AB3 is sparse; confidence_no = 65 because Contra's 80-point ranking + market consensus + sharp money flow provides concrete weight. Not 85 for confidence_no because the briefing does not detail Contra's recent scrim performance or head-to-head history vs AB3. Ignorance mass (28 + 72 = 100) reflects full utilization but shows YES side is weak-footed.", "key_factor": "AB3's map veto strategy (banning Breeze and Pearl) combined with BO3 format's inherent comeback dynamics could exploit Contra's potential map pool weaknesses if AB3 can secure early map wins."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "CONTRA FAVORED: Contra ranks 2nd with 80 circuit points vs AB3's 0 points \u2014 a stark 80-point gap indicating Contra has already proven tournament success while AB3 has not. BETTING CONSENSUS: Pre-match odds favor Contra at 1.25 (80% implied probability), aligning with the 20% market price for AB3. Professional betting markets are typically well-calibrated on esports outcomes. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side has collapsed from 37% (EMA 7-day) to 20% (current), a 31pp fall in 24 hours. This sharp decline on Apr 15 10:00 UTC suggests new information (possible lineup news, scrim results, or expert reassessment) shifted confidence heavily toward Contra. UNDERDOG STRUCTURAL HANDICAP: AB3 starting from 0 circuit points in a group stage match against the 2nd-place team is a significant structural disadvantage. Historical base rate for such underdogs in closed-circuit esports is ~15-20% win probability. BO3 FORMAT MITIGATES ONLY PARTIALLY: While BO3 does allow comebacks, the gap in circuit ranking (0 vs 80 points) suggests skill/experience differential that BO3 format cannot fully overcome. BO3 typically adds 5-8pp to underdog win probability vs BO1. TIME-TO-REVERSAL IMMINENT: Event resolves in ~8 hours. Market price of 20% for AB3 would require a major upset from a team with no demonstrated circuit success. No time remains for new roster announcements or major tactical shifts to swing odds further. VOLUME AND LIQUIDITY LOW: Only $156 USD volume suggests thin market with potential for mispricing, but the directional consensus (80% NO, reflecting Contra dominance) is consistent across betting sites cited in briefing. DATA GAP ON RECENT FORM: Incomplete match statistics in KEY FACTS section limits granular recent performance evaluation. However, circuit standings are authoritative (Contra 2nd, AB3 7th/unranked with 0 points), reducing uncertainty on relative strength. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (Contra win) due to strong ranking signal, betting consensus, and market momentum. Moderate confidence in YES due to limited recent performance data on AB3 and structural underdog upside potential in BO3 format.", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant BO3 matches, the higher-ranked team (by circuit standing and pre-match odds) wins approximately 72-78% of the time. Underdogs with 0 circuit points against 2nd-place teams win ~15-22% of the time."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "SHARP MOVE SIGNAL: YES crashed 33pp on Apr 15 10:00 UTC; market interpreted breaking news as heavily favoring Contra (NO). This suggests informed traders saw something concrete about team status/form. CIRCUIT STANDINGS GAP: Contra ranked 2nd with 80pts vs AB3 ranked 7th with 0pts is a large gap, but gaps alone don't prove match outcome\u2014early-stage tournaments have noise. BETTING ODDS ALIGNMENT: Professional sportsbook odds favor Contra at ~1.25 (80% implied); Polymarket YES at 20% is LOWER than sportsbook consensus, suggesting crowd panic or access to post-odds intel. INCOMPLETE BRIEFING DATA: Player stats table (paganus, dedmos, Peloncito with KDA/win% metrics) is present but fragmented and lacks clarity on which team they belong to or recency. Cannot reliably infer individual form. BO3 FORMAT CONTEXT: BO3 creates comeback risk; single map advantage is not a guarantee. However, 0 circuit points for AB3 suggests systemic underperformance, not just unlucky bracket. NEWS SUMMARY BIAS: Case For YES focuses on Contra's ranking; Case For NO emphasizes map selection and 'early form'\u2014but early form weakness IS the 0-point circuit standing. Briefing does not identify recent roster changes or explain 0-point standing. MARKET MOVEMENT PSYCHOLOGY: Rapid 31pp swing in 24h, with high volatility (7.7\u20138.4pp/hr), indicates emotional repricing rather than gradual information absorption. Suggests crowd fear of Contra's strength or surprise intel. CURRENT LIQUIDITY: $156 USD volume is very low; small trades can move prices sharply in thin markets. Sharp move may reflect 1\u20132 large bets, not deep crowd consensus. TIME CRITICAL: Event TODAY, ~8 hours to resolution. Low time-to-reversal and thin volume mean current 20% YES price reflects recent sentiment spike, not necessarily fundamental reality. If AB3 has chance, it's now priced as a long-shot underdog. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Contra's ranking and sportsbook consensus support NO side (high confidence 62). AB3's 0-point standing and lack of visible form data weaken YES case (confidence 35 is appropriate). Briefing lacks detailed recent match results or player performance trends. DOUBLE-COUNTING CHECK: probability_score (22) + probability_no_score (76) = 98, near 100, reflecting tight two-sided market with modest vig. No unusual ignorance mass; both sides have signal.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Ranking gap is substantial: Contra 2nd place (80 circuit points) vs AB3 7th place (0 points) \u2014 indicates proven tournament success vs unproven competitor. Professional betting consensus heavily favors Contra (1.25 odds \u2248 80% implied probability), aligned with current market price of 80% NO. Sharp money movement: YES collapsed from ~37% EMA to 20% current in 24 hours (-31pp single move Apr 15 10:00 UTC), suggesting informed participants see Contra as decisively stronger. BO3 format does create 'comeback windows' \u2014 one map win keeps AB3 alive \u2014 but this is standard mitigation, not strong enough to overcome ranking disparity. Map selection data (AB3 bans: Breeze, Pearl; Contra bans: Split, Haven) is present but incomplete; unable to assess which team's ban strategy is superior without agent pool and recent scrim data. AB3's 0 circuit points could indicate either poor performance OR recent roster changes; briefing lacks roster stability data, limiting ability to assess upside scenarios. Tournament stage context (Stage 1 already concluded) suggests rosters are relatively locked and form is crystallizing; late-stage surprises less likely than mid-circuit volatility. Insufficient player-level statistics in briefing (partial VLR.gg data with incomplete agent/map breakdowns) limits micro-level prediction; relying on macro standings and betting consensus. Time-to-resolution: ~8 hours remaining; reversal from current 20% YES to victory would require unexpected roster issue for Contra or exceptional AB3 preparation \u2014 both low-probability given market sharp action. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence in NO (Contra favored) based on rankings + betting + sharp money; lower confidence in YES because brief lacks AB3 context (roster changes? new player? synergy building?).", "key_factor": "The 31pp collapse in AB3 odds over 24 hours suggests either late breaking roster/health news or sharp money recognizing Contra's structural competitive advantage; the BO3 format mitigates but does not eliminate Contra's ranking advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market price has collapsed 31pp in 24 hours (sharp move Apr 15 10:00 UTC), but the briefing provides NO contemporaneous news explaining this reversal\u2014suggesting either critical information was released post-briefing or the market is tracking a live match development not yet reflected in static data. The briefing is structurally incomplete: player statistics are fragmented/corrupted (paganus, dedmos, Peloncito stats show partial K/D ratios but no context on which team or recent form), and there is no mention of AB3 Esports' recent record, roster changes, or scrim results despite 0 circuit points being a red flag for either roster instability or a recently-formed/rebranded roster. Contra's 2nd-place standing (80 pts) is a stage-aggregate stat; no map-pool-specific win rates, head-to-head history vs AB3, or recent form trend is provided\u2014Contra could be declining into this match despite the points total. The map ban sequence (AB3 bans Breeze+Pearl; Contra bans Split+Haven) leaves Bind, Abyss, and Corrode (Lotus), but NO analysis of which team's agent pool or site-execution style favors these remaining maps is present in the briefing. BO3 format is intrinsically high-variance for an underdog; AB3 only needs 2 maps, and if map selection lands on an AB3 strength (likely Bind, which they picked), they have a genuine path to an upset. The 20% YES price is extremely suppressed relative to the briefing's statement of betting odds favoring Contra at 1.25 (roughly 44% implied probability for Contra in a 1v1 duel, not 80%)\u2014this suggests the market price is reacting to live information (match in progress or very recent developments) NOT present in the briefing. Absence of evidence is key: no recent match results for AB3 in this stage, no injury/roster roster updates for either team, no mention of coaching changes or tactical innovations (e.g. a newly-implemented agent meta or anti-Contra strat) that could flip a Group B match. If AB3 has a stand-in or rookie player for this match, or if Contra's key player(s) (paganus shows high impact stats but no context on whether he is playing today) are unavailable, the competitive balance shifts dramatically\u2014the briefing is silent on this. Confidence_yes is deliberately low (35) because the briefing does not provide sufficient evidence to reconstruct WHY the market moved -31pp; confidence_no is only moderately high (62) because Contra's 2nd-place ranking is real, but form decay and map-pool variance are unquantified.", "key_factor": "AB3 Esports executes a tactical meta shift or roster substitution (possibly a stand-in player or mid-tournament lineup adjustment) that exploits a specific map pool weakness in Contra's preparation, combined with a psychological momentum swing from a recent upset win that the briefing fails to capture."}], "final_score": 0.21855293274803358, "no_score": 0.7800156449571691, "edge": 0.5058823529411764, "no_edge": -0.09411764705882353, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 65% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0,