ull}
{"run_id": "dc79eb08-d8ee-4392-be24-e0cf2c42bd11", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T22:58:14.804022+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1962583", "question": "Valorant: EDward Gaming vs XLG Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between EDward Gaming and XLG Gaming in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 16 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EDward Gaming\" if EDward Gaming win the match against XLG Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"XLG Gaming\" if XLG Gaming win the match against EDward Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.515, "volume_usd": 3550.53881, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["23008568647592913720451447184928848010517345829502091053040600276174540835553", "2794081175060623172649411692718765429326465683874189408431459329262687654386"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.52, "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: The market resolves YES if EDward Gaming wins the BO3 match scheduled for April 16, 7:00 AM ET; NO if XLG Gaming wins. Resolution sources are vlr.gg or credible reporting consensus. EDG EVIDENCE (Supporting YES): Won recent matches 2-0 vs Trace (Apr 8), 2-1 vs Dragon Ranger (Apr 11), 2-0 vs Nova (Week 1). Already qualified for Stage 1 Playoffs per briefing. ZmjjKK nominated for Player of Week suggests individual star performance. XLG EVIDENCE (Supporting NO): Briefing contains zero performance data for XLG Gaming\u2014no recent match results, standings position, head-to-head record, or player information. Unable to assess XLG's current form, roster strength, or competitive positioning. MARKET PRICES: Current market YES=52% / NO=48% suggests near coin-flip valuation. 7-day YES trend is +1.5pp (slowly rising); 24-hour YES trend is -1.5pp (recent weakness). Sharp moves on Apr 13 (+5.0pp to +7.5pp) and Apr 14 (-9.0pp on NO side) indicate volatility but no clear directional consensus. CONTEXT GAPS: (1) Match timing ambiguous\u2014scheduled April 16 7:00 AM ET; briefing timestamp is Apr 15 22:58 UTC (~2.5 hours before scheduled start). Event is LIVE/IMMINENT. (2) 'Group Omega qualification/elimination situation' mentioned but specific bracket, seeding implications, and whether this is playoff-positioning match are unclear. (3) EDG already qualified for playoffs\u2014unknown if they are resting players or playing for group seeding. (4) No XLG roster, recent results, or meta-alignment data available. ASYMMETRIC DATA: Strong evidence of EDG's recent dominance (4 consecutive wins in group stage). ZERO evidence regarding XLG's capabilities, recent form, or matchup dynamics. This creates high uncertainty on the NO side despite market price parity. CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=28 (low) because while EDG shows strong recent form, lack of XLG data and unknown match context (qualification status, seeding implications, player availability) prevent confident YES estimation. confidence_no=25 (very low) because absence of any XLG performance data makes NO-side evaluation nearly impossible; any NO estimate is essentially uninformed. MARKET EFFICIENCY: Market appears to reflect genuine uncertainty given tight spread (52/48) and recent volatility. EDG's recent 4-0 record likely priced in, but XLG's unknown quality may be underpriced in NO side. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK (Secondary): Match occurs in ~2.5 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT); vlr.gg publication typically rapid for VCT events. Risk of cancellation, forfeit, or tie is minimal given timing. Name matching between 'XLG Gaming' and actual roster should be unambiguous per criteria.", "key_factor": "Briefing provides no head-to-head history, XLG Gaming recent form data, or comparative team strength analysis \u2014 outcome condition (match winner) cannot be reliably predicted from available evidence."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "EDward Gaming enters as the favored side (52%) with concrete recent form: 2-0 vs Trace (Apr 8), 2-1 vs Dragon Ranger (Apr 11), 2-0 vs Nova (Week 1). EDG's record across visible matches is 3 wins in BO3 format, with no losses shown in the briefing period\u2014this consistency over a 2-week span suggests stable team coordination and execution. EDG qualified for playoffs early (confirmed after Apr 8 win vs Trace), indicating they were among the top teams in Group Stage; qualification strength implies tournament-caliber play. ZmjjKK's nomination for Player of the Week (Week 1) points to individual star power and highlights a carry threat that can swing close maps or round sequences. The briefing explicitly notes 'XLG Gaming's current standings or recent match results from available information' are absent\u2014this data gap prevents any counter-narrative about XLG's form or momentum. NO side weakness: XLG Gaming appears nowhere in the match results, standings updates, or player highlights across Weeks 1-3; absence of a team name in a tournament briefing is a red flag for underdog viability. Market pricing (52% YES, 48% NO) reflects confidence in EDG but leaves room for XLG upside if XLG is an undervalued or rising team\u2014however, no briefing evidence supports this. Context clue: The note 'this may be positioning/seeding match' (since EDG already qualified) could cut both ways. If EDG is resting or prioritizing seeding over this specific match, intensity might dip, but 52% pricing already reflects some complacency risk. BO3 format favors consistency and team prep over single-map variance; EDG's 3-0 BO3 record (9 maps across 3 series) suggests depth and adaptability. Sharp price moves on Apr 13 (-7.5pp, +5.0pp, +7.5pp) indicate information or bet flow shifted confidence intraday, stabilizing at 52%; this intraday volatility is small relative to 1.5pp 7-day rise, suggesting market is settling on EDG lean. Confidence in YES is moderate (62) because: EDG form is clear, but XLG is a complete unknown\u2014if XLG is actually a strong team the briefing simply didn't capture, EDG's advantage could be narrower than raw form suggests. Confidence in NO is low (38) because: NO case rests entirely on absence of data (XLG invisibility in briefing) and speculative 'upsets happen' reasoning; no affirmative evidence of XLG strength, recent wins, or form. Probability asymmetry (58 + 35 = 93) reflects this: strong bullish case for EDG anchors 58, but weak bearish case (only 'XLG unknown / upsets possible') anchors 35 with significant ignorance mass\u2014the briefing simply does not empower NO confidence.", "key_factor": "EDward Gaming's demonstrated BO3 dominance (3-0 in recent matches) and early playoff qualification contrast sharply against the near-complete absence of XLG Gaming performance data in the briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains ZERO concrete information about XLG Gaming's record, recent form, head-to-head history, or current standings in Group Omega. This is the central weakness of the NO case\u2014we are betting blind on an opponent we cannot evaluate. EDG's APPARENT STRENGTH: EDward Gaming won 3 consecutive matches (Nova 2-0, Trace 2-0, Dragon Ranger 2-1) and qualified for playoffs early. Surface reading supports YES at ~60-65%. UNDERDOG REFRAME\u2014MOTIVATION & CONTEXT: EDG already qualified for playoffs by April 8. This April 16 match appears to be a GROUP STAGE SEEDING/POSITIONING match after qualification is settled. Teams playing for seeding rather than qualification often show reduced urgency, especially in BO3 (higher variance format). XLG'S HIDDEN ADVANTAGE: XLG Gaming is still fighting for qualification or meaningful seeding in Group Omega. Underdog desperation + EDG's potential motivation decline = upset vector. The briefing's silence on XLG may reflect that they are a lower-seeded or less-publicized team\u2014not necessarily weak, just under-reported. PLAYOFF-QUALIFIED COMPLACENCY: The briefing explicitly states 'EDward Gaming & Xi Lai Gaming qualify for the Stage 1 Playoffs' after April 8. An April 16 match for a team already qualified is a low-stakes positioning game. Historical pattern: playoff-qualified teams often lose momentum or field experimental lineups in final group matches. BO3 VARIANCE & XLG UNKNOWNS: Best-of-3 format has higher upset probability than BO1. Without knowing XLG's map pool, individual player form, or recent scrim results, we cannot confidently dismiss them. EDG's 2-1 vs Dragon Ranger (not dominant) suggests they are beatable by teams with specific map strengths. MARKET PRICING ANALYSIS: YES at 52% is modest for a team on a 3-0 run that qualified early. This suggests professional bettors already price in: (a) qualification-match complacency, (b) unknown quality of XLG, or (c) recent volatility (-7.5pp on Apr 13, then +7.5pp)\u2014signs of uncertainty and overreaction rather than settled conviction. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: I have concrete data favoring EDG (recent wins, qualification, Player of Week nominee). I have NO data on XLG's form, making my NO case speculative (motivation dynamics, complacency, BO3 variance). confidence_yes = 28 (weak data on underdog), confidence_no = 32 (weak counter-data on favorite's complacency). Both low, reflecting genuine ignorance about opponent. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: probability_score = 38 (slightly favors NO as upset play), probability_no_score = 55 (slight edge to favorite on surface form), sum = 93. The 7-point ignorance gap reflects: strong case FOR EDG's recent play (pulling toward YES) balanced against ABSENCE of XLG data and logical motivation/context concerns (pulling toward NO upset). Not a mirror split because briefing asymmetry is real. FINAL ASSESSMENT: EDG is likely still favored, but the briefing's complete silence on XLG + the seeding-match context + BO3 variance + potential complacency make 38% for NO (62% for YES) more honest than market's 52/48. The underdog deserves 5-10 points of respect given data gaps and structural context.", "key_factor": "XLG Gaming's complete absence from briefing data creates asymmetric uncertainty\u2014EDG's early playoff qualification may signal complacency or reduced motivation in a positioning match where XLG fights for relevance."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY (resolves in ~18 hours) \u2014 LIVE/IMMINENT event. Limited time for meaningful new information. Market is pricing this extremely close to a coin flip (52% YES vs 48% NO), suggesting genuine uncertainty. EDG FORM DATA: EDward Gaming demonstrably beat Nova Esports 2-0 (Mar 31), Trace Esports 2-0 (Apr 8), and Dragon Ranger Gaming 2-1 (Apr 11). Three consecutive wins, early playoff qualification, ZmjjKK nominated for Player of the Week. This is positive evidence for EDG. XLG FORM DATA: No match results, standings position, recent wins, or losses provided in briefing for XLG Gaming. Search results explicitly state 'Cannot determine XLG Gaming's current standings or recent match results from available information.' This is a CRITICAL DATA GAP. MARKET ASYMMETRY: YES side has 68 data points (EMA 52%, 7-day trend +1.5pp, sharp moves suggest news-driven trading). NO side has only 13 data points (EMA 49%, falling, single sharp move -9pp Apr 14). YES side is better-liquidity, NO side shows thinner order flow. This suggests YES accumulated more informed bets, but also that NO side lacks detailed backing. BASE RATE LOGIC: Without XLG Gaming's roster strength, recent form, or head-to-head history, this cannot be treated as a 'favorite vs underdog' matchup with confidence. In professional Valorant, evenly-matched group stage teams in BO3 settle near 50-50. EDG's superior documented recent form justifies a slight lean toward EDG, but the absence of XLG data prevents high confidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 35 (EDG form is clear, but XLG unknown prevents high conviction). confidence_no = 28 (XLG is unmeasured; even if they are strong, we have no evidence, so confidence in the NO outcome is even lower than YES). PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current market (52% YES / 48% NO) is nearly neutral. Given EDG's documented form advantage and absence of XLG performance data, a slight EDG lean (52%) is reasonable but not extreme. If XLG had published losses or weak form, probability should be higher (~65%+). If XLG had strong recent wins, it should be lower (~40-45%). RESOLUTION RISK: Match may be canceled, postponed >7 days, end in forfeit, or tie \u2192 resolves 50-50 per rules. With <18 hours to event, cancellation probability is low (~5%), but non-zero. Does not materially shift probability. FINAL ANCHOR: Treat as 'documented strong recent form team (EDG) vs unmeasured opponent (XLG)' in a group stage BO3. Historical frequency suggests ~55-58% for the documented stronger team, but data gaps on both sides warrant conservative positioning near market (52%).", "key_factor": "In professional Valorant group stage BO3 matches between teams of comparable seeding, the favorite (team with superior recent form) wins ~58-62% of the time; evenly-matched teams resolve near 50-50."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "EDward Gaming shows strong recent form: 2-0 vs Trace (Apr 8), 2-1 vs Dragon Ranger (Apr 11), 2-0 vs Nova (Week 1). This is the primary YES-side signal. EDG qualified for playoffs early (confirmed after beating Trace 2-0), suggesting sustained competitive strength across group stage. ZmjjKK Player of Week nomination indicates individual star power on EDG roster. Market price at 52% YES is ONLY +1.5pp above 50% over 7 days despite EDG's undefeated recent record \u2014 suggests undervaluation of EDG's form. XLG Gaming: briefing contains ZERO performance data, recent results, standings position, or head-to-head history. This asymmetry is critical. The search results are incomplete \u2014 XLG Gaming is mentioned only in market title; no tournament context, win-loss record, or roster strength provided. Current market appears to be pricing this as a coin flip (52-48 split) despite robust YES-side evidence and absent NO-side evidence \u2014 classic apathy/uncertainty. Price history shows minimal volatility on YES side (0.5pp/hr) vs higher NO-side volatility (1.0pp/hr), suggesting less confidence in the NO narrative overall. April 13 sharp move (-7.5pp then +5.0pp then +7.5pp) suggests brief fear followed by recovery \u2014 but recovery stalled short of full confidence in EDG. Match is TODAY with ~18 hours to resolution; low time-to-reversal window means psychological momentum from recent wins matters more than pre-tournament expectations. If XLG were a known strong team, briefing would likely mention it for balance; absence suggests either XLG is weaker/less notable or data gap is genuine. Probability_no_score set lower (35) than probability_yes (58) because NO-side narrative has minimal evidentiary support in briefing; confidence_no remains very low (28) reflecting true ignorance about XLG strength. Rational interpretation: EDG is favored by form but market has not aggressively repriced toward EDG despite lack of counter-evidence on XLG; leaves ~7pp of unexplained value on NO side (apathy).", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "EDward Gaming demonstrated consistent BO3 performance: 2-0 vs Trace (April 8), 2-1 vs Dragon Ranger (April 11), 2-0 vs Nova (March 31), establishing a 3-0 record in recent weeks. EDG qualified for Stage 1 Playoffs early (confirmed April 8 after beating Trace Esports), indicating superior group stage performance relative to most competitors. ZmjjKK Player of the Week nomination suggests EDG has at least one top-tier individual performer capable of carrying rounds in high-pressure BO3 formats. XLG Gaming completely absent from provided match results or standings data\u2014cannot confirm their recent form, map pool strengths, player roster, or even whether they remain in contention for playoffs. Group Omega context is mentioned but undefined; if EDG is already qualified, this match may be seed-positioning rather than elimination, potentially creating mental/preparation disadvantage for EDG despite their strength. BO3 format amplifies variance relative to single maps; EDG's consistent 2-0 and 2-1 wins suggest map pool depth, but lack of XLG intel prevents assessing upset risk. Market price (52% YES) reflects modest overweight toward EDG but not heavy confidence; suggests professional bettor uncertainty about XLG's strength or match context. Sharp movements on April 13 (+7.5pp spike) and April 14 (-9.0pp on NO side) indicate late information flow; NO side recent volatility may signal team news (roster, scrim reports, or qualification scenarios) not captured in briefing. Event is TODAY with ~18 hours to resolution; reversal of current 52% YES would require material XLG information (strong scrim leaks, roster advantage, or EDG complacency post-qualification) unlikely to shift market significantly at this stage. Insufficient data on XLG prevents high confidence on either side; confidence_yes elevated only by EDG's documented form; confidence_no capped by complete absence of XLG comparative intelligence.", "key_factor": "EDG's early playoff qualification suggests this Group Omega match may be seeding-dependent rather than elimination-critical, potentially reducing intensity and preparation investment versus a do-or-die scenario for the opponent."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides extensive EDG match history (3 recent wins: 2-0, 2-1, 2-0) but contains ZERO recent match results, standings position, or form trajectory for XLG Gaming \u2014 this asymmetry is a red flag for hidden underdog momentum. EDG qualified for playoffs early (stated: 'EDward Gaming & Xi Lai Gaming qualify for the Stage 1 Playoffs' after Week 2), suggesting this Week 3 Group Omega BO3 may be a seeding/positioning match with lowered motivation or prep intensity vs a team fighting for qualification. Market pricing is near-perfect 52-48 split despite heavy YES-side information advantage in briefing \u2014 suggests informed traders see genuine symmetry that headline stats mask; retail YES bias may be overweighting EDG's recent wins. 24-hour volatility spike on NO side (-9.0pp on Apr 14 01:00 UTC) suggests late intel shift favoring XLG that was not subsequently reversed; this timing (less than 24h before match) hints at roster/tactical news reaching insiders before public. Briefing explicitly states 'specific details about an EDward Gaming vs XLG Gaming BO3 matchup are not clearly present in the provided data' \u2014 both teams' map pool compatibility, head-to-head history, and XLG's recent form are completely opaque. EDG's Player of the Week nomination (ZmjjKK) is Week 1 accolade; no Week 3 performance highlights provided, while XLG Gaming mentions are entirely absent \u2014 absence-of-signal suggests either tactical secrecy or a team not tracked in main reporting. VCT China Group Omega context is mentioned but 'specific bracket details unclear' \u2014 the tournament structure itself is ambiguous, raising risk of meta shifts, map vetoes favoring underdog styles, or seeding advantages not reflected in aggregate stats. BO3 format creates volatility: even a 60-40 favorite wins only ~65% of BO3s; EDG's recent wins are 2-0 and 2-1 (not dominant sweeps), suggesting inconsistent map performance that a prepared XLG could exploit. 18-hour window to match is extremely tight for major roster changes, but illness, last-minute substitution, or visa/travel issues for a key player are low-probability (~2-3%) but high-impact events that flip BO3 odds by 15-25pp instantly. Market shows YES rising 1.5pp over 7 days despite today's -1.5pp 24h dip \u2014 suggests peak retail enthusiasm may have faded, leaving smart money at near-fair value; this is consistent with 50-50 inherent match-up.", "key_factor": "XLG Gaming fields a roster substitution or tactical meta-shift that neutralizes EDG's recent map pool strength, or EDG experiences a critical player injury/illness in the 18 hours before match time that forces a stand-in into a playoff-positioning BO3."}], "final_score": 0.5387493793093604, "no_score": 0.47420536669207514, "edge": 0.1908823529411765, "no_edge": 0.22088235294117653, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 41% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7058823529411765, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0636648068265058, "The Bull": 0.950653498715379, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516341554855095, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0694119332632872, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0635895169605216, "The Contrarian": 1.0694119332632872, "The Bear": 0.7316341554855095}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1962583", "question": "Valorant: EDward Gaming vs XLG Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between EDward Gaming and XLG Gaming in the VCT China Group O