{"run_id": "a0e643bf-02b8-4754-83f4-9da00439b5a6", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T22:59:50.006641+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1979622", "question": "Valorant: LYON vs Tezcat Gaming (BO3) - VCL Latin America North: ACE Masters Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Winners match between LYON and Tezcat Gaming in the VCL Latin America North: ACE Masters Group A, initially scheduled for April 15 at 6:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LYON\" if LYON win the match against Tezcat Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Tezcat Gaming\" if Tezcat Gaming win the match against LYON.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.945, "volume_usd": 1860.7767649999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["93298233377292174866539472721869901931581722964529869136577269452140228886065", "66671225859831278535926116102014238833428780792966953411236737528408635348182"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.88, "probability_yes": 0.88, "probability_no": 0.12, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: The market resolves to 'LYON' if LYON wins the BO3 match; 'Tezcat Gaming' if Tezcat wins. Tie/forfeit/cancellation resolves 50-50. CRITICAL TIMING ISSUE: Briefing timestamp is 2026-04-15 22:59 UTC; match was scheduled for April 15 at 6:00 PM ET (April 15 22:00 UTC). The match should have begun ~1 hour before briefing time and likely concluded by now. Market END DATE is April 16 04:00 UTC (~5 hours from briefing), suggesting resolution window is open but match is likely COMPLETE. SHARP MARKET MOVES SUGGEST OUTCOME CLARITY: The briefing shows YES side rose +43.5pp at Apr 15 22:58 UTC (one minute before briefing timestamp), and NO side fell -9.5pp at same moment. This pattern is consistent with market repricing after match results became known, not pre-match speculation. LYON DOMINANCE IN REGULAR SEASON: LYON finished 7-0 (+77 round differential) vs Tezcat's 4-3 (+38 differential). This 3-game win margin and +39 round differential advantage is substantial and supports LYON being strong favorites. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Briefing states 'The match results show LYON defeating Tezcat Gaming 2-0 in a previous BO3 encounter during the playoffs stage.' If this was a prior playoff match (not today's match), it strongly suggests LYON has demonstrated direct superiority. RATING DIFFERENTIAL: VLR.gg team rankings show LYON at 2000 rating vs Tezcat at 1734 rating (266-point gap), placing LYON #1 and Tezcat #3. This aligns with the regular season performance gap. UNDERDOG UPSET RISK (MODERATED): While BO3 format and map veto allow upsets, Tezcat's mid-table seeding (2nd in regular season but 3rd in ACE Masters qualification) and previous 0-2 loss to LYON suggest upset probability is low (~12%). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence_yes is 82 because briefing strongly supports LYON dominance across multiple metrics (record, differential, ratings, head-to-head). Confidence_no is 45 because the briefing provides no substantive evidence for Tezcat winning\u2014only generic 'playoffs are unpredictable' reasoning without specific Tezcat strengths or game plans. NO EVIDENCE OF MATCH CANCELLATION OR FORFEIT: The briefing provides no indication of cancellation, delay, or forfeit conditions being triggered. Both teams are confirmed as ACE Masters participants. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK IS MINIMAL: vlr.gg typically publishes Valorant results within 1-2 hours of match conclusion. The 2-hour fallback to 'credible reporting' is unlikely to matter given vlr.gg's reliability in esports coverage.", "key_factor": "Briefing data indicates match may have already occurred (EVENT TIMING: TODAY, END DATE 5 hours from briefing timestamp); if match has concluded, outcome is deterministic and confidence should reflect actual result clarity, not pre-match uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.92, "probability_yes": 0.92, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.94, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "LYON's regular season dominance is stark: 7-0 record vs. Tezcat's 4-3, with a +77 round differential vs. +38. This 39-point round differential gap reflects sustained outplaying across 10 maps\u2014not variance. Head-to-head recent result: LYON defeated Tezcat Gaming 2-0 in a playoff BO3 earlier in this tournament. This is direct, proximate evidence of skill gap in the exact format (BO3) and stakes (playoffs) matching today's match. VLR.gg ranking disparity: LYON at 2000 rating (#1) vs. Tezcat at 1734 (#3) quantifies a 266-point skill gap\u2014substantial in competitive Valorant. Market pricing reflects the briefing: YES at 94% is NOT an overreaction; it is well-supported by the data. The 7-day rise (+42.5pp) and 24-hour surge (+43.0pp) occurred as more traders integrated the head-to-head result and standings data. Tezcat Gaming's case is thin: their 4-3 record and +38 differential are respectable but substantially weaker than LYON. Qualification for ACE Masters does not imply competitive parity with the 7-0 seed. Playoff upsets do occur (NO's theoretical case), but require underdog catalyst: superior preparation, map counters, or LYON complacency. None are evidenced in the briefing. LYON shows no signs of letdown; Tezcat shows no new tactical innovation post-2-0 loss. Map veto dynamics (BO3 format) do favor preparation, but LYON's 7-0 record spans diverse map pools and opponents. No specific Tezcat map exploit is documented. Timing concern: Event resolves TODAY in ~5 hours (04:00 UTC Apr 16). At 94% YES pricing with low remaining time, sharp traders would have exploited any 2-3% mispricing already. Stability near 94% suggests market efficiency. Volatility history shows two large swings on Apr 15: +25.5pp (03:00 UTC), -34.0pp (22:00 UTC), +43.5pp (22:58 UTC). The final 43.5pp surge likely corresponds to integration of the 2-0 head-to-head result. No subsequent data has moved the market below 85%. Confidence asymmetry: YES case is data-rich (standings, H2H, ratings, form). NO case relies on generic 'playoff upsets happen' logic without briefing-specific catalysts. Confidence_yes = 94; confidence_no = 35 reflects this gap. Probability_no_score set at 18 (not 6 = 100-94) because independent evaluation of Tezcat's chances requires: (1) recent H2H loss factored in (major weight), (2) generic upset probability, (3) unknown team intangibles. 18% reflects low but non-negligible tail risk; does not assume perfect correlation with YES probability.", "key_factor": "LYON's perfect 7-0 regular season record with +77 round differential and recent 2-0 playoff victory over Tezcat Gaming establishes overwhelming structural dominance."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.08, "probability_yes": 0.08, "probability_no": 0.88, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "LYON enters as heavy favorite: 7-0 regular season, +77 round differential, #1 seed (2000 VLR rating vs Tezcat 1734), and previous 2-0 playoff victory over Tezcat. Market pricing at 94% reflects this dominance rationally. Critical data gap on Tezcat: briefing provides NO recent form data, map preferences, roster changes, or player-level analysis for Tezcat Gaming. Only summary stats available: 4-3 record, +38 differential, #2 seed qualification. Upset structural factors: BO3 format has inherent variance; map veto/agent selection can neutralize rating disparities; Tezcat qualified for ACE Masters (tournament seeding at stake, not inclusion). Single-elimination stakes may favor underdogs with confidence. LYON vulnerabilities (minor but present): Perfect regular season may create psychological pressure or complacency; previous 2-0 victory suggests LYON adapted well, but rematches often differ when underdog has time to prepare counter-strategies. No evidence of recent LYON form trajectory provided (improving or stagnating?). Tezcat's competitive position: +38 round differential is 49% of LYON's +77, indicating Tezcat remains tactically viable and not a bottom-dweller. 4-3 record shows ability to win matches against mid-tier opposition. Qualified for Masters suggests org/investment support. Market volatility and timing concern: YES price rose +43.5pp in 24 hours with sharp moves (+25.5pp, -34.0pp, +43.5pp Apr 15). This late-stage volatility suggests possible information arrival (roster confirmation, scrim results, or betting algorithm adjustments), but briefing provides NO news explaining the swings. Unusual volatility in a 5-hour window before resolution reduces confidence in market equilibrium. Missing evidence for NO: Briefing contains NO concrete recent performance data for Tezcat (no scrim results, no recent match outcomes, no player form indicators). Confidence in NO case is constrained by this asymmetric data gap\u2014high confidence in LYON's domination but weak confidence in Tezcat's inability to compete. Probability asymmetry justified: LYON's 7-0 + previous 2-0 victory + rating gap + +77 differential provide overwhelming evidence for YES. Tezcat's case rests on 'BO3 variance + unkown form + playoff unpredictability'\u2014credible but thin. Leaving ~12pp ignorance mass (8 + 88 \u2260 100) reflects confidence asymmetry: strong data favors YES, weak data against NO. Realistic upset path: Tezcat's coaching staff identified LYON map vetoes and agent strategy; players executed disciplined executes on Tezcat's favored maps; one player (likely IGL or duelist) had career-level series performance; LYON's star player underperformed or faced life circumstances. Plausible but low-probability scenario. Time-to-reversal: Event occurs TODAY in ~5 hours. Market has priced in nearly all available public information (LYON's seed, record, rating, head-to-head). Very little new data can arrive in 5 hours. Probability reversal from 94% to <50% would require breaking news (LYON roster issue, map pool vulnerability exposed). Low likelihood given time window.", "key_factor": "Tezcat Gaming's proven playoff qualification and competitive +38 round differential provide structural foundation for upset in high-variance BO3 format despite LYON's dominant regular season."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "LYON dominance is overwhelming: 7-0 regular season vs Tezcat's 4-3, with +77 round differential vs +38. This ~2:1 quality gap is historically correlated with 75-80% win probability for the favorite in BO3 format. Head-to-head precedent: LYON defeated Tezcat 2-0 in their recent playoff matchup. Repeated matchups in the same season show stable win probability; rematches rarely reverse dominant results (historical reversal rate ~10-15%). Ranking disparity: LYON (2000 rating, #1 seed) vs Tezcat (1734 rating, #2 seed) suggests ~266-point skill gap. In Valorant, this translates to ~3-5% additional win rate advantage. Market price ($0.94 YES) reflects rational belief in LYON dominance, supported by underlying data. Sharp recent moves (+43.5pp in last 2 hours) suggest informed traders confident in LYON, not pure speculation. Tezcat's NO case is weak: 4-3 record and +38 differential indicate they are clearly the inferior team, not an underdog with hidden strengths. Playoff upset potential exists (~20%) but Tezcat shows no special map pool advantages or recent form spike to justify lower LYON odds. Event timing (TODAY, ~5 hours to resolution) means extremely limited time for reversal narrative. Any remaining uncertainty reflects pre-match unknowns (roster changes, psychological state), not emerging evidence. Confidence_yes=82: Strong data alignment (record, differential, head-to-head, ratings) all point to LYON. No contradictory evidence in briefing. Confidence_no=45: Limited data on Tezcat's countervailing strengths. Briefing provides no evidence of recent form shifts, map-specific advantages, or personnel changes favoring Tezcat. Uncertainty reflects general playoff volatility, not Tezcat-specific factors. Probability_score=78 reflects: ~80% base rate for 7-0 seed vs 4-3 opponent, adjusted downward slightly (~-2pp) for playoff single-elimination volatility and the small chance of unexpected roster/health disruptions.", "key_factor": "In professional esports BO3 playoffs, the higher seed (especially one with 7-0 regular season record) wins approximately 75-80% of the time against mid-table opponents. Head-to-head dominance (prior 2-0 victory) increases favorite win rate to 78-85%. Upset probability in single-elimination playoffs is ~15-25%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.88, "probability_yes": 0.88, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "LYON's dominance is overwhelming: 7-0 undefeated regular season vs Tezcat's 4-3, +77 vs +38 round differential \u2014 a massive skill gap Direct head-to-head evidence: briefing explicitly states LYON defeated Tezcat 2-0 in their playoff matchup, establishing recent precedent Rating disparity: LYON ranked #1 (2000) vs Tezcat #3 (1734) on VLR.gg \u2014 266-point gap indicates structural superiority Market price at 94% YES reflects rational appraisal of the evidence, not irrational exuberance \u2014 the data justifies high confidence Crowd psychology: 43pp surge in last 24hrs (+43.5pp at 22:58 UTC Apr 15) suggests sharp move triggered by match confirmation or pre-game intel, not panic buying Upside surprise factor minimal: Tezcat would need to overcome a team that has already beaten them 2-0 AND maintain zero-loss season form \u2014 asymmetric burden Playoff upset logic weak here: single-elimination stakes *can* produce upsets, but only if the teams are closer in skill; 7-0 vs 4-3 is not close NO-side confidence kept low (35) because briefing lacks deep counter-narrative: no injuries, roster changes, or systemic weaknesses mentioned for LYON; no breakout form or meta-shift favoring Tezcat Timing note (TODAY, ~5 hours): market is liquid and near resolution; 94% price unlikely to be a structural mispricing \u2014 traders have full information access Volume ($1,861) is modest, but sharp moves (\u00b143pp) suggest informed traders reacted to available data; not thin-market noise Conclusion: Market vibe is rational greed, not irrational. LYON's dominance is real and priced correctly. NO side left at 18 reflects genuine but low upset probability.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.88, "probability_yes": 0.88, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "LYON dominance baseline: 7-0 record with +77 round differential is undefeated season performance; Tezcat at 4-3 with +38 differential places them 3 wins and 39 rounds behind\u2014this is a massive skill gap in a bo3 format. Head-to-head precedent: LYON already defeated Tezcat Gaming 2-0 in playoff stage according to briefing\u2014same tournament, same stage, same opponent, demonstrating clear read on matchup dynamics. Rating asymmetry: VLR.gg team rankings show LYON at 2000 vs Tezcat at 1734\u2014a 266-point gap (13.3% differential) is substantial in esports team performance metrics. Seeding strength: In double-elimination playoffs with bo3 format, the 1st seed vs 2nd seed matchup typically favors top seed; LYON's perfect regular season form reduces likelihood of collapse. Upset mechanics are real but constrained: While map veto and agent selection allow for tactical exploits, the 7-0 team has already proven they can beat this 4-3 opponent directly in bo3 format, suggesting no hidden counter-strategy gap. Market price asymmetry: YES at 94% is very high; however, this is justified by the empirical evidence (prior 2-0 result + dominant seeding differential). The 6% NO price reflects genuine uncertainty, not misprice. Sharp price movements (\u00b143.5pp last hour): High volatility near match start suggests information arrival or positioning by sharp bettors; late-stage rallies to 94% YES are typical when pre-match confidence crystallizes. This does NOT suggest a hidden upset risk; it suggests market efficiency updating toward the empirically dominant team. Confidence moderation rationale: Although evidence strongly favors LYON, confidence_no is capped at 35 because (a) no detailed Tezcat roster or recent scrimmage data provided, (b) psychological factors (overconfidence, tilt management) are unmeasurable in esports, and (c) single bo3 match retains irreducible ~5-15% upset variance even against superior opponents. Timing context: Match TODAY (~5 hours to start) means any late roster news, player health issues, or strategic leaks would manifest in the price movements already observed. The sustained 88-94% YES pricing reflects market-embedded information; reversal would require extraordinary (illness, forfeiture, walkover) which resolution rules would reset to 50-50. No evidence of anomaly: Briefing contains no red flags (cancellation risk, protest pending, technical issues) that would support NO probability above baseline upset rate.", "key_factor": "LYON's 7-0 regular season dominance with +77 round differential and prior 2-0 playoff head-to-head victory represent exceptionally strong predictive signals in a competitive format where seeding consistency typically translates to playoff performance; however, the sharp +43.5pp price movement 5 hours before match start and volatile overnight trading patterns suggest possible late information asymmetry (roster changes, health issues, or strategic scrims) that warrant confidence moderation."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "LYON's dominance is overwhelming: 7-0 regular season, +77 round diff vs Tezcat's 4-3 and +38 diff; prior 2-0 playoff win establishes direct precedent. Market pricing at 94% YES reflects consensus confidence in LYON, but sharp volatility (\u00b125-43pp swings on Apr 15) signals active disagreement or late information flow \u2014 potential edge for NO side if key intel (roster changes, meta shifts, morale) reached sophisticated bettors late. BLACK SWAN: Tezcat Gaming may have discovered or prepared a specific anti-LYON tactical composition or map-veto strategy during the multi-day playoff window. BO3 format (not BO1) gives map vetoes and champion selection outsized leverage; if Tezcat has identified a 1-2 map pocket where LYON is weak, they can force a decider. Playoff psychology: LYON's perfect record creates expectation weight and potential complacency; Tezcat, as underdog with nothing to lose, may exhibit peak focus. Qualifier-already-secured status (both teams in ACE Masters) reduces motivation asymmetry but does not eliminate it. Market structure weakness: low volume ($1,861 USD) and thin NO side (5 data points vs 27 for YES) suggest incomplete price discovery. Late sharp moves (+43.5pp YES @ 22:58 UTC) could reflect coordinated sharp action or late public consensus shift, not true probability shift. NO side confidence is lower (55 vs 72) because Tezcat's weaker regular season form and 0-2 prior result create genuine competitive headwind. However, BO3 tactical upside and playoff volatility are real \u2014 confidence on YES side is also capped by lack of direct pre-match interviews, roster health status, or post-veto analysis. Event timing is TODAY (~5 hours to resolution): at this stage, share prices will trade near $0.01/$0.99 once the match starts and outcome becomes clear in early maps. Reversal requires Tezcat to win 2 maps before LYON wins 2, an enormous ask given the gap \u2014 but not logically impossible if a single roster absence or tactical surprise manifests. Absence-of-signal: briefing provides no recent injury reports, coaching changes, or player roster confirmations for either team. This silence is louder in a high-stakes playoff context. If Tezcat has a starter benched or LYON has a sub playing, market would not yet reflect it. Probability split (78/32) intentionally does not sum to 100: LYON's YES probability (78) reflects strong baseline evidence; Tezcat's NO probability (32) reflects meaningful playoff upside and tactical variability. The gap (10pp) captures the 'shock' scenario where a meta/roster factor swings the match.", "key_factor": "Tezcat Gaming executes a tactical meta shift or map-pool exploit (e.g., heavily favoring agent compositions or map selection strategies that counter LYON's established playbook) that capitalizes on playoff format unpredictability and recent sharp price volatility suggesting information asymmetry in the market."}], "final_score": 0.8358917979941458, "no_score": 0.2834565182772603, "edge": -0.23911764705882343, "no_edge": 0.6508823529411765, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES price too high: $0.94 (\u2264$0.91); near-resolved, max ROI 5.8%", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7058823529411765, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0636648068265058, "The Bull": 0.950653498715379, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516341554855095, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0694119332632872, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0635895169605216, "The Contrarian": 1.0694119332632872, "The Bear": 0.7316341554855095}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1979622", "question": "Valorant: LYON vs Tezcat Gaming (BO3) - VCL Latin America North: ACE Masters Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Winners match between LYON and Tezcat Gaming in the VCL Latin America North: ACE Masters Group A, initially scheduled for April 15 at 6:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LYON\" if LYON win the match against Tezcat Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Tezcat Gaming\" if Tezcat Gaming win the match against LYON.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.945, "volume_usd": 1860.7767649999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["93298233377292174866539472721869901931581722964529869136577269452140228886065", "66671225859831278535926116102014238833428780792966953411236737528408635348182"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["United States\nUnited States\nMexico\nMexico\nMexico\nColombia\n\nColombia\nColombia