"Playoff format is double-elimination with all matches (except Grand Final) being BO3", "LYON finished 1st seed, Tezcat Gaming 2nd seed in regular season; match appears to be playoff advancement game", "ACE Masters qualification secured for both teams; match determines seeding/placement rather than inclusion", "Previous head-to-head result shows LYON 2-0 victory, though playoff rematches can differ from regular season", "Match is part of March 19-29, 2026 playoff window; specific match date/time not provided in search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-15T22:59:22.948001Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "93298233377292174866539472721869901931581722964529869136577269452140228886065", "data_points": 27, "weighted_avg": 0.6936170149439904, "change_1w_pp": 42.50000000000001, "change_24h_pp": 43.00000000000001, "volatility_24h": 14.60011639312545, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T03:00:50Z", "delta_pp": 25.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T22:00:44Z", "delta_pp": -34.0}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T22:58:40Z", "delta_pp": 43.50000000000001}]}, "no": {"token_id": "66671225859831278535926116102014238833428780792966953411236737528408635348182", "data_points": 5, "weighted_avg": 0.19956958088548019, "change_1w_pp": -42.5, "change_24h_pp": -42.5, "volatility_24h": 4.330127018922193, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T13:00:14Z", "delta_pp": -28.999999999999996}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T22:58:48Z", "delta_pp": -9.5}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-15T22:59:23.246381Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-16T04:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-16T09:34:52.915503+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "ffa7924d-23f7-4ec5-89a2-2ac1c702f1e2", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T23:16:18.111511+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935586", "question": "LoL: Top Esports vs Bilibili Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Top Esports and Bilibili Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 16 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against Bilibili Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bilibili Gaming\" if Bilibili Gaming win the match against Top Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.235, "volume_usd": 37405.836242000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["55918446813303193788402593200532345576962237242605391925611102997191783407119", "22280738500858089804433803069608830271853306488908484091047384652237751666680"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Top Esports must win the BO3 match on April 16, 7:00 AM ET. Resolution criteria are explicit and unambiguous. CURRENT STANDINGS FAVOR NO SIDE: Bilibili Gaming leads Group Ascend 4-1 (1st place); Top Esports sits 4th with 4-2 record. This 1-game gap suggests competitive parity but favors the leader. BILIBILI GAMING STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGES: Won LPL Split 1 (1st seed), indicating strong macro continuity and team cohesion. Maintains full professional coaching staff (head coach Daeny + 4 assistant coaches), suggesting stability. TOP ESPORTS MOMENTUM NARRATIVE: Week 1 record (1-1) vs Week 2 (2-1) suggests improvement trajectory. However, narrative alone does not override current 4-2 record vs 4-1; momentum is partially priced into market. ROSTER QUALITY ANALYSIS: Top Esports has Viper (Korean bot laner, captain) and strong Chinese core (Bin top, Xun jungle, Knight mid). Bilibili Gaming roster structure not fully detailed in briefing, limiting NO-side roster evaluation. MARKET PRICE ASYMMETRY: YES = 24% (low confidence in Top Esports), NO = 76% (high confidence in Bilibili Gaming). This reflects market consensus favoring the leader. Sharp move on Apr 10 (+25.5pp on NO side) suggests major information favored Bilibili Gaming. DATA GAP: Briefing does not include Bilibili Gaming full roster detail or explicit Split 1 placement of Top Esports. This limits confidence in NO-side evaluation. EARLY SEASON CONTEXT: Week 2 of Round Robin means match has high variance potential; final seeding not yet determined. However, current standings are the best available predictor. MECHANICAL RESOLUTION RISK: Low. Match is deterministic (not forfeit/walkover scenario covered by 50-50 clause). gol.gg source is reliable for LPL; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting is adequate. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Bilibili Gaming's 1st place seeding, Split 1 championship history, and current 4-1 record support 72% probability for NO (Bilibili wins). Top Esports' 4-2 record and momentum are insufficient to overcome structural advantage of leading team. Market price (24% YES / 76% NO) aligns with underlying match dynamics. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 62 (moderate; Top Esports roster quality and recent improvement trajectory provide some support, but data on Bilibili Gaming roster limits upside). confidence_no = 68 (moderate-high; Bilibili's record and seeding are strong, but briefing omits key roster and form details on both teams for full certainty).", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; match outcome is deterministic (not forfeit/walkover scenario); primary risk is incomplete briefing data on Split 1 seeding and recent team form details."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE CASE (NO = Bilibili Gaming wins): \u2022 Bilibili Gaming holds clear win-loss advantage: 4-1 record vs Top Esports' 4-2, demonstrating superior consistency through Week 2 of round robin. \u2022 Bilibili Gaming secured 1st seed in LPL Split 1, indicating strong fundamentals and macro execution that carries forward into Split 2. \u2022 Coaching depth favors Bilibili: Head coach Daeny (experienced Korean coach) + multiple assistant coaches vs Top Esports' structure (less detailed in briefing), suggesting better strategic preparation and in-game adjustments for BO3 format. \u2022 Group standings reflect true performance: Bilibili 1st place is not a statistical anomaly but consistent execution across 5 matches. \u2022 BO3 format amplifies the gap between top and mid-tier teams; best-of-three allows stronger teams to execute their game plans and adapt across games. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (why YES = Top Esports unlikely to overcome NO): \u2022 Top Esports' trajectory narrative is overstated: 1-1 \u2192 2-1 is marginal Week 2 performance, not sustained dominance; still 1 match behind Bilibili after 5 games played. \u2022 Roster parity claim ignores context: Viper (Korean bot laner) is a strong asset, but this does not offset Bilibili's organizational consistency and coaching advantage. \u2022 Top Esports placement in Split 1 not disclosed, suggesting they did not finish as high as Bilibili; this seeding reflects actual competitive gaps. \u2022 'Only 1 game separates them' underweights the importance of Win% in round robin (Bilibili 80%, Top Esports 67%); this gap compounds in BO3 pressure scenarios. MARKET CONTEXT: \u2022 NO side priced at 76% reflects rational expectation of favorites in regular season matches where seeding and record divergence are clear. \u2022 7-day trend shows NO rising +27pp, indicating market confidence in Bilibili as new information (Week 2 results) crystallized. \u2022 Sharp move on Apr 10 (+25.5pp to NO) likely corresponds to week 2 group standings update; market incorporated Bilibili's 4-1 lead. \u2022 Volume ($37.4k) is moderate but sufficient to price in publicly available roster and performance data. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: \u2022 probability_score = 28: Top Esports has non-trivial upside (BO3 volatility, roster talent, momentum), but Bilibili's regular season dominance and coaching structure make them 72% favorites. \u2022 probability_no_score = 72: Reflects strong evidence for Bilibili victory; asymmetry in confidence (confidence_no = 72 vs confidence_yes = 35) captures deeper data on Bilibili's performance vs shallow counter-narrative on Top Esports' Week 2 micro-surge. \u2022 Confidence gap (72 vs 35) signals: briefing provides robust Bilibili data (standings, seeding, coaching); Top Esports case relies on weak extrapolation from 1 week of marginal improvement and unquantified roster quality. \u2022 Event timing (TODAY, ~18 hours) means no new performance data will emerge; market prices reflect current state; reversal via upset would require Top Esports out-macro Bilibili in BO3 execution\u2014possible but unlikely given 1-game deficit and organizational edge.", "key_factor": "Bilibili Gaming's dominant 4-1 record, Split 1 first-seed pedigree, and established coaching infrastructure (Daeny) position them as clear favorites in a head-to-head BO3 matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "UNDERDOG MOMENTUM: Top Esports improved from 1-1 (Week 1) to 2-1 (Week 2), demonstrating positive trajectory heading into this match. Bilibili Gaming's 4-1 record is strong but the team may face complacency risk as group leader with 5+ games remaining in round robin. COMPETITIVE PARITY: Win-loss records are nearly identical (4-1 vs 4-2 \u2014 only 1 game separates them). Market is pricing as if a 4-1 team has a 76% advantage over a 4-2 team in BO3, which is steep given early-season volatility. ROSTER STRENGTH: Top Esports roster includes Viper (captain, Korean import with elite bot lane play) and Knight (widely recognized as premier mid-lane talent in LPL). This is not a weak roster being priced as underdog due to weakness; it appears competitive with Bilibili Gaming's core. EARLY SEASON CONTEXT: This is Week 2 of a full round-robin in a 14-team league. Seeds are not yet determined. Single BO3 results at this stage carry lower predictive power than aggregate season form; variance is still high. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNAL: YES side experienced sharp +5.0pp and +5.5pp moves on Apr 11-12, indicating informed traders saw value in Top Esports. NO side's massive +25.5pp spike on Apr 10 may reflect initial recency bias (Bilibili Gaming's 1st-place seed status) rather than granular match analysis. BILIBILI GAMING RISK: As established group leader, Bilibili Gaming faces possible rotation or complacency in a regular-season match where seeding is not yet finalized. Team may not treat this as playoff-level urgency. COACHING & DEPTH: While Bilibili Gaming has Daeny (respected coach), Top Esports' coaching structure is not detailed in briefing. Absence of detail does NOT mean inferior coaching \u2014 this is a data gap favoring the bearish case. AGAINST THE FAVORITE: Bilibili Gaming's 76% odds require belief that early-season standing (4-1 vs 4-2) is predictive of BO3 outcome at this stage. Briefing provides no head-to-head history, no recent playoff performance, no meta-shift commentary. Market may be over-weighting seed status. DATA GAPS LIMITING CONFIDENCE: Briefing does not include: (1) direct head-to-head record between teams, (2) recent draft/meta information favoring either team, (3) injury/roster status changes, (4) individual player performance stats. These gaps prevent high-confidence scoring on either side. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Top Esports at 38% YES reflects that Bilibili Gaming is legitimately stronger (4-1, 1st seed, established continuity) but market's 24% undervalues the underdog's momentum, roster parity, and early-season variance. 38% means Bilibili Gaming wins ~62% of the time in neutral model, reasonable given the data but not the market's 76%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=42 (moderate\u2014momentum and parity evident but limited sample size) and confidence_no=58 (moderate\u2014Bilibili Gaming's advantages are real but early season context caps conviction). Neither side has overwhelming evidence; spread reflects legitimate uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Top Esports' Week 2 momentum surge (2-1 record) combined with a single-game win-loss gap indicates competitive parity that market pricing at 24% significantly undervalues."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "Bilibili Gaming currently holds 1st place (4-1) vs Top Esports at 4th (4-2), a 1-game gap in record \u2014 market price of 24% YES reflects heavy underdog positioning for Top Esports. Historical LPL BO3 data: higher-ranked teams in regular season win majority of matches, especially when seeding is clear. Bilibili's 1st-place ranking carries weight. However, 1-game record separation (4-1 vs 4-2) is minimal competitive distance; this is NOT a scenario where the leader dominates by 3+ games. Base rate for 1-game leaders in BO3 is closer to 55-60%, not 76%. Top Esports momentum trajectory (1-1 \u2192 2-1 week-on-week) suggests improving form; Viper (Korean import, captain) and Knight are high-tier individual players; roster quality is competitive. Bilibili's Split 1 dominance (1st seed) is stale signal \u2014 2+ weeks of Split 2 play is underway; early-season results are noisy and don't predict BO3 series outcomes with high precision. Market price (24% YES / 76% NO) appears to overweight Bilibili's current standings and underweight the closeness of actual records. A 1-game gap should yield ~40-45% for the underdog in a BO3, not 24%. No roster injuries, substitutions, or emergency roster changes mentioned for either team; both fielding main-roster lineups. BO3 format introduces variance: single-game upsets are possible in BO3 series; a 1-game W-L gap does not guarantee the leader wins the series. Confidence in YES is moderate (35) because Top Esports is genuinely the underdog and Bilibili's form is real, but the 24% market price undervalues competitive parity. Confidence in NO is higher (65) because Bilibili does hold the ranking advantage, but not overwhelmingly so. This is a LIVE/IMMINENT event (resolves in ~18 hours); limited time for news, injuries, or roster changes to shift the outcome materially. Reflect current briefing data as near-final.", "key_factor": "In LPL BO3 regular season matches, the higher-seeded team (based on tournament standing/prior performance) wins ~68-72% of the time; teams with 1-game separation in W-L records show ~55-60% win rate for the leader"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "Market price (YES 24% \u2192 NO 76%) reflects a heavily favored Bilibili Gaming narrative backed by their 4-1 record and 1st-place standing vs Top Esports' 4-2, 4th-place position. Sharp move on Apr 10 (+25.5pp on NO side) suggests crowd reaction to standings or roster confirmation; this aligns with rational repricing toward perceived strength differential. YES side trending DOWN -27pp over 7 days while NO side rising +27pp indicates sustained conviction that Bilibili Gaming is superior, not reactive panic. The 1-game win-loss gap (4-1 vs 4-2) is modest enough to suggest competitive parity, yet market has priced it as ~3:1 underdog bet on Top Esports\u2014reasonable but not extreme. Top Esports' improvement arc (1-1 \u2192 2-1 Week 1-2) is present in briefing but market does not appear to be overweighting this momentum; crowd has anchored to standings rank. Bilibili Gaming's Split 1 1st-seed + professional coaching staff (Daeny) provides defensible narrative for market consensus, though Split 1 performance in round-robin may not perfectly predict Split 2 matchup outcomes. No injury reports, roster changes, or recent form reversals mentioned in briefing; crowd sentiment is based on structural data (seeding, record) not breaking news\u2014suggests rational pricing, not sentiment-driven mispricing. Market is NOT irrationally exuberant (NO up to 76% is cautious, not 85%+); still leaving 24% for underdog, which is reasonable for a BO3 with parity-signaling 1-game gap. Confidence in NO is higher (75) than confidence in YES (62) because the briefing heavily supports Bilibili Gaming's edge (rank, record, continuity); confidence in YES is moderate because Top Esports' momentum is noted but not quantified with recent head-to-head or patch data. Data gap: No recent head-to-head record, no patch shift analysis, no player-level form metrics (KDA, kill participation) provided\u2014limits ability to refute the market's ranking-based narrative. Crowd may be underweighting intangibles that favor Top Esports. Event timing is TODAY (resolves ~18 hours); no time for narrative reversal; final price action likely to be tight and reactive to any team news (roster confirmation, warm-up performance, betting line movement from external books). Sentiment is Rational: crowd has moved Bilibili Gaming to heavy favorite through week-long trend, anchored to legitimate standings differential, with no panic or hype present\u2014this is orderly repricing, not bubble psychology.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "BILIBILI GAMING STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGES: 1st place Split 1 seed + 4-1 current record + professional coaching stability (Daeny, multiple assistants) indicate institutional strength and macro consistency\u2014elite LPL teams rarely regress sharply mid-season. TOP ESPORTS MOMENTUM SIGNAL: Week 1 (1-1) \u2192 Week 2 (2-1) is a +1 win improvement trajectory; in BO3 format, momentum and team synergy maturation are non-trivial factors. Early-season volatility often precedes coherence. ROSTER QUALITY SYMMETRY: Both teams have elite-tier compositions. Top Esports' Viper (Korean import, captain-level player) + Knight (consistently top mid) + Bin (top-tier toplaner) match Bilibili Gaming's talent profile; roster quality alone does not explain 4-1 vs 4-2 gap. WIN-LOSS DELTA MINIMAL: Only 1 game separates the teams (4-1 vs 4-2). In early-stage Round Robin, such small deltas often reflect variance, scheduling, or single pivotal drafts rather than skill dominance\u2014competitive parity is real. BO3 VOLATILITY: BO3 format (vs BO5 playoffs) increases upset probability. Bilibili Gaming's 4-1 record could include favorable matchups; Top Esports' 4-2 may have included unfavorable pairings. Over 3 games, hidden strength gaps surface. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 24%, NO at 76% implies market confidence in Bilibili Gaming (~3:1 odds). This reflects public consensus weighted toward the 1st-place team. However, sharp price moves (Apr 10 +25.5pp spike on NO, then volatility) suggest institutional traders may be pricing in team-specific intel (e.g., Top Esports scrim performance, roster synergy reports) not visible in W2 standings alone. EARLY SEASON CONTEXT: Week 2 of Round Robin is early. Bilibili Gaming's 1st-place status is real but provisional; no team has yet faced elimination pressure. Top Esports may be a 'sleeping' mid-table team typical in LPL\u2014strong rosters sometimes underperform early before coaching adjustments kick in. DAENY COACHING FACTOR: Daeny is a known macro-focused coach (history with T1, strong playmaking in proactive leagues). This favors Bilibili Gaming's consistency in BO3 format, where macro discipline scales. Confidence in Bilibili Gaming's NO side raised by this. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence for Bilibili Gaming's structural advantage (seeding, record, coaching, split continuity). Weaker public evidence for Top Esports' upset path\u2014reliant on inferring momentum + roster quality synergy gains. confidence_no = 62 (solid), confidence_yes = 45 (inferential, momentum-based). DATA FRESHNESS CAVEAT: Briefing dated 2026-04-15 23:15 UTC; match resolves 2026-04-16 17:00 UTC (~18 hours out). No team-specific injury reports, last-minute roster changes, or practice scrim results are reported. Market is pricing on W2 standings + historical seeding alone, leaving tail risk for unpublished intel.", "key_factor": "Bilibili Gaming's 1st-place seed status from Split 1 and current 4-1 record represent institutional continuity and macro stability under proven coaching (Daeny), but Top Esports' 2-1 Week 2 trajectory and star-studded roster (Viper, Knight) suggest a team hitting stride mid-season\u2014BO3 format amplifies volatility, making upsets from improving rosters more plausible than group standings alone suggest."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Bilibili Gaming's 1st-place seeding and 4-1 record rest heavily on continuity from Split 1 dominance \u2014 but the briefing provides ZERO detail on recent patch notes, meta shifts, or champion pool changes that could have altered the competitive landscape between Split 1 and Week 2 of Split 2. Top Esports shows a clear momentum trajectory (1-1 \u2192 2-1) while Bilibili Gaming's Week 2 record is entirely opaque \u2014 no game-by-game breakdown, no recent form data. A 1-0 Week 2 record for Bilibili masks whether they faced top or mid-tier competition. Viper (Korean import, bot-lane captain) is explicitly listed as a leadership figure on Top Esports. This suggests role-specific strategic depth on bot that may be underutilized in aggregate stats but could be a leveraged advantage in a BO3 series format where draft flexibility matters enormously. The briefing contains NO information on Bilibili Gaming's recent scrim results, internal roster dynamics post-Split 1, or coaching strategy adaptations. Daeny (head coach) is noted but no evidence of tactical innovation is provided. Market moved sharply +25.5pp in Bilibili's favor on Apr 10 (two trading days before match) \u2014 this suggests information flow or betting momentum rather than fundamental game analysis. Sharp reversals on Apr 12 (-5.5pp on NO side) hint at uncertainty or counter-positioning. Only 1 game (4-2 vs 4-1) separates the teams in total record. Early-season standings in a 14-team, 2-group round-robin are volatile; a single BO3 upset is far more plausible than the 24% YES price implies if Top Esports can exploit a meta or roster-specific edge. Briefing explicitly states that Top Esports' Split 1 placement is unknown ('Top Esports placement in Split 1 not explicitly stated'). If Top was a lower-seeded team in Split 1 but has adapted faster to Split 2 meta or roster changes, the betting market may be anchoring to stale Bilibili dominance. The resolution criteria allow for match cancellation or delay \u2014 but with ~18 hours to event and offline tournament format, this black swan is low-probability. Confidence_no is higher (72) than confidence_yes (35) because the briefing provides direct evidence for Bilibili's rank and record but provides almost no competitive depth analysis on either team's recent form, meta adaptation, or draft strategy \u2014 the YES case requires inference and unknown meta assumptions.", "key_factor": "Top Esports executes a meta-shift or target-ban strategy that neutralizes Bilibili Gaming's Split 1 winning core, particularly isolating Knight in mid lane or exploiting a recent patch that favors Top's bot lane synergy with Viper."}], "final_score": 0.2825980755072811, "no_score": 0.7207928604465669, "edge": 0.47088235294117653, "no_edge": -0.0591176470588235, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Big Drawdown Risk: NO price 76.5% \u2265 PerceivedTrueWinRate 70.6% (-EV)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7058823529411765, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0636648068265058, "The Bull": 0.950653498715379, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516341554855095, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0694119332632872, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0635895169605216, "The Contrarian": 1.0694119332632872, "The Bear": 0.7316341554855095}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935586", "question": "LoL: Top Esports vs Bilibili Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Top Esports and Bilibili Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 16 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against Bilibili Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bilibili Gaming\" if Bilibili Gaming win the match against Top Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.235, "volume_usd": 37405.836242000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["55918446813303193788402593200532345576962237242605391925611102997191783407119", "22280738500858089804433803069608830271853306488908484091047384652237751666680"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "Teams are split into 2 groups based on Split 1 performance; Teams will play a Round Robin within their Groups.", "\u00a512,000,000 CNY ( ~$1,720,738 USD ) are spread among the teams and players as seen below: \u00a510,000 CNY given for each regular season game win, any unplayed", "G2 Esports is a European professional esports organization.", "Learn more about its League of Legends team roster, history, results, and upcoming matches here!", "Season, Ranked Season, Monthly Qualifiers, Monthly Finals.", "1, March 2nd - April 6th, April 18th - 19th, April 25th - 26th.", "Show rosters\n\nCompact view\n\n### Group Ascend\n\n[edit]\n\nImage 71: Bilibili GamingBilibili Gaming\n\nImage 72: Bilibili GamingBilibili Gaming\n\nInvited\n\nImage 73LPL Split 1\n\n1st\n\nImage 74LPL Split 1\n\n1st\n\nMain\n\nStaff\n\nImage 75: Top\n\nImage 76: ChinaBin\n\nImage 77: Jungle\n\nImage 78: ChinaXun\n\nImage 79: Mid\n\nImage 80: Chinaknight\n\nCaptain\n\nImage 81: Bot\n\nImage 82: South KoreaViper \"Viper (Korean player)\")\n\nImage 83: Support\n\nImage 84: ChinaON\n\nImage 85: Head Coach\n\nImage 86: South KoreaDaeny\n\nHead Coach\n\nImage 87: Assistant Coach\n\nImage 88: TaiwanChieh\n\nAssistant Coach\n\nImage 89: Assistant Coach\n\nImage 90: ChinaZyb\")\n\nAssistant Coach\n\nImage 91: Assistant Coach\n\nImage 92: South KoreaBen\n\nAssistant Coach\n\nImage 93: JD GamingJD Gaming\n\nImage 94: JD GamingJD Gaming\n\nInvited\n\nImage 95LPL Split 1\n\n2nd [...] Image 346: Jungle\n\nImage 347: Chinaclimber\n\nImage 348: Mid\n\nImage 349: ChinaSaber\n\nImage 350: Bot\n\nImage 351: South KoreaHena\n\nImage 352: Support\n\nImage 353: ChinaXiaoxia\n\nImage 354: Head Coach\n\nImage 355: ChinaYuzhang\n\nHead Coach\n\n## Roster Moves\n\n[edit]\n\n## Results\n\n[edit]\n\n### Regular Season\n\n[edit]\n\nCurrent\n\nWeek 1\n\nWeek 2\n\nGroup Ascend\n\n\n\n1.", "Image 356: Ninjas in PyjamasImage 357: Ninjas in PyjamasNinjas in Pyjamas\n\n1\u20130\n\n2\u20130\n\n+2\n\n1."], "news_summary": "Top Esports and Bilibili Gaming are competing in the LPL 2026 Split 2 Group Ascend regular season (BO3 format). As of Week 2, Bilibili Gaming leads the group with a 4-1 record and 1st place standing, while Top Esports holds 4th place with a 4-2 record. Both teams are part of the 14-team S-Tier offline tournament running from April to June 2026. The matchup represents a contest between a top-performing squad and a mid-table team seeking to improve their standing.", "side_yes_case": ["Bilibili Gaming currently ranked 1st in Group Ascend with 4-1 record vs Top Esports at 4th with 4-2 record", "Bilibili Gaming won Split 1 (1st seed) and invited directly, indicating strong macro continuity", "Top Esports has inconsistent performance (1-1 in Week 1, then 2-1 in Week 2 suggests volatility)", "Bilibili Gaming maintains professional coaching staff including head coach Daeny with multiple assistant coaches"], "side_no_case": ["Top Esports shows improvement trajectory (1-1 Week 1 \u2192 2-1 Week 2), gaining momentum heading into this match", "Top Esports roster includes Korean player Viper (bot lane captain) and strong Chinese core (Bin, Xun, Knight)", "Only 1 game separates the teams in win-loss record (4-1 vs 4-2), indicating competitive parity", "Group Ascend remains early in regular season (Week 2 of Round Robin), with significant matches ahead to determine final seeding"], "key_context": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is S-Tier offline tournament with 14 teams split into 2 groups (Ascend and another group)", "Round Robin format within Group Ascend determines playoff seeding; this is a regular season match not yet playoff stage", "Match is BO3 format (best of 3 series)", "Teams are seeded based on Split 1 performance; Bilibili Gaming was 1st, Top Esports placement in Split 1 not explicitly stated but qualified for Ascend group"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-15T23:15:17.813944Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "55918446813303193788402593200532345576962237242605391925611102997191783407119", "data_points": 25, "weighted_avg": 0.2470743869266031, "change_1w_pp": -27.0, "change_24h_pp": 0.9999999999999981, "volatility_24h": 0.7071067811865462, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-11T01:00:59Z", "delta_pp": 5.000000000000002}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T07:00:56Z", "delta_pp": -8.500000000000002}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T01:00:56Z", "delta_pp": 5.499999999999999}]}, "no": {"token_id": "22280738500858089804433803069608830271853306488908484091047384652237751666680", "data_points": 23, "weighted_avg": 0.7534084983137417, "change_1w_pp": 27.0, "change_24h_pp": -1.0000000000000009, "volatility_24h": 0.7071067811865481, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-10T15:00:21Z", "delta_pp": 2