 victory is 9 days old in esports terms\u2014entire meta patches, hero nerfs, and tactical philosophies can shift. That match is a weak predictor if Nemiga has since adapted their drafting or laning. BO3 FORMAT RESILIENCE: Nemiga's 8-5 game record (vs Lynx's 8-2) in group suggests Nemiga steals individual games and adapts within series. BO3 is precisely where comebacks and tactical shifts shine. Nemiga's 1-2 loss to Yellow Submarine shows they can take games off top-tier teams. SEEDING ILLUSION: Lynx finished 1st with 10 pts (4-0, 8-2); Nemiga finished 3rd with 10 pts (3-2, 8-5). Same point total despite superior Lynx win-rate signals Nemiga plays closer, more competitive games. This is a sign of tactical parity, not Lynx dominance. SCHEDULE EXHAUSTION (Nemiga offset): Nemiga's recent 1-2 loss + 2-0 qualifier win on same day (April 11\u201312) might indicate fatigue OR confidence-building momentum. Market consensus assumes fatigue; the black swan is momentum. DRAFT SUSTAINABILITY: Lynx's dominant group-stage hero pool and draft patterns are now studied. Nemiga has 9 days of vod review + same-day DreamLeague testing to identify and exploit Lynx's predictable bans/rotations. NO PARALLEL VERIFICATION: Briefing confirms no head-to-head or warm-up data between April 3 and April 12 for this exact matchup. Information gap favors the underdog (Nemiga) because innovation is invisible until Game 1. MARKET OVERWEIGHTING SEEDING: YES at 63% reflects group-stage dominance and H2H, but 9+ days + parallel tournament activity + BO3 format all allow tactical evolution. Nemiga is under-priced if they've genuinely innovated. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence for Lynx (group record, H2H, seeding). Weak evidence for Nemiga's specific capabilities post-April 11 (no vods, no new match data except same-day qualifier). Confidence_yes = 62 (solid but not overwhelming); confidence_no = 48 (data gap on Nemiga's true form today).", "key_factor": "Nemiga Gaming executes a radical mid-series 