{"run_id": "933a3f06-6acf-4f67-8895-85f66de082d9", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:08:07.990251+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1997734", "question": "Counter-Strike: CYBERSHOKE Prospects vs megoshort (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between CYBERSHOKE Prospects and megoshort in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 16 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CYBERSHOKE Prospects\" if CYBERSHOKE Prospects win the match against megoshort.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"megoshort\" if megoshort win the match against CYBERSHOKE Prospects.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.56, "volume_usd": 116.39289499999998, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["70006578146150443506594060583520567100481743666298322286161622470453451443002", "71416711079233552989058663337085785325998800759623119928890867869789928607111"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.56, "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.44, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: A competitive BO1 match will be played on 2026-04-16, with winner determined by in-game performance. YES resolves if CYBERSHOKE Prospects wins; NO if megoshort wins. Tie/forfeit scenarios resolve to 50-50 per criteria. TIMING COHERENCE: EVENT TIMING = LIVE/IMMINENT (starts in ~1.9 hours). The briefing's past-tense match results (losses to Vexar/Enjoy on Apr 12/11, win vs Young TigeRES on Apr 9) are PRIOR encounters, not this market's outcome. These provide form context only. CYBERSHOKE PROSPECTS FORM: Mixed recent results\u2014wins vs Young TigeRES (2-0) on Apr 9, but losses to Enjoy (0-2) and Vexar (0-2) on Apr 11-12. GLuck SixSeven shows inconsistency (losses to TDK, mixed record). This suggests mid-tier competitive level with volatility in BO1 performance. ROSTER/COACHING CHANGES: dezl3bio joined Apr 13; Vert appointed coach Apr 13. These are extremely recent (3 days before match). Limited time for roster chemistry integration in a BO1 format. Could be positive (fresh talent/coaching) or negative (unfamiliar coordination patterns). MEGASHORT DATA GAP: No information available on megoshort's roster, recent form, win/loss record, player skill levels, or competitive standing. This is the dominant uncertainty. Cannot assess whether megoshort is a weak challenger or strong competitor. MARKET PRICING: YES = 56%, NO = 44%. This modest 12pp spread reflects market consensus favoring CYBERSHOKE slightly, but with substantial uncertainty. NO side prices suggest market sees meaningful threat from megoshort despite missing data. PRICE VOLATILITY: NO side fell 8.5pp over 7 days, with sharp moves (\u22129.5pp on Apr 16 11:00 UTC, +5.5pp on Apr 16 13:00 UTC). Suggests recent information shifted market dynamics, but briefing does not explain the moves. May indicate new megoshort roster info or odds adjustment, but this is not documented in briefing. BO1 ELIMINATION: Single-map format means no second-map adaptation. CYBERSHOKE's mixed form (can beat Young TigeRES 2-0 but lose 0-2 to Vexar) suggests high variance in map performance. Without megashort form data, cannot calibrate relative map strength. ESEA ADVANCED TIER: Both teams compete in ESEA Advanced Europe, confirming competitive parity. Parent org CYBERSHOKE Esports sits 6-6 in Season 47, showing middle-of-pack performance level. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: confidence_yes = 42 (CYBERSHOKE form is documented but mixed; roster changes very recent; no head-to-head data). confidence_no = 35 (megashort data entirely absent; cannot evaluate their actual threat level or recent form). Data asymmetry is severe. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Market price (56/44) is reasonable as a starting point given documented CYBERSHOKE presence but absence of megashort data. CYBERSHOKE showed ability to win BO1s but inconsistency dominates. With no megashort intel, defer to market pricing as best available estimate while acknowledging low confidence on both sides due to missing information. RESOLUTION RISK (SECONDARY): Match is imminent; forfeiture/cancellation/tie risks are low unless explicitly announced. Team name matching is clear (CYBERSHOKE Prospects vs megashort\u2014no ambiguity in identifiers).", "key_factor": "Severe information asymmetry: CYBERSHOKE Prospects' recent form and roster details are documented, but megoshort's current roster, recent form, and competitive level are entirely absent from the briefing, preventing meaningful comparative analysis."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.56, "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING AS ANCHOR: YES is priced at 56% vs NO at 44%\u2014a modest 12pp spread that reflects genuine uncertainty. The market's slight lean toward CYBERSHOKE is the strongest signal available given the information vacuum on megoshort. CYBERSHOKE ROSTER STABILITY: Core lineup (pixel, DAN9ARMATURA, SquEzxc, pleynnn, tw1sterzaza) has been together since Sep 2025 (~7 months), providing established team chemistry\u2014critical in a BO1 where adaptation is impossible. RECENT ROSTER INVESTMENT: Addition of dezl3bio (Apr 13) and appointment of coach Vert (Apr 13) signal organizational commitment, but the 3-day integration window before this match is extremely tight for meaningful synergy gains. DEMONSTRATED BO1 CAPABILITY: CYBERSHOKE won 2-0 vs Young TigeRES on Apr 9, proving ability to execute in single-map scenarios within the same competition tier. MIXED RECENT FORM RAISES RISK: Two consecutive losses (Vexar, Enjoy; both 0-2) in CCT Contenders just 4-5 days ago show CYBERSHOKE is inconsistent against stronger regional opposition. This is a 'Prospects' team competing in ESEA Advanced\u2014a sign of developmental tier. PARENT ORG MEDIOCRITY: CYBERSHOKE Esports parent sits 6-6 in ESEA Season 47, neither dominant nor struggling, but reinforcing that this is a mid-tier competitive environment with no guaranteed favorites. MEGOSHORT INTELLIGENCE VACUUM: Briefing contains ZERO data on megoshort's recent form, roster, coaching, or track record. The 44% NO price is essentially a 'we don't know' prior, not evidence of weakness. This asymmetry prevents confident forecasting either direction. BO1 VOLATILITY DISCOUNT: Single-map elimination format means random map pick, veto strategies, and tactical preparation become paramount. CYBERSHOKE's 3-day roster integration could be a liability or immaterial depending on map alignment. Confidence must remain suppressed. PRICE STABILITY DESPITE IMMINENT START: YES has been stable at ~56% for 24h (only -1.0pp swing); NO has been volatile with -8.5pp 7-day decline and sharp moves (\u00b19.5pp, \u00b15.5pp on Apr 16). This suggests NO bettors have been exiting, possibly due to updated team information not reflected in briefing, or liquidity-driven noise. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Match starts in 1.9 hours. For CYBERSHOKE to be <50%, a significant negative catalyst (roster issue, server problem, or new competitive intel) would need to emerge imminently. The tight window limits surprise reversals, but live-game uncertainty still dominates. RESOLUTION CRITERIA SAFETY: No forfeit/cancellation risks evident; match is scheduled and both teams appear active. Standard competitive resolution applies. BULL CASE SUMMARY: CYBERSHOKE's roster tenure, recent BO1 win, and market consensus support a slight YES lean. However, recent losses to stronger teams, lack of megoshort intel, and BO1 volatility prevent high conviction. Confidence is moderated by the asymmetry of available evidence.", "key_factor": "Market-priced slight edge combined with roster stability and recent coaching addition, but severely constrained by imminent BO1 format and lack of megoshort comparative data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR megoshort (NO): The briefing contains ZERO concrete data on megoshort's recent performance, roster, or form. In a BO1 match where single-map variance is extreme, an opponent shrouded in information asymmetry poses structural upside risk. The market has priced megoshort at 44% despite having no stated weaknesses or loss records to evaluate. CYBERSHOKE'S RECENT FORM IS FRAGILE: April 2026 record shows 2 losses in 3 CCT Contenders matches (to Vexar, Enjoy) sandwiched around a single win vs Young TigeRES. This is 1-2 form against stated 'strong opposition'\u2014not dominant. ROSTER INTEGRATION RISK: dezl3bio joined April 13th; Vert appointed as coach April 13th. Match occurs April 16th\u2014only 3 days for integration. In team-based Counter-Strike, fresh roster changes rarely yield immediate synergy. BO1 format offers zero opportunity to adapt mid-series if coordination breaks down. PARENT ORG MEDIOCRITY SIGNALS WEAK TALENT POOL: CYBERSHOKE Esports main roster sits 6-6 in ESEA Season 47. The 'Prospects' designation suggests a lower-tier developmental squad. Prospects teams rarely outperform expectations in competitive leagues without established form. MARKET PRICE VOLATILITY SUGGESTS UNCERTAINTY: NO side fell -8.5pp over 7 days with sharp -9.5pp move on Apr 16 11:00 UTC, then +5.5pp rebound. This volatility (5.1pp/hr) indicates traders lacking conviction; low volume ($116 USD) means shallow liquidity and susceptibility to noise. YES CASE WEAKNESSES: (1) Losses to Vexar and Enjoy undercut the 'improved coordination' narrative\u2014if new additions were working, they should show trending up, not recent down; (2) 2-0 victory over Young TigeRES is a single data point against teams of unknown competitive tier; (3) No information on whether dezl3bio or Vert have prior synergy with this roster. BO1 VOLATILITY AMPLIFIES UNCERTAINTY: A best-of-one match is inherently noisy. CYBERSHOKE's mixed record (1-2 in three recent BO1s in CCT) shows they are not reliable BO1 performers. megoshort's complete absence from briefing means no contradiction of this concern. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY IS ITSELF BEARISH FOR YES: If YES were clearly the superior team, the briefing would likely contain comparative data on megoshort's weakness or CYBERSHOKE's dominance. Instead, the case for YES rests on roster tenure (September 2025) and recent coaching appointments, while NO is defended by silence\u2014a classic sign that the market is pricing in YES primarily by default or narrative ('new coach, new player = improvement') rather than demonstrated edge. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in CYBERSHOKE's vulnerabilities (recent losses, integration risk, BO1 inconsistency)\u2014these are stated in briefing. Low confidence in assessing megoshort's weaknesses\u2014zero data means zero refutation of competence. This asymmetry justifies probability_no_score (55) well above 100 - probability_score (62), leaving ~7pp ignorance mass. TIME-TO-REVERSAL NOTE: Match is imminent (1.9 hours). Any upset requires megoshort to field a better-prepared BO1 team or CYBERSHOKE to suffer a coordination collapse in their first match post-roster-change. Neither is implausible, but neither is heavily evidenced. The imminent timing also means price will move sharply toward 0.01/0.99 once live results emerge\u2014current 56% YES may not reflect true live odds.", "key_factor": "megoshort's complete absence from the briefing makes it impossible to assess their actual strength, roster stability, or recent form\u2014the market may be overweighting CYBERSHOKE's recent additions without penalty for facing an unknown opponent in a BO1."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.54, "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.46, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CYBERSHOKE Prospects recent form is MIXED: 1 win (Young TigeRES 2-0) but 2 losses (Vexar 0-2, Enjoy 0-2) in CCT Contenders within 3 days (Apr 9\u201312). This suggests vulnerability to stronger opposition but BO1 variance is high. Parent org CYBERSHOKE Esports is 6-6 in ESEA Season 47\u2014precisely middling, offering no directional edge. No equivalent megoshort standing data provided. Recent roster disruption: dezl3bio joined Apr 13, Vert appointed coach Apr 13. Match is Apr 16 16:00 UTC (~1.9 hours from briefing timestamp). Only ~72 hours for integration post-roster move\u2014historically, new rosters underperform in first matches due to limited scrim/sync time. BO1 format amplifies single-map variance and removes adaptation; team cohesion becomes more critical, and recent changes create risk. Market price (YES 56%, NO 44%) suggests slight YES favoritism, but this may reflect name recognition bias (CYBERSHOKE is an established org) rather than form analysis. NO comparative data on megoshort: no recent match results, roster strength, or standing provided. This is a CRITICAL DATA GAP. Cannot confidently evaluate megoshort's baseline or recent trajectory. Base rate for regional BO1s between mid-tier European teams with no clear dominance signal: ~50/50 with \u00b15pp variance for roster changes and form. CYBERSHOKE's recent loss streak (2 out of last 3) and fresh coaching setup suggest slight underweight. Confidence in YES limited by: (i) lack of megoshort data, (ii) recent roster integration risk, (iii) recent loss streak. Confidence in NO equally low due to absence of counter-narrative data. Market has been stable on YES (56%, -1pp/week) but NO experienced sharp volatility (Apr 16 11:00 UTC -9.5pp, then +5.5pp at 13:00 UTC), suggesting late uncertainty or information asymmetry. This does not resolve the underlying team-strength question. Anchor: 50 (base coin-flip for evenly-matched regional BO1), adjust +4 for CYBERSHOKE's established lineup tenure (Sep 2025) and prior BO1 win capability, adjust -0 for megoshort (no data), adjust -2 for recent losses and integration risk. Result: 52\u201354.", "key_factor": "Mid-tier Counter-Strike BO1 matches between regional Advanced-division teams: ~48\u201352% win probability for either side absent team-strength differentiation data; roster volatility and recent coaching changes add uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.54, "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Current market price (YES 56%, NO 44%) reflects modest confidence in CYBERSHOKE Prospects, consistent with mixed recent form data. CYBERSHOKE Prospects shows win capability (2-0 vs Young TigeRES on Apr 09) but recent losses to Vexar and Enjoy (both 0-2) demonstrate vulnerability to stronger opponents. BO1 format is high-variance; recent roster addition (dezl3bio Apr 13) and new coach (Vert Apr 13) had only ~3 days to integrate before this match\u2014insufficient time to show coordinated improvement. Parent organization CYBERSHOKE Esports at 6-6 in ESEA Season 47 suggests mid-tier competitive level, neither dominant nor weak. megoshort has zero recent match data in briefing\u2014complete information vacuum on their form, roster changes, or strength relative to CYBERSHOKE Prospects. Price stability on YES side (\u22121.0pp over 7 days, 0.0pp/hr volatility) suggests shallow conviction; NO side showed sharp swings (\u22129.5pp at 11:00 UTC, +5.5pp at 13:00 UTC) indicating uncertainty or algorithmic noise. Total volume ($116 USD) is extremely low\u2014insufficient liquidity to infer strong edge; market price may not reflect sophisticated estimation. No objective basis to favor either team given data asymmetry; current 56%/44% split is marginally reasonable but rests on weak foundation. Event timing (1.9 hours to start) limits new information arrival; probability will crystallize post-match to ~$0.01/$0.99 binary. Sentiment is neither panicked nor exuberant\u2014crowd appears mildly risk-averse to CYBERSHOKE (short of 50%), consistent with mixed form narrative.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.54, "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.46, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CYBERSHOKE Prospects shows mixed April 2026 form: 1-4 record across CCT Contenders (2-0 vs Young TigeRES; 0-2 vs Vexar; 0-2 vs Enjoy) and GLuck SixSeven (1-2 vs TDK, 2-1 vs eternal premium), indicating inconsistent tier-level play. BO1 format amplifies single-map variance and removes the adaptive advantage of best-of series; team cohesion deficits are more exposed in one-shot scenarios. Roster integration risk is acute: dezl3bio added April 13, Vert appointed coach April 13\u2014only 3 days before match. New support players and coaching staff have minimal time to calibrate defaults, utility usage, and anti-stratting against a known opponent. Prospects' core (pixel, DAN9ARMATURA, SquEzxc, pleynnn, tw1sterzaza) have been stable since Sep 2025, providing some continuity. CYBERSHOKE parent org (6-6 in ESEA S47) performs at middling level; prospects team likely reflects similar competitive ceiling (~50% win-rate baseline). No recent intelligence on megoshort's current roster, form, or map pool; absence of negative data does not imply weakness. Unknown opponent in imminent BO1 introduces asymmetric uncertainty. Market price (YES 56%, NO 44%) reflects slight YES favoritism but with low volume ($116 total) and high recent volatility (NO side -9.5pp spike Apr 16 11:00, +5.5pp Apr 16 13:00), suggesting thin liquidity and potential model disagreement among bettors. Imminent event timing (1.9 hours to start) limits scope for late-breaking roster news or map pool revelation that might shift odds. Price is likely to stabilize or shift sharply once match begins. SME assessment: Recent roster changes and lack of megoshort intel create genuine uncertainty; market price of 56\u201344 is defensible as a coin-flip-adjacent split. Confidence on both sides is low (42/35) due to asymmetric data (CYBERSHOKE form is visible, megoshort is opaque) and integration timeline risk.", "key_factor": "BO1 format and very recent roster integration (dezl3bio + coach Vert joined April 13, only 3 days pre-match) create high variance; new players in single-map format have not yet demonstrated map pool synergy or anti-stratting depth."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.54, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "ROSTER INTEGRATION PENALTY (Black Swan Core): dezl3bio joined April 13, Vert appointed April 13\u2014only 3 days before a high-stakes BO1. BO1 eliminates map adaptation; single-map execution under pressure exposes new-team rust. No briefing data on megoshort's roster stability or preparation depth. FORM TRAJECTORY ASYMMETRY: CYBERSHOKE lost 0-2 to Vexar and Enjoy (April 11-12), then immediately rotated roster. Macro losing streak (3 losses in 5 matches) masked by single YTR win. megoshort's form completely unknown\u2014briefing admits 'no specific recent information.' BO1 BRUTALITY: Single-map format punishes teams with internal chemistry gaps or unfamiliar setups. New coach (Vert) has had zero match coordination; new player (dezl3bio) has 32 maps in system but none with *this* specific five. megoshort, if stable, gains asymmetric advantage. META/PREPARATION UNKNOWN: Briefing silent on megoshort's tactical innovation, map pool strategy, or recent scrim performance. CYBERSHOKE's recent losses suggest defensive or strategic vulnerability that a prepared opponent (megoshort) could exploit immediately. MARKET VOLATILITY RED FLAG: NO side fell -8.5pp (7-day) with sharp -9.5pp move at 11:00 UTC, then bounced +5.5pp at 13:00 UTC. Suggests informed traders recognized instability; late-stage betting flux in LIVE/IMMINENT event indicates new information or lineup doubt entering market 2 hours before lock. PARENT ORG MEDIOCRITY: CYBERSHOKE main roster 6-6 in ESEA Season 47. Prospects division signals academy/developmental tier status. megoshort affiliation unknown but could be peer-level or stronger organization masquerading as underdog. SILENCE ON MEGOSHORT: Briefing provides zero megoshort stats, wins, losses, roster timeline, or coaching changes. In a competitive BO1 where both teams are material, absence of NO-side evidence is itself a signal\u2014either underdog is genuinely unknown (higher variance, higher upset potential) or briefing data gap masks a quiet but competent opponent. 56% YES price anchors to CYBERSHOKE brand recognition, not performance quality. Market may be overweighting 'Prospects' team name familiarity over mega's structural competitiveness and CYBERSHOKE's recent 3-day-old integration liability.", "key_factor": "megoshort exploits CYBERSHOKE's ultra-recent roster churn (dezl3bio 3 days old, Vert coaching appointment 72 hours prior) via superior map pool preparation, team cohesion, or tactical adaptation\u2014BO1 format magnifies integration penalty."}], "final_score": 0.52467651515664, "no_score": 0.48389015102022365, "edge": 0.12518518518518518, "no_edge": 0.24518518518518528, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 52% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 41% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6851851851851852, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0702687976791527, "The Bull": 0.9559930478535308, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0562331438919461, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0626106949123544, "The Domain Specialist": 1.059634504436164, "The Contrarian": 1.0571973090855826, "The Bear": 0.73806250214127}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1997734", "question": "Counter-Strike: CYBERSHOKE Prospects vs megoshort (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between CYBERSHOKE Prospects and megoshort in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 16 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CYBERSHOKE Prospects\" if CYBERSHOKE Prospects win the match against megoshort.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"megoshort\" if megoshort win the match against CYBERSHOKE Prospects.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.56