{"run_id": "e4a4f58a-cd12-4629-a757-c7fda7f42ed8", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:34:53.257535+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1997388", "question": "Counter-Strike: eternal premium vs ENJOY (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between eternal premium and ENJOY in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 16 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"eternal premium\" if eternal premium win the match against ENJOY.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ENJOY\" if ENJOY win the match against eternal premium.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 2.083332, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["67418447565145740148049628183458934928396374984561385681568906254935450074754", "18993689477957112524517100654899020916407677112660966505109693640320326009799"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: eternal premium must win the BO1 match against ENJOY to resolve YES. The match is LIVE/IMMINENT (starts in ~2.9 hours), so this is a forward-looking probability, not a retrospective determination. ETERNAL PREMIUM STRENGTH ASSESSMENT: Mixed recent form (1-2 vs Bebop, 2-1 vs BRUTE, 0-2 vs MASONIC, 0-2 vs illwill, 0-2 vs WW) shows inconsistent performance. Ranked #214 globally is mid-tier. MRcreed's 1.21 Rating 3.0 is reasonable but other starters average 0.89-1.01, indicating below-average fragging. Team has roster stability (30+ days) but recent losses to stronger opponents (TDK, CYBERSHOKE Prospects) signal competitive disadvantage. ENJOY ASSESSMENT: NO substantive information provided on ENJOY's roster, ratings, recent form, or ranking. Cannot assess their strength relative to eternal premium. This asymmetric data gap prevents confident comparative analysis. BO1 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-one match has inherently high variance compared to BO3 or BO5. Single-game outcomes are heavily influenced by map selection, day-form variance, and tactical execution. This amplifies uncertainty regardless of team quality gap. MARKET PRICING ANALYSIS: Current prices (YES 42%, NO 58%) suggest modest NO favoritism. Price history shows +5pp movement toward YES over 7 days, possibly reflecting late-arriving information or volatility. Low volume ($2 USD) and near-equilibrium pricing indicate limited informed trading; market may be pricing-in fundamental uncertainty rather than strong conviction. TEMPORAL COHERENCE CHECK: All recent match results (dated 1-3 weeks ago) are PRIOR encounters, not this market outcome. They provide head-to-head context but no direct evidence this specific BO1 will conclude. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 35 because (1) eternal premium's mixed recent form and low average individual ratings provide weak support for YES, but (2) MRcreed's stronger rating and roster stability offer partial countervailing evidence. confidence_no = 38 because (1) ENJOY's complete absence from briefing data prevents high-confidence assessment of NO, but (2) eternal premium's demonstrated losses to stronger opponents and below-average fragging provide some support for NO. Both confidence scores remain low due to data asymmetry and BO1 variance. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: No material oracle risk identified; HLTV.org will publish results shortly after match conclusion. 50-50 tiebreak language (forfeit, cancellation, >7-day delay) is not anticipated given ESEA Advanced scheduled format.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data on ENJOY limits ability to assess relative team strength; BO1 format introduces high variance; market pricing reflects uncertainty rather than strong directional signal."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS NO: The briefing shows NO rising +5.0pp in 24h and 7 days, with a sharp -5.0pp move on Apr 16 at 14:33 UTC (80 minutes before match start). This late repricing suggests recent information or updated sentiment shifted weight to ENJOY. ETERNAL PREMIUM'S FRAGILITY: Individual ratings across the roster are predominantly weak (skept1K, smith, P1kan0, dazzy all in 0.89\u20131.01 range). Only MRcreed achieves 1.21 Rating 3.0\u2014a single bright spot insufficient to carry a BO1 against an unknown but favorited opponent. RECENT FORM DETERIORATION: eternal premium lost 0-2 to TDK and 1-2 to CYBERSHOKE Prospects within the last 2 weeks\u2014tangible evidence of struggle against mid-tier competition. One win (2-1 vs BRUTE) is the only recent W; the rest are losses or narrow escapes. BO1 FORMAT AMPLIFIES VARIANCE: Best-of-one matches eliminate any series-recovery mechanism. eternal premium's inconsistent individual performances and mixed form make them vulnerable to upset losses at higher variance. ENJOY REMAINS OPAQUE: The briefing provides zero data on ENJOY's roster, ratings, recent results, or form. This absence is itself a signal: if ENJOY were notably weaker, the briefing would likely highlight it for YES advocates. The market's 58% NO price on ENJOY despite information vacuum suggests market belief in ENJOY's competitive standing. ESEA ADVANCED TIER & PLACEMENT: eternal premium finished 7-8th in Season 56\u2014mid-pack at best. Against a team the market has repriced to 58% favorite, even with roster continuity and tournament appearances, eternal premium appears outmatched. TIMING & SHARP MOVE: The -5.0pp NO move 80 minutes before match start suggests late-arriving intel or public acknowledgment of eternal premium's weakness. This near-match-start repricing is unlikely to be noise; it reflects real sentiment shift. CASE AGAINST eternal premium: Low frags (except MRcreed), recent losses to named opponents, 7-8th placement in league table, BO1 vulnerability. These weaknesses compound in a single-map format. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO (35) is higher than in YES (28) because the briefing provides concrete evidence of eternal premium's frailty (ratings, recent losses, placement) but offers near-zero comparative data on ENJOY. The NO case rests on eternal premium's visible weakness; the YES case rests on absence of counter-evidence. The latter is weaker ground for high confidence. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT: The market at 58% NO reflects rational repricing away from eternal premium. The +5pp momentum and late sharp move suggest NO may be fairly priced or even underpriced relative to eternal premium's recent form.", "key_factor": "Market repricing away from eternal premium due to recent poor results (losses to TDK 0-2, CYBERSHOKE 1-2) and below-average individual ratings (0.89\u20131.01), with NO side gaining +5pp momentum in 24 hours."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.44, "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE FAVORS UPSETS: BO1 matches inherently reduce sample size and amplify variance \u2014 a single strong map pick or a hot fragging performance can flip outcomes. The market is pricing eternal premium at 42%, but BO1 should compress conventional win probabilities closer to 50% than BO3 matchups. ETERNAL PREMIUM'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: MRcreed's 1.21 Rating 3.0 is materially above the team's other starters (0.89\u20131.01 range). In a BO1 where individual performance spikes matter, a single carry round or a sustained run can swing momentum. This player advantage is under-reported in the briefing. ROSTER STABILITY MATTERS: 30+ days of continuity with five dedicated starters suggests refined defaults and communication \u2014 an asset in BO1 where preparation and coordination are compressed into a single decisive map. The briefing notes this but does not strongly weight it. CRITICAL DATA GAP ON ENJOY: The briefing provides zero recent form data, rating data, roster information, or head-to-head context for ENJOY. When one side is information-rich and the other is information-poor, the market tends to default-price the unknown team higher to hedge uncertainty. This creates an inefficiency: ENJOY's true strength is opaque, yet the market has already discounted eternal premium by 16pp. RECENT LOSSES ARE NOT DISPOSITIVE: eternal premium's recent defeats (TDK 0-2, CYBERSHOKE Prospects 1-2) were in BO3 formats against likely stronger opponents. BO1 reversals are common. The briefing conflates BO3 record with BO1 likelihood, which is a category error for variance-sensitive markets. ETERNAL PREMIUM'S ACTUAL RECORD IS MIXED: 3 wins, 4 losses in sampled BO3 matches over 3 weeks (against Bebop, BRUTE, MASONIC, illwill, WW, OlyBet, Rebels). This is roughly 43% win rate in full series \u2014 consistent with mid-tier ESEA Advanced teams. Extrapolating to a single-map match against an unknown opponent does not justify a 58% NO bias. GLOBAL RANK #214 IS CONTEXT-DEPENDENT: The briefing lists this rank but provides no benchmark for what rank range ENJOY occupies. If ENJOY is unranked or lower-ranked, eternal premium's #214 placement represents a material advantage; if ENJOY is significantly higher-ranked, the market may be rational. Without ENJOY's rank, the briefing offers no comparative ground truth. TIMING AND SHARP MOVES: The market saw a -5pp sharp move on NO at Apr 16 14:33 UTC (only 3 hours before event start). This move is late and suggests either late information ingestion or position closing. With <3 hours to match start, such moves have limited justification \u2014 likely noise or algorithmic rebalancing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on eternal premium's roster, recent form (BO3), and individual ratings. Weak data on ENJOY (no information whatsoever), on BO1-specific dynamics, and on why ENJOY deserves a 16pp favorite premium. Confidence in YES is limited by lack of comparative framing; confidence in NO is limited by the absence of ENJOY data. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: eternal premium is underpriced at 42% given BO1 variance, roster continuity, and MRcreed's above-average rating. ENJOY's 58% price reflects uncertainty-driven default-favoring, not concrete strength signals. A fair BO1 match between mid-tier teams with one having slight player quality advantage should price closer to 48\u201352%. YES at 44% reflects modest underdog edge, not confidence. FINAL BEAR CASE: The market is implicitly treating ENJOY as a known quantity and eternal premium as a below-average team. The briefing data contradicts this asymmetry \u2014 eternal premium's recent record is mediocre but not weak, MRcreed is a genuine plus-player, and BO1 format neutralizes recent series-level losses. ENJOY remains a complete unknown, yet the market has already capitulated 16pp. An upset here requires no extraordinary event; it requires ENJOY to not be materially better than eternal premium, a claim the briefing cannot substantiate.", "key_factor": "BO1 format introduces high variance favoring the underdog, and eternal premium's roster continuity with MRcreed (1.21 Rating) provides a legitimate fragging threat that the market may be underweighting against an unknown ENJOY opponent."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE/IMMINENT (2.9 hours until start). Reversal potential is extremely limited; market is already pricing in available information. MATCH FORMAT: Best-of-one introduces high variance. Single-map outcomes are inherently less predictive than BO3, reducing confidence in either direction. eternal premium STRENGTHS: Established roster (5 starters, 30+ days continuity), MRcreed rated 1.21 (above-average fragger for mid-tier), active tournament schedule indicates competitive rhythm. eternal permanent WEAKNESSES: Recent results poor (losses to TDK 0-2, CYBERSHOKE Prospects 1-2). Most starters rated 0.89\u20131.01 (below-average). Placed 7\u20138th in ESEA S56 standings (mid-pack or lower). ENJOY ASSESSMENT: Zero information provided on roster, recent form, ranking, or individual ratings. This is a critical asymmetry \u2014 we cannot evaluate ENJOY's actual strength. BASE RATE LOGIC: In mid-tier CS leagues, BO1 matches between comparable teams sit near 50-50. eternal premium's ranking (#214) and mixed recent form suggest slight underdog positioning, yet ENJOY's complete anonymity in briefing prevents confident YES/NO separation. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES at 42%, NO at 58% aligns loosely with eternal premium's mediocre form and lower ranking. Modest market conviction (not extreme skew) reflects data uncertainty. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=28 because we have decent data on eternal premium's recent performance and roster, but roster changes/meta shifts can swing BO1 outcomes. confidence_no=32 because ENJOY is a complete unknown \u2014 we cannot validate the 58% NO price; it rests on absence of positive eternal premium information, not positive ENJOY evidence. IGNORANCE MASS: probability_score + probability_no_score = 100, reflecting a genuine binary outcome (one team wins BO1); however, the LOW confidence scores on both sides reflect substantial uncertainty about ENJOY's true strength and meta fit on the selected map.", "key_factor": "BO1 CS matches in mid-tier leagues: ~50% base rate for either team; slight edge to higher-ranked opponent. eternal premium (#214 globally) vs ENJOY (unknown rank): insufficient head-to-head and opponent data."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "Market Price Alignment: YES at 42% matches the current crowd consensus exactly; no obvious mispricing signal detected in the orderbook. Asymmetric Information: Briefing provides detailed eternal premium roster, recent match history (mixed 1-2, 2-1, 0-2 results), and individual player ratings. ENJOY data is entirely absent \u2014 no roster, form, or competitive context available. Crowd Psychology: The market appears to be pricing eternal premium at slight underdog odds (42%) based on their recent losses (TDK 0-2, CYBERSHOKE Prospects 1-2) and below-average individual fragging stats (0.89\u20131.01 range for most starters). This is rational apathy toward YES \u2014 not exuberant, not panicked, just indifference to insufficient data. Ignored Signals on YES side: MRcreed's 1.21 Rating 3.0 is the only strong individual metric and is being underweighted by the crowd. Roster continuity 30+ days suggests cohesion, but losses to mid-tier teams (TDK, CYBERSHOKE) dominate recent narrative. Ignored Signals on NO side: ENJOY has zero briefing coverage. The crowd is pricing them at 58% without any evidence of their strength, recent form, or roster quality. This is pure blind favoritism \u2014 the market is betting against eternal premium's weaknesses rather than betting on ENJOY's strengths. BO1 Variance: Best-of-one format amplifies upset potential and reduces predictive power of season-long form. Crowd may be discounting this volatility. Confidence Asymmetry: High confidence in YES assessment (35 is LOW, reflecting eternal premium's documented weak recent results and low individual ratings). Confidence in NO assessment is similarly weak (40) because ENJOY is a complete unknown \u2014 crowd sentiment on NO side is built on the absence of YES confidence, not affirmative evidence. Temporal Factor: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~2.9 hours). Sharp 5.0pp move toward YES in last 24 hours may reflect late-breaking information (team news, betting sharp action, or pre-game momentum), but volume is minimal ($2 USD), so liquidity is negligible and moves are noise. No Rational Exuberance Detected: Crowd is not aggressively backing either side. Price is anchored to eternal premium's recent poor performance and lack of ENJOY intel. This is rational indifference, not mispricing. Verdict: Market price (42% YES / 58% NO) appears fairly calibrated to available information but relies heavily on asymmetric data. YES side confidence is LOW because eternal premium's recent form is genuinely weak; NO side confidence is similarly LOW because ENJOY is a complete black box. The 42/58 split reflects crowd's cautious lean toward the underdog kill (ENJOY favored) without strong conviction on either side.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "DOMAIN CONTEXT: Counter-Strike competitive matching involves map selection (veto system), economy rounds, tactical execution, and momentum shifts\u2014BO1 eliminates the sample-size stabilization that BO3 provides. A single map magnifies individual performance volatility and captain/IGL decision-making impact. ETERNAL PREMIUM ROSTER STRENGTH: MRcreed at 1.21 Rating 3.0 is above-average for mid-tier ESEA Advanced players (1.0 is baseline); however, skept1K, smith, P1kan0, and dazzy all cluster at 0.89\u20131.01 (below-average fragging). This is a 1-strong-player roster, not a balanced threat. RECENT FORM NEGATIVE SIGNAL: Losses to TDK (0-2) and CYBERSHOKE Prospects (1-2) in April 2026 are recent and direct. CYBERSHOKE Prospects especially is an academy/developing team, not a top-tier opponent; a 1-2 loss to them flags inconsistency. The mixed BO3 record (1-2 vs Bebop, 2-1 vs BRUTE, 0-2 losses to three opponents) shows a team barely maintaining competitive parity. CRITICAL DATA GAP\u2014NO ENJOY INFORMATION: Briefing provides zero roster, ratings, recent form, or ranking for ENJOY. This is a high-confidence blocker. BO1 outcome depends heavily on map matchup, veto execution, and opponent quality\u2014all unknown. Market price of 42% YES likely reflects default uncertainty, not a strong analytical position on either side. ESEA ADVANCED TIER & PLACEMENT: Eternal premium placed 7-8th in Season 56 (mid-pack, not top-4). This is a lower-mid-tier team in a mid-tier league. Odds of 42% suggest market expects near-parity, which is reasonable given zero ENJOY data but excessive confidence in 'no' verdict (58%) is unjustified without opponent intel. MARKET PRICE ACTION: YES side climbed +5.0pp in 24h and +5.0pp over 7 days; NO side fell symmetrically. This suggests late-arriving information (team news, roster confirmation, betting syndicate activity) favoring eternal premium. However, volume is $2 USD\u2014negligible liquidity means price is not anchored by informed traders. Low confidence in market signal. BO1 VARIANCE DOMINANCE: In a single-map elimination format, luck (economy swing, one crucial 1v3 clutch, map-specific meta advantage) swamps team quality difference. For two teams of similar mid-tier standing (eternal premium 7-8th place, ENJOY unknown but presumably ESEA Advanced tier), coin-flip probability is ~45-55%, not 30-70. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in eternal premium's weakness (1.21 avg rating if MRcreed carries, below-average supports, recent losses) justifies confidence_yes=35. However, ENJOY is entirely unknown; cannot assess their strength, form, or countermatch. confidence_no capped at 38 to reflect this ignorance\u2014a 58% NO price cannot be justified without ENJOY data.", "key_factor": "BO1 format creates extreme variance; individual match outcome is nearly 50-50 without map pool, veto history, or opponent roster data\u2014market price of 42/58 reflects rational uncertainty given asymmetric information."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "BRIEFING SILENCE ON ENJOY: No performance data, roster info, recent form, or head-to-head history for ENJOY exists in the briefing. This asymmetry is the primary black swan vector \u2014 we are betting blind on the NO side. BO1 VARIANCE AMPLIFIER: Best-of-one matches are inherently high-variance; a single anti-default read, map pool mismatch, or tactical surprise can flip a 60/40 matchup. eternal premium's 0.89\u20131.01 individual ratings suggest fragile game-sense execution vulnerable to disruption. ROSTER SUBSTITUTION RISK: The briefing lists 'MRcreed (1.21 Rating 3.0)' as the highest-rated player but does NOT confirm he is playing today. A late-match roster swap (academy player sub-in, illness, or technical issue) would crater eternal premium's already marginal fragging power. LATE SHARP MOVE ON NO: Market moved -5.0pp on NO at 2026-04-16 14:33 UTC (3 hours before match) \u2014 suggesting informed traders detected a negative eternal premium signal (roster news, ENJOY intel leak, or map pool reveal) in the final window. This move is atypical for a $2-volume micro-market and warrants weight. ESEA ADVANCED MID-TIER VOLATILITY: ESEA Advanced Season 56 is a mid-tier league where 7-8th-place teams (eternal premium's standing) face frequent upsets due to inconsistent training regimens and meta adaptation gaps. ENJOY, if equally ranked or a dark-horse challenger, has a non-trivial path. ACTIVE TOURNAMENT SCHEDULE FATIGUE: eternal premium competed in GLuck SixSeven and MPKBK CIS LAN in early April 2026 with mixed results (losses to TDK, CYBERSHOKE). Back-to-back grinding without rest can degrade mental sharpness in a BO1 sprint. RATING INFLATION ON ONE PLAYER: MRcreed's 1.21 Rating 3.0 does not offset the collective 0.89\u20131.01 floor for the remaining four players. If MRcreed has an off-map or the team's strats fail to enable him, eternal premium collapses to a sub-1.0 team average. MAPPING & STRATEGIC UNCERTAINTY: No detail on which map(s) are in play. In BO1, map pool comfort and anti-default setup design matter disproportionately. ENJOY may specialize in a map favored by the draw. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 35 reflects weak affirmative data (only MRcreed's rating and roster continuity). confidence_no = 40 reflects the briefing's near-total silence on ENJOY's actual threat level \u2014 we cannot confidently rule out ENJOY strength. Both scores are suppressed.", "key_factor": "ENJOY fields a surprise roster substitution or tactical innovation (e.g., map-specific anti-default setup) that exploits eternal premium's weak individual fragging in a high-variance BO1 format, or eternal premium suffers a key player disconnect/lag issue 10 minutes before match time given the 2.9-hour window."}], "final_score": 0.41559372443530657, "no_score": 0.5845393389762216, "edge": 0.27018518518518525, "no_edge": 0.10018518518518527, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 37% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6851851851851852, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0702687976791527, "The Bull": 0.9559930478535308, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0562331438919461, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0626106949123544, "The Domain Specialist": 1.059634504436164, "The Contrarian": 1.0571973090855826, "The Bear": 0.73806250214127}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1997388", "question": "Counter-Strike: eternal premium vs ENJOY (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between eternal premium and ENJOY in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 16 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"eternal premium\" if eternal premium win the match against ENJOY.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ENJOY\" if ENJOY win the match against eternal premium.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. 