her than informed positioning. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Match resolution is straightforward \u2014 winner takes all, no ambiguity in team name matching (both are primary-team designations). No forfeit/cancellation risk evident from briefing. Criteria are clear and unambiguous. SYMMETRIC IGNORANCE: Both teams lack publicly available information in the briefing. This is a genuine coin-flip scenario from a fundamental standpoint, with the market price (56/44 split) reflecting only orderbook flow, not edge. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: Since no credible data exists on either side, confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (25). The probability_score of 56 is simply deferred to market pricing in the absence of any actionable intelligence. This is NOT a genuine analytical estimate \u2014 it reflects market consensus when the analyst lacks inputs. DUAL-PERSPECTIVE VALIDATION: A probability of 56 for YES implies NO has 44% chance. Given zero data on both sides, neither proposition is defensible independently; both confidence scores are symmetrically low. IMMINENT EVENT CAVEAT: With ~4 hours to start, reversals requiring major surprises (roster leaks, withdrawals, or scandals) are possible but not visible in briefing. This does NOT lower the probability_score itself, but the low confidence scores reflect this temporal compression.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of team performance data, head-to-head history, roster information, or recent form for either team; market probability is based entirely on orderbook pricing with no fundamental information available to validate or challenge it."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.56, "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.44, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.2, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'No relevant search results were returned' for either team's recent performance, roster composition, or head-to-head record. Both the YES and NO