, or meta context provided in briefing. Current market price (YES 56% / NO 44%) appears to be DEFAULT PRICING reflecting mild consensus toward E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS, but this consensus has NO evidentiary foundation in the briefing. Price stability over 7 days (YES -1.5pp, NO -5.0pp) suggests a thin, uninformed market drifting slightly toward YES without material news catalyst. Sharp move on NO side at Apr 16 00:00 UTC (-6.0pp) with minimal context \u2014 likely technical/orderbook adjustment rather than sentiment-driven repricing based on team intel. Volume is extremely low ($8,587 total) \u2014 insufficient liquidity to signal confident crowd conviction on either side. Event timing (TODAY, ~4 hours to start) means reversal is structurally difficult; market has effectively frozen at near-parity with ignorance mass. MARKET PSYCHOLOGY: Neither greed nor fear evident. Absence of noise itself is the signal \u2014 crowd is rationally apathetic because briefing provides NO actionable data. Holding current market prices as-reported reflects crowd's honest uncertainty, not irrational exuberance or panic. Both confidence scores set to 18 (very low) because briefing contains ZERO team-level fundamentals on either side \u2014 NO basis to validate or refute the 56/44 split. Probability_score = 56 mirrors market price only because no contrary evidence exists; this is NOT a conviction signal.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.56, "probability_yes": 0.56, "probability_no": 0.44, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.18, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides NO team statistics, recent match records, roster compositions, coaching staff credentials, meta-game alignment, patch currency, scrim results, or any other standard esports evaluation metrics for either competitor. MARKET PRICE AS ANCHOR: Current market prices (YES 56% / NO 44%) represent the only quantitative signal available. With zero independent information to contradict or refine this signal, defaulting near market price is appropriate. SEARCH FAILURE: 'No relevant search results were returned' for this specific matchup. The briefing contains unrelated rugby, cricket, and football content\u2014not League of Legends competitive intel. IMMINENT EVENT (4.3 HOURS): With event start ~4 hours away, any material new information (roster changes, health issues, technical problems) that would justify sharp deviation from market price is unlikely to surface and trade into the market before kickoff. GERMAN REGIONAL LEAGUE CONTEXT: Prime League 1st Division (German regional LoL circuit) has lower global media coverage than major international leagues; information asymmetry is high for external analysts. CONFIDENCE SEVERELY LIMITED: SME knowledge of German regional LoL competitive dynamics, team histories, and meta-game positioning is insufficient to generate high-confidence probability estimates independent of market price. Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set to 18 (well below the 30-threshold for 'outside confident knowledge') because the briefing offers no technical, performance, or roster data on which to base expert judgment. NO ARBITRAGE SIGNAL: Market prices have been stable (YES -1.5pp in 24h, NO -5.0pp in 7d), and recent sharp move (NO -6.0pp at Apr 16 00:00 UTC) has already dissipated. No evidence of market mispricing or insider information leakage. RESOLUTION MECHANICS ARE SOUND: BO1 format eliminates series-play strategic complexity; match outcome depends entirely on single-game execution, draft, and in-game decision-making\u2014all unknowns in this briefing. DUAL-INDEPENDENCE PRINCIPLE: probability_score (56) and probability_no_score (44) are derived from market prices ONLY, not from independent SME reasoning. The gap (56+44=100) reflects the market's implicit confidence, not domain expertise. Leaving no 'ignorance mass' here because the briefing offers truly zero domain-specific evidence on either side\u2014the only honest representation is to match market odds with correspondingly LOW confidence on both.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains zero substantive team-performance data, roster information, meta alignment, or head-to-head history for either E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS or Team Orange Gaming, making any probability estimate below the confidence threshold for meaningful SME analysis."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.5, "probability_yes": 0.5, "probability_no": 0.5, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.15, "confidence_no": 0.15, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA VOID: The briefing contains zero team stats, head-to-head records, recent form data, roster composition, or patch/meta context for either E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS or Team Orange Gaming. NEWS SUMMARY FAILURE: Search returns only unrelated sports (rugby, cricket, football), no Prime League coverage \u2014 suggests either: (1) briefing document was incomplete/corrupted, (2) market was created with minimal research, or (3) information was deliberately suppressed. MARKET PRICE STABILITY MASKS INFORMATION VACUUM: YES at 56% is only +6pp above even odds. The 1-week EMA stability (-1.5pp to -5pp) suggests weak conviction from both sides, not high-confidence backing of the favorite. SHARP MOVE SIGNAL: NO side dropped -6.0pp on Apr 16 00:00 UTC (16 hours before match). This coordinated move absent accompanying news suggests: a late roster announcement, injury report, or coaching decision reached private channels before public briefing updated. BO1 FORMAT HIGH-VARIANCE: Single-game elimination format amplifies upset probability and reduces predictability versus best-of-series. Meta counter-picks, surprise bans, and tactical innovation have outsized impact in BO1. TEMPORAL CLIFF: Event starts in ~4 hours. Any reversals or late-breaking news (player benching, stand-in sub, patch interpretation surprise) will not propagate to this briefing. Market is trading on stale/absent information. CONTRARIAN ANGLE: The consensus (56% YES) assumes E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS is favored, but this rests on ZERO supporting evidence in the briefing. Market may be anchored to seed position, reputation, or algorithm artifact rather than current form. Orange Gaming may have hidden advantage (recent pickup, evolved playstyle, meta-favorable roster) that goes unreported. DUAL CONFIDENCE COLLAPSE: Inability to source a single credible stat for either team justifies LOW confidence on both sides. This is not a 56-44 split with high conviction; it is a genuine coin flip with information asymmetry favoring one side's private knowledge. RISK OF FORFEITURE/CANCELLATION: Given 7-day no-resolution \u2192 50-50 rule, any match delay or admin dispute (unlikely but non-zero in regional esports) creates optionality that current market pricing does not fully reflect.", "key_factor": "Roster substitution, mid-match technical failure, or undisclosed roster lock due to illness/injury affecting one team hours before match start, combined with complete absence of pre-match intelligence in the briefing indicating information blackout or last-minute changes."}], "final_score": 0.5399231690270612, "no_score": 0.46036392304381046, "edge": 0.13018518518518518, "no_edge": 0.24018518518518528, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 19% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6851851851851852, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0702687976791527, "The Bull": 0.9559930478535308, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0562331438919461, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0626106949123544, "The Domain Specialist": 1.059634504436164, "The Contrarian": 1.0571973090855826, "The Bear": 0.73806250214127}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1993649", "question": "LoL: E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS vs Team Orange Gaming (BO1) - Prime League 1st Division Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS and Team Orange Gaming in the Prime League 1st Division Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 16 at 3:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS\" if E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS win the match against Team Orange Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Orange Gaming\" if Team Orange Gaming win the match against E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T01:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T19:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.555, "volume_usd": 8586.889631000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["76739145544651729676257156278105870891495497942883946398702900651290668335024", "88363323633313845605362797135034231883114939714787169892569395546480251116686"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Other predictions\n\nO: 1,62\n\nPrediction on the game between the Reds and the Crusaders: Can the away team win?", "Rugby\n\n11:24:02\n\nO: 1,83\n\nPrediction on the game between Wests Tigers and Newcastle Knights: Can the visitors continue their dominance?", "Rugby\n\n31:53:02\n\nOther predictions\n\n## Recent Articles\n\nHow to Watch Liverpool vs Fulham Match: Premier League TV Channel, Team News & Betting Odds\n\nHow to Watch Arsenal vs Bournemouth Match: Premier League TV Channel, Team News & Betting Odds\n\nPREVIEW: Unbeaten RR and RCB Set for High-Scoring Showdown\n\nMukul\u2019s last-ball heroics seal dramatic win for LSG\n\nPSL 2026: Spinners, Conway Shine as United Clinch Dominant Victory\n\nHeartbreak for Delhi as Titans Snatch Victory in Nail Biting Finish\n\nSubstance\n\nTo top [...] ## Parramatta Eels and Gold Coast Titans Match Prediction\n\nWhere two elephants fight, the grass suffers, but to me, the points are going to suffer in this game.", "While the attack of the two sides might not be exceptionally sharp, their defence are poor.", "So, if the two sides can capitalise on their defensive vulnerability, why not?", "So my first pick is the Over 50.5 points\n\nSecond, I am backing Parramatta Eels to win this game, and not because the odds are in their favour, but because of their exceptional record playing against the Gold Coast Titans.", "They have won three of their last four games against them, and no doubt they have my full backing.", "Our match prediction: Over 50.5 points odds for a coefficient of 1.70 in the Bc.Game bookmaker.", "[...] Looking at the latest head-to-head odds, 1xbet currently has the Parramatta Eels at $1.60 and the Gold Coast Titans at $2.26.", "Parramatta Eels are listed to cover up to -3.5 points underdogs against the Gold Coast Titans, with odds of $1.83 available at 1xbet."], "news_summary": "No relevant search results were returned for the LoL Prime League 1st Division match between E WIE EINFACH E-SPORTS and Team Orange Gaming scheduled for 2026-04-16 19:00 UTC. The search results contain predictions and coverage of unrelated sports events (rugby, football, cricket, esports in other regions), with no information about the teams, their current form, recent head-to-head records, or roster composition that would inform this matchup.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data to build YES case."], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data to build NO case."], "key_context": ["Prime League 1st Division Regular Season match (BO1 format)", "Event imminent \u2014 4.3 hours until 19:00 UTC start on 2026-04-16"], "prior_match_facts": [], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-16T14:40:57.822805Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "76739145544651729676257156278105870891495497942883946398702900651290668335024", "data_points": 3, "weighted_avg": 0.5560216826339075, "change_1w_pp": -1.4999999999999902, "change_24h_pp": -1.4999999999999902, "volatility_24h": 2.4748737341529106, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "88363323633313845605362797135034231883114939714787169892569395546480251116686", "data_points": 17, "weighted_avg": 0.44213152808986955, "change_1w_pp": -4.999999999999999, "change_24h_pp": -4.999999999999999, "volatility_24h": 1.5903353943953669, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-16T00:00:46Z", "delta_pp": -6.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-16T14:40:58.1