with market, confidence floors set to 25 on both sides to signal profound data asymmetry.", "key_factor": "Market pricing reflects fundamental uncertainty; no reliable team form, roster strength, or head-to-head data exists in briefing to justify confident directional movement."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.44, "probability_yes": 0.44, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides zero concrete information about either team's recent performance, roster composition, win rates, head-to-head record, or current form. The 'NEWS SUMMARY' explicitly states 'No recent form data or team strength assessments are available.' UNDERDOG CASE (YES = Dignitas): Market prices Dignitas at 44% despite complete information vacuum. This suggests either: (a) market has access to unpublished form data, or (b) pricing is arbitrary/soft. If (b), Dignitas may be underpriced. Dignitas brand has historical LoL pedigree (active 2017\u20132019, 2022), suggesting organizational stability that could support competitive roster. FAVORITE CASE (NO = Disguised): Market prices Disguised at 55%, a 11-point edge. However, briefing conflates 'Disguised Toast' (a retired Hearthstone streamer, born 1991) with 'Disguised' (the LoL team). This naming confusion is a RED FLAG \u2014 the briefing may have confused two entirely different entities. If Disguised Toast is a person (not a team), the team 'Disguised' is completely uncharacterized in the briefing. NAMING AMBIGUITY ALERT: The briefing includes extensive content about 'Disguised Toast' as a retired Canadian/Taiwanese Hearthstone player (2017\u20132019, 2022 active years). It is unclear whether 'Disguised' (the LoL team) is related to this person or is a separate entity. This conflation suggests data quality issues and raises doubt about whether market pricing reflects reliable information about the actual LoL team. ELIMINATION