rruption. NO ROSTER INFORMATION: Zero player names, roles, or current lineup data for either Dignitas or Disguised LoL rosters provided. NO FORM DATA: No recent match results, win rates, tournament finishes, or head-to-head history between these teams in 2026 season. NO META CONTEXT: No patch notes, champion pool advantages, draft tendencies, or meta-specific strategic advantages identified. NO COACHING/MANAGEMENT INTEL: No staff changes, team stability indicators, or organizational factors that affect playoff performance. MARKET PRICING SUGGESTS NEAR PARITY: YES at 44%, NO at 55% indicates market believes Disguised is slight favorite (~12% edge). This modest spread aligns with genuine uncertainty. BO3 FORMAT FACTOR: Best-of-3 eliminates single-game variance somewhat, but without form data, cannot assess which team's consistency favors them. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Lower bracket R1 implies both teams are strong enough to reach playoffs; no tier information available to distinguish skill gap. TEMPORAL PROXIMITY: Event starts in ~6 hours. Pre-match odds at 44/55 are likely near market consensus. Without contradictory intel, deferring to market price is appropriate. SME KNOWLEDGE GAP: As a LoL domain specialist, I recognize that predictions require (1) current patch meta, (2) recent VOD analysis, (3) player mechanical skill tier, (4) team chemistry post-roster changes. NONE of these are present. Confidence must be extremely low.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains severe data corruption\u2014mixing Hearthstone player 'Disguised Toast' with a League of Legends team 'Disguised,' and providing no current roster, recent form, meta matchups, or patch-specific information critical to LoL competitive prediction."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO team rosters, recent match records, head-to-head history, patch notes, or current form metrics for either team. The 44/55 market split is thin ($6.2k volume) and may reflect uninformed 'coin flip' pricing rather than analyst consensus. DISGUISED TOAST NAME RED FLAG: The briefing contains extensive Hearthstone player wiki data for 'Disguised Toast' (retired 2019, last active 2022), not a 2026 League of Legends org. This is either a data corruption artifact or a newly-formed/rebranded org with no searchable history\u2014suggests minimal public visibility and possible roster churn. DIGNITAS INSTITUTIONAL ADVANTAGE (tentative): Dignitas is a historically established brand in esports; if the search results omission of them reflects lack of recent controversy, they may have stable infrastructure. However, absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. LOWER-BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: Both teams are in a must-win elimination scenario (EWC NA Qualifier Playoffs, Round 1 lower bracket). One team is likely to collapse under pressure; the underdog (currently priced at 55%) often has less to lose and may execute more cleanly in high-stakes BO3s. PATCH/META UNKNOWN: No League of Legends patch notes or meta assessment in briefing. A recent durability shift, ADC rework, or jungle nerf could asymmetrically favor one team's playstyle. The team that drafted for the OLD meta loses hard. COACHING/PREPARATION EDGE: With match starting in ~6 hours and no access to team prep reports, a well-coordinated underdog with superior reads on the meta and opponent's likely champion pool could steal Games 1\u20132. MARKET MISPRICE SIGNAL: 44/55 split is only 11 percentage points; given complete data vacuum, this is suspiciously precise. Either: (a) bettors have private intel we lack, or (b) the market is barely above random and vulnerable to a flip on new information. CONFIDENCE DEPRESSION: confidence_yes = 22 and confidence_no = 24 reflect genuine epistemic humility. We have NO basis to favor either team. The 10-point gap (42 vs 48) represents uncertainty about whether the market's slight NO lean (55%) is rational or a weak bias toward 'underdog premium.' NO SYMMETRY BREAK: There is no asymmetric evidence favoring YES over NO. Black swan (roster disruption) affects both sides equally in theory, but impacts the LOWER-BRACKET favorite (likely Dignitas) more severely, slightly elevating NO odds to 48.", "key_factor": "Dignitas roster instability or last-minute substitution (e.g., a key player unable to travel, visa delay, or illness 6 hours before match start) forces a strategic shift that Disguised Toast is unexpectedly well-positioned to punish in lower-bracket pressure format."}], "final_score": 0.4691349009081178, "no_score": 0.5326356759771417, "edge": 0.24018518518518522, "no_edge": 0.1301851851851853, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 21% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6851851851851852, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0702687976791527, "The Bull": 0.9559930478535308, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0562331438919461, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0626106949123544, "The Domain Specialist": 1.059634504436164, "The Contrarian": 1.0571973090855826, "The Bear": 0.73806250214127}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1996879", "question": "LoL: Dignitas vs Disguised (BO3) - Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket round 1 match between Dignitas and Disguised in the Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 16 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dignitas\" if Dignitas win the match against Disguised.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Disguised\" if Disguised win the match against Dignitas.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.445, "volume_usd": 6243.875850000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["44344542386215412938578728688595480218558690115668336341448330269391646575450", "19194122347316204573379639489295787419566045324191035901838152433660410436069"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["$26,250\n\nYears acti