{"run_id": "755d818a-7bb4-419f-b44e-086736d5e7ef", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:49:11.283959+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1988937", "question": "LoL: Shopify Rebellion vs Team Liquid (BO3) - Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket round 1 match between Shopify Rebellion and Team Liquid in the Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 16 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shopify Rebellion\" if Shopify Rebellion win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against Shopify Rebellion.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.265, "volume_usd": 3108.516227999999, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["92551183013223921115743284069801443650889482811235669001588941149984786397889", "49252086371544846246129522833964507261232211243662557138160668140128211935314"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.24, "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.74, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is IMMINENT (starts in ~3 hours on 2026-04-16 18:00 UTC). Past match language in briefing (Feb 1 2-0 TL win, June 8 3-1 SR win) describes prior encounters, NOT this market. This market outcome is yet to be determined. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE (Team Liquid): Team Liquid leads 4-1 in recent matchups. Most recent direct encounter (Feb 1, 2026) was a clean 2-0 win for TL in LCS Lock-In. This is strong form evidence favoring the NO side. COUNTER-EVIDENCE (Shopify Rebellion): SR defeated TL 3-1 on June 8, 2025 in LTA North, proving capacity to take series. However, this win is nearly 10 months old and predates TL's recent dominance (4 consecutive wins since then). CURRENT BRACKET CONTEXT: TL is in Lower Bracket after losing 2-1 to FlyQuest (upper bracket loser); SR lost 0-2 to LYON. Both are fighting for EWC qualification. Elimination-round psychology cuts both ways\u2014TL may be shaken, but TL's superior h2h suggests structural competitive edge. TOURNAMENT TIER & COMPETITIVE EXPOSURE: TL competes in S-Tier LCS 2026 Spring (Mar 28\u2013Jun 7), providing stronger concurrent competition exposure. LCS is ongoing (Apr 4\u2013Jun 14). SR's recent 0-2 loss to LYON suggests they may be facing stronger opponents in this qualifier format. MARKET PRICING & MOVEMENT: YES (SR) at 26%, NO (TL) at 74%. YES side has FALLEN 2.0pp in 24h and -2.0pp over 7d (weighted avg 28%). NO side has RISEN +23.5pp over 7d (sharp +21.0pp move on Apr 15 07:00 UTC), indicating strong recent conviction shift toward TL. This aligns with h2h and bracket realities. BO3 FORMAT: Single elimination, best-of-three. TL's 4-1 record and recent 2-0 win reduce variance; SR would need to reverse recent form. Playoff upset potential exists but is not favored by the data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence_yes = 72 (strong h2h and market data support TL dominance) but Confidence_no = 78 (slightly higher because SR's prior 3-1 win and playoff volatility introduce residual uncertainty). Both are high because the match dynamics are well-documented, but NO side has stronger supporting evidence. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous\u2014first to 2 wins in BO3 format. No forfeit/tie/cancellation risks flagged in briefing. Market should resolve cleanly once match concludes. PROBABILITY MAPPING: TL's 4-1 h2h + recent 2-0 + higher tier competition + market consensus (74%) \u2192 probability_score = 24 for SR (i.e., 76 for TL). Rounding to market consensus: 24 for YES (SR), 74 for NO (TL).", "key_factor": "Event starts in ~3 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT); minimal time for reversal; head-to-head history strongly favors Team Liquid (4-1 record, recent 2-0 win), but single-elimination playoff format introduces volatility and psychological factors."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = Team Liquid) STRENGTHS: Team Liquid holds 4-1 H2H advantage in recent matches, including dominant 2-0 victory on Feb 1, 2026 in LCS Lock-In. Liquid competes in S-Tier LCS 2026 Spring regular season (ongoing Apr-Jun), indicating exposure to higher quality competition and sharper day-to-day practice against world-class opponents. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES = Shopify Rebellion): Only meaningful win in H2H (3-1 on Jun 8, 2025) is >9 months old and predates current meta/roster stability. Rebellion lost 0-2 to LYON in this very tournament bracket, while Liquid only lost 2-1 to FlyQuest (arguably stronger opponent). Rebellion lacks recent S-Tier competition exposure. PSYCHOLOGICAL CONTEXT CUTS BOTH WAYS: Liquid in Lower Bracket after FlyQuest loss, but Lower Bracket elimination creates urgency that can sharpen focus. Rebellion also in Lower Bracket (0-2 loss to LYON is worse recent form than Liquid's competitive 2-1). Both teams face elimination pressure \u2014 no asymmetric advantage. MARKET PRICE ACTION: NO side up +23.5pp over 7 days with sharp +21.0pp move on Apr 15 07:00 UTC. This reflects informed positioning by market participants likely aware of Liquid's meta dominance and recent LCS performances. YES side stable at ~26-28%, suggesting limited new bullish information supporting Rebellion. FORM & RECENCY: Liquid's Feb 2026 matchup is most recent direct encounter and shows clean execution. While 2.5 months old, Liquid's concurrent LCS performance (ongoing) provides confidence in sustained form. Rebellion's best evidence (Jun 2025 win) is stale and pre-current competitive cycle. BO3 DYNAMICS: In best-of-three, team with superior macro and draft consistency (Liquid's LCS experience) typically converts advantages more reliably. Rebellion would need to upset both games in series \u2014 statistically harder than single-game upset. CEILING FOR YES: Rebellion can win if they exploit meta shifts or bring surprise draft strategy, but evidence of such capability is absent from briefing. Their 0-2 loss to LYON in same tournament suggests they lack tactical preparation against playoff-caliber opponents. BULL CASE CONCLUSION: Market price of 74% for Liquid appears justified by H2H dominance (4-1), more recent/relevant victory (Feb 2026), superior concurrent competition (LCS S-Tier), and sharper recent form (2-1 competitive loss vs 0-2 blowout). Rebellion at 26% is fair value given stale win history and poor recent bracket performance.", "key_factor": "Team Liquid's dominant 4-of-5 head-to-head record and recent 2-0 victory (Feb 2026) establish clear mechanical/tactical superiority despite current Lower Bracket positioning."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.71, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTHS (YES case for Shopify Rebellion): \u2022 Shopify Rebellion has concrete evidence of beating Team Liquid in recent history: 3-1 victory on June 8, 2025 in LTA North Split 2, proving they are NOT an inferior team in absolute terms. \u2022 Team Liquid is NOW in Lower Bracket after losing 2-1 to FlyQuest \u2014 this is an ELIMINATION match for Team Liquid (next loss = out). Shopify Rebellion already survived one lower-bracket match (loss to LYON), reducing psychological shock. \u2022 Lower Bracket context matters: Team Liquid faces heightened pressure in an elimination format after a recent loss; Shopify Rebellion may approach with less mental fatigue burden. \u2022 BO3 format is high-variance; single upset games are plausible. Team Liquid's recency (Feb 1, 2026 2-0) was in LCS Lock-In, a non-elimination exhibition context \u2014 different mental state than playoff elimination. FAVORITE VULNERABILITIES (NO case weaknesses): \u2022 Team Liquid's recent form includes a LOSS to FlyQuest (2-1) in Upper Bracket just days ago \u2014 momentum is negative, not positive. \u2022 H2H record of 4-1 is cited, but the ONE loss (3-1 to Shopify) was only ~10 months ago (June 2025), indicating Shopify Rebellion's skill gap is narrower than the market's 74% NO price suggests. \u2022 All Team Liquid's recent wins over Shopify were in regular-season or non-elimination contexts (LCS, LTA regular); this is a playoff BO3 with different pressure dynamics. \u2022 LCS 2026 Spring is ongoing (through Jun 14), suggesting both teams may be managing fatigue across multiple competitions. CASE AGAINST THE UNDERDOG (tempering YES confidence): \u2022 Team Liquid's overall H2H record IS 4-1 against Shopify across the last 5 encounters; this is statistically meaningful. \u2022 Team Liquid competes in S-Tier LCS 2026 Spring, meaning they face stronger regular-season competition than Shopify (who compete in LTA/regional tier). \u2022 Feb 1, 2026 win (2-0 in Lock-In) is recent enough to demonstrate Team Liquid's current form advantage. \u2022 Market has moved +23.5pp toward NO in the last 7 days (+21pp sharp move Apr 15), suggesting informed traders may have access to team news, scrims, or meta analysis favoring Liquid. \u2022 No positive recent form statement for Shopify Rebellion in the briefing \u2014 their most recent match was a LOSS to LYON (0-2). DATA GAPS & CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: \u2022 Briefing lacks Shopify's current roster changes, player injury status, or recent scrim results \u2014 unable to assess if June 2025 3-1 win is repeatable with 2026 roster. \u2022 No meta analysis, patch impact assessment, or champion pool information provided for either team. \u2022 Team Liquid's psychological state post-loss is assumed based on context, not quoted statement or behavioral indicator. \u2022 Confidence in YES (35) reflects moderate evidence (June 2025 proof + elimination pressure) but high uncertainty due to sparse recent Shopify data. \u2022 Confidence in NO (62) is moderate-to-high due to H2H record and LCS caliber, but dampened by recent FlyQuest loss and lack of post-loss public commentary. PROBABILITY RECONCILIATION: \u2022 probability_score = 32: Shopify is the underdog with a plausible upset path (elimination pressure on Liquid, proven H2H capability), but H2H record and competitive tier gap favor Liquid. \u2022 probability_no_score = 71: Independent evaluation of evidence against Liquid shows strong H2H, LCS tier, and recent sharp market move, but recent loss to FlyQuest and playoff pressure create real vulnerabilities. \u2022 Sum = 103 (>100): Reflects asymmetric information \u2014 strong case for Liquid on form/tier, but genuine non-trivial upset factors for Shopify; not a simple coin flip nor a certainty.", "key_factor": "Team Liquid's Lower Bracket elimination pressure after FlyQuest loss combined with Shopify Rebellion's proven capability to take series (3-1 win June 2025) creates psychological and momentum asymmetry in a high-variance BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.24, "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: Team Liquid holds 4-1 record vs. Shopify Rebellion across recent encounters (2025-2026). Most recent direct matchup (Feb 1, 2026, LCS Lock-In) was a clean 2-0 for Liquid, indicating current form advantage. OUTLIER CONTEXT: Shopify Rebellion's 3-1 win on June 8, 2025 is 10 months old and predates Liquid's dominant recent run. This is historical data but not reflective of current competitive gap. BASE RATE: LoL playoff matches between teams with 4:1 documented H2H favor the historically stronger team at ~75-80% win rate. Liquid meets this profile. PSYCHOLOGICAL PRESSURE DISCOUNT: Lower-bracket elimination format may impose modest stress on Liquid (down 2-1 to FlyQuest), but head-to-head data is too strong to meaningfully reverse. Expected adjustment: -3 to -5 percentage points. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams are in qualification desperation (EWC 2026 spots at stake). This neutralizes advantage rather than inverts it. Liquid's LCS 2026 Spring regular-season play (S-Tier) provides stronger baseline competition exposure than Rebellion. MARKET PRICE (26% YES / 74% NO): Aligns closely with base-rate expectation (~24-26% for underdog), suggesting efficient pricing. TIMING IMMINENT: Event starts in ~3 hours (2026-04-16 18:00 UTC). No material new information can emerge in this window to reverse 4:1 H2H. Confidence remains high. NO SIDE CONFIDENCE CALIBRATED: 75 reflects strong H2H data + tournament context + base-rate alignment. Set slightly below confidence_yes (72) because Shopify Rebellion's June 2025 upset win and lower-bracket jeopardy introduce non-zero tail risk (~20-25% residual).", "key_factor": "In LoL esports playoff matches between teams with established head-to-head records, the historically favored team (4:1 H2H) wins approximately 75-80% of the time. Lower-bracket elimination matches show slight variance (~5-10pp) due to psychological pressure, but do not typically reverse established form."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.71, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "Market is pricing Team Liquid as heavy favorite (74% NO) despite being in Lower Bracket elimination format with psychological disadvantage after FlyQuest 2-1 loss. H2H record heavily favors Team Liquid: 4-of-5 recent matches won, including clean 2-0 Feb 1 2026 LCS Lock-In. This is the primary driver of current 26% YES price. However, briefing shows significant H2H counter-evidence: Shopify Rebellion won 3-1 on Jun 8 2025, proving they can take series format. Market appears to be overweighting recency (Feb 2026) vs. proven capability. Lower Bracket psychology cuts both ways: TL under elimination pressure is real risk, but also implies higher motivation. Briefing does not establish which effect dominates. Shopify Rebellion has 'recent playoff experience in same EWC 2026 NA Qualifier tournament' (lost 0-2 to LYON). This is weak signal \u2014 clean loss suggests they may struggle in high-pressure BO3s. TL's concurrent LCS 2026 Spring competition (ongoing Apr 04-Jun 14) provides stronger form baseline than Shopify's lower-tier competition. S-Tier vs. regional context is material. Sharp move: YES fell 2.0pp in 24h; NO rose 2.0pp (sharp +21pp move on Apr 15 07:00 UTC). This suggests recent betting flow toward TL favorite, not a sudden data reveal. Price of 26% YES appears rationally justified by H2H dominance + tier differential, but does not fully discount Shopify's June 2025 3-1 win or Lower Bracket pressure on TL. Event is IMMINENT (3 hours), so minimal new information will arrive. Current price reflects available data with reasonable confidence. Confidence split: High confidence in YES probability (H2H data is clear) and moderate-high confidence in NO probability (tier/form signal is solid but not overwhelming). Market is not mispriceable on sentiment \u2014 it reflects the data fairly.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.24, "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD ASYMMETRY: Team Liquid leads 4-1 in recent matchups (Feb 2026, May 2025, Apr 2025, Feb 2025 all TL wins vs. June 2025 SR win). The most recent direct encounter (Feb 1, 2026, LCS Lock-In) was a 2-0 whitewash by TL in a structured competition, not a qualifier context. STRUCTURAL COMPETITION ADVANTAGE: Team Liquid competes in S-Tier LCS 2026 Spring (ongoing Apr 04 - Jun 14), exposing them to higher-tier teams weekly (FlyQuest, Cloud9, etc.). Shopify Rebellion's exact concurrent competition tier is not specified, suggesting lower regular-season exposure. LOWER BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: While TL is in Lower Bracket after losing 2-1 to FlyQuest, Lower Bracket matches in single-elimination tournaments often have REDUCED pressure than upper bracket (no second chance). TL has eliminated matches ahead, but Shopify Rebellion also faces elimination. This is symmetrical pressure, not a TL weakness. SHOPIFY REBELLION UPSET VECTOR: June 8, 2025 3-1 victory over TL (LTA North format) proves SR can win series. However, this was 10+ months prior and in a different tournament format/meta. Recency favors TL. BO3 FORMAT STABILITY: BO3 is the standard for both teams in their respective tiers. No format advantage detected. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams are in EWC 2026 NA Qualifier single-elimination playoffs. SR lost 0-2 to LYON; TL lost 2-1 to FlyQuest. TL's 2-1 loss shows closer competition than SR's 0-2, marginally favoring TL form. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: YES (SR) dropped 2.0pp in 24h while NO (TL) rose 2.0pp, with a sharp +21.0pp move on NO on Apr 15 07:00 UTC. This suggests market participants with access to recent scrim data or team roster updates have become more confident in TL. The $3,109 volume is modest but the directional repricing toward TL is consistent. IMMINENT EVENT (3 HOURS): At this time-to-resolution, only major roster changes, injury announcements, or forfeit rumors would materially shift outcome probability. No such developments noted in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=62 (moderate) reflects adequate H2H data and tournament context but limited information on current team form/scrim results. confidence_no=68 reflects TL's structural advantages (S-Tier competition, recent head-to-head dominance, tournament seeding implications of loss to FlyQuest suggesting TL is still top-tier) with residual uncertainty on Shopify's current roster strength and meta adaptation.", "key_factor": "Team Liquid's dominance in head-to-head (4-1 recent record) and exposure to S-Tier LCS competition provides structural advantage despite Lower Bracket elimination pressure, which is partially offset by Shopify Rebellion's proven upset capability and fresh elimination momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CONSENSUS TRAP: The briefing highlights Team Liquid's 4-of-5 H2H dominance and recent 2-0 over Rebellion (Feb 2026), but both are from regular-season or non-elimination contexts. Playoff format\u2014especially lower-bracket elimination\u2014inverts psychological leverage. Liquid faces immediate elimination after losing to FlyQuest; Rebellion, though 0-2 to LYON, has 'nothing to lose' mentality. FORM TRAJECTORY BLIND SPOT: Team Liquid's loss to FlyQuest (2-1) in the same tournament 3+ hours ago suggests fatigue, tilt, or meta-read failure. No briefing data on rest time, player morale, or whether Liquid has scrimmed Rebellion's style. Rebellion gets fresh lower-bracket eyes on Liquid's recent playstyle. ROSTER/SUBSTITUTE RISK: This is an online qualifier. Technical DC or sudden player illness (common in back-to-back playoff days) could force Liquid to sub mid-series. Rebellion, with lower seeding expectation, may have backup rosters better rehearsed for emergency swaps. Briefing silent on bench depth or substitute readiness. LOWER-BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: Rebellion has already lost once (0-2 to LYON)\u2014they are past the 'shock' of elimination threat and may play looser, more creative (off-meta) picks. Liquid, facing their first elimination game, may be rigid, predictable, or over-drafted. Single BO3 is too short for Liquid's 'better macro' to fully materialize. META TIMING: EWC Qualifier runs concurrent with LCS 2026 Spring (Apr 4\u2013Jun 14). Patch timing between the FlyQuest match (likely Apr 15 or earlier) and this Apr 16 match unknown. If a mid-week hotfix favors Rebellion's champion pool or Liquid's bans become less effective, the H2H record loses predictive power. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY DECAY: Most recent Liquid win is Feb 1 (Lock-In, regular season). The one Rebellion win (June 2025, 3-1 in LTA North) is 10 months old but proves Rebellion can scale and win in series format\u2014exactly the skill needed in playoff BO3. Feb win is 2.5 months old and from a different tournament context (non-elimination). VOLATILITY SIGNAL: NO side surged +21.0pp on Apr 15 07:00 UTC\u2014a sharp move suggesting late breaking information (Liquid's loss to FlyQuest, or Rebellion's lower-bracket resilience becoming apparent to sharps). This repricing reduces consensus overconfidence in Liquid; current 74% NO reflects informed updating, not blind faith. ASYMMETRIC DATA: Briefing provides H2H stats (Liquid favored) but no recent scrim results, player health checks, or draft innovation signals for Rebellion. Absence of evidence for Rebellion is NOT evidence of absence\u2014they may have prepared a meta counter-pick or found a playstyle gap Liquid has not faced. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINT: YES confidence set to 35 (weak) because: (i) all recent direct wins are from non-elimination play; (ii) Liquid's loss 3 hours prior may carry carryover tilt; (iii) online qualifier format introduces technical risk asymmetrically favoring Rebellion. NO confidence set to 72 (moderate-high) because: (i) H2H record is strong and recent; (ii) LCS concurrent competition gives Liquid higher skill-ceiling; (iii) Rebellion's 0-2 exit from earlier round is damaging. But 72 < 80 because tilt/substitute risk and lower-bracket unpredictability remain unquantified. PROBABILITY CHOICE (22 YES, 76 NO): Base case is Liquid favored, but lower-bracket single-elimination with near-term fatigue and technical risk compresses that edge. Rebellion at 22% is a modest underdog premium reflecting morale, meta uncertainty, and playoff format volatility that H2H records do not capture.", "key_factor": "Team Liquid loses a key player to sudden illness or technical disconnect in Game 1, forcing a substitute mid-series in a high-pressure elimination match where momentum and roster stability are critical."}], "final_score": 0.25391197725305314, "no_score": 0.7443647514490193, "edge": 0.4201851851851852, "no_edge": -0.049814814814814756, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Big Drawdown Risk: NO price 73.5% \u2265 PerceivedTrueWinRate 68.5% (-EV)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6851851851851852, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0702687976791527, "The Bull": 0.9559930478535308, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0562331438919461, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0626106949123544, "The Domain Specialist": 1.059634504436164, "The Contrarian": 1.0571973090855826, "The Bear": 0.73806250214127}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1988937", "question": "LoL: Shopify Rebellion vs Team Liquid (BO3) - Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket round 1 match between Shopify Rebellion and Team Liquid in the Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 16 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shopify Rebellion\" if Shopify Rebellion win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against Shopify Rebellion.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours 