.", "key_factor": "Counter-Strike BO3 lower bracket semifinals: ~50% base rate for either team absent specific performance data. Market-calibrated average for Tier 2/3 regional events: ~45-55% split."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.57, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.19, "rationale": "EVENT STATUS: Match is LIVE_OR_PAST (~1 hour into scheduled window). Market prices should be converging toward ~$0.01 or ~$0.99 if outcome is becoming clear, yet prices remain at 42/57 \u2014 suggests match is still ongoing or undecided. PRICE HISTORY MISMATCH: YES side shows +22pp sharp spike (Apr 16 11:00 UTC), then -12pp reversal (Apr 17 00:45 UTC). NO side shows +12pp at same reversal time. This suggests in-match momentum swings, but current market (42/57 for YES) sits BELOW the initial spike, implying current state favors NO or crowd shifted conviction mid-match. ZERO BRIEFING DATA: No team form, recent results, head-to-head record, player rosters, or pre-match analysis provided. Briefing contains only scattered social comments (mentioning Falcons, Vitality, Furia \u2014 none of which appear to be the listed competitors) and generic tournament info. This suggests either data collection failure or extremely low market interest. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Social signals are sparse and off-topic (comments refer to different teams entirely). Market is exhibiting RATIONAL APATHY \u2014 neither side has emotional intensity or narrative support. Prices reflect default uncertainty rather than conviction. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: YES side shows 24.0pp/hr volatility; NO side shows 0.0pp/hr. YES volatility is match-noise (live swings). NO side stability suggests crowd consensus crystallizing around Vasco (57%) despite no supporting briefing data. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Briefing provides ZERO analytical foundation for either team. Current 42/57 split reflects pure market momentum (mid-match swings) not informed opinion. Set both confidence scores LOW (~18-19) and leave ~1pp ignorance mass to reflect data void. SENTIMENT vs PRICE: Market is not exuberant or panicked \u2014 it is INDIFFERENT. Current YES:42% pricing reflects crowd's slight lean toward NO after recent reversals, not emotional conviction. Price movements are technical (match-state dependent) not sentiment-driven. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is online, BO3, Lower Bracket elimination. Forfeit/walkover clause could trigger 50-50 resolution if admin/technical failure. Briefing does not mention any such risk, so standard BO3 completion assumed.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.57, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.19, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Market started ~1 hour ago; BO3 match can last 1.5\u20133 hours depending on map outcomes. Outcome may already be partially determined (1\u20130 or 0\u20131 in series), but briefing does not confirm current score\u2014treating as genuinely LIVE with high uncertainty. ZERO SUBSTANTIVE TEAM DATA: Briefing provides no recent win/loss records, head-to-head history, roster stability, map pool strengths, or individual player form for either Procyon Gaming or Vasco Esports. This is disqualifying for SME confidence in either direction. MARKET SIGNAL WEAK: YES side up +10pp over 7 days and +10pp over 24h; NO side up +12pp over 7 days and +12pp over 24h. Both sides rising suggests market is pricing increasing uncertainty or late-breaking information (e.g., unexpected roster changes, server issues, or qualitative betting volume flux), NOT a convergence on skill differential. SHARP MOVE ASYMMETRY: YES dropped 12pp at Apr 17 00:45 UTC; NO gained +12pp same timestamp. This move occurred ~1 hour before briefing snapshot, suggesting in-match event or live betting cascade\u2014classic LIVE event behavior where interim map results trigger directional shifts. C-TIER TOURNAMENT VOLATILITY: CCT South America Challengers #1 is Valve Tier 2 (online, regional), lower prestige than Major events. Tier 2 online tournaments exhibit higher upset rates due to server latency variance, lower preparation investment by teams, and roster experimentation. This exogenous volatility means historical skill metrics (if available) would be less predictive. MISSING CRITICAL CS2 VARIABLES: (1) Anti-cheat status\u2014VACnet bans or demo reviews immediately before match can alter team roster availability; (2) Server ping/stability\u2014online tournament means ISP or routing issues favor local teams or create parity; (3) Map veto sequence\u2014BO3 CS2 heavily dependent on team map pool, and no pool data provided. Without these, probability is near-coin-flip. CURRENT MARKET PRICING (42% YES / 57% NO) APPEARS RATIONAL GIVEN DATA GAP: The market is pricing NO slight favorite, consistent with a baseline that most underdog paths in BO3 elimination matches favor the 'default' favorite (usually higher seed or recent performer). Absence of evidence for either team suggests market is defaulting to seed position or recent tournament placement\u2014but briefing does not confirm this. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT SLIGHT FAVOR NO: Lower bracket semi-final means both teams are on elimination path (loser out). Teams here have already lost once in the tournament. Historical CS2 meta shows teams with recent wins (upper bracket survivors) have slight psychological edge over teams playing from lower bracket. If Vasco is seeded higher or won recent games, NO advantage is real but small (~55\u201360% range justified). CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=18 and confidence_no=19 (asymmetrically LOW on both sides) reflects genuine epistemic humility\u2014briefing contains no roster names, recent match results, map statistics, or even basic team ranking within CCT South America region. Neither side of the market can be confidently defended with domain expertise when the inputs (player skill, team form, map advantage) are completely absent. Setting both confidences LOW is correct per rules when data is inadequate.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE_OR_PAST with only ~1 hour elapsed; market pricing reflects near-total information vacuum on team form, recent roster changes, anti-cheat integrity, and server stability\u2014three critical CS2 competitive variables that insider traders would exploit, yet briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on any of them."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides zero substantive information about either team's recent form, roster health, map pool, playstyle, or head-to-head record. This is not a close call \u2014 the market is pricing on pure sentiment or external knowledge not captured here. MARKET ANOMALY: YES side surged +22pp on Apr 16 11:00 UTC, then collapsed -12pp at Apr 17 00:45 UTC (during live play). This volatility pattern is consistent with in-match developments (a map loss, a player underperformance, or a roster surprise) rather than pre-game sentiment shifts. EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE_OR_PAST with ~1 hour elapsed. If the first map(s) have already been played, the current pricing reflects early-match evidence. A sharp 12pp move toward NO at 00:45 UTC suggests Vasco may have won Map 1 or Procyon suffered a decisive setback. ONLINE BO3 INFRASTRUCTURE RISK: CCT South America is an online-only tournament. Server stability, regional ISP quality, and client crashes are higher-variance factors in South American esports than LAN events. One team's connection robustness or familiarity with CCT's server infrastructure could be a hidden edge. ROSTER UNCERTAINTY: The briefing mentions 'Furia playing at home with a full arena' in comments, suggesting Furia may be the headline story. If Procyon or Vasco has a roster substitution, injury, or stand-in player not reflected in aggregate stats, this would explain the briefing's silence and the market's high volatility. LOWER BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: This is a lower-bracket elimination match. Teams facing elimination often exhibit high variance (desperation vs. mental collapse). Procyon's +10pp rise over 24 hours could indicate strong momentum, or it could reflect trader over-optimism about a team in a must-win scenario that historically chokes. CONSENSUS BLINDNESS: Zero factual case for either YES or NO in briefing. Market is pricing at 42 YES / 57 NO \u2014 a mild NO lean. Without team-specific intel, this is likely driven by external forums, recent tournament placements, or social sentiment invisible to this analysis. BLACK SWAN MECHANISM: Online BO3 formats create asymmetric risk: if Procyon has a player on a poor connection or a stand-in mid-tournament, Vasco (potentially more stable roster/infrastructure) could exploit this via anti-eco rounds, map selection, and psychological pressure. Conversely, if Vasco is the team with infrastructure/personnel fragility, Procyon's map-by-map adaptability in BO3 could overwhelm them. CONSERVATIVE SCORING: Given that 1 hour of play has already elapsed and the market has just experienced a 12pp swing, the current 42 YES price may already partially encode early match results. However, confidence in both directions is LOW because no public match data (score, map results, player stats) is available in the briefing. RECOMMENDATION: Probability_score of 38 reflects a modest NO lean aligned with current market pricing, but confidence on both sides is capped at ~30 due to structural data poverty. The true driver of resolution is online infrastructure stability and roster continuity \u2014 neither of which is documented here.", "key_factor": "A critical player disconnect, severe lag spike, or client crash affecting one team's server stability during map pivots in a BO3 where online infrastructure reliability is the differentiator, not raw skill."}], "final_score": 0.4348120483132308, "no_score": 0.5621182195856568, "edge": 0.26590909090909093, "no_edge": 0.11590909090909096, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 23% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1997356", "question": "Counter-Strike: Procyon Gaming vs Vasco Esports (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between Procyon Gaming and Vasco Esports in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 16 at 7:45PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Procyon Gaming\" if Procyon Gaming win the match against Vasco Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vasco Esports\" if Vasco Esports win the match against Procyon Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T05:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T23:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.425, "volume_usd": 12042.303353999998, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["102562604279125247807461491888285637418551411350423418858625412233267188503871", "76243782603818305046513662353483231756951275308766411138296637638506661442168"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["My expectation are falcons winning despite i love seeying them lose but i have seen this last dance honeymoon runs before, vitality can't match this", "Best of 3 (Online) * Lower bracket semi-final.", "Login or register to add your comment to the discussion.", "CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by CCT.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 event taking", "Complete overview of the CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1 - Lower Bracket Semi-final #2.", "Furia playing at home with a full arena.", "Please log in and sync your account with Steam to upvote.", "Talk about another bias side for Falcons jfc, they want these turds to win so bad they put the two best teams against each other to play Furia LMAO.", "Vasco matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!"], "news_summary": "Procyon Gaming vs Vasco Esports are facing off in a BO3 Lower Bracket Semi-final match at CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1, an online C-Tier tournament. The event is currently live (started 2026-04-16 23:45 UTC). Search results confirm this is a CCT South America tournament matchup but provide no specific details about team form, recent performance, or pre-match analysis for either squad.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data to build YES case."], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data to build NO case."], "key_context": ["Lower Bracket Semi-final format \u2014 loser is eliminated from the tournament", "Best of 3 (BO3) match format", "Online tournament (CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1)", "C-Tier tournament / Valve Tier 2 event"], "prior_match_facts": [], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T00:46:19.378560Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "102562604279125247807461491888285637418551411350423418858625412233267188503871", "data_points": 3, "weighted_avg": 0.4230954691284095, "change_1w_pp": 9.999999999999998, "change_24h_pp": 9.999999999999998, "volatility_24h": 24.04163056034262, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-16T11:00:52Z", "delta_pp": 22.000000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-17T00:45:51Z", "delta_pp": -12.000000000000005}]}, "no": {"token_id": "76243782603818305046513662353483231756951275308766411138296637638506661442168", "data_points": 2, "weighted_avg": 0.5179244226839415, "change_1w_pp": 11.999999999999995, "change_24h_pp": 11.999999999999995, "volatility_24h": 0.0, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-17T00:45:47Z", "delta_pp": 11.99999