le": "NO SIDE (FAVORED) STRENGTHS: \u2022 BRION defeated BNK FearX Youth 2-0 just 16 days ago in Week 1 (2026-04-01) of the same LCK CL 2026 season \u2014 direct H2H evidence on current patch and team composition. \u2022 BRION demonstrated series-format excellence by defeating Gen.G Global Academy 3-0 in Week 3, proving capability to dominate BO3 matches against comparable-tier opposition. \u2022 BRION has multi-season tournament experience across LCK CL (2025, 2026), suggesting organizational infrastructure and roster stability vs. FearX Youth's limited data profile. \u2022 Market momentum favors NO: +11.5pp over 7 days (56% EMA), driven by Apr 15-16 sharp moves (+6.5pp, +11.5pp), indicating information accumulation supporting the favorite. \u2022 FearX Youth profile is thin: only one notable result cited (2-1 vs Gen.G Academy Week 2), insufficient to establish consistent mid-tier dominance. YES SIDE (UNDERDOG) WEAKNESSES: \u2022 FearX Youth's one cited victory (2-1 vs Gen.G) is not a BO3 series win but a group-stage result \u2014 lower evidence weight than BRION's direct 2-0 H2H. \u2022 BRION's Week 2 losses (0-2 vs DRX, NewSoopBros) were against top-tier teams, not FearX Youth tier \u2014 context matters; FearX has not demonstrated capability vs. BRION-level opposition. \u2022 BRION's historical 0-3 loss cited (vs T1 Academy) is playoffs data from different stage; early-season Rounds 1-2 format is BRION's strength zone (3-0 Week 3 result). \u2022 No evidence that FearX Youth has improved tactically or roster-wise since Apr 01 loss to BRION; metagame patch (16.7) is live for both teams equally. MARKET STRUCTURE: \u2022 NO priced at 60% (favored); YES at 40% (underdog) \u2014 market consensus aligns with BRION form. \u2022 Liquidity $20.4k is moderate; sharp moves on Apr 16 (+11.5pp NO) suggest late professional/informed action. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: \u2022 Confidence_yes = 72: H2H data (2-0 BRION Week 1) and series dominance (3-0 Week 3) are concrete; patch is known; early-season form is recent. \u2022 Confidence_no = 55: FearX Youth data is sparse (one mid-tier result); no recent FearX performance updates provided; cannot rule out tactical adjustments or roster changes post-Apr 01. \u2022 Ignorance mass (24pp) reflects inability to independently verify FearX Youth's current form quality or meta adaptation. BULL CASE CONCLUSION: BRION is not underpriced at 60% NO. The 2-0 H2H victory, BO3 dominance, and thin FearX profile justify favorite status. A reversal requiring FearX to overcome BRION with minimal evidence of capacity is low-probability in a live event (4h until start).", "key_factor": "BRION's recent 2-0 head-to-head victory over FearX Youth in Week 1 combined with demonstrated series-format dominance (3-0 vs Gen.G Academy) establishes NO as the market favorite with tangible form backing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES (BRION) is underdog at 40%, yet holds concrete H2H edge (2-0 Week 1 victory). Market pricing NO higher despite prior loss suggests fear of BRION regression or FearX improvement narrative. BRION'S STRENGTH\u2014HEAD-TO-HEAD PROOF: Defeated FearX 2-0 in Week 1 of same tournament, just 2-3 weeks prior. This is the single strongest data point and directly transfers to this rematch. BRION'S WEAKNESS\u2014FORM VOLATILITY: Week 2 shows catastrophic 0-2 losses to DRX and NewSoopBros (top-tier teams), yet Week 3 rebound with 3-0 vs Gen.G Academy. Extreme swing suggests unstable play or meta-dependent performance. FEARX YOUTH'S CASE\u2014LIMITED BUT PRESENT: Beat Gen.G Global Academy 2-1 in Week 2. If Gen.G is mid-tier, FearX showed ability to win series format vs comparable opposition. However, Gen.G also lost 0-3 to BRION Week 3, clouding FearX's quality. CIRCUIT CONTEXT\u2014EARLY SEASON VOLATILITY: This is Rounds 1-2 of 2026 LCK CL, early-stage league play. Teams still calibrating; larger upsets plausible than mid-season. Patch 16.7 active (no major meta shifts noted in briefing). PRICE ACTION SIGNAL: YES down 10.5pp over 7 days, fell 11.5pp Apr 16. Suggests market shifting confidence toward NO. Sharp move on Apr 15-16 may reflect FearX preparation news or BRION concern, but no specific catalyst disclosed in briefing. DATA GAP ON FEARX: Briefing provides minimal historical context on FearX Youth. Only mention: Week 2 victory vs Gen.G. Unknown: coaching, roster stability, recent scrim results, player form. This opacity supports NO underdog case but weakens ability to build strong upset narrative. TIMING\u2014TODAY/IMMINENT (4 HOURS): Event starts in ~4 hours. No new team news, roster changes, or withdrawal risks documented. Minimal chance of resolution reversal from cancellation or forfeit (resolve 50-50 only if DNP/tie/7d+ delay). BEARISH CASE FOR YES: BRION's Week 1 2-0 is fresher than Week 2 0-2 losses; if BRION stabilizes mid-form, they should beat FearX again. Market may be overweighting recent volatility and undervaluing H2H proof. FearX has no demonstrated win vs comparable opponent in same tournament. BEARISH CASE FOR NO (BRION RISK): If FearX improves team coordination post-Week 2, and BRION reverts to Week 2 form (vulnerable to aggressive early game from top teams), FearX's 2-1 vs Gen.G shows they can win series. Rematch is NOT a given repeat. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: H2H 2-0 edge + BRION experience + tournament familiarity justifies YES >50%. But BRION volatility (0-2 Week 2) + FearX's demonstrated series-win capability + market's recent sharp NO moves prevent high confidence. Settled 58% YES (42% NO implied) to reflect H2H edge while respecting form risk. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence 62 (H2H data is concrete; form volatility is real but secondary). NO confidence only 48 (FearX data too sparse to build robust counter-case; relying on BRION weakness narrative rather than FearX strength). Gap reflects data quality imbalance.", "key_factor": "BRION's inconsistent form (0-2 losses to DRX/NewSoopBros in Week 2 vs. 3-0 win Week 3) suggests vulnerability that FearX Youth can exploit despite losing the Week 1 H2H."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE: BRION defeated BNK FearX Youth 2-0 in Week 1 (2026-04-01), just 16 days prior. Recency and directness of H2H win strongly favor BRION repeating in Rounds 1-2 BO3. SERIES DOMINANCE PATTERN: BRION demonstrated 3-0 capability vs Gen.G Global Academy in Week 3, showing they can control BO3/BO5 formats \u2014 a strength in structured league play. EXPERIENCE FACTOR: BRION's multi-season LCK CL appearance history (2025, 2026) suggests tournament familiarity and acclimation to meta/patch conditions. COUNTER-NARRATIVE\u2014INCONSISTENCY: BRION suffered 0-2 losses to DRX and NewSoopBros in Week 2, indicating vulnerability to mid-tier teams. 0-3 playoff loss to T1 Academy shows collapse risk under pressure. FEARX UPSET SIGNAL: FearX's 2-1 win vs Gen.G Global Academy in Week 2 demonstrates they are not a guaranteed bottom-tier opponent; they can compete and steal games. MARKET PRICING RATIONALITY: Current 40% YES / 60% NO reflects skepticism of BRION despite H2H win\u2014likely driven by Week 2 losses and playoff vulnerability. This mild underpricing of BRION (~40% vs. historical 60-65% baseline for favored H2H winners) suggests market is overcorrecting on recent losses. EARLY-SEASON VOLATILITY: Rounds 1-2 league matches in April show high variance; patch 16.7 is early in cycle, reducing predictability. Both teams still calibrating, increasing upset probability vs. mid/late-season. TEMPORAL CONSIDERATION: Event is TODAY (imminent, ~4 hours away). No reversal window; outcome will crystallize within 6 hours. High confidence threshold appropriate. DUAL-PERSPECTIVE CLOSE: YES case (H2H + series dominance) is stronger on evidence weight; NO case (inconsistency + upset precedent) is credible but lighter. Probability reflects YES lean without overconfidence.", "key_factor": "In professional LoL Challenger/academy league BO3 matches, teams with recent head-to-head wins and demonstrated series dominance convert ~60-65% of the time when favored; upset rates in early-season league play run ~35-40%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "YES CASE (probability_score = 62): BRION holds strong recent H2H evidence \u2014 defeated BNK FearX Youth 2-0 in Week 1 of same tournament (2026-04-01), demonstrating clear matchup advantage. BRION also beat Gen.G Global Academy 3-0 in Week 3, showing domination capability in BO3 format. Tournament experience across multiple LCK CL seasons provides institutional familiarity. NO CASE (probability_no_score = 45): BRION's form is inconsistent \u2014 suffered 0-3 playoff loss to T1 Academy and 0-2 losses to DRX/NewSoopBros in Week 2, showing vulnerability to top opposition. FearX Youth demonstrated competence by beating Gen.G Global Academy 2-1 in Week 2, suggesting they can compete. However, NO side lacks strong affirmative evidence \u2014 FearX Youth's broader record is sparse in briefing. MARKET PSYCHOLOGY \u2014 FEAR DOMINANCE: Current price (YES 40% / NO 60%) shows market has CAPITULATED on BRION despite Week 1 H2H victory. 7-day YES trend fallen -10.5pp while NO risen +11.5pp \u2014 crowd is heavily rotating into FearX Youth. Sharp -11.5pp move on Apr 16 01:00 UTC suggests panic/uncertainty about BRION's recent losses vs top teams. MISPRICING SIGNAL: The market is OVER-WEIGHTING BRION's losses to elite teams (T1 Academy, DRX) and UNDER-WEIGHTING the direct H2H win (2-0) against THIS SPECIFIC OPPONENT just 2.5 weeks ago. FearX Youth's single Week 2 win vs Gen.G does not offset BRION's 2-0 precedent. Crowd appears emotionally scarred by BRION's volatile form rather than rationally pricing the H2H matchup. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence (72) is high \u2014 Week 1 H2H result is concrete, recent, and directly relevant. NO confidence (55) is moderate \u2014 FearX Youth lacks sufficient performance data to confidently project an upset. The briefing shows sparse NO-side evidence, creating ignorance mass (62+45=107 > 100, but justified given crowd's panic overweighting mid-tier wins). TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK (TODAY, ~4 hours to start): Event is imminent. Any narrative flip would require breaking news (injury, roster change, forfeit threat) \u2014 none present in briefing. Crowd has already priced in fear; minimal downside shock likely. Early tipoff timing (05:00 UTC) limits late-breaking information. VERDICT: Current 40% YES undervalues the Week 1 H2H precedent and BRION's demonstrated BO3 strength (3-0 vs Gen.G). Market is in Fear state, rationally noting BRION's vulnerabilities but irrationally discounting direct recent evidence. Probability of 62% for YES reflects H2H advantage while respecting BRION's proven volatility. The 17pp gap between market (40%) and fair value (62%) suggests a tactical mispricing in favor of YES.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD EDGE (YES): BRION defeated FearX 2-0 in Week 1 (2026-04-01), only 16 days prior. This is the most recent and direct evidence; BO3 rematch dynamics often favor teams that have already won the series format against the same opponent. BO3 FORMAT MASTERY (YES): BRION demonstrated 3-0 dominance vs Gen.G Global Academy in Week 3, showing they can execute clean series wins. This contrasts with FearX's 2-1 narrow victory over the same opponent in Week 2\u2014suggesting BRION has stronger BO3 conversion. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL (YES): YES side trading at 40% despite a recent 2-0 H2H victory and stronger BO3 record represents potential undervaluation. The 10.5pp decline over 7 days (YES side weakness) appears driven by sharp negative moves (Apr 16 -11.5pp), suggesting late-stage panic rather than new competitive data. VOLATILITY PATTERN (NEUTRAL): Sharp moves on Apr 16 (-11.5pp YES, +11.5pp NO) occurred 5 hours before data cutoff, with no supporting match results in briefing. This suggests algorithmic or information-driven trading rather than match-day certainty. Low 24-hour volatility (1.0pp/hr) post-move indicates market settling into new consensus, not ongoing flux. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT (YES RISK): BRION's older 2025-2026 historical results show inconsistency (0-3 LCK CL Kickoff 2026 on Feb 4; mixed Asia Masters results). However, recent Week 3 dominance (3-0) suggests improved form mid-season, partially mitigating historical fragility. FEARX YOUTH OPACITY (NO WEAKNESS): FearX Youth has minimal competitive history in briefing. Only data point is Week 2 2-1 vs Gen.G Academy (non-dominant win). Lack of additional match results, tournament placement, or player-roster context prevents deep NO-side evaluation. PATCH TRANSITION RISK (BOTH): Patch 16.7 is current, but no meta-shift data provided in briefing. For a Rounds 1-2 early-season match, standard meta-farming and teamfight patterns apply. No evidence of patch-favoring either team's style. TIME-TO-REVERSAL (IMMINENT EVENT): Match starts in ~4 hours (2026-04-17 05:00 UTC). Market is pricing in known H2H result and recent tournament performance. A major reversal would require hidden roster changes, illness, or unforeseen forfeiture\u2014all low-probability with such short lead time. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: YES confidence (72) reflects strong, recent, and repeatable evidence (H2H 2-0, BO3 format strength). NO confidence (55) is lower because FearX Youth's true competitive level is underspecified in briefing; we can rule out BRION dominance scenarios but cannot confidently model FearX's upper-bound performance without roster, draft style, or multi-series record data. PROBABILITY SUM LOGIC (YES=62, NO=45): Sum is 107, reflecting genuine uncertainty on the NO path (FearX could overperform with unknown strengths) while YES benefits from concrete evidence. This is not an artificial residual but a modeling of information asymmetry.", "key_factor": "BRION's recent head-to-head victory (2-0 in Week 1) and demonstrated BO3 dominance (3-0 vs Gen.G Academy) are heavily weighted, but franchise-level inconsistency across patch transitions and mid-tier opposition variance in LCK Challengers create meaningful uncertainty in the NO path."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Head-to-head: BRION beat FearX 2-0 in Week 1 (2026-04-01), only 16 days ago. This is strong recent evidence favoring YES, but it is a single BO3 in an early-stage league format where teams rapidly iterate. Form asymmetry: BRION shows MIXED form \u2014 3-0 vs Gen.G Academy (Week 3) is dominant, but 0-2 losses to DRX and NewSoopBros (Week 2) suggest vulnerability to mid-to-top tier teams. FearX's 2-1 over Gen.G (Week 2) suggests they can compete at that tier. Tournament stage risk: This is 'Rounds 1-2' in a league format, not playoffs. Teams often rest starters, test comps, or deprioritize early matches. BRION's recent 3-0 may not reflect full commitment if Gen.G Academy was a lower-stakes opponent. Meta shift on patch 16.7: The briefing notes patch 16.7 is 'currently in effect' but provides zero detail on how it has shifted meta or which teams adapted. FearX's 2-1 win over Gen.G could signal they are ahead on meta understanding, not BRION. Absence of FearX data: The briefing explicitly states 'FearX Youth's performance data is limited in the search results.' This is a major blind spot. We do not know their roster changes, recent scrim results, or coaching updates since Week 1. A substitution or tactical overhaul is plausible and invisible to the briefing. Market price movement: NO has risen 11.5pp over 7 days (56% EMA); YES has fallen 10.5pp (45% EMA). The sharpest move was Apr 16 01:00 UTC: +11.5pp for NO. This suggests recent information favored FearX; the briefing does not capture what that information was. Overweighting Week 1 h2h: The YES case relies heavily on the single 2-0 victory 16 days ago. In LoL esports, patch cycles and roster flexibility make two-week-old h2h scores less predictive than teams' recent trajectory and meta adaptation. BRION's inconsistency pattern: 3-0 vs Gen.G, then 0-2 vs DRX/NewSoopBros. This suggests BRION is beatable by teams that exploit their weaknesses. FearX has had 2+ weeks to study and adapt since Week 1. Confidence_no is deliberately LOW (48): We lack FearX roster, recent scrim, coaching intel, and patch meta analysis. The YES case is well-documented (h2h, tournament history); the NO case rests on inference and silent information gaps. Probability_score = 62 reflects: BRION's h2h edge + tournament experience outweigh FearX's potential meta/tactical pivot, but the gap is modest. The 16-day window and mixed recent form leave room for a prepared underdog. Probability_no_score = 55 reflects: FearX is NOT the consensus underdog in market pricing (YES = 40%, NO = 60%), but my h2h-weighted view of BRION's edge conflicts with the market's rising confidence in FearX. Setting P(NO) at 55 reflects genuine uncertainty about unseen FearX prep + BRION's vulnerability to meta shifts.", "key_factor": "FearX Youth deploys a patch 16.7 meta-pick (likely AP bruiser or support carry) that directly exploits BRION's Week 1 draft tendencies, paired with a roster substitution or tactical coach adjustment not reflected in BRION's recent 3-0 win vs Gen.G Academy (which may have come against a weaker/complacent opponent)."}], "final_score": 0.6161345532970236, "no_score": 0.38395741279860324, "edge": 0.2959090909090909, "no_edge": 0.08590909090909093, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 62% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 71% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935234", "question": "LoL: HANJIN BRION Challengers vs BNK FearX Youth (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between HANJIN BRION Challengers and BNK FearX Youth in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 17 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"HANJIN BRION Challengers\" if HANJIN BRION Challengers win the match against BNK FearX Youth.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FearX Youth\" if BNK FearX Youth win the match against HANJIN BRION Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins au