competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T11:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T05:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 15096.041755999997, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["43359096093308637125960640171258674847500939850426755226656462552774667875078", "20264080943098240274976696456847134620965357704131666537462747031646693678319"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.34, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled for 2026-04-17 05:00 UTC (TODAY, ~4 hours from briefing timestamp 00:49 UTC). Event has NOT started yet. No past-tense outcome language in briefing applies to THIS match. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous \u2014 resolves to winning team (BO3 format, first to 2 wins). No edge cases triggered (no cancellation, tie, forfeit, or >7 day delay language present). TEAM IDENTIFICATION: Both team names (T1 Academy, Dplus KIA Challengers) are explicit and unambiguous in briefing and resolution criteria. No name-matching risk. DATA QUALITY: Briefing contains match statistics from OTHER LCK CL encounters (HLE Challengers vs T1 Esports Academy, Nongshim vs FEARX Youth, etc.) but provides ZERO direct intel on T1 Academy vs Dplus KIA Challengers \u2014 no prior head-to-head record, no recent form data, no roster comparisons, no analyst commentary. CASE FOR YES (T1 Academy): Market prices T1 Academy at 66% (YES side). This reflects a 32pp premium over NO side (66 vs 34). Market may be pricing in T1's main-roster pedigree and academy infrastructure, but briefing provides no explicit support for this advantage over Dplus KIA Challengers. CASE FOR NO (Dplus KIA Challengers): Market prices Dplus KIA Challengers at 34% (NO side). Briefing contains no negative data about DKC performance, form, or roster strength. The 34% reflects market bearishness but lacks empirical grounding in briefing. MARKET PRICE HISTORY: YES side (T1 Academy) has risen +15.5pp over 7 days (EMA 69%), suggesting accumulating confidence in T1 Academy. However, 24-hour volatility is 1.6-1.8pp/hr and sharp moves of \u00b15\u20138pp on Apr 13, 15, 16 indicate trader uncertainty and potentially reactive positioning rather than fundamental conviction. VOLUME: $15,096 USD \u2014 moderate volume for a challenger-level match; not high conviction on either side from large traders. RESOLUTION SOURCE: gol.gg/esports/home (official); 2-hour fallback to credible reporting + video evidence. No mechanism risk identified. OUTCOME CONDITION: Will T1 Academy win the BO3 match? Briefing provides zero predictive data. Probability_score = 66 reflects MARKET CONSENSUS, not analytical edge. Confidence on both sides is LOW because briefing offers no team-level or player-level comparison. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (28) and confidence_no (25) are both LOW and close, reflecting symmetric ignorance. YES side gets +3 points only because market aggregate (66%) slightly exceeds neutral (50%), suggesting weak crowd signal. confidence_yes is not 'high' because market price alone is not strong evidence without supporting team data. INDEPENDENCE CHECK: probability_score (66) + probability_no_score (34) = 100. This reflects the binary nature of the match (one team must win) and lack of tie/cancel risk. No dormant mass is appropriate here.", "key_factor": "No direct team statistics, prior matchup history, current form data, or roster information provided in briefing; market probability relies entirely on order-book consensus rather than analytical data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES is priced at 66% (favored), NO at 34% (underdog). The 7-day trend shows YES rising +15.5pp while NO falls -14.5pp, indicating sustained market confidence in T1 Academy despite recent 24-hour volatility (-12.0pp for YES). ORGANIZATION PEDIGREE: T1 is the most successful organization in League of Legends esports globally with unmatched resources, coaching infrastructure, and player development systems. T1 Academy benefits from this institutional advantage in recruitment, training, and strategic depth \u2014 a structural edge that typically persists at the challenger tier. DPLUS KIA CONTEXT: Dplus KIA is a mid-tier LCK org but operates at the main team level; their 'Challengers' designation suggests a lower-tier squad. No evidence of Dplus KIA's recent form, roster strength, or internal investment in challenger development is provided in the briefing. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: The briefing contains NO direct head-to-head history, NO current season win-loss records for either team, NO individual player performance metrics for T1 Academy or Dplus KIA Challengers, and NO recent form data (scrims, past matches this split). The match data shown (HLE vs T1A, Nongshim matches) are OTHER teams \u2014 not actionable for this matchup. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $15,096 USD is modest volume for a prediction market, suggesting limited sharp action and potentially retail-dominated pricing. The market may be pricing T1's brand equity rather than matchup-specific fundamentals. RECENT VOLATILITY: YES fell 12pp in 24 hours (Apr 16 07:00 UTC -5.0pp visible), indicating either new information (injury, roster change?) or profit-taking. This suggests the market is not fully confident and contains uncertainty even on the favored side. EVENT TIMING: Event is TODAY, ~4 hours away. Very little time for major reversals. If T1 Academy were substantially weaker than priced, sharp money would have crushed YES already. The persistence of 66% suggests either genuine parity or that YES is underpriced. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Strong organizational argument for T1 (favored) but zero direct performance evidence. Dplus KIA's weaknesses are inferred from organizational tier, not demonstrated. Confidence on YES is ~35 due to data scarcity; confidence on NO is similarly low (~28) because there is no affirmative case for underdog strength \u2014 only absence of data on T1. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY: YES = 66, NO = 32 leaves 2pp unexplained (market vig, edge uncertainty). Do NOT mechanically invert to 34 on NO side; the bull case for T1 is thin (org prestige only), making true NO probability lower than 34 because no counter-evidence was found. Leaving ignorance mass reflects the reality that both teams are opaque. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is BO3, not single-game, reducing variance. Forfeiture or cancellation resolves 50-50, but no evidence of either risk is provided.", "key_factor": "Market consensus reflecting T1's organizational prestige and academy infrastructure advantage, though severely hampered by absent direct matchup and form data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.3, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides zero concrete information about either team's recent form, win-loss records, player performance trends, or head-to-head history in LCK Challengers League. The match data shown (HLE Challengers vs T1 Esports Academy, Nongshim vs FEARX Youth, Nongshim vs DRX Challengers) are from OTHER matches, not the T1 Academy vs Dplus KIA matchup in question. T1 ACADEMY FAVORITE ASSUMPTIONS: YES is priced at 66% despite the briefing containing NO evidence-based justification. The market appears to rely on: (1) T1 brand recognition as an org, (2) assumption that T1 academy rosters are stronger, (3) possible confusion with main LCK team. Academy-level competition is notoriously volatile and less predictable than main rosters. DPLUS KIA UNDERDOG OPPORTUNITY: NO is priced at 34%, yet the briefing provides no data refuting Dplus KIA's capability. In academy/challenger leagues, mid-table teams often have comparable strength. Without recent form data, assuming a 32pp gap is unjustified. MARKET MOMENTUM SIGNAL \u2014 CAUTION: YES rose +15.5pp over 7 days and has high volatility (1.6pp/hr). This suggests hype-driven pricing rather than data-driven confidence. The 24-hour swing (-12.0pp) shows instability, consistent with a thinly-informed market ($15,096 volume is low for a LoL match). LACK OF ASYMMETRIC EVIDENCE: A true bear case for NO requires either (a) evidence of Dplus KIA strength or (b) evidence of T1 Academy weakness. The briefing contains NEITHER. This is a symmetric ignorance situation \u2014 both sides are equally under-evidenced. The 66/34 split reflects market speculation, not skill-based prediction. ACADEMY-LEVEL VOLATILITY: LCK Challengers League features academy and challenger rosters, which exhibit higher variance in match outcomes than main league. Single-match outcomes are less predictable. A 66% favorite in such a setting is unusually confident absent direct form data. TEMPORAL RISK: Event starts in ~4 hours. No new information is expected to resolve the data gap. The market is essentially betting blind on T1 Academy reputation. CONFIDENCE ASSYMETRY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set LOW (28, 30) because the briefing lacks sufficient evidence for either side. The slight edge in confidence_no (30 vs 28) reflects that the bear case is defensible \u2014 the market is overpricing YES on assumption alone \u2014 but the case for NO is equally thin. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY: probability_score (38) and probability_no_score (42) do not sum to 100, leaving ~20pp ignorance mass. This reflects genuine uncertainty, not a mechanical inverse. The bear argues that YES is overpriced (38 < 66) and NO deserves modest weight (42), but neither claim is high-confidence given absent data.", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA Challengers benefits from severe information asymmetry \u2014 the briefing contains zero direct performance data, recent form metrics, or head-to-head history, leaving market-priced confidence in T1 Academy as assumption-based rather than evidence-backed."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.34, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO direct head-to-head history, recent form, roster strength, or player-level performance comparisons between T1 Academy and Dplus KIA Challengers. BRIEFING CONTAINS UNRELATED MATCHES: All match data shown (HLE Challengers vs T1 Academy, Nongshim vs FEARX, Nongshim vs DRX) are NOT the target matchup. These provide no predictive signal for this specific pairing. T1 ACADEMY AFFILIATION SIGNAL: T1 is the dominant LCK main-roster organization historically; their academy rosters typically outperform standard challengers. This provides weak positive signal for T1 Academy but is NOT quantified in briefing. MARKET PRICE AS PROXY: Current YES price of 66% suggests modest T1 Academy favoritism. Market has risen +15.5pp over 7 days, indicating accumulating confidence in T1 Academy, but high volatility (24h: -12.0pp) reveals uncertainty. NO COMPARABLE BASE RATE: LCK Challengers League academy matches lack published historical success rates. Cannot anchor to 'X% of academy teams beat challengers' or similar. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES side benefits from T1's institutional reputation (weak but real signal). NO side has NO articulated advantage in briefing \u2014 hence lower confidence_no. IMMINENT EVENT (4 HOURS): Very limited time for new information to shift odds materially. Current market price likely reflects available consensus; deviation from 66% would require breaking news (injury, roster change, forfeit threat) \u2014 all unlikely at this stage. RESOLUTION RISK: Match may be canceled or delayed beyond 7 days (resolves 50-50 under criteria). Probability of cancellation/delay is non-zero but historically rare for scheduled LCK CL matches (~2-5%). STRATEGY: Default to market price (66%) as point estimate, given information vacuum and imminent event timing. Reduce both confidence scores equally to reflect dual-sided ignorance, but keep YES slightly higher due to T1 Academy affiliation signal.", "key_factor": "LCK Challengers League \u2014 no reliable historical win-rate baseline for T1 Academy vs. Dplus KIA Challengers; academy/challenger competition lacks published base rates"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.34, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero direct intel on T1 Academy vs Dplus KIA Challengers \u2014 no head-to-head history, no recent form data, no player roster info, no meta context. YES SIDE NARRATIVE: Market prices YES at 66%, suggesting modest but not extreme confidence in T1 Academy. T1 brand carries prestige, but this is an academy team in a challenger league \u2014 lower information asymmetry than main roster matches. NO SIDE NARRATIVE: Market prices NO at 34%, implying modest underdog status for Dplus KIA. No briefing data supports or refutes this positioning. Dplus KIA is not a recognized dominant force in the briefing. PRICE HISTORY SIGNAL: YES rose +15.5pp over 7 days; YES dropped -12pp in last 24 hours. This volatility without new briefing facts suggests crowd is trading on sentiment, not news. Sharp moves (Apr 13 -8.5pp, Apr 15 \u00b17.5pp, Apr 16 -5pp) show no correlation to published events in briefing. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market is pricing a mild T1 Academy favorite based on brand/prestige inference, not on hard matchup data. The 66/34 split feels like a reasonable 'academy team with famous org' default, not a signal of deep analysis. APATHY DETECTION: Briefing provides only generic tournament context (LCK CL Split 2, BO3 format). NO match preview, NO power rankings, NO recent W-L records, NO meta analysis. Market is operating on priors (T1 prestige), not on current intelligence. VOLUME SIGNAL: $15k USD volume is moderate for a pre-event market 4 hours out. Not panic-volume, not euphoria-volume. Suggests casual betting/light interest, consistent with 'apathy' classification. TEMPORAL RISK: Event starts in ~4 hours. Any major reversal (e.g., roster changes, surprise standings) is increasingly unlikely. Current price likely to persist unless breaking news arrives. SYMMETRY OF IGNORANCE: Both YES and NO sides suffer equally from lack of briefing data. Cannot identify either as 'crowded' or 'ignored.' Market is simply assigning T1 a modest edge based on brand, with no contradiction in briefing. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes=28 and confidence_no=25 reflect that briefing provides NO substantive evidence for either team. The 66/34 price is internally consistent but externally unconstrained \u2014 it could plausibly be 55/45 or 75/25 with equal justification from the briefing. Leaving low confidence on both sides flags this epistemic void.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.34, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides extensive match statistics from OTHER LCK CL teams (HLE Challengers, Nongshim Challengers, DRX Challengers, FEARX Youth) but ZERO substantive information on T1 Academy vs Dplus KIA Challengers matchup history, recent results, or player roster composition. NO PRIOR H2H: Despite LCK CL being mid-split (Match 9 reference suggests multiple rounds played), the briefing contains no prior encounters between these two teams that would inform prediction. NO FORM CONTEXT: Cannot assess either team's recent win/loss record, map pool strength, draft tendencies, or mechanical skill trends in current Split 2. NO ROSTER INTEL: Academy/challenger rosters frequently rotate; briefing does not specify starting lineups, substitutions, or whether key players are rested/injured. MARKET PRICE CONSENSUS: YES side at 66% likely reflects T1 org's prestige and academy program reputation (T1 main roster is historically elite), but this is organizational inference, not match-specific analysis. VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hour swing of -12pp on YES side + sharp moves (Apr 13-16) suggest algorithmic/momentum trading rather than new information; no news summary provided for what triggered moves. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-3 introduces higher variance than single games; upset probability higher than single-game market would suggest, especially if teams are closely matched skill-wise. EVENT TIMING IMMINENT: Match starts in ~4 hours UTC; insufficient time for late-breaking roster news or format changes to materially shift probability. Market has crystallized. RESOLUTION CLARITY: Market language is clear (first to 2 wins in BO3); forfeit/walkover scenarios resolve 50-50, reducing tail risk from administrative cancellation. SME ASSESSMENT: Esports outcome prediction at academy/challenger level requires granular rosters, scrim results, meta adaptation, and recent tournament form\u2014NONE of which are present in briefing. This is a pure consensus-price market with no analytical edge available from provided data.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains zero direct head-to-head history, recent form data, or roster composition details for either T1 Academy or Dplus KIA Challengers, making meaningful SME assessment impossible; market price reflects trader consensus rather than analytical edge."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero direct head-to-head history, recent form data, or roster composition for either T1 Academy or Dplus KIA Challengers. Current 66% YES price appears to be derived entirely from T1 brand prestige, not competitive intelligence. T1 ACADEMY STRUCTURAL VULNERABILITY: T1 Academy is a developmental roster that rotates players based on main team needs. If T1's main LCK roster is competing in parallel fixtures (common in split 2 schedule), key academy players may be pulled or benched. Dplus KIA Challengers, conversely, is a full-time challenger team with stable lineup continuity and higher match preparation intensity. TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE SIGNAL: LCK CL Split 2 mid-stage matches (Match 9 context in briefing) suggest high-stakes qualification scenarios. Teams that have built full identity (like Dplus KIA) often outperform academy rotations in BO3 formats where best-of-three punishes inconsistent drafting and communication. MARKET VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: YES side dropped 12pp in last 24 hours (69% EMA to 66% current) despite no fresh negative news reported. This suggests sharp-money traders with insider roster/scheduling knowledge are quietly exiting YES. NO side volatility (1.8pp/hr) exceeds YES (1.6pp/hr), indicating uncertainty favor. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL ON ACADEMY DEPTH: Search results show matches involving HLE Challengers, Nongshim Challengers, DRX Challengers, and FEARX Youth \u2014 but ZERO recent T1 Academy match data or roster updates in the briefing. This conspicuous silence on T1 Academy form is the single largest red flag for contrarian analysis. CHALLENGER TEAM ADVANTAGE IN BO3: Academy rosters often struggle to maintain composure in best-of-three series where draft adaptation and side-selection psychology matter. Dplus KIA, as a permanent challenger entity, has likely refined meta reads and team synergy over longer periods without main-roster interference. CONDITIONING & FATIGUE MISMATCH: If T1 Academy players are filling in for injured/rotated main roster members, or juggling both academy and main team obligations, their conditioning for a BO3 on this specific date is uncertain. Dplus KIA's full-time roster has no such conflict. MARKET CONSENSUS IS BRAND-DRIVEN: The 66% YES price reflects T1's organizational prestige, not granular competitive data. Polymarket prices on academy/challenger matches are often softer than main-league fixtures, creating room for underdog value on full-time challenger teams. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes (28) is capped because the briefing offers no affirmative T1 Academy stats, form trajectory, or roster confirmation. High confidence_no (26) is equally capped because Dplus KIA's recent form and roster health are equally opaque. The 24pp gap between probability_score (62) and probability_no_score (38) reflects the BLACK SWAN: a late roster substitution or roster-pull would dramatically flip the match in Dplus's favor, whereas no comparable +EV flip scenario exists for YES given the lack of positive T1 Academy signal. EVENT TIMING URGENCY: Match is TODAY (4 hours from briefing timestamp). Roster changes or illness-related benching can occur in the final hours before tip-off. At this stage, such a disruption becomes a 5% base probability event with 80-100% conditional impact on outcome, making it material to contrarian analysis.", "key_factor": "T1 Academy roster substitution or key player illness/benching at match time due to T1's main roster competing simultaneously, exposing academy depth weakness that challenger squads are built to exploit."}], "final_score": 0.6241691803485179, "no_score": 0.38115423472590654, "edge": 0.03590909090909089, "no_edge": 0.34590909090909094, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935211", "question": "LoL: T1 Academy vs Dplus KIA Challengers (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between T1 Academy and Dplus KIA Challengers in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 17 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1 Academy\" if T1 Academy win the match against Dplus KIA Challengers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dplus KIA Challengers\" if Dplus KIA Challengers win the match against T1 Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based