 FearX match in LCK Cup 2025 (not 2026): BFX won 2-0 in Week 2. However, 2025 tournament results have limited predictive power for 2026 Rounds 1-2 play; team rosters, meta, and coaching may have changed substantially. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES at 38% / NO at 62% reflects market consensus favoring BNK FearX. Price history shows YES -11.5pp over 7 days (downtrend), with sharp moves on Apr 12-13. This suggests market sentiment has shifted toward BNK FearX, though reasoning behind sharp moves is not disclosed in briefing. STATISTICAL STRENGTH vs CONSISTENCY RISK: BNK FearX shows elite individual performances (Diable's 14-kill game) but inconsistent series results (2-1 loss vs Gen.G, 0-2 vs T1 in LCK Cup Week 2). DRX's top-side advantage (Smash high CSM) could be leveraged in Rounds 1-2 meta if favors laning. DATA QUALITY / CONFIDENCE GAPS: Briefing lacks recent scrim results, coaching staff changes, or meta shifts between LCK Cup 2026 and Rounds 1-2. No explicit coach commentary or team statements provided. confidence_yes and confidence_no both set LOW-MODERATE (35/40) due to tournament context mismatch and reliance on historical LCK Cup data for Rounds 1-2 prediction. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria text is unambiguous: DRX win \u2192 YES, BFX win \u2192 NO. No forfeit/walkover complications expected. Resolution source (gol.gg) is standard and reliable. PROBABILITY ALLOCATION: Aligning with market (38% YES / 62% NO) and briefing evidence suggesting BNK FearX favored despite inconsistency. DRX has laning advantage (Smash CSM) but weaker series record in LCK Cup. Market consensus of 38/62 is reasonable given data; slight upside to YES if DRX's top-side exploits meta advantage, downside if BFX's carries (Aiming, Diable) execute as in DN SOOPers series.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is primarily from LCK Cup 2026 tournament (completed prior to Rounds 1-2), not the official LCK Rounds 1-2 match itself; team form and roster stability between these distinct competitions are unknown."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET POSITIONING: NO is priced at 62% (favored), indicating market consensus that DRX wins. This analysis supports the market favorite. DRX STRENGTHS: - Smash (top) ranked 4th in Rounds 1-2 CSM at 11.42 (strong laning/scaling foundation) - DRX posted 2364 GPM in LCK Cup 2026 (5th best team), indicating resourceful macro play - Recent head-to-head vs BFX showed DRX defeating them 2-0 in Week 2 (2026-04-10) BNK FearX WEAKNESSES (WHY NO WINS): - Lost 0-2 to Gen.G and 1-2 to T1 in LCK Cup Week 2-3, establishing pattern vs elite opponents - Despite Diable's individual excellence (12.13 CSM, 14 kills vs HLE), BFX lost that series to HLE decisively - Aiming's high KDA (7.9) did not translate into consistency\u2014BFX dropped series 0-2 to Gen.G and 1-2 to T1 - Team-level deficiencies: BFX lost to Nongshim 0-2 in Week 3, showing vulnerability across different opponents UNDERDOG APPEAL (LIMITED): - BFX beat BRO 2-1 (Week 1) and DN SOOPers 3-1 (Week 3), proving series wins are possible - Diable's individual playmaking is genuinely elite; high-skill mid can create upset windows - BFX's win vs T1 3-1 in Playoffs Round 2 (2026-04-16) shows capability for upset runs CRITICAL ASYMMETRY: - DRX's H2H vs BFX is 2-0 (Week 2 LCK Cup 2026), suggesting structural advantage - BFX's losses cluster against tier-1 teams (Gen.G, T1, NS); DRX is positioned similarly to those teams in recent form - Individual brilliance (Diable, Aiming) has not translated to series success at scale in recent weeks TIMING & VOLATILITY: - Event is TODAY (6 hours to start); market has stabilized with NO up 11.5pp over 7 days - YES side saw sharp -14pp drop (Apr 12), then -8.5pp and -6pp (Apr 13), suggesting market confidence converging toward NO - Limited time for reversals; DRX starts as clear favorite CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: - confidence_yes = 32 (moderate): BFX's individual stars and prior upset wins vs T1 create non-zero scenario, but data heavily favors DRX - confidence_no = 72 (high): DRX's H2H record, player form rankings, and BFX's inconsistency vs elite teams support NO decisively - Asymmetry reflects strong evidence for DRX; weaker counter-narrative for BFX relying on outlier performances", "key_factor": "BNK FearX's inconsistent record against top-tier opponents (0-2 vs Gen.G, 1-2 vs T1) combined with DRX's superior individual player form (Smash's 11.42 CSM ranking) indicates DRX is the favored matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR BNK FEARX (YES): BNK FearX has concrete evidence of high-level execution\u2014Diable's 12.13 CSM ranks elite, his 14-kill game vs HLE demonstrates mechanical dominance in key moments, and Aiming's 7.9 KDA with 2 quadrakills shows winning teamfight presence. In BO3 format, individual playmaking can swing entire series; FearX beat BRO 2-1 and DN SOOPers 3-1 recently, proving they can close contested matchups. INDIVIDUAL STATS ASYMMETRY: The briefing explicitly shows FearX players (Diable, Aiming) outperforming DRX's Smash (11.42 CSM vs Diable's 12.13). While Smash is 4th-best farmer, Diable's edge + Aiming's KDA superiority suggests FearX mid-bot lane has micro advantage. DRX roster lacks comparable individual stat standouts in the provided data. RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: DRX vs BNK FearX matchup from LCK Cup Week 2 shows BNK WINNING Game 2 decisively (19 kills, 27:34 duration, 55.9 gold efficiency on blue side). This is NOT the market event, but it demonstrates FearX can beat DRX when executing properly. The series was 1-2 loss, not a clean sweep. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES: Kiwoom DRX shows NO standout individual stats in Rounds 1-2 data provided. Smash leads their rosters at 11.42 CSM, but no KDA or multikill rankings appear. This is a significant data gap\u2014DRX's performance is underspecified compared to FearX's clearly articulated playmaking metrics. Against elite individual players, underspecified macro strength is vulnerable. TEAM CONSISTENCY CONCERN: BNK FearX posted losses to Gen.G (0-2) and T1 (1-2), but also beat elite teams (BRO 2-1). DRX's record in the briefing shows losses to HLE (0-2), KT (0-2), and close losses to BRO. Both teams have consistency gaps; FearX's elite-farm mid/bot lane may stabilize BO3s better than raw team metrics suggest. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNALS UNCERTAINTY: YES side moved +4.0pp in 24 hours (from ~34% to 38%), while NO side dropped -4.0pp (from ~66% to 62%) after sharp moves on Apr 13. This reversal suggests late-arriving information favoring DRX's probability, but the volatility itself (2.1pp/hr for NO) indicates the market lacks high conviction. With 6 hours until match, reversals remain possible but require data inflection. DATA FRESHNESS & TIMING RISK: Event starts in ~6 hours (IMMINENT). The briefing data is from 2026-04-17 01:40 UTC, only ~6.5 hours before match. No injury news, roster changes, or meta shifts are documented post-cutoff. For an IMMINENT event, late reversals require material negative news on the favorite; absence of such news actually slightly favors the favorite's current pricing, not the underdog. GOLD EFFICIENCY BENCHMARK: HLE posted 2399/2324 GPM vs BNK FearX in Rounds 1-2, the highest in the tournament. DRX's best GPM entry (2364 GPM vs BRO) is lower than HLE's benchmarks but indicates DRX can generate advantages. FearX allowed 2399 GPM to HLE\u2014an elite opponent\u2014but this does not disqualify them vs DRX unless DRX replicates HLE's macro. NO DIRECT DRX VS FEARX ROUNDS 1-2 DATA: The briefing provides LCK Cup 2026 history but NO Rounds 1-2 head-to-head results between DRX and BNK FearX for this specific event. This is a critical gap. Without direct matchup data for Rounds 1-2, confidence in either side is artificially capped. The market's 62% for NO may reflect bookmaker conservatism rather than strong DRX form. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes set to 35 because FearX's individual stats ARE strong but sample size in provided data is limited (3-4 players tracked), and no Rounds 1-2 macro metrics (teamfights, objective control vs DRX) are provided. confidence_no set to 52 (higher) because DRX's lack of individual standouts is offset by the fact that DRX's absence from stat tables may indicate role-specialization (strong jungler/support not tracked), not weakness. The briefing simply does not provide enough DRX-specific data to confidently refute their favorite status. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: At 42% for YES, this reflects that FearX's elite individual playmaking (Diable, Aiming) and recent series wins (BRO, DNS) are REAL strengths overlooked by the market's heavy NO weighting (62%), but DRX's lack of specific documented weaknesses and the favorite's baseline BO3 advantage (60%+ baseline for favorites in esports) prevent a higher score. The 8pp gap (58% NO vs 50% breakeven) reflects genuine uncertainty, not strong conviction on either side.", "key_factor": "BNK FearX's exceptional individual playmaking (Diable 12.13 CSM, Aiming 7.9 KDA) and proven ability to execute high-kill closeouts suggest underestimation of mechanical ceiling in a BO3 format where individual performance swings matter."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "TEMPORAL CONSTRAINT: Event starts in ~6 hours (TODAY). Market has been trading for ~1 week with stable YES decay (-11.5pp over 7 days, now +4pp in 24h). Sharp moves on Apr 12-13 suggest roster/meta adjustments or injury news that has partially reversed. BASELINE: LCK regular-season BO3s are typically close contests (45-55% split). No historical LCK data available for this exact matchup or team pairing in 2026 Rounds 1-2. YES CASE (DRX WIN): - Smash (DRX top) ranks 4th in Rounds 1-2 CSM (11.42), indicating strong laning & scaling edge over opponent - DRX posted 2364 GPM (5th best in LCK Cup 2026), showing macro/resource efficiency - BNK FearX lost decisively to Gen.G (0-2) and T1 (1-2), revealing vulnerability vs tier-1 opponents - No evidence DRX players underperform vs BNK FearX specifically in Rounds 1-2 pool NO CASE (BNK FEARX WIN): - Diable (BNK mid) exceptional in Rounds 1-2: 12.13 CSM (best), 14 kills vs HLE (single game), 6.5 KDA - Aiming (BNK ADC) elite: 7.9 KDA (top 2 in LCK), 2 quadrakills, 10.47 CSM shows pressure in teamfights - BNK FearX beat DN SOOPers (3-1) and BRO (2-1) in LCK Cup Week 1-3, demonstrating series closure capability - BNK FearX beat T1 (3-1) in LCK Cup Playoffs Round 2 (Week 3), a notable upset vs elite opponent - Hanwha Life Esports posted 2399/2324 GPM vs BNK FearX in Rounds 1-2, but HLE is top-tier; does not establish BNK weakness uniquely MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: - YES at 38% reflects moderate discount vs 50% fair value; market implies ~62% confidence in BNK FearX - NO side volatility (2.1pp/hr vs YES 0.5pp/hr) suggests uncertainty; Apr 13 +22.5pp spike followed by partial reversal (-4pp in 24h) indicates late-breaking info (potentially roster/meta shift) now partially priced out HEAD-TO-HEAD: No prior direct DRX-vs-BNK FearX series documented in Rounds 1-2 2026. LCK Cup 2026 history shows separate encounters but not a direct matchup (only proxies through common opponents). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: - confidence_yes=42: Strong individual carry stats for BNK (Diable, Aiming) are concrete; DRX macro advantage (Smash CSM, team GPM) is reasonable but less granular. No direct head-to-head evidence. Market price aligns with NO bias; limited data to overturn it. - confidence_no=48: BNK's recent form includes losses to Gen.G/T1 but wins vs weaker teams (BRO, DN SOOPers). DRX macro edge is plausible but not overwhelming. Market is fluid (volatility). Insufficient concrete evidence to commit high confidence to BNK underperformance. CONCLUSION: Market price of 38% YES / 62% NO appears rational given BNK FearX's individual star power (Diable, Aiming) and recent series wins, balanced against DRX's farming/macro metrics and BNK's inconsistency vs tier-1 teams. Neither side has definitive edge; low-to-moderate confidence warranted on both.", "key_factor": "LCK BO3 regular season matches show ~45-55% variance between seeded teams; head-to-head history unavailable for this specific pairing in Rounds 1-2 2026"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.35, "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market is pricing BNK FearX as heavily favored (62% NO) despite BNK FearX showing volatile performance in LCK Cup 2026 \u2014 inconsistent against top-tier opponents (0-2 Gen.G, 1-2 T1) but strong vs mid-tier (2-1 BRO, 3-1 DN SOOPers). Kiwoom DRX's individual player metrics are competitive: Smash 11.42 CSM (4th best Rounds 1-2), 2364 GPM team average in LCK Cup (respectable vs Dplus KIA's 2418). Data suggests DRX has structural scaling strength. BNK FearX's Diable (mid) posted elite stats (12.13 CSM, 14 kills vs HLE) and Aiming (ADC) 7.9 KDA with 2 quadrakills \u2014 these are top-tier individual performances that may be driving market pessimism on DRX. Crowd appears to be fearful of BNK FearX's laning/early phase dominance (particularly Diable) rather than rationalizing DRX's late-game scaling potential and Smash's top-lane consistency. Critical data gap: No direct DRX vs BNK FearX head-to-head matchup in briefing for Rounds 1-2 2026. Only LCK Cup 2025 data available showing mixed results. This creates asymmetric confidence \u2014 BNK FearX form is well-documented; DRX's strength is inferred from role-level stats. Market has drifted -11.5pp on YES side over 7 days (currently 35% vs 41% EMA) \u2014 suggests selling pressure on DRX. Recent sharp moves (Apr 12-13: -14pp, -8.5pp, -6.0pp) indicate rapid conviction build toward NO, not gradual reassessment. Event is TODAY in ~6 hours (imminent). Low time-to-reversal; market prices reflect current consensus. Shares will lock within hours \u2014 limited new information arriving to shift odds meaningfully. Apathy on DRX side: Briefing emphasizes BNK FearX individual brilliance (Diable, Aiming) but provides less narrative/context on DRX's team cohesion, draft advantage, or meta fitness \u2014 suggesting market may be underweighting DRX's structural strengths due to narrative void. YES confidence moderate (42): DRX metrics support competitiveness, but lack of direct H2H and weaker narrative presence vs BNK FearX's documented recent dominance create uncertainty. NO confidence solid (58): BNK FearX's elite individual performances and track record vs mid-tier teams are well-supported, though weakness vs top-tier (Gen.G, T1) creates non-zero reversal risk. Confidence not higher due to DRX's unexplored strengths in Rounds 1-2 2026 play.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "BNK FearX shows FEAST-OR-FAMINE pattern: 3-1 wins vs DN SOOPers and 2-1 vs BRO, but 0-2 losses to Gen.G and 1-2 to T1 indicate tier-dependent performance; lack of consistent mid-table matchup results limits predictability. Diable (BNK FearX mid) exceptional in Rounds 1-2: 12.13 CSM peak, 14 kills vs HLE demonstrates carry potential, but this assumes similar draft/meta context in Rounds 1-2 match (Fearless Draft environment shown in LCK Cup 2026). Smash (DRX top) 11.42 CSM (4th in Rounds 1-2), 2364 GPM team stat competitive with top echelon (Dplus KIA 2418 GPM), suggests DRX can secure early resource advantages; however, GPM advantage does not guarantee series victory in BO3. Head-to-head data conflict: 2026-04-10 LCK Cup Week 2 shows BNK FearX 2-0 vs DRX, contradicting market underpricing of YES side; this recent victory is highly relevant but briefing emphasizes DRX vs BRO Week 3 matches (DRX 2-1 win) as more recent form. Aiming (BNK FearX ADC) 7.9 KDA, 2 quadrakills in Rounds 1-2, ranks among elite performers; however, KDA inflation often occurs in stomps or series sweeps\u2014does not indicate consistency against peer-level ADCs like DRX's potential carries. Market price history shows sharp volatility: Apr 12-13 saw -14pp, -8.5pp, -6pp moves on YES side with +22.5pp countermovement on NO side, suggesting major information release (likely team roster changes, patch notes, or upset results); current 38% YES pricing may reflect recent BFX loss momentum rather than fundamental matchup analysis. Tournament context: LCK Cup 2026 (past) vs LCK Rounds 1-2 2026 (this event) are distinct competitions; form carry-over is limited but directional (BFX 1-2 record vs T1/Gen.G suggests vulnerability to structured teamfighting). BO3 format: single-series reversals are common in LCK when draft advantages align; DRX's documented macro edge (tower plates, voidgrub control metrics from DRX vs BFX Week 2 game 3: 6 plates vs 1, 4 voidgrugs vs 2) suggests game-state management edge but not series certainty. Hanwha Life Esports posted 2399 & 2324 GPM against BFX, establishing that LCK Rounds 1-2 meta punishes BFX's resource patterns; DRX's 2364 GPM rating suggests similar or better efficiency. Confidence asymmetry: Strong data on BFX individual mechanics (Diable, Aiming stats) but limited DRX individual performance data beyond Smash; NO-side confidence capped at 55% due to sparse DRX player-level stats. YES-side confidence at 42% reflects conflicting H2H data (Apr 10 BFX 2-0 win) vs recent form weakness.", "key_factor": "BNK FearX demonstrates volatile performance against tier-1 competition (0-2 vs Gen.G, 1-2 vs T1) but exploits weaker opponents effectively; DRX's top-lane resource concentration (Smash 11.42 CSM, 4th in Rounds 1-2) and documented wins vs BRO suggest superior macro control, but historical head-to-head data (2026-04-10 DRX vs BNK FearX showing 2-0 BFX victory) introduces significant uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "BNK FearX's record vs DRX: 2-0 clean sweep in LCK Cup Week 2 (Apr 10, 2026), establishing clear head-to-head dominance over DRX in recent play. This is the strongest signal in the briefing and directly contradicts the market's 62% NO pricing. Market structure asymmetry: YES side (DRX) has traded DOWN -11.5pp over 7 days and DOWN -14.0pp on Apr 12, suggesting systematic erosion of confidence. NO side (BNK FearX) spiked UP +22.5pp on Apr 13, indicating a credible reversal event or news not visible in the briefing. Diable's individual dominance is NOT matched by DRX's corresponding regional star: Smash (DRX top) ranks 4th in CSM (11.42) but Diable's 12.13 CSM and 14-kill game vs HLE suggest superior playmaking scaling. DRX's mid-lane performance data is absent from the briefing\u2014a critical silence. BNK FearX beat BRO 2-1 and DN SOOPers 3-1 in Rounds 1-2, showing consistent execution against middle-tier opponents. DRX's Week 3 match vs BRO (2-2 split, then loss) shows fragility against the same tier. Black swan candidate: Meta patch 16.2 \u2192 16.3 may have favored Diable's champion pool or BNK FearX's bot-lane synergy (Aiming 7.9 KDA). Briefing shows patch transitions but offers NO analysis of how changes affect DRX's play style vs BNK FearX's. Temporal pressure: Event is TODAY at 08:00 UTC (~6 hours). Large price moves occurred Apr 12-13 (4 days ago), suggesting new information has already priced in a BNK FearX edge. The market may have already corrected toward true probability. Morale/motivation asymmetry not addressed: BNK FearX beat T1 3-1 in LCK Cup Playoffs (Apr 16, most recent data point before this match), indicating peak confidence entering Rounds 1-2. DRX's recent form includes losses to HLE (0-2, Week 3). Gold-per-minute benchmarks: HLE's 2399 GPM vs BNK FearX is highest in Rounds 1-2, yet Hanwha is NOT in this matchup. DRX's best GPM (2364 in a Week 3 win vs BRO) is LOWER than BNK FearX's observed defensive efficiency in losses, suggesting resource management gaps. Absence of DRX individual player stats (mid, ADC KDA) in Rounds 1-2 briefing is conspicuous. BNK FearX's playmakers (Diable, Aiming) are documented. Information asymmetry favors NO. Market price suggests 38% confidence in DRX, yet the head-to-head 2-0 BNK FearX sweep is underweighting the evidence. Contrarian position: market may be anchored to DRX's regional pedigree rather than recent form. Risk: DRX roster availability unknown. If a key player (e.g., jungle Oner, mid Zeka) is unavailable or subbed with 6 hours' notice, BNK FearX's prepared gameplan (proven in 2-0 Week 2 sweep) becomes unbeatable.", "key_factor": "Kiwoom DRX suffers a critical mid-lane or jungle collapse due to a patch-driven meta shift favoring BNK FearX's Diable-centric playmaking style, combined with an unexpected roster availability issue (player illness, technical connectivity) that forces DRX to adjust in-game preparation."}], "final_score": 0.3485164508473433, "no_score": 0.661414862362263, "edge": 0.3059090909090909, "no_edge": 0.07590909090909093, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 56.71% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1955492", "question": "LoL: Kiwoom DRX vs BNK FEARX (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Kiwoom DRX and BNK FEARX in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 17 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Kiwoom DRX\" if Kiwoom DRX win the match against BNK FEARX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FEARX\" if BNK FEARX win the match against Kiwoom DRX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.385, "volume_usd": 59893.50550700004, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["56179036764313339206259073053313197970246618591163150212820850061173177576491", "64103897709674004961598894466374714988016036228842750672975824927545783596887"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["| WIN | 3-1 | Red | 19 | 85.9 | 11 | 2 | DNS | 16 | 73 | 4 | 3 | 39:26 | DN SOOPers vs BNK FearX (4) | 16.2 | WEEK3 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| LOSS | | | Blue | 9 | 59.6 | 2 | 0 | DNS | 25 | 75.2 | 9 | 4 | 33:47 | DN SOOPers vs BNK FearX (3) | 16.2 | WEEK3 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | | | Blue | 17 | 54.9 | 10 | 2 | DNS | 10 | 48.8 | 1 | 1 | 25:35 | DN SOOPers vs BNK FearX (2) | 16.2 | WEEK3 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | | | Blue | 19 | 75.3 | 9 | 4 | DNS | 14 | 66.9 | 1 | 1 | 35:14 | DN SOOPers vs BNK FearX (1) | 16.2 | WEEK3 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| LOSS | 1-2 | Blue | 8 | 56.9 | 2 | 1 | T1 | 18 | 65.4 | 8 | 4 | 30:20 | T1 vs BNK FearX (3) | 16.1 | WEEK2 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | | | Red | 26 | 86.2 | 12 | 4 | T1 | 15 | 86 | 6 | 2 | 43:00 | T1 vs BNK FearX (2) | 16.1 | WEEK2 | LCK Cup 2026 | [...] | LOSS | | | Blue | 18 | 73.1 | 3 | 4 | T1 | 25 | 87.9 | 11 | 1 | 39:24 | T1 vs BNK FearX (1) | 16.1 | WEEK2 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| LOSS | 0-2 | Red | 10 | 61.5 | 3 | 2 | GEN | 23 | 70.5 | 11 | 3 | 31:56 | BNK FearX vs Gen.G (2) | 16.1 | WEEK2 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| LOSS | | | Red | 22 | 69.3 | 6 | 3 | GEN | 18 | 73 | 10 | 2 | 34:35 | BNK FearX vs Gen.G (1) | 16.1 | WEEK2 | LCK Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 2-1 | Red | 18 | 74.9 | 8 | 3 | BRO | 12 | 68.5 | 3 | 1 | 36:27 | BRO vs BNK FearX (3) | 16.1 | WEEK1 | LCK Cup 20