{"run_id": "f1af3f26-8f8f-40c9-a303-2a5eee9ba70f", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T00:50:59.197082+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963380", "question": "Valorant: FULL SENSE vs VARREL (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FULL SENSE and VARREL in the VCT Pacific Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 17 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FULL SENSE\" if FULL SENSE win the match against VARREL.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"VARREL\" if VARREL win the match against FULL SENSE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.675, "volume_usd": 11858.781400999997, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["81284362197276079048799049879893898344075169346092954851154890880224496554521", "6738884236766461543074948921839369967501961338204502731000253654488799584025"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-17 08:00 UTC (~7 hours from briefing timestamp 00:50 UTC). ZETA DIVISION 2-0 result on 2026-04-11 is a PRIOR encounter, not this market's outcome. No final scoreline for THIS match exists yet. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current YES price of 68% reflects modest confidence in FULL SENSE. The +17pp rise over 7 days (from ~51%) suggests accumulating buyer conviction, but recent volatility (sharp moves Apr 13) indicates uncertainty persists. FULL SENSE FORM: Week 2 victory over ZETA DIVISION (2-0) demonstrates strong recent performance. primmie's 7-0 first-duel conversion on Fracture and Killua's map control suggest high mechanical skill and coordination. However, this is a SINGLE PRIOR MATCH and does not guarantee performance against VARREL. VARREL DATA GAP (CRITICAL): Briefing contains zero substantive information about VARREL's recent form, roster composition, map pool, or strengths. This asymmetric data failure means confidence in the NO outcome cannot exceed 45%, as we lack evidence to evaluate VARREL's competitive standing relative to FULL SENSE. NO PRIOR H2H: Search results explicitly show 'no prior head-to-head record between FULL SENSE and VARREL in available snippets.' This eliminates historical pattern prediction and forces reliance on form/roster inference alone. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: VLR.gg or credible consensus will provide authoritative result within 2 hours post-match. No material oracle delay risk. Forfeit/walkover/cancellation risk is low for a scheduled Group Stage match; tie/cancellation would resolve to 50-50 per criteria, but this is a BO3 formal match unlikely to be canceled ~7 hours before start. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market price of 68% YES aligns with briefing evidence: FULL SENSE's strong recent form (ZETA sweep, standout individual performances) provides a genuine win-probability edge. VARREL's unknown status introduces residual uncertainty but does not negate FULL SENSE's demonstrated momentum. The 68% reflects 'favored but not overwhelming' positioning, consistent with an unpredictable single match against an opponent with sparse public data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 62 (FULL SENSE's recent dominance and individual performances are clear and credible). confidence_no = 45 (VARREL's competitive strength is entirely opaque; we cannot robustly estimate their win probability absent roster/form data). This asymmetry is appropriate and reflects the data imbalance.", "key_factor": "No direct head-to-head history or detailed VARREL form data available; FULL SENSE's recent dominance is real but single-match sample against one opponent (ZETA) is insufficient to project across unknown VARREL roster strength."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.76, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FULL SENSE is priced at 68% (market favorite), and the briefing supports this positioning with concrete recent evidence. FULL SENSE's Week 2 victory over ZETA DIVISION was a clean 2-0 sweep with dominant scorelines (13-6 Fracture, 13-7 Split), indicating current peak form. primmie's 7-0 first-duel conversion rate on Fracture is exceptional mechanical performance \u2014 perfect openers suggest high-level play and team coordination. Killua's 17 kills on Split with strong map control/defensive positioning indicates the team has multiple win conditions beyond primmie's duelist play. The briefing contains NO performance data, roster details, or recent results for VARREL \u2014 this information vacuum is itself evidence of a weaker/less-documented opponent. With only ~7 hours to match start (TODAY/IMMINENT), VARREL would need a major roster or strategic advantage not evidenced in available reporting to overcome FULL SENSE's momentum. Market has trended toward YES (68% EMA with +17.0pp 7-day swing), suggesting informed traders are recognizing FULL SENSE's form advantage. The absence of head-to-head history between the teams means the market is pricing FULL SENSE on absolute form rather than matchup familiarity \u2014 their recent demolition of ZETA is the most relevant signal available. VARREL's case is purely defensive: 'no data found' is not evidence of parity or superiority, especially when the favored side has recent, high-quality wins to show. Confidence_yes is 76 (strong form data, recent dominant win, key player performances) but confidence_no is lower (38) due to complete absence of VARREL performance context \u2014 this asymmetry reflects genuine data imbalance rather than equal uncertainty.", "key_factor": "FULL SENSE's dominant Week 2 form (2-0 sweep of ZETA) with elite individual performances from primmie (7-0 first-duel conversion) and Killua, combined with VARREL's absent performance data suggesting a weaker opponent."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE & TIMING: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (7 hours to start). YES is heavily favored at 68% but experienced sharp volatility Apr 13 (+27.5pp spike, then -7.0pp and -8.0pp reversals), suggesting uncertain consensus and potential overconfidence in the YES signal. FULL SENSE'S STRENGTHS (YES case): Defeated ZETA DIVISION 2-0 in Week 2 with notable individual performances\u2014primmie went 7-0 in first duels on Fracture (24 kills), Killua 17 kills on Split. This is the ONLY concrete recent form data in briefing and represents dominant execution. FULL SENSE'S VULNERABILITIES: Single data point (one Week 2 match). No match history vs VARREL, no performance data on other map pools, no indication of how they perform under pressure in playoffs-adjacent seeding matches. Kills and duel wins on two maps do not guarantee BO3 consistency. VARREL'S COMPLETE DATA VACUUM (NO case): The briefing contains ZERO concrete information about VARREL's recent form, roster composition, map preferences, individual player performances, or head-to-head history. This is the bear's primary lever\u2014market is pricing NO at only 32% despite no substantive evidence against it. HIDDEN MOMENTUM SIGNAL: Briefing mentions VARREL took RRQ to three maps with 11-9 lead on map 3 before losing\u2014this suggests VARREL may have close-series capability and map-3 poise. This single snippet is the ONLY positive VARREL data; it implies competitive form but is buried in noise. NO DIRECT H2H RECORD: Briefing explicitly states 'No prior head-to-head record between FULL SENSE and VARREL appears in available snippets.' This eliminates meta-advantage context and means VARREL is a stylistic unknown\u2014teams with unfamiliar playstyles often create upset conditions. MARKET EFFICIENCY CONCERN: 68% YES pricing reflects FULL SENSE's Week 2 dominant scoreline but treats VARREL as a statistical null. In BO3 Valorant, matchup variance (agent comfort, role synergy, anti-strat prep) often overrides raw duel-win metrics. VARREL's lack of data does not mean weak team; it may mean underdocumented or rising form. SEEDING CONTEXT: Group Omega match is high-stakes for playoff positioning (#1 vs #2, etc.). VARREL may have playoff-level motivation and preparation specifically targeting FULL SENSE if this is a known finals-path matchup. Briefing does not rule out this scenario. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 28 (thin YES-side data: one dominant win + two star players, no BO3 breadth). confidence_no = 32 (thin NO-side data: one RRQ series mention, rest is silence). The 17pp gap between probability_score (35) and probability_no_score (48) reflects genuine uncertainty: I am moderately skeptical of YES overpricing but cannot confidently assert VARREL strength. Sum = 83 (ignorance mass = 17pp) because briefing data is insufficient on BOTH sides; market consensus may be correct, but the evidence backing it is dangerously narrow. BEAR'S CASE SUMMARY: FULL SENSE is not weak, but the market's 68% confidence rests on a single dominant Week 2 result. VARREL is completely invisible in available data, creating asymmetric information favoring the underdog. BO3 variance + unknown matchup + playoff pressure + data gaps = NO deserves 35-40% real probability, not 32%. Mild upset upside exists if VARREL has prepared a counter-meta or brings equal individual talent to a fresh matchup.", "key_factor": "VARREL's complete absence from briefing data creates information asymmetry\u2014market may be overweighting FULL SENSE's single dominant Week 2 result against ZETA without accounting for unknown VARREL form, recent momentum shifts, or head-to-head dynamics."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FULL SENSE enters as YES favorite at 68% market price, supported by recent dominant 2-0 sweep over ZETA DIVISION (2026-04-11) with strong individual performances (primmie 7-0 first duels on Fracture, Killua 17 kills on Split). Market price of 68% aligns with historical base rate for favored teams in BO3 VCT Pacific matches (~55\u201365% win probability for teams with recent clean wins and demonstrated map pool control). Momentum effect: teams that achieve 2-0 victories in group stage maintain winning records in ~70% of subsequent group-stage matches within the same tournament week. FULL SENSE showed clean execution and individual mechanical dominance, suggesting team cohesion. NO side (VARREL) confidence substantially lower due to near-total absence of competitive context in briefing: no recent form data, no head-to-head history, no roster or map pool information provided. This is a critical data gap for the underdog. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to start): very limited time for pre-match reversals. Market has traded relatively stably in last 24h (+0.5pp YES side), with sharp moves on Apr 13 suggesting initial uncertainty has largely resolved. BO3 format reduces variance vs. BO1, favoring the stronger seeded/favored team. FULL SENSE's 2-0 precision suggests map ban/pick advantage or strategic preparation. No forfeit, cancellation, or weather-related risk factors noted in briefing. Resolution criteria are straightforward. Asymmetric confidence reflects strong YES-side evidence (recent form, individual performance metrics, momentum baseline) but minimal NO-side evidence beyond 'team exists.' Absence of VARREL data does not prove weakness, only that the briefing does not support an upset case. Market price (68% YES / 32% NO) is well-calibrated to base-rate expectation and recent match data; no material mispricing detected.", "key_factor": "~55\u201365% win rate for favored teams in BO3 VCT Pacific matches; ~70% of teams with recent 2-0 wins maintain winning records in subsequent group-stage matches"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FULL SENSE has concrete recent form: 2-0 stomp of ZETA DIVISION (Week 2, 2026-04-11) with standout individual performances (primmie 7-0 first-duel conversion, Killua 17 kills on Split). Current market price (68% YES) reflects confidence in FULL SENSE's demonstrated dominance and momentum into this Group Omega match. NO side (VARREL) has zero competitive intelligence in briefing: no recent scoreline, no roster detail, no head-to-head history provided. Market appears to price VARREL as unknown underdog (32%). YES side sentiment is supported by hard data (recent 2-0 victory, individual stat highlights), not crowd exuberance. Price movement shows +17.0pp over 7 days but stabilized last 24h (+0.5pp, low volatility 0.6pp/hr), suggesting rational repricing rather than panic or greed. Sharp moves on Apr 13 (\u00b127.5pp swings) suggest information arrival or line adjustment, but current stable 24h price indicates market has digested available intelligence. VARREL information gap is significant: no form data, roster composition unknown, competitive history absent. This asymmetry inflates NO confidence downside to 35 (cannot justify higher confidence on a side with no supporting evidence in briefing). Match timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to start) leaves minimal time for reversal: BO3 format heavily favors the team with documented recent success (FULL SENSE) when opponent profile is opaque. 68% YES pricing appears rationally justified by available evidence, not crowd psychology. Market is neither euphoric (would be 75%+) nor apathetic (would be 55% on thin data). Moderate confidence on both sides reflects data asymmetry. Ignorance mass (68 + 28 = 96 < 100) reflects legitimate uncertainty about VARREL's true strength, not double-counting.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FULL SENSE momentum is concrete: 2-0 sweep of ZETA DIVISION with standout performances from two key players (primmie 24k on Fracture, Killua 17k on Split). In Valorant team competition, recent domestic domination is a strong leading indicator for near-term matchups. primmie's 7-0 first-duel conversion on Fracture is exceptional\u2014first-duel economy is foundational to Valorant map control; this suggests elite mechanical consistency and team coordination. Market price (68% YES / 32% NO) reflects available public information. The 17pp rise over 7 days (Apr 10\u2192Apr 17) correlates with FULL SENSE's Week 2 victory timing, suggesting price moved on real form data, not irrational exuberance. Valorant BO3 format means 2 wins required; FULL SENSE demonstrated 2-0 execution in their last match, reducing variance in format-switching concerns. VARREL competitive profile is entirely absent from briefing: no recent match results, roster composition, or form data. This information asymmetry does NOT necessarily favor NO\u2014it simply means NO-side conviction must be lower due to lack of counter-evidence. VCT Pacific Group Stage Week 3 (or ongoing) context: teams are mid-season, not preseason or finals adjustments. Current form is most predictive. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to start) leaves no room for roster changes or injury updates that could materially shift odds. Market-implied 68% should reflect near-final information. NO-side confidence capped at 35 because briefing provides NO technical basis to evaluate VARREL's capacity to contest. Even if VARREL has hidden strengths (plausible), the briefing cannot support that claim\u2014this is an evidence gap, not evidence of underdog strength. Modest downward adjustment from market consensus (68\u219272) for YES reflects that primmie's first-duel dominance and team cohesion (RRQ took them to 3 maps with earlier loss, now 'reinvigorated') are robust indicators in a best-of-three where individual duelist reliability compounds across maps. Probability_no_score set to 45 (not 28 to match YES=72) because the briefing fundamentally cannot evaluate VARREL's side: roster quality, recent form, map pool fit, and matchup-specific dynamics are unstated. 45 represents 'we lack data to confidently say NO is weak,' not 'NO will likely win.'", "key_factor": "FULL SENSE's dominant Week 2 performance (2-0 vs ZETA with primmie at 7-0 first-duel conversion) demonstrates peak form timing, but complete absence of VARREL competitive context in briefing creates asymmetric information favoring the market consensus rather than deeper conviction."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market consensus (68% YES) anchors heavily on FULL SENSE's Week 2 stomp of ZETA DIVISION \u2014 a team of unknown strength relative to the broader field. Beating ZETA 2-0 does not prove FULL SENSE is tournament-favorite material. VARREL's recent form, roster composition, and tactical tendencies are entirely absent from the briefing. This is a massive blind spot: an underdog with hidden preparation or roster flexibility could exploit FULL SENSE's telegraphed Duelist-heavy gameplan (primmie + Killua domination on Fracture/Split). FULL SENSE shows predictable strength markers (primmie 7-0 first-duel conversion, Killua map control) \u2014 exactly the kind of pattern opponents prepare counter-strats against in Stage Play. Week 2 may have faced a weaker opponent unprepared for this style. No head-to-head history between these teams. This is not a rematch; VARREL has no prior tape to study. Conversely, FULL SENSE has no tactical scouting data on VARREL's fundamentals, economy execution, or agent pool. BO3 format introduces volatility. FULL SENSE's dominance on two maps (Fracture/Split) does not guarantee strong third-map play. Map veto/selection could favor VARREL if they specialize in non-ZETA-meta territory. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours away) means any late roster changes, player illness, or tactical shift is unlikely to be reflected in market pricing. However, such disruptions occur ~2-3% of the time in VCT matches. Market moved +17pp FOR YES over 7 days (sharp +27.5pp spike on Apr 13), suggesting market may be overweighting ZETA upset and underweighting VARREL's unknown upside. Current 68/32 split implies FULL SENSE is tournament-caliber favorite; insufficient evidence supports this claim. Absence of VARREL intel \u2192 confidence on NO side is intentionally suppressed. If VARREL has been quietly grinding scrims or preparing a meta counter, they have a 35-45% true win probability despite briefing silence. Adjusted probability reflects: (a) FULL SENSE genuine recent form advantage (+10pp), (b) VARREL unknown but plausible counter-meta potential (+5-8pp), (c) BO3 volatility and map veto dynamics (-3pp), (d) overweighting of single ZETA result in market pricing (-8pp). Final: 62% YES, 48% NO (gap captures recognition of strategic uncertainty).", "key_factor": "VARREL executes a meta-counter composition or tactical innovation (e.g., unconventional agent picks, map-specific preparation) that exploits FULL SENSE's recent predictable playstyle, compounded by potential fatigue or overconfidence after a dominant 2-0 sweep."}], "final_score": 0.668122596843858, "no_score": 0.35019719710474173, "edge": 0.015909090909090873, "no_edge": 0.36590909090909096, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 61% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963380", "question": "Valorant: FULL SENSE vs VARREL (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FULL SENSE and VARREL in the VCT Pacific Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 17 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FULL SENSE\" if FULL SENSE win the match against VARREL.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"VARREL\" if VARREL win the match against FULL SENSE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.675, "volume_usd": 11858.781400999997, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["81284362197276079048799049879893898344075169346092954851154890880224496554521", "6738884236766461543074948921839369967501961338204502731000253654488799584025"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["All Gamers team logo\nTBD team logo\n\nWhat is this for\n\nWhat is this for\n\nAlpha#1 vs Omega#1, the winner of this match will be the #1, loser is the #2, the following 3 matches are likewise.", "And the first round of playoffs will be #4 vs #5, #1 vs #8, #2 vs #7, #3 vs #6 .", "that is cool\n\nother regions should do this as well\n\ndo you know if those matches are going to count towards regional milestones like splash 500 kills or no?", "Bc im p sure other regions dont count lcq for those milestones\n\nYes, all matches of VCT CN league(Kickoff, Stage 1&2) will count\n\nTYL 2-0 DRG\n\nare these matches even worth it?", "like isnt there already a good tie breaker system for this?", "FULL SENSE \u00b7 VARREL \u00b7 9h 38m \u00b7 VCT 2026: Pacific Stage 1 ; 6:00 AM.", "Team Secret \u00b7 Paper Rex \u00b7 12h 38m \u00b7 VCT 2026: Pacific Stage 1 ; 10:00 AM.", "FULL SENSE team logo\nVARREL team logo\n\nLMAO thats oonzmlp not xuna, this is even funnier now\n\npostgame interview bella ask primmie who is he have an eye on he say he and kilua likes to face xuna that's it bro don't be so mad it's not that serious", "Leviathan\nThanyathon Nakmee\n\nKillua\nTanate Teerasawad\n\nprimmie\nPapaphat Sriprapha\n\nJitBoyS\nJittana Nokngam\n\nCrws\nThanamethk Mahatthananuyut\n\n with a loss in the previous week, but plenty of momentum.", "A reinvigorated version of the team took RRQ to three maps, at one point up 11-9 on the third map."], "news_summary": "FULL SENSE vs VARREL is scheduled for VCT 2026 