{"run_id": "eeb6bf65-bdaf-476f-ae72-3abbc5237e3b", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T01:39:08.319766+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935609", "question": "LoL: ThunderTalk Gaming vs Oh My God (BO3) - LPL Group Nirvana", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between ThunderTalk Gaming and Oh My God in the LPL Group Nirvana, initially scheduled for April 17 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ThunderTalk Gaming\" if ThunderTalk Gaming win the match against Oh My God.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Oh My God\" if Oh My God win the match against ThunderTalk Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 16654.033917999997, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["93140706600240672969655435129494062068174170091311600738686858236323020964398", "39723628922410433024072183079063971519100635987786554717781556612773527594374"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.6, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: ThunderTalk Gaming must win the BO3 match against Oh My God on 2026-04-17 at 09:00 UTC (5:00 AM ET). Market resolves to YES if ThunderTalk wins, NO if OMG wins. EVENT TIMING CHECK: Event is TODAY with ~8 hours to start; it has NOT occurred yet. All prior match results are historical context only, not evidence this match has been decided. YES CASE STRENGTHS: ThunderTalk is 1\u20130 (2\u20130 in games) in LPL Split 2; OMG is 0\u20131 (0\u20132 in games). ThunderTalk has established early momentum, OMG has dropped two straight in the main tournament. YES CASE WEAKNESSES: Early LPL records are highly volatile (only 1\u20132 matches played per team). ThunderTalk has minimal recent history provided; no detailed form/roster/scrim data to validate sustained advantage. NO CASE STRENGTHS: OMG defeated Team WE 2\u20130 in EWC Qualifier just 3 days ago (Apr 14), demonstrating they are a competitive team with working strategies. OMG players show strong international credentials (Moham 86.5% KP in EWC, champion-level support play). Split 1 data shows OMG went 9\u201312 (42.86% W%), not a historically weak team. NO CASE WEAKNESSES: OMG's 0\u20132 start in Split 2 is a clear negative momentum indicator. Split 2 is the current, active competition tier; EWC Qualifier (concurrent but secondary) may distract or tire the roster. FORM VS MATCHUP VOLATILITY: At 1\u20132 matches per team played, early-season records are extremely noisy. OMG's 2\u20130 EWC win (Apr 14) vs. their 0\u20132 LPL start creates conflicting signals. Preparation overlap (EWC Qualifier ongoing) may hurt either team's LPL focus. MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: YES at 42%, NO at 58%. Market implies NO favored by ~16 points. This aligns with OMG's recent EWC success offsetting early LPL weakness, and recognition that 1\u20130 vs 0\u20131 is early noise. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Moderate confidence on both sides (60 YES, 65 NO) because early-season LoL is inherently noisy. OMG's Apr 14 EWC victory is concrete proof of current competitive capability, but OMG's Split 2 0\u20132 is equally concrete proof of form issues. ThunderTalk's 1\u20130 is real but based on minimal sample. Neither side has overwhelming evidence. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Negligible. BO3 match will almost certainly complete and produce a clear winner. gol.gg reporting is reliable for LPL. No forfeit/walkover concerns flagged. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Market price of 42/58 appears well-calibrated given conflicting signals (OMG's EWC 2\u20130 win on Apr 14 suggests competitive form; OMG's LPL 0\u20132 suggests early struggle; ThunderTalk's 1\u20130 is small sample; early-season volatility is high). Assign 42 to probability_score (slightly below market to reflect OMG's very recent concrete success vs. noise in early records).", "key_factor": "Early-season records (1\u20130 vs 0\u20131 after 1\u20132 matches) are volatile and unreliable predictors; OMG's concurrent EWC Qualifier participation (2\u20130 vs WE on Apr 14, just 3 days prior) indicates genuine competitive form despite Split 2 stumble, creating uncertainty about which dataset best predicts today's outcome."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = OMG) STRENGTHS: Oh My God defeated Team WE 2\u20130 in the EWC Qualifier just 3 days ago (April 14), demonstrating they can execute decisively against competitive opponents. This is the most recent tangible evidence of OMG's capability and suggests the 0\u20131 Split 2 start may not reflect their true level. Moham (support) posted 86.5% KP in the EWC Qualifier, indicating strong macro coordination. OMG has professional pedigree and international experience. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES = TTG) WEAKNESSES: ThunderTalk Gaming's 1\u20130 record and 2\u20130 game record are pristine but come against an unidentified early-season opponent; early LPL records are notoriously volatile and provide limited predictive value (acknowledged in briefing). ThunderTalk's match history and detailed player statistics are sparse in the briefing, raising questions about whether their 2\u20130 truly reflects superior play or favorable matchups. No recent high-level qualifier results are provided for TTG. FATIGUE & SCHEDULING RISK: Oh My God has played multiple matches in the concurrent EWC 2026 Qualifier (lost to JDG on March 31, lost to LGD on April 12, beat WE on April 14). A match on April 17 is only 3 days after a BO3 win, introducing potential fatigue. However, the April 14 win is also recent evidence of form\u2014a double-edged sword. ThunderTalk's fixture history in the briefing does not show this level of concurrent tournament stress. MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS NO: The NO side (OMG) has gained +9.0pp over 7 days (strong trend) and is currently at 58%, representing the consensus favorite. YES (TTG) has fallen sharply \u221227.0pp over the same period. Sharp moves on April 12 (\u22125.0pp, \u221210.0pp swings on YES) suggest informed traders adjusted when OMG's Split 2 struggles became clear, yet the subsequent +10.5pp reversal on April 12 and stabilization near 58% NO indicates sophisticated traders recognize the recency illusion in early-season records. EARLY-SEASON VOLATILITY FAVORS EXPERIENCE: The briefing explicitly notes that 'early-season records can be volatile' and this match occurs only 13 days into a ~60-day split. In early LPL, teams with established player synergy and recent high-level tournament experience (EWC Qualifier) often outperform those with small sample-size wins. OMG's roster demonstrated coordination in a playoff-format event against Team WE; TTG's recent opponents are unspecified. BULL CASE FOR NO: The market is pricing OMG at 58% but should likely be higher. OMG's 3-day-old BO3 win is stronger evidence than TTG's uncontextualized 2\u20130 start. The \u221227.0pp collapse in YES reflects panic about OMG's 0\u20132 start, but this is exactly when early-season swings are most irrational. Sophisticated money flowing to NO (+121 points on NO vs. +35 on YES) reflects this correction. OMG's split between EWC Qualifier (70% win rate) and LPL Split 1 (42.86% win rate) shows they can perform at high levels when it matters; Split 2 volatility is not evidence of incompetence. CONFIDENCE MODULATION: High confidence in YES (72%) because the structural case for NO is sound: recent qualifier evidence, player pedigree, market momentum, and early-season noise all favor OMG. However, moderate confidence in NO (55%) reflects significant uncertainty: TTG's actual roster strength and recent opponent quality are opaque in the briefing, making it difficult to definitively rule out a genuine 2\u20130 streak. Asymmetric data quality justifies the 10-point confidence gap. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 62% for YES (i.e., 38% for NO) means the NO bull case is strong but not overwhelming. This reflects: (a) OMG's recent qualifier win and experience edge, (b) market consensus at 58% NO is reasonable but slightly undervaluing OMG's recency advantage, (c) TTG's 2\u20130 is real but small-sample and under-documented, and (d) early-season volatility cuts both ways. The 10-point gap between probability_score (62) and probability_no_score (52) reflects the bull's deeper case on NO evidence versus shallower counter-evidence on TTG's true strength.", "key_factor": "ThunderTalk Gaming's perfect 2\u20130 game record and 1\u20130 match start in Split 2 contrasts sharply with Oh My God's 0\u20132 game record and struggling 0\u20131 record, despite OMG's recent qualifier victory."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR YES (ThunderTalk): ThunderTalk enters Split 2 with a pristine 1\u20130 (2\u20130 games) record, a full game ahead of Oh My God's 0\u20131 start. Early-split momentum in Bo3 formats is a documented advantage, particularly when one team has established confidence and the other is searching for form. FATIGUE & DISTRACTION FACTOR (KEY WEAKNESS FOR OMG): Oh My God is simultaneously competing in the EWC 2026 China Qualifier\u2014they played LGD on April 12 (lost 1\u20132), then Team WE on April 14 (won 2\u20130), just 3 days before this LPL match. This concurrent tournament exposure divides preparation resources, mental bandwidth, and physical recovery. ThunderTalk faces no such distraction and can concentrate entirely on Split 2 form. CHAMPION POOL & RECENT SUCCESS: Oh My God's recent EWC qualifier win vs. Team WE (2\u20130) shows capability, but the data reveals high variance\u2014they lost to LGD 1\u20132 and JDG 1\u20132 in the same qualifier window. Their LPL Split 1 record was mediocre (9\u201312, 42.86% W%), suggesting inconsistency rather than sustained excellence. ThunderTalk's lack of detailed champion pool data in the briefing is a gap, but their perfect early-split performance is concrete. EARLY-SEASON VOLATILITY CUTS BOTH WAYS: The briefing correctly notes that early records are 'less predictive of final standings.' However, this volatility typically rewards teams with better preparation and fewer distractions. ThunderTalk's clean start + singular focus favors them; OMG's split attention and 0\u20132 stumble suggest misalignment. SUPPORT PLAYER STRENGTH (MINOR COUNTER): Oh My God's support Moham showed 86.5% KP in EWC Qualifier\u2014elite playmaking. However, KP is a cumulative stat that reflects team macro, not individual excellence in isolation. High KP in a winning bracket (EWC) does not automatically translate to dominance in a fresh LPL match against a rested, momentum-driven opponent. RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD (CONTEXT ONLY): No direct H2H data provided between ThunderTalk and OMG. The briefing schedule grid shows they are scheduled to meet April 17 (this match) and later on May 16, but no prior encounters are documented. Without historical precedent, recent form is the primary signal. MARKET PRICING ASYMMETRY: YES (ThunderTalk) is priced at 42% despite holding a 2\u20130 games lead and a 1\u20130 record advantage. NO is priced at 58%, reflecting overweight on OMG's recent qualifier win. The 7-day YES price movement shows a -27pp decline, suggesting market confidence in OMG has grown\u2014possibly due to the Team WE victory. However, that qualifier win is against a weaker opponent (Team WE, not a top-4 LPL team) and required OMG to shake fatigue from two prior losses in 72 hours. Momentum is being mispriced. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: ThunderTalk's 2\u20130 record and undivided focus provide concrete, measurable advantages (confidence_yes = 42%). However, OMG's recent qualifier win and experienced roster provide a non-zero upset vector\u2014without detailed ThunderTalk champion pool data or head-to-head history, there is genuine uncertainty about whether ThunderTalk's early form is sustainable or a favorable opening draw (confidence_no = 48%). Data on ThunderTalk's historical performance in LPL is absent from the briefing. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Match is TODAY (~8 hours from briefing). No cancellation risk or technical issues noted. Market liquidity is moderate ($16.6k USD), reducing manipulation risk. Resolution will be official and timely. BEAR'S VERDICT: ThunderTalk is underpriced at 42%. They hold a structural advantage (perfect record, singular focus, OMG fatigue from concurrent qualifiers) that is not reflected in market odds weighted toward OMG's 3-day-old qualifier win. The 58% NO price is justified only if OMG's recent success is treated as determinative despite competitive distraction\u2014a bet on pedigree over current state. A sober allocation favors YES at 58\u201362% range; market offers 42%. Probability reflects moderate bear confidence: ThunderTalk favored but not dominant given data gaps on their roster depth and champion pool.", "key_factor": "ThunderTalk's perfect 2\u20130 game record and early-split momentum advantage against an Oh My God team juggling concurrent EWC Qualifier matches with demonstrable fatigue and preparation strain."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "ThunderTalk Gaming enters 1-0 (2-0 games) in LPL 2026 Split 2, showing clean early momentum with no losses yet. Oh My God enters 0-1 (0-2 games) in Split 2, indicating early-split struggles, but this is only 1 match \u2014 insufficient sample to declare form collapse. OMG defeated Team WE 2-0 on Apr 14 (3 days before this match), demonstrating recent competitive capability and suggesting they can win against competent opposition. OMG is managing dual tournament load (EWC Qualifier + LPL Split 2). Apr 12 loss to LGD and Apr 14 win vs WE suggest fatigue risk but also active player development. Head-to-head history absent; no direct precedent between ThunderTalk and OMG in this briefing. Market has shifted significantly: YES side fell 27pp over 7 days (-27.0pp trend), suggesting declining confidence in ThunderTalk despite their 1-0 record. This contrasts with the raw record. Sharp moves on Apr 12 (\u00b110pp swings) correspond to OMG's loss to LGD (Apr 12) and subsequent win vs WE (Apr 14), indicating market reacted positively to the WE result. Early-season LoL records (1-2 matches per team) have historically poor predictive power; OMG's 0-1 start is not a strong signal of sustained underperformance. Market price (42% YES / 58% NO) implies market favors OMG despite ThunderTalk's undefeated record. This suggests informed traders view OMG's recent qualifier win and veteran roster as offsetting early-split stumble. Confidence in YES is moderate (42) due to small sample size and conflicting signals: ThunderTalk's perfect record vs. market's persistent retreat and OMG's recent win. Confidence in NO is similarly moderate (38) due to lack of direct head-to-head data and OMG's 0-2 game record in Split 2, which cannot be fully dismissed as noise. Probability estimates (58 YES, 52 NO) reflect genuine uncertainty. Sum <100 reflects ignorance mass appropriate for early-season esports with thin team samples.", "key_factor": "Early-season LoL match win rates show ~45-55% variance depending on roster stability, recent qualifier fatigue, and head-to-head dynamics. Early splits are volatile; records stabilize only after 5+ matches per team."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "ThunderTalk Gaming enters at 1-0 (2-0 in games) vs OMG's 0-1 (0-2 in games) in LPL 2026 Split 2 \u2014 clear early-season record advantage favoring YES side. Market priced YES at 42%, which is BELOW what pure record differential would suggest (~55-60%). Indicates crowd is discounting ThunderTalk's perfect start. OMG's recent 2-0 win vs Team WE on April 14 (3 days prior) is the primary NO-side momentum signal. This is strong recent evidence of competitive form. OMG also competing in concurrent EWC Qualifier (lost 1-2 to LGD on Apr 12, beat Team WE on Apr 14) \u2014 fatigue/preparation risk is real but not catastrophic for a 3-day gap. No head-to-head history provided between ThunderTalk and OMG; limits direct comparative strength signal. Early-season volatility acknowledged in briefing: records are poor predictors in week 1 of a 14-team tournament. Market correctly reflects this uncertainty rather than extrapolating ThunderTalk's 2-0 start as destiny. YES-side sentiment is muted (42% price, -27pp over 7 days) \u2014 crowd has been gradually abandoning ThunderTalk narrative. This suggests either rational caution or overcorrection. NO-side sentiment has strengthened (+9pp over 7 days, now 58%). Market appears to be pricing OMG's recent qualifier win and inherent uncertainty in early-season records. 42-58 split is relatively balanced, suggesting crowd sees genuine competitive parity. Not a crowded trade on either side. OMG's player-level metrics (Moham 86.5% KP in EWC, Starry's strong bot lane performance) show individual quality that early-season record (0-1) may understate. Briefing contains NO explicit information on ThunderTalk's recent form beyond Split 2 record. ThunderTalk's 2-0 start is impressive but lacks supporting detail on player performance or head-to-head context. Market price (42% YES) appears SLIGHTLY FAVORING the NO side relative to early Win-Loss records alone, but this discount is justified by OMG's immediate qualifier success and tournament volatility. Event is TODAY (8 hours to start) \u2014 any remaining price movement will be driven by final roster confirmations, meta shifts, or last-minute injury news, none of which are visible in briefing. Confidence asymmetry: YES confidence 62 (record data is clear, but lacks depth on ThunderTalk quality); NO confidence 68 (recent qualifier win is strong signal, but OMG's 0-2 Split 2 start is concerning). Both moderately strong.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "ThunderTalk enters 1\u20130 (2\u20130 games) vs. OMG's 0\u20131 (0\u20132 games) in LPL 2026 Split 2 regular season; early momentum and undefeated record provide psychological and structural advantage. Oh My God's recent EWC Qualifier performance (April 12\u201314) shows volatile results: lost 1\u20132 to LGD on April 12, beat Team WE 2\u20130 on April 14, lost 1\u20132 to JDG on March 31. Back-to-back BO3s three days before this match introduce fatigue and mental strain. ThunderTalk's 2\u20130 game record vs. OMG's 0\u20132 suggests superior early-split drafting, execution, and team cohesion\u2014critical in BO3 format where adaptation and composure compound over multiple games. OMG's support player Moham (86.5% KP in EWC Qualifier) and ADC Starry (68.8% KP, 70% W rate in EWC) show individual strength, but team-level coordination under fatigue from concurrent qualifier play is a material risk. Mid-laner Haichao's 4.1 KDA on LeBlanc/Taliyah (100% WR) and Yone (100% WR) indicates individual carry potential; however, LPL Split 1 data shows OMG's mid-laner at 42.86% W rate (9\u201312) in full season, suggesting consistency issues. ThunderTalk's matchup schedule shows they beat Ultra Prime 2\u20130 on April 15 (just 2 days ago), demonstrating recent form and fitness advantage heading into April 17. Early-season volatility is high in LPL; however, the combination of undefeated record + fatigue asymmetry + recent quality win for ThunderTalk tilts the probability toward YES, though OMG's qualifier momentum and individual player talent keeps NO competitive. Market pricing at 42% YES / 58% NO reflects market skepticism of ThunderTalk, likely due to OMG's recent 2\u20130 EWC win and international exposure. However, expert sports analysis would weight the fatigue and preparation gap more heavily. Confidence in YES is moderate-high (68%) because early LPL form is predictive despite volatility, but confidence in NO is lower (55%) because OMG's qualifier fatigue and OMG's Split 1 underperformance (42.86% W) introduce execution risk not fully captured by recent wins.", "key_factor": "Early-season LPL records are volatile proxies for team strength, but ThunderTalk's perfect 2\u20130 game record combined with OMG's concurrent EWC Qualifier participation (April 12\u201314 losses plus a 2\u20130 win over Team WE on April 14) introduces fatigue and preparation asymmetry that favours the fresh team."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "MOMENTUM REVERSAL HIDDEN IN TIMING: OMG just secured a clean 2\u20130 victory vs Team WE in EWC Qualifier on April 14 (3 days before this match), demonstrating recent competitive sharpness. ThunderTalk's 1\u20130 record lacks context on opponent strength; early-split records are volatile and tell little about true form. PSYCHOLOGICAL EDGE TO OMG: A squad that just proved they can execute a 2\u20130 BO3 cleanly carries confidence into a must-win LPL match. ThunderTalk may face 'false confidence' after one win; OMG has recent proof of execution under pressure. FATIGUE ASYMMETRY FAVORING OMG: The briefing notes OMG participated in concurrent EWC Qualifier matches (Apr 12, Apr 14). While this could suggest fatigue, the April 14 victory shows they adapted and won decisively. ThunderTalk's April 15 win vs Ultra Prime (2\u20130) is less recent and offers no fatigue counterweight. SUPPORT PLAY EXCELLENCE: Moham (OMG support) posted 86.5% KP in EWC Qualifier, indicating exceptional playmaking and early-game priority. This is a specialist-level metric; ThunderTalk's support profile is not highlighted in the briefing, creating a potential draft/execution gap. CHAMPION POOL ASYMMETRY: OMG's ban/pick data (Yunara 57%, Malphite 57%, Poppy 43%) suggests strong meta adaptation in recent games. ThunderTalk's champion data is entirely absent from the briefing, a data vacuum that typically masks either a weakness or a hidden strength\u2014but in early-season context, silence often means unproven depth. EARLY-SEASON VOLATILITY: The briefing explicitly notes this is an 'early-season matchup' and 'early records can be volatile.' OMG's 0\u20131 LPL start is an outlier given their 7\u20133 (70%) record in concurrent EWC Qualifier; a reversion to form is plausible. MARKET PRICE DECAY ON YES SIDE: YES probability has fallen 27.0pp over 7 days and saw sharp drops on Apr 12 (\u20135.0pp, \u201310.0pp). This suggests informed traders are rotating away from ThunderTalk after initial hype. The NO side has risen +9.0pp over the same window, indicating market belief in OMG recovery. ABSENCE OF THUNDERTALK DETAIL: The briefing provides extensive player stats, champion pools, and tournament history for OMG but almost no comparative depth on ThunderTalk's roster, playstyle, or recent opponents. This asymmetry in available information often signals that ThunderTalk has less proven international/qualifier pedigree, a risk factor in a BO3. BO3 STRUCTURE FAVORS PREPARATION: OMG has demonstrated adaptability (2\u20131 vs NIP, 2\u20130 vs WE in EWC), suggesting strong coach-driven adjustment within a series. ThunderTalk's 2\u20130 game record is achieved in a single series; no BO3 adaptation data exists. FORM TRAJECTORY INVERSION: OMG's last 3 matches: L (LGD, Apr 12), W (WE, Apr 14), this match TODAY. The trajectory is UP. ThunderTalk's last match before today: W (Ultra Prime, Apr 15). Without earlier context, ThunderTalk's trajectory is unknown and may have been inflated by a weak opponent.", "key_factor": "ThunderTalk's undefeated record (1\u20130, 2\u20130 in games) may reflect a weak opening opponent rather than elite form; OMG's concurrent EWC Qualifier participation (2\u20130 vs WE on April 14, just 3 days prior) signals rising momentum and tactical sharpness despite the LPL 0\u20131 start, creating a form-trajectory reversal that favors OMG in a high-stakes BO3."}], "final_score": 0.5115438728758341, "no_score": 0.5057983931293174, "edge": 0.27590909090909094, "no_edge": 0.10590909090909095, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 51.15% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 55.43% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935609", "question": "LoL: ThunderTalk Gaming vs Oh My God (BO3) - LPL Group Nirvana", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between ThunderTalk Gaming and Oh My God in the LPL Group Nirvana, initially scheduled for April 17 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ThunderTalk Gaming\" if ThunderTalk Gaming win the match against Oh My God.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Oh My God\" if Oh My God win the match against ThunderTalk Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 16654.033917999997, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["93140706600240672969655435129494062068174170091311600738686858236323020964398", "39723628922410433024072183079063971519100635987786554717781556612773527594374"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "AG Super Play are the defending champions, having defeated Weibo Gaming 4-1 in the finals last season.", "They did not defend their title, having lost 2-4 to", "| Banned against Oh My God |\n\n| |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  -