certainty"], "key_context": ["Double-elimination BO3 playoffs format; teams must win 2 maps to advance", "Online event with no LAN advantage factor", "Both teams are Brazilian/South American academy/challenger-level squads", "Event runs Apr 16\u201319; this match is on Apr 16 at 23:45 UTC (already started)"], "prior_match_facts": [], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T01:13:44.247536Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "47906967700588984592886850364880553122735156390156086499656942039030240745093", "data_points": 3, "weighted_avg": 0.5934659860013575, "change_1w_pp": 21.000000000000004, "change_24h_pp": 21.000000000000004, "volatility_24h": 20.506096654409887, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-17T01:00:50Z", "delta_pp": 25.000000000000007}]}, "no": {"token_id": "65978178387597806322565160929974020450634901475345973064343458831561155476875", "data_points": 2, "weighted_avg": 0.3375322204914466, "change_1w_pp": 4.499999999999998, "change_24h_pp": 4.499999999999998, "volatility_24h": 0.0, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-17T01:13:44.572799Z"}, "structured_match": null}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-17T05:45:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-17T11:00:28.579053+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "50898d55-8c21-4c29-882c-b430a86c49ba", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T01:39:19.699356+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1955515", "question": "LoL: Dplus KIA vs T1 (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Dplus KIA and T1 in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 17 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dplus KIA\" if Dplus KIA win the match against T1.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1\" if T1 win the match against Dplus KIA.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 39924.14835299999, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["32012524366321573179345254119203212277749028676605808728407316022076068917966", "96922050127360887243268452133279570302327492327172004415084766976591314199698"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE ISSUE: The briefing states EVENT TIMING = TODAY (event starts in ~9 hours at 2026-04-17 10:00 UTC), yet PRIOR MATCH FACTS describe T1 vs Dplus KIA matchups in 'LCK Cup 2026 Playoffs Round 3' with specific game results (T1 wins 3-2, 2-0, etc.). This suggests either: (a) those are from an EARLIER stage of the same tournament and this is a rematch/group-stage repeat, or (b) data freshness is stale and those matches have already occurred. The DISAMBIGUATION WARNINGS confirm this inconsistency but classify past-tense language as referring to PRIOR encounters, not this market's outcome. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Dplus KIA wins the BO3 match; NO if T1 wins. Forfeits, walkovers, or cancellations resolve 50-50. The match has not yet started. HISTORICAL HEAD-TO-HEAD (2024): T1 defeated Dplus KIA 2-0 twice in LCK Spring 2024 (Weeks 4 & 8). This establishes T1 dominance 2+ years prior but has limited predictive power for 2026 form. LCK CUP 2026 RECORD (from data): Dplus KIA shows losses to Gen.G (0-2), DRX, and T1 in playoff rounds. T1 shows wins vs Dplus KIA in Rounds 1-3 (mixed series outcomes including 3-2 and 2-0 results). If these have already occurred, they provide strong evidence T1 is the stronger team in this tournament, suggesting the upcoming match will also favor T1. If they are still-to-be-played, the context is less clear. STATISTICAL PROFILE (Dplus KIA, LCK Cup 2026): +351 gold differential at 15 min, +21 CS differential, 3.5 wards/min, 45.8% dragon control, 15.1 kills/game (15.5 deaths). Early-game metrics are respectable but volatile performance and high death rate suggests late-game execution issues. STATISTICAL PROFILE (T1, implicit from case): Superior late-game teamfighting, higher kill differentials, better map control in wins. More disciplined macro play. MARKET PRICING: YES (Dplus KIA) = 38%, NO (T1) = 62%. Market heavily favors T1. Price movement: YES fell 12.5pp over 7 days (sharp -14.5pp drop on Apr 13), suggesting growing confidence in T1. This implies professional/informed backing is on the NO side. CONFIDENCE ADJUSTMENTS: confidence_yes = 45 (moderate) because: (1) historical T1 dominance is clear but dated; (2) 2026 LCK Cup data suggests T1 is stronger but temporal ambiguity clouds interpretation; (3) no recent form news. confidence_no = 52 (moderate) because: (1) market pricing and directional movement strongly support T1; (2) historical H2H favors T1; (3) but data freshness concerns and lack of pre-match situational updates limit certainty. Both scores reflect genuine uncertainty amplified by briefing inconsistencies. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: probability_score = 38 (aligned with current market YES price). This reflects: (a) T1 is favored by historical record, 2026 tournament performance (if already played), and market consensus; (b) Dplus KIA's early-game metrics offer modest support but insufficient to overcome T1's demonstrated advantages. probability_no_score = 62 (aligned with market NO price). The two probabilities roughly sum to 100 because market is pricing a two-outcome binary; the slight 2-point buffer (38+62=100) reflects no significant unexplained ambiguity outside the temporal conflict already flagged.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains conflicting temporal signals: PRIOR MATCH FACTS describe T1 defeating Dplus KIA in LCK Cup 2026 Rounds 1-3, but event is scheduled for 2026-04-17 (TODAY, ~9 hours away), creating ambiguity about whether this is a rematch, group-stage repeat, or distinct fixture; additionally, news summary lacks recent form data immediately preceding the match."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = T1 wins) STRENGTHS: \u2022 T1 holds a perfect 2-0 sweep record against Dplus KIA in LCK Spring 2024 (Week 4 and Week 8), demonstrating clear matchup dominance in direct competition. \u2022 T1 exhibits superior late-game execution and teamfighting in prior wins, with higher kill differentials and consistent map control advantages. \u2022 Dplus KIA's recent LCK Cup 2026 playoff performance is weak: 0-2 loss to Gen.G, eliminations to DRX and T1 in early rounds, suggesting confidence collapse or roster issues. \u2022 Historical asymmetry is stark: T1 is Korea's most successful organization with institutional depth; Dplus KIA lacks comparable pedigree. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES = Dplus KIA wins) WEAKNESSES: \u2022 Early-game metric advantages (+351 gold at 15 min, +21 CS differential in LCK Cup 2026) have NOT translated to match wins in recent playoffs\u2014Dplus KIA lost those series despite these stats. \u2022 Vision control and objective prioritization (3.5 wards/min, 45.8% dragon control) are marginal improvements that pale against T1's teamfighting superiority demonstrated in head-to-head. \u2022 Volatile performance profile (15.1 kills per game, 15.5 deaths) suggests inconsistency\u2014exactly what T1's disciplined playstyle exploits. \u2022 LCK Cup 2026 Round 3 games vs T1 are framed as 'competitive' but Dplus KIA ultimately lost the series; calling mixed individual-game results 'tight margins' oversells Dplus KIA's prospects. PROBABILITY REASONING: \u2022 Market price (62% NO) reflects T1 as a clear favorite, supported by historical dominance and recent form. \u2022 Dplus KIA's early-game strengths are real but have been neutralized by T1 in past matchups\u2014this is T1's strength (conversion from mid-game onward). \u2022 The briefing reveals no recent roster changes, meta shifts favoring Dplus KIA, or tactical innovations that would flip the historical 4-0 record into a reversal. \u2022 Event timing (TODAY, 9 hours out) leaves no time for new information that could materially shift expectations; market has already priced in available data. BULL CASE ALIGNMENT: \u2022 As advocate for the favored side, T1's historical dominance, institutional advantage, and Dplus KIA's playoff struggles form a compelling case for NO (T1 wins). \u2022 probability_score = 68 reflects T1 favored but acknowledges ~30% tail risk from early-game metrics and individual-game volatility in LCK Cup 2026. \u2022 probability_no_score = 28 (not mirrored to 32) reflects asymmetric evidence: strong case FOR T1 (multiple vectors), weaker counter-case AGAINST Dplus KIA (metrics haven't won matches). \u2022 Confidence_yes (72) is elevated due to historical data density; confidence_no (35) reflects Dplus KIA's sparse recent evidence and inability to convert statistical leads into series wins.", "key_factor": "T1's dominant historical head-to-head record (4-0 vs Dplus KIA in 2024 LCK Spring) combined with superior late-game execution and teamfighting in playoff contexts."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR YES (Dplus KIA): The briefing data shows Dplus KIA possesses concrete, measurable early-game metrics superior to historical context\u2014+351 gold differential at 15 minutes and +21 CS differential in current LCK Cup 2026 play is not noise; it indicates adaptation to 2026 meta. Vision control asymmetry: Dplus KIA averages 3.5 wards per minute with 45.8% dragon control rate. These metrics suggest improved objective discipline and map awareness relative to 2024, when T1 dominated via superior teamfighting. Head-to-head LCK Cup 2026 data (Rounds 1-3 vs T1) shows Dplus KIA won 2 games (3-2 series loss in Game 5, then Games 4&5 wins). This is NOT a 2-0 sweep\u2014the series was competitive and went to 5 games, contradicting the narrative that T1 is categorically superior. Historical 2024 losses (2-0, 2-0) are 2+ years old. Meta, rosters, and player form evolve significantly. Citing 2024 as primary evidence for a 2026 BO3 is a recency-weighted error favoring T1. Dplus KIA's volatile performance profile (15.1 kills/game, 15.5 deaths) is high-variance, but high variance in a BO3 underdog means upset probability is non-negligible. A single strong early-game execution could carry Game 1; momentum matters in BO3. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES: T1's recent LCK Cup 2026 record vs Dplus KIA shows inconsistency\u2014winning Rounds 1-3 series 3-2 is not dominant. T1 dropped 2 games to an 'inferior' opponent, suggesting they are not as clean or favored as 62% pricing implies. Late-game execution advantage cited in CASE FOR YES is undermined by briefing data showing Dplus KIA competitive in game lengths (33:53, 34:57, 31:33, 32:51 min range across losses and wins). No evidence of T1's superior teamfighting in 2026 LCK Cup data provided. Champion ban patterns (Orianna 37%, Varus 34%, Nautilus 31% vs Dplus KIA) reveal meta volatility. If Dplus KIA's signature champs are consistently banned, they adapt via vision/macro\u2014strengths reflected in their early-game metrics. T1's recent record vs Gen.G and DRX (not provided in briefing) is absent. We only have Dplus KIA's losses to these teams. No comparative data on T1's form relative to tier-1 LCK competition exists in the briefing, creating asymmetric information favoring an upset narrative. EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY (10:00 UTC, ~9 hours away). No breaking roster news, injury reports, or meta-shift announcements are present in the briefing. Absence of such information favors stability\u2014established metrics (Dplus KIA's +351 gold, 3.5 wards/min) likely hold. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Confidence in YES is LOW (35) because Dplus KIA's early-game metrics, while positive, do not guarantee BO3 victory; T1's historical wins (2024) and LCK Cup 2026 series win are real, and 62% market pricing reflects serious expectation. Confidence in NO is MODERATE (62) because T1's vulnerabilities are empirical (2 game losses in recent series) but not overwhelming\u2014a 62% favorite in esports is reasonable, not a lock. The spread (38% vs 62%) underprices Dplus KIA's early-game + vision control edge. A BO3 where one team consistently wins early skirmishes and vision trades can convert early advantage to map control and objective leads. YES deserves 40-45% range, not 38%.", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA's LCK Cup 2026 early-game dominance (+351 gold at 15min, +21 CS) and improved vision control (3.5 wards/min) demonstrate tangible meta-fit advantages that override historical 2024 losses."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.71, "rationale": "\u2022 HISTORICAL H2H DOMINANCE: T1 defeated Dplus KIA 2-0 twice in LCK Spring 2024 (Weeks 4 & 8), establishing a 4-0 clean sweep record. This is the strongest historical signal. \u2022 INSTITUTIONAL QUALITY: T1 is an elite org with consistent championship pedigree; Dplus KIA has lower sustained win rates in high-stakes competition. \u2022 LCK CUP 2026 MIXED RECORD: The briefing shows LCK Cup 2026 playoffs data with T1 vs Dplus KIA across Rounds 1-3 (BO5 series), with T1 winning overall but Dplus KIA securing individual map wins. This suggests closer matches than 2024, but T1 still won the series decisively. \u2022 DPLUS KIA EARLY-GAME METRICS: +351 gold diff @ 15min and +21 CS diff are positive, but insufficient to overcome T1's superior late-game execution and macro control documented in prior encounters. \u2022 VOLATILITY & FORM: Dplus KIA stats (15.1 kills/game, 15.5 deaths) show volatile performance. Losses to Gen.G 0-2 and DRX in earlier rounds suggest inconsistent execution under pressure. \u2022 MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES (Dplus KIA) at 38% reflects underdog status, aligned with historical priors. Sharp move on Apr 13 (-14.5pp on YES) suggests market repricing toward T1 favorite. \u2022 BASE RATE FOR THIS MATCHUP: T1's historical 4-0 record + institutional edge anchors base rate at ~65-70% T1 favorite (~30-35% Dplus KIA). Current 38% YES is slightly generous to the underdog. \u2022 EVENT TIMING: BO3 format occurs TODAY in ~9 hours; insufficient time for roster changes or meta shifts to significantly alter the H2H dynamic. Historical form dominates. \u2022 CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on T1's dominance (2024 H2H + 2026 playoff series) justifies high confidence_no (71). Dplus KIA case relies on early-game micro-metrics that have not historically translated to series wins; confidence_yes is lower (62).", "key_factor": "T1 vs Dplus KIA H2H: T1 won 4-0 in prior 2024 encounters (2-0, 2-0); LCK Cup 2026 playoffs show competitive but split results favoring T1 overall. Base rate: T1 ~65-70% favorite in direct matchups based on historical dominance."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects rational skepticism of Dplus KIA\u2014a reasonable position given T1's historical dominance and recent LCK Cup 2026 playoff struggles by DK. KEY DATA ISSUE: Briefing contains contradictory frame. 'CASE FOR YES' argues T1's superiority (2-0 wins in 2024), but YES label means 'Dplus KIA wins'\u2014the briefing's YES case actually argues AGAINST the YES outcome. This is a structural error in the briefing document itself, not market mispricing. Interpreting the actual match context: T1 has historically dominated Dplus KIA (2-0 in LCK Spring 2024 Week 4 and Week 8), making T1 the clear favorite. Current market price reflects this with 62% on T1. Dplus KIA's LCK Cup 2026 playoff record shows multiple losses (0-2 to Gen.G, losses to DRX, mixed results vs T1 in Rounds 1-3). This recent form supports the NO side (T1 wins). Dplus KIA early-game metrics (+351 gold diff at 15min, +21 CS) are positive micro-indicators, but insufficient to overcome macro weakness in late-game teamfighting and T1's superior execution in prior encounters. LCK Cup 2026 Rounds 1-3 head-to-head games vs T1 show 'mixed results' per briefing, but the summary notes T1 won 3-2 and 2-0 in those series\u2014indicating T1 dominance in the full series, not parity. NO side (T1 confidence=75) is well-supported by historical precedent, recent form, and late-game execution edge. YES side (DK confidence=62) hinges on early-game metrics that have not translated to series wins in LCK Cup 2026. Market has shifted -12.5pp for YES over 7 days, suggesting rational repricing away from Dplus KIA as event approaches\u2014consistent with accumulating evidence of T1's superiority. No new roster changes, meta shifts, or injury news in briefing to suggest a reversal from historical patterns. Event is TODAY (9 hours away)\u2014insufficient time for major sentiment reversals unless new information emerges. Assign 32 to probability_score (Dplus KIA wins) and 68 to probability_no_score (T1 wins). Confidence asymmetry (62 vs 75) reflects stronger evidence for T1's dominance than for an upset.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: This is LCK Cup 2026 Rounds 1-2 (early-stage group play), not the Spring regular season. Meta, rosters, and patch states differ materially from 2024 historical matchups cited in the YES case. HEAD-TO-HEAD IN CURRENT TOURNAMENT (LCK Cup 2026): The briefing shows T1 vs Dplus KIA matches in Playoffs.Round3 with T1 winning 3-2 (W, W, L outcome per game records) and 2-0 (W, W). This is the most recent, patch-relevant data. T1's tournament record vs Dplus KIA is 4-1 in individual games within LCK Cup 2026. DPLUS KIA EARLY-GAME STRENGTH: +351 gold diff at 15min and 3.5 wards/min indicate Dplus KIA can establish early leads and vision control. However, the game-level records show they lose even when winning early (e.g., 14 gold at 15min vs T1's 14 kills\u2014volatility suggests early wins don't convert to series wins). T1 LATE-GAME CLOSURE: Across all recorded matchups in LCK Cup 2026, T1 consistently wins longer games (31:33, 33:53 vs Dplus KIA's shorter losses). T1's kill differential widens in wins (9 kills vs Dplus KIA's 1-3). This is industry-standard T1 playstyle: scale and teamfight execution. DPLUS KIA VOLATILITY: Kill profile (15.1 kills/15.5 deaths per game) and split results (wins vs losses in same series) suggest execution inconsistency or draft-dependent performance. In professional LoL, this volatility typically suppresses win probability in best-of series against stable opponents. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES side fell 12.5pp over 7 days with a sharp -14.5pp drop on Apr 13 03:00 UTC. This suggests market participants received information favoring T1 (likely recent scrim results, patch notes favoring T1 champ pool, or public practice data). The current 38% YES price reflects this recalibration. META EVOLUTION: Dplus KIA's most-banned champs (Orianna 37%, Varus 34%, Nautilus 31%) differ from typical T1 meta. If T1 has adapted their draft/play to 2026 meta while Dplus KIA remains in transition, T1's expected win rate increases. TIMING & IMMINENT EVENT: Event starts in ~9 hours. No new narrative reversals are plausible at this stage (roster changes, emergency substitutions, or scandal would be market-moving but unlikely this close to kickoff). Price stability in last 24h (+0.0pp) suggests market has priced in available information. RESOLUTION CLARITY: Match will be played, no forfeit risk evident. Resolution source (gol.gg) will provide objective scoreline. No ambiguity in team identification. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (T1 win) due to strong recent LCK Cup 2026 head-to-head record (4-1), late-game execution pattern, and market momentum. Moderate confidence in YES reflects Dplus KIA's early-game metrics and patch-variance unknowns (early-game strength doesn't guarantee BO3 series win, especially vs T1's scaling).", "key_factor": "T1's historical 2-0 dominance in 2024 is stale meta context; LCK Cup 2026 playoff games show T1 winning BO3 series 3-2 and 2-0 against Dplus KIA with volatile individual-game outcomes, but the raw head-to-head record in THIS tournament favors T1 decisively while Dplus KIA's early-game metrics (+351 gold diff @ 15min) suggest they can compete early before T1's superior late-game execution closes out."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "CONSENSUS TRAP: The briefing leans heavily on T1's 2024 head-to-head dominance (2-0, 2-0) and late-game superiority, but those matches are ~2 years old and pre-patch 16.3. Meta evolution is NOT mentioned but is near-certain given competitive LoL's patch cycle. SILENT SIGNAL \u2014 ROSTER/META MISMATCH: Dplus KIA's most-banned champions (Orianna 37%, Varus 34%, Nautilus 31%) suggest a specific identity T1 is forced to respect. If T1's ban patterns have not evolved to counter this core identity, DK gains a champion pool advantage. The briefing provides NO T1 ban data or current meta read \u2014 a critical absence. EARLY-GAME TIGHTNESS: LCK Cup 2026 Round 3 games vs T1 show DK winning multiple maps with competitive kill distributions (not blowouts). This is NOT the 2024 narrative of systematic T1 dominance. Suggests the matchup has tightened significantly. FORM TRAJECTORY HIDDEN: Dplus KIA shows a 0-2 loss to Gen.G and losses to DRX in Rounds 1-2, but playoff bracket structure and seeding are unclear. If DK is playing from a lower bracket or tiebreaker scenario with HIGH motivation and limited fatigue, they may perform above aggregate stats. Conversely, if they are mentally tilted from round-robin losses, that risk cuts the other way. Briefing does NOT clarify motivation or bracket position. EARLY-GAME METRICS ARE NOT NEGLIGIBLE: +351 gold at 15 min and +21 CS differential are non-trivial advantages in 2026 meta. If the meta favors early-to-mid game snowball (common in recent LoL patches), DK's strength in this phase could translate to map control wins before T1's teamfighting kicks in. The briefing notes this but minimizes its impact. VOLATILITY IN DK'S PROFILE: 15.1 kills per game with 15.5 deaths suggests high-variance, high-risk play. In a BO3, volatility is DK's BLACK SWAN: Game 1 upset via early-game execution + drafting advantage resets mental state, DK takes Game 2 with momentum, T1 forced into reverse-sweep pressure. Probability of this sequence is ~10-15%, not zero. MARKET PRICE SHIFT: YES side fell 12.5pp over 7 days (sharp -14.5pp on Apr 13), suggesting significant information arrived (likely roster news, scrimmage results, or meta analysis) that favors T1. This is reflected in current 38% YES. However, if that signal was OVER-WEIGHTED (e.g., based on incomplete data or coach commentary taken out of context), a contrarian read sees overshoot downward. DK at 38% may be undervalued if early-game meta advantage is real. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (T1 win) is justified by 2024 head-to-head, late-game stats, and market consensus. Low confidence in YES reflects the briefing's silence on current roster health, scrim results, and patch-specific meta reads. DK's black swan is plausible (5-15% true probability) but not well-evidenced in the briefing\u2014hence low confidence_yes (35) vs moderate confidence_no (62). TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK: Event is TODAY (9 hours away). Any roster surprise, illness, or last-minute meta insight will not reverse the market materially before start. Shares will trade ~$0.99 for T1 once match begins if early drafts favor T1. However, if DK wins Game 1 decisively, YES shares will spike rapidly\u2014indicating the council's consensus was indeed overweighting T1's narrative. RESOLUTION RISK: No forfeiture, cancellation, or tie mentioned in pre-event context. BO3 will complete. Risk of 50-50 resolution is negligible (<1%).", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA exploits a critical meta shift or roster-specific advantage (e.g., champion pool mismatch, mid-lane dominance on patch 16.3 favoring their primary win condition) that neutralizes T1's late-game teamfighting edge, compressing margins and enabling early-game snowball into map control wins before T1's macro stabilizes."}], "final_score": 0.396799276009437, "no_score": 0.6398088182703715, "edge": 0.3159090909090909, "no_edge": 0.06590909090909092, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 61.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0602670516001211, "The Bull": 0.9435703729286524, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0538053760207984, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.056111041369942, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0455611692471798, "The Contrarian": 1.0671826431155376, "The Bear": 0.7735023457177681