if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.355, "volume_usd": 1364.5190320000002, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["50511395647305309621081308333157329672272890889607281164942737776842353055647", "12098225979665053704135459978545793995416598405608583247513026029963794678001"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "EVENT STATUS: Match began 2026-04-17 11:00 UTC; briefing timestamp 11:13 UTC places match approximately 13 minutes into play. Event is LIVE, not concluded. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: YES price dropped 14.5pp sharply at 11:12 UTC (1 minute after match start), suggesting early match data (early rounds, map veto outcome, or team positioning) favored Favbet. This is a significant real-time signal that market participants observed unfavorable conditions for Acend at match open. YES-SIDE STRENGTHS: Acend shows 100% win rate on Anubis (6 consecutive wins) and 80% on Inferno (15 maps). If Acend successfully veto into Anubis or Inferno, these map advantages are material. NO-SIDE STRENGTHS: Favbet achieves 35% 2-0 victory rate (vs. Acend's 22.5%), indicating higher ceiling and consistency in dominant wins. Favbet's 0-2 loss rate of only 10% (vs. Acend's 27.5%) suggests stronger floor and lower risk of collapse. Favbet's 75% Inferno win rate (20 maps) is solid and threatens one of Acend's key maps. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: Only one prior match cited (Acend vs Ursa on Apr 15) \u2014 provides no direct H2H data between Acend and Favbet. Map-specific form data is the primary lever. SHARP MOVE INTERPRETATION: The 14.5pp swing toward NO at match start (11:12 UTC) likely reflects: (1) early round losses for Acend, (2) unfavorable map veto outcome for Acend, or (3) visible skill disparity in opening rounds. Market participants with live access made a coordinated adjustment, signaling reduced confidence in Acend. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Current market prices (YES 36%, NO 64%) align closely with briefing data showing Favbet's superior consistency (35% 2-0 rate, 10% 0-2 loss rate) and lower variance. The sharp move suggests price discovery is ongoing and early evidence slightly favors Favbet. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO (72%) exceeds confidence in YES (45%) because: (a) Favbet's floor (0-2 loss rate 10%) is significantly lower than Acend's (27.5%), providing strong defensive evidence; (b) the live 14.5pp swing toward NO represents real-time match data; (c) Acend's Anubis advantage is map-pool dependent and may not materialize if Favbet vetoes it. Confidence in YES is tempered because early match signals have already moved against Acend. RESOLUTION RISK: If match ends in forfeit/disqualification/walkover at start, market resolves 50-50 per criteria. However, event is already 13 minutes in, suggesting match began normally. Completion risk is secondary at this stage. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Briefing clearly states EVENT_TIMING is LIVE_OR_PAST and provides timestamp 11:13 UTC for data freshness, confirming match is in active progress. No contradiction detected.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE with match in progress (~13 minutes in); final outcome is currently unknown and could change materially before completion; market prices already showing sharp 14.5pp swing at match start suggesting early information affecting odds."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVBET is the correct favorite: market pricing at 64% NO (36% YES) ali