cution (economy, teamfight wins, objective control) not visible in this briefing.", "key_factor": "EVOS received a sharp +14pp market surge at match start (11:17 UTC), suggesting late-breaking in-game information or team execution advantage that the pre-match NO favorite (63%) failed to price in."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Match is LIVE_OR_PAST (started ~2 min ago at 11:15 UTC). Briefing lacks real-time game state, scoreline, or in-progress observations. For live esports events, outcome is likely already partially or fully determined but not yet reflected in market data. MARKET SIGNAL \u2014 RECENT VOLATILITY: YES side jumped +14.0pp at 11:17 UTC (2 min after start), suggesting market-makers detected early match signal favoring EVOS (possible early kill, map control, or team fighting advantage). This sharp move is more reliable than pre-match odds for a live match. CURRENT PRICING DISCORD: Market now shows YES=37%, NO=63%. This is WITHIN the sharp-move recovery range but still favors Dewa. The +14pp spike followed by stability suggests market is partially pricing in mid-game EVOS momentum but retaining significant NO probability. HISTORICAL BASE RATE \u2014 INDONESIAN REGIONAL LEAGUES: MPL Indonesia is a premier regional league but not S-tier globally. Team parity in regional BO3s is high (mean win rate ~50% for established teams). EVOS and Dewa United both appear in official Liquipedia records, indicating professional standing, but no comprehensive head-to-head record is provided beyond 1 Dewa vs NAVI result. INSUFFICIENT TEAM-SPECIFIC DATA: Briefing contains NO direct performance metrics for either EVOS or Dewa United in Season 17 (win-loss record, recent form, roster changes, patch compatibility). Without roster analysis or current season standings, canno