14pp move suggests early kill/map advantage was detected and priced. Current 37/63 may already reflect live game dynamics invisible to briefing. RESOLUTION FRAMEWORK CLEAR: No ambiguity in criteria \u2014 first to 2 wins, cancel/forfeit = 50-50. This reduces binary resolution risk. MARKET VERDICT: Prices appear rationally aligned with uncertainty given zero discriminating data. Neither side shows irrational hype or suppression. The market is indifferent because the briefing is silent on team quality.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL TIMING ISSUE: Event marked LIVE_OR_PAST with start 2026-04-17 11:15 UTC; data refresh time is 11:17 UTC (2 minutes after start). Match is either IN PROGRESS or potentially RESOLVED. Standard pre-game analysis is compromised. SHARP VOLATILITY SPIKE: +14pp YES movement at exactly 11:17 UTC (match start time) suggests real-time game information (early picks, bans, or first-game outcome in BO3) reached traders. This is NOT normal pre-match movement. INSUFFICIENT TEAM DATA: Briefing contains no head-to-head records, recent form, roster strength, or meta-fit analysis for either EVOS or Dewa United. Only one prior H2H reference (Dewa beat NAVI 2-0 on Apr 3) provides no direct competitive baseline. MARKET STRUCTURE: YES at 37-39% (1w EMA), NO at 61-63%. Market implies Dewa United favored by ~24pp absolute spread. Without team strength data, unclear if this reflects true competitive balance or market uncertainty. LIQUIDITY CONSTRAINTS: $1,416 total volume is low for a live esports match; wide bid-ask spread likely (YES/NO sum to 100% only due to vig). Sharp moves at match start indicate thin order book reacting to game events, not consensus skill assessment. RESOLUTION RISK: MPL Indonesia Season 17 format uses Double Round Robin + Hybrid Elimination. Regular season matches use standard BO3 ruleset. No forfeit/disqualification flags reported, so match should resolve to actual winner if completed. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides Philippines tournament history (likely copy-paste contamination from search results) but minimal Indonesia-specific competitive intel. EVOS and Dewa are Indonesia-tier teams; international track records (M7 4th place, MSC 2025 1st) may not transfer to domestic regular season. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINT: With live/past event status and no actionable pre-game data, confidence on BOTH sides must be low. Market price (37% YES) may reflect trader positioning rather than true skill differential. Unable to validate whether the 24pp spread is justified or mispriced. BEST ESTIMATE: Defer to market price as baseline (37% YES) given information vacuum, but flag extreme uncertainty. If match is already in progress or concluded, this probability may be stale within minutes.", "key_factor": "Event is marked LIVE_OR_PAST with start ~2 minutes ago; critical timing gap\u2014if match has already begun or concluded, market may be in resolution stage, making all pre-game analysis obsolete; sharp 14pp YES volatility at 11:17 UTC suggests either a match swing or information event, not normal pre-match trading."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE_OR_PAST status means the match began ~2 min ago (11:15 UTC). Markets are now trading on incomplete information with extreme volatility (\u00b114pp swings at 11:17 UTC). Any technical or roster disruption happening NOW would not yet be reflected in pregame prices. SHARP PRICE MOVE AT MATCH START: YES jumped +14pp and NO crashed -14pp at 11:17 UTC (2 min into event), suggesting either a Game 1 result OR critical in-game information (a player disconnect, substitution, or early stomp) just became visible to informed traders. This is NOT stable pricing. ABSENCE OF TEAM DATA: The briefing contains ZERO performance metrics, recent form, roster composition, or head-to-head history for either EVOS or Dewa United. The only prior match fact (Dewa vs NAVI 2-0 on Apr 3) does not directly inform EVOS vs Dewa. This asymmetric data gap means the 37% YES price is largely speculative rather than fundamentals-based. DEWA'S DOCUMENTARY WIN: Dewa defeated NAVI 2-0 on Apr 3, suggesting they are a competitive mid-tier team with at least one proven dominant matchup. EVOS has no recent documented result in the briefing\u2014creates uncertainty about whether they are favorites or underdogs relative to Dewa. MOBILE LEGENDS TECHNICAL RISK: Mobile Legends matches on mobile devices are acutely vulnerable to network lag, app crashes, and device battery/thermal issues, especially in best-of-3 formats where Game 2/3 momentum shifts are common. A substitute mid-laner or carry would fracture team coordination and shot-calling. BLACK SWAN: If EVOS's primary carry or mid-laner experiences a device failure or critical lag spike forcing a 5-10 minute pause or substitution in Game 2, Dewa (already priced as 63% likely) would be heavily favored to close the series 2-1. Conversely, if this happens to Dewa, EVOS (currently 37%) could rally to 2-1. CONFIDENCE CAPS: confidence_yes = 28 because the briefing provides no EVOS stats, roster, or recent performance to justify a strong YES conviction. confidence_no = 32 because Dewa's single 2-0 win is insufficient to build high conviction on Dewa alone. The +14pp swing at match start suggests Game 1 or early roster news is already priced in, but without visibility into that news, both sides remain low-confidence. CONSENSUS TRAP: Market pricing (37% YES / 63% NO) reflects either a documented Dewa skill advantage or a Game 1 EVOS loss/roster issue, but the briefing does not state which. If the 37% was set pregame on fundamentals, a Game 1 loss for EVOS is already baked in; if it was a pregame mispricing, the +14pp move corrected it. Either way, low confidence on both sides is warranted. DUAL PROBABILITY LOGIC: probability_score = 38 and probability_no_score = 62 are INDEPENDENT. They do NOT sum to 100 because the briefing data quality is asymmetric (some information favors Dewa, but EVOS fundamentals are entirely absent). The 24pp gap reflects honest uncertainty about whether the market has already priced in a Game 1 result or a structural team advantage.", "key_factor": "A key EVOS player (mid-laner or carry) suffers mid-series technical issue, lag spike, or device failure during Game 2 or 3, forcing a substitution or restart that disrupts their momentum and team coordination."}], "final_score": 0.37870678698040827, "no_score": 0.62530154110422, "edge": 0.3209090909090909, "no_edge": 0.06090909090909091, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 31.00% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0554065426114645, "The Bull": 0.9364005760934779, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0512387433906618, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0583860676111567, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0483394048022772, "The Contrarian": 1.073846959547265, "The Bear": 0.7763817059436962}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1966262", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: EVOS vs Dewa United Esports (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between EVOS and Dewa United Esports in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 7:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EVOS\" if EVOS win the match against Dewa United Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dewa United Esports\" if Dewa United Esports win the match against EVOS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T17:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T11:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.37, "volume_usd": 1416.0474209999995, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["24830139107031590406146670022576933461932961001779566584679765135165493602646", "83442930396818055793438689027341744628933455949930193623