any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T18:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T12:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.615, "volume_usd": 15.1282, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["103478517567152944222966887343967162613755382221568903802570863965455972093370", "114544578966993973136194243352693908003401400306358880951110315840343559913128"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (starts ~1.2 hours from data timestamp 2026-04-17 11:19 UTC; scheduled for 12:30 UTC). No match outcome has yet occurred. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if aimclub wins the BO3 match; NO if Drama eSports wins. Forfeits/walkovers/cancellations resolve 50-50 per criteria. DATA VACUUM: Briefing provides zero competitive intelligence on either team\u2014no recent results, form, roster strength, head-to-head record, HLTV rankings, or tournament placement. 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' sections both state 'Insufficient data to build [case].' MARKET PRICE AS PROXY: With no evaluable evidence, the current market price (YES 62% / NO 38%) reflects aggregate trader belief. This is the only signal available and matches the market consensus. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set to 25 (low) because the briefing provides no factual basis to differentiate team quality, form, or likelihood of either outcome. Confidence should not be high when the underlying data is absent. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: probability_score = 62 matches market price; probability_no_score = 38 matches market price. These reflect trader consensus in the absence of briefing-provided evidence, not independent analytical conviction. NO CONTRADICTIONS: Event timing (LIVE/IMMINENT) is internally coherent with data timestamp. No prior match results are cited as evidence for this encounter. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org is the primary source; fallback to credible consensus if HLTV silent >2 hours post-event. No evidence of this risk materializing. SHARP PRICE MOVES: History shows \u00b17\u201310.5pp swings in last 3 hours (Apr 17 08:00\u201311:00 UTC), suggesting recent information or sentiment shift, but no detail provided in briefing to explain driver.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no team form data, head-to-head history, roster information, recent results, or competitive context for either aimclub or Drama eSports; probability_score reflects current market price (62%) as default due to complete absence of evaluable evidence on either side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.3, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES (aimclub) is priced at 62%, indicating marginal market favoritism. With only ~1.2 hours to event start, this represents the most recent consensus from traders with access to team rosters, form, and recent bootcamp results not captured in this briefing. VOLATILITY SIGNAL: Sharp 7.0pp swings at 08:00 and 10:00 UTC suggest new information was absorbed (likely team roster confirmations, odds-setting adjustments, or late lineup changes). The +10.5pp spike favoring YES at 11:00 UTC is the most recent directional move, supporting the 62% final price. DATA GAP \u2014 CRITICAL: The briefing contains zero head-to-head match history, current team roster strength, recent form, player ratings, or map pool data for either aimclub or Drama eSports. Both 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' are marked 'Insufficient data.' This is a structural absence of the evidence needed to build conviction. TOURNAMENT TIER: Exort Series #25 is C-Tier online European CS2. Both teams are competing in a lower-mid tier event, suggesting relatively balanced competition. No evidence that aimclub is a superior squad or Drama eSports is in poor form. VOLUME AND PRICE STABILITY: Only $15 USD traded volume suggests low liquidity and shallow order book. The 62% YES price may reflect one or two informed trader actions rather than consensus. Conversely, the 7-day stability (\u00b11.0pp) suggests the market found an equilibrium once this match was scheduled. BULL CASE FOR YES (aimclub): Market pricing aimclub as slight favorite implies traders believe aimclub has superior recent form, roster depth, or map matchups versus Drama eSports. The 11:00 UTC +10.5pp spike for YES suggests late-arriving information (possibly a confirmed strong player availability for aimclub or Drama eSports roster issue) tipped confidence toward aimclub. If aimclub is a known qualifier or higher-seeded team in Exort's bracket, 62% is justified. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (Drama eSports): NO side pricing at 38% reflects either known poor form, a weaker roster, or unfavorable map/meta alignment. The briefing offers no counter-evidence (no recent wins, no standout player confirmations, no map strength). Silence is weakness for the underdog in a data-sparse market. TIMING RISK: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~80 minutes to start). At this stage, the market has absorbed most available public information. A reversal from 62% to below 50% would require a dramatic late-breaking event (roster disqualification, server failure, delayed start beyond the 7-day window). Such reversals are unlikely in the final hours. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (35) reflects only the market price and volatility direction\u2014not deep fundamental analysis. Confidence in NO is equally low (30) because the briefing provides no affirmative evidence for Drama eSports either. This is a market-price-driven call, not a scouted verdict. Both sides should have confidence <<60. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT: Emitting 62% YES and 38% NO (summing to 100%) reflects the current market price as the best available aggregation of trader beliefs given data scarcity. Deviating significantly from 62% would require hidden information not in this briefing. The slight favoritism toward aimclub (4pp above 50-50) is modest and defensible under uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Market consensus (62% YES pricing) reflects slight favoritism toward aimclub, but insufficient historical data prevents confident directional conviction."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides NO team-specific statistics, recent form data, head-to-head records, player lineups, map pool strengths, or tournament performance metrics for either team. Both the 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' sections are explicitly labeled 'Insufficient data to build [side] case.' MARKET PRICING DISCONNECT: YES is priced at 62% despite the briefing containing zero concrete evidence supporting aimclub's superiority. This suggests the market may be relying on out-of-briefing information (team rankings, recent matches, betting sharps) rather than data provided here. UNDERDOG'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: Drama eSports at 38% may be undervalued IF: (1) the team has form momentum not captured in this briefing, (2) aimclub has recent roster changes or internal issues, or (3) map selection favors Drama's playstyle. None of these can be verified or refuted with provided data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT IS MINIMAL: Exort Series #25 is described as C-Tier, online, featuring 28 teams. No information on whether aimclub or Drama are seeded higher, their prior performance in this tournament, or their competitive tier relative to each other. TEMPORAL URGENCY & ILLIQUIDITY: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.2 hours away). The briefing was published at 11:19 UTC; match starts at 12:30 UTC. Volume is only $15 USD\u2014extremely thin liquidity suggests this market has attracted minimal informed betting, and pricing may reflect casual opinion or default priors rather than expert consensus. SHARP MOVES IN FINAL HOURS: YES dropped -7.0pp at 10:00 UTC and surged +10.5pp at 11:00 UTC (NO mirrored -10.5pp), creating a 17.5pp swing. This volatility in a thin-volume market indicates uncertainty and potential overreaction to unverified information or betting flow, NOT market confidence in fundamental data. SYMMETRICAL IGNORANCE: Both teams lack briefing coverage. The probability_score of 38 (reflecting NO's underdog case) and probability_no_score of 38 (reflecting YES's case) both signal genuine coin-flip uncertainty. This is NOT a weakness\u2014it is an honest reflection of the data vacuum. BEARISH SIGNAL FOR aimclub: If aimclub were clearly superior (e.g., #15 globally vs. Drama at #200), the briefing would likely include ranking context or recent tournament seeding. Its absence suggests either parity or that aimclub's favorite status rests on stale data. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Drama eSports could win if: (1) they have a specialized map pool aimclub struggles on in BO3 format, (2) they have recent roster synergy or a hot-hand player, or (3) aimclub is fatigued from prior matches or roster instability (karrigan/FaZe context in briefing is unrelated but hints at possible regional roster churn). Without data, these remain plausible but unverifiable. CONFIDENCE FLOOR: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set at 25. This reflects that the briefing provides fewer than 2 concrete performance data points for EITHER side, violating the rule for defensible confidence. The market's 62/38 split appears to reflect external information, not the briefing itself.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of team-specific performance data, form metrics, or head-to-head history makes Drama eSports' underdog pricing potentially undervalued by market overconfidence in aimclub's unsubstantiated favorite status."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.2 hours to start). Price reversal is increasingly unlikely; market will resolve within hours. DATA QUALITY CRITICAL GAP: Briefing provides NO head-to-head match history, NO individual team form/ranking for aimclub or Drama eSports, NO roster comparisons, and NO recent tournament results. This is a hard constraint on confidence. TEAM IDENTIFICATION ISSUE: References to 'Lazer Cats', 'Falcons', 'FaZe', 'Vitality', 'karrigan' in the briefing do NOT clarify aimclub or Drama eSports identities, suggesting incomplete or misdirected data gathering. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Exort Series #25 is C-Tier (low-tier), online, European. This category historically shows high variance and unpredictability in outcomes compared to T1 events. Without team-level intel, base-rate prediction for a C-Tier BO3 is near 50%. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current YES 62% / NO 38% is NOT heavily skewed (e.g., not 75/25 or 85/15), suggesting either genuine uncertainty in the market or modest information asymmetry favoring aimclub. The 1-week stability (only \u00b11pp drift) indicates shallow liquidity ($15 USD volume) with low conviction. VOLATILITY & SHARP MOVES: Apr 17 10:00\u201311:00 UTC saw \u00b17\u201310.5pp swings\u2014consistent with low-volume, real-time betting noise rather than major fundamental news drops. No credible reason to treat these moves as skill-based. RESOLUTION RISK: Match may be delayed, cancelled, or forfeited beyond 7 days (resolve 50-50). However, Exort Series is live NOW; forfeit risk is low but non-zero for online EU tournaments. BASE RATE FOR BINARY SPORTS BETTING WITHOUT TEAM DATA: Historical prediction accuracy for esports matches where NO team/player data, recent form, or H2H exists is approximately 48\u201352% (i.e., near-random). Market price of 62/38 is a modest departure from base-rate indifference, likely reflecting real-time order flow or soft information not visible in this briefing. CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set to 28 because the briefing provides ZERO actionable team-level data. The 62/38 market price is acknowledged as the ensemble consensus, but WITHOUT independent corroboration, neither side can be assessed with >35% confidence. The dual-probability format (62 + 38 = 100) is appropriate here because the market has already aggregated available signals; we defer to market price in the absence of better data, but flag severe epistemic limitation.", "key_factor": "In C-Tier online CS2 tournaments with no head-to-head history or team form data available, base-rate prediction approaches ~50% for either outcome; market prices (62/38) reflect modest confidence in YES side, likely driven by minimal available information or real-time betting action rather than strong fundamentals."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no team form data, head-to-head history, recent results, roster strength, or any comparative information on aimclub vs Drama eSports. This is a black-box match. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Current market price (YES 62% / NO 38%) reflects a modest lean toward aimclub, but with only $15 USD volume, this is an illiquid, low-conviction market. The ~24pp spread between YES and NO suggests weak consensus. PRICE STABILITY: 7-day trend is stable (YES -1.0pp, NO +1.0pp), but intraday volatility is moderate (6.6-7.6pp/hr). Sharp reversals on Apr 17 (\u00b17\u201310.5pp moves) suggest reactive market microstructure rather than fundamental conviction. TEMPORAL PROBLEM: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.2 hours to start). At this stage, any rational repricing should have already occurred based on pre-match analysis. The current price likely reflects default assumptions rather than deep team evaluation. APATHY SIGNAL: No news, no team form commentary, no recent match context in briefing. Market appears to be pricing a default or prior reputation, not active sentiment about this specific matchup. Both sides lack narrative support. CONFIDENCE ASSIGNMENT: confidence_yes = 28 (low \u2014 no YES-side evidence presented), confidence_no = 26 (low \u2014 no NO-side evidence presented). Asymmetry is minimal because ignorance is symmetric. Probability_score remains at market price (62) because I have no grounds to contradict it, but confidence in both directions is weak. MISPRICING RISK: The market may be anchoring to team strength indicators not visible in this briefing (e.g., HLTV ranking fragments mentioned but not applied). Without that data, I cannot detect mispricings. Market price may be rational; I am simply blind to the reasoning. RESOLUTION RISK: BO3 format adds variance. Forfeiture/walkover clauses (resolve 50-50 if either team forfeits before match start) introduce ~2-3% tail risk, but do not currently appear priced in given the sharp YES/NO split.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "DOMAIN: Esports competitive gaming; CS2 tournament structure and team performance analysis. 20+ years experience equivalent = veteran esports analyst familiar with Exort Series tier classification, regional European circuits, and BO3 match dynamics. DATA SCARCITY CRITICAL: Briefing explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head results or detailed team form data are available.' This is a red flag for any analytical confidence. Neither team's current lineup, map pool strengths, individual player performance metrics, or recent tournament placement are documented. MARKET PRICE STABILITY: YES side has been stable at ~61% EMA over 7 days with only \u00b11pp drift\u2014suggesting a settled consensus, not recent information shock. The sharp 7pp and 10.5pp reversals in the final 3 hours (08:00\u201311:00 UTC Apr 17) likely reflect breaking news (roster changes, lineup confirmations, or conditional playoff updates) not captured in this briefing. BO3 CONTEXT: Best-of-3 format favors teams with deep map pool discipline, anti-stratting capability, and mental resilience. Without prior H2H data or current team morale/roster status, BO3 unpredictability is high\u2014single Bo1 upsets are common in C-Tier EU online events; BO3 reduces but does not eliminate variance. TOURNAMENT TIER: Exort Series #25 is C-Tier (low elite prestige). Teams competing here are typically mid-tier European squads or academy rosters. Seed/bracket position and recent online form (unknown in briefing) dominate outcomes in C-Tier more than in S-Tier events where top teams' raw skill dominates. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE: Low volume ($15 USD total), modest spread (YES 62\u00a2 vs NO 38\u00a2 mid-price ~50\u00a2), and high volatility (6.6\u20137.6pp/hr) indicate a thin, retail-driven market. The 62/38 split likely reflects general sentiment rather than sharp informed money. No professional esports betting syndicate signals are visible. LIVE/IMMINENT PENALTY: Event starts in ~1.2 hours. Any material reversal (e.g., one team's primary IGL disqualified, server outage, or forfeiture) is now extremely unlikely. Price action will compress rapidly once match begins; early live-play footage (first 5\u201310 rounds) will trigger repricing to ~$0.01/$0.99 depending on map results. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes/confidence_no asymmetry is appropriate here. Briefing provides NO substantive tactical, roster, or form data on EITHER side. The 62/38 split is market-inferred consensus, not SME-derived insight. Confidence on both sides should be LOW (~25\u201330), reflecting data vacuum. Assigning confidence_yes=28 and confidence_no=26 signals that the briefing simply does not support a strong conviction in either direction. RESOLUTION LOGIC: Forfeit/walkover/tie \u2192 50\u201350 resolution. Incompletes \u2192 team who wins advances. Standard esports rules. No ambiguity in resolution path, but match outcome itself is opaque pre-game. RECOMMENDATION: Adopt the market consensus (62/38) as a prior, but do not claim confidence beyond 30 on either side. Real-money traders have seen late-breaking roster/health/technical status info that this briefing lacks. Post-game, shares will rapidly converge to $0.01 or $0.99 depending on first-map result.", "key_factor": "In BO3 format with no head-to-head history or recent team form data available within 1.2 hours of match start, the market price (62/38) likely reflects pre-match betting consensus rather than substantive analytical edge; sharp volatility swings (+10.5pp in final hour) suggest real-money traders are calibrating on live information unavailable in this briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA VACUUM: The briefing contains almost no substantive competitive information\u2014no recent head-to-head history, no team form trajectories, no roster confirmation, no map pool analysis, no recent LAN/online results for either team. This is the opposite of a well-priced market; it is a market being priced on pure sentiment or market-maker default, not evidence. MARKET INSTABILITY SIGNAL: Sharp 7.0pp swings within hours (Apr 17 10:00 UTC and 11:00 UTC) with extremely low volume ($15 USD) suggest thin liquidity and minimal informed trading. The 62% YES price may reflect a default consensus (aimclub name recognition, alphabetic ordering, or a single large retail bet) rather than competitive assessment. BO3 FORMAT VULNERABILITY: Best-of-3 matches in online C-Tier CS2 tournaments are extremely sensitive to single-map upset potential and in-series adaptation. A team down 0\u20131 that reads the opponent's anti-strat and pivots mid-series can equalise and force a decider. Without map pool data, both teams could plausibly hold hidden strengths (e.g., Drama eSports' niche 1\u20132 map dominance). LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING & SUBSTITUTION RISK: With ~1.2 hours until start (12:30 UTC), roster changes, player illness, internet outages, or last-minute coaching pivots remain material. Online-only tournaments (no LAN venue) increase likelihood of connectivity/technical disruptions that favour the team with better backup infrastructure or player redundancy. MISSING CONTEXT ON DRAMA ESPORTS: No briefing data on Drama eSports' recent form, regional ranking, or competitive pedigree. This asymmetry is itself a black swan flag: if Drama is a historically strong regional team (e.g., a rebranded or rising squad), the 38% NO price may be an underdog value trap. EXORT SERIES CONTEXT: C-Tier tournament with 28 teams; main-stage placement may not reflect true ELO difference between aimclub and Drama. Teams competing in secondary European online circuits often have volatile win rates and inconsistent roster stability. ABSENCE OF HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No prior match results between these teams in the briefing. Direct history would normally anchor pricing; its absence leaves the 62% YES as a hollow consensus. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: confidence_yes and confidence_no both set to 28 and 26 respectively\u2014well below 50\u2014because the briefing provides zero actionable evidence on either side. The probability_score (58) and probability_no_score (45) reflect retention of the market price as a weak prior, not an informed conviction. The 13-point gap (58 + 45 = 103) captures the unresolved mass of uncertainty and the possibility of a decisive black swan (roster substitution, map pool mismatch, or online technical failure). CONTRARIAN EDGE: The most likely flip scenario is a last-minute roster change (forced or tactical) that rebalances the meta matchup, combined with Drama eSports' map pool being more versatile than aimclub's in this specific series format. The 62% YES price leaves enough room for a 40\u201345% NO outcome if either team executes an anti-meta strategy or aimclub is caught unprepared.", "key_factor": "A player stand-in or last-minute roster substitution (illness, connectivity failure, or coach-imposed tactical swap) on either team immediately before the series, combined with the BO3 format favoring the team with superior map pool adaptability or anti-stratting preparation."}], "final_score": 0.5902577108127289, "no_score": 0.4110461574397572, "edge": 0.07590909090909093, "no_edge": 0.3059090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 28.14% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0554065426114645, "The Bull": 0.9364005760934779, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0512387433906618, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0583860676111567, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0483394048022772, "The Contrarian": 1.073846959547265, "The Bear": 0.7763817059436962}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2003473", "question": "Counter-Strike: aimclub vs Drama eSports (BO3) - Exort Series Main Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 2 match between aimclub and Drama eSports in the Exort Series Main Stage, initially scheduled for April 17 at 8:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"aimclub\" if aimclub win the match against Drama eSports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Drama eSports\" if Drama eSports win the match against aimclub.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T18:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T12:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.615, "volume_usd": 15.1282, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["103478517567152944222966887343967162613755382221568903802570863965455972093370", "114544578966993973136194243352693908003401400306358880951110315840343559913128"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "ke