is unlikely unless late roster/injury news breaks. Shares will likely move toward $0.01/$0.99 only AFTER outcome becomes clear during/after the match. CONCLUSION: Defer to market price (64% YES) due to absence of historical base rate and conflicting early-season signals. Low confidence on both sides reflects genuine data scarcity for TCL regional play.", "key_factor": "LoL BO3 matches in early-season regional leagues: no reliable historical base rate available; market pricing suggests ~64% implied confidence in Dark Passage"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.64, "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "IMMINENT EVENT (2.5 hours to start): Very limited time for new information to drive major repricing. Market has stabilized around 64% YES over past 7 days with only \u00b10.5pp 24h drift. DATA VACUUM on both sides: Briefing contains fragmentary schedule data (dates, team names) but ZERO meaningful competitive intelligence \u2014 no recent form, no head-to-head records, no player/roster info, no meta context, no coach/manager analysis. CONFLICTING SIGNALS on YES side: 'BoostGate started season with 0-2 loss on Apr 9' suggests weakness, BUT this is Week 1 data (early season volatility is high). Dark Passage's prior result shown as '0-2 Apr 10' (same loss) \u2014 symmetric weakness, not clear advantage for YES. NO CLEAR DOMINANCE NARRATIVE: Both teams appear to have similar early results (0-2 losses in Week 1). The briefing's 'Dark Passage has scheduled matches but limited prior results shown' is euphemism for 'we have no data to evaluate Dark Passage's true strength.' MARKET PRICE REFLECTS IGNORANCE: 64-36 split is modest (not extreme crowd euphoria or panic). Weighted average stable for 7 days suggests price is anchored to pre-match uncertainty, not driven by new signal. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market shows RATIONAL APATHY \u2014 neither side is generating strong emotional buy pressure. Volume is only $3.3K USD, indicating low engagement. The 64% YES reflects mild consensus, not conviction. SHARP MOVES REVEAL NOISE: Apr 14 saw \u00b110pp swings (matched whipsaw), then reverted. No directional persistence, suggesting order-flow noise rather than fundamental repricing from new team data. CONFIDENCE PENALTY for both sides: Lack of meaningful competitive data (roster form, draft tendencies, recent scrim results, meta alignment) means confidence must be low on both YES and NO. The 64-36 market price is a reasonable 'default weak lean' in a data vacuum, but neither side is well-supported. IMMINENT timing + data void = HIGH REVERSAL RISK: Any shock (team roster announcement, injury, technical forfeit threat) could flip this 2.5 hours before match. Low confidence reflects this tail risk. RESOLUTION RULE VULNERABILITY: Match could end 50-50 (forfeit, disqualification, tie, or >7-day delay). No briefing data on team health, discipline record, or league enforcement history.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.64, "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.36, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.22, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.5 hours to start). Any reversal requiring significant new information (injury, roster swap, technical issue) is extremely unlikely at this point. Market pricing at 64/36 is likely near-final. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: The briefing provides a fragmented Liquipedia table showing only two concrete results: BoostGate 0-2 loss on Apr 9 (vs unknown opponent) and Dark Passage 0-2 loss on Apr 10 (vs unknown opponent). Both teams started with losses, providing NO predictive signal for head-to-head matchup. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: Zero prior Dark Passage vs BoostGate matchup data in briefing. TCL Spring is early (Week 1-3 range), so limited sample sizes across the league. CHAMPION/META UNCERTAINTY: Briefing shows champion bans/picks from one match (Game 1-2) but does not attribute them to either team in this matchup or provide coaching analysis. LoL esports outcomes are highly sensitive to meta adaptation, pick/ban phase execution, and coaching adjustments\u2014all opaque in this briefing. MARKET PRICE STABILITY: YES side EMA 64% with -4.0pp 7-day change = STABLE trend. Sharp moves on Apr 14 (\u00b110.0pp) suggest some intraday volatility but no directional collapse; current 64% likely reflects genuine consensus among informed traders, not mispricing. CONFIDENCE PENALTY (YES SIDE): Insufficient team form, no direct matchup history, opaque meta-read \u2192 confidence_yes = 28 (low). Briefing data simply does not support high conviction. CONFIDENCE PENALTY (NO SIDE): Mirror gap\u2014no evidence favoring BoostGate dominance either \u2192 confidence_no = 22 (very low). This is genuine ignorance, not symmetric uncertainty. RESOLUTION RISK: Market includes 50-50 forfeiture/disqualification clause. Given imminent start and low volume ($3,330), execution risk is minimal but non-zero. RECOMMENDATION: Defer to market price (64%) as best available estimate given data poverty. Do not artificially flatten to 50 due to ignorance; the slight YES lean likely reflects subtle intel (team morale, scrim performance, roster chemistry) not visible in Liquipedia tables.", "key_factor": "Early-season TCL matches lack sufficient individual team performance data, champion pool evolution, and meta-read depth to override market pricing; the 0-2 loss cited for BoostGate is from Apr 9 (prior match) and does not directly predict this specific BO3 given the rapid patch/meta shifts in Spring competition."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "BRIEFING OPACITY: The schedule table is severely fragmented\u2014only two prior results visible (BoostGate 0-2 Apr 9, Dark Passage 0-2 Apr 10). Aggregate season stats, win-loss records, and head-to-head history are completely absent. Market confidence (64% YES) is built on almost no data. EARLY-SEASON VOLATILITY: Both teams are 0-2 in their first visible games (Apr 9-10). At this stage in a round-robin, form is highly unstable; a single roster change, meta-read advantage, or psychological momentum shift (e.g., 'we must win or we're out') can swing a BO3 dramatically. BOOSTGATE'S DESPERATION EDGE: A 0-2 start in Week 1-2 is salvageable but creates acute pressure to win Apr 17. Teams in must-win situations often play with higher aggression and pick comfort/unconventional champs, which can exploit overconfident favorites. SILENCE ON ROSTER & COACHING: The briefing contains zero mention of player injuries, roster moves, recent scrims, coaching philosophy, or internal team dynamics. In a 2.5-hour window, a late-season roster swap or injury could occur and not be reflected in public data. META UNKNOWN: No champion pick/ban patterns, role strengths, or patch information provided. If a recent patch (not detailed) favors BoostGate's playstyle or Dark Passage's weakness, the probability shifts dramatically. PSYCHOLOGICAL ASYMMETRY: Dark Passage (also 0-2 Apr 10) may be complacent or demoralized if they lost to perceived weaker opponents. BoostGate, facing elimination-level pressure, may exhibit heightened focus and cohesion. MARKET PRICE DRIFT: YES dropped 4.0pp over 7 days and shows one -10pp spike (Apr 14 13:00 UTC), suggesting informed traders may have detected negative Dark Passage signals not visible in this briefing (roster chatter, scrim results, coaching change). IMMINENT TIMING RISK: With ~2.5 hours to match start, any roster/injury news will not propagate to all markets in real time. Early traders with TCL insider knowledge may have already shifted odds before broader awareness. CONFIDENCE CAPS: Both YES and NO confidences are deliberately low (32 & 28) because the briefing provides almost no actionable evidence. The 64/36 split reflects market consensus, but that consensus rests on minimal data and could evaporate if a single black-swan personnel event occurs pre-match. CONSERVATIVE ADJUSTMENT: Holding YES at 58 (vs market 64) to reflect underdog pressure and unknown roster/meta risks. NO at 45 (vs market 36) to acknowledge BoostGate's desperation-fueled upside. Gap of 13pp captures the irreducible uncertainty and plausible roster-swap flip.", "key_factor": "Dark Passage's jungler or mid-laner is benched or substituted at last minute due to illness/personal emergency, forcing a rookie or academy stand-in into a BO3 against a team now desperate to avoid 0-3 start, inverting the assumed form trajectory."}], "final_score": 0.6076697593307103, "no_score": 0.4033680276827816, "edge": 0.0459090909090909, "no_edge": 0.33590909090909093, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 34.14% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0554065426114645, "The Bull": 0.9364005760934779, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0512387433906618, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0583860676111567, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0483394048022772, "The Contrarian": 1.073846959547265, "The Bear": 0.7763817059436962}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1967164", "question": "LoL: Dark Passage vs BoostGate Esports (BO3) - TCL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Dark Passage and BoostGate Esports in the TCL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 10:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dark Passage\" if Dark Passage win the match against BoostGate Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BoostGate Esports\" if BoostGate Esports win the match against Dark Passage.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T20:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T14:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.645, "volume_usd": 3329.8189410000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["3120784518493380054227769227611993877842877965887776528421560404196314180645", "110809183361117863620901722012546511556040896849871447302784889802066402719825"], "sports_market_ty