{"run_id": "62da0b88-ef17-4d2e-914f-535780760fca", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T14:51:28.913910+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1994987", "question": "Counter-Strike: Spirit vs MOUZ (BO3) - IEM Rio Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 1 match between Spirit and MOUZ in the IEM Rio Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Spirit\" if Spirit win the match against MOUZ.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MOUZ\" if MOUZ win the match against Spirit.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 702880.6319660026, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["1117374806443241211379847654593357736935764919958198603393598217237782739237", "46826523089818328270342608428642509128149631910919156617939811155871305704067"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE CONFIRMED: Briefing data explicitly states EVENT TIMING = LIVE/IMMINENT and match is SCHEDULED (not completed). Past match history (2026-02-08 onwards) are prior encounters, not this event's outcome. Head-to-head record shows Spirit 5W-2L against MOUZ in recent history, providing form context only. BOOKMAKER ODDS EVIDENCE: Spirit listed at 1.98 odds (implicit ~50% probability), positioned as slight favorite. Current market YES price 60% reflects modest Spirit lean. Bookmaker confidence aligns directionally with market, though not identical. RECENT FORM PARITY: Both teams identical on 10-match record (6W-4L). Spirit won 3/5 last matches; MOUZ on 6-map winning streak. Slight edge to MOUZ on trend momentum, offset by Spirit's bookmaker favoritism. RANKING CONTRADICTION: MOUZ ranked #8 (higher) vs Spirit #9 (lower), yet Spirit is bookmaker favorite. This suggests bookmaker model weights recent form/H2H more heavily than static rankings. Head-to-head heavily favors Spirit (5W vs 2W in recent encounters), which explains bookmaker lean. MAP-SPECIFIC ADVANTAGES: Spirit strong on Overpass (71% LAN win rate) and Ancient (62%). MOUZ shows 100% Overpass win rate in recent 6-game sample (contradicts Spirit's 71% but smaller sample size). MOUZ high confidence on Anubis (69% first-ban rate indicates strategic priority). In BO3, map selection/veto is critical; neither team shows dominant advantage across all three likely maps. PLAYER QUALITY: donk and m0NESY among event's highest fantasy scorers, suggesting elite individual talent. MOUZ lacks named high-tier individual standouts in briefing. Talent concentration favors Spirit. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES side up +9.5pp over 7 days, +1.0pp in 24h (stable). Sharp move Apr 16 03:00 UTC +5.0pp suggests informed money moved to Spirit. Declining volatility in 24h suggests consensus is forming. Market confidence in Spirit increasing. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous\u2014standard match win condition. No forfeit/walkover/tie risk explicitly highlighted. Team name matching is clear (Spirit vs MOUZ, both internationally recognized). Resolution source (HLTV) is standard for CS events. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 72 reflects strong bookmaker alignment, H2H record, and player talent evidence. confidence_no = 58 reflects MOUZ's ranking, form streak, and map-specific strengths, but these are weaker signals than Spirit's bookmaker odds and H2H dominance. Data quality on both sides is adequate; no major information gaps. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 62% for Spirit reflects YES favorite position (~1.98 odds \u2248 50% + bookmaker margin/information premium), reinforced by H2H record (5W-2L \u2248 71% historical win rate, but regression to mean in single match expected). NO side (38%) captures MOUZ upside from ranking, form streak, and map variance. Sum = 100 (not double-counting; probabilities are mutually exclusive). LIVE/IMMINENT CAVEAT: With <8 minutes to start, any reversal in odds would signal late information (betting line movements, player/coach statements, illness, equipment issues). Current market structure (YES 60%, NO 40%) reflects pre-match consensus. Once match begins, outcome trajectory will become visible; market will reprice toward $0.01/$0.99 by mid-match or end-of-match regardless of HLTV publication delay.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~8 minutes from briefing timestamp); outcome may already be partially or fully determined; market prices will converge to $0.01/$0.99 once result becomes clear regardless of official HLTV publication timing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.34, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (YES = Spirit) STRENGTHS: \u2014 Bookmaker favorite at 1.98 odds, reflecting professional sportsbook confidence; market has already priced in deep analytical work. \u2014 Decisive head-to-head advantage: 5-0 recent record vs MOUZ (per briefing), a near-complete psychological/confidence edge in direct matchups. \u2014 Elite individual performers: donk and m0NESY ranked among event's highest fantasy scorers, indicating Star Power and consistency. \u2014 Map-specific dominance on two likely deciders: Overpass (71% LAN win rate), Ancient (62% LAN win rate); on a BO3, controlling 2 of 3 maps is decisive. \u2014 Recent form positive: won 3 of last 5 matches; momentum entering playoffs. UNDERDOG SIDE (NO = MOUZ) WEAKNESSES: \u2014 Ranking advantage (#8 vs #9) is marginal and does not override head-to-head record; MOUZ has lost 5 straight direct matchups to Spirit. \u2014 Form metrics are symmetric with Spirit (both 6W-4L in last 10), contradicting the claim of 'better form'; no edge here. \u2014 6-map winning streak is respectable but lacks match-level evidence; individual map streaks do not translate reliably to BO3 outcomes against superior opponents. \u2014 Anubis map confidence (69% first-ban rate) suggests caution rather than dominance; teams ban what they fear or cannot beat. \u2014 Overpass claim (100% win rate in 6 games) is recent sample noise; Spirit's 71% LAN rate over larger samples is more predictive. \u2014 No evidence of key roster changes, coaching upgrades, or strategic innovations to overcome 0-5 h2h deficit. MARKET PRICING ANALYSIS: \u2014 YES has risen +9.5pp over 7 days, reflecting accumulating confidence in Spirit; sharp money moved +5pp on Apr 16 03:00 UTC, suggesting informed flow. \u2014 NO has fallen -9.5pp symmetrically; contrarian positions are being unwound. \u2014 Volume is substantial ($702,881), indicating efficient price discovery; the 60-40 split is not thin. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: \u2014 Base: bookmaker odds (1.98 Spirit) imply ~50% true probability (inverse odds), but market at 60% YES reflects additional confidence from h2h and form data. \u2014 Head-to-head 5-0 is the strongest signal; overweighting this edge (which was earned over 2+ years and multiple tournament contexts) justifies moving above 60%. \u2014 Map pool control (Overpass + Ancient) gives Spirit two win paths; MOUZ must win the decider on a map (likely Anubis) where they lack the same evidence of dominance. \u2014 Probability score of 64 reflects: ~60% base from market, +4-5pp for h2h dominance, with confidence held at 72% due to LIVE/IMMINENT timing (outcome will be determined in ~8 minutes; reversal requires extraordinary in-game collapse from Spirit). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: \u2014 confidence_yes = 72: Strong evidence for Spirit (bookmaker, h2h, individual talent, map advantage). Data is recent and specific. \u2014 confidence_no = 48: MOUZ case relies on ranking (marginal), streak narrative (unreliable), and sample-limited map stats. Lack of h2h success, no clear path to dismantling 0-5 record. Lower confidence reflects thinness of contrarian data. LIVE/IMMINENT RISK ADJUSTMENT: \u2014 Event starts in ~8 minutes; very limited time for external events (roster issues, venue delays) to alter outcome. \u2014 Confidence scores remain solid because fundamental advantage (h2h, form, talent, maps) is already crystallized. \u2014 If Spirit wins map 1 (likely on Overpass), market will likely trade YES to ~90+ before official resolution; if MOUZ wins map 1, contrarian confidence spikes and spread narrows. Current 60-40 pricing is reasonable given zero information about current match state.", "key_factor": "Spirit's bookmaker-derived odds advantage (1.98), superior head-to-head record (5-0 in recent encounters), and elite individual talent (donk, m0NESY) on their strongest map pool."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "MARKET BACKDROP: YES (Spirit) priced at 60%, NO (MOUZ) at 40%. YES side gained +9.5pp over 7 days with a sharp +5pp move on Apr 16 03:00 UTC\u2014suggests confidence in Spirit spiked late, but briefing timing (8 minutes to match start) leaves minimal data refresh window for crucial last-hour shifts. MOUZ FORM SIGNAL: Both teams show identical 6W-4L records over last 10 matches, but MOUZ explicitly described as on a '6-map winning streak' with no corresponding streak cited for Spirit. This temporal recency advantage matters in BO3 momentum contests. RANKING PARADOX: MOUZ ranked #8 globally vs Spirit #9, yet market prices Spirit 60% favorite. Briefing states 'MOUZ ranked slightly higher (#8 vs #9)'\u2014this structural ranking advantage is under-weighted by the 20pp YES bias. Ranking persists across seasons; it reflects sustained performance quality. OVERPASS CONTRADICTION: Spirit cited as favored on Overpass (71% LAN win rate), but MOUZ noted with '100% win rate on Overpass in recent samples (6 games played).' If MOUZ's recent Overpass dominance is true, Spirit's historical 71% LAN stat is stale. Recent > historical in form-based markets. This is a critical vulnerability in Spirit's narrative. ANUBIS MAP CONTROL: MOUZ 69% first-ban rate on Anubis signals genuine map confidence and strategic respect from opponents. First-ban rates indicate opponent fear, not coincidence. Spirit's map pool advantages (Overpass, Ancient) face a team that may either dominate Anubis or force Spirit to ban it, ceding map selection advantage. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT (NOT THIS MATCH): Prior record shows Spirit 5 wins in recent encounters, but also reveals MOUZ took matches in June 2025, March 2025 (2-1), and March 2025 (2-1 again). The '5-0 recent' claim requires clarification: if it's the last 5, the data supports Spirit; but the H2H spread shows MOUZ capable of upsets in Playoffs format (3 Playoff wins for MOUZ visible in the record). BOOKMAKER ODDS CAVEAT: 1.98 odds for Spirit (approx 50% implied) vs market's 60% YES suggests either: (a) betting market is sharper/slower than derivatives, (b) syndicate traders are buying YES on recency bias from Apr 16 spike, or (c) late flow into YES is not information-efficient. Bookmaker parity at ~50% contradicts market 60% confidence. BREVITY OF EVENT WINDOW: LIVE/IMMINENT status (8 minutes to start) means no new match data can be processed. All conviction is baked into the Apr 16 spike. Large sharp moves near event start often reverse when actual play begins; they reflect sentiment/flow, not resolution probability. This structural factor should lower confidence on both sides. MOUZ UNDERVALUATION: At 40% implied probability despite #8 ranking, 6-map winning streak, and 100% recent Overpass record, MOUZ appears to be priced as a 'Spirit favorite' team by reflexive betting rather than matchup-adjusted modeling. Briefing data supports higher MOUZ odds than market reflects. CASE AGAINST SPIRIT: donk's $225k buy-in and m0NESY's fantasy ranking are *achievements*, not predictors. Individual player cost does not drive match outcomes in BO3s; teamplay, map veto, and in-game adaptation do. Spirit's recent form (3 of last 5) is not dominant enough to overcome MOUZ's ranking, current streak, and map-specific strength on Overpass. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong briefing data supports MOUZ upset (ranking, streak, map stats); weak briefing data on Spirit's current form (3 of 5 is modest; no mentioned 'winning streak' despite market pricing). Confidence_yes set to 45 (briefing gaps on Spirit's momentum); confidence_no set to 62 (concrete data on MOUZ advantages and Spirit vulnerabilities). PROBABILITY ALLOCATION: probability_score = 38 reflects MOUZ's true competitive edge overlooked by 60% market price. probability_no_score = 55 (not mechanical 62) reflects that Spirit retains intangible advantages (historical H2H, bookmaker respect at 1.98) not fully captured in form/ranking/map data. Sum = 93, leaving ignorance mass for live-play unknowns.", "key_factor": "MOUZ's current 6-map winning streak and superior ranking (#8 vs #9) combined with demonstrated 100% Overpass win rate in recent play contradicts Spirit's map pool advantages and suggests meta-shift momentum favoring the underdog."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "SPIRIT CASE (YES = 62%): Bookmaker favorite at 1.98 odds translates to ~50% implied probability baseline, but Spirit's concrete advantages push higher: (1) dominant recent H2H (5-0 in last 9 encounters per briefing), (2) elite individual talent (donk, m0NESY top fantasy scorers), (3) strong map pool (71% Overpass, 62% Ancient on LAN), (4) 3 of last 5 wins suggests upward trajectory. MOUZ CASE (NO = 56%): MOUZ's counter-arguments are substantive and non-negligible: (1) higher ranking (#8 vs #9) is a weak but real signal, (2) 6-map winning streak matches Spirit's recent form (both 6W-4L in last 10), (3) 100% Overpass sample (6 games) outperforms Spirit's 71% claim, (4) 69% Anubis first-ban rate suggests strong map-specific preparation. These do not flip the market, but they prevent Spirit from being a heavy favorite. HEAD-TO-HEAD INTERPRETATION: 5-0 H2H dominance is strong, but briefing shows mixed scorelines across formats (2-0 wins, 1-2 losses, 0-2/0-3 losses). This is NOT a clean 5-0 sweep; scoreline variance suggests map-dependent matchups. High-confidence H2H requires more uniform results (e.g., Spirit winning all BO3s decisively). FORM PARITY: Both teams are 6W-4L in last 10. Market pricing at 60/40 reflects Spirit's bookmaker edge + H2H dominance, but MOUZ's ranking inversion (#8 vs #9) and recent consistency reduce confidence in a wide Spirit gap. A 62/56 split (not summing to 100) reflects genuine uncertainty\u2014neither side has overwhelming evidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 68 (Spirit's bookmaker odds, H2H record, and elite player talent provide clear positive signals). confidence_no = 52 (MOUZ's counter-evidence is real but narrower; limited briefing depth on team cohesion, coach changes, or recent roster adjustments that might explain ranking vs. form mismatch). MAP POOL UNCERTAINTY: Spirit's 71% Overpass vs. MOUZ's 100% sample (n=6, smaller) creates conflicting signals. Sample-size issues and LAN vs. online distinctions are not clarified in briefing. This adds noise to both sides. TIMING NOTE (LIVE/IMMINENT): Event is ~8 minutes from start. No sharp news reversals noted in last 24 hours (YES +1.0pp, NO -1.0pp = flat). Market has already incorporated visible information. Probability estimate reflects pre-game state; outcome will rapidly resolve to ~$0.01/$0.99 once match begins.", "key_factor": "In professional Counter-Strike BO3 playoffs between top-10 ranked teams, the higher-seeded or bookmaker-favored team wins approximately 58-65% of the time. Head-to-head record strength (5-0 or similar dominance) historically predicts ~70% win probability, but recent form parity and map-specific vulnerabilities reduce this. MOUZ's higher ranking (#8 vs #9) and recent 6-map streak introduce meaningful uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SENTIMENT ANALYSIS: Market is pricing Spirit at 60% YES, reflecting bookmaker consensus (1.98 odds \u2248 50.5% implied, but adjusted upward by recent form). No crowd panic or irrational exuberance detected. YES SIDE MOMENTUM: 7-day trend +9.5pp on YES (rising), sharp move Apr 16 +5.0pp suggests informed money inbound on Spirit. This aligns with their recent 3-of-5 wins and bookmaker preference. NO SIDE WEAKNESS: 7-day trend -9.5pp on NO (falling), sharp move Apr 16 -5.5pp. Market is discounting MOUZ despite #8 ranking and 6-map streak. Suggests crowd is not fully confident in their form narrative. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINATION: Spirit 5-0 in recent H2H encounters (Feb 2026 2-0, Dec 2025, Aug 2025, Jul 2025, Jun 2025 Loss, Mar 2025 Loss, Mar 2025 Loss, Dec 2024). Historical record strongly favors Spirit\u2014this is major signaling that market is correctly pricing. MAP POOL EDGE: Spirit favored on Overpass (71% LAN) and Ancient (62% LAN). MOUZ shows 100% Overpass win rate in small sample (6 games), but this is likely recency noise vs. Spirit's larger historical dataset. Map data supports YES slightly. PLAYER CALIBER: donk ($225k transfer) and m0NESY among highest fantasy scorers\u2014indicates top-tier individual skill on YES side. MOUZ roster not highlighted similarly in briefing. RANKINGS PARADOX: MOUZ ranked #8 vs Spirit #9 creates mild friction\u2014one data point supporting NO. However, rankings lag recent form; Spirit's H2H and recent wins are more current signals. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: NO side shows higher 24-hr volatility (0.6pp/hr vs 0.4pp/hr on YES). Suggests NO traders are uncertain or nervous; YES holders more committed. Emotional instability on the underdog side typical before tight matches. APATHY CHECK: Briefing contains confusing/irrelevant noise (sugar references, coaching anecdotes, Falcons/Vitality tangents). Market price is NOT reacting to this noise\u2014correctly treating it as non-signal. This is rational behavior. LIVE/IMMINENT DISCOUNT: Event starts in ~8 minutes. Market price of 60% YES is near bookmaker consensus. No obvious late-arriving shock (injury, roster change, tech issue reported). Price has stabilized overnight; no panic reversal expected this late. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $702.8k in volume suggests healthy two-sided participation. Not a thin/illiquid market where price could be wildly off. Crowd has spoken; consensus is moderately confident in Spirit. RECENCY BIAS CHECK: Spirit's 3-of-5 form is recent (within last 10 matches) and H2H is very fresh (Feb 2026 2-0 dominant). Market may be slightly overweighting recent momentum, but not irrationally so given LAN quality. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Market price of 60% YES appears FAIRLY RATIONAL and lightly favoring Spirit. Probability estimate raised to 62% to reflect bookmaker edge, H2H dominance, and map pool advantage. NO side at 38% is not undervalued enough to be a contrarian play\u2014MOUZ has legitimate upset odds but market is appropriately skeptical given recent history.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "DOMAIN CONTEXT: Counter-Strike BO3 playoffs hinge on three variables: (1) player form/rating (tracked via HLTV statistics), (2) map pool matchups (specific team win rates on Overpass, Ancient, Anubis), and (3) LAN versus online differential. This briefing provides granular data on all three. SPIRIT CASE (YES): Bookmaker consensus at 1.98 odds is a strong signal in regulated betting markets; Spirit favored by ~66% implied probability. Spirit won 3/5 recent matches and head-to-head record is 5-0 in recent encounters (decisive evidence of recent dominance). donk and m0NESY are top fantasy scorers at the event, suggesting elite individual performance. Spirit's 71% Overpass LAN win rate is strong. MOUZ CASE (NO): Despite lower seed (#8 vs #9), MOUZ shows superior form ranking and a 6-map winning streak entering playoffs. Critically, MOUZ posted 100% win rate on Overpass (6/6 games) in recent samples\u2014this contradicts or meets Spirit's 71% and suggests MOUZ may have refined their Overpass execution post-briefing data collection. Anubis first-ban rate of 69% indicates high map confidence (willingness to ban suggests either strength or fear, but paired with 6-map streak suggests confidence). BO3 FORMAT RISK: In best-of-three, one team's map veto strategy and their ability to win a single 'upset' map critically shifts probability. MOUZ's equal or superior performance on key veto targets (Overpass especially) means the series is tighter than raw ranking delta suggests. Spirit must win map bans decisively to avoid a 50-50 third map. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECORD CAVEAT: Spirit's 5-0 record is strong but relies on older data (last match Feb 2026, some matches from 2025). In fast-evolving esports, 2-3 month gaps allow meta shifts, roster practice intensity changes, and coaching adjustments (note: briefing mentions 'German coach brought in' for struggling team\u2014context unclear but signals roster volatility in region). MARKET PRICE ACTION: YES side has risen +9.5pp over 7 days and +1.0pp in 24hr, reaching 60% current. Sharp moves on Apr 16 (+5.0pp YES, -5.5pp NO) suggest informed traders (likely esports pros or coaches) shifted confidence toward Spirit in final hours. This is a modest but real signal favoring YES. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: Briefing is strong on Spirit's individual players (donk, m0NESY named) and historical H2H, but MOUZ strengths are inferred from ranking, form, and map stats rather than named player excellence. This asymmetry inflates confidence_yes but warrants lower confidence_no (missing depth on MOUZ individual form). NOISE IN BRIEFING: Several sentences are incoherent or off-topic (e.g., 'graviti heavy favourite,' 'malbs is NA so he's probably taking his +2kg of sugar,' '8 kg of sugar') and reference unrelated tournaments (Vitality, Falcons, FaZe, Cologne). These are data artifacts and ignored. RESOLUTION TIMING: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (8 minutes to start at 15:00 UTC 2026-04-17). At this stage, no reversal of bookmaker consensus is likely without extraordinary information (illness, technical forfeiture). Market price of 60% YES is likely to hold and convert cleanly to $0.99 or $0.01 within 30-60 minutes of match conclusion. PROBABILITY SYNTHESIS: Bookmaker 1.98 odds (~66% YES) slightly overstates Spirit's edge if MOUZ's Overpass 100% is reproducible on LAN under playoff pressure. Market-derived 60% is more conservative and reasonable. My estimate of 62% YES reflects modest confidence that Spirit's H2H + individual player strength outweighs MOUZ's map-specific parity and form rank, but the margin is not overwhelming in BO3 format. CONFIDENCE SPLIT RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 72 because bookmaker consensus, H2H record, and player rating data all align coherently on Spirit. confidence_no = 55 because MOUZ's case rests on form rank, winning streak, and map stats\u2014valuable but shallower than Spirit's individual player + H2H profile. This asymmetry is appropriate.", "key_factor": "Spirit's 5-0 recent head-to-head advantage and bookmaker consensus (1.98 odds) are weighted heavily, but MOUZ's #8 ranking, 6-map streak, and demonstrated 100% Overpass performance (6/6) on LAN suggest the briefing's form metrics may undervalue MOUZ's current ceiling in a BO3 format where map selection discipline is critical."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.52, "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "LIVE/IMMINENT timing (8 minutes to start) means any reversal must stem from factors already in-play, not new news \u2014 confidence ceilings are inherently low for both sides. Market has moved +9.5pp toward YES over 7 days, suggesting professional/sharp money is backing Spirit despite identical recent form (6W-4L both teams) \u2014 this is a strong signal but not dispositive. Head-to-head record (5-0 Spirit) appears overwhelming BUT three of those five encounters are from 2025 or early 2026, and meta/roster shifts are common in Counter-Strike; old H2H data decays fast. MOUZ ranked #8 (vs Spirit #9) and on a 6-map winning streak, yet briefing is silent on HOW those wins were constructed \u2014 if MOUZ has solved a specific map pool angle (e.g., Anubis anti-default or Overpass B-site execute), Spirit's 71% Overpass win rate becomes vulnerable. donk and m0NESY are among highest fantasy scorers, but individual firepower does not guarantee team cohesion; Spirit's recent form (3 of last 5 wins) suggests inconsistency that a hungry MOUZ team on a streak could exploit. Briefing contains substantial noise (references to Falcons, Vitality, FaZe, karrigan, unrelated personnel) \u2014 signal-to-noise ratio is poor, indicating either data contamination or that key match-specific intel (last-minute roster changes, coach adjustments, anti-prep strats) is missing. MOUZ's 100% win rate on Overpass in recent samples (6 games) directly contradicts Spirit's 71% LAN rate; if MOUZ bans Ancient and forces Overpass, Spirit must win that map convincingly or face a MOUZ underdog upset. No briefing mention of Spirit's internal morale, coaching staff adjustments, or anti-meta preparation specific to MOUZ \u2014 absence of confidence-building intel is itself a signal that Spirit's camp may not be as tight as the 60% price implies. BO3 format amplifies variance; at 6-6 form parity, the team with better mid-series adaptation (which we cannot measure from aggregate stats) gains edge. Probability_score set to 52 (barely Spirit favored) because market pricing and bookmaker odds (1.98) align with YES, but multiple counter-signals (MOUZ ranking, winning streak, map confidence, form parity) prevent higher conviction; probability_no_score at 48 reflects symmetric uncertainty.", "key_factor": "MOUZ's 6-map winning streak masks a recent tactical innovation or map-pool repositioning (Anubis confidence surge) that Spirit's prep has not yet fully addressed, combined with potential roster-level fatigue or last-minute personnel adjustments on Spirit's side that the briefing does not capture."}], "final_score": 0.5954157137705338, "no_score": 0.4192265176153733, "edge": 0.09590909090909094, "no_edge": 0.2859090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 62.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0554065426114645, "The Bull": 0.9364005760934779, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0512387433906618, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0583860676111567, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0483394048022772, "The Contrarian": 1.073846959547265, "The Bear": 0.7763817059436962}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1994987", "question": "Counter-Strike: Spirit vs MOUZ (BO3) - IEM Rio Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 1 match between Spirit and MOUZ in the IEM Rio Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Spirit\" if Spirit win the match against MOUZ.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MOUZ\" if MOUZ win the match against Spirit.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 702880.6319660026, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["1117374806443241211379847654593357736935764919958198603393598217237782739237", "46826523089818328270342608428642509128149631910919156617939811155871305704067"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["donk goes for an almost unprecedented $225000 as he and Spirit take on MOUZ in the quarter-finals.", "My expectation are falcons winning despite i love seeying them lose but i have seen this last dance honeymoon runs before, vitality can't match this", "zonic: \"Vitality win a lot of games by people already being scared and thinking that they can't win.", "Falcons had a huge moment on Wednesday, after already qualifying for the IEM Rio playoffs on Tuesday, when they beat Vitality to break up an 18-game winning", "HOTU have opted for changes following their early exit from IEM Rio.", "Vitality/Natus Vincere winner matchup at IEM Rio 2026!", "The German coach has been brought in to help turn the struggling team's fortunes around.", "graviti heavy favourite here, malbs is NA so he's probably taking his +2kg of sugar first thing in the morning.", "the rest of those 8 kg of sugar are covered", "karrigan's stint with FaZe is coming to a close after the team's disastrous IEM Cologne qualifying campaign."], "news_summary": "Spirit and MOUZ face off in the IEM Rio 2026 Playoffs quarter-finals (BO3) on 2026-04-17 at 15:00 UTC. Spirit enters as the bookmaker favorite (1.98 odds) with recent strong form, winning 3 of their last 5 matches. MOUZ, ranked slightly higher (#8 vs #9) and boasting better form metrics, counters with a 6-map winning streak and solid map-specific stats. The match will be played on LAN at the $1M tournament featuring 16 teams. Key Spirit players donk and m0NESY are ranked among the event's highest fantasy scorers.", "side_yes_case": ["Spirit is bookmaker favorite with best odds (1.98)", "Spirit won 3 of last 5 matches", "donk and m0NESY among highest-rated players at the event", "Spirit favored on Overpass (71% win rate on LAN) and Ancient (62% win rate)", "Head-to-head record heavily favors Spirit (5-0 in recent encounters per briefing)"], "side_no_case": ["MOUZ ranked higher (#8 vs Spirit's #9)", "MOUZ has better form ranking", "MOUZ on 6-map winning streak", "MOUZ strong on Anubis with 69% first-ban rate, suggesting map confidence", "MOUZ showed 100% win rate on Overpass in recent samples (6 games played)"], "key_context": ["IEM Rio 2026 Playoffs LAN event with $1M prize pool", "Quarter-finals format; winner advances deeper in tournament", "Match is BO3; map pool includes Overpass, Ancient, and Anubis", "Event runs 2026-04-17; high stakes motivate both teams"], "prior_match_facts": ["2026-02-08 \u2014 winner: Spirit (2-0) @ Playoffs", "2025-12-05 \u2014 winner: Spirit (1-2) @ Stage 3", "2025-08-16 \u2014 winner: Spirit (0-2) @ Playoffs", "2025-08-03 \u2014 winner: Spirit (0-3) @ Playoffs", "2025-07-29 \u2014 winner: Spirit (1-2) @ Group B", "2025-06-19 \u2014 winner: MOUZ (1-2) @ Playoffs", "2025-03-21 \u2014 winner: MOUZ (1-2) @ Group A", "2025-03-15 \u2014 winner: MOUZ (2-1) @ Playoffs", "2024-12-14 \u2014 winner: Spirit (1-2) @ Playoffs"], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T14:51:11.459469Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "1117374806443241211379847654593357736935764919958198603393598217237782739237", "data_points": 37, "weighted_avg": 0.5843647208281807, "change_1w_pp": 9.499999999999996, "change_24h_pp": 1.0000000000000009, "volatility_24h": 0.3750901767477268, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-16T03:00:51Z", "delta_pp": 5.000000000000004}]}, "no": {"token_id": "46826523089818328270342608428642509128149631910919156617939811155871305704067", "data_points": 19, "weighted_avg": 0.4199157764877696, "change_1w_pp": -9.499999999999996, "change_24h_pp": -0.9999999999999953, "volatility_24h": 0.6408699444616552, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:00:48Z", "delta_pp": -5.499999999999999}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-17T14:51:11.772780Z"}, "structured_match": {"provider": "pandascore", "provider_match_id": "1436336", "game": "csgo", "scheduled_at": "2026-04-17T15:00:00Z", "status": "scheduled", "team_a_name": "Spirit", "team_b_name": "MOUZ", "match_format": "BO3", "tournament_name": "Playoffs", "final_score": null, "winner_name": null, "h2h": [{"match_id": "1331905", "scheduled_at": "2026-02-08T12:30:00Z", "winner_name": "Spirit", "score_summary": "2-0", "tournament_name": "Playoffs"}, {"match_id": "1269316", "scheduled_at": "2025-12-05T16:15:00Z", "winner_name": "Spirit", "score_summary": "1-2", "tournament_name": "Stage 3"}, {"match_id": "1221580", "scheduled_at": "2