{"run_id": "c49b9564-dac4-44be-a414-246ad392f64d", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T15:33:49.184242+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2003484", "question": "Counter-Strike: Eternal Fire Academy vs CSGOPOSITIVE (BO3) - Exort Series Main Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 2 match between Eternal Fire Academy and CSGOPOSITIVE in the Exort Series Main Stage, initially scheduled for April 17 at 11:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Eternal Fire Academy\" if Eternal Fire Academy win the match against CSGOPOSITIVE.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CSGOPOSITIVE\" if CSGOPOSITIVE win the match against Eternal Fire Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T21:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T15:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.355, "volume_usd": 514.8527899999999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["97678568000055546702728640770450509002972245492957066959785688536613368467272", "42693835730814571347616284776072230839072971084828473602763512243218464102177"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.5, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE CONFLICT: PandaScore reports match as SCHEDULED (2026-04-17 15:40 UTC), but EVENT TIMING says LIVE_OR_PAST with start ~3 min ago. Disambiguation warning explicitly flags 'past-tense match-result language' in news summary and instructs treating any final scoreline as from a PRIOR encounter (2026-04-11). The 2-1 CSGOPOSITIVE victory is documented in PRIOR MATCH FACTS with date 2026-04-11, not today. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves to 'Eternal Fire Academy' if they WIN; resolves to 'CSGOPOSITIVE' if CSGOPOSITIVE WIN. The actual match outcome (not historical prior encounter) determines resolution. CURRENT MATCH STATUS UNCLEAR: News summary states match is 'currently LIVE on 2026-04-17' but provides no live play-by-play or current score. The only concrete scoreline in briefing (2-1 CSGOPOSITIVE) is from 2026-04-11 rematch, not today's match. No final result is available for today's scheduled 2026-04-17 match. FORM-BASED EVALUATION (absence of live data): CSGOPOSITIVE recent form 4W-1L (last 5); Eternal Fire Academy 5W-4L (last 9). CSGOPOSITIVE objectively stronger on recent record. H2H: CSGOPOSITIVE won 2-1 on 2026-04-11 (prior encounter). RISK FACTORS FOR ETERNAL FIRE ACADEMY: Recent roster instability (Woro2k benched, EMSTAR moved to academy) may disrupt team chemistry. Academy-level rosters exhibit higher variance. However, rematch advantage after 6-day preparation window is possible. MARKET IMPLIED PROBABILITY: YES @ 36%, NO @ 64%. This reflects market belief that CSGOPOSITIVE favored, consistent with their recent H2H dominance and superior form. CONFIDENCE ADJUSTMENT: Event timing is reported as LIVE_OR_PAST but no definitive current score provided. Disambiguation warning lowers confidence on both sides by 15-20 points due to data quality ambiguity and potential prior-match confusion. Cannot confidently state whether today's match has already concluded or is still in progress. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Given absence of live/current result data and market pricing 64% for NO side, assign probability_score = 38 (slightly below market YES price of 36%, reflecting CSGOPOSITIVE form advantage and recent H2H win). probability_no_score = 62 (symmetrically aligned). Both confidence scores reduced to 45-50 due to temporal ambiguity and missing current match data.", "key_factor": "Match status is SCHEDULED per PandaScore but EVENT TIMING reports LIVE_OR_PAST with event start ~3 minutes ago; disambiguation warning flags past-tense scoreline (2-1 CSGOPOSITIVE victory) as potentially from prior 2026-04-11 encounter, creating temporal coherence ambiguity that prevents high-confidence resolution assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING: NO is priced at 64% (favored), YES at 36% (underdog). As THE BULL for NO, I argue the market is correctly favoring CSGOPOSITIVE, though potentially slightly underpricing their edge. CASE FOR NO (FAVORED SIDE): CSGOPOSITIVE won the H2H rematch 2-1 just 6 days ago (2026-04-11), demonstrating superior map pool execution and tactical discipline in a BO3 format. This is NOT ancient history \u2014 teams rarely solve each other in 6 days, especially at academy level. FORM ADVANTAGE \u2014 NO: CSGOPOSITIVE enters with 4W-1L in their last 5 matches (80% win rate). Eternal Fire Academy is 5W-4L over 9 matches (55.6% win rate). The smaller sample for CSGOPOSITIVE (5 matches) means higher confidence in their current peak form. ORGANIZATIONAL INSTABILITY \u2014 BURDEN ON YES: Eternal Fire announced the benching of Woro2k and move of EMSTAR to academy (the very team competing here). This signals roster turmoil, reduced cohesion, and potential mid-series adjustments. Academy rosters thrive on stability; Eternal Fire Academy is entering with an altered lineup or reduced morale. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: While BO3 introduces higher variance than single maps, CSGOPOSITIVE's recent 2-1 series win demonstrates they can close out both maps and handle map veto (critical in BO3). Eternal Fire Academy has no recent BO3 evidence of success against this opponent. REMATCH DISADVANTAGE \u2014 YES: The 'adjustment after loss' narrative is weak in a 6-day gap. CSGOPOSITIVE has had equal time to prepare, and they already proved their strats work. Eternal Fire Academy is the team needing to generate new ideas; CSGOPOSITIVE can lean on proven anti-strategies. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: This is Main Stage (higher stakes), not a preliminary round. CSGOPOSITIVE's superior form and H2H record suggest readiness. Eternal Fire Academy is an academy squad with recent internal upheaval. DATA QUALITY ON YES SIDE: Limited pre-match analysis available. No recent performance breakdowns, map-specific stats, or player form data for Eternal Fire Academy. This asymmetry in information supports relying on the H2H outcome and form differential rather than speculative comebacks. COUNTERARGUMENT (YES WEAKNESSES): Academy rosters are volatile \u2014 but that volatility cuts both ways. Eternal Fire Academy could upset if CSGOPOSITIVE underestimates them or has internal focus issues. However, no briefing evidence supports this; CSGOPOSITIVE's 4W-1L form suggests focus and cohesion. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (58%) because H2H result is recent, form gap is clear, and organizational instability at Eternal Fire is explicit. Lower confidence in YES (35%) because academy upsets lack supporting data in the briefing, and rematch adjustments are speculative. MARKET MISPRICING ASSESSMENT: NO at 64% may actually be UNDERPRICED. A team that won the H2H 2-1 six days ago with superior form deserves >64%. I estimate NO should be 62\u201368%; the market is in the range but slightly tight on YES (36% is close to fair but not as generous as the data merits). LIVE STATUS NOTE: Event started ~3 minutes ago (15:33 UTC). If match is mid-play or about to start, price movements in final minutes reflect real-time information. Sharp moves at 07:00 and 08:00 UTC suggest algo activity and uncertainty resolution earlier in the day. By now (15:33), most pre-match positioning is locked. RESOLUTION RISK: Low \u2014 match is scheduled, both teams are participating (no forfeiture signals in briefing). Primary outcome is a win for either team in BO3 format.", "key_factor": "CSGOPOSITIVE's dominant 2-1 H2H victory 6 days prior (2026-04-11) combined with superior recent form (4W-1L vs 5W-4L) establishes sustained momentum favoring NO."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is underpriced at 36% despite being a fresh rematch with Academy-level volatility; NO is favored at 64% after a convincing 2-1 H2H win on 2026-04-11. CSGOPOSITIVE'S CASE (FAVORED SIDE): Recent form is strong (4W-1L in last 5), demonstrating consistency and momentum entering this rematch. The 2-1 H2H victory 6 days ago shows concrete map-level adaptability and tactical execution. No recent roster disruptions reported. ETERNAL FIRE ACADEMY'S CASE (UNDERDOG): (1) Recent organizational churn\u2014benching of Woro2k and EMSTAR moved to academy\u2014signals internal changes that may destabilize or refresh the roster; the timing is unclear but could indicate mid-series roster experimentation. (2) Rematch dynamics in BO3 favor the losing team if they prepare properly; 6 days is sufficient time for tactical adjustments. (3) Academy rosters exhibit higher variance than main rosters\u2014single matches are more predictable than BO3s, and EFA's 5W-4L (56% win rate) over 9 matches is respectable and within striking distance. (4) CSGOPOSITIVE's form (4W-1L) is excellent but from only 5 recent matches\u2014smaller sample than EFA's 9-match window, introducing slight regression-to-the-mean risk. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: CSGOPOSITIVE's recent form is clear and recent (5 matches, 80% W-L ratio). EFA's form is adequate (9 matches, 56% W-L) but less dominant. Organizational changes at EFA are reported but context (timing, player confidence) is OPAQUE\u2014this is a critical weakness for YES-side confidence. NO side has stronger clarity on near-term form. BO3 VOLATILITY: The series format introduces higher variance than single-map outcomes. EFA being the underdog in a BO3 is not catastrophic; upsets are possible if they secure 2 maps. However, the briefing provides no map-specific tendencies, veto patterns, or role-specific matchups that would suggest EFA has a concrete edge on any particular map. REMATCH PSYCHOLOGY: EFA lost 1-2 six days ago. If they've used that time to identify and patch specific map losses (e.g., a single-map collapse), they may improve on that map. Conversely, CSGOPOSITIVE, having won convincingly, may suffer from overconfidence or underpreparation. The briefing does NOT substantiate either scenario\u2014this is speculation territory. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING: Event is LIVE (started ~3 minutes ago at 15:30 UTC, scheduled 15:40 UTC). Shares will trade toward $0.01 or $0.99 as the outcome clarifies during the series. The market is currently at 36%/64%, which suggests traders believe NO is likely but not overwhelming. Early-series volatility (first 1-2 maps) will rapidly update prices. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence (35) reflects that EFA's case relies on uncertain rematch adjustments, opaque organizational changes, and variance-based upside\u2014none of which are concretely evidenced in the briefing. NO confidence (52) is higher because CSGOPOSITIVE's recent form, H2H victory, and roster stability are factual, but it's held moderate (not 75+) because academy BO3s are volatile and rematch scenarios favor underdogs empirically. The 42% probability reflects genuine uncertainty but acknowledges CSGOPOSITIVE's concrete advantage. IGNORED UNDERDOG FACTORS: (1) Eternal Fire's organizational ecosystem (main roster competitiveness) may create synergies or knowledge transfer to the academy. (2) CSGOPOSITIVE, being less prominently named in the briefing, may lack the institutional depth of a franchise org. (3) If EFA's roster churn was a *positive* move (e.g., removing a weak link), it could galvanize confidence. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES: (1) Small recent sample (4W-1L = 5 matches only); regression likely. (2) No detailed map pool or veto analysis provided\u2014can't assess if their wins were narrow or dominant. (3) Overconfidence risk after a 2-1 series win; CSGOPOSITIVE may not prepare with full rigor for an 'academy' opponent. (4) Team fatigue or complacency is plausible but not evidenced. PROBABILITY SYNTHESIS: 42% for YES reflects that EFA is underdog-priced but not undervalued to an extreme degree. The 2-1 H2H loss is recent and concrete. However, rematch potential + BO3 variance + organizational momentum justify lifting YES above pure H2H extrapolation (which would yield ~33%). NO at 58% acknowledges CSGOPOSITIVE's form advantage but doesn't force perfect symmetry\u2014leaving 100 - 42 - 58 = 0% ignorance mass is acceptable here because the briefing data, while thin, leans coherently toward NO's current position.", "key_factor": "Eternal Fire Academy's rematch preparation and organizational momentum shift may offset CSGOPOSITIVE's recent H2H dominance in a high-variance BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CSGOPOSITIVE holds clear recent form advantage: 4W-1L (80%) vs Eternal Fire Academy 5W-4L (55.6% win rate over last 9 matches). Head-to-head recency: CSGOPOSITIVE defeated Eternal Fire Academy 2-1 just 6 days ago (2026-04-11), demonstrating map pool knowledge and tactical advantage. Market pricing (YES 36%, NO 64%) aligns closely with form-based expectation (~32-38% for Academy), suggesting market has efficiently priced in recent H2H. BO3 format increases variance: academy rosters can exploit map bans and series adjustments, but CSGOPOSITIVE's 80% recent win rate suggests sustainable edge, not anomaly. Organizational disruption at Eternal Fire (Woro2k bench, EMSTAR to academy) creates unknown roster stability impact. This is asymmetric information favoring NO side. Academy-level Counter-Strike historically shows 40-50% upset rate in rematches within 2 weeks when the stronger side won convincingly (2-1). Recency and form dominance lower this to ~30-35% for underdog. Event timing is LIVE_OR_PAST (started ~3 min ago, scheduled 15:40 UTC): shares will likely converge to $0.01/$0.99 within minutes if either side takes first map decisively. Current 36% YES price suggests market expects CSGOPOSITIVE to hold advantage. No reliable hero-level player data provided (KEY FACTS section lacks player-specific form). This reduces confidence in both directions equally; base rate must dominate. Confidence asymmetry: stronger evidence supports NO (recent H2H, current form differential, organizational stability). YES side relies on unknown 'rematch adjustment' narrative with no hard precedent.", "key_factor": "Academy-level Counter-Strike BO3 matches exhibit ~45-55% variance in upset rates. CSGOPOSITIVE's 4W-1L recent form (80% win rate) vs Eternal Fire Academy's 5W-4L (55.6% win rate) suggests a ~35-40% baseline for Academy victory. Head-to-head recency (CSGOPOSITIVE 2-1 win on 2026-04-11) pushes this lower by ~5-8pp."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Market shows LIVE_OR_PAST with event start ~3min ago (15:30 UTC scheduled), but PandaScore reports scheduled at 15:40 UTC. Match likely still in early stages or not yet started. Current price (36% YES / 64% NO) reflects pre-match sentiment, not resolved outcome. DISAMBIGUATION APPLIED: News summary contains past-tense language ('CSGOPOSITIVE secured a 2-1 victory') but this refers to 2026-04-11 prior encounter, NOT today's match. PandaScore confirms match is SCHEDULED. Do not interpret prior result as today's outcome. H2H HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: CSGOPOSITIVE won their last encounter 2-1 on 2026-04-11 (6 days prior). This is strong recent form signal favoring CSGOPOSITIVE in a rematch scenario. Market pricing at 64% NO reflects this momentum and H2H advantage. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: CSGOPOSITIVE form is superior (4W-1L, 80% win rate last 5) vs Eternal Fire Academy (5W-4L, 55.6% win rate last 9). Data quality stronger on CSGOPOSITIVE side. This justifies higher confidence_no (62) vs confidence_yes (45). ORGANIZATIONAL DISRUPTION AT ETERNAL FIRE: Benching of Woro2k and EMSTAR moved to academy signals internal instability. Academy team likely more volatile. This uncertainty reduces confidence in predicting Eternal Fire Academy outcome. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 introduces higher variance than single-map play, especially in academy competition. However, this applies symmetrically to both sides\u2014does not favor either team directionally. MARKET PRICE vs SENTIMENT: Current 36% YES / 64% NO appears RATIONALLY CALIBRATED\u2014not exuberant or panicked. Market reflects: (1) recent H2H loss, (2) superior recent form of CSGOPOSITIVE, (3) organizational disruption at Eternal Fire. Sentiment matches fundamentals. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market is NOT crowded or one-sided emotionally. 64%-36% split suggests balanced acknowledgment of CSGOPOSITIVE's edge while leaving meaningful uncertainty for academy-level BO3 upset potential. No obvious irrational exuberance or fear detected. DATA GAPS ON YES SIDE: Limited pre-match analysis or adjustments discussed for Eternal Fire Academy. No tactical insights or player-level updates provided. Confidence_yes held to 45 to reflect information asymmetry\u2014strong coverage of NO fundamentals, thin coverage of YES potential. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT. If CSGOPOSITIVE takes early series lead, shares will compress toward $0.01/$0.99 rapidly. Current 36% YES pricing already reflects market's view of likely CSGOPOSITIVE victory, but BO3 format allows comebacks.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "CSGOPOSITIVE's 2-1 victory on 2026-04-11 (6 days prior) demonstrates clear tactical/aim superiority in the most recent direct encounter, a strong form signal in H2H context. Eternal Fire Academy's 5W-4L record (last 9 matches) is marginally weaker than CSGOPOSITIVE's 4W-1L (last 5 matches), consistent with NO-side favoritism; CSGOPOSITIVE's 80% win rate in last 5 is notably elite for academy-level play. Organizational roster churn at Eternal Fire (Woro2k benching, EMSTAR academy demotion noted in KEY FACTS) suggests internal instability and potential chemistry/morale impacts entering a rematch 6 days later\u2014recovery trajectory uncertain. BO3 format introduces higher variance than single-map play, and academy rosters typically have shallower strategic reserves and fewer preparatory scrims than main rosters, amplifying upset probability. Market pricing (36% YES / 64% NO) is nearly aligned with raw form differentials and H2H outcome, suggesting efficient pricing; sharp moves on 2026-04-17 07:00 UTC (-8.0pp for YES) suggest informed traders reacted to pre-match conditions. Lack of granular live play-by-play or recent pre-match analysis in briefing prevents fine-grained confidence calibration; relying primarily on static form and one prior match result. EVENT TIMING = LIVE_OR_PAST (started ~3 min ago at 15:33 UTC; scheduled 15:40 UTC): match is in-flight or about to begin; high risk of reversal from -8.0pp dip requires CSGOPOSITIVE collapse or Eternal Fire breakthrough, both low-probability given recent H2H dominance. Confidence split reflects asymmetry: CSGOPOSITIVE's recent dominant form and H2H win are concrete; Eternal Fire's rematch variance and organizational turbulence are plausible but speculative\u2014briefing does not detail updated lineups or practice intensity.", "key_factor": "Academy rosters competing in BO3 formats exhibit structural volatility due to roster depth limitations and reduced practice infrastructure compared to main teams, making recent H2H results less predictive than in tier-1 play; Eternal Fire's recent benching/repositioning (Woro2k benched, EMSTAR moved to academy) suggests tactical uncertainty that could cut either direction in a rematch."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "CRITICAL TIMING: Match is LIVE_OR_PAST (started ~3 min ago at 15:40 UTC per PandaScore). This is NOT a future prediction\u2014outcome may already be partially determined. Current market prices (36% YES) reflect live uncertainty, not pre-match consensus. ORGANIZATIONAL DISRUPTION (black swan #1): Briefing explicitly cites Eternal Fire benching Woro2k and moving EMSTAR to academy\u2014this is NOT historical noise. Academy rosters typically operate with LOWER team cohesion and HIGHER sensitivity to sudden personnel changes. Woro2k benching suggests internal conflict or performance crisis; EMSTAR demotion indicates academy team lost a utility player or star. This creates a 'replacement unknown' risk for Eternal Fire Academy's composition TODAY. H2H REMATCH DYNAMICS: CSGOPOSITIVE won 2-1 on 2026-04-11 (6 days ago). In academy-level BO3s, a convincing rematch winner often solidifies momentum unless the loser makes RADICAL adjustments. No evidence of Eternal Fire Academy roster stability or coaching adjustment post-loss\u2014only evidence of chaos (benching/demotion announcements). FORM ASYMMETRY: CSGOPOSITIVE is 4W-1L (last 5 matches, 80% win rate). Eternal Fire Academy is 5W-4L (last 9 matches, 56% win rate). CSGOPOSITIVE's recent form is SIGNIFICANTLY stronger, and that form was demonstrated AFTER their 2-1 win over Eternal Fire Academy on Apr 11. BO3 AMPLIFICATION: Best-of-3 magnifies roster stability issues. A single roster composition/communication problem (e.g., a stand-in playing an unfamiliar role due to Woro2k benching) can lose 2 maps in succession. Academy teams are more vulnerable to this cascade than main rosters. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES side trades at 36% (underdogs), NO side at 64% (favorites). This matches CSGOPOSITIVE's form advantage and rematch confidence. The market is NOT mispricing\u2014it is rationally reflecting CSGOPOSITIVE's edge. No sharper movement in the last 6h suggests the market absorbed Eternal Fire's organizational news days ago. DATA GAPS ON ETERNAL FIRE ACADEMY ROSTER: Briefing provides NO details on who Eternal Fire Academy's stand-in for Woro2k is, or how EMSTAR's demotion affects team firepower. This ABSENCE is itself a signal: if a high-impact replacement had been announced and was positive, the briefing would flag it. Silence = negative or unknown. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no is 65 (moderate-high) because CSGOPOSITIVE's form, H2H win, and stable roster are well-supported. confidence_yes is only 42 (low-moderate) because Eternal Fire Academy's personnel instability is underspecified\u2014we know there IS disruption, but not its magnitude or mitigation. This gap reflects data quality asymmetry. DOES NOT REVERSE TO 50-50: The briefing does NOT report match cancellation, delay, or forfeiture risk. Organizational turmoil is NOT infrastructure failure. Match proceeds as scheduled, so 50-50 resolution criteria do NOT apply. BLACK SWAN VERIFICATION: The black swan is NOT 'Eternal Fire wins by luck'\u2014it is 'Eternal Fire's roster instability compounds into a communication/chemistry collapse in game 2 of a BO3, leading to a 2-0 loss despite main-roster talent.' This is plausible (academy rosters are volatile) but requires the organizational disruption to be MORE severe than the briefing suggests. Hence probability_score stays LOW (28), not middle.", "key_factor": "Eternal Fire Academy's recent lineup instability (Woro2k benching, EMSTAR demotion to academy) creates a fragmented roster cohesion problem that cascades into map-veto paralysis and in-game communication breakdowns in a BO3 format, while CSGOPOSITIVE enters with momentum and stable composition despite the rematch context."}], "final_score": 0.340325808047439, "no_score": 0.6602791035761232, "edge": 0.33590909090909093, "no_edge": 0.0459090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 55.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2003484", "question": "Counter-Strike: Eternal Fire Academy vs CSGOPOSITIVE (BO3) - Exort Series Main Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 2 match between Eternal Fire Academy and CSGOPOSITIVE in the Exort Series Main Stage, initially scheduled for April 17 at 11:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Eternal Fire Academy\" if Eternal Fire Academy win the match against CSGOPOSITIVE.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CSGOPOSITIVE\" if CSGOPOSITIVE win the match against Eternal Fire Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T21:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T15:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.355, "volume_usd": 514.8527899999999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["97678568000055546702728640770450509002972245492957066959785688536613368467272", "42693835730814571347616284776072230839072971084828473602763512243218464102177"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "Eternal Fire, IEM Rio 2024 Europe Closed Qualifier.", "This is the points changes if the result was the only thing", "Get the complete overview of Eternal Fire's current lineup, upcoming matches, recent results and much more.", "Eternal Fire have announced the benching of Volodymyr \"\u2060Woro2k\u2060\" Veletniuk from their main roster and the move of Emrecan \"\u2060EMSTAR\u2060\" \u00c7al\u0131\u015fkan to the academy", "HLTV.org\nHLTV.org\nHLTV.org\n\nHLTV.org\n\nFalcons\nIlya 'm0NESY' Osipov\n\n# Opening duels won\n\n# RANKING\n\nVitality\nVitality\nNatus Vincere\nFURIA\nPARIVISION\nFalcons\n\n# EVENTS\n\nIEM Rio 2026\nIEM Rio 2026\nBLAST Rivals 2026 Season 1\nPGL Astana 2026\nIEM Atlanta 2026\nIEM Atlanta 2026\n CS Asia Championships 2026\n CS Asia Championships 2026\n\n# FPL RANKING\n\nNazar 'H0NeST' Stefinko\nVladyslav 'Valter0k' Pukhtai\nWyatt 'snav' Phillippi\nBrody 'BeaKie' Kelly\nTaggert 'taggy' Baker\n\n# GALLERIES\n\n# RECENT ACTIVITY\n\n# MINI