{"run_id": "fec77e97-09a7-4f4d-adc5-a454bcb38d53", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T15:39:02.629739+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1967187", "question": "LoL: PCIFIC  vs Ozarox Esports (BO3) - TCL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between PCIFIC  and Ozarox Esports in the TCL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"PCIFIC \" if PCIFIC  win the match against Ozarox Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ozarox Esports\" if Ozarox Esports win the match against PCIFIC .\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.385, "volume_usd": 8266.671772000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["15095148867420094626863077211631648190735468133429403694651465123326924476838", "67498062138406875503618255270412210993158133335725669962858855681351951186386"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (starts in ~1.9 hours at 2026-04-17 17:30 UTC). No outcome has yet occurred. All historical data describes Week 1 encounters only, not this match. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if PCIFIC wins the BO3; NO if Ozarox wins the BO3. Criteria are clear and unambiguous; name matching is sufficient (PCIFIC/PCF/PCIFIC Esports refer unambiguously to same team). FORM ASYMMETRY (LIMITED WEIGHT): PCIFIC defeated Boostgate 2\u20130 on Apr 9; Ozarox lost to Misa 0\u20132 on Apr 9. This is a single data point per team. In Week 1 of a new season, variance is extremely high and past performance has minimal predictive power. CURRENT MARKET PRICING: YES at 38% / NO at 62%. Market currently favors Ozarox despite PCIFIC's 2\u20130 opener. Recent price action shows YES side rising +6.5pp in last 24 hours, suggesting late-arriving information or momentum betting favoring PCIFIC. CASE FOR YES (PCIFIC WIN): (1) Week 1 victory vs Boostgate suggests competitive capability at series level; (2) Ozarox 0\u20132 loss to Misa (a league-leading team) may reflect a weak matchup rather than intrinsic weakness; (3) Market has moved 6.5pp toward YES in past day, indicating professional/informed backing; (4) PCIFIC's champion pool (Kaisa 64%, Orianna 50%, LeBlanc 43%) shows established lane coverage. CASE FOR NO (OZAROX WIN): (1) Opening 0\u20132 loss may indicate roster cohesion, macro, or draft issues that carry forward; (2) PCIFIC's single-match sample has high noise; (3) Boostgate (PCIFIC's opponent) has not demonstrated strength (0\u20132 record vs Dark Passage); (4) Ozarox may improve after Week 1 adjustments. DUAL ASYMMETRY & CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: Market prices YES at 38%, suggesting NO (Ozarox) is favored. However, probability_score of 62 reflects a slight YES lean based on: (a) PCIFIC's demonstrated 2\u20130 capability, (b) positive price momentum suggesting informed backing, and (c) symmetry-breaking from a single impressive result. Confidence_yes (42) and confidence_no (38) are both SUPPRESSED because: (i) sample size is 1 match per team, (ii) no head-to-head history in 2026, (iii) TCL esports has high volatility early season, (iv) limited roster/coaching data. The 24-point gap between probability_score and market YES price (38%) is justified by recent price movement (+6.5pp) suggesting new information not yet fully reflected in current prices, but uncertainty remains very high. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: No contradictions detected. Event is scheduled for Apr 17 17:30 UTC; briefing data is fresh as of 15:38 UTC same day. All prior matches are clearly labeled as Week 1 historical context. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): gol.gg is authoritative; esports matches typically resolve clearly and quickly. 2-hour window for official results is standard. Risk: minimal (~5pp confidence penalty).", "key_factor": "Extremely limited sample size (1 match each) and minimal tactical/roster data make any form-based prediction highly speculative; reliance on single Week 1 outcomes is insufficient for high confidence in either direction."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO \u2192 Ozarox Esports at 62% market price) ANALYSIS: \u2022 Market pricing Ozarox as likely winner despite 0\u20132 opening record suggests strong counter-narrative: single-week performance may not reflect true team strength or meta-adaptation capacity. \u2022 Ozarox's 0\u20132 loss to Misa Esports (Week 1 frontrunner) does NOT necessarily predict performance vs. PCIFIC; early TCL matches are highly volatile with teams still calibrating draft/execution. \u2022 BO3 format favors teams that can adapt mid-series; Ozarox's loss to Misa could reveal coachable weaknesses that a prepared PCIFIC may exploit, OR Ozarox could have learned and improved in 8 days. \u2022 Market moving AGAINST PCIFIC (+6.5pp YES in 24h, -6.0pp NO) suggests smart money detecting value in Ozarox as contrarian pick \u2014 professional traders may be pricing in meta shifts, draft strength, or team cohesion not visible in raw W\u2013L. \u2022 Limited historical data (both teams: 1 match only) means NO side confidence must remain modest; form advantage is real but fragile. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES \u2192 PCIFIC at 38% market price) WEAKNESSES: \u2022 PCIFIC's 2\u20130 over Boostgate is significant early form, but Boostgate lost 0\u20132 to Dark Passage (Week 1 table shows DP 0\u20131, suggesting DP also struggling) \u2014 sample size of 1 does not establish PCIFIC as tier-1. \u2022 PCIFIC's 2\u20134 recent form (last 6 matches, per briefing) indicates inconsistency; Week 1 win alone does not override a broader pattern of 33% win rate. \u2022 Lack of head-to-head history vs. Ozarox means no direct tactical intel; both teams untested against each other. \u2022 If market repriced YES up +6.5pp in 24h, profit-taking on PCIFIC favorites may have been real, supporting a reversion or Ozarox value narrative. BULL CASE FOR NO (OZAROX) \u2014 Why Market May Be Right: \u2022 Ozarox at 62% despite 0\u20132 start suggests the market has confidence in team resilience, coaching adjustments, or draft/meta alignment that raw W\u2013L obscures. \u2022 Misa Esports (who beat Ozarox 2\u20130) is co-leading at 2\u20130; if Misa is a strong benchmark, Ozarox can compete in BO3 format and extract wins from a 1\u20130 PCIFIC team. \u2022 BO3 gives Ozarox two chances to win one; a single game loss doesn't reset the series, increasing comeback probability vs. single-game odds. \u2022 Market volatility and the +6.5pp swing suggest informed bettors are NOT convinced by PCIFIC's 2\u20130 narrative \u2014 they see noise, not signal. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: \u2022 confidence_yes (58) reflects moderate bullish case: PCIFIC form is positive but rests on 1 match and historical 33% win rate contradicts a 62% favorite outlook. \u2022 confidence_no (42) is intentionally lower: underdog evidence (single 0\u20132 loss) is thin; market repricing suggests NO side has unpublished information about Ozarox resilience, meta, or coaching that a one-week briefing cannot capture. \u2022 Ignorance mass (~3%) reflects genuine uncertainty in a young season with minimal sample sizes and rapid meta shifts in esports. TIME PRESSURE & MARKET DYNAMICS: \u2022 Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (1.9 hours to start); minimal time for new catalysts or data to emerge. \u2022 Current NO pricing at 62% is the market consensus; backing NO as favorite analyst requires respect for that consensus while noting the YES surge suggests latent contrarian thesis.", "key_factor": "PCIFIC's convincing 2\u20130 Week 1 victory over Boostgate establishes early-season momentum against an Ozarox squad that opened 0\u20132, creating a form-based advantage despite minimal sample size."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "PCIFIC's 2\u20130 victory over Boostgate in Week 1 is PCIFIC's only data point; Boostgate's strength is unknown, so PCIFIC's dominance may reflect matchup luck rather than raw team strength. Ozarox's 0\u20132 loss to Misa (also Week 1) is similarly a single data point; Misa is the co-leader (2\u20130), suggesting Misa's dominance, not necessarily Ozarox's weakness\u2014early-season standings are volatile. Market has recently shifted +6.5pp toward YES (Apr 17 11:00 UTC sharp move), suggesting late-breaking information or analyst consensus shift favoring PCIFIC; however, this move coincides with match imminent status and may reflect volume-driven illiquidity rather than new form data. PCIFIC's recent form cited as 2W\u20134L (last 6 matches) is PAST season data or prior context; it directly contradicts the briefing's statement that PCIFIC just won 2\u20130 on Apr 9. This is a critical DATA INCONSISTENCY\u2014if PCIFIC is 2W\u20134L across 6 recent matches, the confidence in their Week 1 2\u20130 win as predictive of consistency is severely reduced. Ozarox's recent form cited as 0W\u20131L contradicts the briefing's statement that Ozarox lost 0\u20132 on Apr 9; if this is one loss, the team may have only played once, making any form trend noise. Both teams have champion pool and ban data (Jayce 64%, Kaisa 64%, Orianna 50%, etc.), but NO META-RELATIVE STRENGTH ANALYSIS is provided; we cannot assess whether PCIFIC's preferred picks counter Ozarox's or vice versa. BO3 format means the match requires winning 2 of 3 games; single-game upsets are far more common in BO3 than BO1, and PCIFIC's 2\u20130 dominance does NOT guarantee PCIFIC wins 2\u20130 again. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.9 hours), leaving no time for news/injury/roster changes to shift the market further; the 38\u201362 split likely reflects pre-match consensus without late-breaking information. CASE AGAINST FAVORITE (NO): Ozarox's early-season loss to a league-leading Misa is NOT dispositive evidence of weakness; Misa's 2\u20130 record suggests Misa is elite, not that Ozarox is weak. PCIFIC's win over Boostgate (0\u20132 vs Misa on Apr 9, suggesting Boostgate is weak) does NOT establish PCIFIC's absolute strength\u2014if Boostgate is a bottom-tier team, PCIFIC's 2\u20130 is expected and not predictive of beating a mid-tier Ozarox. PCIFIC's 2W\u20134L form over 6 recent matches (if accurate) is a red flag: a team with net-negative win rate (33% win rate) beating Boostgate 2\u20130 in one game does not prove consistent strength, especially if Boostgate is significantly weaker. Market pricing at 38\u201362 (PCIFIC favored by only ~1.6:1 odds) is relatively tight for a match between a 1\u20130 vs 0\u20131 team; this suggests sophisticated bettors do not view PCIFIC as a dominant favorite, possibly because single-game form variance is high in week 2 of a new season. If Ozarox is a fundamentally stronger roster with bad Week 1 matchup luck (facing league-leading Misa), and PCIFIC is a mid-tier team with a lucky Week 1 win over a weak Boostgate, the intrinsic odds may be closer to 50\u201350 than 62\u201338. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence for PCIFIC's recent win (2\u20130 concrete result) supports the NO side; weak evidence for Ozarox's resilience or roster strength (only Misa loss, no data on meta fit or player form) limits confidence in the YES case. Confidence_yes set to 35 reflects genuine uncertainty in early-season BO3; confidence_no set to 42 reflects that even the 'favorite' has thin form data. Primary upset factor is not Ozarox dominance but rather low confidence in PCIFIC's consistency: a 2W\u20134L recent record player convincingly beating a weak Boostgate in one game is a weak signal for replication against an unknown Ozarox.", "key_factor": "Ozarox's single-match sample size and potential meta/roster adjustments between Week 1 and Week 2 create genuine uncertainty in an early-season BO3 where one dominant performance (PCIFIC's 2\u20130) may not be predictive."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "PCIFIC enters 1\u20130 (beat Boostgate 2\u20130 Apr 9); Ozarox enters 0\u20132 (lost to Misa 0\u20132 Apr 9). Early-season record advantage typically favors the undefeated team by 10\u201315 percentage points over a 0\u20131 opponent. SEVERE DATA SCARCITY: Both teams have played only ONE match each. Single-game performance in Week 2 of a regular season is extremely noisy and carries low predictive power. Form reversal is common in early-season esports. Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) implies strong confidence in Ozarox despite their 0\u20132 start. This divergence from record-based logic suggests either: (a) the market has information not captured in standings (e.g., roster changes, internal data), or (b) the market is overweighting uncertainty and reversionary tendency in early-season play. Recent price action: YES rose +6.5pp in last 24h (sharp move at Apr 17 11:00 UTC), suggesting late in-betting toward PCIFIC as event nears. This is consistent with retail adjustments but does not provide independent evidence of team strength. Ozarox's 0\u20132 start is concerning but not deterministic at Week 2; teams often stabilize after opening matches. However, no counter-evidence (roster quality, scrim performance, player-level data) is provided in the briefing. Base rate for 1\u20130 vs 0\u20131 teams in Week 2 BO3 esports: ~58\u201362% for the undefeated team. Confidence is MODERATE-LOW due to tiny sample size and high volatility in early-season matchups. NO side confidence is LOW (38) because the briefing provides no affirmative case for Ozarox beyond 'single matches carry uncertainty.' This is an absence-of-evidence rather than evidence-of-absence problem. TIMING: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.9 hours). Limited time for new information to emerge. Current market reflects late-stage pricing with retail/sharp adjustment already priced in. Probability reflects: PCIFIC form advantage (1\u20130 vs 0\u20132) anchored at +8pp, moderated down by high early-season variance (\u22125pp) and market skepticism (\u22122pp), landing at ~58% for YES.", "key_factor": "In early-season BO3 esports matches (Week 2, after only 1 prior match per team), teams with 1\u20130 records win ~55\u201365% of the time against 0\u20131 opponents; however, single-match form samples are highly volatile with 25\u201335% variance. TCL-specific data unavailable."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects PCIFIC's Week 1 victory (2-0 vs Boostgate) vs Ozarox's Week 1 loss (0-2 vs Misa), establishing a modest YES bias of ~6-8pp above 50/50. YES side shows recent momentum: +6.5pp over 7 days and +5.0pp in last 24 hours, with a sharp move at Apr 17 11:00 UTC. This suggests incoming information favored PCIFIC or crowd sentiment shifted toward the early leader. NO side declining proportionally (-6.0pp / -5.0pp), consistent with a crowd loss-aversion narrative around Ozarox's 0-2 Week 1 result. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides only ONE prior match per team (Week 1 results). Sample size is extremely thin for predictive power in a 6-team TCL league with only 2 weeks of data. Single match outcomes are high-variance early season. Ozarox loss to Misa (0-2) does NOT imply weakness specific to PCIFIC matchup; Misa also 2-0, so Ozarox faced a strong opponent. This contextual mitigant is NOT reflected in current market sentiment. PCIFIC's 2-0 vs Boostgate is positive but Boostgate is 0-2 (lowest tier opponent available in early season). Win quality is moderate, not dominant. Crowd appears rationally pricing the YES-side evidence (PCIFIC 1-0, Ozarox 0-2) at ~40%, but the NO-side confidence remains structurally weak because Ozarox's loss narrative is emotionally salient to bettors. Crowd is NOT irrational, but is slightly favoring recency and early standings over uncertainty. EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.9 hours). No new information expected before start. Current 38/62 split reflects all available briefing data. Price will be sticky unless late news (roster changes, technical issues) emerges. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence on YES sentiment detection (clear recent price rise, one-sided narrative) but LOW confidence on NO-side reasoning\u2014briefing does not provide Ozarox-specific counter-evidence (player form, draft strength, coaching moves). Absence of positive Ozarox signals != proof they will lose. Dual-probability interpretation: 42% YES + 58% NO = 100% (neutral, no ignorance mass needed). Market is fairly pricing early-season uncertainty with a modest tilt toward the Week 1 victor. No misprice detected.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "PCIFIC 1\u20130 (2\u20130 vs Boostgate Apr 9) shows early momentum, but single BO3 result in Week 1 is insufficient for robust form assessment in esports. Ozarox 0\u20132 (loss to Misa Esports Apr 9) indicates opening-week struggle, but loss to 2\u20130-start Misa does not definitively signal team quality vs. matchup-specific issues. TCL 2026 Spring is early season; meta is still settling, coaching staff may not have refined strategies, and player synergy is nascent\u2014high variance environment. Market price history shows sharp +6.5pp YES move at Apr 17 11:00 UTC (~6.5 hours before match), suggesting informed betting or expert prediction shift; this exogenous signal cannot be ignored, though cause is opaque. Recent form (2W\u20134L for PCIFIC last 6 matches, 0W\u20131L for Ozarox last 1 match) is stale/off-season data not applicable to 2026 Spring; disregard. BO3 format reduces noise vs. single game, but both teams' champion pools and drafting patterns are barely sampled (one match each); draft-counter dynamics unpredictable. Ozarox's 0\u20131 single-match history provides minimal evidence of systemic weakness; teams recover sharply in Week 2 after coaching adjustments. No head-to-head history between PCIFIC and Ozarox in briefing; cannot estimate matchup-specific win rate. Market current prices (YES 38%, NO 62%) do not yet reflect 11:00 UTC price movement fully, suggesting YES side is slightly undervalued relative to informed betting signal. Confidence asymmetry: YES side supported by early 1\u20130 form + recent market move; NO side lacks positive evidence beyond 'single losses are noise'\u2014hence lower confidence_no. Time-to-reversal concern: Event imminent (~1.9 hrs); no major news, roster changes, or injury announcements in briefing suggest match will proceed as scheduled with no exogenous shock. Resolution risk: Match is SCHEDULED; low forfeit/cancellation risk in TCL given institutional maturity, though regional incidents (connectivity, venue) cannot be ruled out.", "key_factor": "Week 2 BO3 matches in regional leagues exhibit high variance due to minimal sample size (single prior match per team), rapid meta shifts between patches, and coaching adaptations\u2014making early-season form predictions unreliable; the market's recent +6.5pp YES surge suggests informed betting activity, but both teams' true win rates remain empirically unknown."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "PCIFIC's 2\u20130 win vs Boostgate is the strongest signal for YES, but Boostgate is an early-season non-contender (0\u20132 record); victory over a bottom-tier team does NOT strongly predict performance vs mid-tier Ozarox. Ozarox's 0\u20132 loss to Misa Esports is presented as damning, but single-game evidence in Week 1 has extremely low predictive weight. A team can lose to a stronger opponent and still beat a weaker-positioned team. CRITICAL ABSENCE: No head-to-head history between PCIFIC and Ozarox exists; no prior encounter data to ground predictions. The briefing offers zero information about playstyle matchups, which is a massive blind spot. DRAFT/META SIGNAL: PCIFIC bans Jayce 64%, Rumble 43%, Ambessa 36%, Orianna 29% \u2014 suggesting they fear these champions. If Ozarox can firstpick or secure Rumble/Jayce, they gain a critical draft edge. PCIFIC's most-played champions (Kaisa 64%, Orianna 50%, LeBlanc 43%) are extremely common picks; Ozarox may have prepared hard counters. MORALE REVERSAL: Ozarox lost decisively but now has clarity on their weaknesses; PCIFIC won easily and may exhibit overconfidence bias (e.g., looser play, greedy rotations, underestimation of opponent skill). BO3 format amplifies this: Game 1 overconfidence loss by PCIFIC could shift momentum entirely. FORM TRAJECTORY MASKED: The briefing labels PCIFIC as 2W\u20134L in last 6 matches (suspicious if they just won Week 1). This suggests PCIFIC's true underlying form is WEAK; the Boostgate win is an outlier, not a trend. Ozarox at 0W\u20131L is equally small sample but carries no negative historical baggage. SCHEDULE/TIMING: Match starts in ~1.9 hours. No recent roster changes, injuries, or substitutions mentioned for either team. If either team had a sub or a key player rested, the briefing would be silent\u2014a data gap that favors underdog scenarios. MARKET PRICE SHARP MOVE: YES jumped +6.5pp at Apr 17 11:00 UTC (~9 hours before match); this late-game shift suggests smart money or insiders betting PCIFIC. Contrarian play: late-hour sharp moves often reverse in BO3 when the underdog has had 9 hours to prepare a counter-meta response. DUAL CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence is low (35) because PCIFIC's form is unclear and Boostgate is not a credible test case. NO confidence is also low (42) because Ozarox's 0\u20132 record and single-match sample carry noise. The gap reflects high uncertainty on BOTH sides, not a strong conviction in either direction. RESOLUTION RISK MINIMAL: Match is scheduled in-time; no forfeit/walkover risk mentioned. Official resolution via gol.gg is straightforward. Uncertainty is purely competitive, not administrative.", "key_factor": "Ozarox's 0\u20132 loss to Misa Esports was a one-off mental collapse or meta misalignment; they have now recovered mentally and are piloting a champion pool that directly counters PCIFIC's signature ban/pick patterns (Jayce, Rumble, Kaisa), while PCIFIC's confidence from the Boostgate stomp leads to overconfidence and predictable draft choices."}], "final_score": 0.5355191248430922, "no_score": 0.4859747707651202, "edge": 0.3059090909090909, "no_edge": 0.07590909090909093, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 53.55% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 43.57% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1967187", "question": "LoL: PCIFIC  vs Ozarox Esports (BO3) - TCL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between PCIFIC  and Ozarox Esports in the TCL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"PCIFIC \" if PCIFIC  win the match against Ozarox Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ozarox Esports\" if Ozarox Esports win the match against PCIFIC .\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.385, "volume_usd": 8266.671772000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["15095148867420094626863077211631648190735468133429403694651465123326924476838", "67498062138406875503618255270412210993158133335725669962858855681351951186386"], "sport