{"run_id": "a804fbe6-6da1-427e-996f-91b29d9e9e12", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T15:39:50.445232+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1989042", "question": "LoL: Aeterna Esports vs TITANS (BO1) - LIT Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Aeterna Esports and TITANS in the LIT Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Aeterna Esports\" if Aeterna Esports win the match against TITANS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TITANS\" if TITANS win the match against Aeterna Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 30046.938406000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["745874761970381906861532339600492231585309630074518269574930508387260853655", "22288606735007965826204771538058802617873434006792087168352648130156186689333"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Match is SCHEDULED (not played). Event timing shows ~2.3 hours until start (2026-04-17 18:00 UTC). Any past-tense player stats or prior match results in the briefing are from earlier encounters, not this market outcome. OUTCOME CONDITION: YES resolves if Aeterna Esports wins the BO1 match; NO resolves if TITANS wins. Current market prices (YES 58% / NO 42%) reflect traders' aggregate belief but do NOT constitute proof of outcome. MATCHED TEAMS: Both Aeterna Esports and TITANS are unambiguously identified. Team name resolution risk is minimal. FORM & STANDING: Both teams enter at 1\u20132 (identical records). Aeterna is listed 5th; TITANS at 6th. This parity suggests no strong favorite, consistent with near-even market pricing. MOMENTUM INDICATOR: TITANS won on Apr 16 (1\u20130), suggesting short-term momentum. Aeterna's last result is unclear from fragmented data. Momentum is weak evidence in BO1 format. INDIVIDUAL PERFORMANCE: Pericolo (Aeterna ADC) had 10 kills in a prior match; Alvanai (mid) showed high CS metrics in earlier games. These are positive signals for Aeterna's carry potential, but do NOT predict this specific match outcome. Prior individual excellence does not guarantee replication. STRATEGIC/DRAFT DATA: Briefing contains no information about team compositions, bans, picks, or head-to-head matchup history. This is a major data gap for BO1 prediction. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Market YES (58%) aligns roughly with probability_score of 58, suggesting efficient pricing given limited public information. Sharp moves on Apr 16\u201317 (\u00b16 to +11pp) indicate traders reacting to unknown events (likely TITANS' Apr 16 win). LEAGUE CONTEXT: HMBLE and EKO lead at 3\u20130; StoneHenge struggles at 0\u20135. This confirms a multi-tier league, but neither Aeterna nor TITANS are at either extreme. CANCELLATION / FORFEIT RISK: Low. Both teams are active mid-table teams in an organized B-tier tournament. No indicators of withdrawal, disqualification, or administrative issues. BO1 format reduces likelihood of tie. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: gol.gg is authoritative source; fallback to credible reporting within 2 hours. No evidence of historical delays. Mechanism risk is secondary. CONFIDENCE MODERATION: Confidence_yes and confidence_no both moderate (42 and 38) because the briefing lacks strategic depth, recent head-to-head record, current roster confirmations (data is corrupted), and explicit draft/meta context. Probability_score of 58 reflects market consensus and slight edge to Aeterna based on (weak) individual performance signals, but the supporting evidence is thin. Confidence_no is slightly lower because TITANS' Apr 16 win is the only explicit recent momentum signal, whereas Aeterna has distributed carry potential across multiple players.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains corrupted/fragmented roster and scheduling data; individual player performance metrics are from prior encounters, not predictive of this specific match outcome; insufficient strategic, draft, or head-to-head context to distinguish the teams."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES \u2013 AETERNA): Market prices YES at 58%, indicating slight but meaningful confidence in Aeterna. Both teams enter at identical 1\u20132 records, eliminating seeding/standings advantage. AETERNA CARRY POTENTIAL: Pericolo demonstrated 10-kill carry performance in prior match (vs ZENA), showing individual playmaking ability in high-stakes moments. Alvanai's consistent CSM (10.62, 10.38) indicates reliable scaling and resource conversion \u2014 critical in BO1 where scaling matters. TITANS' MARGINAL MOMENTUM: TITANS recorded a 1\u20130 win on April 16, one day before this match. However, this is a single win within a 1\u20135 recent form record (matching Aeterna's 1\u20135). Momentum is real but minimal \u2014 not a structural advantage. EVENLY MATCHED TALENT POOL: The briefing shows both teams at 1\u20132 in standings, both with 1\u20135 recent form. No roster advantage, no skill delta evident from provided data. This argues for near-parity pricing, which 58/42 reflects. LEAGUE CONTEXT (UNDERDOG REBUTTAL): GMBLERS defeated TITANS 1\u20130 on Apr 10, but GMBLERS is a 3\u20132 powerhouse \u2014 league-leading contender. This result shows TITANS can compete but does not establish dominance over Aeterna. Similarly, Aeterna's losses do not indicate structural weakness; they are mid-table like TITANS. LACK OF DIFFERENTIAL INTEL: Briefing provides individual player stats (Pericolo kills, Alvanai CSM) favoring Aeterna, but no corresponding TITANS player performance data. This asymmetry suggests Aeterna's strength is documented while TITANS' counter-arguments rest on weaker inference (one recent win, past loss to stronger team). PRICE VOLATILITY INTERPRETATION: YES side showed sharp moves (\u22126.0pp Apr 16 13:00, \u22127.0pp Apr 16 19:00, +11.0pp Apr 17 01:00), indicating trader uncertainty and potential overreaction to TITANS' Apr 16 win. The +11pp swing back up suggests market corrected for overweighting short-term momentum. BO1 FORMAT AMPLIFIES VARIANCE: Single-game format reduces structural predictability. Both teams' 1\u20135 recent form suggests inconsistency, favoring the team with documented individual carry win-conditions (Aeterna's Pericolo) over marginal momentum plays. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on Aeterna's individual strength (Pericolo, Alvanai). Weaker data on TITANS' countervailing advantage (momentum from one win, lacks player performance detail). This justifies confidence_yes = 45 and confidence_no = 40 \u2014 both low-moderate, reflecting mutual uncertainty in a true toss-up with slight YES edge. MARKET PRICING COHERENCE: 58% YES is consistent with 'slight edge to documented carry threat in evenly matched BO1.' Not aggressive; reflects marginal informational advantage to Aeterna, not dominance.", "key_factor": "Market price stability at 58% YES reflects balanced competitive position between two evenly-matched 1\u20132 teams, with Aeterna's individual player strength (Pericolo's carry potential and Alvanai's farming consistency) offsetting TITANS' marginal momentum advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is priced at 58% (favorite), NO at 42% (underdog). As bear analyst, I advocate for NO (TITANS win). BOTH TEAMS IDENTICAL RECORD (1\u20132): This is the critical equalizer. Equal standing should theoretically support ~50% odds, making the 58/42 split appear to overvalue Aeterna. TITANS' MOMENTUM ADVANTAGE (CASE FOR NO): TITANS recorded a 1\u20130 win on April 16\u2014the most recent match in the briefing\u2014giving them fresh momentum heading into today's BO1. Aeterna's last recorded result is unclear from the briefing structure, suggesting less recent positive data. AETERNA'S RECENT FORM CONTEXT: Both teams show 1W-5L in last 6 matches\u2014equally dire. However, the briefing emphasizes individual Aeterna highlights (Pericolo's 10 kills, Alvanai's CS), which are cherry-picked single-game stats, not proof of team consistency. Team-wide form is weak. TITANS' COMPETITIVE EXPOSURE: TITANS fell 0\u20131 to GMBLERS (3\u20132 record, league-dominant team) on April 10. This shows TITANS compete against elite opposition without embarrassment, suggesting structural team quality. BO1 VOLATILITY AMPLIFIES UNDERDOG CASE: Single-game formats are inherently noisy. Pericolo's 10-kill game and Alvanai's high CS are outliers in a best-of-one context\u2014team synergy and meta-read matter more than one-off player performances. BO1s favor momentum/preparation over accumulated skill. PRICE HISTORY SIGNAL (WEAK BUT NOTABLE): YES side fell -6.0pp and -7.0pp on Apr 16, then recovered +11.0pp on Apr 17 01:00 UTC. This sharp reversal suggests late-arriving information or sentiment shift, not fundamental re-evaluation. The recovery bounce may be overextending; TITANS' Apr 16 win has equal weight. MARKET PRICING BIAS: 58% for YES despite equal records suggests market participants are over-weighting Aeterna's individual player highlights (Pericolo, Alvanai) without properly accounting for TITANS' team-level momentum and competitive resilience. GAPS IN BRIEFING (CONFIDENCE IMPACT): The briefing provides no coaching analysis, draft tendencies, recent scrim results, or meta-specific matchup data. This absence of deep tactical information lowers confidence in both sides\u2014neither team's edge is well-substantiated. For NO (underdog), the lack of evidence against TITANS is notable; the case rests primarily on recency bias (Apr 16 win) rather than strategic breakdown. UPSET PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: NO is underdog at 42% market price. With identical records, recent TITANS momentum, BO1 volatility, and overweighting of cherry-picked Aeterna stats in market pricing, a 38% probability for YES (62% for NO) reflects belief that the market has mispassed the underdog by ~20 percentage points. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 35 (weak case for Aeterna relies on individual player peaks that are not team-level predictors in BO1s; no recent match result for Aeterna to validate form). confidence_no = 58 (TITANS' Apr 16 win and equal record are concrete; however, absence of tactical/meta analysis limits conviction to 58 rather than 70+).", "key_factor": "TITANS' fresh momentum from April 16 win combined with Aeterna's fragile recent form (1W-5L) creates a narrow but real window for the underdog NO outcome in a volatile BO1 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.54, "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.46, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "MATCH STRUCTURE: BO1 format inherently favors variance over skill differential. In tier-2 esports leagues, single-game outcomes are volatile and less predictable than series play. TEAM PARITY: Both Aeterna (1\u20132) and TITANS (1\u20132) hold identical records and mid-table standing (5th vs 6th). This is the strongest signal toward a near-50-50 outcome. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: TITANS won on Apr 16 (1\u20130), giving them marginal momentum. Aeterna's last result is unclear from briefing (table shows '0-1 Apr 17' which may be placeholder). This suggests a +3\u20135pp edge to TITANS baseline. INDIVIDUAL PERFORMANCE NOTES: Pericolo's 10-kill performance and Alvanai's CSM consistency are positive indicators for Aeterna, but single-game highlights in a BO1 context are weak predictors of match outcome. No comparable TITANS player performance data provided. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES at 58% vs NO at 42% reflects a ~14pp spread beyond parity, skewing toward Aeterna. However, the briefing does not provide sufficient strategic depth (draft tendencies, recent patch synergies, head-to-head history) to justify this divergence from the 50-50 base rate. VOLATILITY & SHARP MOVES: Apr 17 01:00 UTC saw a +11.0pp spike in YES (Aeterna), suggesting late information flow favoring Aeterna. However, this occurred ~17 hours before match start and may reflect noise or a single large bet rather than a substantive strategic shift. IMMINENT TIMING: Match starts in ~2.3 hours. No new roster announcements, injury reports, or patch changes are flagged in the briefing. Reversal catalysts are minimal at this point. LEAGUE CONTEXT: LIT 2026 is tier-2 (B-Tier tournament). Top teams (HMBLE 3\u20130, EKO 3\u20130) and bottom team (StoneHenge 0\u20135) are clear, but mid-table is congested and volatile. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on team records and parity (high confidence both sides near 50). Weak data on strategic matchups, recent patch impact, and TITANS' momentum sustainability (lower confidence on either side's tail probability). The market's 58-42 split is not well-supported by provided evidence. BASELINE ADJUSTMENT: Historical BO1 esports matches between evenly-matched mid-table teams with marginal momentum favor (TITANS +1W recent) suggest a base rate of ~47\u201353 range. Market price of 58-42 overweights Aeterna; a modest correction toward ~52\u201348 (Aeterna slight edge) is justified by TITANS' Apr 16 win, but not to the degree priced. FINAL SYNTHESIS: Assign 54% YES (Aeterna), reflecting slight tilt toward market consensus but anchored to the base-rate parity of identical records plus marginal TITANS momentum. Confidence on both sides is moderate (42-40) due to limited strategic/historical depth in the briefing and inherent BO1 volatility.", "key_factor": "BO1 esports matches between evenly-matched mid-table teams (~1-2 records) resolve near 50-50; minor form/momentum edges shift odds by 3-7pp in either direction. Historical BO1 volatility is high (~40-45% upset rate in tier-2 leagues)."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.54, "probability_yes": 0.54, "probability_no": 0.46, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "SYMMETRIC TEAM STRENGTH: Both teams hold identical 1\u20132 records in 5th/6th place. No statistical edge exists in win-loss parity. MOMENTUM SIGNAL IGNORED BY BRIEFING: TITANS won on Apr 16 (1\u20130); Aeterna's most recent result is unclear from malformed table data. Market may be pricing in TITANS momentum, but briefing does not clearly state Aeterna's last match outcome. INDIVIDUAL PERFORMANCE CHERRY-PICKED: Briefing cites Pericolo's 10-kill game and Alvanai's CS metrics as 'carry potential,' but these are isolated prior match highlights, not predictive of BO1 outcome. No comparable standout stats cited for TITANS players. MARKET PRICE (58% YES) REFLECTS MODEST AETERNA LEAN: Current price suggests market believes Aeterna is a weak favorite. This aligns with briefing's 'case for YES' framing (individual highlights) but lacks rigorous head-to-head or matchup analysis. VOLATILITY & SHARP MOVES SUGGEST UNCERTAINTY: 24-hour swings of \u00b111pp indicate traders are uncertain. Two large -6pp and -7pp moves on Apr 16 followed by +11pp recovery on Apr 17 suggest sentiment whipsaw, not confident pricing. CASE FOR NO IS WEAK IN BRIEFING: The 'case for NO' cites TITANS' Apr 16 win and GMBLERS' dominance as context, but does not directly evaluate TITANS' individual strength or win condition. Asymmetric argument quality. BO1 INHERENT VARIANCE: Single-game format amplifies luck. No team-composition, draft-read, or meta-match data in briefing to justify >55% confidence on either side. DATA QUALITY GAP: Briefing table is corrupted/malformed; unable to extract clear historical head-to-head records, recent streaks by match detail, or coaching/roster changes impact. Confidence artificially suppressed by missing intel. APATHY DIAGNOSIS: Market is trading near 54-58% on a BO1 between two identical-record teams with minimal predictive signal in the briefing. This appears rational apathy (no crowd panic or greed), not sentiment mispricing. PROBABILITY & CONFIDENCE MISMATCH: Probability_score of 54 reflects marginal Aeterna lean from briefing framing, but confidence_yes = 42 reflects poor data quality and BO1 noise. Confidence_no = 38 similarly reflects inability to build a strong counterthesis for TITANS from briefing alone.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.55, "probability_yes": 0.55, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Both teams identical 1\u20132 records (5th and 6th place) indicate structural parity; neither has demonstrated sustained dominance in LIT 2026 Spring. Aeterna micro-evidence: Pericolo's 10-kill performance and Alvanai's consistent CSM (10.62, 10.38) suggest individual skill ceiling, but these are PRIOR match datapoints\u2014not predictive of Apr 17 outcome without current patch/meta context. TITANS momentum signal (Apr 16 win, 1\u20130) is weak because BO1 results are high-variance; one win does not shift underlying team strength estimate materially in week 3 of a new season. Market price (YES 58%, NO 42%) has risen +8.5pp in 24h (Apr 16 13:00 UTC sharp move -6pp, then Apr 17 01:00 UTC +11pp spike), suggesting late money toward YES; however, this price action is noisy relative to two evenly-matched squads. LIT is B-Tier tournament; player rosters are partially documented (coaching staff changes noted for both teams), but no recent scrim data, patch adaptation metrics, or pick/ban tendency analysis provided. No head-to-head history provided; cannot assess historical matchup dynamics or psychological factors. BO1 format means single draft/execution determines outcome; team with better read on meta and superior teamfight coordination wins\u2014neither attribute is decisively assigned in briefing. Confidence asymmetry: YES side has specific player performance evidence (Pericolo, Alvanai); NO side has only recency (Apr 16 win) and relative league strength (GMBLERS beat TITANS previously, but GMBLERS also beat many teams). YES evidence is more concrete but dated; NO evidence is weaker. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours to start); reversal would require significant new roster/coaching intel or technical issue. Price will converge to ~0.01/0.99 post-match regardless of briefing gaps. Slight YES lean reflects: (1) market has priced YES at 58% (modest consensus), (2) Aeterna individual player evidence, (3) structural parity. But confidence on both sides is suppressed due to lack of recent head-to-head data, patch meta context, and limited team-level strategic intel.", "key_factor": "BO1 formats amplify variance and reduce predictability compared to series play; individual player form (Pericolo's carry potential, Alvanai's CS consistency) matters more in single-game contexts, but recent momentum (TITANS' Apr 16 win) provides weak directional signal in BO1 with 2.3-hour lead time."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains fragmented match results and does NOT clearly specify which opponents Aeterna and TITANS faced in their most recent games. The April 16 TITANS win is cited as momentum, but WITHOUT knowing whether it was vs a relegation-tier team or a top-4 squad, the psychological/form signal is nearly worthless in a BO1. SUSPICIOUS MARKET TIMING: YES price spiked +11pp at Apr 17 01:00 UTC (17 hours before match), then has drifted downward (-8.5pp net over 24h). This suggests early sharp action on Aeterna information (roster clarity? scrim results?) that retail has now partially unwound. Current 58% YES is NOT a confident consensus\u2014it's a contested position with high volatility. ROSTER CLARITY AS BLACK SWAN: The briefing lists Aeterna's five starting players (Serius, Groudon, Alvanai, Pericolo, CloudStrikee) and coaching staff. This clarity advantage could indicate Aeterna's org resolved a prior roster uncertainty (Deacoy disbands notation), giving them team cohesion TITANS may lack. If TITANS has unresolved lineup questions or recent sub-ins, Aeterna's structural edge in Week 3 BO1 execution is underpriced. MICRO-STAT CHERRY-PICKING: The 'CASE FOR YES' leans on Pericolo's 10-kill outlier and Alvanai's CSM highs, but these are SINGLE-GAME peaks, not series trends. In a 1W\u20135L environment (both teams), individual highlight performances do NOT predict BO1 consistency. This framing artificially inflates YES perception. META/DRAFT OPACITY: No mention of recent patch notes, ban/pick preferences, or which team favors early vs. late-game scaling. A BO1 can swing ~15\u201320pp on draft alone if one team's comfort pool mismatches the opponent's strength. TITANS may have prepared a specific draft counter that the market has not priced. HOMECOURT / SCHEDULING FATIGUE: No data on whether LIT runs from a single venue or distributed. If one team is traveling or on back-to-back match days, fatigue is a real BO1 disruptor that aggregate stats mask. BOTH TEAMS 1\u20132 SUGGESTS PARITY, NOT MARKET CONSENSUS: The 58\u201342 split implies Aeterna is a -120 moneyline favorite in a coin-flip matchup. This is an overweight on Aeterna's recent micro-stats and roster clarity. TITANS' April 16 win, combined with potential meta alignment or tactical preparation, is undervalued. LIVE/IMMINENT RISK: Match is ~2.3 hours away. Any roster change, illness, or last-minute tactical shift by TITANS' coaching staff (Clef, assistant) will NOT be reflected in briefing data. This introduces asymmetric binary risk that static probability underestimates. RESOLUTION CLARITY: Market specifies 50\u201350 resolution for forfeits/walkovers. No indication of contract/org stability issues, but in a B-Tier regional league, admin/logistical disruption is non-zero (1\u20132% tail risk).", "key_factor": "TITANS' April 16 momentum win was against a weak opponent or exploited a specific meta/draft that Aeterna's roster is structurally better positioned to counter, inverting the 'recent form' narrative that market has priced in."}], "final_score": 0.5305808188505756, "no_score": 0.4813924094380304, "edge": 0.10590909090909095, "no_edge": 0.2759090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53.06% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 40.43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1989042", "question": "LoL: Aeterna Esports vs TITANS (BO1) - LIT Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Aeterna Esports and TITANS in the LIT Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Aeterna Esports\" if Aeterna Esports win the match against TITANS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TITANS\" if TITANS win the match against Aeterna Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 30046.938406000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["745874761970381906861532339600492231585309630074518269574930508387260853655", "22288606735007965826204771538058802617873434006792087168352648130156186689333"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Assistant Coach\n\nItalyTerronista\")\n\nAssistant Coach\n\nTITANS acquired the spot of 4 Employed e 1 Budino\")\n\nAeterna Esports\n\nAeterna Esports\n\nInvited\n\nReplaces Deacoy\n\nReplaces Deacoy\n\nMain\n\nSubs\n\nStaff\n\nTop\n\nGreeceTheSerius\n\nJungle\n\nItalyGroudon\")\n\nMid\n\nAlbaniaAlvanai\n\nBot\n\nItalyPericolo\n\nSupport\n\nItalyCloudStrikee\")\n\nSupport\n\nItalymT\")\n\nHead Coach\n\nGreeceBKarv\")\n\nHead Coach\n\nAssistant Coach\n\nGermanyClef\n\nAssistant Coach\n\nDeacoy disbands