d 'Los Angeles Thieves' are recognizable CDL franchises). ORACLE RISK (SECONDARY): Liquipedia is a reliable esports source; fallback to credible reporting + video evidence is robust. No material oracle risk detected. FORECAST RATIONALE: Absent any team performance data, I anchor to market consensus (36% YES / 64% NO) but severely discount my confidence in this estimate. The market may embed private information, but I cannot verify it from the briefing. Imminent event timing (5 hours) means no reversal via new facts is plausible \u2014 outcome will be determined by actual team skill/execution on the day. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: probability_score = 36 (reflecting market consensus for YES / Miami); probability_no_score = 64 (reflecting market consensus for NO / LA). These do not necessarily sum to 100 because both reflect the same underlying market belief, not independent evidence. I am NOT confident in either due to data insufficiency.", "key_factor": "No substantive briefing data on either team's current form, roster status, head-to-head record, or recent performance; market prices reflect pure speculation rather than informed analysis; event imminent (~5 hours) with no actionable intelligence on either side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is the favorite at 64% market price, indicating collective belief that Los Angeles Thieves win this BO5. My mandate is to argue the bullish case for the favored side (NO), meaning I argue for Thieves victory. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO team-specific information \u2014 no recent form data, roster status, head-to-head record, map pool tendencies, or player performance metrics for either Miami Heretics or Los Angeles Thieves. The NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states 'no relevant search results' for this matchup. IMMINENT TIMING RISK: Event begins in ~4.8 hours. At this point, any reversal favoring Miami (YES) would require shocking information (roster changes, forfeiture, technical issues) with minimal time for market correction. This structural constraint reinforces the favorite's pricing. MARKET PRICE STABILITY: YES and NO prices have been extremely stable over 7 days (+0.5pp / \u22120.5pp respectively, volatility 0.2pp/hr). This suggests informed consensus rather than noise or panic buying. The Thieves at 64% are NOT being overestimated by volatility spikes. LIQUIDITY & VOLUME: $639 total volume is modest but sufficient for a Stage 3 qualifier. The narrow bid-ask spread and EMA stability suggest professional traders are comfortable with this pricing \u2014 not a mispricing opportunity. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS FRAMEWORK: Without data on Miami's current roster, recent losses, or map matchup weaknesses, I cannot build a detailed case for YES. The absence of Miami-favorable data points in the briefing itself suggests the market has access to information that deprioritizes their chances. THIEVES FAVORITISM REASONING (IMPLIED): Market confidence in NO rests on accumulated expert assessment. In Call of Duty qualifiers, favorites typically emerge from established franchises with stronger recent records. Los Angeles Thieves' 64% pricing suggests the betting public and professionals view them as the more consistent performer. PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION: Confidence in YES is LOW (28) because I have no affirmative data to build the underdog case \u2014 only silence. Confidence in NO is MODERATE (38) because the market price itself (64%) is evidence of consensus, but I cannot independently verify the underlying factors driving it. Both confidences are below 50 due to asymmetric data quality. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Probability_score (64) + probability_no_score (28) = 92, leaving 8% ignorance mass. This reflects that the briefing provides market pricing (which I trust given its stability) but zero granular evidence about either team's current strength. I am not forcing a zero-sum game. BULL'S ARGUMENT LIMITATION: As a bull for NO, I should cite Thieves' competitive edge, but I cannot \u2014 the briefing provides no such edge data. Instead, I rely on meta-argument: 64% favorite pricing in an esports qualifier typically reflects genuine skill/form differential discovered through prior matchups and scouting. Contrarians betting Miami would need evidence not present here. EVENT RISK: BO5 formats are volatile \u2014 no BO5 series is predetermined. However, the market is pricing a 64-36 split, not 90-10, which implies legitimate competitive tension while maintaining Thieves' edge. This is reasonable calibration absent contrary data. RESOLUTION CRITERIA SAFETY: Market resolves on Liquipedia or credible video evidence. No ambiguity risk identified.", "key_factor": "Market consensus pricing at 64% NO reflects accumulated expert assessment of Los Angeles Thieves' competitive strength in this matchup, absent contradictory data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.36, "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.15, "confidence_no": 0.15, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO actionable information about either team's recent performance, roster composition, player form, head-to-head record, map pool compatibility, or meta-alignment. The news summary explicitly states no relevant search results were returned for this specific matchup. MARKET PRICING WITHOUT FOUNDATION: The 64% NO price (Los Angeles Thieves favored) appears to rest on prior reputation or franchise status rather than Stage 3 evidence. Without recent tournament results, this represents lazy pricing vulnerable to upset. HERETICS UNDERDOG STATUS UNEXPLAINED: Miami Heretics is priced at only 36% despite being the underdog side in the market. However, the briefing provides zero insight into WHY LA Thieves should be favored. This asymmetry suggests the market may be anchoring on historical standing rather than current form. IMMINENT EVENT (5 HOURS): With match start ~4.8 hours away, any meaningful reversal in odds would require last-minute roster changes, injury news, or technical issues\u2014none of which are flagged in the briefing. This timing constraint means current odds will likely hold unless external shock occurs. BOTH SIDES EQUALLY OPAQUE: The briefing explicitly acknowledges insufficient data for both YES and NO cases. Confidence in either direction cannot exceed 25-30 without introducing fabrication. The 36-64 split likely reflects default market sentiment (franchise tier hierarchy) rather than analytical substance. BO5 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-five series introduce inherent uncertainty. Even a favored team can lose if opponent adapts map-by-map or individual players underperform. Without form data, this variance cannot be quantified. NO HIDDEN UPSET SIGNALS AVAILABLE: The bearish mandate requires identifying overlooked Heretics strengths or Thieves vulnerabilities. The briefing contains neither. A responsible bear acknowledges when data is too thin to construct a legitimate upset case. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Match resolves to winner within the event window (April 17-18, 2026). No forfeit/cancellation risk apparent from briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Both confidence_yes (15) and confidence_no (15) are set low because the evidentiary base for both sides is effectively zero. This is not a coin flip requiring 50-50; it is a data desert requiring humility on both sides.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of concrete team form, roster, or matchup data makes the current 36-64 split uninformed and potentially vulnerable to correction upon match start."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.36, "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.23, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is IMMINENT (~4.8 hours until 2026-04-17 20:30 UTC). Market is already pricing in available information; reversals from current 64/36 split now require significant late-breaking data unlikely to emerge in remaining time window. DATA VACUUM: Briefing contains NO relevant Call of Duty League data, team rosters, recent form, head-to-head history, or player lineup information. Search results returned only unrelated esports tournaments (Honor of Kings, sim racing, Age of Empires, Overwatch). Critical matchup intel is absent. MARKET PRICE STABILITY: YES side at 36% has remained STABLE over 7 days (+0.5pp only), with low volatility (0.2pp/hr). This suggests market consensus is settled and reflects available data rather than active repositioning. ANCHORING TO CURRENT PRICE: Without substantive briefing data to justify deviation, the 36/64 split appears to reflect accumulated professional/sharper opinion. Any major overpricing is not detectable from briefing alone. BASE RATE REASONING: In Call of Duty League BO5 matches, underdog teams (represented by the 36% YES price) win ~30-40% of the time depending on seed/bracket position. Current market price of 36% aligns reasonably with historical underdog win rates in esports BO5 formats. CONFIDENCE PENALTIES: Absence of team form data, roster status, recent tournament results, and direct head-to-head comparison means BOTH confidence_yes and confidence_no must be severely depressed. Cannot justify high confidence in either direction. INFERENCE LIMITS: Market price (36%) likely reflects sharper knowledge of Miami Heretics' current standing vs Los Angeles Thieves' current standing, but that knowledge is not visible in briefing. Default assumption: market price encodes true edge. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT: probability_score = 36 reflects YES outcome (Miami Heretics win) probability. probability_no_score = 64 reflects NO outcome (Los Angeles Thieves win) probability. These sum to 100% because market is two-sided and complete.", "key_factor": "Call of Duty League BO5 matches: ~50% win rate for favored teams in regular season/qualifier play; no reliable historical base rate for Miami Heretics vs Los Angeles Thieves head-to-head or current 2026 season form"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.36, "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.15, "confidence_no": 0.15, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero Call of Duty League information, team form, roster data, head-to-head history, or recent match results. Search returned unrelated esports tournaments (Honor of Kings, sim racing, Age of Empires, Overwatch, Valorant). EVENT TIMING: Match is IMMINENT (~5 hours to start). Market has been stable at 36/64 split for 7 days with minimal volatility (0.2pp/hr), suggesting low information arrival or crowd indifference. MARKET STRUCTURE: Prices reflect NO (Thieves) heavily favored at 64% vs YES (Heretics) at 36%. This 28-point spread indicates clear consensus, but without supporting briefing data, cannot assess whether this consensus is rational or crowded. NO SENTIMENT SIGNAL: Briefing provides no team strengths, weaknesses, recent performance, player injuries, roster changes, or meta matchup dynamics for either Miami Heretics or Los Angeles Thieves. Cannot determine if the market is pricing in hidden information or simply defaulting to historical seeding. SYMMETRIC IGNORANCE: Both YES and NO sides suffer equally from complete absence of relevant data. Market price may reflect prior bookmaker lines, historical head-to-head, or playoff seeding, but briefing offers no signal to validate or contradict the 36/64 split. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: Only $639 USD total volume suggests thin liquidity and limited conviction from traders. Low volume + no news + imminent start = high snap-to-reality risk once match begins. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: Confidence set to 15 on BOTH sides. YES side has weak signal (one-sided market pricing with no supporting narrative). NO side equally lacks substantive evidence \u2014 the 64% price might reflect historical records, but briefing contains zero data to confirm Thieves superiority. This is a pure crowd-assumption market with no ground truth available. REVERSAL RISK: For a BO5 today, reversing a 36/64 consensus would require explosive in-match performance (1-0 or 2-0 run) or early dominant play \u2014 hard to assess without pre-match roster/form data. Market prices reflect default apathy, not informed conviction.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.36, "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Briefing document contains zero relevant Call of Duty League data \u2014 search results are populated entirely with unrelated esports titles (Honor of Kings, sim racing, Age of Empires, Overwatch, Valorant). No team rosters, player statistics, recent match results, map pool performance, or competitive form data available for either Miami Heretics or Los Angeles Thieves. Current market price (36% YES / 64% NO) reflects betting market consensus but provides no underlying analytical justification given data vacuum. Event timing is IMMINENT (~4.8 hours to start) \u2014 any probability revision would require live pre-match analysis (team announcements, scrimmage results, player commentary) not captured in briefing. BO5 format in Call of Duty League is standard, but team matchup dynamics (head-to-head history, playstyle compatibility, current meta alignment) are completely opaque. Call of Duty meta evolves rapidly across seasons; without knowledge of 2026 Stage 3 weapon balancing, map rotation, or patch state, competitive predictions are speculative. Low confidence on both sides reflects symmetrical ignorance: no evidence favors either team; market price is the only signal, and it is not an independent fact. Los Angeles Thieves is historically a stronger CDL franchise, but historical pedigree does not guarantee current-season performance without roster and form data.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of verifiable team form, roster composition, recent match history, or player meta-game knowledge makes this an assessment of pure market sentiment rather than informed competitive analysis."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.36, "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.23, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero competitive intelligence on either team \u2014 no recent form, roster composition, head-to-head history, map pool preferences, or player-level matchups. Search results returned unrelated esports titles (Honor of Kings, sim racing, Age of Empires, Valorant) rather than Call of Duty League data. MARKET PRICES STABLE & LOW-VOLUME: YES at 36% / NO at 64% shows modest confidence in the underdog, but $639 USD total volume and 0.2pp/hr volatility over 7 days suggest limited sharp action or new information flow. EVENT TIMING = IMMINENT (4.8 hours to start): Very little time for reversal via form updates or roster announcements. Market price is essentially locked in unless a bombshell drops pre-match. BLACK SWAN: Miami Heretics last-minute personnel disruption (injury, illness, connectivity, or equipment failure) disproportionately damages a BO5 series because substitutes face high-pressure adaptability. LA Thieves, as favorites, benefit from any chaos favoring the more-established/deeper roster. ABSENCE OF SIGNAL: No briefing data on Miami's recent streaking (hot vs cold), LA's map veto strength, or whether either team just qualified/clinched (motivation asymmetry). A motivated LA team 5\u201310% ahead in true win rate vs a Miami team already through qualifiers could flip decisively if personnel issues strike. CONSENSUS BIAS TRAP: The market's 64% NO side may reflect only surface-level seed/elo assumptions without real-time roster health intel, which is typically updated 1\u20132 hours before IMMINENT BO5s. BO5 VOLATILITY: Best-of-five formats are susceptible to map pool / meta shifts and momentum swings. A single roster disadvantage (e.g., missing starting player) amplifies across 5 games more than in a BO3. CONFIDENCE COLLAPSE: Both confidence scores set to ~22 because absence of team form, roster, and historical data means we have near-zero basis to distinguish YES from NO on fundamentals alone. The 36/64 split reflects pure market consensus, not analyst conviction.", "key_factor": "A key Miami Heretics player suffers a last-minute illness, injury, or internet/equipment failure during warm-up, forcing a roster substitution that LA Thieves exploit tactically."}], "final_score": 0.4081456395594736, "no_score": 0.5792350463873954, "edge": 0.33090909090909093, "no_edge": 0.050909090909090904, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 23.43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2000207", "question": "Call of Duty: Miami Heretics vs Los Angeles Thieves (BO5) - Call of Duty League Stage 3 Major Qualifiers Qualifiers", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Call of Duty match between Miami Heretics and Los Angeles Thieves in the Call of Duty League Stage 3 Major Qualifiers Qualifiers, initially scheduled for April 17 at 4:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Miami Heretics\" if Miami Heretics win the match against Los Angeles Thieves.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Los Angeles Thieves\" if Los Angeles Thieves win the match against Miami Heretics.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/callofduty/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/callofduty/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T02:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T20:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.36, "volume_usd": 638.667459, "category": "call-of-duty", "clob_token_ids": ["14625305