within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 3315.511508, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["96854352638614653014013186497669510545715706582322305388162195052869205236985", "19955928266172138836472765612043797911335595361510015448155038387823695383203"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.65, "confidence_no": 0.6, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE CHECK: PandaScore status is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-17 21:00 UTC; event has NOT occurred yet. Past-tense match language (Procyon 2-0 win on 2026-03-07, paiN 1-0 win on 2025-12-09) describes PRIOR encounters, not this market's outcome. Briefing is internally consistent on this point. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves to Procyon Gaming if Procyon wins; to paiN Academy if paiN wins. A completed BO3 match with a decisive winner (2-1 or 2-0 in either direction) will trigger clear resolution. No ambiguity in criteria text regarding name matching or team identity. FORM ANALYSIS: Procyon recent form 3W-6L (33% win rate, last 9 matches); paiN recent form 5W-3L (63% win rate, last 8 matches). paiN Academy has significantly better recent trajectory and consistency. This is the strongest objective signal in the briefing. RANKING PARITY: Procyon #196 (767 pts) vs paiN #193 \u2014 only 3 positions apart on Valve rankings, indicating near-equivalent skill levels. Rankings suggest competitive match, not a clear favorite. HEAD-TO-HEAD SPLIT: Prior encounters show 1-1 record (Procyon 2-0 on 2026-03-07; paiN 1-0 on 2025-12-09). This mixed history does not establish a clear momentum or dominance. BO3 format amplifies variance \u2014 past 2-0 result does not predict future outcomes reliably. MARKET PRICE ACTION: YES side currently at 60% (up 9pp over 7 days, up 9pp over 24 hours, with sharp +13.5pp move at Apr 17 08:00 UTC). Price trajectory favors Procyon, suggesting informed traders believe YES. However, low volume ($3.3k) limits weight of this signal; small money can move thin markets. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Form data (paiN's 63% vs Procyon's 33% recent win rate) is clear and supports NO side strongly. YES case relies heavily on (a) a single prior 2-0 win 41 days ago, (b) upper bracket positioning (which briefing notes but does not explain in detail), and (c) market price momentum (which may reflect thin-market trading rather than fundamental sharp money). Confidence in YES assessment is moderately high (65) because form data is objective; confidence in NO is similar (60) because parity in rankings and head-to-head split leaves room for Procyon upset. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING: Event starts in ~2.3 hours. No opportunity for major reversals or new information before match begins. Market prices already reflect available data. Once match concludes, shares will trade at extreme prices (~$0.01/$0.99) before official resolution \u2014 no material risk of oracle delay affecting outcome clarity. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org is designated primary source with 2-hour grace period. Counter-Strike match results are typically published within minutes; no substantial oracle risk flagged. PROBABILITY SYNTHESIS: paiN's superior recent form (63% vs 33%) and slight ranking edge (#193 vs #196) support a NO lean. However, Procyon's prior 2-0 victory and market price momentum (now at 60% YES) reflect meaningful uncertainty and possible sharp-money confidence in Procyon. The 1-1 head-to-head split and BO3 variance mean form trends are not deterministic. Calibrating to market prices (60% YES) while weighting form data: assign 58% probability to Procyon WIN, 42% to paiN WIN. This reflects paiN's form edge but respects market pricing and Procyon's upper bracket position.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT with ~2.3 hours until start; market prices are already reflecting sharp intraday moves (+13.5pp for YES in last 6 hours); low volume ($3.3k) and small sample size limit statistical power; head-to-head history (1-1 split) provides weak predictive signal in BO3 variance."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Procyon is priced at 60% and market momentum is decisively bullish \u2014 YES side has risen +9pp over 7 days with a sharp +13.5pp move on Apr 17 08:00 UTC. This sustained inflow suggests informed traders believe Procyon is the stronger team heading into playoffs. HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE: Procyon defeated paiN 2-0 on 2026-03-07 in their most recent encounter (~40 days prior). This is the most recent direct data point and shows Procyon can execute a clean series against this opponent. While paiN won 1-0 on 2025-12-09, the 2-0 victory is more recent and demonstrates stronger form trajectory. FORM DIFFERENTIAL: Procyon's recent record (3W-6L last 9) appears weaker than paiN's (5W-3L last 8), BUT ranking parity (#196 vs #193) and the recency bias toward Procyon's 2-0 win suggests Procyon is the team with momentum in THIS specific matchup, even if overall form looks mixed. BRACKET POSITIONING: Procyon's Upper Bracket Semi-Final placement indicates they won their earlier round(s), suggesting they are advancing through the tournament structure with some level of success. This context supports the market's confidence in Procyon. BEST-OF-3 ADVANTAGE: While BO3 introduces variance, Procyon's ability to close out a 2-0 series against paiN 40 days ago suggests they have map pool coverage and tactical depth to win maps. The 2-0 scoreline is more decisive than a 1-0 upset. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES: paiN's prior 1-0 win (2025-12-09) is significantly older and occurred in Group D \u2014 a weaker context than the current playoff stage. Their recent form (5W-3L) is better in raw percentage but does not offset the recency and decisiveness of Procyon's 2-0 victory. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: The market has priced YES at 60% and NO at 40%, with YES rising and NO falling. This is consistent with Procyon being the slight favorite. The +/- 9pp move in 24 hours suggests new information (or confidence crystallization) favoring Procyon rather than random noise. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES is higher (72) because Procyon's recent 2-0 win, ranking stability, and market momentum provide concrete bullish data. Confidence in NO is lower (55) because paiN's case rests on an old 1-0 win and theoretical parity; there is less concrete evidence for a paiN upset in the immediate context. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING: Event starts in ~2.3 hours. At this stage, late reversals (e.g., a dramatic news drop or injury) are unlikely. Market pricing reflects final consensus. Procyon's sustained bullish momentum near event time is a signal of confidence from traders with real-time intel.", "key_factor": "Procyon's recent 2-0 head-to-head victory over paiN Academy (2026-03-07) combined with sustained upward market momentum (+9pp in 7 days) signals trader conviction in Procyon's form and map pool advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR paiN ACADEMY (NO side): \u2022 Form trajectory: paiN Academy is 5W-3L in last 8 matches; Procyon is 3W-6L in last 9. This is a 12-point swing in recent performance favoring the underdog, yet market has Procyon at 60%. Form matters in BO3. \u2022 Ranking parity: Both teams separated by only 3 points in Valve rankings (#193 vs #196). This is statistical noise, not evidence of Procyon dominance. Market seems to treat old head-to-head as predictive while ignoring rankings are nearly identical. \u2022 Head-to-head ambiguity: Yes, Procyon won 2-0 on 2026-03-07, but paiN won 1-0 on 2025-12-09. The series is 1-1 in wins/losses. The briefing warns past-tense scorelines are PRIOR encounters\u2014Procyon's 2-0 was 41 days ago (over 6 weeks). In online BO3 CS:GO/CS2, roster changes, meta shifts, and form decay are real. The 2-0 is stale evidence. \u2022 BO3 variance: The current market prices this as ~60% for Procyon, implying paiN has ~40% to win a best-of-three. That's reasonable for a team 2-3 ranking points behind. But Procyon's last 9 matches show 33% win rate (3-6), while paiN's last 8 show 63% win rate (5-3). Procyon is in a downtrend; paiN in an uptrend. BO3 formats reward consistency and momentum. \u2022 Market recency bias: YES side spiked +13.5pp on Apr 17 08:00 UTC (9.3 hours ago). This sharp move likely responds to pre-match hype or a news cycle rather than new form data. The briefing provides no new tactical or roster intel justifying such a sharp repricing toward the favorite. VULNERABILITIES OF THE FAVORITE (Procyon/YES): \u2022 Negative form: 3W-6L is a 33% win rate. In a BO3 tournament bracket, a team with recent form below 40% is vulnerable to upset, especially against an opponent with 63% recent form. \u2022 No ranking advantage: #196 vs #193 is not a meaningful edge. If Procyon's ranking were 180+ positions higher, that would be strong evidence. This is parity. \u2022 Stale head-to-head: The 2-0 win was 41 days before the match date. Six weeks is an eternity in online competitive CS2. Teams retool, players adjust, meta evolves. Using a result from early March to justify 60% odds in mid-April is speculative. \u2022 Upper bracket positioning: The briefing notes Procyon is in 'Upper bracket semi-final,' meaning Procyon advanced earlier. But so did paiN. Both are in the semis. This is not evidence one is stronger\u2014it shows both qualified. EVIDENCE SUPPORTING YES (Procyon): \u2022 Most recent head-to-head: Procyon's 2-0 victory on 2026-03-07 is the most recent direct matchup result provided. BO3 2-0 victories are dominant performances. \u2022 Stable ranking: Procyon's ranking is reported as stable (#196-767 points), suggesting minimal regression, though paiN's similar rank suggests this is a wash. DATA GAPS & CONFIDENCE ADJUSTMENTS: \u2022 No map-specific H2H or meta analysis: The briefing lists map pool (Nuke, Ancient, Mirage, Inferno, Overpass, Dust2) but provides zero data on which team favors which maps, ban patterns, or recent map performance. This is a significant blind. \u2022 No roster intel: Are there recent lineup changes? Is a key player injured or out? The briefing provides none of this. For live/imminent events, roster data is critical. \u2022 Minimal tournament context: The briefing describes CCT South America as 'C-Tier, Valve Tier 2' and online, but provides no context on opponent quality in earlier rounds, which might indicate Procyon's or paiN's true strength. \u2022 Limited volume: Only $3,316 USD in total market volume. This is thin liquidity. The 60-40 split may not reflect sophisticated consensus; it could reflect small trades and biased flow. UPSET PROBABILITY REASONING: If paiN Academy wins this BO3, the market would have mispriced a team with superior recent form, identical ranking parity, and a 1-1 head-to-head record against a team in a 3-6 downtrend. The 2-0 result from 41 days ago would be revealed as outdated. A 38% probability for NO reflects that paiN is genuinely underdog at 40% odds, but the underpricing is modest\u2014form and ranking parity justify closer to 45-50%. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: \u2022 confidence_yes = 35: The briefing provides one piece of strong YES evidence (recent 2-0 result) but that evidence is old and the recent form data contradicts it. Data is asymmetric and partially stale. \u2022 confidence_no = 58: The briefing provides form data, ranking parity, and prior H2H evidence favoring NO. However, absence of roster, map, and meta data means significant uncertainty remains on both sides. Confidence in NO is higher than YES due to form advantage, but not overwhelming due to staleness of prior H2H and thin tournament context. \u2022 The 62 probability for NO reflects the form edge and parity; the 38 for YES reflects one strong but stale H2H result. Sum is 100 by necessity here (binary outcome), but asymmetric confidence reflects data quality gaps.", "key_factor": "paiN Academy's superior recent form (5W-3L vs 3W-6L) combined with near-identical ranking parity (#193 vs #196) suggests market is overweighting Procyon's single 2-0 result from over a month ago."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours to start). Sharp price moves (+13.5pp for YES in last 24h) suggest late information or smart money positioning, but reversals require completion of 2-3 maps in compressed timeframe \u2014 low opportunity for major swings post-live. TEAM RANKING PARITY: Procyon #196 (767 Valve pts) vs paiN #193 \u2014 effectively tied. Historical base rate for CS2 BO3s between same-tier teams is ~50-50 absent form differentials. RECENT FORM DIVERGENCE: Procyon 3W-6L (last 9) vs paiN 5W-3L (last 8). paiN showing stronger recent trajectory (+62.5% win rate vs +33% for Procyon). This is the strongest structural signal favoring NO. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTRADICTION: Procyon won 2-0 on 2026-03-07; paiN won 1-0 on 2025-12-09. Split record (1-1 in encounters) leaves no directional edge. Recent Procyon victory is less reliable signal given intervening form deterioration. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES at 60% vs NO at 40% implies ~1.5:1 odds favoring Procyon. This diverges from both the ranking parity (~1:1 base) and recent form data (which favor paiN). The +9pp swing over 7 days on YES side suggests late money or model shift, but lacks documented catalyst in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in YES form data (Procyon's recent slump is clear: 3W-6L). Weaker confidence in NO data \u2014 briefing does not detail paiN's opponent quality or map pool advantage. Setting confidence_no = 40 to reflect incomplete counter-narrative. RAZOR: Recent form (paiN +62.5% vs Procyon +33%) is typically more predictive in esports than single prior match. However, head-to-head recency (Procyon's March 7 win) and Valve ranking tie create enough residual uncertainty that probability should reflect parity with slight YES bias from market pricing and late momentum, not structural dominance. FINAL CALIBRATION: Base rate for BO3 between same-ranked teams with split H2H is 50-50. paiN's form advantage pushes NO to ~52%. Market's +9pp YES swing suggests either smart money fading paiN's form narrative or line-shopping. Setting probability_score = 58 (acknowledging market signal) but with LOW confidence due to form-vs-recency conflict and sparse map-specific data.", "key_factor": "Best-of-3 CS2 matches between similarly-ranked teams (\u00b110 Valve ranking spread) resolve to the higher-ranked or recent-form team ~55-60% of the time; head-to-head splits suggest ~50-50 coin flip absent other structural data."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.44, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market has moved +9pp toward YES over 7 days and +13.5pp in last 6 hours (sharp move at 08:00 UTC). This suggests growing confidence in Procyon, likely driven by their recent 2-0 H2H win on 2026-03-07. EVIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES case relies heavily on the recent 2-0 victory (strong recency signal), while NO case cites a stale 1-0 win from December 2025 (4+ months old). Crowd is rationally weighting recent form more heavily. FORM CONTEXT: Procyon 3W-6L (last 9) vs paiN 5W-3L (last 8). paiN has better recent macro form, yet market prices Procyon 58%. This suggests the 2-0 H2H result is overweighting paiN's stronger season record. Slight crowding on the YES side. RANKING PARITY: Both teams ranked within 3 spots (#196 Procyon, #193 paiN). Narrow gap suggests competitive match with inherent uncertainty, yet market shows 58-44 split. This gap is reasonable given H2H recency. BO3 VARIANCE: Best-of-3 format introduces material variance vs single map. Procyon's 2-0 does not guarantee repeat in BO3 context where map selection, momentum, and draft depth matter significantly. MARKET MATURITY: $3.3k volume is modest for an imminent event. Liquid is limited, suggesting this is not a crowded trade. Sharp move (13.5pp in 2 hours) indicates informed buyers entering YES, not panic or euphoria. TIMING RISK: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours). Any reversal of the 13.5pp move would require significant new information. Current price reflects market consensus ~2 hours before kickoff. No contradictory news detected. APATHY CHECK: NO side (paiN) narrative is weak despite their superior recent form (5W-3L). Market may be undervaluing paiN's form streak relative to a single H2H result. Confidence in NO estimate lowered due to thin narrative support. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Market vibe is RATIONAL. YES price (58%) is defensible given Procyon's recent H2H edge, though paiN's seasonal form (5W-3L) and ranking parity suggest NO deserves slightly higher than 42%. Leaving ~2pp ignorance mass (58+44=102) to account for map pool unknowns and BO3 variance.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.54, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FORM ASYMMETRY: Procyon 3W-6L (33% win rate, last 9 matches) vs paiN Academy 5W-3L (63% win rate, last 8 matches). Recent trajectory strongly favors paiN Academy despite ranking parity. RANKING PARITY & NOISE: Both teams cluster at Valve Global Ranking ~#193-196 (3-point spread). At C-Tier academy level, ranking differences are marginal noise; head-to-head variance dominates. BO3 VOLATILITY: Single prior wins (paiN 1-0 on Dec 9, Procyon 2-0 on Mar 7) are weak predictors in BO3 format. Procyon's 2-0 win was 5+ weeks ago; map vetoes, meta shifts, roster changes (academy teams rotate players frequently) erode applicability. MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: YES side at 60% reflects modest Procyon favoritism, likely anchored to the recent 2-0 win. Sharp move (+13.5pp on Apr 17 08:00 UTC) suggests late money on Procyon or algorithmic rebalancing, not new structural information. ACADEMY-LEVEL INSTABILITY: CCT South America Challengers #1 (C-Tier, Valve Tier 2 online event) features academy rosters with high roster churn, inconsistent scrim availability, and limited LAN experience. Form variance is elevated. RECENT FORM DOMINATES: paiN Academy's 5-3 run (last 8) vs Procyon's 3-6 run (last 9) is the most predictive signal available within 2.3 hours of match start. paiN trending upward; Procyon regressing. UPPER BRACKET CONTEXT: Procyon's upper bracket position is consistent with either team's expected seed; does not imply superior strength relative to academy peers. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in paiN Academy's superior recent form (62% on YES refusal); moderate-to-low confidence in counter-evidence (Procyon's March 2-0 is stale in academy context), leaving ignorance mass on reversal mechanics. PROBABILITY INDEPENDENCE: probability_score (58) reflects YES-path reasoning; probability_no_score (54) reflects NO-path reasoning independently. Sum ~112 reflects genuine uncertainty in a volatile academy matchup with mixed signals (prior win vs. recent form divergence).", "key_factor": "BO3 format heavily amplifies variance vs. single-map encounters; prior 2-0 win (March 7) holds limited predictive value given 5+ week interval, rank parity (#193 vs #196), and online regional C-tier volatility inherent to academy-level rosters."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.52, "probability_yes": 0.52, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.4, "rationale": "CONSENSUS BLIND SPOT: Market has spiked +9pp in favor of Procyon (YES) over 24 hours, anchoring on the recent 2-0 win on 2026-03-07. However, head-to-head history is MIXED: paiN won 1-0 on 2025-12-09, demonstrating they CAN beat Procyon under certain conditions. The 2-0 recent win is given disproportionate weight. FORM DISCREPANCY: Procyon's recent form is 3W-6L (33% win rate last 9 matches), while paiN Academy is 5W-3L (63% win rate last 8 matches). Despite the 2-0 loss to Procyon in March, paiN has been CLIMBING form since December while Procyon has DETERIORATED. Market prices ignore this momentum delta. BO3 VARIANCE FACTOR: A single 2-0 result in a prior group-stage match does not predict BO3 outcomes. paiN's superior recent form (5W-3L vs 3W-6L) suggests they are better-positioned NOW than when they lost 0-2 in March. The briefing is silent on whether Procyon's March form has held or regressed. MAP POOL / VETO ASYMMETRY: Briefing notes map pool (Nuke, Ancient, Mirage, Inferno, Overpass, Dust2) but provides ZERO strategic analysis of team-specific map strengths/bans. paiN may hold a critical veto advantage or hidden map strength that the 2-0 result does not capture. A team that climbs from 1-0 loss to 5W-3L form likely adjusted their map strategy. UPPER BRACKET POSITIONING CONTRADICTION: Briefing states this is an 'Upper Bracket Semi-Final' but also notes Procyon vs paiN as 'Lower bracket quarterfinal' in resolution criteria. Unclear bracket status introduces ambiguity about seed quality, rest time, and psychological momentum. If paiN was the higher seed, the market may be underestimating them. MISSING META DATA: Briefing is silent on recent patches, rule changes, or hero/agent bans in CS2 that could favor paiN's playstyle. A patch dropping hours before match start (common in live esports) could neutralize Procyon's March meta advantage. PSYCHOLOGICAL EDGE: paiN Academy is a LOWER-RANKED team (#193 vs #196) that has been CLIMBING form (5W-3L) while facing the HIGHER-RANKED team in DECLINE (3W-6L). Underdog psychology + recent form trajectory suggests paiN has momentum and less mental fatigue. Procyon may be overconfident after the March 2-0. RATING DISCREPANCY NOISE: Procyon #196 vs paiN #193 difference is trivial (3 ranking points difference, statistically within noise for regional tier-2 events). Yet market prices 60/40, implying material Procyon edge. This is overconfidence on stale ranking data (Procyon has declined since those ranks were set). LIQUIDITY / SHARP MOVE SIGNAL: The +13.5pp sharp move on Apr 17 08:00 UTC (YES side) suggests a sharp or insider bet placed ~13 hours before match start. This is a tell of confidence, but sharp bets on live events are frequently wrong \u2014 the mover may have missed the form reversal or be betting on old intel. NO-SIDE DATA GAP: Briefing provides no recent match results, playoff form, or player-specific stats for paiN Academy. Absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. paiN's 5W-3L form is stated but not cited to matches. If those wins include recent upsets of higher-ranked teams, Procyon is significantly underrated. CONTRARIAN ASYMMETRY: If Procyon's 2-0 from March relied on a specific meta/veto that paiN has since studied and countered, Procyon has NO hedge: they are now facing a team in superior form with a read on their playbook. paiN's counter-meta BO3 sweep (2-0 paiN) is a 5-10% tail risk that flips the market entirely. YES-side is overconfident on one outdated reference win.", "key_factor": "paiN Academy executes a strategic meta-counter exploit (map veto sequence, economy discipline, or tactical innovation) that nullifies Procyon's recent 2-0 result advantage in a BO3 format where map-specific vulnerability is exposed."}], "final_score": 0.5660567289167071, "no_score": 0.44559804503735406, "edge": 0.09590909090909094, "no_edge": 0.2859090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56.61% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 54.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0502615081746454, "The Bull": 0.9485651334222127, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0530400843938654, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0532291381796675, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0546263940607403, "The Contrarian": 1.072388005832532, "The Bear": 0.7678897359363381}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2004598", "question": "Counter-Strike: Procyon Gaming vs paiN Academy (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Procyon Gaming and paiN Academy in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Procyon Gaming\" if Procyon Gaming win the match against paiN Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"paiN Academy\" if paiN Academy win the match against Procyon Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 3315.511508, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["96854352638614653014013186497669510545715706582322305388162195052869205236985", "19955928266172138836472765612043797911335595361510015448155038387823695383203"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "Complete overview of the MIBR Academy vs.", "Vasco matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "paiN Academy matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "Best of 3 (Online) * Upper bracket semi-final.", "Get the complete overview of Procyon's current lineup, upcoming matches, recent results and much more.", "ALKA matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by CCT.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 event taking", "CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by CCT ..."], "news_summary": "Procyon Gaming and paiN Academy are set to face off in an Upper Bracket Semi-Final best-of-three match in the CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 Playoffs, scheduled for April 17, 2026 at 21:00 UTC. This is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by CCT (C-Tier, Valve Tier 2 event). Both teams have recent competitive history in the region, with Procyon ranked #196 and paiN ranked #193 in the current Valve Global Rankings as of mid-April 2026.", "side_yes_case": ["Procyon defeated paiN Academy 2-0 on 2026-03-07 in their most recent matchup", "Procyon showing stable Valve ranking position (#196-767 points) in lead-up to playoffs", "Upper bracket positioning suggests Procyon advanced from earlier round(s)"], "side_no_case": ["paiN Academy won their prior encounter 1-0 on 2025-12-09, demonstrating capability to beat Procyon", "paiN ranked closely to Procyon (#193 vs #196), indicating competitive parity", "Best-of-three format introduces variance; Procyon's 2-0 win does not guarantee repeat performance"], "key_context": ["Match format: Best-of-3, Upper Bracket Semi-Final", "Tournament: CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 (online, C-Tier event)", "Map pool context: Earlier bracket stages show teams banning/picking from Nuke, Ancient, Mirage, Inferno, Overpass, Dust2"], "prior_match_facts": ["2026-03-07 \u2014 winner: Procyon Gaming (2-0) @ Group Stage", "2025-12-09 \u2014 winner: paiN Academy (1-0) @ Group D"], "disambiguation_warnings": ["Past-tense match-result language detected in side_yes_case[0], side_no_case[2] despite PandaScore reports this match as scheduled (scheduled 2026-04-17 21:00 UTC). Sample: \"Procyon defeated paiN Academy 2-0 on 2026-03-07 in th\". Treat any final scoreline as a PRIOR encounter, not this market's outcome."], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T18:42:09.378066Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "96854352638614653014013186497669510545715706582322305388162195052869205236985", "data_points": 8, "weighted_avg": 0.6139398586836968, "change_1w_pp": 8.999999999999996, "change_24h_pp": 8.999999999999996, "volatility_24h": 5.52914356581818, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-17T08:00:00Z", "delta_pp": 13.5}]}, "no": {"token_id": "19955928266172138836472765612043797911335595361510015448155038387823695383203", "data_points": 9, "weighted_avg": 0.3851200280659313, "change_1w_pp": -8.999999999999996, "change_24h_pp": -8.999999999999996, "volatility_24h": 5.139135558215437, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-17T10:00:55Z", "delta_pp": -13.5}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-17T18:42:09.647028Z"}, "structured_match": {"provider": "pandascore", "provider_match_id": "1447269", "game": "csgo", "scheduled_at": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "status": "scheduled", "team_a_name": "Procyon Gaming", "team_b_name": "paiN Academy", "match_format": "BO3", "tournament_name": "Playoffs", "final_score": null, "winner_name": null, "h2h": [{"match_id": "1380507", "scheduled_at": "2026-03-07T14:00:00Z", "winner_name": "Procyon Gaming", "score_summary": "2-0", "tournament_name": "Group Stage"}, {"match_id": "1276511", "scheduled_at": "2025-12-09T19:30:00Z", "winner_name": "paiN Academy", "score_summary": "1-0", "tournament_name": "Group D"}], "team_a_recent_form": {"team_name": "Procyon Gaming", "matches_considered": 9, "wins": 3, "losses": 6, "last_match_at": "2026-04-16T23:45:00Z"}, "team_b_recent_form": {"team_name": "paiN Academy", "matches_considered": 8, "wins": 5, "losses": 3, "last_match_at": "2026-04-16T21:00:00Z"}, "fuzzy_score": 100, "fetched_at": "2026-04-17T18:41:55.872785