he sharp move may indicate smart money late support, OR it may indicate whale position bias. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in YES (62%) due to clear statistical gap in Stage records. BUT confidence in NO is held at 71% because the briefing is SILENT on Minnesota's internal form, meta fit, roster changes, and head-to-head history \u2014 three major factors that could easily reverse a 36% YES odds. Absence of contrary evidence is NOT evidence of absence. QUALIFIER CONTEXT: This is a Stage 3 Major Qualifiers match, not regular season play. Qualifier matches have different psychological pressure; teams already secured in playoffs may underperform, while teams fighting for qualification may overperform. Briefing does NOT clarify which teams are already locked into Major seeding. TIME-TO-DISRUPTION: Match starts in ~3.3 hours. For a black-swan flip (Vancouver underperforms, Minnesota overperforms), the disruption must already be in motion (late roster change, player illness, emotional shock from recent loss). The briefing was refreshed 2026-04-17 18:43 UTC, ~3.25 hours before match start \u2014 enough time for a last-minute personnel or health issue to break news AFTER data cutoff, but before market locks. Confidence adjusted downward (not 75+) to reflect this temporal risk.", "key_factor": "Minnesota R\u00d8KKR's Stage 4 momentum (2-3) combined with a late-stage roster swap, map-pool meta shift favoring their playstyle, or Vancouver's inconsistency (3-2 in Stage 4) cascading into underperformance under pressure in a BO5 qualifier."}], "final_score": 0.5947829221438111, "no_score": 0.46452121061257623, "edge": 0.33090909090909093, "no_edge": 0.050909090909090904, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 59.48% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 66.14% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, 