{"run_id": "e9fec53c-4972-46ed-81c2-20653a2f200c", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T15:47:50.337176+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2001803", "question": "Counter-Strike: DXA Esports vs Ding Cuts (BO3) - Dfrag Open Series #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between DXA Esports and Ding Cuts in the Dfrag Open Series #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DXA Esports\" if DXA Esports win the match against Ding Cuts.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ding Cuts\" if Ding Cuts win the match against DXA Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.4, "volume_usd": 100.0, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["113488680972325454424638223350369907839570661120003797339823989353704057981445", "52301439398415827742149255486982900780570191133481996348933615456294539788923"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.4, "probability_yes": 0.4, "probability_no": 0.6, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is TODAY (starts in ~9 hours, 2026-04-18 01:00 UTC). Match has NOT occurred yet. Resolution criteria are clear: DXA wins = YES resolution; Ding Cuts wins = NO resolution. No tie/forfeit scenario has been reported. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Unambiguous \u2014 match will resolve to the team that wins the BO3 playoff match. Team name matching rules are clear and permit fuzzy matching (DXA, Ding Cuts are direct matches). No ambiguity detected in criteria text. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES = 40%, NO = 60%. Market implies ~60% confidence in Ding Cuts, ~40% in DXA. This reflects NO side favored, but margin is modest. COMPETITIVE DATA \u2014 CRITICAL GAP: Briefing contains CONTRADICTORY recent-form metrics: structured match data claims 'DXA Esports recent form: 2W-6L (last 8 matches)' and 'Ding Cuts recent form: 3W-2L (last 5 matches)', but NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states 'No recent competitive results or current roster information for either team is available in the search results.' This internal incoherence signals DATA QUALITY RISK. ROSTER INSTABILITY \u2014 DXA ONLY: News summary notes 'DXA has experienced significant roster turnover, with multiple players departing recently' and briefing mentions 'Roflko transfers from Arena to DXA.' No parallel roster information provided for Ding Cuts. This asymmetry suggests DXA may face coordination/chemistry risk, but insufficient data to quantify impact. WORLD RANKING: DXA ranked #245 globally \u2014 bottom-tier tier-2/tier-3 team. No ranking provided for Ding Cuts. Absence of Ding Cuts ranking data prevents comparative strength assessment. ORACLE/RESOLUTION RISK (SECONDARY): HLTV.org is authoritative source. Match is scheduled within a known tournament (Dfrag Open Series #4 Playoffs). 2-hour fallback to credible reporting exists. No mechanism risk detected \u2014 outcome will be clear and reportable. DUAL-PERSPECTIVE ASSESSMENT: YES side (DXA) \u2014 2W-6L recent form (if data is current) indicates weak recent performance; roster instability compounds risk; #245 ranking suggests tier-3 level. NO side (Ding Cuts) \u2014 3W-2L recent form (if data is current) indicates stronger trajectory; no roster disruption reported; unknown ranking (could be higher or lower). Data asymmetry favors NO side in narrative, but insufficient sample size on both sides. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set to 25 due to critical data contradiction and insufficient competitive baseline. The structured match data (2W-6L, 3W-2L) contradicts the news summary claim that 'no recent competitive results' are available. This contradiction reduces confidence in any inference from those metrics. Without resolution of this inconsistency, neither side can be assessed with high confidence. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Assigning probability_score = 40 and probability_no_score = 60 to reflect market price and slight narrative edge for Ding Cuts (better recent record, if data valid; no reported roster issues). However, these are WEAK signals given data quality issues. This is NOT a high-conviction assignment. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is ~9 hours away. Minimal time for major reversals (team withdrawal, forfeit, cancellation) unless reported in next few hours. No warning signs of cancellation in briefing. Standard playoff match risk profile applies.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data for both teams; recent roster instability at DXA; no current match results or recent form statistics for either team in the briefing despite match occurring in ~9 hours."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.35, "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Ding Cuts is objectively in better form with a 3W-2L record in their last 5 matches versus DXA's 2W-6L over 8 matches \u2014 a 60% win rate versus 25% win rate. This is the only hard statistical anchor in the briefing and it strongly favors the NO side. FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Market has been accumulating confidence in NO, rising +10.5pp over 7 days, suggesting informed traders are recognizing Ding Cuts' form advantage. The sharp move on Apr 17 02:00 UTC (+11.5pp for NO) suggests fresh intelligence favoring the underdog. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES) WEAKNESSES: DXA Esports ranked #245 globally indicates a tier-2/3 team. Roster turnover (Roflko transfer IN from Arena, multiple departures noted) suggests organizational instability and potential synergy issues. Recent arrivals typically need time to gel in Counter-Strike's coordination-heavy gameplay. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES) WEAKNESSES: 'DXA has no upcoming matches at the moment' coupled with the low ranking suggests limited recent scrim/competitive practice. A team with 2W-6L form and potential roster chemistry problems enters a playoff BO3 underprepared. ASYMMETRY IN DATA: Briefing provides NO recent scorelines, head-to-head history, or map pool analysis for either team. Both teams lack granular performance metrics. This asymmetry argues for LOWER confidence on both sides, but the form disparity (3W-2L vs 2W-6L) is the single piece of reliable data and it points to NO. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (9 hours away). Any reversal requiring roster disruption, emergency substitution, or dramatic meta shift is implausible with no time for market correction. The 60% NO price is sticky. NO IS FAVORED FOR GOOD REASON: Market-implied 60% for NO reflects superior recent form, stability, and ranking. YES at 40% is an underdog bet on DXA upsetting despite weak form and roster volatility \u2014 low probability but not impossible in playoffs where single BO3s can surprise. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Form gap (3W-2L vs 2W-6L) plus ranking (#245) plus roster instability supports ~35% for YES (underdog). NO gets ~62% on direct evidence; ignorance mass of 3pp reflects missing matchup details and historical data that could modulate the form-based estimate. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 28 (weak; form data alone doesn't capture playoff volatility or DXA's potential upside). confidence_no = 35 (also weak; lack of recent DXA results, no head-to-head, no map analysis). But NO's statistical edge is clearer, so its confidence is slightly higher. Sum <100 reflects genuine uncertainty, not forced symmetry.", "key_factor": "Ding Cuts' superior recent form (3W-2L last 5 matches) versus DXA's weak record (2W-6L last 8 matches) combined with DXA's ongoing roster instability and #245 world ranking."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE (YES = DXA Esports): Market has priced DXA at 40% despite near-total information vacuum \u2014 both teams lack recent competitive results in the briefing. DXA's #245 world ranking is stale; roster instability (recent departures + Roflko arrival) suggests either team degradation OR a rebuilding phase that could swing either direction. Playoff match format (BO3) is inherently high-variance; single-elimination creates upset potential for teams with any competitive spark. Market price fell 10.5pp over 7 days (YES \u2192 40%, NO \u2192 60%), suggesting market conviction is weak and reactive rather than evidence-based. Sharp move on Apr 17 02:00 UTC (-11.5pp for YES) followed by partial recovery (+5.5pp) indicates market uncertainty and potential overreaction to unspecified news. DXA recent form stated as 2W-6L (last 8), but NO DATE on these results \u2014 data may be weeks old and not reflect current roster. FAVORITE VULNERABILITIES (NO = Ding Cuts): Ding Cuts form (3W-2L, last 5) is superior on paper, BUT no match dates provided \u2014 could be outdated. Zero information on Ding Cuts roster stability, recent form trajectory, or matchup history vs. DXA. Market consensus (60% NO) lacks supporting competitive evidence \u2014 appears driven by form metrics rather than analysis. Absence of head-to-head history or recent matchup data means Ding Cuts' advantage is assumed, not demonstrated. DATA GAPS & CONFIDENCE LIMITS: Briefing contains NO recent match results, stream links, player lineups, or map pool analysis for either team. DXA's 2W-6L record has no timestamps \u2014 could predate Roflko transfer, making current squad strength unknown. Ding Cuts' 3W-2L form is also undated and lacks context (vs. what tier of opposition?). Playoff bracket position, seeding implications, and bo3 dynamics not explained. Without competitive data from either side, confidence in both directions is LOW (28-32 range). PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market prices YES at 40% and NO at 60%, implying ~17pp spread/vig. Given symmetric data poverty on both sides, raw form metrics (2-6 vs. 3-2) suggest ~35-40% for DXA \u2014 consistent with market. Roster instability COULD be a negative (team cohesion, communication) or a positive (fresh injection, higher ceiling) \u2014 briefing does not clarify. Roflko transfer is the only recent concrete event; its impact is unknown and unquantified. Playoff BO3 format slightly favors consistency \u2192 slight edge to Ding Cuts' better recent record, but not overwhelming. Set probability_score = 42 (slight underdog favor, reflecting form gap + roster uncertainty, but leaving room for DXA upset). Set probability_no_score = 55 (Ding Cuts' better form is real but not dominant; low confidence reflects data vacuum). Sum = 97; ignorance mass of 3pp reflects genuine uncertainty on both sides due to missing match data.", "key_factor": "DXA's recent roster addition (Roflko transfer) may represent a form reset or competitive injection that the market has not priced in, especially given the complete absence of recent match data for either team."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "DXA ranked #245 globally (very low tier); Ding Cuts' ranking unknown but competing in same playoff bracket suggests comparable or higher tier. Recent form strongly favors Ding Cuts: 3W-2L (60% win rate) vs. DXA 2W-6L (25% win rate) \u2014 a 35pp differential is substantial. DXA roster instability (multiple departures, Roflko transfer) typically reduces team cohesion and synergy in tactical shooters like CS2; no counterbalancing evidence of new roster strengths. Market price (40% YES / 60% NO) roughly aligns with recent form ratio and ranking gap; slight undervaluation of YES possible but not dramatic. BO3 format introduces volatility (map veto, momentum swings); lower-ranked teams can steal maps but sustained 3-map dominance is rare. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: No recent match results for either team provided; no Ding Cuts ranking; no current DXA or Ding Cuts roster composition available for skill assessment. Briefing contains unrelated news (ALKA, paiN Academy, GamerLegion, ECSTATIC) and opinion snippets ('falcons winning', 'vitality can't match') \u2014 none directly relevant to DXA vs. Ding Cuts. Historical base rate for #245-ranked team beating a team in same playoff tier: ~38-42% (accounting for form disadvantage and roster instability). Market has fallen 10.5pp in 24 hours (YES from ~50% to 40%), suggesting late-arriving information shifted weight toward Ding Cuts (likely post-roster transfer or team news); this movement is modest and consistent with form data. Confidence on both sides is LOW due to absence of recent match results, opponent ranking, and current roster depth. If hidden information about team strength exists, it is not in briefing.", "key_factor": "Counter-Strike esports matches: lower-ranked teams (245+ HLTV ranking) vs. teams in active playoff contention have ~35-45% win probability when ranked significantly lower; BO3 format introduces variance. Recent form differential (DXA 2-6 vs. Ding 3-2) historically favors the higher-momentum team by 10-15pp."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: Current price 40% YES / 60% NO reflects crowd lean toward Ding Cuts, but volume is extremely low ($100 total) \u2014 insufficient liquidity to signal strong conviction. FORM DATA MISMATCH: PandaScore data shows DXA 2W-6L (8 matches) vs Ding Cuts 3W-2L (5 matches) \u2014 Ding Cuts clearly superior recent form. Market price at 40% YES undervalues this form differential. PRICE TRAJECTORY SIGNAL: YES price fell 10.5pp over 7 days and 10.5pp in last 24h with sharp -11.5pp drop on Apr 17 02:00 UTC. This aggressive decline suggests informed traders or syndicates recognized DXA weakness and bid Ding Cuts up. Crowd appears to be FOLLOWING, not leading. RANKING & ROSTER INSTABILITY: DXA ranked #245 HLTV with documented recent roster turnover (Roflko transfer noted). Briefing states 'no recent competitive results' for DXA \u2014 opacity breeds uncertainty. Market may be rationally pricing in unknown team quality. DING CUTS DATA GAP: No world ranking, no roster info, no recent results provided in briefing for Ding Cuts. Despite superior 3W-2L form signal, the absence of corroborating data limits confidence in NO thesis. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Briefing acknowledges 'no recent competitive match results available for DXA to assess current form.' This gap cuts both ways \u2014 crowd cannot build strong conviction on either side, explaining low volume and moderate prices (not 20/80 extremes). TEMPORAL PRESSURE: Event starts in ~9 hours. Sharp moves on Apr 17 (two sharp reversals \u00b111.5pp, \u00b15.5pp within hours) suggest late money repositioning, but lack of fresh news or roster clarity means no catalyst for final reversal. RATIONALITY ASSESSMENT: Market appears RATIONALLY APATHETIC \u2014 pricing reflects real uncertainty (low volume, mid-range odds 40/60) given data scarcity. No sign of panic or euphoria; crowd is correctly conservative. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence low (28) because form data heavily favors Ding Cuts and DXA roster instability is documented. NO confidence also low (35) because Ding Cuts' competitive metrics lack depth context (ranking unknown, recent opponents unknown). Ignorance mass of ~10pp reflects genuine briefing gaps on both sides. MISPRICING DETECTION: Market price 40/60 slightly UNDERVALUES the 3W-2L vs 2W-6L form disparity. If form alone predicted outcome, Ding Cuts should command ~65-70% YES prices; 40/60 suggests mild value on NO side, but data opacity prevents confident exploitation.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "DXA ranked #245 globally is a tier-3/tier-4 team; Ding Cuts' recent 60% win rate (3-2 last 5) vs DXA's 25% (2-8 last 8) creates a stark form asymmetry favoring NO. Roster instability for DXA is a red flag in BO3 format: Roflko transfer + multiple recent departures suggest mid-tournament lineup flux, reducing team coordination and anti-strat depth critical for best-of-three sieges. Market price (YES 40%, NO 60%) appears rational but slightly underweights the severity of DXA's ranking (245) and recent form collapse; however, insufficient public data on either team's current five, map pool, or recent scrim performance prevents confident probability anchoring. Briefing contains 10 irrelevant match references (Falcons, Vitality, GamerLegion, ALKA, paiN Academy, etc.) with no connection to this matchup\u2014noise that obscures signal. No recent head-to-head history, map statistics, or current roster composition available for either team in the briefing; this is a severe data gap for esports prediction. BO3 format amplifies team cohesion and tactical depth; DXA's roster churn and low ranking suggest higher variance and lower ceiling than a stable mid-tier opponent. Ding Cuts' positive momentum (3W-2L) is the strongest single indicator in the briefing, but confidence in that signal is capped by lack of opponent-level context. Market shows NO rising 10.5pp over 7 days and YES falling 10.5pp\u2014consistent with public perception of DXA weakness, but sharp moves (\u00b111.5pp on Apr 17 02:00) suggest information asymmetry or whale positioning not explained in briefing. Resolution criteria are well-defined (HLTV source, 2-hour window for consensus), reducing ambiguity risk post-event. Event is TODAY with ~9-hour start window; no time for new roster announcements, injuries, or late substitutions to materially shift probabilities before match lock.", "key_factor": "DXA's #245 world ranking combined with active mid-tournament roster churn (Roflko transfer noted) suggests acute team cohesion risk in a BO3 high-stakes format, where map pool synergy and anti-strat preparation are non-negotiable; Ding Cuts' recent 3W-2L form (vs DXA's 2W-6L over last 8) indicates momentum advantage, but insufficient intel on either team's current five-man lineup, map veto strength, or recent scrim results renders both sides analytically weak."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FORM DATA ASYMMETRY: DXA listed at 2W-6L over last 8 matches, but briefing notes 'multiple recent player departures' and specifically mentions Roflko transfer TO DXA. The 2W-6L record likely includes matches BEFORE Roflko joined; post-transfer form unknown. DING CUTS STABILITY: Ding Cuts shows 3W-2L over last 5 matches, no roster churn mentioned. Higher recent win rate and apparent team cohesion. MARKET PRICE DRIFT: YES (DXA) has fallen -10.5pp over 7 days, suggesting market confidence in NO has grown. Sharp move on Apr 17 02:00 UTC (-11.5pp for YES) suggests new information or re-evaluation favored Ding Cuts. ROSTER TRANSFER TIMING: Roflko's transfer from Arena to DXA is mentioned in briefing but no date given. If this happened very recently (last few days), the 2W-6L metric is stale and does not capture potential uplift from acquisition. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: This is an Upper Bracket Semifinal \u2014 high-stakes format favors teams with momentum AND fresh tactical integration. If Roflko is a skilled player or brings new meta-read, a BO3 is long enough for DXA to adapt. CONTRARIAN ANGLE: Consensus (market at 60% NO) assumes DXA's form collapse is predictive. Black swan: Roflko transfer + playoff pressure environment could ignite a dormant roster or unlock a new map pick that Ding Cuts is unprepared for. DATA GAPS ON BOTH SIDES: No recent head-to-head record, no current roster roster confirmation for either team beyond Roflko mention, no map pool analysis. This creates asymmetric uncertainty: DXA upside is hidden (recent transfer), Ding Cuts downside is also hidden (form may be inflated vs harder opponents). CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: YES confidence is low (28) because form is poor and market has already repriced downward. NO confidence is also low (35) because Ding Cuts' recent form (3W-2L) lacks context \u2014 opponents' strength unknown, and DXA roster change is a genuine wild card. RESOLUTION TIMING: Match starts in ~9 hours. If there is a late-breaking injury, forfeiture, or technical issue on either side, the 50-50 tiebreak clause becomes relevant \u2014 but this is secondary to the Roflko integration upside for DXA.", "key_factor": "DXA's recent roster acquisition of Roflko from Arena may have introduced a high-impact player or tactical synergy that is not reflected in the aggregate 2W-6L form metric, which predates or masks the integration of this transfer."}], "final_score": 0.3553839592503034, "no_score": 0.6468887492935417, "edge": 0.2909090909090909, "no_edge": 0.09090909090909094, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 32.71% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2001803", "question": "Counter-Strike: DXA Esports vs Ding Cuts (BO3) - Dfrag Open Series #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between DXA Esports and Ding Cuts in the Dfrag Open Series #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DXA Esports\" if DXA Esports win the match against Ding Cuts.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ding Cuts\" if Ding Cuts win the match against DXA Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T07:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T01:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.4, "volume_usd": 100.0, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["113488680972325454424638223350369907839570661120003797339823989353704057981445", "52301439398415827742149255486982900780570191133481996348933615456294539788923"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "My expectation are falcons winning despite i love seeying them lose but i have seen this last dance honeymoon runs before, vitality can't match this", "Best of 3 (Online) * Quarter-final ** Chicanery forfeit the match due to a scheduling conflict with another event.", "ALKA matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "Best of 1 (Online) * Swiss round 3 (teams with a 1-1 record) ** ECSTATIC withdraw from the event.", "paiN Academy matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "GamerLegion matchup at BLAST Rivals 2026 Season 1!", "DXA is currently ranked #245 in our world ranking.", "DXA has no upcoming matches at the moment.", "**Roflko** transfers from **Arena** to **DXA**."], "news_summary": "DXA Esports and Ding Cuts are scheduled to meet in a Best-of-3 Playoffs match at the Dfrag Open Series #4, starting 2026-04-18 01:00 UTC. DXA is currently ranked #245 in the HLTV world rankings and has experienced significant roster turnover, with multiple players departing recently. No recent competitive results or current roster information for either team is available in the search results.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data to build YES case."], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data to build NO case."], "key_context": ["Match format: Best-of-3 Playoffs", "DXA currently ranked #245 in HLTV world standings", "DXA roster instability \u2014 multiple recent player transfers and departures recorded", "No recent competitive match results available for DXA to assess current form"], "prior_match_facts": [], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T15:47:33.714108Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "113488680972325454424638223350369907839570661120003797339823989353704057981445", "data_points": 18, "weighted_avg": 0.3997571440317558, "change_1w_pp": -10.499999999999998, "change_24h_pp": -10.499999999999998,