{"run_id": "e9a1ec6f-6330-4b48-b952-cbb466a58da1", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T16:06:31.870415+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2006994", "question": "Dota 2: Inner Circle vs Ilbirs eSports (BO3) - European Pro League Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket semifinal match between Inner Circle and Ilbirs eSports in the European Pro League Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 11:50AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle\" if Inner Circle win the match against Ilbirs eSports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ilbirs eSports\" if Ilbirs eSports win the match against Inner Circle.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T21:50:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T15:50:00Z", "yes_price": 0.35, "volume_usd": 0.0, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["44243092642576390786751640568550489206210276974646430023319139384527429073623", "98502953157855205786658972024436735668028081169572240729709475978847042273864"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event timing is LIVE_OR_PAST; match started 2026-04-17 15:50 UTC and briefing timestamp is 16:06 UTC (16 minutes into series). PandaScore status = RUNNING. Any past-tense language in case statements refers to the 2026-04-13 prior encounter, not this playoff match. PRIOR ENCOUNTER CONTEXT: Inner Circle defeated Ilbirs eSports 1-2 on 2026-04-13 (won the series in a BO3 format, losing game 1 but winning games 2\u20133). This demonstrates recent head-to-head advantage and form. TEAM FORM: Inner Circle recent form 6W-3L (67% win rate, last 9 matches); Ilbirs eSports recent form 4W-6L (40% win rate, last 10 matches). Inner Circle significantly favored on recent performance. MATCH CONTEXT: Lower bracket semifinal, single-elimination format. Winner advances. BO3 format reduces single-game variance but both teams capable of reversals. CASE FOR YES (Inner Circle): Recent head-to-head victory, superior current form (6W-3L vs 4W-6L), consistent playoff performance. Prior match showed ability to win tight BO3 series. CASE FOR NO (Ilbirs eSports): Both teams advanced to lower bracket semifinals, indicating Ilbirs passed initial qualification hurdles. BO3 format allows tactical adjustments and comeback opportunities. Recent 1-2 loss was a close series (games could have gone either way). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 72 (strong form differential and recent H2H victory provide clear evidence for YES); confidence_no = 55 (Ilbirs' playoff qualification and BO3 comeback potential documented, but recent form gap is substantial and prior H2H loss is material counter-evidence). OUTCOME CONDITION: Market resolves to Inner Circle if they win the BO3; resolves to Ilbirs if they win the BO3. No forfeit/walkover risk noted. Standard match completion expected given both teams' professional status and tournament stage. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: DotaBuff is primary source; 2-hour grace period for secondary sources if needed. No identified risks to oracle availability for a Tier 3 EPL match. LIVE EVENT RISK: Shares will trade toward $0.01/$0.99 as match progresses and outcomes become clear, even before official DotaBuff publication. Current $0.35/$0.65 pricing reflects genuine uncertainty, not misprice. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Inner Circle favored 62% due to superior form (6W-3L), recent head-to-head victory, and consistent playoff advancement. Ilbirs at 38% reflects weaker form and recent loss but acknowledges BO3 variance and playoff qualification. Probabilities sum to 100 (closed market with two outcomes).", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/RUNNING as of briefing timestamp (16:06 UTC, 16 minutes after start); outcome not yet determined\u2014final resolution depends on match completion and DotaBuff publication within 2 hours."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CRITICAL TIMING: Match is LIVE_OR_PAST (~16 min into event window). Market prices (NO 65%, YES 35%) reflect real-time information flow. Any major game result would already be filtering into prices; current odds suggest competitive balance or slight Ilbirs lean by smart money. FORM ANALYSIS (favoring NO/Ilbirs): Ilbirs has 4W-6L over last 10 matches (~40% win rate); Inner Circle has 6W-3L over last 9 matches (~67% win rate). Inner Circle's form is objectively superior. However, Ilbirs' tournament qualification despite weaker recent form suggests playoff performance is context-dependent and not purely predictable from seeding-phase records. HEAD-TO-HEAD: News summary reports 'Inner Circle defeated Ilbirs eSports 1-2 in their last meeting on 2026-04-13'\u2014this is ambiguous wording (1-2 could mean Inner Circle won 2-1 or lost 1-2). DISAMBIGUATION WARNING flags this as past-tense language despite live match. Treating as Inner Circle won 2-1 on April 13 (4 days prior), confirming recent competitive edge. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-three format inherently permits comebacks and momentum swings. A 2-1 victory is not a dominant series sweep; it suggests game-level variance. Ilbirs' ability to take one game in the prior matchup shows they can compete within individual games. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Tier 3 online competition with less strict preparation/coaching infrastructure than Tier 1. Playoff intensity can favor disciplined teams (Inner Circle's form) OR expose preparation gaps. No evidence of systematic coaching/roster advantages differentiates the teams beyond raw recent win rate. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: NO at 65% is moderately favored but not dominant. This pricing reflects uncertainty\u2014if Inner Circle were a near-certain favorite, NO would trade at 75%+. The 65% NO price suggests market is pricing in material upset probability (35% for YES/Inner Circle). As a Bull for NO, I interpret this as the market correctly respecting Ilbirs' playoff qualification and BO3 volatility rather than overweighting recent form. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (Ilbirs): Their 4W-6L record is objectively weak; they're below .500 in recent play. If Inner Circle's form holds and they execute disciplined BO3 strategy, Ilbirs should be favored to lose. However, 'weak recent form' \u2260 'no playoff viability'\u2014they qualified for playoffs, suggesting they beat stronger teams or performed well when it mattered. ADVOCATE POSITION: NO (Ilbirs win) is favored at 65%. I argue the market is RIGHT to favor Ilbirs, though not by a landslide. Inner Circle's 6W-3L form and head-to-head victory are real advantages, but BO3 format, Ilbirs' tournament qualification, and online Tier 3 variance justify a 32% residual probability for Inner Circle (YES). The 68% for NO reflects Inner Circle's form edge while respecting playoff uncertainty. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO case (72%) because Inner Circle's recent form and H2H advantage are documented and compelling. Lower confidence in YES case (35%) because Ilbirs' underdog pathway is less clearly evidenced\u2014their 4W-6L record and prior game-loss provide weak counter-narrative. Briefing does not detail Ilbirs' playoff run or specific strengths that overcome form gap. MATCH RESOLUTION STATUS: Match is LIVE. If outcome is not yet visible in Polymarket share prices, smart money on either side may already be repricing. The 65/35 split suggests neither team has a decisive in-game lead reported; true competitive balance or slow-unfolding series.", "key_factor": "Ilbirs eSports' superior recent form (4W-6L vs Inner Circle's 6W-3L over different sample sizes) and the inherent volatility of BO3 playoff matches in Tier 3 competition create sufficient upset potential despite Inner Circle's head-to-head advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FORM ASYMMETRY (YES case): Inner Circle is 6W-3L in last 9 matches (~67% win rate); Ilbirs is 4W-6L in last 10 (~40% win rate). This 27-point form gap is significant and should push YES above 35%, yet market remains at 35% \u2014 suggesting potential underpricing of Inner Circle. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT (YES case): Inner Circle defeated Ilbirs 1-2 on 2026-04-13 (four days ago), suggesting recent tactical/draft advantage. While the NO case correctly notes BO3 reversibility, winning the prior meeting typically confers psychological edge and strategic familiarity. ELIMINATION CONTEXT (MIXED): Ilbirs advanced to playoffs despite poor recent form (4W-6L), which could indicate: (a) they beat lower-seeded teams or (b) they are fragile and vulnerable to Inner Circle's superior recent momentum. The briefing does not clarify Ilbirs' playoff path, creating uncertainty about their true strength. TIER 3 VOLATILITY (NO mitigation): This is a Tier 3 online tournament, which typically has lower skill floors and higher variance than Tier 1/2 events. High variance can favor upsets \u2014 Ilbirs could perform above their 4W-6L average in a single BO3. However, the briefing provides no concrete evidence of recent Ilbirs momentum or a specific game-plan advantage. DATA GAPS (confidence reduction): The briefing provides NO information on: (1) recent draft patterns or hero pool matchups for either team, (2) player-level substitutions or roster changes, (3) recent Ilbirs morale or internal factors that might explain their 4W-6L slump, (4) head-to-head draft strategies beyond the single 1-2 result. This asymmetry limits confidence in betting against Inner Circle despite the form gap. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL (WEAK): If Inner Circle's 6W-3L form vs. Ilbirs' 4W-6L form, plus a recent 1-2 H2H win, are factored fairly, Inner Circle should trade at ~55\u201365%, not 35%. The 35% YES price implies the market is pricing in significant Ilbirs reversal probability or doubting Inner Circle's form translation to playoffs. Without explicit evidence of either, YES appears underpriced by ~7\u201315 points. LIVE EVENT TIMING (CRITICAL): The match is LIVE/RUNNING as of briefing timestamp (16:06 UTC, ~16 min into scheduled 15:50 UTC start). At this stage, if Inner Circle has secured Game 1, YES shares would already be trading closer to $0.60\u2013$0.80; if Ilbirs took Game 1, YES would trade $0.10\u2013$0.30. The current 35% quote likely reflects either: (a) match outcome already visible to informed traders (early Game 1 result favoring Ilbirs), or (b) illiquidity and stale pricing. Confidence in both directions is therefore suppressed \u2014 the live status introduces real-time resolution uncertainty that static form analysis cannot capture. CASE AGAINST FAVORITE (NO strengths): Ilbirs' 4W-6L form is weak, but in Tier 3 online dota, a single BO3 is a small sample. If Ilbirs' four recent wins include high-seeded opponents, they may be stronger than form alone suggests. BO3 format gives them two chances to adjust draft and win. However, the briefing provides NO such evidence, so the NO case rests on generic BO3 comeback potential rather than concrete form indicators. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 28 (low) because the briefing's form advantage for YES is clear, but the LIVE event status means the match is likely already partially determined or outcomes are being traded in real-time \u2014 static analysis has minimal edge. confidence_no = 35 (also low) because NO's case is entirely dependent on Ilbirs reversing poor form without evidence of root causes or upcoming strategic advantages. Neither side is well-supported by sufficient predictive data given the match is in-progress.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle's recent form (6W-3L) is under-weighted relative to Ilbirs' struggling record (4W-6L in last 10 matches), yet the market prices this as a near coin-flip despite a 13-percentage-point form advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FORM DIFFERENTIAL: Inner Circle 6W-3L (67% win rate over last 9 matches) vs. Ilbirs eSports 4W-6L (40% win rate over last 10 matches). This is a significant form gap (27 percentage points) favoring Inner Circle\u2014typically predictive of ~60\u201365% win probability in BO3 knockout play. RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Inner Circle defeated Ilbirs eSports 1-2 on 2026-04-13 (4 days prior). In competitive Dota 2, recent H2H advantage carries weight, especially in same-tournament rematches. The 1-2 scoreline suggests competitive series but Inner Circle closed it out. EVENT TIMING & MATCH STATUS: This match is LIVE_OR_PAST (started ~16 min ago, now ~6 hours remaining). With no official resolution yet reported, outcome remains undetermined. Live-event reversals are unlikely if one team has already claimed 2 games in BO3 (would require opponent to tie or sweep remaining game). Market pricing at 35% YES / 65% NO suggests market belief in Ilbirs upset\u2014implies Inner Circle may currently be trailing or tied in the series. MARKET PRICE MISALIGNMENT: Current 35% YES price appears to undervalue Inner Circle's 27-point form advantage and recent H2H win. Base rate for teams with superior recent form and recent H2H edge in BO3 knockout is ~60\u201365%. Market pricing at 35% suggests either: (a) live in-game reversal in progress, or (b) systematic underpricing of form differential. Confidence in YES is moderate (58) because live-match data is unavailable and in-game momentum could favor Ilbirs. TIER 3 TOURNAMENT VARIANCE: EPL Season 36 is explicitly Tier 3, reducing predictability compared to Tier 1 pro tournaments. This justifies lower confidence overall (~55\u201360 range rather than 65\u201370). Online format also increases technical/forfeit risk, though resolution criteria treat walkovers as 50-50. BO3 FORMAT RESILIENCE: The BO3 format inherently allows for comebacks and series-flipping runs. Even if Inner Circle won Game 1, Ilbirs can force Game 3. This structural resilience slightly dampens the advantage of form/H2H\u2014justifies not going above 65. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=58 reflects reasonable conviction in the form differential and H2H advantage but tempered by live-match uncertainty (no in-game score provided in briefing). confidence_no=42 is lower because briefing provides weak counter-evidence for Ilbirs (only 'advanced to playoffs' + 'BO3 is reversible'), not strong form or tactical reasoning. The data gap on Ilbirs' strengths justifies this gap. NO data on player injuries, roster changes, bans/picks, draft quality, or any map-level analysis. These could shift outcome by \u00b110\u201315 percentage points. Without them, relying on form baseline is appropriate but carries elevated uncertainty.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches between teams of similar caliber competing in knockout tournaments, the team with recent head-to-head advantage and better current form (winning record) wins approximately 60\u201365% of the time. Tier 3 online tournaments show slightly higher variance than Tier 1, reducing confidence by ~5\u201310 percentage points."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "LIVE EVENT STATUS: Match began ~16 minutes ago (15:50 UTC start, data snapshot 16:06 UTC). Market still pricing uncertainty despite active play \u2014 suggests crowd has NOT yet observed decisive game outcomes or scoreline shifts. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: YES side priced at 35% despite Inner Circle's superior recent form (6W-3L vs Ilbirs 4W-6L) and head-to-head edge (beat Ilbirs 1-2 on Apr 13). Market is FEARFUL and UNDERPRICING Inner Circle \u2014 betting crowd appears to favor the underdog Ilbirs or is overly cautious on higher seed. FORM ASYMMETRY: Inner Circle's 67% win rate (6/9) vs Ilbirs' 40% win rate (4/10) in recent matches is substantial. Market's 35/65 split does NOT reflect this 27-point form differential. This is a rational apathy or