rrative, no current match intel, sparse Ilbirs-specific data). Briefing is YES-leaning; NO side lacks depth.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FORM DIFFERENTIAL: Inner Circle 6W-3L (67% win rate) vs Ilbirs 4W-6L (40% win rate) over last 9-10 matches \u2014 27 percentage point spread is substantial in Tier 3 competitive Dota 2. RECENT H2H EDGE: Inner Circle defeated Ilbirs 1-2 on 2026-04-13 (4 days prior). This was in identical playoff stage context. One-game losses are reversible in BO3, but the team that won Game 3 (decider) typically carries psychological/draft advantage. BO3 DOTA DYNAMICS: BO3 format in Dota 2 creates draft-dependent variance. Teams can prepare counter-strategies between games. Ilbirs' 40% form suggests they will struggle to adapt across three games against stronger opposition. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: 35% YES (65% NO) appears to over-weight Ilbirs' playoff qualification and BO3 comeback potential, while under-weighting Inner Circle's clear 6W-3L superiority and recent direct H2H win. A 62% YES probability better reflects form and H2H. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Both teams are in lower bracket semifinals (high stakes). Inner Circle's superior form means they are more likely to execute cleanly under pressure. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES case (recent H2H win + clear form differential = 58). Lower confidence in NO case (Ilbirs have no demonstrable recent form or H2H advantage; 42). This is not symmetric ignorance but rather asymmetric evidence quality. NO RECENT ROSTER/META SHIFTS: Briefing shows no coaching changes, roster swaps, or meta shifts between April 13 and April 17. Same teams, same conditions. This reinforces H2H applicability. TIER 3 VOLATILITY: Tier 3 tournaments have higher variance than Tier 1/2. Individual player form and draft execution matter more than institutional stability. Inner Circle's 67% recent form is a strong signal in this context. TIMING: Event is LIVE (started ~16 min ago per briefing timestamp). Market prices ($0.35/$0.65) reflect pre-match sentiment. No live game data available to refine estimate. Sticking with form + H2H logic.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle's recent 1-2 victory over Ilbirs (April 13) in identical playoff format provides strong form signal, but BO3 reversals are common in Dota 2 due to meta-dependent draft execution and map variance; the market's 35% YES pricing appears to undervalue recent H2H dominance."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "LIVE_OR_PAST timing: Match is ~16 minutes into execution. No live scoreline provided in briefing despite the match being RUNNING. This suggests either (a) no games have completed yet, (b) early game state does not yet reveal outcome trajectory, or (c) delayed reporting. For a LIVE event, confidence on both sides must be heavily discounted unless explicit in-game evidence emerges. Recent form asymmetry: Inner Circle 6W-3L vs Ilbirs 4W-6L favors Inner Circle, but Ilbirs' underdog status in a single-elimination BO3 is a classic black-swan vector. Losing streaks often precede roster changes, tactical recalibration, or strategic desperation that can unlock map-specific or opponent-specific advantages. Prior head-to-head anomaly: Inner Circle beat Ilbirs 1-2 on Apr 13. The notation '1-2' typically means Inner Circle won 2 games to Ilbirs' 1 (or vice versa). The briefing CASE FOR YES claims Inner Circle 'defeated' with 1-2 scoreline, but CASE FOR NO notes 'recent 1-2 loss was close and reversible.' This contradictory framing suggests the prior match was competitive and narrow\u2014not a dominant 2-0. Briefing silence on meta/patch state: No hero-pick trends, recent patch notes, or map-pool data provided. Dota 2 patches shift hero viability dramatically. If a recent patch (post-Apr 13) buffed heroes Ilbirs' roster excels on, or nerfed Inner Circle's comfort picks, the tournament-level evidence becomes stale. Tier 3 online tournament volatility: EPL Season 36 is explicitly Tier 3 with no live crowd, no stadium fatigue mitigation, and regional players. Online tournaments see higher variance due to latency perception, tech issues (not explicitly mentioned but endemic to online Dota), and mental focus fragility over BO3s. Roster/substitution unknowns: Briefing provides no player-level data, recent trades, illness, or stand-in announcements. In a Tier 3 regional league, emergency substitutes or benching mid-tournament is not rare. If Ilbirs has a specialist player on a specific meta hero, they gain asymmetric edge. Psychological momentum inversion: Inner Circle as favorites faces the classic underdog trap\u2014expectation pressure, potential overconfidence, or tactical complacency. Ilbirs, already 'lower seed' by record, may execute flawless discipline if they've identified a specific anti-IC composition or playstyle. BO3 format resiliency: The case for NO correctly notes BO3 allows comebacks. Inner Circle's 6-3 record is solid but not dominant; Ilbirs at 4-6 is weak but not eliminated from any single series. A 2-1 upset is far more plausible than 2-0. Market price inversion concern: YES at 35% and NO at 65% reflects Inner Circle's favoritism, but the briefing's own asymmetric confidence (strong YES case but weaker NO evidence) suggests the market may be overweighting recent form and underweighting meta/tactical volatility in online Dota. No real-time game state data: The briefing provides no kill counts, gold leads, map control, or hero draft clarity as of 16:06 UTC. For a LIVE match ~16 min in, absence of live data is suspicious\u2014either early-game state is unremarkable, or briefing collection was delayed. This increases epistemic humility on both sides.", "key_factor": "Ilbirs eSports executes a tactical meta shift or roster substitution (likely a stand-in player or unconventional pick strategy) that exploits a specific map-pool weakness in Inner Circle's recent form, combined with psychological momentum from being underdogs in a must-win elimination match."}], "final_score": 0.5409889544384815, "no_score": 0.5095979120256294, "edge": 0.34090909090909094, "no_edge": 0.040909090909090895, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 54.10% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 49.71% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2006994", "question": "Dota 2: Inner Circle vs Ilbirs eSports (BO3) - European Pro League Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket semifinal match between Inner Circle and Ilbirs eSports in the European Pro League Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 11:50AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle\" if Inner Circle win the match against Ilbirs eSports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ilbirs eSports\" if Ilbirs eSports win the match against Inner Circle.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-17T21:50:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T15:50:00Z", "yes_price": 0.35, "volume_usd": 0.0, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["44243092642576390786751640568550489206210276974646430023319139384527429073623", "98502953157855205786658972024436735668028081169572240729709475978847042273864"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["European Pro League Season 36 is an online European Dota 2 tournament organized by EPL.", "This Tier 3 tournament takes place from Apr 02 to 18 2026 featuring", "Puck  Nature's Prophet  Tiny  |  | Bans |  |  ---  | Beastmaster  Batrider  Phoenix  Night Stalker  Tusk  Slark  Templar Assassin | Game 1 | Doom  Alchemist  Keeper of the Light  