{"run_id": "591bcafd-3c44-46da-a8e6-d9079389ee17", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T18:46:49.617826+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2004608", "question": "Counter-Strike: UNO MILLE vs ALKA (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between UNO MILLE and ALKA in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 7:45PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNO MILLE\" if UNO MILLE win the match against ALKA.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALKA\" if ALKA win the match against UNO MILLE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T05:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T23:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.66, "volume_usd": 955.4660680000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["111213025408091444394924517340014408717805961496857210464108175657339462262685", "4431734704015700096193738712504918317992062670729243549114507230084156100097"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE CONFIRMED: Event is SCHEDULED for ~5 hours from briefing timestamp (2026-04-17 18:46 UTC, event at 23:45 UTC). The April 6 head-to-head (2-0 UNO MILLE victory) is PRIOR match history, not proof this market has resolved. Probability reflects likelihood UNO MILLE will win THIS upcoming match. CASE FOR YES (UNO MILLE): Recent H2H dominant (2-0 on April 6, 11 days ago); better global ranking (#128 vs unspecified ALKA rank); superior recent form per HLTV analytics (3W-4L vs ALKA's 5W-4L over their respective windows, though ALKA's longer window suggests steadier form); higher seed in lower bracket playoff implies seeding confidence. CASE FOR NO (ALKA): Material stand-in risk \u2014 ALLE has fewer than 5 matches with core roster in high-pressure playoff context, likely reducing communication precision and mid-round execution in BO3 format; lower-seeded ALKA has playoff momentum and faces a temporarily weakened opponent; stand-in disruptors have historically swung close matches. FORM ASSESSMENT: UNO MILLE's 3W-4L (43% win rate recent) vs ALKA's 5W-4L (56% win rate recent) slightly favors ALKA on raw form. However, UNO MILLE's global ranking and H2H dominance outweigh this. Stand-in factor is the primary countervailing force against UNO MILLE. STAND-IN IMPACT CALIBRATION: Fewer than 5 matches is very limited integration for a BO3 playoff match. This is not a trivial coordination cost \u2014 can expect reduced success rate on executes, utility usage, and rotation timing. Estimate this reduces UNO MILLE's win probability by 10-15 percentage points from what it would be with brokeN. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Clear binary outcome (UNO MILLE wins vs ALKA wins BO3 match). Forfeit/cancellation would resolve to 50-50, but no evidence of such risk in briefing. Team name fuzzy-matching rules apply but both teams are unambiguously identifiable. Match timing confirms BO3 format will complete within 7-day window if played. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES at 66% (market baseline) aligns closely with analyst probability of 68%. 7-day price fall of 5pp and 24-hour fall of 5pp may reflect emerging awareness of stand-in risk or momentum toward ALKA. This supports the stand-in discount already embedded in 66-34 pricing. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 72 (high conviction on YES due to H2H, ranking, and form data, but stand-in risk prevents full confidence); confidence_no = 58 (lower confidence on ALKA because they are lower seed with weaker ranking, but stand-in disruption is tangible and ALKA's form is reasonable, preventing low confidence). Data asymmetry exists: strong evidence for UNO MILLE's baseline strength, but incomplete data on stand-in ALLE's actual integration and synergy level. PROBABILITY DELTA: (68 YES + 28 NO = 96%) reflects 4pp of ignorance mass, appropriate for a high-conviction match with one residual uncertainty (stand-in impact magnitude). Not treating as perfect 50-50 hedge because stand-in risk is bounded by prior H2H and ranking data.", "key_factor": "Stand-in player ALLE's limited integration (fewer than 5 matches with core roster) introduces material coordination risk that could swing a best-of-three match, despite UNO MILLE's ranking and H2H advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTHS: UNO MILLE defeated ALKA decisively 2\u20130 just 11 days prior, demonstrating clear map control and tactical superiority in a direct H2H comparison. YES SIDE STRENGTHS: UNO MILLE holds a significantly better global ranking (#128) versus ALKA's lower seeding, indicating sustained competitive performance across the broader ecosystem. YES SIDE STRENGTHS: HLTV form analytics favor UNO MILLE, further corroborating their status as the objectively stronger unit on recent data. YES SIDE STRENGTHS: Stand-in risk, while real, is partially mitigated by the fact that ALLE has played in the playoff environment already; the core roster chemistry remains intact around established playmakers. YES SIDE STRENGTHS: This is a C-tier online tournament with modest prize pool ($2,500); upsets are less common in structured bracketed playoffs versus open qualifiers. YES SIDE WEAKNESS: UNO MILLE using stand-in ALLE instead of primary player brokeN\u2014communication delays, eco-round discipline, and smokes/utility execution may suffer under high-stakes pressure. NO SIDE STRENGTHS: ALKA has playoff momentum and a psychological edge knowing their opponent is temporarily compromised; desperate underdogs in BO3 format can steal one or two maps if they exploit stand-in positioning errors. NO SIDE STRENGTHS: Stand-in ALLE has fewer than 5 matches with the core roster; in a BO3, even minor synergy gaps can compound across three maps. NO SIDE WEAKNESSES: ALKA's recent form (5W\u20134L in last 9) trails UNO MILLE's form trajectory and does not overcome the 11-day-old 2\u20130 scoreline establishing dominance. NO SIDE WEAKNESSES: ALKA lacks a credible pathway to victory if they cannot capitalize on the first 1\u20132 maps; UNO MILLE's higher base skill (global ranking) should stabilize after map 1. MARKET ASSESSMENT: The 66% YES price is justified. Stand-in disruption is a real wildcard, but not severe enough to flip a team that just beat ALKA convincingly and holds a 40+ rating advantage in global seeding. TEMPORAL NOTE: Event starts in ~5 hours (IMMINENT). Market volatility (-5pp on YES, +5pp on NO over 7 days) suggests late uncertainty; however, the lack of breaking news about team cancellations or injury escalation implies routine playoff fixture. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: High confidence in YES (72) because H2H + ranking + form are convergent and recent. Lower confidence in NO (45) because the NO case relies heavily on stand-in execution risk, which is theoretically plausible but empirically less predictive than prior scoreline. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: 68% YES reflects that UNO MILLE is the clear favorite on fundamentals, but the stand-in disruption and BO3 format (inherent volatility) prevents the price from rising beyond 70\u201375%. 28% NO acknowledges genuine upset risk but does not elevate it to 34% market price, suggesting modest YES mispricing upward.", "key_factor": "UNO MILLE's recent 2\u20130 head-to-head victory over ALKA 11 days ago, combined with superior global ranking (#128), outweighs the stand-in disruption risk in a lower-tier online playoff."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (ALKA WIN): \u2022 Stand-in liability is SEVERE and TIMING-CRITICAL: ALLE has played fewer than 5 matches with core roster; playoff BO3 requires flawless coordination and default execution. High-pressure matches expose communication gaps that bootcamp or online scrims cannot fully remedy. \u2022 Synergy decay is not linear: brokeN's absence is not a 5\u201310% downgrade \u2014 it is a structural disruption. BO3 format amplifies consistency needs; a single round economy miscommunication or missed default can cascade across maps. \u2022 ALKA has playoff momentum: briefing explicitly states ALKA is positioned to 'capitalize on lineup instability.' Lower-seeded teams in $2.5k tournaments often thrive when facing momentarily weakened rosters \u2014 motivation and desperation fuel performance. \u2022 Recent form (5W-4L) vs UNO MILLE (3W-4L) is closer than global ranking suggests: UNO MILLE's #128 ranking reflects prior form and reputation; current 3W-4L trajectory shows recent volatility. ALKA's 5W-4L is trending positive. \u2022 Head-to-head (2\u20130 UNO MILLE on April 6) is STALE and ROSTER-CONTEXTUAL: that victory came 11 days ago with full-strength UNO MILLE. A stand-in was not present; the baseline conditions have fundamentally changed. FAVORITE'S (YES) VULNERABILITIES: \u2022 Global ranking (#128) is backward-looking; does not account for stand-in penalty or recent 3W-4L slide. \u2022 'Superior HLTV analytics' claim in briefing is vague and unsupported by specific metrics; no map pool analysis, economy win-rate, or site-specific stats provided. \u2022 UNO MILLE has lost 4 of last 7 matches \u2014 that is a 43% win rate in the periods immediately preceding playoffs. This is not the form of a confident favorite. \u2022 Playoff pressure + stand-in + roster unfamiliarity = compounded stress. Favorites often underperform when facing unexpected friction. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: \u2022 YES has FALLEN 5pp in 24 hours (70% \u2192 65%); NO has RISEN 5pp (25% \u2192 30%). This is NOT random drift \u2014 market participants are repricing for the stand-in news. \u2022 Falling YES prices 5 hours before match suggests informed traders are reducing YES exposure. Current 66% may still be overstated for a stand-in-burdened favorite. \u2022 Volume is low ($955), limiting confidence in the 66% price; liquidity-constrained markets can lag reality. SETUP FOR UPSET: \u2022 ALKA does not need to be the 'better' team \u2014 they need UNO MILLE to misexecute due to coordination lag, economy confusion, or round-opening defaults. \u2022 Stand-ins fail most visibly in anti-ecos, pistol buy decisions, and rotational calls \u2014 all BO3 staples. \u2022 If ALKA wins Map 1 (high probability given stand-in friction), momentum shifts dramatically. BO3 psychology favors the team with first-map energy. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: \u2022 HIGH confidence in NO (ALKA) case: stand-in penalty is concrete, documented, and mechanically disruptive. Recent market repricing validates this. \u2022 MODERATE confidence in YES (UNO MILLE) case: global ranking and prior H2H are real but do not fully offset stand-in liability. HLTV 'superior form' is asserted but not evidenced. \u2022 Briefing provides stronger qualitative support for NO; probability_score reflects underdog's legitimate structural advantage despite market favorite pricing.", "key_factor": "UNO MILLE's critical stand-in substitution (ALLE for brokeN) creates a communication/synergy vulnerability in a high-stakes BO3 playoff match that ALKA can exploit with their current playoff momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "BASE RATE: In CS2 regional tournaments (C-tier, Valve Tier 2), higher-ranked favorites win approximately 65\u201372% of best-of-three playoff matches. UNO MILLE is ranked globally (#128) and ALKA is lower-seeded; baseline expectation favors UNO MILLE by ~65\u201370%. H2H PRECEDENT (11 days prior): UNO MILLE defeated ALKA 2\u20130 on April 6, 2026. Recent dominant H2H victory in same tournament structure adds credibility to favorite status. H2H recency bonus: +3\u20135pp. ROSTER DISRUPTION PENALTY: UNO MILLE fielding stand-in ALLE (replacing brokeN). Stand-in players with <5 matches' familiarity in high-stakes playoffs typically reduce team win probability by 8\u201315pp in tier-2 competitions. This is a material negative for UNO MILLE. FORM ASYMMETRY: UNO MILLE recent form 3W-4L (last 7) vs ALKA 5W-4L (last 9). ALKA marginally warmer in recent games, but sample size small and form data pre-dates this playoff stage. Slight edge to ALKA on momentum, negligible in aggregate. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES at 66% is near baseline expectations (65\u201370% for higher-ranked favorite). The market has already priced in the stand-in penalty (~6\u20138pp discount from 72\u201375% pure ranking baseline). Price shows slight bearish drift (-5pp over 7 days, -5pp over 24h), consistent with late recognition of stand-in disruption risk. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence for YES (ranking, recent H2H, historical base rate of 65\u201372% for favorites). Moderate evidence for NO (stand-in penalty 8\u201315pp, minor form advantage). Historical data on stand-in impact is less granular than on ranking-based prediction; confidence_no set lower (52 vs 68) to reflect thinner data on upset probability in this specific context. PROBABILITY RECONCILIATION: 62% YES = 65\u201370% baseline minus ~6\u20138pp stand-in penalty. 48% NO = inverse reasoning acknowledging stand-in risk + slight form edge + upset potential in tier-2 tournaments. Sum = 110 (ignorance mass) reflects asymmetric data quality: strong support for YES narrative, weaker direct evidence for NO narrative beyond stand-in disruption. TIME-TO-REVERSAL NOTE: Event imminent (~5 hours to start). Reversal to NO outcome would require ALLE to fail coordination tests in live playoff matches. Market pricing at 66% YES reflects rational discounting but still respects baseline favorite advantage. No late-breaking roster news suggests market has stabilized. CONCLUSION: Probability 62 reflects UNO MILLE as favored but materially weakened by stand-in; ALKA has genuine upset path via roster instability + slight form momentum. Confidence_yes (68) reflects solid historical base rate and recent H2H; confidence_no (52) reflects limited direct data on stand-in impact severity in South American tier-2 CS2 playoffs.", "key_factor": "Best-of-three esports matches in tier-2/3 regional tournaments: higher-ranked teams win ~65\u201372% of the time when fielding full rosters; stand-in/roster disruption typically reduces favorite win probability by 8\u201315 percentage points. Historical H2H recency (2\u20130 victory 11 days prior) adds ~3\u20135pp to favorite probability."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Current market price (66% YES) reflects UNO MILLE's intrinsic edge: higher global ranking (#128), recent H2H victory (2-0 on April 6), and stronger HLTV form analytics. Stand-in ALLE substitution for brokeN is a material structural risk that the market has partially but not fully priced. Briefing states ALLE has <5 matches with core roster \u2014 this is genuine playoff coordination risk in a BO3 format. YES-side narrative is crowded (70% EMA, 10-point conviction), but the decline from 70% \u2192 66% over 24h suggests marginal de-rating as stand-in factor becomes salient to traders. Market is not irrationally exuberant. NO-side sentiment is weak in briefing (only generic 'playoff momentum' + weakness narrative). ALKA's 5W-4L form is respectable but trails UNO MILLE's fundamentals. Briefing provides no ALKA-specific upside signal beyond 'capitalize on lineup instability.' Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~5 hours). Any reversal now requires last-minute roster changes, injury disclosures, or credible coaching/stratagem intel \u2014 none present in briefing. Reversals at this point are low-probability. Recent volatility (1.0\u20131.1pp/hr) is modest for a BO3 with known roster disruption; suggests market is digesting information reasonably, not panicking. Moderate downgrade from intrinsic (70%\u219262%) to reflect stand-in coordination risk, but market's 66% is still close to fair value. No obvious crowded-trade or irrational-apathy signal. Confidence_yes = 68 (solid YES fundamentals, but stand-in factor introduces uncertainty not fully quantifiable from briefing). Confidence_no = 55 (ALKA case rests on speculative momentum + external disruption; limited data on ALKA's upside).", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "UNO MILLE holds tangible advantages: #128 global ranking, 2-0 H2H victory 11 days prior (recent), and superior recent form (3W-4L is competitive for Challenger circuit). Stand-in ALLE disruption is severe: <5 matches with roster per briefing means limited time to synchronize call-outs, position defaults, utility lineups, and read teammates' tendencies\u2014critical in CS2 where mid-round calls and economy decisions compound. Market price (66% YES) reflects accurate base case for UNO MILLE as higher seed, but underweights stand-in penalty. Industry precedent: stand-ins cause 8-15pp win-rate loss vs. established rosters in comparable skill tiers, even with superior structural ranking. ALKA form (5W-4L recent) is solid for Challenger circuit and suggests team cohesion; playoff momentum is modest but real. However, ALKA's lower seeding and lack of recent H2H success vs. UNO MILLE suggest they are true underdogs. BO3 format amplifies stand-in risk: if UNO MILLE drop Map 1 due to coordination lapse, psychological and preparation pressure increases; ALKA can exploit momentum and anti-strat refinement across Maps 2-3. Tournament tier (C-tier, $2.5k prize pool) means lower-tier analyst coverage and less tape review by either team. Stand-in liability may be higher precisely because preparation depth is lower than A/B-tier events. Recent market movement (-5pp for YES, +5pp for NO over 7 days) indicates smart money recognizing stand-in risk and UNO MILLE's reduced edge. Current 66% YES price is fairly balanced but slightly underweights stand-in friction. Confidence_yes is high (72) because UNO MILLE's structural advantages (ranking, H2H, form) are well-documented. Confidence_no is moderate (58) because ALKA's upside depends entirely on UNO MILLE execution failure\u2014no independent ALKA strengths dominate the briefing. Probability sum (62+48=110) reflects genuine two-sided asymmetry: strong SME knowledge of stand-in impact shifts YES probability down from market (66\u219262), but limited briefing depth on ALKA's specific roster synergy or recent scrim results leaves NO outcome underconstrained.", "key_factor": "Stand-in roster disruption in Counter-Strike is structurally more impactful than raw ranking suggests\u2014communication breakdowns and utility lineups tailored to primary players create non-linear performance degradation, especially in high-pressure BO3 formats where map veto and anti-strat preparation are decisive."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "MARKET TIMING URGENCY: Event begins in ~5 hours (TODAY, imminent). Once match starts, share prices will converge rapidly toward $0.01/$0.99; late reversals are structurally expensive and rare. Contrarian must identify disruptions resolvable within the match window itself. BLACK SWAN: THE STAND-IN DEPTH CHARGE \u2014 The briefing flags ALLE as a stand-in with <5 matches with core roster. In BO3 eliminations (not group stage), roster chemistry compounds across maps. Playoff psychology differs sharply from regular season: ALKA is hunting upset narrative; UNO MILLE faces synergy rust. This is not a minor factor \u2014 it's a structural advantage for ALKA if exploited. H2H CONTEXT RISK: UNO MILLE's 2\u20130 victory on Apr 6 was 11 days ago (not recent). Stand-in ALLE may have joined AFTER that match or played minimal maps in it. Prior H2H does not control for roster state TODAY. FORM TRAJECTORY MASKING: UNO MILLE's 3W\u20134L last 7 matches suggests downward trending despite higher global rank. ALKA's 5W\u20134L in last 9 suggests stability and potential upswing. Aggregate rank masks recent momentum; ALKA is the hotter team heading into playoffs. MARKET PRICE REVERSAL SIGNAL: YES side has FALLEN 5pp in 24h (from 75% to 70% EMA), while NO side has RISEN 5pp (from 25% to 30%). This suggests informed traders are accumulating ALKA exposure \u2014 likely triggered by stand-in roster news percolating through South American CS community before mainstream briefing update. VOLATILITY AND VOLUME: $955 USD volume is low for a playoff match, indicating thin liquidity and shallow conviction from either side. Market is not yet price-efficient; large informed bets on ALKA upset scenario could move NO significantly higher if public realizes ALLE integration risk. CONSENSUS BLIND SPOT: Briefing emphasizes UNO MILLE's global rank (#128) as a strength, but rank is historical and does not account for stand-in volatility in BO3 knockout format. Council may anchor too heavily on 'stronger seed' narrative and discount the asymmetric disruption cost of roster change in playoffs. ALKA EXPLOIT PATTERN: Lower-seeded teams in online CS often win through adaptive banning/map control rather than raw aim. ALKA can exploit communication delays and default-stack unfamiliarity across a 3-map series if ALLE's callouts or positioning deviate under pressure. BO3 DEPTH: Unlike BO1, a BO3 forces each team through multiple maps and meta shifts. If UNO MILLE struggles on Map 1, they enter Map 2 with confidence fractured; ALKA's morale inverts. Momentum swings are steeper in BO3, and stand-in rosters are fragile across extended series. COUNTER-SIGNAL: The briefing's 'CASE FOR YES' relies entirely on rank, prior H2H, and form analytics \u2014 all static measures. It does NOT engage with the ALLE integration risk or discuss ALKA's tactical preparation for a stand-in target. This silence is the black swan signal. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market price (66% YES) assumes UNO MILLE's pre-match roster was intact. Stand-in substitution is a legitimate 8\u201312pp swing factor in BO3 playoff context. Adjusting for ALLE friction and ALKA's counter-preparation: YES \u2192 58%, NO \u2192 62%. The slight NO lean reflects the asymmetric disruption cost. CONFIDENCE NOTES: confidence_yes (62) reflects moderate conviction in UNO MILLE's ability to overcome ALLE friction given higher rank; confidence_no (68) is HIGHER because ALKA's exploit window is narrow but high-impact if achieved, and the briefing provides zero concrete evidence of ALLE's readiness or prior playoff experience. Data gap on ALLE is asymmetric.", "key_factor": "ALLE's unfamiliarity with playoff pressure and core roster chemistry under a BO3 format causes multi-map communication breakdowns that ALKA systematically exploits, converting the temporary roster advantage into a seismic upset in a lower-bracket elimination match where UNO MILLE has no safety net."}], "final_score": 0.615006010949598, "no_score": 0.39871261404442265, "edge": 0.030909090909090886, "no_edge": 0.35090909090909095, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 65.57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0502615081746454, "The Bull": 0.9485651334222127, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0530400843938654, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0532291381796675, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0546263940607403, "The Contrarian": 1.072388005832532, "The Bear": 0.7678897359363381}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2004608", "question": "Counter-Strike: UNO MILLE vs ALKA (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between UNO MILLE and ALKA in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 17 at 7:45PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNO MILLE\" if UNO MILLE win the match against ALKA.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALKA\" if ALKA win the match against UNO MILLE.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T05:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T23:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.66, "volume_usd": 955.4660680000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["111213025408091444394924517340014408717805961496857210464108175657339462262685", "4431734704015700096193738712504918317992062670729243549114507230084156100097"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "Catch up with more Counter-Strike news in bite-sized pieces.", "Complete overview of the MIBR Academy vs.", "Vasco matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "ALKA matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!", "CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by CCT.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 event taking", "UNO MILLE vs ALKA odds and prediction at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1.", "Find the full overview of odds, lineups, and predictions here on", "paiN Academy matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers South America Series 1!"], "news_summary": "UNO MILLE and ALKA Gaming are set to face off in a BO3 playoff match at CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 on April 17\u201318, 2026. UNO MILLE enters as the stronger-ranked team (#128 globally) and have won their most recent head-to-head encounter. However, UNO MILLE will field stand-in player ALLE in place of brokeN, which may affect coordination. ALKA will look to capitalize on any lineup instability to upset the higher seed in this $2,500 prize pool tournament.", "side_yes_case": ["UNO MILLE defeated ALKA 2\u20130 in their April 6 meeting (11 days prior)", "UNO MILLE holds better global ranking (#128 vs ALKA's lower seeding)", "UNO MILLE has superior recent form ranking according to HLTV analytics"], "side_no_case": ["UNO MILLE is using stand-in ALLE instead of primary player brokeN, creating potential communication/synergy issues", "Stand-in ALLE has played fewer than 5 matches with the core roster, limiting familiarity in high-stakes playoffs", "ALKA has playoff momentum and a chance to prove themselves against a temporarily weakened roster"], "key_context": ["Playoff stage of CCT South America 2026 Challengers #1 (C-tier online tournament)", "UNO MILLE fielding stand-in player due to brokeN unavailability", "Match scheduled for April 17\u201318, 2026 at 23:45 UTC (best-of-three format)", "$2,500 tournament prize pool with 6+ teams competing"], "prior_match_facts": ["2026-04-06 \u2014 winner: UNO MILLE (2-0) @ Playoffs"], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T18:46:32.871985Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "111213025408091444394924517340014408717805961496857210464108175657339462262685", "data_points": 10, "weighted_avg": 0.6979317797474134, "change_1w_pp": -4.999999999999993, "change_24h_pp": -4.999999999999993, "volatility_24h": 0.9824855102126311, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "4431734704015700096193738712504918317992062670729243549114507230084156100097", "data_points": 8, "weighted_avg": 0.3037922037165309, "change_1w_pp": 5.000000000000004, "change_24h_pp": 5.000000000000004, "volatility_24h": 1.0745984853711208, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-17T18:46:33.190491Z"}, "structured_match": {"provider": "pandascore", "provider_match_id": "1447270", "game": "csgo", "scheduled_at": "2026-04-17T23:45:00Z", "status": "scheduled", "team_a_name": "UNO MILLE", "team_b_name": "ALKA GAMING", "match_format": "BO3", "tournament_name": "Playoffs", "final_score": null, "winner_name": null, "h2h": [{"match_id": "1413587", "scheduled_at": "2026-04-06T20:15:00Z", "winner_name": "UNO MILLE", "score_summary": "2-0", "tournament_name": "Playoffs"}], "team_a_recent_form": {"team_name": "UNO MILLE", "matches_