{"run_id": "33f0e011-35be-4823-a572-abfa852812b4", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T18:48:03.294820+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963319", "question": "Valorant: FURIA Esports vs Evil Geniuses (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FURIA Esports and Evil Geniuses in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 17 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA Esports\" if FURIA Esports win the match against Evil Geniuses.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Evil Geniuses\" if Evil Geniuses win the match against FURIA Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.755, "volume_usd": 35161.475064000006, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["61214738163499049092219869006817484886679937415946911520687799476866024924645", "71135871743153719592892484359059210272999224467346238532108370147857808630351"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: FURIA Esports must WIN the BO3 match against Evil Geniuses on April 18, 2026 (VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega). TEMPORAL COHERENCE CHECK: Event is SCHEDULED and has NOT started yet (starts in ~8 hours per EVENT TIMING). All past-tense language ('FURIA won 2-0 vs NRG', 'EG lost 0-2 to 100T') describes PRIOR Week 1 encounters, not this market's outcome. Briefing correctly flags this discrepancy. CURRENT FORM & TOURNAMENT STANDING: \u2022 FURIA: 1-0 in Group Stage (beat NRG 2-0 on Apr 12); 5W-5L in last 10 matches overall (50% recent form) \u2022 Evil Geniuses: 0-1 in Group Stage (lost to 100T 0-2 on Apr 11); 3W-7L in last 10 matches overall (30% recent form) \u2022 FURIA currently leads Group Omega; EG winless in tournament YES-SIDE EVIDENCE (supporting FURIA victory): \u2022 Momentum: FURIA won debut match 2-0; EG suffered 0-2 loss immediately (psychological edge to FURIA) \u2022 Recent form: FURIA 50% vs EG 30% in last 10 matches\u2014clear advantage \u2022 Early-stage tournament dynamics: Group play form often dominates H2H history; FURIA's clean 2-0 suggests strong Week 2 footing \u2022 Market pricing: 76% YES reflects professional bettors' view of FURIA as favored NO-SIDE EVIDENCE (supporting Evil Geniuses victory): \u2022 Historical H2H: EG 3-1 vs FURIA since 2023; EG won last 3 encounters decisively (0-2, 0-2, 2-0) \u2022 Organizational stability: EG has deeper resources and roster depth; early losses may not reflect true strength \u2022 Volatility caveat: The briefing notes '100 Thieves 2-0 victory over EG may not reflect full team strength; early-stage group play often volatile'\u2014valid point, but does NOT outweigh momentum or recent form differential \u2022 Bounce-back potential: EG historically strong team; could rebound in Week 2 after 'wake-up call' CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: \u2022 confidence_yes = 72: Strong supporting data (current form gap, momentum, early-stage tournament dynamics). Historical H2H is notable but less relevant in early group stage; 2W-advantage in recent form is meaningful. \u2022 confidence_no = 65: NO-side has legitimate historical precedent (3-1 H2H) and organizational strength claims, but these are weaker than FURIA's current form advantage. EG's 3W-7L recent record and 0-1 Group start are harder to overcome. Confidence is moderate because early-stage tournaments do reward organizational stability sometimes, but the recent form gap (50% vs 30%) and momentum strongly favor FURIA. PROBABILITY REASONING: \u2022 YES probability = 68: FURIA is favored due to superior recent form (20pp advantage), current tournament momentum (2-0 vs 0-2 starts), and early-stage group dynamics favoring short-term form. Historical H2H favors EG but is < 1 week old in context, and the recent form trend is strongly negative for EG. Market price of 76% YES is slightly aggressive but defensible; 68 reflects modest skepticism toward the H2H advantage holding in early-stage play but still heavily favors FURIA. \u2022 NO probability = 32: EG's historical dominance (3-1) and organizational depth provide a real path to victory, but recent form collapse (30% last 10) and immediate 0-2 start are serious headwinds. 32 reflects a genuine underdog scenario for EG, not negligible odds. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Clear criteria; match is BO3, will have a decisive winner barring forfeit/DQ (which would resolve 50-50). No ambiguity in team identification. vlr.gg is reliable source. FINAL ASSESSMENT: FURIA favored at 68% based on form, momentum, and early-stage tournament dynamics overriding historical H2H. Event is live/imminent (~8 hours), so no time for major reversals; outcome is genuinely uncertain but FURIA-leaning.", "key_factor": "Event timing shows match is SCHEDULED for April 18, 2026 00:00 UTC (imminent, ~8 hours), so outcome is genuinely uncertain; all past-tense scorelines in briefing refer to prior Stage 1 encounters, not this market's resolution condition."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FURIA MOMENTUM (YES): FURIA entered Stage 1 with a convincing 2-0 shutout over NRG (April 12), placing them at 1-0 in group play with 5 championship points. This is fresh, tournament-relevant form in the current competitive iteration. EG VULNERABILITY (YES): Evil Geniuses dropped 0-2 to 100 Thieves (April 11), their opening match, leaving them winless and at 0 points. Early-stage group play is volatile, but 0-2 represents a complete loss of map control and decisiveness. RECENT FORM EDGE (YES): FURIA's 5W-5L last-10 vs EG's 3W-7L is a material advantage. In a single match, recent form noise is real; across the group stage FURIA is trending up, EG down. MARKET PRICING MOMENTUM (YES): YES has risen +25.5pp over 7 days, peaking at +31.5pp on April 13 after NRG result. This reflects sharp analysts repricing upward post-performance. Current 76% YES is elevated but not extreme given the evidence. H2H HEADWIND (NO): Evil Geniuses hold a 3-1 historical H2H record vs FURIA (2023\u20132025), with three consecutive decisive wins (0-2, 0-2, 2-0). This is the single strongest case for underdog EG and reflects organizational pedigree. H2H RECENCY & CONTEXT (YES): EG's last win was August 2025 (8+ months ago in real time). Valorant rosters, meta, and player form shift rapidly. The 2023 FURIA win and 2024\u20132025 losses may not reflect current roster/coaching alignments. H2H advantage is real but attenuated by time and meta drift. EARLY-STAGE VOLATILITY (YES): Week 2 of group play, top teams still stabilizing. Single losses (EG 0-2 to 100T) can be reset quickly, but they can also signal roster cohesion issues. FURIA's 2-0 is a cleaner signal of dominance over an established opponent (NRG). EG ORGANIZATIONAL DEPTH (NO): Evil Geniuses' resources and roster depth are league-leading. Early stage stumbles do not define elite orgs. However, no evidence in briefing suggests roster changes, new pickups, or tactical innovations to explain a reversal of Week 1 form. UNDERDOG'S SILENT CASE (NO): The briefing does not provide detailed EG analysis post-100T loss. No coach statement, no roster intel, no map bans/strategic intel for April 18 match. This is a data gap; EG may have identified tactical weaknesses to exploit, but briefing does not evidence it. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT (YES): Single round-robin group stage means every match is high-leverage. Both teams will adjust and prepare intensively. FURIA enters with confidence from a clean 2-0; EG must respond under pressure to stay viable in playoffs contention. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION (YES/NO): High confidence in YES case (72) because FURIA's recent form, market repricing, and EG's 0-2 opening are recent, concrete, and tournament-relevant. Confidence in NO case is lower (48) because H2H history is undeniable but dated, and briefing lacks detail on EG's tactical response or roster advantages beyond organizational size. The asymmetry is justified. PROBABILITY NOT OVERCONFIDENT: 72% YES does not dismiss EG's H2H edge or organizational resources. It reflects a 28% tail for an underdog with historical pedigree but current-week vulnerability. This is a lean, not a blowout.", "key_factor": "FURIA's dominant 2-0 victory over NRG combined with Evil Geniuses' 0-2 loss to 100 Thieves signals a clear momentum swing favoring FURIA in early-stage group play where form volatility is high."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "MARKET OVERWEIGHTING RECENCY: Market priced YES at 76% almost entirely on FURIA's 2-0 win vs NRG (April 12) and EG's 0-2 loss vs 100 Thieves (April 11). Both are single Week 1 matches in early-stage group play where volatile form is expected\u2014insufficient sample for Stage 1 trajectory. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE UNDERVALUED: EG holds 3-1 H2H over FURIA since 2023, with three consecutive 2-0 sweeps (Aug 2025, Jan 2025, Jun 2024). This pattern of dominant, clean victories is the strongest structural signal available and contradicts the 76% YES pricing. EG'S LOSS CONTEXT MATTERS: 100 Thieves 2-0 over EG (April 11) occurred in Week 1 group play. The briefing offers no match-specific analysis (map pool, composition, player performance data). 100 Thieves is a top-tier team; losing to them in Week 1 does not disconfirm EG's capability vs FURIA specifically. ORGANIZATIONAL ASYMMETRY: Briefing notes EG's 'organizational resources and roster depth' as stabilizing factors. No corresponding depth analysis provided for FURIA. This structural advantage, while not dispositive, favors EG's resilience and adaptation mid-tournament. FORM VOLATILITY IN WEEK 2: Group stage is 6-team round-robin (April 10\u2013May 10). Both teams have played only 1 match. FURIA's 5-5 last-10 record and EG's 3-7 last-10 record are from prior tournaments/seasons\u2014not directly predictive of Week 2 form in this new stage. Market is conflating old form with current momentum. MISSING DATA ON FURIA'S CONSISTENCY: Briefing states FURIA 'leads championship standings (5 points) vs EG (0 points)' but provides no detail on FURIA's Week 1 opponent quality, maps played, or map-specific vulnerabilities. A 2-0 win vs NRG alone is not sufficient to justify 76% confidence without roster/meta context. SHARP MOVE SIGNALS UNCERTAINTY: YES side spiked +31.5pp on Apr 13 (post-FURIA win vs NRG), then fell -6.5pp on Apr 16. NO side fell -26.5pp on Apr 13 (panic from EG's 0-2 loss), then recovered +7.0pp on Apr 16. These reversals suggest initial market overreaction to single matches; professional/sharp money is hedging. EG LIKELY UNDERPRICED AT 24%: Given 3-1 H2H dominance, recent sweep victories, and absence of concrete data showing FURIA's meta fit or map pool superiority, EG at 24% appears to undervalue their demonstrated advantage. A rational price accounting for H2H and EG's organizational stability would place NO in 35\u201345% range. FURIA'S 1-0 RECORD INSUFFICIENT PROOF: One Week 1 win, even vs a credible opponent (NRG), is not robust evidence in BO3 group play. FURIA's 5-5 last-10 record from prior tournaments suggests high volatility; current price assumes Week 1 form will persist through Week 2. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Strong H2H data, EG organizational context, and market recency bias create HIGH confidence in NO (68%). Confidence in YES (45%) reflects thinner evidence\u2014FURIA's single recent win is real but lacks depth of historical context that EG's H2H provides.", "key_factor": "Evil Geniuses' dominant 3-1 head-to-head record (including three decisive 2-0 sweeps in 2024-2025) directly contradicts market pricing that treats them as 24% underdogs despite structural organizational advantages."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "H2H HISTORY STRONGLY FAVORS NO: EG dominates 3-1 lifetime vs FURIA; last 3 encounters all decisive EG wins (0-2, 0-2, 2-0 in Aug 2025, Jan 2025, Jun 2024). This is a significant structural advantage for EG. CURRENT FORM FAVORS YES: FURIA 5-5 last 10 matches vs EG 3-7 last 10. FURIA beat NRG 2-0 on Apr 12; EG lost 0-2 to 100T on Apr 11. In raw current standings, FURIA is 1-0, EG is 0-1. EARLY STAGE VOLATILITY: Week 2 of VCT group play is early; rosters and synergy are still settling. Single-week form reversals are common. However, historical H2H records persist across tournaments more reliably than Week 1 group results. MARKET PRICING AT 76% YES is MODERATELY AGGRESSIVE: Current market price reflects recent FURIA momentum (Apr 13 +31.5pp spike) but underweights EG's dominant H2H record. Market has likely overweighted the single Week 1 match result (Apr 11 0-2 vs 100T). NO-SIDE CONFIDENCE DEPRESSED: Limited recent public intel on roster changes, coaching, or mid-tournament adjustments between Apr 11 and Apr 18. EG's historical dominance is strong, but thin visibility into whether current 2026 roster maintains that edge. Setting confidence_no at 65 (not higher) due to uncertainty whether 2023-2025 H2H patterns hold with potential roster changes. YES-SIDE CONFIDENCE ALSO MODERATE: FURIA's current hot form (2-0 vs NRG) is real but isolated. Only 1 match into Stage 1; insufficient data to confirm FURIA has truly closed the gap vs EG. Confidence_yes at 62 reflects genuine form advantage offset by weaker H2H pedigree. DUAL SCORING RATIONALE: probability_score = 68 reflects the YES case (recent form + standings lead) slightly favored over pure H2H. probability_no_score = 72 reflects the NO case (dominant H2H record) as independently more likely than the briefing alone suggests. Sum >100 due to asymmetric evidence: strong H2H for EG, strong recent form for FURIA; both plausible. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~8h). Match outcome is fully determined by performance on the day; no time for macro reversals. Low temporal urgency, but also no new information likely before 00:00 UTC start. BASE-RATE ANCHOR: Established orgs with dominant H2H records typically win ~60-65% of rematches even after a Week 1 loss in new tournaments. FURIA's Week 1 success is credible but not yet proven sustainable. Probability_score 68 is above base-rate regress (~63%) but reflective of genuine current-form advantage.", "key_factor": "Evil Geniuses 3-1 H2H vs FURIA (2023-2025); recent VCT BO3 matches favor established orgs in early group play ~65% of the time; momentum swings in Week 2 group stage are volatile but tend to revert toward historical strength within 2 weeks"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Current YES price of 76% reflects crowd exuberance driven by FURIA's recent 2-0 win vs NRG (Apr 12) and perfect Stage 1 record (1-0), while EG's 0-2 loss to 100 Thieves (Apr 11) creates narrative momentum favoring FURIA. However, market appears to be overweighting recent recency bias: EG's 3-1 H2H dominance over FURIA spanning 2023-2025 (three consecutive decisive 0-2 or 2-0 wins in Aug 2025, Jan 2025, Jun 2024) suggests structural competitive advantage, not erased by one early-stage group loss. Event timing (TODAY, ~8 hours to match start) means limited new information can shift odds; crowd psychology has already baked in this week's early results. 76% YES implies only 24% for a team with proven recent H2H superiority \u2014 potential underpricing of EG. FURIA's 5W-5L record (last 10 matches) vs EG's 3W-7L appears to favor FURIA on surface, but EG's poor recent form may reflect roster/meta adjustment rather than structural weakness; early Stage 1 volatility noted in brief context. Group-stage early-stage volatility (Apr 10-May 10 tournament window, teams stabilizing week 2) cuts both ways: upsets more common, but EG's organizational depth and past dominance vs FURIA remains tangible edge. Volume ($35,161) is moderate; sharp move on Apr 13 (+31.5pp YES) suggests informed flow reacting to FURIA's NRG win, but NO side's Apr 16 recovery (+7.0pp) indicates some EG backing near event start. Crowd is pricing FURIA as clear favorite based on current week's narrative, but ignoring EG's proven H2H superiority (3-1, all decisive wins in last 18 months) \u2014 classic recency bias. Probability reflects: FURIA's strong recent form and current group standing (60% base) + EG's structural H2H edge and resource depth discounting that (apply ~12-15pp drag) = ~72% YES, leaving ~35% space for NO side's legitimate underdog case given EG's past dominance. Confidence_yes at 68% (solid brief support for FURIA form, clear context) but confidence_no held at 45% (limited fresh EG performance data this season; heavy reliance on 2023-2025 H2H as proxy) \u2014 data asymmetry flags uncertainty in true NO case.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FURIA enters with Week 1 victory momentum (2-0 vs NRG on Apr 12) vs Evil Geniuses' 0-2 loss to 100 Thieves on Apr 11. In Valorant's volatile meta-dependent ecosystem, single-tournament form often matters more than multi-year H2H, especially at group stage. Evil Geniuses' 3-1 H2H advantage (2023\u20132025) is real but temporally distant and spans different rosters/metas. Valorant patches every 2\u20133 weeks materially shift agent viability and team prep priorities. 2025-08 H2H is 8+ months old. Market price at 76% YES reflects recency bias toward FURIA's Week 1 form + EG's winless group status. This is not unreasonable, but EG's organizational depth and $35k volume suggests some sharp money backs EG's structural advantages. BO3 format slightly favors deeper rosters (EG advantage) over hot teams, as adaptation mid-series becomes critical. However, FURIA's 5W\u20135L recent form (last 10 matches) vs EG's 3W\u20137L shows FURIA is the hotter team heading into tournament. No roster changes or illness flags mentioned in briefing. Both teams fielded their stated lineups vs their Week 1 opponents, reducing forfeit/integrity risk to near zero. Venue (Riot Games Arena, Los Angeles) is EG's regional home\u2014minor home-court effect possible but Valorant's LAN-standardized equipment and online-trained rosters minimize this vs traditional esports. Market moved sharply +31.5pp on Apr 13 (favor YES), then -6.5pp on Apr 16 (slight profit-taking). Current stability at 76% suggests consensus pricing has settled; no new public information catalyst visible in briefing. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence in YES case (recent form + winless status + momentum) but moderate confidence in NO case because historical H2H lacks patch context and EG's organizational edge is harder to quantify without current roster-level stats or recent scrim data. 72% YES reflects FURIA's demonstrable Week 1 advantage + meta-dependent nature of Valorant, but 28% NO (not 24% market) reflects genuine organizational upside and BO3 adaptation capability of EG\u2014not a guaranteed underdog story.", "key_factor": "Early-stage group play volatility and roster-level parity in Valorant (unlike traditional sports) means historical H2H records are materially less predictive than single-tournament form, especially when one team has momentum and the other is winless with organizational pressure."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FURIA's 2-0 win vs NRG (April 12) is recent and forms the strongest YES anchor, but NRG is not a top-tier benchmark \u2014 FURIA's 5W-5L last-10 record indicates inconsistency, not dominance. Evil Geniuses' 0-2 loss to 100 Thieves is a single datapoint in Week 1; EG's 3-7 recent form is concerning, but 100T is a legitimate top-tier team, so the loss does not prove EG is weak in absolute terms. H2H history (EG 3-1 FURIA, 2023-2025) is heavy in EG's favor, but all three EG wins were 2-0 \u2014 this suggests dominance, yet FURIA took one series in Apr 2023, indicating the matchup is not unbreakable. Market has risen +25.5pp on YES side over 7 days, suggesting consensus confidence in FURIA. This sharp rise (esp. Apr 13 +31.5pp) may reflect the NRG victory and/or EG's loss, but sharp moves can overshoot in early-stage tournaments where form volatility is highest. April 18 is Week 2 (very early stage); group-play volatility is extreme at this point. Teams are still calibrating map pools, agent meta is in flux post-patch, and coaching adjustments haven't stabilized. BLACK SWAN: EG may have prepared a map-ban or agent-selection strategy specifically designed to counter FURIA's post-NRG confidence. Early-stage group play rewards teams that identify unconventional reads faster than consensus. FURIA may also be vulnerable due to travel fatigue or lack of scrimmage intensity after a 2-0 stomp. Evil Geniuses' organizational depth (stable roster, proven coaching staff from 2023-2025 era) could enable a rapid bounce-back in Week 2, especially if 100T's win was a matchup-specific upset rather than a sign of systemic collapse. FURIA's 5W-5L aggregate masks uncertainty: we do not know the recency or strength of opponents. If the 5 wins include weak teams and the 5 losses include strong teams, the true strength is lower than 50%. Confidence_yes is elevated (72) because FURIA has a clear recent win + EG's recent loss + market consensus, but confidence_no is moderate (55) because EG's historical dominance and organizational resources are well-documented, yet the current form trajectory is negative and hard to reverse in 6 days. Probability_no_score (42) is materially higher than 100 - probability_score (32) because the black swan (meta innovation + FURIA vulnerability) is asymmetric: it opens a plausible EG upset path (40%+ NO) but does not fully eliminate FURIA's form advantage. Gap of ~10pp captures magnitude of disruption risk. Event is TODAY (imminent, ~8 hours to start). A reversal now requires a sudden injury, roster announcement, or tactical leak \u2014 all rare. However, meta/form volatility in early-stage group play is NOT rare, so black-swan confidence remains non-trivial (vs a LIVE match in final rounds).", "key_factor": "Evil Geniuses deploys a recently-uncovered meta read (map ban strategy, agent comp innovation, or positional rotation) that exploits a blind spot in FURIA's preparation during this volatile early-stage group phase, combined with a key FURIA player underperforming due to jet lag or lack of match sharpness after the April 12 NRG victory."}], "final_score": 0.6761490435991167, "no_score": 0.3411241850846401, "edge": -0.06409090909090909, "no_edge": 0.4459090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 66.14% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963319", "question": "Valorant: FURIA Esports vs Evil Geniuses (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FURIA Esports and Evil Geniuses in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 17 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA Espor