{"run_id": "676e69d6-359a-4058-a50c-d85dafa3ffd3", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T16:17:20.984708+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2003495", "question": "Counter-Strike:  Phantom Academy vs Spirit Academy (BO3) - Exort Series Main Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 2 match between  Phantom Academy and Spirit Academy in the Exort Series Main Stage, initially scheduled for April 17 at 2:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" Phantom Academy\" if  Phantom Academy win the match against Spirit Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Spirit Academy\" if Spirit Academy win the match against  Phantom Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T00:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T18:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.27, "volume_usd": 15.641181, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["110138984993261756973756011056418514258658620914492623780638778727393058673435", "97432209044714604284697159427794522859347169952020191020722922848279813366354"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.27, "probability_yes": 0.27, "probability_no": 0.73, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (~2.2 hours to start on 2026-04-17 18:30 UTC). Any past match data in briefing refers to prior encounters, not this resolution. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous. YES resolves if Phantom Academy wins BO3; NO resolves if Spirit Academy wins BO3. Forfeits/walkovers before match starts \u2192 50-50. Incomplete matches with forfeit by opponent \u2192 winner gets resolved. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES = 27%, NO = 73%. Market has recently shifted toward NO (YES down 7.0pp in 24h, rising sharp move at Apr 17 06:00 UTC +7.5pp to NO side). This signal is the strongest available evidence in briefing. STRUCTURED MATCH DATA CONTRADICTION: PandaScore reports Phantom 7W-2L (78% recent win rate) vs Spirit 7W-3L (70% recent win rate), suggesting Phantom is favored. However, this data is NOT corroborated by NEWS SUMMARY or KEY FACTS \u2014 no team intel, rosters, or preparation details appear in search results. Data freshness is 2026-04-17 16:17 UTC (2.2h before match), so timing is current, but source reliability is unverified. NEWS SUMMARY VERDICT: Explicitly states 'no specific information about either team's recent form, roster composition, or head-to-head record' and 'no direct intelligence on either academy team's current competitive status.' This directly contradicts the structured form data, suggesting that PandaScore recent-form metrics may be stale, misaligned, or refer to different competitive contexts (academy vs. main rosters). KEY FACTS ASSESSMENT: Contains generic Counter-Strike news (Valve ranking, player quotes, tournament coverage) but ZERO specific intelligence on Phantom Academy or Spirit Academy. No rosters, no recent match reviews, no preparation intel. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Market price (27% YES / 73% NO) is the most reliable signal because it reflects aggregated trader belief given the data scarcity. However, confidence in BOTH sides is low because the briefing lacks direct team comparison, head-to-head history, current roster verification, or recent form corroboration. BEST ESTIMATE: Adopt market price as baseline (27% YES / 73% NO) due to data insufficiency on both sides. This reflects weak trader conviction on the YES side and slightly stronger conviction on the NO side, but overall low confidence in both directions. CONFIDENCE SCORING: confidence_yes = 32 (PandaScore form data contradicted by news summary; academy teams are unpredictable; 2.2h left allows for last-minute roster changes or forfeit risk). confidence_no = 35 (market price leans NO, but similarly thin intel; NO side also subject to academy volatility and forfeit risk).", "key_factor": "Briefing contains contradictory recent form data (Phantom 7W-2L vs Spirit 7W-3L from PandaScore) that is NOT supported by news summary or KEY FACTS, and no head-to-head history is provided; low confidence in both sides due to insufficient verified intel on academy teams."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO \u2014 Spiri