{"run_id": "e65f7e20-f82e-48c7-9872-b4420694d19f", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T18:49:13.625432+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1957329", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Daystar vs Elevate (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Daystar and Elevate in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Daystar\" if Daystar win the match against Elevate.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Elevate\" if Elevate win the match against Daystar.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T10:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T04:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.775, "volume_usd": 82.825019, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["90880694663558585231913553671674576919990061591283068240704369448168638361291", "77541180161485389783927501805499642789070584708320660998957659716817816860739"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Daystar must win the BO3 match against Elevate on Apr 18, 2026 at 04:00 UTC to resolve YES. TEMPORAL STATUS: Match is SCHEDULED (not yet started). All scorelines in news_summary and prior match facts refer to PRIOR encounters, not this event. Probability must reflect likelihood of Daystar victory in the upcoming match, not certainty of a past result. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECORD: Daystar leads the recent series 3-1 in the last 5 encounters (Feb 2026 2-0 win, Sep 2025 win, Sep 2016 loss, Jun 2026 win, Apr 2024 loss). Most recent direct encounter favored Daystar decisively (2-0 in Feb 2026). RECENT FORM \u2014 DAYSTAR: 5W-5L in last 10 matches per PandaScore. Solid but not dominant. No additional form data provided in briefing. RECENT FORM \u2014 ELEVATE: 3W-7L in last 10 matches per PandaScore. Notably weak recent run. Lost 0-2 to Team Orchid on Apr 11 (one week before this match). Did defeat HL Tauri 2-0 on Mar 28 (playoff win, showing some capability). ELEVATE INCONSISTENCY: Elevate swung from 2-0 victory over HL Tauri (Mar 28) to 0-2 loss to Team Orchid (Apr 11). Recent form is volatile and trending downward. DAYSTAR ADVANTAGE: Clear H2H advantage (3-1 in last 5), stronger recent win-loss ratio (5-5 vs 3-7), and most recent encounter was a 2-0 sweep. These factors support a YES probability in the 65\u201378% range. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Case for NO argues playoff matches may produce surprises. However, Elevate's playoff performance data is mixed (1-1 in visible recent playoff matches). Daystar's lower-bracket position itself is not clarified, limiting ability to assess seeding/bracket advantage. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 78% is slightly higher than conservative estimate of 72%, suggesting market has incorporated additional information or sentiment not visible in the briefing (sharp +27.5pp move on Apr 17 noted in price history). Conservative estimate of 72% reflects reliance on documented H2H and form data only. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes (72) reflects strong H2H record, form differential, and recent dominant performance. confidence_no set to 68 (slightly lower) because Elevate's recent form data is thin, playoff upset potential is real but not quantified, and the briefing lacks detailed roster/tactical analysis to fully evaluate Elevate's comeback capacity. NO TIMING RISK: Event starts in ~12 hours. No cancellation, forfeit, or delay signals present in briefing. Resolution criteria are clear for a standard match completion. CRITERIA CLARITY: Resolution criteria are unambiguous: Daystar win \u2192 YES, Elevate win \u2192 NO. Team name matching is straightforward. No edge cases or forfeit flags detected.", "key_factor": "Event is SCHEDULED but has not occurred yet (starts in ~12 hours); news summary contains past-tense language describing prior encounters, creating mild temporal incoherence; market price history shows sharp YES movement (+27.5pp on Apr 17), suggesting late information may have shifted pricing, but this is not reflected in the briefing data itself."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES \u2014 Daystar): Market consensus at 78% is well-grounded. Daystar has won 3 of the last 5 head-to-head matchups against Elevate, including the most recent encounter (Feb 2026, 2-0 decisive victory). This is not a marginal edge \u2014 it reflects sustained competitive advantage. RECENT FORM DIVERGENCE: Elevate's trajectory has deteriorated sharply. They defeated HL Tauri 2-0 on Mar 28 (13 days before this match), but then suffered a devastating 0-2 loss to Team Orchid on Apr 11 (only 7 days before Daystar match). This 0-2 loss to a strong opponent suggests momentum collapse and potential roster/tactical issues. Daystar's recent form is less detailed in the briefing, but the H2H record and price momentum (+27pp in 7 days) suggest strong confidence from informed traders. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (NO \u2014 Elevate): Elevate's win over HL Tauri, while noteworthy, came against a team that just lost 1-2 to Unreal Nightmare (HL Tauri's record shows inconsistency). Moreover, Elevate's 0-2 shutout to Team Orchid demonstrates they can be completely outmatched at the highest level of this regional circuit. One playoff win does not offset the 0-2 drubbing one week out. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: Daystar is 3-2 H2H vs. Elevate over the tracked period (Feb 2026, Sep 2025, Sep 2016, Jun 2025, Apr 2024). The two most recent encounters favor Daystar decisively (2-0 Feb 2026, and implied dominant win Sep 2025). Elevate's last H2H win was Sep 2016 \u2014 over 5 months ago. This is a structural weakness for the underdog. PLAYOFF CONTEXT AS DOUBLE-EDGED SWORD: While playoffs can produce upsets, Elevate's most recent playoff experience (0-2 to Team Orchid) was a capitulation, not a sign of playoff readiness. Daystar's Feb 2026 victory over Elevate also came in a competitive context (Group B), suggesting Daystar performs consistently across tournament formats. MARKET PRICE MOMENTUM: YES side rose 27pp in 7 days with a sharp +27.5pp move on Apr 17 01:00 UTC (yesterday). This suggests new information or late-stage confidence in Daystar's chances. NO side fell 27.5pp in parallel, with extreme volatility (5.3pp/hr). The market is pricing confidence in Daystar, not panic hedging into Elevate. ROSTER/PLAYER DATA (WEAK SIGNAL): Elevate roster mentions ShibeNuts and BarcodeOP as MVPs in their March win and April loss. The fact that these players appear in both a dominant win (vs. HL Tauri) and a complete loss (vs. Team Orchid) suggests inconsistency at the roster level \u2014 either tactical vulnerability or confidence erosion after the April 11 shutout. COUNTERARGUMENT \u2014 PLAYOFF CHAOS: Elevate's March 28 win shows they can deliver 2-0 victories in high-stakes matches. Playoff formats and single-match volatility mean recent H2H advantage is not deterministic. However, this is offset by the recency and severity of the Apr 11 loss (7 days out). Elevate would need a massive confidence reset in 1 week \u2014 unlikely without roster changes (none reported). COUNTERARGUMENT \u2014 UNKNOWN DAYSTAR FORM: The briefing does not detail Daystar's most recent matches beyond the Feb 2-0 win. Daystar's record is 5W-5L in the last 10 matches \u2014 neutral, not dominant. This introduces uncertainty on Daystar's current state. However, the 5-5 record still outperforms Elevate's 3W-7L, and the H2H record is conclusive. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence is high (78) because the briefing provides clear H2H history, recent form divergence (Elevate's 0-2 loss), and market momentum. NO confidence is moderate (42) because the briefing lacks deep detail on Daystar's recent performance outside H2H, does not explain *why* Elevate lost so badly to Team Orchid, and playoff upsets remain structurally possible even if unlikely. The 22% probability for NO is appropriate given the evidence; the lower confidence reflects data sparseness, not denial of the underdog's theoretical path. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 76% for YES reflects Daystar's structural advantage (H2H record, recent form, market momentum) while respecting ~24% for Elevate's upside case (playoff unpredictability, prior 2-0 win capability, roster experience). This is slightly conservative vs. the 78% market price, reflecting mild skepticism about whether the market may be overweighting recent Elevate collapse, but the difference is small \u2014 the market price appears well-calibrated.", "key_factor": "Daystar's dominant 3-of-5 head-to-head record and recent 2-0 victory (Feb 2026) combined with Elevate's collapse to Team Orchid (0-2, Apr 11) one week prior to this playoff match."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET OVERWEIGHTING H2H RECENCY: The 78% YES price relies heavily on Daystar's Feb 2026 2-0 victory and overall 3-of-5 H2H dominance. However, the briefing explicitly notes 'Playoff matches can produce different results than regular-season encounters'\u2014a critical qualifier the market may undervalue. ELEVATE'S PLAYOFF READINESS SIGNAL: Elevate defeated HL Tauri 2-0 on Mar 28 in a playoff context just ~3 weeks before this match. This is concrete evidence Elevate can win elimination rounds, not mere speculation. The Mar 28 victory came with strong individual performances (ShibeNuts, BarcodeOP MVPs). RECENCY DECAY & FORM VOLATILITY: Elevate's 3W-7L record (last 10 matches) is poor overall, BUT the Apr 11 0-2 loss to Team Orchid is only 1 week old\u2014very recent, suggesting momentum is DOWN. However, Daystar's 5W-5L is also middling. Elevate's volatility (capable of 2-0 wins AND 0-2 losses) suggests upset potential in high-variance playoff format. DAYSTAR FORM IS NOT DOMINANT: Daystar's 5W-5L recent record (last 10 matches) is exactly .500. The briefing provides NO concrete match data showing Daystar's recent playoff performance, map pool strengths, or individual player form. The YES case rests almost entirely on past H2H results, not current state. MARKET MOMENTUM SIGNAL IGNORED: NO side has dropped 27.5pp over 7 days and -22.5pp in 24 hours, with 5.3pp/hr volatility on Apr 16. YES side spiked +27.5pp on Apr 17 01:00 UTC. This sharp movement into YES without corresponding briefing evidence (no new Daystar roster signings, no Elevate injuries mentioned) suggests speculative overshooting rather than fundamental re-evaluation. PLAYOFF BRACKET CONTEXT UNCLEAR: The briefing notes this is 'Lower bracket quarterfinal' or 'group stage'\u2014both suggest elimination pressure where upset probability should be higher than regular-season expectations. BO3 format increases variance; single series is not predictive of overall strength. ELEVATE'S EXPERIENCED ROSTER: ShibeNuts and BarcodeOP are repeatedly listed as MVPs in recent wins, indicating active, capable core. One prior win by Elevate (Sep 2025, noted as 'playoff or high-stakes context') shows they have beaten Daystar in similar formats before. MISSING DATA ON DAYSTAR: The briefing provides zero recent scorelines, map performances, or individual player form for Daystar post-February. Feb 2-0 is 2.5 months old in esports terms. Lack of evidence for YES side should reduce confidence in the favorite, not increase it. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY RED FLAG: Only $83 USD volume suggests shallow market, high susceptibility to whale positioning or speculative late-day moves. Apr 17 01:00 spike into YES (27.5pp) on minimal volume is a weak signal for fundamental strength. ELEVATE'S MARCH 28 PERFORMANCE CONTEXT: Elevate's 2-0 over HL Tauri included 52-point wins on Nighthaven Labs and 43-point wins on Consulate\u2014dominant maps in the tournament pool. If Elevate can replicate this map-pool execution, they have a realistic path to 2-1 or 2-0 upset. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Base rate on H2H (Daystar 3-of-5) and recent form (Daystar 5W-5L vs Elevate 3W-7L) suggests Daystar ~65% fair value. However, Elevate's proven playoff execution (Mar 28 2-0), absence of negative news about Daystar, and high market overweight (78%) into an IMMINENT event with limited time for reversal suggests market is overstating Daystar certainty. Adjusting to 32% for NO reflects realistic upset potential while respecting Daystar's superior H2H record and recent form advantage.", "key_factor": "Elevate's recent 2-0 playoff win vs HL Tauri (Mar 28) demonstrates they can execute in high-stakes matches despite weak overall form, and playoff contexts often neutralize regular-season H2H dominance."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: Daystar won 3 of last 5 encounters (Feb 2026 2-0, Sep 2025 likely 2-0, Jun 2025 1-0). Elevate's only recent H2H win was Sep 2025 (noted as 0-1, likely a close map loss) and Apr 2024 (0-1). Strong H2H advantage strongly favors Daystar. RECENT FORM DISPARITY: Daystar 5W-5L (last 10 matches, balanced); Elevate 3W-7L (last 10 matches, struggling). Elevate's record shows inconsistency\u2014won 2-0 vs HL Tauri (Mar 28) but lost 0-2 to Team Orchid (Apr 11, just 1 week prior). ELEVATE'S CRITICAL WEAKNESS: The 0-2 loss to Team Orchid on Apr 11 is only 7 days before this match. No recovery time, suggests current form slump. Daystar's Feb 2026 2-0 win over Elevate is more recent and demonstrates clear skill gap. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: YES side at 78% reflects the underlying H2H and form advantage. This price is reasonable given Daystar's documented 3-of-5 H2H win rate and superior current form. Market has risen +27pp over 7 days, consistent with accumulating evidence of Daystar strength. PLAYOFF CAVEAT (DOWNSIDE RISK): Best-of-3 playoff matches can produce upsets due to preparation, meta adaptation, and psychological factors. Historical esports data suggests ~25\u201330% upset probability even when favorites hold 3+ H2H wins. Elevate's Mar 28 2-0 victory vs HL Tauri proves they are capable of cohesive play in high-stakes contexts. MAP POOL NEUTRALITY: Both teams share the same map veto pool (Consulate, Nighthaven Labs, Chalet, Bank, Fortress, Border, Lair, Kafe, Clubhouse). No systematic map advantage evident from briefing. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: High confidence in YES (72) because H2H record, recent form, and market price all align. Moderate confidence in NO (58) because esports upsets are common in lower-bracket BO3s and Elevate demonstrated capability 3 weeks ago. The 72/28 split reflects Daystar's clear structural advantage tempered by playoff volatility.", "key_factor": "In esports BO3 lower-bracket playoffs, the favored team (based on recent form and H2H record) wins approximately 70\u201375% of the time; however, upset probability in single-elimination formats is elevated (~25\u201330%) due to preparation, meta shifts, and psychological factors."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.76, "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Daystar owns clear H2H dominance: 3-of-5 recent matchups won, including most recent 2-0 in Feb 2026 only ~10 weeks prior to this event. Elevate's recent form is fragile: 0-2 loss to Team Orchid (Apr 11) just one week before this playoff match signals momentum loss at critical timing. Market price (78% YES) reflects this H2H edge and form divergence rationally. No sign of crowd euphoria \u2014 pricing is grounded in concrete head-to-head record. Elevate's single bright spot (2-0 vs HL Tauri on Mar 28) is overshadowed by the Apr 11 0-2 loss and inconsistent recent performance (3W-7L last 10 matches vs Daystar's 5W-5L). Both teams play same map pool and tournament infrastructure; no unexpected rule changes or venue shifts to introduce volatility. Event timing: ~12 hours away. Market has stabilized at 78/22 with only +0.5pp movement in last 24h, indicating confidence has settled rather than panic-driven spikes. Sharp move on Apr 17 01:00 UTC (+27.5pp YES) likely reflects betting reaction to Elevate's recent weak form, not crowd irrationality \u2014 data-supported shift. Low volume ($83 USD) and small sample (16 YES / 119 NO order points) means thin liquidity, but price itself is consistent with fundamentals. Elevate's NO-side case (playoff unpredictability, roster experience) is theoretically sound but contradicted by recent match data showing form collapse. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH on YES (strong H2H + form data), MODERATE-LOW on NO (requires upset narrative with weak recent evidence).", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.74, "probability_yes": 0.74, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Daystar owns 3-of-5 recent head-to-head matchups with decisive 2-0 wins in Feb 2026 and Sep 2025; H2H track record is strongest predictor in R6S due to team-specific meta reads and map pool mastery. Elevate's Apr 11 loss to Team Orchid (0-2) is only 7 days prior to this playoff; momentum is negative and suggests tactical vulnerability or roster issues that are unlikely to reverse in sub-week timeframe. Elevate's Mar 28 win vs HL Tauri (2-0) shows playoff capability but HL Tauri is lower-tier opponent; Team Orchid (Apr 11 opponent) is demonstrably stronger, indicating Elevate's consistency is fragile. Market price of 78% YES reflects strong consensus on Daystar; no recent roster changes, injuries, or disqualifications reported in briefing to justify reversal from established H2H dynamics. Playoff format does not typically favor underdogs in R6S due to lower variance in competitive integrity; best-of-3 format amplifies stronger team's edge. Low volume ($83 USD) and high volatility on NO side (5.3pp/hr vs 0.3pp/hr on YES) suggests retail uncertainty rather than informed sharp action; this increases noise but does not invalidate H2H fundamentals. Sharp move on Apr 17 01:00 UTC (+27.5pp YES) likely reflects post-match data release or roster confirmation, not contradictory intelligence; timing aligns with tournament scheduling updates. Map veto data across sampled matches shows Daystar and Elevate deploying similar ban strategies; no tactical innovation or veto advantage evident for Elevate. Confidence_no is low (35) because briefing lacks counter-evidence: no Daystar roster issues, no recent tactical meta shift favoring Elevate's playstyle, no health/availability concerns for Daystar's core (SpeakEasy, Reeps96 remain casters' named MVPs in similar regional contexts). Confidence_yes is moderate-high (72) due to strong H2H data and negative Elevate momentum, but tempered by low absolute match volume ($83) and inherent volatility of single BO3 outcome.", "key_factor": "Head-to-head dominance in R6S is highly predictive due to map pool familiarity and meta-read parity within regional circuits, but Elevate's recent 2-0 playoff win vs HL Tauri (late March) suggests mid-tournament momentum that could offset Daystar's February 2-0 victory if tactical prep or map veto strategy shifts."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "DAYSTAR STRENGTHS: Clear H2H dominance (3-2 overall, 2-0 in last direct meeting Feb 2026, 5-5 recent form suggests stability). Market consensus at 78% reflects this legitimately. DAYSTAR VULNERABILITIES: Recent form is exactly 50% (5W-5L last 10). No recent playoff match data in briefing\u2014last confirmed playoff win was Sep 2025. Lower-bracket playoff pressure is unpredictable. No scouting intel on current roster composition or meta adaptation since Feb. ELEVATE WEAKNESSES: 3-7 recent form is severely damaging. Lost 0-2 to Team Orchid just 7 days ago (Apr 11). This suggests form collapse, not just variance. Market is pricing this correctly. ELEVATE BLACK-SWAN WINDOW: (1) Elevate beat HL Tauri 2-0 on Mar 28 in playoff context\u2014they CAN perform under pressure. (2) One week rest advantage vs Daystar if Daystar played a qualifying match. (3) Map veto data shows Elevate's historic strength on Consulate (7-52 vs HLT, 7-52 vs ORC = consistent pick). (4) If Daystar fielded a stand-in or rotated roster for group stage, playoff form may regress. (5) ShibeNuts/BarcodeOP are named MVPs in recent Elevate wins\u2014if these players are hot, individual performance can override aggregate form. MISSING INTEL (HIGH UNCERTAINTY): Briefing is silent on: Daystar's current roster, whether any key Daystar player is injured/benched, Daystar's performance in other Apr 2026 matches (only Feb H2H available), patch/meta changes since Feb, coaching changes, internal morale shifts post-Feb win. This silence cuts against confidence in Daystar's 78% price. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES side jumped +27.5pp on Apr 17 01:00 UTC (sharp move into briefing date). This suggests late-breaking information favoring Daystar (player return, form confirmation, or betting syndicates loading). However, volatility on NO side is 5.3pp/hr vs 0.3pp/hr on YES = NO side is still contested/uncertain. PLAYOFF VARIANCE FACTOR: Elevate's 2-0 over HL Tauri (Mar 28) occurred in same tournament window, same map pool. If Elevate replicated that performance profile (e.g., ShibeNuts/BarcodeOP hot streak continues), they match or exceed Daystar's capability in BO3 single-elimination. Daystar's H2H edge may not transfer to playoffs. RESOLVE TO 50-50 RISK: Briefing notes forfeit/disqualification resolves to 50-50. No intel on team stability, visa issues, or admin disputes in APL. If either team withdraws or match is delayed >7 days, this market becomes a coin flip\u2014currently not priced for this tail risk. CONSENSUS TRAP: Council is likely anchoring on Daystar's 3-2 H2H and recent 2-0, treating regular-season dominance as playoff predictive. In R6S BO3 knockout, single-elimination removes series regression; one team's meta counter or psychological readiness can flip the outcome. Elevate's 2-0 vs HL Tauri (same venue/meta) proves they are not a 22% team in isolation. ADJUSTED PROBABILITY: Daystar remains favored (68 vs 38 for Elevate), reflecting legitimate form and H2H edge. However, confidence_no is deliberately LOW (48) because: (1) Elevate's recent collapse is real and unexplained, (2) missing roster/meta/injury data for both teams, (3) playoff pressure behaves differently than regular-season, (4) one-week confidence gap between Elevate's last match (Apr 11, loss) and this event suggests form regression risk for Elevate. Confidence_yes is 72 because Daystar's H2H record and 5-5 stability are measurable, but not high enough to dismiss a 30% NO scenario in a BO3 knockout with incomplete scouting. GAP BETWEEN SCORES (probability_score 68 + probability_no_score 38 = 106): This reflects genuine uncertainty on the NO side (Elevate's collapse is real, but a single BO3 upset is plausible) and a small double-counting of shared evidence (both teams' tactical flexibility, map pool unknowns). The asymmetry is intentional: a Daystar win is more likely, but a Daystar loss is less implausible than the 22% market price suggests.", "key_factor": "Elevate roster substitution or tactical meta shift (map pool favoring their aggressive playstyle) combined with Daystar's mental lapse in high-pressure lower-bracket playoff context, exploiting the 1-week rest disparity and Daystar's lack of recent playoff reps."}], "final_score": 0.7073745346400548, "no_score": 0.3360444197726937, "edge": -0.0840909090909091, "no_edge": 0.46590909090909094, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Big Drawdown Risk: YES price 77.5% \u2265 PerceivedTrueWinRate 69.1% (-EV)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0508778629618616, "The Bull": 0.9407098700352481, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0540798334052115, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0537396973507898, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0553403376068922, "The Contrarian": 1.0735033923024546, "The Bear": 0.7717490063375423}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1957329", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Daystar vs Elevate (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Daystar and Elevate in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Daystar\" if Daystar win the match against Elevate.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Elevate\" if Elevate win the match against Daystar.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s list