{"run_id": "32488314-3f98-432d-af85-58c17fd6ff59", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T18:41:41.068303+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963307", "question": "Valorant: Cloud9 vs Team Envy (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Cloud9 and Team Envy in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 17 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Cloud9\" if Cloud9 win the match against Team Envy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Envy\" if Team Envy win the match against Cloud9.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 53885.81341799996, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["5312052569409725791485279618248023948269957717024160264600419206032560872948", "88757173931573211189354686915016649151857196409264192635351297597995188666687"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event scheduled for 2026-04-17 21:00 UTC, currently ~2.3 hours away. Any past match results (Jan 26 Cloud9 win, Nov 6 Envy win) are prior encounters only, not predictive of this specific match outcome. OUTCOME CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Cloud9 wins the BO3 match; NO if Team Envy wins. Forfeit/walkover scenarios resolve 50-50 (low probability but noted in criteria). HEAD-TO-HEAD FORM: Recent history shows competitive parity \u2014 Cloud9 won BO3 on 2026-01-26, Team Envy won BO3 on 2025-11-06. Split record with no clear dominance. RECENT SEASON FORM: Both teams 4W-6L in last 10 matches \u2014 identical records indicate evenly matched squads entering this match. CLOUD9 CASE (YES): Won most recent direct encounter (Jan 26, 2026 Kickoff Main Event); demonstrated strong individual performances from Demon1 and key roster. TEAM ENVY CASE (NO): Won prior encounter (Nov 6, 2025); however, roster disruption from canezerra contract termination (hardware ban) introduces preparation/team cohesion uncertainty that could undermine this advantage. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES trading at 66%, NO at 34% \u2014 market has moved +15.5pp in YES's favor over 7 days (sharp moves Apr 13). This suggests informed traders see Cloud9 as slight favorite, but move is not extreme enough to reflect dominant form. ROSTER UNCERTAINTY: Envy's roster adjustment (canezerra departure) is the only material new information. This creates tactical ambiguity \u2014 fresh preparation could help (new synergy) or hurt (reduced preparation time, leadership vacuum). Effect is directionally unclear. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Recent form is perfectly balanced (4-6 each), H2H is split, market shows modest Cloud9 lean (+32pp YES vs +34pp NO pricing). Confidence on both sides is moderate due to lack of recent dominant performance from either team and roster uncertainty on Envy side. LIVE/IMMINENT DISCOUNT: Event starts in 2.3 hours. No in-match data available. Reversal of market lean would require significant unexpected roster announcements or technical issues \u2014 very low probability this late. Confidence is thus slightly suppressed to reflect execution risk and unknown in-game factors. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Primary source vlr.gg with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. Low mechanism risk; once match concludes, market will trade to ~0.01/0.99 before official publication. PROBABILITY SPLIT: probability_score=62 reflects Cloud9 slight edge (market lean + recency of Jan 26 win vs Nov 6 loss + Envy roster disruption headwind). probability_no_score=38 reflects Team Envy's real remaining chances (split H2H, identical form, potential for roster reset to improve prep). Sum <100 due to genuine outcome uncertainty and low probability of 50-50 resolution scenarios.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT with only ~2.3 hours until start; no outcome data available yet; head-to-head history shows split recent results (Cloud9 won Jan 26, Envy won Nov 6) providing weak predictive signal; Team Envy roster disruption (canezerra contract termination) introduces tactical uncertainty that could favor either side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES \u2014 Cloud9 66%): Market has shown sustained conviction, rising +15.5pp over the past week with sharp moves on Apr 13, suggesting informed money flowing to Cloud9. This sustained rise despite both teams having identical 4W-6L recent records indicates non-form factors driving confidence. HEAD-TO-HEAD MOMENTUM: Cloud9 won the most recent direct encounter on Jan 26, 2026 (BO3 format at Kickoff Main Event). While Team Envy won their prior meeting on Nov 6, 2025, the more recent victory belongs to Cloud9, and it occurred at a higher-stakes Kickoff event where Cloud9 demonstrated strong individual performances (Demon1 highlighted). UNDERDOG WEAKNESS \u2014 ROSTER DISRUPTION: Team Envy experienced a notable roster setback: canezerra's contract was terminated due to a hardware ban before he could compete. This is a concrete negative signal for NO \u2014 squad composition disruption near a major stage typically undermines preparation and team synergy, creating asymmetric risk. FORM PARITY MASKED BY SELECTION: Both teams sit at 4W-6L over the last 10 matches, creating surface-level symmetry. However, this masks the recency of Cloud9's Kickoff victory and Envy's roster disruption. When recent form is equal but one side has momentum (recent H2H win + sustained market rise) and the other has roster issues, the favorite's edge sharpens. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: At 66% YES / 34% NO with $53,886 in volume, the market is reflective and liquid. The persistence of the +15.5pp rise over a week, combined with sharp coordinated moves on Apr 13 (\u00b114.5pp and \u00b15.5pp), suggests informed positioning rather than noise. The +3.0pp 24-hour move favoring NO slightly undercuts the weekly trend but does not reverse conviction. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~2.3 hours to start). At this stage, material reversals would require breaking news (roster changes, health issues, technical forfeits). None are noted in the briefing. The price is stable near 66%, suggesting no imminent surprises are priced in. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence is high (72%) because Cloud9 has concrete recent H2H evidence, Demon1 performance data, and sustained market conviction. NO confidence is lower (48%) because Envy's case relies on abstract 'fresh team dynamics' from a roster setback \u2014 a speculative positive that contradicts the concrete negative of losing a player mid-preparation. The briefing provides less evidence to justify a robust counter-case for Envy. PROBABILITY_NO_SCORE RATIONALE: Set to 28 (not 32 = mechanical 100-68) to reflect genuine data asymmetry. The briefing gives strong tactical evidence for Cloud9 (H2H win + Kickoff performance + market momentum). For Envy, it offers only roster disruption (a negative, not a positive case) and abstract 'fresh dynamics.' This is not a symmetric two-sided evaluation; the NO case lacks affirmative evidence and relies on uncertainty. Leaving ~4pp ignorance mass (68+28=96) flags that asymmetry.", "key_factor": "Cloud9's recent head-to-head victory (Jan 26, 2026 BO3 win) combined with strong individual performances from Demon1 at the VCT Kickoff, reinforced by sustained market conviction (+15.5pp over 7 days) despite symmetric recent form (4W-6L both teams)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FORM PARITY: Both Cloud9 and Team Envy are 4W-6L over their last 10 matches \u2014 statistically identical recent performance. The 66-34 price gap assumes Cloud9 superiority that is not reflected in current form data. HEAD-TO-HEAD SPLIT: Prior encounters show one win each \u2014 Cloud9 won 2026-01-26 (Kickoff Playoffs, BO3) and Team Envy won 2025-11-06 (Group Stage, BO3). This is competitive parity, not a trend favoring Cloud9. ROSTER DISRUPTION FACTOR: Team Envy terminated canezerra's contract due to hardware ban before competition \u2014 this represents recent instability that typically impacts team chemistry and preparation in imminent matches (2.3 hours away). The briefing explicitly flags this as a roster adjustment that 'may affect squad composition.' Limited time to absorb roster changes is a downside for Envy, but the briefing provides no details on who replaced canezerra or how severe the impact is. MARKET PRICING TREND VULNERABILITY: YES side rose +15.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 13 (+14.5pp, then +5.5pp). This aggressive rise in Cloud9 pricing may reflect recency bias from their Kickoff win rather than fresh evidence. The 24-hour trend shows YES down -3.0pp, suggesting late-market correction. IMMINENT TIMING DISADVANTAGE FOR UPSET: Event starts in 2.3 hours. For Team Envy to overturn a 32-point price disadvantage, a dramatic reversal or breaking news would be required \u2014 unlikely at this stage. This constrains the upset upside despite underlying form parity. INSUFFICIENT DATA ON TEAM ENVY'S REPLACEMENT: The briefing does not identify who replaced canezerra or provide recent performance data on the substitute. This creates interpretive risk \u2014 Envy could have brought in a high-caliber backup or a weak substitute. Confidence in Envy's downside is thus limited. DEMON1 INDIVIDUAL PERFORMANCE NOTED FOR CLOUD9: Briefing cites 'strong individual performances from key players like Demon1' in Kickoff win. However, individual player form in January matches may not predict April performance. No current individual stats provided for either team. SPREAD AND VOLATILITY: 24-hour volatility on NO side (1.0pp/hr) exceeds YES side (0.8pp/hr), suggesting more uncertainty on Envy's pricing. This is consistent with roster disruption uncertainty affecting the underdog side. COMPETITIVE GROUP FORMAT: Round-robin format with top 4 of 6 advancing means mid-tier teams (both 4W-6L qualify as mid-tier) have high stakes. Both teams will be motivated, reducing the chance of complacency favoring the favorite. CASE AGAINST YES (favorite vulnerabilities): Cloud9's 4W-6L record is losing form heading into an imminent match. Their Kickoff playoff win (Jan 26) is ~2.5 months old and may not reflect current capability. No recent match data provided for Cloud9 post-Kickoff. The market's +15.5pp rise over 7 days appears speculative without fresh competitive evidence. CASE FOR YES (favorite strengths): Cloud9 has the recent head-to-head edge (Jan 26 win) and received mention of individual standout performances (Demon1). Market consensus and price action suggest institutional backing. However, strength is relative \u2014 not overwhelming given form parity. ASYMMETRY IN EVIDENCE: YES side has explicit individual performance callout (Demon1); NO side has roster disruption flagged but no detail on replacement quality. This asymmetry justifies lower confidence_no and probability_no_score, reflecting ignorance rather than strong evidence against Envy. PROBABILITY_SCORE RATIONALE: 38 reflects that while form is equal (50-50 baseline), the market's 66% pricing for Cloud9 is partially justified by recent head-to-head edge and individual performance callouts, but overshoots given (a) identical recent form, (b) roster disruption uncertainty for Envy that could cut either way, and (c) imminent timing reducing narrative-reversal likelihood. Team Envy is underpriced relative to form parity. PROBABILITY_NO_SCORE RATIONALE: 42 (not mechanically = 100 - 38) reflects independent evaluation of the NO case: Envy has form parity, H2H split, and potential edge from roster refresh (if canezerra was underperforming or if replacement is better). However, roster disruption risk is real and unquantified, and Cloud9's Kickoff credential is legitimate. The 42 is higher than 38 because the NO evidence (parity + H2H split) is more concrete than the YES evidence (individual performance mention from 2.5 months ago). The gap (38+42=80, leaving 20pp ignorance) reflects genuine uncertainty given imminent timing and missing roster data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 35 (lower) because market has risen sharply on limited fresh evidence, and form data contradicts the 66-34 split. confidence_no = 38 (slightly higher but still low) because the NO case relies on form parity and H2H split (solid but not decisive), offset by unknown roster replacement impact. Both confidences are low because event is imminent and several key data gaps exist (current rosters, recent scrims, meta shifts).", "key_factor": "Team Envy's recent roster disruption (canezerra contract termination) is being underweighted by the market despite imminent match timing, while both teams show identical 4W-6L form suggesting true competitive parity that should price them closer to 50-50."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.33999999999999997, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours to start). No time for material roster changes or late-breaking information. Market prices will rapidly converge to ~$0.01/$0.99 once play begins or outcome becomes evident. BASELINE FORM PARITY: Both teams report 4W-6L in last 10 matches. In Valorant, identical recent records suggest ~50% base win probability absent other signals. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY (context only, not outcome): Cloud9 won 2026-01-26 (BO3); Team Envy won 2025-11-06 (BO3). Recent 1-1 split shows competitive parity, slight edge to Cloud9 recency. ROSTER DISRUPTION SIGNAL: Team Envy terminated canezerra's contract pre-competition due to hardware ban. This introduces squad composition uncertainty and preparation disruption favoring Cloud9, who appears roster-stable. PRIOR TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Cloud9 defeated Team Envy in VCT 2026 Americas Kickoff Main Event with strong individual performances (Demon1 noted). This is recent, high-stakes evidence of Cloud9 form advantage. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES at 66% / NO at 34% reflects Cloud9 slight favorite. This aligns with: (1) recent H2H win, (2) Kickoff Main Event superiority, (3) Team Envy roster disruption. No major mispricing detected. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side up +15.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves Apr 13. This suggests information flow favoring Cloud9 (likely Kickoff Main Event result and/or canezerra termination news). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=42 (moderate) because Cloud9 form and roster stability are documented, but Valorant esports outcomes are volatile and team-specific preparation (unknown to us) within 2.3 hours is unpredictable. confidence_no=38 (slightly lower) because Team Envy roster disruption is a concrete negative signal, but we lack detailed substitute lineup composition data to fully assess their squad strength post-termination. NO OVERRIDE FACTORS: No cancellation risk, timeout risk, or weather/technical factors noted for this indoor esports event. Match is scheduled and funded. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: 66% reflects market consensus and modest Cloud9 edge from recent H2H, Kickoff Main Event dominance, and Team Envy roster disruption. Not high confidence because (a) Valorant is inherently volatile, (b) 2.3 hours is insufficient to validate full team preparation/morale, (c) individual player performance on the day dominates BO3 outcomes.", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant BO3 series, teams with identical recent form (4W-6L) show ~50% win probability absent roster disruption. Head-to-head splits (1-1 recent) and market consensus at 66% YES reflect Cloud9 recent momentum and VCT 2026 Kickoff success; Team Envy's canezerra contract termination introduces roster uncertainty favoring Cloud9."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.64, "probability_yes": 0.64, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "CURRENT PRICE ANALYSIS: Market is pricing Cloud9 at 66% YES, Team Envy at 34% NO. This reflects a modest but clear favorite stance on Cloud9. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: Cloud9 beat Envy 2-1 on 2026-01-26 (recent); Envy beat Cloud9 2-1 on 2025-11-06 (older). Split history with Cloud9's most recent win, but both teams have demonstrated ability to win BO3s against each other. RECENT FORM PARITY: Both teams are 4W-6L in last 10 matches \u2014 statistically identical records. No form edge for either side. ROSTER/CONTEXT SIGNALS: Briefing mentions Envy terminated canezerra's contract due to hardware ban before competing. This suggests squad composition adjustments, but impact is ambiguous \u2014 could be a weakness (roster instability) or a strength (removing a problem). Briefing does not clarify if canezerra was a starter or backup. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY vs PRICE: Market has risen +15.5pp for YES in the last 7 days (Apr 13 spike +14.5pp, +5.5pp). This suggests growing confidence in Cloud9, possibly driven by recent head-to-head win or perception of roster stability vs Envy's contract termination. No countervailing NO-side momentum. SENTIMENT IMBALANCE: The unidirectional rise (+15.5pp YES, -15.5pp NO) indicates crowd is leaning Cloud9 without obvious new catalyst in the briefing. Head-to-head history is mixed; parity in form should suggest closer odds (~55-45), but market is at 66-34 \u2014 a 17pp skew toward YES. MISSING DATA ON ENVY: Briefing does not quantify how disruptive the canezerra departure is, does not detail Envy's current roster readiness, or provide strategic/preparation analysis. This creates asymmetric information \u2014 Cloud9's YES case is stronger in briefing evidence, but Envy's NO case is under-explained. RATIONAL vs EMOTION: The 66-34 split is not extreme (not >75-25), so panic or greed is not obvious. But the recent uptrend despite matched form records suggests the crowd is reacting to narrative (recent Cloud9 win, Envy roster news) rather than structural edge. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Head-to-head split (1-1 in BO3s) + matched form (4-4) + Cloud9 recency + Envy roster uncertainty warrant Cloud9 slight favorite, but not 66%. Fair price closer to 55-60. Current market shows mild overconfidence in Cloud9 (~+6-11pp too high), creating modest NO-side value. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES side confidence is moderately high (62) \u2014 briefing supports Cloud9 narrative with recent win and form. NO side confidence is lower (48) \u2014 sparse data on Envy's current state, no counter-narrative, and roster change is framed as negative without quantification. IMMINENT TIMING: Event starts in 2.3 hours. Any price reversal now would require major news (lineup announcement, injury, withdrawal). This timing reinforces that final price is unlikely to move significantly \u2014 current 66-34 will likely hold until match starts.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.65, "probability_yes": 0.65, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FORM PARITY: Both Cloud9 and Team Envy are 4-6 in their last 10 matches (40% recent win rate); no form edge either direction. H2H SPLIT: Cloud9 won 2026-01-26 (BO3 format); Team Envy won 2025-11-06 (BO3 format); true 1-1 head-to-head with alternating winners suggests no systemic advantage. ROSTER DISRUPTION: Team Envy terminated canezerra's contract pre-competition due to hardware ban; this is a NEGATIVE signal for Team Envy's preparation depth, but impact magnitude unclear (unclear if canezerra was a starter, what his role was, how well the replacement integrates). MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES has risen +15.5pp over 7 days with sharp +14.5pp move on Apr 13 08:00 UTC; this suggests information flow (possibly leaked roster news, scrim results, or betting syndicate movement). NO side falling to 34% may reflect overreaction rather than fundamental shift. IMMINENT EVENT RISK: With ~2.3 hours until match start, reversal of current 66/34 line requires material new information (injury, full roster revelation, scrim leak). Probability of such reversal in final 2 hours is low, but event has not started\u2014confidence must remain moderate. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides strong evidence for parity (4-4 H2H over two matches, identical recent form); does NOT provide roster depth, player health, scrim performance, or coaching changes. Cannot rule out Team Envy preparing exceptionally well despite roster disruption OR Cloud9 experiencing internal issues\u2014hence moderate-low confidence both directions. VALORANT-SPECIFIC: BO3 format favors teams with deep agent pool flexibility and economy management discipline; neither team's recent form reveals map veto strength, agent pool depth, or mid-round calling quality\u2014gaps in briefing. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: 66/34 split is wide enough to suggest market confidence, but recent sharp movement and rising trend on YES suggests potential short-term directional pressure rather than fundamental evaluation. Bookmakers typically price esports BO3 matches closer to 50/50 unless roster/form gaps are substantial; 66% indicates above-average confidence in Cloud9, possibly justified by January win but concerning given identical recent form and H2H parity.", "key_factor": "Both teams show identical 4W-6L recent form (40% win rate), identical head-to-head split across the two prior encounters, and no clear roster advantage\u2014the market's 66% YES may reflect recency bias from Cloud9's January victory or overweight the January win relative to the November loss."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.54, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "EQUAL RECENT FORM: Both teams are 4W-6L in last 10 matches \u2014 no statistical edge. Consensus favors Cloud9 at 66%, but this is supported largely by a single January win, not current trajectory. H2H PARITY: Head-to-head shows split results (Cloud9 won Jan 26 in playoffs 1-2; Envy won Nov 6 in group stage 2-1). No convincing edge to either side in recent competition. MARKET MOMENTUM ANOMALY: YES side surged +15.5pp over 7 days (Apr 13 spike of +14.5pp), but 24h change is -3.0pp. This suggests sharp overweighting ~4 days ago without recent confirmation. The spike timing (Apr 13) predates April 17 match; unclear what catalyzed it. ENVY ROSTER DISRUPTION (BLACK SWAN): Briefing explicitly notes 'canezerra contract termination due to hardware ban before competing.' This is NOT minor\u2014it signals either (a) a mid-tournament roster swap requiring hastily integrated stand-in, or (b) deeper internal/disciplinary issues. BO3 success hinges on team coordination; last-minute personnel changes are high-friction. TIMING CRITICALITY: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours). If Envy fielded a stand-in or made late changes, there is no time for additional scrims or adjustment. Cloud9's roster appears stable by contrast. LACK OF INTEL ON ENVY REPLACEMENT: Briefing does NOT identify who replaced canezerra or when Envy confirmed their lineup. This silence itself is a red flag for analysis\u2014if Envy is fielding an unfamiliar player in a stage-1 match, their map pool coordination and default executes are at risk. CLOUD9 NARRATIVE SUPPORT: Recent Kickoff win cited; no equivalent recent positive result for Envy. Current market prices (66% YES) may rationally reflect this, but only if Envy's roster is stable. If Envy is disrupted, 66% understates Cloud9's edge. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data supporting Cloud9 stability and recent wins (high confidence_yes). Weak/absent data on Envy's replacement player, integration timeline, and morale post-contract-termination (low confidence_no). The gap reflects incomplete information on the NO side. DUAL-PERSPECTIVE CALIBRATION: P(YES)=58 reflects that Cloud9 is favored but the market's +15.5pp surge lacks recent supporting data. P(NO)=54 reflects genuine competitive parity in abstract form, but is heavily discounted by the canezerra disruption signal. The asymmetry (58 vs 54) is intentional: the black swan depresses NO more than it elevates YES, because roster instability is a larger penalty in BO3 than raw skill gaps. RESOLVE CRITERION RISK: Match scheduled for Apr 17 21:00 UTC. If it starts and completes normally, this black swan fully applies. If Envy forfeits or a walkover occurs, market resolves 50-50 per resolution terms\u2014possible but lower-probability tail risk.", "key_factor": "Team Envy's recent canezerra contract termination (hardware ban) signals deeper roster instability or late-stage substitutions that could degrade their coordination and map pool readiness in a live BO3, especially if a stand-in is fielded without full integration."}], "final_score": 0.6183845463530149, "no_score": 0.38807934909539415, "edge": 0.03590909090909089, "no_edge": 0.34590909090909094, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 53.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0502615081746454, "The Bull": 0.9485651334222127, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0530400843938654, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0532291381796675, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0546263940607403, "The Contrarian": 1.072388005832532, "The Bear": 0.7678897359363381}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963307", "question": "Valorant: Cloud9 vs Team Envy (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Cloud9 and Team Envy in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 17 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Cloud9\" if Cloud9 win the match against Team Envy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Envy\" if Team Envy win the match against Cloud9.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 53885.81341799996, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["5312052569409725791485279618248023948269957717024160264600419206032560872948", "8875717393157321118935468691501664915185719