n Jan 22), demonstrating consistent macro and teamfight execution. Winter Snowdown Group Stage standings show G2 NORD 3-1 vs Frankfurt 1-3 in the same competitive pool, indicating Frankfurt failed against equivalent tier competition. G2 NORD appears in top 3 Gold Per Minute statistics (2399 GPM vs opponents), suggesting superior economy and resource allocation\u2014a systemic advantage not easily negated in BO1. Frankfurt's 3W-7L recent form (last 10 matches) vs G2 NORD's 6W-4L recent form indicates G2 NORD significantly stronger in current meta and player execution. Market price of 76% YES aligns with objective evidence; 7-day price rise (+26pp) reflects growing confidence as recent form data solidified. BO1 format does increase variance (no series buffer), but Frankfurt would need unexpected draft adaptation or severe G2 NORD unforced error\u2014higher bar given skill disparity. Market sharp moves (Apr 16 04:00 UTC -9pp, then +26.5pp recovery) suggest algorithmic/sentiment volatility rather than new Frankfurt-positive intel; no material news cited in briefing. No evidence of Frankfurt roster changes, coaching adjustments, or meta shifts that would close the gap demonstrated in head-to-head and group-stage records. Event timing LIVE/IMMINENT (2.7 hrs) limits time for new information; market reflects accumulated betting sentiment and historical data. Confidence in YES is moderately high (78) due to objective form/H2H data; confidence in NO is lower (72) because Frankfurt lacks positive evidence to support reversal narrative.", "key_factor": "BO1 format creates meaningful variance, but G2 NORD's consistent 2-0 head-to-head dominance, superior macro metrics (top-3 Gold Per Minute), and Frankfurt's 1-3 Winter record suggest structural skill gap that outweighs single-game volatility."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.42,