{"run_id": "ba90cc19-3bd0-49bf-aea9-caa12f8fe9ba", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T18:40:10.142880+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1949873", "question": "LoL: Maryville University vs Citadel Gaming (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Maryville University and Citadel Gaming in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Maryville University\" if Maryville University win the match against Citadel Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Citadel Gaming\" if Citadel Gaming win the match against Maryville University.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.835, "volume_usd": 5722.945933999965, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["112869833988464864107905589119619675148974876563204725099920380592509689644720", "2768672732173641090810011404686098055753087114756720737666319825679433772721"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.79, "probability_yes": 0.79, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Maryville University must win the BO3 match against Citadel Gaming to resolve YES. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Match is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-17 20:00 UTC; briefing data timestamp is 2026-04-17 18:39 UTC (~1.3 hours before start). No past-tense scoreline in briefing, so no prior match confusion. FORM DIFFERENTIAL (primary evidence for YES): Maryville University 7W-3L (70% win rate last 10 matches) vs Citadel Gaming 4W-6L (40% win rate last 10 matches). Maryville outperforms by 30 percentage points in recent form. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES = 84% (market price), Maryville = 70% (form-based). Market is pricing Maryville slightly higher than raw form suggests, but not extreme overvaluation. This modest premium reflects market confidence in Maryville. PRICE HISTORY SIGNAL: YES side has risen +5.0pp in last 24 hours and +4.5pp over 7 days (RISING trend). NO side has fallen -4.5pp over 7 days despite small +1.0pp in last 24 hours. Consistent directional confidence toward Maryville. SHARP MOVE ANALYSIS: Apr 17 01:00 UTC saw NO +6.0pp move (Citadel support), but this was then reversed by subsequent 24-hour action favoring YES. Suggests sharp backing of underdog was overturned by broader market consensus. NO CASE WEAKNESS: Citadel 4W-6L form is losing record; briefing contains no team roster, strategic, or recent matchup data to support Citadel upset. 'CASE FOR NO' explicitly states 'Insufficient data to build NO case.' This is honest and reflects genuine lack of Citadel-favoring evidence. YES CASE SUPPORTED BY: Form differential (Maryville +30pp), market consensus (84% vs 17%), price direction (rising YES trend), and professional structure (BO3 format favors stronger team). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 72 (form data is clear, market consensus is strong, but LIVE/IMMINENT timing means in-match events unknown). confidence_no = 45 (insufficient briefing data on Citadel's strengths, coaching, roster, or meta positioning; underdog upset is possible but entirely unsupported by briefing evidence). LIVE/IMMINENT RISK: Event starts in ~1.3 hours. After shares begin trading, outcome becomes clear within minutes; official resolution delay risk is low. However, current probability_score must reflect real-time unknowns (player performance, draft outcomes, early game flow). Given strong pre-match evidence favoring Maryville, 79% reflects this but leaves meaningful 21% for Citadel upset. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: gol.gg is official source; no name ambiguity (both teams clearly identified). Forfeit/walkover rules would resolve to 50-50, but no indicators of this risk in briefing. PROBABILITY DERIVATION: Base on form (70% Maryville) + market consensus weight (84% Maryville) + small underdog variance = 79% YES. This reflects Maryville as clear favorite but leaves meaningful uncertainty for live competitive risk.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT with no real-time match updates in briefing; probability relies entirely on pre-match form differential and market pricing; any in-game developments unknown."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "FORM EDGE (YES): Maryville is 7-3 in last 10 matches vs. Citadel's 4-6 \u2014 a 30 percentage point win-rate gap (70% vs. 40%) is substantial in LoL esports. In collegiate/NACL BO3 play, recent form typically correlates with match outcomes. MARKET CONSENSUS (YES): YES is priced at 84% (currently the favorite), with steady upward momentum: +4.5pp over 7 days and +5.0pp in last 24 hours. This rising trend reflects either revealed information or market participants recognizing Maryville's form advantage. PRICE STABILITY (YES): NO side has experienced sharp volatility (Apr 14 +7.5pp, then Apr 17 -6.0pp), suggesting uncertainty or noise around Citadel, whereas YES side shows consistent, rising conviction. Conviction in the favorite is typically more reliable than volatility in underdogs. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Citadel's 40% recent win rate places them in the bottom half of NACL standings (where only top 6 advance to playoffs and bottom 2 face relegation). This suggests structural team weakness, not temporary slump. A BO3 against a top-tier team in this context is unfavorable. TEMPORAL CONTEXT: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.3 hours from briefing timestamp). No major roster changes, injuries, or tactical surprises are documented. The 84%/17% prices are likely final market consensus; large reversals require unlikely heroic underperformance by Maryville or unexpected Citadel surge with no supporting data. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three reduces variance and favors the better team. Citadel would need to win 2-0 or 2-1 against a team with 70% recent form \u2014 a high bar with no coaching, roster, or momentum advantage cited. DATA GAPS (NO): The briefing provides NO evidence for Citadel's case \u2014 no recent head-to-head history, no player-level intel, no tactical analysis, and no recent wins vs. comparable teams. Absence of evidence for the underdog, combined with poor form, justifies LOW confidence in NO and LOW probability_no_score. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes is 72 (high) because form data is concrete and directional; confidence_no is 28 (low) because briefing contains no affirmative case FOR Citadel, only an absence of the favorite's form data. This asymmetry reflects the information structure, not false symmetry. ALTERNATIVE SCENARIO (NO): Citadel could win if Maryville has hidden roster issues, if form is a false signal, or if Citadel's lower record masks a recent improvement. None of these are evidenced; they are purely speculatively possible. Market has likely priced these in already at 17%.", "key_factor": "Maryville University's 7W-3L recent form (70% win rate) significantly outpaces Citadel Gaming's 4W-6L record (40% win rate) in a league where form is a reliable predictor of BO3 outcomes."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR CITADEL (NO): The market has priced Maryville at 84% based primarily on a 7W-3L vs 4W-6L record differential \u2014 a 3-win gap across 10 matches. In BO3 format (best-of-three), this translates to only ~1.5 expected game wins per series, making individual match performance highly volatile and upset susceptible. RECORD INTERPRETATION: Maryville's 7W-3L (70%) win rate is solid but not dominant. Citadel's 4W-6L (40%) is weak in aggregate, BUT the briefing provides no: team composition changes, recent meta shifts, player roster updates, head-to-head history, or playoff implications context for either team. MARKET PRICE VOLATILITY AS SIGNAL: NO side experienced sharp moves: +7.5pp on Apr 14, then -6.0pp on Apr 17. This 13.5pp swing in 3 days, combined with low volume ($5,723 USD) and small position sizes, suggests the current 84%/17% split may reflect thin-book consensus rather than deep analytical confidence. CITADEL'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: A 4W-6L team is not 17% likely to win a BO3 if roster-specific matchup factors, recent patch performance, or coaching adjustments favor them. The briefing contains zero analysis of WHY Citadel is losing (close games? meta mismatch? roster synergy issues?). A team 3 games below .500 can still win 1-2 series depending on draft, mid-game execution, and map control. MARYVILLE'S POTENTIAL OVERPRICING: 84% odds require Maryville to win ~2 out of 3 games with high consistency. The briefing provides: (a) no recent Maryville head-to-head data, (b) no playoff seeding pressure analysis, (c) no indication whether Maryville is peaking or coasting. A 70% aggregate win rate does not guarantee 84% BO3 win probability without controlling for series-level variance. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING RISK: Event starts in ~1.3 hours. No late-breaking roster news, injury reports, technical issues, or team mood/morale data are present in the briefing. For a LIVE event, the absence of negative catalyst data does NOT confirm Maryville's favored status \u2014 it only confirms lack of new information. DATA GAPS UNDERMINE BOTH SIDES: The briefing explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head history or current standings data for these specific teams in 2026 Spring is available.' This means: (1) we cannot evaluate Citadel's recent momentum (improving or declining?), (2) we cannot identify draft/playstyle matchup edges, (3) we cannot assess playoff qualification context (is either team fighting for top-6 or avoiding relegation?). These gaps justify LOWERING confidence on both sides. MARYVILLE VULNERABILITIES: Despite 7W-3L, the briefing contains: zero game-by-game analysis, zero commentary on consistency vs. volatility in their wins, zero detail on whether they face stronger or weaker opponents. A 70% win rate in a weak conference section could compress dramatically in BO3 playoff-style intensity. CITADEL COMPETITIVE PLAUSIBILITY: A 40% aggregate rate does NOT equal 17% BO3 probability. If Citadel's recent games include close losses or wins vs. higher-seeded teams, they possess upset credentials. The 4W-6L obscures whether those 6 losses were blowouts (suggests weakness) or tight series (suggests competitiveness). RESOLUTION OF ASYMMETRY: YES is favored at 84%; the briefing provides Maryville's record (7W-3L) as the primary justification. For the NO case (Citadel upset), the briefing provides only Citadel's aggregate record (4W-6L) and zero context on why they COULD win. This asymmetry justifies: (a) high confidence_yes (~35, supported by Maryville's solid win rate), (b) LOW confidence_no (~32, hampered by absent Citadel form context), (c) probability_score of 28 (NOT 16, which would mechanically inverse 84%), acknowledging that the market's certainty exceeds the evidence quality. PROBABILITY CONSTRUCTION: probability_score = 28 reflects: 7W-3L edge is real (~60-65% baseline), but market's 84% embeds false precision given missing head-to-head and playoff context. Citadel at 28% is higher than the 17% market price because BO3 variance and missing form data create upset space. probability_no_score = 32 (NOT 72) because the brief provides zero affirmative case FOR Citadel's win \u2014 only an absence of evidence AGAINST it. Leaving ~40pp of ignorance mass (28 + 32 = 60) signals genuine data scarcity.", "key_factor": "Citadel Gaming's recent form trajectory (4W-6L) shows competitive depth in a BO3 format where individual games matter more than aggregate records, and the market's 84% YES price reflects overconfidence in Maryville despite limited statistical separation."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FORM DIFFERENTIAL: Maryville 7W-3L (70% recent) vs Citadel 4W-6L (40% recent) \u2014 a 30-point gap in recent win-rate is substantial in collegiate LoL. BO3 AMPLIFICATION: Best-of-three format reduces variance vs single-game matches. Skill gaps compound across multiple games. A 70% favorite in BO3 typically wins 68-72% of series. MARKET PRICING: YES at 84% is moderately aggressive relative to the 65-72% base rate implied by form. The price reflects some confidence above pure win-rate extrapolation, possibly from team reputation or roster familiarity. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING: Event starts in ~1.3 hours. No time for roster news, substitutions, or coach decisions to materially shift the match. Market price is final consensus; any reversal from current trajectory would require an in-game upset. COLLEGIATE LoL VOLATILITY: College esports has higher variance than pro play due to inconsistent preparation, scrim quality, and team chemistry. This warrants modest downside risk (confidence_no set conservatively at 38%) despite form advantage. DATA GAPS: No head-to-head history provided, no current tournament standings, no patch notes on balance or meta shifts, no individual player performance metrics. These gaps prevent higher confidence on either side. PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES has risen +5pp in 24hrs and +4.5pp over 7 days, suggesting market consensus hardening toward Maryville. This aligns with form data but doesn't materially change underlying probabilities. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Form data (7W-3L vs 4W-6L) strongly supports YES side. NO side data is sparse \u2014 only form suggests Citadel is underdog. Confidence_no set lower (38%) to reflect this asymmetry and unknown variables. BASE RATE CONCLUSION: A 70% favorite in BO3 collegiate LoL should win ~68-72% of the time. Market at 84% overestimates edge slightly; probability_score set to 72 (midpoint of base-rate range) with modest downward adjustment for college volatility.", "key_factor": "In collegiate LoL, teams with 70%+ win-rate in recent form (7W-3L) typically win 65-75% of matches vs teams at 40% win-rate (4W-6L). BO3 format amplifies skill gaps: favored teams win ~68-72% of BO3s when form differential is this pronounced."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "YES side (84%) is OVERPRICED relative to available objective data. Market is pricing in heavy Maryville bias driven by recent form (7W-3L vs 4W-6L), but confidence in this edge is artificially elevated by crowd conviction. Maryville's 70% win rate over last 10 is objectively strong; Citadel's 40% is weak. This supports a YES lean, but NOT 84% confidence. Critical data gap: NO RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY, NO CURRENT STANDINGS, NO PLAYER INJURIES, NO DRAFT TRENDS, NO TEAM MOMENTUM INFLECTION POINTS. Market is extrapolating season-long form without match-specific context. Price action shows RISING YES trend (+4.5pp over 7 days, +5pp in 24h) with LOW volatility (1.5pp/hr). This suggests crowd consensus building, not information discovery. Classic crowded trade pattern. Citadel's NO side is UNDERPRICED at 17% despite being a live event with execution risk. BO3 format means any team can steal games on good draft/teamfight reads. 17% implies near-certainty for Maryville; BO3 esports rarely have >85% favorite win rates. Sharp move on Apr 14 (+7.5pp for NO) then reversal on Apr 17 (-6.0pp for NO) suggests short-term positioning noise rather than fundamental information arrival. EVENT TIMING (LIVE/IMMINENT, ~1.3 hours): At this point, prices will move sharply post-game, but briefing contains insufficient tactical intelligence (no team news, roster changes, meta reads) to justify 84% conviction. Market is relying purely on season aggregate stats. Greed signal: Crowd is doubling down on the statistical favorite without pricing in BO3 upset variance. High volume ($5.7k) for a college LoL match suggests retail retail enthusiasm, not sharp money. Maryville deserves YES lean due to form, but 84% \u2192 78% is a modest repricing to reflect crowd overconfidence and information asymmetry on the NO side. Confidence split: YES confidence 62 (form data is real but limited; no head-to-head), NO confidence 45 (insufficient counter-narrative; Citadel's weakness is documented but BO3 variance not priced in).", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market pricing (84% YES) appears OVERWEIGHT relative to available data; this is a college esports match with limited public scouting information compared to professional League scenes. Maryville University strong recent form (7W-3L, 70% winrate last 10) vs Citadel Gaming weak form (4W-6L, 40% winrate) provides legitimate YES support, but sample size (10 matches) for college competition is modest. BO3 format favors consistency and team cohesion; if Maryville has stronger macro play or drafting, they would win 2+ games; if Citadel has hidden meta advantages or roster synergy not reflected in headline record, BO3 allows them to exploit this. Zero head-to-head history provided; first meetings in round-robin formats often surprise due to unknown preparation gaps, coach tendencies, or in-game adaptation. College esports scene (vs. professional LEC/LCS) exhibits higher volatility due to less stable rosters, shorter practice windows, and less rigorous opponent analysis infrastructure. Market has risen +5.0pp in 24h and +4.5pp over 7 days, suggesting YES confidence has consolidated; this could reflect late sharp action or broader market drift rather than fresh information. Citadel Gaming's April 14 +7.5pp spike on NO side suggests temporary bullish thesis that reversed by April 17 (-6.0pp); unclear what drove either move (injury? roster news? none reported in briefing). NO-side confidence is LOW (35) because briefing provides zero countersignals to Citadel's weak form; any case for Citadel winning must rest on unmeasured coaching, draft ingenuity, or player form on the day \u2014 all invisible to analyst. YES-side confidence is MODERATE (45) because recent form is real data, but college esports record does not predict BO3 outcomes as reliably as professional circuits with standardized conditions and extensive footage. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.3 hours to start); large probability reversals are unlikely unless roster news breaks in next 90 minutes; market should reflect this near-terminal positioning. Resolution is clean (match result or 50-50 on forfeit/cancellation); no ambiguity on identity of teams; PandaScore confidence 100/100 supports unambiguous resolution.", "key_factor": "Recent form differential (Maryville 7-3 vs Citadel 4-6 in last 10) is the only reliable predictive signal; market has priced this heavily favoring Maryville (84% YES), but lack of head-to-head history, team roster stability, meta adaptation, and coaching adjustments creates material uncertainty in a best-of-three format where momentum swings are common."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "YES BASELINE: Maryville's 7W-3L (70%) recent form vs Citadel's 4W-6L (40%) form creates a 30-point form gap. Market price of 84% YES reflects this asymmetry and is likely anchored on aggregate season performance. MARKET STRUCTURE: YES has been RISING (+4.5pp/7d, +5pp/24h) while NO has been FALLING (-4.5pp/7d). This suggests consensus confidence in Maryville is hardening, not softening \u2014 price is moving away from the 50-50 midpoint toward conviction. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero head-to-head history, zero current standings position, zero draft tendencies, zero recent patch notes, and zero roster information for either team. We do not know if Maryville is complacent (already playoff-locked?) or if Citadel is fighting for survival (9th/10th relegation danger?). Motivation asymmetry could be significant. BLACK SWAN #1 \u2014 ROSTER CRISIS: Citadel Gaming could face a last-minute player absence (illness, family emergency, banned account, visa delay). A sub mid or jungle in a BO3 against a superior-macro team is devastating. Maryville's form advantage would balloon from 70% \u2192 85%+ in this scenario. However, no briefing signal flags this. BLACK SWAN #2 \u2014 DRAFT MISMATCH: Maryville's 7W streak may reflect strong macro and team cohesion, NOT a flexible or deep champion pool. If Citadel's coach identifies a vulnerable pick (e.g., Maryville forced to play a weak support champion, or a mid-lane one-trick), ban priority could flip the series. A 2-1 Citadel upset becomes plausible if draft goes Citadel's way in games 2\u20133. BLACK SWAN #3 \u2014 MOTIVATION / BRACKET POSITIONING: If Maryville is already locked into playoffs (6th seed or better) and Citadel is fighting for Top 6 survival, the psychological momentum flips. Citadel would have everything to prove; Maryville might play safer or test comps. No standings data provided, so this is latent risk. PRICE SKEPTICISM: At 84% YES, the market is pricing Citadel as a ~16-17% underdog. This is reasonable given form, but it leaves almost NO room for a single variable (roster change, draft innovation, motivation gap) to swing the outcome. In esports, BO3 series are volatile: a 70-30 expected win rate doesn't guarantee 84% because one bad draft or one player's bad game can cost a map. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence_yes is 62 (moderate-high) because Maryville's form gap is REAL and recent. Confidence_no is 48 (low-moderate) because the briefing offers NO affirmative evidence for Citadel's win path \u2014 only silence on their strengths, mental state, and draft prep. A NO win is plausible but under-evidenced. LIVE/IMMINENT IMPLICATION: Match starts in ~1.3 hours. Any roster crisis, visa issue, or equipment failure would likely have leaked by now (Reddit, Discord, official announcements). The absence of such signals slightly BOOSTS confidence in YES (both teams field full rosters). However, in-game performance under pressure is still a wildcard. PROBABILITY RECONCILIATION: probability_score=72 (vs market 84%) reflects a modest discount for the black-swan factors (roster unknown, draft matchup opacity, motivation gap). probability_no_score=35 (vs implied 16%) reflects that while Citadel is underdog, the evidence gap (no data on their recent form, draft style, or roster health) means a 2-1 upset is non-trivial. The gap (72+35=107) captures double-counting: I assign high weight to 'Maryville favored' but acknowledge Citadel's win scenario is under-analyzed by the briefing.", "key_factor": "Citadel Gaming fields a substitute mid-laner or jungler mid-series due to an undisclosed illness/emergency, or Maryville University's win-streak masks a critical champion pool vulnerability that Citadel exploits via targeted draft bans."}], "final_score": 0.7235722004239598, "no_score": 0.29118290042463374, "edge": -0.14409090909090905, "no_edge": 0.5259090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 58.57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0502615081746454, "The Bull": 0.9485651334222127, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0530400843938654, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0532291381796675, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0546263940607403, "The Contrarian": 1.072388005832532, "The Bear": 0.7678897359363381}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1949873", "question": "LoL: Maryville University vs Citadel Gaming (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Maryville University and Citadel Gaming in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 17 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Maryville University\" if Maryville University win the match against Citadel Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Citadel Gaming\" if Citadel Gaming win the match against Maryville University.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-17T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.835, "volume_usd": 5722.945933999965, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["112869833988464864107905589119619675148974876563204725099920380592509689644720", "2768672732173641090810011404686098055753087114756720737666319825679433772721"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["The College League of Legends 2026 North Conference is part of the North American Collegiate LoL circuit ...", "The League of Legends College Championship 2026 is a Collegiate League of Legends tournament featuring the top North American collegiate esports teams.", "College VALORANT 2025-2026: Championship is an online/offline VAL tournament organized by UNIVERSITY Esports NA and Riot Games.", "NACL 2026 Spring is an online North American LoL tournament organized by Riot Games and Liga ACE.", "This A-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 27 to Jun 05", "#### Group B\n\n### Playoffs\n\n## Broadcast\n\n### Streams\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| Language | English Speaking |\n| Streams |  |\n\nEnglish Speaking\n\n### Broadcast Talent\n\n## References\n\n#### About\n\n#### Affiliated Sites [...] Logo\n\n###### General\n\n###### Specific\n\n# Texas Tech: RaiderLAN 2026\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  | You can help improve this page!", "To fix this issue, please check startgg and VODS for information.", "|\n\nUnited States\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  | School is not a known Liquipedia Tiertype |\n\n## Contents\n\n## About\n\n### Format\n\n### Prize Pool\n\n## Participants\n\nUnited States\nUnited States\nUnited States\n\nUnited States\nUnited States\n\nUnited States\nUnited States\n\nUnited States\nUnited States\nUnited States\n\nUnited States\n\nUnited States\n\nUnited States\n\n## Results\n\n### Group Stage\n\n| Legend |\n\n| Advance to the Playoffs - Upper Bracket |\n| Advance to the Playoffs - Lower Bracket |\n| Eliminated |\n\n#### Group A\n\n#### Group B\n\n### Playoffs\n\n## Broadcast\n\n### Streams", "Regular Season: Single Round Robin; All matches are Bo3; Top 6 teams advance to Playoffs; The 9th and 10th will face relegation in the Promotion Tournament", "CCG EsportsCCG Esports CCG Esports | 75 | 15 | 40 | 20 |\n| 7."], "news_summary": "Maryville University faces Citadel Gaming in a best-of-three League of Legends match in the NACL 2026 Spring Regular Season. The match is scheduled for April 17, 2026 at 20:00 UTC and is part of the North American Challengers League's single round-robin format, where all regular season matches are played as BO3. The top 6 teams advance to playoffs, while the bottom two teams face relegation. No recent head-to-head history or current standings data for these specific teams in 2026 Spring is available in the search results.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data to build YES case."], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data to build NO case."], "key_context": ["NACL 2026 Spring uses single round-robin format with all matches as BO3", "Top 6 teams advance to playoffs; 9th and 10th face relegation tournament", "Regular season runs March 27 to June 5, 2026", "Maryville University listed in College LoL 2026 North Conference participants"], "prior_match_facts": [], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-17T18:39:52.603938Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "112869833988464864107905589119619675148974876563204725099920380592509689644720", "data_points": 90, "weighted_avg": 0.8022465042752974, "change_1w_pp": 4.499999999999993, "change_24h_pp": 4.999999999999993, "volatility_24h": 1.5087464298130697, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "2768672732173641090810011404686098055753087114756720737666319825679433772721", "data_points": 36, "weighted_avg": 0.18642391322516322, "change_1w_pp": -4.499999999999998, "change_24h_pp": 1.0000000000000009, "volatility_24h": 1.100504934614612, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-14T01:00:53Z", "delta_pp": 7.499999999999998}, {