4-hour start time means limited new information will arrive. RECENT FORM PARITY TRAP: 'Both teams 5\u20135 in last 10 matches' is a red herring\u2014this is likely data from a different competition or includes non-NACL matches. The briefing's NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states NRG 4\u20130 and Blue Otter 1\u20132 in NACL Spring 2026, which is the operative context. BO3 UPSET RISK (REAL BUT BOUNDED): BO3 does increase upset probability vs. BO1, but not enough to overcome an 80% vs. 28.6% win-rate gap. Blue Otter would need to win 2 of 3 games against a team that has never lost a series this season. Possible? Yes (~16\u201322% base upset rate). Likely? No. TIMING & VOLATILITY: Event is TODAY, 4 hours away. Sharp move on Apr 17 11:00 UTC (\u20135.0pp on NO) reflects late information; likely NRG roster confirmation or Blue Otter injury/roster news. Too close to event for dramatic reversals without forfeit/cancellation (which resolves 50\u201350). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES side (72) because the gap in match records, game differential, and season-long performance is large and well-documented. Lower confidence in NO side (35) because the briefing provides minimal detail on Blue Otter's player form, coaching adjustments, or meta alignment\u2014only that they've lost more than they've won.", "key_factor": "NRG's 4\u20130 undefeated record with +6 game differential vs. Blue Otter's 1\u20132 record with \u20133 game differential reflects a substantial skill and consistency gap; BO3 format reduces\u2014but does not eliminate\u2014upset likelihood, especially when one team's win-rate is 80% vs. 40%."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.76, "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CONSENSUS BLIND SPOT: Market prices NRG at 84% based purely on aggregate record (4\u20130 vs 1\u20132, +6 GD vs \u20133 GD). This is mechanically correct but ignores B