{"run_id": "787d37ff-f9b6-4a92-9540-559297cd7056", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T18:55:15.414990+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1989113", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: Bigetron MY by VIT vs Team Rey (BO3) - MPL Malaysia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between Bigetron MY by VIT and Team Rey in the MPL Malaysia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 2:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bigetron MY by VIT\" if Bigetron MY by VIT win the match against Team Rey.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Rey\" if Team Rey win the match against Bigetron MY by VIT.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T12:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T06:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.405, "volume_usd": 72.77401, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["82003091002219860656917021813370913823916273668260532545380745380586926102521", "33053688958634994753172410979017729462180514252013990688129316512169255985662"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-18 06:30 UTC (imminent, ~12 hours away per briefing timestamp). No prior scoreline exists for this matchup\u2014this is a fresh encounter. RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Bigetron MY by VIT wins the BO3 match; NO if Team Rey wins. Normal competitive resolution applies (no forfeit/walkover/tie scenarios evident). FORM DATA ASYMMETRY: Bigetron MY by VIT shows 1W-3L (last 4 matches); Team Rey shows 3W-7L (last 10 matches). Bigetron's recent form is marginally better, but sample sizes are small and form data lacks dates/context. ROSTER STABILITY CONCERN: Bigetron made critical roster changes on 2026-04-16 (middle laner + head coach Kenji joined)\u2014only 1 day before match. This is extremely tight for integration and coordination in a BO3 format. Team Rey roster appears stable per 2026-03-12 data, suggesting better team cohesion. INSUFFICIENT H2H DATA: Briefing explicitly states 'no prior H2H data available.' Cannot anchor probability on head-to-head patterns. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current market prices are YES 40% / NO 60%. Price action shows YES side FALLING (-10.5pp over 7 days; -10.5pp over 24 hours), while NO side RISING (+10.5pp over 7 days; +11.0pp over 24 hours). This suggests marginal shift toward Team Rey, possibly reflecting awareness of Bigetron's recent roster churn. VOLATILITY & VOLUME: Low volume ($73 USD) and moderate volatility (2.2\u20133.2pp/hr) suggest thin liquidity and uncertain participant conviction. Market prices are not deeply informed. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 28 (low) because Bigetron's pre-match roster integration risk is factual but opaque\u2014we lack direct evidence of integration success/failure, player synergy, or coaching effectiveness with the new middle laner/coach. confidence_no = 32 (low-to-moderate) because Team Rey's stable roster is a minor positive but we have no recent performance wins to justify high confidence in their victory. Form data (3W-7L) is middling overall. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 42% YES reflects slight underdog status for Bigetron due to integration risk, offset partially by marginally better recent form. 58% NO reflects Team Rey's roster stability and market price shift, but lack of recent wins prevents higher confidence. Probabilities do not sum to 100 because true uncertainty is high and data quality is poor on both sides. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Liquipedia is primary source; fallback to credible reporting + video evidence if needed. No mechanism risk is evident at this stage. Match is unlikely to be canceled or delayed >7 days given it is a regular season matchup in an active league.", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data: no head-to-head history, no recent match results for either team, and Bigetron's roster changes occurred 1 day before match\u2014temporal proximity prevents reliable team-strength assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS \u2014 Team Rey positioned as safer bet: \u2022 Team Rey roster locked in and stable as of 2026-03-12 with no recent churn; all five positions filled with consistent players. \u2022 Bigetron MY by VIT made critical last-minute changes: new middle lane player AND new head coach both joined 2026-04-16 \u2014 only 1 day before match. Integration risk is severe for a BO3 requiring coordination. \u2022 Market has been rising NO from 50% (7-day EMA) to 60% (current) \u2014 consistent +10.5pp shift over last week, with strong momentum surge on 2026-04-17 (+7.5pp, then +5.5pp). This reflects informed traders pricing in the roster instability. \u2022 Bigetron MY by VIT recent form is weak: 1W-3L in last 4 matches. Even before roster disruption, team was underperforming. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES) WEAKNESSES \u2014 Bigetron MY by VIT vulnerable: \u2022 Last-minute roster turnover in competitive esports is a red flag. Middle lane is a critical strategic position; new player has minimal time to sync with team cohesion, meta calls, and coach's playbook. \u2022 New head coach (Kenji, joined 2026-04-16) has even less runway to implement strategy or read opponents. BO3 is decision-intensive; lack of pre-match preparation and trust amplifies risk. \u2022 Bigetron MY by VIT's 1W-3L record suggests pre-existing structural issues (whether roster, meta fit, or coaching). New personnel alone cannot reverse form in 24 hours. \u2022 Team Rey's 3W-7L (10-match sample) is middling, but the 3 wins are recent and against a MORE stable baseline. No roster churn = lower variance, higher predictability. MARKET PRICING COHERENCE: \u2022 YES side has fallen -10.5pp over 7 days (50% \u2192 40%); NO side has risen +10.5pp (50% \u2192 60%). This is internally consistent and signals that market participants have high confidence in the roster instability thesis. \u2022 24-hour volatility on NO is elevated (3.2pp/hr vs YES 2.2pp/hr), consistent with rapid repricing once Bigetron's recent changes became public. \u2022 Sharp move on 2026-04-17 18:54 UTC: +5.5pp to NO, -5.5pp from YES (matched move). Timing aligns with data collection refresh; likely reflects latest roster intel. CAVEAT \u2014 DATA LIMITATIONS: \u2022 No head-to-head match history provided between these teams. \u2022 Player-level statistics (individual skill, champion pools, synergy) unavailable in briefing. \u2022 Bigetron's new roster integration could be a net positive if the new middle laner and coach are elite talents, but briefing provides no such evidence. \u2022 Team Rey's weak overall record (3W-7L in 10 matches) means NO is not a dominant favorite \u2014 just the safer asset in an uncertain matchup. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: \u2022 Bigetron MY by VIT's last-minute disruption + weak form + new coach/player creates structural disadvantage that outweighs uncertainty. \u2022 Team Rey's roster stability and recent wins (even if limited) make it the 'path of least resistance' \u2014 the team less likely to implode. \u2022 Market's 60-40 split is reasonable but may slightly undervalue Bigetron's integration risk. Setting NO at 62% (vs 60% market) reflects modest bull conviction that roster chaos is being underpriced. \u2022 Confidence in NO is 58% (above 50%, reflecting positive evidence) but not high (below 65%), because Team Rey's own record is mediocre and briefing offers no direct head-to-head or player-level data to confirm NO will execute. \u2022 Confidence in YES is low (35%) due to disruptive roster changes creating execution risk that is hard to overcome in a single BO3 match within 12 hours.", "key_factor": "Team Rey's established roster stability and track record versus Bigetron MY by VIT's disruptive last-minute roster changes (middle laner + head coach joined 2026-04-16, one day before match)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 RECENCY BIAS IN MARKET: YES is priced at 40% despite Bigetron MY by VIT's catastrophic recent form (1W-3L last 4 matches). Market is anchoring on raw win-loss without accounting for roster context. Team Rey's own record (3W-7L last 10) is only marginally better \u2014 the market is treating Team Rey as strong by default, not by evidence. ROSTER TIMING PARADOX: Bigetron MY by VIT added middle laner + head coach Kenji on April 16 (2 days before match). This is EITHER a massive vulnerability (unpracticed new lineup) OR a hidden asset (fresh tactical setup, motivated new players, veteran coach injection). The briefing provides zero evidence of integration problems; market assumes chaos but has no data. TEAM REY'S HIDDEN WEAKNESS \u2014 STAGNATION: Team Rey has NOT made roster changes since March 12 (35+ days old). In a fast-patch esports environment, static rosters accumulate predictability. No evidence in briefing that Rey has adapted meta or strategy. Bigetron's new coach Kenji may have seen Rey's tendencies and built a counter-read. FORM MUST BE CONTEXTUALIZED: Bigetron 1W-3L could reflect mid-roster uncertainty or integration issues NOW RESOLVED. Team Rey 3W-7L shows inconsistency \u2014 they are NOT a stable favorite. The 20pp price gap (60% vs 40%) is too wide given symmetric form weakness. NO PRIOR H2H DATA: Zero head-to-head history provided. This eliminates reverse-matchup advantage for either team. In BO3 with unknown dynamics, newcomers often execute fresh game plans better than established teams on autopilot. MARKET MOMENTUM IS CONTRARIAN SIGNAL: YES fell 10.5pp over 7 days; NO rose 10.5pp. Sharp money moved in on April 17 18:54 UTC (+5.5pp for NO). This suggests informed traders expected YES to underperform. BUT: with <12 hours to match start and zero new concrete information (no scrim results, no patch changes, no player statements), this momentum likely reflects retail panic, not fundamental analysis. Contrarian positioning favors the underdog. CRITICAL DATA GAP ON BOTH SIDES: Briefing offers NO match statistics, NO player form tracking, NO meta context, NO coach history, NO scrim results. Confidence must be suppressed across both sides. Team Rey is not proven strong; Bigetron is not proven weak post-roster update. TEMPORAL PRESSURE LIMITS REVERSAL: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (11.6 hours). Any dramatic underdog win would require Bigetron to execute near-flawlessly immediately post-roster integration. This is plausible but not probable \u2014 confidence for YES case is capped at 28-32 range. Conversely, confidence for NO should also be LIMITED to 35-40 range because market pricing assumes Team Rey is a strong favorite when the data shows only marginal form advantage. AUTONOMY PRINCIPLE APPLIED: probability_score (42) reflects: Bigetron has hidden upside (new tactical setup, fresh motivation) and Team Rey has hidden weakness (static roster stagnation), but near-total absence of concrete performance data on integration means YES cannot be priced higher without speculation. probability_no_score (58) reflects: Team Rey is favored by form only, not by proven strength or evidence of Rey's own quality, so NO's advantage is narrow and vulnerable to Bigetron's unpredictability. Sum = 100 here because the briefing contains symmetric ignorance: neither team's post-roster state is documented. VERDICT: YES is underpriced at 40% conditional on Bigetron's roster integration working. Probability lifted to 42% as bearish case for underdog. NO is only marginally stronger and benefits from market panic-pricing YES down. True 50-50 match with slight edge to Team Rey's form consistency, but margin is <10pp not 20pp.", "key_factor": "Bigetron MY by VIT's extremely recent roster stabilization (April 16) with fresh coaching could unlock synergy and tactical innovation that Team Rey's static lineup has not prepared for."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.4, "probability_yes": 0.4, "probability_no": 0.6, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (starts in ~11.6 hours). Market price at 40% YES / 60% NO suggests informed traders are favoring Team Rey. With insufficient time for major reversals, current market prices should receive weight. ROSTER STABILITY ASYMMETRY: Bigetron MY by VIT made critical roster changes 1 day before match (new middle laner + head coach joined 2026-04-16). Team Rey has established, consistent roster as of 2026-03-12. Integration risk favors Team Rey. RECENT FORM DISADVANTAGE: Bigetron MY by VIT recent form is 1W-3L (last 4 matches). Team Rey recent form is 3W-7L (last 10 matches). While both teams show weak records, Bigetron's decline is steeper and more recent. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT: YES side fell 10.5pp over 7 days and 10.5pp over 24 hours (currently at 40%). NO side rose 10.5pp over 7 days and 11.0pp over 24 hours (currently at 60%). Consistent directional movement suggests information flow favoring Team Rey. NO PRIOR HEAD-TO-HEAD: No H2H data in briefing. Cannot anchor on historical matchup results. DATA GAPS: Cannot establish reliable base rate for Mobile Legends regular season BO3 outcomes without team strength ratings, tournament tier, or comparative win rates. Both recent form records are weak, limiting predictive power. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: Confidence in YES estimate (28) is low due to roster instability, weak recent form, and market price disadvantage working against Bigetron. Confidence in NO estimate (32) is similarly low because Team Rey's recent form (3W-7L) is also poor and provides limited conviction. Market prices drive the 40/60 split more than underlying strength metrics. MARKET PRICE AS SIGNAL: In the absence of strong team-specific data, the current 40/60 split and recent price movement toward NO represent the most reliable signal available. This becomes the anchor for probability estimation.", "key_factor": "Mobile Legends esports matches: no reliable historical base rate available for predicting team victory in regular season BO3s without team strength metrics, head-to-head records, or recent performance data."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market is pricing YES (Bigetron MY by VIT) at 40%, NO (Team Rey) at 60% \u2014 a 20pp spread favoring Team Rey. YES price has FALLEN 10.5pp over 7 days; NO price has RISEN 10.5pp \u2014 consistent directional pressure toward Team Rey. Recent sharp move on 2026-04-17 18:54 UTC: YES down 5.5pp, NO up 5.5pp, occurring ~12 hours before match start \u2014 suggests late information flow favoring Team Rey. Bigetron MY by VIT shows 1W-3L recent form (25% win rate, last 4 matches) \u2014 weak momentum entering imminent match. Team Rey shows 3W-7L recent form (30% win rate, last 10 matches) \u2014 marginally better but still sub-50%, not significantly superior. CRITICAL TIMING SIGNAL: Bigetron MY by VIT made TWO major roster changes on 2026-04-16 (middle laner + head coach joined), only 1 day before match. This is EXTREMELY risky \u2014 new players lack chemistry with established teammates, coordination untested in live BO3. Team Rey has stable, established roster as of 2026-03-12 (roster lock ~36 days before match) \u2014 organizational stability vs. Bigetron's 24-hour roster upheaval. Market sentiment appears RATIONAL here: The crowd is correctly penalizing Bigetron for last-minute roster chaos. Fear is justified, not panic-driven. Volume is thin ($73 USD) \u2014 low liquidity means price reflects weak signal, not expert consensus. Moves could be small retail trades or lineup positioning, not fundamental conviction. Briefing provides NO prior H2H data, NO hero bans/picks, NO coach strategies, NO team scrim results \u2014 analysis is pure form + roster stability. Form favors neither side strongly. Crowd psychology: Team Rey is the 'safer' bet (stable roster, slightly better form trend) and the market has correctly repriced YES downward to reflect Bigetron's chaos penalty. However, confidence on BOTH sides is LOW because (1) form data is weak for both teams, (2) recent roster changes create unknown variance, (3) no H2H precedent, (4) mobile esports upsets are common. Ignorance mass (~4pp) is appropriate: market is not fully confident in either outcome due to missing strategic data (champion picks, coach intent, scrims). Recommendation: Probability_score 38 reflects YES side penalty for roster chaos, but confidence_yes and confidence_no both remain low (28 and 32) due to insufficient match-specific intelligence. The market vibe is 'Fear' (fear of Bigetron's instability), but the fear is DATA-DRIVEN, not irrational exuberance.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "ROSTER TIMING RISK (YES side weakness): New middle laner joined 2026-04-16; head coach Kenji joined same day. BO3 matches demand refined team chemistry, macro coordination, and mid-lane-centric shotcalling. A 24-hour integration window is extremely aggressive for professional play. FORM DATA ASYMMETRY: Bigetron MY by VIT 1W-3L (last 4 matches, recent); Team Rey 3W-7L (last 10 matches, poor overall record). BTR's 25% recent win rate is concerning, but insufficient sample size with new lineup makes extrapolation unreliable. TEAM REY BASELINE: Established roster as of 2026-03-12 (45+ days of integration). Despite 3W-7L, roster stability favors predictable in-game execution versus a team mid-integration crisis. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES (BTR) has fallen -10.5pp over 7 days and -10.5pp in 24 hours, reaching 40%. NO (Rey) has risen +10.5pp and +11.0pp respectively to 60%. Sharp move on 2026-04-17 18:54 UTC (+5.5pp NO, -5.5pp YES) suggests informed market reaction to roster news or internal intel. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $73 total volume indicates low conviction/small market. Prices are not yet at extremes ($0.41/$0.59), suggesting moderate disagreement, not consensus capitulation on BTR. NO PRIOR H2H: Absence of head-to-head data prevents calibration of relative strength. New BTR roster has zero competitive history versus Rey in 2026 context. REGRESSION TO MEAN RISK (YES): If BTR's recent 1W-3L reflects team-wide weakness (not just roster churn), new mid-laner does not resolve it. If it reflects previous mid-laner underperformance, new player may improve outlook, but 24-hour acclimation negates upside. IMMINENT TIMING: Event starts in ~11.6 hours. No time for injury withdrawals, forfeits, or schedule changes that would trigger 50-50 resolution unless match is canceled outright (low probability). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong technical evidence for YES-side underperformance (roster instability, poor form, zero chemistry). Weak evidence for NO-side superiority (Rey's overall record is also poor, no clear competitive advantage demonstrated). Confidence_yes set to 28 (roster risk is real but not deterministic); confidence_no set to 35 (Rey may capitalize but lacks proof of dominance).", "key_factor": "Bigetron MY by VIT's roster overhaul 24 hours before match (new mid-laner and head coach on 2026-04-16) introduces severe coordination risk in a BO3 format requiring precise team synergy; Team Rey's established roster has ~5 weeks of integration post-March roster updates."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "CRITICAL ROSTER TIMING: Bigetron MY by VIT brought in a new middle laner AND head coach on 2026-04-16 \u2014 exactly ONE DAY before this BO3. This is extraordinarily tight integration time for a competitive esports match. INTEGRATION BURDEN: Middle lane is one of the most strategically central positions in Mobile Legends. New mid-laner synergy with junglers, roamers, and team macro-play typically requires 1-2 weeks of scrim blocks and coordination refinement, not 18 hours. COACHING VACUUM: A head coach change 24 hours before a BO3 means no established in-game shot-calling, no calibrated pick/ban strategy vs. Team Rey, and no crisis-management playbook if a game goes sideways. FORM CLIFF: Bigetron MY by VIT is 1W-3L in last 4 matches \u2014 a steep downward trajectory. Adding roster chaos on top of poor form is a multiplier, not a mitigator. MARKET INEFFICIENCY SIGNAL: YES side has fallen 10.5pp in 7 days while NO side has risen 10.5pp. This drift suggests market participants are aware of the roster change and are pricing in disruption. TEAM REY STABILITY: Team Rey roster was last updated 2026-03-12 (>36 days before match). While their 3W-7L record (last 10) is mediocre, they are a KNOWN quantity with established internal communication and trust. BO3 FORMAT PRESSURE: Best-of-3 matches amplify mental tilt and communication breakdown. A new mid-laner + new coach under series pressure is high-variance chaos; Team Rey, though inconsistent, avoids this penalty. ABSENCE OF PRIOR H2H DATA: No head-to-head record in briefing; cannot anchor on a historical win probability. This removes confidence in any pure 'team strength' argument for YES. LIQUIDITY FLOOR: $73 USD volume indicates thin market \u2014 retail/casual flow may not have fully priced in the severity of the roster integration risk. CONTRARIAN PIVOT: The market's 40% YES / 60% NO split appears to ALREADY incorporate some roster concern, but 40% for a team with 1W-3L form AND new mid-laner+coach may still be too generous. The black swan is not that Bigetron underperforms slightly \u2014 it's that the new mid-laner and coach cannot even functionally communicate in-game, causing gank miscoordination, ult timings, and lost teamfights that Team Rey can punish despite their own inconsistency.", "key_factor": "Bigetron MY by VIT's newly-onboarded middle laner (joined 2026-04-16, <48 hours before match) and head coach fail to establish basic synergy under high-pressure BO3 conditions, amplifying the team's recent 1W-3L slump into a decisive series loss."}], "final_score": 0.40412052758838746, "no_score": 0.5940349886786527, "edge": 0.2859090909090909, "no_edge": 0.09590909090909094, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 40.86% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0502615081746454, "The Bull": 0.9485651334222127, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0530400843938654, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0532291381796675, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0546263940607403, "The Contrarian": 1.072388005832532, "The Bear": 0.7678897359363381}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1989113", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: Bigetron MY by VIT vs Team Rey (BO3) - MPL Malaysia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between Bigetron MY by VIT and Team Rey in the MPL Malaysia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 2:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bigetron MY by VIT\" if Bigetron MY by VIT win the match against Team Rey.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Rey\" if Team Rey win the match against Bigetron MY by VIT.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, t