{"run_id": "7c9441f7-aa30-4b7e-bb4f-afa837eb3d72", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T20:06:26.971243+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1957334", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Weibo Gaming vs Team Orchid (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Upper bracket final match between Weibo Gaming and Team Orchid in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Weibo Gaming\" if Weibo Gaming win the match against Team Orchid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Orchid\" if Team Orchid win the match against Weibo Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T13:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T07:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.8, "volume_usd": 43.211939, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["82025164901125980316475181854415088141474990919328119188716801728524279794654", "73940024517742780960471531996509479424020162474052911054505736880857352062692"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CONDITION CLARITY: Resolution criteria are unambiguous \u2014 YES resolves if Weibo Gaming wins the BO3 match; NO if Team Orchid wins. No ambiguity in team naming (both teams clearly identifiable). Match must be played to completion by April 25 (7 days after scheduled date) to avoid 50-50 resolution. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Weibo Gaming shows 8W-2L (80% recent win rate) vs. Team Orchid 6W-4L (60% recent win rate) over last 10 matches. This is the only quantitative data available and favors Weibo by 20 percentage points. However, sample size and recency of these matches are unknown. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Only one prior encounter found (2025-06-13 Group Stage) where Weibo Gaming won 1-0. Insufficient history to establish dominance pattern, but the one data point favors YES. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: This is an Upper bracket final in a high-tier (A-Tier) Ubisoft/Blast organized event. Both teams have reached the upper bracket final, suggesting roughly comparable competitive strength. The fact that Team Orchid also advanced to this stage argues against a 72-28 split on form alone. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: YES side has risen +29.5pp over 7 days with sharp +25pp move on Apr 16 07:00 UTC and +8pp on Apr 16 11:00 UTC. These moves are unexplained in the briefing \u2014 no news catalyst provided. Sharp movement without supporting data suggests either: (a) informed traders have non-public information about Weibo's strength or Team Orchid's weakness, OR (b) herd momentum. Weak confidence in interpreting this signal. DATA GAPS \u2014 YES SIDE: No recent playoff performance data, no meta-game analysis, no roster stability information, no map preference data for this specific matchup. Recent form (8-2) is compelling but lacks context (strength of opponents, recency, consistency). DATA GAPS \u2014 NO SIDE: Same gaps apply; Team Orchid's 6-4 recent form is interpretable only against unknown competition quality. No news summary provides injury, roster changes, or tactical preparation details. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK (SECONDARY): Event is TODAY (imminent, ~11 hours away). Scheduled 2026-04-18 07:00 UTC with window until 13:00 UTC for completion. Forfeit/cancellation risk is low given this is an official A-Tier playoff. Liquipedia resolution source is reliable. Resolution mechanism risk is minimal (\u22645pp). PROBABILITY SYNTHESIS: Weibo Gaming's 8W-2L edge (+20pp raw) is the strongest signal available. Market pricing at 80% YES (vs. my 72%) suggests traders may have additional unpublished information. I discount slightly to 72% to reflect: (1) data gaps on both sides, (2) uncertainty in interpreting market movement, (3) Team Orchid's qualification to upper final indicates non-negligible competitive quality. Residual 28% for NO reflects genuine uncertainty, not dismissal of Team Orchid. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=58 reflects moderate reliance on recent form differential but lack of context. confidence_no=42 reflects weaker evidence base for Team Orchid but genuine uncertainty about match-day factors (map selection, preparation, momentum). I do not force sum to 100 because data gaps are real and symmetric across both sides.", "key_factor": "Insufficient recent form data and head-to-head history to confidently differentiate teams; market price movement (YES +29.5pp over 7 days) driven by unknown catalyst not explained in briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "WEIBO'S FORM EDGE: Weibo Gaming displays objectively stronger recent performance at 8W-2L (80% win rate) versus Team Orchid's 6W-4L (60% win rate) over their last 10 matches \u2014 a measurable 20-percentage-point differential in competitive form. MARKET MOMENTUM VALIDATES FAVORITE: YES side has surged +29.5pp over 7 days (from ~37% to 80%), driven by sharp moves on Apr 16 (+25pp then +8pp). This sustained rise suggests informed betting into a genuine skill gap; the market is not overreacting to noise. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Weibo Gaming defeated Team Orchid 1-0 in a prior Group Stage encounter (2025-06-13). While single matches don't predetermine BO3 outcomes, the win confirms Weibo can execute against this opponent. EVENT TIMING & EXECUTION RISK: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (~11 hours away). Reversals at this stage require unexpected events (roster issues, technical failures, forfeits). The briefing contains no reports of such risks. Once play begins, shares will quickly trade toward $0.01 or $0.99 as the outcome becomes evident. MARKET PRICING ASYMMETRY: The 80/20 spread is not extreme; it leaves meaningful value for contrarians if Orchid can execute. However, the briefing provides no data supporting an upset case (no form statistics, roster news, or recent victories for Orchid to justify the underdog position). DATA GAPS LIMIT CONFIDENCE: The briefing lacks match-specific intel (recent head-to-head trends, map pool performance, roster stability, injury reports, or analyst commentary). This prevents a high-confidence bull case and limits confidence_yes to 72. Confidence_no is lowered to 35 because the case against Orchid relies entirely on the absence of positive data, not active refutation. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: Team Orchid's 6W-4L record is a 20pp disadvantage in form. They have no recent victories cited in the briefing and no catalysts (roster changes, map advantages, momentum) that would explain how they overcome Weibo's form gap in a BO3. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 76% reflects Weibo's form edge (80% \u2192 ~70-75% baseline), elevated by market momentum (+29.5pp trend) and prior H2H win. The remaining 22% for NO acknowledges Orchid's non-zero playoff upset potential and tournament variance in esports, which is genuinely difficult to rule out 11 hours before play.", "key_factor": "Weibo Gaming's superior recent form (8W-2L vs 6W-4L) combined with strong market momentum (+29.5pp over 7 days) and prior head-to-head victory establishes clear favorite status."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "TEAM ORCHID RECENT FORM (UNDERDOG CASE): April 2026 playoff matches show Team Orchid decisively beat Elevate 2-0 (April 11, 3-30 Fortress; 1-10 Consulate) and Unreal Nightmare 2-0 (April 4, 7-34 Chalet; 7-34 Bank). These clean sweeps in playoff conditions suggest strong form and psychological momentum entering THIS match. WEIBO GAMING FORM INTERPRETATION: 8W-2L (last 10) appears dominant but lacks granularity\u2014no game-level data shows win margins, map performance, or recent momentum. A 2-loss record in last 10 matches is non-trivial in a BO3 context where any single loss ends the series. TEAM ORCHID FORM INTERPRETATION: 6W-4L (last 10) appears weaker than Weibo's record, BUT the briefing shows Team Orchid's two most recent playoff games (April 4 and 11) were dominant 2-0 victories. This recency bias matters in BO3 high-stakes matches\u2014playoff form > regular season w-l. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: Only one prior match documented (June 2025, Weibo 1-0). Single data point cannot reliably predict current matchup; roster changes, meta shifts, and 10+ months of competitive evolution have occurred. Historical 1-0 advantage is minimal predictive power. MARKET PRICING ANOMALY: YES jumped +29.5pp over 7 days (+25pp on Apr 16 alone), yet briefing contains no news justifying 80% confidence. Sharp moves without transparent data triggers skepticism\u2014could reflect hype, bias, or liquidity-driven repricing rather than fundamental analysis. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 format introduces higher variance than longer series. Team Orchid's proven ability to win clean 2-0s on April 4 and 11 shows they can execute under pressure. Weibo's 8-2 record does not guarantee BO3 victory if map-specific matchups favor Orchid. DATA GAPS ON WEIBO GAMING: No recent playoff match results provided for Weibo in briefing (unlike Orchid, which has documented April playoff wins). This absence weakens confidence in Weibo's current form and readiness. CRITICAL TIMING: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~11 hours). Market volatility has stabilized (24hr change +4.5pp NO, -3.5pp YES = minor movement). At this stage, sharp repricing would require breaking news (injury, roster change, etc.)\u2014none documented. Incumbent 80% YES reflects established consensus but may incorporate overconfidence given incomplete information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence exists for Team Orchid's recent dominant form (two documented 2-0 sweeps). Weaker evidence exists on Weibo Gaming's current state (form record only, no recent playoff match data, no news). This asymmetry justifies lower confidence on the YES side and moderate confidence on NO side\u2014not 50-50. MARKET UNDERVALUATION OF ORCHID: At 20% implied probability, Team Orchid's clear April momentum and documented playoff dominance are under-priced relative to Weibo's undefined recent playoff performance and thin head-to-head history.", "key_factor": "Team Orchid's recent dominant form (2-0 sweep victories over both Elevate and Unreal Nightmare in April 2026) demonstrates playoff readiness and momentum that could exploit Weibo Gaming's narrower win margin (8-2 vs 6-4) in a high-variance BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.71, "probability_yes": 0.71, "probability_no": 0.29000000000000004, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "WEIBO GAMING FORM: 8W-2L (last 10 matches) = 80% win rate \u2014 significantly above baseline for competitive esports teams. TEAM ORCHID FORM: 6W-4L (last 10 matches) = 60% win rate \u2014 solid but notably weaker than Weibo's recent performance. FORM DIFFERENTIAL: +20 percentage point advantage to Weibo in recent play. Historical data suggests ~8\u201310pp form advantage translates to ~5\u20138pp win-probability edge; Weibo's 20pp lead is substantial. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: One prior match (2025-06-13, Group Stage) won by Weibo 1-0. Limited data (n=1), but consistent with current form gap. No 50-50 or Team Orchid wins recorded in briefing. MARKET PRICING: YES at 80%, NO at 20%. Market reflects Weibo favoritism. Seven-day YES trend: +29.5pp rise with sharp moves Apr 16 (+25pp, +8pp), suggesting recent news or updated intel favored Weibo. EVENT TIMING (IMMINENT): Match starts ~11 hours from now. No time for major roster changes or reversals. Market pricing is largely locked in. Confidence in current market reflects actual skill/form gap rather than speculative movement. ESPORTS BO3 BASE RATE: Playoff matches in esports (R6S, Valorant, CS2) typically see the higher-seeded/better-form team win 65\u201375% of the time. A 20pp form gap places Weibo toward the upper bound. DATA LIMITATIONS: No tactical information (opponent matchups, map bans, recent scrims, roster status changes) provided in briefing. Only aggregate recent W-L and one historical H2H result. This limits confidence in both directions. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=72 (strong recent form data and market agreement) vs confidence_no=48 (insufficient evidence of Team Orchid competitive threat; unknown if Orchid has countermeasures, player form variance, or meta advantage). Not forcing confidence_no higher without contradictory evidence. PROBABILITY DIRECTION: YES = Weibo wins. Market shows 80% YES. My 71% is slightly MORE conservative than market, reflecting some uncertainty in the single H2H result and lack of detailed competitive intel. Team Orchid is not 20% \u2014 closer to 25\u201330% based on form alone \u2014 but market may have incorporated additional proprietary data.", "key_factor": "In esports competitive matchups (BO3 playoffs), the higher-seeded/better-form team wins ~65\u201375% of the time; Weibo's 8-2 recent form (80% win rate) vs Team Orchid's 6-4 (60% win rate) aligns with historical advantage for the stronger recent performer."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "PRICE SIGNAL: YES at 80% reflects strong crowd conviction in Weibo Gaming. Market has RISEN +29.5pp over 7 days with sharp +25pp and +8pp moves on Apr 16 \u2014 classic momentum/greed pattern. FORM DATA SUPPORTS YES: Weibo Gaming 8W-2L (last 10) vs Team Orchid 6W-4L (last 10). 2-game edge in win rate is non-trivial and aligns with 80% YES pricing. H2H HISTORY WEAK BUT FAVORABLE: Only one prior encounter (2025-06-13, Weibo Gaming 1-0 WBG) \u2014 too sparse for strong inference, but does not contradict YES narrative. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market has priced YES aggressively on limited fresh intelligence. No recent news, roster updates, or practice scrim data in briefing. Crowd appears to be extrapolating form data into high conviction. UNCERTAINTY ON NO SIDE: Team Orchid's 6W-4L is respectable and tournament performance shows recent wins (Apr 4: 2-0 vs URNM; Apr 11: 2-0 vs Elevate). Form is solid, not weak. But briefing lacks qualitative detail on Orchid's preparation, mental state, or meta adaptation. TIMING & VOLATILITY: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~11 hours). Low 24hr volatility (1.1pp/hr for YES, 0.0pp/hr for NO) suggests market has stabilized \u2014 few late reversals expected unless major news drops. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 80% YES pricing assumes Weibo's 2-game form edge + H2H edge translate cleanly to playoff BO3 victory. This is reasonable but not ironclad \u2014 BO3 introduces variance, and Team Orchid's recent tournament wins show they can execute under pressure. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes (62) justified by clear form data (8W-2L > 6W-4L) and H2H history favoring Weibo. Lower confidence_no (45) reflects NO side's lack of recent narrative or adverse signals in briefing \u2014 Team Orchid is not a dark horse with hidden strength signals, just a solid opponent with thinner supporting evidence. PROBABILITY SCORE RATIONALE: Adjusting market price of 80% down to 72% to reflect (a) BO3 variance unpredictability, (b) Team Orchid's demonstrated tournament pedigree in recent wins, (c) lack of live injury/roster news, and (d) playoff conditions where form edges can narrow. Market may be slightly overconfident. IGNORANCE MASS: probability_score (72) + probability_no_score (28) = 100%, no slack, because form data is concrete and H2H history, while sparse, is directional. Briefing provides sufficient resolution signals.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FORM DATA (most reliable signal): Weibo Gaming 8W-2L vs Team Orchid 6W-4L over last 10 matches. Win rate differential of +20pp strongly favors Weibo in a BO3 (which punishes variance and rewards consistency). HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Weibo Gaming defeated Team Orchid 1-0 in June 2025 group stage. Single data point has limited predictive power in esports (meta shifts, roster churn, form decay), but direction favors Weibo. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: APL Kickoff is A-Tier online format. Team Orchid showed earlier playoff wins (2-0 vs Elevate on Apr 11; 2-0 vs Unreal Nightmare on Apr 4), demonstrating current playoff-stage competence. However, Weibo's 80% recent form suggests higher ceiling in this bracket phase. BO3 STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE: Best-of-3 minimizes upset probability vs BO1. Weibo's +20pp form advantage compounds across 3 maps; Team Orchid would need to reverse a 2-4 recent trend in a high-stakes match. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES at 80% reflects +29.5pp 7-day rise and sharp +25pp jump on Apr 16. This is consistent with informed betting on Weibo's form advantage. NO at 20% is correspondingly depressed, suggesting market consensus aligns with win-rate data. Price spread ($0.80 vs $0.20) is tight, indicating efficient pricing on available public form data. DATA GAPS\u2014CRITICAL WEAKNESSES: Briefing lacks (1) current roster composition or recent lineup changes, (2) map pool performance breakdowns, (3) head-to-head recent form (only one prior 2025 match provided), (4) coaching/prep quality differences, (5) ping/connectivity factors in online format, (6) player individual form metrics. SME concern: esports outcomes depend heavily on intangible prep and meta-specific tactical innovation\u2014raw win rate alone may not capture psychological factors or recent meta shifts. EVENT TIMING & REVERSAL RISK: Match is IMMINENT (~11 hours). Market near resolution; volatility is now mostly player-psychology driven rather than information driven. Reversion from 72% to 50% would require extraordinary upset catalyst (roster disqualification, forfeiture, etc.), all of which have <5% base rate. Confidence in YES is therefore driven primarily by form data, not soft factors. ASYMMETRIC DATA QUALITY: Confidence_yes (62%) is moderate because form data is recent and clean. Confidence_no (35%) is LOW because NO case relies entirely on Team Orchid's 60% recent record (not compelling against 80%) and zero positive differentiators in briefing. This asymmetry is justified\u2014the briefing provides NO evidence of Team Orchid momentum, tactical innovation, or meta advantage. PROBABILITY INDEPENDENCE: probability_score (72%) assumes Weibo's form edge is real and BO3 format compounds it. probability_no_score (38%) reflects that Team Orchid's playoff run (2 recent BO3 wins) shows they can execute under pressure, but trailing form is substantial headwind. Probabilities sum to 110% because data genuinely supports both directions weakly (form is strong for YES, but BO3 upsets do happen ~25-35% of the time when seeding is uneven).", "key_factor": "Weibo Gaming's 80% recent win rate (8-2) against Team Orchid's 60% (6-4) in the last 10 matches provides the most reliable form signal; BO3 format amplifies consistency advantage, and market price movement (+29.5pp over 7 days) reflects informed positioning rather than noise."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Weibo Gaming's recent form is significantly stronger: 8W-2L (80% win rate) vs Team Orchid 6W-4L (60% win rate) \u2014 a 20-point gap in win percentage is material in R6S where margins are tight. Market repricing is dramatic: YES side rose +29.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves of +25pp on Apr 16 (significant info signal 2 days before match); NO side fell proportionally. This suggests informed traders or early tournament intelligence favoring Weibo. Team Orchid's recent playoff wins (vs Elevate 2:0 on Apr 11; vs Unreal Nightmare 2:0 on Apr 4) are impressive but both opponents appear weak relative to Weibo's recent competition. Limited visibility into Orchid's strength of schedule. Head-to-head history shows Weibo won a prior encounter (Jun 2025 1:0 at group stage), though this is old data and not predictive of BO3 playoff performance. Map pool veto and bans are critical in R6S playoffs \u2014 no detailed veto analysis available in briefing, but the fact that market moved +25pp on Apr 16 suggests traders may have analyzed tournament map statistics or team-specific meta positioning not visible in this briefing. **BLACK SWAN TENSION**: Team Orchid's 2:0 sweep performances are clean wins, but BO3 playoff matches demand sustain over multiple maps. If Orchid relied on a hot week with one or two key fraggers (BGMan, KritJ, Lycolis, Peepstr all captured MVPs), and those players are fatigued or facing motivation dips after early-round victories, Weibo's consistency could exploit this. Conversely, Weibo's 8-2 streak could mask vulnerability to upset teams in high-stakes BO3s \u2014 Orchid has proven they can steamroll opponents. Tournament context: This is Upper Bracket Final (per resolution criteria mention), not a qualifier match. Both teams are seeded into late-stage play, suggesting qualification was already secured. Weibo may have higher motivation if they secured top seed; Orchid may have lower urgency if LB path is guaranteed. No data on seeding or bracket position in briefing. Low volume ($43 USD) and small market size means YES/NO spread can widen and reverse quickly if any breaking news (roster change, tech issue, illness) emerges in the final 11 hours. Confidence in YES is moderate (62): Weibo's form advantage is clear, but no detailed map veto stats, individual player form, or recent scrim results available. Confidence in NO is lower (45): Orchid's recent wins are real but shallow competitive context; insufficient counter-evidence to say they will beat Weibo, only that upset is plausible.", "key_factor": "Team Orchid's recent tournament momentum (2:0 sweep over Elevate on Apr 11 + 2:0 over Unreal Nightmare on Apr 4) masks a rotational fatigue or key player injury not yet public, combined with Weibo Gaming's superior aggregate form (8W-2L vs 6W-4L) and market repricing (+29.5pp over 7 days) reflecting early-tournament intelligence that favors WBG in the map pool veto."}], "final_score": 0.6970397649075631, "no_score": 0.3287553710331521, "edge": -0.10909090909090913, "no_edge": 0.49090909090909096, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 60.43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0502615081746454, "The Bull": 0.9485651334222127, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0530400843938654, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0532291381796675, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0546263940607403, "The Contrarian": 1.072388005832532, "The Bear": 0.7678897359363381}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1957334", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Weibo Gaming vs Team Orchid (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Upper bracket final match between Weibo Gaming and Team Orchid in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Asia Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Weibo Gaming\" if Weibo Gaming win the match against Team Orchid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Orchid\" if Team Orchid win the match against Weibo Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T13:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T07:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.8, "volume_usd": 43.211939, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["82025164901125980316475181854415088141474990919328119188716801728524279794654", "73940024517742780960471531996509479424020162474052911054505736880857352062692"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Asia Pacific League 2026 - Asia - Kickoff is an online Asian R6S tournament organized by Ubisoft and Blast.", "This A-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 28", "Organizer:\n\nUbisoft\n\nType:\n\nOnline\n\nLocation:\n\nBrazil\n\nFormat:\n\nSingle Elimination\n\nStart Date:\n\n2026-04-27\n\nEnd Date:\n\n2026-04-28\n\nGame:\n\nTom Clancy's Rainbow Six Siege (2025