{"run_id": "88baf4ff-121b-4df5-83a7-1a03cc86a107", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T21:10:20.129479+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935655", "question": "LoL: Invictus Gaming vs Bilibili Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Invictus Gaming and Bilibili Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Bilibili Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bilibili Gaming\" if Bilibili Gaming win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.185, "volume_usd": 8048.358879, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["64997586209638633471058518296451792615799407800586322260883870637771360550990", "82040398232259695541406017832093103746317694999608220126854410413797515080908"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.82, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Invictus Gaming must win the BO3 match against Bilibili Gaming on 2026-04-18 to resolve YES. EVENT TIMING: Match is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-18 09:00 UTC (~12 hours from briefing timestamp 2026-04-17 21:10 UTC). Event has NOT occurred; prior match results are context only, not proof of this market's resolution. TEMPORAL COHERENCE CHECK: Briefing contains past-tense language ('won 3 of last 4', 'Aug 28 2025 victory') describing PRIOR encounters, not this match. PandaScore confirms match is SCHEDULED. No contradiction between timing and news; prior H2H data used appropriately as form context. BILIBILI GAMING FORM (STRONG): 60% win rate (15-10) in Split 1 with playoffs appearance. Mid-laner Knight (70.7% KDA), jungler XUN (69.7% KDA), bot-laner Viper (8.4 KDA in playoffs). Recent H2H dominance: 3-of-4 wins including two 2-0 sweeps (Jan 31, Jan 20, 2026). INVICTUS GAMING FORM (WEAK): 28% win rate (7-18) in Split 1, ranked near bottom of 14-team standings (second-to-last per standings table). Significant systemic issues indicated by 6W-4L recent 10-match record still underperforming league average. Last 2 H2H losses to BLG were decisive (2-0 sweeps in Jan 2026). HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: Invictus Gaming won 2-of-5 recent encounters (Aug 28 2025 2-0 victory; Aug 18 2025 1-2 victory). However, Bilibili Gaming's last 2 encounters (Jan 2026) both 2-0 sweeps suggest improved dominance or Invictus Gaming regression. Most recent H2H favors BLG strongly. BO3 FORMAT: Reduces variance vs BO1 but allows upset potential. Invictus Gaming would need to win 2-of-3 games; BLG's form advantage makes this less likely even in multi-game format. MARKET PRICING CONSISTENCY: YES at 18% / NO at 82% aligns with Bilibili Gaming's 3-of-4 H2H wins, 60% Split 1 win rate vs Invictus Gaming's 28%, and stronger recent playoffs performance. Pricing reflects fundamentals accurately. UNCERTAINTY FACTORS: (1) Split 1\u2192Split 2 roster/coaching changes could shift Invictus Gaming trajectory, but no evidence of major restructuring in briefing. (2) Early-season volatility in LoL is real, but Invictus Gaming's 7-18 record indicates depth of problems, not noise. (3) Offline tournament format (LPL 2026 Split 2) eliminates ping/environment excuses. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Bilibili Gaming's superior form (60% vs 28% win rate), recent H2H dominance (3-of-4 wins), and stronger individual player metrics (Knight, XUN, Viper all elite) create a 82% expectation for BLG victory. Invictus Gaming's 28% Split 1 win rate and 2-of-5 recent H2H record support 18% upset probability. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=72 (strong H2H and form data support low Invictus Gaming probability, but BO3 and potential roster changes add ~20pp uncertainty). confidence_no=78 (Bilibili Gaming's Split 1 dominance, recent H2H, and individual player strength are well-documented; slightly higher confidence due to data quality on BLG side).", "key_factor": "Market pricing (18% YES) already reflects Bilibili Gaming's dominance; Invictus Gaming's 28% win rate in Split 1 and 3-of-4 H2H losses create high barrier to upset, but BO3 format and potential roster changes introduce non-trivial reversal risk."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.79, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Bilibili Gaming is priced at 82% and merits strong confidence. They posted 60% win rate in Split 1 (15-10 record) vs Invictus Gaming's catastrophic 28% (7-18). Current form shows 8W-2L in last 10 matches (80%) vs IG's 6W-4L (60%). HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: Bilibili Gaming won 3 of last 4 direct matchups (Jan 31 2-0, Jan 20 0-2, Sept 9 1-3), with two consecutive 2-0 sweeps in 2026. IG's only recent H2H wins came Aug 2025 (5-6 months ago), suggesting momentum has shifted decisively. INDIVIDUAL STAR PERFORMANCE: Bilibili's mid-laner Knight shows elite efficiency (70.7% KDA in Split 1, champion mastery across Ryze 80% WR, Orianna 100% WR, Ziggs 100% WR). Jungler XUN maintains 69.7% efficiency with 100% WR on Xin Zhao (6 games). These are playoff-proven players. TEAM STABILITY SIGNAL: Bilibili Gaming reached LPL Split 1 playoffs (Round 2+) and defeated Weibo Gaming 3-0 and Ninjas in Pyjamas 3-0 in early rounds, suggesting organizational competence and roster cohesion. IG's bottom-tier seeding indicates no such stability. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES CASE FRAGILITY): Invictus Gaming's 28% win rate is near-catastrophic\u2014only ThunderTalk (8%, 1-12) and Ultra Prime (23%, 3-10) rank worse in the full league table. A 7-18 record suggests systemic issues: macro play, drafting, or player form deficiencies unlikely resolved in 2-3 weeks between splits. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES FAVORITE: While BO3 reduces variance vs BO1, Bilibili's superior depth and form mean they are even more likely to win 2 games before IG does. IG would need to outperform baseline expectations; BLG only needs to play to form. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: The 82% NO price is rational given available data. YES side has risen only +4.5pp over 7 days despite IG's slight recent uptick (6W-4L), indicating market skepticism about IG's near-term trajectory. Sharp moves (\u00b17.5pp Apr 11-12) reflect uncertainty but have settled near original lows. CONTRARIAN CONCERN (SMALL): IG won 2 of 5 recent H2H encounters (including Aug 2025 2-0), and the briefing notes early-season form volatility in LoL. If IG made roster/coaching changes, Split 2 form could diverge from Split 1. However, no specific evidence of such changes is provided, and the 5-month gap since IG's last H2H win makes this speculative. TEMPORAL RISK MITIGATION: Event is TODAY (12 hours away), eliminating time for major injury/roster news. Market has fully incorporated available information. The 18% YES price already prices in small upset probability; further drops unlikely unless scandal emerges. CONCLUSION FOR BULL (NO ADVOCATE): Bilibili Gaming is the clear favorite\u2014superior form, dominant H2H record, elite individual players, and organizational proof. IG's catastrophic 28% Split 1 record and lack of recent H2H wins make them heavy underdog. NO at 82% is justified; market may even undervalue BLG if IG's systemic issues remain unresolved.", "key_factor": "Bilibili Gaming's dominant recent form (8W-2L last 10 matches, 60% Split 1 win rate) and 3-of-4 head-to-head superiority over a severely underperforming Invictus Gaming (28% Split 1 record, 6W-4L recent form)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CASE FOR YES (INVICTUS UPSET): Invictus Gaming won 2 of the last 5 head-to-head encounters, including a 2-0 sweep on Aug 28, 2025 and a 1-2 victory on Aug 18, 2025. This proves they CAN beat Bilibili Gaming when conditions align. BO3 format reduces variance compared to BO1: even a weak team with a specific read on opponent comp or meta adaptation can steal a series. Invictus has shown matchup-specific wins in recent H2H history. Split 1 records are snapshot metrics, not destiny. The briefing notes 'early-season form volatility is common in LoL'\u2014major roster changes, coaching staff overhauls, or meta shifts between splits can dramatically alter performance. Invictus's 28% record occurred 2-3 weeks ago; current team composition or scrim results are unknown. Invictus Gaming's recent form shows 6W-4L in last 10 matches. This 60% clip in the immediate pre-tournament window contradicts the terrible Split 1 aggregate and suggests genuine improvement trajectory heading into Split 2. The briefing provides NO detailed champion pool, playstyle strengths, or recent scrim data for Invictus Gaming. Absence of negative data is not evidence of weakness\u2014it is a knowledge gap that favors the underdog case. CASE AGAINST YES (BILIBILI DOMINANCE): Bilibili Gaming won 3 of last 4 head-to-head matchups, including two consecutive 2-0 sweeps in Jan 2026 (Jan 31 and Jan 20). This is recent, season-adjacent data showing a clear H2H edge. Bilibili Gaming's mid-laner Knight posts elite 70.7% KDA efficiency and bot-laner Viper shows 8.4 KDA in playoffs with 9-champion pool flexibility. Individual player quality is demonstrably high and recent (Split 1 playoffs data). Bilibili Gaming's 60% win rate (15-10 in Split 1) places them solidly mid-tier in a 14-team league and well ahead of Invictus's 28%. They reached Split 1 playoffs, suggesting organizational stability and proven meta mastery. Invictus Gaming's 28% record (7-18) is catastrophic and sustained across a full split. While BO3 format helps underdogs, a 28% team lacks the baseline competency to consistently draft, execute, and close games. Even with coaching changes, such a deficit is difficult to overcome in 2-3 weeks. Bilibili Gaming's bot laner Viper is KR (Korean import), suggesting elite mechanical talent. The opposing bot lane is listed as KR Viper (same player, different context), indicating no obvious bot-lane disadvantage for Bilibili. Market price of 82% NO reflects informed consensus from high-stakes betting. While markets can be wrong, the 82% pricing also reflects Bilibili's recent dominance (3 of last 4 H2H wins, latest on Jan 31, 2026). HEAD-TO-HEAD CAVEAT: Invictus's two prior wins (Aug 28 and Aug 18, 2025) occurred 7-8 months before this match, during a different season/meta. Bilibili's three wins are more recent (Jan 20, 31, 2026), suggesting they have adapted post-August. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in Bilibili case (72) because briefing provides explicit, recent data: Split 1 60% record, playoffs results, elite player KDA metrics, and three recent H2H wins. Confidence in Invictus case is lower (35) because: (1) no recent player stats provided; (2) 6W-4L recent form is incompletely contextualized (which 10 matches? versus whom?); (3) no championship pool, coach, or draft tendency data. The absence of supporting detail for Invictus is a critical data gap. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Invictus wins if (a) they execute a cheese draft (e.g., unconventional mid/jungle combo) that Bilibili misreads, (b) meta has shifted dramatically post-Split 1 and favors Invictus's roster, or (c) a key Bilibili player (Knight, Viper, or XUN) underperforms due to preparation gap. Briefing provides zero evidence any of these conditions hold. PROBABILITY FLOOR: Even as a bear, Invictus's 28% Split 1 record, Bilibili's 3-of-4 H2H wins, and Bilibili's playoff pedigree justify a LOW probability for YES. 18% market price is not a mispricing; it is rational. I raise it slightly to 22 to credit the 6W-4L recent form and BO3 upset potential, but I do not invert the market.", "key_factor": "Invictus Gaming's 28% Split 1 record may mask mid-season roster/coaching adjustments or meta shifts that could favor their playstyle in a BO3 format where draft flexibility and adaptation compound."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "INVICTUS GAMING SYSTEMIC COLLAPSE: 28% win rate (7-18) in Split 1 is catastrophic by LPL standards. Only ThunderTalk Gaming (8%) and Ultra Prime (23%) ranked worse. This is not noise\u2014such floors indicate roster dysfunction, strategic misalignment, or coaching failure unlikely to reverse in ~2 weeks. BILIBILI GAMING CONSISTENCY: 60% win rate (15-10) places them squarely mid-tier in a 14-team league. Reached Split 1 playoffs. Knight (70.7% KDA efficiency) and XUN (69.7% efficiency) show sustained individual excellence. Viper's diverse ADC pool (9 champs) indicates flexible draft strength. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: BLG won 3 of last 4 encounters (Jan 31 2-0, Jan 20 2-0, Sept 9 1-3). The two IG wins cited (Aug 28 2-0, Aug 18 1-2) are from 6+ months prior and predate IG's catastrophic form collapse. Recency strongly favors BLG. BO3 FORMAT REDUCES UPSET LIKELIHOOD: While BO3 has higher variance than BO1, a 28%-win-rate team would need to win 2 of 3 games against a mid-tier opponent. Requires sustained excellence IG has not demonstrated. BO3 favors the stronger team when form gap is this wide. SPLIT 1 TRAJECTORY: BLG's playoff run (beat NIP 3-0, WBG 3-0, took JDG to 5 games in finals) proves tournament readiness and coaching adaptability. IG's early-season struggles with no visible wins in recent playoff data suggest structural issues. MARKET PRICING (18% YES / 82% NO): Price heavily favors BLG. This reflects informed consensus from LPL observers. Not mispriced\u2014aligns with underlying form differential and H2H history. BASE RATE CAUTION: Esports form swings can occur (coaching changes, roster swaps, meta shifts), but evidence within the 2-week window is minimal. Without explicit roster/coaching announcements, 28% \u2192 competitive implies unrealistic 200%+ form improvement. NO-SIDE RISK: If IG made unreported roster changes or IG players have personal motivation (revenge narrative), upset becomes plausible. Confidence_no capped at 65 due to this residual structural uncertainty in esports (lack of full roster/coaching transparency in briefing).", "key_factor": "LPL BO3 matchups between teams with 28% vs 60% win-rate splits historically favor the higher-ranked team ~75-80% of the time; head-to-head recency (3 of last 4 to BLG) reinforces this tilting further toward NO."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.74, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES at 18% \u2192 NO at 82% reflects a heavily one-sided consensus favoring Bilibili Gaming. The 7-day price history shows YES rising +4.5pp (suggesting gradual accumulation of confidence in the underdog), but remains deeply underwater. FORM DISPARITY OVERWHELMING: Bilibili Gaming posted 60% win rate (15-10) in Split 1 vs Invictus Gaming's catastrophic 28% (7-18). This is not marginal \u2014 IG ranked 11th of 14 teams; BLG ranked 4th. Current market price (82% for NO) accurately reflects this structural form gap. HEAD-TO-HEAD ASYMMETRY: BLG won 3 of last 4 H2H matches with two recent 2-0 sweeps (Jan 31, Jan 20, 2026). IG's two H2H wins occurred in Aug 2025 (6+ months ago) and are now stale data. Recency and consistency favor BLG decisively. KEY PLAYER PERFORMANCE: BLG's Knight (mid, 70.7% KDA) and XUN (jungle, 69.7% KDA) demonstrated elite efficiency in Split 1. Viper (ADC, 8.4 KDA in playoffs) showed high-level execution under pressure. No comparable elite performance signals from IG players in briefing. PLAYOFF PROGRESSION: BLG reached Split 1 playoffs and demonstrated deep tournament runs (beat WBG 3-0 in Round 2, reached Finals vs JDG). This suggests organizational stability, coaching competence, and mental resilience \u2014 all absent from IG's narrative. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market is NOT irrationally exuberant \u2014 it is rationally pessimistic on IG. The 82% NO price is justified by hard metrics (28% vs 60% win rate, H2H 1-3 recent, playoffs vs non-playoffs). No ignored signal suggests BLG is mispriced downward. UPSET POTENTIAL ACKNOWLEDGED BUT CONSTRAINED: IG could theoretically benefit from mid-split roster/coaching adjustments or meta shifts favoring their champion pool. However, briefing provides ZERO evidence of such changes. Early-season volatility caveat in CASE FOR NO is logical but unsupported by data. LIVE TIMING MATTERS: Event is TODAY (start ~12 hours). Sharp moves Apr 11-12 show brief volatility but no sustained trend away from 82% NO. At this proximity, reversals require concrete evidence (injury, roster news, draft intel) \u2014 none present in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO side (82%) due to multiple converging signals (form, H2H, playoffs, player metrics). Confidence in YES (74%) is moderate because unpredictable in-game variance and potential undocumented roster/coaching changes retain non-zero explanatory power for an 28%-ranked team. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 22% YES (78% NO) reflects (i) BLG's 60% vs IG's 28% form gap (4:1 ratio), (ii) H2H 3-1 recent + deeper playoff pedigree, (iii) elite player execution. The 18% market price is nearly rational; 22% adds modest variance buffer for BO3 format and potential unlisted roster adjustments.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "Split 1 win rate disparity is extreme and persistent: Invictus Gaming 28% (7-18) vs. Bilibili Gaming 60% (15-10), indicating structural team problems (drafting, macro play, laning fundamentals) unlikely to reverse in ~2 weeks without major intervention. Head-to-head recent record heavily favors BLG: 3-of-last-4 victories including consecutive 2-0 sweeps (Jan 31, Jan 20, 2026). Invictus's two wins are from Aug 2025 (5+ months prior), suggesting outdated form data. Individual player efficiency metrics show BLG mid-laner Knight (70.7% KDA efficiency, 5.8 avg KDA) and jungler XUN (69.7% KDA efficiency, 3.7-5.8 KDA range) operating at elite tier; Invictus Gaming roster performance data shows no comparable standout performers. BO3 format reduces upset potential relative to BO1 but does not eliminate it; however, a team posting 28% win rate rarely wins BO3 series against a 60% win-rate opponent absent substitution/coaching mid-series. Timeline context: LPL 2026 Split 2 began Apr 4; this match is April 18 (14 days in). Insufficient time for Invictus Gaming to systematically address Split 1 infrastructure issues (drafting, vision control, objective prioritization) that produced historical 167-point gold differential deficit and -334 gold differential for worst team (ThunderTalk) vs. Invictus's -167 (indicating weak objective macro). Market price (18% YES / 82% NO) reflects professional market consensus; sharp moves on Apr 11-12 (\u00b17-7.5pp swings) suggest institutional confidence in BLG, not significant new information contradicting form-based priors. Confidence_yes is moderate (72) because: Split 1 data is solid, H2H is clear, but (a) roster changes during pre-Split 2 break are possible but undocumented, (b) LoL meta patches between splits can create opportunities for underperforming teams if they drafted early for new meta. Confidence_no is high (78) because: Bilibili Gaming's recent form, playoff qualification, and individual player metrics are well-documented and recent (within weeks). However, not 95+ because LoL esports has shown upset potential in BO3 series when meta shifts occur or coaching adjustments are made mid-season.", "key_factor": "Invictus Gaming's 28% Split 1 win rate (7-18) combined with Bilibili Gaming's 8W-2L recent form and 3-of-4 H2H victories strongly indicate systemic performance gap; BO3 format reduces upset variance but cannot overcome a ~60pp difference in contemporary win rates absent roster overhaul."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.16, "probability_yes": 0.16, "probability_no": 0.82, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "BLG is overwhelming favorite at 82% NO price: 60% W-L in Split 1, 15-10 record, reached playoffs, strong individual performers (Knight 70.7% KDA, XUN 69.7%, Viper 8.4 KDA in playoffs). IG is in deep crisis: 28% W-L in Split 1 (7-18), near-bottom standings (-167 GDM), suggests systemic collapse not just variance. H2H context shows BLG dominance in recent matches: 3-1 in last 4 (Jan 31 2-0, Jan 20 2-0, Sep 9 1-3 loss). IG's wins are older (Aug 28, Aug 18 2025). BLACK SWAN: IG's catastrophic Split 1 performance may have triggered emergency roster changes, coaching staff overhaul, or meta-counter preparation not yet visible in public stats. LoL meta shifts rapidly; a patch or play-style innovation could neutralize BLG's strength. Absence of signal: Briefing contains NO information about IG's current coaching staff, recent roster moves, or evidence of internal restructuring post-crisis. This silence is suspicious for a team with 28% win rate \u2014 typically orgs in freefall make changes. BO3 format amplifies upset risk: While BLG is strong, BO3s allow one team to steal a game-set if they identify a patch exploit or psychological edge. IG losing 7-18 in group play but having 2 recent H2H wins (albeit in 2025) suggests *matchup-specific* vulnerability in BLG, not universal dominance. Form trajectory opacity: IG's 6W-4L in last 10 is much better than 7-18 overall, indicating possible late-season recovery or recency bias in the data snapshot. Exact timing of last 10 games unknown \u2014 if these came late in Split 1 or early in Split 2 prep, IG may be trending upward. Playoff pressure asymmetry: BLG reached Split 1 playoffs (mid-tier seeding at 60%), which is NOT a deep run \u2014 suggests they are vulnerable to teams that study and counter their playoff-tested champions (Knight on Ryze/Orianna, XUN on Pantheon/Wukong). IG may have built comps to exploit these patterns. Meta timing: Briefing dated Apr 17, event Apr 18 \u2014 match is IMMINENT. Patch notes, recent champion buffs/nerfs, or stealth role-swap announcements in the last 24h could flip the script. Market price history shows sharp swings (\u00b17.5pp on Apr 11-12), hinting at new information ingestion. Confidence asymmetry justified: HIGH confidence in NO (78) because BLG's Split 1 dominance and H2H record are recent, concrete, and hard to overturn in ~12 hours. LOW confidence in YES (35) because IG's pathway to victory requires unobserved roster/coaching changes that briefing does not document. The black swan is plausible but data-lean.", "key_factor": "Invictus Gaming deploys a surprise meta-counter roster swap or coaching adjustment mid-tournament that specifically targets Bilibili Gaming's playoff-proven but potentially predictable playstyle, exploiting macro weaknesses not visible in regular-season aggregate stats."}], "final_score": 0.20359067648028265, "no_score": 0.8011777373415617, "edge": 0.5059090909090909, "no_edge": -0.12409090909090903, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.22699386503067492, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.44307944307944325, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.22153972153972162, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0481495936714533, "The Bull": 0.9617091423379212, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0505242668684711, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0511777511792142, "The Domain Specialist": 1.052379936971564, "The Contrarian": 1.0671821968585695, "The Bear": 0.768877112112807}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935655", "question": "LoL: Invictus Gaming vs Bilibili Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Invictus Gaming and Bilibili Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Bilibili Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bilibili Gaming\" if Bilibili Gaming win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T15:00:00Z", "event_start_t