{"run_id": "905a47cb-2ee9-445c-9d04-7315759d2c35", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T21:14:33.158551+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1964376", "question": "LoL: CTBC Flying Oyster vs Deep Cross Gaming (BO3) - LCP Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between CTBC Flying Oyster and Deep Cross Gaming in the LCP Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CTBC Flying Oyster\" if CTBC Flying Oyster win the match against Deep Cross Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Deep Cross Gaming\" if Deep Cross Gaming win the match against CTBC Flying Oyster.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.395, "volume_usd": 331.589407, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["64934566687536300892969617135181715876394728120615636546616880734140378797392", "616791263582492719846285664936551487956974754785403739018620672880681327237"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is scheduled for 2026-04-18 09:00 UTC with briefing timestamp 2026-04-17 21:14 UTC (~12 hours remaining). Event has NOT started; all prior match references are historical context only, not proof of this market's resolution. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Market resolves YES if CTBC Flying Oyster wins the BO3 match; NO if Deep Cross Gaming wins. No ambiguity in team identification or resolution mechanism. Forfeit/cancellation scenarios resolve 50-50, but no current signals of such disruption. RECENT FORM ADVANTAGE: Deep Cross Gaming holds superior recent form (6W-4L last 10 matches) vs CTBC Flying Oyster (4W-6L last 10 matches). This is a 2-win gap favoring the NO side. MOST RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Deep Cross Gaming won 2-1 on 2026-01-31 (less than 3 months ago in 2026), demonstrating current-era advantage. This is the most recent direct encounter and carries highest recency weight. HISTORICAL HEAD-TO-HEAD (3+ months old): CTBC Flying Oyster won 3 of 6 historical encounters (2024-08-21, 2024-07-27, 2024-06-08, 2023-08-19), but these are from 2023-2024 and do not reflect current roster/meta strength relative to the Jan 2026 rematch. MARKET PRICE COHERENCE: YES trading at 40%, NO at 60% reflects market consensus slightly favoring Deep Cross Gaming. This aligns with recent form and recency bias toward the 2026-01-31 win. 7-day trend shows YES falling 10.5pp (market conviction shifting toward NO) following Apr 13 sharp move. CONFIDENCE DISTRIBUTION: confidence_yes = 72 (recent form data is clear; head-to-head history is concrete), confidence_no = 75 (slightly higher due to stronger recent performance and most recent matchup win). Both scores reflect high data quality for a scheduled esports match but acknowledge that live match outcomes have inherent variance; no single stat guarantees victory. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: probability_score = 42 reflects that Deep Cross Gaming's recent form edge (6-4 vs 4-6), most recent head-to-head win (2-1 Jan 2026), and market pricing (60%) favor NO, but CTBC's historical 3-of-6 head-to-head record (older data) prevents assigning <35 to YES. probability_no_score = 58 reflects the NO-side evidence is moderately strong but not overwhelming\u2014BO3 format introduces variance, and CTBC has demonstrated historical competitiveness. NO TEMPORAL INCOHERENCE DETECTED: Disambiguation warning noted past-tense language in side_no_case but this is correctly identified as historical context (2024-07-20, 2026-01-31 prior matches). No contradiction between briefing's 'SCHEDULED' status and historical references. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Low. Official source (gol.gg) with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting is standard. No forfeit/cancellation signals present. This is a secondary consideration and does not materially adjust probability_score.", "key_factor": "Event has not yet started (scheduled ~12 hours from briefing timestamp); outcome depends entirely on live match performance with no predictive advantage beyond recent form and head-to-head history."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO = Deep Cross Gaming): Deep Cross Gaming enters with 6W-4L recent form vs CTBC's 4W-6L \u2014 a decisive 2-win gap that reflects current competitive standing. MARKET MOMENTUM CONFIRMS UNDERVALUATION OF NO: The 7-day price movement shows NO rising +10.5pp while YES fell -10.5pp, indicating informed backing of Deep Cross. The sharp +10.5pp move on Apr 13 (likely driven by recent news/matches) suggests market participants with direct LCP information favor Deep Cross. MOST RECENT H2H DECISIVE: Deep Cross Gaming defeated CTBC 2-1 on 2026-01-31 in Regular Season. This 2.5-month proximity is fresher than the 2024-era data favoring CTBC. Recent matchups are higher signal than stale historical records. HISTORICAL H2H CONTEXT (UNDERDOG WEAKNESS): While CTBC won 3 of ~7 prior encounters, those wins span 2023\u20132024. The most recent TWO encounters (2026-01-31 and 2024-07-20) favor Deep Cross Gaming, suggesting trend reversal or meta shift. VOLATILITY & SPREAD ANALYSIS: 24-hour volatility is minimal (0.6\u20130.7pp/hr), indicating market consensus around NO. Low volume ($332 USD) means the 60/40 split reflects genuine expectation rather than whale positioning. Consensus stability favors the priced-in favorite. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT & STAKES: Both teams compete in LCP Split 2 for championship points and MSI qualification. Deep Cross Gaming's stronger recent record suggests better preparation and team cohesion entering this critical phase. CTBC'S WEAKNESS: 4W-6L recent form indicates structural underperformance. In BO3 format, weaker teams rarely overcome a 2-win form deficit against a hot opponent in tournament play. NO ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION DETECTED: The briefing contains no injury reports, roster changes, or meta revelations favoring CTBC. The market's 60/40 split appears well-calibrated to available information. TEMPORAL URGENCY (MINOR FACTOR): Event starts in ~12 hours. Large reversals are unlikely without breaking news. Probability of late-stage catalyst favoring CTBC is low. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO case (72%) due to recent form, H2H recency, and market consensus. Confidence in YES (55%) reflects historical head-to-head wins and CTBC's historical competitiveness, but these are weaker signals than current form and recent outcomes.", "key_factor": "Deep Cross Gaming's superior recent form (6W-4L vs 4W-6L) combined with momentum shift evidenced by 7-day market movement (+10.5pp in favor of NO) and most recent H2H win on 2026-01-31."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.48, "probability_yes": 0.48, "probability_no": 0.56, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is priced at 40% (underdog), NO at 60% (favorite). Event is TODAY, scheduled 2026-04-18 09:00 UTC (~12 hours away). Time-to-reversal is minimal; sharp moves occurred Apr 13 with -11.0pp drop for YES and +10.5pp rise for NO, suggesting recent sentiment shift toward NO. DEEP CROSS GAMING (FAVORITE) STRENGTHS: Recent regular-season form 6W-4L (60% win rate) vs CTBC's 4W-6L (40% win rate) over last 10 matches\u2014substantial gap favoring NO. Most recent head-to-head on 2026-01-31 shows Deep Cross won 2-1 in a similar regular-season BO3 format, providing direct evidence of recent performance advantage. CTBC FLYING OYSTER (UNDERDOG) CASE: Historical H2H record 3-5 in wins (40% H2H win rate), but unpacking the data reveals important nuance: CTBC won three of five prior encounters at varying tournament levels and score formats (0-3 playoff win in 2024-08-21, 1-2 contender win in 2024-07-27, 0-2 regular-season win in 2024-06-08). This suggests CTBC can win despite unconventional scorelines, indicating potential variance or resilience in tight matches. FORMAT AND CONTEXT FACTOR: The 2026-01-31 match (Deep Cross 2-1) occurred ~2.5 months ago. Current standings show both teams are competing in LCP Split 2 (2026-04-04 onward) with fresh championship points and MSI qualification implications. Roster changes, meta shifts, or preparation intensity over two+ months can materially alter matchup dynamics; the briefing provides no information about roster stability or meta evolution. MISSING DATA GAPS\u2014CRITICAL ASYMMETRY: (1) No individual player or draft/meta analysis provided. (2) No recent scrim results, coaching changes, or internal team form signals beyond the aggregate 10-match win/loss records. (3) No context on whether either team's recent losses were close or blowouts, or whether CTBC's 4W-6L trend shows improvement or decline. (4) No injury/availability reports. These gaps disproportionately weaken confidence in YES because the underdog case relies heavily on overlooked factors that are simply absent from the briefing. MARKET PRICE HISTORY: YES fell 10.5pp over 7 days (from ~50% to 40%), with a sharp -11.0pp move on Apr 13. This suggests coordinated or informed betting into NO side, raising question of whether smart money detected edge\u2014but it could also reflect public perception of recent form without sophisticated analysis. The 24-hour stability (+0.0pp YES, +0.5pp NO) shows no new information overnight. VOLATILITY AND LIQUIDITY: Market volume is low ($332 USD). With minimal liquidity, the price may not reflect true consensus; a small informed bet can move prices. However, the 7-day downtrend for YES is substantial enough to suggest more than noise. UPSET SCENARIO: CTBC could win if (a) they have improved roster coordination or meta-specific preparation over the past 2.5 months since the last matchup; (b) Deep Cross Gaming is complacent or facing internal issues (no evidence provided); (c) the BO3 format favors CTBC's strategic flexibility or individual player matchups (no data provided). None of these are explicitly supported by the briefing. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Deep Cross Gaming's recent form (6W-4L) and most recent H2H victory (2-1 on 2026-01-31) provide concrete, recent evidence for NO. CTBC's underperformance (4W-6L) and loss in the most recent matchup are unfavorable. However, the historical H2H shows CTBC can win, and the absence of granular tactical/player data prevents high confidence in either direction. The 7-day price drop suggests market is pricing in Deep Cross advantage, but with low volume and imminent match start, reversal is unlikely without surprise roster announcement or withdrawal. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 32 (weak underlying data for CTBC; recent form and H2H defeat are material headwinds; no positive signals provided). confidence_no = 38 (better data for Deep Cross, but low liquidity, long time gap since last H2H, and lack of meta/tactical granularity prevent high confidence). Both sides have asymmetric evidence quality; set both low to reflect true uncertainty about factors the briefing does not address.", "key_factor": "CTBC Flying Oyster's 3-5 historical head-to-head record against Deep Cross Gaming masks volatile match outcomes and format-dependent performance that could favor the underdog in a BO3 regular-season context."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "RECENT FORM (STRONGEST SIGNAL): Deep Cross Gaming shows superior current trajectory with 6W-4L last 10 matches vs CTBC Flying Oyster's 4W-6L \u2014 a 2-win differential supporting the NO side. MOST RECENT H2H (2026-01-31): Deep Cross Gaming won 2-1 in their most recent direct matchup, demonstrating form advantage within the same 2026 season. HISTORICAL H2H (2023-2024): CTBC won 4 of 8 prior encounters (50%), but Deep Cross won the 2 most recent pre-2026 matches (2024-07-20 2-0, 2024-08-21 context). Head-to-head does not strongly favor either team historically. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Current market at 40% YES / 60% NO reflects the form differential and recent Deep Cross advantage. Price has declined -10.5pp over 7 days, consistent with market recognition of Deep Cross superiority. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 reduces variance vs single game; favors the team with stronger current form (Deep Cross). TOURNAMENT CONTEXT (MSI QUALIFICATION): Both teams are MSI qualification contenders in LCP Split 2 (2026-04-04 to 2026-06-07), but this is early regular season (18 April), so individual matches carry moderate stakes. No evidence of systematic upset risk. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Form data is clear and recent (confidence_no = 68). Head-to-head history is mixed but trending toward Deep Cross (confidence_yes = 62). Neither side has a dominant structural edge, leaving ~24pp of probability mass to match-day variance and unmeasured factors (draft, meta shifts, player performance). TIME-TO-EVENT: Match starts in ~12 hours (TODAY). No major news or roster changes flagged in briefing; market should reflect stable competitive expectations rather than headline reversals.", "key_factor": "BO3 League of Legends matches: ~50% win rate for either competitor in regular season play; head-to-head records suggest slight edge to Deep Cross Gaming in recent form (1-0 in 2026 direct match, 4W-6L vs 6W-4L in last 10)"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "Current market price (YES=40%, NO=60%) reflects fundamental form differential: Deep Cross Gaming is 6W-4L (60%) vs CTBC Flying Oyster's 4W-6L (40%) \u2014 nearly identical to market odds. Most recent head-to-head (2026-01-31) heavily favors NO side: Deep Cross Gaming won 2-1, demonstrating recent direct advantage. H2H history mixed but slightly favors YES side in raw wins (3 of 6 recorded wins for CTBC), but Deep Cross Gaming's two most recent encounters (2026-01-31 and 2024-07-20) both went to NO. 7-day market movement shows strong drift AWAY from YES (-10.5pp) and TOWARD NO (+10.5pp), indicating crowd reassessment toward NO's form advantage. Sharp move on Apr 13 (YES down -11.0pp, NO up +10.5pp) aligns with season form data becoming more salient \u2014 not a panic spike but rational reweighting. NO side confidence elevated: recent form (6-4), recent head-to-head win (2-1), and market consensus all converge. YES side confidence moderate: weaker current form (4-6), but historical H2H parity and BO3 format (more variance than BO1) leaves upside. No emotional exuberance on either side \u2014 current 40/60 split closely mirrors form records and recent direct result. Market exhibits RATIONAL pricing: the price fairly reflects the information in the briefing. Crowd is not overreacting. Event is TODAY with ~12 hours to start \u2014 any reversal requires significant last-minute news (injury, roster change, etc.) not present in briefing.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "FORM ANALYSIS: Deep Cross Gaming objectively superior in recent 10-match sample (6-4 record) vs CTBC Flying Oyster (4-6 record). In esports, recent form is highly predictive of immediate match outcomes due to meta shifts, roster confidence, and scrim quality. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY: Most recent direct matchup (2026-01-31) favored DCG with 2-1 victory. This is 2.5 months prior to scheduled match, within same competitive season (LCP Split 2 started 2026-04-04). Meta evolution in LoL over 2.5 months is significant but not determinative. HISTORICAL H2H PATTERN: CTBC holds 5 wins to DCG's 3 across 8 prior encounters (2023-2024), but this historical aggregate is heavily backweighted. Three of CTBC's wins occurred in 2023-2024 playoffs/contender groups. DCG's most recent wins (2026-01-31 regular season, 2024-07-20) are more temporally proximate and format-stable (both regular season or equivalent). MARKET PRICE DYNAMICS: YES side has fallen 10.5pp over 7 days (from ~51% to 41%) with sharp -11pp move on Apr 13 14:00 UTC. This suggests informed traders (possibly regional knowledge of team roster changes, scrim results, or injury reports) are shifting probability toward NO. Such consistent directional decay in final 4 days pre-event is meaningful signal in illiquid market ($332 USD volume). BO3 FORMAT CONSIDERATION: BO3 favors consistency and team preparation over single-match variance. DCG's form advantage compounds across three games; one upset win is less likely than in BO1 format. ESPORTS-SPECIFIC FACTOR: LCP is tier-2 regional league (below LEC/LCS). Roster stability, coaching consistency, and practice infrastructure differences between DCG and CTBC are opaque to briefing but may underlie the 10.5pp market repricing. RISK TO NO CASE: CTBC's historical 5-3 H2H record could reflect team identity or playstyle matchup advantages not captured by recent form. BO3 allows mid-series adaptations that could favor CTBC's experience. However, current form overwhelms historical aggregate. TEMPORAL PROXIMITY: Event is ~12 hours away (TODAY category). Prediction market has incorporated all publicly available information. Sharp -11pp move on Apr 13 suggests late-breaking information (roster, injury, or scrim intel) unlikely to reverse without new catalyst.", "key_factor": "Recent form differential (DCG 6W-4L vs CTBC 4W-6L over last 10 matches) combined with DCG's most recent H2H victory (2026-01-31, 2-1) strongly favors the underdog on current market pricing, which has been falling 10.5pp over 7 days despite fundamentals."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has fallen 10.5pp over 7 days (41% \u2192 31% consensus), with a sharp -11pp move on Apr 13. This suggests informed betting flow toward NO, but BO3 matches have high variance and preparation-driven outcomes\u2014a -10pp move may overcorrect if it's based purely on recent form and ignores tactical/roster factors. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Deep Cross Gaming is 6W-4L vs CTBC's 4W-6L (last 10), but the briefing provides NO granularity on momentum direction. If CTBC went 3W-1L in their last 4 (e.g., after Apr 13 data cutoff) while DCG stalled, the market has zero visibility. Absence of recent match dates is a data gap. HEAD-TO-HEAD NOISE: CTBC leads historical H2H 5W-3L (2023\u20132024 records show CTBC 3-0, 1-2, 0-2 wins vs DCG 2-0, 0-1 wins). DCG's most recent win was 2026-01-31 (2-1), but that's 2.5 months old\u2014ancient in competitive LoL where meta patches, roster changes, and scrim performance reshape matchups entirely. The briefing is silent on roster changes or patch notes between Jan 31 and Apr 18. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: BO3 rewards preparation, read-gaming, and best-of-series resilience over single-game form. CTBC's weaker 4W-6L record may reflect inconsistency across different opponents, but if their coaching staff has identified DCG's draft tendencies and CTBC's team cohesion has improved post-roster moves (NOT mentioned but plausible in a 2.5-month gap), a 2-1 upset becomes viable. MOTIVATION & CONTEXT: Both teams are vying for MSI qualification (championship points matter). If CTBC is in a must-win situation (e.g., 7th-8th place after 3 rounds) while DCG is comfortable (3rd-4th), psychological pressure and tactical desperation can flip close BO3s. Briefing provides no tournament standings or playoff seeding context\u2014another data gap favoring upsets. MARKET MISPRICING ON CONSENSUS: The 40% YES price reflects a straightforward 'better recent form \u2192 favored team' heuristic. But Polymarket prices in BO3 esports often underweight preparation and roster-level variance. If CTBC has made a mid-split acquisition or coaching adjustment (common in LCP during regular season), the market will not have repriced until matches resume. ABSENCE OF SCRIM/META SIGNAL: The briefing contains zero information on scrim results, patch notes, or meta shifts since Jan 2026. Deep Cross Gaming's 6W-4L aggregate could mask a vulnerability to CTBC's champion pool or macro style that has emerged in the last month of practice. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (68%) is driven by recent form + market repricing, but moderate confidence (58%) reflects the 2.5-month data gap and lack of granular match context. High confidence in YES (42%) is tempered by the fact that CTBC's 4W-6L record is real and recent; however, it is NOT bottoming-out (suggesting potential for BO3 upset if preparation or psychological factors align). BLACK SWAN MECHANISM: A single roster change (e.g., CTBC's mid laner swapped in a new player who has scrimmed very well, or a DCG key player benched due to illness/form dip not yet reflected in public records) could flip BO3 coaching decisions and pick/ban phases entirely. 12 hours before match start, such roster updates may not have reached Polymarket price consensus yet.", "key_factor": "CTBC Flying Oyster's roster has stabilized or made a key mid-split substitution that shifts meta matchup advantage, or Deep Cross Gaming's recent form trajectory masks vulnerability to CTBC's specific draft/playstyle in a BO3 format where preparation and read-gaming matter more than raw win-rate."}], "final_score": 0.42505925629275554, "no_score": 0.5866971465115328, "edge": 0.2959090909090909, "no_edge": 0.08590909090909093, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 63.43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0481495936714533, "The Bull": 0.9617091423379212, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0505242668684711, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0511777511792142, "The Domain Specialist": 1.052379936971564, "The Contrarian": 1.0671821968585695, "The Bear": 0.768877112112807}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1964376", "question": "LoL: CTBC Flying Oyster vs Deep Cross Gaming (BO3) - LCP Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between CTBC Flying Oyster and Deep Cross Gaming in the LCP Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CTBC Flying Oyster\" if CTBC Flying Oyster win the match against Deep Cross Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Deep Cross Gaming\" if Deep Cross Gaming win the match against CTBC Flying Oyster.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting difference