rp correction is already baked into prices; further volatility unlikely absent major news (injury, forfeit). Current 80/20 split reflects near-certainty pricing from professional sources. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: This is playoffs (higher-stakes environment). Four Angry Men's larger recent match sample (10 vs 4) may indicate higher playoff pedigree/experience, though this is inferential. DATA GAPS ON BOTH SIDES: Briefing lacks head-to-head record, roster quality comparison, map pool compatibility, coach/captain experience, or regional competitive tier placement. Cannot construct granular case for either team. This favors the market consensus (NO at 80%) as a noise-filtering aggregator. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO case (35) is still LOW absolute value because sharp money signal + market consensus are indirect evidence. Confidence in YES case even lower (28) because One Coin's underperformance and absence of offsetting catalysts make it hard to justify the 20% underdog pricing. Leaving 44pp of ignorance mass (22+78=100 but confidence_yes=28, confidence_no=35) reflects genuine uncertainty on both sides due to missing roster/tactical data. BULL THESIS: Four Angry Men are the favored side at 80% for a reason \u2014 sharps exited One Coin, market consensus is unified, and One Coin shows no form advantage to justify 20% pricing. The bull case for NO is that this 80/20 split is actually underpricing Four Angry Men's advantage.", "key_factor": "Four Angry Men's stronger recent form (5W-5L vs One Coin's 2W-2L in last 10/4 matches) combined with market consensus pricing NO at 80%, indicating professional bettors and the broader market favor the underdog team."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FORM ASYMMETRY: One Coin is 2W-2L (last 4 matches) vs Four Angry Men's 5W-5L (last 10 matches). While FAM has more recent data, their 50% win rate over 10 matches signals volatility and lack of momentum heading into playoffs. ONE COIN'S STABILITY: One Coin's 50% form over a shorter window (last 4) suggests they may be on an upswing or at least holding competitive parity with a team priced at 80%. PLAYOFF VOLATILITY: Best-of-three formats in esports R6S are notoriously volatile. A 4-game sample (One Coin) in a BO3 playoff can be deceptive; single maps won/lost in group stage differ from playoff pressure. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE SIGNAL: The sharp 32.5pp drop in YES (Apr 17 01:00 UTC) suggests reactive pricing, not necessarily data-driven conviction. With only $5 volume, liquidity is minimal\u2014prices may reflect thin order flows rather than expert consensus. MISSING ROSTER/TACTICAL DATA: Briefing contains no roster changes, player form, or tactical/map matchup analysis for either team. This is a critical gap for R6S, where team composition and map knowledge heavily influence outcomes. FAM FORM RED FLAG: Five wins and five losses over 10 matches is genuinely inconsistent. If this reflects recent playoff-stage play, FAM may lack the stability expected of an 80% favorite. ONE COIN UNDERDOG POSITIONING: At 20%, One Coin is priced as a genuine underdog. If their 2W-2L reflects competitive matches against similar-tier opponents, they may deserve 25\u201335% odds rather than 20%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence on YES is limited (32) because the briefing provides minimal data on One Coin's actual strengths\u2014only a 2W-2L record without match details. Confidence on NO is also modest (45) because FAM's 5W-5L is similarly vague and could indicate either declining form or natural variance. EVENT TIMING\u2014IMMINENT: Match starts in ~12 hours. No late-breaking roster or tactical updates in the briefing. Both teams' odds likely reflect pre-playoff expectations, not real-time form shifts. PLAUSIBLE UPSET CASE: One Coin wins if they execute superior map picks, secure early round wins on their favored maps, and maintain focus under playoff pressure. FAM's 5W-5L suggests they may struggle with consistency in high-stakes BO3s. HONEST IGNORANCE: The briefing lacks the granular data (recent match scores, map records, player performance metrics, head-to-head precedent) needed to distinguish confidently between 20% and 35% for One Coin. Probability_score of 28 reflects modest upside for the underdog, not conviction.", "key_factor": "One Coin's 2W-2L recent form shows competitive viability in a volatile matchup where Four Angry Men's 5W-5L record suggests inconsistency at playoff pressure."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head record, no recent opponent matchups, no roster composition, no map veto strategy, and no individual player performance data available in briefing. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market price (20% YES / 80% NO) is sharp and reflects strong conviction that Four Angry Men is heavily favored. Market moved -30pp on YES side in last 24h, suggesting informed traders backing NO. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: One Coin 2W-2L (50% in last 4 matches) vs Four Angry Men 5W-5L (50% in last 10 matches) \u2014 both teams show coin-flip records. Form data insufficient to differentiate. ESPORTS BASE RATE: In esports playoff BO3 matches with minimal prior data, underdog teams (priced at 20%) historically win 15-30% of the time depending on the meta, patch cycle, and roster strength. No patch notes or roster changes mentioned. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (12 hours to kickoff). Very short window for reversal. Market price likely reflects late-stage betting intelligence from regional R6S analysts or team insiders who have scouted both rosters. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO is low (28) because market consensus and betting action provide directional signal but no causal evidence (roster, recent scrims, map pool, player form). Confidence in YES is very low (22) because the 20% price suggests One Coin is a severe underdog with no supporting data to contradict that market judgment. RESOLUTION RISK: Match begins in ~12 hours. Playoff BO3 format; no forfeit/cancel precedent noted. Market likely to resolve by EOD April 18. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Anchoring to market price (20% YES) as a proxy for informed consensus in a data-sparse esports match. Slight lift to 28% to account for possibility that market overweights Four Angry Men; no data justifies lifting higher. Assign 72% to NO based on market signal and absence of contrary evidence. IGNORANCE MASS: confidence_yes + confidence_no = 50, leaving 50pp ignorance. This reflects the genuine absence of roster, recent scrim, or head-to-head data in the briefing. A rational model should NOT assume equal priors when the market is this lopsided.", "key_factor": "Esports playoff BO3 matches: ~50% win rate for any given team absent head-to-head or roster-specific data; underdog teams (suggested by 20% market price) win ~15-25% of the time in esports upsets; market price of 20% suggests severe underdog status for One Coin."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.2, "probability_yes": 0.2, "probability_no": 0.8, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market price (YES 20% / NO 80%) reflects strong consensus against One Coin, but this consensus is built on near-total information vacuum, not substantive evidence. Briefing contains NO head-to-head record, NO recent form comparison for these specific teams, NO roster data, NO map preferences, NO strategic intel on either team. One Coin's 2W-2L recent form (last 4) is marginally worse than Four Angry Men's 5W-5L (last 10), but sample sizes are tiny and form context is missing \u2014 insufficient to justify 80/20 split. Sharp move Apr 17 01:00 UTC (-32.5pp for YES) suggests a discrete negative event or insider signal affecting One Coin, but this signal is NOT documented in the briefing; market moved before search results were updated. Low volume ($5 USD) indicates thin liquidity and minimal trader conviction \u2014 price may reflect mechanical/algorithmic positioning rather than genuine belief. Event is TODAY (12 hours to start) \u2014 crowd had 7 days to build a thesis but produced only a lopsided price with no supporting narrative in the briefing. Rational apathy detected: market has priced One Coin as heavy underdog, but the briefing provides zero evidence justifying this \u2014 neither team has documented weaknesses, injuries, or form collapse. Reversed confidence asymmetry: confidence_no (35) is intentionally LOW because the NO-side narrative is equally thin; market consensus on Four Angry Men is NOT backed by visible data. If sharp move on Apr 17 01:00 UTC represents genuine inside information (e.g., One Coin roster issue), the market is pricing rationally but the briefing is stale \u2014 this creates a data-gap penalty on both sides. Probability_score of 20 reflects crowd psychology (crowded trade on NO side) but with weak conviction signals; probability_no_score of 80 mirrors the market but both confidence scores remain depressed due to information deficit.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.75, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'no prior head-to-head record available' and provides no team roster, coaching staff, recent tournament placements, or map pool specialization data\u2014standard inputs for R6 esports match prediction. MARKET SIGNAL INTERPRETATION: The 80% NO price (with sharp 32.5pp downward move on YES side Apr 17 01:00 UTC) suggests informed R6 esports traders have intelligence not present in this briefing; the EMA trend shows sustained conviction toward Four Angry Men (EMA 72% for NO side, +30pp 7-day change). ONE COIN FORM OPACITY: Stated as '2W-2L (last 4 matches)' with no tournament context, opponent strength weighting, or map-specific performance\u2014R6 esports outcomes are highly map-dependent (Chalet, Consulate, Clubhouse, Bank, Kafe carry different meta weight), and form without opponent caliber is near-meaningless. FOUR ANGRY MEN FORM OPACITY: Stated as '5W-5L (last 10 matches)' on a 50% winrate\u2014this is within normal variance and provides no predictive power; no indication of trajectory (improving or declining), opponent quality, or playoff readiness. BRACKET POSITION: Market identifies this as 'Upper bracket quarterfinal 2' implying One Coin/Four Angry Men are seeded contestants; no seed rankings provided in briefing, so cannot assess if this is a presumed upset or expected matchup. TIMING CRITICALITY: Event is TODAY with ~12 hours until start; any reversal toward YES would require rapid new information (roster announcement, player availability confirmation, tactical prep leak). The market's downward pressure on YES suggests information revelation has already occurred off-briefing and participants are circling the true outcome. LIQUIPEDIA RESOLUTION DEPENDENCY: Briefing commits to Liquipedia as authoritative source; however, Liquipedia documentation in briefing shows incomplete bracket data ('TBD' entries throughout), raising operational uncertainty about match completion guarantees. R6 SIEGE TACTICAL COMPLEXITY: Unlike mechanical shooters, R6 outcomes are driven by map knowledge, operator synergy, site execution, and reading opponent utility setup\u2014none of which can be evaluated without roster names, primary operators, and recent VOD data. Team familiarity with vetoed maps (shown in statistics table) is unavailable for One Coin vs Four Angry Men. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_no (35%) reflects that the market's 80% conviction likely rests on R6-specific intelligence (team reputation, recent roster changes, pro circuit gossip) not surfaced in this briefing; confidence_yes (28%) reflects near-total ignorance of One Coin's competitive standing\u2014even the recent form (2W-2L) lacks context for inference. PROBABILITY FLOORS: probability_score of 22 (vs market 20%) is slightly above market to account for residual upside from underdog playoff upset potential and unknown strategic preparation; probability_no_score of 75 (vs market 80%) is slightly below market to reflect genuine data uncertainty, not overconfidence in the consensus. Neither score should exceed 78/28 split given briefing poverty. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE NOTE: $5 USD total volume is minimal; this is a low-liquidity niche market where a single informed bettor on Four Angry Men could have driven the 32.5pp spike on Apr 17. The move lacks statistical reliability as a signal.", "key_factor": "Market pricing (80% NO) reflects sophisticated R6 esports knowledge of Four Angry Men's competitive standing, but the briefing contains severe data gaps\u2014no head-to-head history, no roster composition, no recent map pool compatibility analysis, and conflicting tournament bracket documentation make high-confidence assessment impossible on either side."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.75, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO roster composition, recent player moves, injury reports, or lineup stability signals for either team. This is a 12-hour pre-match window with zero granularity on personnel. MARKET SIGNAL IGNORED: Sharp -32.5pp move on Apr 17 01:00 UTC suggests institutional money fled YES (One Coin) overnight. This timing coincides with Asian competitive esports intel windows \u2014 likely a credible roster/availability shock that casual market hasn't caught. FORM RECORD ASYMMETRY: One Coin is 2W-2L (recent 4 matches); Four Angry Men is 5W-5L (recent 10 matches). Both are volatile, but One Coin's LAST 4 matches show form decay (50% win rate), while Four Angry Men's LAST 5 are above 50% (5W-5L over 10 = weaker long-term, but last 5 could be 3W-2L trending up). BO3 PLAYOFF CEILING EFFECT: In best-of-three eliminations, teams playing with roster uncertainty or motivation mismatches collapse harder than regular season. If One Coin has a suspended/benched player or forced stand-in, that compounds across 3 maps. SILENT BRIEFING ON TACTICAL/META: Zero mention of map pool matchups, recent patch effects, or veto strategy. In R6S, meta shifts (operator bans, map pool rotations) can nullify form records. One Coin may lack coverage for current map pool if recent changes favor Four Angry Men's playstyle. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Both confidence scores are LOW (28, 32) because the briefing is information-starved on BOTH sides. The market consensus (80% NO) is being driven by the sharp price move, not by transparent form or personnel data. This is a classic 'smart money moved first, retail following' setup, which can be right \u2014 but also prone to herding on incomplete info. BLACK SWAN MECHANISM: If One Coin had a key IGL (in-game leader) or operator specialist benched or sidelined 6\u201312 hours before match start, the 80% NO price underestimates the structural damage to their BO3 execution. BO3 is unforgiving: drop Map 1, and morale + adjustability collapse. CONTRARIAN EDGE: Market is NOT seeing roster churn as the primary driver of the 32pp overnight move; instead, it's likely treating the move as 'Four Angry Men trending up' rather than 'One Coin rotting'. If the root cause is One Coin's lineup unavailability, the move is correctly directional but UNDER-SIZED because the impacted match (this BO3) has the highest leverage.", "key_factor": "One Coin's roster stability or key player availability is systematically worse than Four Angry Men's heading into this playoff match, and the market has not priced in a last-minute substitution or illness that forces One Coin to field a sub-optimal lineup in a high-pressure BO3."}], "final_score": 0.23696979607727867, "no_score": 0.7627973407407869, "edge": 0.4909090909090909, "no_edge": -0.10909090909090913, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 34.57% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0481495936714533, "The Bull": 0.9617091423379212, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0505242668684711, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0511777511792142, "The Domain Specialist": 1.052379936971564, "The Contrarian": 1.0671821968585695, "The Bear": 0.768877112112807}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1997387", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: One Coin vs Four Angry Men (BO3) - CN League Kickoff Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between One Coin and Four Angry Men in the CN League Kickoff Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"One Coin\" if One Coin win the match against Four Angry Men.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Four Angry Men\" if Four Angry Men win the match against One Coin.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T15:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T09:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.2, "volume_usd": 5.263156, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["71443214670285683332127487784576986819490502898705266883244878831681669654568", "98090529771989446616557050556137379120426170386158767475102440782137892443090"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Soul's Heart EsportSH\n\nApril 18, 2026 - 18:00 SGT\n\nSH\n\nvs(Bo3)\n\nTBD\n\nWatch here\n\nWatch here\n\nApril 25, 2026 - 12:00 SGT\n\nTBD\n\nvs(Bo3)\n\nTBD\n\nWatch here\n\nWatch here\n\nApril 25, 2026 - 15:00 SGT\n\nTBD\n\nvs(Bo3)\n\nTBD\n\nWatch here\n\nWatch here\n\n\u200b\n\n### Decider Brackets\n\n[edit]\n\n#### 7th Place Decider\n\n[edit]\n\nGrand Final\n\nGrand Final\n\nFinal\n\nGF\n\nHL Tauri EsportsHLT\n\nFURYFURY\n\n#### 5th Place Decider\n\n[edit]\n\nGrand Final\n\nGrand Final\n\nFinal\n\nGF\n\nUnreal