titutions neither team public info nor briefing captures. PATCH TIMING: Briefing does not specify Dota 2 patch version. A patch deployed between briefing assembly and match start (Apr 18 10:00 UTC) could buff heroes favoring South America Rejects' draft style or nerf Aurora's recent meta. Patch notes are not in briefing, creating unquantified strategic risk. PSYCHOLOGICAL/MENTAL FACTOR: Aurora's 7W-2L may breed overconfidence or complacency vs a perceived underdog. South America Rejects, at 50% recent form, may be battle-hardened by tight group-stage matches and more psychologically prepared for a BO3 do-or-die moment. Briefing contains no morale, motivation, or coaching-change intel. CONSENSUS TRAP: Market consensus at 84% YES is well-anchored to Aurora's aggregate form advantage. However, consensus often underweights region-specific tactical innovation, roster health unknowns, and early-tournament adaptation phases. A black-swan flip requires South America Rejects to execute a meta deviation Aurora has not faced and cannot quickly counter\u2014highly plausible in a BO1 or early BO3 game. CONFIDENCE DOWNGRADE: confidence_yes = 35 (low) because briefing provides no Dota-specific hero, draft, patch, or player performance data to anchor Aurora's 7W-2L into tournament context. confidence_no = 28 (very low) because South America Rejects' 2W-2L is too thin to evaluate true ceiling, and no regional meta or roster intelligence is available. The market is pricing on form alone; both teams remain fundamentally opaque. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 72% YES reflects Aurora's raw form advantage (7W-2L) and market consensus, but discounted ~12pp from equilibrium-price consensus (84%) to reflect: (1) South America Rejects' region-specific tactical upside, (2) roster/health unknowns, (3) patch/meta unknown as of briefing close, and (4) early-tournament variance. 28% NO reflects the real 2W-2L underdog path with plausible (if low-probability) upset triggers.", "key_factor": "South America Rejects deploys a pocket meta strategy or hero pool innovation that Aurora's recent 7W-2L form has not faced, exploited by a player roster or tactical adjustment not captured in aggregate recent-form statistics."}], "final_score": 0.7387595113011566, "no_score": 0.2760081278994478, "edge": -0.14409090909090905, "no_edge": 0.5259090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 41.71% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0481495936714533, "The Bull": 0.9617091423379212, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0505242668684711, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0511777511792142, "The Domain Specialist": 1.052379936971564, "The Contrarian": 1.0671821968585695, "The Bear": 0.768877112112807}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2001562", "question": "Dota 2: Aurora vs South America Rejects (BO3) - PGL Wallachia Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Round 1 match between Aurora and South America Rejects in the PGL Wallachia Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 18 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Aurora\" if Aurora win the match against South America Rejects.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"South America Rejects\" if South America Rejects win the match against Aurora.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 