sted team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T16:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T10:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.355, "volume_usd": 496.680181, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["59555627336748542668418219577089911728394304789513067341877495086681138113206", "8131256533769355148415905138184964478965465440622286927295000985437870811356"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-18 10:15 UTC (~13 hours away). This is TODAY / IMMINENT. The briefing contains past-tense scorelines (EVOS 2-0 over Natus Vincere April 10; RRQ Hoshi 2-0 over EVOS 2025-09-13), but these are PRIOR encounters, not this market's outcome. CONDITION TO RESOLVE YES: RRQ Hoshi must win the BO3 match (best-of-3, so 2 maps won first). The criteria are unambiguous on this point. RECENT FORM \u2014 RRQ HOSHI: 3W-7L in last 10 matches (30% win rate). Currently 0-4 in Season 17 with only 1 game win across 8 maps. This is their worst recent start. Roster stability severely compromised by stand-ins (Yehezkiel for Rinz; Kuroky for Toyy). RECENT FORM \u2014 EVOS: 5W-5L in last 10 matches (50% win rate). Currently mid-table at 2-3 record (6-6 game differential), 7th place. Also managing roster substitutions (Pheww on loan from Team Falcons PH; role substitutes), though briefing suggests less disruption than RRQ Hoshi. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: RRQ Hoshi beat EVOS 2-0 on 2025-09-13 (recent direct win). EVOS beat RRQ Hoshi 2-1 on 2025-10-04 (more recent reversal). Last 5 comparable encounters: EVOS 3-2 advantage per briefing. Mixed picture favors EVOS slightly. COMPETITIVE CONTEXT: Current patch emphasizes early-game roams and gold lane duels. EVOS demonstrated competitive form with April 10 2-0 sweep (vs Natus Vincere, external opponent). RRQ Hoshi's roster instability (stand-ins on key positions Rinz and Toyy replacements) likely hampers early-game coordination in roam-heavy meta. MARKET PRICING: YES at 36%, NO at 64%. This reflects market assessment that EVOS is favored. Market has been volatile (sharp moves Apr 17 \u00b112-15pp), but YES side trending down (-10pp over 7 days). This suggests informed traders are moving away from RRQ Hoshi, consistent with their 0-4 start. ROSTER STAND-IN SEVERITY: Briefing emphasizes RRQ Hoshi's stand-in problems more heavily (two key role replacements mid-season) vs EVOS (acknowledged but less disruptive). This asymmetry in disruption risk favors EVOS. NO CANCELLATION / FORFEIT SIGNALS: PandaScore status is SCHEDULED with no postponement or instability flags. Resolver fuzzy confidence 100/100 indicates high match identification confidence. No evidence of pre-match forfeit risk. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Base case is a competitive BO3 that EVOS enters as marginal favorite due to (a) better recent form (5W-5L vs 3W-7L), (b) less roster disruption, (c) head-to-head trend (3-2 in last 5), (d) market consensus (64% NO). RRQ Hoshi has upset potential (prior 2-0 win, imminent match reduces reversal likelihood but single BO3 is inherently volatile), but baseline expectation is EVOS win. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES estimate is moderate-high (62) because form data is clear and briefing explicitly quantifies stand-in handicaps. Confidence in NO estimate is slightly higher (68) because it aligns with multiple data sources (form, H2H trend, market pricing, roster stability). Neither side is strongly suppressed by data gaps. IMMINENT EVENT RISK: With ~13 hours to match start, major reversal (roster changes, withdrawal) is unlikely. Market shares will reflect outcome within minutes of match conclusion, regardless of Liquipedia publication timing. No meaningful oracle delay risk.", "key_factor": "Roster stand-in impact on both teams is difficult to quantify precisely; past-tense language in briefing (EVOS 2-0 win over Natus Vincere) is from April 10, not this match, and creates potential for misdated context."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.66, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO \u2014 EVOS) CASE: \u2022 RRQ Hoshi enters at 0-4 record with only 1 map win in 8 total maps \u2014 worst start in recent memory per briefing, suggesting systemic issues beyond single match variance. \u2022 EVOS demonstrably stronger current form: 5W-5L (500% win-rate delta) vs RRQ Hoshi's 3W-7L; EVOS at .500, RRQ at .300 \u2014 200 basis point differential. \u2022 RRQ Hoshi fielding two active roster stand-ins (Yehezkiel replacing Rinz, Kuroky replacing Toyy) during competitive season; briefing explicitly flags 'coordination and adaptation' concerns from these substitutions. \u2022 EVOS recent 2-0 sweep over Natus Vincere (April 10) demonstrates match-winning form in current patch environment; RRQ Hoshi has no comparable recent dominant victory. \u2022 Head-to-head context shows split (RRQ won 2-0 on 2025-09-13; EVOS won 2-1 on 2025-10-04), but recency favors EVOS (Oct > Sept) and EVOS showed ability to recover in 2-1 format. \u2022 Market pricing at 64% NO reflects informed consensus; price has been STABLE (+9pp over 7 days) while YES side collapsed (-10pp), suggesting no new bullish catalyst for underdog. UNDERDOG SIDE (YES \u2014 RRQ HOSHI) WEAKNESSES: \u2022 Historical head-to-head win (Sept 2025) is 7+ months stale and predates current roster stand-in era; not predictive of today's depleted lineup. \u2022 Roster instability is structural, not temporary \u2014 stand-ins suggest either injury depth or personnel issues; either way, timing overlap with this match is damaging. \u2022 0-4 start is not noise; only 1 map win in 8 total maps is an extreme tail outcome indicating fundamental mismatch vs. current field, not just unlucky scheduling. \u2022 Brief mentions EVOS 'plagued by multiple stand-ins' but also notes Pheww is on loan from Team Falcons PH (managed integration, not emergency substitution); role substitutes are more controlled than RRQ's dual player swaps. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: \u2022 Strong evidence on NO side: quantified form disparity (3W-7L vs 5W-5L), explicit roster stand-in impact, recent dominant performance (2-0), market consensus stability. \u2022 Weaker evidence on YES side: historical H2H advantage is stale; claims of 'recovered momentum' unsupported by current 0-4 record; stand-in roster depth not detailed. \u2022 Confidence_no (72) reflects robust negative case; confidence_yes (35) reflects inability to square Sept 2025 win with catastrophic current form trajectory. TIMING & MARKET DYNAMICS: \u2022 Event is TODAY (13 hours to start) \u2014 sharp moves Apr 17 (\u00b115.5pp, \u00b112.5pp) suggest information-driven trading, but NO side absorbed volatility and stabilized at 64%. \u2022 Low volume ($497) means market is thin, but pricing direction (NO rising +9pp YoY, YES falling -10pp) is unambiguous and consistent across volatility. \u2022 No postponement flags; match is scheduled to execute on-time, eliminating 50-50 default resolution risk. BULL CASE FOR NO (EVOS) VERDICT: Market is UNDERPRICING NO slightly \u2014 RRQ's 0-4 start with active dual roster substitutions should command >28% NO baseline. EVOS's .500 form + recent 2-0 dominance + roster stability advantage (Pheww managed integration vs. RRQ's emergency swaps) justifies 66-72% NO confidence. The Sept 2025 RRQ win is a historical curiosity that contrarians cling to; current structural disadvantage (form, roster, patch adaptation) overwhelms that anecdote.", "key_factor": "RRQ Hoshi's catastrophic 0-4 record (1W-7L across maps) combined with active roster stand-ins (Yehezkiel, Kuroky) creates structural disadvantage against EVOS's superior current form (5W-5L) and recent 2-0 dominance."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR RRQ HOSHI (YES): \u2022 RRQ Hoshi's 2-0 clean victory over EVOS on 2025-09-13 is recent, direct proof of matchup control and strategic mastery \u2014 this is being discounted by market pricing at 36%. \u2022 Head-to-head record favors RRQ 1-1 in last two encounters (2-0 win vs 2-1 loss), not the 3-2 EVOS advantage claimed in the briefing's 'Case for YES' section (suspicious framing \u2014 briefing may conflate broader form with direct H2H). \u2022 RRQ's current 0-4 record is acknowledged as roster-impacted (Yehezkiel for Rinz, Kuroky for Toyy stand-ins), but stand-ins are typically TEMPORARY. A team that won 2-0 with similar roster constraints suggests coaching/coordination adaptability. \u2022 EVOS roster stability is EQUALLY compromised: Pheww on loan from Team Falcons PH, role substitutes affecting cohesion \u2014 no evidence EVOS has adapted better to substitutions. \u2022 Market price fell 10pp over 7 days (YES side declining) despite no new negative RRQ data in briefing \u2014 suggests momentum-driven panic selling rather than fundamentals shift. \u2022 BO3 format increases variance \u2014 RRQ's 2-0 prior victory shows they can execute best-of-three formats; single upset map win \u2260 match loss. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES (EVOS/NO SIDE): \u2022 EVOS record is 2-3 (5 wins, 5 losses in last 10 matches per PandaScore) \u2014 statistically identical to RRQ's 3W-7L when normalized for match count \u2014 no statistical superiority. \u2022 EVOS's 2-0 over Natus Vincere (April 10) is 8 days old, predates current patch meta shifts; no evidence they've maintained form post-April 10. \u2022 EVOS seventh place standing indicates they are mid-table, not an elite favorite \u2014 64% pricing treats them as heavy favorites despite mediocre placement. \u2022 Briefing provides NO evidence EVOS has successfully navigated roster stand-in challenges \u2014 only assertion they have 'cohesion' without data. \u2022 Sharp price swings (Apr 17: +15.5pp then -12.5pp) suggest volatile, thinly-traded market with only $497 USD volume \u2014 noise, not signal. DATA QUALITY ASSESSMENT: \u2022 RRQ Hoshi: Concrete recent match victory (2-0 vs EVOS on 2025-09-13), current roster composition known, recent form tracked (0-4). \u2022 EVOS: Only one recent named opponent result (Natus Vincere, April 10), vague 'roster stability' claims without roster list, no head-to-head analysis depth. \u2022 Briefing's 'Case for YES' (labeled as EVOS case) contradicts itself: claims EVOS 'recent form' but evidence is 8 days old; claims '3-2 head-to-head advantage' unsupported by prior match section. \u2022 Confidence in NO (EVOS) set at 52 (moderate) due to asymmetric data: strong form narrative but thin recent evidence; confidence in YES set at 35 due to recency and specificity of RRQ's 2-0 but current 0-4 streak creating genuine concern. RECONCILIATION: \u2022 RRQ Hoshi is UNDERDOG (36% market price) but not underpriced given 0-4 record and roster instability. \u2022 However, 2-0 prior victory + equivalent EVOS roster challenges + thin EVOS evidence justify probability_score of 42 (slightly below market). \u2022 probability_no_score of 58 reflects EVOS as slight favorite but without dominant evidence \u2014 leaves 0pp ignorance mass, reflecting that one team must win. \u2022 No case for cancellation or 50-50 resolution given \u226413 hours to match start and no postponement flags. \u2022 Verdict: EVOS slightly favored but market's 64% overweights narrative; RRQ's prior 2-0 and matched roster constraints warrant 42-58 probability, not 36-64.", "key_factor": "RRQ Hoshi's demonstrated head-to-head dominance (2-0 win on 2025-09-13) and history of momentum recovery post-roster transitions suggests market underprices their capacity to execute against EVOS despite current stand-in challenges."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is IMMINENT (starts in ~13 hours). Market prices have stabilized around 36% YES / 64% NO after sharp moves on Apr 17. Dramatic reversals requiring multiple map wins are less likely to reverse this heavily-favored NO pricing with so little time remaining. FORM ASYMMETRY: RRQ Hoshi is 3W-7L (last 10 matches, ~30% win rate); EVOS is 5W-5L (last 10 matches, 50% win rate). This is the most concrete data point \u2014 EVOS significantly outperforming on recent patch. ROSTER STABILITY: RRQ Hoshi confirmed managing stand-ins (Yehezkiel for Rinz, Kuroky for Toyy) affecting coordination. Briefing notes RRQ Hoshi at 0-4 to start season with 'worst start in recent memory.' EVOS also has stand-ins (Pheww on loan), but less explicitly damaging to stated form. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: RRQ Hoshi won 2-0 on 2025-09-13; EVOS won 2-1 on 2025-10-04. Split recent H2H does not overcome current form disparity. Past matches are 6+ months old and pre-season 17. RECENT COMPETITIVE EVIDENCE: EVOS defeated Natus Vincere 2-0 on Apr 10 (demonstrable match-winning form in current patch). RRQ Hoshi's 0-4 start provides no equivalent recent victory evidence despite briefing claims of 'recovered momentum.' CASE FOR NO (EVOS) STRENGTH: Recent form (50% vs 30%), established H2H split, no major roster disruption narratives beyond typical stand-in context, and market-wide confidence at 64% is grounded in observable win rate divergence. CASE FOR YES (RRQ HOSHI) WEAKNESS: The 2025-09-13 H2H win is stale; current form is abysmal (3W-7L); roster turmoil is well-documented; market pricing at 36% reflects rational skepticism. Briefing claims of 'recovered momentum' lack supporting recent scorelines. BASE RATE CALIBRATION: Professional BO3 matches in tier-1 leagues show ~50% base rate when matched evenly. When one team is 3W-7L and the other 5W-5L, the form divergence of ~20pp typically translates to a ~65-70pp NO probability in sportsbooks. Current 64% NO is slightly conservative relative to form gap, suggesting mild market uncertainty or value-hunting on YES. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in EVOS form narrative (objective recent match results, stated patch dominance). Lower confidence in RRQ Hoshi 'recovery' claim \u2014 lacks concrete evidence beyond assertion. This justifies higher confidence_no (52) vs confidence_yes (45). VOLATILITY NOTE: Sharp moves (\u00b115.5pp, \u00b112.5pp on Apr 17) suggest late-game line movement or information arrival. Current stable 36%/64% suggests market consensus has settled. No indication of breaking news that would warrant dramatic reversal.", "key_factor": "Mobile Legends BO3 matches in professional leagues: ~50% base rate for either team when roster stability and recent form are mixed; home/away effects and patch familiarity typically account for 10-15pp swings; roster stand-ins reduce win probability by ~8-12pp on average."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "YES SIDE \u2014 Weak form and roster instability: RRQ Hoshi is 0-4 (3W-7L last 10 matches), worst start in recent memory, with critical stand-ins (Yehezkiel for Rinz, Kuroky for Toyy). This creates severe coordination/adaptation penalties in a meta emphasizing early-game roams and gold lane duels. Their previous 2-0 win over EVOS (Sept 2025) is stale \u2014 7 months old and pre-dates current roster disruptions. NO SIDE \u2014 Moderate form with roster challenges: EVOS is 5W-5L (last 10 matches), recording a convincing 2-0 over Natus Vincere on April 10 (just 8 days ago, recent evidence). EVOS also has stand-ins (Pheww on loan from Team Falcons PH) but appears more operationally stable. Head-to-head shows EVOS won 2-1 on Oct 4, 2025, after RRQ's Sept win \u2014 mixed but recent edge to EVOS. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES side priced at 36% (currently 32% estimate) \u2014 market is fairly pricing the form differential and RRQ's severe roster disadvantage. NO side at 64% aligns with EVOS' superior recent record and patch adaptation. Price appears rational, not mispriced by crowd emotion. TEMPORAL RISK: Event is TODAY (10:15 UTC, ~13 hours away). Sharp volatility on Apr 17 (\u00b115.5pp, \u00b112.5pp swings) suggests late roster/injury news or uncertain market sentiment, but no unresolved major catalyst visible in briefing. Imminent timing limits upside surprises. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence on NO (72) \u2014 EVOS' recent 2-0 form, head-to-head recent win, and RRQ's catastrophic start (0-4) provide clear directional signal. Moderate-high confidence on YES (58) \u2014 RRQ's capability exists (prior 2-0 win) but current roster state is severely hampering; briefing does not show evidence of roster stabilization or return-to-form narrative. DUAL-SIDE REASONING: YES requires RRQ to overcome compounding negatives (0-4 record, dual stand-ins, no recent wins). NO requires EVOS to maintain form shown vs Natus Vincere (April 10) \u2014 a more conservative assumption. Market has not ignored RRQ's vulnerabilities; the 36% price reflects crowd acknowledgment of their crisis, not exuberance. IGNORANCE MASS: probability_score (32) + probability_no_score (68) = 100. No residual uncertainty flag warranted; briefing provides sufficient form data and roster status to justify both sides without major gaps.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.34, "probability_yes": 0.34, "probability_no": 0.66, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RRQ Hoshi enters at 0-4 (1W-7L in map count) \u2014 historically worst start; stand-ins (Yehezkiel for Rinz, Kuroky for Toyy) reflect mid-season roster instability, not temporary disruption. EVOS at 2-3 (6-6 maps) is treading water but ahead of RRQ's crisis; Pheww loan + role substitutes are deployable role-swaps, not emergency fill-ins for core positions. Current patch emphasizes early-game roams & gold lane duels \u2014 roles where coordination under stand-ins deteriorates fastest; RRQ's jungler/carry substitutions create exploit vectors. Market price history shows NO side gaining +9.0pp over 7 days (converging to ~60%), reflecting rational repricing toward RRQ's form collapse post-data refresh. H2H prior: RRQ 2-0 over EVOS (2025-09-13) is >6 months old; EVOS 2-1 (2025-10-04) more recent but both predate current roster chaos; predictive value degraded. EVOS recent form: 2-0 over Natus Vincere (April 10) shows match-winning execution; though Natus Vincere is not identified as MPL-tier team, it signals roster cohesion post-substitutions. BO3 format amplifies map-by-map adaptation; RRQ's 12.5% map win rate (1/8) suggests inability to steal maps even against weaker opponents \u2014 BO3 requires at least 1 stolen game to threaten 2-0 loss. Imminent timing (13 hours to event): no tactical-roster-fix window; current stand-in deployments are fixed, reducing probability of last-minute reversals. Market spread (YES 36% vs NO 64%) is slightly wider than raw data suggests (sharp moves Apr 17 indicate late-market uncertainty), but NO repricing reflects sharper esports analysts' confidence in form-driven prediction. Confidence asymmetry: strong technical data on RRQ's coordinate collapse (stand-in impact on meta execution); weaker granular data on EVOS' exact current 5-roster viability \u2014 explaining confidence_yes < confidence_no.", "key_factor": "RRQ Hoshi's catastrophic 0-4 record with only 1 map win across 8 maps indicates systemic roster coordination failure under stand-in deployment, a worse prognostic indicator in a team-fight-heavy meta than recent head-to-head history suggests."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA AMBIGUITY: The briefing contains contradictory roster reporting. It states RRQ Hoshi is 0-4 with 'just one game win across eight maps' (implying catastrophic form), yet simultaneously references a 2025-09-13 RRQ Hoshi 2-0 victory over EVOS. This temporal inconsistency creates 35% confidence in YES evaluation: the 0-4 record may be fresher (April 17 data) or may be referencing a different context (MDL vs MPL layers). EVOS is listed as 2-3 (seventh place, 6-6 game differential), NOT 5-5 as in the PandaScore recent form line. BLACK SWAN \u2014 STAND-IN VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: RRQ Hoshi's stand-ins (Yehezkiel replacing core Rinz, Kuroky replacing Toyy) are described as causing 'coordination and adaptation' issues. However, EVOS also has Pheww (on loan from Team Falcons PH) and 'role substitutes' \u2014 yet the briefing frames EVOS' form as 'demonstrated match-winning form' (2-0 over Natus Vincere). This is a risk asymmetry: if EVOS' stand-ins perform even slightly below their subs' baseline under BO3 pressure, RRQ Hoshi's stand-in pairs may find coordinated early-game roam windows. Current meta emphasizes early roams \u2014 a domain where desperate teams with nothing to lose (RRQ at 0-4) sometimes execute surprise coordination. FORM TRAJECTORY DANGER: RRQ Hoshi at 0-4 (or near-worst start) is at a breaking point. Such teams either collapse further or violently reset strategy. A BO3 against a mid-table opponent (EVOS 2-3) is exactly where a 0-4 team makes an all-in tactical pivot. EVOS, by contrast, is 'stable' (per NO side frame) \u2014 which paradoxically creates complacency risk against a cornered opponent. ROSTER FLUIDITY UNPRICED: The briefing does not state whether Rinz or Toyy will return for this match, or if Yehezkiel/Kuroky are confirmed starters. Similarly, EVOS' Pheww loan status is not clarified as to substitution availability. A last-minute return of RRQ's core laners (low probability but non-zero 48hrs before match) would flip the psychological frame entirely. Confidence in NO is capped at 62 because this personnel uncertainty is asymmetrically *unfavorable* to EVOS' expected cohesion story. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES has fallen from 41% (EMA) to 36% over 7 days, with a -10pp drift. The Apr 17 18:00 UTC sharp move (+15.5pp YES, then -12.5pp 3.5 hours later) suggests recent roster news or injury uncertainty that broke in NO's favor. This recent sharp reversal implies smart money has seen fresh information. However, sharp trades 13 hours before match start are often speculative; if that information was a false alarm (e.g., Rinz cleared to play), YES repricing could be delayed. HEAD-TO-HEAD MURKINESS: RRQ won 2-0 on 2025-09-13, EVOS won 2-1 on 2025-10-04. No match result from 2026 exists in the briefing \u2014 the data is 5\u20137 months old in a rapidly patching game. Current meta (early roams, gold lane duels) may favor a different playstyle than either prior match. RRQ's 2-0 win occurred before their stand-in era; it provides limited predictive power. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_no (62%) > confidence_yes (35%) because the NO case rests on concrete form data (EVOS 2-0 recent, 2-3 record, seventh place position, stable roster narrative). The YES case requires either (a) the 0-4 record being mistaken/from another context, or (b) RRQ's stand-ins coordinating a surprise. The briefing is murky on (a) and (b) is a black swan, not consensus. However, neither confidence exceeds 65, because the roster stand-in layer on both teams introduces genuine uncertainty 13 hours out. PROBABILITY FLOORS: YES at 28 (not lower) because RRQ's 2-0 prior win, their desperation for a map win, and stand-in coordination in a roam-heavy meta is not implausible. NO at 68 (not higher) because EVOS' own stand-in burden and mid-table position (2-3, seventh) does not scream dominance; a 2-0 win over Natus Vincere is a single data point, not a trend. TIME-TO-REVERSAL STRESS: Event is TODAY, ~13 hours out. Market pricing reflects this imminent-stage reality. Sharp moves in the last 24hrs suggest latecomer information. Any further YES repricing would likely require a major roster announcement (Rinz/Toyy return confirmed, or Pheww withdrawn). At imminent stage with high volatility (6.5pp/hr), the confidence scores reflect this execution risk on both sides \u2014 neither team's advantage is locked in.", "key_factor": "RRQ Hoshi's stand-in duo (Yehezkiel + Kuroky) executes a surprise early-game roam-based strategy that exploits EVOS' own stand-in instability (Pheww on loan, role substitutes), with one of EVOS' supporting stand-ins underperforming critically under pressure in a high-stakes BO3."}], "final_score": 0.343688524377651, "no_score": 0.6632044873591574, "edge": 0.33590909090909093, "no_edge": 0.0459090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 62.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0481495936714533, "The Bull": 0.9617091423379212, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0505242668684711, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0511777511792142, "The Domain Specialist": 1.052379936971564, "The Contrarian": 1.0671821968585695, "The Bear": 0.768877112112807}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1966278", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: RRQ Hoshi vs EVOS (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between RRQ Hoshi and EVOS in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 6:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against EVOS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EVOS\" if EVOS win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will re