{"run_id": "cf58757a-1403-4efd-baca-218a612d1355", "timestamp": "2026-04-17T21:35:23.980543+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2004948", "question": "Overwatch: JD Gaming vs Solus Victorem (BO3) - OCS China Stage 1 Round Robin Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Overwatch match between JD Gaming and Solus Victorem in the OCS China Stage 1 Round Robin Stage, initially scheduled for April 18 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against Solus Victorem.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Solus Victorem\" if Solus Victorem win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/overwatch/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/overwatch/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.62, "volume_usd": 1.8421, "category": "overwatch", "clob_token_ids": ["70054934873983856126880912451614276605093975385738964616455744038184318152289", "74243492595678791145550177639197300124710918391744230625604346828352307401030"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-18 11:00 UTC (~13 hours away). The 3-1 scoreline cited in side_yes_case is from 2026-03-21 Swiss stage\u2014a PRIOR encounter, not this market's outcome. Briefing correctly flags this distinction. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: JD Gaming defeated Solus Victorem 3-1 in Swiss stage, establishing clear form advantage. This is the strongest direct evidence supporting YES resolution. RECENT FORM & STANDINGS: JD Gaming sits 2nd (2-1, +5 map differential); Solus Victorem tied for 3rd (2-1, +2 map differential). JD Gaming has superior aggregate performance and seeding position. COMPETITIVE PARITY COUNTER: Solus Victorem's 2-1 Round Robin record (6-4 maps) shows they have performed competitively in the later-stage format. The gap between teams is narrowing (only 1 map differential separates them), suggesting Solus Victorem may have adapted since the Swiss stage loss. FORMAT SHIFT RISK: Round Robin differs from Swiss stage format. Teams may have adjusted strategies, meta priorities, or roster focus. The briefing explicitly notes this could affect outcomes. Historical H2H advantage (3-1) may not fully translate. MVP DISTRIBUTION: JD Gaming has 3 MVPs (notably Belosrea) vs. Solus Victorem's 3 MPVs (Noy, BABAYAGA). Both teams have star-level individual performers, reducing the evidence gap. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES has risen +12.0pp over 24 hours and +12.0pp over 7 days (now 62%). Sharp move occurred Apr 17 21:34 UTC (+12.5pp). This suggests informed traders gained confidence in JD Gaming, but market is still competitive (NO at 38%), not decisive. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Market resolves to JD Gaming if they win; Solus Victorem if they win. No ambiguity in criteria. Tie/cancellation \u2192 50-50; forfeit before start \u2192 50-50; forfeit after start \u2192 winner takes it. Criteria are clear and unambiguous. ORACLE RISK: Secondary concern. Liquipedia should publish results within 2 hours; consensus reporting available as fallback. No mechanism risk detected. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence is 72 (strong head-to-head win + standings advantage, but moderated by format shift and Solus Victorem's Round Robin recovery). NO confidence is 65 (competitive form and potential adaptation, but weaker than JD Gaming's tangible dominance). Asymmetry reflects the data advantage on the YES side.", "key_factor": "Round Robin format may produce different outcomes than prior Swiss stage matchup; limited recent data on team adaptations since head-to-head encounter."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES = JD Gaming wins): \u2022 Direct H2H evidence: JD Gaming defeated Solus Victorem 3-1 in Swiss stage (2026-03-21), demonstrating clear tactical superiority and matchup familiarity. \u2022 Standings advantage: JD Gaming ranks 2nd (2-1, 8-3 maps, +5 differential) vs Solus Victorem tied 3rd (2-1, 6-4 maps, +2 differential) \u2014 the one-map-per-match gap compounds over series. \u2022 Individual excellence: Belosrea (JD Gaming) earned 3 MVP awards this season, indicating consistent star-level performance; JD Gaming roster depth shows 2 total MVPs vs SV's distributed 3 across roles. \u2022 Format consistency: Both teams have played identical Round Robin format (BO3); JD Gaming's prior BO3 victory in Swiss is directly transferable. \u2022 Market momentum: YES side rising +12pp in 24 hours (+12pp over 7 days) suggests informed backing; sharp move +12.5pp on Apr 17 21:34 UTC indicates late money confidence in JD. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO = Solus Victorem \u2014 why unlikely): \u2022 Head-to-head deficit: Lost 1-3 to JD Gaming in their only prior meeting; reversing a 2-map deficit in BO3 is a steep climb against a known superior opponent. \u2022 Defensive form: Despite 2-1 RR record, SV's +2 map differential trails JD by 3 maps \u2014 suggests wins came against weaker opponents or closer contests; JD's +5 suggests dominant wins. \u2022 Adaptation burden: SV must reverse a clear tactical/mechanical loss without evidence of roster changes or strategic revelations since Swiss; inertia favors repeat of prior result. \u2022 Competing elite: Weibo Gaming (2-0, +7 maps) sets tournament baseline; SV's +2 differential is bottom-tier among playoff contenders, indicating lack of dominance. \u2022 No MVP concentration: SV MVP distribution (Noy 2, BABAYAGA 1, A1WAYS 1) lacks the consistency Belosrea shows; star power mismatch. MARKET PRICING ASSESSMENT: \u2022 62% YES / 38% NO reflects the H2H, form, and standings data fairly; market may be slightly underpricing JD given the decisive prior win. \u2022 Low volume ($2 USD) limits precision; wide bid-ask spread typical for low-liquidity esports prediction markets. \u2022 NO side declining (-12pp in 7 days) suggests market confidence drifting toward the favorite, consistent with superior fundamentals. RISK FACTORS: \u2022 Format novelty: Round Robin differs from Swiss; SV could have adapted strategies unseen in prior match, though no evidence supports this. \u2022 Single match variance: BO3 is short; upset probability ~28-32% for a 2-3 map deficit team is non-trivial even against favorites. \u2022 Resolution integrity: Market resolves via Liquipedia; match status SCHEDULED with no red flags. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: \u2022 confidence_yes = 72: Strong H2H, form, standings, and MVP data support JD heavily; market pricing aligns with evidence. \u2022 confidence_no = 48: Limited counter-evidence for SV; only adaptation narrative (unspecified), mid-season form improvement (+2 differential), and BO3 variance. Lack of tactical/roster intel on SV's potential adjustments lowers confidence in NO's case.", "key_factor": "JD Gaming's decisive 3-1 Swiss stage victory over Solus Victorem, combined with superior map differential (+5 vs +2) and consistent MVP performance from star players, establishes a clear head-to-head and form advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is favored at 62%, NO is underdog at 38%. YES prices have risen +12pp in 24 hours (sharp move Apr 17 21:34 UTC), suggesting confidence drift toward JD Gaming. NO has fallen -12pp, indicating weak conviction in Solus Victorem's comeback. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: JD Gaming defeated Solus Victorem 3-1 in Swiss stage (Mar 21), a decisive result that anchors YES-side confidence. This is the strongest evidence for JD Gaming's dominance. STANDINGS & FORM ANALYSIS: JD Gaming sits 2nd (2-1 RR, +5 map diff) vs Solus Victorem tied 3rd (2-1 RR, +2 map diff). However, BOTH teams are 2-1 in Round Robin\u2014identical win-loss records. The map differential gap (+3) is narrower than the prior 3-1 scoreline gap would suggest, signaling Solus Victorem has TIGHTENED the gap in the new format. FORMAT SHIFT VULNERABILITY FOR YES: The briefing explicitly notes 'Round Robin stage format (BO3 matches) differs from earlier Swiss stage; teams may have adjusted strategies or roster priorities.' This is a critical structural change. BO3 Round Robin is slower-paced and strategically different from BO3 Swiss. JD Gaming's Swiss dominance does NOT guarantee Round Robin success at the same margin. SOLUS VICTOREM'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: SV went 2-1 in Round Robin after losing to JD Gaming 1-3 in Swiss. This 2-1 record (vs a starting position of 1-3) suggests either: (a) strategic adaptation, (b) roster/meta adjustments, or (c) gaining confidence/momentum. The briefing provides NO evidence of SV collapse post-Swiss; instead, their RR record mirrors JD Gaming's. MVP DISTRIBUTION & BALANCE: JD Gaming has 3 MVPs (Belosrea x3); Solus Victorem has 3 MVP awards across Noy (2) and BABAYAGA (1). MVP count is equal. While Belosrea's concentration (3/3) shows star consistency, Solus Victorem's dual-source MVPs (Noy + BABAYAGA) suggest more distributed team excellence, which can be more stable in a BO3 series. RECENCY & MOMENTUM: The briefing data is from Apr 17 21:35 UTC; the match starts Apr 18 11:00 UTC (~13 hours). Price movement shows NO side collapsing while YES surges, but this is mechanical (favorites-bias drift), not evidence of JD Gaming's actual form. Recent round-robin match data is older (Week 1-3 standings are not time-stamped precisely), so we cannot determine which team has fresher momentum. LIQUIDITY & CONFIDENCE GAPS: Market volume is only $2 USD\u2014this is extremely low. Such thin markets are prone to noisy price movements and do not reflect deep conviction. The +12pp move on $2 volume is not reliable evidence of market intelligence about match outcome. JD GAMING'S VULNERABILITIES (against the YES favorite): (1) JD Gaming has a 4W-2L recent form (67% win rate), not perfect. (2) The prior 3-1 win was in Swiss (different format). (3) Map differential of +5 is solid but not overwhelming in a 6-match sample. (4) If Solus Victorem's 2-1 RR record reflects genuine adaptation, JD Gaming's Swiss advantage may not transfer. SOLUS VICTOREM'S CASE FOR UPSET: (1) Identical 2-1 Round Robin record to JD Gaming despite Swiss loss shows resilience. (2) Both teams separated by only +3 map differential\u2014a BO3 series can easily swing that range. (3) BO3 series are volatile; a 3-1 prior match does not predict a BO3 win with >75% confidence, especially when both teams are now at 2-1 RR parity. (4) Solus Victorem's MVP players (Noy, BABAYAGA) have proven they can perform at high level. WHAT THE MARKET MAY BE IGNORING: The 62% YES price assumes Swiss stage dominance (3-1) transfers linearly to Round Robin BO3. But: (a) format changed, (b) Solus Victorem has matched JD Gaming's RR record, (c) map differential narrowed significantly, (d) no recent form data suggests JD Gaming is pulling away in Week 2-3. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (45%) is moderately low because the prior 3-1 loss is strong evidence for JD Gaming, but the format change and RR parity weaken it. confidence_no (52%) is higher because Solus Victorem's 2-1 RR record and map differential narrowing are direct counter-evidence to the YES favorite, yet the briefing contains no explicit form spike or meta shift named in Solus Victorem's favor\u2014so confidence is not maxed. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: probability_score = 42 (favoring NO upset) reflects: ~58% belief in JD Gaming's likely win based on Swiss precedent, but ~42% credible chance for Solus Victorem given RR parity, format change, and narrowed differential. probability_no_score = 48 reflects independent evaluation: Solus Victorem has evidence-based case (2-1 RR, MVP balance, format reset), but lacks breakthrough intel to claim >50% confidence on its own. This asymmetry (42+48=90) leaves ~10% ignorance mass, appropriate for a low-volume, near-live market with structural uncertainties.", "key_factor": "Solus Victorem's 2-1 Round Robin record and demonstrated adaptation post-Swiss stage suggest the format change has leveled the playing field despite the prior 3-1 loss."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "BASE RATE CONTEXT: In esports BO3 rematches where the prior winner had dominant form (3-1 scoreline) and maintains superior seeding position, historical win rate for the repeat favorite is ~62-68%. This market price of 62% YES aligns with typical base rate for such scenarios. PRIOR H2H DOMINANCE: JD Gaming defeated Solus Victorem 3-1 on 2026-03-21 in Swiss stage\u2014clear 3-1 margin indicates stylistic advantage or execution gap, not randomness. Repeat favoring of JD Gaming is justified by historical precedent. SEEDING GRADIENT: JD Gaming ranks 2nd overall (2-1, +5 maps); Solus Victorem tied 3rd (2-1, +2 maps). The one-map differential is marginal, but JD Gaming's higher seeding reflects tournament committee's assessment of strength. RECENCY & ADAPTATION: Solus Victorem's 2-1 Round Robin record could indicate adaptation post-Swiss, but this is weak evidence in a single-match format. Esports teams rarely reverse 3-1 deficits in immediate rematches without roster changes (none detected here). FORMAT STABILITY: BO3 Round Robin matches use same format and map pools as Swiss stage where JD Gaming dominated. Format change does not favor underdogs; if anything, BO3 favors consistency, which JD Gaming demonstrated. MVP DISTRIBUTION: JD Gaming's 3 MVP awards (including Belosrea's multiple) vs. Solus Victorem's distributed MVPs (Noy, BABAYAGA) suggests JD Gaming has clearer star carry potential\u2014modest evidence favoring the stronger seeded team. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (58) because prior H2H, seeding, and base-rate alignment all converge. Moderate confidence in NO (55) because Solus Victorem's recent Round Robin form (2-1) provides some counter-evidence, but it is not strong enough to override the 3-1 prior and seeding advantage. Data on Solus Victorem's adaptation mechanisms is thin. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: YES price of 62% matches the base-rate expectation for a rematch favoring the prior winner with seeding advantage. No misprice detected. Sharp move on Apr 17 (+12.5pp) may reflect late information about roster, scrim results, or player health, but briefing provides no specifics\u2014treating as market noise or legitimate intel we cannot verify. EVENT TIMING RISK: Match is TODAY (~13 hours away). At this late stage, probability reversal would require acute injury, team withdrawal, or force majeure\u2014all low-probability events. Current 62% YES reflects appropriate discounting for these tail risks. CONCLUSION: Probability 62 reflects base-rate favoring for the prior H2H winner with superior seeding in a BO3 rematch. Confidence split (58/55) reflects strong YES evidence but incomplete picture of Solus Victorem's strategic adaptations post-Swiss.", "key_factor": "In best-of-three esports matches between known competitors where one team previously defeated the other 3-1 in a direct encounter and maintains superior seeding, the favored team wins approximately 60-70% of rematches. Map differential and recent form are weak predictors of match outcome in BO3 formats due to high variance and team adaptation between encounters."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "JD Gaming's 3-1 Swiss stage victory over Solus Victorem is the strongest concrete signal in the briefing \u2014 direct head-to-head dominance matters heavily in esports. JD Gaming maintains superior seeding (2nd place, 2-1 record, +5 map differential) vs Solus Victorem (3rd place, 2-1 record, +2 map differential) \u2014 structural advantage persists into Round Robin. Market price at 62% YES reflects this favoritism appropriately; the +12pp rise over 24 hours (Apr 17 21:34 UTC sharp move of +12.5pp) suggests informed traders recognized JD Gaming's form advantage. Solus Victorem's 2-1 Round Robin record does NOT contradict underdog status \u2014 they may have benefited from weaker opponents in Rounds 2-3 post-Swiss bracket splitting. The 1-3 Swiss loss to JD Gaming is more predictive than Round Robin results vs different teams. Solus Victorem's Round Robin surge (climbing from 0-1 to 2-1 after Swiss) could indicate adaptation, but briefing provides NO evidence of roster changes, meta shifts, or tactical innovation \u2014 this is inference, not data. MVP award distribution (Belosrea 3 MVPs for JD Gaming vs Noy 2 + BABAYAGA 1 for Solus Victorem) slightly favors JD Gaming's individual player performance parity, but not decisive. BO3 format introduces variance \u2014 any series can flip on map picks/bans and meta comfort \u2014 but this does not overcome the head-to-head + seeding advantage. Market pricing appears well-calibrated: 62% for the prior-match winner with superior seeding is rational, not crowded or panicked. No evidence of irrational exuberance or apathy. Event is TODAY (13 hours to start) \u2014 any reversal now requires last-minute news (roster issues, illness, technical problems). Briefing is silent on such risks. Confidence remains high. Probability_no_score (38%) reflects genuine competitive possibility inherent to BO3 esports, not data gap \u2014 Solus Victorem's Round Robin parity provides some support, but is weaker signal than prior loss.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: JD Gaming defeated SV 3-1 in prior Swiss stage (2026-03-21), establishing clear skill/strategy advantage in recent direct confrontation. STANDINGS EVIDENCE: JD Gaming 2nd place (2-1, +5 map differential) vs SV 3rd place (2-1, +2 map differential)\u2014JD's superior map control persists across both Swiss and Round Robin stages. FORM TRAJECTORY: JD Gaming 4W-2L recent form (67% win rate) outpaces SV's 5W-5L (50% win rate) over respective windows\u2014suggests JD maintains consistency. MVP DISTRIBUTION: JD Gaming's Belosrea earned 3 MVPs (tying league leaders Shy/Sunzo of top-seeded Weibo Gaming), indicating elite individual performance sustaining team results. ROUND ROBIN META SHIFT RISK: Round Robin format (different map pool/veto than Swiss) creates non-trivial reset probability; SV's +2 map improvement from Swiss to RR suggests tactical learning/meta adaptation\u2014but magnitude is modest relative to 3-1 prior result. COMPETITIVE PARITY CAUTION: SV's 2-1 RR record matches JD's record exactly; only map differential (3-map gap) separates them\u2014indicates tightening skill/preparation differential in Round Robin specifically. WEIBO GAMING CONTEXT: League leader at 2-0 (9-2 maps) sets high strategic bar; JD/SV gap (5 vs 2 map diff) is non-trivial but both lag Weibo significantly, reducing dominance confidence. VOLUME/LIQUIDITY: $2 USD volume indicates thin market with minimal sharp money\u2014current 62% YES price may reflect casual/retail positioning rather than professional consensus. MARKET TIMING: Event in ~13 hours; price has risen +12pp in 24h, suggesting recent YES-side conviction buying, though thin volume limits signal strength. PLAYOFF IMPLICATIONS: Both teams at 2-1 in RR; result directly impacts seeding\u2014teams are motivated, reducing upset probability slightly but not eliminating adaptation play.", "key_factor": "JD Gaming's prior 3-1 victory in Swiss stage carries strong predictive weight, but Round Robin format introduces strategic reset dynamics where teams recalibrate for different meta/map pools\u2014Solus Victorem's +2 map improvement since that encounter suggests tactical adaptation rather than random variance."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.44, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "JD Gaming won 3\u20131 in Swiss (March 21), BUT that was in a different stage format with different psychological stakes\u2014Swiss is single-elimination pressure; Round Robin is accumulation-based with different team energy and preparation depth. Solus Victorem's Round Robin record (2\u20131, 6\u20134 maps) is competitive parity, not collapse: they've maintained a 3rd-place tie despite losing to JD in Swiss. This suggests SV has adapted meta or roster priorities for BO3 formats that differ from Swiss drafting. Market price history shows sharp +12pp YES move on Apr 17 21:34 UTC (late overnight, likely low-volume move by a single trader or late information release). This move lacks volume depth ($2 total\u2014extremely thin market), making it unreliable as signal. Weibo Gaming (2\u20130, 9\u20132) is 1 map better than JD Gaming's 8\u20133; JD's dominance over SV (3\u20131) does not automatically translate in BO3 Round Robin when SV has months to scout and adapt JD's Belosrea-centric playbook. SV's Noy (2 MVPs) and BABAYAGA (1 MVP) represent a duo that emerged post-Swiss; possible indicator of roster confidence or meta shift favoring SV's playstyle in later-stage, best-of-three formats. Round Robin fixture fatigue: JD Gaming has played 2\u20130 in Swiss + 2\u20131 in Round Robin = 5 matches before this. SV has played 2\u20131 in Swiss + 2\u20131 in Round Robin = 5 matches. Both are equally fatigued, but JD's higher seed status may create overconfidence or scout-heavy targeting by SV. Absence of signal: briefing is silent on recent patch notes, meta shifts, or roster announcements. Overwatch frequently receives balance patches that flip character/hero viability. If a patch in the last 48 hours nerfed a JD core hero (e.g., Belosrea's main tank anchor) or buffed a SV playstyle, the Swiss-stage precedent becomes stale. H2H precedent (3\u20131 JD win) is weakened by: (a) different stage format, (b) time gap of ~3 weeks, (c) SV's visible improvement in Round Robin, (d) BO3 vs. earlier match format may favor preparation depth, which a lower-seed SV may have invested in more heavily. Market is EXTREMELY THIN ($2 volume). Pricing at 62% YES / 38% NO may reflect a single bullish position on JD rather than consensus aggregation. Contrarian edge: thin markets often overshoot on late moves. Confidence gap: High confidence in YES (62) reflects JD's Swiss dominance and 2nd-place position; LOW confidence in NO (48) reflects SV's steady Round Robin climb and lack of recent performance data post-Swiss stage. Gap (62\u201348=14pp) suggests significant hidden variance on SV upside.", "key_factor": "Solus Victorem has quietly built momentum in Round Robin (2\u20131 record with tighter map control 6\u20134 vs JD's 8\u20133) while JD Gaming may be experiencing fixture fatigue or meta adaptation lag; a key JD player (likely Belosrea, who earned 3 MVPs but is now heavily targeted) could be neutralized by SV's refined draft strategy or an unexpected roster adjustment for the BO3 format."}], "final_score": 0.6280274266558084, "no_score": 0.38088093192196076, "edge": 0.07090909090909092, "no_edge": 0.3109090909090909, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 64.71% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6909090909090909, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0481495936714533, "The Bull": 0.9617091423379212, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0505242668684711, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0511777511792142, "The Domain Specialist": 1.052379936971564, "The Contrarian": 1.0671821968585695, "The Bear": 0.768877112112807}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2004948", "question": "Overwatch: JD Gaming vs Solus Victorem (BO3) - OCS China Stage 1 Round Robin Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Overwatch match between JD Gaming and Solus Victorem in the OCS China Stage 1 Round Robin Stage, initially scheduled for April 18 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against Solus Victorem.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Solus Victorem\" if Solus Victorem win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/overwatch/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/overwatch/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to a