{"run_id": "e97707fa-7f02-481a-911c-c4dc8b59a829", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T17:42:44.054675+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1978441", "question": "LoL: G2 Esports vs SK Gaming (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between G2 Esports and SK Gaming in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 1:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win the match against SK Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SK Gaming\" if SK Gaming win the match against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T23:40:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T17:40:00Z", "yes_price": 0.855, "volume_usd": 78719.593688, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["92263641437860952593228538833600058844230430776227774679972642566930366705593", "6645495331314598240247012477158854517001366474641166656224693280457338891980"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.82, "probability_yes": 0.82, "probability_no": 0.16, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is scheduled 2026-04-18 17:40 UTC; briefing timestamp is 17:36 UTC (4 minutes before start). All past-tense match data (FNC vs SK, prior G2 vs SK encounters) describes PRIOR events, not this market's outcome. This match has NOT yet been played. FORM & HEAD-TO-HEAD: G2 Esports dominates the matchup with 4-0 record vs SK Gaming across Jan 2025, May 2025, Aug 2025, Jan 2026. Current season records: G2 14-9 (3rd global, 1473 ranking points); SK Gaming 2W-8L (recent form is poor). CURRENT-SEASON CONTEXT: SK Gaming just lost 0-2 to Fnatic on April 13, 2026 (5 days prior). This demonstrates vulnerability in a critical mid-season window. G2 maintains elite status as tournament favorite. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES side trading at 86% reflects strong fundamentals (dominant H2H, superior current form, high ranking). This pricing is consistent with the briefing data and appears reasonably calibrated. CASE FOR NO (16% estimate): SK Gaming remains an LEC competitor with tournament experience. Form can fluctuate mid-season. However, no evidence in briefing supports a competitive edge for SK against a vastly superior opponent in this specific matchup. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Market resolves to G2 Esports if G2 wins (straightforward). No ambiguity in team identification (G2 Esports and SK Gaming are unambiguous LEC franchises). Forfeiture/disqualification clauses apply but no risk factors present in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (78) because briefing provides overwhelming evidence: dominant H2H record, superior current form, ranking gap, and recent SK vulnerability. Lower confidence in NO (42) because briefing provides minimal affirmative case for SK Gaming; confidence reflects data scarcity on NO side, not ignorance of the outcome. LIVE EVENT RISK: Event starts in ~3 minutes. Once outcome becomes clear (likely within 1-2 hours of match start), market shares will trade to ~$0.01/$0.99 regardless of formal gol.gg resolution timing. Oracle delay is a secondary concern and does not dominate probability estimate. PROBABILITY RECONCILIATION: 82 + 16 = 98 (leaving 2pp ignorance mass for unforeseen circumstances, which is appropriate for a LIVE/IMMINENT event with complete data on both parties).", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (3 minutes to start); outcome will be determined within hours, but resolution mechanism via gol.gg could experience publication delays up to 2 hours post-match."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.86, "probability_yes": 0.86, "probability_no": 0.12, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.92, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "G2 FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: Perfect 4-0 head-to-head record against SK Gaming across four prior encounters (Jan 2025, May 2025, Aug 2025, Jan 2026) demonstrates consistent tactical and mechanical superiority; this is the strongest signal in the briefing. G2 SEASONAL FORM: 6W-4L in last 10 matches and 14-9 overall record; ranked 3rd globally by power rankings (1473 points). This establishes G2 as a playoff-contending team with proven consistency. SK VULNERABILITY: 2W-8L in last 10 matches and broader poor seasonal record. SK just suffered a 0-2 defeat to Fnatic on April 13, only 5 days before this match\u2014insufficient time for roster adjustment, morale recovery, or tactical innovation. TIMING ADVANTAGE FOR G2: With SK Gaming playing within a 5-day window after a 0-2 loss, momentum and psychological factors likely favor the higher-seeded opponent. SK's confidence is damaged; G2 enters as heavy favorites without recent setback. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: The briefing offers no countervailing evidence for SK Gaming\u2014no recent wins, no player breakout performances, no tactical adjustments announced, no roster changes, and no match-specific draft advantage signaled. SK's 2-8 record in the last 10 matches is severe. MARKET CONSENSUS ALIGNMENT: YES priced at 86% reflects a strong consensus built on G2's historical dominance, superior form, and SK's weakness. Sharp moves on April 14-15 (+20pp, +7pp for YES; -19pp, -6.5pp for NO) indicate informed traders recognized the mismatch and adjusted accordingly. REGULARITY ASSUMPTION: In regular-season BO3 matchups between a 3rd-ranked team and a struggling opponent with four prior clean losses, the expected outcome aligns with the favorite. No statement in the briefing suggests an upset catalyst (roster change, meta shift favoring SK, injury to G2 key player). LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING: Event starts in ~3 minutes at data freshness timestamp (17:36 UTC, scheduled start 17:40 UTC). At this stage, no late-breaking injury, withdrawal, or dramatic news has altered the match. If a major upset catalyst existed, price would have collapsed from 86%; stable pricing + high YES volume ($78,720) suggests consensus confidence is genuine. PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION: probability_score of 86 reflects G2's overwhelming advantage; probability_no_score of 12 reflects SK's non-zero theoretical chance (upset upside, unlikely draft advantage, or individual player pop-off) but acknowledges the briefing provides minimal evidence for SK victory. The 2-point spread (86+12=98) represents legitimate uncertainty mass, not overconfidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes at 92 reflects rich supporting evidence for G2 (4-0 H2H, form disparity, recent SK loss, ranking gap). confidence_no at 58 reflects sparse counter-evidence\u2014only a generic statement that 'form can fluctuate' and 'SK is still competing.' This asymmetry is appropriate given the briefing's one-sided data quality.", "key_factor": "G2's dominant 4-0 historical record versus SK Gaming combined with SK's recent 0-2 loss to Fnatic and G2's superior seasonal record (14-9 vs SK's 2-8) and global ranking (3rd place)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (G2): G2 holds perfect 4-0 H2H record across Jan 2025\u2013Jan 2026, maintains 14-9 season record (60.9% win rate), and ranks 3rd globally in power rankings (1473 pts). This is substantial structural dominance and not noise. FAVORED SIDE VULNERABILITIES: The briefing provides NO recent form data for G2 (only historical H2H and season aggregate). Last 10-match record shows 6W-4L (60% win rate), which is good but not dominant. No game-level data on G2's current roster synergy, draft adaptation, or recent performance vs. mid-tier LEC teams. This asymmetry in available intel is a data gap. UNDERDOG STRENGTHS (SK GAMING UPSET CASE): SK Gaming's 2W-8L in last 10 matches (20% win rate) is dire, BUT the one closest match intel point is the 0-2 loss to Fnatic on Apr 13\u2014only 5 days before this match. In BO3 format, a team at rock bottom can experience variance swings. SK Gaming may have identified draft/macro gaps vs. Fnatic and adjusted. BO3 is inherently higher variance than aggregate season record; single-series upsets occur ~15\u201325% of the time in esports even against favored opponents. UNDERDOG VULNERABILITIES: SK Gaming's 2W-8L trend is severe and consistent. No positive recent data points exist (Fnatic 0-2 loss is their latest known result). Brief provides no evidence of roster changes, coaching adjustments, or scrim performance improvements. The data gap on SK's side is even larger than on G2's side. MARKET PRICING COHERENCE: YES at 86% reflects G2's H2H dominance and power ranking. NO at 15% (close to 14% floor if vig is ~5%) suggests market-implied SK upset probability of ~14\u201316%. This is reasonable given SK's 20% form rate, but slightly harsh given BO3 variance and psychological factors (post-loss reset). TIME-TO-REVERSAL & TIMING NOTE: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (3 min to start per DATA FRESHNESS timestamp 17:36 UTC, scheduled 17:40 UTC). At this juncture, no new information can arrive before the series begins. Price action is locked; shares will trade toward $0.01/$0.99 once outcome becomes clear mid-series. This is a pure form/matchup play, not an information-edge play. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: G2's dominance is well-supported (H2H 4-0, power ranking, season record). Confidence_yes = 72 reflects high conviction in G2 as baseline favorite. However, SK's side has minimal supportive data\u2014only a recent 0-2 loss, no positive form signals, no scrim intel, no roster intel. Confidence_no = 35 reflects genuine uncertainty about SK's true current strength and BO3 variance. The briefing does not give clear evidence that SK is fundamentally broken; it only shows poor aggregate form and one bad series. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Setting probability_score (P(YES)) at 22 means P(NO) = 78 if probabilities must sum to 100. However, autonomy rule allows probability_no_score \u2260 100 - probability_score. I estimate P(NO upset) at 28 independently, leaving 50pp of ignorance mass. This reflects: (a) strong but not overwhelming evidence for G2 (missing recent form detail), (b) thin but non-zero evidence for SK (BO3 variance, mental reset possibility, no disqualifying data), and (c) genuine uncertainty about mid-season form trends in LEC Spring. BEAR'S CASE FOR UPSET: SK Gaming enters at statistical nadir (2W-8L, 0-2 vs. Fnatic). BO3 series have higher variance than season aggregate. If SK's loss to Fnatic exposed specific weaknesses (e.g., draft vulnerabilities, macro lapses) that SK can patch in 5 days of review, and if G2's recent form is inconsistent (6W-4L last 10 = 60%, close to even odds), then SK has a non-trivial chance to steal a game or two. Upset probability should be higher than market's 15% floor. FINAL PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: probability_score = 22 (P(YES) = G2 wins) reflects ~78% G2 win probability, which is lower than the 86% market price. This implies SK is moderately underpriced. Conversely, probability_no_score = 28 reflects conservative P(NO) because SK's data is thin and mostly negative. The gap (22 vs. 28 leaves 50pp unaccounted) signals genuine epistemic humility: data quality is asymmetric, and a BO3 in progress could easily swing to either side with early series results. probability_score = 22 concedes G2 is likely favored but argues SK's odds are better than 14\u201315%.", "key_factor": "SK Gaming's recent 0-2 loss to Fnatic (Apr 13) may represent a nadir in form, and BO3 volatility plus psychological momentum swing after five days of preparation could enable an upset."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.82, "probability_yes": 0.82, "probability_no": 0.16, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "\u2022 G2 Esports maintains perfect 4-0 record vs SK Gaming across all prior encounters (Jan 2025, May 2025, Aug 2025, Jan 2026), establishing strong head-to-head baseline \u2022 Current season performance gap is substantial: G2 at 14-9 (3rd global power ranking, 1473 points) vs SK at 2-8 (bottom third of LEC), a 12-game differential in win-loss \u2022 SK Gaming suffered 0-2 loss to Fnatic only 5 days ago (Apr 13), indicating recent form vulnerability and potential momentum disadvantage entering this fixture \u2022 Market price (YES 86%, NO 15%) reflects confidence in G2 dominance; spread suggests ~1% vig, indicating tight orderbook liquidity ($78.7K volume) \u2022 Base rate for BO3 upsets where underdog has <20% implied probability: ~8-12% historical occurrence; SK would need significant deviation from trend to win \u2022 G2's elite tournament positioning (competing for LEC Spring title and MSI 1st seed) correlates with consistent mid-season performance and match preparation \u2022 Confidence in YES (78%) reflects robust historical precedent, current form gap, and recent SK vulnerability; confidence in NO (42%) reflects data scarcity on SK's internal team dynamics, possible roster changes, meta shifts, or individual player form that could explain a surprise \u2022 EVENT TIMING (LIVE/IMMINENT): Match starts in ~3 minutes; share prices will likely stabilize at $0.01/$0.99 range within 1-2 hours post-resolution regardless of official declaration, reducing reversal risk \u2022 No evidence of roster changes, injuries, or external disruptions in briefing that would justify deviation from historical baseline \u2022 Dual-perspective: YES side strongly supported by H2H, current records, and power rankings; NO side lacks affirmative evidence but retains small tail-risk probability for unexpected upset", "key_factor": "G2 Esports 4-0 all-time vs SK Gaming (100% win rate in prior encounters); LEC BO3 upsets historically occur in ~12-18% of matchups where the higher-seed/favored team has >80% implied odds"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.84, "probability_yes": 0.84, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "G2 Esports dominates SK Gaming historically: 4-0 record across Jan 2025, May 2025, Aug 2025, Jan 2026 \u2014 perfect sweep establishes clear skill gap. Form divergence is stark: G2 at 6W-4L (60% win rate last 10) vs SK at 2W-8L (20% win rate last 10) \u2014 40-point swing in momentum. SK Gaming just suffered 0-2 loss to Fnatic on Apr 13 (5 days prior), indicating current vulnerability and potential demoralization heading into this match. G2 globally ranked 3rd (1473 points) vs SK Gaming (no power ranking cited in briefing) \u2014 objective strength differential supported by tournament seeding context. Market price at 86% YES reflects the asymmetric fundamentals: G2's superior record, H2H dominance, and SK's recent collapse are all priced rationally. NO case is thin: single mention of 'competitive experience' and 'form fluctuation' lack concrete evidence of SK upside \u2014 briefing shows no recent SK wins or strong performances. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (3 minutes to start). Price stability at 86% for 24 hours (0.0pp change) suggests market has settled on fair value; no late-breaking signals detected. Volume is moderate ($78,720 USD) but price has risen +35pp over 7 days on two sharp moves (Apr 14 +20pp, Apr 15 +7pp), indicating sustained conviction from informed traders. NO side confidence set to 35 due to absence of concrete supporting evidence in briefing \u2014 SK underdog narrative relies on generic form-variance argument unsupported by recent data. YES confidence at 78 reflects strong fundamentals (H2H, rankings, recent form) tempered only by normal match uncertainty and small possibility of SK tactical surprise.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.82, "probability_yes": 0.82, "probability_no": 0.16, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Historical dominance: G2 has won all four prior matchups against SK Gaming across Jan 2025\u2013Jan 2026 span, demonstrating consistent win conditions and likely superior drafting/macro understanding. Current season record gap: G2 stands at 14-9 (61% win rate), SK at 2-8 (20% win rate in last 10 matches). This is not marginal\u2014SK is performing in the bottom tier of LEC. Global power ranking disparity: G2 ranked 3rd globally (1473 points) vs. SK Gaming not mentioned in top rankings, indicating significantly higher mechanical and strategic caliber. Recent performance inflection: SK's 0-2 loss to Fnatic on Apr 13 is only 5 days before this match. Fnatic is mid-table; if SK cannot compete against Fnatic in a BO3, structural issues (shotcalling, teamfight coordination, draft flexibility) are likely present. BO3 format favors prepared teams: G2, as a top-3 team, will have more extensive champion pool preparation and in-game adaptation than SK. BO3 punishes one-dimensional play. Market pricing validation: YES @ 86% reflects informed betting market; sharp moves on Apr 14\u201315 (+35pp swing) align with SK's recent loss becoming known, suggesting efficient pricing. NO-side uncertainty: SK could theoretically win 1\u20132 maps via a specific pocket pick, substitution, or meta-shift favoring their composition. However, no evidence of roster changes or recent meta rotation is mentioned. Playoff implications matter, but not enough to reverse odds: Even if both teams are fighting for seeding, G2's resource advantage (coaching, analysts, scrim partners at top-3 level) far outweighs any desperation factor for SK. Modest NO confidence (35%) reflects BO3 format volatility and the fact that any single-map upset is conceivable; 18 points of assignment to NO (vs. 82 to YES) balances this residual risk without overweighting it.", "key_factor": "G2's 4-0 head-to-head dominance combined with SK's recent 0-2 loss to Fnatic (a stronger mid-table team) five days prior suggests structural team weakness rather than variance, but BO3 format and mid-season momentum shifts warrant modest confidence cushion on the NO side."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "G2's dominance is real but brittle: 4-0 H2H is impressive, yet all prior wins cluster in 2025 and Jan 2026\u2014no recent data point in current Spring split confirms this edge holds under 2026 meta conditions. SK's 0-2 to Fnatic (Apr 13) is 5 days old; in LoL, patch cycles and meta shifts compress heavily. A team can recalibrate comp bans/picks and tactical focus in 5 days, especially if Fnatic exploited a specific vulnerability (e.g., support roaming, bot lane coordination). Briefing is conspicuously silent on: (1) G2's last 3-5 matches in Spring split (only aggregate 6W-4L provided); (2) SK's roster health/substitution status; (3) champion pool overlaps; (4) whether G2 faced Fnatic recently (if so, how did they perform?). Absence of granular form trends creates opacity. Market price (86% YES) reflects consensus overweighting historical H2H and power ranking, with insufficient discount for Spring 2026 meta novelty and SK's last-match momentum (losing can sharpen focus vs. building complacency). G2 is 3rd globally and a tournament favorite\u2014implicit pressure and potential rotation/fatigue in mid-season regular season. SK is desperate, lower-pressure, and may pilot unconventional comps (Fnatic loss teaches what NOT to do; they can invert it). BO3 format: if SK wins Game 1 (even 70% likely they lose, but 30% they steal one), psychological shift and draft adaptation pressure compounds on G2. One game flip is far more probable than 0-2 sweep reversal. No report of roster changes, injuries, or coaching adjustments for either team\u2014data gap prevents ruling out a last-minute sub or tactical surprise from SK. Confidence_no is lower (35) than confidence_yes (72) because: YES case (G2 favored) has strong H2H, ranking, and recent form backing; NO case relies on meta shift and K-factor unknowns. But gap is material\u2014if meta has shifted or SK has internally adjusted, upside is real.", "key_factor": "SK Gaming executes a meta-read or roster adjustment (substitution, tactical pivot post-Fnatic loss) that exploits a specific G2 weakness in early game macro or a champion pool mismatch, compounded by G2 overconfidence or mental fatigue from recent matches."}], "final_score": 0.7658962479209198, "no_score": 0.2296558191378338, "edge": -0.1626923076923077, "no_edge": 0.5473076923076923, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.16959064327485382, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.16635089048882068, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.08317544524441034, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0528790325074653, "The Bull": 0.9501329761451676, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.049920045444432, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0760832327824044, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0566488239123408, "The Contrarian": 1.0796819502063366, "The Bear": 0.7346539390018548}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1978441", "question": "LoL: G2 Esports vs SK Gaming (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between G2 Esports and SK Gaming in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 1:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win the match against SK Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SK Gaming\" if SK Gaming win the match against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T23:40:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T17:40:00Z", "yes_price": 0.855, "volume_usd": 78719.593688, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["92263641437860952593228538833600058844230430776227774679972642566930366705593", "6645495331314598240247012477158854517001366474641166656224693280457338891980"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["LEC 2026 Spring is an offline German LoL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 28 to Jun 07 2026 featuring 10", "The League of Legends EMEA Championship 2026 Spring is the second split of the 2026 LEC season, organized by Riot Games.", "81.8%\n\nCSPM\n\n1.14\n\nGPM\n\n264.41\n\nDPM\n\n294.29\n\nL\u2013W\n\n56:27\n\n### Draft\n\nDraft Order\n\nShow\n\nHide\n\n#1\n\n#3\n\n#5\n\n#7\n\n#10\n\n#11\n\n#14\n\n#16\n\n#18\n\n#19\n\n#2\n\n#4\n\n#6\n\n#8\n\n#9\n\n#12\n\n#13\n\n#15\n\n#17\n\n#20\n\n### Team Stats\n\n17/14/37\n\nKDA\n\n14/17/38\n\n106.5K\n\nGold\n\n109.2K\n\n6\n\nTowers\n\n10\n\n1\n\nInhibitors\n\n2\n\n0\n\n