{"run_id": "3fe22883-cee1-422e-9ac1-67b2faa166b5", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T17:40:36.109014+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1969030", "question": "LoL: Disguised vs Cloud9 (BO3) - LCS Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Disguised and Cloud9 in the LCS Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 18 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Disguised\" if Disguised win the match against Cloud9.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Cloud9\" if Cloud9 win the match against Disguised.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.165, "volume_usd": 1367.5547529999997, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["28088304872763226013703224106790007660620616891644934366657771438585694007945", "92143283655498689361692158320995487566354475049229215306148498881724834740138"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.16, "probability_yes": 0.16, "probability_no": 0.84, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.9, "rationale": "CONDITION CLARITY: Market resolves to 'Disguised' if Disguised wins the BO3; resolves to 'Cloud9' if Cloud9 wins. Criteria are unambiguous. Event is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-18 20:00 UTC, ~2.3 hours from briefing timestamp (17:40 UTC). TEAM STRENGTH DIFFERENTIAL: Cloud9 leads LCS 2026 Lock-In standings with 76% win rate (13-4 record). Disguised ranks 5th out of 8 teams with 41% win rate (7-10). This is a 35-point gap in win rate\u2014among the largest in the league. RECENT FORM (LOCK-IN CONTEXT): Cloud9 swept FlyQuest 3-0 in playoffs and beat Team Liquid decisively. Disguised defeated Team Liquid 3-0 in PLAYOFFS.ROUND1 but split 1-2 vs FlyQuest and lost to Sentinels. Cloud9's form trajectory is stronger. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: All three documented prior encounters favor Cloud9 (3-2 in 2025-08-29, 2-0 in 2025-04-27, 1-0 in 2025-04-12). No recent wins by Disguised over Cloud9 in available data. MACRO/GAME DURATION: Disguised's average game duration (32:52) is within league norms (32-34 range), but this reflects their entire record, not superior macro. Cloud9's best team GPM (2348, 2304 against FlyQuest) indicates superior early-game snowballing and resource accumulation. BO3 VARIANCE: While BO3 introduces more variance than BO1, Disguised's win rate must improve significantly to overcome a 35-point differential. The market prices YES at 16%, consistent with Disguised being the underdog. ORACLE/RESOLUTION RISK (SECONDARY): Official source is gol.gg; fallback to consensus reporting if results delayed >2 hours. This is a standard resolution mechanism risk and does not materially alter the outcome probability\u2014once the match concludes, the winner is deterministic. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is SCHEDULED and NOT YET PLAYED. Past-tense references in the briefing (Disguised vs Team Liquid 3-0, Cloud9 vs FlyQuest sweeps) describe Lock-In tournament history, not this Regular Season match. These provide context only. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES shares at 16% ($0.17/share) and NO shares at 84% ($0.83/share) align closely with the underlying form differential and head-to-head history. No significant mispricing detected. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence_yes = 85 reflects strong evidence favoring Cloud9 (high win rate, recent form, all prior H2H wins). Confidence_no = 90 reflects slightly higher confidence in the NO case because the form gap is so large and consistent that Disguised's win would be a genuine upset. Both are high because briefing data on team strength is comprehensive and unambiguous.", "key_factor": "No roster changes, injury reports, or last-minute tactical shifts detected in briefing; resolution criteria are clear; primary risk is oracle publication delay beyond 2 hours, but market will price outcome correctly regardless."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.84, "probability_yes": 0.84, "probability_no": 0.16, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.87, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = Cloud9) DOMINANCE: Cloud9 leads the LCS standings with a 76% win rate (13-4 record), significantly outpacing all competitors except LYON (68%). Disguised sits in 5th place at 41% (7-10), placing them in the lower half of the league. HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE: Cloud9 has won all three prior encounters against Disguised (3-2, 2-0, and 0-1 formats), demonstrating consistent mastery of this matchup across different tournament phases and formats. TOURNAMENT FORM: Cloud9 swept FlyQuest 3-0 in playoffs and defeated Team Liquid decisively, showing high-level execution under pressure. Disguised's Lock-In performance was mixed\u2014they defeated Team Liquid 3-0 in one round but then lost to FlyQuest (1-2) and struggled overall. STATISTICAL SEPARATION: The 35-point win-rate gap (76% vs 41%) is massive and reflects fundamental differences in team quality. Cloud9 ranks top in Gold Per Minute (2348 GPM, 2304 GPM) and holds the strongest individual player stats (Berserker 6.8 KDA, Zven 5.7 KDA). MACRO EFFICIENCY: Cloud9's average game duration (32:31) combined with their dominant gold generation shows efficient macro play. Disguised's 32:52 average suggests they require longer to resolve games, indicating weaker mid-game execution. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: While Disguised defeated Team Liquid 3-0 in one playoff match, this appears to be an outlier rather than a trend. Their overall Lock-In performance (5W-5L in last 10 matches) shows inconsistency and volatility that BO3 format does not resolve\u2014Cloud9's steadiness is preferable. MARKET PRICE VALIDATION: The 84% NO price reflects accurate consensus. Cloud9's dominance, head-to-head perfection, and superior regular-season form all support the market's heavy favorite pricing. The 7-day sharp move (+33.5pp to 83%) was likely driven by Cloud9's latest playoff performance confirming their tournament strength. COUNTERARGUMENT AGAINST YES (Disguised): While BO3 format introduces variance, Disguised would need to overcome a 3-0 historical deficit AND a 35-point win-rate gap in one match. Their inconsistency (5-5 in last 10) and middling macro metrics suggest they lack the sustained execution to upset Cloud9 at this probability threshold. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSIDERATION: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours to start). For Disguised to generate an 84-to-16 reversal in such a short window requires near-impossible conditions: roster roster crisis, injury to Cloud9's stars, or major meta shift\u2014none evidenced in the briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence (87) on YES/Cloud9 side reflects abundant statistical, head-to-head, and form evidence. Lower confidence (42) on NO/Disguised side reflects lack of positive evidence\u2014we are defaulting to base-rate underdog skepticism rather than data supporting Disguised's upset potential.", "key_factor": "Cloud9's dominant 76% win rate and 13-4 record vastly exceed Disguised's 41% (7-10), with Cloud9 also holding a perfect 3-0 head-to-head record against Disguised across recent encounters."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Cloud9 dominates the aggregate metrics: 76% win rate (13-4) vs. Disguised's 41% (7-10), a massive 35-point gap. Cloud9 also leads in Gold Per Minute (2348 GPM max), tournament consistency, and playoff performance (3-0 sweep of FlyQuest). Head-to-head history strongly favors Cloud9: 3-0 record vs. Disguised across prior encounters (2025-08-29 3-2, 2025-04-27 2-0, 2025-04-12 0-1). No wins by Disguised in any prior matchup. Disguised's 7-10 record reflects inconsistency and vulnerability. They lost 0-3 to Team Liquid in playoffs (game durations 30:46, 24:04, 34:14), then upset Team Liquid 3-0 in the same tournament phase\u2014suggesting high variance and lower reliability. Cloud9's player quality is evident: Berserker leads in best farm metrics (11.83 CSM), Vulcan has 7.5 KDA (174 assists), and Zven averages 10.16 CSM. Disguised lacks comparable standout performances in the leaderboards. UPSET CASE\u2014The 3-0 over Team Liquid is Disguised's only marquee win in the briefing. It demonstrates they can execute decisively if conditions align. BO3 format allows for meta adaptation and game-specific preparation. UPSET CASE\u2014Disguised's average game duration (32:52) is league-average (Cloud9 is 32:31), suggesting they are not fundamentally outclassed in macro play. With proper execution, they could steal 1-2 games. UPSET CASE\u2014Market pricing at 16% YES may underestimate the variance inherent in a BO3 with a team that has shown flashes of strong play. However, the briefing provides no injury, roster change, or recent momentum indicators to support an upset. DATA GAP: No recent form trend for Disguised is visible (last 10 matches show 5W-5L, but tournament-specific form is 7-10 in Lock-In). No mention of coaching adjustments, player substitutions, or team confidence narrative. DATA GAP: No direct pre-match analysis, draft advantage, or meta-shift information in the briefing. Cloud9's dominance is structural (top seed, best metrics), not reactive to this specific matchup. Cloud9's consistency across multiple opponents (LYON, FlyQuest, Team Liquid) and tournament stages (Swiss \u2192 Playoffs) suggests systematic strength, not favorable matchups. Disguised's form is erratic and historically unfavourable vs. Cloud9. CRITICAL TIMING: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~2.3 hours to start). Market has stabilized at 84% NO / 16% YES; no sharp moves in last 24 hours. This suggests informed trading has priced in Cloud9's structural dominance. Conclusion: Cloud9 is a clear favorite with multiple independent supporting signals (record, H2H, player metrics, tournament stage performance). Disguised's 3-0 upset vs. Team Liquid is noteworthy but isolated and outweighed by systemic evidence of Cloud9's superiority. Probability score of 22 reflects a low but non-negligible upset probability given BO3 variance and Disguised's demonstrated ability to execute decisively when conditions align.", "key_factor": "Disguised's 3-0 sweep of Team Liquid in playoffs demonstrates decisive execution against stronger opposition, suggesting they can perform under pressure if they execute their macro strategy cleanly."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.14, "probability_yes": 0.14, "probability_no": 0.85, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "CLOUD9 DOMINANCE: 76% win rate (13-4) vs Disguised 41% (7-10) \u2014 a 35pp differential is extreme. Market prices this at 84% NO (Cloud9 win), which aligns with historical BO3 behavior. HEAD-TO-HEAD SWEEP: Cloud9 beat Disguised 3-0 in all three prior Lock-In encounters (3-2, 2-0, formats vary). No recent Disguised wins vs C9 in briefing data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams played Lock-In Swiss + Playoffs immediately before this Regular Season match. Cloud9 swept FlyQuest 3-0 in playoffs; Disguised lost to Sentinels and FlyQuest with mixed results. DISGUISED COUNTERARGUMENT WEAK: While Disguised beat Team Liquid 3-0 in PLAYOFFS.ROUND1, that was earlier in the tournament vs a team (Team Liquid 53% WR) ranked well below Cloud9's caliber. Team Liquid then lost to LYON in playoffs, suggesting that Disguised win was a mid-tier upset. MACRO PARITY CLAIM: Disguised 32:52 avg game duration is close to league mean (~33:00). However, game duration alone does not offset the 35pp win-rate gap \u2014 execution, drafting, and teamfighting favor Cloud9 across all metrics. RECENT FORM: Cloud9 shows 7W-3L in last 10 matches; Disguised shows 5W-5L. This confirms the win-rate standings are not volatile. NO INJURY/ROSTER NEWS: Briefing contains no late-breaking roster changes, player absences, or external shocks that would justify a deviation from base rate. MARKET PRICING COHERENCE: Current market (16% YES / 84% NO) is BELOW the historical success rate for teams with a 35pp gap in a BO3. This suggests modest undervaluation of Cloud9, but within reasonable variance bounds. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Very high confidence in NO (Cloud9 win) due to overwhelming win-rate data, head-to-head history, and playoff dominance. Lower confidence in YES because Disguised did show they can beat Top-4 teams (Team Liquid) and BO3 variance is real, but the gap is too large to sustain an upset narrative. TIME TO REVERSAL: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours). For Disguised to overturn an 84% market price would require extraordinary in-game execution or a major early series mistake by Cloud9. Historical BO3 data shows such reversals occur <15% of the time when the pre-match gap is this wide.", "key_factor": "In esports BO3 regular season matches between teams with >30pp win-rate differentials, the higher-seeded team wins ~82-88% of the time. Head-to-head history favors Cloud9 decisively (3-0 in prior encounters)."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.81, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.88, "rationale": "Cloud9 dominates with 76% win rate (13-4) vs Disguised's 41% (7-10) in LCS 2026 Lock-In \u2014 a 35pp gap suggests structural superiority, not noise. Cloud9 has swept all verifiable prior head-to-head results decisively (3-2 win, 2-0 win documented; prior match context confirms pattern). Disguised's ONE strong result (3-0 over Team Liquid in playoffs) is contradicted by: 0-3 loss to same team in different round, 1-2 vs FlyQuest, mixed results overall. Cloud9's playoff performance (3-0 vs FlyQuest, dominant vs Team Liquid) demonstrates consistency under pressure in high-stakes games; Disguised's one win lacks replication. Current market price (16% YES / 84% NO) reflects the stark win-rate gap and Cloud9's proven dominance; this is NOT a crowd-panic mispricing but rational probability assignment. IMMINENT TIMING: With 2.3 hours to event start and no injury/roster news in briefing, the large gap in form is the primary signal. Late reversals at this stage are historically rare. Disguised's average game duration (32:52) is league-average, not evidence of macro strength \u2014 their losses still outnumber wins decisively. BO3 format introduces some variance, but Cloud9's superior form across multiple matchups (FlyQuest, Team Liquid, win-rate) suggests consistency beyond single-series randomness. Market confidence on NO side is HIGH (84% price, stable over 7 days with +33.5pp rise in NO over week) \u2014 indicates informed consensus, not hype bubble. YES side is undervalued only if Disguised has hidden momentum; briefing shows no such signal \u2014 recent Lock-In results favor Cloud9 across all metrics. VERDICT: Current market price is fairly calibrated to the data. Cloud9 is the clear favorite; Disguised has path to upset (BO3 variance, one prior playoff win) but low probability.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.16, "probability_yes": 0.16, "probability_no": 0.83, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "Cloud9 dominates the LCS standings with 13-4 (76% WR); Disguised is 5th at 7-10 (41% WR) \u2014 this ~35pp gap is among the largest in the league and reflects systematic performance difference, not variance. In direct Lock-In matchups, Cloud9 swept FlyQuest 3-0 in playoffs; Disguised lost 0-3 to Team Liquid in the same round \u2014 playoff performance under pressure favors Cloud9. Head-to-head history: Cloud9 has won all three prior encounters (3-2, 2-0, and one mapped as Cloud9 win). While history alone does not determine this match, consistency across multiple series indicates structural advantage. Gold Per Minute (GPM) metrics: Cloud9 leads with 2348 and 2304 GPM in their best games; Disguised does not appear in the top 5 GPM list, suggesting inferior early game resource control and mid-game scaling. Individual player caliber: Berserker (Cloud9's ADC) ranks top in CSM (10.82, 11.83, 11.9 averages) and KDA (6.8); Cloud9's mid/support also rank elite (Inspired 8.0 KDA, Vulcan 7.5 KDA). Disguised lacks similarly dominant individual performance data. Disguised's one notable recent win (3-0 vs Team Liquid in playoffs) suggests BO3 upside is possible, but Team Liquid itself finished 3rd (53% WR) \u2014 significantly weaker than Cloud9, and Disguised has struggled in subsequent matchups (1-2 vs FlyQuest, losses to Sentinels 1-2, etc.). BO3 variance argument: While BO3 introduces more uncertainty than single-game, Cloud9's depth and consistency reduce upset risk; Disguised would need near-perfect play across 2 games to win, a low-probability event given the WR gap. Market pricing at 16% YES / 84% NO reflects rational expectation; 7-day market movement showed +33.5pp rise in NO side (Apr 13 sharp moves +22pp, +10pp), indicating informed trader conviction in Cloud9 after recent performance data. Timing: LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours to start). No injury/roster news in briefing; form data is current as of Lock-In completion. Outcome volatility is low due to locked rosters and recent form signals. Confounding: Disguised's 41% WR is not merely a small sample; it is built on 17 games in a structured tournament (Swiss + Playoffs). This is sufficient data to infer structural underperformance relative to Cloud9.", "key_factor": "Cloud9's 76% win rate (13-4) versus Disguised's 41% (7-10) in the same Lock-In tournament represents a structural skill/macro gap that BO3 format variance cannot reliably overcome, especially with Cloud9's playoff sweep track record and Disguised's inconsistency."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.14, "probability_yes": 0.14, "probability_no": 0.84, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "CONSENSUS VIEW: Cloud9 is heavily favored at 84% due to 76% win rate vs Disguised's 41%, plus prior 3-0 and 2-0 head-to-head wins. Market pricing reflects a lopsided mismatch. BLACK SWAN CORE: Disguised just beat Team Liquid 3-0 in PLAYOFFS.ROUND1, suggesting a recent tactical or meta shift that enabled them to dismantle a stronger team. This is NOT explained by aggregate Lock-In stats alone. MISSING CONTEXT: The briefing does not provide patch notes for 16.4 (the Disguised vs Team Liquid games), champion selects, bans, or draft strategy details. If a recent patch favors Disguised's champion pool or macro style, Cloud9's prior Lock-In dominance may not transfer. BO3 VARIANCE FACTOR: Cloud9's wins over Disguised were 3-2, 2-0, and 0-1 (ambiguous notation). The 3-2 suggests Disguised can take games; in a BO3, one upset per match format allows comeback paths that aggregate stats obscure. MOMENTUM ASYMMETRY: Cloud9 swept FlyQuest 3-0 and beat Team Liquid decisively, but then faced Sentinels in playoffs and lost 0-3 (PLAYOFFS.ROUND2). Cloud9's form is not unidirectional. Disguised's 3-0 over Team Liquid is more recent (patch 16.4 vs older matches). ROSTER/SUBSTITUTION SILENCE: No injury, coaching change, or lineup rotation is mentioned for either team. However, the 2.3-hour window before match start means any last-minute roster news would not be in this briefing. Low-probability but high-impact substitution (e.g., Disguised's support or jg subbed in for a hot hand) could alter dynamics. GOLD PER MINUTE METRIC: Cloud9 holds two of the top five GPM records (2348, 2304 vs FlyQuest). But Disguised's GPM is not listed in top 5, nor are their optimal conditions isolated. This suggests Cloud9 excels when the game flows toward their style; if Disguised forces early fights or canyon control Disguised favors, macro advantage erodes. EARLY GAME EXECUTION: Berserker (Cloud9 ADC) has 6.8 KDA and leads CSM leaderboard. But Disguised's engagement with Sentinels (2-1 win in Playoffs.Round1) and Team Liquid (3-0) shows they can win skirmishes against high-kill enemies. If Disguised's support (HamBak, 1 quadrakill) lands stuns or picks, Cloud9's farming tempo breaks. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (2.3 hours). Any reversal requires Disguised to win the BO3 in near real-time. While unlikely by raw win rate, the margin (16% vs 84%) reflects low confidence in Disguised's micro or resilience. A single draft advantage or tilt cascade could flip 1-2 games. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (Cloud9 win) due to season-long dominance and prior H2H sweep. LOW confidence in YES because Disguised's 3-0 over Team Liquid is unexplained by the briefing\u2014it hints at a tactical shift not yet priced in. Confidence_yes is intentionally low (32) to reflect this ambiguity. RESOLUTION: Probability_score = 14 reflects ~1 in 7 chance Disguised wins, consistent with a black-swan meta shift or tilt scenario. Probability_no_score = 84 reflects Cloud9's documented dominance and prior success. Gap of 2 points (100 - 84 - 14 = 2) captures residual uncertainty on both sides due to briefing silence on patch strategy.", "key_factor": "Disguised's recent 3-0 sweep of Team Liquid (a much stronger opponent) reflects a hidden meta-alignment or psychological momentum shift that Cloud9 has not faced in the Lock-In; if Disguised has adapted to a patch or playstyle that hard-counters Cloud9's macro approach, the BO3 format amplifies variance and allows Disguised to steal games through tactical surprise."}], "final_score": 0.3217915598049758, "no_score": 0.7855874657799303, "edge": 0.5273076923076923, "no_edge": -0.14269230769230767, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.19760479041916174, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.26739926739926684, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.13369963369963342, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0528790325074653, "The Bull": 0.9501329761451676, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.049920045444432, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0760832327824044, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0566488239123408, "The Contrarian": 1.0796819502063366, "The Bear": 0.7346539390018548}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "