{"run_id": "c5eeebf7-06bd-4564-b04f-c4abfde90cf1", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T17:46:31.679930+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963713", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Shaiikademy vs Chiefs Esports Club (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Oceania Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Shaiikademy and Chiefs Esports Club in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Oceania Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 11:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shaiikademy\" if Shaiikademy win the match against Chiefs Esports Club.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Chiefs Esports Club\" if Chiefs Esports Club win the match against Shaiikademy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T09:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T03:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.13, "volume_usd": 100.84285999999999, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["14314367540223149983249176621443595117707260382175758672587905308115859742075", "63970023374083120747139139734974873827750413507520979862639061618886136556267"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-19 03:00 UTC (EVENT TIMING: TODAY, ~9 hours away). Any past-tense scorelines in the briefing (Chiefs defeats Barbie Boys 2-1 on April 5; Chiefs beats Anios 2-1 on March 29) are PRIOR encounters and provide no direct evidence of this match's outcome. CHIEFS ESPORTS CLUB \u2014 DOCUMENTED RECENT FORM: Chiefs demonstrated competitive strength in the Kickoff tournament with wins over Barbie Boys (2-1, April 5) and Team Anios (2-1, March 29). Roster includes established players (Neptune, Walsh, Relaes, Lunchbox, Playxr). This indicates playoff-ready form and experience. SHAIIKADEMY \u2014 DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO recent match history, NO documented roster composition, NO form statistics, and NO competitive context for Shaiikademy. This is a critical information asymmetry. PandaScore reports only 'recent form: 6W-2L (last 8 matches)', but no specific opponent names, scores, or dates are provided. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES (Shaiikademy) trades at 13%, NO (Chiefs) at 87%. This 74pp gap reflects market consensus heavily favoring Chiefs. The 7-day YES trend is -37.0pp (falling sharply), suggesting institutional or informed traders are moving conviction toward Chiefs. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=28 (LOW) because the briefing provides documented Chiefs form but zero Shaiikademy context. A probability of 18% for YES is sustainable on Chiefs' documented recent wins, but without Shaiikademy data, I cannot confidently rule them out \u2014 hence confidence_yes is depressed. confidence_no=65 (MODERATE) because Chiefs' recent form is clear, but the complete absence of Shaiikademy intel prevents high confidence in a Chiefs victory prediction. If Shaiikademy has hidden strength (e.g., strong form not captured in this briefing), they could upset. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: YES=18 reflects (a) Chiefs' demonstrated playoff form (2 recent BO3 wins), (b) market heavy consensus at 87% NO, (c) data gap that prevents confident Shaiikademy dismissal. If both teams had equal documentation, the gap would likely be narrower; the 18% reflects Chiefs' documented advantage plus market pricing. NO=78 reflects Chiefs' clear recent wins and market conviction, but not 87% because Shaiikademy's unknown form introduces residual upside risk. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous (win = match resolution, forfeit/cancel = 50-50). No technical ambiguity in team name matching (both teams are clearly identifiable in the tournament brackets). NO FORFEIT/CANCEL SIGNAL: No indication in the briefing of match cancellation, rescheduling, or team withdrawal risk. Match is confirmed SCHEDULED.", "key_factor": "Severe asymmetric data availability: Chiefs form is documented (recent wins vs Barbie Boys and Anios), but Shaiikademy roster and recent match history are entirely absent from briefing, preventing balanced competitive assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.87, "probability_yes": 0.87, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = Chiefs) STRENGTHS: Market is correctly pricing Chiefs as heavy favorites (87%) based on documented recent form \u2014 two consecutive BO3 playoff victories (March 29 vs Anios 2-1, April 5 vs Barbie Boys 2-1) demonstrate consistency in tournament pressure situations. CHIEFS ROSTER STABILITY: Named core players (Neptune, Walsh, Relaes, Lunchbox, Playxr) appear in recent match MVPs and roster entries dated 2026-03-11, indicating stable, established lineup heading into playoffs with playoff experience. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES = Shaiikademy): Critical data asymmetry \u2014 Shaiikademy's recent match history, form trend (6W-2L last 8 matches notation provided but no timestamp context or recent playoff performance), roster composition, and playoff-specific pedigree are NOT detailed in briefing. This absence of affirmative case material is itself bearish for the underdog. CHIEFS' PLAYOFF TRAJECTORY: Both recent Chiefs victories are within the same Kickoff tournament (March 29 and April 5 results both marked APL 2026 OCE - Kickoff), indicating sequential playoff progression and momentum into QF1. MAP VETO / STRATEGY UNKNOWN: Both teams' map preferences and veto strategies are TBD at match time. However, Chiefs' recent success across multiple map pools (Chalet, Consulate, Border, Bank in prior matches) suggests adaptability that favors the team with documented recent success. MARKET SIGNAL STRENGTH: NO side moved +37.5pp over 7 days (rising trend) with +17.0pp in last 24 hours, indicating sharp consensus tightening behind Chiefs and NO-side accumulation. YES side fell -37.0pp / -17.0pp respectively, suggesting confidence erosion in Shaiikademy's chances. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK (LIVE IMMINENT): Event starts in ~9 hours. For Shaiikademy to overcome 87% Chiefs pricing, they would need to overturn established recent form disadvantage in a single BO3 with almost no time for new catalysts (roster changes, injury reversals, etc.). Reversal probability is extremely low given temporal constraint. CASE AGAINST SHAIIKADEMY (UNDERDOG): While 6W-2L recent record is marginally better than Chiefs' 6W-4L, Shaiikademy shows NO documented playoff wins in briefing, NO named roster in recent matches, NO map pool adaptability evidence, and NO recent high-stakes BO3 victories. The absence is material \u2014 it suggests weaker playoff credentials. CHIEFS ARE NOT OVERPRICED: At 87%, the market has correctly identified Chiefs as the superior team based on available evidence. The briefing provides zero affirmative case for Shaiikademy beyond raw win-loss ratios, which lack context and fail to account for competition tier, opponent quality, or playoff format performance. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (72) reflects solid documentary evidence supporting Chiefs' recent form; confidence_no (28) reflects severe data deficit on Shaiikademy side \u2014 no recent results, no roster identification, no playoff pedigree mentioned. This asymmetry correctly penalizes the underdog's uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Chiefs' demonstrated recent playoff form (consecutive 2-1 victories over Team Anios and Barbie Boys) combined with established roster experience in high-stakes BO3 formats, while Shaiikademy's current form and recent matchup data remain absent from briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Shaiikademy's form advantage: Shaiikademy posts 6W-2L (75% win rate over 8 matches) vs Chiefs' 6W-4L (60% win rate over 10 matches). This is a statistically material edge in recent trajectory \u2014 Shaiikademy is on hotter form by ~15 percentage points. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: The briefing explicitly states YES prices have FALLEN -37pp over 7 days and -17pp in 24 hours, while NO has RISEN +37.5pp and +17pp respectively. This suggests panic selling of YES rather than evidence-based repricing. At 13%, YES appears oversold relative to Shaiikademy's superior recent win rate. TEMPORAL ASYMMETRY: Chiefs' cited wins (Barbie Boys 2-1 on April 5, Team Anios 2-1 on March 29) are NOW 10-21 days old. Shaiikademy's 6W-2L record is more recent/comprehensive (8-match sample). The briefing offers no comparably fresh Chiefs data to counter Shaiikademy's hot streak. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITY: Chiefs' 6W-4L record includes 4 losses in their last 10 matches \u2014 a 40% loss rate. In a BO3 playoff format, inconsistency at this frequency is a liability. No roster or strategic depth analysis supports Chiefs' 87% pricing. DATA ASYMMETRY ACKNOWLEDGED: The briefing notes 'Shaiikademy's recent match history and form is not detailed in available sources' in the CASE FOR NO. However, PandaScore's authoritative record directly contradicts this \u2014 Shaiikademy: 6W-2L is documented. The briefing's CASE FOR NO relies on a data gap that does not actually exist in the structured match data. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Confidence_yes = 32 (not higher) because: (1) NO has absolute form data too (6W-4L is real, not fake), (2) playoff volatility in BO3 is high, (3) roster/map veto tactics unknown, (4) only ~9 hours to match start limits reversal window. Confidence_no = 68 because: (1) Chiefs' 60% recent win rate is still respectable, (2) playoff experience matters in esports, (3) form advantage for YES is real but not overwhelming in a single BO3 series. LIVE/IMMINENT EFFECT: Event starts in ~9 hours. Price is now largely locked. Sharp move on Apr 17-18 (\u00b110.5pp, \u00b17.5pp, \u00b15.5pp swings) suggests informed traders repositioning. The persistence of 13% YES pricing despite Shaiikademy's form advantage indicates either: (a) Chiefs have hidden map advantages or roster depth not captured in briefing, or (b) market is anchored to old priors and slow to update. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: This is a Lower Bracket Quarterfinal (elimination risk for loser). Single-series BO3 outcomes are inherently volatile. Shaiikademy's 75% recent win rate does not guarantee 75% probability in a single match, but it strongly justifies upward revision from 13%. RESOLUTION RISK MINIMAL: Match is scheduled, not subject to cancellation or forfeit based on current briefing. Liquipedia resolution is standard and trustworthy. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Shaiikademy is the form-based underdog. Chiefs' 87% pricing relies on outdated wins (10-21 days old) and ignores Shaiikademy's superior 8-match recent record. A probability near 28% for YES (72% for NO) reflects: (a) genuine form advantage for Shaiikademy worth ~+15pp, (b) residual playoffs volatility and unknowns worth ~-10-15pp, and (c) respect for Chiefs' respectable 60% baseline. The market has overweighted narrative (Chiefs beat Barbie Boys) and underweighted recency (Shaiikademy's 6W-2L streak).", "key_factor": "Shaiikademy's strong recent form (6W-2L in last 8 matches) significantly outpaces Chiefs' 6W-4L record over 10 matches, suggesting the underdog has superior current momentum despite market mispricing."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.8200000000000001, "probability_source": "synthetic_mirror", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (scheduled 2026-04-19 03:00 UTC, ~9 hours away). Any reversal would require significant evidence to materialize in this window\u2014low probability of late major news changes. MARKET SIGNAL: YES traded from 18% baseline down to 13% current (7-day decline -37pp, 24h decline -17pp). Sharp downward moves on Apr 17-18 suggest informed money/sharps are backing Chiefs. Market is pricing Shaiikademy as a heavy underdog. CHIEFS RECENT FORM: Confirmed wins vs. Barbie Boys 2-1 (Apr 5) and Anios 2-1 (Mar 29). Roster includes Neptune, Walsh, Relaes (named MVPs). Recent 6W-4L in last 10 matches. SHAIIKADEMY DATA GAP: No recent match results, roster composition, or form data provided in briefing. Recent form listed as 6W-2L (last 8), but no context on opponent quality or recency. Cannot assess whether 6W-2L reflects playoff-caliber opponents or stage-dependent variance. BRIEFING ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence on Chiefs (recent playoff wins, named players, 60% recent win rate); minimal evidence on Shaiikademy. confidence_no >> confidence_yes reflects this data imbalance. BASE RATE ANCHOR: Oceania esports playoffs\u2014lower-seeded or unfavored teams win ~25-35% of quarterfinals. Market price of 13% YES is aggressive but plausible if Shaiikademy is perceived as significantly weaker or exhausted from earlier rounds. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Market mentions 'Lower bracket quarterfinal 1' \u2014 both teams may already have losses. Shaiikademy's path/seed unknown; Chiefs' playoff trajectory is clearer. This asymmetry favors the better-documented team. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $101 USD\u2014very thin market. Sharp moves (\u00b110pp in single hours) suggest low friction; actual consensus may be more extreme than current 13% YES implies. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes (32) would require clearer Shaiikademy counter-evidence or underdog discount logic. Instead, I set it LOW (32) because the absence of Shaiikademy data prevents confident support for YES. confidence_no set to 48 (moderate-low) because Chiefs' recent form is strong but limited to 2 confirmed wins in Kickoff; deeper playoff/LAN track record unknown.", "key_factor": "Oceania R6S playoff BO3 matches: insufficient historical sample; lower-seeded/underdog teams win ~25-35% of playoff quarterfinals in esports"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "CRITICAL ASYMMETRY: Briefing contains ZERO concrete data on Shaiikademy's recent form, roster, or playoff track record. Case for YES rests entirely on absence of negative information. Chiefs Esports Club documented: recent wins (Barbie Boys 2-1 Apr 5; Team Anios 2-1 Mar 29), named roster players (Neptune, Walsh, Relaes) with playoff experience. This creates false equivalence: Chiefs have evidence, Shaiikademy have silence. Market price (13% YES / 87% NO) reflects rational fear of unknown opponent rather than evidence-based disparity. A team that exists enough to be scheduled must have some form, but briefing provides zero signal. Disambiguation warning flags past-tense scoreline in side_yes_case as PRIOR encounters, not this match outcome. This undermines the superficial 'Chiefs momentum' narrative\u2014those wins are historical, not predictive. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (9 hours to start). High volatility in last 48 hours (YES dropped 17pp in 24h, NO rose 17pp) suggests panic-driven repricing into match, not new substantive information. Volume only $101 USD suggests illiquid, thin market prone to sentiment whipsaws. Low liquidity amplifies crowd psychology effects. NO side confidence capped at 62: While Chiefs form appears stronger, Shaiikademy's complete absence from briefing narrative creates genuine ignorance mass. Market may be overweighting Chiefs' recent results against unknown-but-plausible Shaiikademy strength. YES side confidence capped at 35: Cannot justify high confidence in 13% when briefing provides zero affirmative case\u2014only Chiefs' prior wins by default. Absence of Shaiikademy data is NOT evidence they are weak. Market sentiment = FEAR: Crowd is running from YES into NO on incomplete information. Sharp moves (Apr 17-18) suggest reactive trading, not analytical depth. Rational apathy signal: If Shaiikademy had recent credible losses or roster issues, briefing would flag them. Silence could indicate middle-tier competence, not incompetence. Current price (~13%) implies Shaiikademy are 6:1 underdogs with no public data supporting that severity.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "CHIEFS ESPORTS CLUB DOCUMENTED FORM: Chiefs beat Barbie Boys 2-1 (April 5) and Team Anios 2-1 (March 29) \u2014 both within Kickoff tournament window, demonstrating mid-tournament consistency and proven map execution across multiple series. SHAIIKADEMY FORM ABSENT FROM BRIEFING: No recent match history, roster composition, or tournament performance provided. The briefing explicitly notes 'Shaiikademy's recent performance is not detailed in available snippets.' This is asymmetric data favoring NO confidence, not YES. PandaScore RECENT FORM METRICS: Shaiikademy listed as 6W-2L (last 8 matches); Chiefs listed as 6W-4L (last 10 matches). Shaiikademy's win% (75%) marginally exceeds Chiefs (60%), but these stats lack tournament context, meta relevance, or recency weighting within Kickoff 2026. MARKET PRICE SIGNALS: YES side trading at 13% (down 37pp over 7 days, -17pp in 24h) indicates sustained sharp movement away from Shaiikademy \u2014 consistent with professional market makers pricing in Chiefs favoritism. Volatility is modest (3.1pp/hr YES), suggesting consensus, not uncertainty spike. LOWER BRACKET QUARTERFINAL CONTEXT: This is a BO3 lower bracket match \u2014 meaningful but not grand finals. Chiefs' documented wins (Anios, Barbie Boys) were both BO3 format, establishing proven execution under playoff pressure. ROSTER INTEL AVAILABLE ONLY FOR CHIEFS: Briefing names Neptune, Walsh, Relaes as Chiefs MVP contributors. No Shaiikademy player names, roles, or recent highlight intel provided \u2014 data asymmetry favors NO confidence over YES. MAP VETO STRATEGY UNKNOWN: 'Map veto and bans remain to be determined' \u2014 cannot assess meta advantage. Chiefs' recent Anios matchup shows skilled veto execution (won 2-1 with mixed map outcomes: Chalet 7-34L, Consulate 7-34L, Bank 1-1 decider). Shaiikademy's veto track record absent. EVENT TIMING (LIVE/IMMINENT): Match starts in ~9 hours. Any reversal from current 13% YES price requires major narrative shift (e.g., pro player illness, technical issues, leaked scrim result). Such events are possible but low-probability in esports. Market will likely trade YES toward $0.01 if Chiefs establish early map advantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 28 reflects thin YES-side evidence and briefing silence on Shaiikademy fundamentals. confidence_no = 62 reflects Chiefs' documented wins, roster names, and favorable market consensus \u2014 but remains below 75 due to lack of head-to-head H2H data and Shaiikademy's hidden 75% W% metric. PROBABILITY NOT FORCE-FITTED: 18 + 72 = 90, leaving 10pp ignorance mass. This reflects genuine asymmetry: strong evidence Chiefs are favored (72), weak evidence Shaiikademy can win (18), and unresolved uncertainty on Shaiikademy's true caliber within Kickoff tournament specifically.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 13% YES reflects justified skepticism toward Shaiikademy given complete absence of recent form data in briefing, while Chiefs show documented playoff pedigree; however, the briefing's silence on Shaiikademy's roster and trajectory prevents high confidence in either direction."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market is heavily skewed toward Chiefs (87% NO) despite Shaiikademy's strong recent form (6W-2L in last 8 matches vs Chiefs' 6W-4L in last 10), suggesting market may be over-weighting recent head-to-head results or roster familiarity. Briefing is conspicuously silent on Shaiikademy's recent match history, MVP performance, and current roster composition\u2014a major data gap that prevents proper evaluation of YES path. Absence of Shaiikademy data creates false confidence in the NO side. Chiefs' recent wins (Barbie Boys 2-1 on April 5, Team Anios 2-1 on March 29) are against mid-tier opponents; no head-to-head results vs Shaiikademy in briefing. Lower bracket playoff context unknown\u2014Chiefs may be fatigued or underestimating a lower-seeded opponent. Map veto is TBD at match time; no ban history or pool preference data provided for either team. In BO3 R6S, veto meta and map pool dominance (e.g., Bank, Border, Chalet) can heavily favor one team's playstyle. Shaiikademy could exploit a meta shift Chiefs have not adapted to. Rock LFO recent form (2-1 vs 6Targets, 2-0 vs Team Anios on April 12) shows that smaller/less-hyped teams are competitive in this Kickoff bracket. Shaiikademy's 6W-2L record is legitimate and suggests underdog potential masked by market bias toward Chiefs' brand recognition. Sharp market moves on April 17\u201318 (YES price fell 37pp over 7 days, 17pp in 24hr) point to sharp money moving against Shaiikademy, but no new match result or injury news is cited in briefing. This could indicate information asymmetry (insiders backing Chiefs) or panic-driven overreaction to sentiment rather than competitive data. Temporal coherence: event is TODAY (9 hours to start, 03:00 UTC April 19). At this stage, low-probability reversals (e.g., key player illness, stand-in substitution, unexpected tactical innovation) are plausible but time-constrained\u2014confidence should remain moderate even on black-swan scenario. Chiefs roster includes Neptune, Walsh, Relaes (listed as MVPs in April 5 match), but briefing does not confirm whether same roster plays today. Substitute (Timbers) is noted on roster as of March 14\u2014if a key player is benched or swapped, veto flexibility and anti-strat ability could shift sharply. Shaiikademy's 6W-2L form in last 8 matches is comparable to or better than Chiefs' 6W-4L in last 10. Market underweighting this suggests overconfidence in Chiefs' playoff seeding/brand, not skill-gap evidence. Lower bracket matchup context: if Chiefs are higher seed or Shaiikademy seeded lower, market bias toward establishment teams (Chiefs) is expected. But Shaiikademy's performance trajectory is positive (6-2 is winning form), and lower bracket upsets are common in BO3 playoffs where one bad map can swing series.", "key_factor": "Shaiikademy fields an unexpected roster change or substitute player with superior map pool/meta knowledge in a specific matchup that Chiefs have not recently encountered, exploiting a tactical weakness in Chiefs' recent veto patterns."}], "final_score": 0.3763779920266213, "no_score": 0.7540287441103303, "edge": 0.5623076923076923, "no_edge": -0.1776923076923077, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 56.43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0528790325074653, "The Bull": 0.9501329761451676, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.049920045444432, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0760832327824044, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0566488239123408, "The Contrarian": 1.0796819502063366, "The Bear": 0.7346539390018548}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963713", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Shaiikademy vs Chiefs Esports Club (BO3) - Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Oceania Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Shaiikademy and Chiefs Esports Club in the Asia-Pacific League Kickoff: Oceania Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 18 at 11:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shaiikademy\" if Shaiikademy win the match against Chiefs Esports Club.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Chiefs Esports Club\" if Chiefs Esports Club win the match against Shaiikademy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T09:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T03:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.13, "volume_usd": 100.84285999999999, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["14314367540223149983249176621443595117707260382175758672587905308115859742075", "63970023374083120747139139734974873827750413507520979862639061618886136556267"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline