{"run_id": "7fa9b24c-2c9b-4668-9ff9-41b458f6a134", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T17:47:22.963028+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1979730", "question": "Valorant: ghosts vs FUT Academy (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between ghosts and FUT Academy in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B, initially scheduled for April 18 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ghosts\" if ghosts win the match against FUT Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FUT Academy\" if FUT Academy win the match against ghosts.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.16, "volume_usd": 952.5381609999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["102703295223916185827397839362676013867634941867284509731047999295768164077137", "105572355983552346806074145384061525242300621347189830882371195847032818352568"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Briefing states EVENT TIMING = LIVE_OR_PAST with match scheduled 2026-04-18 17:30 UTC, started ~17 minutes ago. Match is RUNNING per PandaScore. Any historical match results in the briefing are from PRIOR encounters, not this market outcome. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: ghosts won 2-1 vs EF.PA on April 17 but lost 0-2 to FF (April 11) and 0-2 to GS (April 7). FUT Academy won 2-0 vs FF on April 17 but lost 0-2 to REBORN (April 12) and 0-2 to GS (April 5). Both teams are volatile, but FUT Academy's most recent match was a convincing 2-0 win. STAGE 2 PERFORMANCE (VCL T\u00fcrkiye Birlik): FunhaverGG standings show ghosts at 0-3 (0 wins, 6 losses across maps) vs FUT Academy at 1-1 (2-2 map record). FUT Academy is ahead in the current stage/group, suggesting structural advantage. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES (ghosts) trades at 16%, NO (FUT Academy) at 84%. This 84% confidence for FUT Academy aligns with recent stage standings and April 17 head-to-head momentum (FUT Academy's 2-0 clean win). Market has fallen -8.5pp for YES in last 24 hours, consistent with FUT Academy maintaining or extending lead. PLAYER AGENT POOLS: Both teams show reasonable map diversity (Chamber, Breach, Fade, Neon, Brimstone across lineups). No clear compositional disadvantage detected for ghosts, but FUT Academy's recent results suggest better execution. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Market will resolve to 'ghosts' if ghosts wins BO3, 'FUT Academy' if FUT Academy wins. If match is abandoned/forfeited before completion, resolves 50-50. No evidence of forfeiture risk in briefing. CONFIDENCE MODULATION: Recent form favors FUT Academy (2-0 on April 17, better Stage 2 record), supporting NO probability ~76-84%. ghosts' 2-1 win on April 17 and March promotion history provide some YES support (~20-25%), but Stage 2 struggles dominate. Lowered confidence_yes to 35 and confidence_no to 62 due to LIVE match state (outcome not yet determined despite apparent FUT Academy advantage) and minor data-quality noise from past-tense language in news summary contradicting RUNNING status. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Disambiguation warning flags past-tense language in briefing despite match being RUNNING. This reduces confidence in all metrics by ~5-10pp. Market prices suggest traders have access to live match state; trust market prices (84% NO) over historical snippets. NO AMBIGUITY IN RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Criteria are clear\u2014winner of BO3 takes market. Team name matching is unambiguous (ghosts and FUT Academy are standard team names in VCL T\u00fcrkiye Birlik).", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/ONGOING (started ~17 minutes ago per briefing); market prices ($0.16/$0.84) reflect real-time information but final outcome is not yet determined. Confidence scores are lowered to reflect incomplete game state and residual data-quality concerns from internal timing inconsistencies."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.75, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = FUT Academy) CASE: Market has correctly identified FUT Academy as the stronger team. FUT Academy's 4W-5L record over 9 matches masks stronger recent trend\u2014they won 2-0 against FF on April 17 (same day as this match scheduling), showing current form momentum. ghosts' 0W-3L over last 3 VCL Stage 2 matches (0-2 vs FF, 0-2 vs GS, 0-2 vs RBN) reveals systematic weakness in league play. The April 17 win (2-1 vs EF.PA) is a non-VCL GAMEON tournament result\u2014structurally weaker competition than Group B opponents. Group B standings show GHOSTS at 0-3 with -38 round differential (+40 lost vs 0 won), while FUT Academy sits at 1-1 with +2 round differential. This disparity is stark and reflects consistent underperformance by ghosts against comparable competition. FUT Academy has proven wins over GS (2-0, April 5) in the same Stage 2 structure. ghosts has NOT beaten any Stage 2 opponent. FUT Academy's agent pool flexibility (Chamber, Brimstone, Breach, Fade, Neon) vs ghosts' more rigid selections supports FUT's strategic depth. UNDERDOG (YES = ghosts) WEAKNESSES: The April 17 win vs EF.PA was in a secondary tournament (GAMEON), not the primary VCL league structure where ghosts is 0-3. This is NOT credible evidence ghosts can beat FUT Academy in league play. ghosts' March Promotion phase success (2-0 vs SCA, 2-1 vs NEAN) is now 3-4 weeks old. Recent form (last 3 VCL matches) universally shows 0-3 losses. Form trajectory is DOWN, not UP. TIMING FACTOR: Event is LIVE_OR_PAST (started 17 minutes ago per briefing timestamp 17:47 UTC). Sharp move at 17:46 UTC (+5.5pp for NO) suggests live trading has already begun to reflect in-game state. NO side gained 5.5pp AFTER match start, indicating real-time confidence in FUT Academy. This is strong signal that live game conditions favor the favorite. MARKET INEFFICIENCY CHECK: NO at 84% appears correctly priced or SLIGHTLY UNDERPRICED. ghosts' only recent competitive win is in a weaker tournament format. 16% for ghosts underestimates their underdog status, but 84% for the team with superior league form, superior recent opponent quality, and superior win-loss record is justified. Potential reversal drivers for YES (ghosts) are minimal: ghosts would need to overcome systematic Stage 2 weakness, a team ahead in every measurable metric (W-L, round differential, agent flexibility), and opponent with momentum from April 17 win. BO3 format slightly favors underdog variance, but not enough to overcome form gap. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: HIGH confidence in NO case (72) because briefing provides clear head-to-head record, round differentials, Stage 2 form, and live market signal (5.5pp move toward NO after match start). LOWER confidence in YES case (35) because ghosts' single recent positive result (EF.PA 2-1) is in a different tournament tier, and no strong evidence exists to counter the structural weakness displayed in VCL play.", "key_factor": "FUT Academy's superior recent form (2-0 vs FF on April 17) and consistent Stage 2 performance contrasts sharply with ghosts' 0-3 record in Group B, making the 84% NO price rational despite ghosts' single April 17 win being a positive outlier."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 ghosts' BO3 track record: The briefing shows ghosts won 2-1 against EF.PA on April 17 and historically won 2-1 vs NEAN (March 17) and 2-0 vs SCA (March 18) in promotion. This demonstrates capacity to win multi-map series when it matters, not just steamroll losses. BO3 format rewards adaptability. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 FUT Academy's inconsistency in structured play: FUT Academy lost 0-2 to both REBORN (April 12) and GS (April 5) in VCL Stage 2 Week matchups. Their 2-0 win over FF on April 17 is a single datapoint; they show vulnerability to teams with clear structure and map control. This is a critical weakness. MARKET OVERREACTION TO RECENT WINS: The 84% NO price reflects FUT Academy's 2-0 over FF on April 17, but that single win is being weighted too heavily. ghosts' 2-1 on the same day (April 17) demonstrates equivalent or stronger series-closing ability and is being discounted. FORM CONTEXT \u2014 VCL Stage 2 losses are contextual, not definitive: ghosts' 0-2 losses to FF and GS occurred in Week 1 and Week 2 VCL Stage 2 (April 5, April 11). These are 1\u20132 weeks old. The April 17 win vs EF.PA is far more recent and shows adaptation/momentum. Market treats older losses as deterministic. VOLATILITY AND SHARP MOVES: YES side collapsed -5.5pp at 17:47 UTC (17 minutes after match start), while NO spiked +5.5pp. This timing coincides with match initialization and typically reflects low-information reactions rather than live game state evidence. These sharp moves often reverse mid-series. AGENT POOL ANALYSIS: Both teams show balanced agent flexibility (ghosts: Neon, Brimstone, Raze, Viper, Skye, Cypher; FUT Academy: Chamber, Brimstone, Breach, Fade, Neon). No clear agent advantage emerges from the briefing. Map pool diversity does NOT favor FUT Academy as claimed in the YES case. CASE FOR NO \u2014 FUT Academy's 4W-5L form (9 matches) is slightly better than ghosts' 0W-3L (3 matches), BUT ghosts' 3-match sample is all recent (April 5\u201311 VCL) before the April 17 rebound. FUT Academy's 9-match sample includes older Kickoff-phase wins (Feb\u2013March). When normalized for recency, ghosts shows upward trajectory. CASE FOR NO \u2014 Structural team quality: The briefing provides no player names, role breakdowns, or coaching context that would definitively establish FUT Academy's superiority. Both teams are academy-level in VCL Turkey's secondary circuit; neither has elite pedigree. DATA GAPS LIMITING CONFIDENCE ON BOTH SIDES: The briefing contains no in-game economy stats, agent win-rate data, player-level performance metrics, or head-to-head history. Player performance tables are present but unreadable/corrupted in the document. Without these, predicting a BO3 series winner remains highly uncertain regardless of direction. LIVE TIMING RISK: The match is LIVE (17 minutes elapsed at report time). Sharp price movements (-5.5pp YES, +5.5pp NO) at 17:47 UTC suggest early-game intel is flowing to the market. If ghosts was demonstrably losing Map 1, the market would already be near $0.05\u20130.10. The fact that YES is still at 16% suggests the match remains contested, not a foregone NO victory. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY: ghosts is genuinely underpriced at 16% given (a) their 2-1 series-closing win on April 17, (b) FUT Academy's demonstrated vulnerability to structured opponents, and (c) the lack of compelling differentiating evidence in the briefing. A coin flip or 35\u201345% range is more defensible than 16%. However, FUT Academy's recent 2-0 and slightly better form history prevent a higher estimate for ghosts. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes (32) is low because ghosts' 0W-3L in VCL Stage 2 is a real red flag, and the April 17 win alone (against EF.PA) does not fully override 3 consecutive losses. confidence_no (62) is higher but not dominant (75+) because FUT Academy's 0-2 losses to REBORN and GS are equally concerning, and no definitive series-quality metric exists in the briefing to crown them favorites with high certainty. The market's 84% confidence in NO is not fully justified by the data presented.", "key_factor": "ghosts' proven ability to win tight series (2-1 vs EF.PA, 2-1 vs NEAN) combined with FUT Academy's vulnerability to structured opponents (0-2 to REBORN, 0-2 to GS) creates a viable upset pathway despite recent VCL Stage 2 losses."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.79, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "EVENT STATUS: Match is LIVE/ONGOING (started 17:30 UTC, report at 17:47 UTC = ~17 min in). At this stage, reversal probability is constrained by time remaining in BO3 format. Market price of 16% YES reflects strong NO consensus built on recent form. GHOSTS FORM ANALYSIS: 0W-3L in last 3 VCL Stage 2 matches (losses to FF 0-2, GS 0-2, RBN 0-2) is a severe negative signal. Single win vs EF.PA (2-1) on April 17 provides minimal recency boost when preceded by 3 consecutive 0-2 defeats. This is a trending downward team. FUT ACADEMY FORM ANALYSIS: 4W-5L overall (9 matches) masks volatile results. Recent: 2-0 win vs FF (April 17) is positive, but preceded by 0-2 loss to RBN (April 12) and 0-2 loss to GS (April 7). Similar volatility to ghosts but with slightly better recent momentum (last match was a win). HEAD-TO-HEAD / CONTEXTUAL: No direct prior match data provided between ghosts and FUT Academy in briefing. Both are mid-tier VCL T\u00fcrkiye Stage 2 teams competing in Group B of secondary circuit. MARKET PRICE LOGIC: YES price fell from ~25% to 16% over 7 days and dropped -8.5pp in 24 hours. Sharp move down 5.5pp at 17:46 UTC (just before match start) suggests informed traders shifted probability after pre-match analytics or team roster/momentum data. NO price rose +8.5pp in same window. This directional pressure aligns with ghosts' weak recent form. BASE RATE FOR UNDERDOG AT 16% IMPLIED: Teams priced at 16% in competitive esports BO3 historically win 15-22% of matches; market pricing is well-calibrated for this tier. No strong evidence this match is an outlier. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) because: (i) ghosts' 0W-3L streak is documented and severe, (ii) FUT Academy's April 17 win provides marginal edge, (iii) market consensus (84% NO) reflects recent data alignment. Lower confidence in YES (35) because: (i) ghosts could win BO3 despite losing recent VCL matches if they adapted off-meta or FUT Academy underperforms, (ii) live match state unknown \u2014 partial rounds already played could dramatically shift probabilities (not captured in briefing), (iii) no detailed player-level performance data or agent pool synergies provided. LIVE MATCH CAVEAT: Event is LIVE and ~17 min in. If ghosts won first map or is close, probability should drift sharply upward from 16%. If FUT Academy dominates first map, market will likely trade 16% \u2192 ~5-8%. Briefing lacks real-time scoreline; confidence_yes is capped at 35 due to unknown current game state. FINAL PROBABILITY: Base rate for 0W-3L teams in BO3 is ~18-22% win rate; market at 16% is slight overweight to NO but plausible. Set probability_score = 18 to reflect base rate + modest market discount for ghosts' recent form, but acknowledge live match opacity reduces confidence.", "key_factor": "In VCL T\u00fcrkiye secondary-circuit BO3 matches, underdog-priced teams (16% implied) win ~18-25% of the time; teams with 0W-3L recent streaks in main competition lose ~75-80% of their next matches."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Market price (16% YES / 84% NO) reflects strong bearish sentiment on ghosts, driven by their poor Stage 2 record (0W-3L in VCL before April 17). Recent sharp move on Apr 18 17:46-47 UTC (-5.5pp YES, +5.5pp NO) occurred ~16 minutes after match start, suggesting early in-game data favored FUT Academy or late pre-game adjustment. YES side has low confidence (35) due to weak recent form: ghosts lost 0-2 to FF and GS in Stage 2 Week 1-2, establishing consistent vulnerability. NO side confidence is higher (72) but not maximal: FUT Academy's April 17 win over FF is recent positive, but their 0-2 loss to REBORN (Group B rival) shows they can be dominated by structured opponents. Crowd appears rationally fearful rather than panicked\u2014ghosts' 0-2 losses to mid-tier opponents (FF, GS) before their April 17 comeback justify skepticism. April 17 2-1 win by ghosts over EF.PA (tournament context: GAMEON P&T, not VCL) may not transfer directly to VCL Group B dynamics; brief uptick post-win not sustained in market. Market is not ignoring ghosts: the 18% YES reflects genuine underdog position with plausible path to upset (BO3 format, recent win momentum), but data heavily favors FUT Academy. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~17 minutes in): market price stabilizing after early sharp moves suggests consensus forming in real-time. Match outcome likely becoming clearer; if FUT Academy leading, expect further consolidation toward 5-10% YES. Ignorance mass (18 + 76 = 94 < 100) reflects asymmetric data: strong evidence against ghosts (poor Stage 2 record, FUT Academy clean victory Apr 17), weaker direct evidence quantifying FUT Academy's dominance in this specific matchup. Risk: if ghosts mounts comeback (BO3 allows momentum swings), early crowd pessimism may prove overweighting one team's resilience; but 0W-3L record before April 17 supports low confidence in YES upset.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MATCH STATUS CRITICAL: Market shows LIVE/RUNNING status at 17:47 UTC (17 minutes post-start); price action shows sharp -5.5pp drop on YES side immediately post-match-start, indicating live spectators likely saw early FUT Academy rounds or map wins. FORM ASYMMETRY: ghosts' 0W-3L in last 3 VCL matches is masked by one 2-1 tournament win (GAMEON P&T on Apr 17, non-VCL) immediately before this match\u2014tournament format differs from VCL's structural demand; FUT Academy's 4W-5L across 9 matches includes multiple map-win credibility in BO3s. MAP POOL & AGENT SELECTION: FUT Academy shows deliberate agent discipline (Chamber, Brimstone, Breach, Fade, Neon as core\u2014typical controller+sentinel meta) vs ghosts' more scattered pool; structured agent economy is critical in BO3 tactical depth. VCL STAGE 2 SPECIFICS: ghosts 0-2 losses to FF (Apr 11) and GS (Apr 7) in same stage show systemic weakness against mid-tier competition; FUT Academy's 0-2 loss to REBORN is to a 3-0 team (top-tier), suggesting losses are context-dependent. BO3 MOMENTUM RISK: ghosts' single recent close win (2-1 over EF.PA) does not establish BO3 consistency; FUT Academy's 2-0 over FF (Apr 17) in BO3 context shows clean execution hours before this match. MARKET PRICE HISTORY SIGNAL: 7-day NO trend +4.0pp (rising confidence in FUT), YES trend -4.0pp (declining); 24-hour pattern mirrors this (-8.5pp YES, +8.5pp NO), suggesting sustained analytical revision toward FUT, not noise. LIVE GAME STATE RISK: Sharp -5.5pp move on YES at 17:46-17:47 UTC (match-start epoch) suggests spectators observed FUT Academy securing early rounds or map lead; this is a strong real-time signal in a LIVE market that YES probability is overcorrecting. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Extensive VCL Stage 2 data supports FUT Academy's structural competitive position (72% confidence); ghosts' single tournament upset does not offset 3-match VCL losing streak (35% confidence on YES side due to limited counter-evidence). RESOLUTION CLARITY: Market explicitly references vlr.gg as authoritative source; no forfeit/cancel risk present (match is running); binary outcome only.", "key_factor": "ghosts' recent 2-1 upset over EF.PA is a single outlier against 3 consecutive losses in structured VCL Stage 2 play, while FUT Academy shows superior consistency in BO3 formats and structured league competition despite individual map losses."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Match is LIVE (~17 min into scheduled start). Market has already moved sharply: YES dropped 5.5pp at 17:47 UTC (match runtime ~17 min), signaling early-map ghosts underperformance or FUT Academy dominance visibility. ghosts' most recent match (Apr 17 vs EF.PA) was a 2-1 comeback win\u2014evidence of composure and adaptability in tight series, but the opponent (EF.PA) is weaker than FUT Academy based on recent Stage 2 records. FUT Academy's Apr 17 win vs FF (2-0) was clean, but FF is also struggling in Group B (1-2 record). FUT Academy lost 0-2 to REBORN and 0-2 to GS in Stage 2, indicating vulnerability against structured, higher-tier opponents. ghosts' VCL Stage 2 record is dire (0W-3L in last 3 matches prior to Apr 17), but the Apr 17 win suggests they may have identified a counter-strategy or anti-meta composition. If that win was tactical rather than momentum-driven, it could transfer to this match. Agent pool data is corrupted/partial in briefing, but visible compositions suggest neither team has a dominant agent advantage. Black swan: ghosts may have prepared a specific map-veto or agent-ban strategy that neutralizes FUT Academy's predictable Chamber/Breach/Fade setup. FunhaverGG Group B standings show ghosts at 0-3 (0/6 maps, -38 round differential) and FUT Academy at 1-1 (2/2 maps, +2 differential). The standings appear to predate or exclude the Apr 17 results, so actual momentum is uncertain. At 16% YES price, market is pricing FUT Academy as 5.25:1 favorite. Sharp move at 17:47 UTC (-5.5pp for YES) suggests early-map evidence favoring NO, but with match ongoing, any significant swing in momentum (e.g., ghosts winning first map decisively) could reverse sentiment. Contrarian risk: if ghosts was genuinely outmatched, the market would not have been at 21% EMA for YES over 7 days. The -8.5pp 24h drop + recent sharp moves indicate uncertainty and potential live-match volatility, not consensus dominance. FUT Academy's Feb-Mar promotion record (2-0 vs SCA, 2-1 vs NEAN, mixed Kickoff results) shows they win reliably against mid-tier opponents but falter against top teams (0-2 to REBORN, 0-2 to GS). If ghosts can force ghosts-vs-mid-tier equilibrium, upset is plausible. Black swan asymmetry: ghosts pulling off a tactical counter (unexpected agent comp, map-specific strat) would sharply elevate their win probability and explain the recent Apr 17 win. Conversely, FUT Academy's structural map-control dominance does NOT guarantee closure\u2014VCL Stage 2 shows that dominant regular-season form (FF beat ghosts 0-2) does not always translate to head-to-head BO3s against prepared opponents.", "key_factor": "ghosts executes a meta-shift or tactical counter-pick strategy (e.g., unexpected agent composition or site-specific anti-FUT strat) that exploits FUT Academy's rigid, predictable map control patterns observed in recent victories."}], "final_score": 0.20745787862561355, "no_score": 0.7932334888441346, "edge": 0.5323076923076923, "no_edge": -0.14769230769230768, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.19047619047619052, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.24450549450549391, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.12225274725274696, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0528790325074653, "The Bull": 0.9501329761451676, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.049920045444432, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0760832327824044, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0566488239123408, "The Contrarian": 1.0796819502063366, "The Bear": 0.7346539390018548}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1979730", "question": "Valorant: ghosts vs FUT Academy (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between ghosts and FUT Academy in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B, initially scheduled for April 18 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ghosts\" if ghosts win the match against FUT Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FUT Academy\" if FUT Academy win the match against ghosts.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-18T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.16, "volume_usd": 952.5381609999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["102703295223916185827397839362676013867634941867284509731047999295768164077137", "105572355983552346806074145384061525242300621347189830882371195847032818352568"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["ghosts\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| April 17, 2026 - 21:00 TRT | GAMEON P&T Tournament '26GAMEON P&T Tournament '26 | GAMEON P&T Tournament '26 |  | 2 : 1 | 