ing current form in favor of aged H2H history. News summary acknowledges Man eSports LFO 'faces significant challenge' but this is soft language \u2014 the NO side's 2-0 demolition of Shaiikademy (Apr 12) shows current tournament momentum. Crowd is anchoring on Sept 2025 wins, not recent 2026 performance. BO3 format is inherently volatile; a 2-1 comeback or upset is not implausible. At 82%, market is pricing in ~98% chance ENTERPRISE wins at least 2 of 3 maps, which overstates certainty given form disparity. Roster changes in March 2026 are mentioned for both teams but briefing provides no detail on integration, chemistry, or impact. This uncertainty is being glossed over by the crowd's YES enthusiasm. Volume is extremely low ($29 USD) \u2014 this is a thin, lightly-traded market where small bid-ask spreads or early informational moves can create false consensus. Sharp moves (+14.5pp, -13pp, +9pp on Apr 18) suggest algo/momentum trading rather than fundamental repricing. EVENT TIMING: Event starts in ~9 hours. Any reversal from 82% YES would require very recent adverse news (roster emergency, public analysis shift) with minimal time for adjustment. Market is locked in on current narrative. Crowd psychology: YES side is anchored on past dominance + most recent ENTERPRISE map win; treating Man eSports LFO's tournament momentum as noise. This is classic recency bias layered with historical anchoring \u2014 greed for the favored narrative. Probability_score of 68: YES is favored based on H2H history and one strong recent performance, but ENTERPRISE's 2W-8L recent form is a severe red flag that 82% price does not adequately penalize. 68 reflects YES lean while acknowledging material underperformance. Probability_no_score of 45: NO side has better recent form (5W-5L), tournament momentum (2-0 shutout Apr 12), and BO3 volatility should support ~35-40% baseline, but crowd apathy toward NO case + low volume uncertainty warrant only modest confidence in that estimate. Setting