 data on direct map matchups, draft preferences, or meta fit for 2026 season provided. Map veto data from other matches shows both teams can adapt, but no specific technical advantage identified for ENTERPRISE. Confidence in YES is moderate (58) because: ENTERPRISE does have winning H2H history and named star players (Jigsaw, ChefJeff, Kyro), but current form contradicts market narrative. Confidence in NO is lower (45) because: while Man's form is better, the historical H2H and ENTERPRISE's roster quality suggest Man is not a lock. Insufficient recent direct tactical data to be highly confident in NO. Probability sum (62 + 48 = 110) reflects asymmetric data: strong evidence that ENTERPRISE is overpriced and Man is underpriced, but insufficient granular match-level data to be high-confidence on either side. Market likely overweights stale H2H from Sept 2025.", "key_factor": "ENTERPRISE's historical head-to-head dominance (2-0 in 2025) is substantially weakened by 6+ month gap, roster turnover on both teams in March 2026, and Man eSports LFO's demonstrated current-tournament form (clean 2-0 playoff wins), making this far tighter than the 82% market price suggests."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.52, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "ENTERPRISE's recent form is severely deteriorated: 2W-8L over last 10 matches, despite being market favorite at 82%. Man eSports LFO shows momentum trajectory: 5W-5L over last 10, and has cleanly won two consecutive playoff matches (April 5 vs ENTERPRISE 2-1, April 12 vs Shaiikademy 2-0) with strong map control and MVP consistency. Head-to-head history (Sept 2025) is >6 months stale; rosters have significantly changed. ENTERPRISE added Jigsaw/Brendo/Kyro (March 20), Man eSports LFO hired new analyst/coaching staff (March 28). No 2026 H2H data exists. CRITICAL TIMING: Market volatility spiked April 18 19:00 UTC (+9.0pp YES, -9.0pp NO) \u2014 likely reflects late information (roster moves, scrim results, or injury concerns) not visible in older match records. Sharp reversals (Apr 18 17:00 -13.0pp YES) suggest uncertainty among informed traders. Man eSports LFO's recent opponents (ENTERPRISE April 5, Shaiikademy April 12) were both significantly stronger than Rock LFO (Mar 29, 2-0 stomp), yet Man won convincingly. Suggests true skill elevation, not padding stats. ENTERPRISE's 2W-8L form includes no recent dominant victories; the news summary cites Sept 2025 wins, not recent 2026 performance. Form trajectory heavily favors Man. BO3 format with veto advantage uncertain; map pool meta shifts (latest matches show Chalet, Lair, Consulate, Kafe, Bank, Clubhouse, Nighthaven Labs rotation) may favor one team's pick/ban strategy. Coaching/analyst changes for Man eSports LFO (Safe, Velocityyy, BenjiG all March 28) could signal tactical refresh that ENTERPRISE's staff (Mag retired March 20, ChinaNado moved to EDG) has not yet calibrated against. Market price history shows YES falling from 89% to 82% over 24 hours despite it being the 'favorite' \u2014 suggests informed money is backing underdog or perceiving overvalue on YES side. NO-side case is under-evidenced in briefing (no recent individual player performances, no map-specific trends favoring Man, limited discussion of veto strategy) \u2014 confidence_no kept conservative at 48 to reflect data asymmetry favoring YES narrative.", "key_factor": "Man eSports LFO's recent roster stabilization and coaching additions (Safe, Velocityyy, BenjiG all hired 2026-03-28) have not yet faced ENTERPRISE's current lineup in live competition, and psychological momentum from a dominant 2-0 tournament run (April 5 vs EP 2-1, April 12 vs Shaiikademy 2-0) could exploit ENTERPRISE's shaky recent form (2-8 last 10) if ENTERPRISE underestimates the challenge."}], "final_score": 0.6708054962644835, "no_score": 0.36707047341653654, "edge": -0.12269230769