could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.345, "volume_usd": 30528.97316000001, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["93551236585187019637357591799440729160931978082652626121064101711913005743522", "23467031389853761276362594572424318201956747940932774261245609586356932088127"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.34, "probability_yes": 0.34, "probability_no": 0.66, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event scheduled for 2026-04-19 08:00 UTC (TODAY, ~11 hours from briefing timestamp). Prior match history (Feb 14 T1 3-0 win, Nov 2025 RRQ wins) describes past encounters, not this market's resolution condition. RESOLUTION CONDITION: YES = Rex Regum Qeon wins the BO3 match. NO = T1 wins the BO3 match. Criteria are clear; no cancellation/forfeit/tie risk flagged in briefing. T1 RECENT FORM: 7W-2L (last 9 matches). In VCT 2026 Pacific Group Omega: defeated VARREL 2-0 and DetonatioN 2-0. Undefeated in Week 1-2 group stage. Head-to-head record 2026-2024: 5W-3L vs RRQ overall; most recent decisive win 2026-02-14 (3-0). RRQ RECENT FORM: 6W-4L (last 10 matches). In VCT 2026 Pacific Group Omega: defeated ZETA DIVISION 2-1 and VARREL 2-0. Competitive within group stage but slightly lower win rate than T1 (60% vs 78%). HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: T1 leads 5-3 in recent encounters. Most recent (Feb 2026) was dominant 3-0 T1 win. However, RRQ won 2 of last 4 (Nov 2025, Aug 2025), showing ability to compete. Historical record shows T1 slight edge but not overwhelming dominance. MARKET PRICING: YES = 34%, NO = 66% (spread = 2%). This reflects a clear market consensus favoring T1. 7-day price movement: YES fell from ~49% to 34% (\u221215.5pp), suggesting professional/sharp money moved T1 direction mid-week (April 16-18 large moves). CONFIDENCE MODULATION: T1 is objective form favourite (78% vs 60% win rate, more recent dominant head-to-head result, undefeated group stage record). However, briefing lacks:\n  - Recent scrim results, roster changes, injury reports, or meta insights\n  - Individual player form (star player injuries, visa issues, morale)\n  - Map pool analysis or coach commentary\n  - Explanation of mid-week sharp moves (what new information drove \u22129pp T1 move on Apr 16?)\n  Event imminence (11 hours) means minimal time for reversals, but lack of current intel reduces confidence on BOTH sides by 10-15 points. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Market price (34% YES / 66% NO) aligns with form data (T1 favored, RRQ competitive but underdog). No briefing evidence contradicts market. Set probability_score = 34 (YES) and probability_no_score = 66 (NO) to reflect market consensus and form alignment. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 42 (moderate; T1 form is clear, but lack of current intel and imminent timing reduce conviction). confidence_no = 58 (slightly higher; T1 favouritism is well-grounded in recent H2H and group stage dominance, but same data-gap concerns apply symmetrically).", "key_factor": "Event is TODAY (starts in ~11 hours); no new intelligence since April 18 20:54 UTC briefing; market prices (34/66) reflect aggregate professional and retail positioning, but current form data is stale relative to imminent match."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.7, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = T1) STRENGTHS: T1 is priced at 66% (the heavy favorite) with strong justification \u2014 they bring superior recent form (7W-2L vs RRQ's 6W-4L), a decisive 3-0 head-to-head win just 9 weeks ago (Feb 14), and perfect 2-0 group stage performance vs VARREL and DetonatioN FocusMe. T1's recent dominance is structural, not fluky: their 7-2 record spans 9 matches, indicating consistent execution. RRQ's 6-4 record suggests greater inconsistency and occasional vulnerability. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT FAVORS NO: In the last 5 encounters, T1 has won 3 (including the most recent Feb 14 stomp). The 3-0 scoreline on Feb 14 is extremely recent and demonstrates clean dominance across the entire map pool \u2014 not a nail-biter or lucky win. MARKET MOMENTUM REINFORCES FAVORITE: NO side has risen +15.5pp over 7 days (EMA 62%) and gained +2.0pp in the last 24 hours, while YES side has fallen -15.5pp and -2.0pp respectively. Sharp money has been flowing to NO throughout the week, suggesting informed traders see T1 as the stronger team. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: Both teams are 2-0 in group stage play so far, but T1's opponents (VARREL, DetonatioN) and victories show strong execution. RRQ's wins came against ZETA (2-1, competitive) and VARREL (2-0, clean) \u2014 the ZETA match was closer, suggesting potential inconsistency. UNDERDOG (YES = RRQ) WEAKNESSES: RRQ's record is 6-4, trailing T1 by a full game in recent form. They have won only 2 of their last 5 head-to-head encounters against T1. The Feb 14 loss was a 3-0 shutout, not a competitive BO3 \u2014 suggests a skill gap. RRQ's historical head-to-head wins came in Nov 2025 and Aug 2025 (both over 6 months ago in esports time). More recent form (Feb 14, 2026) strongly favors T1, suggesting the meta or roster shifts have moved in T1's favor. VOLUME AND CONVICTION: $30.5k volume indicates modest but meaningful interest. The sustained rise in NO pricing (+15.5pp weekly) on steady volume reflects consensus that T1 is the rightful favorite, not a speculative mispricing. TIME FACTOR: Event is TODAY (~11 hours away). Very little time remains for major roster changes, patch reversals, or unexpected injuries. The market price reflects information locked in as of yesterday evening. No pending catalysts visible in the briefing that would shift the 66/34 split. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in NO (78) because the case for T1 is data-rich \u2014 recent form, H2H dominance, group stage performance, and market momentum all align. Lower confidence in YES (35) because RRQ's counter-arguments rely on old wins (6+ months) and the most recent H2H result was a 3-0 loss. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: A 28% YES probability (and 70% NO) leaves ~2pp ignorance mass, reflecting that the briefing is comprehensive but live esports always retain tail-risk variance. T1 should be favored, and the market price of 66% NO aligns with a slightly higher underlying win probability (~70-72%), suggesting NO is fairly to slightly underpriced.", "key_factor": "T1's dominant recent form (7W-2L in last 9 matches, 2-0 group stage record) combined with a clean 3-0 head-to-head victory on 2026-02-14 and superior tournament momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is priced at 34% (underdog), NO at 66% (favorite). Market has been falling for YES (-15.5pp over 7 days), suggesting confident NO sentiment despite limited new data. CASE FOR YES (UNDERDOG): RRQ's Group Stage Form is Competitive. RRQ has posted identical 2-0 clean victories (ZETA 2-1, VARREL 2-0) matching T1's undefeated group record. This suggests RRQ is performing well in tournament conditions RIGHT NOW, not on stale form. HEAD-TO-HEAD ASYMMETRY: The briefing shows RRQ won 2 of last 4 H2H (2025-11-01, 2025-08-17) but T1's most recent win was Feb 14 2026 (3-0). However, older matches (2023-2024) all favored T1, suggesting the gap has narrowed. RRQ has shown they CAN compete when conditions favor them. BO3 RESILIENCE SIGNAL: The briefing explicitly notes RRQ 'showed resilience in competitive BO3 format, taking map wins even in losses historically.' This is a structural strength \u2014 RRQ can steal maps and force competitive contests, reducing T1's leverage. TEMPORAL PROXIMITY MATTERS: Recent H2H (Feb 2026, Nov 2025, Aug 2025) are more predictive than 2023-2024 legacy wins. The Nov 2025 RRQ win is only ~5 months old; T1's Feb 2026 3-0 is fresh but was in playoffs (higher stakes, different format). Group stage is lower-pressure and may suit RRQ's style differently. CASE AGAINST YES (T1's Strengths): T1 undefeated in group stage (2-0 vs VARREL, 2-0 vs DetonatioN). T1 has superior recent H2H record (2 wins in last 5). T1's Feb 2026 3-0 demolition is the most recent datapoint and is unambiguous dominance. T1 is ranked higher in Pacific competitive hierarchy based on consistent results. RECENT FORM COMPARISON: T1 7W-2L in last 9 matches vs RRQ 6W-4L in last 10. T1's win rate (77.8%) exceeds RRQ (60%). This is the strongest objective evidence favoring T1 and supports the 66% NO price. However, the gap (18 percentage points in rate) is not insurmountable over a single BO3. PRICE MOMENTUM & MARKET CONFIDENCE: YES has fallen 15.5pp in 7 days with no significant new match data (last completed matches were Apr 12-18, mostly non-RRQ/T1 matchups). This suggests market is pricing in the Feb 2026 3-0 + T1's higher group stage form with high conviction, BUT may be overweighting recency and underweighting RRQ's demonstrated current-tournament competence. DATA GAPS: Briefing lacks 2026 H2H specific to group stage format, player-level form updates, or agent-selection context. Both teams' last matches vs group opponents are recent (Apr 11-12), but no detailed map-level analysis. This creates modest epistemic uncertainty on both sides. FAIR VALUE ASSESSMENT: The 34% YES price reflects T1 favoriteship, but RRQ's identical 2-0 group stage record, historical BO3 competitiveness, and narrowing H2H trend (2 wins in last 4) suggest TRUE YES probability is 40-45%, not 34%. RRQ is likely UNDERPRICED by ~6-11 percentage points. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (62%) because T1 has strong recent form (7W-2L), undefeated group record, and decisive Feb 2026 H2H win. Lower confidence in YES (45%) because RRQ lacks a 2026 head-to-head win AND recent form is merely competitive, not superior. The underdog case rests on structural resilience and fair-value mispricing, not dominant evidence. LIVE EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~11 hours): Reversal of large price moves is low probability at this proximity. Market has settled; sharp money is likely already positioned. This supports sticking with fundamentals rather than expecting late-breaking arbitrage.", "key_factor": "Rex Regum Qeon's recent group stage resilience (2-0 clean victories) and historical BO3 competitiveness suggest the 34% underdog price undervalues their realistic chances in a mid-tournament round-robin match."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "FORM ANALYSIS: T1 currently 7W-2L (last 9 matches); RRQ 6W-4L (last 10 matches). T1's superior recent form is significant and durable. GROUP STAGE RECORD: Both teams 2-0 in completed Week 1-3 matches. RRQ beat ZETA (2-1) and VARREL (2-0); T1 beat VARREL (2-0) and DetonatioN (2-0). T1's victories were cleaner (both 2-0 vs RRQ's 2-1 narrow win). HEAD-TO-HEAD: T1 leads 2-1 in last 5 encounters. Most recent (Feb 14, 2026) was dominant T1 win (3-0). This recency heavily favors T1 in a single BO3 snapshot. MARKET PRICE DRIFT: YES side has fallen 15.5pp over 7 days (now 34% vs 38% 7-day EMA), while NO rose 15.5pp. Suggests smart money recognizing T1 favoritism as event approaches. VOLATILITY & SHARP MOVES: Large swings Apr 16-18 (\u00b17-9pp) but no clear narrative catalyst in briefing; suggests uncertainty noise rather than new team information. BASE RATE FOR HIGHER-SEEDED TEAM: In professional Valorant BO3 group stage, the team with superior recent form and head-to-head edge typically wins 65-70% of the time when margin is this clear. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Week 3 group stage (not elimination). Both teams motivated but not in do-or-die scenario. T1's cleaner victories and undefeated group record suggest tactical mastery. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: High confidence in T1 win (NO = 68%) given durable form gap, H2H advantage, and market repricing. Moderate confidence in RRQ (YES = 32%) because BO3 introduces variance; RRQ's 2-1 win vs ZETA and historical H2H splits (2-2 in older encounters) mean upset is possible but not likely. NO DATA GAPS: Match is TODAY (11h to start); both teams have clear recent match records; head-to-head is well-documented. High resolver confidence (100/100).", "key_factor": "T1 leads recent head-to-head 2-1 (last 5 encounters); in BO3 group stage contexts, higher-ranked teams with stronger recent form convert ~65-70% of matches against mid-tier competitors"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "T1 current form superior: 7W-2L (last 9) vs RRQ 6W-4L (last 10) \u2014 T1 demonstrably hotter entering the match. T1 group stage perfection: 2-0 (VARREL 2-0, DetonatioN 2-0) vs RRQ mixed 2-0 and 2-1 \u2014 T1 cleaner execution in Week 1-3. Recent H2H: T1 won 3-0 on 2026-02-14 (dominant) and leads 2-2 in last 4 matchups \u2014 momentum favors T1. RRQ resilience noted: 2-1 vs ZETA shows competitive BO3 ability; won 2 of last 4 H2H \u2014 not a free underdog, but data-thin. Current market price (34% YES / 66% NO) reflects T1 as clear favorite \u2014 aligned with form differential and recent H2H dominance. Price movement reveals slight nervousness: YES side fell 15.5pp over 7 days, sharp moves Apr 16-18 suggest early uncertainty resolved toward T1. Crowd sentiment NOT irrationally exuberant on either side \u2014 market is pricing a meaningful favorite (T1) and a viable underdog (RRQ); no crowded-trade signal. No major news catalyst or ignored signal in briefing \u2014 match is routine Week 3 group stage; form and H2H are primary inputs. Confidence asymmetry: Strong YES confidence (72) because T1 form data is clear and recent; Strong NO confidence (75) because T1's superiority is well-established in both metrics. Time-to-reversal: ~11 hours to match start \u2014 RRQ would need a significant upset (contradicting recent H2H and form); low probability of surprise narrative shift at this point.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "T1 current form is superior: 7W-2L (78% win rate) in last 9 matches vs RRQ 6W-4L (60% win rate) in last 10 matches\u2014form matters more than ancient H2H. T1 Week 1\u20132 group stage record: 2-0 (VARREL 2-0, DetonatioN 2-0) shows clean, controlled play; RRQ's 2-0 record includes a 2-1 win vs ZETA, indicating they were pushed harder. Most recent H2H (2026-02-14) favors T1 decisively: 3-0 playoff victory demonstrates clean dominance in current meta and roster configuration. RRQ's 2025 H2H wins (Nov 1, Aug 17) are 5\u20138 months old; VCT meta shifts significantly between seasons, and roster adjustments matter in pro Valorant\u20142025 context is substantially weakened. Market price history shows strong NO-side momentum: YES fell 15.5pp over 7 days (EMA 38% \u2192 current 34%), with sharp -9.0pp and -7.5pp moves on Apr 16 and Apr 18. This reflects informed betting flow favoring T1. BO3 format in group play with T1's superior recent form and clean execution favors consistency; RRQ's historical resilience (taking map wins) is outweighed by T1's higher net map differential in 2026. No material injuries, roster changes, or external complications flagged in briefing; both teams are in stable mid-tournament rhythm. Playoff implications are secondary (group stage point accumulation stage), reducing roster stress-testing that might elevate underdog chaos\u2014T1's form advantage compounds. VLR.gg resolution source is reliable with rapid post-match publication; no ambiguity risk affecting confidence.", "key_factor": "T1's dominance in the 2026 season (7W-2L vs RRQ's 6W-4L), combined with their clean 2-0 group stage record and recent 3-0 playoff victory, significantly outweighs RRQ's historical head-to-head wins from 2025 and earlier\u2014meta evolution and roster stability favor the higher-seeded team in mid-tournament BO3 group play."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "T1's recent dominance (7W-2L, 2-0 group stage record) masks critical dependence on a tight core roster; Valorant's IGL-dependent meta means mid-round disruption cascades into round win probability faster than in other esports. The market has been falling 15.5pp over 7 days despite T1's objective strength\u2014this suggests informed traders (likely regional analysts with access to team news) are sensing a vulnerability the public briefing does not disclose. RRQ's resilience in BO3 format (took map wins even in losses historically, 2-1 victory vs ZETA) indicates they can exploit early-series reads if T1's shot-calling is compromised or delayed by roster adjustment. H2H shows RRQ has beaten T1 twice in last 5 meetings (Nov 2025, Aug 2025 playoffs); both were in formats where preparation time favored preparation over pure mechanical dominance\u2014last-minute stand-ins eliminate T1's prep advantage. NO confidence (72%) is higher than YES (62%) because: T1's current form and group stage record are documented and strong; RRQ's map pool matchups vs T1's standard bans/picks are not explicitly detailed in briefing, creating asymmetric blind spots. T1's Feb 2026 3-0 win is 2+ months old; esports patches and meta shifts in Valorant can fundamentally alter agent viability and map control\u2014briefing contains zero post-Feb tactical analysis. Group stage timing (Week 3 of 5) means both teams have reduced urgency compared to playoff stage, but T1's championship pedigree may mask tactical staleness that RRQ's fresher meta reads exploit. Thiskyhall Sala Convention Center in Ho Chi Minh City: If T1 (Korea-based) players have visa, travel fatigue, or timezone adjustment issues not yet visible in prior week matches, Day 2-3 performance can degrade sharply in BO3 format. Market spread ($0.34 YES / $0.66 NO) at 100% vig suggests ~$30k USD volume is still thin for an 11-hour-away match; sharp money has not yet fully positioned, leaving room for late-breaking roster/health news to swing odds 5-10pp in final hours.", "key_factor": "A key T1 player (likely IGL or star duelist) suffers acute illness, injury, or family emergency on match day, forcing a last-minute roster substitution with a stand-in of significantly lower caliber, breaking T1's structural dominance in mid-round calling and entry fragging."}], "final_score": 0.3127267266916731, "no_score": 0.6875574275192439, "edge": 0.3473076923076923, "no_edge": 0.037307692307692264, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5267175572519084, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.012581621277273379, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0062908106386366895, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963403", "question": "Valorant