, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 4059.376138000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["75074637413711102592194195659645544723824357400065774493374924918858854363338", "47521187358561864687767454613260277096422815652648053850442129428966122012725"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CONFIRMED: Match is SCHEDULED for 2026-04-19 08:00 UTC (~11 hours from briefing timestamp). Event has NOT occurred. Criteria unambiguous: first to win the BO3 match resolves to that team; cancel/tie/7-day delay \u2192 50-50; forfeit/walkover at start \u2192 50-50; forfeit mid-match \u2192 winning team wins. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org is primary source; fallback to credible consensus + video evidence if HLTV delays >2 hours post-conclusion. This is standard and low-risk. Name-matching criteria are clear (MOUZ NXT and Ursa are unambiguous in tournament context). FORM DATA ASYMMETRY: MOUZ NXT (4W\u20136L, last 10) shows marginal negative momentum; Ursa (5W\u20134L, last 9) shows marginal positive momentum. Ursa's +1 win differential over similar sample is weak directional signal but lacks statistical power. No head-to-head record, map preferences, or recent opponent quality provided. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES = 36%, NO = 64% (current market consensus). YES side has risen +3.5pp over 7 days; NO side fell -4.0pp. Sharp 8pp NO drop on Apr 18 20:00 UTC suggests late information flow favored MOUZ NXT, but no briefing detail explains it. Market is pricing Ursa as favorite (64% win probability). DATA QUALITY GAP: Briefing provides zero tactical intel, map-pool strengths, recent opponent context, or player-form updates. KEY FACTS section contains unrelated tournament commentary and irrelevant social-media noise (mentions of Vitality, Falcons, Aurora, IEM Rio). News summary explicitly states 'No recent news or form data specific to either team in this matchup was found.' This is a HIGH epistemic barrier. CASE FOR YES (MOUZ NXT): (1) Market has shifted +3.5pp in favor over 7 days, suggesting late information; (2) Ursa form (5\u20134) is only marginally better than MOUZ NXT (4\u20136). (3) BO3 format introduces higher variance; underdog can steal maps. Limited positive evidence. CASE FOR NO (Ursa): (1) Ursa's win rate (5\u20134 = 55.6%) outpaces MOUZ NXT (4\u20136 = 40%); (2) Market consensus 64% implies professional bettors view Ursa as stronger; (3) Ursa is the current-favorite. But this is not strong evidence\u2014form differential is marginal, and no team-specific data supports higher confidence. CONFIDENCE DOWNGRADE RATIONALE: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set below 50 because the briefing provides NO team-specific tactical, map-pool, or recent-opponent data. Market prices reflect expert consensus, but that consensus is not explained by the briefing. This creates HIGH uncertainty about whether market pricing reflects genuine edge or noise. Absent credible team-level intel, confidence in both directions must be LOW. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: probability_score = 38 (slightly below market NO consensus of 64%) reflects: (1) weak YES-side momentum in market (+3.5pp rising), (2) symmetrical weakness in form data, and (3) explicit acknowledgment that briefing provides no justification for a strong directional call. probability_no_score = 62 reflects market consensus (NO favorite) but at reduced confidence due to data gaps. Scores do NOT sum to 100 because ignorance mass (~0) is appropriate given no contradictory briefing evidence, but symmetrical data poverty justifies holding both below typical confidence thresholds. TEMPORAL COHERENCE VERIFIED: Event is SCHEDULED (not live, not past). All prior-match references in briefing are unrelated noise. Criteria are clear. No 50-50 triggers appear imminent (no cancellation signals, no 7-day delay in effect). Resolution will almost certainly depend on actual match outcome.", "key_factor": "Insufficient team-specific form data, head-to-head history, and map pool information to confidently estimate match outcome; market prices reflect expert consensus but briefing provides no tactical or recent-form justification for either team."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO / Ursa): Market currently prices Ursa at 64% to win, reflecting a structural advantage in recent form \u2014 Ursa has won 5 of 9 recent matches (55.6% win rate) versus MOUZ NXT's 4 of 10 (40% win rate), a meaningful 15+ percentage point differential. MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS URSA: Over the last 7 days, NO (Ursa) has FALLEN 4.0pp while YES (MOUZ NXT) has RISEN 3.5pp, but the fall is steeper and the volatility sharper (3.8pp/hr vs 3.6pp/hr), suggesting informed repositioning INTO Ursa (NO prices compress as buyers accumulate), not weakness in Ursa's fundamentals. CRITICAL SHARP MOVE: On Apr 18 20:00 UTC (yesterday evening), NO dropped 8.0pp in a single sharp move \u2014 this is typically a sign of large informed bets INTO the Ursa (NO) side, not against it, as professional traders lock in value before match day. MOUZ NXT WEAKNESS: A 4W-6L record in the last 10 matches shows the team is in a LOSING trend over recent weeks. This is the baseline: MOUZ NXT is underperforming relative to expectation in this Tier-2 competitive landscape. INSUFFICIENT DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD / RECENT NEWS: The briefing explicitly states 'No recent news or form data specific to either team in this matchup was found.' This means both teams' current roster stability, coaching changes, map preparation, or recent scrim results are unknown \u2014 a vacuum that typically favors the team with better recent aggregate form (Ursa). TOURNAMENT CONTEXT (NEUTRAL): NODWIN Clutch Series #7 is a Valve Tier 2 online event with 24 teams and $50K prize pool \u2014 a meaningful but not tier-1 stage. Both teams are in the Group Stage with presumably equal opportunity to advance. No evidence that either team specializes in online-only formats or has structural advantages in this specific tournament. UNDERDOG (YES / MOUZ NXT) WEAKNESSES: MOUZ NXT is trending DOWN in recent matches, has a lower win rate, and shows no documented catalyst or form reversal. Market has begun to reprice away from them (-3.5pp over 7 days on their side), suggesting even the initial YES placement at 36% was generous. LOW LIQUIDITY / EARLY ARBITRAGE: Total volume is only $4,059 USD \u2014 very thin. Early-session asymmetric information or retail overvaluation of MOUZ NXT's brand could have inflated YES prices initially. The subsequent repricing toward Ursa is consistent with informed traders correcting that mispricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 28 (low, because we lack direct evidence of MOUZ NXT's recent form drivers, map picks, or roster changes that could explain their 4W-6L slump), and confidence_no = 32 (also low, but marginally higher because Ursa's 5W-4L is a clear, documented advantage in a data-sparse environment). Neither side can be high-confidence given the absence of recent news, head-to-head data, or tournament-specific context. PROBABILITY_SCORE RATIONALE: 38 for P(YES / MOUZ NXT wins) reflects the market's favoring of Ursa (64% NO) as CORRECT given the form data, but acknowledges substantial uncertainty due to missing information. The 26-point gap (64% NO vs 38% YES) is justified by form difference (~15pp) plus market repricing signal (~8pp) plus uncertainty discount. This is NOT a coin flip \u2014 Ursa has an edge \u2014 but it is neither a dominant favorite (would require 75%+) nor a 50-50.", "key_factor": "Ursa's superior recent form (5W-4L vs MOUZ NXT's 4W-6L over comparable recent periods) combined with market repricing away from MOUZ NXT in the last 24 hours (-4.0pp on NO side), suggesting informed traders are favoring Ursa in this low-information matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "FORM ASYMMETRY: Ursa shows stronger recent record (5W-4L, 55.6% over last 9) vs MOUZ NXT (4W-6L, 40% over last 10), but sample sizes are small (9-10 matches) and insufficient to establish reliable predictive power in a single BO3. MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS YES: YES side has risen +3.5pp in 24 hours and +3.5pp over 7 days (RISING), while NO has fallen -4.0pp/7d including sharp -8.0pp move on Apr 18 20:00 UTC. This suggests informed betting is shifting toward MOUZ NXT despite 36% pricing. SHARP MOVE SIGNAL: The -8.0pp drop on NO side (Apr 18 20:00 UTC) is noteworthy \u2014 this timing coincides with potential team news, roster changes, or sharp money reassessment that the briefing does not explicitly detail. Absence of explanatory news makes this anomaly suspicious: either (a) sharp money knows something unreported, or (b) overreaction volatility. LOW-CONFIDENCE BRIEFING: The briefing explicitly states 'No recent news or form data specific to either team in this matchup was found.' This is a major data gap. Neither team has team-specific form, map pool data, head-to-head history, or recent performance context provided. Both sides operate on form alone, which is weak. URSA FORM NOT DECISIVE: While Ursa's 55.6% win rate is better than MOUZ NXT's 40%, this 15.6pp gap is not overwhelming in a BO3 context where variance (map selection, day-of performance, tactical surprises) is high. A single upset is plausible. MOUZ NXT UPSIDE: MOUZ NXT is an academy/developmental team (NXT = Next Generation). Academy teams can occasionally upset established squads via fresh tactics, reduced pressure, or leveraging practice intensity. Briefing does not rule this out. B-TIER TOURNAMENT VOLATILITY: NODWIN Clutch Series #7 is a Valve Tier 2, online event. Online tournaments show higher volatility than LANs. Academy and mid-tier teams perform less predictably online. This context favors upset probability. VOLUME SIGNAL: $4,059 USD total volume is very low for a day-of event starting in 11 hours. Low liquidity + 36% pricing on YES suggests thin confidence in the NO favorite \u2014 not necessarily YES weakness, but YES opportunity. TEMPORAL URGENCY: Event is TODAY, starting in ~11 hours. Market has stabilized (7d and 24h changes are identical: +3.5pp for YES, -4.0pp for NO), suggesting consensus is forming. If market were wildly mispriced, we'd expect additional moves. However, absence of team-specific news means repricing is incomplete. CONFIDENCE CAPPED AT 28-26: Briefing provides NO match-specific intelligence, no head-to-head data, no map pool analysis, no team news. Both sides operate on generic form data (9-10 recent matches) in a low-liquidity market with unexplained sharp moves. Confidence in BOTH directions must be depressed. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: YES confidence (28) and NO confidence (26) are nearly equal but deliberately non-mirrored. YES has market momentum and a sharp move signal that could indicate sharp money repositioning. NO has better raw form but weaker information quality. Sum (42+45=87) leaves 13pp ignorance mass, reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty on both sides.", "key_factor": "MOUZ NXT's recent upward market momentum (+3.5pp in 24h) coupled with Ursa's form volatility suggests YES underpricing relative to recent betting sentiment shift."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MOUZ NXT recent form: 4W-6L (40% win rate over last 10 matches) \u2014 below 50%, suggesting current struggle. Ursa recent form: 5W-4L (55.6% win rate over last 9 matches) \u2014 above 50%, indicating slight momentum advantage. Market price NO=64% vs YES=36% reflects Ursa favored by 28 percentage points; this is consistent with observed form differential. NO side has risen 4pp over 24hr while YES side has risen 3.5pp \u2014 suggests modest accumulation on Ursa, not panic or sharp reversal. Historical base rate for BO3 matches in Tier 2 online CS tournaments: neither team form-based prediction nor market pricing is highly reliable (confidence cap ~35). Insufficient granular data on: head-to-head record, map-specific strengths/weaknesses, current roster stability, recent scrim results, or tactical adjustments. The briefing contains unrelated esports commentary (Vitality/Falcons/Nuke references) \u2014 noise, not signal for this matchup. Market volume $4,059 is modest; liquidity constraints may allow wider spreads and slower price discovery. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (11 hours to start); reversal of Ursa dominance is theoretically possible but would require unexpected roster changes or tactical breakthroughs \u2014 both low-probability in this timeframe. Current market prices (36/64 split) appear internally consistent with the form data gap (40% vs 55.6%), but neither side has actionable evidence to justify high confidence. Probability_score = 38 (slightly above market YES=36%) reflects modest downward probability anchor from form differential, tempered by high noise and volatility typical of Tier 2 CS. Confidence_yes = 28 and confidence_no = 32: both low due to sparse match-specific intelligence; asymmetry (confidence_no slightly higher) reflects that Ursa's recent form is the only concrete datapoint supporting either thesis.", "key_factor": "BO3 match outcomes in Tier 2 online CS tournaments show no strong predictive edge for teams with marginally better recent form; volatility is high (~50-55% for the favored team in similar matchups)"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.36, "probability_yes": 0.36, "probability_no": 0.64, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market data shows YES side rising +3.5pp over 7 days and +3.5pp over 24 hours, while NO side falling -4.0pp. This suggests mild crowd rotation toward MOUZ NXT, but prices remain skewed toward Ursa (64% vs 36%). Sharp move on NO side (Apr 18 20:00 UTC: -8.0pp) suggests a single informed trade or news event, but briefing contains no corresponding news explanation. This disconnect signals uncertainty in crowd conviction. Recent form slightly favors Ursa (5W-4L vs MOUZ NXT's 4W-6L), which aligns with current NO-favoring price. However, sample sizes are small (9-10 matches) and form data alone is weak evidence for a BO3 matchup. Briefing contains NO team-specific intelligence on MOUZ NXT vs Ursa head-to-head, recent performances, map pool compatibility, or player roster changes. Only generic tournament info and unrelated esports commentary present. Crowd appears rationally apathetic \u2014 low volume ($4,059 USD), weak confidence signals on both sides, and price stability despite event starting in ~11 hours. Market is pricing based on form alone, not active sentiment. YES side sentiment is weak: briefing offers zero bullish case for MOUZ NXT. NO side sentiment equally weak: no explicit bearish narrative against MOUZ NXT. Both confidence scores must remain LOW due to data void. Current price (36% YES / 64% NO) reflects slight underdog positioning of MOUZ NXT. This is rational given worse recent form, but the margin (28pp spread) may be modest overreaction to small sample form differential. Ignorance mass is large (36 + 64 = 100, but both sides lack evidence depth). This reflects genuine forecasting difficulty, not crowded mispricing.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.62, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MOUZ NXT recent form (4W-6L, 40% win rate) vs Ursa (5W-4L, 56% win rate) shows clear structural disadvantage for YES side; in BO3 best-of-three format, single-map performance variance matters less than overall series composure\u2014Ursa's recent form suggests better consistency. Market price movement shows YES rising +3.5pp over 24h and +3.5pp over 7d, while NO has fallen -4.0pp; sharp -8pp move on NO on Apr 18 20:00 UTC suggests late-breaking information favoring MOUZ NXT, but volume is low ($4,059 total) and move may reflect thin liquidity rather than substantive new data. No team-specific head-to-head data, map pool compatibility, or recent scrim/boot camp information provided; this is critical in CS2 where meta-shifts and map veto strategy can override baseline form. Cannot assess whether MOUZ NXT has structural advantages on particular maps that would offset their weaker recent record. B-Tier tournament (Valve Tier 2) with $50k prize pool suggests mid-tier European competition; neither team is top-5 global, reducing likelihood of extreme upsets but also indicating matches are genuinely competitive and form-dependent. BO3 format reduces variance compared to single-map play; weaker team (MOUZ NXT) has two chances to win, but Ursa's 56% win rate and superior recent form give them higher probability of taking 2 of 3 maps. Event timing (TODAY, ~11 hours away) means minimal time for new roster moves, injury reports, or tactical leaks; market prices should stabilize near pre-match consensus shortly before 08:00 UTC. Briefing contains significant noise (unrelated esports commentary, copyright notices, IEM Rio references); no actionable intelligence on either team's current form, coach changes, or roster stability extracted from search results. Confidence capped at 32 for NO and 28 for YES due to lack of head-to-head history, team-specific map performance data, and recent tactical evolution; baseline form differential supports NO but insufficient granularity to rule out MOUZ NXT preparation or map pool mismatch favoring them.", "key_factor": "MOUZ NXT's 40% win rate (4-6) over last 10 matches is significantly weaker than Ursa's 56% (5-4), and in BO3 format, baseline form differential compounds across three map selections\u2014the market's 36% YES price appears reasonably calibrated to this asymmetry, though insufficient team-specific matchup history prevents high-confidence assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MOUZ NXT is explicitly an academy/development roster for Mousesports, historically high-churn and subject to sudden player loans/bench decisions not yet reflected in public briefing data. Ursa's recent form (5-4 in 9 matches) is materially superior to MOUZ NXT's (4-6 in 10 matches), yet market prices MOUZ NXT at only 36% YES \u2014 this suggests the briefing data lag is masking deterioration on the MOUZ NXT side or overweighting brand recognition. Current market pricing shows YES rising +3.5pp in 24h despite no positive news in briefing; this contradictory signal suggests either late liquidity from MOUZ backers (retail bias) or early sharp action on Ursa (smart money recognizing edge) \u2014 the latter interpretation favors a NO flip. Sharp move on NO side (\u22128.0pp on Apr 18 20:00 UTC) occurred ~12 hours before this analysis; this timing is consistent with information entering the market (roster news, scrim results, or map pool revelation) that did not percolate to the briefing document. Tournament context (B-Tier, online, 24-team group stage) means seeding/match order may create scheduling fatigue or mental momentum swings not captured in aggregate win-loss records. Briefing is almost entirely silent on map pools, recent scrim performance, or any specific tactical innovation \u2014 a competitive void suggesting either: (a) data collection failure (more likely for academy teams), or (b) a recent meta shift (e.g., new utility patch or anti-defaults surge) that static record does not capture. Academy teams historically underperform in online tournaments due to lack of main-roster resources (coaching depth, scrim partners, bootcamp facilities); MOUZ NXT's 4-6 record may reflect systemic underinvestment rather than close matches. NO confidence (35%) is deliberately suppressed below YES confidence (28%) because while Ursa's form is superior, the briefing provides NO positive evidence for Ursa specifically \u2014 neither roster stability data, nor recent upset wins, nor tactical insights \u2014 leaving the NO case equally data-starved as YES. Probability gap (32 vs 68) reflects: (1) form differential strongly favoring Ursa, (2) market repricing upward toward YES suggesting late retail backing or algorithmic rebalancing (a contrarian signal to fade), and (3) high uncertainty due to 11-hour window and minimal briefing depth on either team's current competitive state.", "key_factor": "MOUZ NXT roster instability or last-minute lineup substitution (academy team inherently prone to personnel churn) combined with Ursa's demonstrated upward trajectory (5W-4L vs MOUZ NXT's 4W-6L) masking a tactical meta shift favoring Ursa's map pool or anti-defaults strategy."}], "final_score": 0.3719997619235983, "no_score": 0.6297356679140119, "edge": 0.3273076923076923, "no_edge": 0.05730769230769228, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 32.00% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2013403", "question": "Counter-Strike: MOUZ NXT vs Ursa (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 3 match between MOUZ NXT and Ursa in the NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 19 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MOUZ NXT\" if MOUZ NXT win the match against Ursa.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ursa\" if Ursa win the match against MOUZ NXT.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 4059.376138000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["75074637413711102592194195659645544723824357400065774493374924918858854363338", "47521187358561864687767454613260277096422815652648053850442129428966122012725"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["NODWIN Clutch Series #7 is an online European CS2 tournament organized by NODWIN Gaming.", "This B-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 event taking place from", "Today I got to feel a glimpse what true vitality hatewatch felt like.", "Please give us another 0.94 zywoo shitclass.", "All our images are copyrighted and are not allowed to be used in any form of commercial work without explicit permission.", "Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "My expectation are falcons winning despite i love seeying them lose but i have seen this last dance honeymoon runs before, vitality can't match this", "They are always been bad on mirage , while falcons is decent on it (one of their best maps) and nuke was just unlucky to start", "Keep up to date with all of the action as IEM Rio hits the playoffs.", "They made that comeback cuz Aurora played bad, not that HOTU played good."], "news_summary": "MOUZ NXT vs Ursa is scheduled for 2026-04-19 08:00 UTC in the NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, a B-Tier online European CS2 tournament with a $50,000 prize pool featuring 24 teams. The match is a BO3 set to begin in approximately 11 hours. No recent news or form data specific to either team in this matchup was found in the search results.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data to build YES case."], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data to build NO case."], "key_context": ["NODWIN Clutch Series #7 is a Valve Tier 2, online European CS2 tournament", "Group Stage format with 24 competing teams and $50,000 prize pool", "Match is BO3 (best of three maps)"], "prior_match_facts": [], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-18T20:57:01.562643Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "75074637413711102592194195659645544723824357400065774493374924918858854363338", "data_points": 4, "weighted_avg": 0.36434460011988934, "change_1w_pp": 3.4999999999999973, "change_24h_pp": 3.4999999999999973, "volatility_24h": 3.617089069035119, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "47521187358561864687767454613260277096422815652648053850442129428966122012725", "data_points": 7, "weighted_avg": 0.6593181768445578, "change_1w_pp": -4.0000000000000036, "change_24h_pp": -4.0000000000000036, "volatility_24h": 3.7903385952532913, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-18T20:00:58Z", "delta_pp": -8.000000000000007}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-18T20:57:01.803324Z"}, "structured_match": {"provider": "pandascore", "provider_match_id": "1431942", "game": "csgo", "scheduled_at": "2026-04-19T08:00:00Z", "status": "scheduled", "team_a_name": "MOUZ NXT", "team_b_name": "Ursa", "match_format": "BO3", "tournament_name": "Group Stage", "final_score": null, "winner_name": null, "h2h": [], "team_a_recent_form": {"team_name": "MOUZ NXT", "matches_considered": 10, "wins": 4, "losses": 6, "last_match_at": "2026-04-17T14:00:00Z"}, "team_b_recent_form": {"team_name": "Ursa", "matches_considered": 9, "wins": 5, "losses": 4, "last_match_at": "2026-04-16T11:00:00Z"}, "fuzzy_score": 100, "fetched_at": "2026-04-18T2