{"run_id": "f40b4315-0bcb-4148-9072-c0973938bf8e", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T20:58:01.075514+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1964452", "question": "LoL: Team Secret Whales vs Fukuoka SoftBank Hawks Gaming (BO3) - LCP Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Team Secret Whales and Fukuoka SoftBank Hawks Gaming in the LCP Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 19 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Secret Whales\" if Team Secret Whales win the match against Fukuoka SoftBank Hawks Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fukuoka SoftBank Hawks Gaming\" if Fukuoka SoftBank Hawks Gaming win the match against Team Secret Whales.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.715, "volume_usd": 13558.408156000009, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["53088086405623164184642414273142782315740827058093579747684538518147624011922", "105305281919579476426776233106916724415379487496533510962426295917878420134238"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Team Secret Whales must win the BO3 match scheduled for 2026-04-19 09:00 UTC against Fukuoka SoftBank Hawks Gaming. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event has NOT started (scheduled for ~12 hours from briefing timestamp). All prior match facts (Feb 2026, Jan 2026, May 2025, Feb 2025) describe PAST encounters, not this market's event. Head-to-head history is context only. HEAD-TO-HEAD EVIDENCE (YES SIDE): Team Secret Whales show perfect 4\u20130 record in most recent matchups across 2025\u20132026. This demonstrates consistent superior gameplay and strategic advantage over this opponent. Strong signal for YES, but not determinative of a single future match. RECENT FORM CONFLICT: SoftBank Hawks lost 0\u20132 to Ground Zero Gaming on April 12 (one week prior), suggesting poor form. However, SoftBank Hawks opened Split 2 with a 2\u20130 victory over CFO on April 5, indicating capability in the current tournament. Team Secret Whales' most recent Split 2 activity is not detailed in briefing\u2014creates asymmetric information. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES = 72%, NO = 29%. Market has trended sharply upward for YES (+20.0pp over 7 days, with sharp move of +23.5pp on Apr 13). This reflects confidence in Team Secret Whales but also incorporates uncertainty. Spread (72+29=101%) suggests modest vig. IMMINENT EVENT / REVERSAL RISK: With ~12 hours until match start, a major reversal (e.g., team roster change, cancellation, emergency forfeit) is possible but low-probability. Once match begins, outcome is determined by gameplay; no extended delay or cancellation risk is flagged. Per briefing rules, forfeits before start \u2192 50\u201350 resolution; forfeits after start \u2192 winner determined. This does not materially lower probability_score but justifies moderate confidence rather than extreme confidence. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Source is gol.gg/esports/home; fallback to credible reporting + video evidence if no publication within 2 hours. No risk of oracle failure or name-matching ambiguity (team names are clear and unambiguous). This is a SECONDARY risk and should not dominate the assessment. CASE FOR NO (28%): SoftBank Hawks have recent 2\u20130 win in Split 2 (April 5 vs CFO), showing they can compete at this level. BO3 format introduces variance; single best-of-three is inherently less predictable than aggregate record. No detailed form data on Team Secret Whales' current-week performance creates epistemic gap. Market assigns ~28% to NO; this reflects real, non-trivial upset possibility. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=72 reflects strong head-to-head history and market trend. confidence_no=65 reflects weaker NO-side evidence (only one recent Split 2 win for SoftBank Hawks, unclear TSW form in Split 2, and missing matchup-specific preparation data). The NO case is less evidentially grounded but not implausible. PROBABILITY RECONCILIATION: 72 + 28 = 100, which is appropriate here: the match WILL occur and WILL have a winner (barring forfeit/cancellation, both low-probability). Strong YES evidence (H2H 4\u20130, market trend, recent opponent loss) justifies 72. Genuine uncertainty about TSW's Split 2 form and BO3 variance justifies 28 for NO rather than pushing to 20\u201325.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (~12 hours to start); head-to-head history is strong but past-tense and does not guarantee outcome; SoftBank Hawks' recent 0\u20132 loss and 2\u20130 win in Split 2 create conflicting form signals; no current-week team statistics available to resolve the conflict."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.73, "probability_yes": 0.73, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (YES): Team Secret Whales hold an unbroken 4-0 head-to-head record against SoftBank Hawks across multiple splits (Feb 2026, Jan 2026, May 2025, Feb 2025), indicating fundamental skill/stylistic matchup advantage rather than fluky variance. RECENT FORM ADVANTAGE: Team Secret Whales' 8-2 record in their last 10 matches significantly outpaces SoftBank Hawks' 6-4 record, suggesting momentum and consistency favoring the favorite. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: SoftBank Hawks suffered a decisive 0-2 loss to Ground Zero Gaming just one week before this match (April 12, 2026), indicating recent loss of form or confidence entering this fixture. MARKET MOMENTUM VALIDATION: YES side has risen +20pp over 7 days with only modest volatility, suggesting informed accumulation rather than speculative noise. Sharp move on Apr 13 (+23.5pp) likely reflected recognition of Hawks' weak form. COUNTERFACTUAL (NO CASE): SoftBank Hawks' 2-0 opening win vs CFO on April 5 demonstrates baseline competence in Split 2 format, but this single win is outweighed by the subsequent loss to GZ and historical 0-4 H2H record. BO3 FORMAT RISK (MODEST): While best-of-three formats create upset potential versus single-game markets, the persistent H2H disparity (never close) suggests structural dominance transcends format. INCOMPLETE RECENT DATA: Team Secret Whales' most recent Split 2 activity is not detailed in briefing, creating slight asymmetry in confidence. However, 8-2 form and perfect H2H compensate. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is IMMINENT (12 hours to start). For Hawks to overcome a 4-0 H2H deficit and current form disadvantage requires a significant reversal with almost no time for new catalyst emergence. This reinforces the favorite's pricing. VOLUME ADEQUACY: $13,558 USD volume is modest but sufficient for a regional LoL match; liquidity supports the 72-29 price spread without suggesting mechanical distortion. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: Confidence in YES is high (78) because H2H data, form differential, and recent Hawks losses are concrete and recent. Confidence in NO is lower (42) because the underdog case rests primarily on single-tournament win vs CFO and abstract upset potential, with no fresh catalyst visible in briefing.", "key_factor": "Team Secret Whales' perfect 4-0 head-to-head dominance over SoftBank Hawks combined with strong recent form (8-2 in last 10) establishes a structural advantage that the market correctly prices at ~72%."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.65, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 RECENT TOURNAMENT FORM: SoftBank Hawks opened LCP Split 2 with a clean 2\u20130 sweep over CFO (Apr 5), proving they can execute in the offline format and current meta. Team Secret Whales' Split 2 performance is absent from the briefing \u2014 no wins, losses, or matches documented since the tournament began Apr 4. This is a critical data gap favoring the hawk's narrative of adaptation. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 MOMENTUM TRAJECTORY: SoftBank Hawks have momentum within Split 2 context (1\u20130 in tournament play before Apr 12 loss). The Apr 12 loss to Ground Zero Gaming was only 6 days ago, but it occurred in the same tournament structure both teams are competing in NOW. BO3 formats allow for adjustment; one loss does not erase the Apr 5 victory. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 FORM OPACITY: Team Secret Whales' 8W\u20132L record (last 10 matches) is provided without tournament context or date ranges. It is unknown if these wins include Split 2 matches or prior split/tournament play. Recent form is the strongest predictor in esports, and the briefing provides no clarity on TSW's current-split performance. This ambiguity reduces confidence in YES. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY & CONTEXT: TSW's 4\u20130 H2H record is real (Feb 2026, Jan 2026, May 2025, Feb 2025), but the most recent documented match is Feb 2026 (2 months ago). In fast-moving esports environments with meta shifts, roster changes, and coaching adjustments, 2-month-old H2H data is moderately stale. No indication of roster stability or coaching changes is provided. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL \u2014 RISING YES, FALLING NO: YES has risen +20.0pp over 7 days and NO has fallen \u221221.0pp, suggesting market conviction is consolidating behind TSW. However, this trend began Apr 13 and may reflect algorithmic or public sentiment rather than fresh tactical information about Split 2 form. Sharp moves (+23.5pp on Apr 13) lack supporting context in the briefing. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-three matches introduce higher upset variance than BO1. A single poor game or draft by TSW could shift momentum; SoftBank Hawks only need to win 2 games to advance. With 12 hours until start, the inability to update on recent scrims, patch notes, or meta shifts keeps uncertainty elevated. DATA ASYMMETRY CRITICAL GAP: The briefing provides SoftBank Hawks' Split 2 results (Apr 5 win, Apr 12 loss) but offers no specific Split 2 results for Team Secret Whales. This creates a blind spot: we cannot evaluate which team has adapted better to the current tournament format or meta. Confidence in YES must remain moderate given this omission. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: LCP is S-Tier and offline, meaning both teams are competing at a high, equalized level with reduced latency advantages. This narrows the skill gap and makes upsets more plausible than in online-heavy regions. RESOLUTION CRITERIA RISK: Match is scheduled for Apr 19 and event ends Apr 19 by 15:00 UTC. No cancellation or forfeit signal exists, so the match is highly likely to be played. Standard resolution applies. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: High confidence in YES (>70%) is unwarranted because (a) TSW's current Split 2 form is unreported, (b) SoftBank Hawks have shown they can win in the current format (Apr 5 sweep), and (c) H2H data is 2 months old. High confidence in NO is similarly tempered because (a) TSW's historical H2H dominance is undeniable, (b) the 8W\u20132L record, while undated, still suggests overall strength, and (c) market pricing reflects genuine conviction, even if the reasoning is opaque. This is a genuinely uncertain matchup with asymmetric information favoring neither side decisively.", "key_factor": "SoftBank Hawks demonstrated immediate Split 2 form with a 2\u20130 victory over CFO on April 5, while Team Secret Whales' current form in Split 2 remains unreported, creating a potential asymmetry in tournament-specific momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "TEAM SECRET WHALES FORM: 8W\u20132L (last 10 matches) = 80% win rate. This is significantly above league average and indicates strong current condition. FUKUOKA SOFTBANK HAWKS FORM: 6W\u20134L (last 10 matches) = 60% win rate. Competitive but notably weaker than Secret Whales. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: Team Secret Whales hold a clean 4\u20130 record vs SoftBank Hawks in recent encounters (Feb 2026, Jan 2026, May 2025, Feb 2025). Consistent dominance in head-to-head is a reliable signal. RECENT SOFTBANK VULNERABILITY: SoftBank Hawks lost 0\u20132 to Ground Zero Gaming on April 12, 2026 (one week before this match). This suggests current form may be softer than their 6\u20134 record implies. SOFTBANK OPENING SPLIT 2 WIN: SoftBank Hawks did beat CFO 2\u20130 on April 5, 2026, showing they can compete in Split 2. However, this single win does not offset the broader form differential. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 72% closely matches the historical base rate for a 8\u20132 team vs. a 6\u20134 team in BO3 regular season play (70\u201375%). Market appears fairly priced. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side has risen +20pp over 7 days (Apr 13\u201318), suggesting accumulating confidence in Secret Whales. NO side has fallen -21pp. This aligns with form and H2H data. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-three formats allow for upset potential compared to single games, but with a 4\u20130 H2H record and 80% recent form, Secret Whales have structural advantages that persist even in a series. TIMING & IMMINENT EVENT: Match starts in ~12 hours. No material news, roster changes, or injuries are flagged. Form and H2H data remain the dominant signals. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 72 (strong form data, clear H2H, market alignment). confidence_no = 58 (SoftBank has beaten CFO and can win BO3s, but recent 0\u20132 loss and 4\u20130 H2H deficit create a steeper climb; less data favors upset).", "key_factor": "In professional LoL best-of-three regular season matches, teams with 80%+ recent win rates (8-2 form) defeat teams with 60% win rates (6-4 form) approximately 70\u201375% of the time. Head-to-head dominance (4-0 recent record) reinforces this estimate."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.71, "probability_yes": 0.71, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Team Secret Whales hold a pristine 4-0 head-to-head record against SoftBank Hawks across Feb 2026, Jan 2026, May 2025, and Feb 2025, demonstrating consistent tactical/roster superiority over extended period. Current season form favors TSW: 8W-2L (80% win rate) vs SHG 6W-4L (60% win rate) \u2014 20pp gap in recent 10-match performance, substantial in BO3 context. SoftBank Hawks showed weakness one week prior (Apr 12): lost 0-2 to Ground Zero Gaming, suggesting vulnerability or momentum shift heading into this match. Counter: SoftBank Hawks opened Split 2 with 2-0 win vs CFO (Apr 5), proving capability in current tournament patch/meta \u2014 suggests inconsistency rather than collapse. Market has risen +20pp on YES over 7 days (from ~50% to 72%), indicating trader confidence building on TSW form/H2H data \u2014 this is rational, not bubble-driven. NO side has fallen -21pp symmetrically, reflecting downward sentiment, but at 32% it retains credible upset value in BO3 format (single series, not multi-game). Crowd psychology: Market pricing aligns with objective form differentials. No signs of panic or euphoria \u2014 movement is measured (+/- 2pp in 24h, 0.5pp/hr volatility). Imminent timing (12h to start) limits new information arrival; price has likely stabilized near true odds. Low order book friction ($13.6k vol) suggests efficient pricing. BO3 format introduces variance vs BO1, but TSW's 4-0 H2H dominance across multiple BO3s (not single games) is strong signal that series-level matchup dynamics favor them. Confidence asymmetry: Strong YES signals (H2H, form, recent weakness in SHG) warrant high confidence_yes (72). NO side lacks fresh positive data beyond Apr 5 CFO win and inherent BO3 variance \u2014 confidence_no set to 55 reflecting uncertainty rather than counter-evidence. Probability sum 71+32=103 reflects dual-sided evaluation: both sides have supported evidence (TSW dominance + SHG upset potential), legitimizing overlap in belief mass.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Head-to-head dominance (4\u20130 vs SoftBank Hawks across Feb 2026, Jan 2026, May 2025, Feb 2025) is a strong indicator in team-sport esports where meta-game knowledge, coaching familiarity, and player synergy compound over time. Team Secret Whales' recent form: 8W\u20132L (80% win rate last 10 matches) is significantly stronger than SoftBank Hawks' 6W\u20134L (60% win rate), corroborating the h2h pattern. SoftBank Hawks' 0\u20132 loss to Ground Zero Gaming on April 12 (one week prior) is a negative signal, but occurs within the same LCP Split 2 environment, reducing discount for tournament-format unfamiliarity. SoftBank Hawks' 2\u20130 victory over CFO on April 5 (week 1) demonstrates they are not winless in Split 2; however, CFO is not mentioned as a top-tier threat, limiting the strength of this counterargument. Market price (YES 72%, NO 29%) is well-calibrated to the h2h record and recent form differential; the +20pp rise in YES over 7 days likely reflects SoftBank Hawks' April 12 loss becoming public, moving market toward Team Secret Whales. BO3 format introduces variance risk (upset potential higher than BO1), but Team Secret Whales' 4\u20130 record includes multiple BO3 encounters (Feb 14 and Feb 27 2026 playoff matches), suggesting they perform well in extended series against this opponent. Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (starts in ~12 hours); at this stage, no new roster changes, meta shifts, or injury reports are likely to shift the needle significantly\u2014market prices have stabilized (2pp 24-hour move). Confidence in YES is high (72) due to robust h2h data, current-split evidence of Team Secret Whales' superiority, and form disparity; confidence in NO is moderate (58) because SoftBank Hawks demonstrated Split 2 capability vs CFO, and BO3 upset risk is non-negligible, but lack of recent wins vs Team Secret Whales limits conviction. No indication of roster changes, medical issues, or external disruption that would reverse the long-standing h2h pattern in this single match.", "key_factor": "Team Secret Whales' perfect 4\u20130 head-to-head record against SoftBank Hawks spans 14 months of LCP competition across multiple splits and formats (regular season and playoffs), indicating structural team matchup advantage rather than transient form variance; however, SoftBank Hawks' 2\u20130 week-1 victory over CFO in Split 2 suggests they have adapted to the current patch and offline tournament environment."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Team Secret Whales command a pristine 4-0 head-to-head record (Feb, Jan 2026, May 2025, Feb 2025), anchoring YES conviction at baseline 72% market price. Recent form divergence: TSW 8W-2L vs SHG 6W-4L (last 10 matches) suggests TSW momentum, but SHG's 2-0 stomp of CFO on Apr 5 shows they can dominate in Split 2 format. CRITICAL BLINDSPOT: Briefing is silent on TSW's most recent Split 2 performance. No scoreline provided after Apr 4 (GZ beat CFO 2-0). TSW's last documented match in Split 2 is absent\u2014unknown whether they've played, won, or underperformed since tournament start. SHG's Apr 12 loss to GZ (0-2) is FRESH and within 1 week of this match. Momentum is fragile; however, in BO3 best-of-three formats, a team that just absorbed a 0-2 shutout may exhibit tilt, preparation fatigue, or mental reset\u2014either direction unpredictable. Offline tournament context: LCP is an S-Tier offline event. TSW's roster (Vietnamese org, international players per Liquipedia) may be subject to travel lag, scrim quality variance, or meta adaptation delay in first week of offline play that is not captured in aggregate 8W-2L stat. Market price history shows sharp +23.5pp spike for YES on Apr 13 16:00 UTC, followed by volatility. This suggests a news event (roster, odds shift, expert take) not present in briefing\u2014possible hidden information favoring TSW or disfavoring SHG. Roster/coaching data in briefing is fragmented and dated (Nov 2025). No confirmation of current TSW or SHG rosters for Apr 2026 offline event. Player injury, illness, or substitution (especially in 12-hour pre-match window) is plausible but untracked. Meta unknown: No patch notes, champion pool shifts, or tactical innovations mentioned. SHG may have prepared a meta counter to TSW's typical draft/comp that is not visible in historical H2H. Confidence asymmetry: Strong YES data (4-0 H2H, better aggregate form) justifies high confidence_yes (72). But TSW's missing recent Split 2 scoreline and offline tournament volatility keep confidence_no moderate (55) rather than low (25)\u2014the absence of TSW match data is a red flag. Probability_no_score (38) reflects: SHG's demonstrated capability (2-0 CFO, past playoff success), recent match freshness (Apr 12), and meta/roster uncertainty. It does not sum to 100 with probability_score because TSW's form advantage and H2H dominance are strong enough to leave a 6pp gap of retained YES conviction even accounting for black-swan disruptions. Time-to-reversal: Match is TODAY (12 hours away). Major roster changes or admin cancellations are extremely unlikely at this stage. Black swan must be tactical (meta counter prep by SHG) or psychological (TSW complacency / SHG desperation after 0-2 loss) rather than logistical.", "key_factor": "SoftBank Hawks exploit a meta shift or roster/tactical adjustment (unmentioned in briefing) that specifically counters Team Secret Whales' playstyle, or Team Secret Whales suffer a key player absence/underperformance due to offline tournament fatigue or preparation gap in the week since their last recorded Split 2 match."}], "final_score": 0.6906058579619716, "no_score": 0.33241029274951706, "edge": -0.02269230769230768, "no_edge": 0.40730769230769226, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_