{"run_id": "7fd1b295-00e3-4247-9818-953d7af0353a", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T21:07:40.583877+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1955607", "question": "LoL: Kiwoom DRX vs T1 (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Kiwoom DRX and T1 in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 19 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Kiwoom DRX\" if Kiwoom DRX win the match against T1.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1\" if T1 win the match against Kiwoom DRX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.185, "volume_usd": 21295.251847999996, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["78865530796365739217973210297619679283921756023246654351759608822437499729654", "66459651391017888075874064567444998030536755816449441697014382282949900299539"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.82, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: This market resolves YES if Kiwoom DRX wins the BO3 match on 2026-04-19. Match is SCHEDULED and has NOT started yet; all prior match facts describe past encounters only. T1 DOMINANCE (QUANTIFIED): T1 has won all 5 prior H2H meetings against DRX since 2024, including three 2-0 sweeps (2024-06-26, 2024-02-01, 2025-01-18). Most recent encounter (2026-01-18) was a T1 victory, only ~3 months prior. This is not a small sample \u2014 it is consistent, recent, and includes multiple format types. CURRENT FORM ASYMMETRY: T1 5W-5L (last 10); DRX 4W-6L (last 10). T1 is marginally ahead and has positive H2H momentum. DRX is underperforming T1 in raw win rate. DRX COUNTER-CASE LIMITATIONS: Case for YES notes DRX won in July 2023 (9 months ago) and could take maps in BO3 format. However, the rosters, meta, and coaching have shifted substantially since then. The 5-0 record since 2024 directly refutes the 'capability to beat T1' thesis with recent evidence. EARLY-SEASON VOLATILITY: Early Rounds 1-2 matches do carry reset risk and meta uncertainty. However, this is offset by the fact that recent Rounds 1-2 matches (2025-05-08, 2025-04-04) were also won by T1 2-0 and 0-2 (loss) respectively \u2014 suggesting Rounds 1-2 does not inherently favor DRX or create unpredictability in this pairing. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Market prices at YES 18% / NO 82% reflect the H2H dominance and current form gap. The price is stable (\u00b10.5pp/24hr) and has moved consistently toward T1 over the past week (+4.0pp for NO). This suggests informed pricing that captures T1's advantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in T1's NO (82%) is supported by quantified H2H dominance, recent form, and stable market pricing. Confidence in DRX's YES (18%) is lower because the briefing offers no new or compelling evidence that breaks T1's streak; early-season volatility is a soft factor and contradicted by DRX's underperformance in prior Rounds 1-2 matchups. TEMPORAL COHERENCE CHECK: Event is TODAY (start ~13 hours away). No final scoreline has been published yet. All prior match facts are clearly labeled as historical H2H context, not this event's outcome. Briefing is internally coherent. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: gol.gg is the primary source; tie/forfeit/cancel/7-day delay rules are unlikely to trigger in a scheduled S-Tier professional match. Oracle risk is minimal. FINAL ASSESSMENT: T1 is the heavy favorite based on 5-0 H2H record, marginally better current form, and stable market pricing. DRX's win probability is ~18%, reflecting the difficulty of breaking T1's dominance streak despite early-season reset conditions.", "key_factor": "Event is TODAY (13 hours away) with limited recent roster/form data; early-season volatility could surprise, but T1's 5-0 H2H dominance since 2024 is substantial and recent."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.82, "probability_yes": 0.82, "probability_no": 0.18, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "T1 DOMINANCE: T1 has won ALL five prior meetings against DRX since 2024 (most recent: 2026-01-18, 2025-05-08 2-0, 2025-04-04 2-0, 2025-01-18 2-0, 2024-07-28 2-0). Three of five were decisive 2-0 sweeps, indicating consistent edge in game execution and preparation. RECENT FORM SLIGHT EDGE: T1 5W-5L (last 10) vs DRX 4W-6L (last 10) \u2014 T1 maintains marginal form advantage entering the match, suggesting better momentum and adaptation to current patch/meta. META & ROSTER STABILITY: DRX's last win over T1 was July 2023 (nearly 3 years prior). Rosters, meta, and competitive environments have shifted dramatically. T1's string of recent wins (6 consecutive dating to 2024) reflects they have consistently adapted to new metas while DRX has not overcome this gap. MARKET CONSENSUS: 82% NO price reflects strong consensus belief in T1's advantage. With $21k volume and stable 7-day pricing (+4.0pp for NO over the week), the market has absorbed available information and priced T1 as clear favorite. EARLY SEASON VOLATILITY CUTS BOTH WAYS: While 'early season resets' can theoretically introduce variance, the briefing notes T1 and DRX have faced each other multiple times in early-season Rounds 1-2 formats (2025-05-08, 2025-04-04) \u2014 and T1 won both 2-0. Early season does NOT favor DRX in this matchup. DRX CAPABILITY OVERSTATED: The briefing's YES case notes DRX 'won at least 2 games in BO3 format in 2023' \u2014 but this is 3-year-old data with different rosters and meta. Recent 2025-2026 BO3 encounters all went to T1 decisively. TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE IRRELEVANT TO MATCH OUTCOME: The double round-robin and Challenge/lower bracket placement are context, not causal. They do not alter T1's demonstrated superiority in head-to-head play. ASYMMETRIC EVIDENCE: Briefing provides concrete, recent T1 wins (5-0 since 2024) vs. speculative DRX comeback potential (based on 3-year-old data and general volatility arguments). T1 case is fact-anchored; DRX case is theory-dependent. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in T1 win (78) because H2H record, recent form, and market pricing align strongly. Lower confidence in DRX (42) because underdog case relies on meta-shift speculation and early-season volatility rather than hard evidence of DRX capability vs. this specific opponent in 2026.", "key_factor": "T1's perfect 5-0 head-to-head record against DRX since 2024, including three 2-0 sweeps, demonstrates structural superiority in team execution and matchup understanding."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNDERDOG'S CASE (DRX YES at 18%): Market is anchoring too heavily on T1's 5-0 H2H record since 2024 without accounting for structural factors favoring upset potential. Early-season reset: Rounds 1-2 in LoL esports are notoriously volatile \u2014 teams are still calibrating to patch changes, roster synergy is incomplete, and preparation levels vary. This is NOT a mid-season or playoff match where form converges. DRX's recent form is 4W-6L (40% win rate), but T1 is only 5W-5L (50% win rate) \u2014 a marginal 10pp gap. Both teams are middling in current form, contradicting the narrative that T1 is vastly superior RIGHT NOW. Historical H2H is a lagging indicator: T1's last 5 consecutive wins span Jan 2024\u2013Jan 2026 (24 months). League of Legends meta shifts dramatically every 2\u20133 patches. The last DRX win (July 2023) predates current rosters and patch cycles. H2H is informative but not destiny in early season. DRX has taken maps off T1 before (2023 matchups recorded as competitive BO3s). They are not an auto-loss team \u2014 they have demonstrated capability to win games in head-to-head. A BO3 requires winning just 2 of 3 games, not 1. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES (T1 NO at 82%): T1's price reflects overconfidence in historical dominance without proportional weight to current form data. T1 is 5W-5L in last 10 matches \u2014 a .500 team. Being favored at 82% (implying ~4.5:1 odds) for a matchup where both teams have identical recent form (within 10pp) is aggressive pricing that conflates legacy reputation with present capability. BO3 format amplifies variance: Unlike BO1, a BO3 requires consistency across 3 games. A single game upset is plausible; sustaining it twice in a row is harder but possible early season when preparation is uneven. No recent patch-specific data in briefing: The briefing does not reference current patch (likely 14.8 or similar April 2026 patch), meta shifts, or champion pool changes. Without this context, claiming T1's dominance transfers automatically is speculative. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 35 (low) because the briefing provides weak concrete evidence for a DRX upset \u2014 no recent DRX form narrative, no meta advantage analysis, no roster moves or roster strength data. The upset case relies on early-season volatility (plausible but generic) and recent form parity (weak). confidence_no = 72 (moderate-high) because the briefing provides strong H2H dominance (5-0 since 2024) and structural context (BO3, LCK format). However, confidence is capped at 72 rather than 85+ because: (1) recent form gap is narrow (5W-5L vs 4W-6L), (2) no patch-specific or roster-specific data supports T1's superiority in THIS patch, (3) early season volatility is a documented LoL phenomenon not addressed in briefing. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY: probability_score (28) and probability_no_score (72) sum to 100, but the distribution reflects that the case against NO (T1) is stronger on historical data than the case for YES (DRX) on current form. The bear's argument for DRX rests on structural volatility, not concrete edge; the case for T1 rests on proven H2H dominance. This asymmetry is honest to the evidence. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: DRX bans/counters one of T1's signature champion pools, wins 2 early teamfights due to superior macro play in Rounds 1\u20132 meta, and executes cleanly. BO3 allows them to win 2\u20131 or even 2\u20130 if T1 is not fully prepared for early season. Probability: ~25\u201330%, justified by form parity + early-season variance. MARKET MISPRICING?: YES side at 18% may be slightly underpriced (fair value closer to 22\u201328%) given the narrow recent form gap and early-season context. However, T1's historical dominance is real and cannot be dismissed. 18% is defensible, not egregious.", "key_factor": "Early-season Rounds 1-2 volatility and meta reset can neutralize T1's historical H2H dominance when roster synergy and preparation are in flux."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.82, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: T1 has won all 5 documented prior meetings since 2024 (Jan 2024\u2013Jan 2026), with three 2-0 sweeps. No DRX victories in the recent sample. EXTENDED DROUGHT: DRX's last confirmed victory over T1 occurred in July 2023 (>21 months prior to this match). Roster/meta changes do not historically favor the perennial underdog in this pairing. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: T1 (5W\u20135L last 10) vs DRX (4W\u20136L last 10). While both are middling, T1's slight edge in win rate aligns with historical head-to-head pattern. MARKET EFFICIENCY: The 82% NO price closely reflects the empirical base rate (8/8 recent wins for T1 \u2248 100%, market at 82% shows modest underdog premium for DRX). EARLY SEASON VOLATILITY CAVEAT: The briefing notes 'early season divisional matchup' and 'first-round matches are often volatile.' However, this does not overturn the overwhelming historical evidence that T1 beats DRX consistently, regardless of season timing. FORMAT STABILITY: BO3 format is standard; no unusual structural advantage for DRX. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Very high confidence in T1 win (72) based on unambiguous 8-game winning streak. Confidence in DRX win kept moderate (75 on NO side) only because early-season tournaments can surprise\u2014but the base rate strongly supports T1. PROBABILITY_NO (82) JUSTIFIED: 8/8 recent T1 victories + current form data support ~80\u201385% T1 probability; therefore ~15\u201320% DRX probability. Market is pricing DRX at 18%, consistent with base rate. NO RECENT UPSET SIGNALS: No injuries, roster changes, or meta shifts mentioned that would favorer DRX; briefing provides no counter-evidence to the 2+ year T1 dominance.", "key_factor": "T1 vs DRX head-to-head: T1 won 8/8 recent encounters (2024\u20132026); DRX last beat T1 in July 2023. Base rate for T1 victory in this matchup \u2248 100% over past 2+ years."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.82, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "T1 dominance in H2H is overwhelming: 5 consecutive wins vs DRX since 2024, including three 2-0 sweeps. No DRX victory since July 2023 (9+ months ago). This historical signal is strong and recent. Current season form shows T1 at 5W-5L (50% winrate) vs DRX at 4W-6L (40% winrate) across last 10 matches. Marginal difference but T1 slightly ahead. Market price of 18% YES reflects appropriate skepticism of DRX's chances given sustained T1 dominance. This is NOT an extreme outlier price. CASE FOR YES (DRX): Early-season Rounds 1-2 reset narrative is weak without supporting evidence in briefing. DRX's last map-win was in 2023 BO3s, but no recent data showing meta shifts favor them. Roster changes/synergy could help but no evidence provided. CASE FOR NO (T1): Five straight H2H wins, three 2-0 sweeps, consistent dominance across 2024-2026 period. Most recent 2026-01-18 win confirms T1's edge is current-season validated, not historical artifact. Market has been STABLE: YES price moved -4.0pp over 7 days (drifting downward), 24h volatility only 0.4-0.6pp/hr. This suggests low emotional panic or euphoria \u2014 consensus has settled. Volume of $21,295 is moderate but sufficient for a same-day LCK match. No sign of late-money movement or crowd panic reversals. Confidence asymmetry: Strong YES confidence (72) due to clear H2H data and recent wins. Moderate NO confidence (75) because early-season upsets CAN happen in BO3s, and briefing provides no roster/meta intel to definitively rule out DRX surprise. Mispricing check: 18% for DRX when they have 0 wins in 5 recent encounters and 40% season winrate vs T1's 50% appears FAIR, not a value opportunity. Market is not irrationally dismissing DRX. Time-to-reversal risk: Event is TODAY (13 hours away). No new intel will arrive in time to meaningfully shift odds unless breaking news (roster changes, forfeits). Current price reflects available information efficiently.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.82, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "T1's head-to-head dominance is decisive: 5-0 record since 2024 with three clean 2-0 sweeps (2024-02-01, 2024-06-26, 2025-04-04). This level of consistency across 2+ years and multiple roster iterations indicates systematic advantage, not variance. DRX's last victory was July 2023 (>2.75 years ago). The claim that 'meta and rosters have shifted' is true but does not overcome the empirical pattern: T1 has adapted faster to every meta shift since mid-2024. Recent form (last 10 matches): T1 5W-5L vs DRX 4W-6L. T1 is objectively stronger in current form entering this match, contradicting the 'early-season volatility resets everything' narrative. BO3 format favors consistency and execution\u2014exactly T1's strength. DRX would need to win 2 maps against a team that has beaten them 2-0 in five of the last eight encounters. Probability of taking map 1 against T1 is ~30-35% based on H2H; probability of winning 2+ maps is multiplicatively lower (~12-18%). LCK Rounds 1-2 'reset' argument is overstated: records carry over to group play, and T1's preparation advantage (superior coaching, resources, player pool) means they are unlikely to enter an early-season match underprepared against a known opponent. Market price (18% YES / 82% NO) closely aligns with the empirical H2H data and current form differential. The market has correctly priced this as a heavily T1-favored matchup. No major roster changes, injuries, or meta upheaval reported in briefing that would disrupt T1's established dominance pattern. Confidence in YES (DRX) is capped at 72 because early-season BO3 matches do carry inherent volatility, and a single strong game from DRX on map 1 could shift momentum. However, confidence in NO (T1) is high at 78 because the H2H record and form data are robust. Ignorance mass (probability_score + probability_no_score = 100) is appropriate here: the briefing provides sufficient data to evaluate both sides symmetrically, with the YES-side confidence slightly lower due to DRX's weaker recent form vs. T1's consistency.", "key_factor": "T1's perfect 5-0 record against DRX since 2024 with three 2-0 sweeps reflects structural team-composition and macro-gameplay advantages that persist across meta shifts and early-season resets, particularly in BO3 format where consistency across multiple games is critical."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "T1's 5-game winning streak vs DRX is overwhelming: 3x 2-0 sweeps, zero map drops in 2024\u20132025 post-July 2023. Market pricing at 18% YES already reflects this consensus; 82% NO is heavy T1 favorite. However, briefing is conspicuously silent on: (1) T1's recent 5W-5L form (not dominant), (2) DRX's 4W-6L form (weak but not disqualifying for a single BO3), (3) roster/coaching changes not mentioned, (4) meta patch details. Rounds 1-2 is explicitly described as 'reset' with 'records carry over'\u2014suggests early-season volatility and preparation variance matter more than aggregate stats. T1's Jan 2026 victory (most recent, 1-2 loss in Group Stage) shows T1 *lost a map* to DRX just 3 months ago; not a dominant sweep. Black swan: DRX likely invested heavily in Rounds 1-2 prep targeting T1's playstyle given the 5-loss streak motivation. A single map win + meta adaptation (off-meta pick or tactical shift not visible in recent stats) can tilt BO3 momentum, especially if T1 enters with rust or underestimation. Absence of signal: No mention of T1 player absences, coaching changes, or meta shifts that would explain why DRX is priced at only 18%. If briefing is simply extrapolating H2H without considering early-season reset dynamics, market is overconfident in T1. Event timing TODAY (13 hours away) means any late roster news or scrim leaks could shift odds, but current snapshot locks in consensus bias favoring T1. Confidence in YES lowered to 35% because T1's H2H dominance is genuine and recent; but confidence in NO capped at 72% (not 85%+) because early-season format volatility and DRX's desperation-driven prep are underweighted by the 82% price. The gap between probability_score (22) and probability_no_score (76) reflects the asymmetric black swan: DRX's meta/tactical edge would flip the match outright, while T1's favored status doesn't protect against a single BO3 upset in a reset window.", "key_factor": "DRX deploys a newly-scrimmed off-meta comp or roster adjustment (e.g., substitute jungler or support) targeting T1's predictable early-game patterns, exploiting T1's first-match rust in a Rounds 1-2 reset window where preparation asymmetry can negate historical H2H dominance."}], "final_score": 0.2959658052594501, "no_score": 0.7516268944830653, "edge": 0.5073076923076922, "no_edge": -0.12269230769230766, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.22699386503067492, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.34659934659934616, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.17329967329967308, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1955607", "question": "LoL: Kiwoom DRX vs T1 (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Kiwoom DRX and T1 in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 19 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Kiwoom DRX\" if Kiwoom DRX win the match against T1.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1\" if T1 win the match against Kiwoom DRX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the