{"run_id": "d035716c-d774-4ec2-9ea0-1f713d7baf8d", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T21:11:23.120104+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963408", "question": "Valorant: Nongshim RedForce vs Gen.G Esports (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Nongshim RedForce and Gen.G Esports in the VCT Pacific Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 19 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim RedForce\" if Nongshim RedForce win the match against Gen.G Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gen.G Esports\" if Gen.G Esports win the match against Nongshim RedForce.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 3795.410865, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["108110695029595409459895257203049348879038702052466394177166790859213127331868", "53602495839220571111242459110318614574674688661860332666493490263743127149206"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.66, "probability_yes": 0.66, "probability_no": 0.34, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event is scheduled TODAY (Apr 19, 2026 10:00 UTC), ~13 hours from briefing timestamp (Apr 18 21:11 UTC). Match has NOT started. Prior H2H (Nongshim 2-0 Gen.G on Aug 8, 2025) is historical context only, not proof of this event's outcome. FORM DATA: Nongshim RedForce shows strong recent form (8W-2L, 80% win rate last 10 matches). Gen.G Esports shows weaker form (5W-5L, 50% win rate last 10 matches). This 30-point form differential is significant. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Current market YES price 66% aligns closely with briefing's weighted EMA (67%). This suggests market consensus has efficiently incorporated available data. The 66% YES price reflects Nongshim's form advantage. HEAD-TO-HEAD PRECEDENT: Nongshim defeated Gen.G 2-0 in their most recent prior encounter (Aug 8, 2025). While roster compositions may have evolved in 8 months, this provides directional evidence favoring Nongshim. CASE FOR YES (Nongshim 66%): (1) Superior recent form 8W-2L vs 5W-5L; (2) prior H2H victory 2-0; (3) market has priced this favorably with stable YES accumulation (+14.5pp over 7 days); (4) betting market confidence suggests sharp money sees value in Nongshim. CASE FOR NO (Gen.G 34%): (1) Gen.G is a top-tier Korean org with strong competitive pedigree; (2) April 12 match vs Paper Rex showed competitive individual performances (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture all noted as competitive); (3) Gen.G has roster depth and institutional strength; (4) single prior match (Aug 2025) may not reflect current meta/roster state after 8 months. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes is higher (72) because recent form data (8W-2L vs 5W-5L) is concrete and recent. confidence_no is lower (58) because briefing provides limited detail on Gen.G's current roster composition, recent stage performance, or meta-specific strengths. Only one recent match reference (Apr 12 vs Paper Rex) is mentioned without detailed outcome. FORFEITURE/CANCELLATION RISK: Resolution criteria specify 50-50 if match is canceled, delayed >7 days, ends in forfeit, or walkover before start. These are low-probability edge cases (~3-5% combined) given VCT's organizational rigor. Reflected in modest confidence reduction but not probability adjustment. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: VLR.gg is primary source; fallback to credible reporting + video evidence if VLR.gg silent >2 hours post-match. Valorant match outcomes are typically clear and objective (map scores). Low oracle risk (~1-2%). FINAL ASSESSMENT: Probability 66% reflects Nongshim's form edge + prior H2H + market consensus. Probability_no 34% reflects Gen.G's tier-1 status and competitive potential despite recent weaker form. These do NOT sum to 100 due to edge-case resolution risk (~2-4% for cancellation/forfeiture/tie), which is appropriate given LIVE/IMMINENT timing and VCT operational stability.", "key_factor": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (starts in ~13 hours); briefing lacks recent 2026 form data, head-to-head from 2025 may not reflect current roster/meta; Gen.G roster composition and recent stage performance unknown."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FORM ASYMMETRY (FAVORS YES): Nongshim's 8W-2L record over last 10 matches is substantially stronger than Gen.G's 5W-5L. This 3-win gap suggests Nongshim is in better peak condition entering a high-stakes group-stage match. HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE (FAVORS YES): Nongshim defeated Gen.G 2-0 on 2025-08-08 (\u22488 months prior). While roster changes could have occurred, the absence of contradictory evidence and Nongshim's continued strong form suggest they retain a tactical edge. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT (FAVORS YES): At 66% YES, the market has already priced in Nongshim's advantages. The 7-day EMA of 67% shows market confidence has been stable and consensus-driven, not reactive noise. Sharp volatility on Apr 15 (+13pp, +7pp moves) suggests informed bettors reinforced YES conviction. GEN.G'S MIXED SIGNALS (FAVORS YES): Gen.G's April 12 match vs Paper Rex showed 'competitive individual stats' but explicitly lacked 'dominant carries.' Mixed individual performances in a Bo3 format (where clutch playmaking matters) suggest Gen.G may lack a clear win condition. TIMING & VOLATILITY (SLIGHT CAUTION FOR YES): Event is TODAY (~13 hours away). The market's recent +5.5pp move toward NO in the last 24 hours is modest but non-negligible. However, given low absolute volume ($3,795 USD) and that YES still trades at 66%, this appears to be minor late repositioning, not informed counter-thesis. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS ANALYSIS: Gen.G's S-Tier Korean organization pedigree is real, but pedigree \u2260 current form. At 5W-5L, Gen.G has lost half its matches\u2014including to teams in the same tournament. No recent injury reports, coaching changes, or tactical innovations are mentioned for Gen.G that would offset Nongshim's form advantage. RESOLUTION MECHANICS (LOW IMPACT): No forfeit, cancellation, or walkover risks are signaled in briefing. Match is scheduled, offline, in Korea\u2014standard infrastructure. 50-50 scenarios are unlikely unless both teams withdraw simultaneously. CASE FOR NO LIMITATIONS: The CASE FOR NO only cites organization prestige and Apr 12 'competitive' stats. No evidence of Gen.G's recent trajectory reversal, no edge case meta shifts, no roster upgrades mentioned. Briefing lacks depth on Gen.G's preparation or anti-Nongshim stratagem. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market's 66% YES reflects reasonable confidence, not overconfidence. Nongshim's 8-2 form + 2-0 H2H + Gen.G's 5-5 slump justifies probability in the 65\u201372% range. Setting to 68% acknowledges Nongshim's edge while respecting Gen.G's organizational quality and live-match volatility. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes=72 reflects strong form data and H2H evidence. confidence_no=38 reflects weak case against Gen.G\u2014pedigree is not gamestate evidence, and April 12 stats are vague. Asymmetry (72 vs 38) signals briefing favors YES side substantively.", "key_factor": "Nongshim RedForce's dominant recent form (8W-2L vs Gen.G's 5W-5L) combined with a decisive 2-0 head-to-head victory in August 2025 establishes clear momentum and tactical familiarity."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "probability_yes": 0.38, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR GEN.G (NO): Market prices Gen.G at only 34% despite being a top-tier Korean organization competing in a Korean offline tournament where regional teams typically perform strongly. The single H2H reference (Aug 2025 Nongshim 2-0) is 8+ months old and predates the current VCT 2026 roster evolution \u2014 insufficient to anchor modern form. FORM ASYMMETRY: Nongshim's 8W-2L record (80% win rate) is compelling, but Gen.G's 5W-5L (50%) is measured over the same 10-match window. The briefing does not specify whether these wins/losses are from the same tournament, same meta, or comparable competition levels. Gen.G's April 12 match vs Paper Rex shows distributed individual stat competitiveness (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture), suggesting no collapse, only fragmentation. KOREAN HOME ADVANTAGE UNDEREXPLORED: VCT Pacific Stage 1 is explicitly an offline tournament held in Korea. Gen.G, as a historically dominant Korean org, benefits from home-field infrastructure, reduced travel fatigue, and familiarity with local servers/ping. Nongshim also plays in Korea, but Gen.G's organizational depth may translate better to offline LAN conditions than regular online league play. H2H RECENCY & CONTEXT PROBLEM: The 2025-08-08 victory (Nongshim 2-0) is 8+ months old. Player transfers, meta shifts, and mid-season roster adjustments are routine in VCT. The briefing provides zero evidence that either team's roster is stable or that the August result reflects current agent pools, map bans, or anti-stratting. This single data point is brittle. MARKET OVERWEIGHTING H2H: The betting market appears anchored to the prior 2-0 result, driving YES to 66%. However, esports markets frequently misprice based on recency bias and stale H2H records. A 34% price for a top-tier Korean organization in a Korea-based LAN tournament may be artificially suppressed. GEN.G COMPETITIVE PEDIGREE NOT QUANTIFIED: The briefing describes Gen.G as 'top-tier' with 'strong roster depth and competitive pedigree' but provides no ranking, win % in prior VCT stages, or playoff appearance data. This is a data gap \u2014 confidence in NO must be constrained by the absence of comparative strength metrics. VOLATILITY & MARKET UNCERTAINTY: Price history shows sharp moves (Apr 13 -26.5pp; Apr 14 +9.0pp; Apr 15 \u00b113.0pp swings), suggesting informed traders have been repositioning. The 7-day trend shows NO falling -14.5pp, but this may reflect panic-selling ahead of the match rather than fundamental deterioration. Light volume ($3,795) means few data points undergird the current odds. NONGSHIM'S FORM NOT CONTEXTUALIZED: An 8W-2L record is strong, but the briefing does not specify wins vs which opponents, wins vs Meta King teams, or whether the 2 losses occurred recently (suggesting vulnerability to stronger opponents or meta shifts). Without opponent quality adjustment, the record alone is uninformative. NO RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD IN 2026: Nongshim and Gen.G have not yet met in VCT 2026. The April 19 match is early-stage Group Alpha play. Early-stage upsets are more common than post-playoff upsets because seeding is fluid and preparation is incomplete. Gen.G could be a meta-counter pick or have prepared a specific anti-Nongshim strat. RESOLUTION RISK (MINOR): Match is TODAY, 13 hours from briefing timestamp. Cancellation/delay beyond 7 days = 50-50 resolution. This is low-probability but non-zero, slightly favoring neither side. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: Confidence in YES (45) reflects strong form data (8-2) but lacks opponent quality context and is heavily dependent on a stale H2H. Confidence in NO (52) reflects organizational prestige and home-field advantage but lacks quantified competitive metrics. Neither side has airtight evidence; probability_no_score (55) is slightly above 50 because Korean organizational infrastructure + home LAN + market overweighting of old H2H provides a coherent upset narrative, but it remains a genuine toss-up absent fresh head-to-head or roster/meta data.", "key_factor": "Gen.G's organizational pedigree and competitive depth in Korea's offline VCT environment may outweigh a single 2025 H2H result in a fundamentally different competitive landscape."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.32, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Event Category: Professional esports Bo3 match between regional competitors in S-tier offline tournament (VCT Pacific Stage 1). Base Rate Context: Top Korean orgs (Gen.G) historically win ~55-60% of group-stage matches against regional peers; H2H record creates negative adjustment for the losing side. Form Snapshot: Nongshim RedForce 8W-2L (80% last 10); Gen.G Esports 5W-5L (50% last 10) \u2014 Nongshim demonstrates superior current form over a relevant sample. Head-to-Head: Nongshim defeated Gen.G 2-0 on 2025-08-08 (~8.5 months ago). In esports, H2H weight diminishes over time due to roster changes and meta shifts, but this is recent enough to carry meaningful signal (~+8-10pp for Nongshim). Market Pricing: YES at 66-67% (EMA), NO at 33-34%. Market price aligns closely with form differential and H2H advantage; no extreme mispricing detected. Market Stability: YES side weighted EMA 67%, 7-day change +14.5pp (rising); volatility 1.4pp/hr is low for esports. Sharp moves (Apr 15) suggest information updates; current price appears stable and informed. Gen.G Strength: Top-tier Korean org with deep roster (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture show competitive stats vs Paper Rex Apr 12). However, 5W-5L form is below typical elite-team baseline; suggests meta misalignment or roster stability issues rather than structural weakness. Confidence Asymmetry: Strong YES-side confidence (72) due to clear form gap + H2H + market consensus. Moderate NO-side confidence (58) because Gen.G's tier status and Korean offline advantage (tournament in Korea) may compress the probability if meta favors aggressive/structured play; insufficient data on 2026-specific roster evolution and recent scrim results to raise confidence higher. Event Timing (TODAY, 13hrs to start): No time for major reversals; market has settled. Probability reflects pre-match information quality as-is. Data Gaps: No roster change announcements, no recent scrim leaks, no coach/management news; Gen.G's full recent match history vs other Group Alpha teams not provided. This limits confidence_no adjustment upward. Conclusion: Nongshim is the rational favorite by form, H2H, and market consensus. Market price (66-67%) is well-grounded and not exploitable from base-rate perspective. Assign ~68% YES, reflecting form + H2H advantage with modest uncertainty buffer for elite Korean org resilience.", "key_factor": "Top Korean Valorant teams (Gen.G tier) win ~55-60% of matches vs mid-tier regional opponents; recent head-to-head (2-0 loss) depresses Gen.G win probability by ~10-15pp from baseline"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.35, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Current market price (66% YES) is closely aligned with objective form metrics: RedForce 8W-2L vs Gen.G 5W-5L is a compelling 3-win gap that naturally supports a ~65-70% YES probability. H2H precedent (RedForce 2-0 win Aug 2025) reinforces the YES narrative, though this is 8+ months old and esports rosters/meta can shift significantly\u2014market appropriately discounts it rather than overweighting. Gen.G's April 12 performance vs Paper Rex shows competitive individual stats across roster (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture), suggesting they remain dangerous despite 5W-5L record\u2014this provides some NO-side credibility. Market momentum: YES side stable at ~67% EMA over 7 days (+14.5pp rise, then holding), NO side gradually declining (-14.5pp over 7 days). Sharp moves Apr 15 (\u00b113pp swings) suggest initial volatility has settled into consensus. Volume ($3,795 USD) is modest for an S-Tier VCT match hours before start\u2014indicates neither panic nor euphoria; participants are confident in current pricing rather than frantically repositioning. No ignored signals detected: RedForce's clear recent form advantage is the dominant explanatory variable; Gen.G's organizational pedigree is acknowledged but does not overcome recent win-rate gap. TIMING: Event starts in ~13 hours. Market is pricing a stable, data-driven edge (RedForce favored by form). No major unexpected news or roster announcements present in briefing to suggest imminent reversal. Probability_no (35%) reflects NO-side's real but limited upside case: Gen.G is competitive, not helpless, but must overcome a 3-win deficit in recent form\u2014rational crowd pricing this as underdog territory. Sum of probability_score + probability_no_score = 103%, indicating slight double-counting of uncertainty on both sides (legitimate given meta shifts possible in esports), but close to 100% suggests market efficiency.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.55, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Nongshim RedForce enters with strong recent form: 8W-2L (80% win rate) in last 10 matches, indicating cohesive gameplay and meta adaptation. Gen.G Esports shows inconsistent recent form: 5W-5L (50% win rate), suggesting mid-tier competitive positioning or ongoing roster/coaching adjustments. H2H advantage (2025-08-08 victory, 2-0 scoreline) is dated by ~8 months; Valorant patches, agent bans, map pools, and roster changes materially reduce relevance of ancient H2H data. Market price (YES 66%, NO 34%) reflects reasonable confidence in Nongshim but appears slightly underpricing Gen.G's organizational pedigree and playoff experience. Gen.G's April 12 match data (vs Paper Rex) shows individual player depth (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture) but briefing notes 'mixed' and 'no dominant carries'\u2014suggesting execution inconsistency. Offline Korean venue and S-Tier tournament context: both teams are competing in home region (VCT Pacific Stage 1 held in Korea), reducing travel disadvantage variance. Group stage format (2 RR groups, top 4 advance) implies both teams are seeded competitively; neither is an outlier underdog. Event timing (13 hours until match): no reversals with strong evidence possible at this stage; market prices unlikely to shift on new player injury/roster news. Confidence asymmetry: strong data on Nongshim's recent dominance (confidence_yes: 72); weaker visibility into Gen.G's internal cohesion and coaching efficacy post-April 12 (confidence_no: 48). Probability_no_score set to 55 (not 32 = 100-68) because Gen.G's top-tier pedigree and roster talent plausibly justify a 45\u201355% baseline even if current form favors Nongshim; briefing does not rule out upset.", "key_factor": "Recent form (8W-2L vs 5W-5L) is the most reliable predictor in professional Valorant at the group stage level, where metagame shifts and team cohesion matter more than single past H2H results separated by 8+ months."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.48, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES at 66% reflects Nongshim's 8W-2L form (80% win rate) vs Gen.G's 5W-5L (50%), plus Aug 2025 H2H 2-0 win. This is rational but potentially overweighting recent aggregate form without accounting for tournament-specific dynamics. BLACK SWAN VECTOR 1 \u2014 META SHIFT: The briefing provides NO analysis of agent pools, map bans, or recent patch implications for this specific BO3. Gen.G's April 12 match vs Paper Rex is mentioned only for individual stats, not tactical composition. A meta shift favoring Gen.G's agent flexibility (e.g., Omen/Sova heavy meta) could neutralize Nongshim's mechanical edge. BLACK SWAN VECTOR 2 \u2014 OFFLINE TOURNAMENT PSYCHOLOGY: VCT 2026 Pacific Stage 1 is an OFFLINE Korean LAN held in Korea (Gen.G's home region). Gen.G has deep organizational experience in such environments; Nongshim's 8W-2L is likely vs online/mixed opponents. Offline pressure and crowd dynamics can flip 80% favorites to 50-50. BLACK SWAN VECTOR 3 \u2014 ROSTER/PLAYER AVAILABILITY: The briefing is dated 2026-04-18 21:11 UTC, ~13 hours before match. No explicit confirmation of full rosters for either team in this specific match is provided. A last-minute illness, travel delay, or visa issue in a Korean offline tournament is rare but has non-zero probability and would trigger 50-50 resolution. BLACK SWAN VECTOR 4 \u2014 GEN.G FORM TRAJECTORY: Gen.G is 5W-5L over last 10 matches \u2014 a 50% win rate that masks potential upward momentum. The April 12 performance vs Paper Rex shows competitive individual stats (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture all mentioned positively), suggesting Gen.G may be trending up INTO this match, contradicting the static aggregate. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 68 because Nongshim's recent form is clear and verifiable; confidence_no = 52 because the briefing is silent on Gen.G's psychological state, tactical preparation, and offline tournament advantage. This gap reflects data quality asymmetry, not equal uncertainty. PROBABILITY SUM LOGIC: probability_score (62) + probability_no_score (48) = 110%, reflecting the genuine asymmetric upside risk to Gen.G from offline/meta/organizational factors that the briefing does not explicitly measure but competitive Valorant history suggests are material. CONTRARIAN POSITION: The council will likely anchor to Nongshim's 8W-2L form and recent H2H win. The flip scenario is NOT that Nongshim suddenly loses mechanical skill, but that an offline Korean LAN with a top-tier organization (Gen.G) playing in their home region, combined with unobserved meta/tactical preparation, neutralizes form gap and surfaces organizational depth advantage.", "key_factor": "Gen.G deploys a tactical meta innovation (agent/map composition shift) or roster adjustment that exploits a gap in Nongshim's recent scrim data, compounded by offline tournament pressure favoring Gen.G's organizational depth and experience in high-stakes Korean LAN environments."}], "final_score": 0.6471036918452155, "no_score": 0.36373273050272453, "edge": 0.037307692307692264, "no_edge": 0.3473076923076923, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5267175572519084, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.012581621277273379, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0062908106386366895, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963408", "question": "Valorant: Nongshim RedForce vs Gen.G Esports (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Nongshim RedForce and Gen.G Esports in the VCT Pacific Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 19 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nongshim RedForce\" if Nongshim RedForce win the match against Gen.G Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gen.G Esports\" if Gen.G Esports win the match against Nongshim RedForce.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 3795.410865, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["108110695029595409459895257203049348879038702052466394177166790859213127331868", "53602495839220571111242459110318614574674688661860332666493490263743127149206"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Asia-Pacific.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Korea.", "Group Stage: April 3<sup>rd</sup> - May 3<sup>rd</sup>, 2026.", "Each Group has 6 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "VCT 2026: Pacific Stage 1 results, upcoming matches, and VODs.", "ZETA DIVISION roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in North America.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "VCT 2026: Pacific Stage 1 is an offline Korean VAL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 03 to May 17 2026"], "news_summary": "Nongshim RedForce and Gen.G Esports are set to face off in a Best-of-3 match on April 19, 2026 as part of VCT 2026 Pacific Stage 1 Group Alpha. The Group Stage runs from April 3 to May 3, 2026, with all matches played as Bo3 format. Both teams are competing in a two-group round-robin structure where the top 4 teams from each group advance. Gen.G recently competed against Paper Rex on April 12, 2026 in the same tournament, providing insight into their current form.", "side_yes_case": ["Nongshim RedForce previously defeated Gen.G Esports 2-0 on 2025-08-08, establishing a recent head-to-head advantage", "Gen.G's recent match stats vs Paper Rex show mixed individual performances, with no dominant carries standing out", "Nongshim enters as the betting favorite based on prior H2H record"], "side_no_case": ["Gen.G Esports is a top-tier Korean organization with strong roster depth and competitive pedigree in VCT", "Gen.G's April 12 match performance data shows competitive individual stats across multiple players (Karon, ZynX, Lakia, t3xture)"], "key_context": ["VCT 2026 Pacific Stage 1 is an offline tournament held in Korea running April 3 \u2013 May 17, 2026", "Group Stage format: two single-round robin groups of 6 teams each, all Bo3 matches, top 4 advance", "Match is scheduled for April 19, 2026 at 10:00 UTC (within Group Stage window)"], "prior_match_facts": ["2025-08-08 \u2014 winner: Nongshim RedForce (0-2) @ Group Alpha"], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-18T21:11:06.782977Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "108110695029595409459895257203049348879038702052466394177166790859213127331868", "data_points": 127, "weighted_avg": 0.6731299494411848, "change_1w_pp": 14.500000000000002, "change_24h_pp": -1.5000000000000013, "volatility_24h": 1.3999530067300918, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:00:40Z", "delta_pp": -8.500000000000007}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T16:00:44Z", "delta_pp": 13.0}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T23:00:41Z", "delta_pp": 6.999999999999995}]}, "no": {"token_id": "53602495839220571111242459110318614574674688661860332666493490263743127149206", "data_points": 46, "weighted_avg": 0.32735841993458686, "change_1w_pp": -14.500000000000002, "change_24h_pp": 5.499999999999999, "volatility_24h":