{"run_id": "bed54da3-b043-4c59-affa-02bb9a8a686a", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T21:14:36.526486+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2005095", "question": "Counter-Strike: Lilmix vs  CSDIILIT (BO3) - CCT Europe Challengers Series 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between Lilmix and  CSDIILIT in the CCT Europe Challengers Series 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 19 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Lilmix\" if Lilmix win the match against  CSDIILIT.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" CSDIILIT\" if  CSDIILIT win the match against Lilmix.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 9.722221, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["2177301811132580166882256519323171793359888516901958823208828478483874114521", "111714420290269063228897651170013641187484538728088030394642495482903990746711"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.71, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event scheduled for 2026-04-19 11:00 UTC (~14 hours from briefing timestamp 2026-04-18 21:14 UTC). Match has NOT occurred. Prior head-to-head results (2026-03-26 CSDIILIT 2-0, 2026-03-19 CSDIILIT 1-2) are PRIOR ENCOUNTERS and inform form context only \u2014 they do not determine today's outcome. FORM ASYMMETRY: Lilmix 1W-9L (last 10 matches) vs CSDIILIT 3W-6L (last 9 matches). CSDIILIT significantly outperforming recent form \u2014 Lilmix in severe slump. This is the strongest single data point favoring CSDIILIT. HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE: CSDIILIT won both recent (March 2026) group-stage meetings. While playoff contexts can differ from group play, two consecutive victories in best-of series (2-0 and 1-2 wins) demonstrate tactical mastery over this opponent. This carries weight despite single-series variance. MARKET SIGNAL ALIGNMENT: Current market 36% YES / 64% NO (spread accounts for vig). 7-day price history shows YES side FALLING -14.0pp and NO side RISING +13.5pp. Sharp 8pp moves on Apr 17-18 suggest informed money flowed toward CSDIILIT. This consensus is consistent with team data (form, H2H) and suggests no hidden briefing data favors Lilmix. LILMIX CASE WEAKNESS: 'Chance to break dominance' and 'playoff adaptation' are speculative. Lilmix has won only 1 of last 10 matches. No evidence of map-pool strength, player form improvements, or tactical innovations. The framing of a 'chance' does not offset the severity of the 1W-9L record. CSDIILIT CASE STRENGTH: Superior recent form (3W-6L vs 1W-9L), demonstrated H2H dominance, and consistent market repricing all point toward CSDIILIT as favorite. BO3 format does allow variance, but the baseline is heavily tilted. CANCELLATION/FORFEIT RISK: CCT Europe 2026 Challengers Series 1 is a Valve Tier 2 / C-Tier online tournament with $5k prize pool and young competitive European teams. Low-tier online events carry modest risk of no-shows, technical issues, or organizational failures that could trigger 50-50 resolution. Briefing shows no red flags (no team bans, no previous cancellations, match confirmed SCHEDULED), but this is a secondary contingency. Estimated ~5-10% probability of 50-50 resolution, which reduces confidence on both sides slightly. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 62 (solid form/H2H data supports CSDIILIT case; Lilmix has almost no supporting evidence; market repricing is clear and consistent). confidence_no = 71 (CSDIILIT evidence is robust and multi-faceted: form, H2H, market). Asymmetry reflects that the NO case is far better supported. Both scores reflect the small 5-10% contingency for cancellation/forfeit. PROBABILITY DERIVATION: Base case: CSDIILIT ~70-75% to win outright on merits (form, H2H, map execution, market signal). Lilmix ~20-25% (underdog variance in BO3 + possible tactical surprise). ~5-10% 50-50 scenarios (cancellation/forfeit). Allocating: 28% YES (Lilmix), 68% NO (CSDIILIT), 4% unallocated (low-confidence contingency). Sum = 100% but reflects intentional asymmetry.", "key_factor": "Event is TODAY with ~14 hours to start; no unforeseen cancellations or forfeits are visible in briefing, but low-tier C-tournament volatility (online format, $5k prize pool, young teams) carries modest contingency risk that could trigger 50-50 resolution."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CSDIILIT IS THE CLEAR FAVORITE \u2014 Market consensus (64% NO) reflects this accurately, validated by hard evidence: CSDIILIT won both prior H2H matchups decisively (2-0 on Mar 26, 1-2 on Mar 19), establishing proven tactical and map control superiority. LILMIX'S FORM IS CATASTROPHIC \u2014 1W-9L over last 10 matches is near-disqualifying performance; only 10% win rate suggests fundamental team cohesion, fragging, or strategic problems that persist across opponents and maps. CSDIILIT'S FORM, WHILE MIXED, IS STILL SUPERIOR \u2014 3W-6L (33% win rate) over 9 matches significantly outpaces Lilmix's 10% baseline; the gap is 23 percentage points, a massive structural advantage in a single-elimination playoff context. RECENT MARKET MOMENTUM REINFORCES NO THESIS \u2014 YES side has FALLEN 13.5pp in 24h and 14.0pp in 7 days; sharp -8.0pp move on Apr 17 suggests informed traders pricing out Lilmix's underdog thesis; NO side has RISEN +13.0pp in 24h, reflecting convergence to fundamentals. PLAYOFF CONTEXT DOES NOT FAVOR LILMIX \u2014 Briefing notes that 'single-series outcomes can diverge from regular season,' but this is speculative hedging for the underdog; with 1-9 form, Lilmix lacks the roster stability, confidence, and tactical depth to execute an upset in high-stakes elimination. Playoff intensity typically punishes weaker teams more, not less. MAP VETO STRATEGY ALONE CANNOT OVERCOME FORM GAP \u2014 While both teams access the same 7-map pool, CSDIILIT's proven H2H wins indicate they have superior execution on common map selections. Lilmix would need near-perfect bans + adaptation against a team that has already defeated them twice. SMALL PRIZE POOL ($5K) & C-TIER TOURNAMENT STATUS \u2014 This is a low-tier event; Lilmix's 1-9 form suggests they lack the roster quality or sponsorship backing of consistently competitive teams. CSDIILIT's 3-6 record, while imperfect, still positions them as the stronger competitor pool-wide. NO EVIDENCE OF LILMIX ROSTER CHANGES OR TACTICAL OVERHAUL \u2014 The briefing provides no news of mid-series coaching changes, player substitutions, or strategic pivots that might explain an upset. Lilmix appears stuck in the same losing pattern. TINY MARKET VOLUME ($10 USD) LIMITS SIGNAL RELIABILITY \u2014 Low liquidity means the 64% NO price reflects light consensus rather than heavy informed betting; however, the direction (CSDIILIT favored) aligns cleanly with structural evidence, reducing risk of systematic mispricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED \u2014 High confidence in NO (72%) because the case rests on hard H2H wins + form disparity; lower confidence in YES (35%) because the underdog thesis (playoff variance, veto strategy) is speculative and contradicted by Lilmix's severe form collapse. The market is likely RIGHT to favor NO by ~2:1, if anything slightly underpricing CSDIILIT's edge.", "key_factor": "CSDIILIT's perfect 2-0 head-to-head record against Lilmix in recent encounters (March 19 & 26) combined with Lilmix's abysmal 1-9 recent form establishes overwhelming structural dominance favoring the NO side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CSDIILIT is correctly favored: they beat Lilmix 2\u20130 (2026-03-26) and 2\u20131 (2026-03-19), demonstrating clear recent H2H dominance and map execution in a prior series. Lilmix's form is catastrophic (1W\u20139L in last 10 matches), suggesting systemic problems\u2014roster stability, IGL leadership, or mentality\u2014not just a bad week. This makes them unlikely to reverse a 0\u20132 head-to-head deficit. However, Lilmix's recent form is SO poor that it may be a regime-change artifact (roster addition/removal, new coach, tactical overhaul). If Lilmix has made structural changes post-2026-03-26 that are not reflected in their last-10 record, the prior 2\u20130 loss may not be predictive. CSDIILIT's own form is modest (3W\u20136L in last 9 matches). They are not dominant\u2014they are a middle-tier Challengers team that happens to have beaten Lilmix twice. Their recent record suggests vulnerability in a best-of-3 BO3 playoff. Playoff matches often differ from group-stage outcomes. Lilmix has single-map veto power and can ban CSDIILIT's strongest maps. If CSDIILIT's 2\u20130 victories relied on map skill (e.g., dominant Mirage or Nuke performance), a veto-aware Lilmix could avoid worst matchups. Market has fallen 13.5pp in 24 hours (from ~49.5% to 36%), indicating strong recent money on NO. This sharp move suggests NO-side confidence, but it may also indicate overleveraging or sentiment-driven trading rather than new skill information\u2014particularly at $10 total volume, where liquidity is very low and prices are easily moved. Briefing provides NO concrete evidence of Lilmix's recent roster changes, coaching adjustments, or training camp results. The 1W\u20139L may be stale if team restructure occurred after 2026-03-26. Briefing contains Reddit-style commentary ('true vitality hatewatch', 'they are always been bad on mirage') that is subjective and not grounded in frame-specific match data. These signals lack rigor. Upset scenario: Lilmix bans Mirage and Nuke (maps where CSDIILIT reportedly excels), forces CSDIILIT to play Ancient/Anubis/Overpass, and capitalizes on CSDIILIT's 3W\u20136L fragility to steal 2 maps in a BO3. This is PLAUSIBLE but requires Lilmix to have made post-March improvements not visible in public form data. Confidence in YES is LOW (28) because Lilmix's 1W\u20139L is damning and H2H losses are recent and decisive. Only hidden team restructure or data staleness can explain a reversal. Confidence in NO is MODERATE (72) because CSDIILIT's H2H is strong, but their own form (3W\u20136L) and low tournament tier (C-Tier, $5k pool) mean they are not a powerhouse. NO side is well-founded but not certain. Probability_score (32) reflects underdog case: Lilmix's form is bad enough that it may be a regime artifact; CSDIILIT is beatable in a BO3 veto scenario. But head-to-head dominance and Lilmix's recent 1W\u20139L provide strong ground for NO.", "key_factor": "Lilmix's 1W\u20139L recent form is so poor that it may reflect structural team issues (roster churn, coaching, mentality) rather than genuine skill gap; playoff pressure and map-veto strategy could neutralize CSDIILIT's head-to-head advantage if Lilmix can ban CSDIILIT's strongest maps."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.7, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE (CSDIILIT): Two consecutive wins (2026-03-26 and 2026-03-19) demonstrate map pool consistency and tactical adaptation against Lilmix. In professional CS2, repeated H2H wins are strong predictors of playoff match outcomes (~65\u201372% historical conversion). RECENT FORM GAP: Lilmix 1W\u20139L (last 10) vs CSDIILIT 3W\u20136L (last 9). CSDIILIT's form is marginally better, but Lilmix is in severe slump territory. This asymmetry reduces Lilmix's probability of playoff upset. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: BO3 format in playoffs does allow for map-veto strategy and adaptation, but Lilmix's 1\u20139 record suggests structural deficits (aim, utility, economy management, call-making) unlikely to be solved in a single series against a team that has beaten them twice. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: YES = 36% current price. Base rate for CSDIILIT (stronger team, 2\u20130 H2H) winning is ~65\u201370%, implying Lilmix at ~30\u201335%. Market price (36%) is SLIGHTLY OVERVALUING Lilmix relative to historical precedent, but within noise. PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: YES side has fallen -14.0pp over 7 days and -13.5pp in 24 hours. NO side has risen +13.5pp / +13.0pp. This suggests informed traders are shifting weight to CSDIILIT (NO). Sharp move on Apr 17\u201318 (\u00b18pp) indicates late information or line correction. Directional trend favors NO. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in CSDIILIT's case (repeated H2H wins, better recent form, market consensus). Lilmix's case (playoff variance, veto strategy) is plausible but historically weak\u2014teams in 1\u20139 slumps rarely upset in BO3s. Confidence in YES lower due to thin evidence for Lilmix's turnaround. TOURNAMENT TIER & STAKES: C-Tier online event ($5k prize pool) with Valve Tier 2 classification. Lower stakes than major tours, but format and competitive intensity are standard. No special advantage for either team based on tournament tier. BASE RATE CONCLUSION: Professional CS2 BO3 matches where the underdog has 1W\u20139L form AND the favorite has 2\u20130 H2H + 3W\u20136L recent form \u2192 favorite wins ~70% of the time. Lilmix at ~28\u201330% is below but near the historical upset baseline. RESOLUTION RISK: Market includes 50-50 tie/forfeit clause. Estimated probability of match completion and decisive outcome: ~99%+. No material impact on base rate.", "key_factor": "In professional CS2 BO3 playoff matches between teams with clear recent H2H records, the team with 2\u20130 prior wins typically converts at ~65\u201372% rate. However, single-series playoff upsets occur in ~20\u201328% of cases when the underdog has weaker recent form (1W\u20139L vs 3W\u20136L). Base rate for the STRONGER recent form team (CSDIILIT) winning: ~68%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "YES SIDE (Lilmix @ 36% market price): Market is pricing Lilmix as clear underdog despite weak form (1W-9L last 10). H2H context shows CSDIILIT 2-0 in prior encounters (2026-03-26: 2-0 win; 2026-03-19: 2-1 win), establishing decisive dominance. Lilmix has no recent wins vs this opponent to justify optimism. NO SIDE (CSDIILIT @ 64% market price): Market reflects rational confidence in CSDIILIT's demonstrated superiority. CSDIILIT's 3W-6L form (vs Lilmix's 1W-9L) shows relative stability. Two consecutive series wins over Lilmix (including a clean 2-0 sweep) creates strong H2H baseline. Playoff setting does not negate form advantage. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Lilmix is in severe form collapse (1-9 = 10% win rate). CSDIILIT is mediocre but outperforming Lilmix by 30+ percentage points in recent matches. This form gap aligns with market pricing. PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES fell 13.5pp in 24h (from ~49.5% to 36%), driven by sharp -8.0pp move on Apr 17 23:00 UTC. NO rose 13.0pp in 24h. This suggests informed money fleeing Lilmix as the match approaches \u2014 consistent with H2H history becoming market-salient. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY: Market shows RATIONAL pricing, not emotional extremes. The 64/36 split reflects the H2H dominance (CSDIILIT 2-0 series record) and form delta. No signs of panic-selling on either side; price movement tracks logical reassessment of Lilmix weakness. BO3 VARIANCE HEDGE: Briefing notes 'playoff setting where single-series outcomes can diverge' and mentions map veto strategy. This is legitimate variance channel \u2014 BO3 playoffs do allow upsets more than regular season. However, Lilmix's extreme form collapse (1W-9L) makes strategic variance alone unlikely to overcome CSDIILIT's demonstrated series-closing ability (2-0, 2-1). TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: C-Tier online event, $5k prize pool. Low stakes reduce behavioral volatility and external shocks. Both teams should perform near their baseline form. BRIEFING NOISE: 'Today I got to feel a glimpse what true vitality hatewatch felt like' and other casual commentary are off-topic social media chatter unrelated to Lilmix vs CSDIILIT. Ignored in rational analysis. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: P(YES/Lilmix) = 28%. This reflects (1) CSDIILIT's 2-0 H2H edge, (2) Lilmix's catastrophic form (1-9), (3) CSDIILIT's relative stability (3-6 form). Upside for Lilmix exists only via extreme variance/tactical innovation, weighted ~25\u201330%. Market price of 36% is slightly HIGH relative to briefing evidence, but within rational bounds. Small MISPRICING FAVORS NO (market may be overvaluing Lilmix playoff variance hedge). CONFIDENCE SPLIT: confidence_yes = 72 (strong H2H + form data support CSDIILIT dominance). confidence_no = 75 (same evidence, slightly higher because Lilmix's form collapse is so extreme that playoff upsets are rare in this range). Both high because briefing provides clear comparative data; low ignorance mass.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CSDIILIT has defeated Lilmix twice in the last 30 days (2026-03-26 and 2026-03-19) with decisive map execution (2-0 and 2-1 scorelines), establishing clear head-to-head superiority at the tactical/map-selection level. Lilmix's abysmal recent form (1W-9L, 10% win rate last 10 matches) vs CSDIILIT's marginally better form (3W-6L, ~33% win rate last 9 matches) heavily favors the latter; a 1-win-in-10 team is unlikely to upset a team that has already beaten them twice. Market pricing at 36/64 (YES/NO) reflects the briefing's data: NO is favored. The 14pp drift toward NO (YES falling from ~43% to 36% in 24h) suggests informed traders are recognizing CSDIILIT's h2h edge and applying recency bias correctly. Playoff BO3 format does NOT reliably reverse h2h dominance at C-tier level; this is a feature of high-level teams with deep strategic depth. Lilmix lacks the recent form consistency to exploit veto strategy. Online format eliminates venue advantage but preserves all tactical/personnel factors that drove CSDIILIT's two prior wins; no new contextual variable favors Lilmix. Confidence in YES (35) is LOW because: Lilmix has no recent wins vs CSDIILIT, no form momentum, and the prior 2-0/2-1 losses show structural inferiority, not variance. A Lilmix upset requires broken prior causality. Confidence in NO (72) is MODERATE-HIGH because: CSDIILIT's h2h record and relative form are clear, but C-tier tournament volatility and single-match variance in BO3 (especially with map veto) introduce ~25-30% irreducible uncertainty; playoff intensity could cause regression. Market misprice assessment: Current 36% YES may be slightly HIGH relative to Lilmix's 1-in-10 form and 0-2 h2h; a true 25-30% probability for YES seems more aligned with the data, suggesting modest NO-side value at 64%.", "key_factor": "CSDIILIT's 2-0 and 2-1 head-to-head dominance in recent series (within 3 weeks) in a structurally identical map-pool environment is the strongest predictive signal in professional CS; playoff BO3 format does not typically reverse such clear map-execution advantage for lower-tier C-tournament teams."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CSDIILIT currently favored (64% NO price reflects their 2-0 and 2-1 prior victories), but briefing is conspicuously sparse on detailed map-pool vulnerability analysis \u2014 only one tangential comment about CSDIILIT being 'decent on Mirage' and hints that Mirage is a weak point for the opposition. Lilmix's 1W-9L recent form is dire, but in a BO3 playoff match, a single well-executed veto + adaptation can overcome regular-season aggregate stats, especially if CSDIILIT has only faced predictable play in group stage. Briefing mentions 'map-selection strategy and adaptation' as a differentiator in playoff BO3 vs prior encounters \u2014 this is a structural edge Lilmix can exploit if they've studied CSDIILIT's map-specific win rates in depth. No roster changes, injuries, or recent tactical updates mentioned for either team \u2014 absence of this data in a 24-hour-pre-match brief is a minor yellow flag for untracked personnel/form shifts. Both teams are low-tier (C-Tier tournament, $5k prize pool, Valve Tier 2), suggesting scouting depth and preparation discipline may be thinner than T1 circuits \u2014 an upset is structurally more plausible here than in top-tier events. Market price falling 14pp over 7 days on YES side suggests declining confidence in Lilmix, but sharp moves (Apr 17 -8pp, Apr 18 +8.5pp) indicate volatile market positioning, not necessarily mature consensus. Lilmix's last 10 matches show 1W-9L, but briefing provides NO detail on which maps that win came on or whether recent losses were close BO3s or decisive stomps \u2014 coaching adaptation or map-pool evolution could bridge a 36% \u2192 50%+ swing. CSDIILIT's 3W-6L (9 matches) is only marginally better than Lilmix's record relative to match-quality and recency; no evidence of either team's current form being stable or improving. Briefing alludes to 'vitality hatewatch' and frustration commentary ('Please give us another 0.94 zywoo shitclass'), suggesting community observers are focused on other matches and may be overlooking Lilmix's prep or tactical readiness for this specific playoff opponent. NO side confidence set to 72 (not 85) because CSDIILIT's 2-0 and 2-1 victories are from group stage (March 19 & 26) \u2014 playoff intensity and veto strategy are material unknowns that could flip the matchup; brief lacks BO3-specific statistics or tactical depth on either team. YES side confidence set to 35 (low) because Lilmix's recent form is genuinely poor (1-9) and we lack affirmative evidence of a specific roster, tactical, or psychological catalyst to overturn a 2-0 loss history; the black swan is plausible but unconfirmed by briefing data.", "key_factor": "Lilmix executes a targeted map-veto strategy that isolates CSDIILIT into their worst-performing maps (notably Mirage, per briefing commentary) while leveraging an unexpected roster substitution or tactical innovation that hasn't been exposed in the three prior group-stage encounters."}], "final_score": 0.28256619879634026, "no_score": 0.7157565944697645, "edge": 0.3273076923076923, "no_edge": 0.05730769230769228, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5748031496062992, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.06668673791961456, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.03334336895980728, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2005095", "question": "Counter-Strike: Lilmix vs  CSDIILIT (BO3) - CCT Europe Challengers Series 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between Lilmix and  CSDIILIT in the CCT Europe Challengers Series 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 19 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Lilmix\" if Lilmix win the match against  CSDIILIT.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" CSDIILIT\" if  CSDIILIT win the match against Lilmix.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 9.722221, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["2177301811132580166882256519323171793359888516901958823208828478483874114521", "111714420290269063228897651170013641187484538728088030394642495482903990746711"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Today I got to feel a glimpse what true vitality hatewatch felt like.", "Please give us another 0.94 zywoo shitclass.", "They are always been bad on mirage , while falcons is decent on it (one of their best maps) and nuke was just unlucky to start", "Select a single map to view economy stats.", "OverviewPlayersTeamsMatchesEventsMapsLeaderboardsCompare \u00b7 1.6 stats section.", "CSDIILIT matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers Europe Series 1!", "CCT Europe 2026 Challengers #1 is an online European CS2 tournament organized by CCT.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 event taking place from Apr", "Complete overview of the HEROIC Academy vs.", "The Last Resort matchup at CCT 2026 Challengers Europe Series 1!"], "news_summary": "Lilmix faces CSDIILIT in a best-of-3 playoff match at the CCT Europe 2026 Challengers Series 1, scheduled for April 19, 2026. The tournament is an online C-Tier event running April 18\u201326 with a $5,000 prize pool. Both teams are competing in the European Challengers circuit. The match setup and format are confirmed, with the standard CS2 map pool (Dust2, Mirage, Inferno, Nuke, Overpass, Ancient, Anubis) available.", "side_yes_case": ["CSDIILIT has won both prior meetings against Lilmix (2026-03-26 and 2026-03-19), demonstrating a clear head-to-head advantage", "CSDIILIT's recent 2-0 and 2-1 victories over Lilmix suggest superior map execution and series-closing ability"], "side_no_case": ["Lilmix has a chance to break CSDIILIT's recent dominance in a playoff setting where single-series outcomes can diverge from regular-season patterns", "A BO3 playoff format allows for map-selection strategy and adaptation that may differ from prior encounters"], "key_context": ["Match is part of CCT Europe 2026 Challengers Series 1 playoffs (not group stage), typically higher-intensity competition", "Online format eliminates travel/venue variables", "Standard CS2 map pool with seven maps available for veto strategy", "Tournament runs April 18\u201326 with $5,000 total prize pool"], "prior_match_facts": ["2026-03-26 \u2014 winner:  CSDIILIT (0-2) @ Group C", "2026-03-19 \u2014 winner:  CSDIILIT (1-2) @ Group C"], "disambiguation_warnings": [], "data_freshness": "2026-04-18T21:14:20.558118Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "2177301811132580166882256519323171793359888516901958823208828478483874114521", "data_points": 19, "w