{"run_id": "e20d3e27-21c0-4957-9145-8bbd53f721ab", "timestamp": "2026-04-18T21:53:30.982590+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963335", "question": "Valorant: G2 Esports vs Leviat\u00e1n Esports (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between G2 Esports and Leviat\u00e1n Esports in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win the match against Leviat\u00e1n Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leviat\u00e1n Esports\" if Leviat\u00e1n Esports win the match against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.86, "volume_usd": 152132.0931649999, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["104149769634112853375808955805018250307764188157003896088455837310435061261147", "26943164101083235743919519175373027382347728406544753174529351728588876747301"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "probability_yes": 0.42, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "TEMPORAL COHERENCE: Event timing is LIVE_OR_PAST and match started ~53 min ago (21:00 UTC). PandaScore confirms status = RUNNING. The briefing contains no final scoreline or result confirmation \u2014 only pre-match analysis. DISAMBIGUATION WARNING HONORED: Side_yes_case[3] contains past-tense language ('2-1 win in Apr 2025, 2-0 in') referencing PRIOR H2H encounters (2025 and 2024 matches). These are NOT this market's outcome. The current match outcome remains undetermined. MARKET SIGNAL INTERPRETATION: YES price at 86% (NO at 14%) reflects sharp upward movement at Apr 18 21:52 UTC (+18.5pp), coinciding with match start. This suggests live trading activity as match progresses, not a settled outcome. The high YES price likely reflects real-time G2 performance or favorable map outcomes, not pre-game expectation alone. PRE-MATCH CONTEXT (FORM/SEEDING): Leviat\u00e1n entered as favored: 1-0 record, +15 round differential, defeated ENVY 2-1 recently. G2 opened 0-1, 0-2 maps, -7 round differential. H2H record mixed: G2 won 2025 encounters (2-1, 2-0) but Leviat\u00e1n won 2024 encounters (3-1, 2-0). LIVE GAME STATE INFERENCE: The 21:52 UTC sharp move (+18.5pp YES, -14.0pp NO) occurring 52 minutes into a BO3 match suggests mid-match momentum shift favoring G2. BO3 format allows comebacks; a 1-0 map lead for either team is recoverable. Without live scoreline data, the +18.5pp move implies G2 is performing better than pre-match expectations in real time. CONFIDENCE DOWNGRADE FOR LIVE UNCERTAINTY: For LIVE/IMMINENT events, reversal probabilities are highly data-sensitive. The briefing provides no current map score, round counts, or economy state. Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are capped at 35\u201345 to reflect this live-state fog. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: vlr.gg is the primary source with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. Once match concludes (likely within 1\u20132 hours from briefing), official result should be available rapidly. Mechanism risk is LOW and secondary to outcome uncertainty. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Pre-match form slightly favored Leviat\u00e1n, but live +18.5pp YES move at 52 min suggests G2 has recovered or is winning in-game. A BO3 at 50% completion with one team trading up sharply typically reflects that team gaining momentum. Assessed probability: G2 ~42%, Leviat\u00e1n ~58%. These do not sum to 100 because live game state introduces asymmetric outcome uncertainty \u2014 the true probability will resolve to ~99% or ~1% once the match concludes, and we are in the middle of that resolution process. NO FINAL OUTCOME IN BRIEFING: The briefing is internally coherent but deliberately incomplete (match is ongoing). The market will likely trade to $0.01/$0.99 within 1\u20132 hours once the match concludes, regardless of oracle publication delay.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/RUNNING as of briefing timestamp (21:53 UTC, 53 min after start); outcome is being determined in real-time and no final scoreline has been reported in the briefing, making any probability estimate highly volatile and subject to live game state uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES \u2014 G2 WINS): \u2022 G2's recent H2H record is decisively stronger: 2-1 win (Apr 2025) and 2-0 win (Feb 2025) vs. Leviat\u00e1n, showing G2 adapted and dominated in direct matchups within the past 12 months. \u2022 Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 dominance (+15 RD, 1-0 record) is a **early-stage inflated sample**; one match provides minimal predictive power in a 6-team round-robin with 5 remaining matches per team. \u2022 G2's 0-1 opening loss (-7 RD) is early-tournament variance, not evidence of fundamental weakness; G2 has international VCT pedigree and experience that typically allows recovery in group stages. \u2022 Market pricing (86% YES) reflects sophisticated sharp money recognizing G2's H2H edge and the volatility of Week 1 standings; the +34.5pp 7-day rise and +18.5pp sharp move at match kickoff (Apr 18 21:52 UTC) suggest informed backing of G2. \u2022 Leviat\u00e1n's 2024 H2H wins (3-1, 2-0) are 1.5+ years old and predate G2's recent roster/meta adjustments; 2025 data supersedes 2024. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO \u2014 LEVIAT\u00c1N UNLIKELY): \u2022 Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 success is a **single-match sample** in a 10-match group stage; early tournaments are notorious for regression and meta shifts between weeks. \u2022 Leviat\u00e1n has **not proven sustained dominance** vs. G2 in recent competitive windows (0-2 head-to-head in 2025 after winning 2024). \u2022 Group Alpha's field is stacked (MIBR 1-0, LOUD 1-0, Leviat\u00e1n 1-0, plus ENVY, G2, Cloud9); Leviat\u00e1n's +15 RD advantage is marginal in a competitive pool and unlikely to compound against a motivated, experienced G2 team seeking to avoid 0-2. \u2022 No evidence in briefing that Leviat\u00e1n has strengthened roster or meta understanding since their 2024 wins; 2025 results show G2 adaptation. MARKET CONTEXT & TIMING: \u2022 EVENT STATUS: LIVE (started ~53 minutes ago as of data timestamp 21:53 UTC on Apr 18). Match is **actively underway**; sharp late-game moves occurred at +21:52 UTC (+18.5pp YES spike), indicating real-time information flow favoring G2. \u2022 For LIVE events, a reversal from 86% YES would require rapid swing momentum (Leviat\u00e1n taking maps) AND confirmation within the remaining ~3 hours of match window. Market confidence (high YES %) reflects both pre-match analysis (H2H, pedigree) and early map results. \u2022 Volume ($152k USD) is moderate-to-high, supporting that the 86% price reflects genuine consensus, not thin-book artifact. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: \u2022 confidence_yes (62): Strong case for G2 rests on recent H2H data (2025 wins), market momentum, and early-stage variance argument. However, **Leviat\u00e1n's live Week 1 form is still empirical fact** \u2014 they are 1-0 with +15 RD. That cannot be dismissed as noise. \u2022 confidence_no (35): Limited direct evidence for sustained Leviat\u00e1n dominance. The case for NO relies on Week 1 continuation + meta advantage, but no briefing data explicitly supports Leviat\u00e1n's map pool strength, recent scrim performance, or roster cohesion vs. G2's known H2H edge. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: \u2022 72% YES reflects: (a) G2's superior 2025 H2H record (2-1, 2-0 weighted more than 2024 results), (b) market's 86% price as anchor but slightly conservative given brevity of Group Stage, and (c) group-stage volatility that makes Week 1 standings unstable. \u2022 28% NO reflects: (a) Leviat\u00e1n's real 1-0 start and +15 RD are credible, (b) early tournaments can produce surprise winners, and (c) insufficient briefing data on Leviat\u00e1n's current roster depth / meta adaptability \u2014 leaving lower confidence on NO case. \u2022 Sum (72+28=100) is intentional here: briefing provides strong YES evidence but thin NO evidence; the 28 reflects genuine uncertainty about Leviat\u00e1n's sustained form, not a mechanical 100-86=14 anti-calibration.", "key_factor": "Strong recent H2H momentum (2-1 and 2-0 G2 wins in 2025) combined with historical pedigree overcoming Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 dominance in an early-stage group setting where form variance is high."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: Match is LIVE (~53 min in), YES priced at 86%, NO at 14%. Sharp money moved +18.5pp toward YES at match start (21:52 UTC), suggesting informed backing of G2 or live-read advantage. This sharp move AGAINST Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form is a red flag for the favorite. CASE FOR LEVIAT\u00c1N (FAVORITE) \u2014 Why 86% may be justified: - Week 1 dominance: 1-0 record, 2-0 map count, +15 round differential vs ENVY (credible opponent). - G2 opened 0-1, 0-2 maps, -7 round differential \u2014 objectively poor start suggesting internal issues or meta misalignment. - Leviat\u00e1n is ahead in tournament standings with first-week momentum, which historically matters in group stages. - Current match state unknown due to LIVE status, but Leviat\u00e1n entered as statistical favorite on paper. CASE FOR G2 (UNDERDOG) \u2014 Why NO at 14% is underpriced: - H2H recency & consistency: G2 beat Leviat\u00e1n 2-1 (Apr 2025) and 2-0 (Feb 2025). These are THIS YEAR \u2014 not ancient history. 2-1 margin suggests close, competitive, replayable matches. - Leviat\u00e1n's 2025 record vs G2: 0-2. G2 has demonstrated adaptation and execution against THIS specific opponent in recent months. - Opening losses are not deterministic in BO3 group stages (many rounds remain). G2 may have identified draft/strategic issues after Match 1 and corrected them. - Sharp money spike (+18.5pp) INTO YES at match start suggests sophisticated bettors saw value in G2 mid-tournament, not pre-match consensus. - Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 dominance is sample-size limited (one match). Early-stage tournament form is notoriously volatile; regression to mean is common. - G2 has 'pedigree and experience' per briefing \u2014 intangible but real in pressure situations within group stages. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: - Match is LIVE; we have no map-specific intel, ban phases, current score, or live form indicators. Confidence on both sides is artificially suppressed. - Briefing lacks: individual player form, recent scrim results, map pool meta shifts, coaching adjustments, or injury/roster changes between Week 1 and Week 2. - NO-side evidence is THIN (only H2H + theoretical group-stage volatility). We cannot confidently rule out Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form representing genuine competitive superiority. PROBABILITY LOGIC: - G2's 2025 H2H dominance (2-0, 2-1) is concrete. If replayed pre-tournament, G2 would likely be favored at 55-60% based on H2H alone. - But Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 2-0, +15 RD is also concrete and suggests a different, stronger iteration of Leviat\u00e1n than 2025. - Market at 86% YES prices in: Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form is sticky, G2's H2H advantage is outdated/noise, G2's opening loss signals deeper issues. - Counterplay: Leviat\u00e1n's sample is N=1; G2's H2H is recent and repeatable; group-stage volatility favors upsets. - Probability_score = 28 reflects: G2 is a genuine underdog (Leviat\u00e1n's current form matters), but 86% YES is overleveraging recency bias on one match. - Probability_no_score = 68 reflects: Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form is credible, but WITHOUT live map data or deeper intel, confident assessment of a 14% NO outcome is premature. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: - confidence_yes = 35: We have H2H + volatility theory for G2, but live match state is opaque and Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form is real. Low confidence reflects uncertainty on both sides. - confidence_no = 72: Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form is concrete and recent; G2's opening loss is concrete. We CAN speak to why Leviat\u00e1n is favored. But N=1 match and unknown live state limit true high confidence.", "key_factor": "G2's strong recent H2H record (2-1, 2-0 in 2025) combined with group-stage volatility and the underdog mentality required after an opening loss creates a realistic upset scenario against early-stage momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.28, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Match is LIVE (started ~53 minutes ago). Market price at 86% YES reflects live action already underway; sharp move +18.5pp at match start (21:52 UTC) suggests in-match intelligence favoring G2. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side has risen 34.5pp over 7 days and +15pp in 24h. This is a STRONG consensus shift, not noise. At 86%, market is pricing G2 as heavy favorite despite Leviat\u00e1n's 1-0 group record and superior round differential. DISAMBIGUATION APPLIED: Briefing contains past-tense language about 'Apr 2025' and 'Feb 2025' H2H results (2-1 G2, 2-0 G2). These are PRIOR encounters, not this match outcome. Match is confirmed RUNNING per PandaScore (status: RUNNING, scheduled 2026-04-18 21:00 UTC). H2H RECENCY EFFECT: G2 won most recent H2H encounters (Apr 2025: 2-1, Feb 2025: 2-0) against Leviat\u00e1n. However, 2024 encounters favored Leviat\u00e1n (3-1, 2-0). Mixed H2H with recency edge to G2 adds ~8-12pp to G2 probability. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT PARADOX: Leviat\u00e1n is 1-0 in group (2-0 maps, +15 round diff) vs G2's 0-1 (0-2 maps, -7 round diff). This strongly suggests Leviat\u00e1n should be favored on paper. BUT: market and live action contradict this, implying either (a) G2 has adapted mid-tournament, (b) G2's Week 1 loss was anomalous, or (c) live match data shows G2 performing well in this specific series. SHARP MONEY SIGNAL: +18.5pp move at 21:52 UTC (match start + ~52 minutes) on YES side is consistent with professional/informed traders observing G2 winning early maps or demonstrating superior