t briefing indicates Leviat\u00e1n is CURRENTLY favored based on Week 1 performance (1-0, +15 RD vs G2's 0-1, -7 RD). CROWD PSYCHOLOGY MISMATCH: YES side surged +18.5pp in last 1h (21:52 UTC, 2min after event start). This sharp spike suggests irrational exuberance or information asymmetry \u2014 possibly traders reacting to opening map outcomes NOT yet reflected in briefing. Current price (86%) appears DETACHED from pre-match fundamentals. BRIEFING NARRATIVE FAVORS NO: News summary explicitly states 'Leviat\u00e1n enters as strong favorites' and 'G2 must recover from opening loss.' Week 1 standings show Leviat\u00e1n dominating while G2 struggled. Yet market prices G2 at 86% \u2014 a 50+ point inversion from briefing sentiment. H2H HISTORY IS CONFLICTING: G2 won 2025 matches (2-1, 2-0) but Leviat\u00e1n won 2024 (3-1, 2-0). Recent form favors G2, but THIS tournament's early form (2026 Stage 1) favors Leviat\u00e1n. Market may be over-weighting old H2H. LIVE EVENT SIGNAL DECAY: At ~53min into BO3, if Leviat\u00e1n has won opening map(s), NO shares should already be trading near $0.95+. Current 14% NO price suggests either: (a) G2 has mounted a comeback (not reflected in briefing snapshot), or (b) market is pricing pre-match belief, not live action. IGNORANCE ASYMMETRY: Briefing data is stale (21:53 UTC, event started 21:00 UTC). NO-side evaluation lacks real-time score updates; confidence_no capped at 72% due to inability to verify current map states. confidence_yes similarly limited (45%) because if Leviat\u00e1n is ahead live, 86% YES is a trap price. CROWD GREED SIGNAL: YES surge of +18.5pp at market open suggests retail/crowd following old perception of G2 strength (Feb/Apr 2025 H2H wins) rather than THIS stage's actual form (Leviat\u00e1n 1-0, G2 0-1). This is classic misprice: old narrative trading against live reality. PROBABILITY INTERPRETATION: If live score is unknown, briefing fundamentals favor Leviat\u00e1n by ~15-20pp (dominant Week 1, G2's opening loss, +15 RD edge). Market at 86% YES implies >70pp overestimation of G2's probability. probability_score=32 reflects NO-favoring fundamentals; probability_no_score=68 reflects briefing's clear Leviat\u00e1n tilt. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is ongoing; final outcome unknowable from briefing. Low confidence_yes (45%) reflects high uncertainty about live state vs. market price.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "probability_yes": 0.32, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE/RUNNING (~53 min into schedule start). Market price at 86% YES reflects early-event urgency and limited real-time information flow; volatility spikes (+18.5pp at 21:52 UTC) typical of esports mid-match trading. Live trading often overreacts to map wins and first-blood moments. LEVIAT\u00c1N CASE (NO side, 68% probability): Week 1 dominance is real\u20141-0 record, 2-0 maps, +15 RD is objectively strong. However, esports Week 1 outcomes in group play are fragile: single-match samples against one opponent (ENVY 2-1) provide minimal predictive power. Leviat\u00e1n's roster and meta-adaptation data for this specific stage (April 2026) are not provided in briefing; unclear if they've maintained LAN/bootcamp form or face unpredictable scrim/patch variance. G2 ESPORTS CASE (YES side, 32% probability): Opening loss (0-2 maps, -7 RD) is concerning for momentum but NOT determinative in week 2 of a 4-week group stage. G2's H2H record strongly favors them: 2-1 (Apr 2025), 2-0 (Feb 2025)\u2014two consecutive wins in recent VCT stages. This is not noise; it reflects structural team compatibility. Counterbalance: 2024 shows Leviat\u00e1n wins 2-0, 3-1 (playoffs), indicating meta-dependent volatility. HEAD-TO-HEAD ASYMMETRY: G2 won 2025 encounters (2-1, 2-0); Leviat\u00e1n won 2024 encounters (2-0, 3-1). This suggests meta-sensitivity and coaching adjustments matter more than raw skill hierarchy. Current patch (April 2026) state unknown from briefing\u2014no agent-pool, map-pool, or patch-notes data provided. MARKET PRICE INVERSION vs. BRIEF DATA: Market at 86% YES (G2 favored) contradicts briefing's early-stage context (Leviat\u00e1n 1-0, G2 0-1). This inversion likely reflects: (a) sharp money on G2 H2H strength and pedigree, (b) savvy bettors recognizing Week 1 noise in esports groups, (c) potential pre-match analysis not captured in briefing. The +34.5pp rise in YES over 7 days suggests informed traders are backing G2 fundamentally. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (Leviat\u00e1n at 68%) because Week 1 group-play momentum and concrete map/RD data are tangible. Lower confidence in YES (G2 at 32%) because H2H historical context is thin (2024 vs. 2025 meta shifts unexplained) and the opening-loss psychological/preparedness angle is underspecified. Briefing lacks: current roster stability, scrim results, injury/visa status, coaching changes since Feb 2025. LIVE MATCH STATE: At 53 min post-start, map scores likely available in real-time (vlr.gg, Twitch). If G2 is already down 0-1 or up 1-0, market should have repriced sharply toward certainty. Current 86/14 split suggests uncertainty remains (likely 1-0 either way, game 2 ongoing or recent). Once map 2 concludes, shares will trade toward $0.01 or $0.99 if outcome is clear. RESOLUTION RISK: Market specifies vlr.gg as primary resolver with 2-hr window and 7-day re-resolution clause for delays. Valorant group-play matches rarely postpone mid-BO3; completion is virtually certain by ~00:30 UTC 2026-04-19. Low forfeit/DQ risk. FINAL CALIBRATION: G2 is the structural favorite (H2H, pedigree, market sharp money) but faces a real Week 1 performance deficit. Leviat\u00e1n has momentum but thin sample. 32% YES reflects skepticism of the 86% market price; 68% NO reflects briefing's early-stage data in isolation. Ignorance mass (0%) is not justified\u2014both sides have evidence, but confidence gaps reflect information asymmetry on meta/coaching.", "key_factor": "Stage 1 early-week momentum in group-play esports is notoriously unstable; Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 dominance (+15 RD) reflects single-match sample noise in a 6-team round-robin where 5 more matches remain, whereas G2's H2H superiority (2-1, 2-0 in 2025) and pedigree in international VCT events provide structural predictive strength despite the opening loss."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "LIVE EVENT STATUS (53 min elapsed): Match is mid-play. Market has spiked +18.5pp YES in last 24h, suggesting real-time momentum reading or early map result flowing through. Current 86% YES price reflects live data we cannot directly observe; confidence should reflect uncertainty about in-game state. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY SIGNAL: YES side rose +34.5pp over 7 days (71% EMA) and +18.5pp at match start (21:52 UTC, ~1 min after match began). This sharp intra-match move suggests either: (A) G2 won early maps on-stream, or (B) smart money re-pricing G2's edge after observing ban/pick phase. Sharp spike *after* start argues for real match intelligence, not pre-game hype. LEVIAT\u00c1N'S WEEK 1 DOMINANCE MAY NOT TRANSFER: 2-0 vs ENVY (Apr 17) with +15 RD is strong, but ENVY are now 0-1 with 1-2 maps. Leviat\u00e1n's wins came against a struggling opponent; G2's loss (0-2 vs unknown opponent) may have been vs MIBR or LOUD (both 1-0 after Week 1). If G2 lost to MIBR/LOUD and faces Leviat\u00e1n next, G2 has faced tougher opponents and may have strategic adjustments ready. H2H ASYMMETRY (2025 vs 2024): G2 won 2-1 and 2-0 in Feb\u2013Apr 2025 (recent, likely same meta). Leviat\u00e1n won in 2024 (3-1, 2-0 were reverse scorelines, may indicate older patch/different rosters). The 2025 wins favor G2's structural understanding of current Valorant meta. GROUP STAGE VOLATILITY: Early stage results (Week 1 of 5 weeks) are noisy. Leviat\u00e1n's early success is real but not predictive of sustained dominance. G2's loss does not indicate weakness; one match determines nothing in a round-robin group. Regression to the mean is high. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72) because: (A) H2H favors G2 (2025), (B) live market spike +18.5pp suggests G2 performance in-game, (C) 86% market price has incorporated recent data. But confidence_no is only 48 because: (A) we cannot see real-time match state, (B) Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 form is real and could sustain, (C) if Leviat\u00e1n is currently winning maps, they are on a 1-0 trajectory and mental edge. Gap (72 vs 38 prob, 62 vs 48 conf) reflects live-match uncertainty and single-game noise. BLACK SWAN: Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 dominance is real but narrowly targeted at ENVY's specific weaknesses. G2's H2H record (2-1, 2-0 in 2025) shows they have systematic answers to Leviat\u00e1n's utility setup or agent pool. A tactical reset mid-series (G2 adjusts bans/agent picks after Game 1) could unlock a 2-1 comeback win. ABSENCE OF SIGNAL: Briefing does NOT detail which opponent G2 lost to in their opening match. If G2 lost to MIBR or LOUD (top-tier groups), they faced stronger opponents than Leviat\u00e1n's ENVY win. This missing detail suppresses confidence in Leviat\u00e1n's true dominance ranking. STRUCTURAL EDGE (G2): International VCT experience, established coaching staff, and recent 2025 H2H wins suggest G2 has institutional knowledge Leviat\u00e1n (newer roster?) may lack in high-pressure BO3 finals. Early-stage wins do not always predict under-pressure performance.", "key_factor": "G2's opening-loss momentum spiral masks a tactical adjustment window: Leviat\u00e1n's dominant Week 1 form (2-0 maps vs ENVY, +15 RD) may be built on narrow map-pool exploitation or anti-ENVY prep that G2's varied playstyle and recent H2H success (2-0, 2-1 in 2025) can neutralize in a BO3 reset."}], "final_score": 0.553218492123246, "no_score": 0.5339782431919056, "edge": -0.1676923076923077, "no_edge": 0.5523076923076923, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 55.32% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 48.00% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963335", "question": "Valorant: G2 Esports vs Leviat\u00e1n Esports (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between G2 Esports and Leviat\u00e1n Esports in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 18 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win the match against Leviat\u00e1n Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leviat\u00e1n Esports\" if Leviat\u00e1n Esports win the match against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-18T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.86, "volume_usd": 152132.0931649999, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["104149769634112853375808955805018250307764188157003896088455837310435061261147", "26943164101083235743919519175373027382347728406544753174529351728588876747301"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Asia-Pacific.", "Group Stage: April 10<sup>th</sup> - May 10<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "Each Group has 6 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in North America.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "LEVIAT\u00c1N roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "Shopify Rebellion Gold roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "Gen.G roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Cloud9 vs.", "ENVY - Week 2 match of VCT 2026: Americas Stage 1 Valorant event."], "news_summary": "G2 Esports vs Leviat\u00e1n Esports is currently LIVE in VCT 2026 Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha (BO3). According to the latest Group Alpha standings, Leviat\u00e1n has won their first match (1-0 record, 2-0 map count, +15 round differential), while G2 Esports lost their opening fixture (0-1 record, 0-2 map count, -7 round differential). This match is scheduled for April 18, 2026. Leviat\u00e1n enters as strong favorites, having dominated Group Alpha's first week, while G2 must recover from an opening loss.", "side_yes_case": ["Leviat\u00e1n currently leads Group Alpha with a 1-0 record and +15 round differential, demonstrating strong early-stage form.", "G2 Esports opened with a loss (0-2 maps), indicating early tournament struggles.", "Leviat\u00e1n's dominant +15 round differential vs G2's -7 suggests a significant skill/preparation gap this stage.", "Recent H2H favors G2 (2-1 win in Apr 2025, 2-0 in Feb 2025), but Leviat\u00e1n won both 2024 encounters (3-1, 2-0)."], "side_no_case": ["G2 Esports' recent head-to-head record is stronger, winning 2-0 and 2-1 against Leviat\u00e1n in Feb and Apr 2025.", "G2 lost their opening match but remain in a group-stage setting with many rounds remaining to recover.", "Leviat\u00e1n's Week 1 success may not sustain; early tournaments often see stronger teams regress.", "G2 has experience and pedigree in international VCT competition."], "key_context": ["VCT 2026 Americas Stage 1 Group Stage runs April 10 \u2013 May 10, with two 6-team single-round-robin groups; all matches are BO3.", "Top 4 teams from each group advance; Group Alpha is highly competitive with Leviat\u00e1n, MIBR, and LOUD all 1-0 after Week 1.", "Group Alpha Week 1 standings show Leviat\u00e1n (1-0, 2-0 maps), MIBR (1-0, 2-0 maps), LOUD (1-0, 2-1 maps), ENVY (0-1, 1-2 maps), G2 (0-1, 0-2 maps), Cloud9 (0-1, 0-2 maps).", "This is the team's second match of the tournament; early stage momentum can shift rapidly.", "