{"run_id": "c5f597db-d1ce-482a-9580-ec8d7e6bd7d0", "timestamp": "2026-04-19T10:19:12.085301+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2016908", "question": "Dota 2: Nemiga Gaming vs Nigma Galaxy (BO3) - DreamLeague Division 2 Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 match between Nemiga Gaming and Nigma Galaxy in the DreamLeague Division 2 Group A, initially scheduled for April 19 at 8:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nemiga Gaming\" if Nemiga Gaming win the match against Nigma Galaxy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nigma Galaxy\" if Nigma Galaxy win the match against Nemiga Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T18:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T12:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.16, "volume_usd": 4688.070371000001, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["65612054845459126819675662281033137708272167151280969968721119050901698671647", "103638299691749865919989302642425453940741418266463847574859664830638857882239"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.24, "probability_yes": 0.24, "probability_no": 0.72, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Nemiga Gaming wins the BO3 match against Nigma Galaxy on 2026-04-19 12:00 UTC. Resolution is to the team that wins; no forfeit/tie ambiguity applies if match is completed normally. FORM DATA ASYMMETRY: Nigma Galaxy recent form (6W-4L, 60% win rate over last 10) is materially stronger than Nemiga Gaming (5W-5L, 50% win rate). This is the primary YES/NO discriminator in the briefing. MARKET PRICE STRUCTURE: Current NO price at 84% reflects market consensus favoring Nigma. Sharp 24-hour repricing (-34.5pp YES, +12.5pp NO) suggests informed flow into NO position, though briefing provides no explanation for this move. STRUCTURAL DATA GAPS: Briefing contains fragmented context (historical Games of the Future 2025 match results, team org history, PGL Wallachia references) but NO direct head-to-head record, recent playoff/tournament seeding, or patch-specific meta analysis. NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head history or direct competitive context for this specific pairing is evident.' NEMIGA EPL CONTEXT: 3-2 record in European Pro League Season 36 is mentioned but NOT mapped to Nigma's standing in the same league. This is a missed comparison point; without Nigma's EPL record, the 3-2 baseline provides limited predictive value. TEMPORAL COHERENCE: All past-tense match coverage in KEY FACTS (Games of the Future 2025 results from December 2025) are PRIOR encounters and describe neither team's current form for this April 2026 match. These are context only. CASE FOR YES ASSESSMENT: Nemiga 'demonstrated consistency' and '3-2 record' are weak signals when Nigma's form is materially better (6W-4L). The 'fixture preparation and timing advantage' claim is unsupported by briefing data. CASE FOR NO ASSESSMENT: Nigma's 6W-4L form advantage is the only concrete edge identified. Claim that 'limited recent form data' for Nigma is available contradicts the 6W-4L metric explicitly provided by PandaScore. This case is stronger in data but still thin on tournament-specific context. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=35 (weak YES-side data; form disadvantage, no H2H context) vs. confidence_no=52 (stronger form metric for Nigma, market repricing, but still no tournament seeding/meta context). Ignorance mass (24+72=96, leaving 4pp unresolved) reflects genuine data insufficiency on both sides. LIVE/IMMINENT RISK: Event starts in ~1.7 hours. Market will trade to ~$0.01/$0.99 once the match outcome becomes clear in real-time, regardless of Dotabuff publication timing. Resolution mechanism risk is minimal; the outcome condition itself (who wins the BO3) is the primary uncertainty. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 24% YES reflects Nigma's +10pp form advantage (6W-4L vs 5W-5L) and market consensus (84% NO), but avoids over-confidence due to absence of H2H records, tournament seeding, and patch meta. 72% NO is supported by form data and market repricing but capped below 80% due to data insufficiency on European regional dynamics.", "key_factor": "Insufficient recent head-to-head data and conflicting form metrics (Nigma 6W-4L vs Nemiga 5W-5L over last 10 matches) create ambiguity in predictive power; market price movement (-34.5pp YES, +12.5pp NO in 24h) suggests sharp repricing but underlying competitive context remains thin."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.71, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Nigma Galaxy maintains 6W-4L record (60% win rate) vs. Nemiga's 5W-5L (50%) over last 10 matches \u2014 a 10-percentage-point form advantage in a direct head-to-head BO3 is material. This is the single strongest quantified data point in the briefing. MARKET CONVICTION: NO side has risen +12.5pp over 7 days and now commands 84% price. Sharp move of +13.0pp occurred Apr 19 07:00 UTC (just 5 hours before match), suggesting informed late information or model consensus favoring Nigma. YES SIDE COLLAPSE: YES has fallen -34.5pp in 24 hours with two sharp drops (-19.5pp, -16.5pp), indicating systematic selling by traders. This velocity of downward price action before a LIVE/IMMINENT event typically reflects market participants recognizing an informational disadvantage or updated intelligence. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION: Briefing explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head history or direct competitive context for this specific pairing is evident.' This is crucial \u2014 the market is pricing on form differential alone, with no upset narrative (underdog cheese, roster synergy, surprise meta pick) evident. Without such catalysts, the form favorite (Nigma) is the baseline. NEMIGA WEAKNESS: Nemiga's 5W-5L record, while acceptable, shows volatility and no positive momentum. The briefing notes a 3-2 record in European Pro League Season 36, which is merely 'mid-tier' positioning \u2014 no standout performance to justify underdog backing at 16%. CASE AGAINST YES (UNDERDOG UNDERPRICED?): Nemiga would need to overcome a form deficit AND late market selling. No briefing evidence supports: (1) recent roster improvements, (2) meta shift favoring Nemiga's playstyle, (3) head-to-head advantage, (4) psychological momentum, or (5) coaching insights. The 16% price appears to be residual baseline, not informed positioning. TIMING & VOLATILITY: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (1.7 hours to start). Large reversals requiring significant unforeseen events (roster issues at Nigma, technical delay, etc.) are highly unlikely in this window. Price action has already stabilized around 84% NO, consistent with rational market closure before match start. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence on NO side (71%) because form data is clear, market consensus is recent and sharp, and no contradictory narratives exist in briefing. Moderate confidence on YES (32%) because briefing lacks detail on Nemiga's strengths, recent tournaments, or roster context \u2014 leaving open the possibility of unobserved factors favoring the underdog, but without evidence to prioritize that view. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 18% for YES reflects: (1) form deficit (-10pp), (2) recent market selling signal, (3) lack of upset catalysts, (4) imminent timeline reducing reversal likelihood. 78% for NO reflects the inverse. Gap (18 + 78 = 96) represents residual ~4pp ignorance mass due to limited head-to-head or team-specific context.", "key_factor": "Nigma Galaxy's superior recent form (60% win rate vs. 50%) combined with market consensus shift and sharp negative price action on YES side suggests informed traders have identified structural weakness in Nemiga's position."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG FORM ANALYSIS: Nemiga Gaming sits at 5W-5L (50% winrate) across last 10 matches, vs Nigma's 6W-4L (60% winrate). The gap is 10 percentage points \u2014 meaningful but not insurmountable, especially in a volatile BO3 format where variance matters. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL (CRITICAL): YES side has collapsed 34.5pp in 24 hours with sharp 19.5pp and 16.5pp drops on Apr 19. This suggests either: (a) intelligent money recognizing new information, or (b) panic/overreaction. The sharp +13pp bounce on NO at 07:00 UTC hints at late repositioning, not fundamental new data \u2014 a behavioral sign that may indicate overextension. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE FOR UNDERDOG: Best-of-3 inherently favors the underdog more than best-of-1 or best-of-5. Nemiga only needs to win 2 maps; a single strong map pool or meta advantage can swing a series. The 84% NO pricing assumes near-certainty in a format where 1-2 map-level upsets equal series reversal. NIGMA GALAXY DATA GAPS: Briefing provides minimal recent competitive context for Nigma Galaxy. Historical references are from December 2025 Games of the Future (mixed 2:0, 1:2, 0:2, 2:1 results vs lower-tier opponents) \u2014 not recent DreamLeague Division 2 form. The 6W-4L record is stronger, but without recent tournament placement or meta alignment data, confidence in Nigma's current dominance is artificially inflated. NEMIGA EUROPEAN PRO LEAGUE CONTEXT: Nemiga holds a 3-2 record in EPL Season 36, positioning them as competitive mid-tier in European play. This is not a bottom-tier team; they are tournament-ready and not facing a tier-1 international powerhouse. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING RISK: Match starts in 1.7 hours. At this stage, a 16% YES price is near-irreversible absent catastrophic news (roster changes, forfeit, major meta shift). The market has locked in heavy NO conviction with limited time for contradiction. This creates asymmetric payoff: YES shares will only move on genuine game-state upset; NO shares are already pricing near-certainty. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY CONCERN: Only $4,688 USD volume on this market \u2014 very thin. The sharp price moves may reflect small notional repositioning rather than deep institutional conviction. Thin markets are vulnerable to edge-case information and can misprice underdogs. CASE AGAINST NIGMA'S DOMINANCE: The 84% NO pricing implies Nigma is substantially stronger (roughly 5.25:1 odds). The briefing provides no head-to-head history, no recent DreamLeague Division 2 placement data, and no evidence of a tier-2 powerhouse. The recent match results from December 2025 show mixed performances (losses to Vikings). Current form is unclear. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Nemiga wins the series 2-1 or 2-0 if: (a) they exploit a meta matchup advantage (briefing does not rule this out), (b) Nigma's roster has latency/communication issues typical of mixed regional lineups, or (c) Nemiga's recent 5W-5L includes wins against comparable opponents, indicating they can compete at this level. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: High confidence in YES is unwarranted (28%) because the briefing provides only basic form stats and no recent competitive context for either team at DreamLeague Division 2. High confidence in NO is also limited (62%) because NO's case relies primarily on a single 60% vs 50% winrate differential and a price collapse that may be behavioral rather than information-driven. Leaving 22pp of ignorance mass (22+76=98) reflects genuine data gaps. VERDICT: YES is underpriced at 16%. A more neutral valuation accounting for BO3 variance, minimal form gap, and thin market liquidity would place Nemiga at 25-35%. The sharp repricing into 16% suggests market panic or algorithmic herding rather than new match-specific intelligence.", "key_factor": "Nemiga's 5W-5L form parity with Nigma (6W-4L) combined with aggressive recent market repricing suggests potential mispricing of a BO3 format that offers higher variance than the NO side's dominant 84% pricing implies."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "RECENT FORM ADVANTAGE: Nigma Galaxy 6W-4L vs Nemiga Gaming 5W-5L over last 10 matches \u2014 Nigma has +1 win differential, statistically favors NO side. MARKET PRICE STRONGLY SKEWED TOWARD NO: Current 84% NO / 16% YES price is steep. Market has moved -34.5pp on YES side over 24h with sharp drops Apr 19 01:00 UTC (-19.5pp) and 06:00 UTC (-16.5pp), suggesting either late information release or significant odds shift. IMMINENT EVENT TIMING: Match starts in ~1.7 hours. High-confidence sharp moves this close to event are often driven by team roster announcements, injury news, or insider information rather than sentiment drift. Lack of specific news in briefing suggests market may have reacted to undisclosed factors (e.g., Nemiga roster issues, Nigma momentum). SPARSE HISTORICAL HEAD-TO-HEAD: Briefing provides no direct Nemiga vs Nigma matchup history. Cannot anchor on h2h precedent; must rely on form differential and base rates. BASE RATE FOR UNDERDOG IN BO3: Teams at ~33% form (5W-5L = 50% win rate) vs teams at 60% form (6W-4L) typically have 20-28% upset probability in BO3. Current 16% price sits below historical underdog base rate, suggesting either genuine information disadvantage or genuine structural weakness. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in NO (Nigma advantage) because recent form data is clear and market price consensus is extreme. Lower confidence in YES because briefing lacks the negative information that would justify such a steep discount on Nemiga (injury? roster exodus? internal issues?). If that information exists and market priced it in, YES at 16% is appropriate; if information is absent, we have ignorance mass. VOLUME AND LIQUIDITY: $4,688 USD volume is low for esports BO3, suggesting thin order book and potential for mispricing, but also potential for informed traders to have moved price sharply. NO RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD OR TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Briefing references Games of the Future 2025 (Nigma matches Dec 2025, mixed results) and European Pro League Season 36 (Nemiga 3-2), but no unified competitive context or direct comparison. This limits confidence in either direction.", "key_factor": "In professional Dota 2 BO3 matches between teams with similar win-loss records, the higher-form team (6W-4L vs 5W-5L) wins ~65-72% of the time. Underdog upset rates in BO3 format ~18-28% depending on skill tier disparity."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.78, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market has collapsed YES side from 26% (7-day EMA) to 16% current in last 24h, driven by two sharp moves (-19.5pp on Apr 19 01:00 UTC, -16.5pp on Apr 19 06:00 UTC). NO side rose from 81% (7-day EMA) correspondingly (+12.5pp net, peak +13.0pp on Apr 19 07:00 UTC). Crowd is exhibiting FEAR on YES side. The magnitude and timing of the collapse (1.7 hours before match start) suggests new information or panic liquidation rather than fundamental reassessment. Nemiga Gaming raw form (5W-5L last 10) is marginally worse than Nigma Galaxy (6W-4L last 10), but the margin is modest. A 16% YES price implies ~5.25:1 odds against Nemiga, which overstates the form differential. Briefing provides NO recent head-to-head history between these teams in DreamLeague Division 2 context. NO news emerged in last 24h to justify the sudden 34.5pp collapse on YES\u2014crowd may be overreacting to form disparity alone or reacting to match-day intel not in briefing. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (1.7h to start). At this proximity, sharp price moves typically reflect credible late-breaking info or algorithmic panic. However, briefing contains NO evidence of injury, roster change, or tactical surprise for either team. Nemiga's 3-2 European Pro League Season 36 record mentioned as 'consistency' in YES case, but this is mid-tier performance, not dominant. Nigma Galaxy form (6W-4L) is objectively stronger recent record. Market depth is thin ($4,688 USD volume) and volatility is elevated (7.6\u20137.7pp/hr), typical of a crowded short on YES driven by herd behavior rather than deep analysis. Asymmetric data quality: YES case relies on single EPL record (3-2) and fixture scheduling. NO case relies on form differential (6-4 vs 5-5) and market momentum. Neither briefing side provides tactical analysis, roster strength, or meta advantage. Current 16% YES price likely reflects IRRATIONAL FEAR COMPRESSION. If the only evidence is form disparity, 16% undervalues Nemiga's 50% win rate vs Nigma's 60% \u2014 a 10pp edge does not justify 84% odds. Rational price should be ~30\u201335% for YES. However, given imminent start time and lack of counter-signals in briefing for Nemiga (no morale, meta, or preparation advantage evident), confidence in YES recovery is LOW (32%). Crowd may know something briefing does not. NO confidence is moderate (58%) because briefing form data is strong but not decisive in a single BO3 match. Nigma's 6-4 form is meaningful but not overwhelming. Crowd's +13pp surge on NO in last hour suggests herd behavior more than fundamental shift. Probability_no_score (78%) reflects crowd sentiment and form differential. Probability_score (18%) reflects intrinsic match value after stripping panic, BUT tempered by (a) lack of Nemiga's counter-narrative in briefing and (b) imminent-event risk that crowd may have legitimate late-breaking intel. Sum (18+78=96) < 100: Leaving 4pp ignorance mass for unknown match-day developments (team availability, meta surprise, technical issue) not captured in briefing.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "probability_yes": 0.22, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Nigma Galaxy 6W-4L (60% win rate) vs Nemiga Gaming 5W-5L (50% win rate) over last 10 matches\u2014clear statistical edge to NO side. This is the single strongest quantitative signal in the briefing. MARKET PRICE ACTION INTERPRETATION: YES side collapsed from ~26% EMA to 16% in last 24h with two sharp drops (-19.5pp, -16.5pp). This magnitude of sustained sell-off in a ~1.7h pre-match window suggests informed betting (team news, roster changes, or coaching adjustments) rather than random noise. Market efficiency in esports betting is generally high for tier-2 regional matches. BRIEFING DATA QUALITY: The news summary explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head history or direct competitive context for this specific pairing is evident from available sources.' This is a critical gap\u2014without direct matchup data, we cannot assess hero-pool counters, tactical familiarity, or role-specific advantages. This gap justifies LOWER confidence on both sides. NEMIGA CONTEXT WEAKNESS: The case for YES rests on a 3-2 EPL Season 36 record, which is modest (50% in a different tournament tier). EPL standings are weaker signal than direct DreamLeague Division 2 performance. No roster stability data provided; esports teams frequently swap players mid-season. NIGMA HISTORICAL DATA: Briefing includes archival match data from December 2025 (Games of the Future 2025), showing Nigma Galaxy mixed results (2-0 vs Phoenix, 1-2 vs Vikings, 0-2 vs Vikings, 2-1 vs TpaBoTeaM). This is 4+ months old and does not reflect current meta/roster. Limited utility for April 2026 prediction. TIMING RESOLUTION: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (1.7h to start). Resolution will likely occur within 6-8h total (typical BO3 duration ~2-3h + queue time). If outcome becomes apparent mid-broadcast, shares will trade to $0.01/$0.99 before official DotaBuff confirmation. This constrains reversal potential\u2014NO side cannot easily flip from current 84% if Nigma comes out ahead in game 1. BO3 FORMAT DYNAMICS: Best-of-3 favors the higher-seeded/favored team (typically stronger teams win the series after dropping one map). If Nigma Galaxy is favored in overall strength, BO3 amplifies that advantage relative to a single-map format. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: YES volatility (7.6pp/hr) vs NO volatility (7.7pp/hr) nearly identical, suggesting market disagrees internally but not based on one-sided information. The 16% YES price reflects consensus caution, not a flash crash\u2014this is a stable low floor. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Confidence_yes set to 35 because recent form data (6-4 vs 5-5) is reliable but represents ~10 matches each, leaving ~20-30% structural uncertainty. Confidence_no set to 62 because the form advantage is clear AND market consensus is strong, but lack of h2h context prevents certainty above ~70%. Leaving ~8pp ignorance mass (22+76=98) reflects data gaps on both sides. INDUSTRY INSIDER PERSPECTIVE: DreamLeague Division 2 is tier-2 EU regional play. Teams here rarely have stable rosters or coaching investment of tier-1 (OG, Tundra, Liquid). Player transfers, stand-in subs, and form collapse are common in 48h intervals. The 4-month-old data on Nigma Galaxy and near-zero data on Nemiga Galaxy's current roster suggest high variance. However, 6W-4L in last 10 is more recent and credible than league standings.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 16% YES reflects sharp recent sell-off (-34.5pp in 24h) driven by likely public betting intelligence on team form/roster stability; Nigma Galaxy's superior recent record (6W-4L vs 5W-5L) and market consensus heavily favor NO, but imminent event timing and thin briefing data on direct head-to-head dynamics create asymmetric confidence."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "probability_yes": 0.18, "probability_no": 0.76, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market has collapsed 34.5pp in 24 hours on the YES side, with two sharp -19.5pp and -16.5pp drops on Apr 19. This suggests late-breaking information (injury, roster change, scrim results, or leaked meta intel) that has not surfaced in the briefing. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~1.7 hours to start). At this stage, public confidence in NO is crystallizing at 84%, but this price reflects only information available 24+ hours ago. Last-minute roster news or tactical leaks in esports are common 1-2 hours before match start. Briefing data is severely asymmetric: Nemiga recent form is explicitly stated (5W-5L, 10 matches), but Nigma Galaxy form is stated (6W-4L, 10 matches) without context. The 6W-4L is better, but no match dates or opponent tier is provided\u2014Nigma's wins may be against weaker competition in older events (Games of the Future 2025 references are from Dec 2025, ~4.5 months old). No direct head-to-head history between Nemiga and Nigma Galaxy is mentioned in the briefing, eliminating the most reliable micro-signal for BO3 matchup prediction. Nigma Galaxy's recent tournament results in briefing are OLD (December 2025) and from a lower-tier tournament (Games of the Future 2025). No current DreamLeague Division 2 Group A standings or recent form for Nigma is provided, creating opacity on their current state. Nemiga Gaming has a 3-2 record in European Pro League Season 36, placing them mid-table. This is competitive but not dominant. A BO3 loss is entirely plausible and does not contradict the 5W-5L aggregate. The 16% YES price is extreme for a match with such limited public data. Extreme prices in esports betting often indicate either: (a) sharp money has detected a weakness in the favorite, or (b) soft public money has over-reacted to a single signal (e.g., one bad scrim or injury rumor). Black swan: Nigma Galaxy's roster may include a stand-in or substitution (e.g., offlane or mid sub) not reflected in public records. Dota 2 roster changes are often announced on Discord or internal team channels only hours before matches. If Nigma's primary carry or support is benched or ill, their BO3 coherence collapses, and Nemiga\u2014despite lower aggregate form\u2014could exploit this chaos to steal a game or two. Alternative black swan: Nemiga has scouted a specific Nigma Galaxy draft weakness or meta shift in the last 48 hours and prepared a counter-strategy (e.g., anti-carry picks, positioning trap). In BO3 dota, one 5-man meta exploit can swing a single game; Nemiga winning 2-0 or 2-1 becomes viable if they have this edge and execute cleanly. Confidence_yes is LOW (35) because the briefing does not contain roster confirmations, scrim results, or recent Nigma Galaxy competitive activity. Confidence_no is MODERATE (62) because Nigma's aggregate form (6W-4L) is better than Nemiga's (5W-5L), and market confidence at 84% aligns with this, but lack of fresh data on Nigma leaves residual uncertainty. The gap (18 + 76 = 94, below 100) reflects genuine ignorance mass on the NO side. If market is correct at 84% NO, the true probability is likely 80\u201388%. If a roster/tactic black swan materializes in the next ~1.5 hours, Nemiga's win probability could spike to 25\u201340%, implying a 15\u201335% NO move. Output reflects this tail risk compressed into a contrarian 18% YES estimate.", "key_factor": "Nemiga Gaming executes an unexpected meta pivot or pocket-pick strategy that exploits a known Nigma Galaxy weakness in a specific game within the BO3 format, combined with a potential roster substitution or stand-in player on Nigma's side that has not been publicly disclosed."}], "final_score": 0.19930478248616906, "no_score": 0.8019360388249235, "edge": 0.5323076923076923, "no_edge": -0.14769230769230768, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 61.29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "201