{"run_id": "eb50b517-2ffb-4abf-9675-dc87374c39b0", "timestamp": "2026-04-19T16:47:16.081530+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1993879", "question": "Valorant: Eintracht Frankfurt vs CGN Esports (BO3) - VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Eintracht Frankfurt and CGN Esports in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 19 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Eintracht Frankfurt\" if Eintracht Frankfurt win the match against CGN Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"CGN Esports\" if CGN Esports win the match against Eintracht Frankfurt.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.6, "volume_usd": 3082.290470000001, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["51355814446094029997144696228250521770695427598678158005843820256393007891769", "105021998577488392937675621355545727486542968452787082068313781816247141256466"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled 2026-04-19 15:00 UTC; briefing timestamp 16:46 UTC indicates match is ~1.8 hours underway and LIVE_OR_PAST status is RUNNING, not completed. TEMPORAL COHERENCE CHECK: All past-tense match results in briefing (e.g., 'CGN defeated Frankfurt 2-1 on Feb 8 2026') are explicitly flagged as PRIOR encounters per DISAMBIGUATION WARNINGS. No final scoreline for TODAY's match is provided in news_summary or case sections. MISSING LIVE DATA: The briefing provides no current map scores, round counts, or in-match status updates. This is the critical gap\u2014without live game state, outcome probability must be inferred from form and H2H history only. H2H ANALYSIS (form context only): Frankfurt won 3 straight in Jan 2026 (Jan 15, 19, 26), but CGN reversed momentum decisively: Mar 1 3-0 win (most recent prior match, ~1.5 months before current event); Feb 8 2-1 win shows recent capability in high-stakes matchups. Mixed record suggests volatile head-to-head dynamic. RECENT FORM (PandaScore): Frankfurt 7W-3L (70%); CGN 9W-1L (90%). CGN's recent form is sharply stronger, contradicting Frankfurt's historical H2H edge in Jan 2026. MARKET PRICING MOMENTUM: YES side (Frankfurt) has risen +20pp over 7 days and +17pp in 24h, with a sharp +30.5pp spike at 16:00 UTC (match start time). This suggests live match developments favorable to Frankfurt occurred in the first 1-1.5 hours, likely map wins or round dominance. However, sharp reversals (-14.5pp at 16:46 UTC) indicate volatile in-match betting, not settled outcome. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: (1) No live scoreline prevents definitive probability; (2) CGN's superior recent form (90% win rate vs 70%) competes with Frankfurt's historical H2H advantage; (3) market trades at high volatility ($3.5k volume, 7.5pp/hr YES volatility) indicating genuine uncertainty among informed bettors. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Frankfurt's early-match market momentum (+30.5pp at 16:00, not fully reversed) suggests market participants have observed favorable developments (likely map 1 win or dominant round sequence). Assign 58% to YES, reflecting this live signal while acknowledging CGN's superior base form rate and uncertainty from lack of explicit scoreline. CONFIDENCE DEGRADATION: confidence_yes = 32 (live data gap + conflicting form signals reduce confidence in 58% point estimate); confidence_no = 28 (similar reasoning: CGN's form supports NO, but Frankfurt's market momentum undercuts it). Both below 50 due to missing live match state.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/RUNNING as of 16:46 UTC (1.8 hours in), but no live scoreline is provided in the briefing; outcome remains genuinely unknown despite market pricing momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "probability_yes": 0.68, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "FRANKFURT'S STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE: Frankfurt has won 4 of the last 8 head-to-head matches (50%), including a dominant 3-0 sweep of three consecutive encounters in mid-to-late January 2026 (Jan 15, 19, 26), establishing clear recent form dominance. CGN'S MOMENTUM ILLUSION: CGN's most recent prior win (Mar 1, 3-0) appears to be an outlier, not a trend reversal. The previous encounter (Feb 8) was a narrow 2-1 victory, and CGN's win rate history is volatile\u2014the January losses to Frankfurt were decisive (13-4, 13-8, 13-9 scorelines). FORM DIVERGENCE: Frankfurt's 7-3 record (last 10 matches) is respectable and consistent. CGN's 9-1 record appears stronger on surface, but recent head-to-head suggests Frankfurt's form is better-calibrated for THIS specific matchup; map familiarity and tactical preparation favor Frankfurt. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES (Frankfurt) has surged +20pp over 7 days and +17pp in 24 hours, with a sharp +30.5pp move at 16:00 UTC on Apr 19 (within the match window). This volatility reflects in-match information\u2014Frankfurt likely showing stronger early performance or map control, driving price recovery after initial uncertainty. LIVE TIMING PENALTY ON REVERSALS: The match is LIVE (~1.8 hours in as of briefing timestamp). For NO (CGN) to win from this position, a significant comeback would be required with limited time remaining. Such reversals are structurally less likely in BO3 formats when one team has already established advantage. COUNTER-ARGUMENT: CGN's 9-1 recent form cannot be dismissed. However, this record's strength may reflect easier opposition in group stage; Frankfurt's 7-3 record against higher-tier opponents (playoffs, weekly qualifiers) is more predictive of performance in competitive group stage matches. HEAD-TO-HEAD ASYMMETRY: 4-3 Frankfurt in most recent 7 encounters (excluding the isolated Mar 1 outlier). Frankfurt's consistency in January (3 consecutive wins) suggests tactical mastery that CGN has not fully countered. REMAINING UNCERTAINTY: (1) Exact map pool and veto dynamics not specified in briefing; (2) roster changes or substitutions unknown; (3) Frankfurt's Feb 8 loss (2-1) proves CGN is capable of stealing maps even in close series. This prevents full confidence, but does not overturn the structural Frankfurt advantage. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (72) > confidence_no (55) reflects that Frankfurt's recent form, head-to-head record, and market momentum are well-evidenced, while CGN's counter-narrative relies on isolated wins and unconfirmed current form. The briefing provides stronger support for YES than for NO.", "key_factor": "Frankfurt's sustained dominance in recent head-to-head encounters (3 straight wins in January 2026) and superior recent form (7-3 last 10 matches) outweigh CGN's isolated momentum spike in March, particularly given the match is LIVE and the window for dramatic reversals is closing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "probability_yes": 0.35, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES currently at 60% (~$0.60), NO at 40% (~$0.40). Market is favoring Frankfurt significantly. Event is LIVE (started ~1.8 hrs ago at 15:00 UTC on Apr 19), with sharp price swings (+30.5pp YES at 16:00, then -14.5pp at 16:46), suggesting in-game momentum shifts or match progression uncertainty. STRONGEST CASE FOR UNDERDOG (NO / CGN): \u2022 CGN's most recent prior match was Mar 1 2026: dominant 3-0 victory over Frankfurt. This is only 1.5 months old and carries decisive weight (clean sweep) vs Frankfurt's older January win streak (3-2 head-to-head in Jan, but all in weekly qualifiers, not high-stakes playoffs). \u2022 Frankfurt's Jan-Feb dominance reversed sharply: won 3 straight in mid-Jan, then LOST to CGN 2-1 on Feb 8 (playoff context, higher stakes than qualifiers). CGN then won 3-0 in March playoffs. Momentum has shifted to CGN. \u2022 Recent 10-match form is asymmetric: CGN 9-1 vs Frankfurt 7-3. Frankfurt's 3 losses suggest vulnerability; CGN's 9-win streak suggests sustained peak performance heading into this event. \u2022 Market's sharp moves (16:00 +30.5pp YES, 16:46 -14.5pp YES) and current high volatility on YES suggest Frankfurt may be underperforming in-game. Low confidence in market's YES position. WEAKNESSES OF THE FAVORITE (YES / FRANKFURT): \u2022 Frankfurt's recent form (7-3 in last 10) is notably weaker than CGN's 9-1. A 70% win rate vs 90% is material in a high-variance esports format. \u2022 Frankfurt's Jan dominance is stale (~3 months old at time of event). The most recent head-to-head (Mar 1) went CGN's way decisively. \u2022 Frankfurt's one Feb 8 victory was close (2-1), not clean. Suggests competitive fragility under playoff pressure, contrasting with CGN's 3-0 stomp in March. \u2022 No evidence in briefing of Frankfurt's recent patch 11.11 meta dominance or roster/tactical innovations since January. CGN's March win suggests adaptation. CASE FOR YES (FRANKFURT) \u2014 VULNERABILITIES: \u2022 Frankfurt won 3 consecutive qualifiers in January, establishing short-term pattern. But these were lower-tier weekly qualifiers, not playoffs. \u2022 Frankfurt's Jan 26 Bind victory (13-9) shows map mastery on at least one map. However, this is old data (3 months prior). \u2022 No concrete data on Frankfurt's current scrim performance, roster morale, or meta read. Briefing is thin on Frankfurt's recent strengths. TEMPORAL RECENCY ANALYSIS: \u2022 CGN's Mar 1 win is 1.5 months old but is THE most recent prior match and carries highest strategic relevance (both teams knew each other well by then). \u2022 Frankfurt's Jan wins are 3 months old, pre-dating potential meta shifts, roster adjustments, and tactical evolution. \u2022 7-day market price history shows YES rising +20.0pp but with high volatility (+17.0pp in 24h, \u00b130.5pp sharp moves). Suggests the market is overweighting Frankfurt's old January form or reacting to in-game score swings rather than stable structural advantage. LIVE MATCH STATUS AMPLIFICATION: \u2022 Event is LIVE (~1.8 hrs in). Sharp price moves suggest game is NOT a blowout in Frankfurt's favor. A 16:46 UTC drop of -14.5pp on YES (meaning NO gained) after an earlier +30.5pp spike suggests Frankfurt may have taken the lead then conceded map(s). In a BO3, map-level momentum is predictive. \u2022 If Frankfurt were as heavily favored structurally, we would expect stable high YES pricing during live play. Volatility suggests competitive balance or CGN performing better in-game. DATA GAPS / CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINTS: \u2022 No recent patch-specific data on Frankfurt's meta reading or composition. Briefing mentions Patch 11.11 but gives no comparative analysis of team preparedness. \u2022 No information on roster changes, stand-in usage, or player injury for either team in the 2.5 months between Feb-Mar and Apr 19 match. This is a material gap for NO confidence. \u2022 Limited detail on CGN's recent scrim/boot-camp activity. 9-1 form is strong but briefing offers no causal insight into whether it's sustainable vs in-tournament variance. \u2022 Briefing data is sparse on Frankfurt's psychological state post-March loss or tactical adjustments. Did they innovate, or are they repeating prior strats? FINAL PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: \u2022 P(YES) = 35%: Frankfurt faces a CGN team riding a 9-1 form, armed with a dominant 3-0 playoff win just 6 weeks prior. January dominance is stale and has been reversed. In-game volatility suggests competitive tension, not Frankfurt superiority. Frankfurt's 7-3 form is materially weaker. \u2022 P(NO) = 58%: CGN's recency advantage (Mar 1 3-0), better recent form (9-1), and demonstrated ability to win under playoff pressure (Feb 8 close series, Mar 1 stomp) position them as the true favorite despite market misprice. Probability exceeds 50% based on structural evidence. \u2022 Asymmetry (35 + 58 = 93): Reflects strong conviction on NO (underdog) side given recency and form data, but tempered confidence on YES side due to Frankfurt's older but real dominance and lack of current-patch invalidation in briefing. The gap signals the market may be anchoring to Frankfurt's Jan form without properly weighting the March reversal.", "key_factor": "CGN's most recent prior victory (Mar 1, 3-0 dominance) is more temporally proximate and decisively-weighted than Frankfurt's older January win streak, combined with Frankfurt's fragile recent form (7-3 record vs CGN's 9-1)."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "probability_yes": 0.58, "probability_no": 0.42, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE (started 1.8 hours ago, scheduled until ~21:00 UTC). Sharp moves detected (+30.5pp at 16:00, then -14.5pp at 16:46) indicate match progress influencing pricing. With significant time remaining, outcome is NOT yet determined. MARKET PRICE DRIFT: YES side has risen +20pp over 7 days and +17pp in 24h, indicating accumulating confidence in Frankfurt. Current 60% YES price reflects this momentum. NO side shows -20pp 7-day drift and -17pp 24h drift\u2014declining confidence in CGN. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: CGN's 9W-1L (90% recent win rate) is objectively stronger than Frankfurt's 7W-3L (70%). In standard competitive settings, this would favor CGN. However, H2H history and market pricing do not reflect this strength differential equally. HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE (Jan 2026): Frankfurt won 3 consecutive matches in January (Jan 15, 19, 26 scorelines: 13-4, 13-8, 13-9). This recency anchors Frankfurt's H2H credibility despite CGN's stronger current-form rating. RECENT REVERSAL (Feb-Mar 2026): CGN won decisively on Feb 8 (2-1 series) and March 1 (3-0 sweep). This 2-month period shows CGN reversing momentum, contradicting the January narrative. The March 1 3-0 is a clean, dominant victory. BASE RATE CONSIDERATION: In BO3 Valorant matches between teams with balanced/unclear skill advantage, historical data suggests near-parity outcomes. Frankfurt's 60% market price slightly exceeds CGN's form advantage, suggesting market may be overweighting H2H recency (Jan) vs. current form (March-April). VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $3,082 USD volume is modest for esports betting. Low liquidity can permit mispricing; sharp moves (+30.5pp, -14.5pp within 46 min) suggest active traders reacting to live match events, not stable pricing. RATING DIFFERENTIAL ODDITY: Frankfurt's historical ratings (1738\u21921611 range) vs. CGN's (1607\u21921538 range) show Frankfurt at higher absolute skill level across the dataset, supporting the 60% YES pricing despite CGN's superior recent form (9W-1L). UNRESOLVED LIVE STATE: Match is currently RUNNING. No in-match data (map scores, round counts, or win probability from competitive framework) is provided. Market price reflects trader sentiment + early-game observable state, not final outcome. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=62 reflects Frankfurt's H2H dominance, market momentum, and higher historical ratings\u2014but tempered by CGN's superior recent form (9W-1L vs 7W-3L) and Feb-Mar victories. confidence_no=58 reflects CGN's recent strength\u2014but weakened by Frankfurt's consistent H2H record and market skepticism. Neither side has overwhelming evidence; live match state is unknown.", "key_factor": "In competitive BO3 Valorant matches between teams with balanced recent form, the favored team (by rating/form) wins ~58-62% of the time. Frankfurt's 7W-3L recent form (70%) vs CGN's 9W-1L (90%) suggests CGN is currently stronger, but Frankfurt's historical H2H dominance and market pricing (60% YES) suggest Frankfurt remains slightly favored in this specific matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.45, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "LIVE/IMMINENT EVENT: Match started ~1.8 hours ago (15:00 UTC). Market prices should reflect live action or near-completion. Sharp moves (+30.5pp at 16:00 UTC, -14.5pp at 16:46 UTC) suggest real-time information flow. PRICE MOMENTUM: YES side rose +17pp in 24h, now at 60%. Crowd is leaning bullish on Frankfurt. NO side fell -17pp, now at 40%. This is a directional consensus trade, not balanced uncertainty. HISTORICAL DOMINANCE vs RECENT REVERSAL: Frankfurt won 3 straight in Jan 2026 (15th, 19th). But CGN reversed hard: Mar 1 (3-0 win), Feb 8 (2-1 win). Most recent prior match favors CGN heavily (3-0 scoreline 1.5 months ago). Frankfurt's Jan dominance is stale; CGN's Feb-Mar form is fresher. CURRENT-SEASON FORM: Frankfurt 7W-3L (70%), CGN 9W-1L (90%). CGN is statistically stronger this season. Market price (60% Frankfurt) does not fully reflect CGN's superior win rate. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY \u2014 RECENCY BIAS & NARRATIVE LAG: Briefing emphasizes Frankfurt's Jan wins prominently in CASE FOR YES, but glosses over CGN's 3-0 demolition on Mar 1. Market appears to have anchored on Frankfurt's earlier dominance and not fully repriced CGN's recent momentum shift. APATHY ON THE NO SIDE: The NO case (40% market price) mentions CGN's 3-0 win and Feb 8 victory but does not strongly highlight CGN's 90% current-season win rate (9-1). Market undervalues CGN's objective strength relative to Frankfurt's 70% rate. LIVE-ACTION SIGNAL: Sharp +30.5pp jump at 16:00 UTC (1 hour into match) suggests Frankfurt took an early lead or won a map. Sharp -14.5pp reversal at 16:46 UTC implies CGN either equalized or took the series lead. Match is competitive in real-time; final outcome still uncertain. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: Only $3,082 USD. Thin market \u2192 more susceptible to crowd panic buys / narrative-driven swings. The +20pp 7-day YES rally may reflect emotional buying rather than hard evidence. MISMATCHED CONFIDENCE: YES confidence should be moderate (Frankfurt has historical H2H edge, but CGN's form is superior and most recent H2H favors CGN). NO confidence is equally weak \u2014 neither team dominates all dimensions. Neither side has bulletproof fundamentals. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Frankfurt at 60% reflects crowd greed on the Frankfurt narrative + recency bias favoring Jan wins. But CGN's 90% season win rate + 3-0 recent victory justify ~55-58% for Frankfurt at floor. Market is overpriced on YES by 2-5pp due to narrative anchoring. Set probability_score at 62 (slight YES lean due to potential live momentum + Frankfurt's historical H2H edge), but low confidence on both sides due to live uncertainty and mixed fundamentals.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "probability_yes": 0.62, "probability_no": 0.58, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "LIVE/IMMINENT STATUS: Match began 1.8 hours ago (15:00 UTC scheduled, now ~16:46 UTC). Sharp price movements (+30.5pp at 16:00, -14.5pp at 16:46) suggest in-match data (likely map 1 result or mid-series momentum) is driving repricing. NO confidence must remain LOW due to inability to observe match state directly from briefing. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: Frankfurt 7W-3L (70%) vs CGN 9W-1L (90%) in last 10 matches\u2014CGN's recent window form is objectively stronger, contradicting the market's +60% YES implied confidence. This suggests either (1) Frankfurt favored due to H2H dominance, or (2) Frankfurt underweighted despite weaker recent rating window. H2H HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTRADICTION: Frankfurt won Jan 15, 19, 26 (three straight), but CGN reversed with Mar 1 3-0 win (most recent prior encounter ~1.5 months ago). Feb 8 shows CGN won 2-1. The H2H record heavily favors Frankfurt (6W-4L in last 10 H2H), yet recency (Mar 1) and current form (9W-1L) favor CGN. Regency bias cuts both ways. PRICE HISTORY SIGNAL: YES rising +20pp over 7 days (+17pp in 24h) while NO falling -20pp suggests retail/smart money believe Frankfurt momentum is building. However, live match volatility (\u00b114.5pp swings in minutes) indicates current prices reflect partial match resolution, not pre-match analysis. Caution: prices may reflect Map 1 outcome already settled. BO3 VALORANT FORMAT NUANCE: In BO3, the team winning Map 1 gains psychological momentum and map pool control for Map 2 veto advantage. The +30.5pp YES spike at 16:00 (match start +1hr) strongly suggests Frankfurt won Map 1; subsequent -14.5pp correction suggests CGN responded. This is NOT pre-match uncertainty\u2014it reflects live game state. Treat prices as LIVE-MATCH inference, not betting markets. RATING CONVERGENCE: Both teams show tightly clustered rating ranges (Frankfurt 1498\u20131738, CGN 1538\u20131607 across recent match history). No outlier rating suggests teams are skill-matched. The 9W-1L vs 7W-3L difference is NOT a 90% vs 70% skill gap; it reflects recent tournament draw/scheduling variance in a small sample. PATCH STABILITY: Patch 11.11 held across recent matches; no meta shift detected. Map pool (Bind, Ascent, Haven typical) consistent. No technical patch advantage to either team visible in briefing. VOLUME & MARKET DEPTH: $3,082 USD volume over 1 week is THIN for esports; spreads (YES 60%, NO 40%, sum=100% nominal) suggest low-confidence pricing with potential arbitrage. Thin volume means prices are NOT reflecting deep sophisticated betting\u2014they are driven by retail sentiment and live-match observations. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is LIVE and set to conclude by ~21:00 UTC (4 hours remaining per briefing window). If match extends beyond that window, resolution may require VLR.gg monitoring (2-hour publication window). Forfeit/disqualification resolves to 50-50, but unlikely mid-BO3. EXPERT INFERENCE: The +30.5pp YES spike at match start + current 60% YES price suggest Frankfurt winning Map 1 and holding lead through Map 2, but the -14.5pp correction indicates momentum shift (likely CGN won Map 2 or is threatening Map 3). Current 60/40 split reflects ~50/50 Map 3 belief if series is tied 1-1, with slight Frankfurt edge from H2H history. This is NOT a confident 60/40 split\u2014it is live-match noise. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: Frankfurt's Jan dominance +