ted as a potential negative for both. No asymmetric advantage is clearly articulated that would favor Virtus.pro despite weaker recent form. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES side has fallen 42.5pp in 24 hours, with sharp moves at 16:00 UTC (-25pp) and 16:46 UTC (-16.5pp) on Apr 19. These sharp moves occurred AFTER the match started, suggesting in-game events (likely Virtus.pro winning early games or performing well in the series so far) are driving the repricing. Market is responding to live match information not present in briefing. CURRENT MARKET PRICING: YES = 28% / NO = 72% reflects market belief that Virtus.pro is ahead in the match as it runs. The sharp repricing down for YES and up for NO mid-match (16:00\u201316:46 UTC window) suggests real in-game events have shifted the baseline. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (55) reflects the objective form advantage combined with live market repricing away from Tundra. Lower confidence in YES (45) because while Tundra's form is superior, the live match repricing suggests Virtus.pro may be performing better than pre-match expectations indicated, creating uncertainty about whether that form advantage is being realized in this specific series. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous \u2014 first team to win the BO3 (2 games) wins the match. No forfeit, cancel, or tie clauses appear relevant given match is running. PROBABILITY REFLECTS LIVE STATE: Given the match is RUNNING and market has repriced sharply toward NO, probability_score of 32 reflects that Tundra is behind in the live series but retains a plausible path to victory (one win away from tying 1-1, then decider). This is NOT a prediction of pre-match form, but rather an estimate of remaining win probability given apparent current game state implied by market repricing.", "key_factor": "Match is currently LIVE/RUNNING with unknown current game state; no in-game scoreline provided in briefing, creating uncertainty about whether outcome i