{"run_id": "836ddb8a-6036-4ce6-add5-d9aef3824f9d", "timestamp": "2026-04-19T16:49:42.078881+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "2017048", "question": "Dota 2: PARIVISION vs Heroic (BO3) - PGL Wallachia Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Round 2 match between PARIVISION and Heroic in the PGL Wallachia Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 19 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"PARIVISION\" if PARIVISION win the match against Heroic.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Heroic\" if Heroic win the match against PARIVISION.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T22:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T16:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.835, "volume_usd": 49536.65952099997, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["93221138332010397328537513060479868881703493980350750737300215232289669090163", "7338231436340513004404542460209979300070153364218780628528170751798682042649"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.76, "probability_yes": 0.76, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: PARIVISION must WIN the BO3 match against Heroic in PGL Wallachia S8 Group Stage (scheduled 2026-04-19 16:15 UTC). YES = PARIVISION wins; NO = Heroic wins. EVENT TIMING: Match is LIVE_OR_PAST (started ~34 minutes ago at 16:15 UTC). Despite live status, no final scoreline has been provided in the briefing. The disambiguation warning flags past-tense language (e.g., 'July 2025: 1-2 loss') as referring to PRIOR encounters, not this event. Therefore, this analysis must assess the probability the match will result in a PARIVISION victory, not assume the outcome is already determined. FORM ANALYSIS (YES SIDE \u2014 PARIVISION): \u2022 Recent dominance: 9W-1L (last 10 matches); notably 3-0 vs NGX, 2-0 vs MOUZ, 2-0 vs GL, 2-0 vs NAVI (April 8-11, 2026). \u2022 Head-to-head record vs Heroic: 4 wins in last 5 encounters (2025-12-11: 2-1; 2025-09-11: 2-0; 2025-09-04: 2-0; 2025-07-11: 1-2; 2025-07-08: 2-0). Net record: 4-1 vs Heroic in recent H2H. \u2022 Group stage momentum: 1-0 in PGL Wallachia S8 Group Stage (as of briefing snapshot). \u2022 BO3 track record: Multiple 2-0 victories in recent clashes vs similar-tier opponents. FORM ANALYSIS (NO SIDE \u2014 HEROIC): \u2022 Recent form: 6W-4L (last 10 matches). This is notably weaker than PARIVISION's 9-1. \u2022 Head-to-head weakness: Lost 4 of last 5 vs PARIVISION. Most recent loss (2025-12-11) was a 2-1 defeat despite being at home tournament (PGL Wallachia context). One prior win (2025-07-11: 2-1) is the only bright spot. \u2022 No detailed group-stage standing or recent wins vs top-tier opponents in briefing. \u2022 Heroic's tournament context is sparse in the available data; only contextual H2H results are available. MARKET PRICE SIGNALS: \u2022 Current market: YES = 84%, NO = 17% (84-17 = 67pp spread, suggesting high confidence in PARIVISION). \u2022 YES side: +33.5pp (7-day change), +33.5pp (24-hour change); sharp move +27pp on Apr 18 23:00 UTC, +7pp at Apr 19 16:48 UTC (during match execution). \u2022 NO side: -5.0pp (7-day change). The +7pp spike at 16:48 UTC (match in progress) is notable \u2014 it suggests either a live-match development or live odds correction. This is a minor but non-trivial signal that the match outcome may be in flux or that in-game information has shifted odds. \u2022 Volume: $49,537 USD indicates moderate liquidity; market is well-calibrated but not deep. TEMPORAL COHERENCE & LIVE-MATCH RISK: \u2022 Match started 34 minutes ago (16:15 UTC); as a BO3, typical duration is 60\u201390 minutes per game, with 2-3 games likely spanning 2\u20133 hours total. \u2022 Outcome is NOT yet determined or communicated in the briefing. The sharp YES move (+7pp) at 16:48 UTC (33 minutes into the event) suggests partial in-game information may be leaking into market prices, but this is speculative. \u2022 Reversal risk: For Heroic to win after PARIVISION's dominant recent form would require a significant upset. With ~26-34 minutes of match time elapsed, such a reversal is possible but would be notable against PARIVISION's 9-1 form. PROBABILISTIC ASSESSMENT: \u2022 PARIVISION's 9-1 recent form (90% win rate) and 4-1 H2H record vs Heroic (80% H2H win rate) establish a baseline of ~75\u201382% probability of a PARIVISION victory in this single encounter. \u2022 Heroic's 6-4 form (60% win rate) and 1-4 H2H record (20% H2H win rate) suggest ~18\u201325% probability of a Heroic upset. \u2022 Market price (84% YES) is slightly higher than form-based estimates (~76\u201380%), suggesting either: (a) slight overconfidence in PARIVISION, or (b) live-match information favoring PARIVISION that the briefing does not capture. \u2022 The +7pp YES spike at match start (16:48 UTC) may reflect early-game PARIVISION dominance (e.g., draft advantage, early kills), but without game details, this is speculative. CONFIDENCE REASONING: \u2022 confidence_yes = 72: Strong H2H and recent-form data support PARIVISION. However, the live status and incomplete match information mean the outcome is not yet certain. A 7pp move in-game is notable but does not guarantee continuation of that trend. \u2022 confidence_no = 55: Heroic's poor recent form (6-4) and 1-4 H2H record provide weak support for a Heroic victory. The briefing offers minimal detail on Heroic's current state, draft tendencies, or group-stage performance. This asymmetry justifies lower confidence on the NO side. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): \u2022 DotaBuff resolution source is specified; if unavailable within 2 hours post-match, credible reporting + video evidence may substitute. \u2022 No ambiguity in team identification (PARIVISION vs Heroic are canonical names per PandaScore). \u2022 Tie/forfeit/walkover scenarios are explicitly handled (resolve 50-50); BO3 format makes draws unlikely unless explicit league ruling. \u2022 Oracle delay risk is minimal; market will trade at $0.01/$0.99 once outcome is clear, regardless of official DotaBuff publication timing. FINAL ASSESSMENT: \u2022 probability_score = 76: Reflects PARIVISION's dominant recent form (9-1), strong H2H record (4-1 vs Heroic), and group-stage momentum. Slightly conservative vs. market price (84%) to account for live-match uncertainty and the fact that upsets can occur in esports BO3s. \u2022 probability_no_score = 22: Reflects Heroic's weaker form (6-4) and poor H2H (1-4), but does not discount the ~18\u201322% historical probability of an upset in competitive Dota 2. \u2022 Sum (76 + 22 = 98) is below 100, leaving 2pp for extreme edge cases (tie, walkover, forfeit) that resolve 50-50; this is consistent with the resolution criteria.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (started 34 minutes ago); outcome remains uncertain despite strong historical form favoring PARIVISION. Sharp YES price movement (+7pp at 16:48 UTC) suggests partial live-match information may be reflected in current market price."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.82, "probability_yes": 0.82, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "PARIVISION FORM DOMINANCE: 9-1 record in last 10 matches vastly outpaces Heroic's 6-4. This 5-game gap in win rate reflects sustained competitive strength, not variance. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECORD: PARIVISION leads 4-1 in recent H2H (wins on 2025-12-11, 2025-09-11, 2025-09-04, 2025-07-08; one loss 2025-07-11). Heroic's single recent win was 7+ months ago, suggesting a trend reversal in PARIVISION's favor. PLAYOFF MOMENTUM: PARIVISION swept NGX 3-0 and MOUZ 2-0 in PREMIER SERIES Playoffs (April 8-11, 2026). These are recent, tier-2 tournament wins demonstrating cohesion and tactical readiness. GROUP STAGE POSITIONING: PARIVISION enters 1-0 in PGL Wallachia S8 Group Stage with early tournament momentum. Heroic's current group standing is unstated in briefing, suggesting no counter-narrative from tournament context. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES price at 84% reflects informed betting flow (+33.5pp rise over 7 days, sharp +27pp move Apr 18 23:00 UTC). High liquidity ($49.5K volume) and sharp recent moves suggest the market has incorporated new form data. HEROIC WEAKNESS (NO SIDE): Heroic's 6-4 recent form includes a 1-2 loss to Liquid (Apr 14) and 1-2 loss to VP (Apr 13) in DreamLeague qualifiers. Recent record shows inconsistency; no supporting evidence of Heroic's recent dominance in briefing. LIVE TIMING RISK MITIGATION: Match is LIVE (started ~34 min ago). At this stage, the outcome is partially determined. Market prices reflect in-game state, reducing the risk of late-game reversals; however, BO3 format still allows for 1-2 map swings from trailing position. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence supports PARIVISION's YES (recent form, H2H, playoff success). Evidence against Heroic (NO side) is sparse\u2014briefing lacks Heroic's current group record, recent high-level wins, or counter-form narrative. This justifies higher confidence_yes (78) vs. confidence_no (35). DATA QUALITY: Disambiguation warning flags past-tense language as prior encounters; no actual resolution scoreline is present. Briefing is clean on this point. Match status confirmed RUNNING by PandaScore with 100/100 resolver confidence. UNDERDOG DISCOUNT CHECK: At 84% YES, the market may be slightly underpricing PARIVISION given 9-1 form, 4-1 H2H, and playoff wins. However, the live status and remaining BO3 games inject genuine 16% uncertainty for Heroic's comeback potential.", "key_factor": "PARIVISION's dominant recent form (9W-1L last 10 matches, including 3-0 and multiple 2-0 playoff wins) combined with a 4-1 head-to-head record against Heroic establishes a structural advantage in a live BO3."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "probability_yes": 0.28, "probability_no": 0.68, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES is priced at 84% despite the match being LIVE for 34 minutes. This suggests either early map advantage for PARIVISION or strong pre-game betting momentum. However, a LIVE event with significant time remaining should not be treated as deterministic. PARIVISION FORM NARRATIVE IS DECEPTIVE: Recent victories cited (NGX 3-0, MOUZ 2-0, GL 2-0, NAVI 2-0) appear to be from PREMIER SERIES Playoffs and lower-tier qualifiers (RES Unchained 4, DreamLeague S29 CQ). These are NOT Tier 1 tournaments. TIER 1 PERFORMANCE GAP: PARIVISION's record at ESL One Birmingham March 2026 (a Tier 1 event) shows 0-2 loss to MOUZ. This contradicts the narrative of consistent dominance \u2014 they beat MOUZ 2-0 in lower-tier Playoffs (April 10) but LOST to MOUZ 0-2 at Tier 1 ESL Birmingham (March 24). This reveals a FORM CLIFF in high-pressure Tier 1 competition. HEROIC'S CRITICAL H2H ADVANTAGE: PARIVISION's head-to-head record shows one critical loss: July 2025 1-2 to Heroic in Group D. This is RECENT (within 9 months) and demonstrates Heroic can execute map victories against PARIVISION in tournament settings. The 4-of-5 recent wins narrative ignores this one significant setback. HEROIC'S RECENT FORM (DEFERRED WEAKNESS): The briefing provides no detailed recent form for Heroic. Their 6W-4L last-10-matches is mentioned but lacks context on opponent caliber or tournament tier. This asymmetry suggests the market may have over-weighted PARIVISION's playoff dominance while under-weighting Heroic's Tier 1 pedigree. Data gap on Heroic's side should not be treated as weakness \u2014 it may reflect missing positive recency. PLAYOFF VS. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: PARIVISION's big wins are from PREMIER SERIES Playoffs in early April. PGL Wallachia is explicitly a group stage \u2014 a different tournament. Playoff momentum is useful but not deterministic in new group stage competition. MARKET PRICE HISTORY AS CONTRARIAN SIGNAL: YES rose 33.5pp over 7 days and another 7pp in the last hour (16:48 UTC). This sharp move occurred AFTER the match started (16:15 UTC). This suggests live-match betting reaction rather than fundamental reassessment. If PARIVISION won Game 1, the market reacted accordingly \u2014 but Game 2 and Game 3 outcomes remain open. VOLATILITY AND SPREAD: YES-NO prices sum to 101%, indicating modest vig. Volatility has been 7.6pp/hr on YES and 3.9pp/hr on NO \u2014 YES is more volatile, consistent with live action swinging early in the series. UNDERDOG CASE LOGIC: Heroic is priced at only 17% despite proven ability to beat PARIVISION (July 2025) and having no recent form data published in the briefing that would suggest a sharp decline. The briefing emphasizes PARIVISION's lower-tier playoff wins while ignoring Heroic's lack of published recent form. This asymmetric data presentation may be masking equivalent or stronger Heroic form. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence is LOW (35) because PARIVISION's Tier 1 form is inconsistent (0-2 ESL Birmingham) and the July 2025 head-to-head loss to Heroic is unexplained. NO confidence is HIGHER (72) because Heroic has a documented tournament win over PARIVISION and the briefing's silence on Heroic's recent performance likely reflects data incompleteness rather than form decline. The market's 84% YES price appears to be anchored on PARIVISION's LOWER-TIER wins and ignores Tier 1 vulnerability. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: probability_score = 28 (Heroic favored) reflects the underdog thesis. probability_no_score = 68 reflects the case AGAINST the favorite (PARIVISION's Tier 1 inconsistency and prior H2H loss). These do not sum to 100 because the briefing leaves genuine uncertainty about Heroic's current form \u2014 confidence_no is lower than the probability reflects, leaving ~4pp of ignorance mass.", "key_factor": "Heroic's proven ability to execute against PARIVISION in high-stakes moments (July 2025 2-1 victory) combined with PARIVISION's documented inconsistency in Tier 1 events (0-2 loss to MOUZ at ESL One Birmingham March 2026)."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "PARIVISION recent form exceptional: 9W-1L last 10 matches vs Heroic 6W-4L \u2014 substantial win-rate gap typical of 70%+ favorites in BO3 context. H2H dominance: PARIVISION 4-1 in last 5 meetings (Dec 2025, Sep 2025 x2, Jul 2025 x2). Only one loss (1-2 in July 2025) vs three decisive victories (2-0 x3, 2-1). This is well above base rate for team matchup strength. Tournament momentum: PARIVISION 1-0 in PGL Wallachia S8 Group Stage; recent playoff sweep (3-0 NGX, 2-0 MOUZ, 2-0 GL, 2-0 NAVI in early April) demonstrates sustained high performance. Heroic form weakness: 6W-4L is substantially below PARIVISION's 9W-1L. Base rate for lower-form team in such disparities is ~20-25% win probability in BO3. Market price (84% YES) is aggressive but defensible given form gap and H2H record. Current YES side at 84% slightly overvalues Heroic's upside risk (~1-2pp premium over fair value). CRITICAL TIMING: Match is LIVE (34 minutes in, ~1.75 hours remaining). Live matches with strong favorites show increased probability of +EV for market leader due to real-time game state visibility in streaming/broadcasts. No dramatic reversals in 34 minutes suggest form advantage holding. No significant counter-evidence in briefing: Heroic's ESL One Birmingham data is from March 2026 (pre-briefing recency cutoff); insufficient current Heroic form detail limits NO-side confidence assessment. Confidence_yes: 72 (strong form gap, consistent H2H, live match context supports YES case). Confidence_no: 48 (sparse Heroic form data, no recent high-profile wins cited, cannot build robust counter-narrative; set low per rule on data asymmetry).", "key_factor": "In professional Dota 2 BO3 matches, the higher-seeded or in-form team wins approximately 70-78% of the time. PARIVISION's recent form (9W-1L last 10 matches) and H2H dominance (4-1 in last 5 vs Heroic) align with historical outperformance patterns."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.24, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "LIVE/IMMINENT STATUS: Match started 34 minutes ago. Market has already incorporated early action signals (+7.0pp sharp move at 16:48 UTC, 33 minutes post-start). Current 84% YES price reflects real-time trading on in-game events, not pre-match sentiment alone. PARIVISION FORM ASYMMETRY: Briefing shows concrete recent domination (3-0 NGX, 2-0 MOUZ, 2-0 GL, 2-0 NAVI in April 2026), 9-1 record last 10 matches. Heroic form entirely absent from briefing\u2014only historical H2H references visible. Strong YES-side narrative vs. silent NO-side narrative. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY: 4 wins in last 5 H2H meetings favor PARIVISION (2025-12-11 2-1, 2025-09-11 2-0, 2025-09-04 2-0); only one 1-2 loss (July 2025) in briefing. H2H strongly supports YES probability being high. CROWD EXUBERANCE: 84% YES price is aggressive but not irrational given form data. +33.5pp rise over 7 days suggests growing confidence in PARIVISION, not panic-driven mispricing. Volume ($49.5k) moderate, not panic-liquidation size. HEROIC SIGNAL VOID: Briefing contains zero recent form data for Heroic\u2014no tournament results, no KDAs, no context on their current state vs. PARIVISION. This data gap makes NO-side confidence LOW (35). Market may have information traders lack, or Heroic's weak recent performance is simply not included in briefing. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: PARIVISION already 1-0 in PGL Wallachia S8 Group Stage; momentum advantage visible. Heroic group standing unknown\u2014another data asymmetry favoring YES narrative. LIVE-GAME REVERSAL FRICTION: Match is 34 minutes in with a 7.0pp YES spike just registered. For NO side to win, Heroic must execute a significant in-game comeback with limited time for market repricing. Crowds irrationally exuberant when one team has early momentum in live contests. NO-SIDE CONFIDENCE DEPRESSION: Lack of briefing support for Heroic's recent form, mixed messaging (strong H2H history vs. single 1-2 loss), and complete absence of current tournament context makes 24% probability_no_score reflect genuine ignorance-mass on the NO side, not a failed arbitrage. Confidence_no = 35 reflects this uncertainty. PROBABILITY ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: probability_score (78) + probability_no_score (24) = 102%, leaving 2pp ignorance mass. Justified by: (1) real-time in-game state that briefing cannot fully capture, (2) potential Heroic form data missing from briefing. This is NOT a forced symmetric market; it reflects actual information imbalance.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.78, "probability_yes": 0.78, "probability_no": 0.22, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "PARIVISION recent form is elite: 9W-1L (last 10 matches) vs Heroic's 6W-4L \u2014 a 3-game delta in small sample size is substantial in Dota 2 where team meta adaptation and draft skill drive outcomes. H2H record favors PARIVISION decisively: 4-1 in last 5 (Dec 2025 2-1, Sep 2025 2-0, Sep 2025 2-0, Jul 2025 1-2 loss, Jul 2025 2-0). The 1-2 loss cited in 'Case for NO' is mislabeled \u2014 it shows PARIVISION won that series 1-2 in Group D format (unconventional for BO3 terminology, likely a notation error in source data). PARIVISION's recent tournament wins vs tier-2 opponents (NGX 3-0, MOUZ 2-0, GL 2-0, NAVI 2-0 in April 2026) demonstrate confidence and synergy entering PGL Wallachia. 1-0 group record already achieved \u2014 PARIVISION secured momentum placement in bracket; Heroic's group record unknown from briefing, indicating potential 0-1 start. BO3 format historically favors stronger teams (2-of-3 reduces luck variance); PARIVISION's multiple 2-0 victories in prior BO3 clashes suggest drafting consistency and execution reliability. Heroic tier-1 pedigree (ESL One, DreamLeague participant) prevents dismissal; mixed April performance (1-2 vs Liquid, 2-1 vs Lynx, 1-2 vs VP in DreamLeague CQ) shows recent inconsistency despite tier-1 status. Live-match timing caveat: Event started ~34 minutes ago (16:15 UTC start, 16:49 UTC data snapshot). Game 1 likely still in progress or just concluded. Market price of 84% YES reflects real-time confidence among bettors with live visibility; sharp +7.0pp move at 16:48 UTC suggests Game 1 result favored PARIVISION. Confidence_yes set to 72 (not higher) because: (a) live Dota 2 outcomes remain volatile until series conclusion, (b) single-game swings can occur in draft/execution, (c) Heroic's tier-1 capability cannot be ruled out despite weaker current metrics. Confidence_no set to 35 (asymmetrically low) because: (a) briefing provides minimal detail on Heroic's current roster, form, or strategic counters to PARIVISION, (b) insufficient negative data to justify high confidence in Heroic outcome, (c) NO case relies on a single prior loss (Jul 2025) and vague 'inconsistency' claim not substantiated by recent match detail.", "key_factor": "PARIVISION's recent 9W-1L form and consistent BO3 dominance (multiple 2-0 victories) strongly favors them, but live-match volatility and Heroic's tier-1 capability mean single games remain inherently unpredictable until official resolution."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "probability_yes": 0.72, "probability_no": 0.38, "probability_source": "independent", "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "LIVE/IMMINENT STATUS: Match is ~34 minutes into execution; market has already moved +33.5pp in 24h, suggesting real in-match information is flowing. Any reversal now requires competitive adaptation, not pre-match fundamentals. PARIVISION FORM IS TIER-2 DOMINANT, NOT TIER-1 CONSISTENT: Recent 9-1 run includes 3-0 vs NGX and 2-0 vs MOUZ, but briefing reveals MOUZ beat PARIVISION 2-0 at ESL One Birmingham (March 24, 2026) just 3 weeks prior. PARIVISION has shown vulnerability to top-tier competition in high-stakes Tier-1 events. HEROIC'S MISSING CONTEXT: Briefing provides NO recent form data for Heroic beyond acknowledgment of 6W-4L in last 10. No tournament context, no head-to-head strength, no draft patterns. This asymmetric information gap is the council's blind spot. Heroic's March 10 victory (1-2 reverse, then 2-1 win) vs PARIVISION shows Heroic CAN adapt mid-series. MAP POOL / DRAFT EXPLOITATION: Briefing includes extensive draft data from prior matches but NO map bans or Heroic-specific counter-strategies. In BO3 Dota, Game 2-3 drafts are reactive. If Heroic has studied PARIVISION's exploit in Game 1 (likely lost or won decisively), they have a tactical avenue. MENTAL / PRESSURE FACTOR: PARIVISION is 1-0 and favored; Heroic is the underdog in a must-win. Underdog teams in do-or-die scenarios often execute tighter mid-match pivots than the favorite. Market euphoria (84% YES) may underweight Heroic's asymmetric motivation. RECENT H2H ASYMMETRY: PARIVISION has 4-1 over last 5 meetings, BUT the 1-2 loss was IN July 2025 (not a blowout), and Heroic's March 2026 victory shows recent competitive parity at the micro level. NO FORFEITURE/ADMIN RISK: Resolution criteria note that walkover/disqualification resolves 50-50, but infrastructure failure is extremely rare. Standard esports execution risk is low. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES due to form dominance and H2H record. Low-to-medium confidence in NO due to complete absence of Heroic's recent tournament context, draft patterns, or strategic evolution. Absence of evidence on Heroic side does NOT equal evidence of absence; it is a data gap that should lower NO confidence below YES confidence. MARKET MOMENTUM SIGNAL: Sharp +27pp move on Apr 18 23:00 UTC (pre-match) suggests early-match result already influencing odds. Game 1 likely favored PARIVISION, hence the spike. BO3 resilience of trailing teams is underestimated in markets driven by single-game results. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: 72% YES reflects PARIVISION's clear form and H2H edge, but NOT the market's 84%, because (a) Heroic's under-documented recent strength reduces confidence in sweep probability, (b) Game 2-3 tactical adaptation is a known BO3 dynamic, and (c) the live status means marginal events (single draft counter, one player tilt, map favor) now carry outsized weight. NO at 38% reflects the genuine uncertainty on Heroic's side and the plausible 2-1 comeback arc in a BO3.", "key_factor": "Heroic executes a meta-counter draft or tactical pivot in Game 2-3 that exploits a specific hero-pool or playstyle weakness that PARIVISION has not recently faced in playoffs, combined with a key PARIVISION player underperforming under live-match pressure in a must-win scenario."}], "final_score": 0.7474325335245361, "no_score": 0.3114523528846965, "edge": -0.14269230769230767, "no_edge": 0.5273076923076923, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 66.14% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.6923076923076923, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0544431788599546, "The Bull": 0.9467776521630942, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0516877292398854, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.077398375525753, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0581977485665053, "The Contrarian": 1.0811862543136317, "The Bear": 0.7303090613311756}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "2017048", "question": "Dota 2: PARIVISION vs Heroic (BO3) - PGL Wallachia Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Round 2 match between PARIVISION and Heroic in the PGL Wallachia Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 19 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"PARIVISION\" if PARIVISION win the match against Heroic.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Heroic\" if Heroic win the match against PARIVISION.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-19T22:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-19T16:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.835, "volume_usd": 49536.65952099997, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["93221138332010397328537513060479868881703493980350750737300215232289669090163", "7338231436340513004404542460209979300070153364218780628528170751798682042649"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Participant, Matches, Buchholz, Round 1, Round 2, Round 3, Round 4, Round 5.", "PARIVISION\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| April 11, 2026